{"zh": "第一篇 在基督里经历并享受神无边无际的赦免", "en": "Message 1 Experiencing and Enjoying the Unlimited Forgiveness of God in Christ", "norm_zh": "第一篇在基督里经历并享受神无边无际的赦免", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "Message 1 Experiencing and Enjoying the Unlimited Forgiveness of God in Christ"}
{"zh": "读经：尼九17下，诗三二1，八五2，八六5，一三〇4，赛五五7，耶三一34，但九9，太九1~8，二六28，路七47，二三34上，弗一7，西二13，约壹一9", "en": "Scripture Reading: Neh. 9:17b; Psa. 32:1; 85:2; 86:5; 130:4; Isa. 55:7; Jer. 31:34; Dan. 9:9; Matt. 9:1-8; 26:28; Luke 7:47; 23:34a; Eph. 1:7; Col. 2:13; 1 John 1:9", "norm_zh": "读经尼九17下诗三二1八五2八六5一三〇4赛五五7耶三一34但九9太九18二六28路七47二三34上弗一7西二13约壹一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Neh 917b Psa 321 852 865 1304 Isa 557 Jer 3134 Dan 99 Matt 918 2628 Luke 747 2334a Eph 17 Col 213 1 John 19"}
{"zh": "壹 我们的神是赦免的神，有恩典，有怜悯，不轻易发怒，且有丰盛的慈爱—尼九17下，诗八五2，八六5：", "en": "I.\tOur God is a God of forgiveness, gracious and compassionate, long-suffering and abounding in lovingkindness—Neh. 9:17b; Psa. 85:2; 86:5:", "norm_zh": "壹我们的神是赦免的神有恩典有怜悯不轻易发怒且有丰盛的慈爱尼九17下诗八五2八六5", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "I Our God is a God of forgiveness gracious and compassionate longsuffering and abounding in lovingkindnessNeh 917b Psa 852 865"}
{"zh": "一 路加十五章浪子父亲的举动，向我们展示了我们天父赦免的心—路十五20~24：", "en": "A.\tThe actions of the prodigal son’s father in Luke 15 show us the forgiving heart of our heavenly Father—Luke 15:20-24:1", "norm_zh": "一路加十五章浪子父亲的举动向我们展示了我们天父赦免的心路十五2024", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "A The actions of the prodigal sons father in Luke 15 show us the forgiving heart of our heavenly FatherLuke 1520241"}
{"zh": "1 浪子还在回家的路上，父亲看见了，就跑去迎接他；神对悔改罪人赦免的“脚”也是迅速的；祂只想早一点赦免人的罪—20节。", "en": "1.\tWhile the prodigal son was on his way home, the father saw him and ran to meet him; God’s “feet” of forgiveness toward a repentant sinner are also swift; He only wishes He could forgive man of his sins sooner—v. 20.", "norm_zh": "1浪子还在回家的路上父亲看见了就跑去迎接他神对悔改罪人赦免的脚也是迅速的祂只想早一点赦免人的罪20节", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "1 While the prodigal son was on his way home the father saw him and ran to meet him Gods feet of forgiveness toward a repentant sinner are also swift He only wishes He could forgive man of his sins soonerv 20"}
{"zh": "2 我们父亲赦免的心，大过我们求赦免的心；祂爱祂所买的人，甚至过于我们爱自己；祂极其急切地要赦免我们", "en": "2.\tThe forgiving heart of our Father is greater than our desire for forgiveness; He loves those whom He has purchased even more than we love ourselves; He is most eager to forgive us.", "norm_zh": "2我们父亲赦免的心大过我们求赦免的心祂爱祂所买的人甚至过于我们爱自己祂极其急切地要赦免我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:32:55.021351+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh", "norm_en": "2 The forgiving heart of our Father is greater than our desire for forgiveness He loves those whom He has purchased even more than we love ourselves He is most eager to forgive us"}
{"zh": "职事信息摘录：", "en": "Excerpts from the Ministry:", "norm_zh": "职事信息摘录", "norm_en": "Excerpts from the Ministry", "saved_at": "2026-07-03T14:33:19.750621+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate_en2zh"}
{"zh": "三\t如果主的十字架只解决人的罪和人自己，神在宇宙中的仇敌仍然存在，神的计划仍有拦阻；基督的十字架解决撒但—约十二31，来二14：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "C. If the cross of the Lord resolves only man's sins and man himself, God's enemy in the universe still exists, and God's plan is still hindered; the cross of Christ resolves Satan—John 12:31; Heb. 2:14:", "norm_zh": "三如果主的十字架只解决人的罪和人自己神在宇宙中的仇敌仍然存在神的计划仍有拦阻基督的十字架解决撒但约十二31来二14李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T16:04:31.009210+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate"}
{"zh": "壹\t基督复活的必须—林前十五14、17，罗四25，林后五21：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "I. The necessity of Christ's resurrection—1 Cor. 15:14, 17; Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21:", "norm_zh": "壹基督复活的必须林前十五1417罗四25林后五21李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T16:04:31.802804+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经自己的见证是说，“圣经都是神所默示的，于教训、督责、使人归正、教导人学义，都是有益的；叫属神的人得以完全，预备行各样的善事”（提后三16~17）。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "A. The Bible testifies of itself: \"All Scripture is God-breathed and profitable for teaching, for conviction, for correction, for instruction in righteousness, that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work\" (2 Tim. 3:16-17).", "norm_zh": "一圣经自己的见证是说圣经都是神所默示的于教训督责使人归正教导人学义都是有益的叫属神的人得以完全预备行各样的善事提后三1617倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T16:04:36.730415+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate"}
{"zh": "壹\t基督复活的必须—林前十五14、17，罗四25，林后五21：（2023年冬训，第八篇）", "en": "I. THE NECESSITY OF CHRIST'S RESURRECTION—1 Cor. 15:14, 17; Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21:", "norm_zh": "壹基督复活的必须林前十五1417罗四25林后五212023年冬训第八篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:25:37.793628+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I THE NECESSITY OF CHRISTS RESURRECTION1 Cor 1514 17 Rom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "壹\t神所赐给我们的恩典，不是任何物质的东西，也不仅仅是救恩、救赎或天堂；神所赐给我们的恩典，乃是一个神圣的人位；基督是神真实的恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "I. The grace God has given us is not any material thing, nor is it merely salvation, redemption, or heaven; the grace God has given us is a divine person; Christ is the true grace of God—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12:", "norm_zh": "壹神所赐给我们的恩典不是任何物质的东西也不仅仅是救恩救赎或天堂神所赐给我们的恩典乃是一个神圣的人位基督是神真实的恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The grace God has given us is not any material thing nor is it merely salvation redemption or heaven the grace God has given us is a divine person Christ is the true grace of GodJohn 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12"}
{"zh": "一\t唯有基督是真实的恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "A. Only Christ is the true grace—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12:", "norm_zh": "一惟有基督是真实的恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Only Christ is the true graceJohn 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12"}
{"zh": "1\t有些人以为，神爱世人，甚至将救恩、救赎、或天堂赐给相信祂儿子的人；他们信这就是恩典；其他人以为，好房子、好车子、好妻子、好丈夫、或顺从的儿女就是恩典；他们说神爱我们，甚至将许多美好的东西当作恩典赐给我们—约一14、16~17，赛五五1。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. Some think that God so loved the world that He gave salvation, redemption, or heaven to those who believe in His Son; they believe that this is grace; others think that a good house, a fine car, a nice wife, a good husband, or obedient children are grace; they say that God so loved us that He gave us many good things as grace—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1.", "norm_zh": "1有些人以为神爱世人甚至将救恩救赎或天堂赐给相信祂儿子的人他们信这就是恩典其他人以为好房子好车子好妻子好丈夫或顺从的儿女就是恩典他们说神爱我们甚至将许多美好的东西当作恩典赐给我们约一141617赛五五1李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Some think that God so loved the world that He gave salvation redemption or heaven to those who believe in His Son they believe that this is grace others think that a good house a fine car a nice wife a good husband or obedient children are grace they say that God so loved us that He gave us many good things as graceJohn 114 1617 Isa 551"}
{"zh": "2\t但这些东西不是恩典，因为不是神在实际里所赐给我们的—约一14、16~17。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. But these things are not grace, for they are not what God has given us in reality—John 1:14, 16-17.", "norm_zh": "2但这些东西不是恩典因为不是神在实际里所赐给我们的约一141617李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 But these things are not grace for they are not what God has given us in realityJohn 114 1617"}
{"zh": "二\t在腓立比三章八节保罗告诉我们，基督以外的一切都是垃圾、粪土；我们可能认为是恩典的一切东西，实际上是垃圾；基督不是垃圾，祂是全然超绝。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "B. In Philippians 3:8 Paul tells us that everything other than Christ is rubbish, dung; everything we may consider as grace is actually rubbish; Christ is not rubbish; He is altogether superb.", "norm_zh": "二在腓立比三章八节保罗告诉我们基督以外的一切都是垃圾粪土我们可能认为是恩典的一切东西实际上是垃圾基督不是垃圾祂是全然超绝李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In Philippians 38 Paul tells us that everything other than Christ is rubbish dung everything we may consider as grace is actually rubbish Christ is not rubbish He is altogether superb"}
{"zh": "三\t约翰一章一节、十四节和十六节说，“太初有话，话与神同在，话就是神。……话成了肉体，支搭帐幕在我们中间，丰丰满满地有恩典，有实际。……从祂的丰满里我们都领受了，而且恩上加恩”； 所以，恩典乃是三一神成为肉体，来作我们的分，给我们享受。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "C. John 1:1, 14, and 16 say, \"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God... And the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us..., full of grace and reality... For of His fullness we have all received, and grace upon grace\"; therefore, grace is the Triune God incarnated to be our portion for our enjoyment.", "norm_zh": "三约翰一章一节十四节和十六节说太初有话话与神同在话就是神话成了肉体支搭帐幕在我们中间丰丰满满地有恩典有实际从祂的丰满里我们都领受了而且恩上加恩所以恩典乃是三一神成为肉体来作我们的分给我们享受李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-07T17:27:50.886267+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C John 11 14 and 16 say In the beginning was the Word and the Word was with God and the Word was God And the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us full of grace and reality For of His fullness we have all received and grace upon grace therefore grace is the Triune God incarnated to be our portion for our enjoyment"}
{"zh": "读经：提后三15~16，约一1，五39~40，六63，彼前一23，二2，太四4，罗十五4", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 3:15-16; John 1:1; 5:39-40; 6:63; 1 Pet. 1:23; 2:2; Matt. 4:4; Rom. 15:4", "norm_zh": "读经提后三1516约一1五3940六63彼前一23二2太四4罗十五4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 31516 John 11 53940 663 1 Pet 123 22 Matt 44 Rom 154"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经的来源；我们得救以后，要得着属灵的栽培，就不能不认识圣经；两千年来，基督徒都承认一件事，没有一个人不认识圣经，而能好好认识主—提后三16，约一1：", "en": "I. The Source of the Bible; after we are saved, to receive spiritual edification, we must know the Bible; in the past two thousand years Christians all acknowledge that no one can truly know the Lord without knowing the Bible—2 Tim. 3:16; John 1:1:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经的来源我们得救以后要得着属灵的栽培就不能不认识圣经两千年来基督徒都承认一件事没有一个人不认识圣经而能好好认识主提后三16约一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Source of the Bible after we are saved to receive spiritual edification we must know the Bible in the past two thousand years Christians all acknowledge that no one can truly know the Lord without knowing the Bible2 Tim 316 John 11"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经是神的呼出；圣经不是出于人的意思，不是出于人的思想，乃是神将祂的意思，将祂的话语，借着祂的灵，呼到写圣经的人里面—提后三16，彼后一20~21。", "en": "A. The Bible is God-breathed; the Bible is not something that comes from man’s ideas or thoughts; rather, God breathed His thoughts and His words, through His Spirit, into those who wrote the Bible—2 Tim. 3:16; 2 Pet. 1:20-21.", "norm_zh": "一圣经是神的呼出圣经不是出于人的意思不是出于人的思想乃是神将祂的意思将祂的话语借着祂的灵呼到写圣经的人里面提后三16彼后一2021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible is Godbreathed the Bible is not something that comes from mans ideas or thoughts rather God breathed His thoughts and His words through His Spirit into those who wrote the Bible2 Tim 316 2 Pet 12021"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经是人被圣灵推动，从神说出来的；第一是人被圣灵推动；第二是从神说出来；在希腊原文，被圣灵推动的意思，就如同帆船被风推动一样—20~21节：", "en": "B. The Bible is men speaking from God, being borne by the Holy Spirit; first, men were borne by the Spirit; second, men spoke from God; in the original Greek, being borne by the Holy Spirit means being carried along as a ship by the wind—vv. 20-21:", "norm_zh": "二圣经是人被圣灵推动从神说出来的第一是人被圣灵推动第二是从神说出来在希腊原文被圣灵推动的意思就如同帆船被风推动一样2021节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Bible is men speaking from God being borne by the Holy Spirit first men were borne by the Spirit second men spoke from God in the original Greek being borne by the Holy Spirit means being carried along as a ship by the windvv 2021"}
{"zh": "1\t当日写圣经的人，是受了神的灵感，在圣灵的能力之下，被圣灵吹着、带着而说出神的话来—可十二36。", "en": "1. The writers of the Bible received God’s inspiration, and they were under the power of the Holy Spirit, being borne and carried along by Him to speak out God’s word—Mark 12:36.", "norm_zh": "1当日写圣经的人是受了神的灵感在圣灵的能力之下被圣灵吹着带着而说出神的话来可十二36", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The writers of the Bible received Gods inspiration and they were under the power of the Holy Spirit being borne and carried along by Him to speak out Gods wordMark 1236"}
{"zh": "2\t并且他们说话，是从神里面说出来的；是神的灵推动人说的，也是人从神里面说出来的—出三四27。", "en": "2. Furthermore, when they spoke, they spoke from within God; it was the Spirit of God carrying men along to speak, and it was also men speaking from within God—Exo. 34:27.", "norm_zh": "2并且他们说话是从神里面说出来的是神的灵推动人说的也是人从神里面说出来的出三四27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Furthermore when they spoke they spoke from within God it was the Spirit of God carrying men along to speak and it was also men speaking from within GodExo 3427"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经是神在众先知里面说话，并在祂儿子里面说话；旧约是神在众先知里面说话，新约是神在祂儿子我们的主耶稣里面说话—来一1~2。", "en": "C. The Bible is God’s speaking in the prophets and in His Son; the Old Testament is God’s speaking in the prophets; the New Testament is God’s speaking in the Son, our Lord Jesus—Heb. 1:1-2.", "norm_zh": "三圣经是神在众先知里面说话并在祂儿子里面说话旧约是神在众先知里面说话新约是神在祂儿子我们的主耶稣里面说话来一12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Bible is Gods speaking in the prophets and in His Son the Old Testament is Gods speaking in the prophets the New Testament is Gods speaking in the Son our Lord JesusHeb 112"}
{"zh": "四\t圣经是圣灵所启示的；“只等实际的灵来了，祂要引导你们进入一切的实际，因为祂不是凭自己说的，乃是把祂所听见的都说出来；并要把将来的事告诉你们”—约十六13，林前二13。", "en": "D. The Bible is revealed by the Holy Spirit; “But when He, the Spirit of reality, comes, He will guide you into all the reality; for He will not speak from Himself, but whatever He hears He will speak; and He will disclose to you what is to come.”—John 16:13; 1 Cor. 2:13.", "norm_zh": "四圣经是圣灵所启示的只等实际的灵来了祂要引导你们进入一切的实际因为祂不是凭自己说的乃是把祂所听见的都说出来并要把将来的事告诉你们约十六13林前二13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Bible is revealed by the Holy Spirit But when He the Spirit of reality comes He will guide you into all the reality for He will not speak from Himself but whatever He hears He will speak and He will disclose to you what is to comeJohn 1613 1 Cor 213"}
{"zh": "五\t所以全部圣经都是出于神的话语，逐字逐句，一点一画，都是神所默示的，人不可加添，也不可删减—太五18，启二二18~19。", "en": "E. Hence, the entire Bible originates from God; every word and every sentence, every iota and every tittle, are God-inspired; men should neither add to or take away anything from the Holy Scriptures—Matt. 5:18; Rev. 22:18-19.", "norm_zh": "五所以全部圣经都是出于神的话语逐字逐句一点一画都是神所默示的人不可加添也不可删减太五18启二二1819", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Hence the entire Bible originates from God every word and every sentence every iota and every tittle are Godinspired men should neither add to or take away anything from the Holy ScripturesMatt 518 Rev 221819"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的功用—约五39，提后三15，彼前一23，二2，太四4，罗十五4：", "en": "II. The Function of the Bible—John 5:39; 2 Tim. 3:15; 1 Pet. 1:23; 2:2; Matt. 4:4; Rom. 15:4:", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的功用约五39提后三15彼前一23二2太四4罗十五4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The Function of the BibleJohn 539 2 Tim 315 1 Pet 123 22 Matt 44 Rom 154"}
{"zh": "一\t给主耶稣作见证；圣经的第一个功用，是给主耶稣作见证；主耶稣是圣经的题目，是圣经的内容；圣经是主耶稣的说明，是主耶稣的发表—约五39，一1：", "en": "A. To testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible; the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus—John 5:39; 1:1:", "norm_zh": "一给主耶稣作见证圣经的第一个功用是给主耶稣作见证主耶稣是圣经的提目是圣经的内容圣经是主耶稣的说明是主耶稣的发表约五39一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A To testify concerning the Lord Jesus the first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus the Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord JesusJohn 539 11"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经这写的话，若没有主耶稣那活的话作实际，圣经就不过是空洞的道理，虚空的字句—十四16，一14。", "en": "1. The Bible, God’s written Word, must have the Lord Jesus, the living Word, as its reality; otherwise, it is but mere doctrines and empty letters.—14:16; 1:14.", "norm_zh": "1圣经这写的话若没有主耶稣哪活的话作实际圣经就不过是空洞的道理虚空的字句十四16一14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Bible Gods written Word must have the Lord Jesus the living Word as its reality otherwise it is but mere doctrines and empty letters1416 114"}
{"zh": "2\t不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的，就是旧约各部分，无论是摩西的律法、先知的书、诗篇，无不都是为主耶稣作见证，说到主耶稣；我们若要认识主耶稣，就非读圣经，非明白圣经不可—五39。", "en": "2. Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus, but every part of the Old Testament, whether (1) the Law of Moses, (2) the Prophets, or (3) the Psalms, testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus; if we want to know the Lord Jesus, we must read and understand the Bible.—5:39.", "norm_zh": "2不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的就是旧约各部分无论是摩西的律法先知的书诗篇无不都是为主耶稣作见证说到主耶稣我们若要认识主耶稣就非读圣经非明白圣经不可五39", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus but every part of the Old Testament whether 1 the Law of Moses 2 the Prophets or 3 the Psalms testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus if we want to know the Lord Jesus we must read and understand the Bible539"}
{"zh": "二\t使人有得救的智慧；圣经的功用，一面是为着主耶稣，一面是为着我们；在为着我们这一面，圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧—提后三15，箴十九20，西一9。", "en": "B. Making men wise unto salvation; the functions of the Bible are of two aspects: one aspect is to serve the Lord, and the other aspect is to serve us; the first function of the Bible toward us is to make us wise unto salvation.—2 Tim. 3:15; Prov. 19:20; Col. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "二使人有得救的智慧圣经的功用一面是为着主耶稣一面是为着我们在为着我们这一面圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧提后三15箴十九20西一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Making men wise unto salvation the functions of the Bible are of two aspects one aspect is to serve the Lord and the other aspect is to serve us the first function of the Bible toward us is to make us wise unto salvation2 Tim 315 Prov 1920 Col 19"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用，就是使我们得蒙重生—彼前一23、3：", "en": "C. The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated.—1 Pet. 1:23, 3:", "norm_zh": "三圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用就是使我们得蒙重生彼前一233", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated1 Pet 123 3"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经是活神的话，里面含着活神的生命—提后三16，约六63。", "en": "1. The Bible is the Word of the living God, and it contains the life of the living God.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63.", "norm_zh": "1圣经是活神的话里面含着活神的生命提后三16约六63", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Bible is the Word of the living God and it contains the life of the living God2 Tim 316 John 663"}
{"zh": "2\t当我们用信心接受圣经的话到我们里面时，圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面，将神的生命种在我们里面，使我们有了神的生命，而得着重生—彼前一23。", "en": "2. When we receive the word of the Scriptures into us by faith, it comes into us like a seed of life, sowing God’s life into us; thus, we have God’s life and are regenerated.—1 Pet. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "2当我们用信心接受圣经的话到我们里面时圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面将神的生命种在我们里面使我们有了神的生命而得着重生彼前一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we receive the word of the Scriptures into us by faith it comes into us like a seed of life sowing Gods life into us thus we have Gods life and are regenerated1 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "四\t圣经的话有的也像奶一样，能喂养我们，使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大；所以一个初得重生的信徒，必须爱慕圣经的话，像才生的婴孩一样，爱慕那诚实的话奶—二2，来五13。", "en": "D. Some portions of the Scriptures are like milk that can nourish us and make us grow in our spiritual life; hence, a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible, like newborn babes longing for the guileless milk of the word.—2:2; Heb. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "四圣经的话有的也像奶一样能喂养我们使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大所以一个初得重生的信徒必须爱慕圣经的话像才生的婴孩一样爱慕哪诚实的话奶二2来五13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Some portions of the Scriptures are like milk that can nourish us and make us grow in our spiritual life hence a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible like newborn babes longing for the guileless milk of the word22 Heb 513"}
{"zh": "五\t圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物；我们要在神面前作一个活泼而刚强的人，不能单靠食物，也必须靠神口里所出的一切话，就是圣经的话—太四4，耶十五16。", "en": "E. The Bible is food for our spiritual life; if we want to be strong and living before God, we cannot live on bread alone; we need the word that proceeds out of the mouth of God, which is the word of the Bible.—Matt. 4:4; Jer. 15:16.", "norm_zh": "五圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物我们要在神面前作一个活泼而刚强的人不能单靠食物也必须靠神口里所出的一切话就是圣经的话太四4耶十五16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Bible is food for our spiritual life if we want to be strong and living before God we cannot live on bread alone we need the word that proceeds out of the mouth of God which is the word of the BibleMatt 44 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "六\t圣经的教训能叫我们有忍耐，蒙激励，而得有盼望；圣经中也记载了许多事，能作我们的鉴戒，使我们受警戒—罗十五4，林前十11。", "en": "F. The teachings of the Bible can give us endurance, encouragement, and hope; the Bible also records many things as warnings to us that we may be admonished.—Rom. 15:4; 1 Cor. 10:11.", "norm_zh": "六圣经的教训能叫我们有忍耐蒙激励而得有盼望圣经中也记载了许多事能作我们的鉴戒使我们受警戒罗十五4林前十11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The teachings of the Bible can give us endurance encouragement and hope the Bible also records many things as warnings to us that we may be admonishedRom 154 1 Cor 1011"}
{"zh": "叁\t所有世俗的书在性质上是相同的，然而圣经与其他的书不同；圣经是独特的—提后三16，约六63，太四4：", "en": "III. Whereas all secular books are the same in nature, the Bible is different from other books; the Bible is unique.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63; Matt. 4:4:", "norm_zh": "叁所有世俗的书在性质上是相同的然而圣经与其他的书不同圣经是独特的提后三16约六63太四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Whereas all secular books are the same in nature the Bible is different from other books the Bible is unique2 Tim 316 John 663 Matt 44"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经是神的气，而神的气是神的灵，因为神乃是灵；我们必须是不断吸入主的人，一直吸入神的人；我们读圣经该是一种吸入，我们教导圣经该是一种呼出—提后三16，约四24，参二十22。", "en": "A. The Bible is God's breath, and God's breath is God's Spirit, because God is Spirit; we must be those who are continuously inhaling the Lord, constantly inhaling God; our reading of the Bible should be an inhaling, and our teaching of the Bible should be an exhaling.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 4:24; cf. 20:22.", "norm_zh": "一圣经是神的气而神的气是神的灵因为神乃是灵我们必须是不断吸入主的人一直吸入神的人我们读圣经该是一种吸入我们教导圣经该是一种呼出提后三16约四24参二十22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible is Gods breath and Gods breath is Gods Spirit because God is Spirit we must be those who are continuously inhaling the Lord constantly inhaling God our reading of the Bible should be an inhaling and our teaching of the Bible should be an exhaling2 Tim 316 John 424 cf 2022"}
{"zh": "二\t从主耶稣口里所出的话就是灵；我们借着运用我们的灵接受祂的话，就得着那赐人生命的灵；我们读圣经，就该接受生命；我们教导别人圣经的事，他们就该接受生命—六63，五39~40。", "en": "B. The words that proceed out of the mouth of the Lord Jesus are Spirit; when we receive His words by exercising our spirit, we get the Spirit, who gives life; when we read the Bible, we should receive life; when we teach others the things of the Bible, they should receive life.—6:63; 5:39-40.", "norm_zh": "二从主耶稣口里所出的话就是灵我们借着运用我们的灵接受祂的话就得着哪赐人生命的灵我们读圣经就该接受生命我们教导别人圣经的事他们就该接受生命六63五3940", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The words that proceed out of the mouth of the Lord Jesus are Spirit when we receive His words by exercising our spirit we get the Spirit who gives life when we read the Bible we should receive life when we teach others the things of the Bible they should receive life663 53940"}
{"zh": "三\t那灵是神的话；我们读圣经，必须摸著神的话是那灵；基督徒借着圣经蒙光照、受督责、被改正并受教导，这是很平常的，但不多人经历圣经的话是击杀仇敌的剑—弗六17~18：", "en": "C. The Spirit is the word of God; when we read the Bible, we must touch the word of God as the Spirit; it is common for Christians to be enlightened, rebuked, corrected, and instructed by the Bible, but not many experience the word of the Bible as a sword that kills the enemy.—Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "三哪灵是神的话我们读圣经必须摸着神的话是哪灵基督徒借着圣经蒙光照受督责被改正并受教导这是很平常的但不多人经历圣经的话是击杀仇敌的剑弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Spirit is the word of God when we read the Bible we must touch the word of God as the Spirit it is common for Christians to be enlightened rebuked corrected and instructed by the Bible but not many experience the word of the Bible as a sword that kills the enemyEph 61718"}
{"zh": "1\t保罗说到“那灵的剑，那灵就是神的话”；剑不直接是话；剑直接是那灵，然后那灵就是话—17节。", "en": "1. Paul speaks of \"the sword of the Spirit, which Spirit is the word of God\"; the sword is not the word directly; the sword is the Spirit directly, and then the Spirit is the word.—v. 17.", "norm_zh": "1保罗说到哪灵的剑哪灵就是神的话剑不直接是话剑直接是哪灵然后哪灵就是话17节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Paul speaks of the sword of the Spirit which Spirit is the word of God the sword is not the word directly the sword is the Spirit directly and then the Spirit is the wordv 17"}
{"zh": "2\t没有那是灵的话作击杀的剑，多年来我们就无法蒙保守在召会生活里；我们借着话作为那灵的击杀，就能蒙保守在召会生活和职事里—17节。", "en": "2. Without the word as the Spirit to be the killing sword, there would be no way for us to be kept in the church life over the years; we are kept in the church life and in the ministry through the killing of the word as the Spirit.—v. 17.", "norm_zh": "2没有哪是灵的话作击杀的剑多年来我们就无法蒙保守在召会生活里我们借着话作为哪灵的击杀就能蒙保守在召会生活和职事里17节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Without the word as the Spirit to be the killing sword there would be no way for us to be kept in the church life over the years we are kept in the church life and in the ministry through the killing of the word as the Spiritv 17"}
{"zh": "3\t我们需要以活的方式接受神的话，就是接受话作为那灵；然后那灵会成为击杀的剑；这话首先直接击杀我们，然后间接击杀空中黑暗的权势—17~18节。", "en": "3. We need to receive the word of God in a living way, that is, receive the word as the Spirit; then the Spirit will become the killing sword; this word first kills us directly and then kills the power of darkness in the air indirectly.—vv. 17-18.", "norm_zh": "3我们需要以活的方式接受神的话就是接受话作为哪灵然后哪灵会成为击杀的剑这话首先直接击杀我们然后间接击杀空中黑暗的权势1718节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We need to receive the word of God in a living way that is receive the word as the Spirit then the Spirit will become the killing sword this word first kills us directly and then kills the power of darkness in the air indirectlyvv 1718"}
{"zh": "四\t从神口里所出的话，是我们真正的食物，这指明圣经不仅为着分赐生命，也为着滋养；我们教导别人圣经时，该滋养他们—太四4，诗一一九103，耶十五16。", "en": "D. The word that proceeds out of the mouth of God is our real food; this indicates that the Bible is not only for life-imparting but also for nourishing; when we teach the Bible to others, we should nourish them.—Matt. 4:4; Psa. 119:103; Jer. 15:16.", "norm_zh": "四从神口里所出的话是我们真正的食物这指明圣经不仅为着分赐生命也为着滋养我们教导别人圣经时该滋养他们太四4诗一一九103耶十五16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:51:12.894654+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The word that proceeds out of the mouth of God is our real food this indicates that the Bible is not only for lifeimparting but also for nourishing when we teach the Bible to others we should nourish themMatt 44 Psa 119103 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "读经：提后三16，约一1，五39~40，提后三15，彼前一23，二2，太四4，罗十五4，约六63", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 3:16; John 1:1; 5:39-40; 2 Tim. 3:15; 1 Pet. 1:23; 2:2; Matt. 4:4; Rom. 15:4; John 6:63", "norm_zh": "读经提后三16约一1五3940提后三15彼前一23二2太四4罗十五4约六63", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 316 John 11 53940 2 Tim 315 1 Pet 123 22 Matt 44 Rom 154 John 663"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经的来源；我们得救以后，要得着属灵的栽培，就不能不认识圣经；两千年来，基督徒都承认一件事，没有一个人不认识圣经，而能好好认识主—提后三16，约一1：（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "I. The Source of the Bible; after we are saved, if we are to receive spiritual edification, we cannot but know the Bible; in the past two thousand years Christians all acknowledge that no one can truly know the Lord without knowing the Bible—2 Tim. 3:16; John 1:1:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经的来源我们得救以后要得着属灵的栽培就不能不认识圣经两千年来基督徒都承认一件事没有一个人不认识圣经而能好好认识主提后三16约一1真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Source of the Bible after we are saved if we are to receive spiritual edification we cannot but know the Bible in the past two thousand years Christians all acknowledge that no one can truly know the Lord without knowing the Bible2 Tim 316 John 11"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经是神的呼出；圣经不是出于人的意思，不是出于人的思想，乃是神将祂的意思，将祂的话语，借着祂的灵，呼到写圣经的人里面—提后三16，彼后一20~21。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "A. The Bible is God’s breathing out; the Bible is not out of man’s will, nor out of man’s thoughts, but God breathed His thoughts and His words, through His Spirit, into the writers of the Bible—2 Tim. 3:16; 2 Pet. 1:20-21.", "norm_zh": "一圣经是神的呼出圣经不是出于人的意思不是出于人的思想乃是神将祂的意思将祂的话语借着祂的灵呼到写圣经的人里面提后三16彼后一2021真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible is Gods breathing out the Bible is not out of mans will nor out of mans thoughts but God breathed His thoughts and His words through His Spirit into the writers of the Bible2 Tim 316 2 Pet 12021"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经是人被圣灵推动，从神说出来的；第一是人被圣灵推动；第二是从神说出来；在希腊原文，被圣灵推动的意思，就如同帆船被风推动一样—20~21节：（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "B. The Bible is men borne by the Holy Spirit and speaking from God; first, men were borne by the Holy Spirit; second, men spoke from God; in the original Greek, being borne by the Holy Spirit means being carried along as a ship by the wind—vv. 20-21:", "norm_zh": "二圣经是人被圣灵推动从神说出来的第一是人被圣灵推动第二是从神说出来在希腊原文被圣灵推动的意思就如同帆船被风推动一样2021节真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Bible is men borne by the Holy Spirit and speaking from God first men were borne by the Holy Spirit second men spoke from God in the original Greek being borne by the Holy Spirit means being carried along as a ship by the windvv 2021"}
{"zh": "1\t当日写圣经的人，是受了神的灵感，在圣灵的能力之下，被圣灵吹着、带着而说出神的话来—可十二36。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "1. The writers of the Bible received God’s inspiration, and they were under the power of the Holy Spirit, being borne and carried along by Him to speak out God’s word—Mark 12:36.", "norm_zh": "1当日写圣经的人是受了神的灵感在圣灵的能力之下被圣灵吹着带着而说出神的话来可十二36真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The writers of the Bible received Gods inspiration and they were under the power of the Holy Spirit being borne and carried along by Him to speak out Gods wordMark 1236"}
{"zh": "2\t并且他们说话，是从神里面说出来的；是神的灵推动人说的，也是人从神里面说出来的—出三四27。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "2. Furthermore, when they spoke, they spoke from within God; it was the Spirit of God carrying men along to speak, and it was also men speaking from within God—Exo. 34:27.", "norm_zh": "2并且他们说话是从神里面说出来的是神的灵推动人说的也是人从神里面说出来的出三四27真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Furthermore when they spoke they spoke from within God it was the Spirit of God carrying men along to speak and it was also men speaking from within GodExo 3427"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经是神在众先知里面说话，并在祂儿子里面说话；旧约是神在众先知里面说话，新约是神在祂儿子我们的主耶稣里面说话—来一1~2。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "C. The Bible is God’s speaking in the prophets and speaking in His Son; the Old Testament is God’s speaking in the prophets, and the New Testament is God’s speaking in the Son, our Lord Jesus—Heb. 1:1-2.", "norm_zh": "三圣经是神在众先知里面说话并在祂儿子里面说话旧约是神在众先知里面说话新约是神在祂儿子我们的主耶稣里面说话来一12真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Bible is Gods speaking in the prophets and speaking in His Son the Old Testament is Gods speaking in the prophets and the New Testament is Gods speaking in the Son our Lord JesusHeb 112"}
{"zh": "四\t圣经是圣灵所启示的；“只等实际的灵来了，祂要引导你们进入一切的实际，因为祂不是凭自己说的，乃是把祂所听见的都说出来；并要把将来的事告诉你们”—约十六13，林前二13。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "D. The Bible is revealed by the Holy Spirit; “But when He, the Spirit of reality, comes, He will guide you into all the reality; for He will not speak from Himself, but whatever He hears He will speak; and He will disclose to you what is to come.”—John 16:13; 1 Cor. 2:13.", "norm_zh": "四圣经是圣灵所启示的只等实际的灵来了祂要引导你们进入一切的实际因为祂不是凭自己说的乃是把祂所听见的都说出来并要把将来的事告诉你们约十六13林前二13真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Bible is revealed by the Holy Spirit But when He the Spirit of reality comes He will guide you into all the reality for He will not speak from Himself but whatever He hears He will speak and He will disclose to you what is to comeJohn 1613 1 Cor 213"}
{"zh": "五\t所以全部圣经都是出于神的话语，逐字逐句，一点一画，都是神所默示的，人不可加添，也不可删减—太五18，启二二18~19。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "E. Hence, the entire Bible originates from God; every word and every sentence, every iota and every tittle, are God-inspired; men should neither add to nor take away anything—Matt. 5:18; Rev. 22:18-19.", "norm_zh": "五所以全部圣经都是出于神的话语逐字逐句一点一画都是神所默示的人不可加添也不可删减太五18启二二1819真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Hence the entire Bible originates from God every word and every sentence every iota and every tittle are Godinspired men should neither add to nor take away anythingMatt 518 Rev 221819"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的功用—约五39，提后三15，彼前一23，二2，太四4，罗十五4：（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "II. The Function of the Bible—John 5:39; 2 Tim. 3:15; 1 Pet. 1:23; 2:2; Matt. 4:4; Rom. 15:4:", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的功用约五39提后三15彼前一23二2太四4罗十五4真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The Function of the BibleJohn 539 2 Tim 315 1 Pet 123 22 Matt 44 Rom 154"}
{"zh": "一\t给主耶稣作见证；圣经的第一个功用，是给主耶稣作见证；主耶稣是圣经的题目，是圣经的内容；圣经是主耶稣的说明，是主耶稣的发表—约五39，一1：（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "A. To testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible; the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus—John 5:39; 1:1:", "norm_zh": "一给主耶稣作见证圣经的第一个功用是给主耶稣作见证主耶稣是圣经的提目是圣经的内容圣经是主耶稣的说明是主耶稣的发表约五39一1真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A To testify concerning the Lord Jesus the first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus the Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord JesusJohn 539 11"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经这写的话，若没有主耶稣那活的话作实际，圣经就不过是空洞的道理，虚空的字句—十四16，一14。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "1. The Bible, God’s written Word, must have the Lord Jesus, the living Word, as its reality; otherwise, it is but mere doctrines and empty letters—14:16; 1:14.", "norm_zh": "1圣经这写的话若没有主耶稣哪活的话作实际圣经就不过是空洞的道理虚空的字句十四16一14真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Bible Gods written Word must have the Lord Jesus the living Word as its reality otherwise it is but mere doctrines and empty letters1416 114"}
{"zh": "2\t不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的，就是旧约各部分，无论是摩西的律法、先知的书、诗篇，无不都是为主耶稣作见证，说到主耶稣；我们若要认识主耶稣，就非读圣经，非明白圣经不可—五39。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "2. Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus, but every part of the Old Testament, whether the Law of Moses, the Prophets, or the Psalms, testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus; if we want to know the Lord Jesus, we must read and understand the Bible—5:39.", "norm_zh": "2不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的就是旧约各部分无论是摩西的律法先知的书诗篇无不都是为主耶稣作见证说到主耶稣我们若要认识主耶稣就非读圣经非明白圣经不可五39真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus but every part of the Old Testament whether the Law of Moses the Prophets or the Psalms testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus if we want to know the Lord Jesus we must read and understand the Bible539"}
{"zh": "二\t使人有得救的智慧；圣经的功用，一面是为着主耶稣，一面是为着我们；在为着我们这一面，圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧—提后三15，箴十九20，西一9。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "B. To make men wise unto salvation; the functions of the Bible are of two aspects: one aspect is to serve the Lord, and the other aspect is to serve us; toward us, the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation—2 Tim. 3:15; Prov. 19:20; Col. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "二使人有得救的智慧圣经的功用一面是为着主耶稣一面是为着我们在为着我们这一面圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧提后三15箴十九20西一9真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B To make men wise unto salvation the functions of the Bible are of two aspects one aspect is to serve the Lord and the other aspect is to serve us toward us the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation2 Tim 315 Prov 1920 Col 19"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用，就是使我们得蒙重生—彼前一23、3：（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "C. The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated—1 Pet. 1:23, 3:", "norm_zh": "三圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用就是使我们得蒙重生彼前一233真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated1 Pet 123 3"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经是活神的话，里面含着活神的生命—提后三16，约六63。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "1. The Bible is the Word of the living God, and it contains the life of the living God—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63.", "norm_zh": "1圣经是活神的话里面含着活神的生命提后三16约六63真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Bible is the Word of the living God and it contains the life of the living God2 Tim 316 John 663"}
{"zh": "2\t当我们用信心接受圣经的话到我们里面时，圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面，将神的生命种在我们里面，使我们有了神的生命，而得着重生—彼前一23。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "2. When we receive the word of the Scriptures into us by faith, it comes into us like a seed of life, sowing God’s life into us; thus, we have God’s life and are regenerated—1 Pet. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "2当我们用信心接受圣经的话到我们里面时圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面将神的生命种在我们里面使我们有了神的生命而得着重生彼前一23真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we receive the word of the Scriptures into us by faith it comes into us like a seed of life sowing Gods life into us thus we have Gods life and are regenerated1 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "四\t圣经的话有的也像奶一样，能喂养我们，使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大；所以一个初得重生的信徒，必须爱慕圣经的话，像才生的婴孩一样，爱慕那诚实的话奶—二2，来五13。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "D. Some portions of the word of the Bible are also like milk, which can nourish us and cause us to grow gradually in our spiritual life; hence, a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible, like newborn babes longing for the guileless milk of the word—2:2; Heb. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "四圣经的话有的也像奶一样能喂养我们使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大所以一个初得重生的信徒必须爱慕圣经的话像才生的婴孩一样爱慕哪诚实的话奶二2来五13真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Some portions of the word of the Bible are also like milk which can nourish us and cause us to grow gradually in our spiritual life hence a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible like newborn babes longing for the guileless milk of the word22 Heb 513"}
{"zh": "五\t圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物；我们要在神面前作一个活泼而刚强的人，不能单靠食物，也必须靠神口里所出的一切话，就是圣经的话—太四4，耶十五16。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "E. The Bible is food for our spiritual life; if we want to be strong and living before God, we cannot live on bread alone; we need the word that proceeds out of the mouth of God, which is the word of the Bible—Matt. 4:4; Jer. 15:16.", "norm_zh": "五圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物我们要在神面前作一个活泼而刚强的人不能单靠食物也必须靠神口里所出的一切话就是圣经的话太四4耶十五16真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Bible is food for our spiritual life if we want to be strong and living before God we cannot live on bread alone we need the word that proceeds out of the mouth of God which is the word of the BibleMatt 44 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "六\t圣经的教训能叫我们有忍耐，蒙激励，而得有盼望；圣经中也记载了许多事，能作我们的鉴戒，使我们受警戒—罗十五4，林前十11。（真理课程—第一级（卷一），第一课）", "en": "F. The teachings of the Bible can give us endurance, encouragement, and hope; the Bible also records many things as warnings to us that we may be admonished—Rom. 15:4; 1 Cor. 10:11.", "norm_zh": "六圣经的教训能叫我们有忍耐蒙激励而得有盼望圣经中也记载了许多事能作我们的鉴戒使我们受警戒罗十五4林前十11真理课程第一级卷一第一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The teachings of the Bible can give us endurance encouragement and hope the Bible also records many things as warnings to us that we may be admonishedRom 154 1 Cor 1011"}
{"zh": "叁\t所有世俗的书在性质上是相同的，然而圣经与其他的书不同；圣经是独特的—提后三16，约六63，太四4：（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章）", "en": "III. Whereas all secular books are the same in nature, the Bible is different from other books; the Bible is unique—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63; Matt. 4:4:", "norm_zh": "叁所有世俗的书在性质上是相同的然而圣经与其他的书不同圣经是独特的提后三16约六63太四4李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Whereas all secular books are the same in nature the Bible is different from other books the Bible is unique2 Tim 316 John 663 Matt 44"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经是神的气，而神的气是神的灵，因为神乃是灵；我们必须是不断吸入主的人，一直吸入神的人；我们读圣经该是一种吸入，我们教导圣经该是一种呼出—提后三16，约四24，参二十22。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第二章）", "en": "A. The Bible is God's breath, and God's breath is God's Spirit, because God is Spirit; we must be those who are continually inhaling the Lord, always inhaling God; our reading of the Bible should be an inhaling, and our teaching of the Bible should be an exhaling.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 4:24; cf. 20:22.", "norm_zh": "一圣经是神的气而神的气是神的灵因为神乃是灵我们必须是不断吸入主的人一直吸入神的人我们读圣经该是一种吸入我们教导圣经该是一种呼出提后三16约四24参二十22李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible is Gods breath and Gods breath is Gods Spirit because God is Spirit we must be those who are continually inhaling the Lord always inhaling God our reading of the Bible should be an inhaling and our teaching of the Bible should be an exhaling2 Tim 316 John 424 cf 2022"}
{"zh": "二\t从主耶稣口里所出的话就是灵；我们借着运用我们的灵接受祂的话，就得着那赐人生命的灵；我们读圣经，就该接受生命；我们教导别人圣经的事，他们就该接受生命—六63，五39~40。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第二章）", "en": "B. The words that proceed out of the mouth of the Lord Jesus are spirit; when we receive His words by exercising our spirit, we get the Spirit, who gives life; when we read the Bible, we should receive life; when we teach others concerning the Bible, they should receive life.—6:63; 5:39-40.", "norm_zh": "二从主耶稣口里所出的话就是灵我们借着运用我们的灵接受祂的话就得着哪赐人生命的灵我们读圣经就该接受生命我们教导别人圣经的事他们就该接受生命六63五3940李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The words that proceed out of the mouth of the Lord Jesus are spirit when we receive His words by exercising our spirit we get the Spirit who gives life when we read the Bible we should receive life when we teach others concerning the Bible they should receive life663 53940"}
{"zh": "三\t那灵是神的话；我们读圣经，必须摸著神的话是那灵；基督徒借着圣经蒙光照、受督责、被改正并受教导，这是很平常的，但不多人经历圣经的话是击杀仇敌的剑—弗六17~18：（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第二章）", "en": "C. The Spirit is the word of God; when we read the Bible, we must touch the word of God as the Spirit; it is common for Christians to be enlightened, rebuked, corrected, and instructed by the Bible, but not many experience the word of the Bible as a sword that kills the enemy.—Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "三哪灵是神的话我们读圣经必须摸着神的话是哪灵基督徒借着圣经蒙光照受督责被改正并受教导这是很平常的但不多人经历圣经的话是击杀仇敌的剑弗六1718李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Spirit is the word of God when we read the Bible we must touch the word of God as the Spirit it is common for Christians to be enlightened rebuked corrected and instructed by the Bible but not many experience the word of the Bible as a sword that kills the enemyEph 61718"}
{"zh": "1\t保罗说到“那灵的剑，那灵就是神的话”；剑不直接是话；剑直接是那灵，然后那灵就是话—17节。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第二章）", "en": "1. Paul speaks of \"the sword of the Spirit, which Spirit is the word of God\"; the sword is not the word directly; the sword is the Spirit directly, and then the Spirit is the word.—v. 17.", "norm_zh": "1保罗说到哪灵的剑哪灵就是神的话剑不直接是话剑直接是哪灵然后哪灵就是话17节李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Paul speaks of the sword of the Spirit which Spirit is the word of God the sword is not the word directly the sword is the Spirit directly and then the Spirit is the wordv 17"}
{"zh": "2\t没有那是灵的话作击杀的剑，多年来我们就无法蒙保守在召会生活里；我们借着话作为那灵的击杀，就能蒙保守在召会生活和职事里—17节。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第二章）", "en": "2. Without the word as the Spirit to be the killing sword, there would be no way for us to be kept in the church life over the years; we are kept in the church life and in the ministry through the killing of the word as the Spirit.—v. 17.", "norm_zh": "2没有哪是灵的话作击杀的剑多年来我们就无法蒙保守在召会生活里我们借着话作为哪灵的击杀就能蒙保守在召会生活和职事里17节李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Without the word as the Spirit to be the killing sword there would be no way for us to be kept in the church life over the years we are kept in the church life and in the ministry through the killing of the word as the Spiritv 17"}
{"zh": "3\t我们需要以活的方式接受神的话，就是接受话作为那灵；然后那灵会成为击杀的剑；这话首先直接击杀我们，然后间接击杀空中黑暗的权势—17~18节。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第二章）", "en": "3. We need to receive the word of God in a living way, that is, receive the word as the Spirit; then the Spirit will become the killing sword; this word first kills us directly and then kills the power of darkness in the air indirectly.—vv. 17-18.", "norm_zh": "3我们需要以活的方式接受神的话就是接受话作为哪灵然后哪灵会成为击杀的剑这话首先直接击杀我们然后间接击杀空中黑暗的权势1718节李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We need to receive the word of God in a living way that is receive the word as the Spirit then the Spirit will become the killing sword this word first kills us directly and then kills the power of darkness in the air indirectlyvv 1718"}
{"zh": "四\t从神口里所出的话，是我们真正的食物，这指明圣经不仅为着分赐生命，也为着滋养；我们教导别人圣经时，该滋养他们—太四4，诗一一九103，耶十五16。（李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第二章）", "en": "D. The word that proceeds out of the mouth of God is our real food, indicating that the Bible is not only for life-imparting but also for nourishing; when we teach the Bible to others, we should nourish them.—Matt. 4:4; Psa. 119:103; Jer. 15:16.", "norm_zh": "四从神口里所出的话是我们真正的食物这指明圣经不仅为着分赐生命也为着滋养我们教导别人圣经时该滋养他们太四4诗一一九103耶十五16李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:53:10.968517+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The word that proceeds out of the mouth of God is our real food indicating that the Bible is not only for lifeimparting but also for nourishing when we teach the Bible to others we should nourish themMatt 44 Psa 119103 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "读经：提后二15，三16，创一1，三1、6，加四4，弗五32，太十六16~18，启十九17", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 2:15; 3:16; Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; Gal. 4:4; Eph. 5:32; Matt. 16:16-18; Rev. 19:17", "norm_zh": "读经提后二15三16创一1三16加四4弗五32太十六1618启十九17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 215 316 Gen 11 31 6 Gal 44 Eph 532 Matt 161618 Rev 1917"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要认识任何一本书，都需要先抓住它的总纲和中心，也需要对它的结构有正确的分析，而清楚认识它的分段；圣经也有它的总纲、中心和分段—提后二15，三16。", "en": "I. If we want to know any book, we have to grasp its subject and central thought. In addition, we need a proper analysis of its structure and a clear understanding of its sections; the Bible has its own subject, its central thought, and its sections.—2 Tim. 2:15; 3:16.", "norm_zh": "壹我们要认识任何一本书都需要先抓住它的总纲和中心也需要对它的结构有正确的分析而清楚认识它的分段圣经也有它的总纲中心和分段提后二15三16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I If we want to know any book we have to grasp its subject and central thought In addition we need a proper analysis of its structure and a clear understanding of its sections the Bible has its own subject its central thought and its sections2 Tim 215 316"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的总纲只有四句话：神计划创造，撒但背叛破坏，人堕落失去，基督救赎建造—创一1，三1、6，加四4~5：", "en": "II. The subject of the Bible is contained in only four sentences: God planned and created, Satan rebelled and damaged, man fell and was lost, and Christ redeemed and built.—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; Gal. 4:4-5:", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的总纲只有四句话神计划创造撒但背叛破坏人堕落失去基督救赎建造创一1三16加四45", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The subject of the Bible is contained in only four sentences God planned and created Satan rebelled and damaged man fell and was lost and Christ redeemed and builtGen 11 31 6 Gal 445"}
{"zh": "一\t在这总纲里头，有四个人物：第一是神，第二是撒但，第三是人，第四是基督；在全圣经里头几乎就是讲这四个人物—创一1，三1、6，约十七3：", "en": "A. Within this subject, there are four persons: the first is God, the second is Satan, the third is man, and the fourth is Christ; the whole Bible speaks almost exclusively of these four persons.—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; John 17:3:", "norm_zh": "一在这总纲里头有四个人物第一是神第二是撒但第三是人第四是基督在全圣经里头几乎就是讲这四个人物创一1三16约十七3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Within this subject there are four persons the first is God the second is Satan the third is man and the fourth is Christ the whole Bible speaks almost exclusively of these four personsGen 11 31 6 John 173"}
{"zh": "1\t神是计划和创造；计划是在永世里头的，创造是在时间里面的—创一1、26节注1。", "en": "1. God planned and created; He planned in eternity past and created in time.—Gen. 1:1, 26 note 1.", "norm_zh": "1神是计划和创造计划是在永世里头的创造是在时间里面的创一126节注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God planned and created He planned in eternity past and created in timeGen 11 26 note 1"}
{"zh": "2\t撒但是背叛和破坏；神有了祂的计划，并照着祂的计划有所创造，撒但就背叛神，破坏神的创造—三1~7。", "en": "2. Satan rebelled and damaged; God had His plan and created according to His plan, but Satan rebelled against God and damaged God’s creation.—3:1-7.", "norm_zh": "2撒但是背叛和破坏神有了祂的计划并照着祂的计划有所创造撒但就背叛神破坏神的创造三17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Satan rebelled and damaged God had His plan and created according to His plan but Satan rebelled against God and damaged Gods creation317"}
{"zh": "3\t人是堕落和失去；人堕落了，结果就从神的手中，神的用处上失去了—六3，三24。", "en": "3. Man fell and was lost; man fell and, as a result, was lost from God’s hands and from being used by God.—6:3; 3:24.", "norm_zh": "3人是堕落和失去人堕落了结果就从神的手中神的用处上失去了六3三24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Man fell and was lost man fell and as a result was lost from Gods hands and from being used by God63 324"}
{"zh": "4\t基督是救赎和建造；神照着祂的计划创造万有和人类，撒但高傲背叛神，凭着他的恶意破坏神的创造，使人堕落、失去，基督就来救赎，将人建造成祂荣耀的教会—加四4，太十六18。", "en": "4. Christ redeemed and built; God created all things and mankind according to His plan, Satan proudly rebelled against God and damaged God's creation with his evil intent, causing man to fall and be lost, and Christ came to redeem, building man into His glorious church.—Gal. 4:4; Matt. 16:18.", "norm_zh": "4基督是救赎和建造神照着祂的计划创造万有和人类撒但高傲背叛神凭着他的恶意破坏神的创造使人堕落失去基督就来救赎将人建造成祂荣耀的教会加四4太十六18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Christ redeemed and built God created all things and mankind according to His plan Satan proudly rebelled against God and damaged Gods creation with his evil intent causing man to fall and be lost and Christ came to redeem building man into His glorious churchGal 44 Matt 1618"}
{"zh": "二\t在基督徒中间，说到基督，恐怕都仅仅说到救赎，而忽略了，或者说没有看清楚建造的问题；我们不能光是看到救赎，还得看到建造—13~18节：", "en": "B. Among Christians, when speaking about Christ, perhaps they speak only of redemption, while the matter of building is overlooked or missed; we must not see redemption only; we must see the building also.—vv. 13-18:", "norm_zh": "二在基督徒中间说到基督恐怕都仅仅说到救赎而忽略了或者说没有看清楚建造的问提我们不能光是看到救赎还得看到建造1318节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Among Christians when speaking about Christ perhaps they speak only of redemption while the matter of building is overlooked or missed we must not see redemption only we must see the building alsovv 1318"}
{"zh": "1\t在圣经开头的地方，就给我们看见精金、珍珠、还有宝石，这些都是建造的材料—创二10~12。", "en": "1. At the beginning of the Bible, we see pure gold, pearls, and precious stones, which are all building materials.—Gen. 2:10-12.", "norm_zh": "1在圣经开头的地方就给我们看见精金珍珠还有宝石这些都是建造的材料创二1012", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 At the beginning of the Bible we see pure gold pearls and precious stones which are all building materialsGen 21012"}
{"zh": "2\t到了圣经末了的地方，就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了，是用精金、珍珠和宝石建造成功的；神最终所要得着的一个东西，就是一所的建筑—启二一18~21。", "en": "2. At the end of the Bible, we see a building that has come forth, built with pure gold, pearls, and precious stones; what God ultimately desires to obtain is a building.—Rev. 21:18-21.", "norm_zh": "2到了圣经末了的地方就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了是用精金珍珠和宝石建造成功的神最终所要得着的一个东西就是一所的建筑启二一1821", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 At the end of the Bible we see a building that has come forth built with pure gold pearls and precious stones what God ultimately desires to obtain is a buildingRev 211821"}
{"zh": "三\t旧约圣经的总纲是神创造，撒但破坏，人堕落，神应许基督来救赎；在旧约里的基督，乃是人的一个盼望，因为是神所应许给堕落之人的一位救赎主—创一1，三1、6，赛九6。", "en": "C. The subject of the Old Testament is that God created, Satan damaged, man fell, and God promised the coming of Christ for redemption; the Christ in the Old Testament was only a hope for man, because He was only promised by God to the fallen man as a Redeemer.—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; Isa. 9:6.", "norm_zh": "三旧约圣经的总纲是神创造撒但破坏人堕落神应许基督来救赎在旧约里的基督乃是人的一个盼望因为是神所应许给堕落之人的一位救赎主创一1三16赛九6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The subject of the Old Testament is that God created Satan damaged man fell and God promised the coming of Christ for redemption the Christ in the Old Testament was only a hope for man because He was only promised by God to the fallen man as a RedeemerGen 11 31 6 Isa 96"}
{"zh": "四\t新约圣经的总纲是基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人，建造教会；基督照着神的计划，来救赎罪人，建造成为祂荣耀的教会，作祂奥秘的身体，使神在祂里面得着一个团体的器皿，彰显祂自己—加四4~5，太十六18，约二19，弗二21~22，五27。", "en": "D. The subject of the New Testament is Christ coming to redeem sinners and to build up the church according to God’s plan; Christ, according to God’s plan, came to redeem sinners and build them up into His glorious church as His mystical Body for God to have a corporate vessel in Him to express Himself.—Gal. 4:4-5; Matt. 16:18; John 2:19; Eph. 2:21-22; 5:27.", "norm_zh": "四新约圣经的总纲是基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人建造教会基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人建造成为祂荣耀的教会作祂奥秘的身体使神在祂里面得着一个团体的器皿彰显祂自己加四45太十六18约二19弗二2122五27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The subject of the New Testament is Christ coming to redeem sinners and to build up the church according to Gods plan Christ according to Gods plan came to redeem sinners and build them up into His glorious church as His mystical Body for God to have a corporate vessel in Him to express HimselfGal 445 Matt 1618 John 219 Eph 22122 527"}
{"zh": "叁\t圣经的中心乃是基督和教会；圣经不光是启示基督自己，同时也启示基督的一个配偶，基督的一个身体，就是教会—32节，太十六16~18：", "en": "III. The central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church; the Bible not only reveals Christ Himself; it also reveals the bride and the Body of Christ, which is the church.—v. 32; Matt. 16:16-18:", "norm_zh": "叁圣经的中心乃是基督和教会圣经不光是启示基督自己同时也启示基督的一个配偶基督的一个身体就是教会32节太十六1618", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church the Bible not only reveals Christ Himself it also reveals the bride and the Body of Christ which is the churchv 32 Matt 161618"}
{"zh": "一\t基督是圣经的内容，圣经是基督的说明；把基督从圣经里拿去，圣经变作一本空的书；你只有读圣经这一个说明，才能懂得，才能认识基督是怎样一回事—西三11，约十四6。", "en": "A. Christ is the content of the Bible, and the Bible is the explanation of Christ; if we take away Christ from the Bible, the Bible will become an empty book; only when one reads the explanation in the Bible can he understand and know what Christ is.—Col. 3:11; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "一基督是圣经的内容圣经是基督的说明把基督从圣经里拿去圣经变作一本空的书你只有读圣经这一个说明才能懂得才能认识基督是怎样一回事西三11约十四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ is the content of the Bible and the Bible is the explanation of Christ if we take away Christ from the Bible the Bible will become an empty book only when one reads the explanation in the Bible can he understand and know what Christ isCol 311 John 146"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经所说的，乃是基督的一切摆在教会里，借着教会来彰显；所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会，光认识基督还不够，还得有教会—弗五32，三10：", "en": "B. The Bible tells us that everything of Christ is put into the church and expressed through the church; hence, the central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church; it is insufficient to know Christ only; we have to know the church as well.—Eph. 5:32; 3:10:", "norm_zh": "二圣经所说的乃是基督的一切摆在教会里借着教会来彰显所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会光认识基督还不够还得有教会弗五32三10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Bible tells us that everything of Christ is put into the church and expressed through the church hence the central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church it is insufficient to know Christ only we have to know the church as wellEph 532 310"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说，亚当这个人独居不好；到了新约我们就知道，这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶—创二18，林后十一2，弗五31~32。", "en": "1. From the very beginning the Bible reveals this in a type—that it was not good for Adam to live alone; we know from the New Testament that this typifies the fact that Christ needs a bride.—Gen. 2:18; 2 Cor. 11:2; Eph. 5:31-32.", "norm_zh": "1圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说亚当这个人独居不好到了新约我们就知道这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶创二18林后十一2弗五3132", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 From the very beginning the Bible reveals this in a typethat it was not good for Adam to live alone we know from the New Testament that this typifies the fact that Christ needs a brideGen 218 2 Cor 112 Eph 53132"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣来了，那位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说，这是神的羔羊，除去世人罪孽的；他也在那里证实说，娶新妇的就是新郎—约一29，三29。", "en": "2. When the Lord Jesus came, John the Baptist, who was His forerunner, not only declared, This is the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world; he also testified there, He who has the bride is the bridegroom.—John 1:29; 3:29.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣来了哪位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说这是神的羔羊除去世人罪孽的他也在哪里证实说娶新妇的就是新郎约一29三29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When the Lord Jesus came John the Baptist who was His forerunner not only declared This is the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world he also testified there He who has the bride is the bridegroomJohn 129 329"}
{"zh": "3\t到书信里头，使徒保罗说，我把你们这些得救的人，许配给一个丈夫，如同贞洁的童女献给基督—林后十一2。", "en": "3. In the Epistles, the apostle Paul says, I betrothed you, the saved ones, to one Husband to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.—2 Cor. 11:2.", "norm_zh": "3到书信里头使徒保罗说我把你们这些得救的人许配给一个丈夫如同贞洁的童女献给基督林后十一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In the Epistles the apostle Paul says I betrothed you the saved ones to one Husband to present you as a pure virgin to Christ2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "4\t到了启示录，有一个宣告说，羔羊婚娶的时候到了；新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐，预备好了，等候丈夫；那就是神人合一，所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个，成了宇宙的奥秘，就是基督与教会—启十九7，二一2。", "en": "4. In Revelation there is a declaration saying that the marriage of the Lamb has come; the New Jerusalem is prepared as a bride adorned for her husband; that is the oneness of God and man, in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one, becoming the mystery of the universe, which is Christ and the church.—Rev. 19:7; 21:2.", "norm_zh": "4到了启示录有一个宣告说羔羊婚娶的时候到了新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐预备好了等候丈夫哪就是神人合一所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个成了宇宙的奥秘就是基督与教会启十九7二一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 In Revelation there is a declaration saying that the marriage of the Lamb has come the New Jerusalem is prepared as a bride adorned for her husband that is the oneness of God and man in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one becoming the mystery of the universe which is Christ and the churchRev 197 212"}
{"zh": "三\t旧约的中心—引到基督以得救赎；旧约是把人引到基督，要人从祂得着救赎—伯五20，赛五九20。", "en": "C. The center of the Old Testament—leading to Christ for redemption; the Old Testament leads man to Christ that man would be redeemed by Him.—Job 5:20; Isa. 59:20.", "norm_zh": "三旧约的中心引到基督以得救赎旧约是把人引到基督要人从祂得着救赎伯五20赛五九20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The center of the Old Testamentleading to Christ for redemption the Old Testament leads man to Christ that man would be redeemed by HimJob 520 Isa 5920"}
{"zh": "四\t新约的中心—在基督里教会得蒙救赎并建造；新约就给我们看见，在基督里教会怎样得蒙救赎，而被建造—弗二4~5、22。", "en": "D. The center of the New Testament—the church being redeemed and built up in Christ; the New Testament shows us how the church is redeemed and built up in Christ.—Eph. 2:4-5, 22.", "norm_zh": "四新约的中心在基督里教会得蒙救赎并建造新约就给我们看见在基督里教会怎样得蒙救赎而被建造弗二4522", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The center of the New Testamentthe church being redeemed and built up in Christ the New Testament shows us how the church is redeemed and built up in ChristEph 245 22"}
{"zh": "肆\t圣经的分段有好多种分法，我们从其中选出两种比较重要的来看—提后二15，三16：", "en": "IV. There are many ways to subdivide the Bible into sections. We have selected two of the more important ways for our consideration.—2 Tim. 2:15; 3:16:", "norm_zh": "肆圣经的分段有好多种分法我们从其中选出两种比较重要的来看提后二15三16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV There are many ways to subdivide the Bible into sections We have selected two of the more important ways for our consideration2 Tim 215 316"}
{"zh": "一\t照着结构而分—来十一3：", "en": "A. Subdivision according to structure—Heb. 11:3:", "norm_zh": "一照着结构而分来十一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Subdivision according to structureHeb 113"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约：摩西五经；历史：从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记；诗歌：共有六卷：约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌，还加上耶利米哀歌；先知书：被掳前的先知书，被掳后的先知书，被掳后的先知书：", "en": "1. The Old Testament: the Pentateuch; history: from Joshua to Esther; poetry: a total of six books—Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs, plus Lamentations; the books of the prophets: the books of the prophets before the captivity, the books of the prophets during the captivity, and the books of the prophets after the captivity:", "norm_zh": "1旧约摩西五经历史从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记诗歌共有六卷约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌还加上耶利米哀歌先知书被掳前的先知书被掳后的先知书被掳后的先知书", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Old Testament the Pentateuch history from Joshua to Esther poetry a total of six booksJob Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songs plus Lamentations the books of the prophets the books of the prophets before the captivity the books of the prophets during the captivity and the books of the prophets after the captivity"}
{"zh": "a\t被掳前的先知书；共有十一卷；照着写作时间的早晚来排列：俄巴底亚，约珥，约拿，阿摩司，何西阿，以赛亚，弥迦，那鸿，西番雅，耶利米，哈巴谷。", "en": "a. The books of the prophets before the captivity; there are a total of eleven books; arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written: Obadiah, Joel, Jonah, Amos, Hosea, Isaiah, Micah, Nahum, Zephaniah, Jeremiah, and Habakkuk.", "norm_zh": "a被掳前的先知书共有十一卷照着写作时间的早晚来排列俄巴底亚约珥约拿阿摩司何西阿以赛亚弥迦哪鸿西番雅耶利米哈巴谷", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The books of the prophets before the captivity there are a total of eleven books arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written Obadiah Joel Jonah Amos Hosea Isaiah Micah Nahum Zephaniah Jeremiah and Habakkuk"}
{"zh": "b\t被掳后的先知书：共有两卷，就是但以理书和以西结书—结一2，但五13。", "en": "b. The books of the prophets during the captivity: there are a total of two books, which are Daniel and Ezekiel—Ezek. 1:2; Dan. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "b被掳后的先知书共有两卷就是但以理书和以西结书结一2但五13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The books of the prophets during the captivity there are a total of two books which are Daniel and EzekielEzek 12 Dan 513"}
{"zh": "c\t被掳后的先知书：共有三卷，第一个是哈该书，再一个是撒迦利亚书，末了一个是玛拉基书—该一1~8。", "en": "c. The books of the prophets after the captivity: there are a total of three books. The first is Haggai, then Zechariah, and the last one is Malachi.—Hag. 1:1-8.", "norm_zh": "c被掳后的先知书共有三卷第一个是哈该书再一个是撒迦利亚书末了一个是玛拉基书该一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c The books of the prophets after the captivity there are a total of three books The first is Haggai then Zechariah and the last one is MalachiHag 118"}
{"zh": "2\t新约；四福音：新约的头四卷；行传：只有一卷使徒行传；书信：共二十一卷，从罗马书到犹大书；预言：只有一卷启示录。", "en": "2. The New Testament; the four Gospels: the first four books of the New Testament; Acts: only one book, the Acts of the Apostles; the Epistles: there are twenty-one books, from Romans to Jude; prophecy: only one book, Revelation.", "norm_zh": "2新约四福音新约的头四卷行传只有一卷使徒行传书信共二十一卷从罗马书到犹大书预言只有一卷启示录", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The New Testament the four Gospels the first four books of the New Testament Acts only one book the Acts of the Apostles the Epistles there are twentyone books from Romans to Jude prophecy only one book Revelation"}
{"zh": "二\t照灵历而分；这是最好的分法；旧约分三类，新约也分三类—林前二10：", "en": "B. Subdivision according to spiritual experience; this is the best way to subdivide; there are three categories in the Old Testament and three categories in the New—1 Cor. 2:10:", "norm_zh": "二照灵历而分这是最好的分法旧约分三类新约也分三类林前二10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Subdivision according to spiritual experience this is the best way to subdivide there are three categories in the Old Testament and three categories in the New1 Cor 210"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约：历史：从创世记到以斯帖记，共有十七卷，都是讲史事；经历：就是五卷诗歌；约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌；预言：从以赛亚书一直到玛拉基书，共有十七卷。", "en": "1. The Old Testament: history: seventeen books from Genesis to Esther, all of which are about historical events; experience: the five books of poetry—Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs; prophecy: seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi.", "norm_zh": "1旧约历史从创世记到以斯帖记共有十七卷都是讲史事经历就是五卷诗歌约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌预言从以赛亚书一直到玛拉基书共有十七卷", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Old Testament history seventeen books from Genesis to Esther all of which are about historical events experience the five books of poetryJob Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songs prophecy seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi"}
{"zh": "2\t新约：历史：四卷福音加上使徒行传，这五卷是讲历史的；经历：这就是二十一卷书信，从罗马书一直到犹大书；这二十一卷书信专讲基督徒的经历；预言：只有启示录一卷。", "en": "The New Testament: History: The four Gospels plus Acts are five books on history; Experience: These are the twenty-one Epistles from Romans to Jude; these twenty-one books speak of the Christian experiences; Prophecy: There is only one book, the book of Revelation.", "norm_zh": "2新约历史四卷福音加上使徒行传这五卷是讲历史的经历这就是二十一卷书信从罗马书一直到犹大书这二十一卷书信专讲基督徒的经历预言只有启示录一卷", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Testament History The four Gospels plus Acts are five books on history Experience These are the twentyone Epistles from Romans to Jude these twentyone books speak of the Christian experiences Prophecy There is only one book the book of Revelation"}
{"zh": "总纲、中心和分段", "en": "The Subject, the Central Thought, and the Sections", "norm_zh": "总纲中心和分段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Subject the Central Thought and the Sections"}
{"zh": "在圣经开头的地方，就给我们看见精金、珍珠、还有宝石，这些都是建造的材料。到了圣经末了的地方，就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了，是用精金、珍珠和宝石建造成功的。这叫我们知道，神最终所要得着的一个东西，就是一所的建筑，是由祂的儿子来作羔羊，成功救赎之后建造成功的。所以论到基督，不能只看见祂是救赎的，还要看见祂是建造的；祂来救赎，也来建造。神所以创造万有和人类，就是要在宇宙中得着一所的建筑。", "en": "At the beginning of the Bible, we see pure gold, pearls, and precious stones, which are all building materials. At the end of the Bible, we see a building that has come forth, built with pure gold, pearls, and precious stones. This lets us know that the ultimate thing God wants to obtain is a building, which is built after His Son came as the Lamb to accomplish redemption. Therefore, concerning Christ, we cannot see Him only as redeeming, but we must also see Him as building; He came to redeem and also to build. The reason God created all things and mankind is to obtain a building in the universe.", "norm_zh": "在圣经开头的地方就给我们看见精金珍珠还有宝石这些都是建造的材料到了圣经末了的地方就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了是用精金珍珠和宝石建造成功的这叫我们知道神最终所要得着的一个东西就是一所的建筑是由祂的儿子来作羔羊成功救赎之后建造成功的所以论到基督不能只看见祂是救赎的还要看见祂是建造的祂来救赎也来建造神所以创造万有和人类就是要在宇宙中得着一所的建筑", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "At the beginning of the Bible we see pure gold pearls and precious stones which are all building materials At the end of the Bible we see a building that has come forth built with pure gold pearls and precious stones This lets us know that the ultimate thing God wants to obtain is a building which is built after His Son came as the Lamb to accomplish redemption Therefore concerning Christ we cannot see Him only as redeeming but we must also see Him as building He came to redeem and also to build The reason God created all things and mankind is to obtain a building in the universe"}
{"zh": "在全圣经里，一点不差是给我们看见，基督是怎样一回事；但同时也一直给我们看见，基督需要一个教会，如同男子需要一个配偶。圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说，亚当这个人独居不好。到了新约我们就知道，这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶。所以在圣经开头的时候，不仅给我们看见一个亚当，还给我们看见怎样从亚当产生一个夏娃来，作了他的配偶，二人成为一体。圣经里有亚当，也有夏娃。使徒保罗说，“这是极大的奥秘，但我是指着基督和教会说的。”你没有办法在圣经里头，只看见基督，而不看见教会。很多人在那里讲以撒，却忽略了利百加。有以撒，也有利百加。在圣经里头，有神在基督里，来和人接触的故事，但在圣经里，人也站在一个非常重要的地位上。圣经里的中心人物，不光有神在基督里，还有人来作神在基督里的配偶。宇宙的夫妇，就是神与人。在宇宙中，神是惟一的男子，人是神的配偶。人若没有神，如同寡妇一样；神若没有人，也如同一个独居的男子一样。在宇宙里头，必须神与人能配合。", "en": "No doubt the whole Bible shows us Christ. But at the same time it also shows us that Christ needs a church, in the same way that a man needs a wife. From the very beginning the Bible reveals this in a type—that it was not good for Adam to live alone. We know from the New Testament that this typifies the fact that Christ needs a bride. Therefore, at the beginning of the Bible, not only does it reveal to us the one Adam, but it also reveals to us how Eve was produced from Adam to become his bride and how they two became one. There was Adam, and there was Eve. The apostle Paul said, \"This is a great mystery, but I speak with regard to Christ and the church.\" In the Bible one cannot just see Christ without seeing the church. Many talk about Isaac and forget about Rebekah. There is Isaac, and there is Rebekah. In the Bible there is the story of God contacting man through Christ, but there is also man occupying a very important position. The central characters in the Bible are not only God in Christ but also man as the bride of God in Christ. The universal couple is God and man. In the universe God is the only male, and man is the counterpart of God. If man is without God, he is like a widow. If God is without man, He is like a bachelor. In the universe there has to be the matching of God with man.", "norm_zh": "在全圣经里一点不差是给我们看见基督是怎样一回事但同时也一直给我们看见基督需要一个教会如同男子需要一个配偶圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说亚当这个人独居不好到了新约我们就知道这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶所以在圣经开头的时候不仅给我们看见一个亚当还给我们看见怎样从亚当产生一个夏娃来作了他的配偶二人成为一体圣经里有亚当也有夏娃使徒保罗说这是极大的奥秘但我是指着基督和教会说的你没有办法在圣经里头只看见基督而不看见教会很多人在哪里讲以撒却忽略了利百加有以撒也有利百加在圣经里头有神在基督里来和人接触的故事但在圣经里人也站在一个非常重要的地位上圣经里的中心人物不光有神在基督里还有人来作神在基督里的配偶宇宙的夫妇就是神与人在宇宙中神是惟一的男子人是神的配偶人若没有神如同寡妇一样神若没有人也如同一个独居的男子一样在宇宙里头必须神与人能配合", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "No doubt the whole Bible shows us Christ But at the same time it also shows us that Christ needs a church in the same way that a man needs a wife From the very beginning the Bible reveals this in a typethat it was not good for Adam to live alone We know from the New Testament that this typifies the fact that Christ needs a bride Therefore at the beginning of the Bible not only does it reveal to us the one Adam but it also reveals to us how Eve was produced from Adam to become his bride and how they two became one There was Adam and there was Eve The apostle Paul said This is a great mystery but I speak with regard to Christ and the church In the Bible one cannot just see Christ without seeing the church Many talk about Isaac and forget about Rebekah There is Isaac and there is Rebekah In the Bible there is the story of God contacting man through Christ but there is also man occupying a very important position The central characters in the Bible are not only God in Christ but also man as the bride of God in Christ The universal couple is God and man In the universe God is the only male and man is the counterpart of God If man is without God he is like a widow If God is without man He is like a bachelor In the universe there has to be the matching of God with man"}
{"zh": "所以在旧约起头的地方，头一幕所给我们看见的，就是一个男子需要一个配偶的故事。这一个男子就是预表基督，基督就是神的化身；这一个配偶就是预表教会，教会就是人类中被神所拯救出来，要给神建造的一班人。你再往下看，不要说到新约，就是在旧约的时候，神对祂的百姓就一直是站在一个丈夫的地位上。神一直把以色列人当作祂的配偶。慢慢地主耶稣来了，那位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说，这是神的羔羊，除去世人罪孽的；他也在那里证实说，娶新妇的就是新郎。约翰不仅介绍主耶稣是赎罪的羔羊；也介绍主耶稣是娶新妇的新郎。再到书信里头，使徒保罗说，我把你们这些得救的人，许配给一个丈夫，如同贞洁的童女献给基督。他也说，夏娃之于亚当，正如教会之于基督。到了启示录，就是全圣经末了，有一个宣告说，羔羊婚娶的时候到了。到了新耶路撒冷出来的时候，就说，新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐，预备好了，等候丈夫。那就是神人合一，所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个，成了宇宙的奥秘，就是基督与教会。", "en": "Therefore, at the beginning of the Old Testament, the very first scene shown to us is the story of a man needing a counterpart. This man typifies Christ, and Christ is the embodiment of God; this counterpart typifies the church, and the church is a company of people saved by God out of mankind to be built up for God. If you look further, not to mention the New Testament, even in the Old Testament, God always stood in the position of a husband to His people. God always regarded Israel as His counterpart. Gradually the Lord Jesus came, and John the Baptist, who was the forerunner of the Lord Jesus, not only cried out, \"Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!\" but he also testified, \"He who has the bride is the bridegroom.\" John not only introduced the Lord Jesus as the redeeming Lamb, but he also introduced the Lord Jesus as the Bridegroom who has the bride. Then in the Epistles, the apostle Paul said, \"I betrothed you to one husband, to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.\" He also said that as Eve was to Adam, so the church is to Christ. In the book of Revelation, which is the end of the entire Bible, there is an announcement, saying, \"The marriage of the Lamb has come.\" When the New Jerusalem comes forth, it says, \"New Jerusalem, prepared as a bride adorned for her husband.\" That is the oneness of God and man, in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one, becoming the mystery of the universe, which is Christ and the church.", "norm_zh": "所以在旧约起头的地方头一幕所给我们看见的就是一个男子需要一个配偶的故事这一个男子就是预表基督基督就是神的化身这一个配偶就是预表教会教会就是人类中被神所拯救出来要给神建造的一班人你再往下看不要说到新约就是在旧约的时候神对祂的百姓就一直是站在一个丈夫的地位上神一直把以色列人当作祂的配偶慢慢地主耶稣来了哪位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说这是神的羔羊除去世人罪孽的他也在哪里证实说娶新妇的就是新郎约翰不仅介绍主耶稣是赎罪的羔羊也介绍主耶稣是娶新妇的新郎再到书信里头使徒保罗说我把你们这些得救的人许配给一个丈夫如同贞洁的童女献给基督他也说夏娃之于亚当正如教会之于基督到了启示录就是全圣经末了有一个宣告说羔羊婚娶的时候到了到了新耶路撒冷出来的时候就说新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐预备好了等候丈夫哪就是神人合一所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个成了宇宙的奥秘就是基督与教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Therefore at the beginning of the Old Testament the very first scene shown to us is the story of a man needing a counterpart This man typifies Christ and Christ is the embodiment of God this counterpart typifies the church and the church is a company of people saved by God out of mankind to be built up for God If you look further not to mention the New Testament even in the Old Testament God always stood in the position of a husband to His people God always regarded Israel as His counterpart Gradually the Lord Jesus came and John the Baptist who was the forerunner of the Lord Jesus not only cried out Behold the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world but he also testified He who has the bride is the bridegroom John not only introduced the Lord Jesus as the redeeming Lamb but he also introduced the Lord Jesus as the Bridegroom who has the bride Then in the Epistles the apostle Paul said I betrothed you to one husband to present you as a pure virgin to Christ He also said that as Eve was to Adam so the church is to Christ In the book of Revelation which is the end of the entire Bible there is an announcement saying The marriage of the Lamb has come When the New Jerusalem comes forth it says New Jerusalem prepared as a bride adorned for her husband That is the oneness of God and man in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one becoming the mystery of the universe which is Christ and the church"}
{"zh": "关于圣经的中心，我们还可以换一个说法。基督是神活的道，活的话；圣经是神写的道，写的话。基督是活的话，圣经是写的话。基督是圣经的内容，圣经是基督的说明。把基督从圣经里拿去，圣经变作一本空的书，如同空的器皿没有内容一样；同时没有一个人，不明白圣经而能好好认识基督，因为圣经乃是基督的说明。你只有读圣经这一个说明，才能懂得，才能认识基督是怎样一回事。而圣经所说的，乃是基督的一切摆在教会里，借着教会来彰显。所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会，光认识基督还不够，还得有教会。圣经里头所给我们看见的，那个宇宙的中心人物，有头，也有身体。头是基督，身体是教会。所以基督和教会乃是圣经的中心。", "en": "Concerning the center of the Bible, we can also put it in another way. Christ is God's living Word, the living word; the Bible is God's written Word, the written word. Christ is the living word, and the Bible is the written word. Christ is the content of the Bible, and the Bible is the explanation of Christ. If you take Christ out of the Bible, the Bible becomes an empty book, just like an empty vessel without content; at the same time, no one can know Christ well without understanding the Bible, because the Bible is the explanation of Christ. Only by reading the Bible, this explanation, can you understand and know who Christ is. What the Bible speaks of is all that Christ is being placed in the church to be expressed through the church. Therefore, the center of the Bible is Christ and the church; knowing only Christ is not enough, there must also be the church. The central figure of the universe shown to us in the Bible has a Head and also a Body. The Head is Christ, and the Body is the church. Therefore, Christ and the church are the center of the Bible.", "norm_zh": "关于圣经的中心我们还可以换一个说法基督是神活的道活的话圣经是神写的道写的话基督是活的话圣经是写的话基督是圣经的内容圣经是基督的说明把基督从圣经里拿去圣经变作一本空的书如同空的器皿没有内容一样同时没有一个人不明白圣经而能好好认识基督因为圣经乃是基督的说明你只有读圣经这一个说明才能懂得才能认识基督是怎样一回事而圣经所说的乃是基督的一切摆在教会里借着教会来彰显所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会光认识基督还不够还得有教会圣经里头所给我们看见的哪个宇宙的中心人物有头也有身体头是基督身体是教会所以基督和教会乃是圣经的中心", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Concerning the center of the Bible we can also put it in another way Christ is Gods living Word the living word the Bible is Gods written Word the written word Christ is the living word and the Bible is the written word Christ is the content of the Bible and the Bible is the explanation of Christ If you take Christ out of the Bible the Bible becomes an empty book just like an empty vessel without content at the same time no one can know Christ well without understanding the Bible because the Bible is the explanation of Christ Only by reading the Bible this explanation can you understand and know who Christ is What the Bible speaks of is all that Christ is being placed in the church to be expressed through the church Therefore the center of the Bible is Christ and the church knowing only Christ is not enough there must also be the church The central figure of the universe shown to us in the Bible has a Head and also a Body The Head is Christ and the Body is the church Therefore Christ and the church are the center of the Bible"}
{"zh": "（一）历史：在五经之后就是历史书。从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记，共有十二卷：约书亚记、士师记、路得记、撒母耳记上、撒母耳记下、列王纪上、列王纪下、历代志上、历代志下、以斯拉记、尼希米记、以斯帖记。", "en": "1) History: After the Pentateuch are the books of history. There are twelve books from Joshua to Esther: Joshua, Judges, Ruth, 1 Samuel, 2 Samuel, 1 Kings, 2 Kings, 1 Chronicles, 2 Chronicles, Ezra, Nehemiah, and Esther.", "norm_zh": "一历史在五经之后就是历史书从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记共有十二卷约书亚记士师记路得记撒母耳记上撒母耳记下列王纪上列王纪下历代志上历代志下以斯拉记尼希米记以斯帖记", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 History After the Pentateuch are the books of history There are twelve books from Joshua to Esther Joshua Judges Ruth 1 Samuel 2 Samuel 1 Kings 2 Kings 1 Chronicles 2 Chronicles Ezra Nehemiah and Esther"}
{"zh": "（二）诗歌：都是诗歌体裁，共有六卷：约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌，这五卷是相联的；还加上耶利米哀歌，它的体裁也是诗歌，不是散文。这六卷在中文看不出来是诗歌体裁，但在原文清清楚楚地是诗歌体裁，是对耦诗歌，是对句的，一点都不是散文的。", "en": "2) Psalms: There are six books, all in the style of poems. Five books—Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs—are related. Lamentations is also added because it is in the style of poetry rather than prose. In some translated versions, one cannot identify these six books as poems, but in the original, these are clearly in poetic forms, with couplets and matching phrases. They are not at all in the style of prose.", "norm_zh": "二诗歌都是诗歌体裁共有六卷约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌这五卷是相联的还加上耶利米哀歌它的体裁也是诗歌不是散文这六卷在中文看不出来是诗歌体裁但在原文清清楚楚地是诗歌体裁是对耦诗歌是对句的一点都不是散文的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Psalms There are six books all in the style of poems Five booksJob Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songsare related Lamentations is also added because it is in the style of poetry rather than prose In some translated versions one cannot identify these six books as poems but in the original these are clearly in poetic forms with couplets and matching phrases They are not at all in the style of prose"}
{"zh": "（三）先知书：这是旧约的最后一部分，按着时间来分，可以分成三类：", "en": "3) The Books of the Prophets: This is the last part of the Old Testament. It can be divided into three categories chronologically.", "norm_zh": "三先知书这是旧约的最后一部分按着时间来分可以分成三类", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Books of the Prophets This is the last part of the Old Testament It can be divided into three categories chronologically"}
{"zh": "（1）被掳前的先知书：共有十一卷。若照着写作时间的早晚来排列，最早的一个先知可能是俄巴底亚，第二个是约珥，第三个是约拿，第四个是阿摩司，第五个是何西阿，第六个是以赛亚，第七个是弥迦，第八个是那鸿，第九个是西番雅，第十个是耶利米，第十一个是哈巴谷。耶利米比哈巴谷稍微早一点，但是耶利米却延长到被掳时。他开头作先知，是在被掳前，但在末了的时候，是在被掳时。所以有的解经家把他列为被掳前的先知，有的解经家把他列为被掳时的先知。我们赞成把他列在被掳以前，因为他作先知，大部分的时间是在被掳以前。", "en": "1) The Books of the Prophets before the Captivity: There are a total of eleven books. If arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written, the earliest one is probably Obadiah, second is Joel, third is Jonah, fourth is Amos, fifth is Hosea, sixth is Isaiah, seventh is Micah, eighth is Nahum, ninth is Zephaniah, tenth is Jeremiah, and the eleventh is Habakkuk. Jeremiah was a little earlier than Habakkuk, but Jeremiah was extended into the captivity period. Jeremiah began as a prophet before the captivity and ended as one in the captivity. This is why some Bible expositors consider him as a prophet before the captivity, and others consider him as one during the captivity. We suggest considering him as one before the captivity because he spent most of his time as a prophet before the captivity.", "norm_zh": "1被掳前的先知书共有十一卷若照着写作时间的早晚来排列最早的一个先知可能是俄巴底亚第二个是约珥第三个是约拿第四个是阿摩司第五个是何西阿第六个是以赛亚第七个是弥迦第八个是哪鸿第九个是西番雅第十个是耶利米第十一个是哈巴谷耶利米比哈巴谷稍微早一点但是耶利米却延长到被掳时他开头作先知是在被掳前但在末了的时候是在被掳时所以有的解经家把他列为被掳前的先知有的解经家把他列为被掳时的先知我们赞成把他列在被掳以前因为他作先知大部分的时间是在被掳以前", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Books of the Prophets before the Captivity There are a total of eleven books If arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written the earliest one is probably Obadiah second is Joel third is Jonah fourth is Amos fifth is Hosea sixth is Isaiah seventh is Micah eighth is Nahum ninth is Zephaniah tenth is Jeremiah and the eleventh is Habakkuk Jeremiah was a little earlier than Habakkuk but Jeremiah was extended into the captivity period Jeremiah began as a prophet before the captivity and ended as one in the captivity This is why some Bible expositors consider him as a prophet before the captivity and others consider him as one during the captivity We suggest considering him as one before the captivity because he spent most of his time as a prophet before the captivity"}
{"zh": "（2）被掳时的先知书：共有两卷，就是但以理书和以西结书。但以理和以西结这两个人都是在被掳时作先知的。", "en": "2) The Books of the Prophets during the Captivity: There are a total of two books, which are Daniel and Ezekiel. Daniel and Ezekiel were both prophets during the captivity.", "norm_zh": "2被掳时的先知书共有两卷就是但以理书和以西结书但以理和以西结这两个人都是在被掳时作先知的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Books of the Prophets during the Captivity There are a total of two books which are Daniel and Ezekiel Daniel and Ezekiel were both prophets during the captivity"}
{"zh": "（3）被掳后的先知书：共有三卷，第一个是哈该书，再一个是撒迦利亚书，末了一个是玛拉基书。", "en": "3) The Books of the Prophets after the Captivity: There are a total of three books. The first is Haggai, then Zechariah, and the last one is Malachi.", "norm_zh": "3被掳后的先知书共有三卷第一个是哈该书再一个是撒迦利亚书末了一个是玛拉基书", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Books of the Prophets after the Captivity There are a total of three books The first is Haggai then Zechariah and the last one is Malachi"}
{"zh": "四卷福音，一卷行传，末了一卷预言，加上二十一卷书信，一共二十七卷。记圣经卷数最好的方法是中文九九乘法表里的三九二十七，旧约三十九卷，新约二十七卷。", "en": "The four Gospels, Acts, the twenty-one Epistles, plus the last book of prophecy, add up to twenty-seven books. An easy way to memorize the number of books of the Bible is to remember that three times nine equals twenty-seven in the Chinese nine-times-nine multiplication table; that is, there are thirty-nine books in the Old Testament and twenty-seven books in the New Testament.", "norm_zh": "四卷福音一卷行传末了一卷预言加上二十一卷书信一共二十七卷记圣经卷数最好的方法是中文九九乘法表里的三九二十七旧约三十九卷新约二十七卷", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The four Gospels Acts the twentyone Epistles plus the last book of prophecy add up to twentyseven books An easy way to memorize the number of books of the Bible is to remember that three times nine equals twentyseven in the Chinese ninetimesnine multiplication table that is there are thirtynine books in the Old Testament and twentyseven books in the New Testament"}
{"zh": "（二）经历：就是五卷诗歌；约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌。这五卷虽有一点点历史，但不是讲历史；里头也有一点预言，但也不重在说预言。这五卷乃是重在说到那些活在神面前的圣民，他们在神里面属灵的经历。若是光有前一段的历史，没有后面的经历，我们就只能看到他们所遭遇的史实，却不懂得他们在各样遭遇中，里头的光景是怎样。这五卷诗歌在圣经里，刚刚好就把在神面前的选民，在各种遭遇和经历里，他们里面的光景描述出来。我们读这五卷诗歌，就能知道他们在神面前，那些属灵的经历是怎样。", "en": "2) Experience: which are the five books of poetry—Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs. Although these five books contain a little history, they do not speak of history; there is also a little prophecy in them, but they do not focus on prophesying. These five books focus on speaking of those saints who lived in the presence of God and their spiritual experiences in God. If there were only the preceding history without the subsequent experiences, we would see only the historical facts of their encounters but would not understand what their inward condition was in their various encounters. These five books of poetry in the Bible describe exactly the inward condition of the chosen people in the presence of God in their various encounters and experiences. When we read these five books of poetry, we can know what their spiritual experiences in the presence of God were like.", "norm_zh": "二经历就是五卷诗歌约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌这五卷虽有一点点历史但不是讲历史里头也有一点预言但也不重在说预言这五卷乃是重在说到哪些活在神面前的圣民他们在神里面属灵的经历若是光有前一段的历史没有后面的经历我们就只能看到他们所遭遇的史实却不懂得他们在各样遭遇中里头的光景是怎样这五卷诗歌在圣经里刚刚好就把在神面前的选民在各种遭遇和经历里他们里面的光景描述出来我们读这五卷诗歌就能知道他们在神面前哪些属灵的经历是怎样", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Experience which are the five books of poetryJob Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songs Although these five books contain a little history they do not speak of history there is also a little prophecy in them but they do not focus on prophesying These five books focus on speaking of those saints who lived in the presence of God and their spiritual experiences in God If there were only the preceding history without the subsequent experiences we would see only the historical facts of their encounters but would not understand what their inward condition was in their various encounters These five books of poetry in the Bible describe exactly the inward condition of the chosen people in the presence of God in their various encounters and experiences When we read these five books of poetry we can know what their spiritual experiences in the presence of God were like"}
{"zh": "（一）历史：四卷福音加上使徒行传，这五卷是讲历史的。四福音讲主耶稣在地上，和门徒跟随主的经过。行传是讲门徒怎样到各处为主作见证。这五卷都是讲历史的事实。", "en": "1) History: The four Gospels plus Acts are five books on history. The four Gospels cover the experiences of the Lord Jesus on earth together with the experiences of His disciples in following Him. Acts shows us how the disciples testified for the Lord everywhere they went. These five books are all on historical facts.", "norm_zh": "一历史四卷福音加上使徒行传这五卷是讲历史的四福音讲主耶稣在地上和门徒跟随主的经过行传是讲门徒怎样到各处为主作见证这五卷都是讲历史的事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:56:51.762656+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 History The four Gospels plus Acts are five books on history The four Gospels cover the experiences of the Lord Jesus on earth together with the experiences of His disciples in following Him Acts shows us how the disciples testified for the Lord everywhere they went These five books are all on historical facts"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要认识任何一本书，都需要先抓住它的总纲和中心，也需要对它的结构有正确的分析，而清楚认识它的分段；圣经也有它的总纲、中心和分段—提后二15，三16。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "I. If we want to know any book, we have to grasp its subject and central thought. In addition, we need a proper analysis of its structure and a clear understanding of its sections; the Bible has its own subject, its central thought, and its sections—2 Tim. 2:15; 3:16.", "norm_zh": "壹我们要认识任何一本书都需要先抓住它的总纲和中心也需要对它的结构有正确的分析而清楚认识它的分段圣经也有它的总纲中心和分段提后二15三16李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I If we want to know any book we have to grasp its subject and central thought In addition we need a proper analysis of its structure and a clear understanding of its sections the Bible has its own subject its central thought and its sections2 Tim 215 316"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的总纲只有四句话：神计划创造，撒但背叛破坏，人堕落失去，基督救赎建造—创一1，三1、6，加四4~5：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "II. The subject of the Bible is contained in only four sentences: God planned and created, Satan rebelled and damaged, man fell and was lost, and Christ redeemed and built—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; Gal. 4:4-5:", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的总纲只有四句话神计划创造撒但背叛破坏人堕落失去基督救赎建造创一1三16加四45李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The subject of the Bible is contained in only four sentences God planned and created Satan rebelled and damaged man fell and was lost and Christ redeemed and builtGen 11 31 6 Gal 445"}
{"zh": "一\t在这总纲里头，有四个人物：第一是神，第二是撒但，第三是人，第四是基督；在全圣经里头几乎就是讲这四个人物—创一1，三1、6，约十七3：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "A. Within this subject, there are four persons: the first is God, the second is Satan, the third is man, and the fourth is Christ; the whole Bible speaks almost exclusively of these four persons—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; John 17:3:", "norm_zh": "一在这总纲里头有四个人物第一是神第二是撒但第三是人第四是基督在全圣经里头几乎就是讲这四个人物创一1三16约十七3李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Within this subject there are four persons the first is God the second is Satan the third is man and the fourth is Christ the whole Bible speaks almost exclusively of these four personsGen 11 31 6 John 173"}
{"zh": "1\t神是计划和创造；计划是在永世里头的，创造是在时间里面的—创一1、26节注1。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "1. God planned and created; He planned in eternity past and created in time—Gen. 1:1, 26, note 1.", "norm_zh": "1神是计划和创造计划是在永世里头的创造是在时间里面的创一126节注1李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God planned and created He planned in eternity past and created in timeGen 11 26 note 1"}
{"zh": "2\t撒但是背叛和破坏；神有了祂的计划，并照着祂的计划有所创造，撒但就背叛神，破坏神的创造—三1~7。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "2. Satan rebelled and damaged; God had His plan and created according to His plan, but Satan rebelled against God and damaged God’s creation—Gen. 3:1-7.", "norm_zh": "2撒但是背叛和破坏神有了祂的计划并照着祂的计划有所创造撒但就背叛神破坏神的创造三17李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Satan rebelled and damaged God had His plan and created according to His plan but Satan rebelled against God and damaged Gods creationGen 317"}
{"zh": "3\t人是堕落和失去；人堕落了，结果就从神的手中，神的用处上失去了—六3，三24。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "3. Man fell and was lost; man fell and, as a result, was lost from God’s hands and from being used by God—Gen. 6:3; 3:24.", "norm_zh": "3人是堕落和失去人堕落了结果就从神的手中神的用处上失去了六3三24李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Man fell and was lost man fell and as a result was lost from Gods hands and from being used by GodGen 63 324"}
{"zh": "4\t基督是救赎和建造；神照着祂的计划创造万有和人类，撒但高傲背叛神，凭着他的恶意破坏神的创造，使人堕落、失去，基督就来救赎，将人建造成祂荣耀的教会—加四4，太十六18。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "4. Christ redeemed and built; God created all things and mankind according to His plan, Satan proudly rebelled against God and damaged God's creation by his malice, causing man to fall and be lost, and Christ came to redeem and build man into His glorious church—Gal. 4:4; Matt. 16:18.", "norm_zh": "4基督是救赎和建造神照着祂的计划创造万有和人类撒但高傲背叛神凭着他的恶意破坏神的创造使人堕落失去基督就来救赎将人建造成祂荣耀的教会加四4太十六18李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Christ redeemed and built God created all things and mankind according to His plan Satan proudly rebelled against God and damaged Gods creation by his malice causing man to fall and be lost and Christ came to redeem and build man into His glorious churchGal 44 Matt 1618"}
{"zh": "二\t在基督徒中间，说到基督，恐怕都仅仅说到救赎，而忽略了，或者说没有看清楚建造的问题；我们不能光是看到救赎，还得看到建造—13~18节：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "B. Among Christians, when speaking of Christ, they speak only of redemption; the matter of building has always been overlooked or missed; we must not see redemption only; we must see the building also—vv. 13-18:", "norm_zh": "二在基督徒中间说到基督恐怕都仅仅说到救赎而忽略了或者说没有看清楚建造的问提我们不能光是看到救赎还得看到建造1318节李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Among Christians when speaking of Christ they speak only of redemption the matter of building has always been overlooked or missed we must not see redemption only we must see the building alsovv 1318"}
{"zh": "1\t在圣经开头的地方，就给我们看见精金、珍珠、还有宝石，这些都是建造的材料—创二10~12。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "1. At the beginning of the Bible we see pure gold, pearls, and precious stones, which are all building materials—Gen. 2:10-12.", "norm_zh": "1在圣经开头的地方就给我们看见精金珍珠还有宝石这些都是建造的材料创二1012李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 At the beginning of the Bible we see pure gold pearls and precious stones which are all building materialsGen 21012"}
{"zh": "2\t到了圣经末了的地方，就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了，是用精金、珍珠和宝石建造成功的；神最终所要得着的一个东西，就是一所的建筑—启二一18~21。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "2. At the end of the Bible we see a building that has come forth, built of pure gold, pearls, and precious stones; the one thing God ultimately wants to obtain is a building—Rev. 21:18-21.", "norm_zh": "2到了圣经末了的地方就给我们看见有一所建筑出来了是用精金珍珠和宝石建造成功的神最终所要得着的一个东西就是一所的建筑启二一1821李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 At the end of the Bible we see a building that has come forth built of pure gold pearls and precious stones the one thing God ultimately wants to obtain is a buildingRev 211821"}
{"zh": "三\t旧约圣经的总纲是神创造，撒但破坏，人堕落，神应许基督来救赎；在旧约里的基督，乃是人的一个盼望，因为是神所应许给堕落之人的一位救赎主—创一1，三1、6，赛九6。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "C. The subject of the Old Testament is that God created, Satan damaged, man fell, and God promised the coming of Christ for redemption; the Christ in the Old Testament was only a hope for man, because He was only promised by God to the fallen man as a Redeemer.—Gen. 1:1; 3:1, 6; Isa. 9:6.", "norm_zh": "三旧约圣经的总纲是神创造撒但破坏人堕落神应许基督来救赎在旧约里的基督乃是人的一个盼望因为是神所应许给堕落之人的一位救赎主创一1三16赛九6李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The subject of the Old Testament is that God created Satan damaged man fell and God promised the coming of Christ for redemption the Christ in the Old Testament was only a hope for man because He was only promised by God to the fallen man as a RedeemerGen 11 31 6 Isa 96"}
{"zh": "四\t新约圣经的总纲是基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人，建造教会；基督照着神的计划，来救赎罪人，建造成为祂荣耀的教会，作祂奥秘的身体，使神在祂里面得着一个团体的器皿，彰显祂自己—加四4~5，太十六18，约二19，弗二21~22，五27。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "D. The subject of the New Testament is Christ coming to redeem sinners and to build up the church according to God’s plan; Christ, according to God’s plan, comes to redeem sinners and build them up as His glorious church to be His mystical Body, that God may have a corporate vessel in Him to express Himself.—Gal. 4:4-5; Matt. 16:18; John 2:19; Eph. 2:21-22; 5:27.", "norm_zh": "四新约圣经的总纲是基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人建造教会基督照着神的计划来救赎罪人建造成为祂荣耀的教会作祂奥秘的身体使神在祂里面得着一个团体的器皿彰显祂自己加四45太十六18约二19弗二2122五27李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The subject of the New Testament is Christ coming to redeem sinners and to build up the church according to Gods plan Christ according to Gods plan comes to redeem sinners and build them up as His glorious church to be His mystical Body that God may have a corporate vessel in Him to express HimselfGal 445 Matt 1618 John 219 Eph 22122 527"}
{"zh": "叁\t圣经的中心乃是基督和教会；圣经不光是启示基督自己，同时也启示基督的一个配偶，基督的一个身体，就是教会—32节，太十六16~18：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "III. The central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church; the Bible not only reveals Christ Himself, but it also reveals a bride and a Body of Christ, which is the church.—v. 32; Matt. 16:16-18:", "norm_zh": "叁圣经的中心乃是基督和教会圣经不光是启示基督自己同时也启示基督的一个配偶基督的一个身体就是教会32节太十六1618李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church the Bible not only reveals Christ Himself but it also reveals a bride and a Body of Christ which is the churchv 32 Matt 161618"}
{"zh": "一\t基督是圣经的内容，圣经是基督的说明；把基督从圣经里拿去，圣经变作一本空的书；你只有读圣经这一个说明，才能懂得，才能认识基督是怎样一回事—西三11，约十四6。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "A. Christ is the content of the Bible, and the Bible is the explanation of Christ; if we take away Christ from the Bible, the Bible will become an empty book; only when you read the Bible, this explanation, can you understand and know what Christ is.—Col. 3:11; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "一基督是圣经的内容圣经是基督的说明把基督从圣经里拿去圣经变作一本空的书你只有读圣经这一个说明才能懂得才能认识基督是怎样一回事西三11约十四6李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ is the content of the Bible and the Bible is the explanation of Christ if we take away Christ from the Bible the Bible will become an empty book only when you read the Bible this explanation can you understand and know what Christ isCol 311 John 146"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经所说的，乃是基督的一切摆在教会里，借着教会来彰显；所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会，光认识基督还不够，还得有教会—弗五32，三10：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "B. What the Bible says is that everything of Christ is put into the church and expressed through the church; hence, the central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church; it is insufficient to know Christ only, we have to have the church as well.—Eph. 5:32; 3:10:", "norm_zh": "二圣经所说的乃是基督的一切摆在教会里借着教会来彰显所以圣经的中心乃是基督和教会光认识基督还不够还得有教会弗五32三10李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B What the Bible says is that everything of Christ is put into the church and expressed through the church hence the central thought of the Bible is Christ and the church it is insufficient to know Christ only we have to have the church as wellEph 532 310"}
{"zh": "1\t圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说，亚当这个人独居不好；到了新约我们就知道，这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶—创二18，林后十二2，弗五31~32。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "1. At the very beginning of the Bible there are such typifying words, saying that it was not good for the man Adam to live alone; when we come to the New Testament, we know that this typifies that Christ needs a bride.—Gen. 2:18; 2 Cor. 12:2; Eph. 5:31-32.", "norm_zh": "1圣经一开头就有这样预表的话说亚当这个人独居不好到了新约我们就知道这一个乃是预表基督需要一个配偶创二18林后十二2弗五3132李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 At the very beginning of the Bible there are such typifying words saying that it was not good for the man Adam to live alone when we come to the New Testament we know that this typifies that Christ needs a brideGen 218 2 Cor 122 Eph 53132"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣来了，那位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说，这是神的羔羊，除去世人罪孽的；他也在那里证实说，娶新妇的就是新郎—约一29，三29。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "2. The Lord Jesus came; John the Baptist, who was the forerunner of the Lord Jesus, not only cried out, \"Behold, the Lamb of God, who takes away the sin of the world!\"; he also testified there, saying, \"He who has the bride is the bridegroom.\"—John 1:29; 3:29.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣来了哪位作主耶稣先锋的施浸者约翰不仅喊说这是神的羔羊除去世人罪孽的他也在哪里证实说娶新妇的就是新郎约一29三29李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Lord Jesus came John the Baptist who was the forerunner of the Lord Jesus not only cried out Behold the Lamb of God who takes away the sin of the world he also testified there saying He who has the bride is the bridegroomJohn 129 329"}
{"zh": "3\t到书信里头，使徒保罗说，我把你们这些得救的人，许配给一个丈夫，如同贞洁的童女献给基督—林后十一2。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "3. In the Epistles, the apostle Paul says, \"I betrothed you, the saved ones, to one Husband, to present you as a pure virgin to Christ.\"—2 Cor. 11:2.", "norm_zh": "3到书信里头使徒保罗说我把你们这些得救的人许配给一个丈夫如同贞洁的童女献给基督林后十一2李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In the Epistles the apostle Paul says I betrothed you the saved ones to one Husband to present you as a pure virgin to Christ2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "4\t到了启示录，有一个宣告说，羔羊婚娶的时候到了；新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐，预备好了，等候丈夫；那就是神人合一，所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个，成了宇宙的奥秘，就是基督与教会—启十九7，二一2。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "4. In Revelation there is a declaration saying that the marriage of the Lamb has come; the New Jerusalem is prepared as a bride adorned for her husband; that is the union of God and man, in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one, becoming the mystery of the universe, which is Christ and the church.—Rev. 19:7; 21:2.", "norm_zh": "4到了启示录有一个宣告说羔羊婚娶的时候到了新耶路撒冷象新妇妆饰整齐预备好了等候丈夫哪就是神人合一所有蒙救赎的人和救赎主成为一个成了宇宙的奥秘就是基督与教会启十九7二一2李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 In Revelation there is a declaration saying that the marriage of the Lamb has come the New Jerusalem is prepared as a bride adorned for her husband that is the union of God and man in which all the redeemed and the Redeemer become one becoming the mystery of the universe which is Christ and the churchRev 197 212"}
{"zh": "三\t旧约的中心—引到基督以得救赎；旧约是把人引到基督，要人从祂得着救赎—伯五20，赛五九20。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "C. The center of the Old Testament—leading to Christ for redemption; the Old Testament leads man to Christ that man would be redeemed by Him.—Job 5:20; Isa. 59:20.", "norm_zh": "三旧约的中心引到基督以得救赎旧约是把人引到基督要人从祂得着救赎伯五20赛五九20李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The center of the Old Testamentleading to Christ for redemption the Old Testament leads man to Christ that man would be redeemed by HimJob 520 Isa 5920"}
{"zh": "四\t新约的中心—在基督里教会得蒙救赎并建造；新约就给我们看见，在基督里教会怎样得蒙救赎，而被建造—弗二4~5、22。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "D. The center of the New Testament—the church being redeemed and built up in Christ; the New Testament shows us how the church is redeemed and built up in Christ.—Eph. 2:4-5, 22.", "norm_zh": "四新约的中心在基督里教会得蒙救赎并建造新约就给我们看见在基督里教会怎样得蒙救赎而被建造弗二4522李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The center of the New Testamentthe church being redeemed and built up in Christ the New Testament shows us how the church is redeemed and built up in ChristEph 245 22"}
{"zh": "肆\t圣经的分段有好多种分法，我们从其中选出两种比较重要的来看—提后二5，三16：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "IV. There are many ways to subdivide the Bible into sections. We have selected two of the more important ways for our consideration.—2 Tim. 2:5; 3:16:", "norm_zh": "肆圣经的分段有好多种分法我们从其中选出两种比较重要的来看提后二5三16李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV There are many ways to subdivide the Bible into sections We have selected two of the more important ways for our consideration2 Tim 25 316"}
{"zh": "一\t照着结构而分—来十一3：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "A. Subdivision according to structure—Heb. 11:3:", "norm_zh": "一照着结构而分来十一3李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Subdivision according to structureHeb 113"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约：摩西五经；历史：从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记；诗歌：共有六卷：约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌，还加上耶利米哀歌；先知书：被掳前的先知书，被掳后的先知书，被掳后的先知书：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "1. The Old Testament: the Pentateuch; History: from Joshua to Esther; Poetry: there are six books: Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs, plus Lamentations; the Books of the Prophets: the books of the prophets before the captivity, the books of the prophets after the captivity, the books of the prophets after the captivity:", "norm_zh": "1旧约摩西五经历史从约书亚记起一直到以斯帖记诗歌共有六卷约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌还加上耶利米哀歌先知书被掳前的先知书被掳后的先知书被掳后的先知书李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Old Testament the Pentateuch History from Joshua to Esther Poetry there are six books Job Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songs plus Lamentations the Books of the Prophets the books of the prophets before the captivity the books of the prophets after the captivity the books of the prophets after the captivity"}
{"zh": "a\t被掳前的先知书；共有十一卷；照着写作时间的早晚来排列：俄巴底亚，约珥，约拿，阿摩司，何西阿，以赛亚，弥迦，那鸿，西番雅，耶利米，哈巴谷。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "a. The books of the prophets before the captivity; there are a total of eleven books; arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written: Obadiah, Joel, Jonah, Amos, Hosea, Isaiah, Micah, Nahum, Zephaniah, Jeremiah, Habakkuk.", "norm_zh": "a被掳前的先知书共有十一卷照着写作时间的早晚来排列俄巴底亚约珥约拿阿摩司何西阿以赛亚弥迦哪鸿西番雅耶利米哈巴谷李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The books of the prophets before the captivity there are a total of eleven books arranged in chronological order according to the time they were written Obadiah Joel Jonah Amos Hosea Isaiah Micah Nahum Zephaniah Jeremiah Habakkuk"}
{"zh": "b\t被掳后的先知书：共有两卷，就是但以理书和以西结书—结一2，但五13。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "b. The books of the prophets during the captivity: there are a total of two books, which are Daniel and Ezekiel—Ezek. 1:2; Dan. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "b被掳后的先知书共有两卷就是但以理书和以西结书结一2但五13李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The books of the prophets during the captivity there are a total of two books which are Daniel and EzekielEzek 12 Dan 513"}
{"zh": "c\t被掳后的先知书：共有三卷，第一个是哈该书，再一个是撒迦利亚书，末了一个是玛拉基书—该一1~8。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "c. The books of the prophets after the captivity: there are a total of three books. The first is Haggai, then Zechariah, and the last one is Malachi—Hag. 1:1-8.", "norm_zh": "c被掳后的先知书共有三卷第一个是哈该书再一个是撒迦利亚书末了一个是玛拉基书该一18李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c The books of the prophets after the captivity there are a total of three books The first is Haggai then Zechariah and the last one is MalachiHag 118"}
{"zh": "2\t新约；四福音：新约的头四卷；行传：只有一卷使徒行传；书信：共二十一卷，从罗马书到犹大书；预言：只有一卷启示录。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "2. The New Testament; the four Gospels: the first four books of the New Testament; Acts: there is only one book of Acts; the Epistles: there are twenty-one books, from Romans to Jude; Prophecy: there is only one book, the book of Revelation.", "norm_zh": "2新约四福音新约的头四卷行传只有一卷使徒行传书信共二十一卷从罗马书到犹大书预言只有一卷启示录李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The New Testament the four Gospels the first four books of the New Testament Acts there is only one book of Acts the Epistles there are twentyone books from Romans to Jude Prophecy there is only one book the book of Revelation"}
{"zh": "二\t照灵历而分；这是最好的分法；旧约分三类，新约也分三类—林前二10：（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "B. Subdivision according to spiritual experience; this is the best way to subdivide; there are three categories in the Old Testament and three categories in the New—1 Cor. 2:10:", "norm_zh": "二照灵历而分这是最好的分法旧约分三类新约也分三类林前二10李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Subdivision according to spiritual experience this is the best way to subdivide there are three categories in the Old Testament and three categories in the New1 Cor 210"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约：历史：从创世记到以斯帖记，共有十七卷，都是讲史事；经历：就是五卷诗歌；约伯记、诗篇、箴言、传道书、雅歌；预言：从以赛亚书一直到玛拉基书，共有十七卷。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "1. The Old Testament: History: seventeen books from Genesis to Esther, all of which are on history; Experience: these are the five books of poetry: Job, Psalms, Proverbs, Ecclesiastes, and Song of Songs; Prophecy: seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi.", "norm_zh": "1旧约历史从创世记到以斯帖记共有十七卷都是讲史事经历就是五卷诗歌约伯记诗篇箴言传道书雅歌预言从以赛亚书一直到玛拉基书共有十七卷李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Old Testament History seventeen books from Genesis to Esther all of which are on history Experience these are the five books of poetry Job Psalms Proverbs Ecclesiastes and Song of Songs Prophecy seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi"}
{"zh": "2\t新约：历史：四卷福音加上使徒行传，这五卷是讲历史的；经历：这就是二十一卷书信，从罗马书一直到犹大书；这二十一卷书信专讲基督徒的经历；预言：只有启示录一卷。（李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第三篇）", "en": "2. The New Testament: History: the four Gospels plus Acts, which are five books on history; Experience: these are the twenty-one Epistles, from Romans to Jude; these twenty-one Epistles speak of the Christian experiences; Prophecy: there is only one book, the book of Revelation.", "norm_zh": "2新约历史四卷福音加上使徒行传这五卷是讲历史的经历这就是二十一卷书信从罗马书一直到犹大书这二十一卷书信专讲基督徒的经历预言只有启示录一卷李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T02:58:49.910968+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The New Testament History the four Gospels plus Acts which are five books on history Experience these are the twentyone Epistles from Romans to Jude these twentyone Epistles speak of the Christian experiences Prophecy there is only one book the book of Revelation"}
{"zh": "读经：提后三15~17，约十四16，彼前一23，二2，林前十11，诗一一九105、11，箴六23", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 3:15-17; John 14:16; 1 Pet. 1:23; 2:2; 1 Cor. 10:11; Psa. 119:105, 11; Prov. 6:23", "norm_zh": "读经提后三1517约十四16彼前一23二2林前十11诗一一九10511箴六23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 31517 John 1416 1 Pet 123 22 1 Cor 1011 Psa 119105 11 Prov 623"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经的第一个功用，是给主耶稣作见证；主耶稣是圣经的题目，是圣经的内容；圣经是主耶稣的说明，是主耶稣的发表—约五39，路二四27、44、46：", "en": "I. The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the Lord Jesus is the subject and content of the Bible, and the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus.—John 5:39; Luke 24:27, 44, 46:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经的第一个功用是给主耶稣作见证主耶稣是圣经的提目是圣经的内容圣经是主耶稣的说明是主耶稣的发表约五39路二四274446", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus the Lord Jesus is the subject and content of the Bible and the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord JesusJohn 539 Luke 2427 44 46"}
{"zh": "一\t主耶稣是神活的道，圣经是神写的道；圣经这写的道，若没有主耶稣那活的道作实际，圣经就不过是空洞的道理，虚空的字句—提后三16，约十四6。", "en": "A. The Lord Jesus is the living Word of God, whereas the Bible is the written Word of God; if the written Word, the Bible, did not have the living Word, the Lord Jesus, as its reality, the Bible would be nothing but empty doctrines and letters.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "一主耶稣是神活的道圣经是神写的道圣经这写的道若没有主耶稣哪活的道作实际圣经就不过是空洞的道理虚空的字句提后三16约十四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Lord Jesus is the living Word of God whereas the Bible is the written Word of God if the written Word the Bible did not have the living Word the Lord Jesus as its reality the Bible would be nothing but empty doctrines and letters2 Tim 316 John 146"}
{"zh": "二\t有了圣经这清楚确定的说明，明白的启示，主耶稣就能具体的给人认识，确定的给人了解；所以我们若要认识主耶稣，就非读圣经，非明白圣经不可—五39，路二四44。", "en": "B. Since there is the clear, definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures, the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men; hence, if we want to know the Lord Jesus, we must read and understand the Bible.—John 5:39; Luke 24:44.", "norm_zh": "二有了圣经这清楚确定的说明明白的启示主耶稣就能具体的给人认识确定的给人了解所以我们若要认识主耶稣就非读圣经非明白圣经不可五39路二四44", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since there is the clear definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men hence if we want to know the Lord Jesus we must read and understand the BibleJohn 539 Luke 2444"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的功用；在为着我们这一面，圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧，将神在基督里的救法，和人因信得救的途径，启示给我们—提后三15，林前一24。", "en": "II. The functions of the Bible; on the side toward us, the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation, revealing to us how God saves men in Christ and how men may be saved by faith.—2 Tim. 3:15; 1 Cor. 1:24.", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的功用在为着我们这一面圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧将神在基督里的救法和人因信得救的途径启示给我们提后三15林前一24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The functions of the Bible on the side toward us the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation revealing to us how God saves men in Christ and how men may be saved by faith2 Tim 315 1 Cor 124"}
{"zh": "叁\t圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用，就是使我们蒙到重生；圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面，使我们有了神的生命而得着重生—彼前一23，雅一18。", "en": "III. The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated; the word of the Bible is like a seed of life falling into us, causing us to have God's life and be regenerated.—1 Pet. 1:23; James 1:18.", "norm_zh": "叁圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用就是使我们蒙到重生圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面使我们有了神的生命而得着重生彼前一23雅一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated the word of the Bible is like a seed of life falling into us causing us to have Gods life and be regenerated1 Pet 123 James 118"}
{"zh": "肆\t圣经使我们得着重生之后，就教训我们，督责我们，使我们在各方面归正，教导我们在凡事上学义，叫我们这蒙了神的重生，得以在神面前成为完全—提后三16~17。", "en": "IV. After being regenerated, the Bible teaches us, convicts us, corrects us in every aspect, and instructs us in righteousness in all things, so that we who are regenerated by God may be complete before God.—2 Tim. 3:16-17.", "norm_zh": "肆圣经使我们得着重生之后就教训我们督责我们使我们在各方面归正教导我们在凡事上学义叫我们这蒙了神的重生得以在神面前成为完全提后三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV After being regenerated the Bible teaches us convicts us corrects us in every aspect and instructs us in righteousness in all things so that we who are regenerated by God may be complete before God2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "伍\t圣经的教训，也能叫我们有忍耐、蒙安慰、而得有盼望；我们在遭遇苦难的时候，很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立—罗十五4、13。", "en": "V. The teachings of the Bible can also give us endurance, comfort, and hope; when we encounter difficulties, we can easily receive help and establishment from the Bible.—Rom. 15:4, 13.", "norm_zh": "伍圣经的教训也能叫我们有忍耐蒙安慰而得有盼望我们在遭遇苦难的时候很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立罗十五413", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The teachings of the Bible can also give us endurance comfort and hope when we encounter difficulties we can easily receive help and establishment from the BibleRom 154 13"}
{"zh": "陆\t圣经中也记载许多的事，作我们的鉴戒，使我们受警戒；我们每逢读到这些记载的时候，很容易得到前车之鉴，而生了戒心，免蹈前辙—林前十11。", "en": "VI. Many things are recorded in the Bible as examples for our admonition; when we read the Bible, we can be warned by the experiences of some who went before us, and we can be careful not to follow their example.—1 Cor. 10:11.", "norm_zh": "陆圣经中也记载许多的事作我们的鉴戒使我们受警戒我们每逢读到这些记载的时候很容易得到前车之鉴而生了戒心免蹈前辙林前十11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Many things are recorded in the Bible as examples for our admonition when we read the Bible we can be warned by the experiences of some who went before us and we can be careful not to follow their example1 Cor 1011"}
{"zh": "柒\t圣经的话对于我们，许多时候也像明灯照在暗处；我们若要作一个明亮、通达时务的人，就必须明白圣经，有圣经的话存在心中，随时发光照亮我们—彼后一19，罗十三12。", "en": "VII. Often the Bible is like a lamp shining in a dark place; if we want to be enlightened and knowledgeable, we must understand the Bible and keep the word of the Bible in our hearts so that it can shine and enlighten us.—2 Pet. 1:19; Rom. 13:12.", "norm_zh": "柒圣经的话对于我们许多时候也像明灯照在暗处我们若要作一个明亮通达时务的人就必须明白圣经有圣经的话存在心中随时发光照亮我们彼后一19罗十三12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII Often the Bible is like a lamp shining in a dark place if we want to be enlightened and knowledgeable we must understand the Bible and keep the word of the Bible in our hearts so that it can shine and enlighten us2 Pet 119 Rom 1312"}
{"zh": "捌\t人在黑暗里走路，是需要灯光照亮脚步的；把圣经的话存记在心，圣经的话就能作我们脚前的灯，路上的光—诗一一九105，箴六23。", "en": "VIII. People walking in the dark need a lamp to shine on the path of their feet; if we keep the word of the Bible in our heart, it will become a lamp to our feet and a light to our path.—Psa. 119:105; Prov. 6:23.", "norm_zh": "捌人在黑暗里走路是需要灯光照亮脚步的把圣经的话存记在心圣经的话就能作我们脚前的灯路上的光诗一一九105箴六23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII People walking in the dark need a lamp to shine on the path of their feet if we keep the word of the Bible in our heart it will become a lamp to our feet and a light to our pathPsa 119105 Prov 623"}
{"zh": "玖\t圣经的话所发出的光，不只能在我们所行的路上照亮我们的脚步，还能叫我们愚昧人变为通达—诗一〇九103，弗五17。", "en": "IX. The light emitted by the word of the Bible not only can shine on our feet on the path on which we walk, but can also cause us foolish people to become people of understanding—Psa. 119:103, Eph. 5:17.", "norm_zh": "玖圣经的话所发出的光不只能在我们所行的路上照亮我们的脚步还能叫我们愚昧人变为通达诗一〇九103弗五17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The light emitted by the word of the Bible not only can shine on our feet on the path on which we walk but can also cause us foolish people to become people of understandingPsa 119103 Eph 517"}
{"zh": "拾\t圣经的话不只有照亮的能力，也有洁净的能力；照亮是对黑暗的，洁净是对污秽的；我们若常读圣经，不只必蒙光照，也必蒙洁净—诗十九9，一一九9。", "en": "X. In addition to containing the power to enlighten, the word in the Bible has the power to cleanse; enlightenment is in contrast to darkness, and purification is in contrast to filthiness; if we read the Bible frequently, we will not only be enlightened but also kept pure.—Psa. 19:9; 119:9.", "norm_zh": "拾圣经的话不只有照亮的能力也有洁净的能力照亮是对黑暗的洁净是对污秽的我们若常读圣经不只必蒙光照也必蒙洁净诗十九9一一九9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X In addition to containing the power to enlighten the word in the Bible has the power to cleanse enlightenment is in contrast to darkness and purification is in contrast to filthiness if we read the Bible frequently we will not only be enlightened but also kept purePsa 199 1199"}
{"zh": "拾壹\t圣经也能使我们免得犯罪得罪神；我们若将圣经的话藏在心里，圣经的话就能常常提醒我们，使我们免得犯罪得罪神—11节，伯三六10。", "en": "XI. The Bible also prevents us from sinning against God; if we store the words of the Bible in our heart, the words of the Bible can constantly remind us so that we do not sin against God.—v. 11; Job 36:10.", "norm_zh": "拾壹圣经也能使我们免得犯罪得罪神我们若将圣经的话藏在心里圣经的话就能常常提醒我们使我们免得犯罪得罪神11节伯三六10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XI The Bible also prevents us from sinning against God if we store the words of the Bible in our heart the words of the Bible can constantly remind us so that we do not sin against Godv 11 Job 3610"}
{"zh": "拾贰\t圣经的话也是圣灵的宝剑，是我们可以靠着圣灵用以对付撒但和他的使者的；我们能打败那引诱或攻击我们的邪灵、仇敌，都是借着圣经的话—弗六17~18。", "en": "XII. The word in the Bible is also the sword of the Spirit, which we can apply by the Holy Spirit to deal with Satan and his messengers; through the word of the Bible, we can defeat the devil, the enemy, who tempts and attacks us.—Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "拾贰圣经的话也是圣灵的宝剑是我们可以靠着圣灵用以对付撒但和他的使者的我们能打败哪引诱或攻击我们的邪灵仇敌都是借着圣经的话弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XII The word in the Bible is also the sword of the Spirit which we can apply by the Holy Spirit to deal with Satan and his messengers through the word of the Bible we can defeat the devil the enemy who tempts and attacks usEph 61718"}
{"zh": "拾叁\t圣经的话锋利如剑，不只能对付我们属灵的仇敌，并且能将我们里面的魂与灵给我们剖开，能将我们心中的思念和主意给我们辨明—17节，来四12。", "en": "XIII. The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword; it can not only deal with our spiritual enemies but can also divide our soul from our spirit and discern the thoughts and intentions of our heart.—v. 17; Heb. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "拾叁圣经的话锋利如剑不只能对付我们属灵的仇敌并且能将我们里面的魂与灵给我们剖开能将我们心中的思念和主意给我们辨明17节来四12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIII The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword it can not only deal with our spiritual enemies but can also divide our soul from our spirit and discern the thoughts and intentions of our heartv 17 Heb 412"}
{"zh": "拾肆\t圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物；我们肉身的生命如何需要营养，我们属灵的生命也如何需要营养；属灵生命的营养，是只有圣经的话能供应的—耶十五16，太四4，伯二十三12，来五14。", "en": "XIV. The word of the Bible is also food for our spiritual life; just as our physical life needs nourishment, our spiritual life needs nourishment; the word is the only thing that can supply nourishment to our spiritual life.—Jer. 15:16; Matt. 4:4; Job 23:12; Heb. 5:14.", "norm_zh": "拾肆圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物我们肉身的生命如何需要营养我们属灵的生命也如何需要营养属灵生命的营养是只有圣经的话能供应的耶十五16太四4伯二十三12来五14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIV The word of the Bible is also food for our spiritual life just as our physical life needs nourishment our spiritual life needs nourishment the word is the only thing that can supply nourishment to our spiritual lifeJer 1516 Matt 44 Job 2312 Heb 514"}
{"zh": "拾伍\t圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮，也是我们属灵生命的奶；一个初得重生的信徒，必须爱慕圣经的话，“像才生的婴孩爱慕一样”—彼前二2，林前三1~2，来五12~14。", "en": "XV. The word of the Bible is not only solid food for our spiritual life but also milk for our spiritual life; a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible, \"as newborn babes long for it\".—1 Pet. 2:2; 1 Cor. 3:1-2; Heb. 5:12-14.", "norm_zh": "拾伍圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮也是我们属灵生命的奶一个初得重生的信徒必须爱慕圣经的话像才生的婴孩爱慕一样彼前二2林前三12来五1214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XV The word of the Bible is not only solid food for our spiritual life but also milk for our spiritual life a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible as newborn babes long for it1 Pet 22 1 Cor 312 Heb 51214"}
{"zh": "拾陆\t圣经的话，不只能洁净我们外面的行为；并且还能在我们里面洗净我们，叫我们脱离旧造的弱点；叫我们脱去旧造的斑点—弗五16~17，约十五3。", "en": "XVI. The word of the Bible not only can wash our outward actions, but also can wash us inwardly, freeing us from the weaknesses of the old creation and eliminating the spots of the old creation.—Eph. 5:16-17; John 15:3.", "norm_zh": "拾陆圣经的话不只能洁净我们外面的行为并且还能在我们里面洗净我们叫我们脱离旧造的弱点叫我们脱去旧造的斑点弗五1617约十五3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVI The word of the Bible not only can wash our outward actions but also can wash us inwardly freeing us from the weaknesses of the old creation and eliminating the spots of the old creationEph 51617 John 153"}
{"zh": "拾柒\t圣经的话也非常有能力，能像火焚烧，并能像大锤打碎；圣经的话能把人向着神冰冷的心烧得火热，也能把人与神圣洁不合的东西烧灭净尽—耶二三29，五14。", "en": "XVII. The word of the Bible is also very powerful; it is like a burning fire and a smashing hammer; the word of the Bible can burn hearts that are ice cold toward God, and it can also completely burn away things that are contrary to God's holy nature.—Jer. 23:29; 5:14.", "norm_zh": "拾柒圣经的话也非常有能力能像火焚烧并能像大锤打碎圣经的话能把人向着神冰冷的心烧得火热也能把人与神圣洁不合的东西烧灭净尽耶二三29五14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVII The word of the Bible is also very powerful it is like a burning fire and a smashing hammer the word of the Bible can burn hearts that are ice cold toward God and it can also completely burn away things that are contrary to Gods holy natureJer 2329 514"}
{"zh": "拾捌\t圣经的话也像雨、露、甘霖，能灌溉、滋润；我们是神所耕种的田地，是神所栽种的庄稼；圣经的话使我们生长结实—林前三9，可四20，林前三6。", "en": "XVIII. The word of the Bible is also like rain, dew, and abundant showers, which can water and refresh us; we are God's farm, the harvest that God cultivates; the word of the Bible causes us to grow and bear fruit.—1 Cor. 3:9; Mark 4:20; 1 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "拾捌圣经的话也像雨露甘霖能灌溉滋润我们是神所耕种的田地是神所栽种的庄稼圣经的话使我们生长结实林前三9可四20林前三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVIII The word of the Bible is also like rain dew and abundant showers which can water and refresh us we are Gods farm the harvest that God cultivates the word of the Bible causes us to grow and bear fruit1 Cor 39 Mark 420 1 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "拾玖\t圣经的话不只像雨，也像雪滋润我们；雨是在春、夏、秋三季有的，雪是在冬季有的；无论在什么时候，圣经的话都能滋润我们—赛五五10~11。", "en": "XIX. The word of the Bible is not only like rain, but it also refreshes like snow; rain comes in the spring, summer, and fall, but snow comes in the winter; the word of the Bible can refresh us in every season of our condition.—Isa. 55:10-11.", "norm_zh": "拾玖圣经的话不只像雨也像雪滋润我们雨是在春夏秋三季有的雪是在冬季有的无论在什么时候圣经的话都能滋润我们赛五五1011", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIX The word of the Bible is not only like rain but it also refreshes like snow rain comes in the spring summer and fall but snow comes in the winter the word of the Bible can refresh us in every season of our conditionIsa 551011"}
{"zh": "贰拾\t圣经的话也像面镜，能照出我们的本像，映出我们的真情；许多人都是因着读圣经，而看见了自己的真面目，认识了自己的真光景—雅一23，林后三18。", "en": "XX. The word of the Bible is also like a mirror; it reflects our true appearance and condition; by reading the Bible, we see our real countenance and know our true condition.—Jas. 1:23; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "贰拾圣经的话也像面镜能照出我们的本像映出我们的真情许多人都是因着读圣经而看见了自己的真面目认识了自己的真光景雅一23林后三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XX The word of the Bible is also like a mirror it reflects our true appearance and condition by reading the Bible we see our real countenance and know our true conditionJas 123 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "贰壹\t圣经能苏醒复兴人的心魂，能使人有智慧，能快活人的心，能明亮人的眼目—诗十九7~8。", "en": "XXI. The Bible can restore and refresh man's soul, can make man wise, can make man's heart joyous, and can enlighten man's eyes.—Psa. 19:7-8.", "norm_zh": "贰壹圣经能苏醒复兴人的心魂能使人有智慧能快活人的心能明亮人的眼目诗十九78", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXI The Bible can restore and refresh mans soul can make man wise can make mans heart joyous and can enlighten mans eyesPsa 1978"}
{"zh": "贰贰\t主的话─就是圣经的话─乃是灵，乃是生命；所以圣经的话能叫人得着灵，能叫人得着生命；能叫人从灵得生，也能叫人靠灵而活—约六63，罗八4。", "en": "XXII. The Lord’s words—the word of the Bible—are spirit and life; therefore, the word of the Bible enables man to have Spirit and life; it causes man to receive life from the Spirit and to live by the Spirit.—John 6:63; Rom. 8:4.", "norm_zh": "贰贰主的话就是圣经的话乃是灵乃是生命所以圣经的话能叫人得着灵能叫人得着生命能叫人从灵得生也能叫人靠灵而活约六63罗八4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXII The Lords wordsthe word of the Bibleare spirit and life therefore the word of the Bible enables man to have Spirit and life it causes man to receive life from the Spirit and to live by the SpiritJohn 663 Rom 84"}
{"zh": "贰叁\t圣经的话不只能喂养我们的灵性，也能医治我们的身体；因着圣经的话，我们心魂得以舒畅，心灵能以喜乐，身体就必健康—箴四20~24。", "en": "XXIII. The word of the Bible can spiritually nourish us and also heal our flesh; because of the word of the Bible, our soul is refreshed, our spirit can rejoice, and our body will be healthy.—Prov. 4:20-24.", "norm_zh": "贰叁圣经的话不只能喂养我们的灵性也能医治我们的身体因着圣经的话我们心魂得以舒畅心灵能以喜乐身体就必健康箴四2024", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXIII The word of the Bible can spiritually nourish us and also heal our flesh because of the word of the Bible our soul is refreshed our spirit can rejoice and our body will be healthyProv 42024"}
{"zh": "贰肆\t圣经的话是我们的谋士；圣经的话所给我们的建议或见地，远胜过任何的谋士、参事、或顾问—诗一一九24。", "en": "XXIV. The word of the Bible is our counselor; the suggestions or insights given to us by the word of the Bible are far better than those of any counselor, strategist, or consultant.—Psa. 119:24.", "norm_zh": "贰肆圣经的话是我们的谋士圣经的话所给我们的建议或见地远胜过任何的谋士参事或顾问诗一一九24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXIV The word of the Bible is our counselor the suggestions or insights given to us by the word of the Bible are far better than those of any counselor strategist or consultantPsa 11924"}
{"zh": "贰伍\t圣经的话也像磐石可靠；我们的生活工作，若都以圣经的话作根据，就像房子建造在磐石上，稳固可靠—太七24~25。", "en": "XXV. The word of the Bible is also like a rock, reliable and firm; if our life and work are based on the word of the Bible, they will be like a solid and reliable house built on a rock.—Matt. 7:24-25.", "norm_zh": "贰伍圣经的话也像磐石可靠我们的生活工作若都以圣经的话作根据就像房子建造在磐石上稳固可靠太七2425", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXV The word of the Bible is also like a rock reliable and firm if our life and work are based on the word of the Bible they will be like a solid and reliable house built on a rockMatt 72425"}
{"zh": "（一）“给我（主耶稣）作见证。”约翰五章三十九节，路加二十四章二十七节，四十四节，四十六节，约翰五章四十六节。", "en": "1) “Testify concerning Me (the Lord Jesus).” John 5:39, Luke 24:27, 44, 46, John 5:46.", "norm_zh": "一给我主耶稣作见证约翰五章三十九节路加二十四章二十七节四十四节四十六节约翰五章四十六节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Testify concerning Me the Lord Jesus John 539 Luke 2427 44 46 John 546"}
{"zh": "圣经的第一个功用，是给主耶稣作见证。主耶稣是圣经的题目，是圣经的内容；圣经是主耶稣的说明，是主耶稣的发表。主耶稣是神活的道，圣经是神写的道。圣经这写的道，若没有主耶稣那活的道作实际，圣经就不过是空洞的道理，虚空的字句。主耶稣那活的道，若没有圣经这写的道作发表，主耶稣就是玄妙难得认识，渺茫难得捉摸的。但有了圣经这清楚确定的说明，明白的启示，主耶稣就能具体的给人认识，确定的给人了解。不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的，就是旧约各部分，无论是1摩西的律法，2先知的书，或是3诗篇，（旧约共分这三大部分，）无不都是为主耶稣作见证，说到主耶稣的。所以我们若要认识主耶稣，就非读圣经，非明白圣经不可。", "en": "The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus. The Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible; the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus. The Lord Jesus is God’s living Word; the Bible is God’s written Word. The Bible, God’s written Word, must have the Lord Jesus, the living Word, as its reality; otherwise, it is but mere doctrines and empty letters. The Lord Jesus, the living Word, must have the Bible, the written Word, as His expression; otherwise, He is mysterious and difficult to know, vague and hard to grasp. However, since there is the clear, definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures, the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men. Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus, but every part of the Old Testament, whether (1) the Law of Moses, (2) the Prophets, or (3) the Psalms (these are the three major parts of the Old Testament), testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus. Hence, if we want to know the Lord Jesus, we must read and understand the Bible.", "norm_zh": "圣经的第一个功用是给主耶稣作见证主耶稣是圣经的提目是圣经的内容圣经是主耶稣的说明是主耶稣的发表主耶稣是神活的道圣经是神写的道圣经这写的道若没有主耶稣哪活的道作实际圣经就不过是空洞的道理虚空的字句主耶稣哪活的道若没有圣经这写的道作发表主耶稣就是玄妙难得认识渺茫难得捉摸的但有了圣经这清楚确定的说明明白的启示主耶稣就能具体的给人认识确定的给人了解不只新约各书都是启示主耶稣的就是旧约各部分无论是1摩西的律法2先知的书或是3诗篇旧约共分这三大部分无不都是为主耶稣作见证说到主耶稣的所以我们若要认识主耶稣就非读圣经非明白圣经不可", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus The Lord Jesus is the subject and contents of the Bible the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus The Lord Jesus is Gods living Word the Bible is Gods written Word The Bible Gods written Word must have the Lord Jesus the living Word as its reality otherwise it is but mere doctrines and empty letters The Lord Jesus the living Word must have the Bible the written Word as His expression otherwise He is mysterious and difficult to know vague and hard to grasp However since there is the clear definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men Not only every book of the New Testament reveals the Lord Jesus but every part of the Old Testament whether 1 the Law of Moses 2 the Prophets or 3 the Psalms these are the three major parts of the Old Testament testifies and speaks concerning the Lord Jesus Hence if we want to know the Lord Jesus we must read and understand the Bible"}
{"zh": "叫我们有得救的智慧", "en": "To make us wise unto salvation", "norm_zh": "叫我们有得救的智慧", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To make us wise unto salvation"}
{"zh": "（二）“使你…有得救的智慧。”提后三章十五节。", "en": "2) “make you... wise unto salvation” (2 Tim. 3:15).", "norm_zh": "二使你有得救的智慧提后三章十五节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 make you wise unto salvation 2 Tim 315"}
{"zh": "（三）“重生。”彼前一章二十三节，雅各书一章十八节。", "en": "3) “Regeneration” (1 Pet. 1:23; James 1:18).", "norm_zh": "三重生彼前一章二十三节雅各书一章十八节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Regeneration 1 Pet 123 James 118"}
{"zh": "（四）“教训、督责、使人归正、教导人学义，…叫属神的人得以完全。”提后三章十六至十七节。", "en": "4) “teaching, conviction, correction, instruction in righteousness... that the man of God may be complete” (2 Tim. 3:16-17).", "norm_zh": "四教训督责使人归正教导人学义叫属神的人得以完全提后三章十六至十七节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 teaching conviction correction instruction in righteousness that the man of God may be complete 2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "圣经使我们得着重生之后，就教训我们，督责我们，使我们在各方面归正，教导我们在凡事上学义，叫我们这蒙了神的重生，而属于神的人，得以在神面前成为完全。", "en": "After being regenerated by the word of God, the Bible teaches, convicts, corrects, and instructs us in righteousness so that we may be complete before God as regenerated men of God.", "norm_zh": "圣经使我们得着重生之后就教训我们督责我们使我们在各方面归正教导我们在凡事上学义叫我们这蒙了神的重生而属于神的人得以在神面前成为完全", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "After being regenerated by the word of God the Bible teaches convicts corrects and instructs us in righteousness so that we may be complete before God as regenerated men of God"}
{"zh": "叫我们有忍耐、蒙安慰、而得有盼望", "en": "To give us endurance, comfort, and hope", "norm_zh": "叫我们有忍耐蒙安慰而得有盼望", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To give us endurance comfort and hope"}
{"zh": "（五）“教训，…生…忍耐，…安慰，…盼望。”罗马十五章四节。", "en": "5) “instruction... endurance... encouragement... hope” (Rom. 15:4).", "norm_zh": "五教训生忍耐安慰盼望罗马十五章四节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 instruction endurance encouragement hope Rom 154"}
{"zh": "圣经的教训，也能叫我们有忍耐、蒙安慰、而得有盼望。许多信徒，当他们落到患难病困中，无法忍受，伤心失望的时候，因着读到一段或一句圣经，就在心里有了忍受的力量，或蒙到无上的安慰，而得有出乎人意外的盼望。这是我们在遭遇苦难的时候，很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立。", "en": "The teachings of the Bible can also give us endurance, comfort, and hope. Many Christians have fallen into tribulation and sickness. Being unable to bear it, they feel sorrowful and hopeless, but when they read a portion or a sentence of the Bible, they have the enduring strength in their hearts, or they receive unspeakable comfort, and thus obtain hope that is beyond their expectation. This is the help and building up that we can easily receive from the Bible when we experience suffering.", "norm_zh": "圣经的教训也能叫我们有忍耐蒙安慰而得有盼望许多信徒当他们落到患难病困中无法忍受伤心失望的时候因着读到一段或一句圣经就在心里有了忍受的力量或蒙到无上的安慰而得有出乎人意外的盼望这是我们在遭遇苦难的时候很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The teachings of the Bible can also give us endurance comfort and hope Many Christians have fallen into tribulation and sickness Being unable to bear it they feel sorrowful and hopeless but when they read a portion or a sentence of the Bible they have the enduring strength in their hearts or they receive unspeakable comfort and thus obtain hope that is beyond their expectation This is the help and building up that we can easily receive from the Bible when we experience suffering"}
{"zh": "（六）“鉴戒；…警戒。”林前十章十一节。", "en": "6) “types;... admonition” (1 Cor. 10:11).", "norm_zh": "六鉴戒警戒林前十章十一节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 types admonition 1 Cor 1011"}
{"zh": "圣经的话犹如明灯照亮", "en": "The word of the Bible is like a shining lamp.", "norm_zh": "圣经的话犹如明灯照亮", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible is like a shining lamp"}
{"zh": "（七）“如同灯照在暗处。”彼后一章十九节。", "en": "7) “A lamp shining in a dark place” (2 Pet. 1:19).", "norm_zh": "七如同灯照在暗处彼后一章十九节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "7 A lamp shining in a dark place 2 Pet 119"}
{"zh": "圣经的话作我们脚前的灯，路上的光", "en": "The word of the Bible as a lamp to our feet and a light to our path", "norm_zh": "圣经的话作我们脚前的灯路上的光", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible as a lamp to our feet and a light to our path"}
{"zh": "（八）“脚前的灯，…路上的光。”诗篇一百一十九篇一百零五节，箴言六章二十三节。", "en": "8) “A lamp to my feet / And a light to my path” (Psa. 119:105; see also Prov. 6:23).", "norm_zh": "八脚前的灯路上的光诗篇一百一十九篇一百零五节箴言六章二十三节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "8 A lamp to my feet And a light to my path Psa 119105 see also Prov 623"}
{"zh": "（九）“发出亮光，使愚人通达。”诗篇一百十九篇一百三十节。", "en": "9) “gives light, / Imparting understanding to the simple” (Psa. 119:130).", "norm_zh": "九发出亮光使愚人通达诗篇一百十九篇一百三十节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "9 gives light Imparting understanding to the simple Psa 119130"}
{"zh": "有洁净的能力", "en": "Having the power to cleanse", "norm_zh": "有洁净的能力", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Having the power to cleanse"}
{"zh": "（十）“洁净…行为。”诗篇一百一十九篇九节。", "en": "10) “cleanse... way” (Psa. 119:9).", "norm_zh": "十洁净行为诗篇一百一十九篇九节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "10 cleanse way Psa 1199"}
