{"zh": "圣经的话锋利如剑", "en": "The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword", "norm_zh": "圣经的话锋利如剑", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword"}
{"zh": "（十三）“比…两刃的剑更快。”希伯来四章十二节。", "en": "13) “sharper than... any two-edged sword” (Heb. 4:12).", "norm_zh": "十三比两刃的剑更快希伯来四章十二节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "13 sharper than any twoedged sword Heb 412"}
{"zh": "再比方，有一个姊妹正和一个不信的男子进行婚姻。一天她读经读到林后六章十四节，那里所说“你们和不信的原不相配，不要同负一轭”的话，就刺入她的心中，叫她觉出她一个信的人和一个不信的男子进行婚姻，乃是出于她自己的主意，不是出于神的旨意。这样，这节圣经的话，就把她在婚姻的事上，怎样随从她自己的意思，体贴她肉体的爱好，而不随从神的旨意，不体贴神的心意，那真实的光景，给她显明出来；就在她婚姻的事上，把她的心意和神的旨意，分别清楚；就叫她在这样的大事上得蒙拯救，脱离自己肉体的喜爱；不随着肉体和心中行喜好的去行，而顶从神那上好的旨意，使自己蒙到神的喜悦，并得着神的保守。圣经的话在这一类的事上，对于我们常是活泼而有功效的，其锋利甚于两刃的剑。我们里面无论有什么样的调和掺杂，圣经的话都能为我们剖开辨明，而将我们真实的光景带到神约面前，摆在神的面光中，叫我们得蒙拯救，脱离魂，而活在灵里；脱离自己和自己的意念，而活在神和神的心意里。", "en": "A sister who plans to marry an unbeliever may be touched when she reads 2 Corinthians 6:14, which says, “Do not become dissimilarly yoked with unbelievers.” This word can pierce her heart and cause her to see that her desire to marry an unbeliever is according to her own will, not God’s will. Thus, the word enables her to discern that she is following her will and minding the preferences of her flesh rather than God’s will and heart’s desire in the matter of marriage. When the will in her soul is divided from God’s will in her spirit, she will be saved from the desires of her flesh in this important matter. Rather than following her flesh and the desires of her heart, she will obey the peerless will of God. Then she will please God and be preserved by God. In such matters, the word of the Bible is often living and operative to us, and its sharpness is sharper than any two-edged sword. No matter what kind of mixture we have within us, the word of the Bible can divide and discern it for us, and bring our real condition before God, setting it in the light of God’s face, that we may be saved to be delivered from the soul to live in the spirit, and delivered from ourselves and our own thoughts to live in God and His heart’s desire.", "norm_zh": "再比方有一个姊妹正和一个不信的男子进行婚姻一天她读经读到林后六章十四节哪里所说你们和不信的原不相配不要同负一轭的话就刺入她的心中叫她觉出她一个信的人和一个不信的男子进行婚姻乃是出于她自己的主意不是出于神的旨意这样这节圣经的话就把她在婚姻的事上怎样随从她自己的意思体贴她肉体的爱好而不随从神的旨意不体贴神的心意哪真实的光景给她显明出来就在她婚姻的事上把她的心意和神的旨意分别清楚就叫她在这样的大事上得蒙拯救脱离自己肉体的喜爱不随着肉体和心中行喜好的去行而顶从神哪上好的旨意使自己蒙到神的喜悦并得着神的保守圣经的话在这一类的事上对于我们常是活泼而有功效的其锋利甚于两刃的剑我们里面无论有什么样的调和掺杂圣经的话都能为我们剖开辨明而将我们真实的光景带到神约面前摆在神的面光中叫我们得蒙拯救脱离魂而活在灵里脱离自己和自己的意念而活在神和神的心意里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A sister who plans to marry an unbeliever may be touched when she reads 2 Corinthians 614 which says Do not become dissimilarly yoked with unbelievers This word can pierce her heart and cause her to see that her desire to marry an unbeliever is according to her own will not Gods will Thus the word enables her to discern that she is following her will and minding the preferences of her flesh rather than Gods will and hearts desire in the matter of marriage When the will in her soul is divided from Gods will in her spirit she will be saved from the desires of her flesh in this important matter Rather than following her flesh and the desires of her heart she will obey the peerless will of God Then she will please God and be preserved by God In such matters the word of the Bible is often living and operative to us and its sharpness is sharper than any twoedged sword No matter what kind of mixture we have within us the word of the Bible can divide and discern it for us and bring our real condition before God setting it in the light of Gods face that we may be saved to be delivered from the soul to live in the spirit and delivered from ourselves and our own thoughts to live in God and His hearts desire"}
{"zh": "属灵生命的食物", "en": "Food of Spiritual Life", "norm_zh": "属灵生命的食物", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Food of Spiritual Life"}
{"zh": "（十四）“当食物。”耶利米十五章十六节，马太四章四节，约伯记二十三章十二节，希伯来五章十四节。", "en": "14) \"As food\"—Jer. 15:16, Matt. 4:4, Job 23:12, Heb. 5:14.", "norm_zh": "十四当食物耶利米十五章十六节马太四章四节约伯记二十三章十二节希伯来五章十四节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "14 As foodJer 1516 Matt 44 Job 2312 Heb 514"}
{"zh": "（十五）“灵奶。”彼前二章二节，林前三章一至二节，希伯来五章十二至十四节。", "en": "15) \"Milk\"—1 Pet. 2:2, 1 Cor. 3:1-2, Heb. 5:12-14.", "norm_zh": "十五灵奶彼前二章二节林前三章一至二节希伯来五章十二至十四节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "15 Milk1 Pet 22 1 Cor 312 Heb 51214"}
{"zh": "圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮，也是我们属灵生命的奶。干粮是为大人的，奶是为婴孩的。当我们在属灵的生命上长大，对于属灵的事能领会得练达的时候，我们就能从圣经的话里，得到干粮的营养，使我们属灵的生命强壮有力。当我们在属灵的生命上幼稚，对于属灵的事，领会力不够强的时候，圣经的话也有的像奶一样，能喂养我们，使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大。所以一个初得重生的信徒，必须爱慕圣经的话，“像才生的婴孩爱慕一样；”否则，他在属灵的生命上必不能长大，必一直作一个“在基督里为婴孩”的人。", "en": "The Bible is not only solid food but also milk for our spiritual life. Solid food is for adults; milk is for infants. When our spiritual life is mature and we have an understanding of spiritual matters, we can extract the nourishment of solid food from the Bible, strengthening our spiritual life. When our spiritual life is immature and we lack an adequate understanding of spiritual matters, there are portions of the word of the Bible that are like milk, which can nourish us and cause our spiritual life to grow. Therefore, a newly regenerated believer must love the word of the Bible, “as newborn babes long [for the milk]”; otherwise, his spiritual life cannot grow, and he will always be “a babe in Christ.”", "norm_zh": "圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮也是我们属灵生命的奶干粮是为大人的奶是为婴孩的当我们在属灵的生命上长大对于属灵的事能领会得练达的时候我们就能从圣经的话里得到干粮的营养使我们属灵的生命强壮有力当我们在属灵的生命上幼稚对于属灵的事领会力不够强的时候圣经的话也有的像奶一样能喂养我们使我们在属灵的生命上得以渐渐长大所以一个初得重生的信徒必须爱慕圣经的话像才生的婴孩爱慕一样否则他在属灵的生命上必不能长大必一直作一个在基督里为婴孩的人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Bible is not only solid food but also milk for our spiritual life Solid food is for adults milk is for infants When our spiritual life is mature and we have an understanding of spiritual matters we can extract the nourishment of solid food from the Bible strengthening our spiritual life When our spiritual life is immature and we lack an adequate understanding of spiritual matters there are portions of the word of the Bible that are like milk which can nourish us and cause our spiritual life to grow Therefore a newly regenerated believer must love the word of the Bible as newborn babes long for the milk otherwise his spiritual life cannot grow and he will always be a babe in Christ"}
{"zh": "（十六）“洗净。”以弗所五章二十六至二十七节，约翰十五章三节。", "en": "16) \"Cleansing\"—Eph. 5:26-27, John 15:3.", "norm_zh": "十六洗净以弗所五章二十六至二十七节约翰十五章三节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "16 CleansingEph 52627 John 153"}
{"zh": "圣经的话，不只能洁净我们外面的行为，去掉我们外面在行为上所受的玷污，并且还能在我们里面洗净我们，叫我们脱离旧造的弱点。以弗所五章这里所说的，就是这种的洗净─就是主要用祂在我们里面生命的水，借着圣经的话，把我们洗净，叫我们脱去旧造的斑点（以弗所五章二十七节的“玷污”，原文是“斑点”）和皱纹。斑点和皱纹，不是我们在外面行为上所受的玷污，乃是我们在里面旧造生命里所有的弱点。这是主要用圣经的话，配合着祂在我们里面的生命，给我们洗去的。圣灵常使圣经的一句或一段话，活现在我们里面，来配合主在我们里面的生命，使我们脱去旧造的东西，而得在新造里长大。这也是圣经的话，在我们里面的一种洗净功用。", "en": "The word of the Bible washes our outward actions and removes our outward defilement. It also cleanses us inwardly and frees us from the weaknesses of the old creation. Ephesians 5:26 refers to this kind of cleansing—that is, the Lord uses the water of life within us to cleanse us through the word of the Bible, eliminating the spots (the \"spot\" in Ephesians 5:27, which in the original is \"spot\") and wrinkles of the old creation. Spots and wrinkles are not related to the defilement that we acquire from our outward actions but to the weaknesses of the life of the old creation within us. The Lord uses the word in coordination with His life in us to wash away our spots and wrinkles. The Holy Spirit in coordination with the Lord’s life in us frequently enlivens us with a word or sentence in the Bible in order to remove things of the old creation so that we can grow in the new creation. This cleansing is also a function of the word of the Bible within us.", "norm_zh": "圣经的话不只能洁净我们外面的行为去掉我们外面在行为上所受的玷污并且还能在我们里面洗净我们叫我们脱离旧造的弱点以弗所五章这里所说的就是这种的洗净就是主要用祂在我们里面生命的水借着圣经的话把我们洗净叫我们脱去旧造的斑点以弗所五章二十七节的玷污原文是斑点和皱纹斑点和皱纹不是我们在外面行为上所受的玷污乃是我们在里面旧造生命里所有的弱点这是主要用圣经的话配合着祂在我们里面的生命给我们洗去的圣灵常使圣经的一句或一段话活现在我们里面来配合主在我们里面的生命使我们脱去旧造的东西而得在新造里长大这也是圣经的话在我们里面的一种洗净功用", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible washes our outward actions and removes our outward defilement It also cleanses us inwardly and frees us from the weaknesses of the old creation Ephesians 526 refers to this kind of cleansingthat is the Lord uses the water of life within us to cleanse us through the word of the Bible eliminating the spots the spot in Ephesians 527 which in the original is spot and wrinkles of the old creation Spots and wrinkles are not related to the defilement that we acquire from our outward actions but to the weaknesses of the life of the old creation within us The Lord uses the word in coordination with His life in us to wash away our spots and wrinkles The Holy Spirit in coordination with the Lords life in us frequently enlivens us with a word or sentence in the Bible in order to remove things of the old creation so that we can grow in the new creation This cleansing is also a function of the word of the Bible within us"}
{"zh": "圣经的话也非常有能力，能像火焚烧", "en": "The word of the Bible is also very powerful, like a burning fire.", "norm_zh": "圣经的话也非常有能力能像火焚烧", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible is also very powerful like a burning fire"}
{"zh": "（十七）“像火，又像…大锤。”耶利米二十三章二十九节，五章十四节。", "en": "17) \"Like a fire, and like a... hammer\"—Jer. 23:29, 5:14.", "norm_zh": "十七像火又像大锤耶利米二十三章二十九节五章十四节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "17 Like a fire and like a hammerJer 2329 514"}
{"zh": "圣经的话也像雨、露、甘霖，能灌溉、滋润", "en": "The word of the Bible is also like rain, dew, and abundant showers, which can water and refresh us.", "norm_zh": "圣经的话也像雨露甘霖能灌溉滋润", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word of the Bible is also like rain dew and abundant showers which can water and refresh us"}
{"zh": "（十八）“如雨，…露，…细雨，…甘霖。”申命记三十二章二节。", "en": "18) “Like the rain...like the dew...and like abundant showers” (Deut. 32:2).", "norm_zh": "十八如雨露细雨甘霖申命记三十二章二节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "18 Like the rainlike the dewand like abundant showers Deut 322"}
{"zh": "像雪滋润我们", "en": "Refreshing us like snow", "norm_zh": "像雪滋润我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Refreshing us like snow"}
{"zh": "（十九）如“雨雪…滋润。”以赛亚五十五章十至十一节", "en": "19) As “the rain and the snow...water” (Isa. 55:10-11).", "norm_zh": "十九如雨雪滋润以赛亚五十五章十至十一节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:01:49.871375+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "19 As the rain and the snowwater Isa 551011"}
