{"zh": "读经：提后三15~17，约十四16，彼前一23，林前十11，诗一一九105、11，箴六23，彼前二2", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 3:15-17; John 14:16; 1 Pet. 1:23; 1 Cor. 10:11; Psa. 119:105, 11; Prov. 6:23; 1 Pet. 2:2", "norm_zh": "读经提后三1517约十四16彼前一23林前十11诗一一九10511箴六23彼前二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 31517 John 1416 1 Pet 123 1 Cor 1011 Psa 119105 11 Prov 623 1 Pet 22"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经的第一个功用，是给主耶稣作见证；主耶稣是圣经的题目，是圣经的内容；圣经是主耶稣的说明，是主耶稣的发表—约五39，路二四27、44、46：（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "I. The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus; the Lord Jesus is the subject and content of the Bible, and the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord Jesus.—John 5:39; Luke 24:27, 44, 46:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经的第一个功用是给主耶稣作见证主耶稣是圣经的提目是圣经的内容圣经是主耶稣的说明是主耶稣的发表约五39路二四274446李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The first function of the Bible is to testify concerning the Lord Jesus the Lord Jesus is the subject and content of the Bible and the Bible is the explanation and expression of the Lord JesusJohn 539 Luke 2427 44 46"}
{"zh": "一\t主耶稣是神活的道，圣经是神写的道；圣经这写的道，若没有主耶稣那活的道作实际，圣经就不过是空洞的道理，虚空的字句—提后三16，约十四6。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "A. The Lord Jesus is the living Word of God, and the Bible is the written Word of God; if the written Word, the Bible, did not have the living Word, the Lord Jesus, as its reality, the Bible would be nothing but empty doctrines and letters.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "一主耶稣是神活的道圣经是神写的道圣经这写的道若没有主耶稣哪活的道作实际圣经就不过是空洞的道理虚空的字句提后三16约十四6李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Lord Jesus is the living Word of God and the Bible is the written Word of God if the written Word the Bible did not have the living Word the Lord Jesus as its reality the Bible would be nothing but empty doctrines and letters2 Tim 316 John 146"}
{"zh": "二\t有了圣经这清楚确定的说明，明白的启示，主耶稣就能具体的给人认识，确定的给人了解；所以我们若要认识主耶稣，就非读圣经，非明白圣经不可—五39，路二四44。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "B. Since there is the clear, definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures, the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men; therefore, if we want to know the Lord Jesus, we must read and understand the Bible.—John 5:39; Luke 24:44.", "norm_zh": "二有了圣经这清楚确定的说明明白的启示主耶稣就能具体的给人认识确定的给人了解所以我们若要认识主耶稣就非读圣经非明白圣经不可五39路二四44李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since there is the clear definite explanation and plain revelation of the Scriptures the Lord Jesus can be known practically and comprehended definitely by men therefore if we want to know the Lord Jesus we must read and understand the BibleJohn 539 Luke 2444"}
{"zh": "贰\t圣经的功用；在为着我们这一面，圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧，将神在基督里的救法，和人因信得救的途径，启示给我们—提后三15，林前一24。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "II. The functions of the Bible; on our side, the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation, revealing to us how God saves men in Christ and how men may be saved by faith.—2 Tim. 3:15; 1 Cor. 1:24.", "norm_zh": "贰圣经的功用在为着我们这一面圣经的功用第一就是叫我们有得救的智慧将神在基督里的救法和人因信得救的途径启示给我们提后三15林前一24李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The functions of the Bible on our side the first function of the Bible is to make us wise unto salvation revealing to us how God saves men in Christ and how men may be saved by faith2 Tim 315 1 Cor 124"}
{"zh": "叁\t圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用，就是使我们蒙到重生；圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面，使我们有了神的生命而得着重生—彼前一23，雅一18。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "III. The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated; the word of the Bible is like a seed of life falling into us, causing us to have God's life and be regenerated.—1 Pet. 1:23; James 1:18.", "norm_zh": "叁圣经在我们身上第一步具体的功用就是使我们蒙到重生圣经的话就像生命的种子落到我们里面使我们有了神的生命而得着重生彼前一23雅一18李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The first practical function of the Bible in us is to cause us to be regenerated the word of the Bible is like a seed of life falling into us causing us to have Gods life and be regenerated1 Pet 123 James 118"}
{"zh": "肆\t圣经使我们得着重生之后，就教训我们，督责我们，使我们在各方面归正，教导我们在凡事上学义，叫我们这蒙了神的重生，得以在神面前成为完全—提后三16~17。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "IV. After the Bible causes us to be regenerated, it teaches us, convicts us, corrects us in every aspect, and instructs us in righteousness in all things, so that we, who have been regenerated by God, may be complete before God.—2 Tim. 3:16-17.", "norm_zh": "肆圣经使我们得着重生之后就教训我们督责我们使我们在各方面归正教导我们在凡事上学义叫我们这蒙了神的重生得以在神面前成为完全提后三1617李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV After the Bible causes us to be regenerated it teaches us convicts us corrects us in every aspect and instructs us in righteousness in all things so that we who have been regenerated by God may be complete before God2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "伍\t圣经的教训，也能叫我们有忍耐、蒙安慰、而得有盼望；我们在遭遇苦难的时候，很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立—罗十五4、13。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "V. The teachings of the Bible can also cause us to have endurance, to be comforted, and to have hope; when we encounter sufferings, we can easily receive help and establishment from the Bible.—Rom. 15:4, 13.", "norm_zh": "伍圣经的教训也能叫我们有忍耐蒙安慰而得有盼望我们在遭遇苦难的时候很容易从圣经中所得到的帮助和建立罗十五413李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The teachings of the Bible can also cause us to have endurance to be comforted and to have hope when we encounter sufferings we can easily receive help and establishment from the BibleRom 154 13"}
{"zh": "陆\t圣经中也记载许多的事，作我们的鉴戒，使我们受警戒；我们每逢读到这些记载的时候，很容易得到前车之鉴，而生了戒心，免蹈前辙—林前十11。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "VI. Many things are recorded in the Bible as examples for our admonition; whenever we read these records, we can easily be warned by the experiences of those who went before us, and we can be careful not to follow their example.—1 Cor. 10:11.", "norm_zh": "陆圣经中也记载许多的事作我们的鉴戒使我们受警戒我们每逢读到这些记载的时候很容易得到前车之鉴而生了戒心免蹈前辙林前十11李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Many things are recorded in the Bible as examples for our admonition whenever we read these records we can easily be warned by the experiences of those who went before us and we can be careful not to follow their example1 Cor 1011"}
{"zh": "柒\t圣经的话对于我们，许多时候也像明灯照在暗处；我们若要作一个明亮、通达时务的人，就必须明白圣经，有圣经的话存在心中，随时发光照亮我们—彼后一19，罗十三12。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "VII. Often the word of the Bible is like a lamp shining in a dark place to us; if we want to be an enlightened and knowledgeable person, we must understand the Bible and keep the word of the Bible in our hearts so that it can shine and enlighten us at any time.—2 Pet. 1:19; Rom. 13:12.", "norm_zh": "柒圣经的话对于我们许多时候也像明灯照在暗处我们若要作一个明亮通达时务的人就必须明白圣经有圣经的话存在心中随时发光照亮我们彼后一19罗十三12李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII Often the word of the Bible is like a lamp shining in a dark place to us if we want to be an enlightened and knowledgeable person we must understand the Bible and keep the word of the Bible in our hearts so that it can shine and enlighten us at any time2 Pet 119 Rom 1312"}
{"zh": "捌\t人在黑暗里走路，是需要灯光照亮脚步的；把圣经的话存记在心，圣经的话就能作我们脚前的灯，路上的光—诗一一九105，箴六23。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "VIII. People walking in the dark need a lamp to shine on the path of their feet; if we keep the word of the Bible in our heart, the word of the Bible can be a lamp to our feet and a light to our path.—Psa. 119:105; Prov. 6:23.", "norm_zh": "捌人在黑暗里走路是需要灯光照亮脚步的把圣经的话存记在心圣经的话就能作我们脚前的灯路上的光诗一一九105箴六23李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII People walking in the dark need a lamp to shine on the path of their feet if we keep the word of the Bible in our heart the word of the Bible can be a lamp to our feet and a light to our pathPsa 119105 Prov 623"}
{"zh": "玖\t圣经的话所发出的光，不只能在我们所行的路上照亮我们的脚步，还能叫我们愚昧人变为通达—诗一〇九103，弗五17。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "IX. The light emitted by the word of the Bible not only can enlighten our steps on the path we walk but also can cause us foolish people to become understanding—Psa. 119:103, Eph. 5:17.", "norm_zh": "玖圣经的话所发出的光不只能在我们所行的路上照亮我们的脚步还能叫我们愚昧人变为通达诗一〇九103弗五17李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The light emitted by the word of the Bible not only can enlighten our steps on the path we walk but also can cause us foolish people to become understandingPsa 119103 Eph 517"}
{"zh": "拾\t圣经的话不只有照亮的能力，也有洁净的能力；照亮是对黑暗的，洁净是对污秽的；我们若常读圣经，不只必蒙光照，也必蒙洁净—诗十九9，一一九9。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "X. In addition to containing the power to enlighten, the word in the Bible has the power to cleanse; enlightenment is in contrast to darkness, and purification is in contrast to filthiness; if we read the Bible frequently, we will not only be enlightened but also kept pure.—Psa. 19:9; 119:9.", "norm_zh": "拾圣经的话不只有照亮的能力也有洁净的能力照亮是对黑暗的洁净是对污秽的我们若常读圣经不只必蒙光照也必蒙洁净诗十九9一一九9李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X In addition to containing the power to enlighten the word in the Bible has the power to cleanse enlightenment is in contrast to darkness and purification is in contrast to filthiness if we read the Bible frequently we will not only be enlightened but also kept purePsa 199 1199"}
{"zh": "拾壹\t圣经也能使我们免得犯罪得罪神；我们若将圣经的话藏在心里，圣经的话就能常常提醒我们，使我们免得犯罪得罪神—11节，伯三六10。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XI. The Bible also prevents us from sinning against God; if we store the words of the Bible in our heart, the words of the Bible can constantly remind us so that we do not sin against God.—v. 11; Job 36:10.", "norm_zh": "拾壹圣经也能使我们免得犯罪得罪神我们若将圣经的话藏在心里圣经的话就能常常提醒我们使我们免得犯罪得罪神11节伯三六10李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XI The Bible also prevents us from sinning against God if we store the words of the Bible in our heart the words of the Bible can constantly remind us so that we do not sin against Godv 11 Job 3610"}
{"zh": "拾贰\t圣经的话也是圣灵的宝剑，是我们可以靠着圣灵用以对付撒但和他的使者的；我们能打败那引诱或攻击我们的邪灵、仇敌，都是藉着圣经的话—弗六17~18。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XII. The word in the Bible is also the sword of the Spirit, which we can apply by the Holy Spirit to deal with Satan and his messengers; our being able to defeat the evil spirits and the enemy who tempt or attack us is altogether through the word of the Bible.—Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "拾贰圣经的话也是圣灵的宝剑是我们可以靠着圣灵用以对付撒但和他的使者的我们能打败哪引诱或攻击我们的邪灵仇敌都是借着圣经的话弗六1718李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XII The word in the Bible is also the sword of the Spirit which we can apply by the Holy Spirit to deal with Satan and his messengers our being able to defeat the evil spirits and the enemy who tempt or attack us is altogether through the word of the BibleEph 61718"}
{"zh": "拾叁\t圣经的话锋利如剑，不只能对付我们属灵的仇敌，并且能将我们里面的魂与灵给我们剖开，能将我们心中的思念和主意给我们辨明—17节，来四12。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XIII. The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword; it can not only deal with our spiritual enemies, but can also divide our soul from our spirit and discern the thoughts and intentions of our heart.—v. 17; Heb. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "拾叁圣经的话锋利如剑不只能对付我们属灵的仇敌并且能将我们里面的魂与灵给我们剖开能将我们心中的思念和主意给我们辨明17节来四12李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIII The word of the Bible is as sharp as a sword it can not only deal with our spiritual enemies but can also divide our soul from our spirit and discern the thoughts and intentions of our heartv 17 Heb 412"}
{"zh": "拾肆\t圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物；我们肉身的生命如何需要营养，我们属灵的生命也如何需要营养；属灵生命的营养，是只有圣经的话能供应的—耶十五16，太四4，伯二十三12，来五14。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XIV. The word of the Bible is also food for our spiritual life; just as our physical life needs nourishment, our spiritual life also needs nourishment; the nourishment for our spiritual life is what only the word of the Bible can supply.—Jer. 15:16; Matt. 4:4; Job 23:12; Heb. 5:14.", "norm_zh": "拾肆圣经的话也是我们属灵生命的食物我们肉身的生命如何需要营养我们属灵的生命也如何需要营养属灵生命的营养是只有圣经的话能供应的耶十五16太四4伯二十三12来五14李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIV The word of the Bible is also food for our spiritual life just as our physical life needs nourishment our spiritual life also needs nourishment the nourishment for our spiritual life is what only the word of the Bible can supplyJer 1516 Matt 44 Job 2312 Heb 514"}
{"zh": "拾伍\t圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮，也是我们属灵生命的奶；一个初得重生的信徒，必须爱慕圣经的话，“像才生的婴孩爱慕一样”—彼前二2，林前三1~2，来五12~14。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XV. The word of the Bible is not only solid food for our spiritual life but also milk for our spiritual life; a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible, \"as newborn babes long for it.\"—1 Pet. 2:2; 1 Cor. 3:1-2; Heb. 5:12-14.", "norm_zh": "拾伍圣经的话不只是我们属灵生命的干粮也是我们属灵生命的奶一个初得重生的信徒必须爱慕圣经的话像才生的婴孩爱慕一样彼前二2林前三12来五1214李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XV The word of the Bible is not only solid food for our spiritual life but also milk for our spiritual life a newly regenerated believer must long for the word of the Bible as newborn babes long for it1 Pet 22 1 Cor 312 Heb 51214"}
{"zh": "拾陆\t圣经的话，不只能洁净我们外面的行为；并且还能在我们里面洗净我们，叫我们脱离旧造的弱点；叫我们脱去旧造的斑点—弗五16~17，约十五3。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XVI. The word of the Bible not only can cleanse our outward actions but can also wash us inwardly, freeing us from the weaknesses of the old creation and putting away the spots of the old creation.—Eph. 5:16-17; John 15:3.", "norm_zh": "拾陆圣经的话不只能洁净我们外面的行为并且还能在我们里面洗净我们叫我们脱离旧造的弱点叫我们脱去旧造的斑点弗五1617约十五3李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVI The word of the Bible not only can cleanse our outward actions but can also wash us inwardly freeing us from the weaknesses of the old creation and putting away the spots of the old creationEph 51617 John 153"}
{"zh": "拾柒\t圣经的话也非常有能力，能像火焚烧，并能像大锤打碎；圣经的话能把人向着神冰冷的心烧得火热，也能把人与神圣洁不合的东西烧灭净尽—耶二三29，五14。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XVII. The word of the Bible is also very powerful, being like a burning fire and like a smashing hammer; the word of the Bible can burn a person's ice-cold heart toward God to make it burning hot, and can also completely burn away the things of man that are contrary to God's holy nature.—Jer. 23:29; 5:14.", "norm_zh": "拾柒圣经的话也非常有能力能像火焚烧并能像大锤打碎圣经的话能把人向着神冰冷的心烧得火热也能把人与神圣洁不合的东西烧灭净尽耶二三29五14李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVII The word of the Bible is also very powerful being like a burning fire and like a smashing hammer the word of the Bible can burn a persons icecold heart toward God to make it burning hot and can also completely burn away the things of man that are contrary to Gods holy natureJer 2329 514"}
{"zh": "拾捌\t圣经的话也像雨、露、甘霖，能灌溉、滋润；我们是神所耕种的田地，是神所栽种的庄稼；圣经的话使我们生长结实—林前三9，可四20，林前三6。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XVIII. The word of the Bible is also like rain, dew, and abundant showers, which can water and refresh us; we are God's farm, the harvest that God cultivates; the word of the Bible causes us to grow and bear fruit.—1 Cor. 3:9; Mark 4:20; 1 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "拾捌圣经的话也像雨露甘霖能灌溉滋润我们是神所耕种的田地是神所栽种的庄稼圣经的话使我们生长结实林前三9可四20林前三6李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XVIII The word of the Bible is also like rain dew and abundant showers which can water and refresh us we are Gods farm the harvest that God cultivates the word of the Bible causes us to grow and bear fruit1 Cor 39 Mark 420 1 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "拾玖\t圣经的话不只像雨，也像雪滋润我们；雨是在春、夏、秋三季有的，雪是在冬季有的；无论在什么时候，圣经的话都能滋润我们—赛五五10~11。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XIX. The word of the Bible is not only like rain, but it also refreshes like snow; rain comes in the spring, summer, and fall, but snow comes in the winter; the word of the Bible can refresh us in every season of our condition—Isa. 55:10-11.", "norm_zh": "拾玖圣经的话不只像雨也像雪滋润我们雨是在春夏秋三季有的雪是在冬季有的无论在什么时候圣经的话都能滋润我们赛五五1011李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XIX The word of the Bible is not only like rain but it also refreshes like snow rain comes in the spring summer and fall but snow comes in the winter the word of the Bible can refresh us in every season of our conditionIsa 551011"}
{"zh": "贰拾\t圣经的话也像面镜，能照出我们的本像，映出我们的真情；许多人都是因着读圣经，而看见了自己的真面目，认识了自己的真光景—雅一23，林后三18。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XX. The word of the Bible is also like a mirror; it reflects our true appearance and condition; many people, by reading the Bible, see their real countenance and know their true condition—James 1:23; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "贰拾圣经的话也像面镜能照出我们的本像映出我们的真情许多人都是因着读圣经而看见了自己的真面目认识了自己的真光景雅一23林后三18李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XX The word of the Bible is also like a mirror it reflects our true appearance and condition many people by reading the Bible see their real countenance and know their true conditionJames 123 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "贰壹\t圣经能苏醒复兴人的心魂，能使人有智慧，能快活人的心，能明亮人的眼目—诗十九7~8。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XXI. The Bible can restore and refresh man's soul, make him wise, make his heart joyous, and enlighten his eyes—Psa. 19:7-8.", "norm_zh": "贰壹圣经能苏醒复兴人的心魂能使人有智慧能快活人的心能明亮人的眼目诗十九78李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXI The Bible can restore and refresh mans soul make him wise make his heart joyous and enlighten his eyesPsa 1978"}
{"zh": "贰贰\t主的话─就是圣经的话─乃是灵，乃是生命；所以圣经的话能叫人得着灵，能叫人得着生命；能叫人从灵得生，也能叫人靠灵而活—约六63，罗八4。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XXII. The Lord's words—the word of the Bible—are spirit and are life; therefore, the word of the Bible can cause man to receive the Spirit and to receive life, and it can cause man to receive life from the Spirit and to live by the Spirit—John 6:63; Rom. 8:4.", "norm_zh": "贰贰主的话就是圣经的话乃是灵乃是生命所以圣经的话能叫人得着灵能叫人得着生命能叫人从灵得生也能叫人靠灵而活约六63罗八4李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXII The Lords wordsthe word of the Bibleare spirit and are life therefore the word of the Bible can cause man to receive the Spirit and to receive life and it can cause man to receive life from the Spirit and to live by the SpiritJohn 663 Rom 84"}
{"zh": "贰叁\t圣经的话不只能喂养我们的灵性，也能医治我们的身体；因着圣经的话，我们心魂得以舒畅，心灵能以喜乐，身体就必健康—箴四20~24。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XXIII. The word of the Bible can spiritually nourish us and also heal our flesh; because of the word of the Bible, our soul is refreshed, our spirit is made joyous, and our body will be healthy—Prov. 4:20-24.", "norm_zh": "贰叁圣经的话不只能喂养我们的灵性也能医治我们的身体因着圣经的话我们心魂得以舒畅心灵能以喜乐身体就必健康箴四2024李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXIII The word of the Bible can spiritually nourish us and also heal our flesh because of the word of the Bible our soul is refreshed our spirit is made joyous and our body will be healthyProv 42024"}
{"zh": "贰肆\t圣经的话是我们的谋士；圣经的话所给我们的建议或见地，远胜过任何的谋士、参事、或顾问—诗一一九24。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XXIV. The word of the Bible is our counselor; the suggestions or ideas given to us by the word of the Bible are far better than those of any counselor, strategist, or consultant—Psa. 119:24.", "norm_zh": "贰肆圣经的话是我们的谋士圣经的话所给我们的建议或见地远胜过任何的谋士参事或顾问诗一一九24李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXIV The word of the Bible is our counselor the suggestions or ideas given to us by the word of the Bible are far better than those of any counselor strategist or consultantPsa 11924"}
{"zh": "贰伍\t圣经的话也像磐石可靠；我们的生活工作，若都以圣经的话作根据，就像房子建造在磐石上，稳固可靠—太七24~25。（李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道（卷三），第三十一题）", "en": "XXV. The word of the Bible is also like a rock, reliable and firm; if our life and work are based on the word of the Bible, they will be like a solid and reliable house built on a rock—Matt. 7:24-25.", "norm_zh": "贰伍圣经的话也像磐石可靠我们的生活工作若都以圣经的话作根据就像房子建造在磐石上稳固可靠太七2425李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道卷三第三十一提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:04:30.167704+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XXV The word of the Bible is also like a rock reliable and firm if our life and work are based on the word of the Bible they will be like a solid and reliable house built on a rockMatt 72425"}
{"zh": "读经：提后三16~17，申五32~33，启二二18~19，林前十一19，多三10，启十八4", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 3:16-17; Deut. 5:32-33; Rev. 22:18-19; 1 Cor. 11:19; Tit. 3:10; Rev. 18:4", "norm_zh": "读经提后三1617申五3233启二二1819林前十一19多三10启十八4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 31617 Deut 53233 Rev 221819 1 Cor 1119 Tit 310 Rev 184"}
{"zh": "壹\t只有圣经有权威—提后三16~17，赛八20，申十三18：", "en": "I. Only the Bible has the authority to judge.—2 Tim. 3:16-17; Isa. 8:20; Deut. 13:18:", "norm_zh": "壹只有圣经有权威提后三1617赛八20申十三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Only the Bible has the authority to judge2 Tim 31617 Isa 820 Deut 1318"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经自己的见证是说，“圣经都是神所默示的，于教训、督责、使人归正、教导人学义，都是有益的；叫属神的人得以完全，预备行各样的善事”（提后三16~17）。", "en": "A. The Bible testifies of itself: \"All Scripture is God-breathed and profitable for teaching, for conviction, for correction, for instruction in righteousness, that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work\" (2 Tim. 3:16-17).", "norm_zh": "一圣经自己的见证是说圣经都是神所默示的于教训督责使人归正教导人学义都是有益的叫属神的人得以完全预备行各样的善事提后三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible testifies of itself All Scripture is Godbreathed and profitable for teaching for conviction for correction for instruction in righteousness that the man of God may be complete fully equipped for every good work 2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "二\t除了神所默示的话语以外，没有人或团体，可以作有权威的教训；人以信条所记载的，是有权威的，就是取消圣经的权威—提后三16~17：", "en": "B. Other than God's inspired Word, no person or group can have any authoritative teaching; for man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible.—2 Tim. 3:16-17:", "norm_zh": "二除了神所默示的话语以外没有人或团体可以作有权威的教训人以信条所记载的是有权威的就是取消圣经的权威提后三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Other than Gods inspired Word no person or group can have any authoritative teaching for man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "1\t人或若要以为：我们知道圣经的教训，真是专一的，满足的；然而，圣经若真有专一的教训，又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢？—约十二48，启二18。", "en": "1. Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete. If the teaching of the Bible is, indeed, so specific, why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creeds?—John 12:48; Rev. 2:18.", "norm_zh": "1人或若要以为我们知道圣经的教训真是专一的满足的然而圣经若真有专一的教训又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢约十二48启二18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete If the teaching of the Bible is indeed so specific why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creedsJohn 1248 Rev 218"}
{"zh": "2\t如果圣经是有权威的，则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢？信条的权威，足以证明圣经的权威么？这样的作法，乃是羞辱圣经，并非尊重圣经！—十九1~3。", "en": "2. If the Bible indeed so authoritative, why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds? Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible? To do this is to put the Bible to shame. It is not to honor the Bible!—John 19:1-3.", "norm_zh": "2如果圣经是有权威的则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢信条的权威足以证明圣经的权威么这样的作法乃是羞辱圣经并非尊重圣经十九13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If the Bible indeed so authoritative why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible To do this is to put the Bible to shame It is not to honor the BibleJohn 1913"}
{"zh": "三\t当人们以信条代替圣经，将活的和死的联合，归于教会的领袖，而不归于神的名下时，圣灵就将人的和神的，死的和生的，人的权威和神的权威，逐一划得分明—三1，亚四6，林前十二5。", "en": "C. When man replaces the Bible with the creeds, joins the living to the dead, and comes under great church leaders instead of coming under God's name, the Holy Spirit will draw a clear line between what is of man and what is of God, between the dead and the living, and between man's authority and God's authority.—Rev. 3:1; Zech. 4:6; 1 Cor. 12:5.", "norm_zh": "三当人们以信条代替圣经将活的和死的联合归于教会的领袖而不归于神的名下时圣灵就将人的和神的死的和生的人的权威和神的权威逐一划得分明三1亚四6林前十二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C When man replaces the Bible with the creeds joins the living to the dead and comes under great church leaders instead of coming under Gods name the Holy Spirit will draw a clear line between what is of man and what is of God between the dead and the living and between mans authority and Gods authorityRev 31 Zech 46 1 Cor 125"}
{"zh": "四\t所以，现在敬畏神的人们，应当起来，反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则；人的试验越厉害，圣经的权威越显明；真的并不怕人试验；并且一受试验，反将假的显明出来！—太二八18，林前一2。", "en": "D. Hence, all God-fearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace God's word; the more man tested it, the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself; all true things can withstand tests; and tests will only expose the false things!—Matt. 28:18; 1 Cor. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "四所以现在敬畏神的人们应当起来反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则人的试验越厉害圣经的权威越显明真的并不怕人试验并且一受试验反将假的显明出来太二八18林前一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Hence all Godfearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace Gods word the more man tested it the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself all true things can withstand tests and tests will only expose the false thingsMatt 2818 1 Cor 12"}
{"zh": "贰\t我们现在应当只有一本公开的圣经，让人来遵从；我们若在圣经之外，有所订定，无论其内容是如何合经，就叫人轻看了圣经，而重看我们所订定的规章—申五32~33：", "en": "II. We should only have one open Bible now for men to follow; if we institute anything outside the Bible, no matter how scriptural it may appear, we are causing others to despise the Bible and turning their attention to the instituted ordinances.—Deut. 5:32-33:", "norm_zh": "贰我们现在应当只有一本公开的圣经让人来遵从我们若在圣经之外有所订定无论其内容是如何合经就叫人轻看了圣经而重看我们所订定的规章申五3233", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II We should only have one open Bible now for men to follow if we institute anything outside the Bible no matter how scriptural it may appear we are causing others to despise the Bible and turning their attention to the instituted ordinancesDeut 53233"}
{"zh": "一\t圣经已经将教会的制度订定清楚了；我们千万不要在圣经之外，再有一种的订定─即称之为信条、宪章、纲例、章程、规则等都不可─无论我们所订定的是若何的合圣经；不然，我们立刻成功一个宗派—林前十一19，一2，多三10。", "en": "A. The Bible has decreed all institutions of the church in a clear way already; we must never have any decrees, whether they are creeds, constitutions, rules, charters, or ordinances outside the Bible, no matter how scriptural they may appear; otherwise, we will become a sect right away.—1 Cor. 11:19; 1:2; Tit. 3:10.", "norm_zh": "一圣经已经将教会的制度订定清楚了我们千万不要在圣经之外再有一种的订定即称之为信条宪章纲例章程规则等都不可无论我们所订定的是若何的合圣经不然我们立刻成功一个宗派林前十一19一2多三10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Bible has decreed all institutions of the church in a clear way already we must never have any decrees whether they are creeds constitutions rules charters or ordinances outside the Bible no matter how scriptural they may appear otherwise we will become a sect right away1 Cor 1119 12 Tit 310"}
{"zh": "二\t订定规章，必居两种性质之一；不是有权威的，就是没有的；如果有权威，若里面有了错误怎么办？就是没有错误，能否完全呢？若云没有权威，错可修正，缺可补入；是这样的规章复有何用？在圣经外，多此一篇，岂非累赘？—林前十一19，彼后二1。", "en": "B. The institution of any ordinance carries with it one of two characteristics; either it is authoritative, or it is nothing; if such ordinances are to be authoritative, what happens when they contain mistakes? Even if they do not contain any mistakes, can they possibly be perfect? On the other hand, if such ordinances are non-authoritative, and someone can correct whatever is wrong and add whatever is lacking, what good will these ordinances do? Is it not redundant to have another page outside the Bible?—1 Cor. 11:19; 2 Pet. 2:1.", "norm_zh": "二订定规章必居两种性质之一不是有权威的就是没有的如果有权威若里面有了错误怎么办就是没有错误能否完全呢若云没有权威错可修正缺可补入是这样的规章复有何用在圣经外多此一篇岂非累赘林前十一19彼后二1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The institution of any ordinance carries with it one of two characteristics either it is authoritative or it is nothing if such ordinances are to be authoritative what happens when they contain mistakes Even if they do not contain any mistakes can they possibly be perfect On the other hand if such ordinances are nonauthoritative and someone can correct whatever is wrong and add whatever is lacking what good will these ordinances do Is it not redundant to have another page outside the Bible1 Cor 1119 2 Pet 21"}
{"zh": "三\t我们如果有所订定，我们所订定的，就成我们信仰的标准；这样，无论怎样合圣经，总是叫人在圣经之外，另有信仰的标准；现在惟一合经的办法，就是让神的话亲自来引导信徒—提后三16~17。", "en": "C. If we institute anything, our institution will become the standard of our faith. This means that we will be setting up another standard of faith besides the Bible, no matter how scriptural such a standard may appear; now the only scriptural way is to let the word of God Himself guide the believers.—2 Tim. 3:16-17.", "norm_zh": "三我们如果有所订定我们所订定的就成我们信仰的标准这样无论怎样合圣经总是叫人在圣经之外另有信仰的标准现在惟一合经的办法就是让神的话亲自来引导信徒提后三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C If we institute anything our institution will become the standard of our faith This means that we will be setting up another standard of faith besides the Bible no matter how scriptural such a standard may appear now the only scriptural way is to let the word of God Himself guide the believers2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "叁\t教会可以不按着圣经而行，然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威；离弃神的法则者，自然要受审判；这审判的原则，就是在于圣经；要跟从主的人，就当归回到主的法则来—出三三13上，犹3：", "en": "III. The church can act contrary to the Bible, but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority; those who depart from God's law will surely be judged; the principles of judgment are in the Bible; all those who want to follow the Lord must come back to the Lord's ordinances.—Exo. 33:13a; Jude 3:", "norm_zh": "叁教会可以不按着圣经而行然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威离弃神的法则者自然要受审判这审判的原则就是在于圣经要跟从主的人就当归回到主的法则来出三三13上犹3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The church can act contrary to the Bible but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority those who depart from Gods law will surely be judged the principles of judgment are in the Bible all those who want to follow the Lord must come back to the Lords ordinancesExo 3313a Jude 3"}
{"zh": "一\t人们断不能以为环境已经改变了，使徒也没有了，教会也腐败了，所以他们可以不理基督的话，可以随着己意而行—结一1~3，约七6、8：", "en": "A. One cannot assume that since circumstances have changed, the apostles have passed away, and the church has been corrupted, one can therefore ignore the word of Christ and can walk according to his own will.—Ezek. 1:1-3; John 7:6, 8:", "norm_zh": "一人们断不能以为环境已经改变了使徒也没有了教会也腐败了所以他们可以不理基督的话可以随着己意而行结一13约七68", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A One cannot assume that since circumstances have changed the apostles have passed away and the church has been corrupted one can therefore ignore the word of Christ and can walk according to his own willEzek 113 John 76 8"}
{"zh": "1\t罗马教的大原则，就是教会是有权柄的，就是圣经的意思，也应当照着教会所定规的去解释；他们不许信徒读经；他们要人顺服教会过于圣经—启十七1。", "en": "1. The overriding principle in Roman Catholicism is that authority rests with the church and that even the Bible has to be interpreted according to the mandate of the church; it does not allow believers to read the Bible and requires that man obey the church more than he obeys the Bible.—Rev. 17:1.", "norm_zh": "1罗马教的大原则就是教会是有权柄的就是圣经的意思也应当照着教会所定规的去解释他们不许信徒读经他们要人顺服教会过于圣经启十七1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The overriding principle in Roman Catholicism is that authority rests with the church and that even the Bible has to be interpreted according to the mandate of the church it does not allow believers to read the Bible and requires that man obey the church more than he obeys the BibleRev 171"}
{"zh": "2\t更正教的原则，岂不是除了圣经以外，教会是没有权威的么？我们的原则，岂不是要人完全顺服圣经，不顺服教会么？如果我们承认教会权威的存在，我们岂非又回到罗马教的境地去么？—三1。", "en": "2. Does not the principle of Protestantism state that apart from the Bible the church has no authority? Is not our principle that of complete obedience to the Bible and not to the church? If we recognize the existence of the authority of the church, are we not going back to Roman Catholicism?—Rev. 3:1.", "norm_zh": "2更正教的原则岂不是除了圣经以外教会是没有权威的么我们的原则岂不是要人完全顺服圣经不顺服教会么如果我们承认教会权威的存在我们岂非又回到罗马教的境地去么三1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Does not the principle of Protestantism state that apart from the Bible the church has no authority Is not our principle that of complete obedience to the Bible and not to the church If we recognize the existence of the authority of the church are we not going back to Roman CatholicismRev 31"}
{"zh": "二\t神不是呼召我们去发明更好于祂在圣经里所启示的教会组织，祂的命令乃是要我们按着一次交给圣徒的真道而行（犹3）。", "en": "B. God has not called us to invent some institutions better than what the Bible has revealed. His command is that we walk according to the truth once delivered to us (Jude 3).", "norm_zh": "二神不是呼召我们去发明更好于祂在圣经里所启示的教会组织祂的命令乃是要我们按着一次交给圣徒的真道而行犹3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God has not called us to invent some institutions better than what the Bible has revealed His command is that we walk according to the truth once delivered to us Jude 3"}
{"zh": "三\t“我的道，”神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道，来亲近基督的自己—并不是教会的道。我们如果接受教会的话（我们应当记得，话与道在原文常是一样的），就是承认教会是有权威的；我们如果接受基督的话，我们就有基督自己的权威—诗一一九33、69。", "en": "C. \"My word.\" God has called us to keep Christ's own word and to draw near to Christ Himself rather than to the word of the church. If we accept the word of the church, it means that the church has the authority; if we accept the word of Christ, it means that Christ Himself has the authority.—Psa. 119:33, 69.", "norm_zh": "三我的道神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道来亲近基督的自己并不是教会的道我们如果接受教会的话我们应当记得话与道在原文常是一样的就是承认教会是有权威的我们如果接受基督的话我们就有基督自己的权威诗一一九3369", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C My word God has called us to keep Christs own word and to draw near to Christ Himself rather than to the word of the church If we accept the word of the church it means that the church has the authority if we accept the word of Christ it means that Christ Himself has the authorityPsa 11933 69"}
{"zh": "四\t弟兄姊妹引用“工作的再思”时，乃是因看见它所说的某点，是合乎圣经的，所以要照着行，才有益处；如果说，工作的再思如何说，所以该如何行，就不免使人误会你重看这一本书过于圣经了；我们没有意思，也是绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经，我们在言语上也该谨慎—申四2，箴三十6。", "en": "D. When the brothers and sisters quote from the book Rethinking Our Work, they should do so because the point quoted is according to Scripture. This is why we act according to what it says, and only when we act this way will we receive the benefit; if one says that he does this or that because the book says so, others will misunderstand that we consider this book to be more important than the Bible; we have no intention of doing this, and we dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible; we should be careful in our words.—Deut. 4:2; Prov. 30:6.", "norm_zh": "四弟兄姊妹引用工作的再思时乃是因看见它所说的某点是合乎圣经的所以要照着行才有益处如果说工作的再思如何说所以该如何行就不免使人误会你重看这一本书过于圣经了我们没有意思也是绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经我们在言语上也该谨慎申四2箴三十6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D When the brothers and sisters quote from the book Rethinking Our Work they should do so because the point quoted is according to Scripture This is why we act according to what it says and only when we act this way will we receive the benefit if one says that he does this or that because the book says so others will misunderstand that we consider this book to be more important than the Bible we have no intention of doing this and we dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible we should be careful in our wordsDeut 42 Prov 306"}
{"zh": "肆\t我们虽然敬爱许多神在各公会里的仆人，但是我们应当小心！不应当因着敬爱的缘故，就忘记了圣经的权威—赛八20，申十三18，十五5：", "en": "IV. Although we respect many servants of God in the denominations, we must be careful! We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for them.—Isa. 8:20; Deut. 13:18; 15:5:", "norm_zh": "肆我们虽然敬爱许多神在各公会里的仆人但是我们应当小心不应当因着敬爱的缘故就忘记了圣经的权威赛八20申十三18十五5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Although we respect many servants of God in the denominations we must be careful We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for themIsa 820 Deut 1318 155"}
{"zh": "一\t我们敬爱路德，敬爱卫斯理，敬爱喀尔文，敬爱其余神千百的仆人；但是我们应当知道：我们信心和行为的标准，乃是“耶和华如此说”，并不是“路德、卫斯理、喀尔文如此说”—赛十24，五十1，耶二2，结二4。", "en": "A. We respect Luther. We respect John Wesley, Calvin, and thousands of other servants of God. Yet we must know that the standard of our faith and walk is \"thus saith Jehovah\" rather than \"thus saith Luther, Wesley, or Calvin.\"—Isa. 10:24; 50:1; Jer. 2:2; Ezek. 2:4.", "norm_zh": "一我们敬爱路德敬爱卫斯理敬爱喀尔文敬爱其余神千百的仆人但是我们应当知道我们信心和行为的标准乃是耶和华如此说并不是路德卫斯理喀尔文如此说赛十24五十1耶二2结二4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We respect Luther We respect John Wesley Calvin and thousands of other servants of God Yet we must know that the standard of our faith and walk is thus saith Jehovah rather than thus saith Luther Wesley or CalvinIsa 1024 501 Jer 22 Ezek 24"}
{"zh": "二\t我们常欲听从人世的学说，和遗传的教训；但是神的目的，乃是要破除这些，好叫我们重新来到祂话语的面前，听祂圣经的教训；这样，我们所信的，就不是人的智慧，乃是神的大能—赛四十31，林后十二9。", "en": "B. Many times we are inclined to listen to man's philosophy and traditional teachings, but God's intention is to break us away from these things so that we may come afresh before His word and hear the teaching of the Bible. In this way, what we believe in will not be of man's wisdom but will be of the power of God.—Isa. 40:31; 2 Cor. 12:9.", "norm_zh": "二我们常欲听从人世的学说和遗传的教训但是神的目的乃是要破除这些好叫我们重新来到祂话语的面前听祂圣经的教训这样我们所信的就不是人的智慧乃是神的大能赛四十31林后十二9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Many times we are inclined to listen to mans philosophy and traditional teachings but Gods intention is to break us away from these things so that we may come afresh before His word and hear the teaching of the Bible In this way what we believe in will not be of mans wisdom but will be of the power of GodIsa 4031 2 Cor 129"}
{"zh": "三\t神的儿子亲自对我们说，人的遗传是不必遵守的；祂对于专心遵守古人遗传的人说，“这百姓用嘴唇尊敬我，心却远离我；他们将人的吩咐，当作道理教导人，所以拜我也是枉然”（太十五8~9）；因为我们若要遵守人的遗传，我们就要干犯神的诫命（3节）。", "en": "C. The Son of God told us Himself that we need not keep man's tradition. He said of those who were keen to abide by the tradition of their ancestors that \"this people honors Me with their lips, but their heart stays far away from Me; but in vain do they worship Me, teaching as teachings the commandments of men\" (Matt. 15:8-9). If we want to abide by man's tradition, we are transgressing the commandment of God (v. 3).", "norm_zh": "三神的儿子亲自对我们说人的遗传是不必遵守的祂对于专心遵守古人遗传的人说这百姓用嘴唇尊敬我心却远离我他们将人的吩咐当作道理教导人所以拜我也是枉然太十五89因为我们若要遵守人的遗传我们就要干犯神的诫命3节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Son of God told us Himself that we need not keep mans tradition He said of those who were keen to abide by the tradition of their ancestors that this people honors Me with their lips but their heart stays far away from Me but in vain do they worship Me teaching as teachings the commandments of men Matt 1589 If we want to abide by mans tradition we are transgressing the commandment of God v 3"}
{"zh": "只有圣经有权威", "en": "Only the Bible has the authority to judge.", "norm_zh": "只有圣经有权威", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Only the Bible has the authority to judge"}
{"zh": "一个领袖，或一个团体，若有权柄－在圣经之外－教训，则谁能保他们不会错误", "en": "If a leader or a group has the authority apart from the Bible to teach, who can then guarantee that he can be inerrant?", "norm_zh": "一个领袖或一个团体若有权柄在圣经之外教训则谁能保他们不会错误", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If a leader or a group has the authority apart from the Bible to teach who can then guarantee that he can be inerrant"}
{"zh": "然而有的人就要说，现在的信条，是可从圣经里，用许多的证据，证明都是圣经自己的教训的。好，如果圣经会教训信条所教训的，圣经是像信条那样的有权威，则何必在圣经之外，又有信条呢？人或若要以为：我们知道圣经的教训，真是专一的，满足的；然而，圣经若真有专一的教训，又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢？如果圣经是有权威的，则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢？信条的权威，足以证明圣经的权威么？这样的作法，乃是羞辱圣经，并非尊重圣经！圣经自己的见证是说，“圣经都是神所默示的，于教训、督责、使人归正、教导人学义，都是有益的；叫属神的人得以完全，预备行各样的善事。”（提后三16~17）。", "en": "However, some say that the present creeds can be proved to be the very teaching of the Bible by many scriptural proofs. Very well. If the Bible teaches what the creeds teach, and if the Bible is as authoritative as the creeds are, why then do we need the creeds in addition to the Bible? Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete. If the teaching of the Bible is, indeed, so specific, why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creeds? If the Bible is indeed so authoritative, why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds? Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible? To do this is to put the Bible to shame. It is not to honor the Bible! The Bible testifies of itself: \"All Scripture is God-breathed and profitable for teaching, for conviction, for correction, for instruction in righteousness, that the man of God may be complete, fully equipped for every good work\" (2 Tim. 3:16-17).", "norm_zh": "然而有的人就要说现在的信条是可从圣经里用许多的证据证明都是圣经自己的教训的好如果圣经会教训信条所教训的圣经是像信条哪样的有权威则何必在圣经之外又有信条呢人或若要以为我们知道圣经的教训真是专一的满足的然而圣经若真有专一的教训又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢如果圣经是有权威的则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢信条的权威足以证明圣经的权威么这样的作法乃是羞辱圣经并非尊重圣经圣经自己的见证是说圣经都是神所默示的于教训督责使人归正教导人学义都是有益的叫属神的人得以完全预备行各样的善事提后三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "However some say that the present creeds can be proved to be the very teaching of the Bible by many scriptural proofs Very well If the Bible teaches what the creeds teach and if the Bible is as authoritative as the creeds are why then do we need the creeds in addition to the Bible Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete If the teaching of the Bible is indeed so specific why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creeds If the Bible is indeed so authoritative why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible To do this is to put the Bible to shame It is not to honor the Bible The Bible testifies of itself All Scripture is Godbreathed and profitable for teaching for conviction for correction for instruction in righteousness that the man of God may be complete fully equipped for every good work 2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "人以信条所记载的，是有权威的，就是取消圣经的权威", "en": "For man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible!", "norm_zh": "人以信条所记载的是有权威的就是取消圣经的权威", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "For man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible"}
{"zh": "人以信条所记载的，是有权威的，就是取消圣经的权威！叫人不以圣经为程度，而以信条为程度！如果不幸，在信条里有了错误；则人们也应当维持这个错误，像维持其中其他的真理一般。如果不幸，在信条中有了缺点，则圣经也没有机会，可以补满它；简言之，这样的作法，就是取消圣经的高位，叫人的良心不能直接在神面前负责。所以，现在敬畏神的人们，应当起来，反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则。", "en": "For man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible! It causes man to take the creeds as the standard instead of taking the Bible as the standard! If unfortunately there are faults in the creeds, man must uphold these faults in the same way that he upholds all the truths, and if there are shortages in the creeds, the Bible will have no opportunity to make up these shortages. Simply put, this way annuls the high place given to the Bible and bars man's conscience from being directly responsible to God. Hence, all God-fearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace God's word.", "norm_zh": "人以信条所记载的是有权威的就是取消圣经的权威叫人不以圣经为程度而以信条为程度如果不幸在信条里有了错误则人们也应当维持这个错误像维持其中其他的真理一般如果不幸在信条中有了缺点则圣经也没有机会可以补满它简言之这样的作法就是取消圣经的高位叫人的良心不能直接在神面前负责所以现在敬畏神的人们应当起来反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "For man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible It causes man to take the creeds as the standard instead of taking the Bible as the standard If unfortunately there are faults in the creeds man must uphold these faults in the same way that he upholds all the truths and if there are shortages in the creeds the Bible will have no opportunity to make up these shortages Simply put this way annuls the high place given to the Bible and bars mans conscience from being directly responsible to God Hence all Godfearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace Gods word"}
{"zh": "人的试验越厉害，圣经的权威越显明", "en": "The more man tested it, the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself.", "norm_zh": "人的试验越厉害圣经的权威越显明", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The more man tested it the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself"}
{"zh": "无论如何，耶洗别好像是很有智慧的。她以为她自己是可以教导人的，她就连接着管理人。她的错处，就是她不肯让她假冒为神话语的教训，给神的话语来审判，看到底是真是假。她也知道，神所默示的，是有权威的；所以她才假冒她是受神默示的。然而，她忘记了，她这样的受神默示，是否神所默示的话语所允许的。她的权威，不许人疑问，只许人接受。圣经也是如此。它是绝对应当被人接受的。就是为着这个缘故，所以它在过去的时代中，曾受过许多的试验。人的试验越厉害，圣经的权威越显明。真的并不怕人试验。并且一受试验，反将假的显明出来！相信罗马的，乃是愚昧与迷信。相信圣经的，乃是聪明，并满有理由。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "Jezebel may seem very wise. She thinks that she herself can teach others. As a result, she becomes dominating over others as well. Her problem lies in the fact that she is not willing to have her counterfeit teachings to be judged by the Word of God itself and to test if her teachings are indeed true or false. She knows that God's inspiration is authoritative. That is why she counterfeits God's inspiration. However, she forgets whether the way she thinks she is inspired is itself something that is warranted by the inspiration of God. She can entertain no questioning of her authority; one must accept it fully. The same is demanded by the Bible; it requires absolute acceptance. It is for this reason that during the past ages there have been numerous tests. The more man tested it, the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself. All true things can withstand tests. Tests will only expose the false things! It is foolishness and superstition to believe in anything Romish. On the contrary, it is wise and very reasonable to believe in the Bible.", "norm_zh": "无论如何耶洗别好像是很有智慧的她以为她自己是可以教导人的她就连接着管理人她的错处就是她不肯让她假冒为神话语的教训给神的话语来审判看到底是真是假她也知道神所默示的是有权威的所以她才假冒她是受神默示的然而她忘记了她这样的受神默示是否神所默示的话语所允许的她的权威不许人疑问只许人接受圣经也是如此它是绝对应当被人接受的就是为着这个缘故所以它在过去的时代中曾受过许多的试验人的试验越厉害圣经的权威越显明真的并不怕人试验并且一受试验反将假的显明出来相信罗马的乃是愚昧与迷信相信圣经的乃是聪明并满有理由倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jezebel may seem very wise She thinks that she herself can teach others As a result she becomes dominating over others as well Her problem lies in the fact that she is not willing to have her counterfeit teachings to be judged by the Word of God itself and to test if her teachings are indeed true or false She knows that Gods inspiration is authoritative That is why she counterfeits Gods inspiration However she forgets whether the way she thinks she is inspired is itself something that is warranted by the inspiration of God She can entertain no questioning of her authority one must accept it fully The same is demanded by the Bible it requires absolute acceptance It is for this reason that during the past ages there have been numerous tests The more man tested it the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself All true things can withstand tests Tests will only expose the false things It is foolishness and superstition to believe in anything Romish On the contrary it is wise and very reasonable to believe in the Bible"}
{"zh": "只有一本公开的圣经，让人来遵从", "en": "Only have one open Bible for men to follow", "norm_zh": "只有一本公开的圣经让人来遵从", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Only have one open Bible for men to follow"}
{"zh": "千万不要在圣经之外，再有一种的订定─即称之为信条、宪章、纲例、章程、规则", "en": "Never have any decrees, whether they are creeds, constitutions, rules, charters, or ordinances outside the Bible", "norm_zh": "千万不要在圣经之外再有一种的订定即称之为信条宪章纲例章程规则", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Never have any decrees whether they are creeds constitutions rules charters or ordinances outside the Bible"}
{"zh": "在圣经之外，再加上什么信条，就是一个宗派", "en": "To add some creeds to the Bible is a sect", "norm_zh": "在圣经之外再加上什么信条就是一个宗派", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To add some creeds to the Bible is a sect"}
{"zh": "更正教的各种信条，就是表明更正教是主张宗派的。在圣经外，再设立一种信条，无论其如何合乎圣经，都是自建藩篱，将意见不同的人拒在外面。你如果不同心，就请你他往，就是再立一个宗派也可以。神的教会如果不肯接受一切重生的人，而在圣经之外，再加上什么信条，就是一个宗派。感谢神，因为祂呼召我们来遵守基督的道。不然，简单的儿女们，对于现今纷乱的信条、组织和名称，真是不知何所适从。我们所当遵从的，是祂的道，不是教会的话。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（六）非拉铁非（忠心小群））", "en": "The different Protestant creeds show that Protestantism is for sectarianism. To set up any creed outside the Bible, no matter how scriptural it may be, is to build up a wall and to shut out those with different opinions. \"If you are not one with us, please go away to set up another sect.\" If the church of God will not accept all regenerated persons, but will add some creeds to the Bible, it is a sect already. Thank God that He has called us to keep the word of Christ. Otherwise, the simple children will be lost in the present confusion of creeds, organizations, and names. What we should keep is His word and not the church's word.", "norm_zh": "更正教的各种信条就是表明更正教是主张宗派的在圣经外再设立一种信条无论其如何合乎圣经都是自建藩篱将意见不同的人拒在外面你如果不同心就请你他往就是再立一个宗派也可以神的教会如果不肯接受一切重生的人而在圣经之外再加上什么信条就是一个宗派感谢神因为祂呼召我们来遵守基督的道不然简单的儿女们对于现今纷乱的信条组织和名称真是不知何所适从我们所当遵从的是祂的道不是教会的话倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三六非拉铁非忠心小群", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The different Protestant creeds show that Protestantism is for sectarianism To set up any creed outside the Bible no matter how scriptural it may be is to build up a wall and to shut out those with different opinions If you are not one with us please go away to set up another sect If the church of God will not accept all regenerated persons but will add some creeds to the Bible it is a sect already Thank God that He has called us to keep the word of Christ Otherwise the simple children will be lost in the present confusion of creeds organizations and names What we should keep is His word and not the churchs word"}
{"zh": "惟一合经的办法，就是让神的话亲自来引导信徒", "en": "The only scriptural way is to allow God's word to lead the believers personally", "norm_zh": "惟一合经的办法就是让神的话亲自来引导信徒", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The only scriptural way is to allow Gods word to lead the believers personally"}
{"zh": "以圣经的权威为已足", "en": "To be content with the authority of the Bible", "norm_zh": "以圣经的权威为已足", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To be content with the authority of the Bible"}
{"zh": "教会可以不按着圣经而行，然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威", "en": "The church can act contrary to the Bible, but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority.", "norm_zh": "教会可以不按着圣经而行然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The church can act contrary to the Bible but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority"}
{"zh": "审判的原则，就是在于圣经", "en": "The principles of judgment are in the Bible", "norm_zh": "审判的原则就是在于圣经", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The principles of judgment are in the Bible"}
{"zh": "神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道", "en": "God has called us to keep Christ's own word", "norm_zh": "神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "God has called us to keep Christs own word"}
{"zh": "绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经", "en": "Dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible", "norm_zh": "绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible"}
{"zh": "不应当因着敬爱的缘故，就忘记了圣经的权威", "en": "We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for them.", "norm_zh": "不应当因着敬爱的缘故就忘记了圣经的权威", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for them"}
{"zh": "人的遗传是不必遵守的", "en": "We need not keep man's tradition.", "norm_zh": "人的遗传是不必遵守的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We need not keep mans tradition"}
{"zh": "我们信心和行为的标准，乃是“耶和华如此说", "en": "The standard of our faith and walk is \"thus saith Jehovah.\"", "norm_zh": "我们信心和行为的标准乃是耶和华如此说", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The standard of our faith and walk is thus saith Jehovah"}
{"zh": "要知道谁是谁非，就必须根据圣经来断定", "en": "If we want to know who is correct and who is wrong, we must judge everything according to the Bible.", "norm_zh": "要知道谁是谁非就必须根据圣经来断定", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If we want to know who is correct and who is wrong we must judge everything according to the Bible"}
{"zh": "在相信全教会都要在灾难前被提的，有：达秘（J. N. Darby）、克锐（William Kelly）、叨雷（R. A. Torrey）、慕迪（D. L. Moody）、布鲁克（J. H. Brookes）、古锐（J. M. Gray）、加百林（A. C. Gaebeloin）、赛斯（J. A. Saiss）、司可福（C. I. Scofield）等。", "en": "Among those who believe that the whole church will be raptured before the tribulation are J. N. Darby, William Kelly, R. A. Torrey, D. L. Moody, J. H. Brookes, J. M. Gray, A. C. Gaebelein, J. A. Seiss, C. I. Scofield, and others.", "norm_zh": "在相信全教会都要在灾难前被提的有达秘JNDarby克锐WilliamKelly叨雷RATorrey慕迪DLMoody布鲁克JHBrookes古锐JMGray加百林ACGaebeloin赛斯JASaiss司可福CIScofield等", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Among those who believe that the whole church will be raptured before the tribulation are J N Darby William Kelly R A Torrey D L Moody J H Brookes J M Gray A C Gaebelein J A Seiss C I Scofield and others"}
{"zh": "若要跟从人，到底当跟从谁呢", "en": "If you want to follow man, whom should you follow?", "norm_zh": "若要跟从人到底当跟从谁呢", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If you want to follow man whom should you follow"}
{"zh": "只凭着圣经的教训，从圣经找出凭据来", "en": "Relying only on the teaching of the Bible, find out the proofs from the Bible.", "norm_zh": "只凭着圣经的教训从圣经找出凭据来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Relying only on the teaching of the Bible find out the proofs from the Bible"}
{"zh": "我们要知道谁是谁非，就必须根据圣经来断定。只有圣经有权威。我们要从圣经找出凭据来，看到底谁的理由最充分，谁的理由不可恃。", "en": "If we want to know who is correct and who is wrong, we must judge everything according to the Bible. Only the Bible has the authority to judge. We should find out the proofs from the Bible, and we should see whose reasons are most convincing and whose reasons are not trustworthy.", "norm_zh": "我们要知道谁是谁非就必须根据圣经来断定只有圣经有权威我们要从圣经找出凭据来看到底谁的理由最充分谁的理由不可恃", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If we want to know who is correct and who is wrong we must judge everything according to the Bible Only the Bible has the authority to judge We should find out the proofs from the Bible and we should see whose reasons are most convincing and whose reasons are not trustworthy"}
{"zh": "不过有一件事，我们要十分注意的，就是每一次要从圣经中找凭据的时候，不是只把差不多的就引来，不能以为只要有了圣经节就是有了凭据。我们必须注意那一节圣经到底是不是证明那一件事。如果只有圣经节就算凭据，不问圣经是不是证明这一件事的话，就好像一个无用的律师，引许多不相干的律法，来替他的当事人辩护一样。这是不是律法所许可的呢？（倪柝声文集第一辑第十九册，讲经记录（卷三），被提和灾难（一））", "en": "However, we have to be very careful about one thing. We cannot just quote verses every time we look for proof from the Bible. We should not presume that as long as a person has some verses, he has the proof. We must be careful that the verses we quote do indeed prove the things we are discussing. If we only quote verses, without asking whether or not the verses are appropriate to the subject matter, it would be like an incapable lawyer who quotes many irrelevant laws to defend his client. Is this not an unacceptable practice in the law?(CWWN, vol. 19, \"Notes on Scriptural Messages (3),\" THE RAPTURE AND THE TRIBULATION  (1)", "norm_zh": "不过有一件事我们要十分注意的就是每一次要从圣经中找凭据的时候不是只把差不多的就引来不能以为只要有了圣经节就是有了凭据我们必须注意哪一节圣经到底是不是证明哪一件事如果只有圣经节就算凭据不问圣经是不是证明这一件事的话就好像一个无用的律师引许多不相干的律法来替他的当事人辩护一样这是不是律法所许可的呢倪柝声文集第一辑第十九册讲经记录卷三被提和灾难一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "However we have to be very careful about one thing We cannot just quote verses every time we look for proof from the Bible We should not presume that as long as a person has some verses he has the proof We must be careful that the verses we quote do indeed prove the things we are discussing If we only quote verses without asking whether or not the verses are appropriate to the subject matter it would be like an incapable lawyer who quotes many irrelevant laws to defend his client Is this not an unacceptable practice in the lawCWWN vol 19 Notes on Scriptural Messages 3 THE RAPTURE AND THE TRIBULATION 1"}
{"zh": "我是一个全心相信圣经的人。照我看来，圣经是最高的法庭，凡圣经所定规的，我们毫无权利可以稍加疑议。圣灵知道教会应当如何组织，祂已经在圣经里完全启示出来了；乃教会中人竟有以为圣经中所启示的教会组织法，是尚属幼稚的，处今世界进化（？！）的光景中，应当有更完善的组织─究竟这不过是照着罗马教会的原路而进，究竟这不过是自大自高的世人，表明他们轻看神的心意而已。现今中国教会正处过渡的时代，多人都是题本色的教会；但是，本色而不合经，究非主旨；空洞洞的以“中华基督教会”为名，究有何益。愿主在这背道的世代中叫我们忠心！（教会的组织法，请读本报第四期全册）（倪柝声文集第一辑第七册，基督徒报（卷五），问答（四））", "en": "I, for one, believe the Bible with my whole heart. To me, the Bible is the highest court. Whatever is shown in the Bible, we do not have the slightest right to doubt, even a little. The Holy Spirit knows how the church should be organized. He has revealed the matter completely in the Scriptures. However, some in the church feel that the church organization revealed in the Bible is immature and that there should be a better and more complete organization in this age of progression. Actually, this is to follow the same road that the Roman Catholic Church has taken. These are but haughty people who despise the will of God. Today, the churches in China are in a transitional period. Many talk about indigenous churches, but to be indigenous without being scriptural is not the will of the Lord. What good is it simply to have an empty name of the \"Church of Christ in China\"? May the Lord make us faithful in this age of apostasy. (As to the organization of the church, please read the entire fourth issue of this paper.)(CWWN, vol. 7, \"The Christian (5),\" QUESTION AND ANSWER BOX  (4)", "norm_zh": "我是一个全心相信圣经的人照我看来圣经是最高的法庭凡圣经所定规的我们毫无权利可以稍加疑议圣灵知道教会应当如何组织祂已经在圣经里完全启示出来了乃教会中人竟有以为圣经中所启示的教会组织法是尚属幼稚的处今世界进化的光景中应当有更完善的组织究竟这不过是照着罗马教会的原路而进究竟这不过是自大自高的世人表明他们轻看神的心意而已现今中国教会正处过渡的时代多人都是提本色的教会但是本色而不合经究非主旨空洞洞的以中华基督教会为名究有何益愿主在这背道的世代中叫我们忠心教会的组织法请读本报第四期全册倪柝声文集第一辑第七册基督徒报卷五问答四", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:07:31.347722+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I for one believe the Bible with my whole heart To me the Bible is the highest court Whatever is shown in the Bible we do not have the slightest right to doubt even a little The Holy Spirit knows how the church should be organized He has revealed the matter completely in the Scriptures However some in the church feel that the church organization revealed in the Bible is immature and that there should be a better and more complete organization in this age of progression Actually this is to follow the same road that the Roman Catholic Church has taken These are but haughty people who despise the will of God Today the churches in China are in a transitional period Many talk about indigenous churches but to be indigenous without being scriptural is not the will of the Lord What good is it simply to have an empty name of the Church of Christ in China May the Lord make us faithful in this age of apostasy As to the organization of the church please read the entire fourth issue of this paperCWWN vol 7 The Christian 5 QUESTION AND ANSWER BOX 4"}
{"zh": "壹\t只有圣经有权威—提后三16~17，赛八20，申十三18：（倪柝声文集第一辑第十九册，讲经记录（卷三），被提和灾难（一））", "en": "I. Only the Bible has the authority to judge.—2 Tim. 3:16-17; Isa. 8:20; Deut. 13:18:(CWWN, vol. 19, \"Notes on Scriptural Messages (3),\" THE RAPTURE AND THE TRIBULATION  (1)", "norm_zh": "壹只有圣经有权威提后三1617赛八20申十三18倪柝声文集第一辑第十九册讲经记录卷三被提和灾难一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Only the Bible has the authority to judge2 Tim 31617 Isa 820 Deut 1318CWWN vol 19 Notes on Scriptural Messages 3 THE RAPTURE AND THE TRIBULATION 1"}
{"zh": "二\t除了神所默示的话语以外，没有人或团体，可以作有权威的教训；人以信条所记载的，是有权威的，就是取消圣经的权威—提后三16~17：（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "B. Other than God's inspired Word, no person or group can have any authoritative teaching; for man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible—2 Tim. 3:16-17:", "norm_zh": "二除了神所默示的话语以外没有人或团体可以作有权威的教训人以信条所记载的是有权威的就是取消圣经的权威提后三1617倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Other than Gods inspired Word no person or group can have any authoritative teaching for man to consider the creeds as authoritative is for him to annul the authority of the Bible2 Tim 31617"}
{"zh": "1\t人或若要以为：我们知道圣经的教训，真是专一的，满足的；然而，圣经若真有专一的教训，又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢？—约十二48，启二18。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "1. Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete. If the teaching of the Bible is, indeed, so specific, why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creeds?—John 12:48; Rev. 2:18.", "norm_zh": "1人或若要以为我们知道圣经的教训真是专一的满足的然而圣经若真有专一的教训又何必你们出来用信条叫它成为专一的呢约十二48启二18倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Some have conceded that the teachings of the Bible are specific and complete If the teaching of the Bible is indeed so specific why then is there the need to make it more specific with the creedsJohn 1248 Rev 218"}
{"zh": "2\t如果圣经是有权威的，则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢？信条的权威，足以证明圣经的权威么？这样的作法，乃是羞辱圣经，并非尊重圣经！—十九1~3。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "2. If the Bible is indeed so authoritative, why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds? Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible? To do this is to put the Bible to shame. It is not to honor the Bible!—Psa. 19:1-3.", "norm_zh": "2如果圣经是有权威的则何必用信条来证明圣经的权威呢信条的权威足以证明圣经的权威么这样的作法乃是羞辱圣经并非尊重圣经十九13倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If the Bible is indeed so authoritative why then is there the need to prove its authority with the creeds Can the authority of the creeds prove the authority of the Bible To do this is to put the Bible to shame It is not to honor the BiblePsa 1913"}
{"zh": "三\t当人们以信条代替圣经，将活的和死的联合，归于教会的领袖，而不归于神的名下时，圣灵就将人的和神的，死的和生的，人的权威和神的权威，逐一划得分明—三1，亚四6，林前十二5。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "C. When man replaces the Bible with the creeds, joins the living to the dead, and comes under great church leaders instead of coming under God's name, the Holy Spirit will draw a clear line between what is of man and what is of God, between the dead and the living, and between man's authority and God's authority.—Rev. 3:1; Zech. 4:6; 1 Cor. 12:5.", "norm_zh": "三当人们以信条代替圣经将活的和死的联合归于教会的领袖而不归于神的名下时圣灵就将人的和神的死的和生的人的权威和神的权威逐一划得分明三1亚四6林前十二5倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C When man replaces the Bible with the creeds joins the living to the dead and comes under great church leaders instead of coming under Gods name the Holy Spirit will draw a clear line between what is of man and what is of God between the dead and the living and between mans authority and Gods authorityRev 31 Zech 46 1 Cor 125"}
{"zh": "四\t所以，现在敬畏神的人们，应当起来，反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则；人的试验越厉害，圣经的权威越显明；真的并不怕人试验；并且一受试验，反将假的显明出来！—太二八18，林前一2。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "D. Hence, all God-fearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace God's word; the more man tested it, the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself; all true things can withstand tests; tests will only expose the false things!—Matt. 28:18; 1 Cor. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "四所以现在敬畏神的人们应当起来反对一切人所用以代替神的话的规则人的试验越厉害圣经的权威越显明真的并不怕人试验并且一受试验反将假的显明出来太二八18林前一2倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Hence all Godfearing men should now rise up to oppose all ordinances used by man to replace Gods word the more man tested it the more obviously the authority of the Bible manifested itself all true things can withstand tests tests will only expose the false thingsMatt 2818 1 Cor 12"}
{"zh": "叁\t教会可以不按着圣经而行，然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威；离弃神的法则者，自然要受审判；这审判的原则，就是在于圣经；要跟从主的人，就当归回到主的法则来—出三三13上，犹3：（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三）（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "III.\tThe church can act contrary to the Bible, but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority; those who depart from God's law will surely be judged; the principles of judgment are in the Bible; all those who want to follow the Lord must come back to the Lord's ordinances.—Exo. 33:13a; Jude 3:", "norm_zh": "叁教会可以不按着圣经而行然而圣经并不因此而失去其权威离弃神的法则者自然要受审判这审判的原则就是在于圣经要跟从主的人就当归回到主的法则来出三三13上犹3倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The church can act contrary to the Bible but the Bible will not thereby lose its authority those who depart from Gods law will surely be judged the principles of judgment are in the Bible all those who want to follow the Lord must come back to the Lords ordinancesExo 3313a Jude 3"}
{"zh": "一\t人们断不能以为环境已经改变了，使徒也没有了，教会也腐败了，所以他们可以不理基督的话，可以随着己意而行—结一1~3，约七6、8：（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "A.\tOne cannot assume that since circumstances have changed, the apostles have passed away, and the church has been corrupted, one can therefore ignore the word of Christ and can walk according to his own will.—Ezek. 1:1-3; John 7:6, 8:", "norm_zh": "一人们断不能以为环境已经改变了使徒也没有了教会也腐败了所以他们可以不理基督的话可以随着己意而行结一13约七68倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A One cannot assume that since circumstances have changed the apostles have passed away and the church has been corrupted one can therefore ignore the word of Christ and can walk according to his own willEzek 113 John 76 8"}
{"zh": "1\t罗马教的大原则，就是教会是有权柄的，就是圣经的意思，也应当照着教会所定规的去解释；他们不许信徒读经；他们要人顺服教会过于圣经—启十七1。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "1.\tThe overriding principle in Roman Catholicism is that authority rests with the church and that even the Bible has to be interpreted according to the mandate of the church; it does not allow believers to read the Bible and requires that man obey the church more than he obeys the Bible.—Rev. 17:1.", "norm_zh": "1罗马教的大原则就是教会是有权柄的就是圣经的意思也应当照着教会所定规的去解释他们不许信徒读经他们要人顺服教会过于圣经启十七1倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The overriding principle in Roman Catholicism is that authority rests with the church and that even the Bible has to be interpreted according to the mandate of the church it does not allow believers to read the Bible and requires that man obey the church more than he obeys the BibleRev 171"}
{"zh": "2\t更正教的原则，岂不是除了圣经以外，教会是没有权威的么？我们的原则，岂不是要人完全顺服圣经，不顺服教会么？如果我们承认教会权威的存在，我们岂非又回到罗马教的境地去么？—三1。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "2.\tDoes not the principle of Protestantism state that apart from the Bible the church has no authority? Is not our principle that of complete obedience to the Bible and not to the church? If we recognize the existence of the authority of the church, are we not going back to Roman Catholicism?—Rev. 3:1.", "norm_zh": "2更正教的原则岂不是除了圣经以外教会是没有权威的么我们的原则岂不是要人完全顺服圣经不顺服教会么如果我们承认教会权威的存在我们岂非又回到罗马教的境地去么三1倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Does not the principle of Protestantism state that apart from the Bible the church has no authority Is not our principle that of complete obedience to the Bible and not to the church If we recognize the existence of the authority of the church are we not going back to Roman CatholicismRev 31"}
{"zh": "二\t神不是呼召我们去发明更好于祂在圣经里所启示的教会组织，祂的命令乃是要我们按着一次交给圣徒的真道而行（犹3）。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），（五）撒狄（更正的教会））", "en": "B.\tGod has not called us to invent some institutions better than what the Bible has revealed. His command is that we walk according to the truth once delivered to us (Jude 3).", "norm_zh": "二神不是呼召我们去发明更好于祂在圣经里所启示的教会组织祂的命令乃是要我们按着一次交给圣徒的真道而行犹3倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三五撒狄更正的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God has not called us to invent some institutions better than what the Bible has revealed His command is that we walk according to the truth once delivered to us Jude 3"}
{"zh": "三\t“我的道，”神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道，来亲近基督的自己—并不是教会的道。我们如果接受教会的话（我们应当记得，话与道在原文常是一样的），就是承认教会是有权威的；我们如果接受基督的话，我们就有基督自己的权威—诗一一九33、69。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三）（六）非拉铁非（忠心小群））", "en": "C.\t\"My word.\" God has called us to keep Christ's own word and to draw near to Christ Himself rather than to the word of the church. If we accept the word of the church (we should remember that the word is often the same in the original), it means that the church has the authority; but if we accept the word of Christ, it means that Christ Himself has the authority.—Psa. 119:33, 69.", "norm_zh": "三我的道神是召我们来遵守基督自己的道来亲近基督的自己并不是教会的道我们如果接受教会的话我们应当记得话与道在原文常是一样的就是承认教会是有权威的我们如果接受基督的话我们就有基督自己的权威诗一一九3369倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三六非拉铁非忠心小群", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C My word God has called us to keep Christs own word and to draw near to Christ Himself rather than to the word of the church If we accept the word of the church we should remember that the word is often the same in the original it means that the church has the authority but if we accept the word of Christ it means that Christ Himself has the authorityPsa 11933 69"}
{"zh": "四\t弟兄姊妹引用“工作的再思”时，乃是因看见它所说的某点，是合乎圣经的，所以要照着行，才有益处；如果说，工作的再思如何说，所以该如何行，就不免使人误会你重看这一本书过于圣经了；我们没有意思，也是绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经，我们在言语上也该谨慎—申四2，箴三十6。（倪柝声文集第二辑第十二册，敞开的门（卷二），敞开的门（卷二）第十六期）", "en": "D.\tWhen the brothers and sisters quote from the book Rethinking Our Work, they should do so because the point quoted is according to Scripture; this is why we act according to what it says, and only when we act this way will we receive the benefit; if one says that he does this or that because the book says so, others will misunderstand that we consider this book to be more important than the Bible; we have no intention of doing this, and we dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible; we should be careful in our words.—Deut. 4:2; Prov. 30:6.", "norm_zh": "四弟兄姊妹引用工作的再思时乃是因看见它所说的某点是合乎圣经的所以要照着行才有益处如果说工作的再思如何说所以该如何行就不免使人误会你重看这一本书过于圣经了我们没有意思也是绝对不敢高举一本书过于有权威的圣经我们在言语上也该谨慎申四2箴三十6倪柝声文集第二辑第十二册敞开的门卷二敞开的门卷二第十六期", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D When the brothers and sisters quote from the book Rethinking Our Work they should do so because the point quoted is according to Scripture this is why we act according to what it says and only when we act this way will we receive the benefit if one says that he does this or that because the book says so others will misunderstand that we consider this book to be more important than the Bible we have no intention of doing this and we dare not uplift any book more than the authority of the Bible we should be careful in our wordsDeut 42 Prov 306"}
{"zh": "肆\t我们虽然敬爱许多神在各公会里的仆人，但是我们应当小心！不应当因着敬爱的缘故，就忘记了圣经的权威—赛八20，申十三18，十五5：（倪柝声文集第一辑第四册，基督徒报（卷二），默想启示录（中卷），（三）别迦摩（腐败的教会））", "en": "IV.\tAlthough we respect many servants of God in the denominations, we must be careful! We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for them.—Isa. 8:20; Deut. 13:18; 15:5:", "norm_zh": "肆我们虽然敬爱许多神在各公会里的仆人但是我们应当小心不应当因着敬爱的缘故就忘记了圣经的权威赛八20申十三18十五5倪柝声文集第一辑第四册基督徒报卷二默想启示录中卷三别迦摩腐败的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Although we respect many servants of God in the denominations we must be careful We should not neglect the authority of the Bible through our respect for themIsa 820 Deut 1318 155"}
{"zh": "一\t我们敬爱路德，敬爱卫斯理，敬爱喀尔文，敬爱其余神千百的仆人；但是我们应当知道：我们信心和行为的标准，乃是“耶和华如此说”，并不是“路德、卫斯理、喀尔文如此说”—赛十24，五十1，耶二2，结二4。（倪柝声文集第一辑第四册，基督徒报（卷二），默想启示录（中卷），（三）别迦摩（腐败的教会））", "en": "A.\tWe respect Luther, we respect John Wesley, Calvin, and thousands of other servants of God; yet we must know that the standard of our faith and walk is \"thus saith Jehovah\" rather than \"thus saith Luther, Wesley, or Calvin\"—Isa. 10:24; 50:1; Jer. 2:2; Ezek. 2:4.", "norm_zh": "一我们敬爱路德敬爱卫斯理敬爱喀尔文敬爱其余神千百的仆人但是我们应当知道我们信心和行为的标准乃是耶和华如此说并不是路德卫斯理喀尔文如此说赛十24五十1耶二2结二4倪柝声文集第一辑第四册基督徒报卷二默想启示录中卷三别迦摩腐败的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We respect Luther we respect John Wesley Calvin and thousands of other servants of God yet we must know that the standard of our faith and walk is thus saith Jehovah rather than thus saith Luther Wesley or CalvinIsa 1024 501 Jer 22 Ezek 24"}
{"zh": "二\t我们常欲听从人世的学说，和遗传的教训；但是神的目的，乃是要破除这些，好叫我们重新来到祂话语的面前，听祂圣经的教训；这样，我们所信的，就不是人的智慧，乃是神的大能—赛四十31，林后十二9。（倪柝声文集第一辑第五册，基督徒报（卷三），默想启示录（中卷），（四）推雅推喇（罗马的教会））", "en": "B.\tMany times we are inclined to listen to man's philosophy and traditional teachings, but God's intention is to break us away from these things so that we may come afresh before His word and hear the teaching of the Bible; in this way, what we believe in will not be of man's wisdom but will be of the power of God.—Isa. 40:31; 2 Cor. 12:9.", "norm_zh": "二我们常欲听从人世的学说和遗传的教训但是神的目的乃是要破除这些好叫我们重新来到祂话语的面前听祂圣经的教训这样我们所信的就不是人的智慧乃是神的大能赛四十31林后十二9倪柝声文集第一辑第五册基督徒报卷三默想启示录中卷四推雅推喇罗马的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Many times we are inclined to listen to mans philosophy and traditional teachings but Gods intention is to break us away from these things so that we may come afresh before His word and hear the teaching of the Bible in this way what we believe in will not be of mans wisdom but will be of the power of GodIsa 4031 2 Cor 129"}
{"zh": "三\t神的儿子亲自对我们说，人的遗传是不必遵守的；祂对于专心遵守古人遗传的人说，“这百姓用嘴唇尊敬我，心却远离我；他们将人的吩咐，当作道理教导人，所以拜我也是枉然”（太十五8~9）；因为我们若要遵守人的遗传，我们就要干犯神的诫命（3节）。（倪柝声文集第一辑第四册，基督徒报（卷二），默想启示录（中卷），（三）别迦摩（腐败的教会））", "en": "C.\tThe Son of God told us Himself that we need not keep man's tradition; He said of those who were keen to abide by the tradition of their ancestors that \"this people honors Me with their lips, but their heart stays far away from Me; but in vain do they worship Me, teaching as teachings the commandments of men\" (Matt. 15:8-9); if we want to abide by man's tradition, we are transgressing the commandment of God (v. 3).", "norm_zh": "三神的儿子亲自对我们说人的遗传是不必遵守的祂对于专心遵守古人遗传的人说这百姓用嘴唇尊敬我心却远离我他们将人的吩咐当作道理教导人所以拜我也是枉然太十五89因为我们若要遵守人的遗传我们就要干犯神的诫命3节倪柝声文集第一辑第四册基督徒报卷二默想启示录中卷三别迦摩腐败的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:10:28.604366+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Son of God told us Himself that we need not keep mans tradition He said of those who were keen to abide by the tradition of their ancestors that this people honors Me with their lips but their heart stays far away from Me but in vain do they worship Me teaching as teachings the commandments of men Matt 1589 if we want to abide by mans tradition we are transgressing the commandment of God v 3"}
{"zh": "读经：西二9，约一14，创十二2，弗一3，申八7、10，王上十四15，赛五17，启二一1", "en": "Scripture Reading: Col. 2:9; John 1:14; Gen. 12:2; Eph. 1:3; Deut. 8:7, 10; 1 Kings 14:15; Isa. 5:17; Rev. 21:1", "norm_zh": "读经西二9约一14创十二2弗一3申八710王上十四15赛五17启二一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Col 29 John 114 Gen 122 Eph 13 Deut 87 10 1 Kings 1415 Isa 517 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "壹\t旧约乃是神永远经纶一幅表征的图画；旧约中所陈明这幅神永远经纶表征的图画，包括了三十九卷书，但只有四部分：预表、历史、诗歌和申言—来九1、18，弗三9，西二17：", "en": "I. The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of God's eternal economy; the figurative portrait of God's eternal economy presented in the Old Testament spans thirty-nine books, but it is only in four sections—in types, in history, in poetry, and in prophecy.—Heb. 9:1, 18; Eph. 3:9; Col. 2:17:", "norm_zh": "壹旧约乃是神永远经纶一幅表征的图画旧约中所陈明这幅神永远经纶表征的图画包括了三十九卷书但只有四部分预表历史诗歌和申言来九118弗三9西二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy the figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy presented in the Old Testament spans thirtynine books but it is only in four sectionsin types in history in poetry and in prophecyHeb 91 18 Eph 39 Col 217"}
{"zh": "一\t预表的部分有五卷书，从创世记到申命记；历史的部分有十二卷书，从约书亚记到以斯帖记；诗歌的部分有五卷书，从约伯记到雅歌；申言的部分有十七卷书，从以赛亚书到玛拉基书；其中有五卷大申言者书，和十二卷小申言者书。", "en": "A. The section of types is of five books, from Genesis to Deuteronomy; the section of history is of twelve books, from Joshua to Esther; the section of poetry is of five books, from Job to Song of Songs; the section of prophecy is of seventeen books, from Isaiah to Malachi; there are five major prophets and twelve minor ones.", "norm_zh": "一预表的部分有五卷书从创世记到申命记历史的部分有十二卷书从约书亚记到以斯帖记诗歌的部分有五卷书从约伯记到雅歌申言的部分有十七卷书从以赛亚书到玛拉基书其中有五卷大申言者书和十二卷小申言者书", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The section of types is of five books from Genesis to Deuteronomy the section of history is of twelve books from Joshua to Esther the section of poetry is of five books from Job to Song of Songs the section of prophecy is of seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi there are five major prophets and twelve minor ones"}
{"zh": "二\t旧约三十九卷书可以分为三个“五”和两个“十二”；有五卷预表的书，十二卷历史的书，五卷诗歌的书，五卷大申言者的书，和十二卷小申言者的书；这十二位小申言者，是从何西阿到玛拉基。", "en": "B. The thirty-nine books of the Old Testament can be divided into three \"fives\" and two \"twelves\"; there are five books of types, twelve of history, five of poetry, five of the major prophets, and twelve of the minor prophets; the twelve minor prophets are from Hosea to Malachi.", "norm_zh": "二旧约三十九卷书可以分为三个五和两个十二有五卷预表的书十二卷历史的书五卷诗歌的书五卷大申言者的书和十二卷小申言者的书这十二位小申言者是从何西阿到玛拉基", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The thirtynine books of the Old Testament can be divided into three fives and two twelves there are five books of types twelve of history five of poetry five of the major prophets and twelve of the minor prophets the twelve minor prophets are from Hosea to Malachi"}
{"zh": "贰\t在预表里—创世记至申命记揭示三一神具体化身在基督里，作祂永远经纶的中心和圆周，也揭示这位基督作三一神选民的福分和一切—创十二2，约一14，弗一3，西二9：", "en": "IV. In types—Genesis to Deuteronomy unveil the Triune God embodied in Christ as the center and circumference of His eternal economy and also unveil this Christ as the blessing and everything to the Triune God's chosen people—Gen. 12:2; John 1:14; Eph. 1:3; Col. 2:9:", "norm_zh": "贰在预表里创世记至申命记揭示三一神具体化身在基督里作祂永远经纶的中心和圆周也揭示这位基督作三一神选民的福分和一切创十二2约一14弗一3西二9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In typesGenesis to Deuteronomy unveil the Triune God embodied in Christ as the center and circumference of His eternal economy and also unveil this Christ as the blessing and everything to the Triune Gods chosen peopleGen 122 John 114 Eph 13 Col 29"}
{"zh": "一\t在创世记我们看见神的创造与人的堕落；它陈明基督是堕落之人的盼望与拯救；借着基督神要使堕落的人完成祂的定旨—一26，三6~7、15，四4。", "en": "A. In Genesis we see God's creation and man's fall; it presents Christ as the hope and salvation of fallen man; through Christ God will enable fallen man to accomplish His purpose—1:26; 3:6-7, 15; 4:4.", "norm_zh": "一在创世记我们看见神的创造与人的堕落它陈明基督是堕落之人的盼望与拯救借着基督神要使堕落的人完成祂的定旨一26三6715四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In Genesis we see Gods creation and mans fall it presents Christ as the hope and salvation of fallen man through Christ God will enable fallen man to accomplish His purpose126 367 15 44"}
{"zh": "二\t在出埃及记，人堕落以后，神进来用祂奇妙的救赎拯救我们；基督是神子民的救赎、拯救和供应，又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法，这是我们在出埃及记所看见的—十二3~14。", "en": "B. In Exodus, after man's fall, God came in to save us with His marvelous redemption; Christ is the redemption, salvation, and supply of God's people and the means for them to worship and serve God—this is what we see in Exodus—12:3-14.", "norm_zh": "二在出埃及记人堕落以后神进来用祂奇妙的救赎拯救我们基督是神子民的救赎拯救和供应又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法这是我们在出埃及记所看见的十二314", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In Exodus after mans fall God came in to save us with His marvelous redemption Christ is the redemption salvation and supply of Gods people and the means for them to worship and serve Godthis is what we see in Exodus12314"}
{"zh": "三\t在利未记，有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活；基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通、事奉和生活上的一切—一5~8，二2，三2，四5、10，五8，来五5~6，九14、26，十10。", "en": "C. In Leviticus there is the worship and living of the redeemed; Christ is everything to God's redeemed people in their fellowship, service, and living—1:5-8; 2:2; 3:2; 4:5, 10; 5:8; Heb. 5:5-6; 9:14, 26; 10:10.", "norm_zh": "三在利未记有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通事奉和生活上的一切一58二2三2四510五8来五56九1426十10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In Leviticus there is the worship and living of the redeemed Christ is everything to Gods redeemed people in their fellowship service and living158 22 32 45 10 58 Heb 556 914 26 1010"}
{"zh": "四\t民数记启示，这位作我们生活意义、见证、与中心的基督，乃是一直在行动、活动、并往前的；在祂往前时，祂是我们的领导、我们的道路、我们的目标—二2，约十四6。", "en": "D. The book of Numbers reveals that this Christ, who is the meaning of our life, our testimony, and our center, is One who is moving, acting, and always proceeding onward; in His proceeding onward, He is our Leader, our way, and our goal—2:2; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "四民数记启示这位作我们生活意义见证与中心的基督乃是一直在行动活动并往前的在祂往前时祂是我们的领导我们的道路我们的目标二2约十四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The book of Numbers reveals that this Christ who is the meaning of our life our testimony and our center is One who is moving acting and always proceeding onward in His proceeding onward He is our Leader our way and our goal22 John 146"}
{"zh": "五\t申命记启示基督是神子民的指导者和领导者，使他们能进入属天的领域，并有分于祂的丰富—八7、10。", "en": "E. Deuteronomy reveals that Christ is the Instructor and Leader of the people of God that they may be able to enter into the heavenly territory and participate in His riches—8:7, 10.", "norm_zh": "五申命记启示基督是神子民的指导者和领导者使他们能进入属天的领域并有分于祂的丰富八710", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Deuteronomy reveals that Christ is the Instructor and Leader of the people of God that they may be able to enter into the heavenly territory and participate in His riches87 10"}
{"zh": "叁\t在历史里—约书亚记至以斯帖记揭示三一神在祂选民中的行动，使他们取得、承受、并享受祂所应许包罗万有的基督作美地；也揭示祂选民的失败，作为对祂新约选民的警戒—约一1~9，王上十四15：", "en": "III. In history—Joshua to Esther unveil the Triune God's move in His chosen people to possess, inherit, and enjoy His promised all-inclusive Christ as the good land; they also unveil the failures of God's chosen people as a warning to His New Testament chosen people—Josh. 1:1-9; 1 Kings 14:15:", "norm_zh": "叁在历史里约书亚记至以斯帖记揭示三一神在祂选民中的行动使他们取得承受并享受祂所应许包罗万有的基督作美地也揭示祂选民的失败作为对祂新约选民的警戒约一19王上十四15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III In historyJoshua to Esther unveil the Triune Gods move in His chosen people to possess inherit and enjoy His promised allinclusive Christ as the good land they also unveil the failures of Gods chosen people as a warning to His New Testament chosen peopleJosh 119 1 Kings 1415"}
{"zh": "一\t神借着摩西把以色列民，就是亚伯拉罕的后裔，从埃及领出来，经过旷野，到达美地的边界；约书亚记给我们看见，如何取得、占有、并守住美地—六1~16。", "en": "A. God through Moses led the people of Israel, the descendants of Abraham, out of Egypt, through the wilderness, to the border of the good land; the book of Joshua shows us how to gain, to take possession of, and to keep the good land—6:1-16.", "norm_zh": "一神借着摩西把以色列民就是亚伯拉罕的后裔从埃及领出来经过旷野到达美地的边界约书亚记给我们看见如何取得占有并守住美地六116", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God through Moses led the people of Israel the descendants of Abraham out of Egypt through the wilderness to the border of the good land the book of Joshua shows us how to gain to take possession of and to keep the good land6116"}
{"zh": "二\t在士师记里所记载的几位士师，路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯，撒母耳记上、下所记载的以利、撒母耳、扫罗、约拿单、大卫，呈现一幅幅生动的图画，给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地—士一3~11、22，得四13。", "en": "B. The record of quite a few judges in the book of Judges, of Ruth and Boaz in the book of Ruth, and of Eli, Samuel, Saul, Jonathan, and David in the books of 1 and 2 Samuel presents us vivid pictures of how those persons remained in and enjoyed the good land—Judg. 1:3-11, 22; Ruth 4:13.", "norm_zh": "二在士师记里所记载的几位士师路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯撒母耳记上下所记载的以利撒母耳扫罗约拿单大卫呈现一幅幅生动的图画给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上并如何享受美地士一31122得四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The record of quite a few judges in the book of Judges of Ruth and Boaz in the book of Ruth and of Eli Samuel Saul Jonathan and David in the books of 1 and 2 Samuel presents us vivid pictures of how those persons remained in and enjoyed the good landJudg 1311 22 Ruth 413"}
{"zh": "三\t虽然那些图画刻画得很详细，但仍然需要列王纪上、下提供更多人物的图画，给我们看见他们如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地—王上三5~15，王下十八1~8。", "en": "C. Even though those pictures were painted in detail, there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to give us pictures of more persons showing us how they remained in and enjoyed the good land—1 King. 3:5-15; 2 King. 18:1-8.", "norm_zh": "三虽然哪些图画刻画得很详细但仍然需要列王纪上下提供更多人物的图画给我们看见他们如何留在美地上并如何享受美地王上三515王下十八18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Even though those pictures were painted in detail there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to give us pictures of more persons showing us how they remained in and enjoyed the good land1 King 3515 2 King 1818"}
{"zh": "四\t以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关；尼希米记与修复、重建城有关；以斯帖记给我们看见，无所不在、无所不能的神，如何成了隐藏的神，保护在被掳中祂分散的选民—拉七6~10，尼一1~11，二4，四4~5、9，斯一1~2，四14。", "en": "D. The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple, and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair, the rebuilding, of the city. The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect, who were scattered in their captivity—Ezra 7:6-10; Neh. 1:1-11; 2:4; 4:4-5, 9; Esth. 1:1-2; 4:14.", "norm_zh": "四以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关尼希米记与修复重建城有关以斯帖记给我们看见无所不在无所不能的神如何成了隐藏的神保护在被掳中祂分散的选民拉七610尼一111二4四459斯一12四14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair the rebuilding of the city The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect who were scattered in their captivityEzra 7610 Neh 1111 24 445 9 Esth 112 414"}
{"zh": "肆\t在诗歌里—约伯记至雅歌这五卷诗歌揭示，三一神自己（不是伦理或道德）应当是人所追求的，作人的完全—伯四二1~6，歌一12~14，传一2、14：", "en": "IV. In the poetry—the five books of poetry from Job to Song of Songs unveil that the Triune God Himself, not ethics or morality, should be man's pursuit as his perfection—Job 42:1-6; S.S. 1:12-14; Eccl. 1:2, 14:", "norm_zh": "肆在诗歌里约伯记至雅歌这五卷诗歌揭示三一神自己不是伦理或道德应当是人所追求的作人的完全伯四二16歌一1214传一214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In the poetrythe five books of poetry from Job to Song of Songs unveil that the Triune God Himself not ethics or morality should be mans pursuit as his perfectionJob 4216 SS 11214 Eccl 12 14"}
{"zh": "一\t三一神自己（不是伦理或道德）应当是人所追求的，作人的完全；这一句话总括了约伯记中心、内在的启示—四二1~6。", "en": "A. The Triune God Himself, not ethics or morality, should be man's pursuit as his perfection; this one sentence covers the central, intrinsic revelation of Job—42:1-6.", "norm_zh": "一三一神自己不是伦理或道德应当是人所追求的作人的完全这一句话总括了约伯记中心内在的启示四二16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Triune God Himself not ethics or morality should be mans pursuit as his perfection this one sentence covers the central intrinsic revelation of Job4216"}
{"zh": "二\t诗篇揭示，这位神化身成为一个在肉体里的人，作神的受膏者；祂是神所喜悦的，并且被神高举；祂该被神的选民接受、宝爱并高举—二7，八四9。", "en": "B. The Psalms unveil that this God was incarnated to be a man in the flesh to be His Anointed, who is His delight, who has been exalted by Him, and who should be received, treasured, and exalted by His chosen people—2:7; 84:9.", "norm_zh": "二诗篇揭示这位神化身成为一个在肉体里的人作神的受膏者祂是神所喜悦的并且被神高举祂该被神的选民接受宝爱并高举二7八四9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Psalms unveil that this God was incarnated to be a man in the flesh to be His Anointed who is His delight who has been exalted by Him and who should be received treasured and exalted by His chosen people27 849"}
{"zh": "三\t传道书揭示，在日光之下，人生的一切都是虚空的虚空—一2、14。", "en": "C. Ecclesiastes unveils that all things in the human life under the sun are vanity of vanities—1:2, 14.", "norm_zh": "三传道书揭示在日光之下人生的一切都是虚空的虚空一214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Ecclesiastes unveils that all things in the human life under the sun are vanity of vanities12 14"}
{"zh": "四\t雅歌给我们看见，基督作三一神的具体化身，乃是神选民惟一的满足；因此，我们应当追求神作我们的完全，也应当追求基督作我们的满足—一12~14，四12~14，五1。", "en": "D. Song of Songs shows that Christ as the embodiment of the Triune God is the unique satisfaction to God's chosen people; thus, we should pursue God as our perfection, and we should pursue after Christ as our satisfaction—1:12-14; 4:12-14; 5:1.", "norm_zh": "四雅歌给我们看见基督作三一神的具体化身乃是神选民惟一的满足因此我们应当追求神作我们的完全也应当追求基督作我们的满足一1214四1214五1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Song of Songs shows that Christ as the embodiment of the Triune God is the unique satisfaction to Gods chosen people thus we should pursue God as our perfection and we should pursue after Christ as our satisfaction11214 41214 51"}
{"zh": "伍\t在申言者的申言里—以赛亚书至玛拉基书揭示三一神具体化身在基督里，要来作神人，以完成救赎，好成就神永远的经纶；这要终极完成于新天新地—赛七14，九6，五三，六五17，六六22，彼后三13，启二一1：", "en": "V. In the prophets' prophesying—the books of prophecy from Isaiah to Malachi unveil that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the God-man to accomplish redemption for the fulfillment of God's eternal economy; this will consummate in the new heaven and new earth—Isa. 7:14; 9:6; 53; 65:17; 66:22; 2 Pet. 3:13; Rev. 21:1:", "norm_zh": "伍在申言者的申言里以赛亚书至玛拉基书揭示三一神具体化身在基督里要来作神人以完成救赎好成就神永远的经纶这要终极完成于新天新地赛七14九6五三六五17六六22彼后三13启二一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V In the prophets prophesyingthe books of prophecy from Isaiah to Malachi unveil that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the Godman to accomplish redemption for the fulfillment of Gods eternal economy this will consummate in the new heaven and new earthIsa 714 96 53 6517 6622 2 Pet 313 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "一\t众申言者（从以赛亚到玛拉基）所释放的启示，着重强调的乃是：神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结，就像亚当与夏娃的联结一样；至终，二者在性情上和生命上成为一—创一26，结四三4~7。", "en": "A. The crucial emphasis of the revelation released by all the prophets from Isaiah to Malachi is that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people, like the union of Adam with Eve; eventually, the two became one in nature and in life.—Gen. 1:26; Ezek. 43:4-7.", "norm_zh": "一众申言者从以赛亚到玛拉基所释放的启示着重强调的乃是神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结就像亚当与夏娃的联结一样至终二者在性情上和生命上成为一创一26结四三47", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The crucial emphasis of the revelation released by all the prophets from Isaiah to Malachi is that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people like the union of Adam with Eve eventually the two became one in nature and in lifeGen 126 Ezek 4347"}
{"zh": "二\t小申言者书的中心思想包含许多事情，从神的审判开始；神要审判世界；罪人当预备迎见神；基督这永远的神圣者，来到地上，出生为人；祂进入死，并从死里复活，使神的救恩延伸到万国—珥三2上，摩四12，弥五2，拿一17，二10，三2。", "en": "B. The central thought of the Minor Prophets involves many things, beginning with God's judgment; God will judge the world; sinners should prepare to meet God; Christ as the eternally divine One came to the earth and was born to be human; He entered into death and resurrected from it for the extending of God's salvation to all the nations—Joel 3:2a; Amos 4:12; Micah 5:2; Jonah 1:17; 2:10; 3:2.", "norm_zh": "二小申言者书的中心思想包含许多事情从神的审判开始神要审判世界罪人当预备迎见神基督这永远的神圣者来到地上出生为人祂进入死并从死里复活使神的救恩延伸到万国珥三2上摩四12弥五2拿一17二10三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The central thought of the Minor Prophets involves many things beginning with Gods judgment God will judge the world sinners should prepare to meet God Christ as the eternally divine One came to the earth and was born to be human He entered into death and resurrected from it for the extending of Gods salvation to all the nationsJoel 32a Amos 412 Micah 52 Jonah 117 210 32"}
{"zh": "三\t悔改并相信祂的罪人，必蒙神赦免其罪，并蒙神称义，得着神圣的生命，使他们得以在神圣的光中行走，成为基督的大能者，在基督第二次显现时，与基督一同受神差遣—摩四12，弥七18~19，哈二4，弥七8~9，珥三11下。", "en": "C. Sinners who repent and believe in Him will be forgiven of their sins and justified by God to have the divine life that they may walk in the divine light and become the mighty ones of Christ, sent with Him by God in His second appearing—Amos 4:12; Micah 7:18-19; Hab. 2:4; Micah 7:8-9; Joel 3:11b.", "norm_zh": "三悔改并相信祂的罪人必蒙神赦免其罪并蒙神称义得着神圣的生命使他们得以在神圣的光中行走成为基督的大能者在基督第二次显现时与基督一同受神差遣摩四12弥七1819哈二4弥七89珥三11下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Sinners who repent and believe in Him will be forgiven of their sins and justified by God to have the divine life that they may walk in the divine light and become the mighty ones of Christ sent with Him by God in His second appearingAmos 412 Micah 71819 Hab 24 Micah 789 Joel 311b"}
{"zh": "四\t祂要如公义的日头升起，又要作立约的使者而来，在锡安作王，并牧养以色列；然后复兴的千年国要被带进来—玛四2，三1，弥四7下，何十四4~8，启二十4、6，太十九28。", "en": "D. He will arise as the Sun of righteousness and come as the Angel of the covenant to reign in Zion and shepherd Israel; then the millennium of the restoration will be brought in—Mal. 4:2; 3:1; Micah 4:7b; Hosea 14:4-8; Rev. 20:4, 6; Matt. 19:28.", "norm_zh": "四祂要如公义的日头升起又要作立约的使者而来在锡安作王并牧养以色列然后复兴的千年国要被带进来玛四2三1弥四7下何十四48启二十46太十九28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D He will arise as the Sun of righteousness and come as the Angel of the covenant to reign in Zion and shepherd Israel then the millennium of the restoration will be brought inMal 42 31 Micah 47b Hosea 1448 Rev 204 6 Matt 1928"}
{"zh": "五\t以赛亚书预言到新天新地，使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及，如新耶路撒冷所说明的—六五17，六六22，启二一1。", "en": "E. Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth as illustrated by the New Jerusalem.—Isa. 65:17; 66:22; Rev. 21:1.", "norm_zh": "五以赛亚书预言到新天新地使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及如新耶路撒冷所说明的六五17六六22启二一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth as illustrated by the New JerusalemIsa 6517 6622 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "陆\t以上各点向我们陈明一幅生动的图画，说到旧约中那在神永远经纶里，并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督；启示出基督是神经纶的中心与普及—但二35，弗一10，西一18，三10~11。", "en": "VI. All the above points present us a vivid portrait of the all-inclusive Christ in and for God's eternal economy in the Old Testament, revealing Christ as the centrality and universality of God's economy—Dan. 2:35; Eph. 1:10; Col. 1:18; 3:10-11.", "norm_zh": "陆以上各点向我们陈明一幅生动的图画说到旧约中哪在神永远经纶里并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督启示出基督是神经纶的中心与普及但二35弗一10西一18三1011", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI All the above points present us a vivid portrait of the allinclusive Christ in and for Gods eternal economy in the Old Testament revealing Christ as the centrality and universality of Gods economyDan 235 Eph 110 Col 118 31011"}
{"zh": "创世记的中心思想乃是：基督是堕拯救，神要借基督使堕落的人成就祂的定旨。", "en": "The central thought of Genesis is that Christ is the salvation of the fallen, and God wants to make fallen man fulfill His purpose through Christ.", "norm_zh": "创世记的中心思想乃是基督是堕拯救神要借基督使堕落的人成就祂的定旨", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The central thought of Genesis is that Christ is the salvation of the fallen and God wants to make fallen man fulfill His purpose through Christ"}
{"zh": "基督是神子民的救赎、拯救和供应，又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法，使他们在祂里面与神建造在一起，叫他们与神相见，彼此交通，而且互为居所。出埃及记从始至终，都给我们看见基督。祂是逾越节，是我们蒙救赎的方法。祂是神子民的大救恩，拯救我们脱离法老─撒但的手。祂是吗哪和活水，是我们生命的供应。再者，红海表征我们受浸归入基督的死（林前十2）。罗马书六章三节说，受浸归入基督的人，是受浸归入祂的死。", "en": "Christ is the redemption, salvation, and supply of God’s people and the means for them to worship and serve God so that in Him they may be built up with God together for them and God to meet, communicate, and dwell mutually. We see Christ throughout the book of Exodus. As the Passover, He is the means of our redemption. As the great salvation for God’s people, He saves us out of the hand of Pharaoh, Satan. As the manna and the living water, He is our life supply. Furthermore, the Red Sea signifies Christ’s death in which we are baptized (1Cor.10:2). Romans 6:3 says that those who are baptized into Christ are baptized into His death.", "norm_zh": "基督是神子民的救赎拯救和供应又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法使他们在祂里面与神建造在一起叫他们与神相见彼此交通而且互为居所出埃及记从始至终都给我们看见基督祂是逾越节是我们蒙救赎的方法祂是神子民的大救恩拯救我们脱离法老撒但的手祂是吗哪和活水是我们生命的供应再者红海表征我们受浸归入基督的死林前十2罗马书六章三节说受浸归入基督的人是受浸归入祂的死", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Christ is the redemption salvation and supply of Gods people and the means for them to worship and serve God so that in Him they may be built up with God together for them and God to meet communicate and dwell mutually We see Christ throughout the book of Exodus As the Passover He is the means of our redemption As the great salvation for Gods people He saves us out of the hand of Pharaoh Satan As the manna and the living water He is our life supply Furthermore the Red Sea signifies Christs death in which we are baptized 1Cor102 Romans 63 says that those who are baptized into Christ are baptized into His death"}
{"zh": "基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通、事奉和生活上的一切。司可福博士（Dr. C. I. Scofield）曾指出，利未记的每一页都可看到基督。在利未记，基督是一切。祂是供物，祂是大祭司，祂是蒙神救赎之人生活上的一切。所以，利未记是一卷论到基督且满了基督的书。（利未记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "Christ is everything in the fellowship, service, and life of God’s redeemed. Dr. C. I. Scofield once pointed out that Christ can be seen in every page of this book. In Leviticus Christ is everything. He is the offerings, He is the high priest, and He is everything in the living of God’s redeemed people. Leviticus, therefore, is a book on Christ and full of Christ.", "norm_zh": "基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通事奉和生活上的一切司可福博士DrCIScofield曾指出利未记的每一页都可看到基督在利未记基督是一切祂是供物祂是大祭司祂是蒙神救赎之人生活上的一切所以利未记是一卷论到基督且满了基督的书利未记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Christ is everything in the fellowship service and life of Gods redeemed Dr C I Scofield once pointed out that Christ can be seen in every page of this book In Leviticus Christ is everything He is the offerings He is the high priest and He is everything in the living of Gods redeemed people Leviticus therefore is a book on Christ and full of Christ"}
{"zh": "在摩西之后，神使用约书亚，把祂的选民带进所应许的美地", "en": "After Moses, God used Joshua to bring His chosen people into the promised good land", "norm_zh": "在摩西之后神使用约书亚把祂的选民带进所应许的美地", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "After Moses God used Joshua to bring His chosen people into the promised good land"}
{"zh": "照着从约书亚记到以斯帖记所记载的历史，其内在的启示乃是向我们揭示，神永远的经纶如何在地上由祂的选民所施行。神永远的经纶完全是关于基督的，也是为着基督的，主要是在于基督的身位和国度。关于基督身位的一面，旧约历史的记载，保持了基督家谱的世系，为着祂借成为肉体来成为人；关于基督国度的一面，旧约历史保持了神的国这一条线，为着基督在地上建立祂神圣的国度。这两个项目形成以色列历史书中神圣启示管治的线。", "en": "The intrinsic revelation of the history according to the record from Joshua to Esther is to unveil to us how the eternal economy of God was carried out by His elect on the earth. The eternal economy of God is altogether concerning Christ and for Christ, mainly in the person of Christ and the kingdom of Christ. Regarding the person of Christ, the record of history in the Old Testament keeps a lineage of the genealogy of Christ for His coming through His incarnation to be a man. Regarding the kingdom of Christ, the Old Testament history keeps a line on the kingdom of God for Christ to establish His divine kingdom on the earth. These two items form the governing line of the divine revelation in the books of the history of Israel.", "norm_zh": "照着从约书亚记到以斯帖记所记载的历史其内在的启示乃是向我们揭示神永远的经纶如何在地上由祂的选民所施行神永远的经纶完全是关于基督的也是为着基督的主要是在于基督的身位和国度关于基督身位的一面旧约历史的记载保持了基督家谱的世系为着祂借成为肉体来成为人关于基督国度的一面旧约历史保持了神的国这一条线为着基督在地上建立祂神圣的国度这两个项目形成以色列历史书中神圣启示管治的线", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The intrinsic revelation of the history according to the record from Joshua to Esther is to unveil to us how the eternal economy of God was carried out by His elect on the earth The eternal economy of God is altogether concerning Christ and for Christ mainly in the person of Christ and the kingdom of Christ Regarding the person of Christ the record of history in the Old Testament keeps a lineage of the genealogy of Christ for His coming through His incarnation to be a man Regarding the kingdom of Christ the Old Testament history keeps a line on the kingdom of God for Christ to establish His divine kingdom on the earth These two items form the governing line of the divine revelation in the books of the history of Israel"}
{"zh": "关于以色列人的历史书，给我们看见，如何经历基督是神所赐给我们的美地，作我们的分", "en": "The books of history concerning the children of Israel show us how to experience Christ as the good land given to us by God to be our portion.", "norm_zh": "关于以色列人的历史书给我们看见如何经历基督是神所赐给我们的美地作我们的分", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The books of history concerning the children of Israel show us how to experience Christ as the good land given to us by God to be our portion"}
{"zh": "神的同在是隐藏的，祂以最智慧的方式运用祂的主宰保守祂的选民", "en": "God's presence is hidden, and He, in the wisest manner, exercises His sovereignty to preserve His elect.", "norm_zh": "神的同在是隐藏的祂以最智慧的方式运用祂的主宰保守祂的选民", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods presence is hidden and He in the wisest manner exercises His sovereignty to preserve His elect"}
{"zh": "以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关；尼希米记与修复、重建城有关；以斯帖记给我们看见，无所不在、无所不能的神，如何成了隐藏的神，保护在被掳中祂分散的选民。", "en": "The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple, and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair, the rebuilding, of the city. The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect, who were scattered in their captivity.", "norm_zh": "以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关尼希米记与修复重建城有关以斯帖记给我们看见无所不在无所不能的神如何成了隐藏的神保护在被掳中祂分散的选民", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair the rebuilding of the city The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect who were scattered in their captivity"}
{"zh": "从以赛亚书至玛拉基，揭示三一神具体化身在基督里，要来作神人（赛七14，九6），以完成救赎（五三），好按照旧约前面三类的各卷书，成就神永远的经纶；也揭示经过过程并终极完成之三一神在基督里的成就，要终极完成于新天新地（赛六五17，六六22，彼后三13，启二一1）。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "From Isaiah to Malachi unveils that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the God-man (Isa. 7:14; 9:6) to accomplish redemption (ch. 53) for the fulfillment of God's eternal economy according to the preceding three categories of the books in the Old Testament; it also unveils that the accomplishment of the processed and consummated Triune God in Christ will consummate in the new heaven and new earth (Isa. 65:17; 66:22; 2 Pet. 3:13; Rev. 21:1).", "norm_zh": "从以赛亚书至玛拉基揭示三一神具体化身在基督里要来作神人赛七14九6以完成救赎五三好按照旧约前面三类的各卷书成就神永远的经纶也揭示经过过程并终极完成之三一神在基督里的成就要终极完成于新天新地赛六五17六六22彼后三13启二一1李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "From Isaiah to Malachi unveils that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the Godman Isa 714 96 to accomplish redemption ch 53 for the fulfillment of Gods eternal economy according to the preceding three categories of the books in the Old Testament it also unveils that the accomplishment of the processed and consummated Triune God in Christ will consummate in the new heaven and new earth Isa 6517 6622 2 Pet 313 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "众申言者（从以赛亚到玛拉基）所释放的启示，着重强调的乃是：神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结，在性情上和生命上成为一", "en": "The revelation released by the prophets (from Isaiah to Malachi) stresses that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people, to be one with them in nature and in life.", "norm_zh": "众申言者从以赛亚到玛拉基所释放的启示着重强调的乃是神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结在性情上和生命上成为一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The revelation released by the prophets from Isaiah to Malachi stresses that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people to be one with them in nature and in life"}
{"zh": "小申言者书的中心思想", "en": "The central thought of the Minor Prophets", "norm_zh": "小申言者书的中心思想", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The central thought of the Minor Prophets"}
{"zh": "以赛亚书预言到新天新地，使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及", "en": "Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth", "norm_zh": "以赛亚书预言到新天新地使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth"}
{"zh": "一幅生动的图画—旧约中那在神永远经纶里，并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督", "en": "A vivid portrait—the all-inclusive Christ in and for God's eternal economy in the Old Testament", "norm_zh": "一幅生动的图画旧约中哪在神永远经纶里并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:13:02.763319+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A vivid portraitthe allinclusive Christ in and for Gods eternal economy in the Old Testament"}
{"zh": "壹\t旧约乃是神永远经纶一幅表征的图画；旧约中所陈明这幅神永远经纶表征的图画，包括了三十九卷书，但只有四部分：预表、历史、诗歌和申言—来九1、18，弗三9，西二17：（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "I. The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of God's eternal economy; the figurative portrait of God's eternal economy presented in the Old Testament spans thirty-nine books, but it is only in four sections—in types, in history, in poetry, and in prophecy—Heb. 9:1, 18; Eph. 3:9; Col. 2:17:", "norm_zh": "壹旧约乃是神永远经纶一幅表征的图画旧约中所陈明这幅神永远经纶表征的图画包括了三十九卷书但只有四部分预表历史诗歌和申言来九118弗三9西二17李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy the figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy presented in the Old Testament spans thirtynine books but it is only in four sectionsin types in history in poetry and in prophecyHeb 91 18 Eph 39 Col 217"}
{"zh": "一\t预表的部分有五卷书，从创世记到申命记；历史的部分有十二卷书，从约书亚记到以斯帖记；诗歌的部分有五卷书，从约伯记到雅歌；申言的部分有十七卷书，从以赛亚书到玛拉基书；其中有五卷大申言者书，和十二卷小申言者书。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "A. The section of types is of five books, from Genesis to Deuteronomy; the section of history is of twelve books, from Joshua to Esther; the section of poetry is of five books, from Job to Song of Songs; the section of prophecy is of seventeen books, from Isaiah to Malachi; there are five major prophets and twelve minor ones", "norm_zh": "一预表的部分有五卷书从创世记到申命记历史的部分有十二卷书从约书亚记到以斯帖记诗歌的部分有五卷书从约伯记到雅歌申言的部分有十七卷书从以赛亚书到玛拉基书其中有五卷大申言者书和十二卷小申言者书李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The section of types is of five books from Genesis to Deuteronomy the section of history is of twelve books from Joshua to Esther the section of poetry is of five books from Job to Song of Songs the section of prophecy is of seventeen books from Isaiah to Malachi there are five major prophets and twelve minor ones"}
{"zh": "二\t旧约三十九卷书可以分为三个“五”和两个“十二”；有五卷预表的书，十二卷历史的书，五卷诗歌的书，五卷大申言者的书，和十二卷小申言者的书；这十二位小申言者，是从何西阿到玛拉基。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "B. The thirty-nine books of the Old Testament can be divided into three \"fives\" and two \"twelves\"; there are five books of types, twelve of history, five of poetry, five of the major prophets, and twelve of the minor prophets; the twelve minor prophets are from Hosea to Malachi", "norm_zh": "二旧约三十九卷书可以分为三个五和两个十二有五卷预表的书十二卷历史的书五卷诗歌的书五卷大申言者的书和十二卷小申言者的书这十二位小申言者是从何西阿到玛拉基李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The thirtynine books of the Old Testament can be divided into three fives and two twelves there are five books of types twelve of history five of poetry five of the major prophets and twelve of the minor prophets the twelve minor prophets are from Hosea to Malachi"}
{"zh": "贰\t在预表里—创世记至申命记揭示三一神具体化身在基督里，作祂永远经纶的中心和圆周，也揭示这位基督作三一神选民的福分和一切—创十二2，约一14，弗一3，西二9：（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "IV. In the types—Genesis to Deuteronomy unveil the Triune God embodied in Christ as the center and circumference of His eternal economy and also unveil this Christ as the blessing and everything to the Triune God's chosen people—Gen. 12:2; John 1:14; Eph. 1:3; Col. 2:9:", "norm_zh": "贰在预表里创世记至申命记揭示三一神具体化身在基督里作祂永远经纶的中心和圆周也揭示这位基督作三一神选民的福分和一切创十二2约一14弗一3西二9李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In the typesGenesis to Deuteronomy unveil the Triune God embodied in Christ as the center and circumference of His eternal economy and also unveil this Christ as the blessing and everything to the Triune Gods chosen peopleGen 122 John 114 Eph 13 Col 29"}
{"zh": "一\t在创世记我们看见神的创造与人的堕落；它陈明基督是堕落之人的盼望与拯救；借着基督神要使堕落的人完成祂的定旨—一26，三6~7、15，四4。（民数记生命读经，第一篇；创世记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "A. In Genesis we see God's creation and man's fall; it presents Christ as the hope and salvation of fallen man; through Christ God will enable fallen man to accomplish His purpose—1:26; 3:6-7, 15; 4:4.", "norm_zh": "一在创世记我们看见神的创造与人的堕落它陈明基督是堕落之人的盼望与拯救借着基督神要使堕落的人完成祂的定旨一26三6715四4民数记生命读经第一篇创世记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In Genesis we see Gods creation and mans fall it presents Christ as the hope and salvation of fallen man through Christ God will enable fallen man to accomplish His purpose126 367 15 44"}
{"zh": "二\t在出埃及记，人堕落以后，神进来用祂奇妙的救赎拯救我们；基督是神子民的救赎、拯救和供应，又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法，这是我们在出埃及记所看见的—十二3~14。（民数记生命读经，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "B. In Exodus, after man's fall, God came in to save us with His marvelous redemption; Christ is the redemption, salvation, and supply of God's people and the means for them to worship and serve God—this is what we see in Exodus—12:3-14.", "norm_zh": "二在出埃及记人堕落以后神进来用祂奇妙的救赎拯救我们基督是神子民的救赎拯救和供应又是他们敬拜和事奉神的方法这是我们在出埃及记所看见的十二314民数记生命读经第一篇出埃及记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In Exodus after mans fall God came in to save us with His marvelous redemption Christ is the redemption salvation and supply of Gods people and the means for them to worship and serve Godthis is what we see in Exodus12314"}
{"zh": "三\t在利未记，有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活；基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通、事奉和生活上的一切—一5~8，二2，三2，四5、10，五8，来五5~6，九14、26，十10。（民数记生命读经，第一篇；利未记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "C. In Leviticus there is the redeemed's worship and living; Christ is everything to God's redeemed in their fellowship, service, and living—1:5-8; 2:2; 3:2; 4:5, 10; 5:8; Heb. 5:5-6; 9:14, 26; 10:10.", "norm_zh": "三在利未记有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通事奉和生活上的一切一58二2三2四510五8来五56九1426十10民数记生命读经第一篇利未记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In Leviticus there is the redeemeds worship and living Christ is everything to Gods redeemed in their fellowship service and living158 22 32 45 10 58 Heb 556 914 26 1010"}
{"zh": "四\t民数记启示，这位作我们生活意义、见证、与中心的基督，乃是一直在行动、活动、并往前的；在祂往前时，祂是我们的领导、我们的道路、我们的目标—二2，约十四6。（民数记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "D. The book of Numbers reveals that this Christ, who is the meaning of our life, our testimony, and our center, is One who is moving, acting, and always proceeding onward; in His proceeding onward, He is our Leader, our way, and our goal—2:2; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "四民数记启示这位作我们生活意义见证与中心的基督乃是一直在行动活动并往前的在祂往前时祂是我们的领导我们的道路我们的目标二2约十四6民数记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The book of Numbers reveals that this Christ who is the meaning of our life our testimony and our center is One who is moving acting and always proceeding onward in His proceeding onward He is our Leader our way and our goal22 John 146"}
{"zh": "五\t申命记启示基督是神子民的指导者和领导者，使他们能进入属天的领域，并有分于祂的丰富—八7、10。（申命记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "E. Deuteronomy reveals that Christ is the Instructor and Leader of the people of God that they may be able to enter into the heavenly territory and participate in His riches—8:7, 10.", "norm_zh": "五申命记启示基督是神子民的指导者和领导者使他们能进入属天的领域并有分于祂的丰富八710申命记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Deuteronomy reveals that Christ is the Instructor and Leader of the people of God that they may be able to enter into the heavenly territory and participate in His riches87 10"}
{"zh": "叁\t在历史里—约书亚记至以斯帖记揭示三一神在祂选民中的行动，使他们取得、承受、并享受祂所应许包罗万有的基督作美地；也揭示祂选民的失败，作为对祂新约选民的警戒—约一1~9，王上十四15：（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "III. In history—Joshua to Esther unveil the Triune God's move in His chosen people to possess, inherit, and enjoy His promised all-inclusive Christ as the good land; they also unveil the failures of God's chosen people as a warning to His New Testament chosen people—Josh. 1:1-9; 1 Kings 14:15:", "norm_zh": "叁在历史里约书亚记至以斯帖记揭示三一神在祂选民中的行动使他们取得承受并享受祂所应许包罗万有的基督作美地也揭示祂选民的失败作为对祂新约选民的警戒约一19王上十四15李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III In historyJoshua to Esther unveil the Triune Gods move in His chosen people to possess inherit and enjoy His promised allinclusive Christ as the good land they also unveil the failures of Gods chosen people as a warning to His New Testament chosen peopleJosh 119 1 Kings 1415"}
{"zh": "一\t神借着摩西把以色列民，就是亚伯拉罕的后裔，从埃及领出来，经过旷野，到达美地的边界；约书亚记给我们看见，如何取得、占有、并守住美地—六1~16。（列王纪生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "A. God led the people of Israel, the descendants of Abraham, out of Egypt through Moses, through the wilderness, to the border of the good land; the book of Joshua shows us how to gain, to take possession of, and to keep the good land.—6:1-16.", "norm_zh": "一神借着摩西把以色列民就是亚伯拉罕的后裔从埃及领出来经过旷野到达美地的边界约书亚记给我们看见如何取得占有并守住美地六116列王纪生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God led the people of Israel the descendants of Abraham out of Egypt through Moses through the wilderness to the border of the good land the book of Joshua shows us how to gain to take possession of and to keep the good land6116"}
{"zh": "二\t在士师记里所记载的几位士师，路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯，撒母耳记上、下所记载的以利、撒母耳、扫罗、约拿单、大卫，呈现一幅幅生动的图画，给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地—士一3~11、22，得四13。（列王纪生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "B. The record of quite a few judges in the book of Judges, of Ruth and Boaz in the book of Ruth, and of Eli, Samuel, Saul, Jonathan, and David in the books of 1 and 2 Samuel presents us vivid pictures of how those persons remained in and enjoyed the good land.—Judg. 1:3-11, 22; Ruth 4:13.", "norm_zh": "二在士师记里所记载的几位士师路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯撒母耳记上下所记载的以利撒母耳扫罗约拿单大卫呈现一幅幅生动的图画给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上并如何享受美地士一31122得四13列王纪生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The record of quite a few judges in the book of Judges of Ruth and Boaz in the book of Ruth and of Eli Samuel Saul Jonathan and David in the books of 1 and 2 Samuel presents us vivid pictures of how those persons remained in and enjoyed the good landJudg 1311 22 Ruth 413"}
{"zh": "三\t虽然那些图画刻画得很详细，但仍然需要列王纪上、下提供更多人物的图画，给我们看见他们如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地—王上三5~15，王下十八1~8。（列王纪生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "C. Even though those pictures were painted in detail, there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to give us pictures of more persons showing us how they remained in and enjoyed the good land.—1 Kings 3:5-15; 2 Kings 18:1-8.", "norm_zh": "三虽然哪些图画刻画得很详细但仍然需要列王纪上下提供更多人物的图画给我们看见他们如何留在美地上并如何享受美地王上三515王下十八18列王纪生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Even though those pictures were painted in detail there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to give us pictures of more persons showing us how they remained in and enjoyed the good land1 Kings 3515 2 Kings 1818"}
{"zh": "四\t以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关；尼希米记与修复、重建城有关；以斯帖记给我们看见，无所不在、无所不能的神，如何成了隐藏的神，保护在被掳中祂分散的选民—拉七6~10，尼一1~11，二4，四4~5、9，斯一1~2，四14。（以斯拉记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "D. The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple, and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair, the rebuilding, of the city. The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect, who were scattered in their captivity.—Ezra 7:6-10; Neh. 1:1-11; 2:4; 4:4-5, 9; Esth. 1:1-2; 4:14.", "norm_zh": "四以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关尼希米记与修复重建城有关以斯帖记给我们看见无所不在无所不能的神如何成了隐藏的神保护在被掳中祂分散的选民拉七610尼一111二4四459斯一12四14以斯拉记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The book of Ezra is concerned with the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple and the book of Nehemiah is concerned with the repair the rebuilding of the city The book of Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became the hiding God in protecting His captured elect who were scattered in their captivityEzra 7610 Neh 1111 24 445 9 Esth 112 414"}
{"zh": "肆\t在诗歌里—约伯记至雅歌这五卷诗歌揭示，三一神自己（不是伦理或道德）应当是人所追求的，作人的完全—伯四二1~6，歌一12~14，传一2、14：（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "IV. In the poetry—the five books of poetry from Job to Song of Songs unveil that the Triune God Himself, not ethics or morality, should be man's pursuit as his perfection.—Job 42:1-6; S. S. 1:12-14; Eccl. 1:2, 14:", "norm_zh": "肆在诗歌里约伯记至雅歌这五卷诗歌揭示三一神自己不是伦理或道德应当是人所追求的作人的完全伯四二16歌一1214传一214李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In the poetrythe five books of poetry from Job to Song of Songs unveil that the Triune God Himself not ethics or morality should be mans pursuit as his perfectionJob 4216 S S 11214 Eccl 12 14"}
{"zh": "一\t三一神自己（不是伦理或道德）应当是人所追求的，作人的完全；这一句话总括了约伯记中心、内在的启示—四二1~6。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "A. The Triune God Himself, not ethics or morality, should be man's pursuit as his perfection; this one sentence covers the central, intrinsic revelation of Job.—Job 42:1-6.", "norm_zh": "一三一神自己不是伦理或道德应当是人所追求的作人的完全这一句话总括了约伯记中心内在的启示四二16李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Triune God Himself not ethics or morality should be mans pursuit as his perfection this one sentence covers the central intrinsic revelation of JobJob 4216"}
{"zh": "二\t诗篇揭示，这位神化身成为一个在肉体里的人，作神的受膏者；祂是神所喜悦的，并且被神高举；祂该被神的选民接受、宝爱并高举—二7，八四9。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "B. The Psalms unveil that this God was incarnated to be a man in the flesh to be His Anointed, who is His delight, who has been exalted by Him, and who should be received, treasured, and exalted by His chosen people.—Psa. 2:7; 84:9.", "norm_zh": "二诗篇揭示这位神化身成为一个在肉体里的人作神的受膏者祂是神所喜悦的并且被神高举祂该被神的选民接受宝爱并高举二7八四9李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Psalms unveil that this God was incarnated to be a man in the flesh to be His Anointed who is His delight who has been exalted by Him and who should be received treasured and exalted by His chosen peoplePsa 27 849"}
{"zh": "三\t传道书揭示，在日光之下，人生的一切都是虚空的虚空—一2、14。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "C. Ecclesiastes unveils that all things in the human life under the sun are vanity of vanities.—Eccl. 1:2, 14.", "norm_zh": "三传道书揭示在日光之下人生的一切都是虚空的虚空一214李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Ecclesiastes unveils that all things in the human life under the sun are vanity of vanitiesEccl 12 14"}
{"zh": "四\t雅歌给我们看见，基督作三一神的具体化身，乃是神选民惟一的满足；因此，我们应当追求神作我们的完全，也应当追求基督作我们的满足—一12~14，四12~14，五1。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "D. Song of Songs shows that Christ as the embodiment of the Triune God is the unique satisfaction to God's chosen people; thus, we should pursue God as our perfection, and we should pursue after Christ as our satisfaction.—S. S. 1:12-14; 4:12-14; 5:1.", "norm_zh": "四雅歌给我们看见基督作三一神的具体化身乃是神选民惟一的满足因此我们应当追求神作我们的完全也应当追求基督作我们的满足一1214四1214五1李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Song of Songs shows that Christ as the embodiment of the Triune God is the unique satisfaction to Gods chosen people thus we should pursue God as our perfection and we should pursue after Christ as our satisfactionS S 11214 41214 51"}
{"zh": "伍\t在申言者的申言里—以赛亚书至玛拉基书揭示三一神具体化身在基督里，要来作神人，以完成救赎，好成就神永远的经纶；这要终极完成于新天新地—赛七14，九6，五三，六五17，六六22，彼后三13，启二一1：（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "V. In the prophesying of the prophets—the books of prophecy from Isaiah to Malachi unveil that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the God-man to accomplish redemption for the fulfillment of God's eternal economy; this will consummate in the new heaven and new earth.—Isa. 7:14; 9:6; 53; 65:17; 66:22; 2 Pet. 3:13; Rev. 21:1:", "norm_zh": "伍在申言者的申言里以赛亚书至玛拉基书揭示三一神具体化身在基督里要来作神人以完成救赎好成就神永远的经纶这要终极完成于新天新地赛七14九6五三六五17六六22彼后三13启二一1李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V In the prophesying of the prophetsthe books of prophecy from Isaiah to Malachi unveil that the Triune God embodied in Christ will come to be the Godman to accomplish redemption for the fulfillment of Gods eternal economy this will consummate in the new heaven and new earthIsa 714 96 53 6517 6622 2 Pet 313 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "一\t众申言者（从以赛亚到玛拉基）所释放的启示，着重强调的乃是：神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结，就像亚当与夏娃的联结一样；至终，二者在性情上和生命上成为一—创一26，结四三4~7。（何西阿书生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "A. The crucial emphasis of the revelation released by all the prophets from Isaiah to Malachi is that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people, like the union of Adam with Eve; eventually, the two became one in nature and in life—Gen. 1:26; Ezek. 43:4-7.", "norm_zh": "一众申言者从以赛亚到玛拉基所释放的启示着重强调的乃是神要与祂所拣选的人有生机的联结就像亚当与夏娃的联结一样至终二者在性情上和生命上成为一创一26结四三47何西阿书生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The crucial emphasis of the revelation released by all the prophets from Isaiah to Malachi is that God wants to have an organic union with His chosen people like the union of Adam with Eve eventually the two became one in nature and in lifeGen 126 Ezek 4347"}
{"zh": "二\t小申言者书的中心思想包含许多事情，从神的审判开始；神要审判世界；罪人当预备迎见神；基督这永远的神圣者，来到地上，出生为人；祂进入死，并从死里复活，使神的救恩延伸到万国—珥三2上，摩四12，弥五2，拿一17，二10，三2。（何西阿书生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "B. The central thought of the Minor Prophets involves many things, beginning with God's judgment; God will judge the world; sinners should prepare to meet God; Christ as the eternally divine One came to the earth and was born to be human; He entered into death and resurrected from it for the extending of God's salvation to all the nations—Joel 3:2a; Amos 4:12; Mic. 5:2; Jonah 1:17; 2:10; 3:2.", "norm_zh": "二小申言者书的中心思想包含许多事情从神的审判开始神要审判世界罪人当预备迎见神基督这永远的神圣者来到地上出生为人祂进入死并从死里复活使神的救恩延伸到万国珥三2上摩四12弥五2拿一17二10三2何西阿书生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The central thought of the Minor Prophets involves many things beginning with Gods judgment God will judge the world sinners should prepare to meet God Christ as the eternally divine One came to the earth and was born to be human He entered into death and resurrected from it for the extending of Gods salvation to all the nationsJoel 32a Amos 412 Mic 52 Jonah 117 210 32"}
{"zh": "三\t悔改并相信祂的罪人，必蒙神赦免其罪，并蒙神称义，得着神圣的生命，使他们得以在神圣的光中行走，成为基督的大能者，在基督第二次显现时，与基督一同受神差遣—摩四12，弥七18~19，哈二4，弥七8~9，珥三11下。（何西阿书生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "C. Sinners who repent and believe in Him will be forgiven of their sins and justified by God to have the divine life that they may walk in the divine light and become the mighty ones of Christ, sent with Him by God in His second appearing—Amos 4:12; Mic. 7:18-19; Hab. 2:4; Mic. 7:8-9; Joel 3:11b.", "norm_zh": "三悔改并相信祂的罪人必蒙神赦免其罪并蒙神称义得着神圣的生命使他们得以在神圣的光中行走成为基督的大能者在基督第二次显现时与基督一同受神差遣摩四12弥七1819哈二4弥七89珥三11下何西阿书生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Sinners who repent and believe in Him will be forgiven of their sins and justified by God to have the divine life that they may walk in the divine light and become the mighty ones of Christ sent with Him by God in His second appearingAmos 412 Mic 71819 Hab 24 Mic 789 Joel 311b"}
{"zh": "四\t祂要如公义的日头升起，又要作立约的使者而来，在锡安作王，并牧养以色列；然后复兴的千年国要被带进来—玛四2，三1，弥四7下，何十四4~8，启二十4、6，太十九28。（何西阿书生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "D. He will arise as the Sun of righteousness and come as the Angel of the covenant to reign in Zion and shepherd Israel; then the millennium of the restoration will be brought in—Mal. 4:2; 3:1; Mic. 4:7b; Hos. 14:4-8; Rev. 20:4, 6; Matt. 19:28.", "norm_zh": "四祂要如公义的日头升起又要作立约的使者而来在锡安作王并牧养以色列然后复兴的千年国要被带进来玛四2三1弥四7下何十四48启二十46太十九28何西阿书生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D He will arise as the Sun of righteousness and come as the Angel of the covenant to reign in Zion and shepherd Israel then the millennium of the restoration will be brought inMal 42 31 Mic 47b Hos 1448 Rev 204 6 Matt 1928"}
{"zh": "五\t以赛亚书预言到新天新地，使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及，如新耶路撒冷所说明的—六五17，六六22，启二一1。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "E. Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth as illustrated by the New Jerusalem—Isa. 65:17; 66:22; Rev. 21:1.", "norm_zh": "五以赛亚书预言到新天新地使基督在整个新天新地里作中心和普及如新耶路撒冷所说明的六五17六六22启二一1李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Isaiah prophesied about the new heaven and new earth for Christ to be the centrality and universality in the entire new heaven and new earth as illustrated by the New JerusalemIsa 6517 6622 Rev 211"}
{"zh": "陆\t以上各点向我们陈明一幅生动的图画，说到旧约中那在神永远经纶里，并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督；启示出基督是神经纶的中心与普及—但二35，弗一10，西一18，三10~11。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第二篇）", "en": "VI. All the above points present us a vivid portrait of the all-inclusive Christ in and for God's eternal economy in the Old Testament, revealing Christ as the centrality and universality of God's economy—Dan. 2:35; Eph. 1:10; Col. 1:18; 3:10-11.", "norm_zh": "陆以上各点向我们陈明一幅生动的图画说到旧约中哪在神永远经纶里并为着神永远经纶之包罗万有的基督启示出基督是神经纶的中心与普及但二35弗一10西一18三1011李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:16:08.181143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI All the above points present us a vivid portrait of the allinclusive Christ in and for Gods eternal economy in the Old Testament revealing Christ as the centrality and universality of Gods economyDan 235 Eph 110 Col 118 31011"}
{"zh": "读经：路二40、52，约五19，一29，三14，二十19~22，徒八1、12，十三1~4，罗八16，十二4~5，彼前二4~8，启二十1~2", "en": "Scripture Reading: Luke 2:40, 52; John 5:19; 1:29; 3:14; 20:19-22; Acts 8:1, 12; 13:1-4; Rom. 8:16; 12:4-5; 1 Pet. 2:4-8; Rev. 20:1-2", "norm_zh": "读经路二4052约五19一29三14二十1922徒八112十三14罗八16十二45彼前二48启二十12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Luke 240 52 John 519 129 314 201922 Acts 81 12 1314 Rom 816 1245 1 Pet 248 Rev 2012"}
{"zh": "壹\t旧约是神永远经纶表征的图画，新约乃是神永远经纶实际的完成；马太福音至约翰福音揭示，三一神经过过程并终极完成，成为包罗万有赐生命的灵—路二40、52，约五19，一29，三14，二十19~22：", "en": "I. The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of God's eternal economy, and the New Testament is the practical fulfillment of God's eternal economy; Matthew through John reveals the Triune God, processed and consummated, becoming the all-inclusive, life-giving Spirit—Luke 2:40, 52; John 5:19; 1:29; 3:14; 20:19-22:", "norm_zh": "壹旧约是神永远经纶表征的图画新约乃是神永远经纶实际的完成马太福音至约翰福音揭示三一神经过过程并终极完成成为包罗万有赐生命的灵路二4052约五19一29三14二十1922", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Old Testament is a figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy and the New Testament is the practical fulfillment of Gods eternal economy Matthew through John reveals the Triune God processed and consummated becoming the allinclusive lifegiving SpiritLuke 240 52 John 519 129 314 201922"}
{"zh": "一\t借着祂的成为肉体成了神人—路二40、52，约八58。", "en": "A. Through His incarnation to become the God-man—Luke 2:40, 52; John 8:58.", "norm_zh": "一借着祂的成为肉体成了神人路二4052约八58", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through His incarnation to become the GodmanLuke 240 52 John 858"}
{"zh": "二\t借着祂的人性生活过神人的生活—路四42~43，约五19，四34，十七4。", "en": "B. Through His human living to live the God-man's life—Luke 4:42-43; John 5:19; 4:34; 17:4.", "norm_zh": "二借着祂的人性生活过神人的生活路四4243约五19四34十七4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Through His human living to live the Godmans lifeLuke 44243 John 519 434 174"}
{"zh": "三\t借着祂包罗万有的死，救赎祂失丧的受造之物，并释放祂神圣的生命—一29，三14。", "en": "C. Through His all-inclusive death to redeem His lost creation and to release His divine life—John 1:29; 3:14.", "norm_zh": "三借着祂包罗万有的死救赎祂失丧的受造之物并释放祂神圣的生命一29三14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Through His allinclusive death to redeem His lost creation and to release His divine lifeJohn 129 314"}
{"zh": "四\t借着祂的复活，将祂自己分赐到祂所救赎的选民里面，作他们的生命和一切—二十19~22，十一25、40~44、48~53。", "en": "D. Through His resurrection to dispense Himself into His redeemed chosen people as their life and everything—John 20:19-22; 11:25, 40-44, 48-53.", "norm_zh": "四借着祂的复活将祂自己分赐到祂所救赎的选民里面作他们的生命和一切二十1922十一2540444853", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Through His resurrection to dispense Himself into His redeemed chosen people as their life and everythingJohn 201922 1125 4044 4853"}
{"zh": "贰\t使徒行传揭示，包罗万有赐生命的灵，作那是神具体化身之基督的实际，扩展祂自己，为着产生神的众召会—八1、12，十三1~4：", "en": "II.\tThe Book of Acts unveils the all-inclusive, life-giving Spirit spreading Himself as the reality of Christ, who is the embodiment of God, for the producing of the churches of God.—Acts 8:1, 12; 13:1-4:", "norm_zh": "贰使徒行传揭示包罗万有赐生命的灵作哪是神具体化身之基督的实际扩展祂自己为着产生神的众召会八112十三14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The Book of Acts unveils the allinclusive lifegiving Spirit spreading Himself as the reality of Christ who is the embodiment of God for the producing of the churches of GodActs 81 12 1314"}
{"zh": "一\t使徒行传可视为新约的分界线或“背脊”；这卷书把福音书和书信（包括启示录）分开—一1~二八31。", "en": "A. The book of Acts may be considered the dividing line, or the \"backbone,\" of the New Testament; this book divides the four Gospels from the Epistles, which include the book of Revelation—Acts 1:1—28:31.", "norm_zh": "一使徒行传可视为新约的分界线或背脊这卷书把福音书和书信包括启示录分开一1二八31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The book of Acts may be considered the dividing line or the backbone of the New Testament this book divides the four Gospels from the Epistles which include the book of RevelationActs 112831"}
{"zh": "二\t行传的主题乃是复活的基督在升天里，凭着那灵，借着门徒，为着产生众召会—神的国—的繁殖—一1~二八31：", "en": "B. The subject of Acts is the propagation of the resurrected Christ in His ascension, by the Spirit, through the disciples, for the producing of the churches—the kingdom of God—Acts 1:1—28:31:", "norm_zh": "二行传的主提乃是复活的基督在升天里凭着哪灵借着门徒为着产生众召会神的国的繁殖一1二八31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The subject of Acts is the propagation of the resurrected Christ in His ascension by the Spirit through the disciples for the producing of the churchesthe kingdom of GodActs 112831"}
{"zh": "1\t复活基督的繁殖是由基督在祂升天里所完成的；基督在祂的升天里，得着宇宙中所有的能力和所有的权柄；带着这样的权柄和能力，这位升天者，正在执行祂宇宙、永远的繁殖—一9~11。", "en": "1. The propagation of the resurrected Christ is carried out by Christ in His ascension; in His ascension Christ has all the power and all the authority in the universe; with such authority and power, the ascended One is carrying out His universal and eternal propagation—Acts 1:9-11.", "norm_zh": "1复活基督的繁殖是由基督在祂升天里所完成的基督在祂的升天里得着宇宙中所有的能力和所有的权柄带着这样的权柄和能力这位升天者正在执行祂宇宙永远的繁殖一911", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The propagation of the resurrected Christ is carried out by Christ in His ascension in His ascension Christ has all the power and all the authority in the universe with such authority and power the ascended One is carrying out His universal and eternal propagationActs 1911"}
{"zh": "2\t复活基督的繁殖是凭着那灵，尤其是凭着经纶的灵；在使徒行传，我们看见经纶的灵如何执行基督的繁殖—二1~4。", "en": "2. The propagation of the resurrected Christ is by the Spirit, in particular, the economical Spirit; in the book of Acts we see the economical Spirit for the carrying out of Christ's propagation—Acts 2:1-4.", "norm_zh": "2复活基督的繁殖是凭着哪灵尤其是凭着经纶的灵在使徒行传我们看见经纶的灵如何执行基督的繁殖二14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The propagation of the resurrected Christ is by the Spirit in particular the economical Spirit in the book of Acts we see the economical Spirit for the carrying out of Christs propagationActs 214"}
{"zh": "3\t基督的繁殖也是借着门徒；复活的基督在祂的升天里，借着祂的见证人繁殖祂自己，乃是为着产生众召会，众召会就是神的国—九31。", "en": "3. The propagation of Christ is also through the disciples; through His witnesses the resurrected Christ in His ascension propagates Himself for the producing of the churches, which are the kingdom of God—Acts 9:31.", "norm_zh": "3基督的繁殖也是借着门徒复活的基督在祂的升天里借着祂的见证人繁殖祂自己乃是为着产生众召会众召会就是神的国九31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The propagation of Christ is also through the disciples through His witnesses the resurrected Christ in His ascension propagates Himself for the producing of the churches which are the kingdom of GodActs 931"}
{"zh": "三\t神的国乃是由基督的繁殖所产生的生命范围；神的国就是神的扩大，而这位神的具体化身就是基督；这基督的扩大就是众召会—六7，九31。", "en": "C. The kingdom of God is a sphere of life produced by the propagation of Christ; the kingdom of God is the expansion of God, and the embodiment of this God is Christ; this expansion of Christ is the churches—Acts 6:7; 9:31.", "norm_zh": "三神的国乃是由基督的繁殖所产生的生命范围神的国就是神的扩大而这位神的具体化身就是基督这基督的扩大就是众召会六7九31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The kingdom of God is a sphere of life produced by the propagation of Christ the kingdom of God is the expansion of God and the embodiment of this God is Christ this expansion of Christ is the churchesActs 67 931"}
{"zh": "叁\t罗马书至启示录揭示，包罗万有赐生命的灵借着将众召会变化成为那作神长子之基督的形像，而将众召会建造成为终极完成之三一神的生机体，作基督的身体，这要终极完成于新耶路撒冷，作终极完成之三一神永远的扩大和彰显—罗十二4~5，彼前二4~8，启二十1~2：", "en": "III. Romans to Revelation unveil the all-inclusive life-giving Spirit building up the churches into the organism of the consummated Triune God as the Body of Christ, by transforming them into the image of Christ as the firstborn Son of God, which will consummate in the New Jerusalem as the eternal enlargement and expression of the consummated Triune God.—Rom. 12:4-5; 1 Pet. 2:4-8; Rev. 20:1-2:", "norm_zh": "叁罗马书至启示录揭示包罗万有赐生命的灵借着将众召会变化成为哪作神长子之基督的形像而将众召会建造成为终极完成之三一神的生机体作基督的身体这要终极完成于新耶路撒冷作终极完成之三一神永远的扩大和彰显罗十二45彼前二48启二十12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Romans to Revelation unveil the allinclusive lifegiving Spirit building up the churches into the organism of the consummated Triune God as the Body of Christ by transforming them into the image of Christ as the firstborn Son of God which will consummate in the New Jerusalem as the eternal enlargement and expression of the consummated Triune GodRom 1245 1 Pet 248 Rev 2012"}
{"zh": "一\t神在永远里是单独的，祂有一个心愿，就是要得着基督的身体，能作祂的生机体；所以祂就有一个经纶，为着满足祂的这个心愿，以产生基督的身体—弗四12，林前十二27。", "en": "A. God is alone in eternity; His heart's desire is to have the Body of Christ that it may be His organism; hence, He has an economy to satisfy His heart's desire to produce the Body of Christ.—Eph. 4:12; 1 Cor. 12:27.", "norm_zh": "一神在永远里是单独的祂有一个心愿就是要得着基督的身体能作祂的生机体所以祂就有一个经纶为着满足祂的这个心愿以产生基督的身体弗四12林前十二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God is alone in eternity His hearts desire is to have the Body of Christ that it may be His organism hence He has an economy to satisfy His hearts desire to produce the Body of ChristEph 412 1 Cor 1227"}
{"zh": "二\t在四卷福音书里，只有两次题到召会，但是没有题到基督的身体；使徒行传说到众召会，但也没有题到基督的身体；基督的身体只在书信中题及—弗四12，林前十二27：", "en": "B. In the four Gospels the church is mentioned only twice, but the Body of Christ is not mentioned; Acts speaks of the churches, but also does not mention the Body of Christ; the Body of Christ is mentioned only in the Epistles.—Eph. 4:12; 1 Cor. 12:27:", "norm_zh": "二在四卷福音书里只有两次提到召会但是没有提到基督的身体使徒行传说到众召会但也没有提到基督的身体基督的身体只在书信中提及弗四12林前十二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In the four Gospels the church is mentioned only twice but the Body of Christ is not mentioned Acts speaks of the churches but also does not mention the Body of Christ the Body of Christ is mentioned only in the EpistlesEph 412 1 Cor 1227"}
{"zh": "1\t在罗马书中，保罗只有一处题到基督的身体，就是在十二章四至五节；那里说，“正如我们一个身体上有好些肢体，但肢体不都有一样的功用；我们这许多人，在基督里是一个身体，并且各个互相作肢体，也是如此”。", "en": "1. In Romans, Paul mentions the Body of Christ only in one place, and that is in 12:4-5, which says, \"For just as in one body we have many members, and all the members do not have the same function, so we who are many are one body in Christ, and individually members one of another.\"", "norm_zh": "1在罗马书中保罗只有一处提到基督的身体就是在十二章四至五节哪里说正如我们一个身体上有好些肢体但肢体不都有一样的功用我们这许多人在基督里是一个身体并且各个互相作肢体也是如此", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In Romans Paul mentions the Body of Christ only in one place and that is in 1245 which says For just as in one body we have many members and all the members do not have the same function so we who are many are one body in Christ and individually members one of another"}
{"zh": "2\t罗马书简短的题到基督的身体，下一卷的哥林多前书就大讲特讲基督的身体—4~5节。", "en": "2. Whereas Romans briefly mentions the Body of Christ, the next book, 1 Corinthians, deals with it extensively.—vv. 4-5.", "norm_zh": "2罗马书简短的提到基督的身体下一卷的哥林多前书就大讲特讲基督的身体45节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Whereas Romans briefly mentions the Body of Christ the next book 1 Corinthians deals with it extensivelyvv 45"}
{"zh": "3\t以弗所书明显的是讲基督的身体，几乎每一章都讲到基督的身体；它不是大体的讲，乃是细讲深讲—四12：", "en": "3. Ephesians is obviously on the Body of Christ; almost every chapter refers to the Body of Christ; it speaks of the Body of Christ not in a general way but in a detailed and deep way.—Eph. 4:12:", "norm_zh": "3以弗所书明显的是讲基督的身体几乎每一章都讲到基督的身体它不是大体的讲乃是细讲深讲四12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Ephesians is obviously on the Body of Christ almost every chapter refers to the Body of Christ it speaks of the Body of Christ not in a general way but in a detailed and deep wayEph 412"}
{"zh": "a\t以弗所一章是讲神圣三一的分赐，就是父的分赐、子的分赐和灵的分赐，末了还有升天、超越之基督的输供；这两样的结果就产生召会；这召会就是基督的身体—22~23节。", "en": "a. Ephesians 1 is on the dispensing of the Divine Trinity, that is, the dispensing of the Father, of the Son, and of the Spirit, and then there is also the transmission of the ascended and transcendent Christ; these two things issue in the church, which is the Body of Christ—vv. 22-23.", "norm_zh": "a以弗所一章是讲神圣三一的分赐就是父的分赐子的分赐和灵的分赐末了还有升天超越之基督的输供这两样的结果就产生召会这召会就是基督的身体2223节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Ephesians 1 is on the dispensing of the Divine Trinity that is the dispensing of the Father of the Son and of the Spirit and then there is also the transmission of the ascended and transcendent Christ these two things issue in the church which is the Body of Christvv 2223"}
{"zh": "（一）基督身体里有灵的故事，有主的故事，还有父神的故事；这些调和起来就是基督的身体—林前十二13。", "en": "1) The Body of Christ involves the Spirit, the Lord, and God the Father; all these added together equal the Body of Christ—1 Cor. 12:13.", "norm_zh": "一基督身体里有灵的故事有主的故事还有父神的故事这些调和起来就是基督的身体林前十二13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Body of Christ involves the Spirit the Lord and God the Father all these added together equal the Body of Christ1 Cor 1213"}
{"zh": "（二）基督的身体所以能够成为身体，乃是因为灵在里面，主在里面，并且父也在里面—弗四6。", "en": "2) The Body of Christ can be the Body of Christ because the Spirit, the Lord, and the Father are in the Body.—Eph. 4:6.", "norm_zh": "二基督的身体所以能够成为身体乃是因为灵在里面主在里面并且父也在里面弗四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Body of Christ can be the Body of Christ because the Spirit the Lord and the Father are in the BodyEph 46"}
{"zh": "b\t以弗所书讲基督的身体，讲得最重的是第四章；四节说，一个身体和一位灵（就是那灵）；接下去说到一主，还有一位父。", "en": "b. In Ephesians the strongest emphasis on the Body of Christ is in chapter four; verse 4 speaks of one Body and one Spirit (the Spirit); it goes on to speak of one Lord and one Father.", "norm_zh": "b以弗所书讲基督的身体讲得最重的是第四章四节说一个身体和一位灵就是哪灵接下去说到一主还有一位父", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b In Ephesians the strongest emphasis on the Body of Christ is in chapter four verse 4 speaks of one Body and one Spirit the Spirit it goes on to speak of one Lord and one Father"}
{"zh": "4\t在歌罗西书中一章里，保罗给我们看见，基督是一切受造之物的首生者，万有是借着祂并为着祂造的；祂也是召会身体的头；二章进一步给我们看见，基督的身体需要长大，而基督身体的长大是从元首基督长大的，因为这一切的供应都来自基督—19节。", "en": "4. In Colossians chapter one, Paul shows us that Christ is the Firstborn of all creation, in whom and for whom all things were created; He is also the Head of the Body, the church; chapter two further shows us that the Body of Christ needs to grow, and the growth of the Body of Christ is out from Christ the Head, because all this supply comes from Christ.—v. 19.", "norm_zh": "4在歌罗西书中一章里保罗给我们看见基督是一切受造之物的首生者万有是借着祂并为着祂造的祂也是召会身体的头二章进一步给我们看见基督的身体需要长大而基督身体的长大是从元首基督长大的因为这一切的供应都来自基督19节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 In Colossians chapter one Paul shows us that Christ is the Firstborn of all creation in whom and for whom all things were created He is also the Head of the Body the church chapter two further shows us that the Body of Christ needs to grow and the growth of the Body of Christ is out from Christ the Head because all this supply comes from Christv 19"}
{"zh": "三\t神的经纶以基督为其中心与普及，使基督在凡事上居首位，也产生召会作基督的身体，终极完成于圣城新耶路撒冷—西一18，弗四12：", "en": "C. God's economy, with Christ as its centrality and universality, makes Christ preeminent in all things, and also produces the church as the Body of Christ, consummating in the holy city, the New Jerusalem.—Col. 1:18; Eph. 4:12:", "norm_zh": "三神的经纶以基督为其中心与普及使基督在凡事上居首位也产生召会作基督的身体终极完成于圣城新耶路撒冷西一18弗四12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Gods economy with Christ as its centrality and universality makes Christ preeminent in all things and also produces the church as the Body of Christ consummating in the holy city the New JerusalemCol 118 Eph 412"}
{"zh": "1\t基督的身体乃是由祂肢体所构成的生机体—罗十二5。", "en": "1. The Body of Christ is an organism constituted with His members—Rom. 12:5.", "norm_zh": "1基督的身体乃是由祂肢体所构成的生机体罗十二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Body of Christ is an organism constituted with His membersRom 125"}
{"zh": "2\t基督的身体需要用基督那追测不尽的丰富，借着神圣的分赐而得建造—弗三8~11、2。", "en": "2. The Body of Christ needs to be built up with the unsearchable riches of Christ through the divine dispensing—Eph. 3:8-11, 2.", "norm_zh": "2基督的身体需要用基督哪追测不尽的丰富借着神圣的分赐而得建造弗三8112", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Body of Christ needs to be built up with the unsearchable riches of Christ through the divine dispensingEph 3811 2"}
{"zh": "3\t基督的身体乃是基督的丰满，就是那在万有中充满万有者的丰满，作祂的彰显—一22~23，三19：", "en": "3. The Body of Christ is the fullness of Christ as the One who fills all in all to be His expression—1:22-23; 3:19:", "norm_zh": "3基督的身体乃是基督的丰满就是哪在万有中充满万有者的丰满作祂的彰显一2223三19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Body of Christ is the fullness of Christ as the One who fills all in all to be His expression12223 319"}
{"zh": "a\t神的经纶就是神的目的，乃是要把祂自己在祂神圣的三一里，分赐到祂所拣选并救赎的人里面，作他们的生命和性情，使他们能与祂一样，好作祂团体的彰显—提前一4，弗一3~23。", "en": "A.\tGod's economy is His intention to dispense Himself in His Divine Trinity into His chosen and redeemed people to be their life and nature so that they may be the same as He is for His corporate expression.—1 Tim. 1:4; Eph. 1:3-23.", "norm_zh": "a神的经纶就是神的目的乃是要把祂自己在祂神圣的三一里分赐到祂所拣选并救赎的人里面作他们的生命和性情使他们能与祂一样好作祂团体的彰显提前一4弗一323", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods economy is His intention to dispense Himself in His Divine Trinity into His chosen and redeemed people to be their life and nature so that they may be the same as He is for His corporate expression1 Tim 14 Eph 1323"}
{"zh": "b\t神救赎我们为要使我们在生命和性情上成为神，使祂能得着基督的身体，终极完成于新耶路撒冷，作神的扩大和彰显，直到永远—一7，四16，启二一2。", "en": "B.\tGod redeemed us for the purpose of making us God in life and nature so that He can have the Body of Christ, which consummates in the New Jerusalem as God's enlargement and expression for eternity.—1:7; 4:16; Rev. 21:2.", "norm_zh": "b神救赎我们为要使我们在生命和性情上成为神使祂能得着基督的身体终极完成于新耶路撒冷作神的扩大和彰显直到永远一7四16启二一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God redeemed us for the purpose of making us God in life and nature so that He can have the Body of Christ which consummates in the New Jerusalem as Gods enlargement and expression for eternity17 416 Rev 212"}
{"zh": "肆\t“当我们告诉人，新约向我们揭示什么时，我们应当告诉他们以上所说，新约作神永远经纶实际之完成的三部分。我们若能背诵这三部分的三个定义，那就更好。”（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，三一神的启示与行动，第三篇）", "en": "IV. \"When we tell people what the New Testament unveils we should tell them what we have spoken of above concerning its three sections as the practical fulfillment of God's eternal economy. It would be very good if we were able to recite the three definitions of these three sections.\"", "norm_zh": "肆当我们告诉人新约向我们揭示什么时我们应当告诉他们以上所说新约作神永远经纶实际之完成的三部分我们若能背诵这三部分的三个定义哪就更好李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册三一神的启示与行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV When we tell people what the New Testament unveils we should tell them what we have spoken of above concerning its three sections as the practical fulfillment of Gods eternal economy It would be very good if we were able to recite the three definitions of these three sections"}
{"zh": "使徒行传可视为新约的分界线或“背脊”。这卷书把福音书和书信（包括启示录）分开。福音书陈明一位得着完成的救赎主和祂所成就的救赎。在使徒行传里有这位已经得着完成之救赎主的繁殖，以及祂为着产生众召会所成就的救赎。然后在书信里有信徒的造就，和众召会的建造。", "en": "The book of Acts may be considered the dividing line, or the \"backbone,\" of the New Testament. This book divides the four Gospels from the Epistles, which include the book of Revelation. The Gospels present a completed Redeemer and His accomplished redemption. In Acts we have the propagation of the completed Redeemer and His accomplished redemption for the producing of the churches. Then in the Epistles we have the edifying of the believers and the building up of the churches.", "norm_zh": "使徒行传可视为新约的分界线或背脊这卷书把福音书和书信包括启示录分开福音书陈明一位得着完成的救赎主和祂所成就的救赎在使徒行传里有这位已经得着完成之救赎主的繁殖以及祂为着产生众召会所成就的救赎然后在书信里有信徒的造就和众召会的建造", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The book of Acts may be considered the dividing line or the backbone of the New Testament This book divides the four Gospels from the Epistles which include the book of Revelation The Gospels present a completed Redeemer and His accomplished redemption In Acts we have the propagation of the completed Redeemer and His accomplished redemption for the producing of the churches Then in the Epistles we have the edifying of the believers and the building up of the churches"}
{"zh": "繁殖是一件生产的事。因此，繁殖就是生产。复活的基督在祂升天里的繁殖，产生众召会。众召会乃是复活的基督在祂升天里的产品。因此，众召会是基督繁殖的产品。使徒行传第一次题到“召会”一词，是在五章十一节。此后，这卷书多次说到召会。", "en": "Propagation is a matter of production. Therefore, propagation is production. The propagation of the resurrected Christ in His ascension produces the churches. The churches are the product of the resurrected Christ in His ascension. Therefore, the churches are the product of Christ's propagation. The first mention of the word \"church\" in Acts is in 5:11. After this, this book speaks of the church many times.", "norm_zh": "繁殖是一件生产的事因此繁殖就是生产复活的基督在祂升天里的繁殖产生众召会众召会乃是复活的基督在祂升天里的产品因此众召会是基督繁殖的产品使徒行传第一次提到召会一词是在五章十一节此后这卷书多次说到召会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Propagation is a matter of production Therefore propagation is production The propagation of the resurrected Christ in His ascension produces the churches The churches are the product of the resurrected Christ in His ascension Therefore the churches are the product of Christs propagation The first mention of the word church in Acts is in 511 After this this book speaks of the church many times"}
{"zh": "神的国", "en": "The kingdom of God", "norm_zh": "神的国", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:18:49.356549+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The kingdom of God"}
