{"zh": "读经：出二十1~17，三四28，诗十九7，罗七14，林后三6，提后三16，约五39~40，林后三15~18", "en": "Scripture Reading: Exo. 20:1-17; 34:28; Psa. 19:7; Rom. 7:14; 2 Cor. 3:6; 2 Tim. 3:16; John 5:39-40; 2 Cor. 3:15-18", "norm_zh": "读经出二十117三四28诗十九7罗七14林后三6提后三16约五3940林后三1518", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Exo 20117 3428 Psa 197 Rom 714 2 Cor 36 2 Tim 316 John 53940 2 Cor 31518"}
{"zh": "一\t律法总是将制定律法者是怎样的人显明出来—出二十1~17。", "en": "A.\tA law is always a revelation of what kind of person has enacted that law.—Exo. 20:1-17.", "norm_zh": "一律法总是将制定律法者是怎样的人显明出来出二十117", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A law is always a revelation of what kind of person has enacted that lawExo 20117"}
{"zh": "二\t神认为十条诫命，十条律法，乃是“十句话”—这进一步指明，律法是神自己的启示，因为一个人所说的话，就把那个人启示出来—申四13，出三四28，二十1：", "en": "B. God regards the Ten Commandments, the ten laws, as “ten words”—this further indicates that the law is God’s revelation of Himself, since the words a person speaks are a revelation of that person.—Deut. 4:13; Exo. 34:28; 20:1:", "norm_zh": "二神认为十条诫命十条律法乃是十句话这进一步指明律法是神自己的启示因为一个人所说的话就把哪个人启示出来申四13出三四28二十1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God regards the Ten Commandments the ten laws as ten wordsthis further indicates that the law is Gods revelation of Himself since the words a person speaks are a revelation of that personDeut 413 Exo 3428 201"}
{"zh": "4\t神是义的—诗十一7，出二十5。", "en": "4. God is righteous—Psa. 11:7; Exo. 20:5.", "norm_zh": "4神是义的诗十一7出二十5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 God is righteousPsa 117 Exo 205"}
{"zh": "四\t基督是律法（即神的见证）的实际；神的见证表征基督，神的具体化身，是神所是之活的描绘—二9，一15，约一18：", "en": "D. Christ is the reality of the law as the testimony of God; the testimony of God signifies Christ, the embodiment of God, as the living portrait of what God is.—Col. 2:9; 1:15; John 1:18:", "norm_zh": "四基督是律法即神的见证的实际神的见证表征基督神的具体化身是神所是之活的描绘二9一15约一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Christ is the reality of the law as the testimony of God the testimony of God signifies Christ the embodiment of God as the living portrait of what God isCol 29 115 John 118"}
{"zh": "1\t律法是神的十句话，将神启示给祂的百姓；照样，基督是神的话，将神启示给我们—1、14节。", "en": "1.\tAs the law is the ten words of God that reveal God to His people, so Christ is the Word of God revealing God to us.—vv. 1, 14.", "norm_zh": "1律法是神的十句话将神启示给祂的百姓照样基督是神的话将神启示给我们114节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 As the law is the ten words of God that reveal God to His people so Christ is the Word of God revealing God to usvv 1 14"}
{"zh": "2\t我们不该想要从外面遵守律法，乃该让基督从我们里面活出来，使我们能成为神的见证，就是神彰显的扩展和扩大—罗八4，腓一20~21。", "en": "2.\tWe should not try to keep the law from without but let Christ live Himself out from within so that we may become the testimony of God, the expansion and enlargement of God's expression.—Rom. 8:4; Phil. 1:20-21.", "norm_zh": "2我们不该想要从外面遵守律法乃该让基督从我们里面活出来使我们能成为神的见证就是神彰显的扩展和扩大罗八4腓一2021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We should not try to keep the law from without but let Christ live Himself out from within so that we may become the testimony of God the expansion and enlargement of Gods expressionRom 84 Phil 12021"}
{"zh": "一\t两种对待律法的人—爱神的寻求者和遵守律法字句的人—参创二9，林后三6、15~16：", "en": "B.\tThere are two kinds of people dealing with the law—the loving seekers of God and the letter-keepers of the law.—cf. Gen. 2:9; 2 Cor. 3:6, 15-16:", "norm_zh": "一两种对待律法的人爱神的寻求者和遵守律法字句的人参创二9林后三61516", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There are two kinds of people dealing with the lawthe loving seekers of God and the letterkeepers of the lawcf Gen 29 2 Cor 36 1516"}
{"zh": "1\t作诗的人是爱神的寻求者，他们爱那作为神的见证和神活话的律法—诗四二2，一一九2、10、127、147：", "en": "1.\tThe psalmists were the loving seekers of God, loving the law as the testimony of God and as His living word:—Psa. 42:2; 119:2, 10, 127, 147:", "norm_zh": "1作诗的人是爱神的寻求者他们爱哪作为神的见证和神活话的律法诗四二2一一九210127147", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The psalmists were the loving seekers of God loving the law as the testimony of God and as His living wordPsa 422 1192 10 127 147"}
{"zh": "a\t他们爱神—十八1，七三25，一一六1。", "en": "a.\tThey loved God.—Psa. 18:1; 73:25; 116:1.", "norm_zh": "a他们爱神十八1七三25一一六1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a They loved GodPsa 181 7325 1161"}
{"zh": "c\t他们宝爱神的律法—14、72、127节。", "en": "b.\tThey treasured the law of God.—vv. 14, 72, 127.", "norm_zh": "c他们宝爱神的律法1472127节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b They treasured the law of Godvv 14 72 127"}
{"zh": "d\t他们尝到律法的甘美—103节。", "en": "c.\tThey tasted the sweetness of the law.—v. 103.", "norm_zh": "d他们尝到律法的甘美103节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c They tasted the sweetness of the lawv 103"}
{"zh": "e\t他们仰望并默想神的话—147~148节。", "en": "d.\tThey hoped in the word of God and mused upon it.—vv. 147-148.", "norm_zh": "e他们仰望并默想神的话147148节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d They hoped in the word of God and mused upon itvv 147148"}
{"zh": "2\t热中犹太教者，就是墨守成规，拘泥于教条的遵守律法字句者，无心为着神，只为着杀死人的律法字句，在神之外寻求律法—太十五8，加六12~13。", "en": "2.\tThe Judaizers, the legal and dogmatic letter-keepers of the law, had a heart not for God but for the killing letter of the law, seeking the law apart from God.—Matt. 15:8; Gal. 6:12-13.", "norm_zh": "2热中犹太教者就是墨守成规拘泥于教条的遵守律法字句者无心为着神只为着杀死人的律法字句在神之外寻求律法太十五8加六1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Judaizers the legal and dogmatic letterkeepers of the law had a heart not for God but for the killing letter of the law seeking the law apart from GodMatt 158 Gal 61213"}
{"zh": "3\t大数的扫罗得救以前，为律法大发热心；身为热中犹太教者，他甚至是亵渎神的，逼迫人的—腓三5~6，提前一13。", "en": "3. Before he was saved, Saul of Tarsus was zealous for the law; as a Judaizer, he was even a blasphemer of God and a persecutor of man.—Phil. 3:5-6; 1 Tim. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "3大数的扫罗得救以前为律法大发热心身为热中犹太教者他甚至是亵渎神的逼迫人的腓三56提前一13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Before he was saved Saul of Tarsus was zealous for the law as a Judaizer he was even a blasphemer of God and a persecutor of manPhil 356 1 Tim 113"}
{"zh": "二\t我们来就近律法的态度，若只是关切字句的诫命，我们所有的就是律法在杀死人的字句这一面—约五39~40，林后三6：", "en": "B.\tIf our attitude in coming to the law is to care only for the commandments in letters, we will have the law in the aspect of the killing letter:—John 5:39-40; 2 Cor. 3:6:", "norm_zh": "二我们来就近律法的态度若只是关切字句的诫命我们所有的就是律法在杀死人的字句这一面约五3940林后三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B If our attitude in coming to the law is to care only for the commandments in letters we will have the law in the aspect of the killing letterJohn 53940 2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t我们到律法这里来，若不在爱里寻求神，反而把律法与活的神这生命的源头分开，那原本为要带进生命，本身却不能赐生命的律法，对我们就成为定罪和杀死的元素—参约五39~40，加三21。", "en": "2. If in coming to the law we do not seek God in love but rather separate the law from the living God as the source of life, the law, which was intended to result in life but cannot give life of itself, will become a condemning and killing element to us—cf. John 5:39-40; Gal. 3:21.", "norm_zh": "2我们到律法这里来若不在爱里寻求神反而把律法与活的神这生命的源头分开哪原本为要带进生命本身却不能赐生命的律法对我们就成为定罪和杀死的元素参约五3940加三21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If in coming to the law we do not seek God in love but rather separate the law from the living God as the source of life the law which was intended to result in life but cannot give life of itself will become a condemning and killing element to uscf John 53940 Gal 321"}
{"zh": "三\t然而，我们若将律法的每一部分—所有的诫命、规条、律例、训辞和判语，当作我们所爱之神呼出的话，我们就会有律法赐生命之灵的这一面—提后三16，约六63：", "en": "C. However, if we take every part of the law—all the commandments, ordinances, statutes, precepts, and judgments—as the word breathed out by the God whom we love, we will have the law in the aspect of the life-giving Spirit.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63:", "norm_zh": "三然而我们若将律法的每一部分所有的诫命规条律例训辞和判语当作我们所爱之神呼出的话我们就会有律法赐生命之灵的这一面提后三16约六63", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C However if we take every part of the lawall the commandments ordinances statutes precepts and judgmentsas the word breathed out by the God whom we love we will have the law in the aspect of the lifegiving Spirit2 Tim 316 John 663"}
{"zh": "1\t我们若爱神，谦卑自己，把律法当作神活的话，借以接触祂并住在祂里面，律法就要成为管道，借此将神圣的生命和本质传输给我们，作我们的供应和滋养—63节，加三5，彼后一11。", "en": "1.\tIf we love God, humble ourselves, and regard the law as His living word through which we contact Him and abide in Him, the law will become a channel through which the divine life and substance are conveyed to us for our supply and nourishment.—v. 63; Gal. 3:5; 2 Pet. 1:11.", "norm_zh": "1我们若爱神谦卑自己把律法当作神活的话借以接触祂并住在祂里面律法就要成为管道借此将神圣的生命和本质传输给我们作我们的供应和滋养63节加三5彼后一11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 If we love God humble ourselves and regard the law as His living word through which we contact Him and abide in Him the law will become a channel through which the divine life and substance are conveyed to us for our supply and nourishmentv 63 Gal 35 2 Pet 111"}
{"zh": "叁\t律法有两面的功用—罗五20，加三23~24，诗一一九2、130：", "en": "III.\tThe function of the law has two aspects:—Rom. 5:20; Gal. 3:23-24; Psa. 119:2, 130:", "norm_zh": "叁律法有两面的功用罗五20加三2324诗一一九2130", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The function of the law has two aspectsRom 520 Gal 32324 Psa 1192 130"}
{"zh": "一\t在消极一面，律法暴露人的罪，叫罪人服在神面前；律法也将神所拣选的人看守在其监管之下，使他们可以被带到基督面前—罗三20，五20，七7~8，三19，加三23~24。", "en": "A. On the negative side, the law exposes man's sin and subdues sinners before God; the law also guards God's chosen people in its custody that they might be conducted to Christ.—Rom. 3:20; 5:20; 7:7-8; 3:19; Gal. 3:23-24.", "norm_zh": "一在消极一面律法暴露人的罪叫罪人服在神面前律法也将神所拣选的人看守在其监管之下使他们可以被带到基督面前罗三20五20七78三19加三2324", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A On the negative side the law exposes mans sin and subdues sinners before God the law also guards Gods chosen people in its custody that they might be conducted to ChristRom 320 520 778 319 Gal 32324"}
{"zh": "二\t在积极一面，律法是神活的见证，其功用是将活神供应给寻求祂的人，也是神活的话，其功用是将神自己作为生命和光，分赐到那些爱律法的人里面—诗一一九2、88、25、116、130。", "en": "B. On the positive side, as God's living testimony, the law functions to minister the living God to His seekers, and as God's living word, the law functions to dispense God Himself as life and light into those who love the law.—Psa. 119:2, 88, 25, 116, 130.", "norm_zh": "二在积极一面律法是神活的见证其功用是将活神供应给寻求祂的人也是神活的话其功用是将神自己作为生命和光分赐到哪些爱律法的人里面诗一一九28825116130", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B On the positive side as Gods living testimony the law functions to minister the living God to His seekers and as Gods living word the law functions to dispense God Himself as life and light into those who love the lawPsa 1192 88 25 116 130"}
{"zh": "肆\t律法是神活的话，将神的本质灌注到爱祂的寻求者里面，使他们成为祂的见证，以完成祂永远的经纶—提后三16，约六57，徒一8：", "en": "IV.\tThe law is the living word of God to infuse His substance into His loving seekers to make them His testimony for the fulfillment of His eternal economy:—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:57; Acts 1:8:", "norm_zh": "肆律法是神活的话将神的本质灌注到爱祂的寻求者里面使他们成为祂的见证以完成祂永远的经纶提后三16约六57徒一8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The law is the living word of God to infuse His substance into His loving seekers to make them His testimony for the fulfillment of His eternal economy2 Tim 316 John 657 Acts 18"}
{"zh": "二\t律法作为神的十句话乃是神的气，将祂的成分传输到接受祂话的人里面—提后三16，耶十五16：", "en": "B.\tThe law as God's ten words is His breath to convey His element into the ones who receive His words.—2 Tim. 3:16; Jer. 15:16:", "norm_zh": "二律法作为神的十句话乃是神的气将祂的成分传输到接受祂话的人里面提后三16耶十五16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The law as Gods ten words is His breath to convey His element into the ones who receive His words2 Tim 316 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "1\t基督自己是神真实而活的律法，是神的话，神的气，神的彰显—西二9，约一18。", "en": "1.\tChrist Himself is God's real and living law, the Word of God, the breath of God, the expression of God.—Col. 2:9; John 1:18.", "norm_zh": "1基督自己是神真实而活的律法是神的话神的气神的彰显西二9约一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christ Himself is Gods real and living law the Word of God the breath of God the expression of GodCol 29 John 118"}
{"zh": "伍\t作为神的话，律法最高、最内在的功用乃是将神的本质分赐到我们里面，使我们与神是一，在生命、性情和彰显上，但不在神格上，与神一式一样—三19，林前六17：", "en": "V.\tThe highest and most intrinsic function of the law as God's word is to impart God's substance into us to make us one with God, the same as God in life, nature, and expression but not in the Godhead:—Eph. 3:19; 1 Cor. 6:17:", "norm_zh": "伍作为神的话律法最高最内在的功用乃是将神的本质分赐到我们里面使我们与神是一在生命性情和彰显上但不在神格上与神一式一样三19林前六17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The highest and most intrinsic function of the law as Gods word is to impart Gods substance into us to make us one with God the same as God in life nature and expression but not in the GodheadEph 319 1 Cor 617"}
{"zh": "二\t当我们借着神的话，被祂的本质注入时，我们就成了祂所是的，祂神圣的属性也彰显在我们的人性美德里—弗三19，罗九23。", "en": "B.\tWhen we are infused with God's substance through His word, we become what He is, and His divine attributes are expressed in our human virtues.—Eph. 3:19; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "二当我们借着神的话被祂的本质注入时我们就成了祂所是的祂神圣的属性也彰显在我们的人性美德里弗三19罗九23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we are infused with Gods substance through His word we become what He is and His divine attributes are expressed in our human virtuesEph 319 Rom 923"}
{"zh": "三\t我们遵守律法的要求，不是靠我们自己的努力，乃是凭那借着我们接触主，从祂所注入到我们里面的一切；一旦神的本质完全注入到我们里面，神自己这颁赐律法者，就要从我们里面遵守祂自己的律法—弗三20，罗八4，帖前二13。", "en": "C.\tWe keep the requirements of the law not by our own efforts but with what has been infused into us of the Lord through our contact with Him; once we have been thoroughly infused with God's substance, He Himself, the Law-giver, from within us will keep His own law.—Eph. 3:20; Rom. 8:4; 1 Thes. 2:13.", "norm_zh": "三我们遵守律法的要求不是靠我们自己的努力乃是凭哪借着我们接触主从祂所注入到我们里面的一切一旦神的本质完全注入到我们里面神自己这颁赐律法者就要从我们里面遵守祂自己的律法弗三20罗八4帖前二13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We keep the requirements of the law not by our own efforts but with what has been infused into us of the Lord through our contact with Him once we have been thoroughly infused with Gods substance He Himself the Lawgiver from within us will keep His own lawEph 320 Rom 84 1 Thes 213"}
{"zh": "陆\t借着神活的话而被神的本质所灌注，我们成为真正敬拜神的人，就是照着神的所是，符合神的所是，并返照神的所是，使神得着荣耀的人—约四24，五39~40，林后三18：", "en": "VI.\tBy being infused with God's substance through His living word, we become the true worshippers of God, those who are according to what God is, who correspond to what God is, and who reflect what God is for His glory:—John 4:24; 5:39-40; 2 Cor. 3:18:", "norm_zh": "陆借着神活的话而被神的本质所灌注我们成为真正敬拜神的人就是照着神的所是符合神的所是并返照神的所是使神得着荣耀的人约四24五3940林后三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI By being infused with Gods substance through His living word we become the true worshippers of God those who are according to what God is who correspond to what God is and who reflect what God is for His gloryJohn 424 53940 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "一\t真正敬拜神的人乃是被神注入并活出神，因而成为照着神所是并符合神所是的人；这种人的生活符合神的生活，并返照祂的所是，这就是耶稣活的见证—18节，弗三19，罗九23，八4。", "en": "A.\tA true worshipper of God is one who is infused with God and lives out God, who thereby becomes a person according to what God is and corresponding to what He is; the living of such a person corresponds to God's living and reflects what He is—this is the living testimony of Jesus.—v. 18; Eph. 3:19; Rom. 9:23; 8:4.", "norm_zh": "一真正敬拜神的人乃是被神注入并活出神因而成为照着神所是并符合神所是的人这种人的生活符合神的生活并返照祂的所是这就是耶稣活的见证18节弗三19罗九23八4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A true worshipper of God is one who is infused with God and lives out God who thereby becomes a person according to what God is and corresponding to what He is the living of such a person corresponds to Gods living and reflects what He isthis is the living testimony of Jesusv 18 Eph 319 Rom 923 84"}
{"zh": "柒\t地上最崇高的职业，就是花时间让神注入，使我们因神发光并将神照耀出来；这完成神永远的经纶，将祂自己作到人里面，使祂得着祂的见证，就是祂那扩大、扩展的彰显—林后三15~18。", "en": "VII.\tThe highest profession on earth is to spend time being infused with God so that we can glow with God and shine forth God; this accomplishes the eternal economy of God to work Himself into man so that He may have His testimony, His enlarged and expanded expression.—2 Cor. 3:15-18.", "norm_zh": "柒地上最崇高的职业就是花时间让神注入使我们因神发光并将神照耀出来这完成神永远的经纶将祂自己作到人里面使祂得着祂的见证就是祂哪扩大扩展的彰显林后三1518", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The highest profession on earth is to spend time being infused with God so that we can glow with God and shine forth God this accomplishes the eternal economy of God to work Himself into man so that He may have His testimony His enlarged and expanded expression2 Cor 31518"}
{"zh": "基督—律法的实际，作神的见证和神的话", "en": "Christ—the Reality of the Law as the Testimony and the Word of God", "norm_zh": "基督律法的实际作神的见证和神的话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Christthe Reality of the Law as the Testimony and the Word of God"}
{"zh": "一百三十二节说，“求你转向我，怜恤我，好像你素常待那些爱你名的人。”这节指明诗人爱神的名。五十五节说，“耶和华阿，我夜间记念你的名，遵守你的律法。”诗人夜间醒来，记念神的名。愿我们都爱神的名并记念神的名。", "en": "Verse 132 says, \"Turn to me, and have compassion on me, /As is Your custom with those who love Your name.\" This verse indicates that the psalmist loved God's name. Verse 55 says, \"I have remembered Your name in the night, O Jehovah,/And have kept Your law.\" When the psalmist awoke during the night, he remembered God's name. May we all love God's name and remember it.", "norm_zh": "一百三十二节说求你转向我怜恤我好像你素常待哪些爱你名的人这节指明诗人爱神的名五十五节说耶和华阿我夜间记念你的名遵守你的律法诗人夜间醒来记念神的名愿我们都爱神的名并记念神的名", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:31:05.082568+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Verse 132 says Turn to me and have compassion on me As is Your custom with those who love Your name This verse indicates that the psalmist loved Gods name Verse 55 says I have remembered Your name in the night O JehovahAnd have kept Your law When the psalmist awoke during the night he remembered Gods name May we all love Gods name and remember it"}
