{"zh": "一\t律法总是将制定律法者是怎样的人显明出来—出二十1~17。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十篇，第三段*）", "en": "A.\tA law is always a revelation of what kind of person has enacted that law.—Exo. 20:1-17.", "norm_zh": "一律法总是将制定律法者是怎样的人显明出来出二十1172015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第六十篇第三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A law is always a revelation of what kind of person has enacted that lawExo 20117"}
{"zh": "二\t神认为十条诫命，十条律法，乃是“十句话”—这进一步指明，律法是神自己的启示，因为一个人所说的话，就把那个人启示出来—申四13，出三四28，二十1：（1999年安那翰全时间训练，第十五篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十一篇，第九段*）", "en": "B. God regards the Ten Commandments, the ten laws, as “ten words”—this is a further indication that the law is God’s revelation of Himself, since the words a person speaks are a revelation of that person.—Deut. 4:13; Exo. 34:28; 20:1:", "norm_zh": "二神认为十条诫命十条律法乃是十句话这进一步指明律法是神自己的启示因为一个人所说的话就把哪个人启示出来申四13出三四28二十11999年安哪翰全时间训练第十五篇出埃及记生命读经第五十一篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God regards the Ten Commandments the ten laws as ten wordsthis is a further indication that the law is Gods revelation of Himself since the words a person speaks are a revelation of that personDeut 413 Exo 3428 201"}
{"zh": "4\t神是义的—诗十一7，出二十5。（2015年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，出二十1注1*）", "en": "4. God is righteous.—Psa. 11:7; Exo. 20:5.", "norm_zh": "4神是义的诗十一7出二十52015年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本出二十1注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 God is righteousPsa 117 Exo 205"}
{"zh": "四\t基督是律法（即神的见证）的实际；神的见证表征基督，神的具体化身，是神所是之活的描绘—二9，一15，约一18：（2015年夏训，第一篇；诗篇生命读经，第四十篇，第八段**）", "en": "D. Christ is the reality of the law as the testimony of God; the testimony of God signifies Christ, the embodiment of God, as the living portrait of what God is.—Col. 2:9; 1:15; John 1:18:", "norm_zh": "四基督是律法即神的见证的实际神的见证表征基督神的具体化身是神所是之活的描绘二9一15约一182015年夏训第一篇诗篇生命读经第四十篇第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Christ is the reality of the law as the testimony of God the testimony of God signifies Christ the embodiment of God as the living portrait of what God isCol 29 115 John 118"}
{"zh": "1\t律法是神的十句话，将神启示给祂的百姓；照样，基督是神的话，将神启示给我们—1、14节。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十一篇，第三十九段*）", "en": "1\tAs the law is the ten words of God that reveal God to His people, so Christ is the Word of God revealing God to us.—vv. 1, 14.", "norm_zh": "1律法是神的十句话将神启示给祂的百姓照样基督是神的话将神启示给我们114节2015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十一篇第三十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 As the law is the ten words of God that reveal God to His people so Christ is the Word of God revealing God to usvv 1 14"}
{"zh": "2\t我们不该想要从外面遵守律法，乃该让基督从我们里面活出来，使我们能成为神的见证，就是神彰显的扩展和扩大—罗八4，腓一20~21。（2015年夏训，第一篇；希伯来书生命读经，第六十三篇，第十九段**）", "en": "2\tWe should not try to keep the law from without but let Christ live Himself out from within so that we may become the testimony of God, the expansion and enlargement of God's expression.—Rom. 8:4; Phil. 1:20-21.", "norm_zh": "2我们不该想要从外面遵守律法乃该让基督从我们里面活出来使我们能成为神的见证就是神彰显的扩展和扩大罗八4腓一20212015年夏训第一篇希伯来书生命读经第六十三篇第十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We should not try to keep the law from without but let Christ live Himself out from within so that we may become the testimony of God the expansion and enlargement of Gods expressionRom 84 Phil 12021"}
{"zh": "一\t两种对待律法的人—爱神的寻求者和遵守律法字句的人—参创二9，林后三6、15~16：（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第十五段，第十七段**）", "en": "B.\tThere are two kinds of people dealing with the law—the loving seekers of God and the letter-keepers of the law.—cf. Gen. 2:9; 2 Cor. 3:6, 15-16:", "norm_zh": "一两种对待律法的人爱神的寻求者和遵守律法字句的人参创二9林后三615162015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第十五段第十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There are two kinds of people dealing with the lawthe loving seekers of God and the letterkeepers of the lawcf Gen 29 2 Cor 36 1516"}
{"zh": "1\t作诗的人是爱神的寻求者，他们爱那作为神的见证和神活话的律法—诗四二2，一一九2、10、127、147：（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第三十九段**）", "en": "1\tThe psalmists were the loving seekers of God, loving the law as the testimony of God and as His living word:—Psa. 42:2; 119:2, 10, 127, 147:", "norm_zh": "1作诗的人是爱神的寻求者他们爱哪作为神的见证和神活话的律法诗四二2一一九2101271472015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第三十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The psalmists were the loving seekers of God loving the law as the testimony of God and as His living wordPsa 422 1192 10 127 147"}
{"zh": "a\t他们爱神—十八1，七三25，一一六1。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第二十段**）", "en": "a\tThey loved God.—Psa. 18:1; 73:25; 116:1.", "norm_zh": "a他们爱神十八1七三25一一六12015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a They loved GodPsa 181 7325 1161"}
{"zh": "c\t他们宝爱神的律法—14、72、127节。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第三十八段*）", "en": "b\tThey treasured the law of God.—vv. 14, 72, 127.", "norm_zh": "c他们宝爱神的律法1472127节2015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第三十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b They treasured the law of Godvv 14 72 127"}
{"zh": "d\t他们尝到律法的甘美—103节。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第四十段*）", "en": "c\tThey tasted the sweetness of the law.—v. 103.", "norm_zh": "d他们尝到律法的甘美103节2015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第四十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c They tasted the sweetness of the lawv 103"}
{"zh": "e\t他们仰望并默想神的话—147~148节。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第四十二段*）", "en": "d\tThey hoped in the word of God and mused upon it.—vv. 147-148.", "norm_zh": "e他们仰望并默想神的话147148节2015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第四十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d They hoped in the word of God and mused upon itvv 147148"}
{"zh": "2\t热中犹太教者，就是墨守成规，拘泥于教条的遵守律法字句者，无心为着神，只为着杀死人的律法字句，在神之外寻求律法—太十五8，加六12~13。（2015年夏训，第一篇***）", "en": "2\tThe Judaizers, the legal and dogmatic letter-keepers of the law, had a heart not for God but for the killing letter of the law, seeking the law apart from God.—Matt. 15:8; Gal. 6:12-13.", "norm_zh": "2热中犹太教者就是墨守成规拘泥于教条的遵守律法字句者无心为着神只为着杀死人的律法字句在神之外寻求律法太十五8加六12132015年夏训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Judaizers the legal and dogmatic letterkeepers of the law had a heart not for God but for the killing letter of the law seeking the law apart from GodMatt 158 Gal 61213"}
{"zh": "3\t大数的扫罗得救以前，为律法大发热心；身为热中犹太教者，他甚至是亵渎神的，逼迫人的—腓三5~6，提前一13。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第五十一段）", "en": "3. Before he was saved, Saul of Tarsus was zealous for the law; as a Judaizer, he was even a blasphemer of God and a persecutor of man.—Phil. 3:5-6; 1 Tim. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "3大数的扫罗得救以前为律法大发热心身为热中犹太教者他甚至是亵渎神的逼迫人的腓三56提前一132015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第五十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Before he was saved Saul of Tarsus was zealous for the law as a Judaizer he was even a blasphemer of God and a persecutor of manPhil 356 1 Tim 113"}
{"zh": "二\t我们来就近律法的态度，若只是关切字句的诫命，我们所有的就是律法在杀死人的字句这一面—约五39~40，林后三6：（2011年冬训，第八篇；诗篇生命读经，第四十篇，第二十段*）", "en": "B.\tIf our attitude in coming to the law is to care only for the commandments in letters, we will have the law in the aspect of the killing letter:—John 5:39-40; 2 Cor. 3:6:", "norm_zh": "二我们来就近律法的态度若只是关切字句的诫命我们所有的就是律法在杀死人的字句这一面约五3940林后三62011年冬训第八篇诗篇生命读经第四十篇第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B If our attitude in coming to the law is to care only for the commandments in letters we will have the law in the aspect of the killing letterJohn 53940 2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t我们到律法这里来，若不在爱里寻求神，反而把律法与活的神这生命的源头分开，那原本为要带进生命，本身却不能赐生命的律法，对我们就成为定罪和杀死的元素—参约五39~40，加三21。（2011年冬训，第八篇；圣经恢复本，出十九8注1 *）", "en": "2. If in coming to the law we do not seek God in love but rather separate the law from the living God as the source of life, the law, which was intended to result in life but cannot give life of itself, will become a condemning and killing element to us.—cf. John 5:39-40; Gal. 3:21.", "norm_zh": "2我们到律法这里来若不在爱里寻求神反而把律法与活的神这生命的源头分开哪原本为要带进生命本身却不能赐生命的律法对我们就成为定罪和杀死的元素参约五3940加三212011年冬训第八篇圣经恢复本出十九8注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If in coming to the law we do not seek God in love but rather separate the law from the living God as the source of life the law which was intended to result in life but cannot give life of itself will become a condemning and killing element to uscf John 53940 Gal 321"}
{"zh": "三\t然而，我们若将律法的每一部分—所有的诫命、规条、律例、训辞和判语，当作我们所爱之神呼出的话，我们就会有律法赐生命之灵的这一面—提后三16，约六63：（2011年冬训，第八篇；圣经恢复本，诗一一九50注1*）", "en": "C. However, if we take every part of the law—all the commandments, ordinances, statutes, precepts, and judgments—as the word breathed out by the God whom we love, we will have the law in the aspect of the life-giving Spirit.—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:63:", "norm_zh": "三然而我们若将律法的每一部分所有的诫命规条律例训辞和判语当作我们所爱之神呼出的话我们就会有律法赐生命之灵的这一面提后三16约六632011年冬训第八篇圣经恢复本诗一一九50注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C However if we take every part of the lawall the commandments ordinances statutes precepts and judgmentsas the word breathed out by the God whom we love we will have the law in the aspect of the lifegiving Spirit2 Tim 316 John 663"}
{"zh": "1\t我们若爱神，谦卑自己，把律法当作神活的话，借以接触祂并住在祂里面，律法就要成为管道，借此将神圣的生命和本质传输给我们，作我们的供应和滋养—63节，加三5，彼后一11。（2015年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，出十九8注1）", "en": "1.\tIf we love God, humble ourselves, and regard the law as His living word through which we contact Him and abide in Him, the law will become a channel through which the divine life and substance are conveyed to us for our supply and nourishment.—v. 63; Gal. 3:5; 2 Pet. 1:11.", "norm_zh": "1我们若爱神谦卑自己把律法当作神活的话借以接触祂并住在祂里面律法就要成为管道借此将神圣的生命和本质传输给我们作我们的供应和滋养63节加三5彼后一112015年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本出十九8注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 If we love God humble ourselves and regard the law as His living word through which we contact Him and abide in Him the law will become a channel through which the divine life and substance are conveyed to us for our supply and nourishmentv 63 Gal 35 2 Pet 111"}
{"zh": "叁\t律法有两面的功用—罗五20，加三23~24，诗一一九2、130：（2015年夏训，第一篇；诗篇生命读经，第四十篇，第二十一段*）", "en": "III.\tThe function of the law has two aspects:—Rom. 5:20; Gal. 3:23-24; Psa. 119:2, 130:", "norm_zh": "叁律法有两面的功用罗五20加三2324诗一一九21302015年夏训第一篇诗篇生命读经第四十篇第二十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The function of the law has two aspectsRom 520 Gal 32324 Psa 1192 130"}
{"zh": "一\t在消极一面，律法暴露人的罪，叫罪人服在神面前；律法也将神所拣选的人看守在其监管之下，使他们可以被带到基督面前—罗三20，五20，七7~8，三19，加三23~24。（2015年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，诗一一九50注1*）", "en": "A. On the negative side, the law exposes man's sin and subdues sinners before God; the law also guards God's chosen people in its custody that they might be conducted to Christ.—Rom. 3:20; 5:20; 7:7-8; 3:19; Gal. 3:23-24.", "norm_zh": "一在消极一面律法暴露人的罪叫罪人服在神面前律法也将神所拣选的人看守在其监管之下使他们可以被带到基督面前罗三20五20七78三19加三23242015年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本诗一一九50注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A On the negative side the law exposes mans sin and subdues sinners before God the law also guards Gods chosen people in its custody that they might be conducted to ChristRom 320 520 778 319 Gal 32324"}
{"zh": "二\t在积极一面，律法是神活的见证，其功用是将活神供应给寻求祂的人，也是神活的话，其功用是将神自己作为生命和光，分赐到那些爱律法的人里面—诗一一九2、88、25、116、130。（2015年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，诗一一九50注1**）", "en": "B. On the positive side, as God's living testimony, the law functions to minister the living God to His seekers, and as God's living word, the law functions to dispense God Himself as life and light into those who love the law.—Psa. 119:2, 88, 25, 116, 130.", "norm_zh": "二在积极一面律法是神活的见证其功用是将活神供应给寻求祂的人也是神活的话其功用是将神自己作为生命和光分赐到哪些爱律法的人里面诗一一九288251161302015年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本诗一一九50注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B On the positive side as Gods living testimony the law functions to minister the living God to His seekers and as Gods living word the law functions to dispense God Himself as life and light into those who love the lawPsa 1192 88 25 116 130"}
{"zh": "肆\t律法是神活的话，将神的本质灌注到爱祂的寻求者里面，使他们成为祂的见证，以完成祂永远的经纶—提后三16，约六57，徒一8：（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第十四段**）", "en": "IV.\tThe law is the living word of God to infuse His substance into His loving seekers to make them His testimony for the fulfillment of His eternal economy:—2 Tim. 3:16; John 6:57; Acts 1:8:", "norm_zh": "肆律法是神活的话将神的本质灌注到爱祂的寻求者里面使他们成为祂的见证以完成祂永远的经纶提后三16约六57徒一82015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The law is the living word of God to infuse His substance into His loving seekers to make them His testimony for the fulfillment of His eternal economy2 Tim 316 John 657 Acts 18"}
{"zh": "二\t律法作为神的十句话乃是神的气，将祂的成分传输到接受祂话的人里面—提后三16，耶十五16：（2015年夏训，第一篇***）", "en": "B.\tThe law as God's ten words is His breath to convey His element into those who receive His words:—2 Tim. 3:16; Jer. 15:16:", "norm_zh": "二律法作为神的十句话乃是神的气将祂的成分传输到接受祂话的人里面提后三16耶十五162015年夏训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The law as Gods ten words is His breath to convey His element into those who receive His words2 Tim 316 Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "1\t基督自己是神真实而活的律法，是神的话，神的气，神的彰显—西二9，约一18。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第五十八段**）", "en": "1.\tChrist Himself is God's real and living law, the Word of God, the breath of God, the expression of God.—Col. 2:9; John 1:18.", "norm_zh": "1基督自己是神真实而活的律法是神的话神的气神的彰显西二9约一182015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第五十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christ Himself is Gods real and living law the Word of God the breath of God the expression of GodCol 29 John 118"}
{"zh": "伍\t作为神的话，律法最高、最内在的功用乃是将神的本质分赐到我们里面，使我们与神是一，在生命、性情和彰显上，但不在神格上，与神一式一样—三19，林前六17：（2015年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，王上四30注1**）", "en": "V.\tThe highest and most intrinsic function of the law as God's word is to impart God's substance into us to make us one with God, the same as God in life, nature, and expression but not in the Godhead:—Eph. 3:19; 1 Cor. 6:17:", "norm_zh": "伍作为神的话律法最高最内在的功用乃是将神的本质分赐到我们里面使我们与神是一在生命性情和彰显上但不在神格上与神一式一样三19林前六172015年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本王上四30注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The highest and most intrinsic function of the law as Gods word is to impart Gods substance into us to make us one with God the same as God in life nature and expression but not in the GodheadEph 319 1 Cor 617"}
{"zh": "二\t当我们借着神的话，被祂的本质注入时，我们就成了祂所是的，祂神圣的属性也彰显在我们的人性美德里—弗三19，罗九23。（2015年夏训，第一篇***）", "en": "B.\tWhen we are infused with God's substance through His word, we become what He is, and His divine attributes are expressed in our human virtues.—Eph. 3:19; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "二当我们借着神的话被祂的本质注入时我们就成了祂所是的祂神圣的属性也彰显在我们的人性美德里弗三19罗九232015年夏训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we are infused with Gods substance through His word we become what He is and His divine attributes are expressed in our human virtuesEph 319 Rom 923"}
{"zh": "三\t我们遵守律法的要求，不是靠我们自己的努力，乃是凭那借着我们接触主，从祂所注入到我们里面的一切；一旦神的本质完全注入到我们里面，神自己这颁赐律法者，就要从我们里面遵守祂自己的律法—弗三20，罗八4，帖前二13。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第十四段**）", "en": "C.\tWe keep the requirements of the law not by our own efforts but with what has been infused into us of the Lord through our contact with Him; once we have been thoroughly infused with God's substance, He Himself, the Law-giver, from within us will keep His own law.—Eph. 3:20; Rom. 8:4; 1 Thes. 2:13.", "norm_zh": "三我们遵守律法的要求不是靠我们自己的努力乃是凭哪借着我们接触主从祂所注入到我们里面的一切一旦神的本质完全注入到我们里面神自己这颁赐律法者就要从我们里面遵守祂自己的律法弗三20罗八4帖前二132015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We keep the requirements of the law not by our own efforts but with what has been infused into us of the Lord through our contact with Him once we have been thoroughly infused with Gods substance He Himself the Lawgiver from within us will keep His own lawEph 320 Rom 84 1 Thes 213"}
{"zh": "陆\t借着神活的话而被神的本质所灌注，我们成为真正敬拜神的人，就是照着神的所是，符合神的所是，并返照神的所是，使神得着荣耀的人—约四24，五39~40，林后三18：（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第五十三段**）", "en": "VI.\tBy being infused with God's substance through His living word, we become the true worshippers of God, those who are according to what God is, who correspond to what God is, and who reflect what God is for His glory:—John 4:24; 5:39-40; 2 Cor. 3:18:", "norm_zh": "陆借着神活的话而被神的本质所灌注我们成为真正敬拜神的人就是照着神的所是符合神的所是并返照神的所是使神得着荣耀的人约四24五3940林后三182015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第五十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI By being infused with Gods substance through His living word we become the true worshippers of God those who are according to what God is who correspond to what God is and who reflect what God is for His gloryJohn 424 53940 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "一\t真正敬拜神的人乃是被神注入并活出神，因而成为照着神所是并符合神所是的人；这种人的生活符合神的生活，并返照祂的所是，这就是耶稣活的见证—18节，弗三19，罗九23，八4。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十二篇，第五十三段）", "en": "A.\tA true worshipper of God is one who is infused with God and lives out God, who thereby becomes a person according to what God is and corresponding to what He is; the living of such a person corresponds to God's living and reflects what He is—this is the living testimony of Jesus.—v. 18; Eph. 3:19; Rom. 9:23; 8:4.", "norm_zh": "一真正敬拜神的人乃是被神注入并活出神因而成为照着神所是并符合神所是的人这种人的生活符合神的生活并返照祂的所是这就是耶稣活的见证18节弗三19罗九23八42015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第五十二篇第五十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A true worshipper of God is one who is infused with God and lives out God who thereby becomes a person according to what God is and corresponding to what He is the living of such a person corresponds to Gods living and reflects what He isthis is the living testimony of Jesusv 18 Eph 319 Rom 923 84"}
{"zh": "柒\t地上最崇高的职业，就是花时间让神注入，使我们因神发光并将神照耀出来；这完成神永远的经纶，将祂自己作到人里面，使祂得着祂的见证，就是祂那扩大、扩展的彰显—林后三15~18。（2015年夏训，第一篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十二篇，第三十二段**）", "en": "VII.\tThe highest profession on earth is to spend time being infused with God so that we can glow with God and shine forth God; this accomplishes the eternal economy of God to work Himself into man so that He may have His testimony, His enlarged and expanded expression.—2 Cor. 3:15-18.", "norm_zh": "柒地上最崇高的职业就是花时间让神注入使我们因神发光并将神照耀出来这完成神永远的经纶将祂自己作到人里面使祂得着祂的见证就是祂哪扩大扩展的彰显林后三15182015年夏训第一篇出埃及记生命读经第六十二篇第三十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:34:21.230732+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The highest profession on earth is to spend time being infused with God so that we can glow with God and shine forth God this accomplishes the eternal economy of God to work Himself into man so that He may have His testimony His enlarged and expanded expression2 Cor 31518"}
{"zh": "读经：出二十1~12，三四27~29，赛五四5，耶二2，三一3、32，结十六8，何二19~20", "en": "Scripture Reading: Exo. 20:1-12; 34:27-29; Isa. 54:5; Jer. 2:2; 31:3, 32; Ezek. 16:8; Hos. 2:19-20", "norm_zh": "读经出二十112三四2729赛五四5耶二2三一332结十六8何二1920", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Exo 20112 342729 Isa 545 Jer 22 313 32 Ezek 168 Hos 21920"}
{"zh": "壹\t全本圣经的主题、神经纶的内容、以及整个宇宙的秘密，乃是神与祂所拣选并救赎的人之间神圣的罗曼史—歌一2~4，耶二2，三一3，弗五32，启十九7：", "en": "I.\tThe subject of the entire Bible, the content of God's economy, and the secret of the entire universe are the divine romance between God and His chosen and redeemed people:—S.S. 1:2-4; Jer. 2:2; 31:3; Eph. 5:32; Rev. 19:7:", "norm_zh": "壹全本圣经的主提神经纶的内容以及整个宇宙的秘密乃是神与祂所拣选并救赎的人之间神圣的罗曼史歌一24耶二2三一3弗五32启十九7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The subject of the entire Bible the content of Gods economy and the secret of the entire universe are the divine romance between God and His chosen and redeemed peopleSS 124 Jer 22 313 Eph 532 Rev 197"}
{"zh": "四\t我们不是运用心思和意志来遵守律法，乃是借着爱这位作我们丈夫的主，因而有分于祂的生命和性情，与祂成为一，作祂的扩大和彰显—参罗七18~25。", "en": "D. We keep the law not by exercising our mind and will but by loving the Lord as our Husband and thereby partaking of His life and nature to become one with Him as His enlargement and expression.—cf. Rom. 7:18-25.", "norm_zh": "四我们不是运用心思和意志来遵守律法乃是借着爱这位作我们丈夫的主因而有分于祂的生命和性情与祂成为一作祂的扩大和彰显参罗七1825", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D We keep the law not by exercising our mind and will but by loving the Lord as our Husband and thereby partaking of His life and nature to become one with Him as His enlargement and expressioncf Rom 71825"}
{"zh": "一\t神领祂的百姓出埃及，又将律法颁赐给他们，乃是追求他们，向他们求婚，并寻求得着他们的情爱—耶三一3，何二19~20。", "en": "A.\tIn bringing His people out of Egypt and giving His law to them, God was courting them, wooing them, and seeking to win their affection.—Jer. 31:3; Hos. 2:19-20.", "norm_zh": "一神领祂的百姓出埃及又将律法颁赐给他们乃是追求他们向他们求婚并寻求得着他们的情爱耶三一3何二1920", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In bringing His people out of Egypt and giving His law to them God was courting them wooing them and seeking to win their affectionJer 313 Hos 21920"}
{"zh": "二\t耶利米二章二节，三十一章三十二节，和以西结十六章八节指明，在神的山借着颁赐律法所立的约，乃是婚约；借此，神聘以色列人归祂自己—出二四7~8，三四27~28， 参林后十一2：", "en": "B. Jer. 2:2, 31:32, and Ezek. 16:8 indicate that the covenant enacted at the mountain of God through the giving of the law was an engagement covenant, by which God betrothed the children of Israel to Himself.—Exo. 24:7-8; 34:27-28; cf. 2 Cor. 11:2:", "norm_zh": "二耶利米二章二节三十一章三十二节和以西结十六章八节指明在神的山借着颁赐律法所立的约乃是婚约借此神聘以色列人归祂自己出二四78三四2728参林后十一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Jer 22 3132 and Ezek 168 indicate that the covenant enacted at the mountain of God through the giving of the law was an engagement covenant by which God betrothed the children of Israel to HimselfExo 2478 342728 cf 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "三\t以西结十六章八节和耶利米三十一章三十二节都用约这个字，指在出埃及二十章所颁赐的律法；神颁赐律法时，聘以色列人归祂自己，以色列人便与神订了婚；这就是耶利米二章二节所说“新婚的爱情”。", "en": "C.\tBoth Ezekiel 16:8 and Jeremiah 31:32 use the word covenant, a word that refers to the law given in Exodus 20; when God gave the law, He betrothed Israel unto Himself, and Israel became engaged to Him; this is what Jeremiah 2:2 refers to in saying, \"The love of your bridal days.\"", "norm_zh": "三以西结十六章八节和耶利米三十一章三十二节都用约这个字指在出埃及二十章所颁赐的律法神颁赐律法时聘以色列人归祂自己以色列人便与神订了婚这就是耶利米二章二节所说新婚的爱情", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Both Ezekiel 168 and Jeremiah 3132 use the word covenant a word that refers to the law given in Exodus 20 when God gave the law He betrothed Israel unto Himself and Israel became engaged to Him this is what Jeremiah 22 refers to in saying The love of your bridal days"}
{"zh": "四\t神颁赐律法的目标，是要使祂的选民与祂成为一，就如妻子与她的丈夫成为一；然后律法要将神的本质分赐到他们里面，引他们到神里面，并且使他们在生命和性情上与神联结—创二24，何二19~20，耶三一33。", "en": "D.\tGod's goal in giving the law was to make His chosen people one with Him as a wife is one with her husband; the law would then impart God's substance into them, usher them into God, and unite them with God in life and nature.—Gen. 2:24; Hos. 2:19-20; Jer. 31:33.", "norm_zh": "四神颁赐律法的目标是要使祂的选民与祂成为一就如妻子与她的丈夫成为一然后律法要将神的本质分赐到他们里面引他们到神里面并且使他们在生命和性情上与神联结创二24何二1920耶三一33", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods goal in giving the law was to make His chosen people one with Him as a wife is one with her husband the law would then impart Gods substance into them usher them into God and unite them with God in life and natureGen 224 Hos 21920 Jer 3133"}
{"zh": "叁\t神将律法赐给祂百姓时，寻找爱祂的人；并且颁赐律法乃是办理神的百姓和神的订婚—32节，结十六8，出三四27，何二19~20：", "en": "III.\tIn giving His law to His people, God was seeking lovers, and the giving of the law was a transaction in which God's people became engaged to Him:—v. 32; Ezek. 16:8; Exo. 34:27; Hos. 2:19-20:", "norm_zh": "叁神将律法赐给祂百姓时寻找爱祂的人并且颁赐律法乃是办理神的百姓和神的订婚32节结十六8出三四27何二1920", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III In giving His law to His people God was seeking lovers and the giving of the law was a transaction in which Gods people became engaged to Himv 32 Ezek 168 Exo 3427 Hos 21920"}
{"zh": "一\t律法乃是神和祂百姓之间的婚约—耶三一32，出三四27，林后十一2：", "en": "A.\tThe law was an engagement covenant between God and His people:—Jer. 31:32; Exo. 34:27; 2 Cor. 11:2:", "norm_zh": "一律法乃是神和祂百姓之间的婚约耶三一32出三四27林后十一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The law was an engagement covenant between God and His peopleJer 3132 Exo 3427 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "1\t神以永远的爱爱祂的百姓—耶三一3，加六16，帖前一4，弗一4。", "en": "1.\tGod loves His people with an eternal love.—Jer. 31:3; Gal. 6:16; 1 Thes. 1:4; Eph. 1:4.", "norm_zh": "1神以永远的爱爱祂的百姓耶三一3加六16帖前一4弗一4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God loves His people with an eternal loveJer 313 Gal 616 1 Thes 14 Eph 14"}
{"zh": "2\t出埃及记前十九章乃是神追求祂的百姓，甚至与他们“约会”，正如耶利米二章二节所指明的。", "en": "2.\tIn the first nineteen chapters of Exodus, God was courting, even \"dating,\" His people, as indicated by Jeremiah 2:2.", "norm_zh": "2出埃及记前十九章乃是神追求祂的百姓甚至与他们约会正如耶利米二章二节所指明的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the first nineteen chapters of Exodus God was courting even dating His people as indicated by Jeremiah 22"}
{"zh": "二\t以色列人和神订婚发生在出埃及二十章神的山那里，而律法是正式的证书，敍述这个订婚的条件；十诫，特别是前五条，乃是神和祂的百姓之间订婚的条件—出二十1~12。", "en": "B.\tThe betrothal of Israel took place at the mountain of God in Exodus 20, and the law was the official paper stating the conditions for this engagement; the Ten Commandments, especially the first five, gave the terms of the engagement between God and His people.—Exo. 20:1-12.", "norm_zh": "二以色列人和神订婚发生在出埃及二十章神的山哪里而律法是正式的证书敍述这个订婚的条件十诫特别是前五条乃是神和祂的百姓之间订婚的条件出二十112", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The betrothal of Israel took place at the mountain of God in Exodus 20 and the law was the official paper stating the conditions for this engagement the Ten Commandments especially the first five gave the terms of the engagement between God and His peopleExo 20112"}
{"zh": "三\t前五条诫命是在亲密的气氛中颁赐的；当神爱恋地追求祂的百姓时，一再亲密地使用“耶和华你的神”这个说法—2、12节：", "en": "C.\tThe first five commandments were given in an atmosphere of intimacy, with the expression Jehovah your God uttered intimately again and again as God lovingly courted His people:—vv. 2, 12:", "norm_zh": "三前五条诫命是在亲密的气氛中颁赐的当神爱恋地追求祂的百姓时一再亲密地使用耶和华你的神这个说法212节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The first five commandments were given in an atmosphere of intimacy with the expression Jehovah your God uttered intimately again and again as God lovingly courted His peoplevv 2 12"}
{"zh": "四\t律法是订婚证书，婚约，其最高的功用，乃是将神的选民带到与神成为一，如同妻子与丈夫成为一，使他们成为祂扩大并扩展的彰显，就是祂的见证—参创二24，启二二17， 出二五21~22，三八21。", "en": "D. The law is an engagement paper, an engagement covenant, the highest function of which is to bring God's chosen people into oneness with Him, as a wife is brought into oneness with her husband, to make them His enlarged and expanded expression, which is His testimony.—cf. Gen. 2:24; Rev. 22:17; Exo. 25:21-22; 38:21.", "norm_zh": "四律法是订婚证书婚约其最高的功用乃是将神的选民带到与神成为一如同妻子与丈夫成为一使他们成为祂扩大并扩展的彰显就是祂的见证参创二24启二二17出二五2122三八21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The law is an engagement paper an engagement covenant the highest function of which is to bring Gods chosen people into oneness with Him as a wife is brought into oneness with her husband to make them His enlarged and expanded expression which is His testimonycf Gen 224 Rev 2217 Exo 252122 3821"}
{"zh": "2\t当神的子民爱神，花时间在祂的话里与祂交通，神就将祂神圣的元素注入他们里面，使他们与祂成为一，作祂的配偶，在生命、性情和彰显上与祂一样—申三十20上，罗九23。", "en": "2\tAs God's people love God and spend time to fellowship with Him in His word, God infuses them with His divine element, making them one with Him as His spouse, the same as He is in life, nature, and expression.—Deut. 30:20a; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "2当神的子民爱神花时间在祂的话里与祂交通神就将祂神圣的元素注入他们里面使他们与祂成为一作祂的配偶在生命性情和彰显上与祂一样申三十20上罗九23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 As Gods people love God and spend time to fellowship with Him in His word God infuses them with His divine element making them one with Him as His spouse the same as He is in life nature and expressionDeut 3020a Rom 923"}
{"zh": "二\t只要我们爱主和主的话，只要我们与祂同在而被祂注入，我们自己所作不到的，祂就要在我们里面来作成—约十四21，腓二13，罗八4：", "en": "B.\tAs long as we love the Lord and His word and as long as we stay with Him to be infused with Him, He will do in us what we cannot do ourselves:—John 14:21; Phil. 2:13; Rom. 8:4:", "norm_zh": "二只要我们爱主和主的话只要我们与祂同在而被祂注入我们自己所作不到的祂就要在我们里面来作成约十四21腓二13罗八4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B As long as we love the Lord and His word and as long as we stay with Him to be infused with Him He will do in us what we cannot do ourselvesJohn 1421 Phil 213 Rom 84"}
{"zh": "4\t因着我们爱神，我们也爱神活的话；这活的话将祂的本质注入我们里面，就使我们因祂发光—耶十五16，出三四28~29：", "en": "4\tBecause we love God, we also love His living word, which infuses His substance into us to cause us to glow with Him.—Jer. 15:16; Exo. 34:28-29:", "norm_zh": "4因着我们爱神我们也爱神活的话这活的话将祂的本质注入我们里面就使我们因祂发光耶十五16出三四2829", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Because we love God we also love His living word which infuses His substance into us to cause us to glow with HimJer 1516 Exo 342829"}
{"zh": "a\t摩西在何烈山（西乃山）顶，没有挣扎努力去履行律法的要求；反之，他是被神借着与他说话所注入，而他发光的脸不过是返照神的所是—28~29节，参林后三18~四6。", "en": "a\tWhen Moses was on the top of Mount Horeb (Mount Sinai), he was not striving or working to fulfill the requirements of the law; rather, he was being infused with God by God's speaking with him, and his glowing face was simply a reflection of what God is—Exo. 34:28-29; cf. 2 Cor. 3:18.—vv. 28-29; cf. 2 Cor. 3:18—4:6.", "norm_zh": "a摩西在何烈山西乃山顶没有挣扎努力去履行律法的要求反之他是被神借着与他说话所注入而他发光的脸不过是返照神的所是2829节参林后三18四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a When Moses was on the top of Mount Horeb Mount Sinai he was not striving or working to fulfill the requirements of the law rather he was being infused with God by Gods speaking with him and his glowing face was simply a reflection of what God isExo 342829 cf 2 Cor 318vv 2829 cf 2 Cor 31846"}
{"zh": "b\t我们被主所注入，自然而然就会发光，成为祂活的描绘、祂的见证；我们不会努力挣扎，只会发光。", "en": "b\tAs we are infused with the Lord, we will shine spontaneously to become His living portrait, His testimony; we will not work or strive but simply glow.", "norm_zh": "b我们被主所注入自然而然就会发光成为祂活的描绘祂的见证我们不会努力挣扎只会发光", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b As we are infused with the Lord we will shine spontaneously to become His living portrait His testimony we will not work or strive but simply glow"}
{"zh": "三\t那些借着爱神和神的话而遵守律法，因而与神成为一的人，过神人的生活，有神的形像，是神的描绘和神的复制—约十四21，腓三9~11，罗九23，约十二24。", "en": "C.\tThose who keep the law by loving God and His word to become one with Him have the living of a God-man to bear the image of God, being a portrait of God and a duplication of God.—John 14:21; Phil. 3:9-11; Rom. 9:23; John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "三哪些借着爱神和神的话而遵守律法因而与神成为一的人过神人的生活有神的形像是神的描绘和神的复制约十四21腓三911罗九23约十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Those who keep the law by loving God and His word to become one with Him have the living of a Godman to bear the image of God being a portrait of God and a duplication of GodJohn 1421 Phil 3911 Rom 923 John 1224"}
{"zh": "神将律法赐给祂选民的心意，是要他们成为爱祂的人", "en": "God's intention in giving the law to His chosen people was that they become those who love Him.", "norm_zh": "神将律法赐给祂选民的心意是要他们成为爱祂的人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods intention in giving the law to His chosen people was that they become those who love Him"}
