{"zh": "神寻找一班爱祂的人", "en": "God is seeking a people to love Him", "norm_zh": "神寻找一班爱祂的人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:35:43.824398+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "God is seeking a people to love Him"}
{"zh": "壹\t全本圣经的主题、神经纶的内容、以及整个宇宙的秘密，乃是神与祂所拣选并救赎的人之间神圣的罗曼史—歌一2~4，耶二2，三一3，弗五32，启十九7：（2015年夏训，第二篇；新约总论，第二百一十三篇，第二十八段**）", "en": "I.\tThe subject of the entire Bible, the content of God's economy, and the secret of the entire universe are the divine romance between God and His chosen and redeemed people:—S.S. 1:2-4; Jer. 2:2; 31:3; Eph. 5:32; Rev. 19:7:", "norm_zh": "壹全本圣经的主提神经纶的内容以及整个宇宙的秘密乃是神与祂所拣选并救赎的人之间神圣的罗曼史歌一24耶二2三一3弗五32启十九72015年夏训第二篇新约总论第二百一十三篇第二十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The subject of the entire Bible the content of Gods economy and the secret of the entire universe are the divine romance between God and His chosen and redeemed peopleSS 124 Jer 22 313 Eph 532 Rev 197"}
{"zh": "四\t我们不是运用心思和意志来遵守律法，乃是借着爱这位作我们丈夫的主，因而有分于祂的生命和性情，与祂成为一，作祂的扩大和彰显—参罗七18~25。（2015年夏训，第二篇；圣经恢复本，出二十6注1）", "en": "D. We keep the law not by exercising our mind and will but by loving the Lord as our Husband and thereby partaking of His life and nature to become one with Him as His enlargement and expression.—cf. Rom. 7:18-25.", "norm_zh": "四我们不是运用心思和意志来遵守律法乃是借着爱这位作我们丈夫的主因而有分于祂的生命和性情与祂成为一作祂的扩大和彰显参罗七18252015年夏训第二篇圣经恢复本出二十6注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D We keep the law not by exercising our mind and will but by loving the Lord as our Husband and thereby partaking of His life and nature to become one with Him as His enlargement and expressioncf Rom 71825"}
{"zh": "一\t神领祂的百姓出埃及，又将律法颁赐给他们，乃是追求他们，向他们求婚，并寻求得着他们的情爱—耶三一3，何二19~20。（2015年夏训，第二篇；圣经恢复本，出二十6注1）", "en": "A.\tIn bringing His people out of Egypt and giving His law to them, God was courting them, wooing them, and seeking to win their affection.—Jer. 31:3; Hos. 2:19-20.", "norm_zh": "一神领祂的百姓出埃及又将律法颁赐给他们乃是追求他们向他们求婚并寻求得着他们的情爱耶三一3何二19202015年夏训第二篇圣经恢复本出二十6注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In bringing His people out of Egypt and giving His law to them God was courting them wooing them and seeking to win their affectionJer 313 Hos 21920"}
{"zh": "二\t耶利米二章二节，三十一章三十二节，和以西结十六章八节指明，在神的山借着颁赐律法所立的约，乃是婚约；借此，神聘以色列人归祂自己—出二四7~8，三四27~28， 参林后十一2：（2015年夏训，第二篇；圣经恢复本，出二十6注1*）", "en": "B. Jer. 2:2, 31:32, and Ezek. 16:8 indicate that the covenant enacted at the mountain of God through the giving of the law was an engagement covenant, by which God betrothed Israel unto Himself.—Exo. 24:7-8; 34:27-28; cf. 2 Cor. 11:2:", "norm_zh": "二耶利米二章二节三十一章三十二节和以西结十六章八节指明在神的山借着颁赐律法所立的约乃是婚约借此神聘以色列人归祂自己出二四78三四2728参林后十一22015年夏训第二篇圣经恢复本出二十6注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Jer 22 3132 and Ezek 168 indicate that the covenant enacted at the mountain of God through the giving of the law was an engagement covenant by which God betrothed Israel unto HimselfExo 2478 342728 cf 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "三\t以西结十六章八节和耶利米三十一章三十二节都用约这个字，指在出埃及二十章所颁赐的律法；神颁赐律法时，聘以色列人归祂自己，以色列人便与神订了婚；这就是耶利米二章二节所说“新婚的爱情”。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第七段**）", "en": "C.\tBoth Ezekiel 16:8 and Jeremiah 31:32 use the word covenant, a word that refers to the law given in Exodus 20; when God gave the law, He betrothed Israel unto Himself, and Israel became engaged to Him; this is what Jeremiah 2:2 refers to in saying, \"the love of your bridal days.\"", "norm_zh": "三以西结十六章八节和耶利米三十一章三十二节都用约这个字指在出埃及二十章所颁赐的律法神颁赐律法时聘以色列人归祂自己以色列人便与神订了婚这就是耶利米二章二节所说新婚的爱情2015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Both Ezekiel 168 and Jeremiah 3132 use the word covenant a word that refers to the law given in Exodus 20 when God gave the law He betrothed Israel unto Himself and Israel became engaged to Him this is what Jeremiah 22 refers to in saying the love of your bridal days"}
{"zh": "四\t神颁赐律法的目标，是要使祂的选民与祂成为一，就如妻子与她的丈夫成为一；然后律法要将神的本质分赐到他们里面，引他们到神里面，并且使他们在生命和性情上与神联结—创二24，何二19~20，耶三一33。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十五篇，第三十九段*）", "en": "D.\tGod's goal in giving the law was to make His chosen people one with Him as a wife is one with her husband; the law would then impart God's substance into them, usher them into God, and unite them with God in life and nature.—Gen. 2:24; Hos. 2:19-20; Jer. 31:33.", "norm_zh": "四神颁赐律法的目标是要使祂的选民与祂成为一就如妻子与她的丈夫成为一然后律法要将神的本质分赐到他们里面引他们到神里面并且使他们在生命和性情上与神联结创二24何二1920耶三一332015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十五篇第三十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods goal in giving the law was to make His chosen people one with Him as a wife is one with her husband the law would then impart Gods substance into them usher them into God and unite them with God in life and natureGen 224 Hos 21920 Jer 3133"}
{"zh": "叁\t神将律法赐给祂百姓时，寻找爱祂的人；并且颁赐律法乃是办理神的百姓和神的订婚—32节，结十六8，出三四27，何二19~20：（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第〇段**，第六段）", "en": "III.\tIn giving His law to His people, God was seeking lovers, and the giving of the law was a transaction in which God's people became engaged to Him:—v. 32; Ezek. 16:8; Exo. 34:27; Hos. 2:19-20:", "norm_zh": "叁神将律法赐给祂百姓时寻找爱祂的人并且颁赐律法乃是办理神的百姓和神的订婚32节结十六8出三四27何二19202015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第〇段第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III In giving His law to His people God was seeking lovers and the giving of the law was a transaction in which Gods people became engaged to Himv 32 Ezek 168 Exo 3427 Hos 21920"}
{"zh": "一\t律法乃是神和祂百姓之间的婚约—耶三一32，出三四27，林后十一2：（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第九段**）", "en": "A.\tThe law was an engagement covenant between God and His people:—Jer. 31:32; Exo. 34:27; 2 Cor. 11:2:", "norm_zh": "一律法乃是神和祂百姓之间的婚约耶三一32出三四27林后十一22015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The law was an engagement covenant between God and His peopleJer 3132 Exo 3427 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "1\t神以永远的爱爱祂的百姓—耶三一3，加六16，帖前一4，弗一4。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第二十七段*）", "en": "1.\tGod loves His people with an eternal love—Jer. 31:3; Gal. 6:16; 1 Thes. 1:4; Eph. 1:4.", "norm_zh": "1神以永远的爱爱祂的百姓耶三一3加六16帖前一4弗一42015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第二十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God loves His people with an eternal loveJer 313 Gal 616 1 Thes 14 Eph 14"}
{"zh": "2\t出埃及记前十九章乃是神追求祂的百姓，甚至与他们“约会”，正如耶利米二章二节所指明的。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第九段*）", "en": "2.\tIn the first nineteen chapters of Exodus, God was courting, even \"dating,\" His people, as indicated by Jeremiah 2:2.", "norm_zh": "2出埃及记前十九章乃是神追求祂的百姓甚至与他们约会正如耶利米二章二节所指明的2015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the first nineteen chapters of Exodus God was courting even dating His people as indicated by Jeremiah 22"}
{"zh": "二\t以色列人和神订婚发生在出埃及二十章神的山那里，而律法是正式的证书，敍述这个订婚的条件；十诫，特别是前五条，乃是神和祂的百姓之间订婚的条件—出二十1~12。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第八段*）", "en": "B.\tThe betrothal of Israel took place at the mountain of God in Exodus 20, and the law was the official paper stating the conditions for this engagement; the Ten Commandments, especially the first five, gave the terms of the engagement between God and His people.—Exo. 20:1-12.", "norm_zh": "二以色列人和神订婚发生在出埃及二十章神的山哪里而律法是正式的证书敍述这个订婚的条件十诫特别是前五条乃是神和祂的百姓之间订婚的条件出二十1122015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The betrothal of Israel took place at the mountain of God in Exodus 20 and the law was the official paper stating the conditions for this engagement the Ten Commandments especially the first five gave the terms of the engagement between God and His peopleExo 20112"}
{"zh": "三\t前五条诫命是在亲密的气氛中颁赐的；当神爱恋地追求祂的百姓时，一再亲密地使用“耶和华你的神”这个说法—2、12节：（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第十八段**）", "en": "C.\tThe first five commandments were given in an atmosphere of intimacy, with the expression Jehovah your God uttered intimately again and again as God lovingly courted His people:—vv. 2, 12:", "norm_zh": "三前五条诫命是在亲密的气氛中颁赐的当神爱恋地追求祂的百姓时一再亲密地使用耶和华你的神这个说法212节2015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The first five commandments were given in an atmosphere of intimacy with the expression Jehovah your God uttered intimately again and again as God lovingly courted His peoplevv 2 12"}
{"zh": "四\t律法是订婚证书，婚约，其最高的功用，乃是将神的选民带到与神成为一，如同妻子与丈夫成为一，使他们成为祂扩大并扩展的彰显，就是祂的见证—参创二24，启二二17， 出二五21~22，三八21。（2015年夏训，第二篇；圣经恢复本，出二十6注1**）", "en": "D. The law is an engagement paper, an engagement covenant, the highest function of which is to bring God's chosen people into oneness with God, as a wife is brought into oneness with her husband, making them His enlarged and expanded expression, which is His testimony.—cf. Gen. 2:24; Rev. 22:17; Exo. 25:21-22; 38:21.", "norm_zh": "四律法是订婚证书婚约其最高的功用乃是将神的选民带到与神成为一如同妻子与丈夫成为一使他们成为祂扩大并扩展的彰显就是祂的见证参创二24启二二17出二五2122三八212015年夏训第二篇圣经恢复本出二十6注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The law is an engagement paper an engagement covenant the highest function of which is to bring Gods chosen people into oneness with God as a wife is brought into oneness with her husband making them His enlarged and expanded expression which is His testimonycf Gen 224 Rev 2217 Exo 252122 3821"}
{"zh": "2\t当神的子民爱神，花时间在祂的话里与祂交通，神就将祂神圣的元素注入他们里面，使他们与祂成为一，作祂的配偶，在生命、性情和彰显上与祂一样—申三十20上，罗九23。（2015年夏训，第二篇；圣经恢复本，出二十6注1*）", "en": "2\tAs God's people love God and spend time to fellowship with Him in His word, God infuses them with His divine element, making them one with Him as His spouse, the same as He is in life, nature, and expression.—Deut. 30:20a; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "2当神的子民爱神花时间在祂的话里与祂交通神就将祂神圣的元素注入他们里面使他们与祂成为一作祂的配偶在生命性情和彰显上与祂一样申三十20上罗九232015年夏训第二篇圣经恢复本出二十6注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 As Gods people love God and spend time to fellowship with Him in His word God infuses them with His divine element making them one with Him as His spouse the same as He is in life nature and expressionDeut 3020a Rom 923"}
{"zh": "二\t只要我们爱主和主的话，只要我们与祂同在而被祂注入，我们自己所作不到的，祂就要在我们里面来作成—约十四21，腓二13，罗八4：（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十三篇，第三段**）", "en": "B.\tAs long as we love the Lord and His word and as long as we stay with Him to be infused with Him, He will do in us what we cannot do ourselves:—John 14:21; Phil. 2:13; Rom. 8:4:", "norm_zh": "二只要我们爱主和主的话只要我们与祂同在而被祂注入我们自己所作不到的祂就要在我们里面来作成约十四21腓二13罗八42015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第六十三篇第三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B As long as we love the Lord and His word and as long as we stay with Him to be infused with Him He will do in us what we cannot do ourselvesJohn 1421 Phil 213 Rom 84"}
{"zh": "4\t因着我们爱神，我们也爱神活的话；这活的话将祂的本质注入我们里面，就使我们因祂发光—耶十五16，出三四28~29：（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十三篇，第三十四段**）", "en": "4\tBecause we love God, we also love His living word, which infuses His substance into us to cause us to glow with Him.—Jer. 15:16; Exo. 34:28-29:", "norm_zh": "4因着我们爱神我们也爱神活的话这活的话将祂的本质注入我们里面就使我们因祂发光耶十五16出三四28292015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十三篇第三十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Because we love God we also love His living word which infuses His substance into us to cause us to glow with HimJer 1516 Exo 342829"}
{"zh": "a\t摩西在何烈山（西乃山）顶，没有挣扎努力去履行律法的要求；反之，他是被神借着与他说话所注入，而他发光的脸不过是返照神的所是—28~29节，参林后三18~四6。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十四篇，第十八段*）", "en": "a\tWhen Moses was on the top of Mount Horeb (Mount Sinai), he was not striving or working to fulfill the requirements of the law; rather, he was being infused with God by God's speaking with him, and his glowing face was simply a reflection of what God is—Exo. 34:28-29; cf. 2 Cor. 3:18.—vv. 28-29; cf. 2 Cor. 3:18—4:6.", "norm_zh": "a摩西在何烈山西乃山顶没有挣扎努力去履行律法的要求反之他是被神借着与他说话所注入而他发光的脸不过是返照神的所是2829节参林后三18四62015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第六十四篇第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a When Moses was on the top of Mount Horeb Mount Sinai he was not striving or working to fulfill the requirements of the law rather he was being infused with God by Gods speaking with him and his glowing face was simply a reflection of what God isExo 342829 cf 2 Cor 318vv 2829 cf 2 Cor 31846"}
{"zh": "b\t我们被主所注入，自然而然就会发光，成为祂活的描绘、祂的见证；我们不会努力挣扎，只会发光。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十四篇，第二十段）", "en": "b\tAs we are infused with the Lord, we will shine spontaneously to become His living portrait, His testimony; we will not work or strive but simply glow.", "norm_zh": "b我们被主所注入自然而然就会发光成为祂活的描绘祂的见证我们不会努力挣扎只会发光2015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第六十四篇第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b As we are infused with the Lord we will shine spontaneously to become His living portrait His testimony we will not work or strive but simply glow"}
{"zh": "三\t那些借着爱神和神的话而遵守律法，因而与神成为一的人，过神人的生活，有神的形像，是神的描绘和神的复制—约十四21，腓三9~11，罗九23，约十二24。（2015年夏训，第二篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十五篇，第四十三段**）", "en": "C.\tThose who keep the law by loving God and His word to become one with Him have the living of a God-man to bear the image of God, being a portrait of God and a duplication of God.—John 14:21; Phil. 3:9-11; Rom. 9:23; John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "三哪些借着爱神和神的话而遵守律法因而与神成为一的人过神人的生活有神的形像是神的描绘和神的复制约十四21腓三911罗九23约十二242015年夏训第二篇出埃及记生命读经第五十五篇第四十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:38:05.284392+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Those who keep the law by loving God and His word to become one with Him have the living of a Godman to bear the image of God being a portrait of God and a duplication of GodJohn 1421 Phil 3911 Rom 923 John 1224"}
{"zh": "读经：创三15，九8~17，加三14、16、29，撒下七12~14上，赛四二6，四九8，耶三一31~34，来八8~12", "en": "Scripture Reading: Gen. 3:15; 9:8-17; Gal. 3:14, 16, 29; 2 Sam. 7:12-14a; Isa. 42:6; 49:8; Jer. 31:31-34; Heb. 8:8-12", "norm_zh": "读经创三15九817加三141629撒下七1214上赛四二6四九8耶三一3134来八812", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Gen 315 9817 Gal 314 16 29 2 Sam 71214a Isa 426 498 Jer 313134 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "壹\t神与堕落之人所立的约，见于创世记三章十五节女人的后裔—创九9，三15：", "en": "I.\tThe covenant that God made with fallen man can be seen with the seed of the woman in Genesis 3:15:—Gen. 9:9; 3:15:", "norm_zh": "壹神与堕落之人所立的约见于创世记三章十五节女人的后裔创九9三15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The covenant that God made with fallen man can be seen with the seed of the woman in Genesis 315Gen 99 315"}
{"zh": "三\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之女人的后裔，分赐到我们里面，在我们里面伤蛇的头，使我们成为女人的团体后裔，得胜的男孩子，执行神对古蛇的审判，并作神时代的器皿，以转移时代，引进神国的实现─启十二5、9。", "en": "C.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of the woman, dispensed into us to bruise the serpent's head in us and to make us the corporate seed of the woman, the overcoming man-child, to carry out God's judgment on the ancient serpent and to be God's dispensational instrument to change the age and usher in the manifestation of God's kingdom.—Rev. 12:5, 9.", "norm_zh": "三复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之女人的后裔分赐到我们里面在我们里面伤蛇的头使我们成为女人的团体后裔得胜的男孩子执行神对古蛇的审判并作神时代的器皿以转移时代引进神国的实现启十二59", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of the woman dispensed into us to bruise the serpents head in us and to make us the corporate seed of the woman the overcoming manchild to carry out Gods judgment on the ancient serpent and to be Gods dispensational instrument to change the age and usher in the manifestation of Gods kingdomRev 125 9"}
{"zh": "二\t虹的三种主要颜色是蓝色（蓝宝石宝座的颜色，表征神的公义）、红色（圣别之火的颜色，表征神的圣别）、以及黄色（光耀的金银合金的颜色，表征神的荣耀）─26节，诗八九14，结一4、13、27，来十二29，一3。", "en": "B. The three main colors of the rainbow are blue (the color of the sapphire throne, signifying God's righteousness), red (the color of the holy fire, signifying God's holiness), and yellow (the color of the glowing electrum, signifying God's glory).—v. 26; Psa. 89:14; Ezek. 1:4, 13, 27; Heb. 12:29; 1:3.", "norm_zh": "二虹的三种主要颜色是蓝色蓝宝石宝座的颜色表征神的公义红色圣别之火的颜色表征神的圣别以及黄色光耀的金银合金的颜色表征神的荣耀26节诗八九14结一41327来十二29一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The three main colors of the rainbow are blue the color of the sapphire throne signifying Gods righteousness red the color of the holy fire signifying Gods holiness and yellow the color of the glowing electrum signifying Gods gloryv 26 Psa 8914 Ezek 14 13 27 Heb 1229 13"}
{"zh": "1\t神向亚伯拉罕所应许的福，物质的一面就是美地；这美地预表包罗万有的基督作为包罗万有赐生命的灵─创十二7，十三15，十七8，林前十五45下，林后三17。", "en": "1. The physical aspect of the blessing that God promised to Abraham was the good land; this good land typifies the all-inclusive Christ as the all-inclusive, life-giving Spirit.—Gen. 12:7; 13:15; 17:8; 1 Cor. 15:45b; 2 Cor. 3:17.", "norm_zh": "1神向亚伯拉罕所应许的福物质的一面就是美地这美地预表包罗万有的基督作为包罗万有赐生命的灵创十二7十三15十七8林前十五45下林后三17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The physical aspect of the blessing that God promised to Abraham was the good land this good land typifies the allinclusive Christ as the allinclusive lifegiving SpiritGen 127 1315 178 1 Cor 1545b 2 Cor 317"}
{"zh": "2\t基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是亚伯拉罕的福，就是向亚伯拉罕所应许之亚伯拉罕的后裔和美地的实际；今天我们的福乃是神自己，祂具体化身在基督里并实化为那灵，好分赐到我们里面，作我们的享受─创十七8，加三14。", "en": "2. Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the blessing of Abraham, the reality of both the seed of Abraham and the good land promised to Abraham; our blessing today is God Himself, who is embodied in Christ and realized as the Spirit to be dispensed into us for our enjoyment.—Gen. 17:8; Gal. 3:14.", "norm_zh": "2基督作为赐生命的灵乃是亚伯拉罕的福就是向亚伯拉罕所应许之亚伯拉罕的后裔和美地的实际今天我们的福乃是神自己祂具体化身在基督里并实化为哪灵好分赐到我们里面作我们的享受创十七8加三14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the blessing of Abraham the reality of both the seed of Abraham and the good land promised to Abraham our blessing today is God Himself who is embodied in Christ and realized as the Spirit to be dispensed into us for our enjoymentGen 178 Gal 314"}
{"zh": "二\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之大卫的子孙，大卫的后裔，分赐到我们里面，为使我们在神永远的国里，在基督的复活里，有分于祂君王的职分─提后二12，启二十4、6。", "en": "B.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David, the seed of David, dispensed into us for us to share His kingship in His resurrection in the eternal kingdom of God.—2 Tim. 2:12; Rev. 20:4, 6.", "norm_zh": "二复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之大卫的子孙大卫的后裔分赐到我们里面为使我们在神永远的国里在基督的复活里有分于祂君王的职分提后二12启二十46", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David the seed of David dispensed into us for us to share His kingship in His resurrection in the eternal kingdom of God2 Tim 212 Rev 204 6"}
{"zh": "三\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之大卫的子孙，大卫的后裔，国度的后裔（种子），分赐到我们里面，把我们作成国度之子，在生命中作王，活在国度的实际里，使我们在国度实现时被祂接去，并与祂一同回来，作团体砸人的石头，消灭世上的国，并成为一座大山，就是神的国，充满全地─可四26，太十三18~23、38，来十一5~6，创五21~24，但二34~35。", "en": "C.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David, the seed of David, the seed of the kingdom, dispensed into us to make us the sons of the kingdom, reigning in life to live in the reality of the kingdom so that we may be translated by Him and return with Him in the manifestation of the kingdom as the corporate smiting stone to annihilate the kingdoms of this world and become a great mountain, the kingdom of God, that fills the whole earth.—Mark 4:26; Matt. 13:18-23, 38; Heb. 11:5-6; Gen. 5:21-24; Dan. 2:34-35.", "norm_zh": "三复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之大卫的子孙大卫的后裔国度的后裔种子分赐到我们里面把我们作成国度之子在生命中作王活在国度的实际里使我们在国度实现时被祂接去并与祂一同回来作团体砸人的石头消灭世上的国并成为一座大山就是神的国充满全地可四26太十三182338来十一56创五2124但二3435", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David the seed of David the seed of the kingdom dispensed into us to make us the sons of the kingdom reigning in life to live in the reality of the kingdom so that we may be translated by Him and return with Him in the manifestation of the kingdom as the corporate smiting stone to annihilate the kingdoms of this world and become a great mountain the kingdom of God that fills the whole earthMark 426 Matt 131823 38 Heb 1156 Gen 52124 Dan 23435"}
{"zh": "伍\t基于耶利米预言到新约，耶利米书这卷旧约的书也可视为新约的书─二13，十七9，十三23，二三5~6，三一31~34，来八8~12：", "en": "V.\tBased on the fact that Jeremiah prophesies concerning the new covenant, the book of Jeremiah may be considered an Old Testament book that is also a New Testament book.—Jer. 2:13; 17:9; 13:23; 23:5-6; 31:31-34; Heb. 8:8-12:", "norm_zh": "伍基于耶利米预言到新约耶利米书这卷旧约的书也可视为新约的书二13十七9十三23二三56三一3134来八812", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Based on the fact that Jeremiah prophesies concerning the new covenant the book of Jeremiah may be considered an Old Testament book that is also a New Testament bookJer 213 179 1323 2356 313134 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "一\t基督自己就是神所赐给我们的新约，新遗命─赛四二6，四九8：", "en": "A.\tChrist Himself is the new covenant, the new testament, given to us by God.—Isa. 42:6; 49:8:", "norm_zh": "一基督自己就是神所赐给我们的新约新遗命赛四二6四九8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ Himself is the new covenant the new testament given to us by GodIsa 426 498"}
{"zh": "1\t神的救恩、神的祝福、以及神一切的丰富都已经立约给了我们；这约就是基督—四二6，四九8。", "en": "1.\tGod's salvation, God's blessings, and all of God's riches have been covenanted to us, and this covenant is Christ:—Isa. 42:6; 49:8.", "norm_zh": "1神的救恩神的祝福以及神一切的丰富都已经立约给了我们这约就是基督四二6四九8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods salvation Gods blessings and all of Gods riches have been covenanted to us and this covenant is ChristIsa 426 498"}
{"zh": "2\t接受并享受基督作我们这约的路，乃是借着呼求我们主基督的名，操练我们的灵，照着我们的灵而活，住留在我们灵里；与我们的灵同在的，就是这位基督─四二5~6，亚十二1，罗八4下，启一10上，提后四22，赛十二3~4。", "en": "2.\tThe way to receive and enjoy Christ as the covenant to us is to exercise our spirit, to live according to our spirit, and to remain in our spirit, with which is the very Christ, by calling on the Lord's name.—Isa. 42:5-6; Zech. 12:1; Rom. 8:4b; Rev. 1:10a; 2 Tim. 4:22; Isa. 12:3-4.", "norm_zh": "2接受并享受基督作我们这约的路乃是借着呼求我们主基督的名操练我们的灵照着我们的灵而活住留在我们灵里与我们的灵同在的就是这位基督四二56亚十二1罗八4下启一10上提后四22赛十二34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The way to receive and enjoy Christ as the covenant to us is to exercise our spirit to live according to our spirit and to remain in our spirit with which is the very Christ by calling on the Lords nameIsa 4256 Zech 121 Rom 84b Rev 110a 2 Tim 422 Isa 1234"}
{"zh": "二\t新遗命的内容包括以下四项福分，作为神给我们的遗赠─耶三一31~34，来八8~12：", "en": "B. The contents of the new testament comprise the following four blessings as bequests given to us by God.—Jer. 31:31-34; Heb. 8:8-12:", "norm_zh": "二新遗命的内容包括以下四项福分作为神给我们的遗赠耶三一3134来八812", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The contents of the new testament comprise the following four blessings as bequests given to us by GodJer 313134 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "1\t“我要将我的律法赐在他们心思里，并且将这些律法写在他们心上”─10节：", "en": "1.\t\"I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them.\"—v. 10:", "norm_zh": "1我要将我的律法赐在他们心思里并且将这些律法写在他们心上10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe themv 10"}
{"zh": "a\t每一种生命都有一个律，甚至都是一个律─箴三十19上。", "en": "a.\tEvery life has a law and even is a law.—Prov. 30:19a.", "norm_zh": "a每一种生命都有一个律甚至都是一个律箴三十19上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Every life has a law and even is a lawProv 3019a"}
{"zh": "b\t神的生命是最高的生命，这生命的律是最高的律─赛四十30~31。", "en": "b\tGod's life is the highest life, and the law of this life is the highest law.—Isa. 40:30-31.", "norm_zh": "b神的生命是最高的生命这生命的律是最高的律赛四十3031", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Gods life is the highest life and the law of this life is the highest lawIsa 403031"}
{"zh": "c\t三一神已经经过成为肉体、钉死、复活并升天的过程，成了生命之灵的律，装置在我们灵里─罗八3、11、34、16。", "en": "c\tThe Triune God has been processed through incarnation, crucifixion, resurrection, and ascension to become the law of the Spirit of life installed in our spirit.—Rom. 8:3, 11, 34, 16.", "norm_zh": "c三一神已经经过成为肉体钉死复活并升天的过程成了生命之灵的律装置在我们灵里罗八3113416", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c The Triune God has been processed through incarnation crucifixion resurrection and ascension to become the law of the Spirit of life installed in our spiritRom 83 11 34 16"}
{"zh": "d\t生命的律，生命之灵的律，乃是经过过程之三一神作赐生命的灵住在我们的灵里─2~3、11、34节。", "en": "d\tThe law of life, the law of the Spirit of life, is the processed Triune God as the life-giving Spirit dwelling in our spirit.—vv. 2-3, 11, 34.", "norm_zh": "d生命的律生命之灵的律乃是经过过程之三一神作赐生命的灵住在我们的灵里231134节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d The law of life the law of the Spirit of life is the processed Triune God as the lifegiving Spirit dwelling in our spiritvv 23 11 34"}
{"zh": "e\t生命的律乃是生命自发的能力；这律是生命所具自然的特性，和自有、自动的功能。", "en": "e\tThe law of life is the spontaneous power of life; it is the natural characteristic and the innate, automatic function of life.", "norm_zh": "e生命的律乃是生命自发的能力这律是生命所具自然的特性和自有自动的功能", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "e The law of life is the spontaneous power of life it is the natural characteristic and the innate automatic function of life"}
{"zh": "f\t生命之灵的律已经装置好，且正在运行，我们必须借着把这律的“开关打开”，而与这律合作─帖前五16~18，路八15。", "en": "f\tWe need to cooperate with the installed and operating law of the Spirit of life by \"switching on\" this law.—1 Thes. 5:16-18; Luke 8:15.", "norm_zh": "f生命之灵的律已经装置好且正在运行我们必须借着把这律的开关打开而与这律合作帖前五1618路八15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "f We need to cooperate with the installed and operating law of the Spirit of life by switching on this law1 Thes 51618 Luke 815"}
{"zh": "2\t“我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民”─来八10：", "en": "2\t\"I will be God to them, and they will be a people to Me.\"—Heb. 8:10:", "norm_zh": "2我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民来八10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 I will be God to them and they will be a people to MeHeb 810"}
{"zh": "a\t神作我们的神，意即神是我们的产业；而我们作神的子民，意即我们乃是神的产业─弗一11、14、18，三21。", "en": "a\tFor God to be our God means that He is our inheritance, and for us to be His people means that we are His inheritance.—Eph. 1:11, 14, 18; 3:21.", "norm_zh": "a神作我们的神意即神是我们的产业而我们作神的子民意即我们乃是神的产业弗一111418三21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a For God to be our God means that He is our inheritance and for us to be His people means that we are His inheritanceEph 111 14 18 321"}
{"zh": "b\t在新约里，我们有特权得着神作我们的神，我们作祂的子民─乃是生命使我们能在与神的交通中享受神，好叫祂被我们所认识、领会，且由我们活出─约壹一3、7。", "en": "b\tIn the new covenant we have the privilege of having God as our God and of being His people—the capability of life for us to participate in the enjoyment of God in fellowship with Him so that He can be known by us, apprehended by us, and lived by us.—1 John 1:3, 7.", "norm_zh": "b在新约里我们有特权得着神作我们的神我们作祂的子民乃是生命使我们能在与神的交通中享受神好叫祂被我们所认识领会且由我们活出约壹一37", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b In the new covenant we have the privilege of having God as our God and of being His peoplethe capability of life for us to participate in the enjoyment of God in fellowship with Him so that He can be known by us apprehended by us and lived by us1 John 13 7"}
{"zh": "3\t“他们各人绝不用教导自己同国之民，各人也绝不用教导自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我”─来八11：", "en": "3\t\"They shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother, saying, Know the Lord; for all will know Me from the little one to the great one among them.\"—Heb. 8:11:", "norm_zh": "3他们各人绝不用教导自己同国之民各人也绝不用教导自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我来八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 They shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother saying Know the Lord for all will know Me from the little one to the great one among themHeb 811"}
{"zh": "a\t生命的功能使我们能以生命内里的方式认识神—约壹五11，来八11。", "en": "a\tThe capacity of life enables us to know God in the inward way of life.—1 John 5:11; Heb. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "a生命的功能使我们能以生命内里的方式认识神约壹五11来八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The capacity of life enables us to know God in the inward way of life1 John 511 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "b\t我们能凭生命的感觉，就是我们里面神圣生命的感觉、知觉，而从里面主观地认识神─罗八6，弗四18~20，腓三10上。", "en": "b\tWe can know God subjectively from within by the sense of life, which is the feeling, the consciousness, of the divine life within us.—Rom. 8:6; Eph. 4:18-20; Phil. 3:10a.", "norm_zh": "b我们能凭生命的感觉就是我们里面神圣生命的感觉知觉而从里面主观地认识神罗八6弗四1820腓三10上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We can know God subjectively from within by the sense of life which is the feeling the consciousness of the divine life within usRom 86 Eph 41820 Phil 310a"}
{"zh": "c\t认识神就是要活神；借着我们里面神圣生命那自然、自动的功用，我们就有性能认识神、活神、甚至在神的生命和性情上与祂成为一，使我们作祂团体的彰显—来八11，腓三10，罗九23。", "en": "c\tTo know God is to live God; through the spontaneous, automatic function of the divine life within us, we have the capacity to know God, to live God, and even to be one with God in His life and nature so that we may be His corporate expression.—Heb. 8:11; Phil. 3:10; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "c认识神就是要活神借着我们里面神圣生命哪自然自动的功用我们就有性能认识神活神甚至在神的生命和性情上与祂成为一使我们作祂团体的彰显来八11腓三10罗九23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c To know God is to live God through the spontaneous automatic function of the divine life within us we have the capacity to know God to live God and even to be one with God in His life and nature so that we may be His corporate expressionHeb 811 Phil 310 Rom 923"}
{"zh": "4\t“我要宽恕他们的不义，绝不再记念他们的罪”─来八12：", "en": "4\t\"I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I shall by no means remember anymore.\"—Heb. 8:12:", "norm_zh": "4我要宽恕他们的不义绝不再记念他们的罪来八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I shall by no means remember anymoreHeb 812"}
{"zh": "a\t基督为我们的罪成就了平息，以平息神的公义，也就是满足了神公义的要求，使我们得以与神和好─二17。", "en": "a\tChrist made propitiation for our sins to appease God's righteousness, to reconcile us by satisfying the demands of God's righteousness.—Heb. 2:17.", "norm_zh": "a基督为我们的罪成就了平息以平息神的公义也就是满足了神公义的要求使我们得以与神和好二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Christ made propitiation for our sins to appease Gods righteousness to reconcile us by satisfying the demands of Gods righteousnessHeb 217"}
{"zh": "b\t基督那又宝贵又有功效的血，解决了我们一切的难处，使我们得以维持在与神不断地交通中，不断地享受祂生机的救恩─约壹一7~9，二1~2。", "en": "b\tThe precious and all-efficacious blood of Christ resolves all our problems so that we can remain constantly in fellowship with God to continually enjoy His organic salvation.—1 John 1:7-9; 2:1-2.", "norm_zh": "b基督哪又宝贵又有功效的血解决了我们一切的难处使我们得以维持在与神不断地交通中不断地享受祂生机的救恩约壹一79二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The precious and allefficacious blood of Christ resolves all our problems so that we can remain constantly in fellowship with God to continually enjoy His organic salvation1 John 179 212"}
{"zh": "c\t神一赦免我们，就从祂的记忆里涂抹我们的罪，不再记念—一9，二2。", "en": "c\tOnce God forgives us, He erases our sins from His memory and remembers them no longer:—1 John 1:9; 2:2.", "norm_zh": "c神一赦免我们就从祂的记忆里涂抹我们的罪不再记念一9二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Once God forgives us He erases our sins from His memory and remembers them no longer1 John 19 22"}
{"zh": "d\t神赦免我们的罪，结果使我们恢复与祂的交通，而敬畏祂，并且爱祂─诗一三〇4，路七47。", "en": "d\tGod's forgiveness of our sins results in our fearing Him and loving Him in our restored fellowship with Him.", "norm_zh": "d神赦免我们的罪结果使我们恢复与祂的交通而敬畏祂并且爱祂诗一三〇4路七47", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d Gods forgiveness of our sins results in our fearing Him and loving Him in our restored fellowship with Him"}
{"zh": "陆\t至终，新约要产生新耶路撒冷，就是神的新约的具体化身，以团体的方式彰显神到极致，直到永远─加四26~28、31。", "en": "VI.\tThe new covenant will ultimately issue in the New Jerusalem, the embodiment of God's new covenant to express God in a corporate way to the uttermost for eternity.—Gal. 4:26-28, 31.", "norm_zh": "陆至终新约要产生新耶路撒冷就是神的新约的具体化身以团体的方式彰显神到极致直到永远加四262831", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The new covenant will ultimately issue in the New Jerusalem the embodiment of Gods new covenant to express God in a corporate way to the uttermost for eternityGal 42628 31"}
{"zh": "神和人所立的约，都是说出神对人的心意", "en": "God's covenants with man all reveal His desire toward man.", "norm_zh": "神和人所立的约都是说出神对人的心意", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods covenants with man all reveal His desire toward man"}
{"zh": "创世记十二章一节至三节、七节，十三章十四节至十七节，十五章一节至二十节，十七章一节至二十一节，二十一章十二节，二十二章十六至十八节。", "en": "Gen. 12:1-3, 7; 13:14-17; 15:1-20; 17:1-21; 21:12; 22:16-18.", "norm_zh": "创世记十二章一节至三节七节十三章十四节至十七节十五章一节至二十节十七章一节至二十一节二十一章十二节二十二章十六至十八节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gen 1213 7 131417 15120 17121 2112 221618"}
{"zh": "这几处圣经所说的话，加起来就是神与蒙召的亚伯拉罕所立的约。这是一个正统的约，是一个恩典的约，和新约是相联的，并且是新约的根据。这个约可以分作七个点来说它。", "en": "The words spoken in these scriptures, when added together, are the covenant that God made with the called Abraham. This is an orthodox covenant, a covenant of grace; it is related to the new covenant and is the basis of the new covenant. This covenant can be spoken of in seven points.", "norm_zh": "这几处圣经所说的话加起来就是神与蒙召的亚伯拉罕所立的约这是一个正统的约是一个恩典的约和新约是相联的并且是新约的根据这个约可以分作七个点来说它", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The words spoken in these scriptures when added together are the covenant that God made with the called Abraham This is an orthodox covenant a covenant of grace it is related to the new covenant and is the basis of the new covenant This covenant can be spoken of in seven points"}
{"zh": "神要借着亚伯拉罕得着国度。这个大国，在旧约时候是以色列国，到新约时候是教会，到将来时候是千年国度，在永世里是新天新地。换一句话说，已过的以色列国，现在的教会，将来的千年国度，以及永远里的新天新地，这些都是神的国，都是神要借亚伯拉罕得着的。", "en": "God wanted to gain the kingdom through Abraham. This great nation was the nation of Israel in the Old Testament age, the church in the New Testament age, the millennial kingdom in the coming age, and the new heaven and the new earth in eternity. In other words, the past nation of Israel, the present church, the future millennial kingdom, and the new heaven and the new earth in eternity are all the kingdom of God, which God wanted to gain through Abraham.", "norm_zh": "神要借着亚伯拉罕得着国度这个大国在旧约时候是以色列国到新约时候是教会到将来时候是千年国度在永世里是新天新地换一句话说已过的以色列国现在的教会将来的千年国度以及永远里的新天新地这些都是神的国都是神要借亚伯拉罕得着的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "God wanted to gain the kingdom through Abraham This great nation was the nation of Israel in the Old Testament age the church in the New Testament age the millennial kingdom in the coming age and the new heaven and the new earth in eternity In other words the past nation of Israel the present church the future millennial kingdom and the new heaven and the new earth in eternity are all the kingdom of God which God wanted to gain through Abraham"}
{"zh": "这一个约是以割礼为记号", "en": "This covenant has circumcision as its sign.", "norm_zh": "这一个约是以割礼为记号", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "This covenant has circumcision as its sign"}
{"zh": "关于这新约，圣经多处题到。马太二十六章二十七至二十八节，主耶稣设立晚餐的时候说，这是我用血所立的新约。林前十一章二十五节，也说同样的话。希伯来八章六至十三节说，神和祂的百姓立一个新约。希伯来七章二十二节说，这个约是个更美的约。希伯来十三章二十节说，这个约是个永远的约。（请参考“更美之约”，又名“什么是新约”。）", "en": "The Bible speaks of this covenant in many places. In Matthew 26:27-28, when the Lord Jesus established the Lord's supper, He said that this is the new covenant established in His blood. First Corinthians 11:25 also says the same thing. Hebrews 8:6-13 says that God consummated a new covenant with His people. Hebrews 7:22 says that this covenant is a better covenant. Hebrews 13:20 says that this covenant is an eternal covenant. (Please refer to \"The Better Covenant,\" also known as \"What Is the New Covenant?\")", "norm_zh": "关于这新约圣经多处提到马太二十六章二十七至二十八节主耶稣设立晚餐的时候说这是我用血所立的新约林前十一章二十五节也说同样的话希伯来八章六至十三节说神和祂的百姓立一个新约希伯来七章二十二节说这个约是个更美的约希伯来十三章二十节说这个约是个永远的约请参考更美之约又名什么是新约", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Bible speaks of this covenant in many places In Matthew 262728 when the Lord Jesus established the Lords supper He said that this is the new covenant established in His blood First Corinthians 1125 also says the same thing Hebrews 8613 says that God consummated a new covenant with His people Hebrews 722 says that this covenant is a better covenant Hebrews 1320 says that this covenant is an eternal covenant Please refer to The Better Covenant also known as What Is the New Covenant"}
{"zh": "神也应许要除去我们一切的罪恶，不再记念我们的罪愆", "en": "God also promised to take away all our sins and remember our transgressions no more.", "norm_zh": "神也应许要除去我们一切的罪恶不再记念我们的罪愆", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "God also promised to take away all our sins and remember our transgressions no more"}
{"zh": "因此按照神的定规，新约的时候还没有来到，新约是将来的事；但是因着主耶稣已经流血，出了代价，并且已经复活，住在大能的生命里面，所以神就能根据这一点，提前把新约的功能，应用在我们这些信的人身上，叫我们预尝新约的福分。因此我们应该知道，新约的福分，到将来以色列人都要有分，这是耶利米三十一章，和罗马十一章二十五至二十七节所告诉我们的。", "en": "Hence, according to God's ordination, the time of the new covenant has not yet fully arrived; the new covenant still involves something related to the future, but based on the fact that the Lord Jesus shed His blood, was resurrected, and now dwells in us in life, God can apply the function of the new covenant to us who believe so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant. Therefore, we should know that in the future the Israelites will all participate in the blessing of the new covenant; this is revealed in Jeremiah 31 and Romans 11:25-27.", "norm_zh": "因此按照神的定规新约的时候还没有来到新约是将来的事但是因着主耶稣已经流血出了代价并且已经复活住在大能的生命里面所以神就能根据这一点提前把新约的功能应用在我们这些信的人身上叫我们预尝新约的福分因此我们应该知道新约的福分到将来以色列人都要有分这是耶利米三十一章和罗马十一章二十五至二十七节所告诉我们的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hence according to Gods ordination the time of the new covenant has not yet fully arrived the new covenant still involves something related to the future but based on the fact that the Lord Jesus shed His blood was resurrected and now dwells in us in life God can apply the function of the new covenant to us who believe so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant Therefore we should know that in the future the Israelites will all participate in the blessing of the new covenant this is revealed in Jeremiah 31 and Romans 112527"}
{"zh": "凡主耶稣所成功的事实，都是我们享受的分", "en": "Every fact that the Lord Jesus accomplished is a portion for us to enjoy.", "norm_zh": "凡主耶稣所成功的事实都是我们享受的分", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Every fact that the Lord Jesus accomplished is a portion for us to enjoy"}
{"zh": "这一个约和前面被补充的约，一直延长下来到新约。凡是亚伯拉罕的约里头，和大卫的约里头的那些重点，都需要在主耶稣的身上才能实现。还不仅如此，连前面挪亚的约，和亚当堕落之后神和他所立的约里面的重点，都需要在这一位主耶稣身上得着成全。所以祂来了，就流了祂的宝血，作代价，应付了前约的要求，并且从死里复活，有了复活的生命，作祂执行这约的能力，好把新约完全实行到我们身上来。因着这缘故，我们今天就能在神面前，有了神的生命，得着神所给我们各样的福，并且成为神的国，在这个掌权的范围里头，建造成为神的居所，有神的同在。", "en": "This covenant and the preceding covenant it supplemented extend all the way to the new covenant. All of the main points in Abraham's covenant and David's covenant can be realized only in the Lord Jesus. Furthermore, even the main points in the preceding covenant with Noah and the covenant God made with Adam after his fall need to be fulfilled in this very Lord Jesus. Therefore, He came and shed His blood as the price to meet the requirements of the former covenant, and He resurrected from the dead, having the resurrection life as His power to execute this covenant, so that the new covenant might be fully carried out in us. Because of this, today we can be before God, have God's life, receive every blessing that God has given us, become God's kingdom, be built as a dwelling place of God in this ruling realm, and have God's presence.", "norm_zh": "这一个约和前面被补充的约一直延长下来到新约凡是亚伯拉罕的约里头和大卫的约里头的哪些重点都需要在主耶稣的身上才能实现还不仅如此连前面挪亚的约和亚当堕落之后神和他所立的约里面的重点都需要在这一位主耶稣身上得着成全所以祂来了就流了祂的宝血作代价应付了前约的要求并且从死里复活有了复活的生命作祂执行这约的能力好把新约完全实行到我们身上来因着这缘故我们今天就能在神面前有了神的生命得着神所给我们各样的福并且成为神的国在这个掌权的范围里头建造成为神的居所有神的同在", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "This covenant and the preceding covenant it supplemented extend all the way to the new covenant All of the main points in Abrahams covenant and Davids covenant can be realized only in the Lord Jesus Furthermore even the main points in the preceding covenant with Noah and the covenant God made with Adam after his fall need to be fulfilled in this very Lord Jesus Therefore He came and shed His blood as the price to meet the requirements of the former covenant and He resurrected from the dead having the resurrection life as His power to execute this covenant so that the new covenant might be fully carried out in us Because of this today we can be before God have Gods life receive every blessing that God has given us become Gods kingdom be built as a dwelling place of God in this ruling realm and have Gods presence"}
{"zh": "请大家记得，这些光景集合起来延长下去，最终的结果就是新耶路撒冷的出现。新耶路撒冷把这一切都包括里头。家在里头，国在里头，殿在里头，掌权的宝座在里头，神的同在在里头，神的生命在里头，属天的福，属地的福，各种样的福都在里头。到那个时候，神就要照着祂历代和人来往所立的约，实行一切，和人永远同住。", "en": "Please remember that when these conditions are brought together and extended, the ultimate result will be the manifestation of the New Jerusalem. The New Jerusalem includes all of these things. The house is in it, the kingdom is in it, the temple is in it, the throne of authority is in it, God's presence is in it, God's life is in it, and the heavenly blessings, earthly blessings, and all kinds of blessings are in it. At that time God will fulfill everything according to the covenants He made in His dealings with man throughout the ages and dwell with man eternally.", "norm_zh": "请大家记得这些光景集合起来延长下去最终的结果就是新耶路撒冷的出现新耶路撒冷把这一切都包括里头家在里头国在里头殿在里头掌权的宝座在里头神的同在在里头神的生命在里头属天的福属地的福各种样的福都在里头到哪个时候神就要照着祂历代和人来往所立的约实行一切和人永远同住", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Please remember that when these conditions are brought together and extended the ultimate result will be the manifestation of the New Jerusalem The New Jerusalem includes all of these things The house is in it the kingdom is in it the temple is in it the throne of authority is in it Gods presence is in it Gods life is in it and the heavenly blessings earthly blessings and all kinds of blessings are in it At that time God will fulfill everything according to the covenants He made in His dealings with man throughout the ages and dwell with man eternally"}
{"zh": "未了还有几点，是我们读经的人关于这个约应当知道的。在神的约里头，有很大的部分是包括应许的。比如在第一个约里头，祂应许人，生养众多；在第二个约里头，祂应许女人的后裔要来；在亚伯拉罕的约里头，祂应许亚伯拉罕要得着许多的后裔。", "en": "Finally, there are a few points that we who read the Scriptures should know concerning this covenant. Within God's covenant, a large part consists of promises. For example, in the first covenant, He promised man to be fruitful and multiply; in the second covenant, He promised that the descendant of the woman would come; in Abraham's covenant, He promised Abraham that he would obtain many descendants.", "norm_zh": "未了还有几点是我们读经的人关于这个约应当知道的在神的约里头有很大的部分是包括应许的比如在第一个约里头祂应许人生养众多在第二个约里头祂应许女人的后裔要来在亚伯拉罕的约里头祂应许亚伯拉罕要得着许多的后裔", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Finally there are a few points that we who read the Scriptures should know concerning this covenant Within Gods covenant a large part consists of promises For example in the first covenant He promised man to be fruitful and multiply in the second covenant He promised that the descendant of the woman would come in Abrahams covenant He promised Abraham that he would obtain many descendants"}
{"zh": "但是在约里头不光有应许，在约里头也有事实。比如在末了这一个约里头，神说祂要赦免我们的罪，除去我们的不义，这就不是应许，而是一个已经成功的事实。我们今天所以罪得赦免，不是因为神应许说，祂要赦免我们，乃是神已经赦免了我们；我们今天得救，乃是接受一个已经赦免的事实。在新约里头，神除去人的罪不是个应许，乃是个事实。主耶稣在十字架上老早就把除去人罪的这件事完成了，神就把这件事摆在新约里头，当作一个事实来告诉人说，你的罪已经赦免了，只要你接受就是了。", "en": "However, in the covenant there are not only promises; in the covenant there are also facts. For instance, in this last covenant, God said that He would forgive our sins and take away our unrighteousness; this is not a promise but an accomplished fact. Today our sins are forgiven not because God promised that He would forgive us but because He has already forgiven us; our being saved today is the acceptance of an accomplished fact of forgiveness. In the new covenant, God's taking away of man's sins is not a promise but a fact. Long ago on the cross the Lord Jesus accomplished the taking away of man's sins, and God put this fact into the new covenant to tell man, as a fact, 'Your sins are forgiven; you only need to accept it.'", "norm_zh": "但是在约里头不光有应许在约里头也有事实比如在末了这一个约里头神说祂要赦免我们的罪除去我们的不义这就不是应许而是一个已经成功的事实我们今天所以罪得赦免不是因为神应许说祂要赦免我们乃是神已经赦免了我们我们今天得救乃是接受一个已经赦免的事实在新约里头神除去人的罪不是个应许乃是个事实主耶稣在十字架上老早就把除去人罪的这件事完成了神就把这件事摆在新约里头当作一个事实来告诉人说你的罪已经赦免了只要你接受就是了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "However in the covenant there are not only promises in the covenant there are also facts For instance in this last covenant God said that He would forgive our sins and take away our unrighteousness this is not a promise but an accomplished fact Today our sins are forgiven not because God promised that He would forgive us but because He has already forgiven us our being saved today is the acceptance of an accomplished fact of forgiveness In the new covenant Gods taking away of mans sins is not a promise but a fact Long ago on the cross the Lord Jesus accomplished the taking away of mans sins and God put this fact into the new covenant to tell man as a fact Your sins are forgiven you only need to accept it"}
{"zh": "我要将我的律法放在他们里面，写在他们心上", "en": "I will put My law within them and write it upon their hearts", "norm_zh": "我要将我的律法放在他们里面写在他们心上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:40:56.938329+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I will put My law within them and write it upon their hearts"}
{"zh": "壹\t神与堕落之人所立的约，见于创世记三章十五节女人的后裔—创九9，三15：（2015年夏训，第六篇；李常受文集一九五九年第三册，圣经的十条路线，第七篇，第十八段*；李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册，新约圣经中奇妙的基督，第一章，第七段**）", "en": "I.\tThe covenant that God made with fallen man can be seen in the seed of the woman in Genesis 3:15:—Gen. 9:9; 3:15:", "norm_zh": "壹神与堕落之人所立的约见于创世记三章十五节女人的后裔创九9三152015年夏训第六篇李常受文集一九五九年第三册圣经的十条路线第七篇第十八段李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册新约圣经中奇妙的基督第一章第七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The covenant that God made with fallen man can be seen in the seed of the woman in Genesis 315Gen 99 315"}
{"zh": "三\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之女人的后裔，分赐到我们里面，在我们里面伤蛇的头，使我们成为女人的团体后裔，得胜的男孩子，执行神对古蛇的审判，并作神时代的器皿，以转移时代，引进神国的实现─启十二5、9。（2015年夏训，第六篇；李常受文集一九九三年第二册，一九九三年相调特会信息—关于主的恢复和我们当前的需要，第五篇，第一百三十三段**）", "en": "C.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of the woman, dispensed into us to bruise the serpent's head in us and to make us the corporate seed of the woman, the overcoming man-child, to carry out God's judgment on the ancient serpent and to be God's dispensational instrument to change the age and usher in the manifestation of God's kingdom.—Rev. 12:5, 9.", "norm_zh": "三复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之女人的后裔分赐到我们里面在我们里面伤蛇的头使我们成为女人的团体后裔得胜的男孩子执行神对古蛇的审判并作神时代的器皿以转移时代引进神国的实现启十二592015年夏训第六篇李常受文集一九九三年第二册一九九三年相调特会信息关于主的恢复和我们当前的需要第五篇第一百三十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of the woman dispensed into us to bruise the serpents head in us and to make us the corporate seed of the woman the overcoming manchild to carry out Gods judgment on the ancient serpent and to be Gods dispensational instrument to change the age and usher in the manifestation of Gods kingdomRev 125 9"}
{"zh": "二\t虹的三种主要颜色是蓝色（蓝宝石宝座的颜色，表征神的公义）、红色（圣别之火的颜色，表征神的圣别）、以及黄色（光耀的金银合金的颜色，表征神的荣耀）─26节，诗八九14，结一4、13、27，来十二29，一3。（2015年夏训，第六篇；以西结书生命读经，第十二篇，第四十三段**）", "en": "B. The three primary colors of the rainbow are blue (the color of the sapphire throne, signifying God's righteousness), red (the color of the sanctifying fire, signifying God's holiness), and yellow (the color of the glowing electrum, signifying God's glory).—v. 26; Psa. 89:14; Ezek. 1:4, 13, 27; Heb. 12:29; 1:3.", "norm_zh": "二虹的三种主要颜色是蓝色蓝宝石宝座的颜色表征神的公义红色圣别之火的颜色表征神的圣别以及黄色光耀的金银合金的颜色表征神的荣耀26节诗八九14结一41327来十二29一32015年夏训第六篇以西结书生命读经第十二篇第四十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The three primary colors of the rainbow are blue the color of the sapphire throne signifying Gods righteousness red the color of the sanctifying fire signifying Gods holiness and yellow the color of the glowing electrum signifying Gods gloryv 26 Psa 8914 Ezek 14 13 27 Heb 1229 13"}
{"zh": "1\t神向亚伯拉罕所应许的福，物质的一面就是美地；这美地预表包罗万有的基督作为包罗万有赐生命的灵─创十二7，十三15，十七8，林前十五45下，林后三17。（2015年夏训，第六篇；新约总论，第十五篇，第十五段*）", "en": "1. The physical aspect of the blessing that God promised to Abraham was the good land; this good land typifies the all-inclusive Christ as the all-inclusive, life-giving Spirit.—Gen. 12:7; 13:15; 17:8; 1 Cor. 15:45b; 2 Cor. 3:17.", "norm_zh": "1神向亚伯拉罕所应许的福物质的一面就是美地这美地预表包罗万有的基督作为包罗万有赐生命的灵创十二7十三15十七8林前十五45下林后三172015年夏训第六篇新约总论第十五篇第十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The physical aspect of the blessing that God promised to Abraham was the good land this good land typifies the allinclusive Christ as the allinclusive lifegiving SpiritGen 127 1315 178 1 Cor 1545b 2 Cor 317"}
{"zh": "2\t基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是亚伯拉罕的福，就是向亚伯拉罕所应许之亚伯拉罕的后裔和美地的实际；今天我们的福乃是神自己，祂具体化身在基督里并实化为那灵，好分赐到我们里面，作我们的享受─创十七8，加三14。（2015年夏训，第六篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册，神圣启示的中心路线，第八篇，第四十九段**）", "en": "2. Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the blessing of Abraham, the reality of both the seed of Abraham and the good land promised to Abraham; our blessing today is God Himself, who is embodied in Christ and realized as the Spirit to be dispensed into us for our enjoyment.—Gen. 17:8; Gal. 3:14.", "norm_zh": "2基督作为赐生命的灵乃是亚伯拉罕的福就是向亚伯拉罕所应许之亚伯拉罕的后裔和美地的实际今天我们的福乃是神自己祂具体化身在基督里并实化为哪灵好分赐到我们里面作我们的享受创十七8加三142015年夏训第六篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册神圣启示的中心路线第八篇第四十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the blessing of Abraham the reality of both the seed of Abraham and the good land promised to Abraham our blessing today is God Himself who is embodied in Christ and realized as the Spirit to be dispensed into us for our enjoymentGen 178 Gal 314"}
{"zh": "二\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之大卫的子孙，大卫的后裔，分赐到我们里面，为使我们在神永远的国里，在基督的复活里，有分于祂君王的职分─提后二12，启二十4、6。（2015年夏训，第六篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册，神圣启示的中心路线，第八篇，第六十二段*）", "en": "B.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David, the seed of David, dispensed into us for us to share His kingship in His resurrection in the eternal kingdom of God.—2 Tim. 2:12; Rev. 20:4, 6.", "norm_zh": "二复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之大卫的子孙大卫的后裔分赐到我们里面为使我们在神永远的国里在基督的复活里有分于祂君王的职分提后二12启二十462015年夏训第六篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册神圣启示的中心路线第八篇第六十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David the seed of David dispensed into us for us to share His kingship in His resurrection in the eternal kingdom of God2 Tim 212 Rev 204 6"}
{"zh": "三\t复活的基督作为赐生命的灵，乃是那变了形像之大卫的子孙，大卫的后裔，国度的后裔（种子），分赐到我们里面，把我们作成国度之子，在生命中作王，活在国度的实际里，使我们在国度实现时被祂接去，并与祂一同回来，作团体砸人的石头，消灭世上的国，并成为一座大山，就是神的国，充满全地─可四26，太十三18~23、38，来十一5~6，创五21~24，但二34~35。（2015年夏训，第六篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第二册，主恢复中的五个重点，第三章，第三十四段**）", "en": "C.\tThe resurrected Christ as the life-giving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David, the seed of David, the seed of the kingdom, dispensed into us to make us the sons of the kingdom, reigning in life to live in the reality of the kingdom so that we may be translated by Him and return with Him in the manifestation of the kingdom as the corporate smiting stone to annihilate the kingdoms of this world and become a great mountain, the kingdom of God, that fills the whole earth.—Mark 4:26; Matt. 13:18-23, 38; Heb. 11:5-6; Gen. 5:21-24; Dan. 2:34-35.", "norm_zh": "三复活的基督作为赐生命的灵乃是哪变了形像之大卫的子孙大卫的后裔国度的后裔种子分赐到我们里面把我们作成国度之子在生命中作王活在国度的实际里使我们在国度实现时被祂接去并与祂一同回来作团体砸人的石头消灭世上的国并成为一座大山就是神的国充满全地可四26太十三182338来十一56创五2124但二34352015年夏训第六篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第二册主恢复中的五个重点第三章第三十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The resurrected Christ as the lifegiving Spirit is the transfigured descendant of David the seed of David the seed of the kingdom dispensed into us to make us the sons of the kingdom reigning in life to live in the reality of the kingdom so that we may be translated by Him and return with Him in the manifestation of the kingdom as the corporate smiting stone to annihilate the kingdoms of this world and become a great mountain the kingdom of God that fills the whole earthMark 426 Matt 131823 38 Heb 1156 Gen 52124 Dan 23435"}
{"zh": "伍\t基于耶利米预言到新约，耶利米书这卷旧约的书也可视为新约的书─二13，十七9，十三23，二三5~6，三一31~34，来八8~12：（2015年夏训，第七篇；耶利米书生命读经，第三十九篇，第九段*）", "en": "V.\tBased on the fact that Jeremiah prophesies concerning the new covenant, the book of Jeremiah may be considered an Old Testament book that is also a New Testament book—2:13; 17:9; 13:23; 23:5-6; 31:31-34; Heb. 8:8-12:", "norm_zh": "伍基于耶利米预言到新约耶利米书这卷旧约的书也可视为新约的书二13十七9十三23二三56三一3134来八8122015年夏训第七篇耶利米书生命读经第三十九篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Based on the fact that Jeremiah prophesies concerning the new covenant the book of Jeremiah may be considered an Old Testament book that is also a New Testament book213 179 1323 2356 313134 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "一\t基督自己就是神所赐给我们的新约，新遗命─赛四二6，四九8：（2015年夏训，第七篇；圣经恢复本，赛四二6注2*）", "en": "A.\tChrist Himself is the new covenant, the new testament, given to us by God—Isa. 42:6; 49:8:", "norm_zh": "一基督自己就是神所赐给我们的新约新遗命赛四二6四九82015年夏训第七篇圣经恢复本赛四二6注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ Himself is the new covenant the new testament given to us by GodIsa 426 498"}
{"zh": "1\t神的救恩、神的祝福、以及神一切的丰富都已经立约给了我们；这约就是基督—四二6，四九8。（2015年夏训，第七篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第四十六篇，第九段）", "en": "1.\tGod's salvation, God's blessings, and all of God's riches have been covenanted to us, and this covenant is Christ:—42:6; 49:8.", "norm_zh": "1神的救恩神的祝福以及神一切的丰富都已经立约给了我们这约就是基督四二6四九82015年夏训第七篇以赛亚书生命读经第四十六篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods salvation Gods blessings and all of Gods riches have been covenanted to us and this covenant is Christ426 498"}
{"zh": "2\t接受并享受基督作我们这约的路，乃是借着呼求我们主基督的名，操练我们的灵，照着我们的灵而活，住留在我们灵里；与我们的灵同在的，就是这位基督─四二5~6，亚十二1，罗八4下，启一10上，提后四22，赛十二3~4。（2015年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第三百七十七篇，第十六段*）", "en": "2.\tThe way to receive and enjoy Christ as the covenant to us is to exercise our spirit, to live according to our spirit, and to remain in our spirit, with which is the very Christ, by calling on Christ our Lord's name.—Isa. 42:5-6; Zech. 12:1; Rom. 8:4b; Rev. 1:10a; 2 Tim. 4:22; Isa. 12:3-4.", "norm_zh": "2接受并享受基督作我们这约的路乃是借着呼求我们主基督的名操练我们的灵照着我们的灵而活住留在我们灵里与我们的灵同在的就是这位基督四二56亚十二1罗八4下启一10上提后四22赛十二342015年夏训第七篇新约总论第三百七十七篇第十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The way to receive and enjoy Christ as the covenant to us is to exercise our spirit to live according to our spirit and to remain in our spirit with which is the very Christ by calling on Christ our Lords nameIsa 4256 Zech 121 Rom 84b Rev 110a 2 Tim 422 Isa 1234"}
{"zh": "二\t新遗命的内容包括以下四项福分，作为神给我们的遗赠─耶三一31~34，来八8~12：（2015年夏训，第七篇；圣经恢复本，来八12注1**）", "en": "B. The contents of the new testament include the following four blessings as God's bequests to us.—Jer. 31:31-34; Heb. 8:8-12:", "norm_zh": "二新遗命的内容包括以下四项福分作为神给我们的遗赠耶三一3134来八8122015年夏训第七篇圣经恢复本来八12注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The contents of the new testament include the following four blessings as Gods bequests to usJer 313134 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "1\t“我要将我的律法赐在他们心思里，并且将这些律法写在他们心上”─10节：（2003年安那翰全时间训练，第二十四篇）", "en": "1.\t\"I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them.\"—v. 10:", "norm_zh": "1我要将我的律法赐在他们心思里并且将这些律法写在他们心上10节2003年安哪翰全时间训练第二十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe themv 10"}
{"zh": "a\t每一种生命都有一个律，甚至都是一个律─箴三十19上。（2015年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第三百七十八篇，第十段**）", "en": "a.\tEvery life has a law and even is a law.—Prov. 30:19a.", "norm_zh": "a每一种生命都有一个律甚至都是一个律箴三十19上2015年夏训第七篇新约总论第三百七十八篇第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Every life has a law and even is a lawProv 3019a"}
{"zh": "b\t神的生命是最高的生命，这生命的律是最高的律─赛四十30~31。（2015年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第三百七十八篇，第十段**）", "en": "b\tGod's life is the highest life, and the law of this life is the highest law.—Isa. 40:30-31.", "norm_zh": "b神的生命是最高的生命这生命的律是最高的律赛四十30312015年夏训第七篇新约总论第三百七十八篇第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Gods life is the highest life and the law of this life is the highest lawIsa 403031"}
{"zh": "c\t三一神已经经过成为肉体、钉死、复活并升天的过程，成了生命之灵的律，装置在我们灵里─罗八3、11、34、16。（1999年国际华语特会，第三篇；李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册，在安那翰以及杭庭顿滩市的聚会，第九章，第五段**）", "en": "c\tThe Triune God has been processed through incarnation, crucifixion, resurrection, and ascension to become the law of the Spirit of life installed in our spirit.—Rom. 8:3, 11, 34, 16.", "norm_zh": "c三一神已经经过成为肉体钉死复活并升天的过程成了生命之灵的律装置在我们灵里罗八31134161999年国际华语特会第三篇李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册在安哪翰以及杭庭顿滩市的聚会第九章第五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c The Triune God has been processed through incarnation crucifixion resurrection and ascension to become the law of the Spirit of life installed in our spiritRom 83 11 34 16"}
{"zh": "d\t生命的律，生命之灵的律，乃是经过过程之三一神作赐生命的灵住在我们的灵里─2~3、11、34节。（2015年夏训，第七篇；罗马书生命读经，第六十七篇，第六段*）", "en": "d\tThe law of life, the law of the Spirit of life, is the processed Triune God as the life-giving Spirit dwelling in our spirit.—vv. 2-3, 11, 34.", "norm_zh": "d生命的律生命之灵的律乃是经过过程之三一神作赐生命的灵住在我们的灵里231134节2015年夏训第七篇罗马书生命读经第六十七篇第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d The law of life the law of the Spirit of life is the processed Triune God as the lifegiving Spirit dwelling in our spiritvv 23 11 34"}
{"zh": "e\t生命的律乃是生命自发的能力；这律是生命所具自然的特性，和自有、自动的功能。（2015年夏训，第七篇；希伯来书生命读经，第三十七篇，第十一段**）", "en": "e\tThe law of life is the spontaneous power of life; it is the natural characteristic and the innate, automatic function of life.", "norm_zh": "e生命的律乃是生命自发的能力这律是生命所具自然的特性和自有自动的功能2015年夏训第七篇希伯来书生命读经第三十七篇第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "e The law of life is the spontaneous power of life it is the natural characteristic and the innate automatic function of life"}
{"zh": "f\t生命之灵的律已经装置好，且正在运行，我们必须借着把这律的“开关打开”，而与这律合作─帖前五16~18，路八15。（2015年夏训，第七篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，三一神作三部分人的生命，第六篇，第三十八段*）", "en": "f\tWe need to cooperate with the installed and operating law of the Spirit of life by \"switching on\" this law.—1 Thes. 5:16-18; Luke 8:15.", "norm_zh": "f生命之灵的律已经装置好且正在运行我们必须借着把这律的开关打开而与这律合作帖前五1618路八152015年夏训第七篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册三一神作三部分人的生命第六篇第三十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "f We need to cooperate with the installed and operating law of the Spirit of life by switching on this law1 Thes 51618 Luke 815"}
{"zh": "2\t“我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民”─来八10：（2003年安那翰全时间训练，第二十四篇）", "en": "2\t\"I will be God to them, and they will be a people to Me.\"—Heb. 8:10:", "norm_zh": "2我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民来八102003年安哪翰全时间训练第二十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 I will be God to them and they will be a people to MeHeb 810"}
{"zh": "a\t神作我们的神，意即神是我们的产业；而我们作神的子民，意即我们乃是神的产业─弗一11、14、18，三21。（2015年夏训，第七篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第四十七篇，第十四段*）", "en": "a\tFor God to be our God means that He is our inheritance, and for us to be His people means that we are His inheritance.—Eph. 1:11, 14, 18; 3:21.", "norm_zh": "a神作我们的神意即神是我们的产业而我们作神的子民意即我们乃是神的产业弗一111418三212015年夏训第七篇以赛亚书生命读经第四十七篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a For God to be our God means that He is our inheritance and for us to be His people means that we are His inheritanceEph 111 14 18 321"}
{"zh": "b\t在新约里，我们有特权得着神作我们的神，我们作祂的子民─乃是生命使我们能在与神的交通中享受神，好叫祂被我们所认识、领会，且由我们活出─约壹一3、7。（1999年冬训，第四篇；希伯来书生命读经，第三十六篇，第三十六段**）", "en": "b\tIn the new covenant we have the privilege of having God as our God and of being His people—the capability of life for us to participate in the enjoyment of God in fellowship with Him so that He can be known by us, apprehended by us, and lived by us.—1 John 1:3, 7.", "norm_zh": "b在新约里我们有特权得着神作我们的神我们作祂的子民乃是生命使我们能在与神的交通中享受神好叫祂被我们所认识领会且由我们活出约壹一371999年冬训第四篇希伯来书生命读经第三十六篇第三十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b In the new covenant we have the privilege of having God as our God and of being His peoplethe capability of life for us to participate in the enjoyment of God in fellowship with Him so that He can be known by us apprehended by us and lived by us1 John 13 7"}
{"zh": "3\t“他们各人绝不用教导自己同国之民，各人也绝不用教导自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我”─来八11：（2003年安那翰全时间训练，第二十四篇）", "en": "3\t\"They shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother, saying, Know the Lord; for all will know Me from the little one to the great one among them.\"—Heb. 8:11:", "norm_zh": "3他们各人绝不用教导自己同国之民各人也绝不用教导自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我来八112003年安哪翰全时间训练第二十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 They shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother saying Know the Lord for all will know Me from the little one to the great one among themHeb 811"}
{"zh": "a\t生命的功能使我们能以生命内里的方式认识神—约壹五11，来八11。（2015年夏训，第七篇；约翰福音生命读经，第三十八篇，第三十七段**）", "en": "a\tThe function of life enables us to know God in the inward way of life.—1 John 5:11; Heb. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "a生命的功能使我们能以生命内里的方式认识神约壹五11来八112015年夏训第七篇约翰福音生命读经第三十八篇第三十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The function of life enables us to know God in the inward way of life1 John 511 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "b\t我们能凭生命的感觉，就是我们里面神圣生命的感觉、知觉，而从里面主观地认识神─罗八6，弗四18~20，腓三10上。（2015年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第八十八篇，第十五段*）", "en": "b\tWe can know God subjectively from within by the sense of life, which is the feeling, the consciousness, of the divine life within us.—Rom. 8:6; Eph. 4:18-20; Phil. 3:10a.", "norm_zh": "b我们能凭生命的感觉就是我们里面神圣生命的感觉知觉而从里面主观地认识神罗八6弗四1820腓三10上2015年夏训第七篇新约总论第八十八篇第十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We can know God subjectively from within by the sense of life which is the feeling the consciousness of the divine life within usRom 86 Eph 41820 Phil 310a"}
{"zh": "c\t认识神就是要活神；借着我们里面神圣生命那自然、自动的功用，我们就有性能认识神、活神、甚至在神的生命和性情上与祂成为一，使我们作祂团体的彰显—来八11，腓三10，罗九23。（2015年夏训，第七篇；耶利米书生命读经，第三十九篇，第十八段**）", "en": "c\tTo know God is to live God; through the spontaneous, automatic function of the divine life within us, we have the capacity to know God, to live God, and even to be one with God in His life and nature so that we may be His corporate expression.—Heb. 8:11; Phil. 3:10; Rom. 9:23.", "norm_zh": "c认识神就是要活神借着我们里面神圣生命哪自然自动的功用我们就有性能认识神活神甚至在神的生命和性情上与祂成为一使我们作祂团体的彰显来八11腓三10罗九232015年夏训第七篇耶利米书生命读经第三十九篇第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c To know God is to live God through the spontaneous automatic function of the divine life within us we have the capacity to know God to live God and even to be one with God in His life and nature so that we may be His corporate expressionHeb 811 Phil 310 Rom 923"}
{"zh": "4\t“我要宽恕他们的不义，绝不再记念他们的罪”─来八12：（2003年安那翰全时间训练，第二十四篇）", "en": "4\t\"I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I shall by no means remember anymore.\"—Heb. 8:12:", "norm_zh": "4我要宽恕他们的不义绝不再记念他们的罪来八122003年安哪翰全时间训练第二十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I shall by no means remember anymoreHeb 812"}
{"zh": "a\t基督为我们的罪成就了平息，以平息神的公义，也就是满足了神公义的要求，使我们得以与神和好─二17。（2015年夏训，第七篇；希伯来书生命读经，第八篇，第十六段*）", "en": "a\tChrist made propitiation for our sins to appease God's righteousness, to reconcile us by satisfying the demands of God's righteousness.—Heb. 2:17.", "norm_zh": "a基督为我们的罪成就了平息以平息神的公义也就是满足了神公义的要求使我们得以与神和好二172015年夏训第七篇希伯来书生命读经第八篇第十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Christ made propitiation for our sins to appease Gods righteousness to reconcile us by satisfying the demands of Gods righteousnessHeb 217"}
{"zh": "b\t基督那又宝贵又有功效的血，解决了我们一切的难处，使我们得以维持在与神不断地交通中，不断地享受祂生机的救恩─约壹一7~9，二1~2。（2015年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第一百四十五篇，第二十三段**）", "en": "b\tThe precious and all-efficacious blood of Christ resolves all our problems so that we can remain constantly in fellowship with God to continually enjoy His organic salvation.—1 John 1:7-9; 2:1-2.", "norm_zh": "b基督哪又宝贵又有功效的血解决了我们一切的难处使我们得以维持在与神不断地交通中不断地享受祂生机的救恩约壹一79二122015年夏训第七篇新约总论第一百四十五篇第二十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The precious and allefficacious blood of Christ resolves all our problems so that we can remain constantly in fellowship with God to continually enjoy His organic salvation1 John 179 212"}
{"zh": "c\t神一赦免我们，就从祂的记忆里涂抹我们的罪，不再记念—一9，二2。（1999年国际华语特会，第二篇；李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道，第六题，第十一段*）", "en": "c\tOnce God forgives us, He erases our sins from His memory and remembers them no longer.—1 John 1:9; 2:2.", "norm_zh": "c神一赦免我们就从祂的记忆里涂抹我们的罪不再记念一9二21999年国际华语特会第二篇李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道第六提第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Once God forgives us He erases our sins from His memory and remembers them no longer1 John 19 22"}
{"zh": "d\t神赦免我们的罪，结果使我们恢复与祂的交通，而敬畏祂，并且爱祂─诗一三〇4，路七47。（1999年国际华语特会，第二篇；李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册，圣经要道，第六题，第四十二段，第五十二段*）", "en": "d\tGod's forgiveness of our sins results in our fearing Him and loving Him in our restored fellowship with Him.", "norm_zh": "d神赦免我们的罪结果使我们恢复与祂的交通而敬畏祂并且爱祂诗一三〇4路七471999年国际华语特会第二篇李常受文集一九三二至一九四九年第三册圣经要道第六提第四十二段第五十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d Gods forgiveness of our sins results in our fearing Him and loving Him in our restored fellowship with Him"}
{"zh": "陆\t至终，新约要产生新耶路撒冷，就是神的新约的具体化身，以团体的方式彰显神到极致，直到永远─加四26~28、31。（2015年夏训，第七篇；耶利米书生命读经，第三十三篇，第二十四段*）", "en": "VI.\tThe new covenant will ultimately issue in the New Jerusalem, the embodiment of God's new covenant to express God in a corporate way to the uttermost for eternity.—Gal. 4:26-28, 31.", "norm_zh": "陆至终新约要产生新耶路撒冷就是神的新约的具体化身以团体的方式彰显神到极致直到永远加四2628312015年夏训第七篇耶利米书生命读经第三十三篇第二十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:42:47.166792+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The new covenant will ultimately issue in the New Jerusalem the embodiment of Gods new covenant to express God in a corporate way to the uttermost for eternityGal 42628 31"}
{"zh": "读经：约壹一5~7，赛五十10~11，诗三六9，一一九130、105，十九8下，太五8，弗五8上，约八12，太五14上", "en": "Scripture Reading: 1 John 1:5-7; Isa. 50:10-11; Psa. 36:9; 119:130, 105; 19:8b; Matt. 5:8; Eph. 5:8a; John 8:12; Matt. 5:14a", "norm_zh": "读经约壹一57赛五十1011诗三六9一一九130105十九8下太五8弗五8上约八12太五14上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 1 John 157 Isa 501011 Psa 369 119130 105 198b Matt 58 Eph 58a John 812 Matt 514a"}
{"zh": "一\t光是神的照耀，神的彰显；当神得着彰显的时候，那个彰显的性质就是光—5节，约八12，赛六3：", "en": "A.\tLight is God's shining, God's expression; when God is expressed, the nature of that expression is light.—v. 5; John 8:12; Isa. 6:3:", "norm_zh": "一光是神的照耀神的彰显当神得着彰显的时候哪个彰显的性质就是光5节约八12赛六3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Light is Gods shining Gods expression when God is expressed the nature of that expression is lightv 5 John 812 Isa 63"}
{"zh": "1\t在神圣的光中行，就是在神圣的光中生活、行动、行事并为人；这光就是神自己—约八12，约壹一7。", "en": "1.\tTo walk in the divine light is to live, move, act, and have our being in the divine light, which is God Himself.—John 8:12; 1 John 1:7.", "norm_zh": "1在神圣的光中行就是在神圣的光中生活行动行事并为人这光就是神自己约八12约壹一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To walk in the divine light is to live move act and have our being in the divine light which is God HimselfJohn 812 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "2\t神圣的光照耀时，神圣的事物对我们就成为实际的—12节，弗四21，约十四6。", "en": "2.\tWhen the divine light shines, the divine things become real to us.—v. 12; Eph. 4:21; John 14:6.", "norm_zh": "2神圣的光照耀时神圣的事物对我们就成为实际的12节弗四21约十四6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When the divine light shines the divine things become real to usv 12 Eph 421 John 146"}
{"zh": "一\t光，是从神来的，不是从人来的—10节，创一3。", "en": "A.\tLight comes from God alone, not from man.—v. 10; Gen. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "一光是从神来的不是从人来的10节创一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Light comes from God alone not from manv 10 Gen 13"}
{"zh": "二\t属灵的黑暗，不是人的火所能除去的，这火绝不会带进真正属灵的光；我们自己所点的火，永远不是属灵之光的源头—赛五十11，利十1~2：", "en": "B.\tSpiritual darkness cannot be removed by human fire, which never brings in genuine spiritual light; our own fire cannot be the source of spiritual light.—Isa. 50:11; Lev. 10:1-2:", "norm_zh": "二属灵的黑暗不是人的火所能除去的这火绝不会带进真正属灵的光我们自己所点的火永远不是属灵之光的源头赛五十11利十12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Spiritual darkness cannot be removed by human fire which never brings in genuine spiritual light our own fire cannot be the source of spiritual lightIsa 5011 Lev 1012"}
{"zh": "1\t基督徒不能借着自己的火来走属灵的道路；他应当倚靠耶和华的名，仗赖自己的神—1~2节，赛五十10，约八12。", "en": "1.\tA Christian cannot advance in the spiritual pathway by his own fire; he should trust in the name of Jehovah and rely on his God.—vv. 1-2; Isa. 50:10; John 8:12.", "norm_zh": "1基督徒不能借着自己的火来走属灵的道路他应当倚靠耶和华的名仗赖自己的神12节赛五十10约八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A Christian cannot advance in the spiritual pathway by his own fire he should trust in the name of Jehovah and rely on his Godvv 12 Isa 5010 John 812"}
{"zh": "2\t属灵的光，不是从我们的感觉和思想来的—利十1~2，约壹一7。", "en": "2.\tSpiritual light does not come from our own feelings or thoughts.—Lev. 10:1-2; 1 John 1:7.", "norm_zh": "2属灵的光不是从我们的感觉和思想来的利十12约壹一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Spiritual light does not come from our own feelings or thoughtsLev 1012 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "3\t人越往自己里面找光，就越没有光，因为光不在那里—5节，约八12。", "en": "3.\tThe more a person searches inwardly for light, the more he will not find light, because light is not there.—v. 5; John 8:12.", "norm_zh": "3人越往自己里面找光就越没有光因为光不在哪里5节约八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The more a person searches inwardly for light the more he will not find light because light is not therev 5 John 812"}
{"zh": "一\t我们在神的光中才能看见光，并看见事情的真相—9节：", "en": "A.\tThrough God's light we see light and the true condition of things:—v. 9:", "norm_zh": "一我们在神的光中才能看见光并看见事情的真相9节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through Gods light we see light and the true condition of thingsv 9"}
{"zh": "1\t诗篇三十六篇九节里的第一个光是指光照的光，第二个光是指事情的真相。", "en": "1.\tThe first light in Psalm 36:9 is the enlightening light, and the second light denotes the true nature of things.", "norm_zh": "1诗篇三十六篇九节里的第一个光是指光照的光第二个光是指事情的真相", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The first light in Psalm 369 is the enlightening light and the second light denotes the true nature of things"}
{"zh": "二\t在神的光中才能看见神所看见的，这就是在神的光中得见光—诗三六9，约八12。", "en": "B.\tWhen we are in God's light, we see what God sees; this is seeing light in God's light.—Psa. 36:9; John 8:12.", "norm_zh": "二在神的光中才能看见神所看见的这就是在神的光中得见光诗三六9约八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we are in Gods light we see what God sees this is seeing light in Gods lightPsa 369 John 812"}
{"zh": "伍\t神是光，这光凝聚在神的话中；因此，神的话乃是神这神圣之光的具体化—约壹一5，诗一一九105、130：", "en": "V. God is light, and this light is consolidated in the Word; therefore, the Word of God is the embodiment of God as the divine light—1 John 1:5; Psa. 119:105, 130:", "norm_zh": "伍神是光这光凝聚在神的话中因此神的话乃是神这神圣之光的具体化约壹一5诗一一九105130", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V God is light and this light is consolidated in the Word therefore the Word of God is the embodiment of God as the divine light1 John 15 Psa 119105 130"}
{"zh": "一\t神的话是神圣之光的“凝聚”，所以每当我们来到神的话前，我们应当觉得我们是在光的气氛中—三六9，一一九105。", "en": "A.\tThe Word is the consolidation of the divine light, so whenever we come to the Word, we should sense that we are in an atmosphere of light.—Psa. 36:9; 119:105.", "norm_zh": "一神的话是神圣之光的凝聚所以每当我们来到神的话前我们应当觉得我们是在光的气氛中三六9一一九105", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Word is the consolidation of the divine light so whenever we come to the Word we should sense that we are in an atmosphere of lightPsa 369 119105"}
{"zh": "二\t我们若以正确的态度来到神的话前，我们就会在光中，并在光之下，而不仅是接受光而已—约壹一6~7。", "en": "B.\tIf we come to the Word with a proper attitude, we will be in the light and under the light and not merely receive light.—1 John 1:6-7.", "norm_zh": "二我们若以正确的态度来到神的话前我们就会在光中并在光之下而不仅是接受光而已约壹一67", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B If we come to the Word with a proper attitude we will be in the light and under the light and not merely receive light1 John 167"}
{"zh": "陆\t在爱神之寻求者的经历里，神的话就是光的范围—诗三六9，一一九130：", "en": "VI.\tIn the experience of God's loving seekers, the Word of God is a realm of light:—Psa. 36:9; 119:130:", "norm_zh": "陆在爱神之寻求者的经历里神的话就是光的范围诗三六9一一九130", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI In the experience of Gods loving seekers the Word of God is a realm of lightPsa 369 119130"}
{"zh": "一\t因着神的话乃是光的范围，神的话一解开，就发出亮光—130节。", "en": "A.\tBecause the Word is a realm of light, the opening of God's words gives light.—v. 130.", "norm_zh": "一因着神的话乃是光的范围神的话一解开就发出亮光130节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Because the Word is a realm of light the opening of Gods words gives lightv 130"}
{"zh": "2\t光的果子与三一神有关—太十九17，罗五21，约十四17：", "en": "2\tThe fruit of the light is related to the Triune God:—Matt. 19:17; Rom. 5:21; John 14:17:", "norm_zh": "2光的果子与三一神有关太十九17罗五21约十四17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The fruit of the light is related to the Triune GodMatt 1917 Rom 521 John 1417"}
{"zh": "2\t国度乃是主耶稣照耀在我们身上，国度也是主耶稣借着照耀在我们身上而有的扩展—彼前二9，太四23，出十九6。", "en": "2\tThe kingdom is the Lord Jesus shining over us, and the kingdom is the spreading of the Lord Jesus by shining over us.—1 Pet. 2:9; Matt. 4:23; Exo. 19:6.", "norm_zh": "2国度乃是主耶稣照耀在我们身上国度也是主耶稣借着照耀在我们身上而有的扩展彼前二9太四23出十九6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The kingdom is the Lord Jesus shining over us and the kingdom is the spreading of the Lord Jesus by shining over us1 Pet 29 Matt 423 Exo 196"}
{"zh": "柒\t神的话在我们的经历中对我们是不是光的范围，乃在于我们来到神话语前的态度和光景—诗一一九105，约壹一5~7：", "en": "VII.\tWhether or not the Word is a realm of light to us in our experience depends on our attitude and condition in coming to the Word:—Psa. 119:105; 1 John 1:5-7:", "norm_zh": "柒神的话在我们的经历中对我们是不是光的范围乃在于我们来到神话语前的态度和光景诗一一九105约壹一57", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII Whether or not the Word is a realm of light to us in our experience depends on our attitude and condition in coming to the WordPsa 119105 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "二\t我们全人的各部分应当敞开，接受主的光照—箴二十27，诗六七1。", "en": "B.\tAll the chambers of our being should be open to receive the Lord's shining.—Prov. 20:27; Psa. 67:1.", "norm_zh": "二我们全人的各部分应当敞开接受主的光照箴二十27诗六七1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B All the chambers of our being should be open to receive the Lords shiningProv 2027 Psa 671"}
{"zh": "三\t我们需要对付我们的心，而向主有一个正确的心—路八13~15，耶二九13，西三23：", "en": "C.\tWe need to deal with our heart and have a proper heart toward the Lord.—Luke 8:13-15; Jer. 29:13; Col. 3:23:", "norm_zh": "三我们需要对付我们的心而向主有一个正确的心路八1315耶二九13西三23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We need to deal with our heart and have a proper heart toward the LordLuke 81315 Jer 2913 Col 323"}
{"zh": "2\t惟独神是光，惟独神是光的源头，也惟独在神的光中，我们才能见光—诗三六9，约壹一5，约八12。", "en": "2\tOnly God is light, only God is the source of light, and only in the light of God can we see light.—Psa. 36:9; 1 John 1:5; John 8:12.", "norm_zh": "2惟独神是光惟独神是光的源头也惟独在神的光中我们才能见光诗三六9约壹一5约八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Only God is light only God is the source of light and only in the light of God can we see lightPsa 369 1 John 15 John 812"}
{"zh": "1\t在神的经纶中并在神的召会里，只有一个窗，一个启示，和一个异象—徒九4~5，二六19，创六16，弗四3~4。", "en": "1\tIn God's economy and in God's church there is only one window, one revelation, and one vision.—Acts 9:4-5; 26:19; Gen. 6:16; Eph. 4:3-4.", "norm_zh": "1在神的经纶中并在神的召会里只有一个窗一个启示和一个异象徒九45二六19创六16弗四34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In Gods economy and in Gods church there is only one window one revelation and one visionActs 945 2619 Gen 616 Eph 434"}
{"zh": "2\t我们必须照着这时代的异象事奉神，而这异象乃是借着这时代的职事而有的—徒二六19。", "en": "2\tWe need to serve God according to the vision of the age, which comes through the ministry of the age.—Acts 26:19.", "norm_zh": "2我们必须照着这时代的异象事奉神而这异象乃是借着这时代的职事而有的徒二六19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:43:56.144386+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We need to serve God according to the vision of the age which comes through the ministry of the ageActs 2619"}
