{"zh": "a\t生命出于光；光是生命的关键—约八12，一4。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九五三年第三册，生命的认识，第十四篇，第十六段*；以赛亚书生命读经，第三十七篇，第四段*）", "en": "a\tLife comes from light; light is the key to life.—John 8:12; 1:4.", "norm_zh": "a生命出于光光是生命的关键约八12一42015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九五三年第三册生命的认识第十四篇第十六段以赛亚书生命读经第三十七篇第四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Life comes from light light is the key to lifeJohn 812 14"}
{"zh": "b\t在神那一面，先有生命，然后有光；在我们这一面，先有光，然后有生命—诗三六9，约一1、4~5，八12，林后四6，徒二六13。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册，新约圣经中奇妙的基督，第二十一章，第五段**）", "en": "b\tOn God's side, there is first life and then light; on our side, there is first light and then life.—Psa. 36:9; John 1:1, 4-5; 8:12; 2 Cor. 4:6; Acts 26:13.", "norm_zh": "b在神哪一面先有生命然后有光在我们这一面先有光然后有生命诗三六9约一145八12林后四6徒二六132015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第二册新约圣经中奇妙的基督第二十一章第五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b On Gods side there is first life and then light on our side there is first light and then lifePsa 369 John 11 45 812 2 Cor 46 Acts 2613"}
{"zh": "5\t光照耀到哪里，生命就供应到哪里—约一4，八12，林后四6，三18。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九七九年第一册，生命信息卷二，第六十九章，第三十八段*）", "en": "5\tWhere the light shines, there the life supply goes.—John 1:4; 8:12; 2 Cor. 4:6; 3:18.", "norm_zh": "5光照耀到哪里生命就供应到哪里约一4八12林后四6三182015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九七九年第一册生命信息卷二第六十九章第三十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Where the light shines there the life supply goesJohn 14 812 2 Cor 46 318"}
{"zh": "6\t神变化我们的路是借着光照；光照耀到哪里，生命就供应到哪里，使我们变化—18节，四6。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九七九年第一册，生命信息卷二，第六十九章，第三十八段**）", "en": "6\tGod's way of transforming us is through enlightening; wherever the light shines, life is supplied to that place for our transformation.—v. 18; 4:6.", "norm_zh": "6神变化我们的路是借着光照光照耀到哪里生命就供应到哪里使我们变化18节四62015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九七九年第一册生命信息卷二第六十九章第三十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Gods way of transforming us is through enlightening wherever the light shines life is supplied to that place for our transformationv 18 46"}
{"zh": "1\t虽然有光是好的，但光必须更深地透入，直到成为生命—约一4，八12，十二36，林后三18。（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十九篇，第四十五段**）", "en": "1\tAlthough it is good to have light, the light must penetrate deeper until it becomes life.—John 1:4; 8:12; 12:36; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "1虽然有光是好的但光必须更深地透入直到成为生命约一4八12十二36林后三182015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第五十九篇第四十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Although it is good to have light the light must penetrate deeper until it becomes lifeJohn 14 812 1236 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "2\t当光更深入达到我们的灵里，光就成了生命，我们便得着生命的供应—玛四2，林后三18。（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第五十九篇，第四十七段*）", "en": "2\tWhen light goes deeper, reaching into our spirit, it becomes life, and we receive the life supply.—Mal. 4:2; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "2当光更深入达到我们的灵里光就成了生命我们便得着生命的供应玛四2林后三182015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第五十九篇第四十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When light goes deeper reaching into our spirit it becomes life and we receive the life supplyMal 42 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "一\t爱神的寻求者所经历的福，乃是被神的话浇灌—2~3节：（2015年夏训，第四篇***）", "en": "A.\tGod's loving seekers experience the blessing of being watered by the Word:—vv. 2-3:", "norm_zh": "一爱神的寻求者所经历的福乃是被神的话浇灌23节2015年夏训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods loving seekers experience the blessing of being watered by the Wordvv 23"}
{"zh": "二\t爱神的寻求者所经历的福，乃是借着神的话吸取神—西二7上，耶十五16，约一1，西二19：（2015年夏训，第四篇；*）", "en": "B.\tGod's loving seekers experience the blessing of absorbing God through the Word:—Col. 2:7a; Jer. 15:16; John 1:1; Col. 2:19:", "norm_zh": "二爱神的寻求者所经历的福乃是借着神的话吸取神西二7上耶十五16约一1西二192015年夏训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Gods loving seekers experience the blessing of absorbing God through the WordCol 27a Jer 1516 John 11 Col 219"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若接触主，并且花时间用许多祷告读主的话，就会将神吸取到我们里面，作为使我们长大的元素—三16，约六63下，西二19。（2015年夏训，第四篇；歌罗西书生命读经，第四十六篇，第三十五段**）", "en": "2\tIf we contact the Lord and spend time in the Word with much prayer, we will absorb God into us to be the element that causes us to grow.—3:16; John 6:63b; Col. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "2我们若接触主并且花时间用许多祷告读主的话就会将神吸取到我们里面作为使我们长大的元素三16约六63下西二192015年夏训第四篇歌罗西书生命读经第四十六篇第三十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we contact the Lord and spend time in the Word with much prayer we will absorb God into us to be the element that causes us to grow316 John 663b Col 219"}
{"zh": "二\t说圣经都是神的呼出，就是说圣经是那是灵之神的气，呼出—提后三16上，约二十22：（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第二十段*）", "en": "B.\tTo say that all Scripture is God-breathed is to say that the Bible is the breath, the breathing out, of God, who is Spirit.—2 Tim. 3:16a; John 20:22:", "norm_zh": "二说圣经都是神的呼出就是说圣经是哪是灵之神的气呼出提后三16上约二十222015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B To say that all Scripture is Godbreathed is to say that the Bible is the breath the breathing out of God who is Spirit2 Tim 316a John 2022"}
{"zh": "1\t因着圣经就是神的呼出，圣经就有神的成分—提后三16上，约五39。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第一篇，第六十二段**）", "en": "1\tBecause the Bible is the breathing out of God, the Bible has the element of God.—2 Tim. 3:16a; John 5:39.", "norm_zh": "1因着圣经就是神的呼出圣经就有神的成分提后三16上约五392015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第一篇第六十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Because the Bible is the breathing out of God the Bible has the element of God2 Tim 316a John 539"}
{"zh": "2\t圣经不仅是神的呼出，并且是神把祂的自己呼到祂的话里—提后三16上，约一1、14，五39，六63下。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九五九年第三册，认识圣经，第一篇，第五十五段**）", "en": "2\tThe Bible is not only the breathing out of God but is God Himself breathed into His Word.—2 Tim. 3:16a; John 1:1, 14; 5:39; 6:63b.", "norm_zh": "2圣经不仅是神的呼出并且是神把祂的自己呼到祂的话里提后三16上约一114五39六63下2015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九五九年第三册认识圣经第一篇第五十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Bible is not only the breathing out of God but is God Himself breathed into His Word2 Tim 316a John 11 14 539 663b"}
{"zh": "三\t神已经在祂的话里把自己呼出来，使我们能借着祂的话吸入祂，将祂吸入—耶十五16，诗一一九57，罗十13：（2015年夏训，第四篇；*）", "en": "C.\tGod has breathed Himself out in the Word so that we can inhale Him, breathe Him in, through the Word:—Jer. 15:16; Psa. 119:57; Rom. 10:13:", "norm_zh": "三神已经在祂的话里把自己呼出来使我们能借着祂的话吸入祂将祂吸入耶十五16诗一一九57罗十132015年夏训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God has breathed Himself out in the Word so that we can inhale Him breathe Him in through the WordJer 1516 Psa 11957 Rom 1013"}
{"zh": "1\t神在圣经里已将祂自己呼出，因此我们读圣经，应当是接受神的气—提后三16上，约二十22。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第七段**）", "en": "1\tGod has breathed Himself out in the Scriptures, and thus our reading of the Scriptures should be the receiving of God's breath.—2 Tim. 3:16a; John 20:22.", "norm_zh": "1神在圣经里已将祂自己呼出因此我们读圣经应当是接受神的气提后三16上约二十222015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God has breathed Himself out in the Scriptures and thus our reading of the Scriptures should be the receiving of Gods breath2 Tim 316a John 2022"}
{"zh": "2\t神将祂自己呼出时，乃是呼出祂自己；我们借着神的话接触神时，就是吸入神—约二十22，提后三16上，耶十五16。（2015年夏训，第四篇；李常受文集一九八四年第一册，教师训练，第一章，第七段**）", "en": "2\tWhen God breathes Himself out, He exhales Himself, and when we contact God through the Word, we inhale God.—John 20:22; 2 Tim. 3:16a; Jer. 15:16.", "norm_zh": "2神将祂自己呼出时乃是呼出祂自己我们借着神的话接触神时就是吸入神约二十22提后三16上耶十五162015年夏训第四篇李常受文集一九八四年第一册教师训练第一章第七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When God breathes Himself out He exhales Himself and when we contact God through the Word we inhale GodJohn 2022 2 Tim 316a Jer 1516"}
{"zh": "二\t当我们有神作我们的业分，我们就有神自己作我们的一切—诗七三26，一一九57，十六5，赛十二2。（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十篇，第十二段**）", "en": "B.\tWhen we have God as our portion, we have God Himself as everything to us.—Psa. 73:26; 119:57; 16:5; Isa. 12:2.", "norm_zh": "二当我们有神作我们的业分我们就有神自己作我们的一切诗七三26一一九57十六5赛十二22015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第六十篇第十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we have God as our portion we have God Himself as everything to usPsa 7326 11957 165 Isa 122"}
{"zh": "三\t我们越以正确的方式来到圣经跟前，这本书的著者—神自己，就越成为我们的业分—诗七三26，十六5，约五39~40。（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十篇，第十九段**）", "en": "C.\tThe more we come to the Bible in the proper way, the more the Author of this book—God Himself—becomes our portion.—Psa. 73:26; 16:5; John 5:39-40.", "norm_zh": "三我们越以正确的方式来到圣经跟前这本书的着者神自己就越成为我们的业分诗七三26十六5约五39402015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第六十篇第十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The more we come to the Bible in the proper way the more the Author of this bookGod Himselfbecomes our portionPsa 7326 165 John 53940"}
{"zh": "四\t神能作我们的业分，因为在神的话里、凭神的话且借神的话，祂对我们是真实、现时、实际、可享受且便利的—诗一一九103，三四8。（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十篇，第十四段**）", "en": "D.\tGod can be our portion because in the Word, by the Word, and through the Word He is real, present, practical, enjoyable, and available to us.—Psa. 119:103; 34:8.", "norm_zh": "四神能作我们的业分因为在神的话里凭神的话且借神的话祂对我们是真实现时实际可享受且便利的诗一一九103三四82015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第六十篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God can be our portion because in the Word by the Word and through the Word He is real present practical enjoyable and available to usPsa 119103 348"}
{"zh": "二\t在民数记六章二十五至二十六节的祝福里，提到面和脸：（2015年夏训，第四篇；民数记生命读经，第十一篇，第二十六段**）", "en": "B.\tIn the blessing in Numbers 6:25-26, we have both the face and the countenance:", "norm_zh": "二在民数记六章二十五至二十六节的祝福里提到面和脸2015年夏训第四篇民数记生命读经第十一篇第二十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In the blessing in Numbers 62526 we have both the face and the countenance"}
{"zh": "1\t面指一个人的同在，脸指那人的表情—诗二十四6，民六25，林后三18。（2015年夏训，第四篇；圣经恢复本，民六26注1*）", "en": "1\tThe face denotes the presence of a person, and the countenance denotes the expression of the person.—Psa. 24:6; Num. 6:25; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "1面指一个人的同在脸指哪人的表情诗二十四6民六25林后三182015年夏训第四篇圣经恢复本民六26注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The face denotes the presence of a person and the countenance denotes the expression of the personPsa 246 Num 625 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "2\t当经过过程并终极完成的三一神，借着祂话语的功用分赐到我们里面时，我们就有神的面，也有祂的脸—十三14，四6。（2015年夏训，第四篇；圣经恢复本，民六26注1**）", "en": "2\tWhen the processed and consummated Triune God is dispensed into us through the function of the Word, we have the face of God and also His countenance.—2 Cor. 13:14; 4:6.", "norm_zh": "2当经过过程并终极完成的三一神借着祂话语的功用分赐到我们里面时我们就有神的面也有祂的脸十三14四62015年夏训第四篇圣经恢复本民六26注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When the processed and consummated Triune God is dispensed into us through the function of the Word we have the face of God and also His countenance2 Cor 1314 46"}
{"zh": "三\t我们若忠心地借着话接触主，就会经历祂面的光照—6节，三16、18：（2015年夏训，第四篇；出埃及记生命读经，第六十篇，第二十四段*）", "en": "C.\tIf we are faithful in contacting the Lord through the Word, we will experience the shining of His face.—v. 6; 3:16, 18:", "norm_zh": "三我们若忠心地借着话接触主就会经历祂面的光照6节三16182015年夏训第四篇出埃及记生命读经第六十篇第二十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:47:38.013088+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C If we are faithful in contacting the Lord through the Word we will experience the shining of His facev 6 316 18"}
{"zh": "读经：太二六28，约一17，创四六、四九，徒十八9，六6，林前一，加三，四4，弗一17", "en": "Scripture Reading: Matt. 26:28; John 1:17; Gen. 46; 49; Acts 18:9; 6:6; 1 Cor. 1; Gal. 3; 4:4; Eph. 1:17", "norm_zh": "读经太二六28约一17创四六四九徒十八9六6林前一加三四4弗一17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Matt 2628 John 117 Gen 46 49 Acts 189 66 1 Cor 1 Gal 3 44 Eph 117"}
{"zh": "壹\t神永远的目的是显在新约里；“恩典和真理，都是由耶稣基督来的”所以到了基督，才是恩典时代，才有新约，才看得见神永远的目的—约一17，来八8~13，十16，耶三一31，林后三6，来十三20~21：", "en": "I. God's eternal purpose is manifested in the New Testament; \"grace and reality came through Jesus Christ,\" so it is only when Christ came that there was the age of grace, that there was the New Testament, and that we could see God's eternal purpose.—John 1:17; Heb. 8:8-13; 10:16; Jer. 31:31; 2 Cor. 3:6; Heb. 13:20-21:", "norm_zh": "壹神永远的目的是显在新约里恩典和真理都是由耶稣基督来的所以到了基督才是恩典时代才有新约才看得见神永远的目的约一17来八813十16耶三一31林后三6来十三2021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Gods eternal purpose is manifested in the New Testament grace and reality came through Jesus Christ so it is only when Christ came that there was the age of grace that there was the New Testament and that we could see Gods eternal purposeJohn 117 Heb 8813 1016 Jer 3131 2 Cor 36 Heb 132021"}
{"zh": "一\t神永远的目的，就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去；神喜欢进到人里面与人联合，叫人有祂的生命，有祂的性情—约一17，创一27：", "en": "A. God's eternal purpose is to work Himself into the man whom He created; God likes to enter into man and be joined to man so that man would have His life and nature.—John 1:17; Gen. 1:27:", "norm_zh": "一神永远的目的就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去神喜欢进到人里面与人联合叫人有祂的生命有祂的性情约一17创一27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods eternal purpose is to work Himself into the man whom He created God likes to enter into man and be joined to man so that man would have His life and natureJohn 117 Gen 127"}
{"zh": "1\t祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分，祂就是要人像祂，祂就是要人得荣耀；所以，祂造人的时候，是照着自己的形像造人—弗一4~5，罗八30，创一27。", "en": "1. He wants man to obtain the sonship of His Son, He wants man to be like Him, and He wants man to be glorified; therefore, when He created man, He created him in His own image.—Eph. 1:4-5; Rom. 8:30; Gen. 1:27.", "norm_zh": "1祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分祂就是要人像祂祂就是要人得荣耀所以祂造人的时候是照着自己的形像造人弗一45罗八30创一27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 He wants man to obtain the sonship of His Son He wants man to be like Him and He wants man to be glorified therefore when He created man He created him in His own imageEph 145 Rom 830 Gen 127"}
{"zh": "2\t神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里，祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子；换句话说，祂是示意：生命树的果子是应该吃的，不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的—二8~9。", "en": "2. God placed the created man in the Garden of Eden, and He only forbade man to eat of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil; in other words, He was implying that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten, but this was for man to choose of his own initiative.—Gen. 2:8-9.", "norm_zh": "2神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子换句话说祂是示意生命树的果子是应该吃的不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的二89", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 God placed the created man in the Garden of Eden and He only forbade man to eat of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil in other words He was implying that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten but this was for man to choose of his own initiativeGen 289"}
{"zh": "3\t头一个人虽然失败了，堕落了，第二个人，就是末后的亚当，却达到了神永远的目的！—林前十五45、47：", "en": "3. Although the first man failed and fell, the second man, who is the last Adam, has attained God's eternal purpose!—1 Cor. 15:45, 47:", "norm_zh": "3头一个人虽然失败了堕落了第二个人就是末后的亚当却达到了神永远的目的林前十五4547", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Although the first man failed and fell the second man who is the last Adam has attained Gods eternal purpose1 Cor 1545 47"}
{"zh": "a\t这就是“道成了肉身，住在我们中间，充充满满地有恩典有真理”的主耶稣—约一14。", "en": "a. This is the Lord Jesus, who is \"the Word became flesh, tabernacled among us, full of grace and reality.\"—John 1:14.", "norm_zh": "a这就是道成了肉身住在我们中间充充满满地有恩典有真理的主耶稣约一14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a This is the Lord Jesus who is the Word became flesh tabernacled among us full of grace and realityJohn 114"}
{"zh": "b\t虽然从来没有人看见神，但是，有一个人，就是在父怀里的独生子，将祂表明出来了—18。", "en": "b. Although no one has ever seen God, there is one, the only begotten Son, who is in the bosom of the Father, who has declared Him.—v. 18.", "norm_zh": "b虽然从来没有人看见神但是有一个人就是在父怀里的独生子将祂表明出来了18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Although no one has ever seen God there is one the only begotten Son who is in the bosom of the Father who has declared Himv 18"}
{"zh": "4\t神就是要把祂作到人里面去，就是要人像祂儿子的形状，这是神永远的目的，这也就是新约—罗八28、29。", "en": "4. God wants to work Himself into man and wants man to be conformed to the image of His Son; this is God's eternal purpose, and this is also the New Testament.—Rom. 8:28-29.", "norm_zh": "4神就是要把祂作到人里面去就是要人像祂儿子的形状这是神永远的目的这也就是新约罗八2829", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 God wants to work Himself into man and wants man to be conformed to the image of His Son this is Gods eternal purpose and this is also the New TestamentRom 82829"}
{"zh": "二\t主以新约的原则对待祂的教会；主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下，要教会按着约与祂来往，按着约与祂交涉，直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切；主说，“……这是我立新约的血”—太二六28，来八8：", "en": "B. The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant; the Lord has placed the church under the principle of the new covenant, wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and to deal with Him according to the covenant, until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish; the Lord said, \"...this is My blood of the new covenant.\"—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 8:8:", "norm_zh": "二主以新约的原则对待祂的教会主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下要教会按着约与祂来往按着约与祂交涉直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切主说这是我立新约的血太二六28来八8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant the Lord has placed the church under the principle of the new covenant wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and to deal with Him according to the covenant until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish the Lord said this is My blood of the new covenantMatt 2628 Heb 88"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们，有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约；并且严格说来，新约是要到那些日子以后，就是千禧年开始的时候才立的。", "en": "1. Heb. 8:8 clearly tells us that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah; and strictly speaking, the new covenant will not be made until after those days, which is at the beginning of the millennium.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约并且严格说来新约是要到哪些日子以后就是千禧年开始的时候才立的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Heb 88 clearly tells us that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah and strictly speaking the new covenant will not be made until after those days which is at the beginning of the millennium"}
{"zh": "2\t主是用祂的血立了新约，使我们能预先得着新约的福；所以我们说，今天是新约的时代，乃是由于主特别的恩典—太二六28。", "en": "2. The Lord established the new covenant with His blood, enabling us to have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant; therefore, we say that today is the new covenant age, which is because of the Lord's special grace.—Matt. 26:28.", "norm_zh": "2主是用祂的血立了新约使我们能预先得着新约的福所以我们说今天是新约的时代乃是由于主特别的恩典太二六28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Lord established the new covenant with His blood enabling us to have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant therefore we say that today is the new covenant age which is because of the Lords special graceMatt 2628"}
{"zh": "三\t我们要认识什么是新约，必须先认识什么是约；要认识什么是约，必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实—约十四13~14，十六13、二十27。", "en": "C. To know what the new covenant is, we must first know what a covenant is; to know what a covenant is, we must first know what God's promise is and what God's fact is.—John 14:13-14; 16:13; 20:27.", "norm_zh": "三我们要认识什么是新约必须先认识什么是约要认识什么是约必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实约十四1314十六13二十27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C To know what the new covenant is we must first know what a covenant is to know what a covenant is we must first know what Gods promise is and what Gods fact isJohn 141314 1613 2027"}
{"zh": "贰\t神的话在恩典方面，总括地说，可以分为三种：（一）神所给我们的应许，（二）神所已经为我们成功的事实，（三）神与人立的约，就是神所绝对要作的—十四11~12，徒二17~36。", "en": "II. God's Word in the aspect of grace may be summed up into three categories: 1) the promises of God to us, 2) the facts which God has accomplished for us, and 3) the covenants which God has made with man which He Himself will definitely fulfill.—John 14:11-12; Acts 2:17-36.", "norm_zh": "贰神的话在恩典方面总括地说可以分为三种一神所给我们的应许二神所已经为我们成功的事实三神与人立的约就是神所绝对要作的十四1112徒二1736", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Gods Word in the aspect of grace may be summed up into three categories 1 the promises of God to us 2 the facts which God has accomplished for us and 3 the covenants which God has made with man which He Himself will definitely fulfillJohn 141112 Acts 21736"}
{"zh": "叁\t应许是与事实不同的，应许是将来的，事实是已往的；应许是要作的，事实是已作的；应许是神要为人作什么，事实是神已经为人作成了什么—代下一9，弗六2~3，罗四13~14，来十一39~40：", "en": "III. A promise is different from a fact; promise is related to the future, while fact is related to the past; promise is something to be done, while fact is something already done; promise means that God will do something for man, while fact means that God has already done something for man.—2 Chron. 1:9; Eph. 6:2-3; Rom. 4:13-14; Heb. 11:39-40:", "norm_zh": "叁应许是与事实不同的应许是将来的事实是已往的应许是要作的事实是已作的应许是神要为人作什么事实是神已经为人作成了什么代下一9弗六23罗四1314来十一3940", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III A promise is different from a fact promise is related to the future while fact is related to the past promise is something to be done while fact is something already done promise means that God will do something for man while fact means that God has already done something for man2 Chron 19 Eph 623 Rom 41314 Heb 113940"}
{"zh": "一\t关于神的应许有以下四个原则—代下一9，弗六2~3，罗四13~14，来十一39~40：", "en": "A. Concerning God's promises, there are the following four principles:—2 Chron. 1:9; Eph. 6:2-3; Rom. 4:13-14; Heb. 11:39-40:", "norm_zh": "一关于神的应许有以下四个原则代下一9弗六23罗四1314来十一3940", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Concerning Gods promises there are the following four principles2 Chron 19 Eph 623 Rom 41314 Heb 113940"}
{"zh": "1\t神的应许是需要求神成就的—代下一9。", "en": "1. God's promise requires our prayer that it may be fulfilled—2 Chron. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "1神的应许是需要求神成就的代下一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods promise requires our prayer that it may be fulfilled2 Chron 19"}
{"zh": "2\t神的应许如果是有条件的，人必须履行了所应当履行的条件，才能得着所应许的；不然的话，应许就有取消的可能—弗六2~3。", "en": "2. If God's promise is conditional, man must fulfill His condition in order to obtain the promise; otherwise, the promise may be revoked—Eph. 6:2-3.", "norm_zh": "2神的应许如果是有条件的人必须履行了所应当履行的条件才能得着所应许的不然的话应许就有取消的可能弗六23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If Gods promise is conditional man must fulfill His condition in order to obtain the promise otherwise the promise may be revokedEph 623"}
{"zh": "3\t人若在神的应许之外用血气的力量作了什么，或者加上什么，应许也有废弃落空的可能—罗四13~14。", "en": "3. If, apart from God's promise, man uses the strength of his flesh to act or to add something, the promise may become of none effect—Rom. 4:13-14.", "norm_zh": "3人若在神的应许之外用血气的力量作了什么或者加上什么应许也有废弃落空的可能罗四1314", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If apart from Gods promise man uses the strength of his flesh to act or to add something the promise may become of none effectRom 41314"}
{"zh": "4\t神的应许是要等到神的时候到了，才能实现—来十一39~40。", "en": "4. God's promises are fulfilled in God's time—Heb. 11:39-40.", "norm_zh": "4神的应许是要等到神的时候到了才能实现来十一3940", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Gods promises are fulfilled in Gods timeHeb 113940"}
{"zh": "二\t神的应许如何能成功在我们身上—林后十三3，赛四一10：", "en": "B. How God's Promise is Accomplished in Us—2 Cor. 13:3; Isa. 41:10:", "norm_zh": "二神的应许如何能成功在我们身上林后十三3赛四一10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B How Gods Promise is Accomplished in Us2 Cor 133 Isa 4110"}
{"zh": "1\t每一次当我们在神的话里看见一个应许的时候，我们必须好好地祷告，祷告到神的灵在我们里面兴起，叫我们里面深深地觉得，这个应许是神为着我们的—哀三8。", "en": "1. Every time we see a promise in God's Word we must really pray. We must pray until the Spirit of God is so stirred in us that we feel deeply that this promise is intended of God for us.—Lam. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "1每一次当我们在神的话里看见一个应许的时候我们必须好好地祷告祷告到神的灵在我们里面兴起叫我们里面深深地觉得这个应许是神为着我们的哀三8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Every time we see a promise in Gods Word we must really pray We must pray until the Spirit of God is so stirred in us that we feel deeply that this promise is intended of God for usLam 38"}
{"zh": "2\t如果这个应许是没有条件的，我们就可以立时运用信心接受这个应许；同时相信神必定按着祂所应许的成功在我们身上；我们就赞美神，感谢神—可十一22，太十四27。", "en": "2. If there is no condition attached to this promise, we can immediately exercise our faith to receive it; believing at the same time that God will surely accomplish in us what He has promised; we praise and thank God.—Mark 11:22; Matt. 14:27.", "norm_zh": "2如果这个应许是没有条件的我们就可以立时运用信心接受这个应许同时相信神必定按着祂所应许的成功在我们身上我们就赞美神感谢神可十一22太十四27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If there is no condition attached to this promise we can immediately exercise our faith to receive it believing at the same time that God will surely accomplish in us what He has promised we praise and thank GodMark 1122 Matt 1427"}
{"zh": "3\t如果这个应许是有条件的，我们就要履行所当履行的条件，然后再借着祷告来到神的面前，求神凭着祂的信实和公义而行，求神将祂的应许成就在我们的身上—来十三5。", "en": "3. If the promise has certain conditions, we need to fulfill the conditions. Then we come to God through prayer and ask Him to act according to His faithfulness and righteousness and fulfill His promise in us.—Heb. 13:5.", "norm_zh": "3如果这个应许是有条件的我们就要履行所当履行的条件然后再借着祷告来到神的面前求神凭着祂的信实和公义而行求神将祂的应许成就在我们的身上来十三5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If the promise has certain conditions we need to fulfill the conditions Then we come to God through prayer and ask Him to act according to His faithfulness and righteousness and fulfill His promise in usHeb 135"}
{"zh": "肆\t事实是神已经成功了的工作—加四4，来九26，彼后一3：", "en": "IV. Facts are God's accomplished work.—Gal. 4:4; Heb. 9:26; 2 Pet. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "肆事实是神已经成功了的工作加四4来九26彼后一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Facts are Gods accomplished workGal 44 Heb 926 2 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "一\t对于神的事实，我们的需要，不是祷告求神来作，乃是相信神已经作了；我们一相信神的事实，我们就有了经历；事实，相信，经历，乃是神定规的次序，也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则，这是我们必须记得的—太二一22，罗四18：", "en": "A. Concerning God's facts, our need is not to pray to ask God to do them, but to believe that God has already done them; once we believe God's facts, we have the experience; fact, faith, and experience is the order ordained by God, and it is also the greatest principle in the spiritual life; this we must remember.—Matt. 21:22; Rom. 4:18:", "norm_zh": "一对于神的事实我们的需要不是祷告求神来作乃是相信神已经作了我们一相信神的事实我们就有了经历事实相信经历乃是神定规的次序也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则这是我们必须记得的太二一22罗四18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Concerning Gods facts our need is not to pray to ask God to do them but to believe that God has already done them once we believe Gods facts we have the experience fact faith and experience is the order ordained by God and it is also the greatest principle in the spiritual life this we must rememberMatt 2122 Rom 418"}
{"zh": "1\t神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了，我们就不用求，只要取用就够了—弗二5~6。", "en": "1. God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness. We do not need to ask; we only need to claim.—Eph. 2:5-6.", "norm_zh": "1神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了我们就不用求只要取用就够了弗二56", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness We do not need to ask we only need to claimEph 256"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣如何是已经钉在十字架上了，我们的旧人也如何是已经和祂同钉在十字架上了；这是事实，这是神借着基督已经成功的事实—罗六6。", "en": "2. Just as the Lord Jesus has been crucified, so also our old man has been crucified with Him; this is a fact, a fact which God has already accomplished through Christ.—Rom. 6:6.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣如何是已经钉在十字架上了我们的旧人也如何是已经和祂同钉在十字架上了这是事实这是神借着基督已经成功的事实罗六6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Just as the Lord Jesus has been crucified so also our old man has been crucified with Him this is a fact a fact which God has already accomplished through ChristRom 66"}
{"zh": "3\t尽管有的时候有试探来，但是我们仍旧相信神所作的，过于我们的感觉和经历；我们真看见这个事实是事实的时候，经历就自然而然会来到—约二十27。", "en": "3. Although at times temptations come, we still believe what God has done more than our feelings and experiences; when we truly see that this fact is a fact, the experience will naturally follow.—John 20:27.", "norm_zh": "3尽管有的时候有试探来但是我们仍旧相信神所作的过于我们的感觉和经历我们真看见这个事实是事实的时候经历就自然而然会来到约二十27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Although at times temptations come we still believe what God has done more than our feelings and experiences when we truly see that this fact is a fact the experience will naturally followJohn 2027"}
{"zh": "二\t关于神的事实的几个原则—林前二10，诗三三4，太二一21：", "en": "B. Some Principles Concerning God's Facts—1 Cor. 2:10; Psa. 33:4; Matt. 21:21:", "norm_zh": "二关于神的事实的几个原则林前二10诗三三4太二一21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Some Principles Concerning Gods Facts1 Cor 210 Psa 334 Matt 2121"}
{"zh": "1\t要先找出什么是神的事实；这个是需要圣灵来启示的—林前二10。", "en": "1. We need to discover what God's fact is; for this, revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary.—1 Cor. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1要先找出什么是神的事实这个是需要圣灵来启示的林前二10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We need to discover what Gods fact is for this revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary1 Cor 210"}
{"zh": "2\t知道了某一件事是神的事实之后，就抓住神的话，相信你已经是按着神的话所说的那样了，相信神的事实是怎样，你也是怎样了—来十一3。", "en": "2. Once we see what God's fact is, we need to hold on to God's Word and believe that we are just as God's Word says. We need to believe that just as God's fact says, so we are.—Heb. 11:3.", "norm_zh": "2知道了某一件事是神的事实之后就抓住神的话相信你已经是按着神的话所说的哪样了相信神的事实是怎样你也是怎样了来十一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Once we see what Gods fact is we need to hold on to Gods Word and believe that we are just as Gods Word says We need to believe that just as Gods fact says so we areHeb 113"}
{"zh": "3\t你就凭着这个信心，一面感谢神，因为你已经是这样了；另一面你就行出来，显出你已是这样了—林后四13。", "en": "3. We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way; on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such.—2 Cor. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "3你就凭着这个信心一面感谢神因为你已经是这样了另一面你就行出来显出你已是这样了林后四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such2 Cor 413"}
{"zh": "4\t任何时候，你遇见试探或者试验，总要相信：神的话，神的事实，比你的感觉更靠得住；你只管满心相信神的话，神要负责叫你有经历—太二一21。", "en": "4. Whenever temptation or trial comes to us, we must believe that God's Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings. We need only to fully believe God's Word; then God will be responsible to give us the experience.—Matt. 21:21.", "norm_zh": "4任何时候你遇见试探或者试验总要相信神的话神的事实比你的感觉更靠得住你只管满心相信神的话神要负责叫你有经历太二一21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Whenever temptation or trial comes to us we must believe that Gods Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings We need only to fully believe Gods Word then God will be responsible to give us the experienceMatt 2121"}
{"zh": "5\t事实需要人有信心，因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路—来十一：", "en": "5. Fact requires our faith, for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experience—Heb. 11:", "norm_zh": "5事实需要人有信心因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路来十一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Fact requires our faith for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experienceHeb 11"}
{"zh": "a\t神的事实是在基督里的；所以人必须在基督里，才能享受神在基督里的事实—林前一5。", "en": "a. God's fact is in Christ; therefore, we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ.—1 Cor. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "a神的事实是在基督里的所以人必须在基督里才能享受神在基督里的事实林前一5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Gods fact is in Christ therefore we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ1 Cor 15"}
{"zh": "b\t当我们与基督联合的时候，我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实—加三27、29。", "en": "b. When we are united with Christ, we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in Christ.—Gal. 3:27, 29.", "norm_zh": "b当我们与基督联合的时候我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实加三2729", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b When we are united with Christ we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in ChristGal 327 29"}
{"zh": "c\t我们在基督里了，还得常住在基督里；这样，神的事实才能成为我们的经历，才能一直在我们身上显明出来—约十五4。", "en": "c. Though we are already in Christ, we also need to abide in Christ; by this means, God's fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through us.—John 15:4.", "norm_zh": "c我们在基督里了还得常住在基督里这样神的事实才能成为我们的经历才能一直在我们身上显明出来约十五4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Though we are already in Christ we also need to abide in Christ by this means Gods fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through usJohn 154"}
{"zh": "伍\t如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实，我们就得求神给我们启示，给我们光，叫我们能看见；是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道；这个是可以求的；我们求，是求看见—弗一17，太七7。", "en": "V. If we have not seen God's fact as fact, we need to ask God to give us revelation, to give us light, that we may see; it is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know; we can ask for such a spirit; what we ask for is the vision.—Eph. 1:17; Matt. 7:7.", "norm_zh": "伍如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实我们就得求神给我们启示给我们光叫我们能看见是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道这个是可以求的我们求是求看见弗一17太七7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V If we have not seen Gods fact as fact we need to ask God to give us revelation to give us light that we may see it is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know we can ask for such a spirit what we ask for is the visionEph 117 Matt 77"}
{"zh": "陆\t我们对于神的应许，必须用信心接受；我们对于神的事实，不只当用信心接受，并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实—来十一1，林后四13，诗一一九49：", "en": "VI. We must receive God's promise with our faith, while we must not only receive God's fact with our faith, but also enjoy what God has accomplished.—Heb. 11:1; 2 Cor. 4:13; Psa. 119:49:", "norm_zh": "陆我们对于神的应许必须用信心接受我们对于神的事实不只当用信心接受并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实来十一1林后四13诗一一九49", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI We must receive Gods promise with our faith while we must not only receive Gods fact with our faith but also enjoy what God has accomplishedHeb 111 2 Cor 413 Psa 11949"}
{"zh": "一\t我们在寻求主的应许之前，必须先对付不单纯的心—林后十一3，弗六5。", "en": "A. Before we ask God for His promise, we must first deal with our impure heart.—2 Cor. 11:3; Eph. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "一我们在寻求主的应许之前必须先对付不单纯的心林后十一3弗六5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we ask God for His promise we must first deal with our impure heart2 Cor 113 Eph 65"}
{"zh": "二\t在得着神的应许之后，我们就要用它—诗一三〇7，罗四20。", "en": "B. After receiving God's promise we need to make use of it—Psa. 130:7, Rom. 4:20.", "norm_zh": "二在得着神的应许之后我们就要用它诗一三〇7罗四20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B After receiving Gods promise we need to make use of itPsa 1307 Rom 420"}
{"zh": "三\t真有了神的应许的人，他的态度和行为，常是安息镇定—徒二七25，十八9。", "en": "C. Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable way—Acts 27:25; 18:9.", "norm_zh": "三真有了神的应许的人他的态度和行为常是安息镇定徒二七25十八9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable wayActs 2725 189"}
{"zh": "四\t我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后，信心是一直看那个事实，算那个事实为事实的；如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实，甚至否定神的事实，那就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心—诗三一24，来三12。", "en": "D. Once we have seen God's fact, our faith must continue to look at God's fact, counting the fact as fact; if due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning God's fact, even denying God's fact, this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards God's fact—Psa. 31:24; Heb. 3:12.", "norm_zh": "四我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后信心是一直看哪个事实算哪个事实为事实的如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实甚至否定神的事实哪就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心诗三一24来三12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Once we have seen Gods fact our faith must continue to look at Gods fact counting the fact as fact if due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning Gods fact even denying Gods fact this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards Gods factPsa 3124 Heb 312"}
{"zh": "柒\t亲爱的弟兄姊妹们，“我们若将起初确实的信心，坚持到底，就在基督里有分了。”—倪柝声。", "en": "VII. Dear brothers and sisters, \"If we hold fast the beginning of our assurance firm to the end, we have become partners of Christ.\" —Watchman Nee.", "norm_zh": "柒亲爱的弟兄姊妹们我们若将起初确实的信心坚持到底就在基督里有分了倪柝声", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII Dear brothers and sisters If we hold fast the beginning of our assurance firm to the end we have become partners of Christ Watchman Nee"}
{"zh": "马太二十六章二十八节：“因为这是我立约的血，为多人流出来，使罪得赦。”（“约”有古卷作“新约”）", "en": "Matt. 26:28: \"For this is My blood of the covenant, which is poured out for many for forgiveness of sins.\" (\"covenant\" in some manuscripts is \"new covenant\")", "norm_zh": "马太二十六章二十八节因为这是我立约的血为多人流出来使罪得赦约有古卷作新约", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Matt 2628 For this is My blood of the covenant which is poured out for many for forgiveness of sins covenant in some manuscripts is new covenant"}
{"zh": "希伯来八章八至十三节：“所以主指责祂的百姓说，日子将到，我要与以色列家和犹大家，另立新约；不像我拉着他们祖宗的手，领他们出埃及的时候，与他们所立的约；因为他们不恒心守我的约，我也不理他们；这是主说的。主又说，那些日子以后，我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样：我要将我的律法放在他们心意里面，写在他们心上；我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民；他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻，和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我。因为我要宽恕他们的不义，不再记念他们的罪愆。既说新约，就以前约为旧了。但那渐旧渐衰的，就必快归无有了。”", "en": "Heb. 8:8-13: \"For finding fault with them He says, Behold, the days are coming, says the Lord, and I will consummate a new covenant upon the house of Israel and upon the house of Judah, not according to the covenant which I made with their fathers in the day when I took them by their hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt, because they did not continue in My covenant, and I disregarded them, says the Lord. For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days, says the Lord: I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them; and I will be God to them, and they shall be a people to Me. And they shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother, saying, Know the Lord; for all will know Me, from the little one to the great one among them. For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I will by no means remember anymore. In saying new, He has made the first old. Now that which is becoming old and growing decrepit is near to disappearing.\"", "norm_zh": "希伯来八章八至十三节所以主指责祂的百姓说日子将到我要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约不像我拉着他们祖宗的手领他们出埃及的时候与他们所立的约因为他们不恒心守我的约我也不理他们这是主说的主又说哪些日子以后我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样我要将我的律法放在他们心意里面写在他们心上我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我因为我要宽恕他们的不义不再记念他们的罪愆既说新约就以前约为旧了但哪渐旧渐衰的就必快归无有了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Heb 8813 For finding fault with them He says Behold the days are coming says the Lord and I will consummate a new covenant upon the house of Israel and upon the house of Judah not according to the covenant which I made with their fathers in the day when I took them by their hand to lead them out of the land of Egypt because they did not continue in My covenant and I disregarded them says the Lord For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days says the Lord I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe them and I will be God to them and they shall be a people to Me And they shall by no means each teach his fellow citizen and each his brother saying Know the Lord for all will know Me from the little one to the great one among them For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I will by no means remember anymore In saying new He has made the first old Now that which is becoming old and growing decrepit is near to disappearing"}
{"zh": "希伯来十章十六节：“主说，那些日子以后，我与他们所立的约乃是这样；我要将我的律法写在他们心上，又要放在他们的里面。”", "en": "Heb. 10:16: \"This is the covenant which I will covenant with them after those days, says the Lord: I will write My laws on their hearts, and also put them in their mind.\"", "norm_zh": "希伯来十章十六节主说哪些日子以后我与他们所立的约乃是这样我要将我的律法写在他们心上又要放在他们的里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Heb 1016 This is the covenant which I will covenant with them after those days says the Lord I will write My laws on their hearts and also put them in their mind"}
{"zh": "耶利米三十一章三十一至三十四节：“耶和华说，日子将到，我要与以色列家和犹大家，另立新约。不像我拉着他们祖宗的手，领他们出埃及地的时候，与他们所立的约；我虽作他们的丈夫，他们却背了我的约；这是耶和华说的。耶和华说，那些日子以后，我与以色列家所立的约，乃是这样；我要将我的律法放在他们里面，写在他们心上；我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民。他们各人不再教导自己的邻舍和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识耶和华；因为他们从最小的，到至大的，都必认识我；我要赦免他们的罪孽，不再记念他们的罪恶；这是耶和华说的。”", "en": "Jer. 31:31-34: \"Indeed, days are coming, declares Jehovah, when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah, not like the covenant which I made with their fathers in the day I took them by their hand to bring them out from the land of Egypt, My covenant which they broke, although I was their Husband, declares Jehovah. But this is the covenant which I will make with the house of Israel after those days, declares Jehovah: I will put My law within them, and on their hearts I will write it; and I will be their God, and they shall be My people. And they will no longer teach, each man his neighbor and each man his brother, saying, Know Jehovah; for they will all know Me, from the little one of them even to the great one of them, declares Jehovah; for I will forgive their iniquity, and their sin I will remember no more.\"", "norm_zh": "耶利米三十一章三十一至三十四节耶和华说日子将到我要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约不像我拉着他们祖宗的手领他们出埃及地的时候与他们所立的约我虽作他们的丈夫他们却背了我的约这是耶和华说的耶和华说哪些日子以后我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样我要将我的律法放在他们里面写在他们心上我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民他们各人不再教导自己的邻舍和自己的弟兄说你该认识耶和华因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我我要赦免他们的罪孽不再记念他们的罪恶这是耶和华说的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jer 313134 Indeed days are coming declares Jehovah when I will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah not like the covenant which I made with their fathers in the day I took them by their hand to bring them out from the land of Egypt My covenant which they broke although I was their Husband declares Jehovah But this is the covenant which I will make with the house of Israel after those days declares Jehovah I will put My law within them and on their hearts I will write it and I will be their God and they shall be My people And they will no longer teach each man his neighbor and each man his brother saying Know Jehovah for they will all know Me from the little one of them even to the great one of them declares Jehovah for I will forgive their iniquity and their sin I will remember no more"}
{"zh": "林后三章六节：“祂叫我们能承当这新约的执事；不是凭着字句，乃是凭着灵；因为那字句是叫人死，灵是叫人活。”（看圣经小字注）", "en": "2 Cor. 3:6: \"Who has also made us sufficient as ministers of a new covenant, ministers not of the letter but of the Spirit; for the letter kills, but the Spirit gives life.\" (see marginal note)", "norm_zh": "林后三章六节祂叫我们能承当这新约的执事不是凭着字句乃是凭着灵因为哪字句是叫人死灵是叫人活看圣经小字注", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Cor 36 Who has also made us sufficient as ministers of a new covenant ministers not of the letter but of the Spirit for the letter kills but the Spirit gives life see marginal note"}
{"zh": "希伯来十三章二十至二十一节：“但愿赐平安的神，就是那凭永约之血使群羊的大牧人我主耶稣，从死里复活的神，在各样善事上，成全你们，叫你们遵行祂的旨意，又借着耶稣基督在你们心里行祂所喜悦的事；愿荣耀归给祂，直到永永远远。阿们。”", "en": "Heb. 13:20-21: \"Now the God of peace, He who brought up from the dead our Lord Jesus, the great Shepherd of the sheep, in the blood of an eternal covenant, perfect you in every good work for the doing of His will, doing in us that which is well pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ; to Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.\"", "norm_zh": "希伯来十三章二十至二十一节但愿赐平安的神就是哪凭永约之血使群羊的大牧人我主耶稣从死里复活的神在各样善事上成全你们叫你们遵行祂的旨意又借着耶稣基督在你们心里行祂所喜悦的事愿荣耀归给祂直到永永远远阿们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Heb 132021 Now the God of peace He who brought up from the dead our Lord Jesus the great Shepherd of the sheep in the blood of an eternal covenant perfect you in every good work for the doing of His will doing in us that which is well pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ to Him be the glory forever and ever Amen"}
{"zh": "新约是一切属灵生活的根基", "en": "The new covenant is the foundation of all spiritual life.", "norm_zh": "新约是一切属灵生活的根基", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The new covenant is the foundation of all spiritual life"}
{"zh": "新约是一切属灵生活的根基。我们的罪能得赦免，我们的良心有平安，是因为有新约；我们能顺服神，行神所喜悦的事，是因为有新约；我们能直接地与神交通，在里面更深地认识神，也是因为有新约。如果没有新约，那，罪得赦免是没有把握的；顺服神，行神旨意，是难以如愿的；与神交通，以及认识神，不过是外面的、普通的，难有更深的。但是，感谢神，有一个新约，这新约是祂立的约，所以我们能安息在祂的约上。", "en": "The new covenant is the foundation of all spiritual life. Our sins can be forgiven, and our conscience can have peace, because of the new covenant; we can obey God and do the things that please Him, because of the new covenant; and we can directly fellowship with God and know God more deeply inwardly, also because of the new covenant. If there were no new covenant, then there would be no assurance of the forgiveness of sins; obeying God and doing God's will would be difficult to accomplish; fellowship with God and knowing God would be merely outward and common, and it would be difficult to have anything deeper. But thanks be to God, there is a new covenant; this new covenant is a covenant that He made, so we can rest in His covenant.", "norm_zh": "新约是一切属灵生活的根基我们的罪能得赦免我们的良心有平安是因为有新约我们能顺服神行神所喜悦的事是因为有新约我们能直接地与神交通在里面更深地认识神也是因为有新约如果没有新约哪罪得赦免是没有把握的顺服神行神旨意是难以如愿的与神交通以及认识神不过是外面的普通的难有更深的但是感谢神有一个新约这新约是祂立的约所以我们能安息在祂的约上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The new covenant is the foundation of all spiritual life Our sins can be forgiven and our conscience can have peace because of the new covenant we can obey God and do the things that please Him because of the new covenant and we can directly fellowship with God and know God more deeply inwardly also because of the new covenant If there were no new covenant then there would be no assurance of the forgiveness of sins obeying God and doing Gods will would be difficult to accomplish fellowship with God and knowing God would be merely outward and common and it would be difficult to have anything deeper But thanks be to God there is a new covenant this new covenant is a covenant that He made so we can rest in His covenant"}
{"zh": "那位写“永久磐石为我开”（诗歌七三一首）的弟兄，是一个患了十多年肺病的人，他病重的时候，写了一首诗，其中有一节说：", "en": "The brother who wrote \"Rock of Ages, Cleft for Me\" was a person who suffered from tuberculosis for over ten years; when he was gravely ill, he wrote a hymn, one stanza of which says:", "norm_zh": "哪位写永久磐石为我开诗歌七三一首的弟兄是一个患了十多年肺病的人他病重的时候写了一首诗其中有一节说", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The brother who wrote Rock of Ages Cleft for Me was a person who suffered from tuberculosis for over ten years when he was gravely ill he wrote a hymn one stanza of which says"}
{"zh": "安息于主信实，何等甘甜，因祂爱真是奇妙。", "en": "How sweet to rest upon the Lord's faithfulness, for His love is truly wonderful.", "norm_zh": "安息于主信实何等甘甜因祂爱真是奇妙", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "How sweet to rest upon the Lords faithfulness for His love is truly wonderful"}
{"zh": "安息于主恩约，何等甘甜，因这约永远可靠。", "en": "Resting on the Lord's covenant of grace, how sweet it is, because this covenant is forever reliable.", "norm_zh": "安息于主恩约何等甘甜因这约永远可靠", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Resting on the Lords covenant of grace how sweet it is because this covenant is forever reliable"}
{"zh": "他懂得什么叫作约，所以他安息在主的约上。", "en": "He knew what a covenant was, so he rested on the Lord's covenant.", "norm_zh": "他懂得什么叫作约所以他安息在主的约上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "He knew what a covenant was so he rested on the Lords covenant"}
{"zh": "神永远的目的是显在新约里", "en": "God's eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant.", "norm_zh": "神永远的目的是显在新约里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant"}
{"zh": "神永远的目的是显在新约里。所以一个属乎主的人，如果不知道什么是新约，他在经历上就不能认识神永远的目的。我们要知道，“从亚当到摩西，死就作了王……就如罪作王叫人死……。”（罗五14、21）在那个时代中，神永远的目的还没有显明。虽然神曾传福音给亚伯拉罕说，万国都必因你得福（加三8），给我们看见一点恩典的影儿；但是，我们还没有看见恩典的本体。“律法本是借着摩西传的”（约一17），但“律法本是外添的”（罗五20），律法根本不在神永远之目的的系统里，“……众先知和律法说预言，到约翰为止。”（太十一13）“恩典和真理，都是由耶稣基督来的”（约一17），所以到了基督，才是恩典时代，才有新约，才看得见神永远的目的。神永远的目的是显在新约里。所以我们需要认识新约，才能盼望神永远的目的在我们身上有成功的那一天。我们如果不认识新约，我们就摸不着救恩的本质，我们至多只能摸着一点边缘。我们如果认识一点新约，可以说，我们摸着宇宙中的一个大宝藏了！", "en": "God's eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant. Therefore, if a person who belongs to the Lord does not know what the new covenant is, he cannot know God's eternal purpose in his experience. We need to know, \"From Adam to Moses, death reigned... even as sin reigned in death...\" (Rom. 5:14, 21). In that age, God's eternal purpose was not yet manifested. Although God preached the gospel to Abraham, saying, \"In you all the nations shall be blessed\" (Gal. 3:8), giving us a shadow of grace, we have not yet seen the substance of grace. \"For the law was given through Moses\" (John 1:17), but \"the law entered in alongside\" (Rom. 5:20); the law is not at all in the system of God's eternal purpose: \"...all the prophets and the law prophesied until John\" (Matt. 11:13). \"Grace and reality came through Jesus Christ\" (John 1:17); therefore, when we come to Christ, it is the age of grace, there is the new covenant, and God's eternal purpose can be seen. God's eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant. Therefore, we need to know the new covenant so that we can hope that God's eternal purpose will be accomplished in us one day. If we do not know the new covenant, we cannot touch the essence of salvation; at most, we can touch only a little of its border. If we know something of the new covenant, we can say that we have touched a great treasure in the universe!", "norm_zh": "神永远的目的是显在新约里所以一个属乎主的人如果不知道什么是新约他在经历上就不能认识神永远的目的我们要知道从亚当到摩西死就作了王就如罪作王叫人死罗五1421在哪个时代中神永远的目的还没有显明虽然神曾传福音给亚伯拉罕说万国都必因你得福加三8给我们看见一点恩典的影儿但是我们还没有看见恩典的本体律法本是借着摩西传的约一17但律法本是外添的罗五20律法根本不在神永远之目的的系统里众先知和律法说预言到约翰为止太十一13恩典和真理都是由耶稣基督来的约一17所以到了基督才是恩典时代才有新约才看得见神永远的目的神永远的目的是显在新约里所以我们需要认识新约才能盼望神永远的目的在我们身上有成功的哪一天我们如果不认识新约我们就摸不着救恩的本质我们至多只能摸着一点边缘我们如果认识一点新约可以说我们摸着宇宙中的一个大宝藏了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant Therefore if a person who belongs to the Lord does not know what the new covenant is he cannot know Gods eternal purpose in his experience We need to know From Adam to Moses death reigned even as sin reigned in death Rom 514 21 In that age Gods eternal purpose was not yet manifested Although God preached the gospel to Abraham saying In you all the nations shall be blessed Gal 38 giving us a shadow of grace we have not yet seen the substance of grace For the law was given through Moses John 117 but the law entered in alongside Rom 520 the law is not at all in the system of Gods eternal purpose all the prophets and the law prophesied until John Matt 1113 Grace and reality came through Jesus Christ John 117 therefore when we come to Christ it is the age of grace there is the new covenant and Gods eternal purpose can be seen Gods eternal purpose is manifested in the new covenant Therefore we need to know the new covenant so that we can hope that Gods eternal purpose will be accomplished in us one day If we do not know the new covenant we cannot touch the essence of salvation at most we can touch only a little of its border If we know something of the new covenant we can say that we have touched a great treasure in the universe"}
{"zh": "神永远的目的到底是什么呢？简单地说，神永远的目的，就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去。神喜欢进到人里面与人联合，叫人有祂的生命，有祂的性情。祂在创立世界以前，就是在永远里，在时间还没有开始的时候，在祂创造天地，创造万物，创造人类之先，就有这个目的。祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分，祂就是要人像祂，祂就是要人得荣耀（弗一4~5，罗八30）。所以，祂造人的时候，是照着自己的形像造人（创一27）。当初在伊甸园当中，有生命树和分别善恶的树；神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里，祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子。换句话说，祂是示意：生命树的果子是应该吃的，不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的。照着圣经的启示来看，生命树是指明神的（诗三六9，约一4，十一25，十四6，约壹五1）。人如果吃生命树的果子，人就有了生命，神就进到人的里面了。我们知道，神所造的头一个人，就是首先的亚当，他失败了，堕落了，他不只没有接受神的生命，反而因吃了分别善恶树的果子，而与赐生命的神隔绝了。但是，我们要感谢赞美神，头一个人虽然失败了，堕落了，第二个人，就是末后的亚当（林前十五45、47），却达到了神永远的目的！在宇宙里，至少有一个人是和神调在一起的，就是神而人，人而神的拿撒勒人耶稣。这就是“道成了肉身，住在我们中间，充充满满地有恩典有真理”（约一14）的主耶稣。虽然从来没有人看见神，但是，有一个人，就是在父怀里的独生子，将祂表明出来了（18）。祂是神而人的，神就是要把祂作到人里面去，就是要人像祂儿子的形状（罗八28、29），把人作到神所要求、神所喜悦的地步。这是神永远的目的，这也就是新约。", "en": "What is God's eternal purpose after all? Simply speaking, God's eternal purpose is to work Himself into the man whom He created. God desires to enter into man to be united with him, that man may have His life and His nature. He had this purpose before the foundation of the world, that is, in eternity, before time began, and before He created the heavens and the earth, all things, and mankind. He wants man to obtain the sonship, He wants man to be like Him, and He wants man to be glorified (Eph. 1:4-5; Rom. 8:30). Therefore, when He created man, He created man in His own image (Gen. 1:27). In the beginning, in the midst of the garden of Eden, there were the tree of life and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil; God placed the created man in the garden of Eden, and He only forbade man to eat of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil. In other words, He indicated that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten, but this required man to choose it of his own initiative. According to the revelation of the Bible, the tree of life signifies God (Psa. 36:9; John 1:4; 11:25; 14:6; 1 John 5:1). If man eats the fruit of the tree of life, man has life, and God enters into man. We know that the first man created by God, who was the first Adam, failed and fell; he not only did not receive God's life, but because of eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil, he was separated from God, the Giver of life. But we want to thank and praise God that although the first man failed and fell, the second man, who is the last Adam (1 Cor. 15:45, 47), achieved God's eternal purpose! In the universe, there is at least one man who is mingled with God, who is the God-man, the man-God, Jesus of Nazareth. This is the Lord Jesus, of whom it is said, \"the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us... full of grace and reality\" (John 1:14). Although no one has ever seen God, there is one, the only begotten Son who is in the bosom of the Father, who has declared Him (v. 18). He is the God-man, and God wants to work Him into man, that is, to conform man to the image of His Son (Rom. 8:28-29), to work man to the extent that is required by God and well-pleasing to Him. This is God's eternal purpose, and this is the new covenant.", "norm_zh": "神永远的目的到底是什么呢简单地说神永远的目的就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去神喜欢进到人里面与人联合叫人有祂的生命有祂的性情祂在创立世界以前就是在永远里在时间还没有开始的时候在祂创造天地创造万物创造人类之先就有这个目的祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分祂就是要人像祂祂就是要人得荣耀弗一45罗八30所以祂造人的时候是照着自己的形像造人创一27当初在伊甸园当中有生命树和分别善恶的树神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子换句话说祂是示意生命树的果子是应该吃的不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的照着圣经的启示来看生命树是指明神的诗三六9约一4十一25十四6约壹五1人如果吃生命树的果子人就有了生命神就进到人的里面了我们知道神所造的头一个人就是首先的亚当他失败了堕落了他不只没有接受神的生命反而因吃了分别善恶树的果子而与赐生命的神隔绝了但是我们要感谢赞美神头一个人虽然失败了堕落了第二个人就是末后的亚当林前十五4547却达到了神永远的目的在宇宙里至少有一个人是和神调在一起的就是神而人人而神的拿撒勒人耶稣这就是道成了肉身住在我们中间充充满满地有恩典有真理约一14的主耶稣虽然从来没有人看见神但是有一个人就是在父怀里的独生子将祂表明出来了18祂是神而人的神就是要把祂作到人里面去就是要人像祂儿子的形状罗八2829把人作到神所要求神所喜悦的地步这是神永远的目的这也就是新约", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "What is Gods eternal purpose after all Simply speaking Gods eternal purpose is to work Himself into the man whom He created God desires to enter into man to be united with him that man may have His life and His nature He had this purpose before the foundation of the world that is in eternity before time began and before He created the heavens and the earth all things and mankind He wants man to obtain the sonship He wants man to be like Him and He wants man to be glorified Eph 145 Rom 830 Therefore when He created man He created man in His own image Gen 127 In the beginning in the midst of the garden of Eden there were the tree of life and the tree of the knowledge of good and evil God placed the created man in the garden of Eden and He only forbade man to eat of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil In other words He indicated that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten but this required man to choose it of his own initiative According to the revelation of the Bible the tree of life signifies God Psa 369 John 14 1125 146 1 John 51 If man eats the fruit of the tree of life man has life and God enters into man We know that the first man created by God who was the first Adam failed and fell he not only did not receive Gods life but because of eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil he was separated from God the Giver of life But we want to thank and praise God that although the first man failed and fell the second man who is the last Adam 1 Cor 1545 47 achieved Gods eternal purpose In the universe there is at least one man who is mingled with God who is the Godman the manGod Jesus of Nazareth This is the Lord Jesus of whom it is said the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us full of grace and reality John 114 Although no one has ever seen God there is one the only begotten Son who is in the bosom of the Father who has declared Him v 18 He is the Godman and God wants to work Him into man that is to conform man to the image of His Son Rom 82829 to work man to the extent that is required by God and wellpleasing to Him This is Gods eternal purpose and this is the new covenant"}
{"zh": "主以新约的原则对待祂的教会", "en": "The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant.", "norm_zh": "主以新约的原则对待祂的教会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant"}
{"zh": "我们说今天是新约的时代，是什么意思呢？在这里，我们只能简单地提起一下，到第三章，我们再比较仔细一点说到它。我们知道，神从来没有与外邦人立过约。我们既没有旧约，从何而有新约呢？希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们，有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约。并且严格说来，新约是要到那些日子以后（来八80），就是千禧年开始的时候才立的。既然如此，我们怎么能说今天是新约的时代呢？这没有别的，这就是说，主以新约的原则对待祂的教会。主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下，要教会按着约与祂来往，按着约与祂交涉，直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切。主说，“……这是我立新约的血”（太二六28）。主是用祂的血立了新约，使我们能预先得着新约的福。所以我们说，今天是新约的时代，乃是由于主特别的恩典。所以，我们在经历上必须认识什么是新约，我们才能说我们是活在新约时代中的人。", "en": "What do we mean when we say that today is the age of the new covenant? Here we can only mention it briefly; in chapter 3 we will speak of it in more detail. We know that God has never made a covenant with the Gentiles. Since we did not have the old covenant, how can we have the new covenant? Hebrews 8:8 tells us clearly that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah. And strictly speaking, the new covenant will not be enacted until after those days (Heb. 8:10), which is at the beginning of the millennium. This being the case, how can we say that today is the age of the new covenant? This is nothing else but to say that the Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant. The Lord has placed the church under the principle of the new covenant, wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and to deal with Him according to the covenant, until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish. The Lord said, \"...this is My blood of the covenant\" (Matt. 26:28). The Lord enacted the new covenant with His blood so that we could have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant. Therefore, when we say that today is the age of the new covenant, it is because of the Lord's special grace. Therefore, we must know in our experience what the new covenant is before we can say that we are those living in the age of the new covenant.", "norm_zh": "我们说今天是新约的时代是什么意思呢在这里我们只能简单地提起一下到第三章我们再比较仔细一点说到它我们知道神从来没有与外邦人立过约我们既没有旧约从何而有新约呢希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约并且严格说来新约是要到哪些日子以后来八80就是千禧年开始的时候才立的既然如此我们怎么能说今天是新约的时代呢这没有别的这就是说主以新约的原则对待祂的教会主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下要教会按着约与祂来往按着约与祂交涉直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切主说这是我立新约的血太二六28主是用祂的血立了新约使我们能预先得着新约的福所以我们说今天是新约的时代乃是由于主特别的恩典所以我们在经历上必须认识什么是新约我们才能说我们是活在新约时代中的人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "What do we mean when we say that today is the age of the new covenant Here we can only mention it briefly in chapter 3 we will speak of it in more detail We know that God has never made a covenant with the Gentiles Since we did not have the old covenant how can we have the new covenant Hebrews 88 tells us clearly that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah And strictly speaking the new covenant will not be enacted until after those days Heb 810 which is at the beginning of the millennium This being the case how can we say that today is the age of the new covenant This is nothing else but to say that the Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant The Lord has placed the church under the principle of the new covenant wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and to deal with Him according to the covenant until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish The Lord said this is My blood of the covenant Matt 2628 The Lord enacted the new covenant with His blood so that we could have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant Therefore when we say that today is the age of the new covenant it is because of the Lords special grace Therefore we must know in our experience what the new covenant is before we can say that we are those living in the age of the new covenant"}
{"zh": "认识神的应许和神的事实", "en": "Knowing God's promises and God's facts.", "norm_zh": "认识神的应许和神的事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Knowing Gods promises and Gods facts"}
{"zh": "我们要认识什么是新约，必须先认识什么是约；要认识什么是约，必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实。所以，我们要先说一点神的应许和神的事实，然后再说什么是神的约，什么是新约，什么是新约内容的特点。我们特别要说到：律法是怎样放在人的里面，写在人的心上；生命运行的大能是如何；神如何在生命的律里作我们的神，我们如何在生命的律里作神的子民；以及我们如何在里面有知识，对于神有更深的认识。（什么是新约，引言）", "en": "To know what the new covenant is, we must first know what a covenant is; to know what a covenant is, we must first know what God's promises are and what God's facts are. Therefore, we must first say something about God's promises and God's facts, and then speak of what God's covenant is, what the new covenant is, and what the characteristics of the content of the new covenant are. In particular, we will speak of how the law is put into man and written upon his heart; how the power of the operation of life is; how God is our God in the law of life and how we are God's people in the law of life; and how we have inward knowledge to know God more deeply. (What Is the New Covenant, Introduction)", "norm_zh": "我们要认识什么是新约必须先认识什么是约要认识什么是约必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实所以我们要先说一点神的应许和神的事实然后再说什么是神的约什么是新约什么是新约内容的特点我们特别要说到律法是怎样放在人的里面写在人的心上生命运行的大能是如何神如何在生命的律里作我们的神我们如何在生命的律里作神的子民以及我们如何在里面有知识对于神有更深的认识什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To know what the new covenant is we must first know what a covenant is to know what a covenant is we must first know what Gods promises are and what Gods facts are Therefore we must first say something about Gods promises and Gods facts and then speak of what Gods covenant is what the new covenant is and what the characteristics of the content of the new covenant are In particular we will speak of how the law is put into man and written upon his heart how the power of the operation of life is how God is our God in the law of life and how we are Gods people in the law of life and how we have inward knowledge to know God more deeply What Is the New Covenant Introduction"}
{"zh": "现在我们先来看什么是神的应许。", "en": "Now let us see what is meant by God's promises.", "norm_zh": "现在我们先来看什么是神的应许", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Now let us see what is meant by Gods promises"}
{"zh": "应许是与事实不同的，应许是将来的，事实是已往的。应许是要作的，事实是已作的。应许是神要为人作什么，事实是神已经为人作成了什么。应许是你们若这样，我就这样；事实是神爱我们，知道我们的无能而为我们所成功的事情。应许有许多是有条件的；我们履行了条件，就要得着所应许的。事实并不需要我们苦求，只要我们看见了事实是事实，相信事实是事实就可以了。", "en": "A promise is different from a fact. Promise is related to the future, while fact is related to the past. Promise is something to be done, while fact is something already done. Promise means that God will do something for man, while fact means that God has already done something for man. Promise means if you do such and such, then I will do such and such. Fact means that God loves us and, knowing our impotence, has accomplished something for us. Many of the promises are conditional. If we fulfill the conditions, we shall receive what has been promised. Facts do not require our supplication. We only need to see that the facts are facts and believe them as such.", "norm_zh": "应许是与事实不同的应许是将来的事实是已往的应许是要作的事实是已作的应许是神要为人作什么事实是神已经为人作成了什么应许是你们若这样我就这样事实是神爱我们知道我们的无能而为我们所成功的事情应许有许多是有条件的我们履行了条件就要得着所应许的事实并不需要我们苦求只要我们看见了事实是事实相信事实是事实就可以了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A promise is different from a fact Promise is related to the future while fact is related to the past Promise is something to be done while fact is something already done Promise means that God will do something for man while fact means that God has already done something for man Promise means if you do such and such then I will do such and such Fact means that God loves us and knowing our impotence has accomplished something for us Many of the promises are conditional If we fulfill the conditions we shall receive what has been promised Facts do not require our supplication We only need to see that the facts are facts and believe them as such"}
{"zh": "所以，对于神的应许，我们要大声唱说：", "en": "Therefore, concerning God's promises, we need to sing with a loud voice:", "norm_zh": "所以对于神的应许我们要大声唱说", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Therefore concerning Gods promises we need to sing with a loud voice"}
{"zh": "神的应许不能废去，句句都是坚定。", "en": "God's promises cannot be done away; every word will be established.", "norm_zh": "神的应许不能废去句句都是坚定", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods promises cannot be done away every word will be established"}
{"zh": "信心从来不用凭据，因神言出必行。", "en": "Faith never asks for evidence, for whatever God says, He will do.", "norm_zh": "信心从来不用凭据因神言出必行", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Faith never asks for evidence for whatever God says He will do"}
{"zh": "（副）天地虽能被焚烧，小山大山虽倾倒，", "en": "(Chorus) Though heaven and earth may be consumed and the mountains and hills fall,", "norm_zh": "副天地虽能被焚烧小山大山虽倾倒", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Chorus Though heaven and earth may be consumed and the mountains and hills fall"}
{"zh": "但那相信主的人，必见主话得成。", "en": "But he who believes in the Lord shall see His words fulfilled.", "norm_zh": "但哪相信主的人必见主话得成", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "But he who believes in the Lord shall see His words fulfilled"}
{"zh": "神如果迟延不给我们，就是违反事实", "en": "If God delays His giving to us, it is a contradiction to fact.", "norm_zh": "神如果迟延不给我们就是违反事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If God delays His giving to us it is a contradiction to fact"}
{"zh": "对于神的应许，我们如果不求，不履行条件，还有得不着的可能，还有废弃落空的可能。可是，神的事实，不会因为我们不求，就不成功在我们身上；因为已经是事实了，所以不用求了（这是指神的事实本身说的，不是指我们个人的经历说的）。一切神的事实，神从来没有一次要我们特别作什么去得着的，都是只要我们简简单单地一相信就成。神的应许还有迟延的可能，神的事实是不能迟延的。我们不可能接受了神的事实，而说再要等几年神才给我们。神所已经成就了的，神所已经在基督里赐给我们的，不能迟延到将来才给我们。神如果迟延不给我们，就是违反事实。", "en": "With regard to God's promises, if we do not ask concerning them, or if we do not fulfill the conditions, we may not obtain them; the promises may become void as far as we are concerned. But concerning God's facts, even though we do not ask, He will still fulfill them in us. They are facts; therefore, we do not need to ask concerning them. (This refers to God's facts themselves, not to our individual experiences.) God has never asked us to do anything in order to obtain His facts. All He requires is that we simply believe. There may be a delay with God's promise, but God's facts can never be late. We can never say that we have received God's facts and then say that we need to wait a few years for God to give them to us. What God has accomplished and what He has already given to us in Christ can never be postponed to some future time. If God delays His giving to us, it is a contradiction to fact.", "norm_zh": "对于神的应许我们如果不求不履行条件还有得不着的可能还有废弃落空的可能可是神的事实不会因为我们不求就不成功在我们身上因为已经是事实了所以不用求了这是指神的事实本身说的不是指我们个人的经历说的一切神的事实神从来没有一次要我们特别作什么去得着的都是只要我们简简单单地一相信就成神的应许还有迟延的可能神的事实是不能迟延的我们不可能接受了神的事实而说再要等几年神才给我们神所已经成就了的神所已经在基督里赐给我们的不能迟延到将来才给我们神如果迟延不给我们就是违反事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "With regard to Gods promises if we do not ask concerning them or if we do not fulfill the conditions we may not obtain them the promises may become void as far as we are concerned But concerning Gods facts even though we do not ask He will still fulfill them in us They are facts therefore we do not need to ask concerning them This refers to Gods facts themselves not to our individual experiences God has never asked us to do anything in order to obtain His facts All He requires is that we simply believe There may be a delay with Gods promise but Gods facts can never be late We can never say that we have received Gods facts and then say that we need to wait a few years for God to give them to us What God has accomplished and what He has already given to us in Christ can never be postponed to some future time If God delays His giving to us it is a contradiction to fact"}
{"zh": "像以弗所二章五至六节，说到神因祂爱我们的大爱，“当我们死在过犯中的时候，便叫我们与基督一同活过来……祂又叫我们与基督耶稣一同复活，一同坐在天上。”这里有三个“一同”，两个“叫”。这里所说的是神的应许呢，还是神的事实？神的话告诉我们，这些都是事实。是神叫我们与基督一同活过来，是神叫我们与基督一同复活，一同坐在天上。这都是已经成功的事实。既是事实，我们就应当感谢赞美神，就应当对撒但显出我们是已经与基督一同复活、升天了。不是显出某种态度好叫我们复活、升天，乃是显出一种态度，说出我们是已经与基督一同复活、升天了。", "en": "In Ephesians 2:4-6 we read: \"But God, being rich in mercy because of His great love with which He loved us, even when we were dead in offenses, made us alive together with Christ ... and raised us up together and seated us together in the heavenlies in Christ Jesus.\" There are three \"withs\" and two \"mades\" in this verse. Are the things mentioned here God's promises or God's facts? God's Word tells us that these are all facts. It is God who has made us alive together with Christ, and it is God who has raised us up with Christ and seated us in the heavenly places with Christ. These are all accomplished facts. Since this is so, we ought to praise and thank God. We ought to take an attitude towards Satan that we have been raised up together and that we have ascended together with Christ. We should not take an attitude of hope that we may be raised up or that we may ascend. Our attitude should be one which indicates that we have been raised up, that we have ascended.", "norm_zh": "像以弗所二章五至六节说到神因祂爱我们的大爱当我们死在过犯中的时候便叫我们与基督一同活过来祂又叫我们与基督耶稣一同复活一同坐在天上这里有三个一同两个叫这里所说的是神的应许呢还是神的事实神的话告诉我们这些都是事实是神叫我们与基督一同活过来是神叫我们与基督一同复活一同坐在天上这都是已经成功的事实既是事实我们就应当感谢赞美神就应当对撒但显出我们是已经与基督一同复活升天了不是显出某种态度好叫我们复活升天乃是显出一种态度说出我们是已经与基督一同复活升天了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In Ephesians 246 we read But God being rich in mercy because of His great love with which He loved us even when we were dead in offenses made us alive together with Christ and raised us up together and seated us together in the heavenlies in Christ Jesus There are three withs and two mades in this verse Are the things mentioned here Gods promises or Gods facts Gods Word tells us that these are all facts It is God who has made us alive together with Christ and it is God who has raised us up with Christ and seated us in the heavenly places with Christ These are all accomplished facts Since this is so we ought to praise and thank God We ought to take an attitude towards Satan that we have been raised up together and that we have ascended together with Christ We should not take an attitude of hope that we may be raised up or that we may ascend Our attitude should be one which indicates that we have been raised up that we have ascended"}
{"zh": "相信神的话是实在的", "en": "Believe that God's Word is true", "norm_zh": "相信神的话是实在的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Believe that Gods Word is true"}
{"zh": "我们要知道，没有一个属乎主的人所接受的生命不是复活和升天的生命。如果以为这种生命是要求而后得的，就是还不知道神所已经成功的事实。神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了，我们就不用求，只要取用就够了。阿利路亚！荣耀的事实，已成的事实，基督所已经成功的事实，神在基督里都已经赐给我们了！", "en": "We must know that there is not one of the Lord's people who has not received a life of resurrection and ascension. If we consider that this life can only be obtained by our asking for it, we do not know what God has accomplished. God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness. We do not need to ask; we only need to claim. Hallelujah, this glorious fact, this accomplished fact, this fact which Christ has accomplished, has been given to us by God in Christ!", "norm_zh": "我们要知道没有一个属乎主的人所接受的生命不是复活和升天的生命如果以为这种生命是要求而后得的就是还不知道神所已经成功的事实神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了我们就不用求只要取用就够了阿利路亚荣耀的事实已成的事实基督所已经成功的事实神在基督里都已经赐给我们了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must know that there is not one of the Lords people who has not received a life of resurrection and ascension If we consider that this life can only be obtained by our asking for it we do not know what God has accomplished God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness We do not need to ask we only need to claim Hallelujah this glorious fact this accomplished fact this fact which Christ has accomplished has been given to us by God in Christ"}
{"zh": "……我们除了相信神的话是实在的之外，我们也不能再作什么了。所以，对于神的事实，我们的需要，不是祷告求神来作，乃是相信神已经作了。我们一相信神的事实，我们就有了经历。事实，相信，经历，乃是神定规的次序，也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则，这是我们必须记得的。", "en": "...we cannot do any more than believe that God's Word is true. Therefore, what is needed is not for us to ask God to do something, but for us to believe what God has already done. Whenever we believe God's facts, the experience automatically follows. Fact, faith, and experience — this is the order which God has ordained. This great principle in the spiritual life must be remembered.", "norm_zh": "我们除了相信神的话是实在的之外我们也不能再作什么了所以对于神的事实我们的需要不是祷告求神来作乃是相信神已经作了我们一相信神的事实我们就有了经历事实相信经历乃是神定规的次序也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则这是我们必须记得的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "we cannot do any more than believe that Gods Word is true Therefore what is needed is not for us to ask God to do something but for us to believe what God has already done Whenever we believe Gods facts the experience automatically follows Fact faith and experience this is the order which God has ordained This great principle in the spiritual life must be remembered"}
{"zh": "关于神的事实，我们从前面所举的例子里，可以说有以下几个原则：", "en": "From what we have seen in the previous examples there are the following principles:", "norm_zh": "关于神的事实我们从前面所举的例子里可以说有以下几个原则", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "From what we have seen in the previous examples there are the following principles"}
{"zh": "（一）要先找出什么是神的事实。这个是需要圣灵来启示的。", "en": "1) We need to discover what God's fact is. For this, revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary.", "norm_zh": "一要先找出什么是神的事实这个是需要圣灵来启示的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We need to discover what Gods fact is For this revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary"}
{"zh": "（二）知道了某一件事是神的事实之后，就抓住神的话，相信你已经是按着神的话所说的那样了，相信神的事实是怎样，你也是怎样了。", "en": "2) Once we see what God's fact is, we need to hold on to God's Word and believe that we are just as God's Word says. We need to believe that just as God's fact says, so we are.", "norm_zh": "二知道了某一件事是神的事实之后就抓住神的话相信你已经是按着神的话所说的哪样了相信神的事实是怎样你也是怎样了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Once we see what Gods fact is we need to hold on to Gods Word and believe that we are just as Gods Word says We need to believe that just as Gods fact says so we are"}
{"zh": "（三）你就凭着这个信心，一面感谢神，因为你已经是这样了；另一面你就行出来，显出你已是这样了。", "en": "3) We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way; on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such.", "norm_zh": "三你就凭着这个信心一面感谢神因为你已经是这样了另一面你就行出来显出你已是这样了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such"}
{"zh": "（四）任何时候，你遇见试探或者试验，总要相信：神的话，神的事实，比你的感觉更靠得住。你只管满心相信神的话，神要负责叫你有经历。你如果注意到你的经历，你就要失败，反而一点经历都没有。相信神的事实，是我们的责任；叫我们有经历，是神的责任。我们如果相信神的事实，我们灵性的生活就要一日比一日长进。", "en": "4) Whenever temptation or trial comes to us, we must believe that God's Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings. We need only to fully believe God's Word; then God will be responsible to give us the experience. If we pay attention to our experience first, we shall fail and not have any experience. Our responsibility is to believe God's fact; God's responsibility is to grant us the experience. If we believe God's fact, our spiritual life will grow every day.", "norm_zh": "四任何时候你遇见试探或者试验总要相信神的话神的事实比你的感觉更靠得住你只管满心相信神的话神要负责叫你有经历你如果注意到你的经历你就要失败反而一点经历都没有相信神的事实是我们的责任叫我们有经历是神的责任我们如果相信神的事实我们灵性的生活就要一日比一日长进", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Whenever temptation or trial comes to us we must believe that Gods Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings We need only to fully believe Gods Word then God will be responsible to give us the experience If we pay attention to our experience first we shall fail and not have any experience Our responsibility is to believe Gods fact Gods responsibility is to grant us the experience If we believe Gods fact our spiritual life will grow every day"}
{"zh": "（五）事实需要人有信心，因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路。神的事实是在基督里的。所以人必须在基督里，才能享受神在基督里的事实。当我们与基督联合的时候，我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实。我们必须记得，我们得救的时候，就已经与基督联合了，就已经在基督里了（林前一，加三，罗六）。不过许多人虽然是“在基督里”了，却不“常住”在基督里。他们不用信心站在神在基督里所给他们的地位上，他们就失去神的事实在他们身上的效能。所以，我们在基督里了，还得常住在基督里。这样，神的事实才能成为我们的经历，才能一直在我们身上显明出来。", "en": "5) Fact requires our faith, for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experience. God's fact is in Christ; therefore, we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ. When we are united with Christ, we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in Christ. We must remember that when we were saved, we were united with Christ and were put into Christ (1 Cor. 1; Gal. 3; Rom. 6). But many, though they are \"in Christ,\" do not \"abide\" in Christ. Since they do not stand by faith upon the position which God has given them in Christ, they lose the effect which God's fact has toward them. Therefore, though we are already in Christ, we also need to abide in Christ. By this means, God's fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through us.", "norm_zh": "五事实需要人有信心因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路神的事实是在基督里的所以人必须在基督里才能享受神在基督里的事实当我们与基督联合的时候我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实我们必须记得我们得救的时候就已经与基督联合了就已经在基督里了林前一加三罗六不过许多人虽然是在基督里了却不常住在基督里他们不用信心站在神在基督里所给他们的地位上他们就失去神的事实在他们身上的效能所以我们在基督里了还得常住在基督里这样神的事实才能成为我们的经历才能一直在我们身上显明出来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Fact requires our faith for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experience Gods fact is in Christ therefore we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ When we are united with Christ we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in Christ We must remember that when we were saved we were united with Christ and were put into Christ 1 Cor 1 Gal 3 Rom 6 But many though they are in Christ do not abide in Christ Since they do not stand by faith upon the position which God has given them in Christ they lose the effect which Gods fact has toward them Therefore though we are already in Christ we also need to abide in Christ By this means Gods fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through us"}
{"zh": "需要看见神的事实是事实", "en": "We need to see that God's facts are facts", "norm_zh": "需要看见神的事实是事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We need to see that Gods facts are facts"}
{"zh": "我们在前面一再地说，神的事实是神已经作成了的，我们不应当求祂再作什么。但是，如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实，我们就得求神给我们启示，给我们光，叫我们能看见。是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道（弗一）。这个是可以求的。我们求，是求看见。我们不是求神再作那件事，乃是求神叫我们看见神已经作成那件事。这个我们必须分别清楚。现在我们举几个具体的例来说明它：", "en": "We have mentioned repeatedly that God's fact is something which He has already accomplished and that we do not need to ask Him to do anything. However, if we have not seen God's fact as fact, we need to ask God to give us revelation, to give us light, that we may see. It is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know (Eph. 1). We can ask for such a spirit. What we ask for is the vision. We do not ask that God will do that very thing again, but that He may show us that He has already accomplished that thing. We must be clear about this difference. Following are some further examples to clarify this matter.", "norm_zh": "我们在前面一再地说神的事实是神已经作成了的我们不应当求祂再作什么但是如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实我们就得求神给我们启示给我们光叫我们能看见是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道弗一这个是可以求的我们求是求看见我们不是求神再作哪件事乃是求神叫我们看见神已经作成哪件事这个我们必须分别清楚现在我们举几个具体的例来说明它", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have mentioned repeatedly that Gods fact is something which He has already accomplished and that we do not need to ask Him to do anything However if we have not seen Gods fact as fact we need to ask God to give us revelation to give us light that we may see It is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know Eph 1 We can ask for such a spirit What we ask for is the vision We do not ask that God will do that very thing again but that He may show us that He has already accomplished that thing We must be clear about this difference Following are some further examples to clarify this matter"}
{"zh": "例三：像圣灵的浇灌，已经是一个事实了。有一位姊妹一直不清楚。有一个晚上，她关着门在那里读行传第二章。她一面读，一面求神给她启示。神开了她的眼睛，叫她从这一章圣经里看见三点：", "en": "(3) A certain sister was not clear that the outpouring of the Holy Spirit is already a fact. One night she closed her door and read Acts 2. While reading this portion of the Word, she asked God to give her a revelation. God opened her eyes and showed her three things in this chapter:", "norm_zh": "例三像圣灵的浇灌已经是一个事实了有一位姊妹一直不清楚有一个晚上她关着门在哪里读行传第二章她一面读一面求神给她启示神开了她的眼睛叫她从这一章圣经里看见三点", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 A certain sister was not clear that the outpouring of the Holy Spirit is already a fact One night she closed her door and read Acts 2 While reading this portion of the Word she asked God to give her a revelation God opened her eyes and showed her three things in this chapter"}
{"zh": "（一）基督已经被神的右手高举，又从父受了所应许的圣灵，就把圣灵浇灌下来了。", "en": "1) Christ has been exalted to the right hand of God, and having received the promise of the Holy Spirit from the Father, has poured down the Holy Spirit.", "norm_zh": "一基督已经被神的右手高举又从父受了所应许的圣灵就把圣灵浇灌下来了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christ has been exalted to the right hand of God and having received the promise of the Holy Spirit from the Father has poured down the Holy Spirit"}
{"zh": "（二）神已经立祂为主为基督了。", "en": "2) God has made Him both Lord and Christ.", "norm_zh": "二神已经立祂为主为基督了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 God has made Him both Lord and Christ"}
{"zh": "（三）这应许（就是上一句所说的领受所赐的圣灵），是给以色列人和他们的儿女，并一切在远方的人的。", "en": "3) This promise of receiving the Holy Spirit is for the Israelites and for their children, and also for those who are afar off.", "norm_zh": "三这应许就是上一句所说的领受所赐的圣灵是给以色列人和他们的儿女并一切在远方的人的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 This promise of receiving the Holy Spirit is for the Israelites and for their children and also for those who are afar off"}
{"zh": "她看见圣灵已经浇灌下来了是一个事实。她是一个已经悔改，已经奉耶稣基督的名受浸的人，她是包括在“远方的人”之内的，所以她也有分于这个应许，就是有分于第三十八节所说“就必领受所赐的圣灵”的应许。她这样一看见，就充满了喜乐，不住地赞美主。", "en": "She saw that it is a fact that the Holy Spirit has been poured out. Since she was one who had repented and had been baptized in the name of Jesus Christ, she was included in those who were \"afar off.\" She realized, therefore, that she had a part in the promise, that is, that she had a part in what is mentioned in verse 38, \"Ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit.\" When she saw this, she was full of joy and could not cease to praise the Lord.", "norm_zh": "她看见圣灵已经浇灌下来了是一个事实她是一个已经悔改已经奉耶稣基督的名受浸的人她是包括在远方的人之内的所以她也有分于这个应许就是有分于第三十八节所说就必领受所赐的圣灵的应许她这样一看见就充满了喜乐不住地赞美主", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "She saw that it is a fact that the Holy Spirit has been poured out Since she was one who had repented and had been baptized in the name of Jesus Christ she was included in those who were afar off She realized therefore that she had a part in the promise that is that she had a part in what is mentioned in verse 38 Ye shall receive the gift of the Holy Spirit When she saw this she was full of joy and could not cease to praise the Lord"}
{"zh": "不需要求神再作那件事", "en": "No need to ask God to do that thing again", "norm_zh": "不需要求神再作哪件事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "No need to ask God to do that thing again"}
{"zh": "我们在前面已经说了神的应许与神的事实有什么分别，现在我们再总括地说一点神的应许与神的事实有什么根本不同的地方。", "en": "We have mentioned the contrast between God's promise and God's fact. Now let us summarize the basic difference between God's fact and God's promise.", "norm_zh": "我们在前面已经说了神的应许与神的事实有什么分别现在我们再总括地说一点神的应许与神的事实有什么根本不同的地方", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have mentioned the contrast between Gods promise and Gods fact Now let us summarize the basic difference between Gods fact and Gods promise"}
{"zh": "在圣经里面，应许是神要作一件事情之前所说的话语，事实是神既作一件事情之后所说的话语。", "en": "In the Scriptures, promise is the word spoken by God before the thing happens, while fact is the word spoken by God after the thing has happened.", "norm_zh": "在圣经里面应许是神要作一件事情之前所说的话语事实是神既作一件事情之后所说的话语", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the Scriptures promise is the word spoken by God before the thing happens while fact is the word spoken by God after the thing has happened"}
{"zh": "享用神所已经成功的事实", "en": "Enjoying what God has accomplished", "norm_zh": "享用神所已经成功的事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Enjoying what God has accomplished"}
{"zh": "我们对于神的应许，必须用信心接受。我们对于神的事实，不只当用信心接受，并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实。所以，我们读神的话的时候，最要紧的一件事，就是应当分别什么是神的应许，什么是神的事实。每一次我们读到一个地方，讲到神的恩典，就是讲到神如何为我们工作的地方，就得问说，这是一个应许呢，或者这是一个事实？如果是一个应许，并且是一个有条件的应许，你就应当履行其中所说的条件，并且好好地祷告。直等到神在你里面给你有把握，知道这一个应许是为着你的，你就很自然地有了信心，知道神已经听了你的祷告，你就很自然地会赞美神。虽然神所应许的还没有立即实现，但是，你因为已经有了信心，就好像那一件东西已经在你手里一样。如果是一个事实，你就可以立即运用信心，感谢神说，“神啊，是的，已经是这样的了。”你相信你自己真是这样的了，并且实行一若你是这样的。你借着这样的实行，证明你的信心。", "en": "We must receive God's promises with faith. With respect to God's facts, we must not only receive them with faith, but we must also enjoy the facts that God has already accomplished. Therefore, when we read God's Word, the most important thing is to distinguish what are God's promises and what are God's facts. Every time we read a portion concerning God's grace, that is, a place where it speaks of how God works for us, we must ask, \"Is this a promise, or is this a fact?\" If it is a promise, and a conditional promise, you should fulfill the conditions mentioned in it and pray properly. Until God gives you assurance within, knowing that this promise is for you, then you will spontaneously have faith, knowing that God has heard your prayer, and you will spontaneously praise God. Although what God has promised has not been immediately fulfilled, because you already have faith, it is as if that thing is already in your hand. If it is a fact, you can immediately exercise faith and thank God, saying, \"O God, yes, it is already so.\" You believe that you are indeed such, and practice as if you are such. Through such practice, you prove your faith.", "norm_zh": "我们对于神的应许必须用信心接受我们对于神的事实不只当用信心接受并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实所以我们读神的话的时候最要紧的一件事就是应当分别什么是神的应许什么是神的事实每一次我们读到一个地方讲到神的恩典就是讲到神如何为我们工作的地方就得问说这是一个应许呢或者这是一个事实如果是一个应许并且是一个有条件的应许你就应当履行其中所说的条件并且好好地祷告直等到神在你里面给你有把握知道这一个应许是为着你的你就很自然地有了信心知道神已经听了你的祷告你就很自然地会赞美神虽然神所应许的还没有立即实现但是你因为已经有了信心就好像哪一件东西已经在你手里一样如果是一个事实你就可以立即运用信心感谢神说神啊是的已经是这样的了你相信你自己真是这样的了并且实行一若你是这样的你借着这样的实行证明你的信心", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must receive Gods promises with faith With respect to Gods facts we must not only receive them with faith but we must also enjoy the facts that God has already accomplished Therefore when we read Gods Word the most important thing is to distinguish what are Gods promises and what are Gods facts Every time we read a portion concerning Gods grace that is a place where it speaks of how God works for us we must ask Is this a promise or is this a fact If it is a promise and a conditional promise you should fulfill the conditions mentioned in it and pray properly Until God gives you assurance within knowing that this promise is for you then you will spontaneously have faith knowing that God has heard your prayer and you will spontaneously praise God Although what God has promised has not been immediately fulfilled because you already have faith it is as if that thing is already in your hand If it is a fact you can immediately exercise faith and thank God saying O God yes it is already so You believe that you are indeed such and practice as if you are such Through such practice you prove your faith"}
{"zh": "对付不单纯的心", "en": "Dealing with an Impure Heart", "norm_zh": "对付不单纯的心", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Dealing with an Impure Heart"}
{"zh": "（一）我们在寻求主的应许之前，必须先对付不单纯的心。因为心思纷乱的人，或者情感太热的人，很容易以为东也是神给他的应许，西也是神给他的应许；昨天也有应许，今天也有应许。他的神的应许，是抽签似的得来的，是纷至沓来的。这样的神的应许是十有八九不可靠的，是会受欺骗的（这不是说，神的应许不可靠；乃是说，他所以为是神给他的应许，是他自己想出来的，不是神给他的）。心情有偏向，心志坚硬而又主观的人，如果把心思中所记忆的神的话，如果把正合乎他自己心情的神的话，如果把他主观见解的神的话，拿来当作神所给他的应许，也往往不可靠，结果反而使他灰心失望，反而使他对神的话怀疑起来。所以，我们在寻求神的应许之前，要先求神光照我们的心，叫我们认识自己的心；要求神清洁我们的心，也求神给我们恩典，叫我们肯放下自己，让我们能安静地仰望神。这样，神如果给我们应许，必定是自自然然地，清清楚楚地在我们心的深处。", "en": "1) Before we ask God for His promise, we must first deal with our impure heart. Those who are full of confusing thoughts or are too emotional will very likely consider that this is God's promise for them, or that that is God's promise for them. Yesterday there was a promise, today there is another promise. To them, obtaining God's promises is like drawing from a lottery, taking one lot after another. Nine times out of ten such promises are undependable and might be deceiving. (This does not mean that God's promises are not dependable, but that what such people consider to be God's promise is something they themselves have conceived, not something which God has given to them.) If those who have natural inclinations or hardness of will subjectively use what they have remembered of God's Word in their mind, or if they use those words of God which suit their moods, or explain God's Word in their subjective way and treat these as God's promises, their \"promises\" will usually be undependable. The result is that they will become disappointed, even doubtful of God's Word. Therefore, before we ask for God's promise, we need to ask Him to enlighten our heart that we may know our heart. We need to ask God to purify our heart. We also need to ask God to grant us grace, making us willing to lay down our selves so that we may quietly look unto Him. Then if God gives us a promise, we shall be spontaneously and clearly impressed from the deepest part of our heart.", "norm_zh": "一我们在寻求主的应许之前必须先对付不单纯的心因为心思纷乱的人或者情感太热的人很容易以为东也是神给他的应许西也是神给他的应许昨天也有应许今天也有应许他的神的应许是抽签似的得来的是纷至沓来的这样的神的应许是十有八九不可靠的是会受欺骗的这不是说神的应许不可靠乃是说他所以为是神给他的应许是他自己想出来的不是神给他的心情有偏向心志坚硬而又主观的人如果把心思中所记忆的神的话如果把正合乎他自己心情的神的话如果把他主观见解的神的话拿来当作神所给他的应许也往往不可靠结果反而使他灰心失望反而使他对神的话怀疑起来所以我们在寻求神的应许之前要先求神光照我们的心叫我们认识自己的心要求神清洁我们的心也求神给我们恩典叫我们肯放下自己让我们能安静地仰望神这样神如果给我们应许必定是自自然然地清清楚楚地在我们心的深处", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Before we ask God for His promise we must first deal with our impure heart Those who are full of confusing thoughts or are too emotional will very likely consider that this is Gods promise for them or that that is Gods promise for them Yesterday there was a promise today there is another promise To them obtaining Gods promises is like drawing from a lottery taking one lot after another Nine times out of ten such promises are undependable and might be deceiving This does not mean that Gods promises are not dependable but that what such people consider to be Gods promise is something they themselves have conceived not something which God has given to them If those who have natural inclinations or hardness of will subjectively use what they have remembered of Gods Word in their mind or if they use those words of God which suit their moods or explain Gods Word in their subjective way and treat these as Gods promises their promises will usually be undependable The result is that they will become disappointed even doubtful of Gods Word Therefore before we ask for Gods promise we need to ask Him to enlighten our heart that we may know our heart We need to ask God to purify our heart We also need to ask God to grant us grace making us willing to lay down our selves so that we may quietly look unto Him Then if God gives us a promise we shall be spontaneously and clearly impressed from the deepest part of our heart"}
{"zh": "（二）在得着神的应许之后，我们就要用它。司布真有这样的几句话：“信徒啊，我求你不要把主的应许当作展览会里的古玩；你应当天天用它们来作安慰的泉源，在患难中随时仰赖祂。”（《荒漠甘泉》八月十二日）这是有经历的话。", "en": "2) After receiving God's promise we need to make use of it. Charles Spurgeon once said, \"O believer, I beseech you do not treat God's promises as if they were curiosities for a museum; but use them as everyday sources of comfort. Trust the Lord whenever your time of need comes on.\" These are words of experience.", "norm_zh": "二在得着神的应许之后我们就要用它司布真有这样的几句话信徒啊我求你不要把主的应许当作展览会里的古玩你应当天天用它们来作安慰的泉源在患难中随时仰赖祂荒漠甘泉八月十二日这是有经历的话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 After receiving Gods promise we need to make use of it Charles Spurgeon once said O believer I beseech you do not treat Gods promises as if they were curiosities for a museum but use them as everyday sources of comfort Trust the Lord whenever your time of need comes on These are words of experience"}
{"zh": "将起初确实的信心，坚持到底", "en": "Holding Fast the Beginning of the Assurance Firm to the End", "norm_zh": "将起初确实的信心坚持到底", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Holding Fast the Beginning of the Assurance Firm to the End"}
{"zh": "（三）真有了神的应许的人，他的态度和行为，常是安息镇定，一若那应许已经实现了一样。像保罗在哥林多为道迫切的时候，主在异像中对他说了“不要怕，只管讲，不要闭口；有我与你同在，必没有人下手害你……”之后，他就在那里住了一年零六个月（徒十八）。又如保罗在那一次往罗马的途中，遭遇海中的危险的时候，他能站在同船的人中间说，“众位可以放心，我信神祂怎样对我说，事情也要怎样成就。”他不只信神的应许，他也用神的应许来应许人，安慰人。我们再看，“保罗说了这话，就拿着饼，在众人面前祝谢了神，擘开吃。”这是保罗信神应许的态度和行为。他这一种的态度和行为给了人深刻的印象，结果叫别人，“都放下心，也就吃了。”（徒二七，）", "en": "3) Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable way, as if the promise had come true. For example, when Paul was zealous for the work at Corinth, the Lord spoke to him in a vision: \"Be not afraid, but speak and hold not thy peace: for I am with thee, and no man shall set on thee to harm thee.\" After this, he dwelt there a year and six months (Acts 18). On another occasion when Paul was on the way to Rome and ran into danger at sea, he could stand among those who were with him in the ship and say, \"Be of good cheer: for I believe God, that it shall be even so as it hath been spoken unto me.\" He not only believed God's promise, but also used God's promise as a promise and a comfort to others. \"And when he had said this, and had taken bread, he gave thanks to God in the presence of all; and he brake it, and began to eat.\" This was Paul's manner and action after he believed God's promise. Such manner gave those with him a deep impression. The result was that \"they were all of good cheer, and themselves also took food\" (Acts 27).", "norm_zh": "三真有了神的应许的人他的态度和行为常是安息镇定一若哪应许已经实现了一样像保罗在哥林多为道迫切的时候主在异像中对他说了不要怕只管讲不要闭口有我与你同在必没有人下手害你之后他就在哪里住了一年零六个月徒十八又如保罗在哪一次往罗马的途中遭遇海中的危险的时候他能站在同船的人中间说众位可以放心我信神祂怎样对我说事情也要怎样成就他不只信神的应许他也用神的应许来应许人安慰人我们再看保罗说了这话就拿着饼在众人面前祝谢了神擘开吃这是保罗信神应许的态度和行为他这一种的态度和行为给了人深刻的印象结果叫别人都放下心也就吃了徒二七", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable way as if the promise had come true For example when Paul was zealous for the work at Corinth the Lord spoke to him in a vision Be not afraid but speak and hold not thy peace for I am with thee and no man shall set on thee to harm thee After this he dwelt there a year and six months Acts 18 On another occasion when Paul was on the way to Rome and ran into danger at sea he could stand among those who were with him in the ship and say Be of good cheer for I believe God that it shall be even so as it hath been spoken unto me He not only believed Gods promise but also used Gods promise as a promise and a comfort to others And when he had said this and had taken bread he gave thanks to God in the presence of all and he brake it and began to eat This was Pauls manner and action after he believed Gods promise Such manner gave those with him a deep impression The result was that they were all of good cheer and themselves also took food Acts 27"}
{"zh": "有一个圣徒说，“神每一个应许都是建立在四个根基上的：神的公义，神的圣洁，神的恩典，神的真实。神的公义，不让祂失信；神的圣洁，不让祂欺骗；神的恩典，不让祂遗忘；神的真实，不让祂改变。”（《荒漠甘泉》三月八日）还有一个圣徒说，“应许虽然迟延，决不会延得太迟的。”（十月九日）这都是认识神的人所说的有经历的话。", "en": "A saint has said that every promise of God is built upon four pillars: God's justice, God's holiness, God's grace, and God's truth. God's justice will not suffer Him to be faithless; God's holiness will not suffer Him to deceive; God's grace will not suffer Him to forget; and God's truth will not suffer Him to change. Another saint has said that though the promise tarry, it can never come too late. These are all words of experience from those who know God.", "norm_zh": "有一个圣徒说神每一个应许都是建立在四个根基上的神的公义神的圣洁神的恩典神的真实神的公义不让祂失信神的圣洁不让祂欺骗神的恩典不让祂遗忘神的真实不让祂改变荒漠甘泉三月八日还有一个圣徒说应许虽然迟延决不会延得太迟的十月九日这都是认识神的人所说的有经历的话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A saint has said that every promise of God is built upon four pillars Gods justice Gods holiness Gods grace and Gods truth Gods justice will not suffer Him to be faithless Gods holiness will not suffer Him to deceive Gods grace will not suffer Him to forget and Gods truth will not suffer Him to change Another saint has said that though the promise tarry it can never come too late These are all words of experience from those who know God"}
{"zh": "（四）我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后，信心是一直看那个事实，算那个事实为事实的。什么时候自己有了失败，就当找出失败的原因，也定罪那个失败的原因，定罪那个失败的行为。如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实，甚至否定神的事实，那就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心（来三），你就要求神除去你不信的恶心。", "en": "4) Once we have seen God's fact, our faith must continue to look at God's fact, counting the fact as fact. Whenever we have a failure, we need to discover the reason for the failure. We need to condemn both the reason for failure and the act of failing. If due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning God's fact, even denying God's fact, this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards God's fact (Heb. 3). At this point we need to ask God to remove the evil heart of unbelief.", "norm_zh": "四我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后信心是一直看哪个事实算哪个事实为事实的什么时候自己有了失败就当找出失败的原因也定罪哪个失败的原因定罪哪个失败的行为如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实甚至否定神的事实哪就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心来三你就要求神除去你不信的恶心", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:51:09.793229+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Once we have seen Gods fact our faith must continue to look at Gods fact counting the fact as fact Whenever we have a failure we need to discover the reason for the failure We need to condemn both the reason for failure and the act of failing If due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning Gods fact even denying Gods fact this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards Gods fact Heb 3 At this point we need to ask God to remove the evil heart of unbelief"}
{"zh": "壹\t神永远的目的是显在新约里；“恩典和真理，都是由耶稣基督来的”所以到了基督，才是恩典时代，才有新约，才看得见神永远的目的—约一17，来八8~13，十16，耶三一31，林后三6，来十三20~21：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "I. God's eternal purpose is manifested in the New Testament; \"grace and reality came through Jesus Christ\"; therefore, only when we come to Christ is there the age of grace, the New Testament, and the seeing of God's eternal purpose.—John 1:17; Heb. 8:8-13; 10:16; Jer. 31:31; 2 Cor. 3:6; Heb. 13:20-21:", "norm_zh": "壹神永远的目的是显在新约里恩典和真理都是由耶稣基督来的所以到了基督才是恩典时代才有新约才看得见神永远的目的约一17来八813十16耶三一31林后三6来十三2021李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Gods eternal purpose is manifested in the New Testament grace and reality came through Jesus Christ therefore only when we come to Christ is there the age of grace the New Testament and the seeing of Gods eternal purposeJohn 117 Heb 8813 1016 Jer 3131 2 Cor 36 Heb 132021"}
{"zh": "一\t神永远的目的，就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去；神喜欢进到人里面与人联合，叫人有祂的生命，有祂的性情—约一17，创一27：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "A. God's eternal purpose is that He wants to work Himself into the man whom He created; God likes to enter into man and be joined to man so that man would have His life and nature.—John 1:17; Gen. 1:27:", "norm_zh": "一神永远的目的就是神要把祂自己作到祂所创造的人里面去神喜欢进到人里面与人联合叫人有祂的生命有祂的性情约一17创一27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods eternal purpose is that He wants to work Himself into the man whom He created God likes to enter into man and be joined to man so that man would have His life and natureJohn 117 Gen 127"}
{"zh": "1\t祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分，祂就是要人像祂，祂就是要人得荣耀；所以，祂造人的时候，是照着自己的形像造人—弗一4~5，罗八30，创一27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "1. He wants man to obtain His sonship, He wants man to be like Him, and He wants man to be glorified; therefore, when He created man, He created him in His own image.—Eph. 1:4-5; Rom. 8:30; Gen. 1:27.", "norm_zh": "1祂就是要人得着祂儿子的名分祂就是要人像祂祂就是要人得荣耀所以祂造人的时候是照着自己的形像造人弗一45罗八30创一27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 He wants man to obtain His sonship He wants man to be like Him and He wants man to be glorified therefore when He created man He created him in His own imageEph 145 Rom 830 Gen 127"}
{"zh": "2\t神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里，祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子；换句话说，祂是示意：生命树的果子是应该吃的，不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的—二8~9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "2. God placed the created man in the garden of Eden; He only forbade man to eat the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil; in other words, He was indicating that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten, but this was for man to choose on his own initiative.—2:8-9.", "norm_zh": "2神把造好的人安置在伊甸园里祂只禁止人吃分别善恶树的果子换句话说祂是示意生命树的果子是应该吃的不过这是要人自己主动来拣选的二89李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 God placed the created man in the garden of Eden He only forbade man to eat the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil in other words He was indicating that the fruit of the tree of life should be eaten but this was for man to choose on his own initiative289"}
{"zh": "3\t头一个人虽然失败了，堕落了，第二个人，就是末后的亚当，却达到了神永远的目的！—林前十五45、47：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "3. Although the first man failed and fell, the second man, who is the last Adam, reached God's eternal purpose!—1 Cor. 15:45, 47:", "norm_zh": "3头一个人虽然失败了堕落了第二个人就是末后的亚当却达到了神永远的目的林前十五4547李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Although the first man failed and fell the second man who is the last Adam reached Gods eternal purpose1 Cor 1545 47"}
{"zh": "a\t这就是“道成了肉身，住在我们中间，充充满满地有恩典有真理”的主耶稣—约一14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "a. This is the Lord Jesus, \"the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us, full of grace and reality.\"—John 1:14.", "norm_zh": "a这就是道成了肉身住在我们中间充充满满地有恩典有真理的主耶稣约一14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a This is the Lord Jesus the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us full of grace and realityJohn 114"}
{"zh": "b\t虽然从来没有人看见神，但是，有一个人，就是在父怀里的独生子，将祂表明出来了—18。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "b. Although no one has ever seen God, yet there is a man, the only begotten Son, who is in the bosom of the Father, who has declared Him.—v. 18.", "norm_zh": "b虽然从来没有人看见神但是有一个人就是在父怀里的独生子将祂表明出来了18李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Although no one has ever seen God yet there is a man the only begotten Son who is in the bosom of the Father who has declared Himv 18"}
{"zh": "4\t神就是要把祂作到人里面去，就是要人像祂儿子的形状，这是神永远的目的，这也就是新约—罗八28、29。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "4. God wants to work Himself into man and wants man to be conformed to the image of His Son; this is God's eternal purpose, and this is the New Testament.—Rom. 8:28, 29.", "norm_zh": "4神就是要把祂作到人里面去就是要人像祂儿子的形状这是神永远的目的这也就是新约罗八2829李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 God wants to work Himself into man and wants man to be conformed to the image of His Son this is Gods eternal purpose and this is the New TestamentRom 828 29"}
{"zh": "二\t主以新约的原则对待祂的教会；主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下，要教会按着约与祂来往，按着约与祂交涉，直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切；主说，“……这是我立新约的血”—太二六28，来八8：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "B. The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant; the Lord has put the church under the principle of the new covenant, wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and deal with Him according to the covenant, until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish; the Lord says, \"...this is My blood of the new covenant.\"—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 8:8:", "norm_zh": "二主以新约的原则对待祂的教会主是把教会摆在新约的原则之下要教会按着约与祂来往按着约与祂交涉直到祂成功祂所要成功的一切主说这是我立新约的血太二六28来八8李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Lord deals with His church by the principle of the new covenant the Lord has put the church under the principle of the new covenant wanting the church to contact Him according to the covenant and deal with Him according to the covenant until He accomplishes all that He wants to accomplish the Lord says this is My blood of the new covenantMatt 2628 Heb 88"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们，有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约；并且严格说来，新约是要到那些日子以后，就是千禧年开始的时候才立的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "1. Hebrews 8:8 clearly tells us that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah; and strictly speaking, the new covenant will not be established until after those days, which is at the beginning of the millennium.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来八章八节明明告诉我们有一天神是要与以色列家和犹大家另立新约并且严格说来新约是要到哪些日子以后就是千禧年开始的时候才立的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Hebrews 88 clearly tells us that one day God will make a new covenant with the house of Israel and with the house of Judah and strictly speaking the new covenant will not be established until after those days which is at the beginning of the millennium"}
{"zh": "2\t主是用祂的血立了新约，使我们能预先得着新约的福；所以我们说，今天是新约的时代，乃是由于主特别的恩典—太二六28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "2. The Lord established the new covenant with His blood, so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant; therefore, we say that today is the new covenant age because of the Lord's special grace.—Matt. 26:28.", "norm_zh": "2主是用祂的血立了新约使我们能预先得着新约的福所以我们说今天是新约的时代乃是由于主特别的恩典太二六28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Lord established the new covenant with His blood so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant therefore we say that today is the new covenant age because of the Lords special graceMatt 2628"}
{"zh": "三\t我们要认识什么是新约，必须先认识什么是约；要认识什么是约，必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实—约十四13~14，十六13、二十27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，引言）", "en": "C. To know what the new covenant is, we must first know what a covenant is; to know what a covenant is, we must first know what God's promise is and what God's fact is.—John 14:13-14; 16:13; 20:27.", "norm_zh": "三我们要认识什么是新约必须先认识什么是约要认识什么是约必须先认识什么是神的应许和什么是神的事实约十四1314十六13二十27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约引言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C To know what the new covenant is we must first know what a covenant is to know what a covenant is we must first know what Gods promise is and what Gods fact isJohn 141314 1613 2027"}
{"zh": "贰\t神的话在恩典方面，总括地说，可以分为三种：（一）神所给我们的应许，（二）神所已经为我们成功的事实，（三）神与人立的约，就是神所绝对要作的—十四11~12，徒二17~36。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "II. God's Word in the aspect of grace may be summed up into three categories: 1) the promises of God to us, 2) the facts which God has accomplished for us, and 3) the covenants which God has made with man which He Himself will definitely fulfill.—John 14:11-12; Acts 2:17-36.", "norm_zh": "贰神的话在恩典方面总括地说可以分为三种一神所给我们的应许二神所已经为我们成功的事实三神与人立的约就是神所绝对要作的十四1112徒二1736李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Gods Word in the aspect of grace may be summed up into three categories 1 the promises of God to us 2 the facts which God has accomplished for us and 3 the covenants which God has made with man which He Himself will definitely fulfillJohn 141112 Acts 21736"}
{"zh": "叁\t应许是与事实不同的，应许是将来的，事实是已往的；应许是要作的，事实是已作的；应许是神要为人作什么，事实是神已经为人作成了什么—代下一9，弗六2~3，罗四13~14，来十一39~40：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "III. A promise is different from a fact; promise is related to the future, while fact is related to the past; promise is something to be done, while fact is something already done; promise means that God will do something for man, while fact means that God has already done something for man.—2 Chron. 1:9; Eph. 6:2-3; Rom. 4:13-14; Heb. 11:39-40:", "norm_zh": "叁应许是与事实不同的应许是将来的事实是已往的应许是要作的事实是已作的应许是神要为人作什么事实是神已经为人作成了什么代下一9弗六23罗四1314来十一3940李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III A promise is different from a fact promise is related to the future while fact is related to the past promise is something to be done while fact is something already done promise means that God will do something for man while fact means that God has already done something for man2 Chron 19 Eph 623 Rom 41314 Heb 113940"}
{"zh": "一\t关于神的应许有以下四个原则—代下一9，弗六2~3，罗四13~14，来十一39~40：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "A. There are the following four principles concerning God's promises:—2 Chron. 1:9; Eph. 6:2-3; Rom. 4:13-14; Heb. 11:39-40:", "norm_zh": "一关于神的应许有以下四个原则代下一9弗六23罗四1314来十一3940李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A There are the following four principles concerning Gods promises2 Chron 19 Eph 623 Rom 41314 Heb 113940"}
{"zh": "1\t神的应许是需要求神成就的—代下一9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "1. God's promise requires our prayer that it may be fulfilled—2 Chron. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "1神的应许是需要求神成就的代下一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods promise requires our prayer that it may be fulfilled2 Chron 19"}
{"zh": "2\t神的应许如果是有条件的，人必须履行了所应当履行的条件，才能得着所应许的；不然的话，应许就有取消的可能—弗六2~3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "2. If God's promise is conditional, man must fulfill His condition in order to obtain the promise; otherwise, the promise may be revoked—Eph. 6:2-3.", "norm_zh": "2神的应许如果是有条件的人必须履行了所应当履行的条件才能得着所应许的不然的话应许就有取消的可能弗六23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If Gods promise is conditional man must fulfill His condition in order to obtain the promise otherwise the promise may be revokedEph 623"}
{"zh": "3\t人若在神的应许之外用血气的力量作了什么，或者加上什么，应许也有废弃落空的可能—罗四13~14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "3. If, apart from God's promise, man uses the strength of his flesh to act or to add something, the promise may become of none effect—Rom. 4:13-14.", "norm_zh": "3人若在神的应许之外用血气的力量作了什么或者加上什么应许也有废弃落空的可能罗四1314李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If apart from Gods promise man uses the strength of his flesh to act or to add something the promise may become of none effectRom 41314"}
{"zh": "4\t神的应许是要等到神的时候到了，才能实现—来十一39~40。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "4. God's promises are fulfilled in God's time—Heb. 11:39-40.", "norm_zh": "4神的应许是要等到神的时候到了才能实现来十一3940李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Gods promises are fulfilled in Gods timeHeb 113940"}
{"zh": "二\t神的应许如何能成功在我们身上—林后十三3，赛四一10：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "B. How God's Promise is Accomplished in Us—2 Cor. 13:3; Isa. 41:10:", "norm_zh": "二神的应许如何能成功在我们身上林后十三3赛四一10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B How Gods Promise is Accomplished in Us2 Cor 133 Isa 4110"}
{"zh": "1\t每一次当我们在神的话里看见一个应许的时候，我们必须好好地祷告，祷告到神的灵在我们里面兴起，叫我们里面深深地觉得，这个应许是神为着我们的—哀三8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "1. Every time we see a promise in God's Word we must really pray. We must pray until the Spirit of God is so stirred in us that we feel deeply that this promise is intended of God for us.—Lam. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "1每一次当我们在神的话里看见一个应许的时候我们必须好好地祷告祷告到神的灵在我们里面兴起叫我们里面深深地觉得这个应许是神为着我们的哀三8李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Every time we see a promise in Gods Word we must really pray We must pray until the Spirit of God is so stirred in us that we feel deeply that this promise is intended of God for usLam 38"}
{"zh": "2\t如果这个应许是没有条件的，我们就可以立时运用信心接受这个应许；同时相信神必定按着祂所应许的成功在我们身上；我们就赞美神，感谢神—可十一22，太十四27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "2. If there is no condition attached to this promise, we can immediately exercise our faith to receive it; believing at the same time that God will accomplish in us what He has promised; we praise and thank God.—Mark 11:22; Matt. 14:27.", "norm_zh": "2如果这个应许是没有条件的我们就可以立时运用信心接受这个应许同时相信神必定按着祂所应许的成功在我们身上我们就赞美神感谢神可十一22太十四27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If there is no condition attached to this promise we can immediately exercise our faith to receive it believing at the same time that God will accomplish in us what He has promised we praise and thank GodMark 1122 Matt 1427"}
{"zh": "3\t如果这个应许是有条件的，我们就要履行所当履行的条件，然后再借着祷告来到神的面前，求神凭着祂的信实和公义而行，求神将祂的应许成就在我们的身上—来十三5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "3. If the promise has certain conditions, we need to fulfill the conditions. Then we come to God through prayer and ask Him to act according to His faithfulness and righteousness and fulfill His promise in us.—Heb. 13:5.", "norm_zh": "3如果这个应许是有条件的我们就要履行所当履行的条件然后再借着祷告来到神的面前求神凭着祂的信实和公义而行求神将祂的应许成就在我们的身上来十三5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If the promise has certain conditions we need to fulfill the conditions Then we come to God through prayer and ask Him to act according to His faithfulness and righteousness and fulfill His promise in usHeb 135"}
{"zh": "肆\t事实是神已经成功了的工作—加四4，来九26，彼后一3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "IV. Facts are God's accomplished work.—Gal. 4:4; Heb. 9:26; 2 Pet. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "肆事实是神已经成功了的工作加四4来九26彼后一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Facts are Gods accomplished workGal 44 Heb 926 2 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "一\t对于神的事实，我们的需要，不是祷告求神来作，乃是相信神已经作了；我们一相信神的事实，我们就有了经历；事实，相信，经历，乃是神定规的次序，也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则，这是我们必须记得的—太二一22，罗四18：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "A. Concerning God's facts, what is needed is not for us to pray and ask God to do it, but to believe that God has already done it; once we believe God's facts, we have the experience; fact, faith, and experience is the order ordained by God, and is also a greatest principle in the spiritual life; this we must remember.—Matt. 21:22; Rom. 4:18:", "norm_zh": "一对于神的事实我们的需要不是祷告求神来作乃是相信神已经作了我们一相信神的事实我们就有了经历事实相信经历乃是神定规的次序也是灵性生活中一个最大的原则这是我们必须记得的太二一22罗四18李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Concerning Gods facts what is needed is not for us to pray and ask God to do it but to believe that God has already done it once we believe Gods facts we have the experience fact faith and experience is the order ordained by God and is also a greatest principle in the spiritual life this we must rememberMatt 2122 Rom 418"}
{"zh": "1\t神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了，我们就不用求，只要取用就够了—弗二5~6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "1. God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness. We do not need to ask; we only need to claim.—Eph. 2:5-6.", "norm_zh": "1神在基督里已经将一切关乎生命和虔敬的事赐给我们了我们就不用求只要取用就够了弗二56李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God has given us in Christ all that pertains to life and godliness We do not need to ask we only need to claimEph 256"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣如何是已经钉在十字架上了，我们的旧人也如何是已经和祂同钉在十字架上了；这是事实，这是神借着基督已经成功的事实—罗六6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "2. Even as the Lord Jesus has been crucified on the cross, so also our old man has been crucified with Him on the cross; this is a fact, a fact which God has already accomplished through Christ.—Rom. 6:6.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣如何是已经钉在十字架上了我们的旧人也如何是已经和祂同钉在十字架上了这是事实这是神借着基督已经成功的事实罗六6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Even as the Lord Jesus has been crucified on the cross so also our old man has been crucified with Him on the cross this is a fact a fact which God has already accomplished through ChristRom 66"}
{"zh": "3\t尽管有的时候有试探来，但是我们仍旧相信神所作的，过于我们的感觉和经历；我们真看见这个事实是事实的时候，经历就自然而然会来到—约二十27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "3. Even though sometimes temptations come, we still believe what God has done more than our feelings and experiences; when we truly see that this fact is a fact, the experience will come naturally.—John 20:27.", "norm_zh": "3尽管有的时候有试探来但是我们仍旧相信神所作的过于我们的感觉和经历我们真看见这个事实是事实的时候经历就自然而然会来到约二十27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Even though sometimes temptations come we still believe what God has done more than our feelings and experiences when we truly see that this fact is a fact the experience will come naturallyJohn 2027"}
{"zh": "二\t关于神的事实的几个原则—林前二10，诗三三4，太二一21：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "B. Some Principles Concerning God's Facts—1 Cor. 2:10; Psa. 33:4; Matt. 21:21:", "norm_zh": "二关于神的事实的几个原则林前二10诗三三4太二一21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Some Principles Concerning Gods Facts1 Cor 210 Psa 334 Matt 2121"}
{"zh": "1\t要先找出什么是神的事实；这个是需要圣灵来启示的—林前二10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "1. We need to first discover what God's fact is; for this, revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary.—1 Cor. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1要先找出什么是神的事实这个是需要圣灵来启示的林前二10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We need to first discover what Gods fact is for this revelation from the Holy Spirit is necessary1 Cor 210"}
{"zh": "2\t知道了某一件事是神的事实之后，就抓住神的话，相信你已经是按着神的话所说的那样了，相信神的事实是怎样，你也是怎样了—来十一3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "2. Once we see what God's fact is, we need to hold on to God's Word and believe that we are just as God's Word says. We need to believe that just as God's fact says, so we are.—Heb. 11:3.", "norm_zh": "2知道了某一件事是神的事实之后就抓住神的话相信你已经是按着神的话所说的哪样了相信神的事实是怎样你也是怎样了来十一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Once we see what Gods fact is we need to hold on to Gods Word and believe that we are just as Gods Word says We need to believe that just as Gods fact says so we areHeb 113"}
{"zh": "3\t你就凭着这个信心，一面感谢神，因为你已经是这样了；另一面你就行出来，显出你已是这样了—林后四13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "3. We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way; on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such.—2 Cor. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "3你就凭着这个信心一面感谢神因为你已经是这样了另一面你就行出来显出你已是这样了林后四13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We need by faith on one hand to praise God that we are this way on the other hand we need to act and manifest that we are such2 Cor 413"}
{"zh": "4\t任何时候，你遇见试探或者试验，总要相信：神的话，神的事实，比你的感觉更靠得住；你只管满心相信神的话，神要负责叫你有经历—太二一21。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "4. Whenever temptation or trial comes to us, we must believe that God's Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings. We need only to fully believe God's Word; then God will be responsible to give us the experience.—Matt. 21:21.", "norm_zh": "4任何时候你遇见试探或者试验总要相信神的话神的事实比你的感觉更靠得住你只管满心相信神的话神要负责叫你有经历太二一21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Whenever temptation or trial comes to us we must believe that Gods Word and His fact are more dependable than our feelings We need only to fully believe Gods Word then God will be responsible to give us the experienceMatt 2121"}
{"zh": "5\t事实需要人有信心，因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路—来十一：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "5. Fact requires our faith, for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experience—Heb. 11:", "norm_zh": "5事实需要人有信心因为信心是将事实化作经历的惟一的路来十一李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Fact requires our faith for faith is the only way by which the fact may be realized in our experienceHeb 11"}
{"zh": "a\t神的事实是在基督里的；所以人必须在基督里，才能享受神在基督里的事实—林前一5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "a. God's fact is in Christ; therefore, we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ.—1 Cor. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "a神的事实是在基督里的所以人必须在基督里才能享受神在基督里的事实林前一5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a Gods fact is in Christ therefore we must be in Christ in order to enjoy the fact which God has accomplished in Christ1 Cor 15"}
{"zh": "b\t当我们与基督联合的时候，我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实—加三27、29。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "b. When we are united with Christ, we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in Christ.—Gal. 3:27, 29.", "norm_zh": "b当我们与基督联合的时候我们才能经历神在基督里所已经成功的事实加三2729李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b When we are united with Christ we shall experience the fact which God has accomplished in ChristGal 327 29"}
{"zh": "c\t我们在基督里了，还得常住在基督里；这样，神的事实才能成为我们的经历，才能一直在我们身上显明出来—约十五4。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "c. Though we are already in Christ, we also need to abide in Christ. By this means, God's fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through us.—John 15:4.", "norm_zh": "c我们在基督里了还得常住在基督里这样神的事实才能成为我们的经历才能一直在我们身上显明出来约十五4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Though we are already in Christ we also need to abide in Christ By this means Gods fact will become our experience and will continue to be manifested through usJohn 154"}
{"zh": "伍\t如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实，我们就得求神给我们启示，给我们光，叫我们能看见；是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道；这个是可以求的；我们求，是求看见—弗一17，太七7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "V. If we have not seen God's fact as fact, we need to ask God to give us revelation, to give us light, that we may see; it is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know; we can ask for such a spirit; what we ask for is the vision.—Eph. 1:17; Matt. 7:7.", "norm_zh": "伍如果我们没有看见神的事实是事实我们就得求神给我们启示给我们光叫我们能看见是智慧和启示的灵能叫我们知道这个是可以求的我们求是求看见弗一17太七7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V If we have not seen Gods fact as fact we need to ask God to give us revelation to give us light that we may see it is the spirit of wisdom and revelation that will cause us to know we can ask for such a spirit what we ask for is the visionEph 117 Matt 77"}
{"zh": "陆\t我们对于神的应许，必须用信心接受；我们对于神的事实，不只当用信心接受，并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实—来十一1，林后四13，诗一一九49：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "VI. We must receive God's promise with our faith; we must not only receive God's fact with our faith, but also enjoy what God has accomplished.—Heb. 11:1; 2 Cor. 4:13; Psa. 119:49:", "norm_zh": "陆我们对于神的应许必须用信心接受我们对于神的事实不只当用信心接受并且还要享用神所已经成功的事实来十一1林后四13诗一一九49李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI We must receive Gods promise with our faith we must not only receive Gods fact with our faith but also enjoy what God has accomplishedHeb 111 2 Cor 413 Psa 11949"}
{"zh": "一\t我们在寻求主的应许之前，必须先对付不单纯的心—林后十一3，弗六5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "A. Before we ask God for His promise, we must first deal with our impure heart.—2 Cor. 11:3; Eph. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "一我们在寻求主的应许之前必须先对付不单纯的心林后十一3弗六5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we ask God for His promise we must first deal with our impure heart2 Cor 113 Eph 65"}
{"zh": "二\t在得着神的应许之后，我们就要用它—诗一三〇7，罗四20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "B. After receiving God's promise we need to make use of it—Psa. 130:7, Rom. 4:20.", "norm_zh": "二在得着神的应许之后我们就要用它诗一三〇7罗四20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B After receiving Gods promise we need to make use of itPsa 1307 Rom 420"}
{"zh": "三\t真有了神的应许的人，他的态度和行为，常是安息镇定—徒二七25，十八9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "C. Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable way—Acts 27:25; 18:9.", "norm_zh": "三真有了神的应许的人他的态度和行为常是安息镇定徒二七25十八9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Those who really have a promise from God usually behave and act in a peaceful and stable wayActs 2725 189"}
{"zh": "四\t我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后，信心是一直看那个事实，算那个事实为事实的；如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实，甚至否定神的事实，那就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心—诗三一24，来三12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "D. Once we have seen God's fact, our faith must continue to look at God's fact, counting the fact as fact; if due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning God's fact, even denying God's fact, this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards God's fact—Psa. 31:24; Heb. 3:12.", "norm_zh": "四我们对于神的事实有了一次看见之后信心是一直看哪个事实算哪个事实为事实的如果因着自己的失败而怀疑神的事实甚至否定神的事实哪就证明你对神的事实存着不信的恶心诗三一24来三12李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Once we have seen Gods fact our faith must continue to look at Gods fact counting the fact as fact if due to our own failure we become doubtful concerning Gods fact even denying Gods fact this proves that we have an evil heart of unbelief towards Gods factPsa 3124 Heb 312"}
{"zh": "柒\t亲爱的弟兄姊妹们，“我们若将起初确实的信心，坚持到底，就在基督里有分了。”—倪柝声（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第一章）", "en": "VII. Dear brothers and sisters, \"If we hold fast the beginning of our assurance firm to the end, we have become partners of Christ.\" —Watchman Nee", "norm_zh": "柒亲爱的弟兄姊妹们我们若将起初确实的信心坚持到底就在基督里有分了倪柝声李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:53:24.513836+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII Dear brothers and sisters If we hold fast the beginning of our assurance firm to the end we have become partners of Christ Watchman Nee"}
{"zh": "读经：启四2~3，十1，创六、九，十五4~6、9~21，撒下七4~16，诗八九19~37，二五14，加三5~9，来八6、10~12，耶三一31~32，太二六26~30", "en": "Scripture Reading: Rev. 4:2-3; 10:1; Gen. 6; 9; 15:4-6, 9-21; 2 Sam. 7:4-16; Psa. 89:19-37; 25:14; Gal. 3:5-9; Heb. 8:6, 10-12; Jer. 31:31-32; Matt. 26:26-30", "norm_zh": "读经启四23十1创六九十五46921撒下七416诗八九1937二五14加三59来八61012耶三一3132太二六2630", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Rev 423 101 Gen 6 9 1546 921 2 Sam 7416 Psa 891937 2514 Gal 359 Heb 86 1012 Jer 313132 Matt 262630"}
{"zh": "壹\t神所立的约比神的应许和神的事实更荣耀；神与人立约，是神降卑祂自己来受约的拘束，来受约的限制—启四2~3，十1：", "en": "I. The covenant which God has made is more glorious than either His promise or His fact; God's making a covenant with man is His condescending to be bound and limited by the covenant.—Rev. 4:2-3; 10:1:", "norm_zh": "壹神所立的约比神的应许和神的事实更荣耀神与人立约是神降卑祂自己来受约的拘束来受约的限制启四23十1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The covenant which God has made is more glorious than either His promise or His fact Gods making a covenant with man is His condescending to be bound and limited by the covenantRev 423 101"}
{"zh": "一\t神的应许是宝贵的，当你遇见疾病、痛苦、艰难的时候，神的应许对于你就好像河流在干旱之地，又象大磐石的影子在疲乏之地—赛三二，三五。", "en": "A. God's promise is precious; when you have illness, pain, or difficulty, God's promise is to you like streams in a dry place and like the shadow of a great rock in a weary land—Isa. 32, 35.", "norm_zh": "一神的应许是宝贵的当你遇见疾病痛苦艰难的时候神的应许对于你就好像河流在干旱之地又象大磐石的影子在疲乏之地赛三二三五", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods promise is precious when you have illness pain or difficulty Gods promise is to you like streams in a dry place and like the shadow of a great rock in a weary landIsa 32 35"}
{"zh": "二\t还有比神的应许更容易得着的，就是神的事实；神不只把祂快要成就的应许赐给我们，神并且把祂已经成功的事实赐给我们了—林后四，二14，三18，来九15~17、22、26~28。", "en": "B. There is something even more available than God's promise, which is God's facts; God not only gives us His promises which are about to be fulfilled, but God has also given us His accomplished facts—2 Cor. 4; 2:14; 3:18; Heb. 9:15-17, 22, 26-28.", "norm_zh": "二还有比神的应许更容易得着的就是神的事实神不只把祂快要成就的应许赐给我们神并且把祂已经成功的事实赐给我们了林后四二14三18来九1517222628", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There is something even more available than Gods promise which is Gods facts God not only gives us His promises which are about to be fulfilled but God has also given us His accomplished facts2 Cor 4 214 318 Heb 91517 22 2628"}
{"zh": "三\t约有什么意义呢？约是讲信义，讲律法的；约只能按信义、公理、律法而执行—申七9，约壹一9。", "en": "C. What is the meaning of a covenant? A covenant speaks of faithfulness and law; a covenant must be carried out strictly according to faithfulness, justice, and law.—Deut. 7:9; 1 John 1:9.", "norm_zh": "三约有什么意义呢约是讲信义讲律法的约只能按信义公理律法而执行申七9约壹一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C What is the meaning of a covenant A covenant speaks of faithfulness and law a covenant must be carried out strictly according to faithfulness justice and lawDeut 79 1 John 19"}
{"zh": "四\t以神的肯受拘束而与人立约而言，约是神的恩典最高的表示—启四2~3。", "en": "D. As far as God's willingness to be bound in making a covenant with man is concerned, the covenant is the highest expression of God's grace.—Rev. 4:2-3.", "norm_zh": "四以神的肯受拘束而与人立约而言约是神的恩典最高的表示启四23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D As far as Gods willingness to be bound in making a covenant with man is concerned the covenant is the highest expression of Gods graceRev 423"}
{"zh": "贰\t神借着约向人表示祂的心意—创六、九：", "en": "II. Through the Covenant God Shows His Intention to Man—Gen. 6, 9:", "norm_zh": "贰神借着约向人表示祂的心意创六九", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Through the Covenant God Shows His Intention to ManGen 6 9"}
{"zh": "一\t神对人有一个好心意，人不懂，人不明白，神就给人一个约，使人有凭据可抓—九8~17、20。", "en": "A. God has a good intention toward man, but man does not understand or see; therefore, God gives man a covenant so that he may have some evidence to cling to.—9:8-17, 20.", "norm_zh": "一神对人有一个好心意人不懂人不明白神就给人一个约使人有凭据可抓九81720", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God has a good intention toward man but man does not understand or see therefore God gives man a covenant so that he may have some evidence to cling to9817 20"}
{"zh": "二\t神给人一个约，明明告诉人祂的心意是如何，好像把祂的心打开来给人看，人才能知道祂的心是如何—12~15节。", "en": "B. God gives man a covenant to show him clearly what His intention is, as if He is opening His heart to man so that man can see what His heart is really like.—vv. 12-15.", "norm_zh": "二神给人一个约明明告诉人祂的心意是如何好像把祂的心打开来给人看人才能知道祂的心是如何1215节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God gives man a covenant to show him clearly what His intention is as if He is opening His heart to man so that man can see what His heart is really likevv 1215"}
{"zh": "叁\t神借着约扩充人信心的度量—十五4~6、9~21：", "en": "III. Through the Covenant God Enlarges the Measure of Man's Faith—15:4-6, 9-21:", "norm_zh": "叁神借着约扩充人信心的度量十五46921", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Through the Covenant God Enlarges the Measure of Mans Faith1546 921"}
{"zh": "一\t神与亚伯拉罕立约，就是神扩充亚伯拉罕信心度量的方法；神不只应许亚伯拉罕要作，神并且与亚伯拉罕立约去作—8节与注1。", "en": "A. God's making a covenant with Abraham was God's way of enlarging the measure of Abraham's faith; God not only promised Abraham what He would do, but God even made a covenant with him to do it.—v. 8 and note 1.", "norm_zh": "一神与亚伯拉罕立约就是神扩充亚伯拉罕信心度量的方法神不只应许亚伯拉罕要作神并且与亚伯拉罕立约去作8节与注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods making a covenant with Abraham was Gods way of enlarging the measure of Abrahams faith God not only promised Abraham what He would do but God even made a covenant with him to do itv 8 and note 1"}
{"zh": "二\t在这样一个约的坚固之下，亚伯拉罕信心的度量自然而然地扩充了—5、8~21节，来十一8~10。", "en": "B. By the strengthening of such a covenant, the measure of Abraham's faith was naturally enlarged.—vv. 5, 8-21; Heb. 11:8-10.", "norm_zh": "二在这样一个约的坚固之下亚伯拉罕信心的度量自然而然地扩充了5821节来十一810", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B By the strengthening of such a covenant the measure of Abrahams faith was naturally enlargedvv 5 821 Heb 11810"}
{"zh": "肆\t神借着约给人以凭据—撒下七4~16，诗八九19~37：", "en": "IV. Through the Covenant God Gives Man a Pledge—2 Sam. 7:4-16; Psa. 89:19-37:", "norm_zh": "肆神借着约给人以凭据撒下七416诗八九1937", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Through the Covenant God Gives Man a Pledge2 Sam 7416 Psa 891937"}
{"zh": "一\t神所以与人立约，祂就是要人有胆量来问祂，要求祂按着正义成就祂约里所说的；神是受约的拘束的，神必须按着正义行事—20~28节。", "en": "A. The reason God makes a covenant with man is that man may become bold enough to inquire of Him and demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant according to righteousness; God is bound by the covenant; He must act according to righteousness.—vv. 20-28.", "norm_zh": "一神所以与人立约祂就是要人有胆量来问祂要求祂按着正义成就祂约里所说的神是受约的拘束的神必须按着正义行事2028节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The reason God makes a covenant with man is that man may become bold enough to inquire of Him and demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant according to righteousness God is bound by the covenant He must act according to righteousnessvv 2028"}
{"zh": "二\t神喜欢人按着约来亲近祂，祈求祂，甚至来问祂；神喜欢人要求祂履行祂在约里所应许的一切—49节，一四三1。", "en": "B. God delights that man draw near to Him, pray to Him, and even inquire of Him according to the covenant; God delights that man demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant.—v. 49; 143:1.", "norm_zh": "二神喜欢人按着约来亲近祂祈求祂甚至来问祂神喜欢人要求祂履行祂在约里所应许的一切49节一四三1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God delights that man draw near to Him pray to Him and even inquire of Him according to the covenant God delights that man demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenantv 49 1431"}
{"zh": "伍\t诗篇二十五篇十四节告诉我们说，“耶和华的秘密与敬畏祂的人同在，祂必将祂的约指示他们”：", "en": "V. Psalm 25:14 tells us, \"The secret (lit.) of Jehovah is with them that fear him; and he will show them his covenant\":", "norm_zh": "伍诗篇二十五篇十四节告诉我们说耶和华的秘密与敬畏祂的人同在祂必将祂的约指示他们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Psalm 2514 tells us The secret lit of Jehovah is with them that fear him and he will show them his covenant"}
{"zh": "一\t如果没有神的启示，你仍旧没有能力，你仍旧抓不牢神的话；所以我们需要神在我们的灵里给我们一个指示—14节，林前二10，来十二28。", "en": "A. Unless God reveals it, you will still have no power; you still cannot hold fast God's word; therefore, God must show it to us in our spirit.—v. 14; 1 Cor. 2:10; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "一如果没有神的启示你仍旧没有能力你仍旧抓不牢神的话所以我们需要神在我们的灵里给我们一个指示14节林前二10来十二28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Unless God reveals it you will still have no power you still cannot hold fast Gods word therefore God must show it to us in our spiritv 14 1 Cor 210 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "二\t敬畏祂是什么意思呢？敬畏祂，就是尊祂为大，就是高举祂；一心寻求神的旨意，完全顺服神的旨意的人，就是敬畏祂的人—彼前一17，来十二28。", "en": "B. What does it mean to fear Him? To fear means to magnify, to exalt Him; a person who fears God is one who seeks God's will with a full heart, with the intention of completely submitting to God's way.—1 Pet. 1:17; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "二敬畏祂是什么意思呢敬畏祂就是尊祂为大就是高举祂一心寻求神的旨意完全顺服神的旨意的人就是敬畏祂的人彼前一17来十二28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B What does it mean to fear Him To fear means to magnify to exalt Him a person who fears God is one who seeks Gods will with a full heart with the intention of completely submitting to Gods way1 Pet 117 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "陆\t新约继承亚伯拉罕的约—加三5~9：", "en": "VI. THE NEW COVENANT CONTINUES THE COVENANT OF ABRAHAM—Gal. 3:5-9:", "norm_zh": "陆新约继承亚伯拉罕的约加三59", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI THE NEW COVENANT CONTINUES THE COVENANT OF ABRAHAMGal 359"}
{"zh": "一\t新约是继承神与亚伯拉罕所立的约，新约是发挥亚伯拉罕的约的；加拉太第三章给我们看见，新约与亚伯拉罕的约是一个系统—6~9节：", "en": "A. The new covenant is a continuation and development of the covenant God made with Abraham; Galatians 3 shows us that the new covenant and the covenant made with Abraham are of the same line.—vv. 6-9:", "norm_zh": "一新约是继承神与亚伯拉罕所立的约新约是发挥亚伯拉罕的约的加拉太第三章给我们看见新约与亚伯拉罕的约是一个系统69节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant is a continuation and development of the covenant God made with Abraham Galatians 3 shows us that the new covenant and the covenant made with Abraham are of the same linevv 69"}
{"zh": "1\t神与以色列人所立律法的约，虽然是在亚伯拉罕的约和新约之间，但是，律法是为过犯添上的，根本是外添的—加三，罗五。", "en": "1. Between Abraham's covenant and the new covenant there is the covenant of law made with Israel. However, the law was added because of transgression; it is basically an addition—Gal. 3; Rom. 5.", "norm_zh": "1神与以色列人所立律法的约虽然是在亚伯拉罕的约和新约之间但是律法是为过犯添上的根本是外添的加三罗五", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Between Abrahams covenant and the new covenant there is the covenant of law made with Israel However the law was added because of transgression it is basically an additionGal 3 Rom 5"}
{"zh": "2\t惟有亚伯拉罕的约和新约，是本乎信，是本乎应许的，所以是一个系统—加三6~9，来八。", "en": "2. Only the covenant made with Abraham and the new covenant are of faith and promise. For this reason, they are of the same line.—Gal. 3:6-9; Heb. 8.", "norm_zh": "2惟有亚伯拉罕的约和新约是本乎信是本乎应许的所以是一个系统加三69来八", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Only the covenant made with Abraham and the new covenant are of faith and promise For this reason they are of the same lineGal 369 Heb 8"}
{"zh": "二\t希伯来八章七节说，“那前约若没有瑕疵，就无处寻求后约了”：", "en": "B. Hebrews 8:7 says, \"For if that first covenant was faultless, no place would have been sought for a second\":", "norm_zh": "二希伯来八章七节说哪前约若没有瑕疵就无处寻求后约了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Hebrews 87 says For if that first covenant was faultless no place would have been sought for a second"}
{"zh": "1\t律法只是要求人行善，律法并没有给人生命和能力去行善—罗八3，七7、12、15~17、24~25。", "en": "1. The law requires man to do good, but it does not give man the life and power to do good—Rom. 8:3; 7:7, 12, 15-17, 24-25.", "norm_zh": "1律法只是要求人行善律法并没有给人生命和能力去行善罗八3七71215172425", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The law requires man to do good but it does not give man the life and power to do goodRom 83 77 12 1517 2425"}
{"zh": "2\t约版还没有拿下山，以色列人就已经背约了；这就是前约的瑕疵—出三二1~8。", "en": "2. Even before the tables of the covenant were brought down from the mountain, the children of Israel had become unfaithful to the covenant; this was the fault of the first covenant—Exo. 32:1-8.", "norm_zh": "2约版还没有拿下山以色列人就已经背约了这就是前约的瑕疵出三二18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Even before the tables of the covenant were brought down from the mountain the children of Israel had become unfaithful to the covenant this was the fault of the first covenantExo 3218"}
{"zh": "3\t此后，以色列人也没有能遵守神的约；他们在旷野惹神发怒，试探神，并且观看神的作为有四十年之久—来三10。", "en": "3. After this, the children of Israel continued to fail in keeping God's covenant; they provoked God in the wilderness. They tried Him by testing Him and saw His works forty years.—Heb. 3:10.", "norm_zh": "3此后以色列人也没有能遵守神的约他们在旷野惹神发怒试探神并且观看神的作为有四十年之久来三10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 After this the children of Israel continued to fail in keeping Gods covenant they provoked God in the wilderness They tried Him by testing Him and saw His works forty yearsHeb 310"}
{"zh": "4\t保罗的经历也告诉我们，律法的本身是属灵的，但是律法对于肉体有所不能行；这就是前约的瑕疵—罗八3。", "en": "4. Paul's experience also tells us that the law itself is spiritual, but the law could not perform, in that it was weak through the flesh; this, too, was the fault of the first covenant—Rom. 8:3.", "norm_zh": "4保罗的经历也告诉我们律法的本身是属灵的但是律法对于肉体有所不能行这就是前约的瑕疵罗八3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Pauls experience also tells us that the law itself is spiritual but the law could not perform in that it was weak through the flesh this too was the fault of the first covenantRom 83"}
{"zh": "柒\t新约是更美之约；新约，乃是凭着更美之应许立的—来八6，七22：", "en": "VII. The new covenant is the better covenant; the new covenant is enacted upon better promises—Heb. 8:6; 7:22:", "norm_zh": "柒新约是更美之约新约乃是凭着更美之应许立的来八6七22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The new covenant is the better covenant the new covenant is enacted upon better promisesHeb 86 722"}
{"zh": "一\t新约，是把神的律法放在人的心意里面，写在人的心上的—八10，十16，耶三一33，参林后三3：", "en": "A. The new covenant imparts God's laws into man's mind and inscribes them upon man's heart—Heb. 8:10; 10:16; Jer. 31:33; cf. 2 Cor. 3:3:", "norm_zh": "一新约是把神的律法放在人的心意里面写在人的心上的八10十16耶三一33参林后三3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant imparts Gods laws into mans mind and inscribes them upon mans heartHeb 810 1016 Jer 3133 cf 2 Cor 33"}
{"zh": "1\t新约中，命令你的是神，叫你能遵行神的旨意的也是神—来八10。", "en": "1. In the new covenant, the One who demands of us is God, and the One who enables us to do the will of God is also God!—Heb. 8:10.", "norm_zh": "1新约中命令你的是神叫你能遵行神的旨意的也是神来八10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In the new covenant the One who demands of us is God and the One who enables us to do the will of God is also GodHeb 810"}
{"zh": "2\t新约，是神给你生命和能力，叫你能行神所要你行的善，叫神能作你的神，叫你也能作神的子民—八章，多二。", "en": "2. The new covenant is a covenant in which God gives you life and power to do the good He intends you to do, so that He may be your God and you may be His people—Heb. 8; Titus 2.", "norm_zh": "2新约是神给你生命和能力叫你能行神所要你行的善叫神能作你的神叫你也能作神的子民八章多二", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The new covenant is a covenant in which God gives you life and power to do the good He intends you to do so that He may be your God and you may be His peopleHeb 8 Titus 2"}
{"zh": "3\t新约，能叫人决不用人的教导而在里面更深地认识神—来八10~11，约壹二27，参约十四23。", "en": "3. The new covenant enables man to know God more deeply and in an inward way, without being taught by his fellow citizen—Heb. 8:10-11; 1 John 2:27; cf. John 14:23.", "norm_zh": "3新约能叫人决不用人的教导而在里面更深地认识神来八1011约壹二27参约十四23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The new covenant enables man to know God more deeply and in an inward way without being taught by his fellow citizenHeb 81011 1 John 227 cf John 1423"}
{"zh": "二\t新约里有神的应许和事实—来六13~18：", "en": "B. THE NEW COVENANT INCLUDES GOD'S PROMISES AND GOD'S FACTS—Heb. 6:13-18:", "norm_zh": "二新约里有神的应许和事实来六1318", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B THE NEW COVENANT INCLUDES GODS PROMISES AND GODS FACTSHeb 61318"}
{"zh": "1\t约是神的应许必要成就的保证；我们不能说，所有神的应许都是神的约；但是我们敢说，所有神的约都有神的应许—15~16节。", "en": "1. The covenant is the guarantee that God's promise will definitely be fulfilled; we cannot say that all of God's promises are His covenants, but we dare to say that all of God's covenants include His promises—vv. 15-16.", "norm_zh": "1约是神的应许必要成就的保证我们不能说所有神的应许都是神的约但是我们敢说所有神的约都有神的应许1516节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The covenant is the guarantee that Gods promise will definitely be fulfilled we cannot say that all of Gods promises are His covenants but we dare to say that all of Gods covenants include His promisesvv 1516"}
{"zh": "2\t新约所以是更美之约，就是因为这约是凭更美之应许立的—八6，七22，九23，十二24。", "en": "2. The new covenant is a better covenant because it is enacted upon better promises—Heb. 8:6; 7:22; 9:23; 12:24.", "norm_zh": "2新约所以是更美之约就是因为这约是凭更美之应许立的八6七22九23十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The new covenant is a better covenant because it is enacted upon better promisesHeb 86 722 923 1224"}
{"zh": "3\t神的约里不只有应许，也有遗命；遗命就是有所遗留，有遗物，有遗产；所遗留的东西就是事实—九15~18。", "en": "3. In God's covenant there is not only the promise, but also the testament; a testament, or will, indicates that there is an estate, a bequest; the things bequeathed are the facts—Heb. 9:15-18.", "norm_zh": "3神的约里不只有应许也有遗命遗命就是有所遗留有遗物有遗产所遗留的东西就是事实九1518", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In Gods covenant there is not only the promise but also the testament a testament or will indicates that there is an estate a bequest the things bequeathed are the factsHeb 91518"}
{"zh": "捌\t新约的时代—耶三一31~32，太二六26~30：", "en": "VIII. THE AGE OF THE NEW COVENANT—Jer. 31:31-32; Matt. 26:26-30:", "norm_zh": "捌新约的时代耶三一3132太二六2630", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII THE AGE OF THE NEW COVENANTJer 313132 Matt 262630"}
{"zh": "一\t神与什么人立新约；神立新约，不是与外邦人立的，乃是与以色列家和犹大家立的—耶三一31~32，来八8~12。", "en": "A. With Whom God Made the New Covenant; God Made the New Covenant, Not with the Gentiles, but with the Houses of Israel and Judah—Jer. 31:31-32; Heb. 8:8-12.", "norm_zh": "一神与什么人立新约神立新约不是与外邦人立的乃是与以色列家和犹大家立的耶三一3132来八812", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A With Whom God Made the New Covenant God Made the New Covenant Not with the Gentiles but with the Houses of Israel and JudahJer 313132 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "二\t神在什么时候立新约；我们相信是指千禧年开始的时候说的—耶三一31~33，来八8~12。", "en": "B. When God Makes the New Covenant; We Believe That It Refers to the Beginning of the Millennium—Jer. 31:31-33; Heb. 8:8-12.", "norm_zh": "二神在什么时候立新约我们相信是指千禧年开始的时候说的耶三一3133来八812", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When God Makes the New Covenant We Believe That It Refers to the Beginning of the MillenniumJer 313133 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "三\t今天怎么是新约的时代；主耶稣在被卖的那夜，“拿起杯来，祝谢了，递给他们，说，你们都喝这个，因为这是我立新约的血……”—太二六26~30：", "en": "C. How Today Is the Age of the New Covenant; In the Night the Lord Jesus Was Betrayed, \"taking the cup and giving thanks, He gave it to them, saying, Drink of it, all of you; for this is My blood of the new (lit.) covenant ...\"—Matt. 26:26-30:", "norm_zh": "三今天怎么是新约的时代主耶稣在被卖的哪夜拿起杯来祝谢了递给他们说你们都喝这个因为这是我立新约的血太二六2630", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C How Today Is the Age of the New Covenant In the Night the Lord Jesus Was Betrayed taking the cup and giving thanks He gave it to them saying Drink of it all of you for this is My blood of the new lit covenant Matt 262630"}
{"zh": "1\t因主莫大的恩典，这新约应用到所有蒙恩的人身上来了—28节。", "en": "1. Because of the Lord's exceeding grace, the new covenant applies to all those who are found by grace—v. 28.", "norm_zh": "1因主莫大的恩典这新约应用到所有蒙恩的人身上来了28节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Because of the Lords exceeding grace the new covenant applies to all those who are found by gracev 28"}
{"zh": "2\t从祂受死那天起，新约就设立起来了；这是主的大恩典，使我们能以预享新约的福—26~29节。", "en": "2. From the day He died, the new covenant was established; this is the Lord's great grace, so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant.—vv. 26-29.", "norm_zh": "2从祂受死哪天起新约就设立起来了这是主的大恩典使我们能以预享新约的福2629节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 From the day He died the new covenant was established this is the Lords great grace so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenantvv 2629"}
{"zh": "3\t主是以新约的原则建造我们，以新约的福赐给我们—参加三14。", "en": "3. The Lord is building us up today by the principle of the new covenant and blessing us with the blessing of the new covenant.—cf. Gal. 3:14.", "norm_zh": "3主是以新约的原则建造我们以新约的福赐给我们参加三14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Lord is building us up today by the principle of the new covenant and blessing us with the blessing of the new covenantcf Gal 314"}
{"zh": "4\t祂的血不只解决了罪的问题，祂的血也立了新约；所以，这一个时代诚然是新约的时代！—太二六28，路二二20，来九15，十二24，林前十一25。", "en": "4. His blood not only solved the problem of sin, but also established the new covenant; therefore, this age is truly the new covenant age.—Matt. 26:28; Luke 22:20; Heb. 9:15; 12:24; 1 Cor. 11:25.", "norm_zh": "4祂的血不只解决了罪的问提祂的血也立了新约所以这一个时代诚然是新约的时代太二六28路二二20来九15十二24林前十一25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 His blood not only solved the problem of sin but also established the new covenant therefore this age is truly the new covenant ageMatt 2628 Luke 2220 Heb 915 1224 1 Cor 1125"}
{"zh": "玖\t新约的内容；新约包含了三大部分—来八10~12：", "en": "IX. The content of the new covenant; the new covenant includes three parts—Heb. 8:10-12:", "norm_zh": "玖新约的内容新约包含了三大部分来八1012", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The content of the new covenant the new covenant includes three partsHeb 81012"}
{"zh": "一\t神把律法放在人的心意里面，写在人的心上；神作了他们的神，他们作了神的子民；这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合—10节，罗八2。", "en": "A. God imparts His laws into man's mind and inscribes them upon man's heart; God becomes their God, and they become God's people; this means that God Himself enters into man to be one with man.—v. 10; Rom. 8:2.", "norm_zh": "一神把律法放在人的心意里面写在人的心上神作了他们的神他们作了神的子民这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合10节罗八2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God imparts His laws into mans mind and inscribes them upon mans heart God becomes their God and they become Gods people this means that God Himself enters into man to be one with manv 10 Rom 82"}
{"zh": "二\t这律法在人的里面，叫人决不用人的教导而认识神；这是里面地认识神—来八11，约壹二27。", "en": "B. These laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others; this is the inward knowledge of God.—Heb. 8:11; 1 John 2:27.", "norm_zh": "二这律法在人的里面叫人决不用人的教导而认识神这是里面地认识神来八11约壹二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B These laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others this is the inward knowledge of GodHeb 811 1 John 227"}
{"zh": "三\t神要宽恕人的不义，也不再记念人的罪愆；这是赦罪—来八12，十17，参二17，约壹二2。", "en": "C. God will make propitiation for man's unrighteousnesses; neither will He remember man's sins; this is forgiveness.—Heb. 8:12; 10:17; cf. 2:17; 1 John 2:2.", "norm_zh": "三神要宽恕人的不义也不再记念人的罪愆这是赦罪来八12十17参二17约壹二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God will make propitiation for mans unrighteousnesses neither will He remember mans sins this is forgivenessHeb 812 1017 cf 217 1 John 22"}
{"zh": "其次，我们来看神与亚伯拉罕立约的事。", "en": "Now let us come to the matter of God's making a covenant with Abraham.", "norm_zh": "其次我们来看神与亚伯拉罕立约的事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Now let us come to the matter of Gods making a covenant with Abraham"}
{"zh": "亚伯拉罕在拯救侄儿罗得，和拒绝所多玛王的财物，这两件事上所显出的，是热爱、勇敢和清洁（创十四）。但在这事以后，神来对亚伯拉罕说，“你不要惧怕，我是你的盾牌，必大大地赏赐你。”（十五）这就给我们看见，亚伯拉罕此时的心情，一面不免担心四王有一天或者还要来，一面又不免因罗得的离开和自己的无子而暗自伤感，所以神就在这样的时候来坚固他，安慰他。可是从亚伯拉罕的回答中可以看出，神的这个应许，并没有叫亚伯拉罕的心意满足。他说，“主耶和华啊，我既无子，你还赐我什么呢？并且要承受我家业的，是大马色人以利以谢。”这就显出他还没有知道神的应许是多么恩典。他消极，他有他自己的想法，他有他自己的安排。神怎么作呢？神说，“这人必不成为你的后嗣，你本身所生的，才成为你的后嗣。于是领他走到外边，说，你向天观看，数算众星，能数得过来么？又对他说，你的后裔将要如此。”神在这里对亚伯拉罕所说的是什么呢？是应许，不是事实。亚伯拉罕呢，现在能信神的这个应许了，神就以此为他的义。亚伯拉罕因为信了神的应许，他就成了信心的祖宗。", "en": "In saving his nephew, Lot, and refusing the offer of the King of Sodom, Abraham manifested his love, his zeal, his bravery, and his cleanness (Gen. 14:14-23). Then, after these things, God came to speak to Abraham saying, \"Fear not, Abram: I am thy shield and thy exceeding great reward\" (Gen. 15:1). This verse shows that at this time Abraham's feeling was on one hand that of anxiety, fearing that the four kings might come again and on the other hand sorrow for Lot's departure and for his own state of childlessness. It was at this time that God came to him to strengthen and comfort him. But from Abraham's answer we see that this promise of God did not fully satisfy him. He asked, \"What wilt thou give me, seeing I go childless, and he that shall be possessor of my house is Eliezer of Damascus?\" (v. 2). This shows that he had not yet known or seen how gracious God's promise was. He was negative. He had his own idea and his own arrangement as well. So what did God do? God said, \"This man shall not be thine heir; but he that shall come forth out of thine own bowels shall be thine heir. And he brought him forth abroad, and said, Look now toward heaven, and number the stars, if thou be able to number them: and he said unto him, So shall thy seed be\" (vv. 4-5). What was it that God spoke here to Abraham? It was a promise, not a fact. What about Abraham? Now he could believe God's promise; therefore, God reckoned it to him as righteousness (v. 6). Because Abraham believed in God's promise, he became the father of faith.", "norm_zh": "亚伯拉罕在拯救侄儿罗得和拒绝所多玛王的财物这两件事上所显出的是热爱勇敢和清洁创十四但在这事以后神来对亚伯拉罕说你不要惧怕我是你的盾牌必大大地赏赐你十五这就给我们看见亚伯拉罕此时的心情一面不免担心四王有一天或者还要来一面又不免因罗得的离开和自己的无子而暗自伤感所以神就在这样的时候来坚固他安慰他可是从亚伯拉罕的回答中可以看出神的这个应许并没有叫亚伯拉罕的心意满足他说主耶和华啊我既无子你还赐我什么呢并且要承受我家业的是大马色人以利以谢这就显出他还没有知道神的应许是多么恩典他消极他有他自己的想法他有他自己的安排神怎么作呢神说这人必不成为你的后嗣你本身所生的才成为你的后嗣于是领他走到外边说你向天观看数算众星能数得过来么又对他说你的后裔将要如此神在这里对亚伯拉罕所说的是什么呢是应许不是事实亚伯拉罕呢现在能信神的这个应许了神就以此为他的义亚伯拉罕因为信了神的应许他就成了信心的祖宗", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In saving his nephew Lot and refusing the offer of the King of Sodom Abraham manifested his love his zeal his bravery and his cleanness Gen 141423 Then after these things God came to speak to Abraham saying Fear not Abram I am thy shield and thy exceeding great reward Gen 151 This verse shows that at this time Abrahams feeling was on one hand that of anxiety fearing that the four kings might come again and on the other hand sorrow for Lots departure and for his own state of childlessness It was at this time that God came to him to strengthen and comfort him But from Abrahams answer we see that this promise of God did not fully satisfy him He asked What wilt thou give me seeing I go childless and he that shall be possessor of my house is Eliezer of Damascus v 2 This shows that he had not yet known or seen how gracious Gods promise was He was negative He had his own idea and his own arrangement as well So what did God do God said This man shall not be thine heir but he that shall come forth out of thine own bowels shall be thine heir And he brought him forth abroad and said Look now toward heaven and number the stars if thou be able to number them and he said unto him So shall thy seed be vv 45 What was it that God spoke here to Abraham It was a promise not a fact What about Abraham Now he could believe Gods promise therefore God reckoned it to him as righteousness v 6 Because Abraham believed in Gods promise he became the father of faith"}
{"zh": "我们再看神与大卫立约的事。", "en": "Now let us see the history of the covenant which God made with David.", "norm_zh": "我们再看神与大卫立约的事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Now let us see the history of the covenant which God made with David"}
{"zh": "撒下七章四至十六节所说的，和诗篇八十九篇十九至三十七节所说的是同一件事。不过撒下第七章没有说明神如何与大卫立约，乃是诗篇第八十九篇告诉我们，耶和华差遣先知拿单去对大卫所说的话乃是一个约。诗篇所说的，和撒母耳记下所说的是同一件事，不是两件事。神在这里把祂的话当作凭据给大卫和大卫的子孙，祂喜欢人抓住祂的话，要求祂履行。神喜欢人这样作。祂把约给人当凭据，就是盼望人这样作。", "en": "Second Samuel 7:4-16 speaks of the same thing as Psalm 89:19-37. However, 2 Samuel 7 does not say clearly how God made a covenant with David. It is in Psalm 89 where we find that when the Lord sent the prophet Nathan to David, what he spoke to David was a covenant. Psalm 89 and 2 Samuel 7 speak of the same thing, not of two different things. In both of these passages God gave His word to David and his descendants as a pledge. He likes for man to take hold of His word and ask Him to fulfill it. He loves for man to do this. He gave a covenant to man as a pledge, hoping that man would ask Him to fulfill it.", "norm_zh": "撒下七章四至十六节所说的和诗篇八十九篇十九至三十七节所说的是同一件事不过撒下第七章没有说明神如何与大卫立约乃是诗篇第八十九篇告诉我们耶和华差遣先知拿单去对大卫所说的话乃是一个约诗篇所说的和撒母耳记下所说的是同一件事不是两件事神在这里把祂的话当作凭据给大卫和大卫的子孙祂喜欢人抓住祂的话要求祂履行神喜欢人这样作祂把约给人当凭据就是盼望人这样作", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Second Samuel 7416 speaks of the same thing as Psalm 891937 However 2 Samuel 7 does not say clearly how God made a covenant with David It is in Psalm 89 where we find that when the Lord sent the prophet Nathan to David what he spoke to David was a covenant Psalm 89 and 2 Samuel 7 speak of the same thing not of two different things In both of these passages God gave His word to David and his descendants as a pledge He likes for man to take hold of His word and ask Him to fulfill it He loves for man to do this He gave a covenant to man as a pledge hoping that man would ask Him to fulfill it"}
{"zh": "我们已经说过，神所给我们的恩典的话语，其中包括神的应许，神的事实和神的约，而神的约里又包括神的应许和神的事实。现在我们要来看在神的约里所包括的神的应许和神的事实。圣经给我们看见，神的约就是神的应许，不过，神的应许是神的口所说的，神的约是神所起誓立的（来六）。应许会使神受拘束，约更会使神受拘束。神与亚伯拉罕立约的时候，指着自己起誓，因为“神愿意为那承受应许的人，格外显明祂的旨意是不更改的，就起誓为证”。神起了誓是决不后悔的（七）。所以约是更使神受限制，受拘束的。", "en": "We have seen before that the word of grace which God has given us includes God's promises, God's facts, and God's covenants. We have also seen that God's covenants include God's promises and God's facts. Now let us see God's promises and God's facts which are included in God's covenants. The Scriptures show us that God's covenant is God's promise, except that God's promise was spoken by God's mouth, and God's covenant was made by an oath (Heb. 6:17). The promise binds God, and much more, the covenant binds God. When God made a covenant with Abraham He swore by Himself (Heb. 6:13-14). \"Wherefore God, willing to show more abundantly to the heirs of the promise the unchangeableness of His counsel, intervened by an oath\" (Heb. 6:17). For \"the Lord has sworn and will not regret it\" (Heb. 7:21). Therefore, a covenant limits God and binds God more than a promise.", "norm_zh": "我们已经说过神所给我们的恩典的话语其中包括神的应许神的事实和神的约而神的约里又包括神的应许和神的事实现在我们要来看在神的约里所包括的神的应许和神的事实圣经给我们看见神的约就是神的应许不过神的应许是神的口所说的神的约是神所起誓立的来六应许会使神受拘束约更会使神受拘束神与亚伯拉罕立约的时候指着自己起誓因为神愿意为哪承受应许的人格外显明祂的旨意是不更改的就起誓为证神起了誓是决不后悔的七所以约是更使神受限制受拘束的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have seen before that the word of grace which God has given us includes Gods promises Gods facts and Gods covenants We have also seen that Gods covenants include Gods promises and Gods facts Now let us see Gods promises and Gods facts which are included in Gods covenants The Scriptures show us that Gods covenant is Gods promise except that Gods promise was spoken by Gods mouth and Gods covenant was made by an oath Heb 617 The promise binds God and much more the covenant binds God When God made a covenant with Abraham He swore by Himself Heb 61314 Wherefore God willing to show more abundantly to the heirs of the promise the unchangeableness of His counsel intervened by an oath Heb 617 For the Lord has sworn and will not regret it Heb 721 Therefore a covenant limits God and binds God more than a promise"}
{"zh": "希伯来九章十五至十八节所说的那一段话，很清楚地给我们看见，新约里有应许，也有事实。第十六节说，“凡有遗命，必须等到留遗命的人死了。”（“遗命”原文与“约”字同—圣经小字注）所以，“约”在圣经中有两个意思：（一）是“条约”，（二）是“遗命”。因此，可以说，新约是一个约；也可以说，新约是一个遗命。", "en": "Hebrews 9:15-18 clearly shows us that in the new covenant there are promises and there are also facts. Verse 16 says, \"For where there is a testament there must of necessity be the death of him who made it.\" In the original text, testament and covenant are the same word. Therefore, the word covenant has two meanings in the Scriptures: first it is a covenant, or contract, and second it is a testament, or will. Hence, we can say that the new covenant is a covenant, and we can also say that it is a will.", "norm_zh": "希伯来九章十五至十八节所说的哪一段话很清楚地给我们看见新约里有应许也有事实第十六节说凡有遗命必须等到留遗命的人死了遗命原文与约字同圣经小字注所以约在圣经中有两个意思一是条约二是遗命因此可以说新约是一个约也可以说新约是一个遗命", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 91518 clearly shows us that in the new covenant there are promises and there are also facts Verse 16 says For where there is a testament there must of necessity be the death of him who made it In the original text testament and covenant are the same word Therefore the word covenant has two meanings in the Scriptures first it is a covenant or contract and second it is a testament or will Hence we can say that the new covenant is a covenant and we can also say that it is a will"}
{"zh": "希伯来八章十至十二节说，“主又说，那些日子以后，我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样：我要将我的律法放在他们心意里面，写在他们心上；我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民；他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我。因为我要宽恕他们的不义，不再记念他们的罪愆。”这一段圣经很清楚地给我们看见，新约包含了三大部分：", "en": "Hebrews 8:10-12 says, \"For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days, says the Lord: I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them, and I will be God to them, and they shall be a people to Me. And they shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother, saying, Know the Lord, for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them. For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I will by no means remember anymore.\" This passage clearly reveals that the new covenant includes three parts:", "norm_zh": "希伯来八章十至十二节说主又说哪些日子以后我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样我要将我的律法放在他们心意里面写在他们心上我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我因为我要宽恕他们的不义不再记念他们的罪愆这一段圣经很清楚地给我们看见新约包含了三大部分", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 81012 says For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days says the Lord I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe them and I will be God to them and they shall be a people to Me And they shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother saying Know the Lord for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I will by no means remember anymore This passage clearly reveals that the new covenant includes three parts"}
{"zh": "（一）神把律法放在人的心意里面，写在人的心上；神作了他们的神，他们作了神的子民。这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合。", "en": "1) God imparts His laws into man's mind and inscribes them upon man's heart. God becomes their God, and they become God's people. This means that God Himself enters into man to be one with man.", "norm_zh": "一神把律法放在人的心意里面写在人的心上神作了他们的神他们作了神的子民这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God imparts His laws into mans mind and inscribes them upon mans heart God becomes their God and they become Gods people This means that God Himself enters into man to be one with man"}
{"zh": "（二）这律法在人的里面，叫人决不用人的教导而认识神。这是里面地认识神。", "en": "2) These laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others. This is the inward knowledge of God.", "norm_zh": "二这律法在人的里面叫人决不用人的教导而认识神这是里面地认识神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 These laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others This is the inward knowledge of God"}
{"zh": "（三）神要宽恕人的不义，也不再记念人的罪愆。这是赦罪。", "en": "3) God will make propitiation for man's unrighteousnesses; neither will He remember man's sins. This is forgiveness.", "norm_zh": "三神要宽恕人的不义也不再记念人的罪愆这是赦罪", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:56:44.356983+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 God will make propitiation for mans unrighteousnesses neither will He remember mans sins This is forgiveness"}
{"zh": "壹\t神所立的约比神的应许和神的事实更荣耀；神与人立约，是神降卑祂自己来受约的拘束，来受约的限制—启四2~3，十1：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "I. The covenant which God has made is more glorious than either His promise or His fact; God's making a covenant with man is His condescending to be bound and limited by the covenant—Rev. 4:2-3; 10:1:", "norm_zh": "壹神所立的约比神的应许和神的事实更荣耀神与人立约是神降卑祂自己来受约的拘束来受约的限制启四23十1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The covenant which God has made is more glorious than either His promise or His fact Gods making a covenant with man is His condescending to be bound and limited by the covenantRev 423 101"}
{"zh": "一\t神的应许是宝贵的，当你遇见疾病、痛苦、艰难的时候，神的应许对于你就好像河流在干旱之地，又象大磐石的影子在疲乏之地—赛三二，三五。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "A. God's promise is precious; when you have illness, pain, or difficulty, God's promise is to you like streams in a dry place and like the shadow of a great rock in a weary land—Isa. 32, 35.", "norm_zh": "一神的应许是宝贵的当你遇见疾病痛苦艰难的时候神的应许对于你就好像河流在干旱之地又象大磐石的影子在疲乏之地赛三二三五李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods promise is precious when you have illness pain or difficulty Gods promise is to you like streams in a dry place and like the shadow of a great rock in a weary landIsa 32 35"}
{"zh": "二\t还有比神的应许更容易得着的，就是神的事实；神不只把祂快要成就的应许赐给我们，神并且把祂已经成功的事实赐给我们了—林后四，二14，三18，来九15~17、22、26~28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "B. But there is something more available than God's promise, which is God's fact; God not only gives us the promises that He is about to fulfill, but He has also given us the facts that He has already accomplished—2 Cor. 4, 2:14, 3:18; Heb. 9:15-17, 22, 26-28.", "norm_zh": "二还有比神的应许更容易得着的就是神的事实神不只把祂快要成就的应许赐给我们神并且把祂已经成功的事实赐给我们了林后四二14三18来九1517222628李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B But there is something more available than Gods promise which is Gods fact God not only gives us the promises that He is about to fulfill but He has also given us the facts that He has already accomplished2 Cor 4 214 318 Heb 91517 22 2628"}
{"zh": "三\t约有什么意义呢？约是讲信义，讲律法的；约只能按信义、公理、律法而执行—申七9，约壹一9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "C. What is the meaning of a covenant? A covenant speaks of faithfulness and law; a covenant can only be carried out according to faithfulness, justice, and law.—Deut. 7:9; 1 John 1:9.", "norm_zh": "三约有什么意义呢约是讲信义讲律法的约只能按信义公理律法而执行申七9约壹一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C What is the meaning of a covenant A covenant speaks of faithfulness and law a covenant can only be carried out according to faithfulness justice and lawDeut 79 1 John 19"}
{"zh": "四\t以神的肯受拘束而与人立约而言，约是神的恩典最高的表示—启四2~3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "D. As far as God's willingness to be bound in making a covenant with man is concerned, the covenant is the highest expression of God's grace.—Rev. 4:2-3.", "norm_zh": "四以神的肯受拘束而与人立约而言约是神的恩典最高的表示启四23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D As far as Gods willingness to be bound in making a covenant with man is concerned the covenant is the highest expression of Gods graceRev 423"}
{"zh": "贰\t神借着约向人表示祂的心意—创六、九：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "II. God expresses His heart to man through the covenant—Gen. 6, 9:", "norm_zh": "贰神借着约向人表示祂的心意创六九李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II God expresses His heart to man through the covenantGen 6 9"}
{"zh": "一\t神对人有一个好心意，人不懂，人不明白，神就给人一个约，使人有凭据可抓—九8~17、20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "A. God has a good intention toward man, but man does not know or understand it; therefore, God gives man a covenant so that he might have some evidence to cling to.—9:8-17, 20.", "norm_zh": "一神对人有一个好心意人不懂人不明白神就给人一个约使人有凭据可抓九81720李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God has a good intention toward man but man does not know or understand it therefore God gives man a covenant so that he might have some evidence to cling to9817 20"}
{"zh": "二\t神给人一个约，明明告诉人祂的心意是如何，好像把祂的心打开来给人看，人才能知道祂的心是如何—12~15节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "B. God gives man a covenant to show him clearly what His intention is, as if He is opening His heart for man to see, so that man can know what His heart is like.—vv. 12-15.", "norm_zh": "二神给人一个约明明告诉人祂的心意是如何好像把祂的心打开来给人看人才能知道祂的心是如何1215节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God gives man a covenant to show him clearly what His intention is as if He is opening His heart for man to see so that man can know what His heart is likevv 1215"}
{"zh": "叁\t神借着约扩充人信心的度量—十五4~6、9~21：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "III. Through the covenant God enlarges the measure of man's faith—15:4-6, 9-21:", "norm_zh": "叁神借着约扩充人信心的度量十五46921李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Through the covenant God enlarges the measure of mans faith1546 921"}
{"zh": "一\t神与亚伯拉罕立约，就是神扩充亚伯拉罕信心度量的方法；神不只应许亚伯拉罕要作，神并且与亚伯拉罕立约去作—8节与注1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "A. God's making a covenant with Abraham was God's way of enlarging the measure of Abraham's faith; God not only promised Abraham what He would do, but He also made a covenant with him to do it.—v. 8 and note 1.", "norm_zh": "一神与亚伯拉罕立约就是神扩充亚伯拉罕信心度量的方法神不只应许亚伯拉罕要作神并且与亚伯拉罕立约去作8节与注1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods making a covenant with Abraham was Gods way of enlarging the measure of Abrahams faith God not only promised Abraham what He would do but He also made a covenant with him to do itv 8 and note 1"}
{"zh": "二\t在这样一个约的坚固之下，亚伯拉罕信心的度量自然而然地扩充了—5、8~21节，来十一8~10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "B. By the strengthening of such a covenant, the measure of Abraham's faith was naturally enlarged.—vv. 5, 8-21; Heb. 11:8-10.", "norm_zh": "二在这样一个约的坚固之下亚伯拉罕信心的度量自然而然地扩充了5821节来十一810李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B By the strengthening of such a covenant the measure of Abrahams faith was naturally enlargedvv 5 821 Heb 11810"}
{"zh": "肆\t神借着约给人以凭据—撒下七4~16，诗八九19~37：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "IV. Through the Covenant God Gives Man a Pledge—2 Sam. 7:4-16; Psa. 89:19-37:", "norm_zh": "肆神借着约给人以凭据撒下七416诗八九1937李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Through the Covenant God Gives Man a Pledge2 Sam 7416 Psa 891937"}
{"zh": "一\t神所以与人立约，祂就是要人有胆量来问祂，要求祂按着正义成就祂约里所说的；神是受约的拘束的，神必须按着正义行事—20~28节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "A. The reason God makes a covenant with man is that man may become bold enough to inquire of Him and demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant according to righteousness; God is bound by the covenant; He must act according to righteousness.—vv. 20-28.", "norm_zh": "一神所以与人立约祂就是要人有胆量来问祂要求祂按着正义成就祂约里所说的神是受约的拘束的神必须按着正义行事2028节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The reason God makes a covenant with man is that man may become bold enough to inquire of Him and demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant according to righteousness God is bound by the covenant He must act according to righteousnessvv 2028"}
{"zh": "二\t神喜欢人按着约来亲近祂，祈求祂，甚至来问祂；神喜欢人要求祂履行祂在约里所应许的一切—49节，一四三1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "B. God delights that man draw near to Him, pray to Him, and even inquire of Him according to the covenant; God delights that man demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenant.—v. 49; 143:1.", "norm_zh": "二神喜欢人按着约来亲近祂祈求祂甚至来问祂神喜欢人要求祂履行祂在约里所应许的一切49节一四三1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God delights that man draw near to Him pray to Him and even inquire of Him according to the covenant God delights that man demand Him to fulfill what He has promised in the covenantv 49 1431"}
{"zh": "伍\t诗篇二十五篇十四节告诉我们说，“耶和华的秘密与敬畏祂的人同在，祂必将祂的约指示他们”：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "V. Psalm 25:14 tells us, \"The secret of Jehovah is with them that fear him, and he will show them his covenant\":", "norm_zh": "伍诗篇二十五篇十四节告诉我们说耶和华的秘密与敬畏祂的人同在祂必将祂的约指示他们李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Psalm 2514 tells us The secret of Jehovah is with them that fear him and he will show them his covenant"}
{"zh": "一\t如果没有神的启示，你仍旧没有能力，你仍旧抓不牢神的话；所以我们需要神在我们的灵里给我们一个指示—14节，林前二10，来十二28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "A. Unless God reveals it, you will still have no power; you still cannot hold fast God's word; therefore, God must show it to us in our spirit.—v. 14; 1 Cor. 2:10; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "一如果没有神的启示你仍旧没有能力你仍旧抓不牢神的话所以我们需要神在我们的灵里给我们一个指示14节林前二10来十二28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Unless God reveals it you will still have no power you still cannot hold fast Gods word therefore God must show it to us in our spiritv 14 1 Cor 210 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "二\t敬畏祂是什么意思呢？敬畏祂，就是尊祂为大，就是高举祂；一心寻求神的旨意，完全顺服神的旨意的人，就是敬畏祂的人—彼前一17，来十二28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第二章）", "en": "B. What does it mean to fear Him? To fear means to magnify, to exalt Him; a person who fears God is one who seeks God's will with a full heart, with the intention of completely submitting to God's way.—1 Pet. 1:17; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "二敬畏祂是什么意思呢敬畏祂就是尊祂为大就是高举祂一心寻求神的旨意完全顺服神的旨意的人就是敬畏祂的人彼前一17来十二28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B What does it mean to fear Him To fear means to magnify to exalt Him a person who fears God is one who seeks Gods will with a full heart with the intention of completely submitting to Gods way1 Pet 117 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "陆\t新约继承亚伯拉罕的约—加三5~9：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "VI. THE NEW COVENANT CONTINUES THE COVENANT OF ABRAHAM—Gal. 3:5-9:", "norm_zh": "陆新约继承亚伯拉罕的约加三59李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI THE NEW COVENANT CONTINUES THE COVENANT OF ABRAHAMGal 359"}
{"zh": "一\t新约是继承神与亚伯拉罕所立的约，新约是发挥亚伯拉罕的约的；加拉太第三章给我们看见，新约与亚伯拉罕的约是一个系统—6~9节：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "A. The new covenant is a continuation and development of the covenant God made with Abraham; Galatians 3 shows us that the new covenant and the covenant made with Abraham are of the same line.—vv. 6-9:", "norm_zh": "一新约是继承神与亚伯拉罕所立的约新约是发挥亚伯拉罕的约的加拉太第三章给我们看见新约与亚伯拉罕的约是一个系统69节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant is a continuation and development of the covenant God made with Abraham Galatians 3 shows us that the new covenant and the covenant made with Abraham are of the same linevv 69"}
{"zh": "1\t神与以色列人所立律法的约，虽然是在亚伯拉罕的约和新约之间，但是，律法是为过犯添上的，根本是外添的—加三，罗五。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "1. Between Abraham's covenant and the new covenant there is the covenant of law made with Israel. However, the law was added because of transgression; it is basically an addition—Gal. 3; Rom. 5.", "norm_zh": "1神与以色列人所立律法的约虽然是在亚伯拉罕的约和新约之间但是律法是为过犯添上的根本是外添的加三罗五李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Between Abrahams covenant and the new covenant there is the covenant of law made with Israel However the law was added because of transgression it is basically an additionGal 3 Rom 5"}
{"zh": "2\t惟有亚伯拉罕的约和新约，是本乎信，是本乎应许的，所以是一个系统—加三6~9，来八。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "2. Only the covenant made with Abraham and the new covenant are of faith and promise; for this reason, they are of the same line—Gal. 3:6-9; Heb. 8.", "norm_zh": "2惟有亚伯拉罕的约和新约是本乎信是本乎应许的所以是一个系统加三69来八李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Only the covenant made with Abraham and the new covenant are of faith and promise for this reason they are of the same lineGal 369 Heb 8"}
{"zh": "二\t希伯来八章七节说，“那前约若没有瑕疵，就无处寻求后约了”：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "B. Hebrews 8:7 says, \"For if that first covenant was faultless, no place would have been sought for a second\":", "norm_zh": "二希伯来八章七节说哪前约若没有瑕疵就无处寻求后约了李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Hebrews 87 says For if that first covenant was faultless no place would have been sought for a second"}
{"zh": "1\t律法只是要求人行善，律法并没有给人生命和能力去行善—罗八3，七7、12、15~17、24~25。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "1. The law requires man to do good, but it does not give man the life and power to do good—Rom. 8:3; 7:7, 12, 15-17, 24-25.", "norm_zh": "1律法只是要求人行善律法并没有给人生命和能力去行善罗八3七71215172425李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The law requires man to do good but it does not give man the life and power to do goodRom 83 77 12 1517 2425"}
{"zh": "2\t约版还没有拿下山，以色列人就已经背约了；这就是前约的瑕疵—出三二1~8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "2. Even before the tables of the covenant were brought down from the mountain, the children of Israel had become unfaithful to the covenant; this was the fault of the first covenant—Exo. 32:1-8.", "norm_zh": "2约版还没有拿下山以色列人就已经背约了这就是前约的瑕疵出三二18李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Even before the tables of the covenant were brought down from the mountain the children of Israel had become unfaithful to the covenant this was the fault of the first covenantExo 3218"}
{"zh": "3\t此后，以色列人也没有能遵守神的约；他们在旷野惹神发怒，试探神，并且观看神的作为有四十年之久—来三10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "3. After this, the children of Israel continued to fail in keeping God's covenant; they provoked God in the wilderness, tried Him by testing Him and saw His works forty years—Heb. 3:10.", "norm_zh": "3此后以色列人也没有能遵守神的约他们在旷野惹神发怒试探神并且观看神的作为有四十年之久来三10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 After this the children of Israel continued to fail in keeping Gods covenant they provoked God in the wilderness tried Him by testing Him and saw His works forty yearsHeb 310"}
{"zh": "4\t保罗的经历也告诉我们，律法的本身是属灵的，但是律法对于肉体有所不能行；这就是前约的瑕疵—罗八3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "4. Paul's experience also tells us that the law itself is spiritual, but the law could not perform, in that it was weak through the flesh; this, too, was the fault of the first covenant—Rom. 8:3.", "norm_zh": "4保罗的经历也告诉我们律法的本身是属灵的但是律法对于肉体有所不能行这就是前约的瑕疵罗八3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Pauls experience also tells us that the law itself is spiritual but the law could not perform in that it was weak through the flesh this too was the fault of the first covenantRom 83"}
{"zh": "柒\t新约是更美之约；新约，乃是凭着更美之应许立的—来八6，七22：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "VII. The new covenant is a better covenant; the new covenant is enacted upon better promises—Heb. 8:6; 7:22:", "norm_zh": "柒新约是更美之约新约乃是凭着更美之应许立的来八6七22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The new covenant is a better covenant the new covenant is enacted upon better promisesHeb 86 722"}
{"zh": "一\t新约，是把神的律法放在人的心意里面，写在人的心上的—八10，十16，耶三一33，参林后三3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "A. The new covenant imparts God's laws into man's mind and inscribes them upon man's heart—Heb. 8:10; 10:16; Jer. 31:33; cf. 2 Cor. 3:3:", "norm_zh": "一新约是把神的律法放在人的心意里面写在人的心上的八10十16耶三一33参林后三3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant imparts Gods laws into mans mind and inscribes them upon mans heartHeb 810 1016 Jer 3133 cf 2 Cor 33"}
{"zh": "1\t新约中，命令你的是神，叫你能遵行神的旨意的也是神—来八10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "1. In the new covenant, the One who demands of us is God, and the One who enables us to do the will of God is also God—Heb. 8:10.", "norm_zh": "1新约中命令你的是神叫你能遵行神的旨意的也是神来八10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In the new covenant the One who demands of us is God and the One who enables us to do the will of God is also GodHeb 810"}
{"zh": "2\t新约，是神给你生命和能力，叫你能行神所要你行的善，叫神能作你的神，叫你也能作神的子民—八章，多二。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "2. The new covenant is a covenant in which God gives you life and power to do the good He intends you to do, so that He may be your God and you may be His people—Heb. 8; Titus 2.", "norm_zh": "2新约是神给你生命和能力叫你能行神所要你行的善叫神能作你的神叫你也能作神的子民八章多二李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The new covenant is a covenant in which God gives you life and power to do the good He intends you to do so that He may be your God and you may be His peopleHeb 8 Titus 2"}
{"zh": "3\t新约，能叫人决不用人的教导而在里面更深地认识神—来八10~11，约壹二27，参约十四23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "3. The new covenant enables man to know God more deeply and in an inward way, without being taught by his fellow citizen—Heb. 8:10-11; 1 John 2:27; cf. John 14:23.", "norm_zh": "3新约能叫人决不用人的教导而在里面更深地认识神来八1011约壹二27参约十四23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The new covenant enables man to know God more deeply and in an inward way without being taught by his fellow citizenHeb 81011 1 John 227 cf John 1423"}
{"zh": "二\t新约里有神的应许和事实—来六13~18：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "B. THE NEW COVENANT INCLUDES GOD'S PROMISES AND GOD'S FACTS—Heb. 6:13-18:", "norm_zh": "二新约里有神的应许和事实来六1318李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B THE NEW COVENANT INCLUDES GODS PROMISES AND GODS FACTSHeb 61318"}
{"zh": "1\t约是神的应许必要成就的保证；我们不能说，所有神的应许都是神的约；但是我们敢说，所有神的约都有神的应许—15~16节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "1. A covenant is the guarantee that God's promise will definitely be fulfilled; we cannot say that all of God's promises are His covenants, but we dare to say that all of God's covenants include His promises—vv. 15-16.", "norm_zh": "1约是神的应许必要成就的保证我们不能说所有神的应许都是神的约但是我们敢说所有神的约都有神的应许1516节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A covenant is the guarantee that Gods promise will definitely be fulfilled we cannot say that all of Gods promises are His covenants but we dare to say that all of Gods covenants include His promisesvv 1516"}
{"zh": "2\t新约所以是更美之约，就是因为这约是凭更美之应许立的—八6，七22，九23，十二24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "2. The new covenant is a better covenant because it is enacted upon better promises—Heb. 8:6; 7:22; 9:23; 12:24.", "norm_zh": "2新约所以是更美之约就是因为这约是凭更美之应许立的八6七22九23十二24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The new covenant is a better covenant because it is enacted upon better promisesHeb 86 722 923 1224"}
{"zh": "3\t神的约里不只有应许，也有遗命；遗命就是有所遗留，有遗物，有遗产；所遗留的东西就是事实—九15~18。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "3. In God's covenant there is not only the promise, but also the testament; a testament, or will, indicates that there is an estate, a bequest; the things bequeathed are the facts—Heb. 9:15-18.", "norm_zh": "3神的约里不只有应许也有遗命遗命就是有所遗留有遗物有遗产所遗留的东西就是事实九1518李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In Gods covenant there is not only the promise but also the testament a testament or will indicates that there is an estate a bequest the things bequeathed are the factsHeb 91518"}
{"zh": "捌\t新约的时代—耶三一31~32，太二六26~30：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "VIII. THE AGE OF THE NEW COVENANT—Jer. 31:31-32; Matt. 26:26-30:", "norm_zh": "捌新约的时代耶三一3132太二六2630李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII THE AGE OF THE NEW COVENANTJer 313132 Matt 262630"}
{"zh": "一\t神与什么人立新约；神立新约，不是与外邦人立的，乃是与以色列家和犹大家立的—耶三一31~32，来八8~12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "A. With Whom God Made the New Covenant; God Made the New Covenant, Not with the Gentiles, but with the Houses of Israel and Judah—Jer. 31:31-32; Heb. 8:8-12.", "norm_zh": "一神与什么人立新约神立新约不是与外邦人立的乃是与以色列家和犹大家立的耶三一3132来八812李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A With Whom God Made the New Covenant God Made the New Covenant Not with the Gentiles but with the Houses of Israel and JudahJer 313132 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "二\t神在什么时候立新约；我们相信是指千禧年开始的时候说的—耶三一31~33，来八8~12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "B. When God Made the New Covenant; We Believe That It Refers to the Beginning of the Millennium—Jer. 31:31-33; Heb. 8:8-12.", "norm_zh": "二神在什么时候立新约我们相信是指千禧年开始的时候说的耶三一3133来八812李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When God Made the New Covenant We Believe That It Refers to the Beginning of the MillenniumJer 313133 Heb 8812"}
{"zh": "三\t今天怎么是新约的时代；主耶稣在被卖的那夜，“拿起杯来，祝谢了，递给他们，说，你们都喝这个，因为这是我立新约的血……”—太二六26~30：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "C. Why Today Is the New Covenant Age; In the Night the Lord Jesus Was Betrayed, \"taking the cup and giving thanks, He gave it to them, saying, Drink of it, all of you; for this is My blood of the new (lit.) covenant ...\"—Matt. 26:26-30:", "norm_zh": "三今天怎么是新约的时代主耶稣在被卖的哪夜拿起杯来祝谢了递给他们说你们都喝这个因为这是我立新约的血太二六2630李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Why Today Is the New Covenant Age In the Night the Lord Jesus Was Betrayed taking the cup and giving thanks He gave it to them saying Drink of it all of you for this is My blood of the new lit covenant Matt 262630"}
{"zh": "1\t因主莫大的恩典，这新约应用到所有蒙恩的人身上来了—28节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "1. Because of the Lord's exceeding grace, the new covenant applies to all those who are found by grace.—v. 28.", "norm_zh": "1因主莫大的恩典这新约应用到所有蒙恩的人身上来了28节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Because of the Lords exceeding grace the new covenant applies to all those who are found by gracev 28"}
{"zh": "2\t从祂受死那天起，新约就设立起来了；这是主的大恩典，使我们能以预享新约的福—26~29节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "2.\tFrom the day He died, the new covenant was established; this is the Lord's great grace, so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenant—vv. 26-29.", "norm_zh": "2从祂受死哪天起新约就设立起来了这是主的大恩典使我们能以预享新约的福2629节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 From the day He died the new covenant was established this is the Lords great grace so that we may have a foretaste of the blessing of the new covenantvv 2629"}
{"zh": "3\t主是以新约的原则建造我们，以新约的福赐给我们—参加三14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "3.\tThe Lord is building us up today by the principle of the new covenant and blessing us with the blessing of the new covenant—cf. Gal. 3:14.", "norm_zh": "3主是以新约的原则建造我们以新约的福赐给我们参加三14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Lord is building us up today by the principle of the new covenant and blessing us with the blessing of the new covenantcf Gal 314"}
{"zh": "4\t祂的血不只解决了罪的问题，祂的血也立了新约；所以，这一个时代诚然是新约的时代！—太二六28，路二二20，来九15，十二24，林前十一25。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "4.\tHis blood not only solved the problem of sin, but also established the new covenant; therefore, this age is truly the new covenant age!—Matt. 26:28; Luke 22:20; Heb. 9:15; 12:24; 1 Cor. 11:25.", "norm_zh": "4祂的血不只解决了罪的问提祂的血也立了新约所以这一个时代诚然是新约的时代太二六28路二二20来九15十二24林前十一25李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 His blood not only solved the problem of sin but also established the new covenant therefore this age is truly the new covenant ageMatt 2628 Luke 2220 Heb 915 1224 1 Cor 1125"}
{"zh": "玖\t新约的内容；新约包含了三大部分—来八10~12：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "IX.\tThe content of the new covenant; the new covenant includes three parts—Heb. 8:10-12:", "norm_zh": "玖新约的内容新约包含了三大部分来八1012李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The content of the new covenant the new covenant includes three partsHeb 81012"}
{"zh": "一\t神把律法放在人的心意里面，写在人的心上；神作了他们的神，他们作了神的子民；这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合—10节，罗八2。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "A.\tGod imparts His laws into man's mind and inscribes them upon man's heart; God becomes their God, and they become God's people; this means that God Himself enters into man to be one with man—v. 10; Rom. 8:2.", "norm_zh": "一神把律法放在人的心意里面写在人的心上神作了他们的神他们作了神的子民这就是神自己进到人里面与人联合10节罗八2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God imparts His laws into mans mind and inscribes them upon mans heart God becomes their God and they become Gods people this means that God Himself enters into man to be one with manv 10 Rom 82"}
{"zh": "二\t这律法在人的里面，叫人决不用人的教导而认识神；这是里面地认识神—来八11，约壹二27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "B.\tThese laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others; this is the inward knowledge of God—Heb. 8:11; 1 John 2:27.", "norm_zh": "二这律法在人的里面叫人决不用人的教导而认识神这是里面地认识神来八11约壹二27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B These laws which are within man enable man to know God without the teaching of others this is the inward knowledge of GodHeb 811 1 John 227"}
{"zh": "三\t神要宽恕人的不义，也不再记念人的罪愆；这是赦罪—来八12，十17，参二17，约壹二2。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第三章）", "en": "C.\tGod will make propitiation for man's unrighteousnesses; neither will He remember man's sins; this is forgiveness—Heb. 8:12; 10:17; cf. 2:17; 1 John 2:2.", "norm_zh": "三神要宽恕人的不义也不再记念人的罪愆这是赦罪来八12十17参二17约壹二2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T03:59:03.755310+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God will make propitiation for mans unrighteousnesses neither will He remember mans sins this is forgivenessHeb 812 1017 cf 217 1 John 22"}
{"zh": "读经：来九15~17，八6，十二24，十三20，林前十一23~26，太二六28，路二二19~20", "en": "Scripture Reading: Heb. 9:15-17; 8:6; 12:24; 13:20; 1 Cor. 11:23-26; Matt. 26:28; Luke 22:19-20", "norm_zh": "读经来九1517八6十二24十三20林前十一2326太二六28路二二1920", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Heb 91517 86 1224 1320 1 Cor 112326 Matt 2628 Luke 221920"}
{"zh": "壹\t新约是“约”也是“遗命”—来九15~18：", "en": "I. The New Covenant Is a Covenant and Also a Testament—Heb. 9:15-18:", "norm_zh": "壹新约是约也是遗命来九1518", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The New Covenant Is a Covenant and Also a TestamentHeb 91518"}
{"zh": "一\t与我们立约的是神，神是站在我们对方的；成功这约的是主，因这约是用主的血立的—八8，九12。", "en": "A. God is the covenanting party who stands opposite to us; it is the Lord who has accomplished the covenant, for this covenant was made with the Lord's blood—8:8; 9:12.", "norm_zh": "一与我们立约的是神神是站在我们对方的成功这约的是主因这约是用主的血立的八8九12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God is the covenanting party who stands opposite to us it is the Lord who has accomplished the covenant for this covenant was made with the Lords blood88 912"}
{"zh": "二\t从神那一方面来说，神与我们立约，所以是约；从主耶稣这一方面来说，是祂死了所留下给我们永远的产业，所以是遗命—九1~28。", "en": "B. As far as God is concerned, He made a covenant with us, so it is a covenant; as far as the Lord Jesus is concerned, it was through His death that He bequeathed an eternal inheritance to us, so it is a testament—9:1-28.", "norm_zh": "二从神哪一方面来说神与我们立约所以是约从主耶稣这一方面来说是祂死了所留下给我们永远的产业所以是遗命九128", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B As far as God is concerned He made a covenant with us so it is a covenant as far as the Lord Jesus is concerned it was through His death that He bequeathed an eternal inheritance to us so it is a testament9128"}
{"zh": "三\t“约”，不必本人死才生效；但“遗命”，必须等到留遗命的人死了才生效—16~17节。", "en": "C. For a covenant to become effective, the death of the covenanting one is not required, but for a testament to become effective, the death of the testator is required—vv. 16-17.", "norm_zh": "三约不必本人死才生效但遗命必须等到留遗命的人死了才生效1617节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C For a covenant to become effective the death of the covenanting one is not required but for a testament to become effective the death of the testator is requiredvv 1617"}
{"zh": "贰\t主耶稣是留遗命的人—林前十一23~26：", "en": "II. THE LORD JESUS BEING THE TESTATOR—1 Cor. 11:23-26:", "norm_zh": "贰主耶稣是留遗命的人林前十一2326", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II THE LORD JESUS BEING THE TESTATOR1 Cor 112326"}
{"zh": "一\t这“新约”就是耶利米书所说的那一个最荣耀的新约，现在因主耶稣的血，竟然叫这约成为我们所得的产业，叫我们能以享受其中所说的一切了！—来九15~17。", "en": "A. The new covenant here is the very glorious new covenant mentioned in the book of Jeremiah. Now, through the blood of the Lord Jesus, this covenant has become our inheritance so that we can enjoy all its contents.—Heb. 9:15-17.", "norm_zh": "一这新约就是耶利米书所说的哪一个最荣耀的新约现在因主耶稣的血竟然叫这约成为我们所得的产业叫我们能以享受其中所说的一切了来九1517", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant here is the very glorious new covenant mentioned in the book of Jeremiah Now through the blood of the Lord Jesus this covenant has become our inheritance so that we can enjoy all its contentsHeb 91517"}
{"zh": "二\t凡从遗命有所得着的，就是他所得着的不是他本来所有的，不是他自己作工得来的，乃是主耶稣所遗留给他的—路二二20，来九16~17。", "en": "B. When we inherit something through a will, we receive what we did not originally possess. Through the new covenant we received something which we did not work for, but which has been bequeathed to us by the Lord Jesus.—Luke 22:20; Heb. 9:16-17.", "norm_zh": "二凡从遗命有所得着的就是他所得着的不是他本来所有的不是他自己作工得来的乃是主耶稣所遗留给他的路二二20来九1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we inherit something through a will we receive what we did not originally possess Through the new covenant we received something which we did not work for but which has been bequeathed to us by the Lord JesusLuke 2220 Heb 91617"}
{"zh": "叁\t主耶稣是执行遗命的人—15节，八6，十二24：", "en": "III. THE LORD JESUS BEING THE EXECUTOR OF THE TESTAMENT—v. 15; 8:6; 12:24:", "norm_zh": "叁主耶稣是执行遗命的人15节八6十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III THE LORD JESUS BEING THE EXECUTOR OF THE TESTAMENTv 15 86 1224"}
{"zh": "一\t按着死来说，留遗命的是主耶稣；按着复活来说，执行遗命的也是主耶稣—九14~15节。", "en": "A. As far as death is concerned, the Lord Jesus is the Testator; but as far as resurrection is concerned, He is the Executor of the will.—9:14-15.", "norm_zh": "一按着死来说留遗命的是主耶稣按着复活来说执行遗命的也是主耶稣九1415节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As far as death is concerned the Lord Jesus is the Testator but as far as resurrection is concerned He is the Executor of the will91415"}
{"zh": "二\t主耶稣把血带进圣所，说明留遗命的人已经死了；主耶稣在天上作新约的中保，说明祂是有能力执行遗命的人—15、24节。", "en": "B. The Lord Jesus brought the blood into the Holy of Holies, indicating that the Testator had died; the Lord Jesus is the Mediator of the new covenant in the heavens, indicating that He is the One who has the power to execute the testament.—vv. 15, 24.", "norm_zh": "二主耶稣把血带进圣所说明留遗命的人已经死了主耶稣在天上作新约的中保说明祂是有能力执行遗命的人1524节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Lord Jesus brought the blood into the Holy of Holies indicating that the Testator had died the Lord Jesus is the Mediator of the new covenant in the heavens indicating that He is the One who has the power to execute the testamentvv 15 24"}
{"zh": "三\t主在天上，祂不只作大祭司，祂也作中保，就是作约的“执行者”，叫新约在我们身上有效力—11、15节，十二22~24。", "en": "C. In the heavens the Lord is not only the High Priest, but also the Mediator, the Executor, of the new covenant, so that it may become effective in us.—vv. 11, 15; 12:22-24.", "norm_zh": "三主在天上祂不只作大祭司祂也作中保就是作约的执行者叫新约在我们身上有效力1115节十二2224", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the heavens the Lord is not only the High Priest but also the Mediator the Executor of the new covenant so that it may become effective in usvv 11 15 122224"}
{"zh": "四\t按神的信实和公义说，这约，是永不能背、永不能废的；按主复活的能力来说，这约是永远有效力的—九25~28。", "en": "D. According to God's faithfulness and righteousness, this covenant is inviolable and irrevocable; according to the Lord's resurrection power, this covenant is forever effective.—9:25-28.", "norm_zh": "四按神的信实和公义说这约是永不能背永不能废的按主复活的能力来说这约是永远有效力的九2528", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D According to Gods faithfulness and righteousness this covenant is inviolable and irrevocable according to the Lords resurrection power this covenant is forever effective92528"}
{"zh": "肆\t“凡有遗命，必须等到留遗命的人死了；因为人死了，遗命才有效力……”—16~17节：", "en": "IV. \"Where there is a testament there must of necessity be the death of him who made it. For a testament is confirmed where there has been death, since it has no force when he who made it is living...\"—vv. 16-17:", "norm_zh": "肆凡有遗命必须等到留遗命的人死了因为人死了遗命才有效力1617节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Where there is a testament there must of necessity be the death of him who made it For a testament is confirmed where there has been death since it has no force when he who made it is livingvv 1617"}
{"zh": "一\t我们每逢吃这饼，喝这杯的时候，就是宣告主已经死了；留遗命的人已经死了，现在遗命有效力了！我们的主，是负责的执行者，我们必定能得着遗命里所有的一切—路二二19~20，来九15~17。", "en": "A. Whenever we eat the bread and drink the cup, we declare that the Lord has died; the Testator has died, and now the testament, the will, has become effective! Since our Lord is a responsible Executor, we shall receive all the bequests in the testament.—Luke 22:19-20; Heb. 9:15-17.", "norm_zh": "一我们每逢吃这饼喝这杯的时候就是宣告主已经死了留遗命的人已经死了现在遗命有效力了我们的主是负责的执行者我们必定能得着遗命里所有的一切路二二1920来九1517", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Whenever we eat the bread and drink the cup we declare that the Lord has died the Testator has died and now the testament the will has become effective Since our Lord is a responsible Executor we shall receive all the bequests in the testamentLuke 221920 Heb 91517"}
{"zh": "二\t我们的主所遗留给我们的，有三大部分，就是洁净（罪得赦免后的洁净），生命和能力，以及更深地认识神；这三部分包括我们灵性生活一切的需要；我们应当用信心来取用遗命里所有的一切——八10~12，十19~23。", "en": "B. What our Lord has bequeathed to us includes three major parts: cleansing (cleansing which comes through the forgiveness of sins), life and power, and a deeper knowledge of God; these three parts comprise all the needs of our spiritual life; we should receive by faith all that is included in the testament.—8:10-12; 10:19-23.", "norm_zh": "二我们的主所遗留给我们的有三大部分就是洁净罪得赦免后的洁净生命和能力以及更深地认识神这三部分包括我们灵性生活一切的需要我们应当用信心来取用遗命里所有的一切八1012十1923", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B What our Lord has bequeathed to us includes three major parts cleansing cleansing which comes through the forgiveness of sins life and power and a deeper knowledge of God these three parts comprise all the needs of our spiritual life we should receive by faith all that is included in the testament81012 101923"}
{"zh": "三\t所以我们每逢喝的时候，我们所看见的不是物质的葡萄汁或者葡萄酒，而是主用血所立的新约；主要我们长久地记得，新约所包括的一切，是我们可以长久享受的—路二二18~20，林前十一26。", "en": "C. Therefore, when we drink, what we see is not the grape juice or the wine itself, but a new covenant which the Lord established with His blood; the Lord wants us to remember that we can enjoy constantly all that is included in the new covenant.—Luke 22:18-20; 1 Cor. 11:26.", "norm_zh": "三所以我们每逢喝的时候我们所看见的不是物质的葡萄汁或者葡萄酒而是主用血所立的新约主要我们长久地记得新约所包括的一切是我们可以长久享受的路二二1820林前十一26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Therefore when we drink what we see is not the grape juice or the wine itself but a new covenant which the Lord established with His blood the Lord wants us to remember that we can enjoy constantly all that is included in the new covenantLuke 221820 1 Cor 1126"}
{"zh": "伍\t新约的稳妥；新约是用血立的，所以新约是可靠的，是稳妥的—太二六28，来十三20：", "en": "V. The security of the new covenant; the new covenant was established through the blood; therefore, the new covenant is dependable; it is secure.—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 13:20:", "norm_zh": "伍新约的稳妥新约是用血立的所以新约是可靠的是稳妥的太二六28来十三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The security of the new covenant the new covenant was established through the blood therefore the new covenant is dependable it is secureMatt 2628 Heb 1320"}
{"zh": "一\t新约，为什么必须用血来立呢？为什么用血立的约才有功效呢？—罗五12~14：", "en": "A. Why must the new covenant be established through the blood? Why is a covenant effective only when it is established with the blood?—Rom. 5:12-14:", "norm_zh": "一新约为什么必须用血来立呢为什么用血立的约才有功效呢罗五1214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Why must the new covenant be established through the blood Why is a covenant effective only when it is established with the bloodRom 51214"}
{"zh": "1\t当基督还没有来到地上的时候，我们人受到两个大亏损：第一个是因亚当犯罪而受的亏损，第二个是因我们不能遵行神的律法而受的亏损—13节。", "en": "1. Before Christ came to the earth, man suffered two great losses: first, he suffered because of Adam's sin, and second, he suffered because he could not keep God's law.—v. 13.", "norm_zh": "1当基督还没有来到地上的时候我们人受到两个大亏损第一个是因亚当犯罪而受的亏损第二个是因我们不能遵行神的律法而受的亏损13节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Before Christ came to the earth man suffered two great losses first he suffered because of Adams sin and second he suffered because he could not keep Gods lawv 13"}
{"zh": "2\t从亚当到摩西，死作了王；从摩西到基督，不只死作了王，并且罪也作了王；但是，感谢神，主耶稣的流血却替我们解决了这两个问题—15~21节。", "en": "2. From Adam to Moses death reigned, and from Moses to Christ not only did death reign, but sin also reigned; but praise God, the blood of the Lord Jesus has solved these two problems for us!—vv. 15-21.", "norm_zh": "2从亚当到摩西死作了王从摩西到基督不只死作了王并且罪也作了王但是感谢神主耶稣的流血却替我们解决了这两个问提1521节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 From Adam to Moses death reigned and from Moses to Christ not only did death reign but sin also reigned but praise God the blood of the Lord Jesus has solved these two problems for usvv 1521"}
{"zh": "3\t主耶稣的血洗净了我们的罪，并且也恢复了我们与神的关系；主耶稣的血不只叫我们与神和好，也是把神自己给我们了—弗二5~6，西20、22。", "en": "3. The blood of the Lord Jesus cleanses us from our sins and has also restored our relationship with God; the blood of the Lord Jesus not only reconciled us to God but also brings God Himself to us.—Eph. 2:5-6; Col. 1:20, 22.", "norm_zh": "3主耶稣的血洗净了我们的罪并且也恢复了我们与神的关系主耶稣的血不只叫我们与神和好也是把神自己给我们了弗二56西2022", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The blood of the Lord Jesus cleanses us from our sins and has also restored our relationship with God the blood of the Lord Jesus not only reconciled us to God but also brings God Himself to usEph 256 Col 120 22"}
{"zh": "4\t基督的血不只是成功了救赎，并且是成功了永远的救赎；基督用自己的血，只一次进入圣所，成了永远赎罪的事—来九12。", "en": "4. The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption; it also accomplished an eternal redemption; Christ, through His own blood entered once for all into the Holy of Holies, having found an eternal redemption.—Heb. 9:12.", "norm_zh": "4基督的血不只是成功了救赎并且是成功了永远的救赎基督用自己的血只一次进入圣所成了永远赎罪的事来九12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption it also accomplished an eternal redemption Christ through His own blood entered once for all into the Holy of Holies having found an eternal redemptionHeb 912"}
{"zh": "5\t主的血一面是为赎罪而流，在消极方面，除去了那些害我们的；一面是为立新约而流，在积极方面，恢复了我们所已经失去的产业，并赐给了我们新的东西；所以，主的血不只是为赎罪，也是为恢复—14~15节。", "en": "5. On one hand the Lord's blood was shed for redemption; on the negative side, it removes those things which damage us; on the other hand His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant; on the positive side, it restores the inheritance we have lost and also gives us new things; therefore, the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restoration.—vv. 14-15.", "norm_zh": "5主的血一面是为赎罪而流在消极方面除去了哪些害我们的一面是为立新约而流在积极方面恢复了我们所已经失去的产业并赐给了我们新的东西所以主的血不只是为赎罪也是为恢复1415节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 On one hand the Lords blood was shed for redemption on the negative side it removes those things which damage us on the other hand His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant on the positive side it restores the inheritance we have lost and also gives us new things therefore the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restorationvv 1415"}
{"zh": "二\t血是根基，约是字据；血是立约的根基，约是用血立的字据—九12~14：", "en": "B. The blood is the base while the covenant is the contract, the writing; the blood is the base upon which the covenant is established, while the covenant is the contract established with the blood.—9:12-14:", "norm_zh": "二血是根基约是字据血是立约的根基约是用血立的字据九1214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The blood is the base while the covenant is the contract the writing the blood is the base upon which the covenant is established while the covenant is the contract established with the blood91214"}
{"zh": "1\t我们就凭着这用主耶稣的血所立的新约，来承受神所给我们的属灵的产业—十三20。", "en": "1. It is by this new covenant, established with the blood of the Lord Jesus, that we receive the spiritual inheritance which God has given us.—13:20.", "norm_zh": "1我们就凭着这用主耶稣的血所立的新约来承受神所给我们的属灵的产业十三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 It is by this new covenant established with the blood of the Lord Jesus that we receive the spiritual inheritance which God has given us1320"}
{"zh": "2\t所以新约是一绝对合法的事件，是完全按着神公义的手续立的；是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据—九22。", "en": "2. Therefore, the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter, established fully according to God's righteous procedures; it is a document established for us by God through the blood of Christ.—9:22.", "norm_zh": "2所以新约是一绝对合法的事件是完全按着神公义的手续立的是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据九22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Therefore the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter established fully according to Gods righteous procedures it is a document established for us by God through the blood of Christ922"}
{"zh": "3\t感谢神，祂不只有恩典，祂并且将祂的恩典借着一个约表明出来—出二四8，来九20：", "en": "3. Praise God! He not only has grace, but He expresses His grace through a covenant.—Exo. 24:8; Heb. 9:20:", "norm_zh": "3感谢神祂不只有恩典祂并且将祂的恩典借着一个约表明出来出二四8来九20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Praise God He not only has grace but He expresses His grace through a covenantExo 248 Heb 920"}
{"zh": "a\t我们所得的是神的恩典，但神是用血与我们立约，叫我们凭着约求神按着祂的公义待我们；我们是站在恩典的地位上的，但是，恩典是借着义通到我们身上的——太二六28，罗五21。", "en": "a. What we receive is God's grace, but God has used the blood to make a covenant with us, so that through the covenant we may ask God to deal with us according to His righteousness; we stand upon the ground of grace, but grace comes to us through righteousness.—Matt. 26:28; Rom. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "a我们所得的是神的恩典但神是用血与我们立约叫我们凭着约求神按着祂的公义待我们我们是站在恩典的地位上的但是恩典是借着义通到我们身上的太二六28罗五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a What we receive is Gods grace but God has used the blood to make a covenant with us so that through the covenant we may ask God to deal with us according to His righteousness we stand upon the ground of grace but grace comes to us through righteousnessMatt 2628 Rom 521"}
{"zh": "b\t我们是站在血的根基，公义的根基上与神来往，神就不能不把约里所有的一切成就在我们身上—来九20。", "en": "b. We are standing upon the foundation of the blood, the foundation of righteousness, to deal with God; therefore, God has no choice but to fulfill in us all that is in the covenant.—Heb. 9:20.", "norm_zh": "b我们是站在血的根基公义的根基上与神来往神就不能不把约里所有的一切成就在我们身上来九20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We are standing upon the foundation of the blood the foundation of righteousness to deal with God therefore God has no choice but to fulfill in us all that is in the covenantHeb 920"}
{"zh": "4\t基督徒的生活没有别的，就是抓住神的话语而生活，就是相信神是信实的，是公义的—约壹一9。", "en": "4. The Christian's life has no other secret than living by holding on to God's Word, believing that God is faithful and righteous.—1 John 1:9.", "norm_zh": "4基督徒的生活没有别的就是抓住神的话语而生活就是相信神是信实的是公义的约壹一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The Christians life has no other secret than living by holding on to Gods Word believing that God is faithful and righteous1 John 19"}
{"zh": "5\t立新约的血，把我们的罪的问题解决了，也使神能把天上各样属灵的福气，一切关乎生命和敬虔的事都赐给我们；凡新约里所载明的，都是我们因血所当得的福气—弗二11~13，彼后一3。", "en": "5. The blood of the new covenant solves the problem of our sins and enables God to give us all spiritual blessings in the heavenlies, and all things that pertain to life and godliness; all of the things that are clearly written in the new covenant are our rightful blessings through the blood.—Eph. 2:11-13; 2 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "5立新约的血把我们的罪的问提解决了也使神能把天上各样属灵的福气一切关乎生命和敬虔的事都赐给我们凡新约里所载明的都是我们因血所当得的福气弗二1113彼后一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 The blood of the new covenant solves the problem of our sins and enables God to give us all spiritual blessings in the heavenlies and all things that pertain to life and godliness all of the things that are clearly written in the new covenant are our rightful blessings through the bloodEph 21113 2 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "6\t所以，我们凭着约求，不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西，乃是把本是属乎我们的东西，好像是寄存在神那里的东西领回来—彼前一3~5。", "en": "6. Therefore, when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us. Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us.—1 Pet. 1:3-5.", "norm_zh": "6所以我们凭着约求不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西乃是把本是属乎我们的东西好像是寄存在神哪里的东西领回来彼前一35", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Therefore when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us1 Pet 135"}
{"zh": "三\t希伯来十三章二十至二十一节，这是一个信心的祷告，也是圣经中一个大的祷告：", "en": "C. Hebrews 13:20-21—this is a prayer of faith, and it is also a great prayer in the Scriptures:", "norm_zh": "三希伯来十三章二十至二十一节这是一个信心的祷告也是圣经中一个大的祷告", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Hebrews 132021this is a prayer of faith and it is also a great prayer in the Scriptures"}
{"zh": "1\t他要神凭永约之血，叫从死里复活的耶稣基督，住在我们里面，使我们能遵行神的旨意，行神所喜悦的事—21节，十二28。", "en": "1. The writer of Hebrews asked God, through the blood of the eternal covenant, to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us, so that we may do God's will and accomplish the things well-pleasing to Him.—v. 21; 12:28.", "norm_zh": "1他要神凭永约之血叫从死里复活的耶稣基督住在我们里面使我们能遵行神的旨意行神所喜悦的事21节十二28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The writer of Hebrews asked God through the blood of the eternal covenant to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us so that we may do Gods will and accomplish the things wellpleasing to Himv 21 1228"}
{"zh": "2\t一个有信心的祷告，一个大的祷告，就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告—十三20。", "en": "2. A prayer with faith, a great prayer, is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lord's blood.—13:20.", "norm_zh": "2一个有信心的祷告一个大的祷告就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告十三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 A prayer with faith a great prayer is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lords blood1320"}
{"zh": "新约的稳妥", "en": "The Security of the New Covenant", "norm_zh": "新约的稳妥", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Security of the New Covenant"}
{"zh": "基督的血不只是成功了救赎，并且是成功了永远的救赎。旧约时代的人所靠的牛羊的血，是叫人每年想起罪来；基督用自己的血，只一次进入圣所，成了永远赎罪的事。基督的血，洗净了我们的良心，我们就不再有罪的控告了。感谢神，基督的血，永远地、完全地解决了罪的问题。", "en": "The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption; it also accomplished an eternal redemption. The blood of bulls and goats, upon which the people of the Old Testament depended, only reminded them of sin every year; but Christ, through His own blood, entered once for all into the Holy of Holies, having found an eternal redemption. The blood of Christ purifies our conscience so that we no longer have any \"conscience of sins.\" Praise God, the blood of Christ eternally and completely solves the problem of sin!", "norm_zh": "基督的血不只是成功了救赎并且是成功了永远的救赎旧约时代的人所靠的牛羊的血是叫人每年想起罪来基督用自己的血只一次进入圣所成了永远赎罪的事基督的血洗净了我们的良心我们就不再有罪的控告了感谢神基督的血永远地完全地解决了罪的问提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption it also accomplished an eternal redemption The blood of bulls and goats upon which the people of the Old Testament depended only reminded them of sin every year but Christ through His own blood entered once for all into the Holy of Holies having found an eternal redemption The blood of Christ purifies our conscience so that we no longer have any conscience of sins Praise God the blood of Christ eternally and completely solves the problem of sin"}
{"zh": "基督的血，叫我们的罪得着赦免，我们知道这一个，已经是够荣耀的事。凡是感觉罪的羞耻，知道罪的可恨的人都知道这个。我们感谢神，主耶稣的血不只为我们解决了罪和死的问题，并且恢复了我们所已经失去的产业，也把我们从前所没有的给我们。这血作了一件最奇妙的事，就是叫我们得着神。主耶稣的血不只赎罪，叫我们不受罪的报应，也把我们从伊甸园里所失去的完全恢复过来，并且把新的东西给我们。主说，“这杯是用我血所立的新约”（路二二）。主的血一面是为赎罪而流，在消极方面，除去了那些害我们的；一面是为立新约而流，在积极方面，恢复了我们所已经失去的产业，并赐给了我们新的东西。所以，主的血不只是为赎罪，也是为恢复。把我们所失去的恢复过来，并且把我们从前所没有的，加给我们。", "en": "The blood of Christ enables us to receive the forgiveness of sin. Just to realize this much is a most glorious thing. Those who sense the shamefulness of sin and know how hateful sin is, all realize this. But we praise God that the blood of the Lord Jesus not only solves the problem of sin and death, but it also restores the inheritance we have lost and brings us what we did not have in the past. This blood has done a most wonderful thing: it has enabled us to obtain God. The blood of the Lord Jesus not only redeems from sin so that we will not suffer its consequences, but also completely restores what we lost in the Garden of Eden and adds new things as well. The Lord Jesus said, \"This cup is the new covenant in my blood\" (Luke 22:20). On one hand the Lord's blood was shed for redemption. It removes on the negative side those things which damage us. On the other hand His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant. It restores on the positive side the inheritance we have lost and also gives us new things. Therefore, the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restoration, restoring what we have lost and bringing that which we did not have in the past.", "norm_zh": "基督的血叫我们的罪得着赦免我们知道这一个已经是够荣耀的事凡是感觉罪的羞耻知道罪的可恨的人都知道这个我们感谢神主耶稣的血不只为我们解决了罪和死的问提并且恢复了我们所已经失去的产业也把我们从前所没有的给我们这血作了一件最奇妙的事就是叫我们得着神主耶稣的血不只赎罪叫我们不受罪的报应也把我们从伊甸园里所失去的完全恢复过来并且把新的东西给我们主说这杯是用我血所立的新约路二二主的血一面是为赎罪而流在消极方面除去了哪些害我们的一面是为立新约而流在积极方面恢复了我们所已经失去的产业并赐给了我们新的东西所以主的血不只是为赎罪也是为恢复把我们所失去的恢复过来并且把我们从前所没有的加给我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The blood of Christ enables us to receive the forgiveness of sin Just to realize this much is a most glorious thing Those who sense the shamefulness of sin and know how hateful sin is all realize this But we praise God that the blood of the Lord Jesus not only solves the problem of sin and death but it also restores the inheritance we have lost and brings us what we did not have in the past This blood has done a most wonderful thing it has enabled us to obtain God The blood of the Lord Jesus not only redeems from sin so that we will not suffer its consequences but also completely restores what we lost in the Garden of Eden and adds new things as well The Lord Jesus said This cup is the new covenant in my blood Luke 2220 On one hand the Lords blood was shed for redemption It removes on the negative side those things which damage us On the other hand His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant It restores on the positive side the inheritance we have lost and also gives us new things Therefore the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restoration restoring what we have lost and bringing that which we did not have in the past"}
{"zh": "所以新约是一绝对合法的事件，是完全按着神公义的手续立的。新约，不是神空口说的几句话，乃是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据。我们要知道，神的救恩，在主耶稣钉十字架之先，都是神的恩典作的；在主耶稣钉十字架之后，都是神的义作的。这不是说，主钉十字架之后，就没有恩典；这乃是说，恩典好像水，公义好像水管，神的恩典是借着公义的水管流到我们身上。所以罗马五章二十一节说，“就如罪作王叫人死，照样，恩典也借着义作王，叫人因我们的主耶稣基督得永生。”恩典是借着义作王的。神不单独给人恩典，神是借着义把祂的恩典给人。神爱我们，所以主耶稣来为我们死，这是神的恩典。如果神不爱我们，不施恩典，主耶稣就不来为我们成就赎罪的工作。但是，主耶稣为我们死了，救赎已成，那我们信主得救，就是神的义救我们了。", "en": "Therefore, the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter. It was established wholly according to the procedure of God's righteousness. The new covenant is not a few mere verbal statements made by God, but a contract in writing which God has established through Christ's blood for us. It is important to realize that God's salvation before the crucifixion of the Lord Jesus was all accomplished by His grace, but that after the Lord's crucifixion it was accomplished by His righteousness. This does not mean that after the Lord's crucifixion there was no grace, but only that grace is like water, and righteousness is like the water pipe. God's grace flows to us through the pipe of righteousness. Therefore, Romans 5:21 says, \"even as sin reigned unto death, so also grace might reign through righteousness unto eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.\" Grace reigns through righteousness. God does not give grace to man by itself; He gives grace to man through righteousness. God loves us, and the Lord Jesus came to die for us. This is God's grace. If God did not love us and give us grace, the Lord Jesus would not have come to accomplish redemption for us. But the Lord Jesus has died for us and redemption has been accomplished. Because of this, when we believe in the Lord we are saved; this salvation is through His righteousness.", "norm_zh": "所以新约是一绝对合法的事件是完全按着神公义的手续立的新约不是神空口说的几句话乃是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据我们要知道神的救恩在主耶稣钉十字架之先都是神的恩典作的在主耶稣钉十字架之后都是神的义作的这不是说主钉十字架之后就没有恩典这乃是说恩典好像水公义好像水管神的恩典是借着公义的水管流到我们身上所以罗马五章二十一节说就如罪作王叫人死照样恩典也借着义作王叫人因我们的主耶稣基督得永生恩典是借着义作王的神不单独给人恩典神是借着义把祂的恩典给人神爱我们所以主耶稣来为我们死这是神的恩典如果神不爱我们不施恩典主耶稣就不来为我们成就赎罪的工作但是主耶稣为我们死了救赎已成哪我们信主得救就是神的义救我们了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Therefore the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter It was established wholly according to the procedure of Gods righteousness The new covenant is not a few mere verbal statements made by God but a contract in writing which God has established through Christs blood for us It is important to realize that Gods salvation before the crucifixion of the Lord Jesus was all accomplished by His grace but that after the Lords crucifixion it was accomplished by His righteousness This does not mean that after the Lords crucifixion there was no grace but only that grace is like water and righteousness is like the water pipe Gods grace flows to us through the pipe of righteousness Therefore Romans 521 says even as sin reigned unto death so also grace might reign through righteousness unto eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord Grace reigns through righteousness God does not give grace to man by itself He gives grace to man through righteousness God loves us and the Lord Jesus came to die for us This is Gods grace If God did not love us and give us grace the Lord Jesus would not have come to accomplish redemption for us But the Lord Jesus has died for us and redemption has been accomplished Because of this when we believe in the Lord we are saved this salvation is through His righteousness"}
{"zh": "站在恩典的地位上", "en": "Standing on the Ground of Grace", "norm_zh": "站在恩典的地位上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Standing on the Ground of Grace"}
{"zh": "我们要说，没有主耶稣的血，我们什么都不应当得；借着主耶稣的血，我们就应当得着一切。我们借着主耶稣的血，就有权柄享受约里所有的一切。我们凭着主耶稣的血，要求神按着祂的约赐福给我们的时候，神就不能不公义，祂必须按着约里所有的给我们。这新约，是主用祂自己的血立的。主已经付上了血的代价，我们就是求神按着血在神面前的价值，把约里所有的成功在我们的身上。有一位弟兄说，“没有人知道血所包含的有多少”。我们不能明白这血的价值，我们不必凭着我们的眼睛来看血的价值。我们是求神按着血在祂面前的价值，照主用血所立的约待我们。我们只要对神说，“我要这个，因为你是立约的神。”我们的神是永不失信的神，祂必不会违背祂的约。", "en": "We must say that without the blood of the Lord Jesus we are not entitled to anything. But through the blood of the Lord Jesus we are entitled to everything! Through the blood of the Lord Jesus we have the right to enjoy all that is in the covenant. When, by the blood of the Lord Jesus, we ask God to give His blessings to us according to the covenant, God cannot be unrighteous. He must give them to us according to the covenant. This new covenant was made by the Lord with His own blood. The Lord has paid the price of the blood. Now we can ask God to accomplish upon us all that is in the covenant according to the value of the blood which is before Him. A brother once said, \"No one really knows how much the blood includes.\" We may not understand the value of the blood, nor do we need to see the value of the blood. But we can ask God to treat us according to the value of the blood before Him and according to the covenant which the Lord made with His blood. We need only tell God: \"I want this, for You are the God of the covenant.\" Our God can never be unfaithful; He will not break His covenant.", "norm_zh": "我们要说没有主耶稣的血我们什么都不应当得借着主耶稣的血我们就应当得着一切我们借着主耶稣的血就有权柄享受约里所有的一切我们凭着主耶稣的血要求神按着祂的约赐福给我们的时候神就不能不公义祂必须按着约里所有的给我们这新约是主用祂自己的血立的主已经付上了血的代价我们就是求神按着血在神面前的价值把约里所有的成功在我们的身上有一位弟兄说没有人知道血所包含的有多少我们不能明白这血的价值我们不必凭着我们的眼睛来看血的价值我们是求神按着血在祂面前的价值照主用血所立的约待我们我们只要对神说我要这个因为你是立约的神我们的神是永不失信的神祂必不会违背祂的约", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must say that without the blood of the Lord Jesus we are not entitled to anything But through the blood of the Lord Jesus we are entitled to everything Through the blood of the Lord Jesus we have the right to enjoy all that is in the covenant When by the blood of the Lord Jesus we ask God to give His blessings to us according to the covenant God cannot be unrighteous He must give them to us according to the covenant This new covenant was made by the Lord with His own blood The Lord has paid the price of the blood Now we can ask God to accomplish upon us all that is in the covenant according to the value of the blood which is before Him A brother once said No one really knows how much the blood includes We may not understand the value of the blood nor do we need to see the value of the blood But we can ask God to treat us according to the value of the blood before Him and according to the covenant which the Lord made with His blood We need only tell God I want this for You are the God of the covenant Our God can never be unfaithful He will not break His covenant"}
{"zh": "所以，我们凭着约求，不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西，乃是把本是属乎我们的东西，好像是寄存在神那里的东西领回来。凭着约的祈求，并不是无根据的祈求，乃是把主在约里所给我们的东西去领回来。我们凭着约向神求的时候，神因着约的缘故，不能不站在我们一边。所以，我们凭着血所立的新约到神面前，许多时候，只要“领”，不必“求”。这不是说，我们今天不必祷告；乃是说，我们今天的祷告，“领”的成分应当过于“求”的成分。有一位认识主的弟兄说，“自从各各他以后，圣经里一切的“求”字，都当换作“拿”字。”这话，每一个认识神的人，每一个知道什么叫作各各他，什么叫作血的人，都要说阿们。弟兄姊妹们，我们必须记得：我们凭着血，是要神把我们所应该得的给我们。所以我们一直说，神现在对待我们的原则，是根据于祂的义，不只是祂的恩典。现在新约所给我们的，都是我们应当得的。神按着公义，不能不把约里所载明的给我们，因我们是凭着约向神领取一切。", "en": "Therefore, when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us. Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us. To pray according to the covenant is not to pray without basis, but to claim what God has given us in the covenant. When we pray according to the covenant, God cannot but stand on our side. Therefore, when we come to God through the new covenant established by the blood, many times we just need to claim and not to ask. This does not mean that today we do not need to pray, but that our prayer should consist more of claiming than of asking. A brother who knows the Lord has said that since the time of Golgotha all the asking in the Scriptures should be changed to taking. Those who know the Lord, who know the place Golgotha, and who know what the blood means will say \"Amen!\" Brothers and sisters, we must remember that through the blood we are asking God to give us that to which we are entitled. This is why we say repeatedly that the principle upon which God now treats us is based upon His righteousness, not only upon His grace. What is offered to us in the new covenant, then, is all that we are entitled to receive. According to His righteousness God has no choice but to give us what is clearly written in the new covenant, for we are claiming it from God according to the covenant.", "norm_zh": "所以我们凭着约求不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西乃是把本是属乎我们的东西好像是寄存在神哪里的东西领回来凭着约的祈求并不是无根据的祈求乃是把主在约里所给我们的东西去领回来我们凭着约向神求的时候神因着约的缘故不能不站在我们一边所以我们凭着血所立的新约到神面前许多时候只要领不必求这不是说我们今天不必祷告乃是说我们今天的祷告领的成分应当过于求的成分有一位认识主的弟兄说自从各各他以后圣经里一切的求字都当换作拿字这话每一个认识神的人每一个知道什么叫作各各他什么叫作血的人都要说阿们弟兄姊妹们我们必须记得我们凭着血是要神把我们所应该得的给我们所以我们一直说神现在对待我们的原则是根据于祂的义不只是祂的恩典现在新约所给我们的都是我们应当得的神按着公义不能不把约里所载明的给我们因我们是凭着约向神领取一切", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Therefore when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us To pray according to the covenant is not to pray without basis but to claim what God has given us in the covenant When we pray according to the covenant God cannot but stand on our side Therefore when we come to God through the new covenant established by the blood many times we just need to claim and not to ask This does not mean that today we do not need to pray but that our prayer should consist more of claiming than of asking A brother who knows the Lord has said that since the time of Golgotha all the asking in the Scriptures should be changed to taking Those who know the Lord who know the place Golgotha and who know what the blood means will say Amen Brothers and sisters we must remember that through the blood we are asking God to give us that to which we are entitled This is why we say repeatedly that the principle upon which God now treats us is based upon His righteousness not only upon His grace What is offered to us in the new covenant then is all that we are entitled to receive According to His righteousness God has no choice but to give us what is clearly written in the new covenant for we are claiming it from God according to the covenant"}
{"zh": "希伯来十三章二十至二十一节：“但愿赐平安的神，就是那凭永约之血使群羊的大牧人我主耶稣，从死里复活的神，在各样善事上，成全你们，叫你们遵行祂的旨意，又借着耶稣基督在你们心里行祂所喜悦的事；愿荣耀归给祂，直到永永远远。阿们。”这是一个信心的祷告，也是圣经中一个大的祷告。他要神凭永约之血，叫从死里复活的耶稣基督，住在我们里面，使我们能遵行神的旨意，行神所喜悦的事。这给我们看见，一个有信心的祷告，一个大的祷告，就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告。我们应当有凭着约，抓住约来祈求的信心。我们要凭着约对神说，“神啊！我是凭着你的约来求你”。这样的祈求是有能力的，这样的信心是有功效的。相信约，是会增加我们胆量向神祈求的。", "en": "Hebrews 13:20-21: \"Now the God of peace, He who brought up from the dead our Lord Jesus, the great Shepherd of the sheep, in the blood of an eternal covenant, perfect you in every good work for the doing of His will, doing in us that which is well pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ; to Him be the glory forever and ever. Amen.\" This is a prayer of faith. This is also a great prayer in the Scriptures. The writer of Hebrews asked God, through the blood of the eternal covenant, to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us, so that we may do God's will and accomplish the things well-pleasing to Him. This shows us that a prayer with faith, a great prayer, is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lord's blood. We need the faith to pray by clinging to the covenant. We must tell God by the covenant, \"O God, I am praying to You by Your covenant.\" This kind of prayer is powerful and effective. Our faith in the covenant will increase our boldness in prayer to God.", "norm_zh": "希伯来十三章二十至二十一节但愿赐平安的神就是哪凭永约之血使群羊的大牧人我主耶稣从死里复活的神在各样善事上成全你们叫你们遵行祂的旨意又借着耶稣基督在你们心里行祂所喜悦的事愿荣耀归给祂直到永永远远阿们这是一个信心的祷告也是圣经中一个大的祷告他要神凭永约之血叫从死里复活的耶稣基督住在我们里面使我们能遵行神的旨意行神所喜悦的事这给我们看见一个有信心的祷告一个大的祷告就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告我们应当有凭着约抓住约来祈求的信心我们要凭着约对神说神啊我是凭着你的约来求你这样的祈求是有能力的这样的信心是有功效的相信约是会增加我们胆量向神祈求的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 132021 Now the God of peace He who brought up from the dead our Lord Jesus the great Shepherd of the sheep in the blood of an eternal covenant perfect you in every good work for the doing of His will doing in us that which is well pleasing in His sight through Jesus Christ to Him be the glory forever and ever Amen This is a prayer of faith This is also a great prayer in the Scriptures The writer of Hebrews asked God through the blood of the eternal covenant to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us so that we may do Gods will and accomplish the things wellpleasing to Him This shows us that a prayer with faith a great prayer is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lords blood We need the faith to pray by clinging to the covenant We must tell God by the covenant O God I am praying to You by Your covenant This kind of prayer is powerful and effective Our faith in the covenant will increase our boldness in prayer to God"}
{"zh": "我们必须记得，我们有凭着约向神祈求的权利。我们可以求神照着约行事。但是，我们如果没有信心，就求来求去都没有用。神在新约里所给你的一切东西，都存留在那里，好像人把钱都存在银行里一样。你如果信，你就去支取好了。新约，是用主耶稣的血立的，所以新约是稳妥可靠的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "We must remember that we have the right to pray to God according to the covenant. We may ask God to act according to the covenant, but without faith the prayer will be useless. All that God has given us in the new covenant is deposited as one deposits money in the bank. If we believe, we have only to draw it out. The new covenant was established with the blood of the Lord Jesus; therefore, the new covenant is secure and trustworthy.", "norm_zh": "我们必须记得我们有凭着约向神祈求的权利我们可以求神照着约行事但是我们如果没有信心就求来求去都没有用神在新约里所给你的一切东西都存留在哪里好像人把钱都存在银行里一样你如果信你就去支取好了新约是用主耶稣的血立的所以新约是稳妥可靠的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:02:09.643064+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must remember that we have the right to pray to God according to the covenant We may ask God to act according to the covenant but without faith the prayer will be useless All that God has given us in the new covenant is deposited as one deposits money in the bank If we believe we have only to draw it out The new covenant was established with the blood of the Lord Jesus therefore the new covenant is secure and trustworthy"}
{"zh": "壹\t新约是“约”也是“遗命”—来九15~18：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "I. The New Covenant Is a Covenant and Also a Testament—Heb. 9:15-18:", "norm_zh": "壹新约是约也是遗命来九1518李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The New Covenant Is a Covenant and Also a TestamentHeb 91518"}
{"zh": "一\t与我们立约的是神，神是站在我们对方的；成功这约的是主，因这约是用主的血立的—八8，九12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "A. God is the covenanting party who stands opposite to us; it is the Lord who has accomplished the covenant, for this covenant was made with the Lord's blood.—8:8; 9:12.", "norm_zh": "一与我们立约的是神神是站在我们对方的成功这约的是主因这约是用主的血立的八8九12李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God is the covenanting party who stands opposite to us it is the Lord who has accomplished the covenant for this covenant was made with the Lords blood88 912"}
{"zh": "二\t从神那一方面来说，神与我们立约，所以是约；从主耶稣这一方面来说，是祂死了所留下给我们永远的产业，所以是遗命—九章。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "B. As far as God is concerned, He made a covenant with us, and therefore it is a covenant; as far as the Lord Jesus is concerned, it was through His death that He bequeathed an eternal inheritance to us, and therefore it is a testament—Heb. 9.", "norm_zh": "二从神哪一方面来说神与我们立约所以是约从主耶稣这一方面来说是祂死了所留下给我们永远的产业所以是遗命九章李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B As far as God is concerned He made a covenant with us and therefore it is a covenant as far as the Lord Jesus is concerned it was through His death that He bequeathed an eternal inheritance to us and therefore it is a testamentHeb 9"}
{"zh": "三\t“约”，不必本人死才生效；但“遗命”，必须等到留遗命的人死了才生效—16~17节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "C. For a covenant to become effective, the death of the covenanting one is not required, but for a testament to become effective, the death of the testator is required.—vv. 16-17.", "norm_zh": "三约不必本人死才生效但遗命必须等到留遗命的人死了才生效1617节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C For a covenant to become effective the death of the covenanting one is not required but for a testament to become effective the death of the testator is requiredvv 1617"}
{"zh": "贰\t主耶稣是留遗命的人—林前十一23~26：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "II. THE LORD JESUS BEING THE TESTATOR—1 Cor. 11:23-26:", "norm_zh": "贰主耶稣是留遗命的人林前十一2326李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II THE LORD JESUS BEING THE TESTATOR1 Cor 112326"}
{"zh": "一\t这“新约”就是耶利米书所说的那一个最荣耀的新约，现在因主耶稣的血，竟然叫这约成为我们所得的产业，叫我们能以享受其中所说的一切了！—来九15~17。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "A. The new covenant here is the very glorious new covenant mentioned in the book of Jeremiah. Now, through the blood of the Lord Jesus, this covenant has become our inheritance so that we can enjoy all its contents.—Heb. 9:15-17.", "norm_zh": "一这新约就是耶利米书所说的哪一个最荣耀的新约现在因主耶稣的血竟然叫这约成为我们所得的产业叫我们能以享受其中所说的一切了来九1517李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new covenant here is the very glorious new covenant mentioned in the book of Jeremiah Now through the blood of the Lord Jesus this covenant has become our inheritance so that we can enjoy all its contentsHeb 91517"}
{"zh": "二\t凡从遗命有所得着的，就是他所得着的不是他本来所有的，不是他自己作工得来的，乃是主耶稣所遗留给他的—路二二20，来九16~17。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "B. When we inherit something through a will, we receive what we did not originally possess. Through the new covenant we received something which we did not work for, but which has been bequeathed to us by the Lord Jesus.—Luke 22:20; Heb. 9:16-17.", "norm_zh": "二凡从遗命有所得着的就是他所得着的不是他本来所有的不是他自己作工得来的乃是主耶稣所遗留给他的路二二20来九1617李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When we inherit something through a will we receive what we did not originally possess Through the new covenant we received something which we did not work for but which has been bequeathed to us by the Lord JesusLuke 2220 Heb 91617"}
{"zh": "叁\t主耶稣是执行遗命的人—15节，八6，十二24：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "III. THE LORD JESUS BEING THE EXECUTOR OF THE TESTAMENT—v. 15; 8:6; 12:24:", "norm_zh": "叁主耶稣是执行遗命的人15节八6十二24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III THE LORD JESUS BEING THE EXECUTOR OF THE TESTAMENTv 15 86 1224"}
{"zh": "一\t按着死来说，留遗命的是主耶稣；按着复活来说，执行遗命的也是主耶稣—九14~15节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "A. As far as death is concerned, the Lord Jesus is the Testator; but as far as resurrection is concerned, He is the Executor of the will.—9:14-15.", "norm_zh": "一按着死来说留遗命的是主耶稣按着复活来说执行遗命的也是主耶稣九1415节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As far as death is concerned the Lord Jesus is the Testator but as far as resurrection is concerned He is the Executor of the will91415"}
{"zh": "二\t主耶稣把血带进圣所，说明留遗命的人已经死了；主耶稣在天上作新约的中保，说明祂是有能力执行遗命的人—15、24节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "B. The Lord Jesus brought the blood into the Holy of Holies, indicating that the Testator had died; the Lord Jesus as the Mediator of the new covenant in the heavens indicates that He is the One who has the power to execute the testament.—vv. 15, 24.", "norm_zh": "二主耶稣把血带进圣所说明留遗命的人已经死了主耶稣在天上作新约的中保说明祂是有能力执行遗命的人1524节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Lord Jesus brought the blood into the Holy of Holies indicating that the Testator had died the Lord Jesus as the Mediator of the new covenant in the heavens indicates that He is the One who has the power to execute the testamentvv 15 24"}
{"zh": "三\t主在天上，祂不只作大祭司，祂也作中保，就是作约的“执行者”，叫新约在我们身上有效力—11、15节，十二22~24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "C. In the heavens the Lord is not only the High Priest, but also the Mediator, the Executor, of the new covenant, so that it may become effective in us.—vv. 11, 15; 12:22-24.", "norm_zh": "三主在天上祂不只作大祭司祂也作中保就是作约的执行者叫新约在我们身上有效力1115节十二2224李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the heavens the Lord is not only the High Priest but also the Mediator the Executor of the new covenant so that it may become effective in usvv 11 15 122224"}
{"zh": "四\t按神的信实和公义说，这约，是永不能背、永不能废的；按主复活的能力来说，这约是永远有效力的—九25~28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "D. According to God's faithfulness and righteousness, this covenant is inviolable and irrevocable; according to the Lord's resurrection power, this covenant is forever effective.—Heb. 9:25-28.", "norm_zh": "四按神的信实和公义说这约是永不能背永不能废的按主复活的能力来说这约是永远有效力的九2528李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D According to Gods faithfulness and righteousness this covenant is inviolable and irrevocable according to the Lords resurrection power this covenant is forever effectiveHeb 92528"}
{"zh": "肆\t“凡有遗命，必须等到留遗命的人死了；因为人死了，遗命才有效力……”—16~17节：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "IV. \"For where there is a testament, the death of him who made the testament must of necessity be established. For a testament is confirmed in the case of the dead...\"—vv. 16-17:", "norm_zh": "肆凡有遗命必须等到留遗命的人死了因为人死了遗命才有效力1617节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV For where there is a testament the death of him who made the testament must of necessity be established For a testament is confirmed in the case of the deadvv 1617"}
{"zh": "一\t我们每逢吃这饼，喝这杯的时候，就是宣告主已经死了；留遗命的人已经死了，现在遗命有效力了！我们的主，是负责的执行者，我们必定能得着遗命里所有的一切—路二二19~20，来九15~17。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "A. Whenever we eat the bread and drink the cup, we declare that the Lord has died; the Testator has died, and now the testament, the will, has become effective! Since our Lord is a responsible Executor, we shall receive all the bequests in the testament.—Luke 22:19-20; Heb. 9:15-17.", "norm_zh": "一我们每逢吃这饼喝这杯的时候就是宣告主已经死了留遗命的人已经死了现在遗命有效力了我们的主是负责的执行者我们必定能得着遗命里所有的一切路二二1920来九1517李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Whenever we eat the bread and drink the cup we declare that the Lord has died the Testator has died and now the testament the will has become effective Since our Lord is a responsible Executor we shall receive all the bequests in the testamentLuke 221920 Heb 91517"}
{"zh": "二\t我们的主所遗留给我们的，有三大部分，就是洁净（罪得赦免后的洁净），生命和能力，以及更深地认识神；这三部分包括我们灵性生活一切的需要；我们应当用信心来取用遗命里所有的一切——八10~12，十19~23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "B. What the Lord has bequeathed to us in His testament includes three major items: (1) cleansing which comes through the forgiveness of sins, (2) life and power, and (3) an inward knowledge of God; these three items comprise all the needs of our spiritual life; we should receive by faith all that is included in the testament.—Heb. 8:10-12; 10:19-23.", "norm_zh": "二我们的主所遗留给我们的有三大部分就是洁净罪得赦免后的洁净生命和能力以及更深地认识神这三部分包括我们灵性生活一切的需要我们应当用信心来取用遗命里所有的一切八1012十1923李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B What the Lord has bequeathed to us in His testament includes three major items 1 cleansing which comes through the forgiveness of sins 2 life and power and 3 an inward knowledge of God these three items comprise all the needs of our spiritual life we should receive by faith all that is included in the testamentHeb 81012 101923"}
{"zh": "三\t所以我们每逢喝的时候，我们所看见的不是物质的葡萄汁或者葡萄酒，而是主用血所立的新约；主要我们长久地记得，新约所包括的一切，是我们可以长久享受的—路二二18~20，林前十一26。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第五章）", "en": "C. Therefore, when we drink, what we see is not the grape juice or the wine itself, but a new covenant which the Lord established with His blood; the Lord wants us to remember that we can enjoy constantly all that is included in the new covenant.—Luke 22:18-20; 1 Cor. 11:26.", "norm_zh": "三所以我们每逢喝的时候我们所看见的不是物质的葡萄汁或者葡萄酒而是主用血所立的新约主要我们长久地记得新约所包括的一切是我们可以长久享受的路二二1820林前十一26李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Therefore when we drink what we see is not the grape juice or the wine itself but a new covenant which the Lord established with His blood the Lord wants us to remember that we can enjoy constantly all that is included in the new covenantLuke 221820 1 Cor 1126"}
{"zh": "伍\t新约的稳妥；新约是用血立的，所以新约是可靠的，是稳妥的—太二六28，来十三20：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "V. The security of the new covenant; the new covenant was established through the blood; therefore, the new covenant is dependable; it is secure.—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 13:20:", "norm_zh": "伍新约的稳妥新约是用血立的所以新约是可靠的是稳妥的太二六28来十三20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The security of the new covenant the new covenant was established through the blood therefore the new covenant is dependable it is secureMatt 2628 Heb 1320"}
{"zh": "一\t新约，为什么必须用血来立呢？为什么用血立的约才有功效呢？—罗五12~14：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "A. Why must the new covenant be established through the blood? Why is a covenant effective only when it is established with the blood?—Rom. 5:12-14:", "norm_zh": "一新约为什么必须用血来立呢为什么用血立的约才有功效呢罗五1214李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Why must the new covenant be established through the blood Why is a covenant effective only when it is established with the bloodRom 51214"}
{"zh": "1\t当基督还没有来到地上的时候，我们人受到两个大亏损：第一个是因亚当犯罪而受的亏损，第二个是因我们不能遵行神的律法而受的亏损—13节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "1. Before Christ came to the earth, man suffered two great losses: first, he suffered because of Adam's sin, and second, he suffered because he could not keep God's law.—v. 13.", "norm_zh": "1当基督还没有来到地上的时候我们人受到两个大亏损第一个是因亚当犯罪而受的亏损第二个是因我们不能遵行神的律法而受的亏损13节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Before Christ came to the earth man suffered two great losses first he suffered because of Adams sin and second he suffered because he could not keep Gods lawv 13"}
{"zh": "2\t从亚当到摩西，死作了王；从摩西到基督，不只死作了王，并且罪也作了王；但是，感谢神，主耶稣的流血却替我们解决了这两个问题—15~21节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "2. From Adam to Moses death reigned; from Moses to Christ not only did death reign, but sin also reigned; but praise God, the blood of the Lord Jesus has solved these two problems for us!—vv. 15-21.", "norm_zh": "2从亚当到摩西死作了王从摩西到基督不只死作了王并且罪也作了王但是感谢神主耶稣的流血却替我们解决了这两个问提1521节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 From Adam to Moses death reigned from Moses to Christ not only did death reign but sin also reigned but praise God the blood of the Lord Jesus has solved these two problems for usvv 1521"}
{"zh": "3\t主耶稣的血洗净了我们的罪，并且也恢复了我们与神的关；主耶稣的血不只叫我们与神和好，也是把神自己给我们了—弗二5~6，西20、22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "3. The blood of the Lord Jesus cleanses us from our sins and has also restored our relationship with God; the blood of the Lord Jesus not only reconciles us with God, but also gives God Himself to us.—Eph. 2:5-6; Col. 1:20, 22.", "norm_zh": "3主耶稣的血洗净了我们的罪并且也恢复了我们与神的关主耶稣的血不只叫我们与神和好也是把神自己给我们了弗二56西2022李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The blood of the Lord Jesus cleanses us from our sins and has also restored our relationship with God the blood of the Lord Jesus not only reconciles us with God but also gives God Himself to usEph 256 Col 120 22"}
{"zh": "4\t基督的血不只是成功了救赎，并且是成功了永远的救赎；基督用自己的血，只一次进入圣所，成了永远赎罪的事—来九12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "4. The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption; it also accomplished an eternal redemption; Christ, through His own blood, entered once for all into the Holy of Holies, having found an eternal redemption.—Heb. 9:12.", "norm_zh": "4基督的血不只是成功了救赎并且是成功了永远的救赎基督用自己的血只一次进入圣所成了永远赎罪的事来九12李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The blood of Christ not only accomplished redemption it also accomplished an eternal redemption Christ through His own blood entered once for all into the Holy of Holies having found an eternal redemptionHeb 912"}
{"zh": "5\t主的血一面是为赎罪而流，在消极方面，除去了那些害我们的；一面是为立新约而流，在积极方面，恢复了我们所已经失去的产业，并赐给了我们新的东西；所以，主的血不只是为赎罪，也是为恢复—14~15节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "5. On the one hand, the Lord's blood was shed for redemption, removing on the negative side those things which damage us; on the other hand, His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant, restoring on the positive side the inheritance we have lost and also giving us new things; therefore, the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restoration.—vv. 14-15.", "norm_zh": "5主的血一面是为赎罪而流在消极方面除去了哪些害我们的一面是为立新约而流在积极方面恢复了我们所已经失去的产业并赐给了我们新的东西所以主的血不只是为赎罪也是为恢复1415节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 On the one hand the Lords blood was shed for redemption removing on the negative side those things which damage us on the other hand His blood was shed for the establishing of the new covenant restoring on the positive side the inheritance we have lost and also giving us new things therefore the blood of the Lord Jesus is not only for redemption but also for restorationvv 1415"}
{"zh": "二\t血是根基，约是字据；血是立约的根基，约是用血立的字据—九12~14：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "B. The blood is the base, and the covenant is the contract; the blood is the base upon which the covenant is established, and the covenant is the contract established with the blood.—Heb. 9:12-14:", "norm_zh": "二血是根基约是字据血是立约的根基约是用血立的字据九1214李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The blood is the base and the covenant is the contract the blood is the base upon which the covenant is established and the covenant is the contract established with the bloodHeb 91214"}
{"zh": "1\t我们就凭着这用主耶稣的血所立的新约，来承受神所给我们的属灵的产业—十三20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "1. It is by this new covenant, established with the blood of the Lord Jesus, that we receive the spiritual inheritance which God has given us.—Heb. 13:20.", "norm_zh": "1我们就凭着这用主耶稣的血所立的新约来承受神所给我们的属灵的产业十三20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 It is by this new covenant established with the blood of the Lord Jesus that we receive the spiritual inheritance which God has given usHeb 1320"}
{"zh": "2\t所以新约是一绝对合法的事件，是完全按着神公义的手续立的；是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据—九22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "2. Therefore, the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter, established fully according to God's righteous procedures; it is a document established for us by God through the blood of Christ.—Heb. 9:22.", "norm_zh": "2所以新约是一绝对合法的事件是完全按着神公义的手续立的是神借基督的血为我们所立的一种字据九22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Therefore the new covenant is an absolutely legal matter established fully according to Gods righteous procedures it is a document established for us by God through the blood of ChristHeb 922"}
{"zh": "3\t感谢神，祂不只有恩典，祂并且将祂的恩典借着一个约表明出来—出二四8，来九20：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "3. Praise God, He not only has grace, but He also expresses His grace through a covenant.—Exo. 24:8; Heb. 9:20:", "norm_zh": "3感谢神祂不只有恩典祂并且将祂的恩典借着一个约表明出来出二四8来九20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Praise God He not only has grace but He also expresses His grace through a covenantExo 248 Heb 920"}
{"zh": "a\t我们所得的是神的恩典，但神是用血与我们立约，叫我们凭着约求神按着祂的公义待我们；我们是站在恩典的地位上的，但是，恩典是借着义通到我们身上的——太二六28，罗五21。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "a. What we receive is God's grace, but God has used the blood to make a covenant with us, so that through the covenant we may ask God to deal with us according to His righteousness; we stand upon the ground of grace, but grace comes to us through righteousness.—Matt. 26:28; Rom. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "a我们所得的是神的恩典但神是用血与我们立约叫我们凭着约求神按着祂的公义待我们我们是站在恩典的地位上的但是恩典是借着义通到我们身上的太二六28罗五21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a What we receive is Gods grace but God has used the blood to make a covenant with us so that through the covenant we may ask God to deal with us according to His righteousness we stand upon the ground of grace but grace comes to us through righteousnessMatt 2628 Rom 521"}
{"zh": "b\t我们是站在血的根基，公义的根基上与神来往，神就不能不把约里所有的一切成就在我们身上—来九20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "b. We are standing upon the foundation of the blood, the foundation of righteousness, to deal with God. Therefore, God has no choice but to fulfill in us all that is in the covenant.—Heb. 9:20.", "norm_zh": "b我们是站在血的根基公义的根基上与神来往神就不能不把约里所有的一切成就在我们身上来九20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We are standing upon the foundation of the blood the foundation of righteousness to deal with God Therefore God has no choice but to fulfill in us all that is in the covenantHeb 920"}
{"zh": "4\t基督徒的生活没有别的，就是抓住神的话语而生活，就是相信神是信实的，是公义的—约壹一9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "4. The Christian's life has no other secret than living by holding on to God's Word, believing that God is faithful and righteous.—1 John 1:9.", "norm_zh": "4基督徒的生活没有别的就是抓住神的话语而生活就是相信神是信实的是公义的约壹一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The Christians life has no other secret than living by holding on to Gods Word believing that God is faithful and righteous1 John 19"}
{"zh": "5\t立新约的血，把我们的罪的问题解决了，也使神能把天上各样属灵的福气，一切关乎生命和敬虔的事都赐给我们；凡新约里所载明的，都是我们因血所当得的福气—弗二11~13，彼后一3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "5. The blood of the new covenant solves the problem of our sins, and enables God to give us all spiritual blessings in the heavenlies, and all things that pertain to life and godliness; all of the things that are clearly written in the new covenant are our rightful blessings through the blood.—Eph. 2:11-13; 2 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "5立新约的血把我们的罪的问提解决了也使神能把天上各样属灵的福气一切关乎生命和敬虔的事都赐给我们凡新约里所载明的都是我们因血所当得的福气弗二1113彼后一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 The blood of the new covenant solves the problem of our sins and enables God to give us all spiritual blessings in the heavenlies and all things that pertain to life and godliness all of the things that are clearly written in the new covenant are our rightful blessings through the bloodEph 21113 2 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "6\t所以，我们凭着约求，不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西，乃是把本是属乎我们的东西，好像是寄存在神那里的东西领回来—彼前一3~5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "6. Therefore, when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us. Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us.—1 Pet. 1:3-5.", "norm_zh": "6所以我们凭着约求不是去求得不是属乎我们的东西乃是把本是属乎我们的东西好像是寄存在神哪里的东西领回来彼前一35李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Therefore when we ask according to the covenant we are not asking for things which do not belong to us Rather we are claiming the items which have always belonged to us and have been reserved in God for us1 Pet 135"}
{"zh": "三\t希伯来十三章二十至二十一节，这是一个信心的祷告，也是圣经中一个大的祷告：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "C. Hebrews 13:20-21 is a prayer of faith, and it is also a great prayer in the Scriptures:", "norm_zh": "三希伯来十三章二十至二十一节这是一个信心的祷告也是圣经中一个大的祷告李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Hebrews 132021 is a prayer of faith and it is also a great prayer in the Scriptures"}
{"zh": "1\t他要神凭永约之血，叫从死里复活的耶稣基督，住在我们里面，使我们能遵行神的旨意，行神所喜悦的事—21节，十二28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "1. The writer of Hebrews asked God, through the blood of the eternal covenant, to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us, so that we may do God's will and accomplish the things well-pleasing to Him.—v. 21; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "1他要神凭永约之血叫从死里复活的耶稣基督住在我们里面使我们能遵行神的旨意行神所喜悦的事21节十二28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The writer of Hebrews asked God through the blood of the eternal covenant to cause the resurrected Jesus Christ to dwell in us so that we may do Gods will and accomplish the things wellpleasing to Himv 21 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "2\t一个有信心的祷告，一个大的祷告，就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告—十三20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第四章）", "en": "2. A prayer with faith, a great prayer, is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lord's blood.—Heb. 13:20.", "norm_zh": "2一个有信心的祷告一个大的祷告就是站在主流血所立的永约上头来祷告十三20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:05:02.465027+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 A prayer with faith a great prayer is one prayed by standing upon the eternal covenant of the Lords bloodHeb 1320"}
{"zh": "读经：来八10~12，罗五12，约壹一7、9，太二六28，来一8~9，诗三二5，箴二八13", "en": "Scripture Reading: Heb. 8:10-12; Rom. 5:12; 1 John 1:7, 9; Matt. 26:28; Heb. 1:8-9; Psa. 32:5; Prov. 28:13", "norm_zh": "读经来八1012罗五12约壹一79太二六28来一89诗三二5箴二八13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Heb 81012 Rom 512 1 John 17 9 Matt 2628 Heb 189 Psa 325 Prov 2813"}
{"zh": "壹\t新约的内容是包含三大部分，这是希伯来八章十至十二节告诉我们的：", "en": "I. The contents of the new covenant include three major parts; this is what Hebrews 8:10-12 tells us:", "norm_zh": "壹新约的内容是包含三大部分这是希伯来八章十至十二节告诉我们的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The contents of the new covenant include three major parts this is what Hebrews 81012 tells us"}
{"zh": "一\t以神永远的目的来说，神是先把祂的生命和能力赐给我们；然后在生命的律里作我们的神，叫我们在生命的律里作祂的子民；叫我们在里面对于祂有更深的认识；赦罪不过是达到祂的目的的一个手续，所以圣经在这里把赦罪摆在最后说—来八10~12。", "en": "A. According to God's eternal purpose, He first imparted His life and power into us; then He became our God in the law of life that we might be His people in the law of life, that we might have a deeper knowledge of Him; since forgiveness of sins is only a procedure by which to achieve His purpose, Scripture puts forgiveness of sins at the very end—Heb. 8:10-12.", "norm_zh": "一以神永远的目的来说神是先把祂的生命和能力赐给我们然后在生命的律里作我们的神叫我们在生命的律里作祂的子民叫我们在里面对于祂有更深的认识赦罪不过是达到祂的目的的一个手续所以圣经在这里把赦罪摆在最后说来八1012", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A According to Gods eternal purpose He first imparted His life and power into us then He became our God in the law of life that we might be His people in the law of life that we might have a deeper knowledge of Him since forgiveness of sins is only a procedure by which to achieve His purpose Scripture puts forgiveness of sins at the very endHeb 81012"}
{"zh": "二\t以我们属灵的经历来说，我们总是先得洁净（因罪得赦免而得的洁净），然后在生命的律里作神的子民，在里面对于神有更深的认识—8~12节。", "en": "B. According to our spiritual experience, we first obtain cleansing, that is, the cleansing which comes from forgiveness; then we become God's people in the law of life, and then we possess a deeper knowledge of God in an inward way—vv. 8-12.", "norm_zh": "二以我们属灵的经历来说我们总是先得洁净因罪得赦免而得的洁净然后在生命的律里作神的子民在里面对于神有更深的认识812节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to our spiritual experience we first obtain cleansing that is the cleansing which comes from forgiveness then we become Gods people in the law of life and then we possess a deeper knowledge of God in an inward wayvv 812"}
{"zh": "贰\t凭圣经来看，罪，是有“罪性”与“罪行”的分别的—罗五12，约壹一7：", "en": "II. According to the Scriptures, sin has two aspects: the nature of sin and the act of sin—Rom. 5:12; 1 John 1:7:", "norm_zh": "贰凭圣经来看罪是有罪性与罪行的分别的罗五12约壹一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II According to the Scriptures sin has two aspects the nature of sin and the act of sinRom 512 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "一\t罪性，是“住在人里面的罪”，是罪在人里面作主，辖制人、主使人去犯罪的—罗五12，约壹一8。", "en": "A. The nature of sin is \"sin that dwells in man,\" mastering and governing him and inciting him to commit sins—Rom. 5:12; 1 John 1:8.", "norm_zh": "一罪性是住在人里面的罪是罪在人里面作主辖制人主使人去犯罪的罗五12约壹一8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The nature of sin is sin that dwells in man mastering and governing him and inciting him to commit sinsRom 512 1 John 18"}
{"zh": "二\t罪行，是“显在人外面的罪”，是在人日常生活中所显出的—罗六6，约壹一7。", "en": "B. Sinful acts are the sins which are manifested outwardly in our daily life.—Rom. 6:6; 1 John 1:7.", "norm_zh": "二罪行是显在人外面的罪是在人日常生活中所显出的罗六6约壹一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Sinful acts are the sins which are manifested outwardly in our daily lifeRom 66 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "三\t所以，罪行是需要得着赦免，得着洗净的；罪性是需要脱离，需要得着释放的—7~8节。", "en": "C. Therefore, the sinful acts need to be forgiven and cleansed, but we also need to be delivered and released from our sinful nature—vv. 7-8.", "norm_zh": "三所以罪行是需要得着赦免得着洗净的罪性是需要脱离需要得着释放的78节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Therefore the sinful acts need to be forgiven and cleansed but we also need to be delivered and released from our sinful naturevv 78"}
{"zh": "四\t主耶稣的血是对付我们在神面前的罪状，是洗净我们的良心的—太二六28，启一5。", "en": "D. The blood of the Lord Jesus deals with the charges of sin against us before God and purifies our conscience—Matt. 26:28; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "四主耶稣的血是对付我们在神面前的罪状是洗净我们的良心的太二六28启一5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The blood of the Lord Jesus deals with the charges of sin against us before God and purifies our conscienceMatt 2628 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "五\t主耶稣的十字架，是对付我们的旧人，是叫我们脱离罪的权势，从罪得着释放的—罗六6。", "en": "E. The cross of the Lord Jesus deals with our old man, delivering us from the power of sin and freeing us from sin itself—Rom. 6:6.", "norm_zh": "五主耶稣的十字架是对付我们的旧人是叫我们脱离罪的权势从罪得着释放的罗六6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The cross of the Lord Jesus deals with our old man delivering us from the power of sin and freeing us from sin itselfRom 66"}
{"zh": "叁\t罪需要赦免—约壹一9，太二六28，来九22，约壹二12，徒十43：", "en": "III. Sins Need to be Forgiven—1 John 1:9; Matt. 26:28; Heb. 9:22; 1 John 2:12; Acts 10:43:", "norm_zh": "叁罪需要赦免约壹一9太二六28来九22约壹二12徒十43", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Sins Need to be Forgiven1 John 19 Matt 2628 Heb 922 1 John 212 Acts 1043"}
{"zh": "一\t一个真被圣灵光照的人，没有不为罪自己责备自己的；就是在这样的时候，神的赦免是他所需要的—约十六8、13：", "en": "A. A person who is truly enlightened by the Holy Spirit cannot help but condemn himself concerning sin; it is at this moment he needs God's forgiveness.—John 16:8, 13:", "norm_zh": "一一个真被圣灵光照的人没有不为罪自己责备自己的就是在这样的时候神的赦免是他所需要的约十六813", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A person who is truly enlightened by the Holy Spirit cannot help but condemn himself concerning sin it is at this moment he needs Gods forgivenessJohn 168 13"}
{"zh": "1\t就在这样的时候，有一个福音传给我们说，主耶稣被钉在十字架上，流出祂的宝血，就是要使罪得赦，就是要使人的罪恶得洗去—太二六28，启一5。", "en": "1. Perhaps at this time the gospel is preached telling how the Lord Jesus was crucified on the cross and how He shed His precious blood for the forgiveness of sin that men might be washed of their sin.—Matt. 26:28; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "1就在这样的时候有一个福音传给我们说主耶稣被钉在十字架上流出祂的宝血就是要使罪得赦就是要使人的罪恶得洗去太二六28启一5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Perhaps at this time the gospel is preached telling how the Lord Jesus was crucified on the cross and how He shed His precious blood for the forgiveness of sin that men might be washed of their sinMatt 2628 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "2\t我们听见了这福音，我们一信，我们的罪就得赦免了，我们的良心就得洗净了—徒十43，二六18，来九14。", "en": "2. When a person hears this gospel and believes, his sins are forgiven and his conscience is purified.—Acts 10:43; 26:18; Heb. 9:14.", "norm_zh": "2我们听见了这福音我们一信我们的罪就得赦免了我们的良心就得洗净了徒十43二六18来九14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When a person hears this gospel and believes his sins are forgiven and his conscience is purifiedActs 1043 2618 Heb 914"}
{"zh": "二\t“你的罪赦免了。……你的信救了你，平平安安地回去吧”；这一个赦免，在她真是一个大的福音！这一个赦免，叫她不再暗自悲伤；这一个赦免，叫她满了平安—路七36~50。", "en": "B. \"Thy sins are forgiven.... Thy faith hath saved thee; go in peace\"; this forgiveness to her was a great gospel! This forgiveness enabled her to no longer feel sorry for herself; this forgiveness caused her to be full of peace.—Luke 7:36-50.", "norm_zh": "二你的罪赦免了你的信救了你平平安安地回去吧这一个赦免在她真是一个大的福音这一个赦免叫她不再暗自悲伤这一个赦免叫她满了平安路七3650", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Thy sins are forgiven Thy faith hath saved thee go in peace this forgiveness to her was a great gospel This forgiveness enabled her to no longer feel sorry for herself this forgiveness caused her to be full of peaceLuke 73650"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经给我们看见，有的病是犯罪的结果—可二3~12，约五14：", "en": "C. The Scriptures indicate that some illnesses are the result of committing sin.—Mark 2:3-12; John 5:14:", "norm_zh": "三圣经给我们看见有的病是犯罪的结果可二312约五14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Scriptures indicate that some illnesses are the result of committing sinMark 2312 John 514"}
{"zh": "1\t主知道这一个瘫子的病因是罪，所以先对他说，“小子，你的罪赦了”；然后再对他说，“我吩咐你起来，拿你的褥子回家去吧”—可二5。", "en": "1. The Lord knew that with this man sick of palsy, the cause of his illness was sin. For this reason He first spoke to the sick man, \"Son, thy sins are forgiven\"; then He said, \"I say unto thee, Arise, take up thy bed, and go unto thy house.\"—Mark 2:5.", "norm_zh": "1主知道这一个瘫子的病因是罪所以先对他说小子你的罪赦了然后再对他说我吩咐你起来拿你的褥子回家去吧可二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lord knew that with this man sick of palsy the cause of his illness was sin For this reason He first spoke to the sick man Son thy sins are forgiven then He said I say unto thee Arise take up thy bed and go unto thy houseMark 25"}
{"zh": "2\t哦，罪得赦了，病也得治了，这是何等大的福音！—5、10~12节。", "en": "2. The sins were forgiven and the sickness was healed. What a great gospel this is!—vv. 5, 10-12.", "norm_zh": "2哦罪得赦了病也得治了这是何等大的福音51012节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The sins were forgiven and the sickness was healed What a great gospel this isvv 5 1012"}
{"zh": "肆\t赦免是靠神的义—太二六28，来一8~9：", "en": "IV. Forgiveness is Based Upon God's Righteousness—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 1:8-9:", "norm_zh": "肆赦免是靠神的义太二六28来一89", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Forgiveness is Based Upon Gods RighteousnessMatt 2628 Heb 189"}
{"zh": "一\t我们的神是圣洁的神，是喜爱公义，恨恶罪恶的神—彼前一15~16，来一9。", "en": "A. Our God is a holy God, One who loves righteousness and hates lawlessness.—1 Pet. 1:15-16; Heb. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "一我们的神是圣洁的神是喜爱公义恨恶罪恶的神彼前一1516来一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Our God is a holy God One who loves righteousness and hates lawlessness1 Pet 11516 Heb 19"}
{"zh": "二\t我们犯了罪，神不能不定我们的罪；按着神的性情来说，祂是圣洁的，所以祂不能容让罪；按着神作事的手续来说，祂是公义的，所以祂不能不刑罚罪；按着祂的自己说，祂是荣耀的，所以罪人不能亲近祂，亲近祂的就必定死—罗八3，提前六16。", "en": "B. Whenever we commit sin, God must condemn us for our sin; according to God's nature He is holy; therefore, He cannot tolerate sin; according to God's way of doing things, He is righteous; therefore, He must punish sin; in Himself God is also glorious; for this reason sinners cannot approach Him; those who do approach Him will surely die.—Rom. 8:3; 1 Tim. 6:16.", "norm_zh": "二我们犯了罪神不能不定我们的罪按着神的性情来说祂是圣洁的所以祂不能容让罪按着神作事的手续来说祂是公义的所以祂不能不刑罚罪按着祂的自己说祂是荣耀的所以罪人不能亲近祂亲近祂的就必定死罗八3提前六16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Whenever we commit sin God must condemn us for our sin according to Gods nature He is holy therefore He cannot tolerate sin according to Gods way of doing things He is righteous therefore He must punish sin in Himself God is also glorious for this reason sinners cannot approach Him those who do approach Him will surely dieRom 83 1 Tim 616"}
{"zh": "三\t恩典从来没有自己作王，恩典乃是借着义作王的；神乃是先审判了我们的罪，然后才赦免我们的—罗五17~21，赛五三。", "en": "III. Grace never reigns by itself; grace reigns through righteousness; first God judges our sins; then He forgives us—Rom. 5:17-21; Isa. 53.", "norm_zh": "三恩典从来没有自己作王恩典乃是借着义作王的神乃是先审判了我们的罪然后才赦免我们的罗五1721赛五三", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Grace never reigns by itself grace reigns through righteousness first God judges our sins then He forgives usRom 51721 Isa 53"}
{"zh": "四\t凡受过恩典的教训的人就要说，我们的神赦免人的罪，是恩义两全的—罗五18~21。", "en": "IV. Those who are taught by grace will say that our God's forgiving of men's sins is perfect in both grace and righteousness—Rom. 5:18-21.", "norm_zh": "四凡受过恩典的教训的人就要说我们的神赦免人的罪是恩义两全的罗五1821", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Those who are taught by grace will say that our Gods forgiving of mens sins is perfect in both grace and righteousnessRom 51821"}
{"zh": "伍\t赦免是新约的特点—来八12，十17，二17：", "en": "V. Forgiveness is the characteristic of the new covenant—Heb. 8:12; 10:17; 2:17:", "norm_zh": "伍赦免是新约的特点来八12十17二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Forgiveness is the characteristic of the new covenantHeb 812 1017 217"}
{"zh": "一\t希伯来八章十二节：“我要宽恕他们的不义，不再记念他们的罪愆”；这是新约所给我们的福分之一；这是指神在基督里赦免我们的罪说的：", "en": "A. Hebrews 8:12: \"For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I will by no means remember anymore\"; this is one of the blessings given to us in the new covenant; this refers to God's forgiving us our sins in Christ:", "norm_zh": "一希伯来八章十二节我要宽恕他们的不义不再记念他们的罪愆这是新约所给我们的福分之一这是指神在基督里赦免我们的罪说的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hebrews 812 For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I will by no means remember anymore this is one of the blessings given to us in the new covenant this refers to Gods forgiving us our sins in Christ"}
{"zh": "1\t神把我们的罪愆都忘记了，不是祂掩面不看，或者故意遗忘，乃是因基督的血把我们的罪状涂抹了，把我们的罪恶洗去了—赛四四21~22，来一3，启一5。", "en": "1. God's forgetting of our sins is not that He hides His face or purposely ignores them, but that Christ's blood has blotted out the charges of sin against us and washed us from our sins—Isa. 44:21-22; Heb. 1:3; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "1神把我们的罪愆都忘记了不是祂掩面不看或者故意遗忘乃是因基督的血把我们的罪状涂抹了把我们的罪恶洗去了赛四四2122来一3启一5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods forgetting of our sins is not that He hides His face or purposely ignores them but that Christs blood has blotted out the charges of sin against us and washed us from our sinsIsa 442122 Heb 13 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "2\t神今天是把祂自己约束在约里，祂乐意受约的限制；祂说“要宽恕我们的不义”，就必定宽恕我们的不义；祂说“不再记念我们的罪愆”，就必定不再记念我们的罪愆。", "en": "2. Today God is confining Himself to the covenant; He is willing to be restricted by the covenant; when He said, \"I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses,\" He will do it; and when He said, \"their sins I will by no means remember anymore,\" He will not remember.", "norm_zh": "2神今天是把祂自己约束在约里祂乐意受约的限制祂说要宽恕我们的不义就必定宽恕我们的不义祂说不再记念我们的罪愆就必定不再记念我们的罪愆", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Today God is confining Himself to the covenant He is willing to be restricted by the covenant when He said I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses He will do it and when He said their sins I will by no means remember anymore He will not remember"}
{"zh": "二\t神看见了主耶稣的血，就赦免了我们的罪，就不再记念我们的罪愆；这是新约的特点—九12~14。", "en": "B. When God sees the blood of the Lord Jesus, He forgives our sins and by no means remembers them anymore; this is a characteristic of the new covenant—Heb. 9:12-14.", "norm_zh": "二神看见了主耶稣的血就赦免了我们的罪就不再记念我们的罪愆这是新约的特点九1214", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When God sees the blood of the Lord Jesus He forgives our sins and by no means remembers them anymore this is a characteristic of the new covenantHeb 91214"}
{"zh": "陆\t认罪与赦免—约壹一5~7、9，诗三二5，箴二八13，太二六28：", "en": "VI. Confession of Sin and Forgiveness—1 John 1:5-7, 9; Psa. 32:5; Prov. 28:13; Matt. 26:28:", "norm_zh": "陆认罪与赦免约壹一579诗三二5箴二八13太二六28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Confession of Sin and Forgiveness1 John 157 9 Psa 325 Prov 2813 Matt 2628"}
{"zh": "一\t一个人得救了之后，是不可仍在罪中活着，是不可再犯罪的—罗六，约五14，八11。", "en": "A. After a person is saved, he should not continue in sin, and he must sin no more—Rom. 6, John 5:14, 8:11.", "norm_zh": "一一个人得救了之后是不可仍在罪中活着是不可再犯罪的罗六约五14八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A After a person is saved he should not continue in sin and he must sin no moreRom 6 John 514 811"}
{"zh": "二\t信徒仍有犯罪的可能，有偶然被过犯所胜，被引诱跌倒的可能—约壹一5~10，加六1。", "en": "B. Believers still have the possibility of sinning, the possibility of being overtaken in some offense and of being tempted to fall—1 John 1:5-10; Gal. 6:1.", "norm_zh": "二信徒仍有犯罪的可能有偶然被过犯所胜被引诱跌倒的可能约壹一510加六1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Believers still have the possibility of sinning the possibility of being overtaken in some offense and of being tempted to fall1 John 1510 Gal 61"}
{"zh": "三\t约壹三章九节说，“凡从神生的，就不犯罪，因为神的种住在他里面；他也不能犯罪，因为他是由神生的”；这乃是就重生之人的习惯与性质而言。", "en": "C. In 1 John 3:9 we read that \"Whosoever is begotten of God doeth no sin, because his seed abideth in him: and he cannot sin, because he is begotten of God.\" This refers to the habit and nature of a regenerated person.", "norm_zh": "三约壹三章九节说凡从神生的就不犯罪因为神的种住在他里面他也不能犯罪因为他是由神生的这乃是就重生之人的习惯与性质而言", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In 1 John 39 we read that Whosoever is begotten of God doeth no sin because his seed abideth in him and he cannot sin because he is begotten of God This refers to the habit and nature of a regenerated person"}
{"zh": "四\t约壹一章九节说，“我们若认自己的罪，神是信实的，是公义的，必要赦免我们的罪，洗净我们一切的不义”：", "en": "D. First John 1:9 says, \"If we confess our sins, He is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness\":", "norm_zh": "四约壹一章九节说我们若认自己的罪神是信实的是公义的必要赦免我们的罪洗净我们一切的不义", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D First John 19 says If we confess our sins He is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness"}
{"zh": "1\t我们如果承认了自己的罪，就要抓住祂与我们所立的约，向祂求赦免，求洁净—9节。", "en": "1. If we confess our sins, we must, by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us, expect Him to forgive and cleanse us.—v. 9.", "norm_zh": "1我们如果承认了自己的罪就要抓住祂与我们所立的约向祂求赦免求洁净9节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 If we confess our sins we must by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us expect Him to forgive and cleanse usv 9"}
{"zh": "2\t赦罪是约里的事；我们若按着神的话来认罪，神必按着祂的约赦免我们的罪—徒十43。", "en": "2. Forgiveness of sins is something in the covenant; if we confess according to God's Word, God will forgive us according to His covenant.—Acts 10:43.", "norm_zh": "2赦罪是约里的事我们若按着神的话来认罪神必按着祂的约赦免我们的罪徒十43", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Forgiveness of sins is something in the covenant if we confess according to Gods Word God will forgive us according to His covenantActs 1043"}
{"zh": "3\t神与我们立约，就是要我们按着约来对祂说话；祂要我们用信心求祂；我们求神为我们成就约里的话—来十23。", "en": "3. God has made a covenant with us so that we may speak to Him according to His covenant; He wants us to ask by faith; we ask God to fulfill what is in the covenant—Heb. 10:23.", "norm_zh": "3神与我们立约就是要我们按着约来对祂说话祂要我们用信心求祂我们求神为我们成就约里的话来十23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 God has made a covenant with us so that we may speak to Him according to His covenant He wants us to ask by faith we ask God to fulfill what is in the covenantHeb 1023"}
{"zh": "4\t这里所说的认罪，是在神的光照之下看见了罪；神的光是不容让任何一件罪的；人在神光照之下看见了罪，并且定罪为罪，而来到神面前认罪，神是要赦免这样的人的罪，洗净这样的人的不义—约壹一7、9。", "en": "4. The confession referred to here is something we do after seeing sin in God's light; God's light does not tolerate sin; when a person truly sees sin in God's light, condemns sin as sin, and comes to God to confess his sin, God will forgive such a person's sin and cleanse his unrighteousness—1 John 1:7, 9.", "norm_zh": "4这里所说的认罪是在神的光照之下看见了罪神的光是不容让任何一件罪的人在神光照之下看见了罪并且定罪为罪而来到神面前认罪神是要赦免这样的人的罪洗净这样的人的不义约壹一79", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The confession referred to here is something we do after seeing sin in Gods light Gods light does not tolerate sin when a person truly sees sin in Gods light condemns sin as sin and comes to God to confess his sin God will forgive such a persons sin and cleanse his unrighteousness1 John 17 9"}
{"zh": "5\t至于有的人把认罪当作护身符似的，他天天在宝血之下说谎，天天在宝血之下发脾气，这是断乎不可的。", "en": "5. Some people take shelter in the confession of sin: day by day they continue to speak lies under the precious blood, and day by day they continue to lose their temper under the precious blood — this is definitely wrong.", "norm_zh": "5至于有的人把认罪当作护身符似的他天天在宝血之下说谎天天在宝血之下发脾气这是断乎不可的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Some people take shelter in the confession of sin day by day they continue to speak lies under the precious blood and day by day they continue to lose their temper under the precious blood this is definitely wrong"}
{"zh": "6\t启示录四章三节说，“又有虹围着宝座”；虹是什么记号呢？虹是神与挪亚立约的记号；虹围着宝座，就是说神绝没有忘记祂所立的约，也就是说神绝不能不听人在约里的祷告。", "en": "6. Revelation 4:3 says that there is a rainbow around the throne; what sign is the rainbow? The rainbow is the sign of the covenant which God made with Noah; the rainbow around the throne means that God has never forgotten that covenant; it also means that God must listen to man's prayer if he prays according to the covenant.", "norm_zh": "6启示录四章三节说又有虹围着宝座虹是什么记号呢虹是神与挪亚立约的记号虹围着宝座就是说神绝没有忘记祂所立的约也就是说神绝不能不听人在约里的祷告", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Revelation 43 says that there is a rainbow around the throne what sign is the rainbow The rainbow is the sign of the covenant which God made with Noah the rainbow around the throne means that God has never forgotten that covenant it also means that God must listen to mans prayer if he prays according to the covenant"}
{"zh": "一\t我为什么忧惧疑惑？神岂未曾将我罪过", "en": "A. Why should I worry, doubt and fear? Has God not caused His Son to bear", "norm_zh": "一我为什么忧惧疑惑神岂未曾将我罪过", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Why should I worry doubt and fear Has God not caused His Son to bear"}
{"zh": "归祂儿子身上？主所为我还清的债，", "en": "My sins upon the tree? The debt that Christ for me has paid,", "norm_zh": "归祂儿子身上主所为我还清的债", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "My sins upon the tree The debt that Christ for me has paid"}
{"zh": "公义的神能否再来 要我重新清偿？", "en": "Can the righteous God demand payment again of me?", "norm_zh": "公义的神能否再来要我重新清偿", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Can the righteous God demand payment again of me"}
{"zh": "二\t你的救赎永远完全，你已还清每一文钱", "en": "B. Redemption full the Lord has made, And all my debts has fully paid,", "norm_zh": "二你的救赎永远完全你已还清每一文钱", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Redemption full the Lord has made And all my debts has fully paid"}
{"zh": "—我们所有罪戾；神的忿怒不能威胁，", "en": "—From law to set me free; I fear not for the wrath of God,", "norm_zh": "我们所有罪戾神的忿怒不能威胁", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "From law to set me free I fear not for the wrath of God"}
{"zh": "因我已经洒上宝血，靠恩已经称义。", "en": "For I've been sprinkled with His blood, It wholly covers me.", "norm_zh": "因我已经洒上宝血靠恩已经称义", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "For Ive been sprinkled with His blood It wholly covers me"}
{"zh": "三\t你既为我领得赦免，你既给我白白恩典", "en": "C. For me forgiveness He has gained, And full acquittal was obtained,", "norm_zh": "三你既为我领得赦免你既给我白白恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C For me forgiveness He has gained And full acquittal was obtained"}
{"zh": "—罪债一起清算；神就不会两面讨偿：", "en": "—All debts of sin are paid; God would not have His claim on two,", "norm_zh": "罪债一起清算神就不会两面讨偿", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "All debts of sin are paid God would not have His claim on two"}
{"zh": "先在我的中保身上……后又要我归还。", "en": "First on His Son, my Surety true, And then upon me laid.", "norm_zh": "先在我的中保身上后又要我归还", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "First on His Son my Surety true And then upon me laid"}
{"zh": "四\t所以我心，你当安息，你的救主所有功绩，", "en": "D. So now I have full peace and rest, My Savior Christ hath done the best", "norm_zh": "四所以我心你当安息你的救主所有功绩", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D So now I have full peace and rest My Savior Christ hath done the best"}
{"zh": "已使你得开释； 当信祂的有效宝血，", "en": "And set me wholly free; By His all-efficacious blood,", "norm_zh": "已使你得开释当信祂的有效宝血", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "And set me wholly free By His allefficacious blood"}
{"zh": "不怕神再将你弃绝，因主已为你死。", "en": "I ne'er could be condemned by God, For He has died for me!", "norm_zh": "不怕神再将你弃绝因主已为你死", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I neer could be condemned by God For He has died for me"}
{"zh": "一个罪人知道了自己是罪人，一相信主耶稣，他的罪就得着了赦免，这是毫无疑问的。但是，一个人已经信主，已经得着了赦免之后，还需要不需要赦免呢？要回答这个问题，我们必须先说明三点：", "en": "When a sinner knows that he is a sinner and believes in the Lord Jesus, his sins are forgiven. This is beyond doubt. The question is, after a person has believed in the Lord and received forgiveness, does he need to be forgiven further? In order to answer this question we must first consider three facts:", "norm_zh": "一个罪人知道了自己是罪人一相信主耶稣他的罪就得着了赦免这是毫无疑问的但是一个人已经信主已经得着了赦免之后还需要不需要赦免呢要回答这个问提我们必须先说明三点", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "When a sinner knows that he is a sinner and believes in the Lord Jesus his sins are forgiven This is beyond doubt The question is after a person has believed in the Lord and received forgiveness does he need to be forgiven further In order to answer this question we must first consider three facts"}
{"zh": "（一）一个人得救了之后，是不可仍在罪中活着（罗六），是不可再犯罪的（约五，八）。", "en": "1) After a person is saved, he should not continue to live in sin (Rom. 6:1-2), and he should not commit sin again (John 5:14; 8:11).", "norm_zh": "一一个人得救了之后是不可仍在罪中活着罗六是不可再犯罪的约五八", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 After a person is saved he should not continue to live in sin Rom 612 and he should not commit sin again John 514 811"}
{"zh": "（二）信徒仍有犯罪的可能（约壹一），有偶然被过犯所胜，被引诱跌倒的可能（加六，林前十）。象矶法的装假，象巴拿巴的随伙装假，象哥林多的那一个弟兄犯了淫乱的罪（犯这罪的后果是可怕的，一面肉体要败坏，一面被教会革除），都是事实。", "en": "2) There is still the possibility that a believer can commit sin (1 John 1:8, 10), and it is possible that a Christian can be overtaken in some offense and be tempted and fall (Gal. 6:1; 1 Cor. 10:12). There are the examples of Peter's hypocrisy in Antioch, Barnabas pretending with a group, and the brother in Corinth who committed fornication (Gal. 2:11-13; 1 Cor. 5:1-2, 5, 11). In the case of the brother who committed fornication, the consequence was very serious; on the one hand his body was corrupted, and on the other hand he was excommunicated by the church.", "norm_zh": "二信徒仍有犯罪的可能约壹一有偶然被过犯所胜被引诱跌倒的可能加六林前十象矶法的装假象巴拿巴的随伙装假象哥林多的哪一个弟兄犯了淫乱的罪犯这罪的后果是可怕的一面肉体要败坏一面被教会革除都是事实", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 There is still the possibility that a believer can commit sin 1 John 18 10 and it is possible that a Christian can be overtaken in some offense and be tempted and fall Gal 61 1 Cor 1012 There are the examples of Peters hypocrisy in Antioch Barnabas pretending with a group and the brother in Corinth who committed fornication Gal 21113 1 Cor 512 5 11 In the case of the brother who committed fornication the consequence was very serious on the one hand his body was corrupted and on the other hand he was excommunicated by the church"}
{"zh": "我们把以上三点弄清楚了之后，我们就要说，越与神有交通，越在神光中的人（神就是光，所以与神交通就是在光中），就越需要赦免，就越需要洗净，这是约壹一章五至七节清清楚楚地告诉我们的。那么，我们怎样能得着赦免呢？我们来看圣经怎么说。", "en": "If we are clear concerning these three points, we will admit that the more fellowship we have with God and the more we walk in the light of God, the more we need forgiveness and cleansing. God is light; therefore to have fellowship with God means to be in the light. This is shown clearly in 1 John 1:5-7. How then can we obtain forgiveness? Let us see what the Bible says.", "norm_zh": "我们把以上三点弄清楚了之后我们就要说越与神有交通越在神光中的人神就是光所以与神交通就是在光中就越需要赦免就越需要洗净这是约壹一章五至七节清清楚楚地告诉我们的哪么我们怎样能得着赦免呢我们来看圣经怎么说", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If we are clear concerning these three points we will admit that the more fellowship we have with God and the more we walk in the light of God the more we need forgiveness and cleansing God is light therefore to have fellowship with God means to be in the light This is shown clearly in 1 John 157 How then can we obtain forgiveness Let us see what the Bible says"}
{"zh": "约壹一章九节说，“我们若认自己的罪，神是信实的，是公义的，必要赦免我们的罪，洗净我们一切的不义。”这告诉我们，一个人信主之后若犯了罪，是需要承认才得着赦免。我们要“认自己的罪”！我们如果认了自己的罪，神是信实的，是公义的，必要赦免我们的罪，洗净我们一切的不义。什么叫神的信实？什么叫神的公义？神的信实，是指神的话语说的；神的公义，是指神的行事说的。神说话是信实的，神行事是公义的。祂既然说了必要赦免我们的罪，就必定赦免我们的罪；祂既然说了要洗净我们一切的不义，就必定洗净我们一切的不义。祂既然差遣祂的儿子为我们的罪死了，祂就不能不赦免我们的罪，不能不洗净我们一切的不义。所以，我们如果承认了自己的罪，就要抓住祂与我们所立的约，向祂求赦免，求洁净。", "en": "1 John 1:9 says, \"If we confess our sins, he is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins, and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness.\" It is clear from this verse that if a believer commits sin, he needs to confess it in order to be forgiven. We must \"confess our sins.\" If we confess our sins, God is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness. We might ask what God's faithfulness is and what God's righteousness is. God's faithfulness refers to the words which He speaks, while God's righteousness refers to the way in which He does things. In speaking God is faithful, and in acting God is righteous. Since He has said that He will forgive us our sins, He surely will forgive us our sins. Since He has said that He will cleanse us from all unrighteousness, He surely will cleanse us from all unrighteousness. Since He sent His Son to die for our sins, He cannot help but cleanse and forgive us our sins. Therefore, if we confess our sins, we must, by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us, expect Him to forgive and cleanse us.", "norm_zh": "约壹一章九节说我们若认自己的罪神是信实的是公义的必要赦免我们的罪洗净我们一切的不义这告诉我们一个人信主之后若犯了罪是需要承认才得着赦免我们要认自己的罪我们如果认了自己的罪神是信实的是公义的必要赦免我们的罪洗净我们一切的不义什么叫神的信实什么叫神的公义神的信实是指神的话语说的神的公义是指神的行事说的神说话是信实的神行事是公义的祂既然说了必要赦免我们的罪就必定赦免我们的罪祂既然说了要洗净我们一切的不义就必定洗净我们一切的不义祂既然差遣祂的儿子为我们的罪死了祂就不能不赦免我们的罪不能不洗净我们一切的不义所以我们如果承认了自己的罪就要抓住祂与我们所立的约向祂求赦免求洁净", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:08:10.518967+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 John 19 says If we confess our sins he is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness It is clear from this verse that if a believer commits sin he needs to confess it in order to be forgiven We must confess our sins If we confess our sins God is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and to cleanse us from all unrighteousness We might ask what Gods faithfulness is and what Gods righteousness is Gods faithfulness refers to the words which He speaks while Gods righteousness refers to the way in which He does things In speaking God is faithful and in acting God is righteous Since He has said that He will forgive us our sins He surely will forgive us our sins Since He has said that He will cleanse us from all unrighteousness He surely will cleanse us from all unrighteousness Since He sent His Son to die for our sins He cannot help but cleanse and forgive us our sins Therefore if we confess our sins we must by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us expect Him to forgive and cleanse us"}
{"zh": "壹\t新约的内容是包含三大部分，这是希伯来八章十至十二节告诉我们的：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "I. The contents of the new covenant include three major parts; this is what Hebrews 8:10-12 tells us:", "norm_zh": "壹新约的内容是包含三大部分这是希伯来八章十至十二节告诉我们的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The contents of the new covenant include three major parts this is what Hebrews 81012 tells us"}
{"zh": "一\t以神永远的目的来说，神是先把祂的生命和能力赐给我们；然后在生命的律里作我们的神，叫我们在生命的律里作祂的子民；叫我们在里面对于祂有更深的认识；赦罪不过是达到祂的目的的一个手续，所以圣经在这里把赦罪摆在最后说—来八10~12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. According to God's eternal purpose, He first imparted His life and power into us; then He became our God in the law of life that we might be His people in the law of life, that we might have a deeper knowledge of Him; since forgiveness of sins is only a procedure by which to achieve His purpose, Scripture puts forgiveness of sins at the very end—Heb. 8:10-12.", "norm_zh": "一以神永远的目的来说神是先把祂的生命和能力赐给我们然后在生命的律里作我们的神叫我们在生命的律里作祂的子民叫我们在里面对于祂有更深的认识赦罪不过是达到祂的目的的一个手续所以圣经在这里把赦罪摆在最后说来八1012李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A According to Gods eternal purpose He first imparted His life and power into us then He became our God in the law of life that we might be His people in the law of life that we might have a deeper knowledge of Him since forgiveness of sins is only a procedure by which to achieve His purpose Scripture puts forgiveness of sins at the very endHeb 81012"}
{"zh": "二\t以我们属灵的经历来说，我们总是先得洁净（因罪得赦免而得的洁净），然后在生命的律里作神的子民，在里面对于神有更深的认识—8~12节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. According to our spiritual experience, we first obtain cleansing (the cleansing which comes from forgiveness), then we become God's people in the law of life, and then we possess a deeper knowledge of God in an inward way—vv. 8-12.", "norm_zh": "二以我们属灵的经历来说我们总是先得洁净因罪得赦免而得的洁净然后在生命的律里作神的子民在里面对于神有更深的认识812节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to our spiritual experience we first obtain cleansing the cleansing which comes from forgiveness then we become Gods people in the law of life and then we possess a deeper knowledge of God in an inward wayvv 812"}
{"zh": "贰\t凭圣经来看，罪，是有“罪性”与“罪行”的分别的—罗五12，约壹一7：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "II. According to the Scriptures, sin has two aspects: the nature of sin and the act of sin—Rom. 5:12; 1 John 1:7:", "norm_zh": "贰凭圣经来看罪是有罪性与罪行的分别的罗五12约壹一7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II According to the Scriptures sin has two aspects the nature of sin and the act of sinRom 512 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "一\t罪性，是“住在人里面的罪”，是罪在人里面作主，辖制人、主使人去犯罪的—罗五12，约壹一8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. The nature of sin is \"sin that dwells in man,\" mastering and governing him and inciting him to commit sins—Rom. 5:12; 1 John 1:8.", "norm_zh": "一罪性是住在人里面的罪是罪在人里面作主辖制人主使人去犯罪的罗五12约壹一8李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The nature of sin is sin that dwells in man mastering and governing him and inciting him to commit sinsRom 512 1 John 18"}
{"zh": "二\t罪行，是“显在人外面的罪”，是在人日常生活中所显出的—罗六6，约壹一7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. Sinful acts are \"the sins which are manifested outwardly,\" which are manifested in our daily life—Rom. 6:6; 1 John 1:7.", "norm_zh": "二罪行是显在人外面的罪是在人日常生活中所显出的罗六6约壹一7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Sinful acts are the sins which are manifested outwardly which are manifested in our daily lifeRom 66 1 John 17"}
{"zh": "三\t所以，罪行是需要得着赦免，得着洗净的；罪性是需要脱离，需要得着释放的—7~8节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "C. Therefore, the sinful acts need to be forgiven and cleansed, but we also need to be delivered and released from our sinful nature—vv. 7-8.", "norm_zh": "三所以罪行是需要得着赦免得着洗净的罪性是需要脱离需要得着释放的78节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Therefore the sinful acts need to be forgiven and cleansed but we also need to be delivered and released from our sinful naturevv 78"}
{"zh": "四\t主耶稣的血是对付我们在神面前的罪状，是洗净我们的良心的—太二六28，启一5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "D. The blood of the Lord Jesus deals with the charges of sin against us before God and purifies our conscience—Matt. 26:28; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "四主耶稣的血是对付我们在神面前的罪状是洗净我们的良心的太二六28启一5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The blood of the Lord Jesus deals with the charges of sin against us before God and purifies our conscienceMatt 2628 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "五\t主耶稣的十字架，是对付我们的旧人，是叫我们脱离罪的权势，从罪得着释放的—罗六6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "E. The cross of the Lord Jesus deals with our old man, delivering us from the power of sin and freeing us from sin itself—Rom. 6:6.", "norm_zh": "五主耶稣的十字架是对付我们的旧人是叫我们脱离罪的权势从罪得着释放的罗六6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The cross of the Lord Jesus deals with our old man delivering us from the power of sin and freeing us from sin itselfRom 66"}
{"zh": "叁\t罪需要赦免—约壹一9，太二六28，来九22，约壹二12，徒十43：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "III. Sins Need to be Forgiven—1 John 1:9; Matt. 26:28; Heb. 9:22; 1 John 2:12; Acts 10:43:", "norm_zh": "叁罪需要赦免约壹一9太二六28来九22约壹二12徒十43李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Sins Need to be Forgiven1 John 19 Matt 2628 Heb 922 1 John 212 Acts 1043"}
{"zh": "一\t一个真被圣灵光照的人，没有不为罪自己责备自己的；就是在这样的时候，神的赦免是他所需要的—约十六8、13：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. A person who is truly enlightened by the Holy Spirit cannot help but condemn himself concerning sin; it is at this moment he needs God's forgiveness.—John 16:8, 13:", "norm_zh": "一一个真被圣灵光照的人没有不为罪自己责备自己的就是在这样的时候神的赦免是他所需要的约十六813李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A A person who is truly enlightened by the Holy Spirit cannot help but condemn himself concerning sin it is at this moment he needs Gods forgivenessJohn 168 13"}
{"zh": "1\t就在这样的时候，有一个福音传给我们说，主耶稣被钉在十字架上，流出祂的宝血，就是要使罪得赦，就是要使人的罪恶得洗去—太二六28，启一5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "1. Perhaps at this time the gospel is preached telling how the Lord Jesus was crucified on the cross and how He shed His precious blood for the forgiveness of sin that men might be washed of their sin.—Matt. 26:28; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "1就在这样的时候有一个福音传给我们说主耶稣被钉在十字架上流出祂的宝血就是要使罪得赦就是要使人的罪恶得洗去太二六28启一5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Perhaps at this time the gospel is preached telling how the Lord Jesus was crucified on the cross and how He shed His precious blood for the forgiveness of sin that men might be washed of their sinMatt 2628 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "2\t我们听见了这福音，我们一信，我们的罪就得赦免了，我们的良心就得洗净了—徒十43，二六18，来九14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "2. When a person hears this gospel and believes, his sins are forgiven and his conscience is purified.—Acts 10:43; 26:18; Heb. 9:14.", "norm_zh": "2我们听见了这福音我们一信我们的罪就得赦免了我们的良心就得洗净了徒十43二六18来九14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When a person hears this gospel and believes his sins are forgiven and his conscience is purifiedActs 1043 2618 Heb 914"}
{"zh": "二\t“你的罪赦免了。……你的信救了你，平平安安地回去吧”；这一个赦免，在她真是一个大的福音！这一个赦免，叫她不再暗自悲伤；这一个赦免，叫她满了平安—路七36~50。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. \"Thy sins are forgiven.... Thy faith hath saved thee; go in peace\"; this forgiveness to her was a great gospel! It enabled her to no longer feel sorry for herself, but rather to be full of peace.—Luke 7:36-50.", "norm_zh": "二你的罪赦免了你的信救了你平平安安地回去吧这一个赦免在她真是一个大的福音这一个赦免叫她不再暗自悲伤这一个赦免叫她满了平安路七3650李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Thy sins are forgiven Thy faith hath saved thee go in peace this forgiveness to her was a great gospel It enabled her to no longer feel sorry for herself but rather to be full of peaceLuke 73650"}
{"zh": "三\t圣经给我们看见，有的病是犯罪的结果—可二3~12，约五14：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "C. The Scriptures indicate that some illnesses are the result of committing sin.—Mark 2:3-12; John 5:14:", "norm_zh": "三圣经给我们看见有的病是犯罪的结果可二312约五14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Scriptures indicate that some illnesses are the result of committing sinMark 2312 John 514"}
{"zh": "1\t主知道这一个瘫子的病因是罪，所以先对他说，“小子，你的罪赦了”；然后再对他说，“我吩咐你起来，拿你的褥子回家去吧”—可二5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "1. The Lord knew that with this man sick of palsy, the cause of his illness was sin. For this reason He first spoke to the sick man, \"Son, thy sins are forgiven\"; then He said, \"I say unto thee, Arise, take up thy bed, and go unto thy house.\"—Mark 2:5.", "norm_zh": "1主知道这一个瘫子的病因是罪所以先对他说小子你的罪赦了然后再对他说我吩咐你起来拿你的褥子回家去吧可二5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lord knew that with this man sick of palsy the cause of his illness was sin For this reason He first spoke to the sick man Son thy sins are forgiven then He said I say unto thee Arise take up thy bed and go unto thy houseMark 25"}
{"zh": "2\t哦，罪得赦了，病也得治了，这是何等大的福音！—5、10~12节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "2. The sins were forgiven and the sickness was healed. What a great gospel this is!—vv. 5, 10-12.", "norm_zh": "2哦罪得赦了病也得治了这是何等大的福音51012节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The sins were forgiven and the sickness was healed What a great gospel this isvv 5 1012"}
{"zh": "肆\t赦免是靠神的义—太二六28，来一8~9：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "IV. Forgiveness is Based Upon God's Righteousness—Matt. 26:28; Heb. 1:8-9:", "norm_zh": "肆赦免是靠神的义太二六28来一89李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Forgiveness is Based Upon Gods RighteousnessMatt 2628 Heb 189"}
{"zh": "一\t我们的神是圣洁的神，是喜爱公义，恨恶罪恶的神—彼前一15~16，来一9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. Our God is not only a holy God, but One who loves righteousness and hates lawlessness.—1 Pet. 1:15-16; Heb. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "一我们的神是圣洁的神是喜爱公义恨恶罪恶的神彼前一1516来一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Our God is not only a holy God but One who loves righteousness and hates lawlessness1 Pet 11516 Heb 19"}
{"zh": "二\t我们犯了罪，神不能不定我们的罪；按着神的性情来说，祂是圣洁的，所以祂不能容让罪；按着神作事的手续来说，祂是公义的，所以祂不能不刑罚罪；按着祂的自己说，祂是荣耀的，所以罪人不能亲近祂，亲近祂的就必定死—罗八3，提前六16。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. Whenever we commit sin, God must condemn us for our sin; according to God's nature He is holy; therefore, He cannot tolerate sin; according to God's way of doing things, He is righteous; therefore, He must punish sin; in Himself God is also glorious; for this reason sinners cannot approach Him, and those who do approach Him will surely die.—Rom. 8:3; 1 Tim. 6:16.", "norm_zh": "二我们犯了罪神不能不定我们的罪按着神的性情来说祂是圣洁的所以祂不能容让罪按着神作事的手续来说祂是公义的所以祂不能不刑罚罪按着祂的自己说祂是荣耀的所以罪人不能亲近祂亲近祂的就必定死罗八3提前六16李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Whenever we commit sin God must condemn us for our sin according to Gods nature He is holy therefore He cannot tolerate sin according to Gods way of doing things He is righteous therefore He must punish sin in Himself God is also glorious for this reason sinners cannot approach Him and those who do approach Him will surely dieRom 83 1 Tim 616"}
{"zh": "三\t恩典从来没有自己作王，恩典乃是借着义作王的；神乃是先审判了我们的罪，然后才赦免我们的—罗五17~21，赛五三。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "C. Grace never reigns by itself; grace reigns through righteousness; first God judges our sins; then He forgives us—Rom. 5:17-21; Isa. 53.", "norm_zh": "三恩典从来没有自己作王恩典乃是借着义作王的神乃是先审判了我们的罪然后才赦免我们的罗五1721赛五三李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Grace never reigns by itself grace reigns through righteousness first God judges our sins then He forgives usRom 51721 Isa 53"}
{"zh": "四\t凡受过恩典的教训的人就要说，我们的神赦免人的罪，是恩义两全的—罗五18~21。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "D. Those who are taught by grace realize that God's way of forgiving men their sins is perfect in both grace and righteousness—Rom. 5:18-21.", "norm_zh": "四凡受过恩典的教训的人就要说我们的神赦免人的罪是恩义两全的罗五1821李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Those who are taught by grace realize that Gods way of forgiving men their sins is perfect in both grace and righteousnessRom 51821"}
{"zh": "伍\t赦免是新约的特点—来八12，十17，二17：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "V. Forgiveness is the Characteristic of the New Covenant—Heb. 8:12; 10:17; 2:17:", "norm_zh": "伍赦免是新约的特点来八12十17二17李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Forgiveness is the Characteristic of the New CovenantHeb 812 1017 217"}
{"zh": "一\t希伯来八章十二节：“我要宽恕他们的不义，不再记念他们的罪愆”；这是新约所给我们的福分之一；这是指神在基督里赦免我们的罪说的：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. Hebrews 8:12: \"For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses, and their sins I will by no means remember anymore\"; this is one of the blessings given to us in the new covenant; this refers to God's forgiving us our sins in Christ:", "norm_zh": "一希伯来八章十二节我要宽恕他们的不义不再记念他们的罪愆这是新约所给我们的福分之一这是指神在基督里赦免我们的罪说的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hebrews 812 For I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses and their sins I will by no means remember anymore this is one of the blessings given to us in the new covenant this refers to Gods forgiving us our sins in Christ"}
{"zh": "1\t神把我们的罪愆都忘记了，不是祂掩面不看，或者故意遗忘，乃是因基督的血把我们的罪状涂抹了，把我们的罪恶洗去了—赛四四21~22，来一3，启一5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "1. God's forgetting of our sins is not that He hides His face or purposely ignores them, but that Christ's blood has blotted out the charges of sin against us and washed us from our sins—Isa. 44:21-22; Heb. 1:3; Rev. 1:5.", "norm_zh": "1神把我们的罪愆都忘记了不是祂掩面不看或者故意遗忘乃是因基督的血把我们的罪状涂抹了把我们的罪恶洗去了赛四四2122来一3启一5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods forgetting of our sins is not that He hides His face or purposely ignores them but that Christs blood has blotted out the charges of sin against us and washed us from our sinsIsa 442122 Heb 13 Rev 15"}
{"zh": "2\t神今天是把祂自己约束在约里，祂乐意受约的限制；祂说“要宽恕我们的不义”，就必定宽恕我们的不义；祂说“不再记念我们的罪愆”，就必定不再记念我们的罪愆。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "2. Today God is confining Himself to the covenant; He is willing to be restricted by the covenant; when He said, \"I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses,\" He will do it; and when He said, \"their sins I will by no means remember anymore,\" He will not remember.", "norm_zh": "2神今天是把祂自己约束在约里祂乐意受约的限制祂说要宽恕我们的不义就必定宽恕我们的不义祂说不再记念我们的罪愆就必定不再记念我们的罪愆李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Today God is confining Himself to the covenant He is willing to be restricted by the covenant when He said I will be propitious to their unrighteousnesses He will do it and when He said their sins I will by no means remember anymore He will not remember"}
{"zh": "二\t神看见了主耶稣的血，就赦免了我们的罪，就不再记念我们的罪愆；这是新约的特点—九12~14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. When God sees the blood of the Lord Jesus, He forgives our sins and by no means remembers them anymore; this is a characteristic of the new covenant—Heb. 9:12-14.", "norm_zh": "二神看见了主耶稣的血就赦免了我们的罪就不再记念我们的罪愆这是新约的特点九1214李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When God sees the blood of the Lord Jesus He forgives our sins and by no means remembers them anymore this is a characteristic of the new covenantHeb 91214"}
{"zh": "陆\t认罪与赦免—约壹一5~7、9，诗三二5，箴二八13，太二六28：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "VI. Confession of Sin and Forgiveness—1 John 1:5-7, 9; Psa. 32:5; Prov. 28:13; Matt. 26:28:", "norm_zh": "陆认罪与赦免约壹一579诗三二5箴二八13太二六28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Confession of Sin and Forgiveness1 John 157 9 Psa 325 Prov 2813 Matt 2628"}
{"zh": "一\t一个人得救了之后，是不可仍在罪中活着，是不可再犯罪的—罗六，约五14，八11。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "A. After a person is saved, he must not continue to live in sin and must not sin anymore—Rom. 6, John 5:14, 8:11.", "norm_zh": "一一个人得救了之后是不可仍在罪中活着是不可再犯罪的罗六约五14八11李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A After a person is saved he must not continue to live in sin and must not sin anymoreRom 6 John 514 811"}
{"zh": "二\t信徒仍有犯罪的可能，有偶然被过犯所胜，被引诱跌倒的可能—约壹一5~10，加六1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "B. Believers still have the possibility of sinning, of being overtaken in some offense, and of being tempted to fall—1 John 1:5-10; Gal. 6:1.", "norm_zh": "二信徒仍有犯罪的可能有偶然被过犯所胜被引诱跌倒的可能约壹一510加六1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Believers still have the possibility of sinning of being overtaken in some offense and of being tempted to fall1 John 1510 Gal 61"}
{"zh": "三\t约壹三章九节说，“凡从神生的，就不犯罪，因为神的种住在他里面；他也不能犯罪，因为他是由神生的”；这乃是就重生之人的习惯与性质而言。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "C. In 1 John 3:9 we read that \"Whosoever is begotten of God doeth no sin, because his seed abideth in him: and he cannot sin, because he is begotten of God\"; this refers to the habit and nature of a regenerated person.", "norm_zh": "三约壹三章九节说凡从神生的就不犯罪因为神的种住在他里面他也不能犯罪因为他是由神生的这乃是就重生之人的习惯与性质而言李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In 1 John 39 we read that Whosoever is begotten of God doeth no sin because his seed abideth in him and he cannot sin because he is begotten of God this refers to the habit and nature of a regenerated person"}
{"zh": "四\t约壹一章九节说，“我们若认自己的罪，神是信实的，是公义的，必要赦免我们的罪，洗净我们一切的不义”：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "D. First John 1:9 says, \"If we confess our sins, God is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness\":", "norm_zh": "四约壹一章九节说我们若认自己的罪神是信实的是公义的必要赦免我们的罪洗净我们一切的不义李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D First John 19 says If we confess our sins God is faithful and righteous to forgive us our sins and cleanse us from all unrighteousness"}
{"zh": "1\t我们如果承认了自己的罪，就要抓住祂与我们所立的约，向祂求赦免，求洁净—9节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "1. If we confess our sins, we must, by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us, expect Him to forgive and cleanse us.—v. 9.", "norm_zh": "1我们如果承认了自己的罪就要抓住祂与我们所立的约向祂求赦免求洁净9节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 If we confess our sins we must by taking hold of the covenant which He has made with us expect Him to forgive and cleanse usv 9"}
{"zh": "2\t赦罪是约里的事；我们若按着神的话来认罪，神必按着祂的约赦免我们的罪—徒十43。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "2. Forgiveness of sins is something in the covenant; if we confess according to God's Word, God will forgive us according to His covenant.—Acts 10:43.", "norm_zh": "2赦罪是约里的事我们若按着神的话来认罪神必按着祂的约赦免我们的罪徒十43李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Forgiveness of sins is something in the covenant if we confess according to Gods Word God will forgive us according to His covenantActs 1043"}
{"zh": "3\t神与我们立约，就是要我们按着约来对祂说话；祂要我们用信心求祂；我们求神为我们成就约里的话—来十23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "3. God has made a covenant with us so that we may speak to Him according to His covenant; He wants us to ask by faith that He fulfill what is in the covenant—Heb. 10:23", "norm_zh": "3神与我们立约就是要我们按着约来对祂说话祂要我们用信心求祂我们求神为我们成就约里的话来十23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 God has made a covenant with us so that we may speak to Him according to His covenant He wants us to ask by faith that He fulfill what is in the covenantHeb 1023"}
{"zh": "4\t这里所说的认罪，是在神的光照之下看见了罪；神的光是不容让任何一件罪的；人在神光照之下看见了罪，并且定罪为罪，而来到神面前认罪，神是要赦免这样的人的罪，洗净这样的人的不义—约壹一7、9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "4. The confession referred to here is something we do after seeing sin in God's light; God's light does not tolerate sin; when a person truly sees sin in God's light, condemns sin as sin, and comes to God to confess his sin, God will forgive such a person's sin and cleanse his unrighteousness—1 John 1:7, 9.", "norm_zh": "4这里所说的认罪是在神的光照之下看见了罪神的光是不容让任何一件罪的人在神光照之下看见了罪并且定罪为罪而来到神面前认罪神是要赦免这样的人的罪洗净这样的人的不义约壹一79李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The confession referred to here is something we do after seeing sin in Gods light Gods light does not tolerate sin when a person truly sees sin in Gods light condemns sin as sin and comes to God to confess his sin God will forgive such a persons sin and cleanse his unrighteousness1 John 17 9"}
{"zh": "5\t至于有的人把认罪当作护身符似的，他天天在宝血之下说谎，天天在宝血之下发脾气，这是断乎不可的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "5. Some people take shelter in the confession of sin: day by day they continue to speak lies under the precious blood, and day by day they continue to lose their temper under the precious blood — this is definitely wrong.", "norm_zh": "5至于有的人把认罪当作护身符似的他天天在宝血之下说谎天天在宝血之下发脾气这是断乎不可的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Some people take shelter in the confession of sin day by day they continue to speak lies under the precious blood and day by day they continue to lose their temper under the precious blood this is definitely wrong"}
{"zh": "6\t启示录四章三节说，“又有虹围着宝座”；虹是什么记号呢？虹是神与挪亚立约的记号；虹围着宝座，就是说神绝没有忘记祂所立的约，也就是说神绝不能不听人在约里的祷告。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第六章）", "en": "6. Revelation 4:3 says, \"And there was a rainbow around the throne\"; what sign is the rainbow? The rainbow is the sign of the covenant which God made with Noah; the rainbow around the throne means that God has never forgotten that covenant, which also means that God must listen to man's prayer if he prays according to the covenant.", "norm_zh": "6启示录四章三节说又有虹围着宝座虹是什么记号呢虹是神与挪亚立约的记号虹围着宝座就是说神绝没有忘记祂所立的约也就是说神绝不能不听人在约里的祷告李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第六章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:10:40.100202+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Revelation 43 says And there was a rainbow around the throne what sign is the rainbow The rainbow is the sign of the covenant which God made with Noah the rainbow around the throne means that God has never forgotten that covenant which also means that God must listen to mans prayer if he prays according to the covenant"}
{"zh": "读经：约壹二29，五4、6、14、18，来八10，弗三17上，诗四4，可四28，箴四23，结三六26", "en": "Scripture Reading: 1 John 2:29; 5:4, 6, 14, 18; Heb. 8:10; Eph. 3:17a; Psa. 4:4; Mark 4:28; Prov. 4:23; Ezek. 36:26", "norm_zh": "读经约壹二29五461418来八10弗三17上诗四4可四28箴四23结三六26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 1 John 229 54 6 14 18 Heb 810 Eph 317a Psa 44 Mark 428 Prov 423 Ezek 3626"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要说到神如何把律法放在我们里面，写在我们心上，我们还得从重生说起；因为重生是圣灵把神非受造的生命放在人的灵里，重生乃是生命的问题—约壹二29，五4、6、14、18：", "en": "I. When speaking of how God has put His law within us and has inscribed it upon our hearts, we must start from regeneration; for regeneration means that the Holy Spirit has put the uncreated life of God into man's spirit; regeneration is a matter of life.—1 John 2:29; 5:4, 6, 14, 18:", "norm_zh": "壹我们要说到神如何把律法放在我们里面写在我们心上我们还得从重生说起因为重生是圣灵把神非受造的生命放在人的灵里重生乃是生命的问提约壹二29五461418", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I When speaking of how God has put His law within us and has inscribed it upon our hearts we must start from regeneration for regeneration means that the Holy Spirit has put the uncreated life of God into mans spirit regeneration is a matter of life1 John 229 54 6 14 18"}
{"zh": "一\t要说到重生，我们还得从人的创造说起；创世记二章七节说，“耶和华神用地上的尘土造人，将生命的气吹在他的鼻孔里，他就成了一个活的魂”：", "en": "A. Before we can speak adequately of regeneration we must say something regarding the creation of man; we read in Genesis 2:7 that \"Jehovah God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul\":", "norm_zh": "一要说到重生我们还得从人的创造说起创世记二章七节说耶和华神用地上的尘土造人将生命的气吹在他的鼻孔里他就成了一个活的魂", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we can speak adequately of regeneration we must say something regarding the creation of man we read in Genesis 27 that Jehovah God formed man of the dust of the ground and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life and man became a living soul"}
{"zh": "1\t神将生命的气吹入人的身体就成为灵，同时这灵与身体接触，就产生了魂；这是我们里面属灵、属魂两个生命的来源—创二7。", "en": "1. When God breathed the breath of life into man's body, it became the spirit; and at the same time, when this spirit came into contact with the body, it produced the soul; this is the way in which the spiritual life and the soulish life originated in man.—Gen. 2:7.", "norm_zh": "1神将生命的气吹入人的身体就成为灵同时这灵与身体接触就产生了魂这是我们里面属灵属魂两个生命的来源创二7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When God breathed the breath of life into mans body it became the spirit and at the same time when this spirit came into contact with the body it produced the soul this is the way in which the spiritual life and the soulish life originated in manGen 27"}
{"zh": "2\t一个人是分作三部分的，就是灵、魂、体；新约圣经也是这样把人分作三部分；象帖前五章二十三节说，“又愿你们的灵，与魂，与身子，得蒙保守。”", "en": "2. Man is composed of three parts: the spirit, the soul, and the body; the New Testament also shows that man is tripartite; as 1 Thes. 5:23 says, \"May your spirit and soul and body be preserved entire.\"", "norm_zh": "2一个人是分作三部分的就是灵魂体新约圣经也是这样把人分作三部分象帖前五章二十三节说又愿你们的灵与魂与身子得蒙保守", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Man is composed of three parts the spirit the soul and the body the New Testament also shows that man is tripartite as 1 Thes 523 says May your spirit and soul and body be preserved entire"}
{"zh": "3\t体就是“世界知觉”的所在，魂就是“自己知觉”的所在，灵就是“神知觉”的所在—约四24，太十六26，罗八11。", "en": "3. The body is the seat of world-consciousness; the soul is the seat of self-consciousness; and the spirit is the seat of God-consciousness.—John 4:24; Matt. 16:26; Rom. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "3体就是世界知觉的所在魂就是自己知觉的所在灵就是神知觉的所在约四24太十六26罗八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The body is the seat of worldconsciousness the soul is the seat of selfconsciousness and the spirit is the seat of GodconsciousnessJohn 424 Matt 1626 Rom 811"}
{"zh": "4\t灵借着魂管理全人：灵要有动作，就达意于魂，魂就运动身体，以服从灵的命令—帖前五23节注5：", "en": "4. Through the soul, the spirit controls man's whole being. Whenever the spirit wants to do something, it passes its intention on to the soul, and the soul exercises the body to obey the command from the spirit.—1 Thes. 5:23, note 5:", "norm_zh": "4灵借着魂管理全人灵要有动作就达意于魂魂就运动身体以服从灵的命令帖前五23节注5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Through the soul the spirit controls mans whole being Whenever the spirit wants to do something it passes its intention on to the soul and the soul exercises the body to obey the command from the spirit1 Thes 523 note 5"}
{"zh": "a\t按着神的安排，灵乃是最高的部分，应当管治全人。", "en": "a. According to God's arrangement, the human spirit is the highest part of man and should rule his whole being.", "norm_zh": "a按着神的安排灵乃是最高的部分应当管治全人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a According to Gods arrangement the human spirit is the highest part of man and should rule his whole being"}
{"zh": "b\t然而意志是人格最主要的部分，又是属于魂的；人（魂）的意志能有自主的权柄，它可以拣选到底是由灵来掌权，或是由体来掌权，还是由己来掌权—徒十一23。", "en": "b. Yet, the will is the most prominent part of man's personality and belongs to the soul. The will of man is also able to make its own choice. It can choose whether to be ruled by the spirit, by the body, or by the self.—Acts 11:23.", "norm_zh": "b然而意志是人格最主要的部分又是属于魂的人魂的意志能有自主的权柄它可以拣选到底是由灵来掌权或是由体来掌权还是由己来掌权徒十一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Yet the will is the most prominent part of mans personality and belongs to the soul The will of man is also able to make its own choice It can choose whether to be ruled by the spirit by the body or by the selfActs 1123"}
{"zh": "二\t神造人的目的；神有一个永远的目的，就是要把祂自己给人—创二9、16：", "en": "B. God's purpose in creating man; God has an eternal purpose, which is to give Himself to man—Gen. 2:9, 16:", "norm_zh": "二神造人的目的神有一个永远的目的就是要把祂自己给人创二916", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Gods purpose in creating man God has an eternal purpose which is to give Himself to manGen 29 16"}
{"zh": "1\t人原来是神所创造的，所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的；以人原来受造的生命来说，是正直的，是好的—二7，传七29，创一26。", "en": "1. Originally man was made by God; man's original life was made by God also; as far as man's original created life was concerned, it was upright and it was good.—2:7; Eccl. 7:29; Gen. 1:26.", "norm_zh": "1人原来是神所创造的所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的以人原来受造的生命来说是正直的是好的二7传七29创一26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Originally man was made by God mans original life was made by God also as far as mans original created life was concerned it was upright and it was good27 Eccl 729 Gen 126"}
{"zh": "2\t但是，以神永远的目的来说，人还没有神自己那非受造的生命；所以，人还需要拣选神，需要拣选神的生命—二16~17。", "en": "2. But as far as God's eternal purpose, man had not yet received the uncreated life of God; therefore, man still needed to choose God and God's life.—2:16-17.", "norm_zh": "2但是以神永远的目的来说人还没有神自己哪非受造的生命所以人还需要拣选神需要拣选神的生命二1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 But as far as Gods eternal purpose man had not yet received the uncreated life of God therefore man still needed to choose God and Gods life21617"}
{"zh": "三\t人的堕落—17节，三6，弗二1、5，西二13，来九27：", "en": "C. Man's Fall—v. 17; 3:6; Eph. 2:1, 5; Col. 2:13; Heb. 9:27:", "norm_zh": "三人的堕落17节三6弗二15西二13来九27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Mans Fallv 17 36 Eph 21 5 Col 213 Heb 927"}
{"zh": "1\t那人（亚当）竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子，竟然不拣选生命，人堕落了，人犯罪了—创三6。", "en": "1. The man Adam did not choose life. He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eat.—Gen. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1哪人亚当竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子竟然不拣选生命人堕落了人犯罪了创三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The man Adam did not choose life He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eatGen 36"}
{"zh": "2\t当初神对亚当说，“你吃的日子必定死”；所以这里的死，不只是肉体要死，必定是灵先死了；死的意思就是远离生命；乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通，已经失去他敏锐的知觉—二17，弗二1。", "en": "2. At the beginning God said to Adam, \"In the day that you eat of it you shall surely die\"; therefore, the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires; death simply means to be estranged from life; it means that his spirit has lost its fellowship with God, it has lost its keen sense.—Gen. 2:17; Eph. 2:1.", "norm_zh": "2当初神对亚当说你吃的日子必定死所以这里的死不只是肉体要死必定是灵先死了死的意思就是远离生命乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通已经失去他敏锐的知觉二17弗二1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 At the beginning God said to Adam In the day that you eat of it you shall surely die therefore the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires death simply means to be estranged from life it means that his spirit has lost its fellowship with God it has lost its keen senseGen 217 Eph 21"}
{"zh": "3\t祂既然有了一个美意，祂既然有了一个永远的计划，祂就必定要成功祂永远的旨意；祂要来解决人的罪，将堕落的人救回；祂要借着祂的儿子将祂的生命释放出来；祂要借着圣灵来重生人—约十二24。", "en": "3. Since He has a good pleasure and since He has an eternal plan, He will accomplish His eternal will; He has to solve the problem of man's sin and redeem fallen man; He has to release His life through His Son, and He has to regenerate man through the Holy Spirit.—John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "3祂既然有了一个美意祂既然有了一个永远的计划祂就必定要成功祂永远的旨意祂要来解决人的罪将堕落的人救回祂要借着祂的儿子将祂的生命释放出来祂要借着圣灵来重生人约十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Since He has a good pleasure and since He has an eternal plan He will accomplish His eternal will He has to solve the problem of mans sin and redeem fallen man He has to release His life through His Son and He has to regenerate man through the Holy SpiritJohn 1224"}
{"zh": "四\t神的救法—彼前二24，西三3，赛五三11~12，来九28，民二一9：", "en": "D. The Way of God's Salvation—1 Pet. 2:24; Col. 3:3; Isa. 53:11-12; Heb. 9:28; Num. 21:9:", "norm_zh": "四神的救法彼前二24西三3赛五三1112来九28民二一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Way of Gods Salvation1 Pet 224 Col 33 Isa 531112 Heb 928 Num 219"}
{"zh": "1\t基督在十字架上，亲身担当了我们的罪，就是“使我们既然在罪上死，就得以在义上活”；这就是摩西在旷野举蛇所预表的—彼前二24，民二一9，约三14，罗八3。", "en": "1. Christ Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross, \"that we, having died unto sins, might live unto righteousness\"; this was typified when Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness.—1 Pet. 2:24; Num. 21:9; John 3:14; Rom. 8:3.", "norm_zh": "1基督在十字架上亲身担当了我们的罪就是使我们既然在罪上死就得以在义上活这就是摩西在旷野举蛇所预表的彼前二24民二一9约三14罗八3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christ Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross that we having died unto sins might live unto righteousness this was typified when Moses lifted up the serpent in the wilderness1 Pet 224 Num 219 John 314 Rom 83"}
{"zh": "2\t基督在十字架上受死，就将祂（基督）里面所藏着的神的生命释放出来；因为基督就是那一粒麦子落在地里死了，神的生命就释放出来了—约十二24。", "en": "2. The life of God which is in Christ was released when Christ died on the cross; for Christ is the grain of wheat which fell into the earth and died, and God's life was released.—John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "2基督在十字架上受死就将祂基督里面所藏着的神的生命释放出来因为基督就是哪一粒麦子落在地里死了神的生命就释放出来了约十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The life of God which is in Christ was released when Christ died on the cross for Christ is the grain of wheat which fell into the earth and died and Gods life was releasedJohn 1224"}
{"zh": "3\t所以神借耶稣基督从死里复活，就重生了我们—彼前一3。", "en": "3. Therefore, God regenerated us through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.—1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "3所以神借耶稣基督从死里复活就重生了我们彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Therefore God regenerated us through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "五\t重生，是“从水和圣灵生的”—约三3~8：", "en": "E. Regeneration is to be \"born of the water and of the Spirit\"—John 3:3-8:", "norm_zh": "五重生是从水和圣灵生的约三38", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Regeneration is to be born of the water and of the SpiritJohn 338"}
{"zh": "1\t人因着悔改而进入水，人因着相信而进入圣灵；人这样进入水，又进入圣灵，就是从水和圣灵生的—徒二38，二十21。", "en": "1. Because of repentance man enters into the water, and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit; by entering into the water and the Spirit, he is born of water and of the Spirit.—Acts 2:38; 20:21.", "norm_zh": "1人因着悔改而进入水人因着相信而进入圣灵人这样进入水又进入圣灵就是从水和圣灵生的徒二38二十21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Because of repentance man enters into the water and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit by entering into the water and the Spirit he is born of water and of the SpiritActs 238 2021"}
{"zh": "2\t悔改而进入水，就结束了旧人的生命；相信而进入圣灵，就得着了神的生命；这样一来，就是重生—二38。", "en": "2. Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man; by believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain God's life; this is regeneration.—Acts 2:38.", "norm_zh": "2悔改而进入水就结束了旧人的生命相信而进入圣灵就得着了神的生命这样一来就是重生二38", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man by believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain Gods life this is regenerationActs 238"}
{"zh": "3\t使人重生的工作，在主观方面，完全是圣灵自己作的（在客观方面，完全是基督作的）；所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到“从水生”，而三次提到“从圣灵生”—约三3、5~6、8。", "en": "3. The work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit (objectively, it is accomplished completely by Christ); therefore, in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being \"born of water,\" while he mentioned being \"born of the Spirit\" three times.—John 3:3, 5-6, 8.", "norm_zh": "3使人重生的工作在主观方面完全是圣灵自己作的在客观方面完全是基督作的所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到从水生而三次提到从圣灵生约三3568", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit objectively it is accomplished completely by Christ therefore in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being born of water while he mentioned being born of the Spirit three timesJohn 33 56 8"}
{"zh": "六\t重生，是“从圣灵生”；圣灵来叫人悔改，叫人“为罪……自己责备自己”—5节，十六8。", "en": "F. Regeneration means that we have been \"born of the Spirit\"; the Spirit comes to \"convict the world concerning sin\" and cause man to repent.—v. 5; 16:8.", "norm_zh": "六重生是从圣灵生圣灵来叫人悔改叫人为罪自己责备自己5节十六8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Regeneration means that we have been born of the Spirit the Spirit comes to convict the world concerning sin and cause man to repentv 5 168"}
{"zh": "七\t重生不是别的，乃是人在自己的生命之外，再得着神的生命；我们一得着重生，就有“权柄作神的儿女”—一12~13：", "en": "G. Regeneration is nought else but the fact of man, in addition to his own life, receiving the life of God; once we are regenerated, we have the \"authority to become children of God.\"—1:12-13:", "norm_zh": "七重生不是别的乃是人在自己的生命之外再得着神的生命我们一得着重生就有权柄作神的儿女一1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G Regeneration is nought else but the fact of man in addition to his own life receiving the life of God once we are regenerated we have the authority to become children of God11213"}
{"zh": "1\t神的生命，是有神的性情的；所以我们一得着神的生命，就“得与神的性情有分”—彼后一4：", "en": "1. In God's life is God's nature; therefore, when we have God's life, we become \"partakers of the divine nature.\"—2 Pet. 1:4:", "norm_zh": "1神的生命是有神的性情的所以我们一得着神的生命就得与神的性情有分彼后一4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In Gods life is Gods nature therefore when we have Gods life we become partakers of the divine nature2 Pet 14"}
{"zh": "a\t“人的灵是耶和华的灯”；亚当堕落后，这个灵就黑暗了—箴二十27。", "en": "a. \"The spirit of man is the lamp of Jehovah\"; after Adam's fall, man's spirit became darkened.—Prov. 20:27.", "norm_zh": "a人的灵是耶和华的灯亚当堕落后这个灵就黑暗了箴二十27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The spirit of man is the lamp of Jehovah after Adams fall mans spirit became darkenedProv 2027"}
{"zh": "b\t当圣灵重生我们，将神的生命放到我们的里面，就叫我们的灵活过来，就好像把灯点亮了一般—弗二5~6。", "en": "b. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us and put God's life into us, He made our spirit alive; it was like lighting a lamp.—Eph. 2:5-6.", "norm_zh": "b当圣灵重生我们将神的生命放到我们的里面就叫我们的灵活过来就好像把灯点亮了一般弗二56", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b When the Holy Spirit regenerated us and put Gods life into us He made our spirit alive it was like lighting a lampEph 256"}
{"zh": "2\t人如果说他重生了，而他对于神从来不认识，对于罪一点感觉都没有，就这个人的重生是可疑惑的。", "en": "2. If a man says that he is regenerated, yet has no knowledge of God and no feeling concerning sin, his regeneration is doubtful.", "norm_zh": "2人如果说他重生了而他对于神从来不认识对于罪一点感觉都没有就这个人的重生是可疑惑的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If a man says that he is regenerated yet has no knowledge of God and no feeling concerning sin his regeneration is doubtful"}
{"zh": "八\t当圣灵重生我们的时候，还赐给我们一个“新心”，将“新灵”放在我们里面—结三六26~27。", "en": "H. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us, He gave us a \"new heart\" and a \"new spirit.\"—Ezek. 36:26-27.", "norm_zh": "八当圣灵重生我们的时候还赐给我们一个新心将新灵放在我们里面结三六2627", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H When the Holy Spirit regenerated us He gave us a new heart and a new spiritEzek 362627"}
{"zh": "九\t基督在十字架上所成功的是客观的，圣灵住在我们里面，要把客观的事实变成我们主观的经历；真理的圣灵是把人带进到实际里去的—约十四16~17、26。", "en": "IX. What Christ accomplished on the cross is objective, but the Spirit indwelling us turns the objective facts into our subjective experience; the Spirit of reality guides man into all the reality.—John 14:16-17, 26.", "norm_zh": "九基督在十字架上所成功的是客观的圣灵住在我们里面要把客观的事实变成我们主观的经历真理的圣灵是把人带进到实际里去的约十四161726", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX What Christ accomplished on the cross is objective but the Spirit indwelling us turns the objective facts into our subjective experience the Spirit of reality guides man into all the realityJohn 141617 26"}
{"zh": "十\t我们所得的这个生命是完全的，却不是成熟的；所以人重生之后，还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新，让这生命能完全于全人的各部分—西三4，彼前二2节注5。", "en": "X. This life which we have obtained is complete, yet it has not matured; therefore, after regeneration man needs a long process of renewal by the Holy Spirit until this life is perfected in every part of his being.—Col. 3:4; 1 Pet. 2:2, note 5.", "norm_zh": "十我们所得的这个生命是完全的却不是成熟的所以人重生之后还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新让这生命能完全于全人的各部分西三4彼前二2节注5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X This life which we have obtained is complete yet it has not matured therefore after regeneration man needs a long process of renewal by the Holy Spirit until this life is perfected in every part of his beingCol 34 1 Pet 22 note 5"}
{"zh": "贰\t生命的律；“我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面，写在他们心上”—来八10：", "en": "II. The law of life; \"I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them\"—Heb. 8:10:", "norm_zh": "贰生命的律我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面写在他们心上来八10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The law of life I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe themHeb 810"}
{"zh": "一\t在旧约，律法是放在人的外面，写在石版上的；在新约，律法是放在我们里面，写在我们心上的—林后三3，出二四12，申四13：", "en": "A. In the old covenant the law was placed outside of man and written on tables of stone; in the new covenant the law is put inside of man and inscribed upon his heart.—2 Cor. 3:3; Exo. 24:12; Deut. 4:13:", "norm_zh": "一在旧约律法是放在人的外面写在石版上的在新约律法是放在我们里面写在我们心上的林后三3出二四12申四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the old covenant the law was placed outside of man and written on tables of stone in the new covenant the law is put inside of man and inscribed upon his heart2 Cor 33 Exo 2412 Deut 413"}
{"zh": "1\t放在外面，写在石版上的，必定是字句—林后三6。", "en": "1. That which was placed outside of man and written upon tables of stone must be of the letter—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1放在外面写在石版上的必定是字句林后三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 That which was placed outside of man and written upon tables of stone must be of the letter2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t那么，能放在我们里面，能写在我们心上的是什么律法呢？乃是一个生命的律；神放在我们里面的律，乃是出于神放在我们里面的生命—罗八2。", "en": "2. In that case, what is the law that can be put inside of us and inscribed upon our hearts? It is the law of life; the law which God imparted into us comes from the life which God imparted into us.—Rom. 8:2.", "norm_zh": "2哪么能放在我们里面能写在我们心上的是什么律法呢乃是一个生命的律神放在我们里面的律乃是出于神放在我们里面的生命罗八2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In that case what is the law that can be put inside of us and inscribed upon our hearts It is the law of life the law which God imparted into us comes from the life which God imparted into usRom 82"}
{"zh": "二\t神放在我们里面的既然是生命，所以必定有律，也必定有自自然然的功用；这个律会把生命自自然然地“律”出来；只要我们不拦阻它，它总是自自然然地出来—2~4、7~11节。", "en": "B. Since what God has imparted into us is life, the law of the life must also be there, and it must have its spontaneous function; this law will spontaneously live out the life in us; as long as we do not hinder it, it will spontaneously come forth.—vv. 2-4, 7-11.", "norm_zh": "二神放在我们里面的既然是生命所以必定有律也必定有自自然然的功用这个律会把生命自自然然地律出来只要我们不拦阻它它总是自自然然地出来24711节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since what God has imparted into us is life the law of the life must also be there and it must have its spontaneous function this law will spontaneously live out the life in us as long as we do not hinder it it will spontaneously come forthvv 24 711"}
{"zh": "叁\t心挂着良心，挂着心思，挂着意志，挂着情感—弗三17上，一18节注2：", "en": "III. The heart includes the conscience, the mind, the will, and the emotion.—Eph. 3:17a; 1:18 note 2:", "norm_zh": "叁心挂着良心挂着心思挂着意志挂着情感弗三17上一18节注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The heart includes the conscience the mind the will and the emotionEph 317a 118 note 2"}
{"zh": "一\t心挂着良心；例如：“我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去”，这里的“天良”，就是“良心”—来十22，九14，约壹三20。", "en": "A. The heart includes the conscience; for example, \"Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience,\" where the \"conscience\" here is the \"conscience.\"—Heb. 10:22; 9:14; 1 John 3:20.", "norm_zh": "一心挂着良心例如我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去这里的天良就是良心来十22九14约壹三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The heart includes the conscience for example Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience where the conscience here is the conscienceHeb 1022 914 1 John 320"}
{"zh": "二\t心挂着心思；例如：“心里怀着恶念”，“心里议论”，“心里妄想”，“心里起疑念”，都是在心里的故事—太九4，可二6，路一66。", "en": "B. The heart includes the mind; for example, \"thinking evil things in your hearts,\" \"reasoning in the heart,\" \"the imagination of the heart,\" and \"the questionings of the heart\" are all matters in the heart.—Matt. 9:4; Mark 2:6; Luke 1:66.", "norm_zh": "二心挂着心思例如心里怀着恶念心里议论心里妄想心里起疑念都是在心里的故事太九4可二6路一66", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The heart includes the mind for example thinking evil things in your hearts reasoning in the heart the imagination of the heart and the questionings of the heart are all matters in the heartMatt 94 Mark 26 Luke 166"}
{"zh": "三\t心挂着意志；例如：“立定心志”，“心里顺服”，“本心所酌定的”，“心中的……主意”，可见心是挂着意志的部分—徒十一23，罗六17，林后九7，来四12。", "en": "C. The heart includes the will; for example, \"with purpose of heart,\" \"obeyed out from the heart,\" \"purposed in his heart,\" and \"intents of the... heart,\" showing that the heart is the part that includes the will.—Acts 11:23; Rom. 6:17; 2 Cor. 9:7; Heb. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "三心挂着意志例如立定心志心里顺服本心所酌定的心中的主意可见心是挂着意志的部分徒十一23罗六17林后九7来四12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The heart includes the will for example with purpose of heart obeyed out from the heart purposed in his heart and intents of the heart showing that the heart is the part that includes the willActs 1123 Rom 617 2 Cor 97 Heb 412"}
{"zh": "四\t心挂着情感；例如：“心里冰凉”，“心……火热”，“心里不要忧愁”，“心就喜乐”，可见心是挂着情感的部分—创四五26，路二四32，约十四1，十六22。", "en": "D. The heart includes the emotion; for example, \"Jacob's heart fainted,\" \"heart... burn,\" \"Let not your heart be troubled,\" and \"your heart will rejoice,\" showing that the heart is the part that includes the emotion.—Gen. 45:26; Luke 24:32; John 14:1; 16:22.", "norm_zh": "四心挂着情感例如心里冰凉心火热心里不要忧愁心就喜乐可见心是挂着情感的部分创四五26路二四32约十四1十六22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The heart includes the emotion for example Jacobs heart fainted heart burn Let not your heart be troubled and your heart will rejoice showing that the heart is the part that includes the emotionGen 4526 Luke 2432 John 141 1622"}
{"zh": "五\t以律的本身来说，是单数的；以这个律运行的功用来说，是多数的；这好像自来水，源头是一个，但管子是多数的—来八10，十16。", "en": "E. As far as the law itself is concerned, it is singular; but concerning the function of this law in our being, it is plural; this is just like running water; the source is one, but the pipes are many.—Heb. 8:10; 10:16.", "norm_zh": "五以律的本身来说是单数的以这个律运行的功用来说是多数的这好像自来水源头是一个但管子是多数的来八10十16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E As far as the law itself is concerned it is singular but concerning the function of this law in our being it is plural this is just like running water the source is one but the pipes are manyHeb 810 1016"}
{"zh": "肆\t心是生命的进出口—诗四4，可四28：", "en": "IV. The Heart Being the Gate of Our Being—Psa. 4:4; Mark 4:28:", "norm_zh": "肆心是生命的进出口诗四4可四28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The Heart Being the Gate of Our BeingPsa 44 Mark 428"}
{"zh": "一\t心是在灵与魂之间的；所以，凡要进入灵的，都得通过心而入；凡要从灵发出的，都得通过心而出—箴四23，太五3、8：", "en": "A. The heart is between the spirit and the soul; therefore, all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart, and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heart.—Prov. 4:23; Matt. 5:3, 8:", "norm_zh": "一心是在灵与魂之间的所以凡要进入灵的都得通过心而入凡要从灵发出的都得通过心而出箴四23太五38", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The heart is between the spirit and the soul therefore all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heartProv 423 Matt 53 8"}
{"zh": "1\t人外面所结的果，都是由心发出的；所以心是最要紧的东西—可四28，太十二33~37，箴四23。", "en": "1. The fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart, and for this reason the heart is the most important thing.—Mark 4:28; Matt. 12:33-37; Prov. 4:23.", "norm_zh": "1人外面所结的果都是由心发出的所以心是最要紧的东西可四28太十二3337箴四23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart and for this reason the heart is the most important thingMark 428 Matt 123337 Prov 423"}
{"zh": "2\t心是生命运行的必经之路；所以，神的生命要进到我们里面，总是先打动我们的心；如果心没有忧伤，没有悔改，神的生命就没有法子进来—林后五14，徒二37~38，参太三2。", "en": "2. The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves; therefore, before God's life enters into us, what must be touched first is our heart; if our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented, God's life cannot enter.—2 Cor. 5:14; Acts 2:37-38; cf. Matt. 3:2.", "norm_zh": "2心是生命运行的必经之路所以神的生命要进到我们里面总是先打动我们的心如果心没有忧伤没有悔改神的生命就没有法子进来林后五14徒二3738参太三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves therefore before Gods life enters into us what must be touched first is our heart if our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented Gods life cannot enter2 Cor 514 Acts 23738 cf Matt 32"}
{"zh": "二\t心是生命的一个开关—箴四23，太十二33~37，参结三六26~27：", "en": "B. The Heart is the Switch of Life—Prov. 4:23; Matt. 12:33-37; cf. Ezek. 36:26-27:", "norm_zh": "二心是生命的一个开关箴四23太十二3337参结三六2627", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Heart is the Switch of LifeProv 423 Matt 123337 cf Ezek 362627"}
{"zh": "1\t你的生命能不能向外发展出去，是看你的心向神是不是开启的—箴四23。", "en": "1. Whether the life within us can grow depends upon whether our heart is open toward God.—Prov. 4:23.", "norm_zh": "1你的生命能不能向外发展出去是看你的心向神是不是开启的箴四23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Whether the life within us can grow depends upon whether our heart is open toward GodProv 423"}
{"zh": "2\t心只能爱神而不能摸着神，心只能倾向神而不能与神交通；能摸着神，能与神交通的，乃是灵—约十四24。", "en": "2. The heart can love God, but it cannot touch God; the heart can incline to God, but cannot have fellowship with God; only the spirit can touch God and have fellowship with God.—John 14:24.", "norm_zh": "2心只能爱神而不能摸着神心只能倾向神而不能与神交通能摸着神能与神交通的乃是灵约十四24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The heart can love God but it cannot touch God the heart can incline to God but cannot have fellowship with God only the spirit can touch God and have fellowship with GodJohn 1424"}
{"zh": "3\t你的心好像电灯开关，一开，灯就亮了；一关，灯就熄了；你的心如果向神是开着的，神与你交通，与你来往，就是容易的事—太五3、8。", "en": "3. Our heart is like the electric switch; when it is turned on, the light goes on. When it is shut off, the light goes out. If our heart is open to God, it is easy for God to have fellowship with us—Matt. 5:3, 8.", "norm_zh": "3你的心好像电灯开关一开灯就亮了一关灯就熄了你的心如果向神是开着的神与你交通与你来往就是容易的事太五38", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Our heart is like the electric switch when it is turned on the light goes on When it is shut off the light goes out If our heart is open to God it is easy for God to have fellowship with usMatt 53 8"}
{"zh": "4\t圣灵重生了我们以后，我们是得着了一个非受造的生命，就是神的生命；如果我们的心有了问题，神的生命就要受很大的拦阻—十二33~37。", "en": "4. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us, we received the uncreated life of God; if our heart has problems, God's life will be greatly hindered—Matt. 12:33-37.", "norm_zh": "4圣灵重生了我们以后我们是得着了一个非受造的生命就是神的生命如果我们的心有了问提神的生命就要受很大的拦阻十二3337", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 When the Holy Spirit regenerated us we received the uncreated life of God if our heart has problems Gods life will be greatly hinderedMatt 123337"}
{"zh": "三\t以弗所四章十七节，“所以我这样说，且在主里见证，你们行事为人，不要再像外邦人在他们心思的虚妄里行事为人”：", "en": "C. Ephesians 4:17, \"This therefore I say and testify in the Lord, that you no longer walk as the Gentiles also walk in the vanity of their mind\":", "norm_zh": "三以弗所四章十七节所以我这样说且在主里见证你们行事为人不要再像外邦人在他们心思的虚妄里行事为人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Ephesians 417 This therefore I say and testify in the Lord that you no longer walk as the Gentiles also walk in the vanity of their mind"}
{"zh": "1\t我们人有三个得知识的机关：在身体方面的是头脑，在灵方面的是直觉，在魂方面的是悟性，这悟性又是受直觉支配的—出三一3：", "en": "1. In our human being there are three organs of perception: in our body there is the brain, in our spirit there is the intuition, and in our soul there is the mind. Our mind should be governed by our intuition.—Exo. 31:3:", "norm_zh": "1我们人有三个得知识的机关在身体方面的是头脑在灵方面的是直觉在魂方面的是悟性这悟性又是受直觉支配的出三一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In our human being there are three organs of perception in our body there is the brain in our spirit there is the intuition and in our soul there is the mind Our mind should be governed by our intuitionExo 313"}
{"zh": "a\t悟性是介乎直觉与头脑之间的；悟性，把直觉的意思表明出来，叫头脑去想出来—弗四17，诗一一九34、125。", "en": "a. In between the intuition and the brain is our mind; the mind expresses the meaning of the intuition and causes the brain to make it clear.—Eph. 4:17; Psa. 119:34, 125.", "norm_zh": "a悟性是介乎直觉与头脑之间的悟性把直觉的意思表明出来叫头脑去想出来弗四17诗一一九34125", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a In between the intuition and the brain is our mind the mind expresses the meaning of the intuition and causes the brain to make it clearEph 417 Psa 11934 125"}
{"zh": "b\t心思所以虚妄，领会力所以昏昧，所以与神的生命隔绝，都是因里面愚昧，都是因心硬丢弃了一切的感觉—弗四17~18。", "en": "b. The reasons the mind becomes vain, the understanding darkens, and we become estranged from the life of God are due to our inner ignorance and the hardness of our heart which cause us to forsake all feeling—Eph. 4:17-18.", "norm_zh": "b心思所以虚妄领会力所以昏昧所以与神的生命隔绝都是因里面愚昧都是因心硬丢弃了一切的感觉弗四1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The reasons the mind becomes vain the understanding darkens and we become estranged from the life of God are due to our inner ignorance and the hardness of our heart which cause us to forsake all feelingEph 41718"}
{"zh": "2\t总而言之，心一硬，就与神的生命隔绝，就越发愚昧，就越发不能领会了；这样，生命的发展就有了阻碍—太十三4。", "en": "2. In summary, we can say that when the heart is hardened, we become estranged from the life of God, we become ignorant and unable to understand; the result is that the growth of life is hindered—Matt. 13:4.", "norm_zh": "2总而言之心一硬就与神的生命隔绝就越发愚昧就越发不能领会了这样生命的发展就有了阻碍太十三4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In summary we can say that when the heart is hardened we become estranged from the life of God we become ignorant and unable to understand the result is that the growth of life is hinderedMatt 134"}
{"zh": "3\t不是生命的律不在我们的里面运行，生命的律是等着往外“律”出去，它要从我们里面的各部分“律”出去—参罗八13。", "en": "3. It is not that the law of life does not move in us — the law of life is always waiting to spread out through our inward parts—cf. Rom. 8:13.", "norm_zh": "3不是生命的律不在我们的里面运行生命的律是等着往外律出去它要从我们里面的各部分律出去参罗八13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 It is not that the law of life does not move in us the law of life is always waiting to spread out through our inward partscf Rom 813"}
{"zh": "四\t石心的软化与生命的运行—结三六26，罗八6：", "en": "D. The Softening of the Stony Heart and the Moving of Life—Ezek. 36:26; Rom. 8:6:", "norm_zh": "四石心的软化与生命的运行结三六26罗八6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Softening of the Stony Heart and the Moving of LifeEzek 3626 Rom 86"}
{"zh": "1\t以西结三十六章二十五至二十七节，至少说到五件事，就是：（一）用清水洗净我们；（二）赐给我们一个新心；（三）将新灵放在我们里面；（四）除掉我们的石心，赐给我们肉心；（五）将神的灵放在我们里面。", "en": "1. Ezekiel 36:25-27 speaks of at least five things: 1) we have been cleansed with clean water; 2) we have been given a new heart; 3) we have a new spirit within us; 4) our stony heart has been removed, and we have been given a heart of flesh; and 5) God's Spirit has been put within us.", "norm_zh": "1以西结三十六章二十五至二十七节至少说到五件事就是一用清水洗净我们二赐给我们一个新心三将新灵放在我们里面四除掉我们的石心赐给我们肉心五将神的灵放在我们里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Ezekiel 362527 speaks of at least five things 1 we have been cleansed with clean water 2 we have been given a new heart 3 we have a new spirit within us 4 our stony heart has been removed and we have been given a heart of flesh and 5 Gods Spirit has been put within us"}
{"zh": "2\t这五件事合起来的结果，就是使我们顺从神的律例，谨守遵行神的典章。", "en": "2. The result of putting these five things together is that we might walk in God's statutes and keep His ordinances.", "norm_zh": "2这五件事合起来的结果就是使我们顺从神的律例谨守遵行神的典章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The result of putting these five things together is that we might walk in Gods statutes and keep His ordinances"}
{"zh": "3\t我们的心只有一个；石心是指心的硬而言，肉心是指心的软而言—参出三二9，林后三3。", "en": "3. We have only one heart; a stony heart refers to the hardness of the heart, while the fleshly heart refers to the softness of the heart.—cf. Exo. 32:9; 2 Cor. 3:3.", "norm_zh": "3我们的心只有一个石心是指心的硬而言肉心是指心的软而言参出三二9林后三3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We have only one heart a stony heart refers to the hardness of the heart while the fleshly heart refers to the softness of the heartcf Exo 329 2 Cor 33"}
{"zh": "4\t神的生命要从我们里面往外去，神总是打动我们的心，软化我们的石心；有的人是受神的爱打动，有的人是被神的管教打动—五14，四16~18，来十二6~7，参耶四八11，罗八28。", "en": "4. When God's life desires to move out within us, He always touches our heart first, causing our stony heart to be softened; some people are touched by God's love, others by His disciplining.—5:14; 4:16-18; Heb. 12:6-7; cf. Jer. 48:11; Rom. 8:28.", "norm_zh": "4神的生命要从我们里面往外去神总是打动我们的心软化我们的石心有的人是受神的爱打动有的人是被神的管教打动五14四1618来十二67参耶四八11罗八28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 When Gods life desires to move out within us He always touches our heart first causing our stony heart to be softened some people are touched by Gods love others by His disciplining514 41618 Heb 1267 cf Jer 4811 Rom 828"}
{"zh": "5\t当你肯顺服神一下的时候，神的生命就运行出来了；神的生命就是这样在你的里面运行不息—6、13节。", "en": "5. If you are willing to obey God, His life will move out; in this manner, God's life will continue to move in you without ceasing.—vv. 6, 13.", "norm_zh": "5当你肯顺服神一下的时候神的生命就运行出来了神的生命就是这样在你的里面运行不息613节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 If you are willing to obey God His life will move out in this manner Gods life will continue to move in you without ceasingvv 6 13"}
{"zh": "希伯来八章十节：“主又说，那些日子以后，我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样；我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面，写在他们心上，我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民。”（这里的“律法”照原文该译作“诸律法”；“里面”照原文，有“心意”的意思在里头，光译作“心意”又不够，所以把它译作“心意里面”。）", "en": "Hebrews 8:10: \"For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days, says the Lord: I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them, and I will be God to them, and they shall be a people to Me.\" (Here \"law\" according to the original text should be translated \"laws\"; \"inside\" according to the original text has the meaning of \"mind\" in it, and to translate it simply as \"mind\" is not enough, so it is translated as \"inside the mind.\")", "norm_zh": "希伯来八章十节主又说哪些日子以后我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面写在他们心上我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民这里的律法照原文该译作诸律法里面照原文有心意的意思在里头光译作心意又不够所以把它译作心意里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 810 For this is the covenant which I will covenant with the house of Israel after those days says the Lord I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe them and I will be God to them and they shall be a people to Me Here law according to the original text should be translated laws inside according to the original text has the meaning of mind in it and to translate it simply as mind is not enough so it is translated as inside the mind"}
{"zh": "希伯来十章十六节，照原文该译作：“主说，那些日子以后，我与他们所立的约乃是这样：我要将我的诸律法放在他们心上，写在他们的心意里面。”", "en": "Hebrews 10:16, according to the original text, should be translated: \"This is the covenant which I will covenant with them after those days, says the Lord: I will put My laws upon their hearts and upon their minds I will inscribe them.\"", "norm_zh": "希伯来十章十六节照原文该译作主说哪些日子以后我与他们所立的约乃是这样我要将我的诸律法放在他们心上写在他们的心意里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 1016 according to the original text should be translated This is the covenant which I will covenant with them after those days says the Lord I will put My laws upon their hearts and upon their minds I will inscribe them"}
{"zh": "以上这两处圣经，都是先说到“放”，然后说到“写”。不过第八章是先提“心意里面”，后提“心上”；第十章是先提“心上”，后提“心意里面”。不论它是先说心意里面，后说心上，或者是先说心上，后说心意里面，两处都是说到“放”，都是说到“写”，都是说到“心意”，都是说到“心上”。所以两处都是说到一件事。", "en": "These two verses both speak first of imparting or of inscribing. They are different in this respect: in 8:10 the mind is first mentioned and then the heart, while in 10:16, the heart is mentioned first and then the mind. Whether the mind or the heart is mentioned first, both passages speak of imparting or inscribing, and both mention the mind and the heart. Therefore both speak of the same thing.", "norm_zh": "以上这两处圣经都是先说到放然后说到写不过第八章是先提心意里面后提心上第十章是先提心上后提心意里面不论它是先说心意里面后说心上或者是先说心上后说心意里面两处都是说到放都是说到写都是说到心意都是说到心上所以两处都是说到一件事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "These two verses both speak first of imparting or of inscribing They are different in this respect in 810 the mind is first mentioned and then the heart while in 1016 the heart is mentioned first and then the mind Whether the mind or the heart is mentioned first both passages speak of imparting or inscribing and both mention the mind and the heart Therefore both speak of the same thing"}
{"zh": "我们知道，以上这两处的话，都是引自耶利米三十一章三十三节。这一节，照原文可以译作：“耶和华说，那些日子以后，我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样：我要将我的律法放在他们里面的诸部分里头，写在他们心上；我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民。”", "en": "We must also realize that both these passages are quotations from Jeremiah 31:33, which reads: \"But this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days, saith Jehovah: I will put my law in their inward parts, and in their heart will I write it; and I will be their God, and they shall be my people.\"", "norm_zh": "我们知道以上这两处的话都是引自耶利米三十一章三十三节这一节照原文可以译作耶和华说哪些日子以后我与以色列家所立的约乃是这样我要将我的律法放在他们里面的诸部分里头写在他们心上我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must also realize that both these passages are quotations from Jeremiah 3133 which reads But this is the covenant that I will make with the house of Israel after those days saith Jehovah I will put my law in their inward parts and in their heart will I write it and I will be their God and they shall be my people"}
{"zh": "人原来是神所创造的（创二），所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的。以人原来受造的生命来说，是正直的（传七），是好的（创一）。但是，以神永远的目的来说，人还没有神自己那非受造的生命。所以，人还需要拣选神，需要拣选神的生命。（在希腊文里，说到“生命”，有三个字：（一）“白阿司”，是指着肉体的生命说的。主耶稣说到寡妇把她一切“养生”（路二一）的都投上了，就是用这个字。（二）“朴宿克”，就是叫人有生机的生命，就是人天然的生命，就是魂的生命。圣经中说到人的生命时，就是用这个字（太十六，路九）。（三）“奏厄”，就是最高的生命，灵的生命，非受造的生命。圣经说到“永生”（约三）时，就是用这个字。）", "en": "Originally man was made by God (Gen. 2); man's original life was made by God also. As far as man's original created life was concerned, it was upright (Eccl. 7) and it was good (Gen. 1). But as far as God's eternal purpose, man had not yet received the uncreated life of God. Therefore man still needed to choose God and God's life. (In Greek there are three different words, all of which translate into the one English word, life. One of these words is bios. It refers to life in the flesh. The Lord Jesus spoke of the widow who put all her living into the treasury (Luke 21); the word translated living is from the word bios. The second Greek word is the word psuche. Psuche refers to man's natural life, which is the soul-life. When the Scriptures speak specifically of man's life, this is the word used (Matt. 16; Luke 9). The third word for life is zoe. Zoe is the highest life, the spiritual life, and the uncreated life. When the Scriptures speak of eternal life, as in John 3, the word used is zoe.)", "norm_zh": "人原来是神所创造的创二所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的以人原来受造的生命来说是正直的传七是好的创一但是以神永远的目的来说人还没有神自己哪非受造的生命所以人还需要拣选神需要拣选神的生命在希腊文里说到生命有三个字一白阿司是指着肉体的生命说的主耶稣说到寡妇把她一切养生路二一的都投上了就是用这个字二朴宿克就是叫人有生机的生命就是人天然的生命就是魂的生命圣经中说到人的生命时就是用这个字太十六路九三奏厄就是最高的生命灵的生命非受造的生命圣经说到永生约三时就是用这个字", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Originally man was made by God Gen 2 mans original life was made by God also As far as mans original created life was concerned it was upright Eccl 7 and it was good Gen 1 But as far as Gods eternal purpose man had not yet received the uncreated life of God Therefore man still needed to choose God and Gods life In Greek there are three different words all of which translate into the one English word life One of these words is bios It refers to life in the flesh The Lord Jesus spoke of the widow who put all her living into the treasury Luke 21 the word translated living is from the word bios The second Greek word is the word psuche Psuche refers to mans natural life which is the soullife When the Scriptures speak specifically of mans life this is the word used Matt 16 Luke 9 The third word for life is zoe Zoe is the highest life the spiritual life and the uncreated life When the Scriptures speak of eternal life as in John 3 the word used is zoe"}
{"zh": "但是，那人（亚当）竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子，竟然不拣选生命，人堕落了，人犯罪了。人的灵本来还能与神来往，现在人的灵与神“隔绝了”（弗四），就向神“死了”（西二，弗二）。当初神对亚当说，“你吃的日子必定死”（创二17）。以亚当的肉身来说，他吃了分别善恶树的果子之后，还活了几百岁（五）。所以这里的死，不只是肉体要死，必定是灵先死了。死的意思就是远离生命。神是生命的神，亚当远离神，就是远离生命。我们要知道，亚当的灵死了，不是说他的灵没有了，乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通，已经失去他敏锐的知觉。亚当的灵死了，灵还是有的，只是对神死了，亚当失去灵的本能了。人一堕落，人就受血气（魂）的支配，而属乎肉体了（罗七）。人不能领会神的事（林前二），人不服神的律法，也是不能服，而且属肉体的人不能得神的喜欢（罗八）了。", "en": "However, the man Adam did not choose life. He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eat. Before that time it was possible for man's spirit to have fellowship with God, but after man fell, his spirit became estranged from God (Eph. 4) and dead to God (Col. 2; Eph. 2). God told Adam from the beginning that the day he ate of the tree of knowledge of good and evil he would surely die (Gen. 2:17). As far as Adam's flesh was concerned, after he ate the fruit of the tree of knowledge of good and evil, he lived for several hundred years (Gen. 5). Therefore, the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires. Death simply means to be estranged from life, and, as we know, God is a God of life. By being estranged from God, Adam was estranged from life. We know that Adam's spirit died. This does not mean that his spirit disappeared, but that his spirit lost its fellowship with God; it lost its keen sense. When Adam's spirit died it was still there but it was dead to God. Adam had lost the function of his spirit. After man fell, he became dominated by his soul and was fleshly (Rom. 7). He could no longer understand the things of God (1 Cor. 2). Man also was not subject to the law of God, neither could he be. Furthermore, according to Romans 8, man in the flesh cannot please God.", "norm_zh": "但是哪人亚当竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子竟然不拣选生命人堕落了人犯罪了人的灵本来还能与神来往现在人的灵与神隔绝了弗四就向神死了西二弗二当初神对亚当说你吃的日子必定死创二17以亚当的肉身来说他吃了分别善恶树的果子之后还活了几百岁五所以这里的死不只是肉体要死必定是灵先死了死的意思就是远离生命神是生命的神亚当远离神就是远离生命我们要知道亚当的灵死了不是说他的灵没有了乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通已经失去他敏锐的知觉亚当的灵死了灵还是有的只是对神死了亚当失去灵的本能了人一堕落人就受血气魂的支配而属乎肉体了罗七人不能领会神的事林前二人不服神的律法也是不能服而且属肉体的人不能得神的喜欢罗八了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "However the man Adam did not choose life He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eat Before that time it was possible for mans spirit to have fellowship with God but after man fell his spirit became estranged from God Eph 4 and dead to God Col 2 Eph 2 God told Adam from the beginning that the day he ate of the tree of knowledge of good and evil he would surely die Gen 217 As far as Adams flesh was concerned after he ate the fruit of the tree of knowledge of good and evil he lived for several hundred years Gen 5 Therefore the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires Death simply means to be estranged from life and as we know God is a God of life By being estranged from God Adam was estranged from life We know that Adams spirit died This does not mean that his spirit disappeared but that his spirit lost its fellowship with God it lost its keen sense When Adams spirit died it was still there but it was dead to God Adam had lost the function of his spirit After man fell he became dominated by his soul and was fleshly Rom 7 He could no longer understand the things of God 1 Cor 2 Man also was not subject to the law of God neither could he be Furthermore according to Romans 8 man in the flesh cannot please God"}
{"zh": "重生，是“从神生的”（约一），是“出于天”的（林前十五）。", "en": "Regeneration means to be born of God (John 1), to be born of heaven (1 Cor. 15).", "norm_zh": "重生是从神生的约一是出于天的林前十五", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Regeneration means to be born of God John 1 to be born of heaven 1 Cor 15"}
{"zh": "重生是从水和圣灵生的", "en": "Regeneration is to be born of water and of the Spirit.", "norm_zh": "重生是从水和圣灵生的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Regeneration is to be born of water and of the Spirit"}
{"zh": "重生，是“从水和圣灵生的”（约三）。对于这里所说的“从水和圣灵生的”，我们要略加一点的解释。当施浸约翰出来传道施浸的时候，他说，“我是用水给你们施浸，祂却要用圣灵给你们施浸”（可一）。施浸约翰是把水和圣灵连在一起说，主耶稣在这里也是把水和圣灵连在一起说。约翰在那里所说的“水”既是施浸的水，就主耶稣在这里所说的“水”也必是施浸的水。主耶稣当时回答尼哥底母的话，必定是尼哥底母一听就明白的；当时许多人都知道约翰用水施浸，所以主耶稣一提到水，尼哥底母就能领会到这是指着约翰用水施浸说的；如果主耶稣所说的“水”另有别的意思，就叫尼哥底母不容易领会了。所以“水”是指着施浸的水说的。约翰所施的浸是悔改的浸，是告诉百姓，当信那在他以后要来的，就是耶稣（徒十九）。约翰来用水施悔改的浸，还不能叫人重生；必须“从水和圣灵生的”，才是重生。悔改的浸的意思是说，不只人的行为是恶的，是死的，需要悔改，就是人的自己也是坏的，也是死的，需要埋葬，需要受浸。一个人到水里去受浸，就是在神面前承认自己的行为是恶的，承认自己这一个人是坏的，是死在罪中的，所以只配死而埋葬。但是，人光是这样“从水”，还不能生；人必须“从水和圣灵”，才能生。人还必须接受主耶稣所赐的圣灵，才能得着神的生命。施浸的约翰先来传“悔改”（可一），主耶稣就紧接着加上“信”。悔改是叫人脱离一切属乎我们的，相信是叫人进入一切属乎神的。人因着悔改而进入水，人因着相信而进入圣灵。人这样进入水，又进入圣灵，就是从水和圣灵生的。悔改而进入水，就结束了旧人的生命；相信而进入圣灵，就得着了神的生命。这样一来，就是重生。", "en": "Regeneration also means to be born of the water and of the Spirit (John 3). Concerning this we need some explanation. When John the Baptist came preaching and baptizing, he said, \"I baptized you in water; but he shall baptize you in the Holy Spirit\" (Mark 1). John the Baptist put water and the Holy Spirit together, and the Lord Jesus also put water and the Holy Spirit together. The water to which John referred is the water of baptism; hence, the water to which the Lord Jesus referred must also be the water of baptism. The words spoken to Nicodemus by the Lord Jesus must have been words which could be easily understood. At that time many knew that John baptized with water; so when the Lord Jesus mentioned water, Nicodemus would readily understand that this referred to the water of baptism practiced by John. If the water mentioned by the Lord Jesus had implied something else, it would have been difficult for Nicodemus to understand. The water spoken of, therefore, must have referred to the water of baptism. The baptism which John practiced was the baptism of repentance. He told people that they should believe on Him that should come after him, that is, on Jesus (Acts 19). The baptism of repentance which John performed could not cause men to be regenerated. To be regenerated, one must be born both of water and of the Holy Spirit. The baptism of repentance means not only that man's actions are evil and dead and he needs to repent; it means also that man himself is corrupt and dead and needs to be buried, that is, to be baptized. When a man goes down into the water to be baptized, he admits before God that his actions are evil and confesses that his whole being is corrupt and dead in sin; therefore he deserves only death and burial. But man is not born merely \"of water.\" He must be born \"of water and of the Spirit.\" He must also receive the Holy Spirit which the Lord Jesus gives in order to obtain God's life. John the Baptist came preaching \"Repent!\" (Mark 1), to which the Lord Jesus immediately added, \"Believe\". Repentance causes man to leave all that is of himself, while believing causes man to enter into all that is of God. Because of repentance man enters into the water, and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit. By entering into the water and the Spirit, he is born of water and of the Spirit. Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man. By believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain God's life. This is regeneration.", "norm_zh": "重生是从水和圣灵生的约三对于这里所说的从水和圣灵生的我们要略加一点的解释当施浸约翰出来传道施浸的时候他说我是用水给你们施浸祂却要用圣灵给你们施浸可一施浸约翰是把水和圣灵连在一起说主耶稣在这里也是把水和圣灵连在一起说约翰在哪里所说的水既是施浸的水就主耶稣在这里所说的水也必是施浸的水主耶稣当时回答尼哥底母的话必定是尼哥底母一听就明白的当时许多人都知道约翰用水施浸所以主耶稣一提到水尼哥底母就能领会到这是指着约翰用水施浸说的如果主耶稣所说的水另有别的意思就叫尼哥底母不容易领会了所以水是指着施浸的水说的约翰所施的浸是悔改的浸是告诉百姓当信哪在他以后要来的就是耶稣徒十九约翰来用水施悔改的浸还不能叫人重生必须从水和圣灵生的才是重生悔改的浸的意思是说不只人的行为是恶的是死的需要悔改就是人的自己也是坏的也是死的需要埋葬需要受浸一个人到水里去受浸就是在神面前承认自己的行为是恶的承认自己这一个人是坏的是死在罪中的所以只配死而埋葬但是人光是这样从水还不能生人必须从水和圣灵才能生人还必须接受主耶稣所赐的圣灵才能得着神的生命施浸的约翰先来传悔改可一主耶稣就紧接着加上信悔改是叫人脱离一切属乎我们的相信是叫人进入一切属乎神的人因着悔改而进入水人因着相信而进入圣灵人这样进入水又进入圣灵就是从水和圣灵生的悔改而进入水就结束了旧人的生命相信而进入圣灵就得着了神的生命这样一来就是重生", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Regeneration also means to be born of the water and of the Spirit John 3 Concerning this we need some explanation When John the Baptist came preaching and baptizing he said I baptized you in water but he shall baptize you in the Holy Spirit Mark 1 John the Baptist put water and the Holy Spirit together and the Lord Jesus also put water and the Holy Spirit together The water to which John referred is the water of baptism hence the water to which the Lord Jesus referred must also be the water of baptism The words spoken to Nicodemus by the Lord Jesus must have been words which could be easily understood At that time many knew that John baptized with water so when the Lord Jesus mentioned water Nicodemus would readily understand that this referred to the water of baptism practiced by John If the water mentioned by the Lord Jesus had implied something else it would have been difficult for Nicodemus to understand The water spoken of therefore must have referred to the water of baptism The baptism which John practiced was the baptism of repentance He told people that they should believe on Him that should come after him that is on Jesus Acts 19 The baptism of repentance which John performed could not cause men to be regenerated To be regenerated one must be born both of water and of the Holy Spirit The baptism of repentance means not only that mans actions are evil and dead and he needs to repent it means also that man himself is corrupt and dead and needs to be buried that is to be baptized When a man goes down into the water to be baptized he admits before God that his actions are evil and confesses that his whole being is corrupt and dead in sin therefore he deserves only death and burial But man is not born merely of water He must be born of water and of the Spirit He must also receive the Holy Spirit which the Lord Jesus gives in order to obtain Gods life John the Baptist came preaching Repent Mark 1 to which the Lord Jesus immediately added Believe Repentance causes man to leave all that is of himself while believing causes man to enter into all that is of God Because of repentance man enters into the water and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit By entering into the water and the Spirit he is born of water and of the Spirit Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man By believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain Gods life This is regeneration"}
{"zh": "重生，虽然是“从水和圣灵生”，但使人重生的工作，在主观方面，完全是圣灵自己作的（在客观方面，完全是基督作的）。所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到“从水生”，而三次提到“从圣灵生”。", "en": "Although regeneration is to be \"born of water and of the Spirit,\" the work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit. (Objectively, it is accomplished completely by Christ.) Therefore, in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being \"born of water,\" while he mentioned being \"born of the Spirit\" three times.", "norm_zh": "重生虽然是从水和圣灵生但使人重生的工作在主观方面完全是圣灵自己作的在客观方面完全是基督作的所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到从水生而三次提到从圣灵生", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Although regeneration is to be born of water and of the Spirit the work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit Objectively it is accomplished completely by Christ Therefore in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being born of water while he mentioned being born of the Spirit three times"}
{"zh": "重生，是“从圣灵生”。圣灵来叫人悔改，叫人“为罪……自己责备自己”（约十六）；圣灵引导人用信心接受主耶稣作救主；圣灵进入这样悔改而相信的人里面，将神的生命赐给他，叫他得着重生。圣灵光照人，叫人悔改，引导人相信，叫人接受神的生命，都是用圣经的话语，福音的真道。所以圣经说，神用福音，用真道生了我们（林前四，雅一）。我们蒙了重生，不是由于能坏的种子，乃是由于不能坏的种子，是借着神活泼常存的道（彼前一）。神是借着圣灵用祂的话，将祂的生命送到我们里面，种在我们里面。我们因着圣灵的感动，而相信神的话，神的生命就进入我们里面。神的话里面藏着神的生命。并且神的话“就是生命”（约六）。所以我们一接受神的话，我们就得着神的生命。", "en": "Regeneration means that we have been \"born of the Spirit.\" The Spirit comes to \"convict the world concerning sin\" (John 16) and cause man to repent; He leads man to receive the Lord Jesus by faith; He then enters into such a believer who has repented and imparts God's life to him that he might be regenerated. The Spirit enlightens man, causes him to repent, leads him to believe, and causes him to receive God's life. He does all this by using the words in the Scripture, that is, by means of the word of truth of the gospel. Therefore the Scriptures say that God regenerates us by the gospel and by the word of truth (1 Cor. 4; James 1). We have been \"begotten again, not of corruptible seed, but of incorruptible, through the word of God, which liveth and abideth\" (1 Pet. 1). Through the Spirit and by the use of His words, God imparted and sowed His life into us. Because the Holy Spirit touched us, we believed God's words, and God's life entered into us. God's life is embodied in His words. Moreover, God's words are life (John 6). Therefore, when we receive God's words, we receive God's life.", "norm_zh": "重生是从圣灵生圣灵来叫人悔改叫人为罪自己责备自己约十六圣灵引导人用信心接受主耶稣作救主圣灵进入这样悔改而相信的人里面将神的生命赐给他叫他得着重生圣灵光照人叫人悔改引导人相信叫人接受神的生命都是用圣经的话语福音的真道所以圣经说神用福音用真道生了我们林前四雅一我们蒙了重生不是由于能坏的种子乃是由于不能坏的种子是借着神活泼常存的道彼前一神是借着圣灵用祂的话将祂的生命送到我们里面种在我们里面我们因着圣灵的感动而相信神的话神的生命就进入我们里面神的话里面藏着神的生命并且神的话就是生命约六所以我们一接受神的话我们就得着神的生命", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Regeneration means that we have been born of the Spirit The Spirit comes to convict the world concerning sin John 16 and cause man to repent He leads man to receive the Lord Jesus by faith He then enters into such a believer who has repented and imparts Gods life to him that he might be regenerated The Spirit enlightens man causes him to repent leads him to believe and causes him to receive Gods life He does all this by using the words in the Scripture that is by means of the word of truth of the gospel Therefore the Scriptures say that God regenerates us by the gospel and by the word of truth 1 Cor 4 James 1 We have been begotten again not of corruptible seed but of incorruptible through the word of God which liveth and abideth 1 Pet 1 Through the Spirit and by the use of His words God imparted and sowed His life into us Because the Holy Spirit touched us we believed Gods words and Gods life entered into us Gods life is embodied in His words Moreover Gods words are life John 6 Therefore when we receive Gods words we receive Gods life"}
{"zh": "重生叫人所得着的生命，不是属肉体的，乃是属灵的。这个生命象风一样的无形可见（三），却是人所能感觉得到的，是非常实际的。", "en": "The life which we receive at the time of regeneration is not fleshly life, but spiritual. Like the wind, this life is without form and cannot be seen (John 3). Yet it is very practical and can be realized by man.", "norm_zh": "重生叫人所得着的生命不是属肉体的乃是属灵的这个生命象风一样的无形可见三却是人所能感觉得到的是非常实际的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The life which we receive at the time of regeneration is not fleshly life but spiritual Like the wind this life is without form and cannot be seen John 3 Yet it is very practical and can be realized by man"}
{"zh": "重生是人在自己的生命之外，再得着神的生命", "en": "Regeneration is that in addition to his own life, man receives the life of God.", "norm_zh": "重生是人在自己的生命之外再得着神的生命", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Regeneration is that in addition to his own life man receives the life of God"}
{"zh": "所以重生不是别的，乃是人在自己的生命之外，再得着神的生命。", "en": "Therefore, regeneration is simply this: that in addition to his own life, man receives the life of God.", "norm_zh": "所以重生不是别的乃是人在自己的生命之外再得着神的生命", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Therefore regeneration is simply this that in addition to his own life man receives the life of God"}
{"zh": "人重生之后，还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新", "en": "After a man is regenerated, he still needs the long, continuous renewing of the Holy Spirit.", "norm_zh": "人重生之后还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "After a man is regenerated he still needs the long continuous renewing of the Holy Spirit"}
{"zh": "（一）心挂着良心　例如：“我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去”（来十），这里的“天良”，就是“良心”。“心若责备”（约壹三），责备是良心的功用。可见良心是在心的系统之内。所以说，心挂着良心。", "en": "1) The heart includes the conscience. We see this in Hebrews 10 which says, \"Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience....\" First John 3 says, \"If our heart condemns us....\" To condemn is the function of the conscience, and we see from these verses that the conscience is within the system of the heart. For this reason we say that the heart includes the conscience.", "norm_zh": "一心挂着良心例如我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去来十这里的天良就是良心心若责备约壹三责备是良心的功用可见良心是在心的系统之内所以说心挂着良心", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The heart includes the conscience We see this in Hebrews 10 which says Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience First John 3 says If our heart condemns us To condemn is the function of the conscience and we see from these verses that the conscience is within the system of the heart For this reason we say that the heart includes the conscience"}
{"zh": "（二）心挂着心思　例如：“心里怀着恶念”（太九），“心里议论”（可二），“心里妄想”（路一），“心里起疑念”（路二四），都是在心里的故事。“心里明白”（太十三），“存在心里，反复思想”（路二），“心中的思念”（来四），都可见心是挂着心思的部分。所以说，心挂着心思。", "en": "2) The heart includes the mind. In Matthew 9 we read: \"Why are you thinking evil things in your hearts?\" Mark 2 speaks of reasoning in the heart; Luke 1 speaks of the imagination of the heart; and Luke 24 of the questionings of the heart. Understanding also takes place in the heart (Matt. 13). Mary kept certain sayings and pondered them in her heart (Luke 2), and according to Hebrews 4, thoughts are in the heart. From these verses we can see clearly that the heart includes the mind.", "norm_zh": "二心挂着心思例如心里怀着恶念太九心里议论可二心里妄想路一心里起疑念路二四都是在心里的故事心里明白太十三存在心里反复思想路二心中的思念来四都可见心是挂着心思的部分所以说心挂着心思", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The heart includes the mind In Matthew 9 we read Why are you thinking evil things in your hearts Mark 2 speaks of reasoning in the heart Luke 1 speaks of the imagination of the heart and Luke 24 of the questionings of the heart Understanding also takes place in the heart Matt 13 Mary kept certain sayings and pondered them in her heart Luke 2 and according to Hebrews 4 thoughts are in the heart From these verses we can see clearly that the heart includes the mind"}
{"zh": "（三）心挂着意志　例如：“立定心志”（徒十一），“心里顺服”（罗六），“本心所酌定的”（林后九），“心中的……主意”（来四），可见心是挂着意志的部分。所以说，心挂着意志。", "en": "3) The heart includes the will. Acts 11 has this phrase: \"with purpose of heart\"; Romans 6 mentions having \"obeyed out from the heart\"; 2 Corinthians 9 says that one can purpose in his heart; and Hebrews 4 speaks of the \"intents of the heart.\" These verses show us clearly that the heart includes the will.", "norm_zh": "三心挂着意志例如立定心志徒十一心里顺服罗六本心所酌定的林后九心中的主意来四可见心是挂着意志的部分所以说心挂着意志", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The heart includes the will Acts 11 has this phrase with purpose of heart Romans 6 mentions having obeyed out from the heart 2 Corinthians 9 says that one can purpose in his heart and Hebrews 4 speaks of the intents of the heart These verses show us clearly that the heart includes the will"}
{"zh": "（四）心挂着情感　例如：“心里冰凉”（创四五），“心……火热”（路二四），“心里不要忧愁”（约十四），“心就喜乐”（十六），可见心是挂着情感的部分。所以说，心挂着情感。", "en": "4) The heart includes the emotion. Genesis 45 has \"his heart was cold\"; Luke 24 mentions \"heart... burning\"; John 14 says, \"Let not your heart be troubled\"; and John 16 says, \"your heart will rejoice.\" These verses show us clearly that the heart includes the emotion.", "norm_zh": "四心挂着情感例如心里冰凉创四五心火热路二四心里不要忧愁约十四心就喜乐十六可见心是挂着情感的部分所以说心挂着情感", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The heart includes the emotion Genesis 45 has his heart was cold Luke 24 mentions heart burning John 14 says Let not your heart be troubled and John 16 says your heart will rejoice These verses show us clearly that the heart includes the emotion"}
{"zh": "心是在灵与魂之间的。所以，凡要进入灵的，都得通过心而入；凡要从灵发出的，都得通过心而出。箴言四章二十三节说，“你要保守你心，胜过保守一切；因为一生的出口是由心发出。”这意思是说，心是生命的出口；换句话说，人外面所结的果，都是由心发出的。所以心是最要紧的东西。", "en": "The heart is between the spirit and the soul. Therefore all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart, and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heart. Proverbs 4:23 says, \"Keep thy heart with all diligence; for out of it are the issues of life.\" This means that the heart is the exit through which the life flows out. In other words, the fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart, and for this reason the heart is the most important thing.", "norm_zh": "心是在灵与魂之间的所以凡要进入灵的都得通过心而入凡要从灵发出的都得通过心而出箴言四章二十三节说你要保守你心胜过保守一切因为一生的出口是由心发出这意思是说心是生命的出口换句话说人外面所结的果都是由心发出的所以心是最要紧的东西", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The heart is between the spirit and the soul Therefore all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heart Proverbs 423 says Keep thy heart with all diligence for out of it are the issues of life This means that the heart is the exit through which the life flows out In other words the fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart and for this reason the heart is the most important thing"}
{"zh": "心是生命运行的必经之路。所以，神的生命要进到我们里面，总是先打动我们的心。如果心没有忧伤，没有悔改，神的生命就没有法子进来。神若不是叫我们感觉罪恶的痛苦，就是叫我们尝到神爱的甘甜，或是觉得基督的宝贵，总是先来打动我们的心，叫我们忧伤，叫我们悔改。在这里，心里的忧伤是良心的故事，悔改是心思的转变。当我们的心这样被打动的时候，我们的意志一决定，我们的心就相信，从这里一接受基督，神的生命就进到我们里面了，神的生命就种在我们里面了（彼前一）。", "en": "The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves. Therefore, before God's life enters into us, what must be touched first is our heart. If our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented, God's life cannot enter. Whether God causes us to feel the sufferings of sin, the sweetness of His love, or the preciousness of Christ, He always does it by touching our heart, causing us to feel sorrowful and bringing us to repentance. The sorrowfulness of the heart is the specific function of the conscience, and being repentant is the turning of the mind. When our heart is thus touched, our will decides and our heart believes. By this receiving of Christ, the life of God enters into us and is planted within us (1 Pet. 1).", "norm_zh": "心是生命运行的必经之路所以神的生命要进到我们里面总是先打动我们的心如果心没有忧伤没有悔改神的生命就没有法子进来神若不是叫我们感觉罪恶的痛苦就是叫我们尝到神爱的甘甜或是觉得基督的宝贵总是先来打动我们的心叫我们忧伤叫我们悔改在这里心里的忧伤是良心的故事悔改是心思的转变当我们的心这样被打动的时候我们的意志一决定我们的心就相信从这里一接受基督神的生命就进到我们里面了神的生命就种在我们里面了彼前一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves Therefore before Gods life enters into us what must be touched first is our heart If our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented Gods life cannot enter Whether God causes us to feel the sufferings of sin the sweetness of His love or the preciousness of Christ He always does it by touching our heart causing us to feel sorrowful and bringing us to repentance The sorrowfulness of the heart is the specific function of the conscience and being repentant is the turning of the mind When our heart is thus touched our will decides and our heart believes By this receiving of Christ the life of God enters into us and is planted within us 1 Pet 1"}
{"zh": "一粒生命的种子种在地里，是能生长的，并且是一直生长下去的。但是，它的生长不是没有条件的。比方：种子种下去以后，从来不浇水，也没有雨水，就要拦阻它的生长。不只生命是这样，就是物理也是这样。象电，它的力量是大的，但是，一个小小的开关一关，就能把它停了。不错，生命的力量是大的、是自然的；但是，如果有东西阻碍它的发展，不履行它发展的条件，那它就发展不来，似乎它的发展是有止境的了。", "en": "A grain of wheat planted into the earth will begin to grow and continue to grow. However, its growth does require certain conditions. For instance, if the seed is planted but is never watered, its growth will be hindered. We see this same principle not only in life, but also in physics. Electricity is powerful, but when the little switch is turned off, the flow of electricity is stopped. It is true that life is powerful and spontaneous, but if there is something hindering its development or if the conditions for its development are absent, it will not grow. It will appear as if the growth has stopped.", "norm_zh": "一粒生命的种子种在地里是能生长的并且是一直生长下去的但是它的生长不是没有条件的比方种子种下去以后从来不浇水也没有雨水就要拦阻它的生长不只生命是这样就是物理也是这样象电它的力量是大的但是一个小小的开关一关就能把它停了不错生命的力量是大的是自然的但是如果有东西阻碍它的发展不履行它发展的条件哪它就发展不来似乎它的发展是有止境的了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A grain of wheat planted into the earth will begin to grow and continue to grow However its growth does require certain conditions For instance if the seed is planted but is never watered its growth will be hindered We see this same principle not only in life but also in physics Electricity is powerful but when the little switch is turned off the flow of electricity is stopped It is true that life is powerful and spontaneous but if there is something hindering its development or if the conditions for its development are absent it will not grow It will appear as if the growth has stopped"}
{"zh": "神的生命要从我们里面往外去", "en": "God's life wants to move out from within us.", "norm_zh": "神的生命要从我们里面往外去", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:14:37.798438+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods life wants to move out from within us"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要说到神如何把律法放在我们里面，写在我们心上，我们还得从重生说起；因为重生是圣灵把神非受造的生命放在人的灵里，重生乃是生命的问题—约壹二29，五4、6、14、18：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "I. When speaking of how God has put His law within us and has inscribed it upon our hearts, we must start from regeneration; for regeneration means that the Holy Spirit has put the uncreated life of God into man's spirit; regeneration is a matter of life.—1 John 2:29; 5:4, 6, 14, 18:", "norm_zh": "壹我们要说到神如何把律法放在我们里面写在我们心上我们还得从重生说起因为重生是圣灵把神非受造的生命放在人的灵里重生乃是生命的问提约壹二29五461418李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I When speaking of how God has put His law within us and has inscribed it upon our hearts we must start from regeneration for regeneration means that the Holy Spirit has put the uncreated life of God into mans spirit regeneration is a matter of life1 John 229 54 6 14 18"}
{"zh": "一\t要说到重生，我们还得从人的创造说起；创世记二章七节说，“耶和华神用地上的尘土造人，将生命的气吹在他的鼻孔里，他就成了一个活的魂”：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. Before we can speak adequately of regeneration we must say something regarding the creation of man; we read in Genesis 2:7 that \"Jehovah God formed man of the dust of the ground, and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life; and man became a living soul\":", "norm_zh": "一要说到重生我们还得从人的创造说起创世记二章七节说耶和华神用地上的尘土造人将生命的气吹在他的鼻孔里他就成了一个活的魂李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we can speak adequately of regeneration we must say something regarding the creation of man we read in Genesis 27 that Jehovah God formed man of the dust of the ground and breathed into his nostrils the breath of life and man became a living soul"}
{"zh": "1\t神将生命的气吹入人的身体就成为灵，同时这灵与身体接触，就产生了魂；这是我们里面属灵、属魂两个生命的来源—创二7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. When God breathed the breath of life into man's body, it became the spirit; and at the same time, when this spirit came into contact with the body, it produced the soul; this is the way in which the spiritual life and the soulish life originated in man.—Gen. 2:7.", "norm_zh": "1神将生命的气吹入人的身体就成为灵同时这灵与身体接触就产生了魂这是我们里面属灵属魂两个生命的来源创二7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When God breathed the breath of life into mans body it became the spirit and at the same time when this spirit came into contact with the body it produced the soul this is the way in which the spiritual life and the soulish life originated in manGen 27"}
{"zh": "2\t一个人是分作三部分的，就是灵、魂、体；新约圣经也是这样把人分作三部分；象帖前五章二十三节说，“又愿你们的灵，与魂，与身子，得蒙保守。”（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. Man is composed of three parts: the spirit, the soul, and the body; the New Testament also shows that man is tripartite; for example, 1 Thes. 5:23 says, \"May your spirit and soul and body be preserved entire.\"", "norm_zh": "2一个人是分作三部分的就是灵魂体新约圣经也是这样把人分作三部分象帖前五章二十三节说又愿你们的灵与魂与身子得蒙保守李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Man is composed of three parts the spirit the soul and the body the New Testament also shows that man is tripartite for example 1 Thes 523 says May your spirit and soul and body be preserved entire"}
{"zh": "3\t体就是“世界知觉”的所在，魂就是“自己知觉”的所在，灵就是“神知觉”的所在—约四24，太十六26，罗八11。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. The body is the seat of world-consciousness; the soul is the seat of self-consciousness; and the spirit is the seat of God-consciousness.—John 4:24; Matt. 16:26; Rom. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "3体就是世界知觉的所在魂就是自己知觉的所在灵就是神知觉的所在约四24太十六26罗八11李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The body is the seat of worldconsciousness the soul is the seat of selfconsciousness and the spirit is the seat of GodconsciousnessJohn 424 Matt 1626 Rom 811"}
{"zh": "4\t灵借着魂管理全人：灵要有动作，就达意于魂，魂就运动身体，以服从灵的命令—帖前五23节注5：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "4. Through the soul, the spirit controls man's whole being. Whenever the spirit wants to do something, it passes its intention on to the soul, and the soul exercises the body to obey the command from the spirit.—1 Thes. 5:23, note 5:", "norm_zh": "4灵借着魂管理全人灵要有动作就达意于魂魂就运动身体以服从灵的命令帖前五23节注5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Through the soul the spirit controls mans whole being Whenever the spirit wants to do something it passes its intention on to the soul and the soul exercises the body to obey the command from the spirit1 Thes 523 note 5"}
{"zh": "a\t按着神的安排，灵乃是最高的部分，应当管治全人。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "a. According to God's arrangement, the human spirit is the highest part of man and should rule his whole being.", "norm_zh": "a按着神的安排灵乃是最高的部分应当管治全人李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a According to Gods arrangement the human spirit is the highest part of man and should rule his whole being"}
{"zh": "b\t然而意志是人格最主要的部分，又是属于魂的；人（魂）的意志能有自主的权柄，它可以拣选到底是由灵来掌权，或是由体来掌权，还是由己来掌权—徒十一23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "b. Yet, the will is the most prominent part of man's personality and belongs to the soul. The will of man is also able to make its own choice. It can choose whether to be ruled by the spirit, by the body, or by the self.—Acts 11:23.", "norm_zh": "b然而意志是人格最主要的部分又是属于魂的人魂的意志能有自主的权柄它可以拣选到底是由灵来掌权或是由体来掌权还是由己来掌权徒十一23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Yet the will is the most prominent part of mans personality and belongs to the soul The will of man is also able to make its own choice It can choose whether to be ruled by the spirit by the body or by the selfActs 1123"}
{"zh": "二\t神造人的目的；神有一个永远的目的，就是要把祂自己给人—创二9、16：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. God's purpose in creating man; God has an eternal purpose, which is to give Himself to man—Gen. 2:9, 16:", "norm_zh": "二神造人的目的神有一个永远的目的就是要把祂自己给人创二916李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Gods purpose in creating man God has an eternal purpose which is to give Himself to manGen 29 16"}
{"zh": "1\t人原来是神所创造的，所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的；以人原来受造的生命来说，是正直的，是好的—二7，传七29，创一26。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Originally man was made by God; man's original life was made by God also; as far as man's original created life was concerned, it was upright and it was good.—2:7; Eccl. 7:29; Gen. 1:26.", "norm_zh": "1人原来是神所创造的所以人原有的生命也是神所创造的以人原来受造的生命来说是正直的是好的二7传七29创一26李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Originally man was made by God mans original life was made by God also as far as mans original created life was concerned it was upright and it was good27 Eccl 729 Gen 126"}
{"zh": "2\t但是，以神永远的目的来说，人还没有神自己那非受造的生命；所以，人还需要拣选神，需要拣选神的生命—二16~17。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. But as far as God's eternal purpose, man had not yet received the uncreated life of God; therefore man still needed to choose God and God's life.—2:16-17.", "norm_zh": "2但是以神永远的目的来说人还没有神自己哪非受造的生命所以人还需要拣选神需要拣选神的生命二1617李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 But as far as Gods eternal purpose man had not yet received the uncreated life of God therefore man still needed to choose God and Gods life21617"}
{"zh": "三\t人的堕落—17节，三6，弗二1、5，西二13，来九27：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. MAN'S FALL—v. 17; 3:6; Eph. 2:1, 5; Col. 2:13; Heb. 9:27:", "norm_zh": "三人的堕落17节三6弗二15西二13来九27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C MANS FALLv 17 36 Eph 21 5 Col 213 Heb 927"}
{"zh": "1\t那人（亚当）竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子，竟然不拣选生命，人堕落了，人犯罪了—创三6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. The man Adam did not choose life. He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eat.—Gen. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1哪人亚当竟然吃了神所禁止吃的分别善恶树的果子竟然不拣选生命人堕落了人犯罪了创三6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The man Adam did not choose life He sinned and became fallen by eating the fruit of the tree of the knowledge of good and evil which God forbade him to eatGen 36"}
{"zh": "2\t当初神对亚当说，“你吃的日子必定死”；所以这里的死，不只是肉体要死，必定是灵先死了；死的意思就是远离生命；乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通，已经失去他敏锐的知觉—二17，弗二1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. God told Adam from the beginning, \"in the day that you eat of it you shall surely die\"; therefore, the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires; death simply means to be estranged from life; but that his spirit lost its fellowship with God; it lost its keen sense.—Gen. 2:17; Eph. 2:1.", "norm_zh": "2当初神对亚当说你吃的日子必定死所以这里的死不只是肉体要死必定是灵先死了死的意思就是远离生命乃是说他的灵对于神已经失去交通已经失去他敏锐的知觉二17弗二1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 God told Adam from the beginning in the day that you eat of it you shall surely die therefore the death spoken of here implies that the spirit will die before the flesh expires death simply means to be estranged from life but that his spirit lost its fellowship with God it lost its keen senseGen 217 Eph 21"}
{"zh": "3\t祂既然有了一个美意，祂既然有了一个永远的计划，祂就必定要成功祂永远的旨意；祂要来解决人的罪，将堕落的人救回；祂要借着祂的儿子将祂的生命释放出来；祂要借着圣灵来重生人—约十二24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. Since He has a good pleasure and since He has an eternal plan, He will surely accomplish His eternal will; He will solve the problem of man's sin and redeem fallen man; He will release His life through His Son, and He will regenerate man through the Holy Spirit.—John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "3祂既然有了一个美意祂既然有了一个永远的计划祂就必定要成功祂永远的旨意祂要来解决人的罪将堕落的人救回祂要借着祂的儿子将祂的生命释放出来祂要借着圣灵来重生人约十二24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Since He has a good pleasure and since He has an eternal plan He will surely accomplish His eternal will He will solve the problem of mans sin and redeem fallen man He will release His life through His Son and He will regenerate man through the Holy SpiritJohn 1224"}
{"zh": "四\t神的救法—彼前二24，西三3，赛五三11~12，来九28，民二一9：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. THE WAY OF GOD'S SALVATION—1 Pet. 2:24; Col. 3:3; Isa. 53:11-12; Heb. 9:28; Num. 21:9:", "norm_zh": "四神的救法彼前二24西三3赛五三1112来九28民二一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D THE WAY OF GODS SALVATION1 Pet 224 Col 33 Isa 531112 Heb 928 Num 219"}
{"zh": "1\t基督在十字架上，亲身担当了我们的罪，就是“使我们既然在罪上死，就得以在义上活”；这就是摩西在旷野举蛇所预表的—彼前二24，民二一9，约三14，罗八3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Christ Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross, \"that we, having died unto sins, might live unto righteousness\"; this was typified by Moses lifting up the serpent in the wilderness.—1 Pet. 2:24; Num. 21:9; John 3:14; Rom. 8:3.", "norm_zh": "1基督在十字架上亲身担当了我们的罪就是使我们既然在罪上死就得以在义上活这就是摩西在旷野举蛇所预表的彼前二24民二一9约三14罗八3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christ Himself bore our sins in His body on the cross that we having died unto sins might live unto righteousness this was typified by Moses lifting up the serpent in the wilderness1 Pet 224 Num 219 John 314 Rom 83"}
{"zh": "2\t基督在十字架上受死，就将祂（基督）里面所藏着的神的生命释放出来；因为基督就是那一粒麦子落在地里死了，神的生命就释放出来了—约十二24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. The life of God which is in Christ was released when Christ died on the cross; for Christ is the grain of wheat which fell into the earth and died; when Christ died, God's life was released.—John 12:24.", "norm_zh": "2基督在十字架上受死就将祂基督里面所藏着的神的生命释放出来因为基督就是哪一粒麦子落在地里死了神的生命就释放出来了约十二24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The life of God which is in Christ was released when Christ died on the cross for Christ is the grain of wheat which fell into the earth and died when Christ died Gods life was releasedJohn 1224"}
{"zh": "3\t所以神借耶稣基督从死里复活，就重生了我们—彼前一3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. Therefore, God regenerated us through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead.—1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "3所以神借耶稣基督从死里复活就重生了我们彼前一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Therefore God regenerated us through the resurrection of Jesus Christ from the dead1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "五\t重生，是“从水和圣灵生的”—约三3~8：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "E. Regeneration is to be \"born of water and the Spirit.\"—John 3:3-8:", "norm_zh": "五重生是从水和圣灵生的约三38李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Regeneration is to be born of water and the SpiritJohn 338"}
{"zh": "1\t人因着悔改而进入水，人因着相信而进入圣灵；人这样进入水，又进入圣灵，就是从水和圣灵生的—徒二38，二十21。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Because of repentance man enters into the water, and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit; by entering into the water and the Spirit, he is born of water and of the Spirit—Acts 2:38; 20:21.", "norm_zh": "1人因着悔改而进入水人因着相信而进入圣灵人这样进入水又进入圣灵就是从水和圣灵生的徒二38二十21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Because of repentance man enters into the water and because of faith he enters into the Holy Spirit by entering into the water and the Spirit he is born of water and of the SpiritActs 238 2021"}
{"zh": "2\t悔改而进入水，就结束了旧人的生命；相信而进入圣灵，就得着了神的生命；这样一来，就是重生—二38。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man; by believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain God's life; this is regeneration—Acts 2:38.", "norm_zh": "2悔改而进入水就结束了旧人的生命相信而进入圣灵就得着了神的生命这样一来就是重生二38李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through repentance we enter into the water and terminate the life of the old man by believing we enter into the Holy Spirit and obtain Gods life this is regenerationActs 238"}
{"zh": "3\t使人重生的工作，在主观方面，完全是圣灵自己作的（在客观方面，完全是基督作的）；所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到“从水生”，而三次提到“从圣灵生”—约三3、5~6、8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. The work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit (objectively, it is accomplished completely by Christ); therefore, in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being \"born of water,\" while he mentioned being \"born of the Spirit\" three times—John 3:3, 5-6, 8.", "norm_zh": "3使人重生的工作在主观方面完全是圣灵自己作的在客观方面完全是基督作的所以主耶稣在约翰第三章一次提到从水生而三次提到从圣灵生约三3568李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The work which brings a man subjectively to regeneration is accomplished completely by the Holy Spirit objectively it is accomplished completely by Christ therefore in John 3 the Lord Jesus spoke only once of being born of water while he mentioned being born of the Spirit three timesJohn 33 56 8"}
{"zh": "六\t重生，是“从圣灵生”；圣灵来叫人悔改，叫人“为罪……自己责备自己”—5节，十六8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "F. Regeneration means that we have been \"born of the Spirit\"; the Spirit comes to cause man to repent and to \"convict the world concerning sin\"—v. 5; 16:8.", "norm_zh": "六重生是从圣灵生圣灵来叫人悔改叫人为罪自己责备自己5节十六8李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Regeneration means that we have been born of the Spirit the Spirit comes to cause man to repent and to convict the world concerning sinv 5 168"}
{"zh": "七\t重生不是别的，乃是人在自己的生命之外，再得着神的生命；我们一得着重生，就有“权柄作神的儿女”—一12~13：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "G. Regeneration is nought else but the fact of man, in addition to his own life, receiving the life of God; once we receive regeneration, we have the \"authority to become children of God\"—1:12-13:", "norm_zh": "七重生不是别的乃是人在自己的生命之外再得着神的生命我们一得着重生就有权柄作神的儿女一1213李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G Regeneration is nought else but the fact of man in addition to his own life receiving the life of God once we receive regeneration we have the authority to become children of God11213"}
{"zh": "1\t神的生命，是有神的性情的；所以我们一得着神的生命，就“得与神的性情有分”—彼后一4：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. In God's life is God's nature; therefore, once we receive God's life, we \"become partakers of the divine nature\"—2 Pet. 1:4:", "norm_zh": "1神的生命是有神的性情的所以我们一得着神的生命就得与神的性情有分彼后一4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In Gods life is Gods nature therefore once we receive Gods life we become partakers of the divine nature2 Pet 14"}
{"zh": "a\t“人的灵是耶和华的灯”；亚当堕落后，这个灵就黑暗了—箴二十27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "a. \"The spirit of man is the lamp of Jehovah\"; after Adam's fall, this spirit became darkened—Prov. 20:27.", "norm_zh": "a人的灵是耶和华的灯亚当堕落后这个灵就黑暗了箴二十27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The spirit of man is the lamp of Jehovah after Adams fall this spirit became darkenedProv 2027"}
{"zh": "b\t当圣灵重生我们，将神的生命放到我们的里面，就叫我们的灵活过来，就好象把灯点亮了一般—弗二5~6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "b. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us and put God's life into us, He made our spirit alive; it was like lighting a lamp—Eph. 2:5-6.", "norm_zh": "b当圣灵重生我们将神的生命放到我们的里面就叫我们的灵活过来就好象把灯点亮了一般弗二56李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b When the Holy Spirit regenerated us and put Gods life into us He made our spirit alive it was like lighting a lampEph 256"}
{"zh": "2\t人如果说他重生了，而他对于神从来不认识，对于罪一点感觉都没有，就这个人的重生是可疑惑的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. If a man says that he is regenerated, yet has no knowledge of God and no feeling concerning sin, his regeneration is doubtful.", "norm_zh": "2人如果说他重生了而他对于神从来不认识对于罪一点感觉都没有就这个人的重生是可疑惑的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If a man says that he is regenerated yet has no knowledge of God and no feeling concerning sin his regeneration is doubtful"}
{"zh": "八\t当圣灵重生我们的时候，还赐给我们一个“新心”，将“新灵”放在我们里面—结三六26~27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "H. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us, He also gave us a \"new heart\" and put a \"new spirit\" within us—Ezek. 36:26-27.", "norm_zh": "八当圣灵重生我们的时候还赐给我们一个新心将新灵放在我们里面结三六2627李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H When the Holy Spirit regenerated us He also gave us a new heart and put a new spirit within usEzek 362627"}
{"zh": "九\t基督在十字架上所成功的是客观的，圣灵住在我们里面，要把客观的事实变成我们主观的经历；真理的圣灵是把人带进到实际里去的—约十四16~17、26。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "IX. What Christ accomplished on the cross is objective, but the Spirit indwelling us turns the objective facts into our subjective experience; the Spirit of reality guides man into all the reality.—John 14:16-17, 26.", "norm_zh": "九基督在十字架上所成功的是客观的圣灵住在我们里面要把客观的事实变成我们主观的经历真理的圣灵是把人带进到实际里去的约十四161726李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX What Christ accomplished on the cross is objective but the Spirit indwelling us turns the objective facts into our subjective experience the Spirit of reality guides man into all the realityJohn 141617 26"}
{"zh": "十\t我们所得的这个生命是完全的，却不是成熟的；所以人重生之后，还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新，让这生命能完全于全人的各部分—西三4，彼前二2节注5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "X. This life which we have obtained is complete, yet it is not matured; therefore, after regeneration man needs a long process of renewal by the Holy Spirit until this life is perfected in every part of his being.—Col. 3:4; 1 Pet. 2:2, note 5.", "norm_zh": "十我们所得的这个生命是完全的却不是成熟的所以人重生之后还需要圣灵长久继续不断地更新让这生命能完全于全人的各部分西三4彼前二2节注5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X This life which we have obtained is complete yet it is not matured therefore after regeneration man needs a long process of renewal by the Holy Spirit until this life is perfected in every part of his beingCol 34 1 Pet 22 note 5"}
{"zh": "贰\t生命的律；“我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面，写在他们心上”—来八10：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "II. The law of life; \"I will impart My laws into their mind, and on their hearts I will inscribe them\"—Heb. 8:10:", "norm_zh": "贰生命的律我要将我的诸律法放在他们心意里面写在他们心上来八10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The law of life I will impart My laws into their mind and on their hearts I will inscribe themHeb 810"}
{"zh": "一\t在旧约，律法是放在人的外面，写在石版上的；在新约，律法是放在我们里面，写在我们心上的—林后三3，出二四12，申四13：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. In the old covenant the law was placed outside of man and written on tables of stone; in the new covenant the law is put inside of man and inscribed upon his heart—2 Cor. 3:3; Exo. 24:12; Deut. 4:13:", "norm_zh": "一在旧约律法是放在人的外面写在石版上的在新约律法是放在我们里面写在我们心上的林后三3出二四12申四13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the old covenant the law was placed outside of man and written on tables of stone in the new covenant the law is put inside of man and inscribed upon his heart2 Cor 33 Exo 2412 Deut 413"}
{"zh": "1\t放在外面，写在石版上的，必定是字句—林后三6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. That which was placed outside of man and written upon tables of stone must be of the letter—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1放在外面写在石版上的必定是字句林后三6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 That which was placed outside of man and written upon tables of stone must be of the letter2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t那么，能放在我们里面，能写在我们心上的是什么律法呢？乃是一个生命的律；神放在我们里面的律，乃是出于神放在我们里面的生命—罗八2。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. In that case, what is the law that can be put inside of us and inscribed upon our hearts? It is the law of life; the law which God imparted into us comes from the life which God imparted into us.—Rom. 8:2.", "norm_zh": "2哪么能放在我们里面能写在我们心上的是什么律法呢乃是一个生命的律神放在我们里面的律乃是出于神放在我们里面的生命罗八2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In that case what is the law that can be put inside of us and inscribed upon our hearts It is the law of life the law which God imparted into us comes from the life which God imparted into usRom 82"}
{"zh": "二\t神放在我们里面的既然是生命，所以必定有律，也必定有自自然然的功用；这个律会把生命自自然然地“律”出来；只要我们不拦阻它，它总是自自然然地出来—2~4、7~11节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. Since what God has imparted into us is life, the law of the life must also be there, and it must have its spontaneous function; this law will spontaneously live out the life in us; as long as we do not hinder it, it will spontaneously come forth.—vv. 2-4, 7-11.", "norm_zh": "二神放在我们里面的既然是生命所以必定有律也必定有自自然然的功用这个律会把生命自自然然地律出来只要我们不拦阻它它总是自自然然地出来24711节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since what God has imparted into us is life the law of the life must also be there and it must have its spontaneous function this law will spontaneously live out the life in us as long as we do not hinder it it will spontaneously come forthvv 24 711"}
{"zh": "叁\t心挂着良心，挂着心思，挂着意志，挂着情感—弗三17上，一18节注2：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "III. The heart includes the conscience, the mind, the will, and the emotion—Eph. 3:17a; 1:18, note 2:", "norm_zh": "叁心挂着良心挂着心思挂着意志挂着情感弗三17上一18节注2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The heart includes the conscience the mind the will and the emotionEph 317a 118 note 2"}
{"zh": "一\t心挂着良心；例如：“我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去”，这里的“天良”，就是“良心”—来十22，九14，约壹三20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. The heart includes the conscience; for example: \"Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience,\" here \"tian-liang\" [good conscience] is the \"conscience\"—Heb. 10:22; 9:14; 1 John 3:20.", "norm_zh": "一心挂着良心例如我们心中天良的亏欠已经洒去这里的天良就是良心来十22九14约壹三20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The heart includes the conscience for example Having our hearts sprinkled from an evil conscience here tianliang good conscience is the conscienceHeb 1022 914 1 John 320"}
{"zh": "二\t心挂着心思；例如：“心里怀着恶念”，“心里议论”，“心里妄想”，“心里起疑念”，都是在心里的故事—太九4，可二6，路一66。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. The heart includes the mind; for example: \"thinking evil things in your hearts,\" \"reasoning in the heart,\" \"imagination of the heart,\" \"questionings of the heart\" — all are matters in the heart.—Matt. 9:4; Mark 2:6; Luke 1:66.", "norm_zh": "二心挂着心思例如心里怀着恶念心里议论心里妄想心里起疑念都是在心里的故事太九4可二6路一66李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The heart includes the mind for example thinking evil things in your hearts reasoning in the heart imagination of the heart questionings of the heart all are matters in the heartMatt 94 Mark 26 Luke 166"}
{"zh": "三\t心挂着意志；例如：“立定心志”，“心里顺服”，“本心所酌定的”，“心中的……主意”，可见心是挂着意志的部分—徒十一23，罗六17，林后九7，来四12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. The heart includes the will; for example, \"with purpose of heart,\" \"obeyed out from the heart,\" \"purposed in his heart,\" \"intents of the heart,\" showing that the heart is the part that includes the will—Acts 11:23; Rom. 6:17; 2 Cor. 9:7; Heb. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "三心挂着意志例如立定心志心里顺服本心所酌定的心中的主意可见心是挂着意志的部分徒十一23罗六17林后九7来四12李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The heart includes the will for example with purpose of heart obeyed out from the heart purposed in his heart intents of the heart showing that the heart is the part that includes the willActs 1123 Rom 617 2 Cor 97 Heb 412"}
{"zh": "四\t心挂着情感；例如：“心里冰凉”，“心……火热”，“心里不要忧愁”，“心就喜乐”，可见心是挂着情感的部分—创四五26，路二四32，约十四1，十六22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. The heart includes the emotion; for example, \"Jacob's heart fainted,\" \"heart... burn,\" \"heart be troubled,\" \"heart will rejoice,\" showing that the heart is the part that includes the emotion—Gen. 45:26; Luke 24:32; John 14:1; 16:22.", "norm_zh": "四心挂着情感例如心里冰凉心火热心里不要忧愁心就喜乐可见心是挂着情感的部分创四五26路二四32约十四1十六22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The heart includes the emotion for example Jacobs heart fainted heart burn heart be troubled heart will rejoice showing that the heart is the part that includes the emotionGen 4526 Luke 2432 John 141 1622"}
{"zh": "五\t以律的本身来说，是单数的；以这个律运行的功用来说，是多数的；这好象自来水，源头是一个，但管子是多数的—来八10，十16。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "E. As far as the law itself is concerned, it is singular; but concerning the function of this law in our being, it is plural; it is just like running water; the source is one, but the pipes are many—Heb. 8:10; 10:16.", "norm_zh": "五以律的本身来说是单数的以这个律运行的功用来说是多数的这好象自来水源头是一个但管子是多数的来八10十16李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E As far as the law itself is concerned it is singular but concerning the function of this law in our being it is plural it is just like running water the source is one but the pipes are manyHeb 810 1016"}
{"zh": "肆\t心是生命的进出口—诗四4，可四28：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "IV. The Heart Being the Gate of Our Being—Psa. 4:4; Mark 4:28:", "norm_zh": "肆心是生命的进出口诗四4可四28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The Heart Being the Gate of Our BeingPsa 44 Mark 428"}
{"zh": "一\t心是在灵与魂之间的；所以，凡要进入灵的，都得通过心而入；凡要从灵发出的，都得通过心而出—箴四23，太五3、8：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. The heart is between the spirit and the soul; therefore, all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart, and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heart—Prov. 4:23; Matt. 5:3, 8:", "norm_zh": "一心是在灵与魂之间的所以凡要进入灵的都得通过心而入凡要从灵发出的都得通过心而出箴四23太五38李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The heart is between the spirit and the soul therefore all that enters into the spirit must pass through the heart and all that comes forth from the spirit must also pass through the heartProv 423 Matt 53 8"}
{"zh": "1\t人外面所结的果，都是由心发出的；所以心是最要紧的东西—可四28，太十二33~37，箴四23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. The fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart, and for this reason the heart is the most important thing—Mark 4:28; Matt. 12:33-37; Prov. 4:23.", "norm_zh": "1人外面所结的果都是由心发出的所以心是最要紧的东西可四28太十二3337箴四23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The fruit which man produces outwardly comes out of his heart and for this reason the heart is the most important thingMark 428 Matt 123337 Prov 423"}
{"zh": "2\t心是生命运行的必经之路；所以，神的生命要进到我们里面，总是先打动我们的心；如果心没有忧伤，没有悔改，神的生命就没有法子进来—林后五14，徒二37~38，参太三2。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves; therefore, before God's life enters into us, what must be touched first is our heart; if our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented, God's life cannot enter—2 Cor. 5:14; Acts 2:37-38; cf. Matt. 3:2.", "norm_zh": "2心是生命运行的必经之路所以神的生命要进到我们里面总是先打动我们的心如果心没有忧伤没有悔改神的生命就没有法子进来林后五14徒二3738参太三2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The heart is the necessary path through which the life moves therefore before Gods life enters into us what must be touched first is our heart if our heart has not become sorrowful and has not yet repented Gods life cannot enter2 Cor 514 Acts 23738 cf Matt 32"}
{"zh": "二\t心是生命的一个开关—箴四23，太十二33~37，参结三六26~27：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. The Heart is the Switch of Life—Prov. 4:23; Matt. 12:33-37; cf. Ezek. 36:26-27:", "norm_zh": "二心是生命的一个开关箴四23太十二3337参结三六2627李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Heart is the Switch of LifeProv 423 Matt 123337 cf Ezek 362627"}
{"zh": "1\t你的生命能不能向外发展出去，是看你的心向神是不是开启的—箴四23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Whether the life within us can grow depends upon whether our heart is open toward God—Prov. 4:23.", "norm_zh": "1你的生命能不能向外发展出去是看你的心向神是不是开启的箴四23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Whether the life within us can grow depends upon whether our heart is open toward GodProv 423"}
{"zh": "2\t心只能爱神而不能摸着神，心只能倾向神而不能与神交通；能摸着神，能与神交通的，乃是灵—约十四24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. The heart can love God, but it cannot touch God; the heart can incline to God, but cannot have fellowship with God; only the spirit can touch God and have fellowship with God—John 14:24.", "norm_zh": "2心只能爱神而不能摸着神心只能倾向神而不能与神交通能摸着神能与神交通的乃是灵约十四24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The heart can love God but it cannot touch God the heart can incline to God but cannot have fellowship with God only the spirit can touch God and have fellowship with GodJohn 1424"}
{"zh": "3\t你的心好象电灯开关，一开，灯就亮了；一关，灯就熄了；你的心如果向神是开着的，神与你交通，与你来往，就是容易的事—太五3、8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. Our heart is like the electric switch; when it is turned on, the light goes on. When it is shut off, the light goes out. If our heart is open to God, it is easy for God to have fellowship with us.—Matt. 5:3, 8.", "norm_zh": "3你的心好象电灯开关一开灯就亮了一关灯就熄了你的心如果向神是开着的神与你交通与你来往就是容易的事太五38李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Our heart is like the electric switch when it is turned on the light goes on When it is shut off the light goes out If our heart is open to God it is easy for God to have fellowship with usMatt 53 8"}
{"zh": "4\t圣灵重生了我们以后，我们是得着了一个非受造的生命，就是神的生命；如果我们的心有了问题，神的生命就要受很大的拦阻—十二33~37。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "4. When the Holy Spirit regenerated us, we received the uncreated life of God; if our heart has problems, God's life will be greatly hindered.—Matt. 12:33-37.", "norm_zh": "4圣灵重生了我们以后我们是得着了一个非受造的生命就是神的生命如果我们的心有了问提神的生命就要受很大的拦阻十二3337李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 When the Holy Spirit regenerated us we received the uncreated life of God if our heart has problems Gods life will be greatly hinderedMatt 123337"}
{"zh": "三\t以弗所四章十七节，“所以我这样说，且在主里见证，你们行事为人，不要再像外邦人在他们心思的虚妄里行事为人”：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. Ephesians 4:17, \"This therefore I say and testify in the Lord, that you no longer walk as the Gentiles also walk in the vanity of their mind\":", "norm_zh": "三以弗所四章十七节所以我这样说且在主里见证你们行事为人不要再像外邦人在他们心思的虚妄里行事为人李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Ephesians 417 This therefore I say and testify in the Lord that you no longer walk as the Gentiles also walk in the vanity of their mind"}
{"zh": "1\t我们人有三个得知识的机关：在身体方面的是头脑，在灵方面的是直觉，在魂方面的是悟性，这悟性又是受直觉支配的—出三一3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. In our human being there are three organs of perception: in our body there is the brain, in our spirit there is the intuition, and in our soul there is the mind. Our mind should be governed by our intuition.—Exo. 31:3:", "norm_zh": "1我们人有三个得知识的机关在身体方面的是头脑在灵方面的是直觉在魂方面的是悟性这悟性又是受直觉支配的出三一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In our human being there are three organs of perception in our body there is the brain in our spirit there is the intuition and in our soul there is the mind Our mind should be governed by our intuitionExo 313"}
{"zh": "a\t悟性是介乎直觉与头脑之间的；悟性，把直觉的意思表明出来，叫头脑去想出来—弗四17，诗一一九34、125。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "a. In between the intuition and the brain is our mind; the mind expresses the meaning of the intuition and causes the brain to make it clear.—Eph. 4:17; Psa. 119:34, 125.", "norm_zh": "a悟性是介乎直觉与头脑之间的悟性把直觉的意思表明出来叫头脑去想出来弗四17诗一一九34125李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a In between the intuition and the brain is our mind the mind expresses the meaning of the intuition and causes the brain to make it clearEph 417 Psa 11934 125"}
{"zh": "b\t心思所以虚妄，领会力所以昏昧，所以与神的生命隔绝，都是因里面愚昧，都是因心硬丢弃了一切的感觉—弗四17~18。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "b. The reasons the mind becomes vain, the understanding darkens, and we become estranged from the life of God are due to our inner ignorance and the hardness of our heart which cause us to forsake all feeling.—Eph. 4:17-18.", "norm_zh": "b心思所以虚妄领会力所以昏昧所以与神的生命隔绝都是因里面愚昧都是因心硬丢弃了一切的感觉弗四1718李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The reasons the mind becomes vain the understanding darkens and we become estranged from the life of God are due to our inner ignorance and the hardness of our heart which cause us to forsake all feelingEph 41718"}
{"zh": "2\t总而言之，心一硬，就与神的生命隔绝，就越发愚昧，就越发不能领会了；这样，生命的发展就有了阻碍—太十三4。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. In summary, we can say that when the heart is hardened, we become estranged from the life of God, we become ignorant and unable to understand. The result is that the growth of life is hindered.—Matt. 13:4.", "norm_zh": "2总而言之心一硬就与神的生命隔绝就越发愚昧就越发不能领会了这样生命的发展就有了阻碍太十三4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In summary we can say that when the heart is hardened we become estranged from the life of God we become ignorant and unable to understand The result is that the growth of life is hinderedMatt 134"}
{"zh": "3\t不是生命的律不在我们的里面运行，生命的律是等着往外“律”出去，它要从我们里面的各部分“律”出去—参罗八13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. It is not that the law of life does not move in us — the law of life is always waiting to spread out through our inward parts.—cf. Rom. 8:13.", "norm_zh": "3不是生命的律不在我们的里面运行生命的律是等着往外律出去它要从我们里面的各部分律出去参罗八13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 It is not that the law of life does not move in us the law of life is always waiting to spread out through our inward partscf Rom 813"}
{"zh": "四\t石心的软化与生命的运行—结三六26，罗八6：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. The Softening of the Stony Heart and the Moving of Life—Ezek. 36:26; Rom. 8:6:", "norm_zh": "四石心的软化与生命的运行结三六26罗八6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Softening of the Stony Heart and the Moving of LifeEzek 3626 Rom 86"}
{"zh": "1\t以西结三十六章二十五至二十七节，至少说到五件事，就是：（一）用清水洗净我们；（二）赐给我们一个新心；（三）将新灵放在我们里面；（四）除掉我们的石心，赐给我们肉心；（五）将神的灵放在我们里面。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Ezekiel 36:25-27 speaks of at least five things: 1) we have been cleansed with clean water; 2) we have been given a new heart; 3) we have a new spirit within us; 4) our stony heart has been removed, and we have been given a heart of flesh; and 5) God's Spirit has been put within us.", "norm_zh": "1以西结三十六章二十五至二十七节至少说到五件事就是一用清水洗净我们二赐给我们一个新心三将新灵放在我们里面四除掉我们的石心赐给我们肉心五将神的灵放在我们里面李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Ezekiel 362527 speaks of at least five things 1 we have been cleansed with clean water 2 we have been given a new heart 3 we have a new spirit within us 4 our stony heart has been removed and we have been given a heart of flesh and 5 Gods Spirit has been put within us"}
{"zh": "2\t这五件事合起来的结果，就是使我们顺从神的律例，谨守遵行神的典章。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. The result of putting these five things together is that we might walk in God's statutes and keep His ordinances.", "norm_zh": "2这五件事合起来的结果就是使我们顺从神的律例谨守遵行神的典章李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The result of putting these five things together is that we might walk in Gods statutes and keep His ordinances"}
{"zh": "3\t我们的心只有一个；石心是指心的硬而言，肉心是指心的软而言—参出三二9，林后三3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. We have only one heart; a stony heart refers to the hardness of the heart, while the fleshly heart refers to the softness of the heart—cf. Exo. 32:9; 2 Cor. 3:3.", "norm_zh": "3我们的心只有一个石心是指心的硬而言肉心是指心的软而言参出三二9林后三3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 We have only one heart a stony heart refers to the hardness of the heart while the fleshly heart refers to the softness of the heartcf Exo 329 2 Cor 33"}
{"zh": "4\t神的生命要从我们里面往外去，神总是打动我们的心，软化我们的石心；有的人是受神的爱打动，有的人是被神的管教打动—五14，四16~18，来十二6~7，参耶四八11，罗八28。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "4. When God's life desires to move out within us, He always touches our heart first, causing our stony heart to be softened; some people are touched by God's love, others by His disciplining.—2 Cor. 5:14; 4:16-18; Heb. 12:6-7; cf. Jer. 48:11; Rom. 8:28.", "norm_zh": "4神的生命要从我们里面往外去神总是打动我们的心软化我们的石心有的人是受神的爱打动有的人是被神的管教打动五14四1618来十二67参耶四八11罗八28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 When Gods life desires to move out within us He always touches our heart first causing our stony heart to be softened some people are touched by Gods love others by His disciplining2 Cor 514 41618 Heb 1267 cf Jer 4811 Rom 828"}
{"zh": "5\t当你肯顺服神一下的时候，神的生命就运行出来了；神的生命就是这样在你的里面运行不息—6、13节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "5. If you are willing to obey God, His life will move out; in this manner, God's life will continue to move in you without ceasing.—vv. 6, 13.", "norm_zh": "5当你肯顺服神一下的时候神的生命就运行出来了神的生命就是这样在你的里面运行不息613节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:18:47.227081+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 If you are willing to obey God His life will move out in this manner Gods life will continue to move in you without ceasingvv 6 13"}
{"zh": "读经：来八10，弗五21，可十二30，弗一19~20，三20，加四19，林后三18，约壹三2", "en": "Scripture Reading: Heb. 8:10; Eph. 5:21; Mark 12:30; Eph. 1:19-20; 3:20; Gal. 4:19; 2 Cor. 3:18; 1 John 3:2", "norm_zh": "读经来八10弗五21可十二30弗一1920三20加四19林后三18约壹三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Heb 810 Eph 521 Mark 1230 Eph 11920 320 Gal 419 2 Cor 318 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "壹\t希伯来八章十节的下一半有话说，“我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民”；这说出了神的心意，这说出了神从永远到永远的目的；神要在生命的律里作我们的神，我们要在生命的律里作神的子民：", "en": "I. In the second part of Hebrews 8:10 it says, \"I will be God to them, and they shall be a people to Me\"; this tells us what is on God's heart and what His purpose is from eternity to eternity; God wants to be our God, and we need to be His people according to the law of life:", "norm_zh": "壹希伯来八章十节的下一半有话说我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民这说出了神的心意这说出了神从永远到永远的目的神要在生命的律里作我们的神我们要在生命的律里作神的子民", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I In the second part of Hebrews 810 it says I will be God to them and they shall be a people to Me this tells us what is on Gods heart and what His purpose is from eternity to eternity God wants to be our God and we need to be His people according to the law of life"}
{"zh": "一\t神永远的目的；就是神要作神；神是神，并且，神要在人中间作神；要我们宣告祂是神，只有祂是神，其余的都不是—出二十1~8，太六9，诗一〇五3，八1。", "en": "A. God's eternal purpose; that is, God wants to be God; God is God, and, furthermore, God wants to be God among men; to have us declare that He is God, that only He is God, and that all others are not—Exo. 20:1-8; Matt. 6:9; Psa. 105:3; 8:1.", "norm_zh": "一神永远的目的就是神要作神神是神并且神要在人中间作神要我们宣告祂是神只有祂是神其余的都不是出二十18太六9诗一〇五3八1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods eternal purpose that is God wants to be God God is God and furthermore God wants to be God among men to have us declare that He is God that only He is God and that all others are notExo 2018 Matt 69 Psa 1053 81"}
{"zh": "二\t神要住在以色列人中间作神—出二五8，二九45~46，利二五38，二六12~13。", "en": "B. God Desires to Dwell Among the Children of Israel as Their God—Exo. 25:8; 29:45-46; Lev. 25:38; 26:12-13.", "norm_zh": "二神要住在以色列人中间作神出二五8二九4546利二五38二六1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God Desires to Dwell Among the Children of Israel as Their GodExo 258 294546 Lev 2538 261213"}
{"zh": "三\t道成了肉身住在人中间表明神；这就是“以马内利”，就是“神与我们同在”了—太一23。", "en": "C. The Word became flesh and tabernacled among men to declare God; this is \"Emmanuel,\" which is \"God with us\"—Matt. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "三道成了肉身住在人中间表明神这就是以马内利就是神与我们同在了太一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Word became flesh and tabernacled among men to declare God this is Emmanuel which is God with usMatt 123"}
{"zh": "四\t神住在教会里作神；道成了肉身住在人中间，还受空间和时间的限制；等到教会被建立，“被建造成为灵宫”，教会就“成为神借着圣灵居住的所在”了—彼前二5，弗二22。", "en": "D. God dwells in the church as God; when the Word became flesh and tabernacled among men, He was limited by space and time; when the church was built \"as a spiritual house,\" it became \"God's dwelling place in spirit\"—1 Pet. 2:5; Eph. 2:22.", "norm_zh": "四神住在教会里作神道成了肉身住在人中间还受空间和时间的限制等到教会被建立被建造成为灵宫教会就成为神借着圣灵居住的所在了彼前二5弗二22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God dwells in the church as God when the Word became flesh and tabernacled among men He was limited by space and time when the church was built as a spiritual house it became Gods dwelling place in spirit1 Pet 25 Eph 222"}
{"zh": "五\t神在国度时代作以色列家的神—来八8~10，耶三一31~34。", "en": "E. In the Kingdom Age God Will be the God of the House of Israel—Heb. 8:8-10; Jer. 31:31-34.", "norm_zh": "五神在国度时代作以色列家的神来八810耶三一3134", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E In the Kingdom Age God Will be the God of the House of IsraelHeb 8810 Jer 313134"}
{"zh": "六\t神在将来的永远里住在人中间作神—启二一3~4。", "en": "F. In Eternity Future God Will Dwell Among Men as God—Rev. 21:3-4.", "norm_zh": "六神在将来的永远里住在人中间作神启二一34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F In Eternity Future God Will Dwell Among Men as GodRev 2134"}
{"zh": "七\t神作父与神作神—约二十17，林后五11，来十二29：", "en": "G. God as the Father and God as God—John 20:17; 2 Cor. 5:11; Heb. 12:29:", "norm_zh": "七神作父与神作神约二十17林后五11来十二29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G God as the Father and God as GodJohn 2017 2 Cor 511 Heb 1229"}
{"zh": "1\t说祂是父，是说到生命，是说到祂与我们有了父子生命上的关系；说祂是神，是说到祂的地位，是说祂是创造的主—约一12~13，来四13。", "en": "1. God as our Father is a matter of life, showing that we are related to Him as a son is related to a father; while God as God is a matter of position, showing that He is the Creator.—John 1:12-13; Heb. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "1说祂是父是说到生命是说到祂与我们有了父子生命上的关系说祂是神是说到祂的地位是说祂是创造的主约一1213来四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God as our Father is a matter of life showing that we are related to Him as a son is related to a father while God as God is a matter of position showing that He is the CreatorJohn 11213 Heb 413"}
{"zh": "2\t我们认识神是父，我们敢投在祂的怀抱里；我们认识神是神，只有俯伏在地敬拜祂。", "en": "2. When we know God as the Father, we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom. And when we know God as God, we must bow down and worship Him.", "norm_zh": "2我们认识神是父我们敢投在祂的怀抱里我们认识神是神只有俯伏在地敬拜祂", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we know God as the Father we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom And when we know God as God we must bow down and worship Him"}
{"zh": "3\t我们认识神是神，我们就要“以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华”；就要“存敬畏的心”向祂下拜；凡是认识神是神，自己站在仆人地位的，都要敬拜神—诗二九2，五7，启二二9。", "en": "3. When we know God as God, we must \"worship Jehovah in holy array\" and bow down to Him \"in fear\"; anyone who knows God as God and stands upon the position of a servant must worship God.—Psa. 29:2; 5:7; Rev. 22:9.", "norm_zh": "3我们认识神是神我们就要以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华就要存敬畏的心向祂下拜凡是认识神是神自己站在仆人地位的都要敬拜神诗二九2五7启二二9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 When we know God as God we must worship Jehovah in holy array and bow down to Him in fear anyone who knows God as God and stands upon the position of a servant must worship GodPsa 292 57 Rev 229"}
{"zh": "八\t神在生命的律里作神—来八10，约四23~24：", "en": "H. God as God in the Law of Life—Heb. 8:10; John 4:23-24:", "norm_zh": "八神在生命的律里作神来八10约四2324", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H God as God in the Law of LifeHeb 810 John 42324"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来八章十节下一半的话乃是说神在生命的律里作我们的神，我们在生命的律里作神的子民；我们与神，神与我们，两者的关系都是在生命的交通里。", "en": "1. The second half of Hebrews 8:10 says that God is our God in the law of life and we are God's people in the law of life; we and God, God and we, both have our relationships in the fellowship of life.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来八章十节下一半的话乃是说神在生命的律里作我们的神我们在生命的律里作神的子民我们与神神与我们两者的关系都是在生命的交通里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The second half of Hebrews 810 says that God is our God in the law of life and we are Gods people in the law of life we and God God and we both have our relationships in the fellowship of life"}
{"zh": "2\t约翰四章二十四节说，“神是灵，所以拜祂的，必须用灵和真拜祂”；这是说，只有与神的质相同的才能敬拜神，只有灵能敬拜灵，只有在灵里的敬拜才是在真实里的敬拜。", "en": "2. John 4:24 says, \"God is Spirit; and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and reality\"; this means that only the element in man which is the same as God can worship God. Only the spirit can worship Spirit. Only worship which is in the spirit is true worship.", "norm_zh": "2约翰四章二十四节说神是灵所以拜祂的必须用灵和真拜祂这是说只有与神的质相同的才能敬拜神只有灵能敬拜灵只有在灵里的敬拜才是在真实里的敬拜", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 John 424 says God is Spirit and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and reality this means that only the element in man which is the same as God can worship God Only the spirit can worship Spirit Only worship which is in the spirit is true worship"}
{"zh": "3\t所以，我们必须先是神的儿女，然后才能作神的子民；神是在生命的律里作我们的神，我们是在生命的律里作神的子民—23~24节。", "en": "3. Therefore, before we can be God's people, we must first become God's children; God becomes our God in the law of life, and we are God's people in the law of life—vv. 23-24.", "norm_zh": "3所以我们必须先是神的儿女然后才能作神的子民神是在生命的律里作我们的神我们是在生命的律里作神的子民2324节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Therefore before we can be Gods people we must first become Gods children God becomes our God in the law of life and we are Gods people in the law of lifevv 2324"}
{"zh": "贰\t生命运行的两个条件—弗五21，可十二30：", "en": "II. Two Conditions for the Moving of Life—Eph. 5:21; Mark 12:30:", "norm_zh": "贰生命运行的两个条件弗五21可十二30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Two Conditions for the Moving of LifeEph 521 Mark 1230"}
{"zh": "一\t一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉—弗五21，参彼前五5：", "en": "A. The first condition is to obey the first sense of life—Eph. 5:21; cf. 1 Pet. 5:5:", "norm_zh": "一一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉弗五21参彼前五5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first condition is to obey the first sense of lifeEph 521 cf 1 Pet 55"}
{"zh": "1\t我们只要有一点感觉，我们就要顺服这一个感觉；你顺服这一点感觉，你的饥渴就增加一点；你再顺服，你就再加上感觉，你立刻看见，你的里面活了—腓二12~13。", "en": "1. Whenever we have a little sense, we should obey this sense; when we obey this sense, our hunger and thirst increase slightly; if we obey again, more sense will be added, and we will immediately see that we are alive from within—Phil. 2:12-13.", "norm_zh": "1我们只要有一点感觉我们就要顺服这一个感觉你顺服这一点感觉你的饥渴就增加一点你再顺服你就再加上感觉你立刻看见你的里面活了腓二1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Whenever we have a little sense we should obey this sense when we obey this sense our hunger and thirst increase slightly if we obey again more sense will be added and we will immediately see that we are alive from withinPhil 21213"}
{"zh": "2\t你还没有顺服你里面的头一个感觉之先，你不要管以后怎样；我们这样一步一步向前走的时候，有一件事是很宝贵的，就是你如果越过神去作什么，你立刻发觉有“圣灵禁止”，立刻觉得“耶稣的灵不许”—来十一8，徒十六7。", "en": "2. Before you obey the first sense within you, do not worry about what will happen afterward; as we go on in this way step by step, there is one thing that is very precious, which is that if you go beyond God to do anything, you will immediately sense \"the forbidding of the Holy Spirit\" and immediately feel that \"the Spirit of Jesus suffers you not\"—Heb. 11:8; Acts 16:7.", "norm_zh": "2你还没有顺服你里面的头一个感觉之先你不要管以后怎样我们这样一步一步向前走的时候有一件事是很宝贵的就是你如果越过神去作什么你立刻发觉有圣灵禁止立刻觉得耶稣的灵不许来十一8徒十六7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Before you obey the first sense within you do not worry about what will happen afterward as we go on in this way step by step there is one thing that is very precious which is that if you go beyond God to do anything you will immediately sense the forbidding of the Holy Spirit and immediately feel that the Spirit of Jesus suffers you notHeb 118 Acts 167"}
{"zh": "二\t还有一个条件，就是要爱神—可十二30，约十四21：", "en": "B. Another condition is to love God—Mark 12:30; John 14:21:", "norm_zh": "二还有一个条件就是要爱神可十二30约十四21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Another condition is to love GodMark 1230 John 1421"}
{"zh": "1\t照许多圣徒的经历来说，神是先把祂的生命种在他们里面，然后用爱来打动他们的心情；信是把生命接受进来，爱是把生命流露出去—一12~13。", "en": "1. According to the experience of many saints, God first plants His life in them and then touches their emotion with love; to believe is to take in life, while to love is to flow out life.—1:12-13.", "norm_zh": "1照许多圣徒的经历来说神是先把祂的生命种在他们里面然后用爱来打动他们的心情信是把生命接受进来爱是把生命流露出去一1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to the experience of many saints God first plants His life in them and then touches their emotion with love to believe is to take in life while to love is to flow out life11213"}
{"zh": "2\t罗马十二章一至二节所说的，能给我们证明这件事；保罗先说，“弟兄们，我以神的诸慈悲劝你们”，这是先打动心情；然后“将身体献上当作活祭”，这是意志的行为；然后“悟性更新而变化，叫你们察验何为神的善良、纯全、可喜悦的旨意”，这是心思里明白神的旨意。", "en": "2. Romans 12:1-2 can prove these things for us; Paul first said, \"I beg you therefore, brothers, through the compassions of God...\" By these words he first touched their emotion; then he said, \"Present your bodies a living sacrifice.\" With these words his intention was to move the will; then he told them, \"Be transformed by the renewing of the mind, that you may prove by testing what the will of God is, that which is good and well-pleasing and perfect.\" This is the knowing of God's will in the mind.", "norm_zh": "2罗马十二章一至二节所说的能给我们证明这件事保罗先说弟兄们我以神的诸慈悲劝你们这是先打动心情然后将身体献上当作活祭这是意志的行为然后悟性更新而变化叫你们察验何为神的善良纯全可喜悦的旨意这是心思里明白神的旨意", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Romans 1212 can prove these things for us Paul first said I beg you therefore brothers through the compassions of God By these words he first touched their emotion then he said Present your bodies a living sacrifice With these words his intention was to move the will then he told them Be transformed by the renewing of the mind that you may prove by testing what the will of God is that which is good and wellpleasing and perfect This is the knowing of Gods will in the mind"}
{"zh": "3\t如果我们要生命向外发展，要生命长大，我们就得尽心、尽魂、尽悟性、尽力量爱主我们的神！—可十二30。", "en": "3. If we want the life within us to spread to the outside, if we want the life to grow, we need to love the Lord our God with all our heart, with all our soul, with all our understanding, and with all our strength!—Mark 12:30.", "norm_zh": "3如果我们要生命向外发展要生命长大我们就得尽心尽魂尽悟性尽力量爱主我们的神可十二30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If we want the life within us to spread to the outside if we want the life to grow we need to love the Lord our God with all our heart with all our soul with all our understanding and with all our strengthMark 1230"}
{"zh": "叁\t生命运行的两个功用—参腓三10~11，林后四10~12：", "en": "III. The Two Functions of the Moving of Life—cf. Phil. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 4:10-12:", "norm_zh": "叁生命运行的两个功用参腓三1011林后四1012", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The Two Functions of the Moving of Lifecf Phil 31011 2 Cor 41012"}
{"zh": "一\t一个就是死的功用，一个就是复活的功用；死的功用是去病的功用，复活的功用是得健康的功用—11~12节。", "en": "A. One is the function of death, and the other is the function of resurrection; the function of death is to remove the illness, while the function of resurrection is to give us health.—vv. 11-12.", "norm_zh": "一一个就是死的功用一个就是复活的功用死的功用是去病的功用复活的功用是得健康的功用1112节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A One is the function of death and the other is the function of resurrection the function of death is to remove the illness while the function of resurrection is to give us healthvv 1112"}
{"zh": "二\t主的那个十字架，第一个成分是死，第二个成分是活；罗马六章告诉我们，这两个成分，是基督的生命顶有力量，顶有功用的成分—4~10节。", "en": "B. The first element of the Lord's cross is death, while the second element is life; Romans 6 tells us that these two elements are the most powerful and useful elements in the life of Christ.—vv. 4-10.", "norm_zh": "二主的哪个十字架第一个成分是死第二个成分是活罗马六章告诉我们这两个成分是基督的生命顶有力量顶有功用的成分410节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The first element of the Lords cross is death while the second element is life Romans 6 tells us that these two elements are the most powerful and useful elements in the life of Christvv 410"}
{"zh": "三\t十字架是当你的心被神打动以后，你把自己献在神的手里，祂的生命在你的里面一直在那里运行，运行的时候，死的功用除去你里面不该有的；同时活的功用叫你活出神本性里的一切丰盛来，你的里面就有了亮光，有了喜乐，有了平安—6节，罗八13。", "en": "C. The cross is when your heart is touched by God and you offer yourself into His hand, and His life is continually moving within you; when it is moving, the function of death eliminates the things in you which you should not have; at the same time, the function of life causes you to live out all the riches of the Godhead, so that you are full of light, full of joy, and full of peace.—v. 6; Rom. 8:13.", "norm_zh": "三十字架是当你的心被神打动以后你把自己献在神的手里祂的生命在你的里面一直在哪里运行运行的时候死的功用除去你里面不该有的同时活的功用叫你活出神本性里的一切丰盛来你的里面就有了亮光有了喜乐有了平安6节罗八13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The cross is when your heart is touched by God and you offer yourself into His hand and His life is continually moving within you when it is moving the function of death eliminates the things in you which you should not have at the same time the function of life causes you to live out all the riches of the Godhead so that you are full of light full of joy and full of peacev 6 Rom 813"}
{"zh": "四\t但愿我们顺着神生命的运行往前行，让祂的生命在我们里面能通过各部分，能毫无阻碍地运行着，能一直有所除去，能一直有所增加—6节，约壹二27。", "en": "D. May we go on according to the moving of God's life so that His life in us can reach all the different parts, moving without hindrance, always eliminating something and always adding something.—v. 6; 1 John 2:27.", "norm_zh": "四但愿我们顺着神生命的运行往前行让祂的生命在我们里面能通过各部分能毫无阻碍地运行着能一直有所除去能一直有所增加6节约壹二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D May we go on according to the moving of Gods life so that His life in us can reach all the different parts moving without hindrance always eliminating something and always adding somethingv 6 1 John 227"}
{"zh": "肆\t生命运行的大能，是“不能毁坏之生命的大能”；这个生命运行的大能大力，是使主耶稣从死里复活的大能大力；也就是这个生命运行的大能大力，要充充足足成就一切超过我们所求所想的—弗一19~20，三20：", "en": "IV. The power of the moving of life is the \"power of an indestructible life\"; this power and might of the moving of life is the power and might that raised the Lord Jesus from the dead; and it is this power and might of the moving of life that will do superabundantly above all that we ask or think.—Eph. 1:19-20; 3:20:", "norm_zh": "肆生命运行的大能是不能毁坏之生命的大能这个生命运行的大能大力是使主耶稣从死里复活的大能大力也就是这个生命运行的大能大力要充充足足成就一切超过我们所求所想的弗一1920三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The power of the moving of life is the power of an indestructible life this power and might of the moving of life is the power and might that raised the Lord Jesus from the dead and it is this power and might of the moving of life that will do superabundantly above all that we ask or thinkEph 11920 320"}
{"zh": "一\t能叫人的心倾向神；人的心在神的手中，好像陇沟的水，随意流转；只要我们肯把心放在神的手中，祂能转动我们—林后三18，箴二一1。", "en": "A. It can cause man's heart to incline toward God; man's heart is in the hand of Jehovah as the watercourses: He turneth it whithersoever He will; as long as we are willing to put our heart in God's hand, He can turn us.—2 Cor. 3:18; Prov. 21:1.", "norm_zh": "一能叫人的心倾向神人的心在神的手中好像陇沟的水随意流转只要我们肯把心放在神的手中祂能转动我们林后三18箴二一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A It can cause mans heart to incline toward God mans heart is in the hand of Jehovah as the watercourses He turneth it whithersoever He will as long as we are willing to put our heart in Gods hand He can turn us2 Cor 318 Prov 211"}
{"zh": "二\t能叫人顺服神—腓二12~13，参林后七15，弗六5。", "en": "B. It Enables Man to Obey God—Phil. 2:12-13; cf. 2 Cor. 7:15; Eph. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "二能叫人顺服神腓二1213参林后七15弗六5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B It Enables Man to Obey GodPhil 21213 cf 2 Cor 715 Eph 65"}
{"zh": "三\t能叫人行神所预备叫他们行的善—弗二10，多二14：", "en": "C. It Enables Man to Do the Works Which God Has Prepared—Eph. 2:10; Titus 2:14:", "norm_zh": "三能叫人行神所预备叫他们行的善弗二10多二14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It Enables Man to Do the Works Which God Has PreparedEph 210 Titus 214"}
{"zh": "1\t这个工作，是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的，可以说是“神的杰作”—弗二10。", "en": "1. This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus. We can say that it is God's masterpiece.—Eph. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1这个工作是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的可以说是神的杰作弗二10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus We can say that it is Gods masterpieceEph 210"}
{"zh": "2\t祂救了我们，祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了，祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作，叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善—多二14。", "en": "2. He has saved us and put His life in us! It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for us.—Titus 2:14.", "norm_zh": "2祂救了我们祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善多二14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He has saved us and put His life in us It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for usTitus 214"}
{"zh": "四\t能叫人尽心竭力作工；神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力，所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力；这个炸力，就是神的生命运行的大能；就是这个生命的大能，叫我们能殷勤地作工，能尽心竭力地作工—林前十五10，西一29。", "en": "E. It Enables Man to Labor and Struggle; what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power; hence, what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power; this exploding power is the power of the working of God's life; it is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work—1 Cor. 15:10; Col. 1:29.", "norm_zh": "四能叫人尽心竭力作工神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力这个炸力就是神的生命运行的大能就是这个生命的大能叫我们能殷勤地作工能尽心竭力地作工林前十五10西一29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E It Enables Man to Labor and Struggle what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power hence what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power this exploding power is the power of the working of Gods life it is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work1 Cor 1510 Col 129"}
{"zh": "五\t能叫人有活的新鲜的事奉—林后三5~6，罗七6，二28~29：", "en": "E. It Enables Man to Have a Living and Fresh Service—2 Cor. 3:5-6; Rom. 7:6; 2:28-29:", "norm_zh": "五能叫人有活的新鲜的事奉林后三56罗七6二2829", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E It Enables Man to Have a Living and Fresh Service2 Cor 356 Rom 76 22829"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约的事奉是字句的，新约的事奉是凭着灵的；旧约的事奉是陈旧的，新约的事奉是新鲜的；旧约的事奉是杀死人的，新约的事奉是叫人活的—林后三6。", "en": "1. Service in the old covenant was of the letter, but service in the new covenant is of the spirit. The service of the old covenant was old, but the service of the new covenant is fresh. The service of the old covenant killed, but the service of the new covenant gives life.—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1旧约的事奉是字句的新约的事奉是凭着灵的旧约的事奉是陈旧的新约的事奉是新鲜的旧约的事奉是杀死人的新约的事奉是叫人活的林后三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Service in the old covenant was of the letter but service in the new covenant is of the spirit The service of the old covenant was old but the service of the new covenant is fresh The service of the old covenant killed but the service of the new covenant gives life2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t新约的事奉，乃是与基督发生关系，由里面运行出来的；新约的事奉是属灵的，是启示的，是新鲜的—罗七6。", "en": "2. The service of the new covenant is something which is the result of having a relationship with Christ and is worked out from within; the service of the new covenant is spiritual, of revelation, and in newness.—Rom. 7:6.", "norm_zh": "2新约的事奉乃是与基督发生关系由里面运行出来的新约的事奉是属灵的是启示的是新鲜的罗七6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The service of the new covenant is something which is the result of having a relationship with Christ and is worked out from within the service of the new covenant is spiritual of revelation and in newnessRom 76"}
{"zh": "3\t新约的事奉是需要“本于”神，“倚靠”神，也“归于”神的；保罗这福音的执事，是照着神恩典的恩赐；这恩赐“是照祂运行的大能赐给我的”—罗十一36。", "en": "3. The service of the new covenant is of God, through God, and to God; Paul, a minister of this gospel, was according to the gift of the grace of God; this gift \"was given to me according to the operation of His power\"—Rom. 11:36.", "norm_zh": "3新约的事奉是需要本于神倚靠神也归于神的保罗这福音的执事是照着神恩典的恩赐这恩赐是照祂运行的大能赐给我的罗十一36", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The service of the new covenant is of God through God and to God Paul a minister of this gospel was according to the gift of the grace of God this gift was given to me according to the operation of His powerRom 1136"}
{"zh": "伍\t生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通，生命就能发展到一个地步，使“基督成形”在我们里面；基督渐渐成形在我们里面，我们就渐渐“变化”，而变化的目标就是“象祂”—加四19，林后18，约壹三2：", "en": "V. As the law of life works in us in ever-expanding spheres, life can develop to such a degree that \"Christ be formed\" in us; as Christ is gradually formed in us, we are gradually \"transformed,\" and the goal of transformation is to be \"like Him\"—Gal. 4:19; 2 Cor. 3:18; 1 John 3:2:", "norm_zh": "伍生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通生命就能发展到一个地步使基督成形在我们里面基督渐渐成形在我们里面我们就渐渐变化而变化的目标就是象祂加四19林后18约壹三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V As the law of life works in us in everexpanding spheres life can develop to such a degree that Christ be formed in us as Christ is gradually formed in us we are gradually transformed and the goal of transformation is to be like HimGal 419 2 Cor 318 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "一\t基督成形；基督的生命，本来是完全的；但是祂受了我们的限制，以致基督还未成形在我们里面，这是生命的发展受了阻碍；保罗为加拉太的信徒“再受生产之苦”，是直等到基督成形在他们里面—加四19，参约十四20。", "en": "A. Christ being formed; the life of Christ is complete, but it is restricted by us, so that Christ is not yet fully formed in us, which means that the growth of life is hindered; Paul was \"in travail again\" for the Galatian believers until Christ was formed in them—Gal. 4:19; cf. John 14:20.", "norm_zh": "一基督成形基督的生命本来是完全的但是祂受了我们的限制以致基督还未成形在我们里面这是生命的发展受了阻碍保罗为加拉太的信徒再受生产之苦是直等到基督成形在他们里面加四19参约十四20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ being formed the life of Christ is complete but it is restricted by us so that Christ is not yet fully formed in us which means that the growth of life is hindered Paul was in travail again for the Galatian believers until Christ was formed in themGal 419 cf John 1420"}
{"zh": "二\t变化—罗十二1~2，弗四23，参来三7~8：", "en": "B.\tTransformation:—Rom. 12:1-2; Eph. 4:23; cf. Heb. 3:7-8:", "norm_zh": "二变化罗十二12弗四23参来三78", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B TransformationRom 1212 Eph 423 cf Heb 378"}
{"zh": "1\t“变化”是必须先献上身体，其次是需要悟性的更新，这是罗马十二章一至二节所告诉我们的；圣灵的工作，总是从中心到圆周的；因为灵是特别与悟性发生关系的，所以，灵先得更新，然后更新到悟性，然后人在行为上就渐渐改变了。", "en": "1. According to Romans 12:1-2 there are two prerequisites for transformation: one is the presentation of our bodies; the other is the renewing of our mind; the work of the Holy Spirit is always from the center to the circumference; because the spirit is especially related to the mind, the spirit must be renewed first; then the mind must be renewed; finally, man's behavior will gradually be changed.", "norm_zh": "1变化是必须先献上身体其次是需要悟性的更新这是罗马十二章一至二节所告诉我们的圣灵的工作总是从中心到圆周的因为灵是特别与悟性发生关系的所以灵先得更新然后更新到悟性然后人在行为上就渐渐改变了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to Romans 1212 there are two prerequisites for transformation one is the presentation of our bodies the other is the renewing of our mind the work of the Holy Spirit is always from the center to the circumference because the spirit is especially related to the mind the spirit must be renewed first then the mind must be renewed finally mans behavior will gradually be changed"}
{"zh": "2\t变化不象重生，重生是一下子成功的事；变化是一个程序，是渐渐地，天天地变化着。", "en": "2. Transformation is not like regeneration; regeneration is something that happens once for all, but transformation is a daily gradual process.", "norm_zh": "2变化不象重生重生是一下子成功的事变化是一个程序是渐渐地天天地变化着", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Transformation is not like regeneration regeneration is something that happens once for all but transformation is a daily gradual process"}
{"zh": "3\t但愿主怜悯我们，叫我们的心能在祂面前软下来！同时，我们还得相信腓立比二章十三节的话说，“因为你们立志行事，都是神在你们里面运行，为要成就祂的美意”。", "en": "3. May the Lord be merciful to us that our heart may be softened before Him. At the same time we need to believe Philippians 2:13: \"For it is God Who operates in you both the willing and the working for His good pleasure.\"", "norm_zh": "3但愿主怜悯我们叫我们的心能在祂面前软下来同时我们还得相信腓立比二章十三节的话说因为你们立志行事都是神在你们里面运行为要成就祂的美意", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 May the Lord be merciful to us that our heart may be softened before Him At the same time we need to believe Philippians 213 For it is God Who operates in you both the willing and the working for His good pleasure"}
{"zh": "三\t变化与相似—罗八29，腓三10、21：", "en": "C. Transformation and Conformation—Rom. 8:29; Phil. 3:10, 21:", "norm_zh": "三变化与相似罗八29腓三1021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Transformation and ConformationRom 829 Phil 310 21"}
{"zh": "1\t“变化”是说到过程，“相似”是说到完成；“变化”是主的生命在我们里面逐渐长大，使我们达到与主同样形质的地步；“相似”是变化到与主同形质了—罗八29。", "en": "1. \"Transformation\" speaks of a process, while \"conformation\" speaks of the completed work; \"Transformation\" means that the Lord's life gradually grows up in us, that we are the same as the Lord; \"Conformation\" means that we are transformed completely and are the same in form and nature as the Lord—Rom. 8:29.", "norm_zh": "1变化是说到过程相似是说到完成变化是主的生命在我们里面逐渐长大使我们达到与主同样形质的地步相似是变化到与主同形质了罗八29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Transformation speaks of a process while conformation speaks of the completed work Transformation means that the Lords life gradually grows up in us that we are the same as the Lord Conformation means that we are transformed completely and are the same in form and nature as the LordRom 829"}
{"zh": "2\t人如果要改变成功象神所定规的模型的形状，就必须从里面有本质上的改变，就是必须有神的生命进入他的灵里，让这生命渗透他整个人，直到全人由本质的改变而达到形状上完全的改变—林后三18。", "en": "2. If a person wants to be transformed and be conformed to the image of the prototype that God has ordained, he must have a change of nature from within. God's life must enter into his spirit and permeate his whole being until he is completely changed in nature. Accordingly, there will be a complete conformation in image.—2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "2人如果要改变成功象神所定规的模型的形状就必须从里面有本质上的改变就是必须有神的生命进入他的灵里让这生命渗透他整个人直到全人由本质的改变而达到形状上完全的改变林后三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If a person wants to be transformed and be conformed to the image of the prototype that God has ordained he must have a change of nature from within Gods life must enter into his spirit and permeate his whole being until he is completely changed in nature Accordingly there will be a complete conformation in image2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "四\t变化的目标就是“象祂”，而完全地象祂是要等到“主显现”的时候，就是“身体得赎”的日子来到，才能完全地象祂—约壹三2，腓三21。", "en": "D. The goal of transformation is to be \"like Him,\" and complete likeness to Him must wait until \"the Lord appears,\" which is when the day of \"the redemption of our body\" comes, so that we may be completely like Him—1 John 3:2; Phil. 3:21.", "norm_zh": "四变化的目标就是象祂而完全地象祂是要等到主显现的时候就是身体得赎的日子来到才能完全地象祂约壹三2腓三21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The goal of transformation is to be like Him and complete likeness to Him must wait until the Lord appears which is when the day of the redemption of our body comes so that we may be completely like Him1 John 32 Phil 321"}
{"zh": "五\t纯洁自己—约壹三3，林后七1，雅四8，赛一16：", "en": "E. Purifying Oneself—1 John 3:3; 2 Cor. 7:1; Jas. 4:8; Isa. 1:16:", "norm_zh": "五纯洁自己约壹三3林后七1雅四8赛一16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Purifying Oneself1 John 33 2 Cor 71 Jas 48 Isa 116"}
{"zh": "1\t洁净是指干净而言，意思就是没有污秽；纯洁呢，不只没有污秽，并且没有杂质。", "en": "1. To be clean means to be without defilement, but purifying means not only to be without defilement, but also to be without mixture.", "norm_zh": "1洁净是指干净而言意思就是没有污秽纯洁呢不只没有污秽并且没有杂质", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To be clean means to be without defilement but purifying means not only to be without defilement but also to be without mixture"}
{"zh": "2\t我们是要借着生命的光在里面的照亮，叫我们认识自己的真相，叫我们除去一切祂所不喜悦的—约一4，诗三六9。", "en": "2. We are to, through the shining of the light of life within us, know ourselves and eliminate all that displeases Him.—John 1:4; Psa. 36:9.", "norm_zh": "2我们是要借着生命的光在里面的照亮叫我们认识自己的真相叫我们除去一切祂所不喜悦的约一4诗三六9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We are to through the shining of the light of life within us know ourselves and eliminate all that displeases HimJohn 14 Psa 369"}
{"zh": "3\t更深的纯洁，就是从神启示而来的，从基督复活的生命里出来的东西，也不可让它停留；因为一个生命的长大，是有新陈代谢的作用的；凡真出于复活的生命的，永远不会过去，永远是新的；但需要保守在圣灵的新鲜里—参弗四16，林后四7。", "en": "3. Deeper purification means that even that which comes from God's revelation, which issues from the resurrection life of Christ, should not be allowed to remain; because the growth of a life has the process of metabolism; anything which truly comes from the resurrection life will never be lost; it will forever be fresh; but it needs to be kept in the newness of the Holy Spirit—cf. Eph. 4:16; 2 Cor. 4:7.", "norm_zh": "3更深的纯洁就是从神启示而来的从基督复活的生命里出来的东西也不可让它停留因为一个生命的长大是有新陈代谢的作用的凡真出于复活的生命的永远不会过去永远是新的但需要保守在圣灵的新鲜里参弗四16林后四7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Deeper purification means that even that which comes from Gods revelation which issues from the resurrection life of Christ should not be allowed to remain because the growth of a life has the process of metabolism anything which truly comes from the resurrection life will never be lost it will forever be fresh but it needs to be kept in the newness of the Holy Spiritcf Eph 416 2 Cor 47"}
{"zh": "十条诫命的第一条是：“除了我以外，你不可有别的神。”第二条是：“不可为自己雕刻偶像，也不可作什么形像，仿佛上天、下地和地底下、水中的百物，不可跪拜那些像，也不可事奉它，因为我耶和华你的神是忌邪的神……。”第三条是：“不可妄称耶和华你神的名……”。第四条是：“当记念安息日，守为圣日。”以上这四条诫命，把神的心意启示出来了，把祂向人正式的要求说出来了，把祂创造的目的，救赎的目的都说出来了。这没有别的，就是神要作神。神是神，并且，神要在人中间作神。", "en": "The first of the Ten Commandments is: \"Thou shalt have no other gods before me.\" The second is: \"Thou shalt not make unto thee a graven image, nor any likeness of any thing that is in heaven above, or that is in the earth beneath, or that is in the water under the earth: thou shalt not bow down thyself unto them, nor serve them: for I Jehovah thy God am a jealous God.\" The third commandment is: \"Thou shalt not take the name of Jehovah thy God in vain.\" The fourth is: \"Remember the sabbath day, to keep it holy.\" In these four commandments God revealed His will and clearly unveiled His formal requirements for man. Here He spoke clearly of the purpose of His creation and the purpose of His redemption. The purpose is simply that God wants to be God. God is God, and He wants to be God among men.", "norm_zh": "十条诫命的第一条是除了我以外你不可有别的神第二条是不可为自己雕刻偶像也不可作什么形像仿佛上天下地和地底下水中的百物不可跪拜哪些像也不可事奉它因为我耶和华你的神是忌邪的神第三条是不可妄称耶和华你神的名第四条是当记念安息日守为圣日以上这四条诫命把神的心意启示出来了把祂向人正式的要求说出来了把祂创造的目的救赎的目的都说出来了这没有别的就是神要作神神是神并且神要在人中间作神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The first of the Ten Commandments is Thou shalt have no other gods before me The second is Thou shalt not make unto thee a graven image nor any likeness of any thing that is in heaven above or that is in the earth beneath or that is in the water under the earth thou shalt not bow down thyself unto them nor serve them for I Jehovah thy God am a jealous God The third commandment is Thou shalt not take the name of Jehovah thy God in vain The fourth is Remember the sabbath day to keep it holy In these four commandments God revealed His will and clearly unveiled His formal requirements for man Here He spoke clearly of the purpose of His creation and the purpose of His redemption The purpose is simply that God wants to be God God is God and He wants to be God among men"}
{"zh": "在新约，主所教的祷告，也是一个大启示。这一个祷告，也是表明了神的心意，就是神要作神。主说，“你们祷告，要这样说，我们在天上的父，愿人都尊你的名为圣……。”神的名在天上，只有神能用，在地上却有人妄称神的名，可是，神却隐藏祂的自己，好像没有祂一样。但是，到了有一天，我们的主教导祂的门徒祷告说，“我们在天上的父，愿人都尊你的名为圣……。”主要我们这样祷告，就是要我们宣告祂是神，只有祂是神，其余的都不是。我们在这里也要象写诗的人一样，“要以祂的圣名夸耀。”（诗一〇五）我们也要说，“耶和华我们的主啊，你的名在全地何其美！”（八）我们的神啊，但愿“你从婴孩和吃奶的口中，完全了赞美的话”！（太二一）", "en": "In the New Testament, the prayer which the Lord taught His disciples was also a great revelation. In this prayer, He also reveals God's will — that God wants to be God. The Lord said, \"Pray, then, like this: Our Father Who is in the heavens, let Your name be sanctified.\" In the heavens God's name can only be used by God, but on earth there are people who take His name in vain, and yet He hides Himself as if He did not exist. However, one day our Lord taught His disciples to pray, \"Our Father Who is in the heavens, let Your name be sanctified.\" The Lord's purpose in wanting us to pray in this way is that we would declare that only He is God. The rest are not. We need to glory in His holy name as the Psalmist did (Psa. 105). We need to say: \"O Jehovah, our Lord, how excellent is thy name in all the earth\" (Psa. 8). O God, may Your praise be perfected in \"the mouth of babes and sucklings\"! (Matt. 21).", "norm_zh": "在新约主所教的祷告也是一个大启示这一个祷告也是表明了神的心意就是神要作神主说你们祷告要这样说我们在天上的父愿人都尊你的名为圣神的名在天上只有神能用在地上却有人妄称神的名可是神却隐藏祂的自己好像没有祂一样但是到了有一天我们的主教导祂的门徒祷告说我们在天上的父愿人都尊你的名为圣主要我们这样祷告就是要我们宣告祂是神只有祂是神其余的都不是我们在这里也要象写诗的人一样要以祂的圣名夸耀诗一〇五我们也要说耶和华我们的主啊你的名在全地何其美八我们的神啊但愿你从婴孩和吃奶的口中完全了赞美的话太二一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the New Testament the prayer which the Lord taught His disciples was also a great revelation In this prayer He also reveals Gods will that God wants to be God The Lord said Pray then like this Our Father Who is in the heavens let Your name be sanctified In the heavens Gods name can only be used by God but on earth there are people who take His name in vain and yet He hides Himself as if He did not exist However one day our Lord taught His disciples to pray Our Father Who is in the heavens let Your name be sanctified The Lords purpose in wanting us to pray in this way is that we would declare that only He is God The rest are not We need to glory in His holy name as the Psalmist did Psa 105 We need to say O Jehovah our Lord how excellent is thy name in all the earth Psa 8 O God may Your praise be perfected in the mouth of babes and sucklings Matt 21"}
{"zh": "神是神！但希奇的是祂乐意住在人的中间。神吩咐摩西为祂造圣所，明说“使我可以住在他们中间”（出二五）。神“要住在以色列人中间，作他们的神。他们必知道我是耶和华他们的神，是将他们从埃及地领出来的，为要住在他们中间；我是耶和华他们的神”。神要摩西代祂晓谕以色列人说，“我是耶和华你们的神；曾领你们从埃及地出来……要作你们的神。”（利二五）底下更说出神的心意，就是“我要在你们中间行走，我要作你们的神，你们要作我的子民”（二六）。神是神！太高太大了！但是，祂竟然来住在人中间作神！", "en": "Although God is God, the marvelous fact is that He desires to dwell among men. God commanded Moses to build Him a sanctuary, saying clearly, \"... that I may dwell among them\" (Exo. 25). Again He said, \"And I will dwell among the children of Israel, and will be their God. And they shall know that I am Jehovah their God, that brought them forth out of the land of Egypt, that I might dwell among them: I am Jehovah their God.\" God wanted Moses to tell the children of Israel plainly that He was Jehovah their God who brought them forth out of the land of Egypt to give them the land of Canaan and to be their God (Lev. 25). What follows speaks even more of God's desire: \"And I will walk among you, and will be your God, and ye shall be my people\" (Lev. 26). God is God! He is very high and very great! Yet He comes to dwell among men to be their God.", "norm_zh": "神是神但希奇的是祂乐意住在人的中间神吩咐摩西为祂造圣所明说使我可以住在他们中间出二五神要住在以色列人中间作他们的神他们必知道我是耶和华他们的神是将他们从埃及地领出来的为要住在他们中间我是耶和华他们的神神要摩西代祂晓谕以色列人说我是耶和华你们的神曾领你们从埃及地出来要作你们的神利二五底下更说出神的心意就是我要在你们中间行走我要作你们的神你们要作我的子民二六神是神太高太大了但是祂竟然来住在人中间作神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Although God is God the marvelous fact is that He desires to dwell among men God commanded Moses to build Him a sanctuary saying clearly that I may dwell among them Exo 25 Again He said And I will dwell among the children of Israel and will be their God And they shall know that I am Jehovah their God that brought them forth out of the land of Egypt that I might dwell among them I am Jehovah their God God wanted Moses to tell the children of Israel plainly that He was Jehovah their God who brought them forth out of the land of Egypt to give them the land of Canaan and to be their God Lev 25 What follows speaks even more of Gods desire And I will walk among you and will be your God and ye shall be my people Lev 26 God is God He is very high and very great Yet He comes to dwell among men to be their God"}
{"zh": "我们认识神是父，我们敢投在祂的怀抱里；我们认识神是神，只有俯伏在地敬拜祂。我们是神的儿女，我们活在祂的爱里，我们欢乐地享受祂所给我们的一切。我们作神的子民，我们是站在人的地位上，我们敬拜祂，我们赞美祂。我们认识神是神，我们就要“以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华”（诗二九）。就要“存敬畏的心”向祂下拜（五）。哦！一个认识神是神的人，在一切的事上，都不敢不敬畏主，都不敢不注重自己的衣服—行为。凡是容留罪的，凡是放松随便的，凡是任意妄为的，凡是目空一切的，都是不认识神是神的人。我们要知道，“被造的，没有一样在祂面前不显然的；原来万物，在那与我们有关系的主眼前，都是赤露敞开的。”（来四）所以，“暗昧无益的事，不要与人同行，倒要责备……因为他们暗中所行的，就是提起来，也是可耻的。”暗昧是怕在神面前敞开的；不敢在神面前敞开的，就是可耻的。保罗说，“我们既知道主是可畏的，所以劝人。”（林后五）我们不敢不敬畏主，我们要劝人说，除非你没有悔改，除非你没有得救；若是你实在悔改过，实在得救了，你就要知道，“我们的神乃是烈火”（来十二）。如果你不认真对付一切该对付的罪，总有一天要落在永生神的手里，那真是可怕的！（十）神暂时隐藏，你想祂是睡觉了么？神忍耐宽容等你悔改，你想祂是可以轻慢的么？圣经告诉我们说，“神是轻慢不得的。”（加六）所以，弟兄姊妹们哪，我们必须敬畏神。", "en": "When we know God as the Father, we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom. And when we know God as God, we must bow down and worship Him. We are God's children, living in His love and gladly enjoying all that He gives us. We are also His people, standing upon the position of a man, worshipping and praising Him. Because God is God we need to worship Him in holy array (Psa. 29) and in fear (Psa. 5). Anyone who knows God as God in all things cannot but fear Him and pay attention to such things as his clothing and behavior. Anyone who is loose, careless, haughty, doing whatever he will, and allowing sin to remain, is one who does not know God as God. We know that \"there is no creature that is not manifest before Him, but all things are naked and laid bare to the eyes of Him to Whom we are accountable\" (Heb. 4). Therefore, \"Do not participate in the unfruitful works of darkness, but rather even expose them; for the things which are done by them in secret it is shameful even to speak of.\" If a man is afraid to open up anything to God, that is called darkness. Anything which a man dares not open to God is a shame. Paul said, \"Knowing therefore the fear of the Lord, we persuade men\" (2 Cor. 5). We dare not but fear the Lord and entreat men, telling them that unless they are non-repentant or unsaved they must know that \"our God is a consuming fire\" (Heb. 12). If man does not deal seriously with all the sins which should be dealt with, he will fall, one day, into the hands of the living God. This will be a terrible experience (Heb. 10). Do you think that God is sleeping because He temporarily hides Himself? God is patient and tolerant, waiting for you to repent. Do you think that He can be mocked? The Scriptures tell us \"God is not mocked\" (Gal. 6). Brothers and sisters, we must fear God.", "norm_zh": "我们认识神是父我们敢投在祂的怀抱里我们认识神是神只有俯伏在地敬拜祂我们是神的儿女我们活在祂的爱里我们欢乐地享受祂所给我们的一切我们作神的子民我们是站在人的地位上我们敬拜祂我们赞美祂我们认识神是神我们就要以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华诗二九就要存敬畏的心向祂下拜五哦一个认识神是神的人在一切的事上都不敢不敬畏主都不敢不注重自己的衣服行为凡是容留罪的凡是放松随便的凡是任意妄为的凡是目空一切的都是不认识神是神的人我们要知道被造的没有一样在祂面前不显然的原来万物在哪与我们有关系的主眼前都是赤露敞开的来四所以暗昧无益的事不要与人同行倒要责备因为他们暗中所行的就是提起来也是可耻的暗昧是怕在神面前敞开的不敢在神面前敞开的就是可耻的保罗说我们既知道主是可畏的所以劝人林后五我们不敢不敬畏主我们要劝人说除非你没有悔改除非你没有得救若是你实在悔改过实在得救了你就要知道我们的神乃是烈火来十二如果你不认真对付一切该对付的罪总有一天要落在永生神的手里哪真是可怕的十神暂时隐藏你想祂是睡觉了么神忍耐宽容等你悔改你想祂是可以轻慢的么圣经告诉我们说神是轻慢不得的加六所以弟兄姊妹们哪我们必须敬畏神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "When we know God as the Father we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom And when we know God as God we must bow down and worship Him We are Gods children living in His love and gladly enjoying all that He gives us We are also His people standing upon the position of a man worshipping and praising Him Because God is God we need to worship Him in holy array Psa 29 and in fear Psa 5 Anyone who knows God as God in all things cannot but fear Him and pay attention to such things as his clothing and behavior Anyone who is loose careless haughty doing whatever he will and allowing sin to remain is one who does not know God as God We know that there is no creature that is not manifest before Him but all things are naked and laid bare to the eyes of Him to Whom we are accountable Heb 4 Therefore Do not participate in the unfruitful works of darkness but rather even expose them for the things which are done by them in secret it is shameful even to speak of If a man is afraid to open up anything to God that is called darkness Anything which a man dares not open to God is a shame Paul said Knowing therefore the fear of the Lord we persuade men 2 Cor 5 We dare not but fear the Lord and entreat men telling them that unless they are nonrepentant or unsaved they must know that our God is a consuming fire Heb 12 If man does not deal seriously with all the sins which should be dealt with he will fall one day into the hands of the living God This will be a terrible experience Heb 10 Do you think that God is sleeping because He temporarily hides Himself God is patient and tolerant waiting for you to repent Do you think that He can be mocked The Scriptures tell us God is not mocked Gal 6 Brothers and sisters we must fear God"}
{"zh": "我们的主降生在木匠的家里是作人（太十三），祂受施浸约翰的浸是作人，祂三次拒绝魔鬼的试探是作人，“祂自己既然被试探而受苦”是作人（来二），祂在十字架上被人讥诮却不下来是作人。主尚且如此，何况我们呢。", "en": "Our Lord being born in a carpenter's house was to be a man (Matt. 13), His being baptized by John the Baptist was to be a man, His rejecting the devil's temptation three times was to be a man, \"since He Himself has suffered being tempted\" was to be a man (Heb. 2), and His being mocked on the cross yet not coming down was to be a man. Since the Lord was such, how much more we?", "norm_zh": "我们的主降生在木匠的家里是作人太十三祂受施浸约翰的浸是作人祂三次拒绝魔鬼的试探是作人祂自己既然被试探而受苦是作人来二祂在十字架上被人讥诮却不下来是作人主尚且如此何况我们呢", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Our Lord being born in a carpenters house was to be a man Matt 13 His being baptized by John the Baptist was to be a man His rejecting the devils temptation three times was to be a man since He Himself has suffered being tempted was to be a man Heb 2 and His being mocked on the cross yet not coming down was to be a man Since the Lord was such how much more we"}
{"zh": "凡是认识神是神，自己站在仆人地位的，都要敬拜神（二二）。那“坐在神的殿里，自称是神”的，必定是抵挡主的（帖后二）。那能行奇事迷惑在地上的人说要拜那兽的，也必定是假冒的基督（太二24）。凡认识神是神的人，就敬拜神。这个，是能叫神得着荣耀的。", "en": "Anyone who knows God as God and takes the position of a slave will worship Him (Rev. 22). Surely he who \"sitteth in the temple of God, setting himself forth as God,\" is the one who opposes the Lord (2 Thes. 2). He who is able to do signs and deceive people upon the earth, telling them to worship the beast is surely the false Christ (Matt. 24). Anyone who knows God as God will worship Him. This is what glorifies God.", "norm_zh": "凡是认识神是神自己站在仆人地位的都要敬拜神二二哪坐在神的殿里自称是神的必定是抵挡主的帖后二哪能行奇事迷惑在地上的人说要拜哪兽的也必定是假冒的基督太二24凡认识神是神的人就敬拜神这个是能叫神得着荣耀的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Anyone who knows God as God and takes the position of a slave will worship Him Rev 22 Surely he who sitteth in the temple of God setting himself forth as God is the one who opposes the Lord 2 Thes 2 He who is able to do signs and deceive people upon the earth telling them to worship the beast is surely the false Christ Matt 24 Anyone who knows God as God will worship Him This is what glorifies God"}
{"zh": "一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉。除非一个人没有重生，他才没有感觉；如果他是重生了，总是有一点感觉的。有一个基督徒是作医师的，他问一个传道人说，“属灵的起头和属灵的长进，是从饥渴起头的，但是，有许多人，他不觉得饥，他不觉得渴，那么，如何叫这样的人能觉得饥，能觉得渴呢？”那个传道人就说，“你是医师，你知道人有生命。除非这个人死了，他才没有食欲；如果他没有死，多少总是有食欲的。那么你如何加增他的食欲呢？你给他药吃。他吃一点药，食欲加增一点，吃到后来，食欲就正常了。所以，我们只要有一点感觉，我们就要顺服这一个感觉。你顺服这一点感觉，你的饥渴就增加一点；你再顺服一点感觉，你的饥渴又多增加一点。你的感觉加强，你就多顺服一点；你多顺服一点，你的感觉就更强。你再顺服，你就再加上感觉，你立刻看见，你的里面活了。”生命在我们里面的运行就是这样。它转到你的心情部分，叫你向着神去；再转到你的心思部分，叫你向着神去；再转到你的心志部分，叫你向着神去。这样一圈一圈地转，你的生命就加多，你的生命就加深，你的生命就加高了。所以，我们总要从顺服最小的感觉起。一有感觉，就得顺服。", "en": "The first condition is to obey the first sense of life. Unless a man is not regenerated, he will have some sense of life. A Christian who was a medical doctor asked a preacher the following question: \"Both the beginning and the growth of our spiritual life start with hunger and thirst. However, many people do not feel hungry or thirsty. When that is the case, how can we cause them to become hungry and thirsty?\" The reply was: \"You are a medical doctor. You know that a man has life. Unless a man is dead, he will have some appetite. Then how do you increase his appetite? You prescribe something for him to increase his appetite. As he takes medicine, his appetite increases little by little. You continue this until his appetite is restored to normal. Therefore, whenever we have a little sense, we should obey this sense. When we obey this sense, our hunger and thirst increase slightly. When we obey more, the hunger and thirst increases again and our sense becomes stronger. Then we obey a little more. The more we obey, the stronger the sense will be. By taking this way we become alive from within.\" The Lord's life moves within us in the same way. It moves into our emotion, causing us to turn to God; it moves into our mind, causing us to turn to God; then it moves into our will, causing us to turn to God. By such continuous moving and turning, the life within us will be increased, deepened, and caused to grow. Therefore, we need to begin by obeying the least sense. Whenever there is a sense, we should obey.", "norm_zh": "一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉除非一个人没有重生他才没有感觉如果他是重生了总是有一点感觉的有一个基督徒是作医师的他问一个传道人说属灵的起头和属灵的长进是从饥渴起头的但是有许多人他不觉得饥他不觉得渴哪么如何叫这样的人能觉得饥能觉得渴呢哪个传道人就说你是医师你知道人有生命除非这个人死了他才没有食欲如果他没有死多少总是有食欲的哪么你如何加增他的食欲呢你给他药吃他吃一点药食欲加增一点吃到后来食欲就正常了所以我们只要有一点感觉我们就要顺服这一个感觉你顺服这一点感觉你的饥渴就增加一点你再顺服一点感觉你的饥渴又多增加一点你的感觉加强你就多顺服一点你多顺服一点你的感觉就更强你再顺服你就再加上感觉你立刻看见你的里面活了生命在我们里面的运行就是这样它转到你的心情部分叫你向着神去再转到你的心思部分叫你向着神去再转到你的心志部分叫你向着神去这样一圈一圈地转你的生命就加多你的生命就加深你的生命就加高了所以我们总要从顺服最小的感觉起一有感觉就得顺服", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The first condition is to obey the first sense of life Unless a man is not regenerated he will have some sense of life A Christian who was a medical doctor asked a preacher the following question Both the beginning and the growth of our spiritual life start with hunger and thirst However many people do not feel hungry or thirsty When that is the case how can we cause them to become hungry and thirsty The reply was You are a medical doctor You know that a man has life Unless a man is dead he will have some appetite Then how do you increase his appetite You prescribe something for him to increase his appetite As he takes medicine his appetite increases little by little You continue this until his appetite is restored to normal Therefore whenever we have a little sense we should obey this sense When we obey this sense our hunger and thirst increase slightly When we obey more the hunger and thirst increases again and our sense becomes stronger Then we obey a little more The more we obey the stronger the sense will be By taking this way we become alive from within The Lords life moves within us in the same way It moves into our emotion causing us to turn to God it moves into our mind causing us to turn to God then it moves into our will causing us to turn to God By such continuous moving and turning the life within us will be increased deepened and caused to grow Therefore we need to begin by obeying the least sense Whenever there is a sense we should obey"}
{"zh": "爱神", "en": "Loving God", "norm_zh": "爱神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Loving God"}
{"zh": "以弗所二章十节说，“我们原是祂的工作，在基督耶稣里造成的，为要叫我们行善，就是神所预备叫我们行的。”这个工作，是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的，可以说是“神的杰作”。什么叫“杰作”呢？“杰作”，就是最好的作物，最好的作品，不能比这再好了。神把人救得来，是在基督耶稣里把他造成到最好的地步，这是生命的大能在人里面运行而成的。这是新约的特点。神把人造成到好得不能再好的地步，就是要人满足于自己么？不。祂为的是“要叫我们行善”。行些什么善呢？行“神所预备叫我们行的”。哦，这标准太高了。神所预备叫我们行的善，必是神自己所认为是善的善。只有发源于“爱”的善，才是神自己所认为是善的善。不是发源于“爱”的善，就是“将所有的周济……人，又舍己身叫人焚烧”，仍然无益。发源于“爱”的善，不是普通所谓的善，乃是由爱的生命所流出来的善，是本着爱而行出来的善。神所预备叫我们行的善，只有凭着神的生命才能行。感谢神，祂救了我们，祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了，祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作，叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善。这是福音，这是新约的荣耀，阿利路亚！", "en": "Ephesians 2:10 says, \"We are His workmanship, created in Christ Jesus for good works, which God before prepared that we should walk in them.\" This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus. We can say that it is God's masterpiece. A masterpiece is simply the most excellent, fine piece of work, the best production. Nothing can be better than a masterpiece. God has not only saved His people, but in Christ Jesus He has made them into a masterpiece. This has been done through the working of the power of His life in man. This is an aspect of the characteristic of the new covenant. God has made man into such a masterpiece that He could not do better. This has not been done so that man could be satisfied in himself, but so that God's purpose of fulfilling the good works which He has prepared before might be accomplished. What a wonderfully high standard! The good works which God has prepared for us must be something which He considers to be good. Only that which has its origin in love is the good works which God considers good. Any good work that does not originate from love, even bestowing all our goods to feed the poor, or even giving our body to be burned for others, is still not profitable. The good works which originate from love are not ordinary good works, but good works which issue from a life of love and which are done based on the principle of love. The good works which God has prepared for us to do can only be fulfilled and lived out by God's life. Praise God, He has saved us and put His life in us! It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for us. This is the gospel. This is the glory of the new covenant! Hallelujah!", "norm_zh": "以弗所二章十节说我们原是祂的工作在基督耶稣里造成的为要叫我们行善就是神所预备叫我们行的这个工作是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的可以说是神的杰作什么叫杰作呢杰作就是最好的作物最好的作品不能比这再好了神把人救得来是在基督耶稣里把他造成到最好的地步这是生命的大能在人里面运行而成的这是新约的特点神把人造成到好得不能再好的地步就是要人满足于自己么不祂为的是要叫我们行善行些什么善呢行神所预备叫我们行的哦这标准太高了神所预备叫我们行的善必是神自己所认为是善的善只有发源于爱的善才是神自己所认为是善的善不是发源于爱的善就是将所有的周济人又舍己身叫人焚烧仍然无益发源于爱的善不是普通所谓的善乃是由爱的生命所流出来的善是本着爱而行出来的善神所预备叫我们行的善只有凭着神的生命才能行感谢神祂救了我们祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善这是福音这是新约的荣耀阿利路亚", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ephesians 210 says We are His workmanship created in Christ Jesus for good works which God before prepared that we should walk in them This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus We can say that it is Gods masterpiece A masterpiece is simply the most excellent fine piece of work the best production Nothing can be better than a masterpiece God has not only saved His people but in Christ Jesus He has made them into a masterpiece This has been done through the working of the power of His life in man This is an aspect of the characteristic of the new covenant God has made man into such a masterpiece that He could not do better This has not been done so that man could be satisfied in himself but so that Gods purpose of fulfilling the good works which He has prepared before might be accomplished What a wonderfully high standard The good works which God has prepared for us must be something which He considers to be good Only that which has its origin in love is the good works which God considers good Any good work that does not originate from love even bestowing all our goods to feed the poor or even giving our body to be burned for others is still not profitable The good works which originate from love are not ordinary good works but good works which issue from a life of love and which are done based on the principle of love The good works which God has prepared for us to do can only be fulfilled and lived out by Gods life Praise God He has saved us and put His life in us It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for us This is the gospel This is the glory of the new covenant Hallelujah"}
{"zh": "使徒保罗说，“祂所赐我的恩，不是徒然的。”这怎么见得呢？因他“比众使徒格外劳苦”。他说，“这原不是我，乃是神的恩与我同在。”他之所以能格外劳苦，并不是他的身体特别比人好，也不是他比别人特别殷勤，乃是因神的恩与他同在（林前十五）。他说，“我们传扬祂，是用诸般的智慧，劝戒各人，教导各人；要把各人在基督里完完全全地引到神面前。”他怎能这样呢？他说，“我也为此劳苦，照着祂在我里面运用的大能，尽心竭力。”这里的“大能”，也可以译作“炸力”。换句话说，神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力，所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力。使徒保罗作工，不是他有魄力，乃是他有炸力。这一个炸力在他里面一直炸，叫他能勤劳地，能尽心竭力地把各人在基督里完完全全引到神面前。这个炸力，就是神的生命运行的大能。就是这个生命的大能，叫我们能殷勤地作工，能尽心竭力地作工。“格外劳苦”，“尽心竭力”，都是证明里面的恩典，里面的生命的大能。这给我们看见，神赐我们恩典，不是叫我们作一个属灵的欣赏者，不是叫我们作一个属灵的自娱者，乃是要我们比别人格外劳苦，要我们尽心竭力。如果有谁说他是主的仆人，而他却是一味自爱，懒惰不肯作工；他就不只是懒，也必是恶的（太二五）。这样的仆人，是被主定罪的。所以，弟兄姊妹们，我们不要空讲道理，我们必须仰望神而把祂的恩典活出来，把祂的大能彰显出来。", "en": "The Apostle Paul said: \"His grace which was bestowed upon me was not found vain\" (1 Cor. 15). We know this was true because he labored more abundantly than all the other apostles. Yet he says, \"Not I, but the grace of God which was with me.\" He could labor more abundantly than others, not because his body was stronger, nor because he was more diligent than others, but because the grace of God was with him. He says further, \"Whom we announce, warning every man and teaching every man in all wisdom, that we may present every man full grown in Christ; for which also I labor, struggling according to His operation which operates in me in power.\" The word \"power\" here can also be translated \"exploding power.\" In other words, what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power; hence, what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power. The Apostle Paul worked, not because he was energetic in himself, but because within him there was an exploding power. This exploding power exploded continually within him, enabling him to labor diligently and to struggle to bring all men before God perfect in Christ. This exploding power is the power of the working of God's life! It is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work. To labor more abundantly and to strive or struggle prove both the inner grace and the power of the inner life. This indicates that God gives us grace, not to make us those who appreciate spirituality, nor that we might enjoy our own spirituality, but that we may be more diligent, laboring and striving more than others. If anyone says that he is the Lord's servant, and yet continues to love himself, to be lazy, and not to work, then he is not only slothful, he is also surely evil (Matt. 25). This kind of servant is condemned by the Lord. Therefore, we must not talk about empty doctrines. We must look to God that we may live out His grace and manifest His power.", "norm_zh": "使徒保罗说祂所赐我的恩不是徒然的这怎么见得呢因他比众使徒格外劳苦他说这原不是我乃是神的恩与我同在他之所以能格外劳苦并不是他的身体特别比人好也不是他比别人特别殷勤乃是因神的恩与他同在林前十五他说我们传扬祂是用诸般的智慧劝戒各人教导各人要把各人在基督里完完全全地引到神面前他怎能这样呢他说我也为此劳苦照着祂在我里面运用的大能尽心竭力这里的大能也可以译作炸力换句话说神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力使徒保罗作工不是他有魄力乃是他有炸力这一个炸力在他里面一直炸叫他能勤劳地能尽心竭力地把各人在基督里完完全全引到神面前这个炸力就是神的生命运行的大能就是这个生命的大能叫我们能殷勤地作工能尽心竭力地作工格外劳苦尽心竭力都是证明里面的恩典里面的生命的大能这给我们看见神赐我们恩典不是叫我们作一个属灵的欣赏者不是叫我们作一个属灵的自娱者乃是要我们比别人格外劳苦要我们尽心竭力如果有谁说他是主的仆人而他却是一味自爱懒惰不肯作工他就不只是懒也必是恶的太二五这样的仆人是被主定罪的所以弟兄姊妹们我们不要空讲道理我们必须仰望神而把祂的恩典活出来把祂的大能彰显出来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Apostle Paul said His grace which was bestowed upon me was not found vain 1 Cor 15 We know this was true because he labored more abundantly than all the other apostles Yet he says Not I but the grace of God which was with me He could labor more abundantly than others not because his body was stronger nor because he was more diligent than others but because the grace of God was with him He says further Whom we announce warning every man and teaching every man in all wisdom that we may present every man full grown in Christ for which also I labor struggling according to His operation which operates in me in power The word power here can also be translated exploding power In other words what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power hence what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power The Apostle Paul worked not because he was energetic in himself but because within him there was an exploding power This exploding power exploded continually within him enabling him to labor diligently and to struggle to bring all men before God perfect in Christ This exploding power is the power of the working of Gods life It is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work To labor more abundantly and to strive or struggle prove both the inner grace and the power of the inner life This indicates that God gives us grace not to make us those who appreciate spirituality nor that we might enjoy our own spirituality but that we may be more diligent laboring and striving more than others If anyone says that he is the Lords servant and yet continues to love himself to be lazy and not to work then he is not only slothful he is also surely evil Matt 25 This kind of servant is condemned by the Lord Therefore we must not talk about empty doctrines We must look to God that we may live out His grace and manifest His power"}
{"zh": "新约的事奉与旧约的事奉是大不相同的。旧约的事奉是字句的，新约的事奉是凭着灵的；旧约的事奉是陈旧的，新约的事奉是新鲜的；旧约的事奉是杀死人的，新约的事奉是叫人活的。换句话说，旧约的事奉是按着写在那里的一条一条的字句，奉行故事地在那里事奉；新约的事奉是凭着灵，是灵在人里面要人怎么动，人才怎么动；灵在人里面要人怎样说，人才怎样说；灵在人里面要人怎样祷告，人才怎样祷告。可以说，旧约的事奉是外面的，新约的事奉是里面的。旧约“字句”的事奉，结果是“杀死”人的；新约“灵”的事奉，结果是“叫人活”的。再换句话说，凭着“字句”的事奉是死的，活在“基督里”的事奉是活的；凭着“字句”的事奉是陈旧的，活在“基督里”的事奉是新鲜的；凭着“字句”的事奉是字句的，活在“基督里”的事奉是属灵的。总而言之：凡是凭着外面，凭着字句，凭着老一套的事奉，都是旧约的事奉；凡是凭着里面，凭着灵，凭着新鲜的事奉，都是新约的事奉。凡是照着外面抄袭模仿而来的，都不是新约的事奉。新约的事奉，乃是与基督发生关系，由里面运行出来的。新约的事奉是属灵的，是启示的，是新鲜的。新约的事奉是需要“本于”神，“倚靠”神，也“归于”神的（罗十一）。事奉的力量是本于祂，事奉的经过是倚靠祂，事奉的结果是归于祂；这是灵的事奉，这是活的事奉，这是新约的事奉。", "en": "The New Testament service is very different from the Old Testament service. The Old Testament service is of the letter, and the New Testament service is of the Spirit; the Old Testament service is old, and the New Testament service is fresh; the Old Testament service kills, and the New Testament service gives life. In other words, the Old Testament service is according to the letters written there, serving there in a routine way; the New Testament service is by the Spirit; as the Spirit wants man to move inwardly, so man moves; as the Spirit wants man to speak inwardly, so man speaks; as the Spirit wants man to pray inwardly, so man prays. We can say that the Old Testament service is outward, and the New Testament service is inward. The Old Testament service of \"the letter\" results in \"killing\" people, whereas the New Testament service of \"the Spirit\" results in \"giving life\" to people. In other words again, the service by \"the letter\" is dead, and the service lived \"in Christ\" is living; the service by \"the letter\" is old, and the service lived \"in Christ\" is fresh; the service by \"the letter\" is of the letter, and the service lived \"in Christ\" is spiritual. In short: all service that is by the outward, by the letter, and by the old way is the Old Testament service; all service that is by the inward, by the Spirit, and by freshness is the New Testament service. Any service that comes from copying and imitating outwardly is not the New Testament service. The New Testament service is related to Christ and is operated out from within. The New Testament service is spiritual, revelatory, and fresh. The New Testament service needs to be \"out of\" God, \"through\" God, and \"unto\" God (Rom. 11). The strength of the service is out of Him, the process of the service is through Him, and the result of the service is unto Him; this is the service of the Spirit, this is the living service, this is the New Testament service.", "norm_zh": "新约的事奉与旧约的事奉是大不相同的旧约的事奉是字句的新约的事奉是凭着灵的旧约的事奉是陈旧的新约的事奉是新鲜的旧约的事奉是杀死人的新约的事奉是叫人活的换句话说旧约的事奉是按着写在哪里的一条一条的字句奉行故事地在哪里事奉新约的事奉是凭着灵是灵在人里面要人怎么动人才怎么动灵在人里面要人怎样说人才怎样说灵在人里面要人怎样祷告人才怎样祷告可以说旧约的事奉是外面的新约的事奉是里面的旧约字句的事奉结果是杀死人的新约灵的事奉结果是叫人活的再换句话说凭着字句的事奉是死的活在基督里的事奉是活的凭着字句的事奉是陈旧的活在基督里的事奉是新鲜的凭着字句的事奉是字句的活在基督里的事奉是属灵的总而言之凡是凭着外面凭着字句凭着老一套的事奉都是旧约的事奉凡是凭着里面凭着灵凭着新鲜的事奉都是新约的事奉凡是照着外面抄袭模仿而来的都不是新约的事奉新约的事奉乃是与基督发生关系由里面运行出来的新约的事奉是属灵的是启示的是新鲜的新约的事奉是需要本于神倚靠神也归于神的罗十一事奉的力量是本于祂事奉的经过是倚靠祂事奉的结果是归于祂这是灵的事奉这是活的事奉这是新约的事奉", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Testament service is very different from the Old Testament service The Old Testament service is of the letter and the New Testament service is of the Spirit the Old Testament service is old and the New Testament service is fresh the Old Testament service kills and the New Testament service gives life In other words the Old Testament service is according to the letters written there serving there in a routine way the New Testament service is by the Spirit as the Spirit wants man to move inwardly so man moves as the Spirit wants man to speak inwardly so man speaks as the Spirit wants man to pray inwardly so man prays We can say that the Old Testament service is outward and the New Testament service is inward The Old Testament service of the letter results in killing people whereas the New Testament service of the Spirit results in giving life to people In other words again the service by the letter is dead and the service lived in Christ is living the service by the letter is old and the service lived in Christ is fresh the service by the letter is of the letter and the service lived in Christ is spiritual In short all service that is by the outward by the letter and by the old way is the Old Testament service all service that is by the inward by the Spirit and by freshness is the New Testament service Any service that comes from copying and imitating outwardly is not the New Testament service The New Testament service is related to Christ and is operated out from within The New Testament service is spiritual revelatory and fresh The New Testament service needs to be out of God through God and unto God Rom 11 The strength of the service is out of Him the process of the service is through Him and the result of the service is unto Him this is the service of the Spirit this is the living service this is the New Testament service"}
{"zh": "生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通，生命就能发展到一个地步，使“基督成形”在我们里面（加四）。基督渐渐成形在我们里面，我们就渐渐“变化”（林后三），而变化的目标就是“象祂”（约壹三）。基督成形在我们里面，是与神的生命在我们里面的运行分不开的。神的生命成为我们里面的成分有多少，基督成形在我们里面也有多少，我们的变化就也有多少。人的里面充满着基督的生命，人的外面把基督活出来，把基督彰显出来，这就是罗马八章二十九节所说的“与祂儿子的像同形质”。这是保罗的追求，也是保罗的经历。这是神的儿女今天应该有的追求，也是今天可能有的经历。至于完全象祂，那是要等到“主显现”的时候，就是“身体得赎”的日子来到，才能完全地象祂。", "en": "As the law of life operates in us circle after circle, life can develop to such an extent that \"Christ is formed\" in us (Gal. 4). As Christ is gradually formed in us, we are gradually \"transformed\" (2 Cor. 3), and the goal of transformation is to be \"like Him\" (1 John 3). Christ being formed in us is inseparable from the operation of God's life within us. To whatever extent God's life becomes our inward constituent, to that extent Christ is formed in us, and to that extent we are transformed. To be filled with the life of Christ inwardly and to live Christ out and manifest Him outwardly is to be \"conformed to the image of His Son,\" as spoken of in Romans 8:29. This was Paul's pursuit, and it was also Paul's experience. This is the pursuit that God's children should have today, and it is also the experience they can have today. As for being completely like Him, we must wait until the time of \"the Lord's appearing,\" which is the coming of the day of \"the redemption of our body,\" to be completely like Him.", "norm_zh": "生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通生命就能发展到一个地步使基督成形在我们里面加四基督渐渐成形在我们里面我们就渐渐变化林后三而变化的目标就是象祂约壹三基督成形在我们里面是与神的生命在我们里面的运行分不开的神的生命成为我们里面的成分有多少基督成形在我们里面也有多少我们的变化就也有多少人的里面充满着基督的生命人的外面把基督活出来把基督彰显出来这就是罗马八章二十九节所说的与祂儿子的像同形质这是保罗的追求也是保罗的经历这是神的儿女今天应该有的追求也是今天可能有的经历至于完全象祂哪是要等到主显现的时候就是身体得赎的日子来到才能完全地象祂", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "As the law of life operates in us circle after circle life can develop to such an extent that Christ is formed in us Gal 4 As Christ is gradually formed in us we are gradually transformed 2 Cor 3 and the goal of transformation is to be like Him 1 John 3 Christ being formed in us is inseparable from the operation of Gods life within us To whatever extent Gods life becomes our inward constituent to that extent Christ is formed in us and to that extent we are transformed To be filled with the life of Christ inwardly and to live Christ out and manifest Him outwardly is to be conformed to the image of His Son as spoken of in Romans 829 This was Pauls pursuit and it was also Pauls experience This is the pursuit that Gods children should have today and it is also the experience they can have today As for being completely like Him we must wait until the time of the Lords appearing which is the coming of the day of the redemption of our body to be completely like Him"}
{"zh": "象祂", "en": "like Him", "norm_zh": "象祂", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "like Him"}
{"zh": "我们已经说过，变化的目标就是“象祂”，而完全地象祂是要等到“主显现”的时候，就是“身体得赎”的日子来到，才能完全地象祂。所以我们也必须说到一点关于“身体得赎”的事。我们已经看见，亚当堕落后，灵先死了，人完全受魂的支配，完全属乎肉体了，而后身体也死了（创五，罗八），这是从灵死直到身体死。当人得重生的时候是灵先活，圣灵借着十字架的工作治死我们身体的恶行（罗八，西三），叫我们天天拒绝自己。叫我们因着里面生命的运行，一天过一天，在本质上有了更多的改变，在形状上也有了更多的改变，以致与神儿子的像相似。到有一天，“主若显现，我们必要象祂，因为必得见祂的真体”（约壹三）。这就是保罗所等候的“身体得赎”（罗八）；这就是腓立比三章二十一节所说的，“祂要按着那能叫万有归服自己的大能，将我们这卑贱的身体改变形状，和祂自己荣耀的身体相似。”以上的这些话给我们看见，神的救法是从灵活起，直到身体得赎。我们要知道，罗马八章十三节所说的“必要活着”，乃是指身体天天在经历上的活着而言，不是指身体得赎说的。圣经告诉我们，“复活”与“改变”是一个奥秘。“身体得赎”而与“祂自己荣耀的身体相似”，又是太荣耀了！使徒约翰相信这个有一天必定实现，所以说，“主若显现，我们必要象祂，因为必得见祂的真体。”这是新约的特点，这是新约的荣耀！弟兄姊妹们哪，我们不要信得太迟了！（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "We have said already that the goal of transformation is to be like Him. But complete likeness to Him must wait until the Lord appears. That is the time of the redemption of our body. Then we will be wholly like Him. For this reason we must also say a word concerning the redemption of the body. We have seen that when Adam fell the spirit died first, and man became completely controlled by the soul and completely in the flesh. Later, the body also died (Gen. 5; Rom. 8). This means that the death which took place in the spirit eventually reached the body. When man is regenerated his spirit is made alive first. Then through the work of the cross the Holy Spirit puts to death the evil practices of our body (Rom. 8; Col. 3), causing us to deny ourselves daily. Through the operation of the life in us day by day we are being changed increasingly both in our nature and in our form, so that we may be conformed to the image of the Son of God. Eventually one day when the Lord appears \"we shall be like him; for we shall see him even as he is\" (1 John 3). This is the redemption of the body for which Paul was waiting (Rom. 8); this matter is also mentioned in Philippians 3:21, where Paul says that the Lord Jesus will \"transfigure the body of our humiliation, conforming it to the body of His glory, according to the operation of Him Who is able even to subject all things to Himself.\" From these verses we see that God's salvation begins with making our spirit alive and ends with the redemption of our body. The phrase \"you will live\" mentioned in Romans 8:13 refers to our daily experience of living in the body. It does not refer to the redemption of our body. The Scriptures tell us that resurrection and transformation are a mystery. The redemption of the body in which we are made like unto His own glorious body is also exceedingly glorious. The Apostle John believed that this would be fulfilled one day. Therefore, he said that when the Lord appears, we shall be like Him for we shall see Him as He is. This is the characteristic of the new covenant. This is also the glory of the new covenant! Brothers and sisters, let us not be too late in believing.", "norm_zh": "我们已经说过变化的目标就是象祂而完全地象祂是要等到主显现的时候就是身体得赎的日子来到才能完全地象祂所以我们也必须说到一点关于身体得赎的事我们已经看见亚当堕落后灵先死了人完全受魂的支配完全属乎肉体了而后身体也死了创五罗八这是从灵死直到身体死当人得重生的时候是灵先活圣灵借着十字架的工作治死我们身体的恶行罗八西三叫我们天天拒绝自己叫我们因着里面生命的运行一天过一天在本质上有了更多的改变在形状上也有了更多的改变以致与神儿子的像相似到有一天主若显现我们必要象祂因为必得见祂的真体约壹三这就是保罗所等候的身体得赎罗八这就是腓立比三章二十一节所说的祂要按着哪能叫万有归服自己的大能将我们这卑贱的身体改变形状和祂自己荣耀的身体相似以上的这些话给我们看见神的救法是从灵活起直到身体得赎我们要知道罗马八章十三节所说的必要活着乃是指身体天天在经历上的活着而言不是指身体得赎说的圣经告诉我们复活与改变是一个奥秘身体得赎而与祂自己荣耀的身体相似又是太荣耀了使徒约翰相信这个有一天必定实现所以说主若显现我们必要象祂因为必得见祂的真体这是新约的特点这是新约的荣耀弟兄姊妹们哪我们不要信得太迟了李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:22:35.414801+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have said already that the goal of transformation is to be like Him But complete likeness to Him must wait until the Lord appears That is the time of the redemption of our body Then we will be wholly like Him For this reason we must also say a word concerning the redemption of the body We have seen that when Adam fell the spirit died first and man became completely controlled by the soul and completely in the flesh Later the body also died Gen 5 Rom 8 This means that the death which took place in the spirit eventually reached the body When man is regenerated his spirit is made alive first Then through the work of the cross the Holy Spirit puts to death the evil practices of our body Rom 8 Col 3 causing us to deny ourselves daily Through the operation of the life in us day by day we are being changed increasingly both in our nature and in our form so that we may be conformed to the image of the Son of God Eventually one day when the Lord appears we shall be like him for we shall see him even as he is 1 John 3 This is the redemption of the body for which Paul was waiting Rom 8 this matter is also mentioned in Philippians 321 where Paul says that the Lord Jesus will transfigure the body of our humiliation conforming it to the body of His glory according to the operation of Him Who is able even to subject all things to Himself From these verses we see that Gods salvation begins with making our spirit alive and ends with the redemption of our body The phrase you will live mentioned in Romans 813 refers to our daily experience of living in the body It does not refer to the redemption of our body The Scriptures tell us that resurrection and transformation are a mystery The redemption of the body in which we are made like unto His own glorious body is also exceedingly glorious The Apostle John believed that this would be fulfilled one day Therefore he said that when the Lord appears we shall be like Him for we shall see Him as He is This is the characteristic of the new covenant This is also the glory of the new covenant Brothers and sisters let us not be too late in believing"}
{"zh": "壹\t希伯来八章十节的下一半有话说，“我要作他们的神，他们要作我的子民”；这说出了神的心意，这说出了神从永远到永远的目的；神要在生命的律里作我们的神，我们要在生命的律里作神的子民：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "I. In the second part of Hebrews 8:10 it says, \"I will be God to them, and they shall be a people to Me\"; this tells us what is on God's heart and what His purpose is from eternity to eternity; God wants to be our God, and we need to be His people according to the law of life:", "norm_zh": "壹希伯来八章十节的下一半有话说我要作他们的神他们要作我的子民这说出了神的心意这说出了神从永远到永远的目的神要在生命的律里作我们的神我们要在生命的律里作神的子民李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I In the second part of Hebrews 810 it says I will be God to them and they shall be a people to Me this tells us what is on Gods heart and what His purpose is from eternity to eternity God wants to be our God and we need to be His people according to the law of life"}
{"zh": "一\t神永远的目的；就是神要作神；神是神，并且，神要在人中间作神；要我们宣告祂是神，只有祂是神，其余的都不是—出二十1~8，太六9，诗一〇五3，八1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. God's eternal purpose; that is, God wants to be God; God is God, and furthermore, God wants to be God among men; He wants us to declare that He is God, that He alone is God, and that all else are not—Exo. 20:1-8; Matt. 6:9; Psa. 105:3; 8:1.", "norm_zh": "一神永远的目的就是神要作神神是神并且神要在人中间作神要我们宣告祂是神只有祂是神其余的都不是出二十18太六9诗一〇五3八1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods eternal purpose that is God wants to be God God is God and furthermore God wants to be God among men He wants us to declare that He is God that He alone is God and that all else are notExo 2018 Matt 69 Psa 1053 81"}
{"zh": "二\t神要住在以色列人中间作神—出二五8，二九45~46，利二五38，二六12~13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. God Desires to Dwell Among the Children of Israel as Their God—Exo. 25:8; 29:45-46; Lev. 25:38; 26:12-13.", "norm_zh": "二神要住在以色列人中间作神出二五8二九4546利二五38二六1213李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God Desires to Dwell Among the Children of Israel as Their GodExo 258 294546 Lev 2538 261213"}
{"zh": "三\t道成了肉身住在人中间表明神；这就是“以马内利”，就是“神与我们同在”了—太一23。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. The Word became flesh and tabernacled among men to declare God; this is \"Emmanuel,\" which is \"God with us\"—Matt. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "三道成了肉身住在人中间表明神这就是以马内利就是神与我们同在了太一23李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Word became flesh and tabernacled among men to declare God this is Emmanuel which is God with usMatt 123"}
{"zh": "四\t神住在教会里作神；道成了肉身住在人中间，还受空间和时间的限制；等到教会被建立，“被建造成为灵宫”，教会就“成为神借着圣灵居住的所在”了—彼前二5，弗二22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. God dwells in the church as God; when the Word became flesh and tabernacled among men, He was limited by space and time; when the church was built, \"built as a spiritual house,\" the church \"became God's dwelling place in spirit\"—1 Pet. 2:5; Eph. 2:22.", "norm_zh": "四神住在教会里作神道成了肉身住在人中间还受空间和时间的限制等到教会被建立被建造成为灵宫教会就成为神借着圣灵居住的所在了彼前二5弗二22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God dwells in the church as God when the Word became flesh and tabernacled among men He was limited by space and time when the church was built built as a spiritual house the church became Gods dwelling place in spirit1 Pet 25 Eph 222"}
{"zh": "五\t神在国度时代作以色列家的神—来八8~10，耶三一31~34。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "E. In the Kingdom Age God Will be the God of the House of Israel—Heb. 8:8-10; Jer. 31:31-34.", "norm_zh": "五神在国度时代作以色列家的神来八810耶三一3134李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E In the Kingdom Age God Will be the God of the House of IsraelHeb 8810 Jer 313134"}
{"zh": "六\t神在将来的永远里住在人中间作神—启二一3~4。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "F. In Eternity Future God Will Dwell Among Men as God—Rev. 21:3-4.", "norm_zh": "六神在将来的永远里住在人中间作神启二一34李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F In Eternity Future God Will Dwell Among Men as GodRev 2134"}
{"zh": "七\t神作父与神作神—约二十17，林后五11，来十二29：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "G. God as the Father and God as God—John 20:17; 2 Cor. 5:11; Heb. 12:29:", "norm_zh": "七神作父与神作神约二十17林后五11来十二29李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G God as the Father and God as GodJohn 2017 2 Cor 511 Heb 1229"}
{"zh": "1\t说祂是父，是说到生命，是说到祂与我们有了父子生命上的关系；说祂是神，是说到祂的地位，是说祂是创造的主—约一12~13，来四13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. God as our Father is a matter of life, showing that we are related to Him as a son is related to a father; while God as God is a matter of position, showing that He is the Creator.—John 1:12-13; Heb. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "1说祂是父是说到生命是说到祂与我们有了父子生命上的关系说祂是神是说到祂的地位是说祂是创造的主约一1213来四13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God as our Father is a matter of life showing that we are related to Him as a son is related to a father while God as God is a matter of position showing that He is the CreatorJohn 11213 Heb 413"}
{"zh": "2\t我们认识神是父，我们敢投在祂的怀抱里；我们认识神是神，只有俯伏在地敬拜祂。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. When we know God as the Father, we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom. And when we know God as God, we must bow down and worship Him.", "norm_zh": "2我们认识神是父我们敢投在祂的怀抱里我们认识神是神只有俯伏在地敬拜祂李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we know God as the Father we will dare to throw ourselves upon His bosom And when we know God as God we must bow down and worship Him"}
{"zh": "3\t我们认识神是神，我们就要“以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华”；就要“存敬畏的心”向祂下拜；凡是认识神是神，自己站在仆人地位的，都要敬拜神—诗二九2，五7，启二二9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. When we know God as God, we must \"worship Jehovah in holy array\"; we must bow down to Him \"in fear\"; everyone who knows God as God and stands in the position of a servant must worship God.—Psa. 29:2; 5:7; Rev. 22:9.", "norm_zh": "3我们认识神是神我们就要以圣洁的妆饰敬拜耶和华就要存敬畏的心向祂下拜凡是认识神是神自己站在仆人地位的都要敬拜神诗二九2五7启二二9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 When we know God as God we must worship Jehovah in holy array we must bow down to Him in fear everyone who knows God as God and stands in the position of a servant must worship GodPsa 292 57 Rev 229"}
{"zh": "八\t神在生命的律里作神—来八10，约四23~24：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "H. God as God in the Law of Life—Heb. 8:10; John 4:23-24:", "norm_zh": "八神在生命的律里作神来八10约四2324李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H God as God in the Law of LifeHeb 810 John 42324"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来八章十节下一半的话乃是说神在生命的律里作我们的神，我们在生命的律里作神的子民；我们与神，神与我们，两者的关系都是在生命的交通里。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. The second half of Hebrews 8:10 says that God is our God in the law of life and we are God's people in the law of life; we and God, God and we, both have our relationships in the fellowship of life.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来八章十节下一半的话乃是说神在生命的律里作我们的神我们在生命的律里作神的子民我们与神神与我们两者的关系都是在生命的交通里李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The second half of Hebrews 810 says that God is our God in the law of life and we are Gods people in the law of life we and God God and we both have our relationships in the fellowship of life"}
{"zh": "2\t约翰四章二十四节说，“神是灵，所以拜祂的，必须用灵和真拜祂”；这是说，只有与神的质相同的才能敬拜神，只有灵能敬拜灵，只有在灵里的敬拜才是在真实里的敬拜。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. John 4:24 says, \"God is Spirit; and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and reality\"; this means that only the element in man which is the same as God can worship God. Only the spirit can worship Spirit. Only worship which is in the spirit is true worship.", "norm_zh": "2约翰四章二十四节说神是灵所以拜祂的必须用灵和真拜祂这是说只有与神的质相同的才能敬拜神只有灵能敬拜灵只有在灵里的敬拜才是在真实里的敬拜李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 John 424 says God is Spirit and those who worship Him must worship in spirit and reality this means that only the element in man which is the same as God can worship God Only the spirit can worship Spirit Only worship which is in the spirit is true worship"}
{"zh": "3\t所以，我们必须先是神的儿女，然后才能作神的子民；神是在生命的律里作我们的神，我们是在生命的律里作神的子民—23~24节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. Therefore, before we can be God's people, we must first become God's children; God becomes our God in the law of life, and we are God's people in the law of life.—vv. 23-24.", "norm_zh": "3所以我们必须先是神的儿女然后才能作神的子民神是在生命的律里作我们的神我们是在生命的律里作神的子民2324节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Therefore before we can be Gods people we must first become Gods children God becomes our God in the law of life and we are Gods people in the law of lifevv 2324"}
{"zh": "贰\t生命运行的两个条件—弗五21，可十二30：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "II. Two Conditions for the Moving of Life—Eph. 5:21; Mark 12:30:", "norm_zh": "贰生命运行的两个条件弗五21可十二30李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Two Conditions for the Moving of LifeEph 521 Mark 1230"}
{"zh": "一\t一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉—弗五21，参彼前五5：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. The first condition is to obey the first sense of life—Eph. 5:21; cf. 1 Pet. 5:5:", "norm_zh": "一一个条件就是要顺服生命的头一个感觉弗五21参彼前五5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first condition is to obey the first sense of lifeEph 521 cf 1 Pet 55"}
{"zh": "1\t我们只要有一点感觉，我们就要顺服这一个感觉；你顺服这一点感觉，你的饥渴就增加一点；你再顺服，你就再加上感觉，你立刻看见，你的里面活了—腓二12~13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Whenever we have a little sense, we should obey this sense; when you obey this sense, your hunger and thirst increase slightly; when you obey again, you will have more sense, and you will immediately see that you are alive within.—Phil. 2:12-13.", "norm_zh": "1我们只要有一点感觉我们就要顺服这一个感觉你顺服这一点感觉你的饥渴就增加一点你再顺服你就再加上感觉你立刻看见你的里面活了腓二1213李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Whenever we have a little sense we should obey this sense when you obey this sense your hunger and thirst increase slightly when you obey again you will have more sense and you will immediately see that you are alive withinPhil 21213"}
{"zh": "2\t你还没有顺服你里面的头一个感觉之先，你不要管以后怎样；我们这样一步一步向前走的时候，有一件事是很宝贵的，就是你如果越过神去作什么，你立刻发觉有“圣灵禁止”，立刻觉得“耶稣的灵不许”—来十一8，徒十六7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. Before you obey the first sense within you, do not care about what comes after; as we go on step by step in this way, one thing is very precious—if you go beyond God to do anything, you will immediately sense \"the forbidding of the Holy Spirit\" and immediately feel that \"the Spirit of Jesus suffers you not.\"—Heb. 11:8; Acts 16:7.", "norm_zh": "2你还没有顺服你里面的头一个感觉之先你不要管以后怎样我们这样一步一步向前走的时候有一件事是很宝贵的就是你如果越过神去作什么你立刻发觉有圣灵禁止立刻觉得耶稣的灵不许来十一8徒十六7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Before you obey the first sense within you do not care about what comes after as we go on step by step in this way one thing is very preciousif you go beyond God to do anything you will immediately sense the forbidding of the Holy Spirit and immediately feel that the Spirit of Jesus suffers you notHeb 118 Acts 167"}
{"zh": "二\t还有一个条件，就是要爱神—可十二30，约十四21：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. Another condition is to love God—Mark 12:30; John 14:21:", "norm_zh": "二还有一个条件就是要爱神可十二30约十四21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Another condition is to love GodMark 1230 John 1421"}
{"zh": "1\t照许多圣徒的经历来说，神是先把祂的生命种在他们里面，然后用爱来打动他们的心情；信是把生命接受进来，爱是把生命流露出去—一12~13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. According to the experience of many saints, God first plants His life within them and then touches their emotion with love; faith is to receive life in, and love is to flow life out.—1:12-13.", "norm_zh": "1照许多圣徒的经历来说神是先把祂的生命种在他们里面然后用爱来打动他们的心情信是把生命接受进来爱是把生命流露出去一1213李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to the experience of many saints God first plants His life within them and then touches their emotion with love faith is to receive life in and love is to flow life out11213"}
{"zh": "2\t罗马十二章一至二节所说的，能给我们证明这件事；保罗先说，“弟兄们，我以神的诸慈悲劝你们”，这是先打动心情；然后“将身体献上当作活祭”，这是意志的行为；然后“悟性更新而变化，叫你们察验何为神的善良、纯全、可喜悦的旨意”，这是心思里明白神的旨意。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. Romans 12:1-2 can prove these things for us; Paul first said, \"I beg you therefore, brothers, through the compassions of God...\"; this is first touching the emotion; then \"Present your bodies a living sacrifice\"; this is an act of the will; then \"Be transformed by the renewing of the mind, that you may prove by testing what the will of God is, that which is good and well-pleasing and perfect\"; this is the knowing of God's will in the mind.", "norm_zh": "2罗马十二章一至二节所说的能给我们证明这件事保罗先说弟兄们我以神的诸慈悲劝你们这是先打动心情然后将身体献上当作活祭这是意志的行为然后悟性更新而变化叫你们察验何为神的善良纯全可喜悦的旨意这是心思里明白神的旨意李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Romans 1212 can prove these things for us Paul first said I beg you therefore brothers through the compassions of God this is first touching the emotion then Present your bodies a living sacrifice this is an act of the will then Be transformed by the renewing of the mind that you may prove by testing what the will of God is that which is good and wellpleasing and perfect this is the knowing of Gods will in the mind"}
{"zh": "3\t如果我们要生命向外发展，要生命长大，我们就得尽心、尽魂、尽悟性、尽力量爱主我们的神！—可十二30。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. If we want the life within us to spread to the outside, if we want the life to grow, we need to love the Lord our God with all our heart, with all our soul, with all our understanding, and with all our strength!—Mark 12:30.", "norm_zh": "3如果我们要生命向外发展要生命长大我们就得尽心尽魂尽悟性尽力量爱主我们的神可十二30李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 If we want the life within us to spread to the outside if we want the life to grow we need to love the Lord our God with all our heart with all our soul with all our understanding and with all our strengthMark 1230"}
{"zh": "叁\t生命运行的两个功用—参腓三10~11，林后四10~12：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "III. The Two Functions of the Moving of Life—cf. Phil. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 4:10-12:", "norm_zh": "叁生命运行的两个功用参腓三1011林后四1012李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The Two Functions of the Moving of Lifecf Phil 31011 2 Cor 41012"}
{"zh": "一\t一个就是死的功用，一个就是复活的功用；死的功用是去病的功用，复活的功用是得健康的功用—11~12节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. One is the function of death, and the other is the function of resurrection; the function of death is to remove the illness, while the function of resurrection is to give us health—vv. 11-12.", "norm_zh": "一一个就是死的功用一个就是复活的功用死的功用是去病的功用复活的功用是得健康的功用1112节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A One is the function of death and the other is the function of resurrection the function of death is to remove the illness while the function of resurrection is to give us healthvv 1112"}
{"zh": "二\t主的那个十字架，第一个成分是死，第二个成分是活；罗马六章告诉我们，这两个成分，是基督的生命顶有力量，顶有功用的成分—4~10节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. The first element of the Lord's cross is death, while the second element is life; Romans 6 tells us that these two elements are the most powerful and useful elements in the life of Christ—vv. 4-10.", "norm_zh": "二主的哪个十字架第一个成分是死第二个成分是活罗马六章告诉我们这两个成分是基督的生命顶有力量顶有功用的成分410节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The first element of the Lords cross is death while the second element is life Romans 6 tells us that these two elements are the most powerful and useful elements in the life of Christvv 410"}
{"zh": "三\t十字架是当你的心被神打动以后，你把自己献在神的手里，祂的生命在你的里面一直在那里运行，运行的时候，死的功用除去你里面不该有的；同时活的功用叫你活出神本性里的一切丰盛来，你的里面就有了亮光，有了喜乐，有了平安—6节，罗八13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. The cross is when your heart is touched by God and you offer yourself into God's hand, and His life is continually moving within you; when it is moving, the function of death eliminates the things in you which you should not have; at the same time, the function of life causes you to live out all the riches of the Godhead, so that you are full of light, full of joy, and full of peace—v. 6; Rom. 8:13.", "norm_zh": "三十字架是当你的心被神打动以后你把自己献在神的手里祂的生命在你的里面一直在哪里运行运行的时候死的功用除去你里面不该有的同时活的功用叫你活出神本性里的一切丰盛来你的里面就有了亮光有了喜乐有了平安6节罗八13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The cross is when your heart is touched by God and you offer yourself into Gods hand and His life is continually moving within you when it is moving the function of death eliminates the things in you which you should not have at the same time the function of life causes you to live out all the riches of the Godhead so that you are full of light full of joy and full of peacev 6 Rom 813"}
{"zh": "四\t但愿我们顺着神生命的运行往前行，让祂的生命在我们里面能通过各部分，能毫无阻碍地运行着，能一直有所除去，能一直有所增加—6节，约壹二27。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. May we go on according to the moving of God's life so that His life in us can reach all the different parts, moving without hindrance, always eliminating something and always adding something—v. 6; 1 John 2:27.", "norm_zh": "四但愿我们顺着神生命的运行往前行让祂的生命在我们里面能通过各部分能毫无阻碍地运行着能一直有所除去能一直有所增加6节约壹二27李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D May we go on according to the moving of Gods life so that His life in us can reach all the different parts moving without hindrance always eliminating something and always adding somethingv 6 1 John 227"}
{"zh": "肆\t生命运行的大能，是“不能毁坏之生命的大能”；这个生命运行的大能大力，是使主耶稣从死里复活的大能大力；也就是这个生命运行的大能大力，要充充足足成就一切超过我们所求所想的—弗一19~20，三20：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "IV. The operating power of life is the \"power of an indestructible life\"; this great power of the operation of life is the great power that raised the Lord Jesus from the dead; and it is this great power of the operation of life that will do superabundantly above all that we ask or think—Eph. 1:19-20; 3:20:", "norm_zh": "肆生命运行的大能是不能毁坏之生命的大能这个生命运行的大能大力是使主耶稣从死里复活的大能大力也就是这个生命运行的大能大力要充充足足成就一切超过我们所求所想的弗一1920三20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The operating power of life is the power of an indestructible life this great power of the operation of life is the great power that raised the Lord Jesus from the dead and it is this great power of the operation of life that will do superabundantly above all that we ask or thinkEph 11920 320"}
{"zh": "一\t能叫人的心倾向神；人的心在神的手中，好像陇沟的水，随意流转；只要我们肯把心放在神的手中，祂能转动我们—林后三18，箴二一1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. It can cause man's heart to incline toward God; man's heart is in the hand of Jehovah as the watercourses: He turneth it whithersoever He will; as long as we are willing to put our heart in God's hand He can turn us—2 Cor. 3:18; Prov. 21:1.", "norm_zh": "一能叫人的心倾向神人的心在神的手中好像陇沟的水随意流转只要我们肯把心放在神的手中祂能转动我们林后三18箴二一1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A It can cause mans heart to incline toward God mans heart is in the hand of Jehovah as the watercourses He turneth it whithersoever He will as long as we are willing to put our heart in Gods hand He can turn us2 Cor 318 Prov 211"}
{"zh": "二\t能叫人顺服神—腓二12~13，参林后七15，弗六5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B. It Enables Man to Obey God—Phil. 2:12-13; cf. 2 Cor. 7:15; Eph. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "二能叫人顺服神腓二1213参林后七15弗六5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B It Enables Man to Obey GodPhil 21213 cf 2 Cor 715 Eph 65"}
{"zh": "三\t能叫人行神所预备叫他们行的善—弗二10，多二14：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. It Enables Man to Do the Works Which God Has Prepared—Eph. 2:10; Titus 2:14:", "norm_zh": "三能叫人行神所预备叫他们行的善弗二10多二14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It Enables Man to Do the Works Which God Has PreparedEph 210 Titus 214"}
{"zh": "1\t这个工作，是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的，可以说是“神的杰作”—弗二10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus. We can say that it is God's masterpiece.—Eph. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1这个工作是神在基督耶稣里亲自作成的可以说是神的杰作弗二10李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This work was accomplished by God Himself in Christ Jesus We can say that it is Gods masterpieceEph 210"}
{"zh": "2\t祂救了我们，祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了，祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作，叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善—多二14。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. He has saved us and put His life in us! It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for us.—Titus 2:14.", "norm_zh": "2祂救了我们祂把祂的生命放在我们里面了祂是借着这生命的大能来成就这杰作叫我们能行祂所预备叫我们行的善多二14李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He has saved us and put His life in us It is through the power of this life that the masterpiece can be accomplished and that we can do the good works which He has prepared for usTitus 214"}
{"zh": "四\t能叫人尽心竭力作工；神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力，所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力；这个炸力，就是神的生命运行的大能；就是这个生命的大能，叫我们能殷勤地作工，能尽心竭力地作工—林前十五10，西一29。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. It Enables Man to Labor and Strive; what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power; hence, what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power; this exploding power is the power of the working of God's life; it is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work—1 Cor. 15:10; Col. 1:29.", "norm_zh": "四能叫人尽心竭力作工神在保罗里面所运用的是炸力所以保罗在外面行出来的也是炸力这个炸力就是神的生命运行的大能就是这个生命的大能叫我们能殷勤地作工能尽心竭力地作工林前十五10西一29李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D It Enables Man to Labor and Strive what God was operating inwardly was an exploding power hence what Paul was working outwardly was also an exploding power this exploding power is the power of the working of Gods life it is the power of this life which enables us to labor diligently and to strive in our work1 Cor 1510 Col 129"}
{"zh": "五\t能叫人有活的新鲜的事奉—林后三5~6，罗七6，二28~29：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "E. It Enables Man to Have a Living and Fresh Service—2 Cor. 3:5-6; Rom. 7:6; 2:28-29:", "norm_zh": "五能叫人有活的新鲜的事奉林后三56罗七6二2829李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E It Enables Man to Have a Living and Fresh Service2 Cor 356 Rom 76 22829"}
{"zh": "1\t旧约的事奉是字句的，新约的事奉是凭着灵的；旧约的事奉是陈旧的，新约的事奉是新鲜的；旧约的事奉是杀死人的，新约的事奉是叫人活的—林后三6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. Service in the old covenant was of the letter, but service in the new covenant is of the spirit. The service of the old covenant was old, but the service of the new covenant is fresh. The service of the old covenant killed, but the service of the new covenant gives life.—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "1旧约的事奉是字句的新约的事奉是凭着灵的旧约的事奉是陈旧的新约的事奉是新鲜的旧约的事奉是杀死人的新约的事奉是叫人活的林后三6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Service in the old covenant was of the letter but service in the new covenant is of the spirit The service of the old covenant was old but the service of the new covenant is fresh The service of the old covenant killed but the service of the new covenant gives life2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "2\t新约的事奉，乃是与基督发生关系，由里面运行出来的；新约的事奉是属灵的，是启示的，是新鲜的—罗七6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. The service of the new covenant is something which is the result of having a relationship with Christ and is worked out from within; the service of the new covenant is spiritual, of revelation, and in newness.—Rom. 7:6.", "norm_zh": "2新约的事奉乃是与基督发生关系由里面运行出来的新约的事奉是属灵的是启示的是新鲜的罗七6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The service of the new covenant is something which is the result of having a relationship with Christ and is worked out from within the service of the new covenant is spiritual of revelation and in newnessRom 76"}
{"zh": "3\t新约的事奉是需要“本于”神，“倚靠”神，也“归于”神的；保罗这福音的执事，是照着神恩典的恩赐；这恩赐“是照祂运行的大能赐给我的”—罗十一36。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. The service of the new covenant is of God, through God, and to God; Paul's becoming a minister of this gospel was according to the gift of God's grace; this gift \"was given to me according to the operation of His power\"—Rom. 11:36.", "norm_zh": "3新约的事奉是需要本于神倚靠神也归于神的保罗这福音的执事是照着神恩典的恩赐这恩赐是照祂运行的大能赐给我的罗十一36李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The service of the new covenant is of God through God and to God Pauls becoming a minister of this gospel was according to the gift of Gods grace this gift was given to me according to the operation of His powerRom 1136"}
{"zh": "伍\t生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通，生命就能发展到一个地步，使“基督成形”在我们里面；基督渐渐成形在我们里面，我们就渐渐“变化”，而变化的目标就是“象祂”—加四19，林后三18，约壹三2：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "V. As the law of life works in us in ever-expanding spheres, life can develop to such a degree that \"Christ be formed\" in us; as Christ is gradually formed in us, we are gradually \"transformed,\" and the goal of transformation is to be \"like Him\"—Gal. 4:19; 2 Cor. 3:18; 1 John 3:2:", "norm_zh": "伍生命的律在我们里面一圈一圈地运行得通生命就能发展到一个地步使基督成形在我们里面基督渐渐成形在我们里面我们就渐渐变化而变化的目标就是象祂加四19林后三18约壹三2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V As the law of life works in us in everexpanding spheres life can develop to such a degree that Christ be formed in us as Christ is gradually formed in us we are gradually transformed and the goal of transformation is to be like HimGal 419 2 Cor 318 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "一\t基督成形；基督的生命，本来是完全的；但是祂受了我们的限制，以致基督还未成形在我们里面，这是生命的发展受了阻碍；保罗为加拉太的信徒“再受生产之苦”，是直等到基督成形在他们里面—加四19，参约十四20。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "A. Christ being formed; the life of Christ is complete, but it is restricted by us; therefore, Christ is not yet fully formed in us; this means that the growth of life is hindered; Paul was in \"travail again\" for the Galatian believers until Christ was formed in them—Gal. 4:19; cf. John 14:20.", "norm_zh": "一基督成形基督的生命本来是完全的但是祂受了我们的限制以致基督还未成形在我们里面这是生命的发展受了阻碍保罗为加拉太的信徒再受生产之苦是直等到基督成形在他们里面加四19参约十四20李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Christ being formed the life of Christ is complete but it is restricted by us therefore Christ is not yet fully formed in us this means that the growth of life is hindered Paul was in travail again for the Galatian believers until Christ was formed in themGal 419 cf John 1420"}
{"zh": "二\t变化—罗十二1~2，弗四23，参来三7~8：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "B.\tTransformation:—Rom. 12:1-2; Eph. 4:23; cf. Heb. 3:7-8:", "norm_zh": "二变化罗十二12弗四23参来三78李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B TransformationRom 1212 Eph 423 cf Heb 378"}
{"zh": "1\t“变化”是必须先献上身体，其次是需要悟性的更新，这是罗马十二章一至二节所告诉我们的；圣灵的工作，总是从中心到圆周的；因为灵是特别与悟性发生关系的，所以，灵先得更新，然后更新到悟性，然后人在行为上就渐渐改变了。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. According to Romans 12:1-2 there are two prerequisites for \"transformation\": one is the presentation of our bodies; the other is the renewing of our mind; the work of the Holy Spirit is always from the center to the circumference; because the spirit is especially related to the mind, the spirit must be renewed first; then the mind must be renewed; finally, man's behavior will gradually be changed.", "norm_zh": "1变化是必须先献上身体其次是需要悟性的更新这是罗马十二章一至二节所告诉我们的圣灵的工作总是从中心到圆周的因为灵是特别与悟性发生关系的所以灵先得更新然后更新到悟性然后人在行为上就渐渐改变了李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to Romans 1212 there are two prerequisites for transformation one is the presentation of our bodies the other is the renewing of our mind the work of the Holy Spirit is always from the center to the circumference because the spirit is especially related to the mind the spirit must be renewed first then the mind must be renewed finally mans behavior will gradually be changed"}
{"zh": "2\t变化不象重生，重生是一下子成功的事；变化是一个程序，是渐渐地，天天地变化着。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. Transformation is not like regeneration; regeneration is something that happens once for all, but transformation is a daily gradual process.", "norm_zh": "2变化不象重生重生是一下子成功的事变化是一个程序是渐渐地天天地变化着李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Transformation is not like regeneration regeneration is something that happens once for all but transformation is a daily gradual process"}
{"zh": "3\t但愿主怜悯我们，叫我们的心能在祂面前软下来！同时，我们还得相信腓立比二章十三节的话说，“因为你们立志行事，都是神在你们里面运行，为要成就祂的美意”。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. May the Lord be merciful to us that our heart may be softened before Him. At the same time we need to believe Philippians 2:13: \"For it is God Who operates in you both the willing and the working for His good pleasure.\"", "norm_zh": "3但愿主怜悯我们叫我们的心能在祂面前软下来同时我们还得相信腓立比二章十三节的话说因为你们立志行事都是神在你们里面运行为要成就祂的美意李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 May the Lord be merciful to us that our heart may be softened before Him At the same time we need to believe Philippians 213 For it is God Who operates in you both the willing and the working for His good pleasure"}
{"zh": "三\t变化与相似—罗八29，腓三10、21：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "C. Transformation and Conformation—Rom. 8:29; Phil. 3:10, 21:", "norm_zh": "三变化与相似罗八29腓三1021李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Transformation and ConformationRom 829 Phil 310 21"}
{"zh": "1\t“变化”是说到过程，“相似”是说到完成；“变化”是主的生命在我们里面逐渐长大，使我们达到与主同样形质的地步；“相似”是变化到与主同形质了—罗八29。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. \"Transformation\" speaks of a process, \"conformation\" speaks of the completed work; \"transformation\" means that the Lord's life gradually grows up in us, that we are the same as the Lord; \"conformation\" means that we are transformed completely and are the same in form and nature as the Lord—Rom. 8:29.", "norm_zh": "1变化是说到过程相似是说到完成变化是主的生命在我们里面逐渐长大使我们达到与主同样形质的地步相似是变化到与主同形质了罗八29李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Transformation speaks of a process conformation speaks of the completed work transformation means that the Lords life gradually grows up in us that we are the same as the Lord conformation means that we are transformed completely and are the same in form and nature as the LordRom 829"}
{"zh": "2\t人如果要改变成功象神所定规的模型的形状，就必须从里面有本质上的改变，就是必须有神的生命进入他的灵里，让这生命渗透他整个人，直到全人由本质的改变而达到形状上完全的改变—林后三18。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. If a person wants to be transformed and be conformed to the image of the prototype that God has ordained, he must have a change of nature from within. God's life must enter into his spirit and permeate his whole being until he is completely changed in nature. Accordingly, there will be a complete conformation in image.—2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "2人如果要改变成功象神所定规的模型的形状就必须从里面有本质上的改变就是必须有神的生命进入他的灵里让这生命渗透他整个人直到全人由本质的改变而达到形状上完全的改变林后三18李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If a person wants to be transformed and be conformed to the image of the prototype that God has ordained he must have a change of nature from within Gods life must enter into his spirit and permeate his whole being until he is completely changed in nature Accordingly there will be a complete conformation in image2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "四\t变化的目标就是“象祂”，而完全地象祂是要等到“主显现”的时候，就是“身体得赎”的日子来到，才能完全地象祂—约壹三2，腓三21。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "D. The goal of transformation is to be \"like Him,\" and complete likeness to Him must wait until \"the Lord appears,\" which is the time of the \"redemption of our body\"; only then can we be wholly like Him—1 John 3:2; Phil. 3:21.", "norm_zh": "四变化的目标就是象祂而完全地象祂是要等到主显现的时候就是身体得赎的日子来到才能完全地象祂约壹三2腓三21李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The goal of transformation is to be like Him and complete likeness to Him must wait until the Lord appears which is the time of the redemption of our body only then can we be wholly like Him1 John 32 Phil 321"}
{"zh": "五\t纯洁自己—约壹三3，林后七1，雅四8，赛一16：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "E. Purifying Oneself—1 John 3:3; 2 Cor. 7:1; Jas. 4:8; Isa. 1:16:", "norm_zh": "五纯洁自己约壹三3林后七1雅四8赛一16李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Purifying Oneself1 John 33 2 Cor 71 Jas 48 Isa 116"}
{"zh": "1\t洁净是指干净而言，意思就是没有污秽；纯洁呢，不只没有污秽，并且没有杂质。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "1. To be clean means to be without defilement, but purifying means not only to be without defilement, but also to be without mixture.", "norm_zh": "1洁净是指干净而言意思就是没有污秽纯洁呢不只没有污秽并且没有杂质李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To be clean means to be without defilement but purifying means not only to be without defilement but also to be without mixture"}
{"zh": "2\t我们是要借着生命的光在里面的照亮，叫我们认识自己的真相，叫我们除去一切祂所不喜悦的—约一4，诗三六9。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "2. We are to do this through the shining of the light of life within us, so that we may know ourselves and eliminate all that displeases Him—John 1:4; Psa. 36:9.", "norm_zh": "2我们是要借着生命的光在里面的照亮叫我们认识自己的真相叫我们除去一切祂所不喜悦的约一4诗三六9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We are to do this through the shining of the light of life within us so that we may know ourselves and eliminate all that displeases HimJohn 14 Psa 369"}
{"zh": "3\t更深的纯洁，就是从神启示而来的，从基督复活的生命里出来的东西，也不可让它停留；因为一个生命的长大，是有新陈代谢的作用的；凡真出于复活的生命的，永远不会过去，永远是新的；但需要保守在圣灵的新鲜里—参弗四16，林后四7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第七章）", "en": "3. Deeper purification means that even that which comes from God's revelation, which issues from the resurrection life of Christ, should not be allowed to remain; because there is the process of metabolism in the growth of life; anything which truly comes from the resurrection life will never be lost; it will forever be fresh; however, it must be kept in the newness of the Holy Spirit—cf. Eph. 4:16; 2 Cor. 4:7.", "norm_zh": "3更深的纯洁就是从神启示而来的从基督复活的生命里出来的东西也不可让它停留因为一个生命的长大是有新陈代谢的作用的凡真出于复活的生命的永远不会过去永远是新的但需要保守在圣灵的新鲜里参弗四16林后四7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:24:47.947679+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Deeper purification means that even that which comes from Gods revelation which issues from the resurrection life of Christ should not be allowed to remain because there is the process of metabolism in the growth of life anything which truly comes from the resurrection life will never be lost it will forever be fresh however it must be kept in the newness of the Holy Spiritcf Eph 416 2 Cor 47"}
{"zh": "读经：来八11，约十七3，约壹二20、27，彼后一2、8，加一6，但十一32，约壹一5~7", "en": "Scripture Reading: Heb. 8:11; John 17:3; 1 John 2:20, 27; 2 Pet. 1:2, 8; Gal. 1:6; Dan. 11:32; 1 John 1:5-7", "norm_zh": "读经来八11约十七3约壹二2027彼后一28加一6但十一32约壹一57", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Heb 811 John 173 1 John 220 27 2 Pet 12 8 Gal 16 Dan 1132 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "壹\t神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点，就是认识神的自己；新约的特点，就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己—来八11，约十七3：", "en": "I. Through the Spirit, God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point, that is, to know Himself; the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life—Heb. 8:11; John 17:3:", "norm_zh": "壹神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点就是认识神的自己新约的特点就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己来八11约十七3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Through the Spirit God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point that is to know Himself the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of lifeHeb 811 John 173"}
{"zh": "一\t何西阿四章六节说，“我的民因无知识而灭亡”；这里所说的无知识，就是无认识神的知识；以色列人所以那样背道以至于灭亡，最大的原因，就是因为他们不认识神。", "en": "A. Hosea 4:6 says, \"My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge\"; the lack of knowledge in this verse is the lack of knowing God Himself; the children of Israel were disobedient to the extent that they were destroyed; this was mainly due to the fact that they did not know God.", "norm_zh": "一何西阿四章六节说我的民因无知识而灭亡这里所说的无知识就是无认识神的知识以色列人所以哪样背道以至于灭亡最大的原因就是因为他们不认识神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hosea 46 says My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge the lack of knowledge in this verse is the lack of knowing God Himself the children of Israel were disobedient to the extent that they were destroyed this was mainly due to the fact that they did not know God"}
{"zh": "二\t新约的特点，就是神在生命的律里启示我们，引导我们，叫我们能敬拜神，事奉神，与神有交通，而一步一步地长进，而越过越认识神—约四24，西一6。", "en": "B. The characteristic of the new covenant is that God gives us revelation and guidance in the law of life. He enables us to worship Him, to serve Him, and to have fellowship with Him, so that we may go on step by step and get to know Him more and more.—John 4:24; Col. 1:6.", "norm_zh": "二新约的特点就是神在生命的律里启示我们引导我们叫我们能敬拜神事奉神与神有交通而一步一步地长进而越过越认识神约四24西一6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The characteristic of the new covenant is that God gives us revelation and guidance in the law of life He enables us to worship Him to serve Him and to have fellowship with Him so that we may go on step by step and get to know Him more and moreJohn 424 Col 16"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩膏的教训—来八11，约壹二20、27：", "en": "II. The Teaching of the Anointing—Heb. 8:11; 1 John 2:20, 27:", "norm_zh": "贰恩膏的教训来八11约壹二2027", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The Teaching of the AnointingHeb 811 1 John 220 27"}
{"zh": "一\t希伯来八章十一节：“他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻，和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我”；这里所说的，与约壹二章二十七节所说“你们从主所受的恩膏，住在你们里面，并不用人教训你们；自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们”的话正相合。", "en": "A. Hebrews 8:11 says, \"They shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother, saying, Know the Lord, for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them\"; what is spoken of here corresponds exactly with the words of 1 John 2:27, which say, \"The anointing which you have received from Him abides in you, and you have no need that anyone teach you; but as His anointing teaches you concerning all things.\"", "norm_zh": "一希伯来八章十一节他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我这里所说的与约壹二章二十七节所说你们从主所受的恩膏住在你们里面并不用人教训你们自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们的话正相合", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hebrews 811 says They shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother saying Know the Lord for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them what is spoken of here corresponds exactly with the words of 1 John 227 which say The anointing which you have received from Him abides in you and you have no need that anyone teach you but as His anointing teaches you concerning all things"}
{"zh": "二\t灵有交通的功用；圣灵就是在人的灵里引导人敬拜神，引导人与神交通—约四24。", "en": "B. The spirit has the function of fellowship; the Holy Spirit guides man in his spirit to worship God and to have fellowship with God—John 4:24.", "norm_zh": "二灵有交通的功用圣灵就是在人的灵里引导人敬拜神引导人与神交通约四24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The spirit has the function of fellowship the Holy Spirit guides man in his spirit to worship God and to have fellowship with GodJohn 424"}
{"zh": "三\t灵有良心的功用；圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何；如果我们错了，圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们—徒二四16，林后一12。", "en": "C. The spirit has the function of conscience; the Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk; if we are wrong, the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscience—Acts 24:16; 2 Cor. 1:12.", "norm_zh": "三灵有良心的功用圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何如果我们错了圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们徒二四16林后一12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The spirit has the function of conscience the Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk if we are wrong the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscienceActs 2416 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "四\t灵有直觉的功用；人的身体有它的知觉，人的灵也有它的知觉；这灵的知觉，我们所以称它为“直觉”，是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的—来四12，创二7注5。", "en": "D. The spirit has the function of intuition; the human body has its sense, and the human spirit also has its sense; we call the sense of the spirit \"intuition\" because it comes directly from the spirit—Heb. 4:12; Gen. 2:7, note 5.", "norm_zh": "四灵有直觉的功用人的身体有它的知觉人的灵也有它的知觉这灵的知觉我们所以称它为直觉是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的来四12创二7注5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The spirit has the function of intuition the human body has its sense and the human spirit also has its sense we call the sense of the spirit intuition because it comes directly from the spiritHeb 412 Gen 27 note 5"}
{"zh": "五\t恩膏是在灵的直觉里—约壹二20、27：", "en": "E. The Anointing is in the Intuition of the Spirit—1 John 2:20, 27:", "norm_zh": "五恩膏是在灵的直觉里约壹二2027", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Anointing is in the Intuition of the Spirit1 John 220 27"}
{"zh": "1\t主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们，意思就是圣灵在灵的直觉里教训我们，叫我们在灵里有所觉得，象膏油涂在人的身体上叫人有所觉得一样—20节。", "en": "1. The Lord's anointing teaches us all things. This means that the Holy Spirit teaches us in the intuition of the spirit, causing us to have some feeling in our spirit, just as when ointment is applied to man's body, causing him to have some sensation.—v. 20.", "norm_zh": "1主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们意思就是圣灵在灵的直觉里教训我们叫我们在灵里有所觉得象膏油涂在人的身体上叫人有所觉得一样20节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lords anointing teaches us all things This means that the Holy Spirit teaches us in the intuition of the spirit causing us to have some feeling in our spirit just as when ointment is applied to mans body causing him to have some sensationv 20"}
{"zh": "2\t知道是灵知道，明白是心思明白；我们是借着灵的直觉来“知道”一件事，然后心思里得着亮光，“明白”直觉所知道的事；这一种的知道，是比心思中的明白更深的。", "en": "2. We know in our spirit, but we understand with our mind; we know a certain thing through the intuition of the spirit; then the mind is enlightened to understand what the intuition knows; this kind of knowing is deeper than the understanding in the mind.", "norm_zh": "2知道是灵知道明白是心思明白我们是借着灵的直觉来知道一件事然后心思里得着亮光明白直觉所知道的事这一种的知道是比心思中的明白更深的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We know in our spirit but we understand with our mind we know a certain thing through the intuition of the spirit then the mind is enlightened to understand what the intuition knows this kind of knowing is deeper than the understanding in the mind"}
{"zh": "六\t外面再复述—罗六3，林前三16，五6，六2~3、9、15、19，雅四4：", "en": "F. Outward Repetition—Rom. 6:3; 1 Cor. 3:16; 5:6; 6:2-3, 9, 15, 19; James 4:4:", "norm_zh": "六外面再复述罗六3林前三16五6六2391519雅四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Outward RepetitionRom 63 1 Cor 316 56 623 9 15 19 James 44"}
{"zh": "1\t我们如果读新约的书信，就要看见，有许多的教导是复述的，是因教会有了难处才说的。新约的书信常说到“岂不知”—罗六3，林前三16，五6，六2~3，雅四4。", "en": "1. When we read the Epistles in the New Testament, we realize that many teachings are repetitions. They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church. In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase, \"Know ye not?\"—Rom. 6:3; 1 Cor. 3:16; 5:6; 6:2-3; Jas. 4:4.", "norm_zh": "1我们如果读新约的书信就要看见有许多的教导是复述的是因教会有了难处才说的新约的书信常说到岂不知罗六3林前三16五6六23雅四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we read the Epistles in the New Testament we realize that many teachings are repetitions They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase Know ye notRom 63 1 Cor 316 56 623 Jas 44"}
{"zh": "2\t圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说，乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的—林前三16。", "en": "2. The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within, but simply repeat what the anointing has already said.—1 Cor. 3:16.", "norm_zh": "2圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的林前三16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within but simply repeat what the anointing has already said1 Cor 316"}
{"zh": "3\t里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的，但是外面的不能代替里面的；里面的说话，是活的，是生命的；这是新约的特点—林后三6。", "en": "3. The inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful, but the outward must not replace that which is inward; the inward speaking is living and of life; this is the characteristic of the new covenant.—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "3里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的但是外面的不能代替里面的里面的说话是活的是生命的这是新约的特点林后三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful but the outward must not replace that which is inward the inward speaking is living and of life this is the characteristic of the new covenant2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "七\t悟性必须更新—罗十二2，西一9：", "en": "G. The Mind Must be Renewed—Rom. 12:2; Col. 1:9:", "norm_zh": "七悟性必须更新罗十二2西一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G The Mind Must be RenewedRom 122 Col 19"}
{"zh": "1\t我们的悟性必须更新，然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的—二2。", "en": "1. Our mind must be renewed. Only then can we understand what the anointing is teaching us.—Col. 2:2.", "norm_zh": "1我们的悟性必须更新然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Our mind must be renewed Only then can we understand what the anointing is teaching usCol 22"}
{"zh": "2\t更新的工作是圣灵作的；罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见，是先“将身体献上当作活祭”，然后才是“悟性更新而变化”。", "en": "2. The work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit; Romans 12:1-2 makes it clear that first we must \"present our bodies as a living sacrifice,\" and then we may \"be transformed by the renewing of the mind.\"", "norm_zh": "2更新的工作是圣灵作的罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见是先将身体献上当作活祭然后才是悟性更新而变化", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit Romans 1212 makes it clear that first we must present our bodies as a living sacrifice and then we may be transformed by the renewing of the mind"}
{"zh": "3\t以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见，更新悟性的灵，是要在经历上先“脱去……从前行为上的旧人”；所以，悟性的更新是要借着十字架的。", "en": "3. Ephesians 4:22-23 shows us that for the renewing of the spirit of the mind we must, in our experience, first \"put off... the old man regarding our former manner of life\"; therefore, the renewing of the mind is something which is done through the cross.", "norm_zh": "3以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见更新悟性的灵是要在经历上先脱去从前行为上的旧人所以悟性的更新是要借着十字架的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Ephesians 42223 shows us that for the renewing of the spirit of the mind we must in our experience first put off the old man regarding our former manner of life therefore the renewing of the mind is something which is done through the cross"}
{"zh": "八\t用圣经校对里面的感觉—约壹四6，约十六13：", "en": "H. Checking Our Inner Feeling by the Scriptures—1 John 4:6; John 16:13:", "norm_zh": "八用圣经校对里面的感觉约壹四6约十六13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H Checking Our Inner Feeling by the Scriptures1 John 46 John 1613"}
{"zh": "1\t里面的感觉是活的；但是，外面的圣经是准的；光有圣经的话，只是准，只是稳，不活；光有里面的感觉，可能有时活而不准，活而不稳—诗一一九105。", "en": "1. The inner sense is living, but the Scriptures without are accurate; if we merely have the words of the Scripture, there is accuracy and security, but no life; on the other hand, having merely the inner sense may be living, but not accurate; or it may be living, but not secure.—Psa. 119:105.", "norm_zh": "1里面的感觉是活的但是外面的圣经是准的光有圣经的话只是准只是稳不活光有里面的感觉可能有时活而不准活而不稳诗一一九105", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The inner sense is living but the Scriptures without are accurate if we merely have the words of the Scripture there is accuracy and security but no life on the other hand having merely the inner sense may be living but not accurate or it may be living but not securePsa 119105"}
{"zh": "2\t以色列人出埃及的时候，在他们前面，有云柱，是白日的引导者；有火柱，是黑夜的引导者；如果没有黑夜，就用不着灯和光—出十三21~22。", "en": "2. When the Israelites came out of Egypt, they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night; without the night there is no need for the lamp and the light.—Exo. 13:21-22.", "norm_zh": "2以色列人出埃及的时候在他们前面有云柱是白日的引导者有火柱是黑夜的引导者如果没有黑夜就用不着灯和光出十三2122", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When the Israelites came out of Egypt they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night without the night there is no need for the lamp and the lightExo 132122"}
{"zh": "3\t生命加上真理，才是真的能力，才是稳的力量；我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上。", "en": "3. Life plus truth equals real power. Life and truth result in secure strength; we need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth.", "norm_zh": "3生命加上真理才是真的能力才是稳的力量我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Life plus truth equals real power Life and truth result in secure strength we need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth"}
{"zh": "叁\t两种的认识神—来八11，何六6，彼后一2、8：", "en": "III. Two Ways of Knowing God—Heb. 8:11; Hos. 6:6; 2 Pet. 1:2, 8:", "norm_zh": "叁两种的认识神来八11何六6彼后一28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Two Ways of Knowing GodHeb 811 Hos 66 2 Pet 12 8"}
{"zh": "一\t第一个认识的意思是指普通的认识，第二个认识的意思是指在直觉里的认识—2、8节：", "en": "A. The first knowing signifies the ordinary knowledge; the second knowing refers to knowledge in the intuition.—vv. 2, 8:", "norm_zh": "一第一个认识的意思是指普通的认识第二个认识的意思是指在直觉里的认识28节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first knowing signifies the ordinary knowledge the second knowing refers to knowledge in the intuitionvv 2 8"}
{"zh": "1\t普通的认识，是客观的认识，是外面的认识；在直觉里的认识，是主观的认识，是里面的认识—8节。", "en": "1. The ordinary knowledge is the objective, outward knowledge, while the intuitive knowledge is the subjective, inward knowledge.—v. 8.", "norm_zh": "1普通的认识是客观的认识是外面的认识在直觉里的认识是主观的认识是里面的认识8节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The ordinary knowledge is the objective outward knowledge while the intuitive knowledge is the subjective inward knowledgev 8"}
{"zh": "2\t属灵的东西是要尝的；感谢神，新约的特点，不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西，并且叫我们能尝到神—诗三四8，来六4~5。", "en": "2. The spiritual things need to be tasted; thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things; it even enables us to taste God Himself.—Psa. 34:8; Heb. 6:4-5.", "norm_zh": "2属灵的东西是要尝的感谢神新约的特点不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西并且叫我们能尝到神诗三四8来六45", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The spiritual things need to be tasted thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things it even enables us to taste God HimselfPsa 348 Heb 645"}
{"zh": "二\t三步地认识神；凭圣经看来，人对于神的认识是分作三步的—诗一〇三7，来八11：", "en": "B. Knowing God in Three Steps; according to the Scriptures, man's knowing God can be divided into three steps—Psa. 103:7, Heb. 8:11:", "norm_zh": "二三步地认识神凭圣经看来人对于神的认识是分作三步的诗一〇三7来八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Knowing God in Three Steps according to the Scriptures mans knowing God can be divided into three stepsPsa 1037 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "1\t第一步是认识神的作为，第二步是认识神的法则，第三步是认识神的自己；认识神的作为和法则，还不过是外面的认识；在里面认识神的性情，认识神的自己，才是更深的认识，这是最宝贵的—诗一〇三7，来八11。", "en": "1. The first step is to know God's doings; the second step is to know God's ways; and the third step is to know God Himself; to know God's doings and ways are only outward knowing, but the inward knowing of God's nature and knowing God Himself is the deeper knowing; this is the most precious—Psa. 103:7, Heb. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "1第一步是认识神的作为第二步是认识神的法则第三步是认识神的自己认识神的作为和法则还不过是外面的认识在里面认识神的性情认识神的自己才是更深的认识这是最宝贵的诗一〇三7来八11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The first step is to know Gods doings the second step is to know Gods ways and the third step is to know God Himself to know Gods doings and ways are only outward knowing but the inward knowing of Gods nature and knowing God Himself is the deeper knowing this is the most preciousPsa 1037 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "2\t认识神的作为；神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事—出七~十一、十四、十七。", "en": "2. To know God's doings; God's doings are the miracles and wonders which He performs—Exo. 7-11, 14, 17.", "norm_zh": "2认识神的作为神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事出七十一十四十七", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 To know Gods doings Gods doings are the miracles and wonders which He performsExo 711 14 17"}
{"zh": "3\t认识神的法则，也可以说就是认识神作事的原则；象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求，他就是站在神的公义一边来求神—创十八23~33，民十六46~48，撒上十五22。", "en": "3. To know God's ways means to know the principle by which God does things; for example, when Abraham prayed for Sodom, he prayed by standing on the side of God's righteousness.—Gen. 18:23-33; Num. 16:46-48; 1 Sam. 15:22.", "norm_zh": "3认识神的法则也可以说就是认识神作事的原则象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求他就是站在神的公义一边来求神创十八2333民十六4648撒上十五22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 To know Gods ways means to know the principle by which God does things for example when Abraham prayed for Sodom he prayed by standing on the side of Gods righteousnessGen 182333 Num 164648 1 Sam 1522"}
{"zh": "4\t认识神的性情，就是认识神的自己—诗二五8，八六5，太十17，徒三14，林后一3：", "en": "4. To know God's nature means to know God Himself.—Psa. 25:8; 86:5; Matt. 10:17; Acts 3:14; 2 Cor. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "4认识神的性情就是认识神的自己诗二五8八六5太十17徒三14林后一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 To know Gods nature means to know God HimselfPsa 258 865 Matt 1017 Acts 314 2 Cor 13"}
{"zh": "a\t祂的性情是良善正直的，是圣洁的；这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己—诗二五8。", "en": "a. His nature is goodness, uprightness and holiness; this nature will express God Himself through light.—Psa. 25:8.", "norm_zh": "a祂的性情是良善正直的是圣洁的这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己诗二五8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a His nature is goodness uprightness and holiness this nature will express God Himself through lightPsa 258"}
{"zh": "b\t多少时候，我们的一言一行，良心虽然不定罪，但是，里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服，好像不阿们似的，那就是神生命性情的感觉，那是超过良心的感觉的；我们如果有学习，如果肯顺服，我们就在这里摸着神的自己，就在这里认识神的自己。", "en": "b. Many times, both in our words and in our actions, although our conscience may not condemn us, there is still within a sense of discomfort, a sense which does not say \"amen.\" This is the sense of the nature of God's life, and it exceeds the feeling of the conscience; if we have learned and are willing to obey, it is at such times that we touch God Himself. On these occasions we will know God Himself.", "norm_zh": "b多少时候我们的一言一行良心虽然不定罪但是里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服好像不阿们似的哪就是神生命性情的感觉哪是超过良心的感觉的我们如果有学习如果肯顺服我们就在这里摸着神的自己就在这里认识神的自己", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Many times both in our words and in our actions although our conscience may not condemn us there is still within a sense of discomfort a sense which does not say amen This is the sense of the nature of Gods life and it exceeds the feeling of the conscience if we have learned and are willing to obey it is at such times that we touch God Himself On these occasions we will know God Himself"}
{"zh": "5\t在直觉里认识神—约十七3，林前二11~12：", "en": "5. Knowing God in Our Intuition—John 17:3; 1 Cor. 2:11-12:", "norm_zh": "5在直觉里认识神约十七3林前二1112", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Knowing God in Our IntuitionJohn 173 1 Cor 21112"}
{"zh": "a\t人有了永生，人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神，这永生有一种功能叫人认识神—约十七3。", "en": "a. When a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before. This eternal life has a function which enables man to know God.—John 17:3.", "norm_zh": "a人有了永生人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神这永生有一种功能叫人认识神约十七3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a When a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before This eternal life has a function which enables man to know GodJohn 173"}
{"zh": "b\t我们所领受的，并不是世上的灵，乃是从神来的灵，叫我们能知道神开恩赐给我们的事；这智慧和启示的灵，总是叫信徒能“真知道祂”；我们的直觉需要智慧和启示。", "en": "b. We have received not the spirit of the world but the Spirit which is from God, that we may know the things which have been graciously given to us by God; this spirit of wisdom and revelation always enables the believers to \"truly know Him\"; our intuition needs wisdom and revelation.", "norm_zh": "b我们所领受的并不是世上的灵乃是从神来的灵叫我们能知道神开恩赐给我们的事这智慧和启示的灵总是叫信徒能真知道祂我们的直觉需要智慧和启示", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We have received not the spirit of the world but the Spirit which is from God that we may know the things which have been graciously given to us by God this spirit of wisdom and revelation always enables the believers to truly know Him our intuition needs wisdom and revelation"}
{"zh": "c\t启示是在灵的直觉里，光照是照在魂的心思里；在直觉里是觉得的知道，在心思里是看见而明白；神就是这样赐给我们智慧和启示的灵，叫我们真知道祂，也真明白祂—弗一17~18。", "en": "c. Revelation is in the intuition of the spirit, while enlightenment is in the mind of the soul; in the intuition we know by sensing, while in the mind we understand by seeing; thus, God gives us the spirit of wisdom and revelation, that we may truly know Him and truly understand Him.—Eph. 1:17-18.", "norm_zh": "c启示是在灵的直觉里光照是照在魂的心思里在直觉里是觉得的知道在心思里是看见而明白神就是这样赐给我们智慧和启示的灵叫我们真知道祂也真明白祂弗一1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Revelation is in the intuition of the spirit while enlightenment is in the mind of the soul in the intuition we know by sensing while in the mind we understand by seeing thus God gives us the spirit of wisdom and revelation that we may truly know Him and truly understand HimEph 11718"}
{"zh": "d\t我们如果每件事都在灵里寻求神的旨意，结果就要叫我们“在真知道神里长大”，意思就是我们在认识神的知识上逐渐长大—西一9~10。", "en": "d. If in everything we seek God's will in our spirit, the result will be that we \"grow by the full knowledge of God,\" which means that we will grow gradually in our knowledge of God.—Col. 1:9-10.", "norm_zh": "d我们如果每件事都在灵里寻求神的旨意结果就要叫我们在真知道神里长大意思就是我们在认识神的知识上逐渐长大西一910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d If in everything we seek Gods will in our spirit the result will be that we grow by the full knowledge of God which means that we will grow gradually in our knowledge of GodCol 1910"}
{"zh": "6\t劳伦斯说，“如果你的心要认识神，爱是惟一的道路。人心的喜好与情绪是不同的，情绪合宜的出路就是爱，爱的目的物就是神。”", "en": "6. Brother Lawrence said that if our heart can in any measure come to know God, it can do so only through love. He also said that the pleasures of man's heart are different from his sentiments. The proper outlet of sentiments is love, and the object of love is God.", "norm_zh": "6劳伦斯说如果你的心要认识神爱是惟一的道路人心的喜好与情绪是不同的情绪合宜的出路就是爱爱的目的物就是神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Brother Lawrence said that if our heart can in any measure come to know God it can do so only through love He also said that the pleasures of mans heart are different from his sentiments The proper outlet of sentiments is love and the object of love is God"}
{"zh": "肆\t我们在里面认识神有多深，我们就在外面彰显神也有多深—加一16，徒二三3：", "en": "IV. The degree of our inward knowledge of God determines the extent of our outward expression of Him.—Gal. 1:16; Acts 23:3:", "norm_zh": "肆我们在里面认识神有多深我们就在外面彰显神也有多深加一16徒二三3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The degree of our inward knowledge of God determines the extent of our outward expression of HimGal 116 Acts 233"}
{"zh": "一\t彰显于胆量和鉴别；保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人，就是因他对于神的儿子的认识，是从启示来的；真认识神的人，就有胆量宣告：住在我们里面的，比那敌基督者的灵更大！—加一6，但十一32，林后五16，约壹四4。", "en": "A. Manifested in boldness and discernment; the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation; those who truly know God have the boldness to declare: He who dwells in us is greater than the spirit of the antichrist!—Gal. 1:6; Dan. 11:32; 2 Cor. 5:16; 1 John 4:4.", "norm_zh": "一彰显于胆量和鉴别保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人就是因他对于神的儿子的认识是从启示来的真认识神的人就有胆量宣告住在我们里面的比哪敌基督者的灵更大加一6但十一32林后五16约壹四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Manifested in boldness and discernment the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation those who truly know God have the boldness to declare He who dwells in us is greater than the spirit of the antichristGal 16 Dan 1132 2 Cor 516 1 John 44"}
{"zh": "二\t彰显于敬畏；敬畏神，是随时、随地、随事，都不敢随便，都有敬畏神的存心—徒十六：", "en": "B. Manifested in fear; to fear God means that anywhere, at any time, in any activity, we dare not be loose; within there is the attitude of fearing God—Acts 16:", "norm_zh": "二彰显于敬畏敬畏神是随时随地随事都不敢随便都有敬畏神的存心徒十六", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Manifested in fear to fear God means that anywhere at any time in any activity we dare not be loose within there is the attitude of fearing GodActs 16"}
{"zh": "1\t象保罗工作的脚步，一再受神的禁止，他敬畏神—徒二三3~5。", "en": "1. For example, the steps Paul took in his work were, many times, forbidden by God; he feared God.—Acts 23:3-5.", "norm_zh": "1象保罗工作的脚步一再受神的禁止他敬畏神徒二三35", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 For example the steps Paul took in his work were many times forbidden by God he feared GodActs 2335"}
{"zh": "2\t真认识神的人，是束上“心中的腰”的人，在他的言语、态度、动作上，是一点都不敢放松的—彼前一13。", "en": "2. Those who truly know God are those who gird up \"the loins of their mind\"; there is nothing loose in their words, attitude, and actions.—1 Pet. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "2真认识神的人是束上心中的腰的人在他的言语态度动作上是一点都不敢放松的彼前一13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Those who truly know God are those who gird up the loins of their mind there is nothing loose in their words attitude and actions1 Pet 113"}
{"zh": "三\t彰显于敬拜；以真诚拜神，就是承认神是神，也承认我们是谁；祂是无限的完全，配得着无限的敬重；真认识神的人，对神才有真诚的敬拜—创三二30，提前二5。", "en": "C. Manifested in worship; to worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is, and ourselves as what in very fact we are; He is infinitely perfect, worthy of infinite adoration; only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truth.—Gen. 32:30; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "三彰显于敬拜以真诚拜神就是承认神是神也承认我们是谁祂是无限的完全配得着无限的敬重真认识神的人对神才有真诚的敬拜创三二30提前二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Manifested in worship to worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is and ourselves as what in very fact we are He is infinitely perfect worthy of infinite adoration only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truthGen 3230 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "四\t彰显于敬虔；真认识神的人，就要把神彰显出来，这就是敬虔的生活；我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命，而要把这生命的本性表达出来，就需要在敬虔上操练自己—提前四7。", "en": "D. Manifested in godliness; those who truly know God will manifest God, and this is a godly life; within us we already have the godly life of God, but to manifest the nature of this life, we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness—1 Tim. 4:7", "norm_zh": "四彰显于敬虔真认识神的人就要把神彰显出来这就是敬虔的生活我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命而要把这生命的本性表达出来就需要在敬虔上操练自己提前四7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Manifested in godliness those who truly know God will manifest God and this is a godly life within us we already have the godly life of God but to manifest the nature of this life we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness1 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "伍\t操练敬虔，在基督耶稣里敬虔度日，是一种属灵的追求；但是，有的形态，可以说是病态，是有缺欠的，我们要分开来说一下—提后三12，提前四7：", "en": "V. Exercising unto godliness, or living godly in Christ Jesus, is a spiritual pursuit; but some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects, which we will speak of separately.—2 Tim. 3:12; 1 Tim. 4:7:", "norm_zh": "伍操练敬虔在基督耶稣里敬虔度日是一种属灵的追求但是有的形态可以说是病态是有缺欠的我们要分开来说一下提后三12提前四7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Exercising unto godliness or living godly in Christ Jesus is a spiritual pursuit but some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects which we will speak of separately2 Tim 312 1 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "一\t懒惰；有的基督徒生性懒惰，就是不肯劳动，不肯操作，就拿祷告，拿属灵的话作他懒惰的护符；我们要说，这是病态，这不是敬虔—罗十二11，徒二十19，林前十五58。", "en": "A. Laziness; some Christians, it seems, were born lazy; they neither like to labor nor to work, using prayer and spiritual words as a shelter for their laziness; we must say that this is a sick condition; this is not godliness.—Rom. 12:11; Acts 20:19; 1 Cor. 15:58.", "norm_zh": "一懒惰有的基督徒生性懒惰就是不肯劳动不肯操作就拿祷告拿属灵的话作他懒惰的护符我们要说这是病态这不是敬虔罗十二11徒二十19林前十五58", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Laziness some Christians it seems were born lazy they neither like to labor nor to work using prayer and spiritual words as a shelter for their laziness we must say that this is a sick condition this is not godlinessRom 1211 Acts 2019 1 Cor 1558"}
{"zh": "二\t拘谨；有的基督徒把拘谨当作敬虔，弄得他这个人象个假人；所以，我们操练敬虔的时候，应该是活泼新鲜的，是神从我们这个人的言语态度里出来—罗十二15，启三1。", "en": "B. Rigidness; some Christians think that godliness means to be rigid, which makes them appear artificial; therefore, whenever we exercise ourselves unto godliness, we should be living and fresh; it must be God who comes forth in our words and in our attitude.—Rom. 12:15; Rev. 3:1.", "norm_zh": "二拘谨有的基督徒把拘谨当作敬虔弄得他这个人象个假人所以我们操练敬虔的时候应该是活泼新鲜的是神从我们这个人的言语态度里出来罗十二15启三1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Rigidness some Christians think that godliness means to be rigid which makes them appear artificial therefore whenever we exercise ourselves unto godliness we should be living and fresh it must be God who comes forth in our words and in our attitudeRom 1215 Rev 31"}
{"zh": "三\t冷硬；但这并非说我们可以对人没有爱，没有礼貌；我们想想看，这一种的自以为敬虔，这一种的冷硬，能吸引人羡慕神么？—来十二14，罗十二10，彼前一22。", "en": "C. Cold and hard; this is not to say, however, that we may be negligent in love and in courtesy toward others; let us not think that such a self-assumed godliness and such a cold, hardhearted attitude will ever attract others to long after God.—Heb. 12:14; Rom. 12:10; 1 Pet. 1:22.", "norm_zh": "三冷硬但这并非说我们可以对人没有爱没有礼貌我们想想看这一种的自以为敬虔这一种的冷硬能吸引人羡慕神么来十二14罗十二10彼前一22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Cold and hard this is not to say however that we may be negligent in love and in courtesy toward others let us not think that such a selfassumed godliness and such a cold hardhearted attitude will ever attract others to long after GodHeb 1214 Rom 1210 1 Pet 122"}
{"zh": "四\t被动；有的基督徒，操练敬虔，特别是学盖恩夫人，学劳伦斯的“与神同在”，这是可敬可慕的；可是，有的基督徒学习他们而流于被动，却是可惜的—罗十二10、13。", "en": "D. Passive; some Christians who admire Madame Guyon and Brother Lawrence (who practiced the presence of God) seek to practice godliness as they did. This is something to be respected. It is even desirable. However, unfortunately, there are others who imitate them and become passive.—Rom. 12:10, 13.", "norm_zh": "四被动有的基督徒操练敬虔特别是学盖恩夫人学劳伦斯的与神同在这是可敬可慕的可是有的基督徒学习他们而流于被动却是可惜的罗十二1013", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Passive some Christians who admire Madame Guyon and Brother Lawrence who practiced the presence of God seek to practice godliness as they did This is something to be respected It is even desirable However unfortunately there are others who imitate them and become passiveRom 1210 13"}
{"zh": "陆\t需要神继续的赦免与洗净—弗一5~7，约壹一5~7：", "en": "VI. The Need for God's Continual Forgiveness and Cleansing—Eph. 1:5-7; 1 John 1:5-7:", "norm_zh": "陆需要神继续的赦免与洗净弗一57约壹一57", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The Need for Gods Continual Forgiveness and CleansingEph 157 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "一\t像以弗所第一章，先说神“预定我们，借着耶稣基督得儿子的名分”，因为这是目的；后说“我们借这爱子的血，得蒙救赎，过犯得以赦免”，因为这是手续；神要把生命给我们之前，神必须先赦免我们的罪，先洁净我们。", "en": "A. As in Ephesians 1, first it says that God 'predestinated us unto sonship through Jesus Christ to Himself,' because this is the purpose; later it says, 'we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of offenses,' because this is the procedure; before God can give us life, He must first forgive our sins and cleanse us.", "norm_zh": "一像以弗所第一章先说神预定我们借着耶稣基督得儿子的名分因为这是目的后说我们借这爱子的血得蒙救赎过犯得以赦免因为这是手续神要把生命给我们之前神必须先赦免我们的罪先洁净我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As in Ephesians 1 first it says that God predestinated us unto sonship through Jesus Christ to Himself because this is the purpose later it says we have redemption through His blood the forgiveness of offenses because this is the procedure before God can give us life He must first forgive our sins and cleanse us"}
{"zh": "二\t生命要求交通，也带进交通；交通就带进光；光要求血；这四件东西也是循环不已的；这个循环叫我们在生命里前进；一直这样一周一周的往前转，我们就要在神的生命里一直前进不已—诗三六9，约壹一5~7。", "en": "B. Life requires fellowship and also brings in fellowship; fellowship brings in light; and light requires the blood; these four things are also in a continuous cycle; this cycle causes us to move ahead in life; as we pass through one cycle after another, we will continue to move on in God's life.—Psa. 36:9; 1 John 1:5-7.", "norm_zh": "二生命要求交通也带进交通交通就带进光光要求血这四件东西也是循环不已的这个循环叫我们在生命里前进一直这样一周一周的往前转我们就要在神的生命里一直前进不已诗三六9约壹一57", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Life requires fellowship and also brings in fellowship fellowship brings in light and light requires the blood these four things are also in a continuous cycle this cycle causes us to move ahead in life as we pass through one cycle after another we will continue to move on in Gods lifePsa 369 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "三\t我们认识神是在生命的律里认识神，是在直觉里认识神，这是非常实际的；这是新约的高峰，这是新约的荣耀！—来八11，约十七3。", "en": "C. It is in the law of life and in the intuition that we know God, and this is very practical; this is the climax of the new covenant, this is the glory of the new covenant!—Heb. 8:11; John 17:3.", "norm_zh": "三我们认识神是在生命的律里认识神是在直觉里认识神这是非常实际的这是新约的高峰这是新约的荣耀来八11约十七3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It is in the law of life and in the intuition that we know God and this is very practical this is the climax of the new covenant this is the glory of the new covenantHeb 811 John 173"}
{"zh": "新约的特点，就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己", "en": "The characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life", "norm_zh": "新约的特点就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life"}
{"zh": "神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点，就是认识神的自己。神把律法放在我们心意里面，写在我们心上，不过是神的手续，为要达到更深的目的，就是认识神的自己。不错，与神交通是目的，但同时交通也是神的手续，为要达到更深的目的，就是认识神的自己。我们要知道，神的目的就是要将祂自己组织在我们里面，要与我们打成一片。新约的特点，就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己，来完成这一个目的。", "en": "Through the Spirit, God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point, that is, to know Himself. God imparts His laws into our mind and inscribes them upon our hearts. This is merely a procedure by which God achieves His deeper purpose, which is to know God Himself. While it is true that to have fellowship with God is purposeful in itself, at the same time the fellowship we have with God is His procedure to obtain a deeper purpose, which is to know God Himself. We know that God's purpose is to constitute us with Himself that He may become completely blended with us. Thus the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life, and in this way fulfill God's purpose.", "norm_zh": "神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点就是认识神的自己神把律法放在我们心意里面写在我们心上不过是神的手续为要达到更深的目的就是认识神的自己不错与神交通是目的但同时交通也是神的手续为要达到更深的目的就是认识神的自己我们要知道神的目的就是要将祂自己组织在我们里面要与我们打成一片新约的特点就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己来完成这一个目的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Through the Spirit God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point that is to know Himself God imparts His laws into our mind and inscribes them upon our hearts This is merely a procedure by which God achieves His deeper purpose which is to know God Himself While it is true that to have fellowship with God is purposeful in itself at the same time the fellowship we have with God is His procedure to obtain a deeper purpose which is to know God Himself We know that Gods purpose is to constitute us with Himself that He may become completely blended with us Thus the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life and in this way fulfill Gods purpose"}
{"zh": "我们再读希伯来八章十一节：“他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻，和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我。”（这里的“不用”在原文是一个很重的辞，可译作“决不用”）这里所说的，与约壹二章二十七节所说“你们从主所受的恩膏，住在你们里面，并不用人教训你们；自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们；这恩膏是真的，不是假的；你们要按这恩膏的教训，住在主里面”的话正相合。一个有神生命的人所以决不用人教导，是因有主的恩膏住在他里面，在凡事上教导他。这是非常实际的，神的话说“决不用”，就是“决不用”。主的恩膏是常住在我们里面。恩典越大，好像我们越有点信不来，所以神的话说了“这恩膏是真的”，接着又说“不是假的”。我们千万不要因自己属灵的情形不正常，就怀疑神的话。我们的神所说的，和祂所成就的是一致的。我们要相信神的话，我们也要感谢赞美祂。我们要说到恩膏的教训，还得先从人的灵的三种功用说起。人的灵的功用可以分为三大部分，就是直觉、交通和良心。现在我们把这三个功用分开来说一下。", "en": "Hebrews 8:11 reads: \"And they shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother, saying, Know the Lord, for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them.\" The phrase \"by no means\" is a very strong word in the original text. What is mentioned here coincides with 1 John 2:27: \"The anointing which ye received of him abideth in you, and ye need not that any one teach you; but as his anointing teaches you concerning all things, and is true, and is no lie, and even as it taught you, ye abide in him.\" The reason why one who has the life of God does not need the teaching of others at all is because he has the Lord's anointing abiding in him, and it teaches him concerning all things. This is a very practical matter. When God's Word says \"by no means,\" it means just that — \"by no means.\" The Lord's anointing always abides in us. It seems the greater the grace is, the more difficult it is for us to believe; therefore, the Word of God says that this anointing \"is true\" and then follows with the phrase \"and is no lie.\" We should not doubt God's Word simply because our spiritual condition is abnormal. What God says is consistent with what He accomplishes. We need to believe God's Word, and we also need to thank and praise Him. To speak of the teaching of the anointing, we must first begin with the three functions of the human spirit. The functions of the human spirit can be divided into three main parts: intuition, fellowship, and conscience. Let us consider them separately.", "norm_zh": "我们再读希伯来八章十一节他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我这里的不用在原文是一个很重的辞可译作决不用这里所说的与约壹二章二十七节所说你们从主所受的恩膏住在你们里面并不用人教训你们自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们这恩膏是真的不是假的你们要按这恩膏的教训住在主里面的话正相合一个有神生命的人所以决不用人教导是因有主的恩膏住在他里面在凡事上教导他这是非常实际的神的话说决不用就是决不用主的恩膏是常住在我们里面恩典越大好像我们越有点信不来所以神的话说了这恩膏是真的接着又说不是假的我们千万不要因自己属灵的情形不正常就怀疑神的话我们的神所说的和祂所成就的是一致的我们要相信神的话我们也要感谢赞美祂我们要说到恩膏的教训还得先从人的灵的三种功用说起人的灵的功用可以分为三大部分就是直觉交通和良心现在我们把这三个功用分开来说一下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hebrews 811 reads And they shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother saying Know the Lord for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them The phrase by no means is a very strong word in the original text What is mentioned here coincides with 1 John 227 The anointing which ye received of him abideth in you and ye need not that any one teach you but as his anointing teaches you concerning all things and is true and is no lie and even as it taught you ye abide in him The reason why one who has the life of God does not need the teaching of others at all is because he has the Lords anointing abiding in him and it teaches him concerning all things This is a very practical matter When Gods Word says by no means it means just that by no means The Lords anointing always abides in us It seems the greater the grace is the more difficult it is for us to believe therefore the Word of God says that this anointing is true and then follows with the phrase and is no lie We should not doubt Gods Word simply because our spiritual condition is abnormal What God says is consistent with what He accomplishes We need to believe Gods Word and we also need to thank and praise Him To speak of the teaching of the anointing we must first begin with the three functions of the human spirit The functions of the human spirit can be divided into three main parts intuition fellowship and conscience Let us consider them separately"}
{"zh": "主耶稣的血洗净了良心，叫良心清洁，感觉敏锐了。圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何（罗马八章十六节的“灵……同证”，九章一节的“有我良心被圣灵感动，给我作见证”，林前五章三节的“灵……判断”，和林后一章十二节的“良心见证”，都是说到灵有良心的功用）。如果我们错了，圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们。我们要注意，良心所定罪的，神必定定罪。断乎不会良心都定罪了，而神不定罪的。所以良心如果说这是错了，就必定是错了。既然错了，就必须悔改，必须认罪，必须靠主的宝血洗净。我们的良心清洁无亏，我们才能坦然无惧地事奉神。", "en": "The blood of the Lord Jesus purifies the conscience, making it clean and causing its sense to be keen. The Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk (Rom. 8:16 says, \"The Spirit Himself witnesses with our spirit\"; Rom. 9:1 says, \"My conscience bearing witness with me in the Holy Spirit\"; 1 Cor. 5:3 reveals that the spirit judges; and 2 Cor. 1:12 says that our conscience testifies. These all indicate that the spirit has the function of conscience). If we are wrong, the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscience. We must pay attention to the fact that what the conscience condemns, God will also condemn. It cannot be that the conscience has condemned something, yet God justifies it. If our conscience says we are wrong, then we must be wrong. Since we are wrong, we must repent, confess, and be cleansed by the Lord's precious blood. If our conscience is pure and void of offense, then we can serve God with boldness and without fear.", "norm_zh": "主耶稣的血洗净了良心叫良心清洁感觉敏锐了圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何罗马八章十六节的灵同证九章一节的有我良心被圣灵感动给我作见证林前五章三节的灵判断和林后一章十二节的良心见证都是说到灵有良心的功用如果我们错了圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们我们要注意良心所定罪的神必定定罪断乎不会良心都定罪了而神不定罪的所以良心如果说这是错了就必定是错了既然错了就必须悔改必须认罪必须靠主的宝血洗净我们的良心清洁无亏我们才能坦然无惧地事奉神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The blood of the Lord Jesus purifies the conscience making it clean and causing its sense to be keen The Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk Rom 816 says The Spirit Himself witnesses with our spirit Rom 91 says My conscience bearing witness with me in the Holy Spirit 1 Cor 53 reveals that the spirit judges and 2 Cor 112 says that our conscience testifies These all indicate that the spirit has the function of conscience If we are wrong the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscience We must pay attention to the fact that what the conscience condemns God will also condemn It cannot be that the conscience has condemned something yet God justifies it If our conscience says we are wrong then we must be wrong Since we are wrong we must repent confess and be cleansed by the Lords precious blood If our conscience is pure and void of offense then we can serve God with boldness and without fear"}
{"zh": "人的身体有它的知觉，人的灵也有它的知觉。人的灵的知觉，是在全人最里面的地方。它会表示“愿意”，它会“知道”人心里的议论，它会深深“叹息”，它会“悲叹”，它会“着急”，它会为道“迫切”，它会“火热”，它会“定意”，它会被“捆绑”，它会“快活”，它会“畅快欢喜”。这都是灵的直觉的功用。（可以说，灵所有的知觉，差不多有魂那么多。这个就叫我们需要学习如何分别什么是属灵的，什么是属魂的。我们必须经过十字架和圣灵深深的工作，我们才能知道什么是属灵的，什么是属魂的。）", "en": "Just as a man's body has its senses, a man's spirit also has its senses. The senses of a man's spirit are in the innermost part of the whole man. It can express \"willingness\"; it can \"know\" the reasonings in a man's heart; it can \"sigh deeply\"; it can \"groan\"; it can be \"provoked\"; it can be \"constrained\" by the word; it can be \"fervent\"; it can \"purpose\"; it can be \"bound\"; it can be \"refreshed\"; and it can \"rejoice.\" All these are the functions of the intuition of the spirit. (We may say that the spirit has almost as many senses as the soul. This makes it necessary for us to learn how to discern what is spiritual and what is soulish. We must go through a deep work of the cross and the Holy Spirit before we can know what is spiritual and what is soulish.)", "norm_zh": "人的身体有它的知觉人的灵也有它的知觉人的灵的知觉是在全人最里面的地方它会表示愿意它会知道人心里的议论它会深深叹息它会悲叹它会着急它会为道迫切它会火热它会定意它会被捆绑它会快活它会畅快欢喜这都是灵的直觉的功用可以说灵所有的知觉差不多有魂哪么多这个就叫我们需要学习如何分别什么是属灵的什么是属魂的我们必须经过十字架和圣灵深深的工作我们才能知道什么是属灵的什么是属魂的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Just as a mans body has its senses a mans spirit also has its senses The senses of a mans spirit are in the innermost part of the whole man It can express willingness it can know the reasonings in a mans heart it can sigh deeply it can groan it can be provoked it can be constrained by the word it can be fervent it can purpose it can be bound it can be refreshed and it can rejoice All these are the functions of the intuition of the spirit We may say that the spirit has almost as many senses as the soul This makes it necessary for us to learn how to discern what is spiritual and what is soulish We must go through a deep work of the cross and the Holy Spirit before we can know what is spiritual and what is soulish"}
{"zh": "这灵的知觉，我们所以称它为“直觉”，是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的。人平常的感觉，都是有因而起；或是因为人，或是因为物，或是因为事，就发出某种的感觉。如果是可喜的，就喜乐；如果是可忧的，就忧愁。这样的感觉是有因的，所以不得称为“直觉”。我们所说的直觉，是无所凭依而直接从人里面发出来的。", "en": "We call the sense of the spirit \"intuition\" because it comes directly from the spirit. Normally, a person's feeling is aroused by some external factors such as persons, things, or events. If it is something which should cause rejoicing, we rejoice; if it is something which should cause sorrow, we feel sorrowful. Such feelings have their causes; therefore, we do not call these intuition. The intuition we are speaking of is the sense which comes directly from inside man without any apparent cause.", "norm_zh": "这灵的知觉我们所以称它为直觉是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的人平常的感觉都是有因而起或是因为人或是因为物或是因为事就发出某种的感觉如果是可喜的就喜乐如果是可忧的就忧愁这样的感觉是有因的所以不得称为直觉我们所说的直觉是无所凭依而直接从人里面发出来的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We call the sense of the spirit intuition because it comes directly from the spirit Normally a persons feeling is aroused by some external factors such as persons things or events If it is something which should cause rejoicing we rejoice if it is something which should cause sorrow we feel sorrowful Such feelings have their causes therefore we do not call these intuition The intuition we are speaking of is the sense which comes directly from inside man without any apparent cause"}
{"zh": "主的恩膏住在我们里面，在凡事上教训我们，所以我们才决不用人来教导。这恩膏能在凡事上教训我们，就是直觉的功用。圣灵就是借着灵的直觉发表祂的意思。直觉具有一种本能，就是知道圣灵那样的感动到底有什么意思。所以，我们如果要遵行神的旨意，不必去问人，也不必问自己，只要随从直觉的指示就可以了。", "en": "The Lord's anointing abides in us and teaches us concerning all things, so we have absolutely no need for anyone to teach us. That this anointing can teach us in all things is the function of the intuition. The Holy Spirit expresses Himself through the intuition of the spirit. The intuition is an innate ability to know what the moving of the Holy Spirit means. For this reason, if we want to do God's will, it is not necessary to ask others, nor is it necessary to ask ourselves. We need only to follow the guidance of the intuition.", "norm_zh": "主的恩膏住在我们里面在凡事上教训我们所以我们才决不用人来教导这恩膏能在凡事上教训我们就是直觉的功用圣灵就是借着灵的直觉发表祂的意思直觉具有一种本能就是知道圣灵哪样的感动到底有什么意思所以我们如果要遵行神的旨意不必去问人也不必问自己只要随从直觉的指示就可以了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Lords anointing abides in us and teaches us concerning all things so we have absolutely no need for anyone to teach us That this anointing can teach us in all things is the function of the intuition The Holy Spirit expresses Himself through the intuition of the spirit The intuition is an innate ability to know what the moving of the Holy Spirit means For this reason if we want to do Gods will it is not necessary to ask others nor is it necessary to ask ourselves We need only to follow the guidance of the intuition"}
{"zh": "我们如果读新约的书信，就要看见，有许多的教导是复述的，是因教会有了难处才说的。新约的书信常说到“岂不知”。这“岂不知”就是说你已经听见过了，你里面已经知道了，但是你不理，你索性让它去，所以神就借着圣经说“岂不知”。圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说，乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的。是因我们属灵的情形不正常，我们有了病态，我们忽略了里面的教训，所以主就一再借着祂的仆人，用圣经的话，在外面来复述恩膏在人里面所已经说的。主的恩膏在我们里面已经教训过了，所以，我们总得从里面听起。我们要记得，里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的，但是外面的不能代替里面的。里面的说话，是活的，是生命的。这是新约的特点，是我们每一个属乎神的人都该重视的。", "en": "When we read the Epistles in the New Testament, we realize that many teachings are repetitions. They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church. In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase, \"Know ye not?\" \"Know ye not\" means that though we had heard something and we had known something inside, we had ignored it. We had simply let it go. Therefore, through the Scriptures God says, \"Know ye not?\" The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within, but simply repeat what the anointing has already said. Because we are spiritually sick and abnormal, and because we have neglected the inner teaching, the Lord through His servant uses the words of the Scriptures, repeating outwardly what the anointing has spoken inwardly. The Lord's anointing has taught us inwardly, so we must start listening from within. We must see that the inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful. The outward teaching, however, must not replace that which is inward. The inward speaking is living and of life. This is the characteristic of the new covenant. Everyone who belongs to God must pay attention to this matter.", "norm_zh": "我们如果读新约的书信就要看见有许多的教导是复述的是因教会有了难处才说的新约的书信常说到岂不知这岂不知就是说你已经听见过了你里面已经知道了但是你不理你索性让它去所以神就借着圣经说岂不知圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的是因我们属灵的情形不正常我们有了病态我们忽略了里面的教训所以主就一再借着祂的仆人用圣经的话在外面来复述恩膏在人里面所已经说的主的恩膏在我们里面已经教训过了所以我们总得从里面听起我们要记得里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的但是外面的不能代替里面的里面的说话是活的是生命的这是新约的特点是我们每一个属乎神的人都该重视的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "When we read the Epistles in the New Testament we realize that many teachings are repetitions They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase Know ye not Know ye not means that though we had heard something and we had known something inside we had ignored it We had simply let it go Therefore through the Scriptures God says Know ye not The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within but simply repeat what the anointing has already said Because we are spiritually sick and abnormal and because we have neglected the inner teaching the Lord through His servant uses the words of the Scriptures repeating outwardly what the anointing has spoken inwardly The Lords anointing has taught us inwardly so we must start listening from within We must see that the inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful The outward teaching however must not replace that which is inward The inward speaking is living and of life This is the characteristic of the new covenant Everyone who belongs to God must pay attention to this matter"}
{"zh": "主的恩膏是在我们灵的直觉里，在凡事上教训我们。但是，有的时候，我们的心思不能领会灵里的感觉。所以，我们的悟性必须更新，然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的。罗马十二章二节给我们看见，先是“悟性更新而变化”。然后才能“察验何为神的善良、纯全、可喜悦的旨意”。歌罗西一章九节给我们看见，先有“属灵的悟性”，然后才能“满心知道神的旨意”。所以，悟性的更新是必须的。", "en": "The Lord's anointing is in the intuition of our spirit and it teaches us concerning all things, but sometimes our mind cannot understand the sense in the spirit. For this reason our mind must be renewed. Only then can we understand what the anointing is teaching us. Romans 12:2 shows us that first the mind must be renewed and transformed; then we can prove what is God's good, well-pleasing, and perfect will. Colossians 1:9 shows us that we must first have the spiritual understanding; then we will be filled with the full knowledge of God's will. Therefore, the renewing of the mind is essential.", "norm_zh": "主的恩膏是在我们灵的直觉里在凡事上教训我们但是有的时候我们的心思不能领会灵里的感觉所以我们的悟性必须更新然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的罗马十二章二节给我们看见先是悟性更新而变化然后才能察验何为神的善良纯全可喜悦的旨意歌罗西一章九节给我们看见先有属灵的悟性然后才能满心知道神的旨意所以悟性的更新是必须的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Lords anointing is in the intuition of our spirit and it teaches us concerning all things but sometimes our mind cannot understand the sense in the spirit For this reason our mind must be renewed Only then can we understand what the anointing is teaching us Romans 122 shows us that first the mind must be renewed and transformed then we can prove what is Gods good wellpleasing and perfect will Colossians 19 shows us that we must first have the spiritual understanding then we will be filled with the full knowledge of Gods will Therefore the renewing of the mind is essential"}
{"zh": "那么，问题是悟性如何能更新呢？提多书三章五节说“圣灵的更新”，这给我们看见，更新的工作是圣灵作的。罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见，是先“将身体献上当作活祭”，然后才是“悟性更新而变化”。所以，悟性的更新是根据于奉献的。以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见，更新悟性的灵，是要在经历上先“脱去……从前行为上的旧人”。所以，悟性的更新是要借着十字架的。照原文，以弗所四章二十三节应该译作“又要在你们悟性的灵里被更新”。可见更新是从灵里更新起，然后更新到悟性。我们已经说过，圣灵的工作是从中心作到圆周的。人的心，人的深处，如果有了问题，如果不对付，那么悟性的更新是不可能的。所以圣灵先更新悟性的灵，然后更新到悟性。总括地说，是我们因受神的激励，将身体献上当作活祭之后，圣灵就借着十字架，叫我们在经历上用意志脱去从前行为上的旧人。借着祂的生命，更充满地进到我们里面，叫我们的灵得着更新，而达到悟性的更新。并且这一种更新是圣灵长久、继续不断的一个工作。说到这里，我们又要感谢赞美神说，什么都是祂恩典的工作，我们除了领受之外，除了感谢祂、赞美祂之外，真没有别的什么话好说了。", "en": "Then, the question is, how can the mind be renewed? Titus 3:5 speaks of the 'renewing of the Holy Spirit,' which shows us that the work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit. Romans 12:1-2 shows us that first we 'present our bodies as a living sacrifice,' and then we are 'transformed by the renewing of the mind.' Therefore, the renewing of the mind is based on consecration. Ephesians 4:22-23 shows us that to renew the spirit of the mind, we must first in our experience 'put off the old man concerning his former manner of life.' Therefore, the renewing of the mind is through the cross. According to the original text, Ephesians 4:23 should be translated, 'And that you be renewed in the spirit of your mind.' This shows that the renewing begins from the spirit and then reaches the mind. We have already said that the work of the Holy Spirit is from the center to the circumference. If there is a problem in a man's heart, in his depths, and it is not dealt with, the renewing of the mind is impossible. Therefore, the Holy Spirit first renews the spirit of the mind, and then He renews the mind. In summary, because of God's constraining we present our bodies as a living sacrifice. Following that, the Holy Spirit through the cross causes us in our experience to exercise our will to put off the old man concerning his former manner of life, so that through His life entering more fully into us, our spirit may be renewed and our mind may also be renewed. This renewing is a prolonged and continuous work of the Holy Spirit. When we come to this point, we need to thank and praise God that everything is the work of His grace. We have nothing else to do except to receive His grace and to praise and thank Him.", "norm_zh": "哪么问提是悟性如何能更新呢提多书三章五节说圣灵的更新这给我们看见更新的工作是圣灵作的罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见是先将身体献上当作活祭然后才是悟性更新而变化所以悟性的更新是根据于奉献的以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见更新悟性的灵是要在经历上先脱去从前行为上的旧人所以悟性的更新是要借着十字架的照原文以弗所四章二十三节应该译作又要在你们悟性的灵里被更新可见更新是从灵里更新起然后更新到悟性我们已经说过圣灵的工作是从中心作到圆周的人的心人的深处如果有了问提如果不对付哪么悟性的更新是不可能的所以圣灵先更新悟性的灵然后更新到悟性总括地说是我们因受神的激励将身体献上当作活祭之后圣灵就借着十字架叫我们在经历上用意志脱去从前行为上的旧人借着祂的生命更充满地进到我们里面叫我们的灵得着更新而达到悟性的更新并且这一种更新是圣灵长久继续不断的一个工作说到这里我们又要感谢赞美神说什么都是祂恩典的工作我们除了领受之外除了感谢祂赞美祂之外真没有别的什么话好说了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Then the question is how can the mind be renewed Titus 35 speaks of the renewing of the Holy Spirit which shows us that the work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit Romans 1212 shows us that first we present our bodies as a living sacrifice and then we are transformed by the renewing of the mind Therefore the renewing of the mind is based on consecration Ephesians 42223 shows us that to renew the spirit of the mind we must first in our experience put off the old man concerning his former manner of life Therefore the renewing of the mind is through the cross According to the original text Ephesians 423 should be translated And that you be renewed in the spirit of your mind This shows that the renewing begins from the spirit and then reaches the mind We have already said that the work of the Holy Spirit is from the center to the circumference If there is a problem in a mans heart in his depths and it is not dealt with the renewing of the mind is impossible Therefore the Holy Spirit first renews the spirit of the mind and then He renews the mind In summary because of Gods constraining we present our bodies as a living sacrifice Following that the Holy Spirit through the cross causes us in our experience to exercise our will to put off the old man concerning his former manner of life so that through His life entering more fully into us our spirit may be renewed and our mind may also be renewed This renewing is a prolonged and continuous work of the Holy Spirit When we come to this point we need to thank and praise God that everything is the work of His grace We have nothing else to do except to receive His grace and to praise and thank Him"}
{"zh": "我们再说，主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们，是千真万确的。生命的律在我们里面，是“决不用”人教导的；这不是过火的话，是圣经实在如此说的。但是，另一面，我们要防止受欺骗，防止走极端，我们还得用圣经的话来校对我们里面的感觉。", "en": "We say again that the Lord's anointing is in us, teaching us in all things. This is a true and definite matter. The law of life in us does not need any man's teaching at all. This is not an overstatement. The Scripture has indeed said so. But on the other hand we need to prevent ourselves from being deceived and from going to extremes. We need to check our inner feelings by the words in the Scriptures.", "norm_zh": "我们再说主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们是千真万确的生命的律在我们里面是决不用人教导的这不是过火的话是圣经实在如此说的但是另一面我们要防止受欺骗防止走极端我们还得用圣经的话来校对我们里面的感觉", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We say again that the Lords anointing is in us teaching us in all things This is a true and definite matter The law of life in us does not need any mans teaching at all This is not an overstatement The Scripture has indeed said so But on the other hand we need to prevent ourselves from being deceived and from going to extremes We need to check our inner feelings by the words in the Scriptures"}
{"zh": "圣灵是“真理的灵”（约十四），是引导我们“进入一切的真理”的（约十六）。所以，里面的感觉如果是出乎圣灵的，这个感觉就必定与圣经所说的相合。里面的感觉如果与圣经所说的不合，这个感觉就必定不准确。我们要知道，里面的感觉是活的；但是，外面的圣经是准的。光有圣经的话，只是准，只是稳，不活；光有里面的感觉，可能有时活而不准，活而不稳。这好比一列火车，车头里有汽力，车外面有路轨。如果光有外面的路轨，而车头里没有汽力，这一列车就开不动；如果光有车头的汽力，而外面没有路轨，这一列车开出去就要闯祸。圣经给我们看见，以色列人出埃及的时候，在他们前面，有云柱，是白日的引导者；有火柱，是黑夜的引导者。我们属灵的情形正常的时候，就象在青天白日之下行走。但是，我们属灵的情形并非一直如此。圣经也说神的话是脚前的灯，路上的光；如果没有黑夜，就用不着灯和光。所以，当我们里面明亮的时候，我们里面的感觉是清楚的，是有把握的；当我们里面黑暗的时候，我们里面的感觉是模糊的，是不稳的。那就必须用圣经的话，来把我们里面的感觉校对一下。生命加上真理，才是真的能力，才是稳的力量。我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上。我们每一个举动，我们每一个思想，我们每一个决断，都要用圣经的话把它校对一下，好让我们不偏不倚地向前走去。", "en": "The Holy Spirit is the Spirit of truth (John 14). He guides us into all the truth (John 16). Therefore, if our inner sense is of the Holy Spirit, this sense must correspond with what the Scriptures say. If the inner sense does not match the words of the Scriptures, this sense is inaccurate. We know that the inner sense is living, and we also know that the Scriptures without are accurate. If we merely have the words of the Scripture, there is accuracy and security, but no life. On the other hand, having merely the inner sense may be living, but not accurate; or it may be living, but not secure. Our experience needs to be like a train which has power inside the locomotive and rails outside. If there are only rails without but no power within the locomotive, the train will not move. On the other hand, if there is only power within the locomotive but no rails without, the train will run without control and have an accident. The Scriptures show us that when the Israelites came out of Egypt, they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night. When our spiritual condition is normal, we are walking in the bright daylight. But our spiritual condition is not always like this. The Scriptures also say that God's Word is a lamp unto our feet and a light unto our path. Without the night there is no need for the lamp and the light. When we are bright within, our inner sense is clear and sure. When we are dark within, our inner sense is blurry and uncertain. Then we must use the words of the Scriptures to verify our inner sense. Life plus truth equals real power. Life and truth result in secure strength. We need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth. Every action, every thought, and every decision needs to be checked against the words in the Scriptures, so that we may go on without being sidetracked.", "norm_zh": "圣灵是真理的灵约十四是引导我们进入一切的真理的约十六所以里面的感觉如果是出乎圣灵的这个感觉就必定与圣经所说的相合里面的感觉如果与圣经所说的不合这个感觉就必定不准确我们要知道里面的感觉是活的但是外面的圣经是准的光有圣经的话只是准只是稳不活光有里面的感觉可能有时活而不准活而不稳这好比一列火车车头里有汽力车外面有路轨如果光有外面的路轨而车头里没有汽力这一列车就开不动如果光有车头的汽力而外面没有路轨这一列车开出去就要闯祸圣经给我们看见以色列人出埃及的时候在他们前面有云柱是白日的引导者有火柱是黑夜的引导者我们属灵的情形正常的时候就象在青天白日之下行走但是我们属灵的情形并非一直如此圣经也说神的话是脚前的灯路上的光如果没有黑夜就用不着灯和光所以当我们里面明亮的时候我们里面的感觉是清楚的是有把握的当我们里面黑暗的时候我们里面的感觉是模糊的是不稳的哪就必须用圣经的话来把我们里面的感觉校对一下生命加上真理才是真的能力才是稳的力量我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上我们每一个举动我们每一个思想我们每一个决断都要用圣经的话把它校对一下好让我们不偏不倚地向前走去", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Holy Spirit is the Spirit of truth John 14 He guides us into all the truth John 16 Therefore if our inner sense is of the Holy Spirit this sense must correspond with what the Scriptures say If the inner sense does not match the words of the Scriptures this sense is inaccurate We know that the inner sense is living and we also know that the Scriptures without are accurate If we merely have the words of the Scripture there is accuracy and security but no life On the other hand having merely the inner sense may be living but not accurate or it may be living but not secure Our experience needs to be like a train which has power inside the locomotive and rails outside If there are only rails without but no power within the locomotive the train will not move On the other hand if there is only power within the locomotive but no rails without the train will run without control and have an accident The Scriptures show us that when the Israelites came out of Egypt they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night When our spiritual condition is normal we are walking in the bright daylight But our spiritual condition is not always like this The Scriptures also say that Gods Word is a lamp unto our feet and a light unto our path Without the night there is no need for the lamp and the light When we are bright within our inner sense is clear and sure When we are dark within our inner sense is blurry and uncertain Then we must use the words of the Scriptures to verify our inner sense Life plus truth equals real power Life and truth result in secure strength We need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth Every action every thought and every decision needs to be checked against the words in the Scriptures so that we may go on without being sidetracked"}
{"zh": "普通的认识，与在直觉里的认识的不同，我们可以用一个比喻来说明。比方说，有一种糖和有一种盐，从外面看去，它们都是很白很细，好像是一样的。等到吃到口里，你才知道，哪是糖，哪是盐；你才知道，糖是那么一种味道，盐是那么一种味道。你在外面用眼睛去认识糖与盐，不及你在里面用舌头去尝糖与盐。我们对于神的认识也是这样。外面所给你的认识，不过是普通的认识；你里面的认识，才是准确的认识。什么时候，神在我们里面，把祂自己给我们尝一下，就要叫我们有说不出的喜乐。诗篇三十四篇八节说，“你们要尝尝，便知道祂是美善。”希奇，神是我们可以尝的。还有，希伯来六章四至五节说，“论到那些已经蒙了光照，尝过天恩的滋味……尝过神善道的滋味……并来世权能的人。”这给我们看见，属灵的东西是要尝的。感谢神，新约的特点，不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西，并且叫我们能尝到神。哦，这是何等大的福气，又是何等大的荣耀，阿利路亚！", "en": "We can illustrate the difference between ordinary knowledge and intuitive knowledge in the following way. Suppose sugar and salt are put before us. They both appear about the same. Both are white and fine, but when they are put into our mouth we know which is sugar and which is salt. The sugar has the taste of sugar, and the salt has the taste of salt. Although we may use our eyes to know the sugar and the salt from without, it is not as accurate as tasting them with our tongue. Our knowledge of God is the same. The outward knowledge is only an ordinary knowledge, but the inward knowledge is the accurate knowledge. When God gives us a taste of Himself in us, we experience unspeakable joy. Psalm 34:8 says, \"Oh taste and see that Jehovah is good.\" It is wonderful! We can taste God! Hebrews 6:4-5 mentions: \"... those who were once enlightened, and who have tasted of the heavenly gift, and have become partakers of the Holy Spirit, and have tasted the good word of God, and the works of power of the coming age.\" This shows us that the spiritual things need to be tasted. Thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things; it even enables us to taste God Himself. What a great blessing and what a great glory this is!", "norm_zh": "普通的认识与在直觉里的认识的不同我们可以用一个比喻来说明比方说有一种糖和有一种盐从外面看去它们都是很白很细好像是一样的等到吃到口里你才知道哪是糖哪是盐你才知道糖是哪么一种味道盐是哪么一种味道你在外面用眼睛去认识糖与盐不及你在里面用舌头去尝糖与盐我们对于神的认识也是这样外面所给你的认识不过是普通的认识你里面的认识才是准确的认识什么时候神在我们里面把祂自己给我们尝一下就要叫我们有说不出的喜乐诗篇三十四篇八节说你们要尝尝便知道祂是美善希奇神是我们可以尝的还有希伯来六章四至五节说论到哪些已经蒙了光照尝过天恩的滋味尝过神善道的滋味并来世权能的人这给我们看见属灵的东西是要尝的感谢神新约的特点不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西并且叫我们能尝到神哦这是何等大的福气又是何等大的荣耀阿利路亚", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We can illustrate the difference between ordinary knowledge and intuitive knowledge in the following way Suppose sugar and salt are put before us They both appear about the same Both are white and fine but when they are put into our mouth we know which is sugar and which is salt The sugar has the taste of sugar and the salt has the taste of salt Although we may use our eyes to know the sugar and the salt from without it is not as accurate as tasting them with our tongue Our knowledge of God is the same The outward knowledge is only an ordinary knowledge but the inward knowledge is the accurate knowledge When God gives us a taste of Himself in us we experience unspeakable joy Psalm 348 says Oh taste and see that Jehovah is good It is wonderful We can taste God Hebrews 645 mentions those who were once enlightened and who have tasted of the heavenly gift and have become partakers of the Holy Spirit and have tasted the good word of God and the works of power of the coming age This shows us that the spiritual things need to be tasted Thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things it even enables us to taste God Himself What a great blessing and what a great glory this is"}
{"zh": "三步地认识神", "en": "Knowing God in Three Steps", "norm_zh": "三步地认识神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Knowing God in Three Steps"}
{"zh": "神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事。象以色列人在埃及看见神所降的十灾；象神用大东风使海水一夜退去，水便分开，海就成了干地；象以色列人在旷野得着击打磐石的活水，天天有从天上降下来的吗哪等等，都是神的作为。象福音书里所说的五饼二鱼给五千人吃饱了还有余；象瞎子看见，瘸子行走，长大麻风的得洁净，聋子听见，死人复活等等，也都是神的作为。象今天有的人的疾病得着神的医治，或者行路遇险得着神的保护，也都是神的作为。但是，我们如果晓得神的作为，是算不得认识神的；因为这种认识是浅的，是外面的。", "en": "God's doings are the miracles and wonders which He performs. The children of Israel in the land of Egypt, for instance, saw the ten plagues which God sent; another example is when God sent the great east wind, causing the water of the Red Sea to recede in one night, so that the water was divided and the sea became dry ground; two other examples are: the children of Israel obtaining living water from the smitten rock in the wilderness and the daily manna sent down from heaven, and so forth—all of these were God's doings. Likewise, the feeding of the five thousand with five loaves and two fishes; the blind receiving sight, the lame walking, the lepers being cleansed, the deaf hearing, and the dead being raised, and so forth—these were also God's doings. Today some people have been healed of their illness by God, or have been protected by God from danger on a journey; these are all God's doings. But if we only know God's doings, we cannot be considered as knowing God; this kind of knowing is shallow and outward.", "norm_zh": "神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事象以色列人在埃及看见神所降的十灾象神用大东风使海水一夜退去水便分开海就成了干地象以色列人在旷野得着击打磐石的活水天天有从天上降下来的吗哪等等都是神的作为象福音书里所说的五饼二鱼给五千人吃饱了还有余象瞎子看见瘸子行走长大麻风的得洁净聋子听见死人复活等等也都是神的作为象今天有的人的疾病得着神的医治或者行路遇险得着神的保护也都是神的作为但是我们如果晓得神的作为是算不得认识神的因为这种认识是浅的是外面的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods doings are the miracles and wonders which He performs The children of Israel in the land of Egypt for instance saw the ten plagues which God sent another example is when God sent the great east wind causing the water of the Red Sea to recede in one night so that the water was divided and the sea became dry ground two other examples are the children of Israel obtaining living water from the smitten rock in the wilderness and the daily manna sent down from heaven and so forthall of these were Gods doings Likewise the feeding of the five thousand with five loaves and two fishes the blind receiving sight the lame walking the lepers being cleansed the deaf hearing and the dead being raised and so forththese were also Gods doings Today some people have been healed of their illness by God or have been protected by God from danger on a journey these are all Gods doings But if we only know Gods doings we cannot be considered as knowing God this kind of knowing is shallow and outward"}
{"zh": "认识神的法则，也可以说就是认识神作事的原则。象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求，他就是站在神的公义一边来求神。他认识神是公义的神，神行事不能与祂的公义相背。这是亚伯拉罕认识神作事的法则。象那一次摩西看见耶和华的荣光显现的时候，就对亚伦说，“拿你的香炉，把坛上的火盛在其中，又加上香，快快带到会众那里，为他们赎罪，因为有忿怒从耶和华那里出来，瘟疫已经发作了。”这就是摩西知道神的法则，知道人这边怎样作，神就要怎样作。象撒母耳对扫罗说，“听命胜于献祭，顺从胜于公羊的脂油，”就是认识神的法则。象大卫“不肯用白得之物作燔祭”献给神，就是认识神的法则。", "en": "To know God's ways means to know the principle by which God does things. For example, when Abraham prayed for Sodom, he prayed by standing on the side of God's righteousness. He knew that because God is a righteous God, He could not act contrary to His righteousness. This means that Abraham knew God's way of doing things. Another example can be seen in the incident where Moses saw the glory of Jehovah manifested, and told Aaron, \"Take thy censer, and put fire therein from off the altar, and lay incense thereon, and carry it quickly unto the congregation, and make atonement for them: for there is wrath gone out from Jehovah; the plague is begun.\" This means that Moses knew God's ways. He knew that if man would act in a certain way, then God would respond in a certain way. Samuel told Saul: \"Behold, to obey is better than sacrifice, and to hearken than the fat of rams.\" This refers to knowing God's ways. A further example is when David refused to offer burnt offerings which cost him nothing to God. This also refers to knowing God's ways.", "norm_zh": "认识神的法则也可以说就是认识神作事的原则象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求他就是站在神的公义一边来求神他认识神是公义的神神行事不能与祂的公义相背这是亚伯拉罕认识神作事的法则象哪一次摩西看见耶和华的荣光显现的时候就对亚伦说拿你的香炉把坛上的火盛在其中又加上香快快带到会众哪里为他们赎罪因为有忿怒从耶和华哪里出来瘟疫已经发作了这就是摩西知道神的法则知道人这边怎样作神就要怎样作象撒母耳对扫罗说听命胜于献祭顺从胜于公羊的脂油就是认识神的法则象大卫不肯用白得之物作燔祭献给神就是认识神的法则", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To know Gods ways means to know the principle by which God does things For example when Abraham prayed for Sodom he prayed by standing on the side of Gods righteousness He knew that because God is a righteous God He could not act contrary to His righteousness This means that Abraham knew Gods way of doing things Another example can be seen in the incident where Moses saw the glory of Jehovah manifested and told Aaron Take thy censer and put fire therein from off the altar and lay incense thereon and carry it quickly unto the congregation and make atonement for them for there is wrath gone out from Jehovah the plague is begun This means that Moses knew Gods ways He knew that if man would act in a certain way then God would respond in a certain way Samuel told Saul Behold to obey is better than sacrifice and to hearken than the fat of rams This refers to knowing Gods ways A further example is when David refused to offer burnt offerings which cost him nothing to God This also refers to knowing Gods ways"}
{"zh": "什么叫作认识神的自己呢？认识神的性情，就是认识神的自己。我们已经说过，每一种生命，都有一种特性，象鱼有鱼的特性，鸟有鸟的特性。我们的神，祂的生命当然也有特性。这特性，就是祂的性情。祂的性情是良善正直的（诗二五，八六，太十九），是圣洁的。这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己。我们一得重生，就有了神的生命，也有了神的性情。我们在里面摸着祂的性情，我们就在里面摸着祂的自己。这就是认识神的自己。", "en": "What does it mean to know God Himself? To know God's nature means to know God Himself. It has been mentioned before that every kind of life has its own characteristics. Fish have the characteristics of fish and birds have the characteristics of birds. God's life also has its characteristic. This characteristic is His nature. His nature is goodness, uprightness (Psa. 25; 86; Matt. 19) and holiness. This nature will express God Himself through light. When we are born again we obtain God's life and receive God's nature. When we touch His nature in us, we also touch God Himself in us. This is knowing God Himself.", "norm_zh": "什么叫作认识神的自己呢认识神的性情就是认识神的自己我们已经说过每一种生命都有一种特性象鱼有鱼的特性鸟有鸟的特性我们的神祂的生命当然也有特性这特性就是祂的性情祂的性情是良善正直的诗二五八六太十九是圣洁的这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己我们一得重生就有了神的生命也有了神的性情我们在里面摸着祂的性情我们就在里面摸着祂的自己这就是认识神的自己", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "What does it mean to know God Himself To know Gods nature means to know God Himself It has been mentioned before that every kind of life has its own characteristics Fish have the characteristics of fish and birds have the characteristics of birds Gods life also has its characteristic This characteristic is His nature His nature is goodness uprightness Psa 25 86 Matt 19 and holiness This nature will express God Himself through light When we are born again we obtain Gods life and receive Gods nature When we touch His nature in us we also touch God Himself in us This is knowing God Himself"}
{"zh": "比方说，有一个罪，在良心的感觉里是非对付不可，对付了才平安。而在里面那一种神圣的知觉里，比良心的感觉更深的知觉里，对于这个罪，是恨恶，是厌烦；并不是怕这个罪的刑罚，乃是恨这个罪的本身。这种恨恶，就是从神圣洁的性情里发出来的。人摸着神的自己一下，人对于神的圣洁的认识，就不是言语可以形容的。有的时候，真要象约伯一样说，“我从前风闻有你，现在亲眼看见你。因此我厌恶自己，在尘土和炉灰中懊悔。”在明朗的阳光之下总显出微尘，照样，在神的圣洁之下总显出我们的污秽。怪不得彼得那天碰见主的自己一下，就俯伏在主膝前说，“主啊，离开我，我是个罪人。”（路五）多少时候，我们的一言一行，良心虽然不定罪，但是，里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服，好像不阿们似的，那就是神生命性情的感觉，那是超过良心的感觉的。我们如果有学习，如果肯顺服，我们就在这里摸着神的自己，就在这里认识神的自己。", "en": "For instance, if there is some sin, our conscience feels that it must be dealt with, and only if it is dealt with can there be peace. Yet, inside of us there is a holy sense, a sense which is even deeper than the conscience. Deep within there is a disgust and a hatred for the sin itself. This kind of hatred comes from God's holy nature. When man touches God Himself, his knowledge of God's holiness is beyond human description. Sometimes our sensation is the same as Job's: \"I had heard of thee by the hearing of the ear; but now mine eye seeth thee: wherefore I abhor myself and repent in dust and ashes.\" Just as fine dust is always revealed under clear sunlight, so our filthiness is always revealed under God's holiness. No wonder when Peter touched the Lord Himself that day, he fell down at the Lord's knees, saying, \"Depart from me, for I am a sinful man, Lord\" (Luke 5). Many times, although our conscience does not condemn our every word and action, yet deep within there is always a vague feeling of discomfort, as if there is no Amen; that is the feeling of God's life and nature, which is beyond the feeling of the conscience. If we have some learning and are willing to obey, we will touch God Himself and know God Himself here.", "norm_zh": "比方说有一个罪在良心的感觉里是非对付不可对付了才平安而在里面哪一种神圣的知觉里比良心的感觉更深的知觉里对于这个罪是恨恶是厌烦并不是怕这个罪的刑罚乃是恨这个罪的本身这种恨恶就是从神圣洁的性情里发出来的人摸着神的自己一下人对于神的圣洁的认识就不是言语可以形容的有的时候真要象约伯一样说我从前风闻有你现在亲眼看见你因此我厌恶自己在尘土和炉灰中懊悔在明朗的阳光之下总显出微尘照样在神的圣洁之下总显出我们的污秽怪不得彼得哪天碰见主的自己一下就俯伏在主膝前说主啊离开我我是个罪人路五多少时候我们的一言一行良心虽然不定罪但是里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服好像不阿们似的哪就是神生命性情的感觉哪是超过良心的感觉的我们如果有学习如果肯顺服我们就在这里摸着神的自己就在这里认识神的自己", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "For instance if there is some sin our conscience feels that it must be dealt with and only if it is dealt with can there be peace Yet inside of us there is a holy sense a sense which is even deeper than the conscience Deep within there is a disgust and a hatred for the sin itself This kind of hatred comes from Gods holy nature When man touches God Himself his knowledge of Gods holiness is beyond human description Sometimes our sensation is the same as Jobs I had heard of thee by the hearing of the ear but now mine eye seeth thee wherefore I abhor myself and repent in dust and ashes Just as fine dust is always revealed under clear sunlight so our filthiness is always revealed under Gods holiness No wonder when Peter touched the Lord Himself that day he fell down at the Lords knees saying Depart from me for I am a sinful man Lord Luke 5 Many times although our conscience does not condemn our every word and action yet deep within there is always a vague feeling of discomfort as if there is no Amen that is the feeling of Gods life and nature which is beyond the feeling of the conscience If we have some learning and are willing to obey we will touch God Himself and know God Himself here"}
{"zh": "认识神的自己，是新约最大的福气，最大的荣耀。认识神的自己，不是凭肉体可以认识的，乃是在直觉里认识的。怎样在直觉里认识神呢？我们要来看圣经如何说。", "en": "To know God Himself is the greatest blessing and the greatest glory in the new covenant. God Himself cannot be known by the flesh, but only by the intuition. Let us see what the Scriptures say about knowing God in our intuition.", "norm_zh": "认识神的自己是新约最大的福气最大的荣耀认识神的自己不是凭肉体可以认识的乃是在直觉里认识的怎样在直觉里认识神呢我们要来看圣经如何说", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To know God Himself is the greatest blessing and the greatest glory in the new covenant God Himself cannot be known by the flesh but only by the intuition Let us see what the Scriptures say about knowing God in our intuition"}
{"zh": "约翰十七章三节说，“认识你独一的真神，并且认识你所差来的耶稣基督，这就是永生。”这告诉我们，每一个有永生的人，就是认识神和主耶稣的人。换句话说，人有了永生，人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神，这永生有一种功能叫人认识神。我们认识神，是凭着里面的生命来认识一位我们已经认识的神。不是象雅典人那样凭着他们的理智，推想而敬拜一位“未识之神”（徒十七）。所以，若有人说他有永生，而他却从来不认识神，就这人所说的得了永生是可疑惑的，是字句的。说得重一点，这样的人必定没有永生。所以，我们如果要认识神，就必须先有“永生”。", "en": "John 17:3 says: \"And this is eternal life, that they may know You, the only true God, and Him Whom You have sent, Jesus Christ.\" This verse tells us that every one who has eternal life knows God and the Lord Jesus. In other words, when a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before. This eternal life has a function which enables man to know God. We know God, the One who has been made known to us, by the life within. We are not like the people of Athens who, by reasoning and inference, worshipped an unknown God (Acts 17). Therefore, if someone says that he has eternal life and yet has never known God, then his claim to have eternal life is doubtful — it is only in the letter. To put it even stronger, this kind of person does not have eternal life. If we want to know God we must first have \"eternal life\".", "norm_zh": "约翰十七章三节说认识你独一的真神并且认识你所差来的耶稣基督这就是永生这告诉我们每一个有永生的人就是认识神和主耶稣的人换句话说人有了永生人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神这永生有一种功能叫人认识神我们认识神是凭着里面的生命来认识一位我们已经认识的神不是象雅典人哪样凭着他们的理智推想而敬拜一位未识之神徒十七所以若有人说他有永生而他却从来不认识神就这人所说的得了永生是可疑惑的是字句的说得重一点这样的人必定没有永生所以我们如果要认识神就必须先有永生", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "John 173 says And this is eternal life that they may know You the only true God and Him Whom You have sent Jesus Christ This verse tells us that every one who has eternal life knows God and the Lord Jesus In other words when a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before This eternal life has a function which enables man to know God We know God the One who has been made known to us by the life within We are not like the people of Athens who by reasoning and inference worshipped an unknown God Acts 17 Therefore if someone says that he has eternal life and yet has never known God then his claim to have eternal life is doubtful it is only in the letter To put it even stronger this kind of person does not have eternal life If we want to know God we must first have eternal life"}
{"zh": "以弗所一章十七至十八节说，“求我们主耶稣基督的神，荣耀的父，将那智慧和启示的灵（编者：按原文无“赐人”二字）赏给你们，使你们真知道祂；并且照明你们心中的眼睛，使你们知道祂的……。”这告诉我们，使徒为着那些已经得着重生的在以弗所的信徒祈求，愿意他们得着那智慧和启示的灵，好叫他们在直觉里真知道神。无论这智慧和启示的灵，是信徒灵中所已有潜藏的功能，因着祷告得着神的启发也好，或者是因着祈求，而圣灵在信徒的灵中，叫他重新得着智慧和启示也好，这智慧和启示的灵，总是叫信徒能“真知道祂”。我们的直觉需要智慧和启示。", "en": "Ephesians 1:17-18 says, \"That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ, the Father of glory, may give to you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the full knowledge of Him, the eyes of your heart having been enlightened, that you may know...\" These verses tell us that the Apostle prayed for the believers at Ephesus who had been regenerated, that they might receive the spirit of wisdom and revelation, and that they might have the full knowledge of God in their intuition. Whether this spirit of wisdom and revelation is a function which has been hidden in the spirit of the believer and which will be uncovered by God through prayer, or whether it is through prayer that the Holy Spirit causes the believer to receive anew the wisdom and revelation in his spirit, is difficult to say; in any case, this spirit of wisdom and revelation enables the believer to have the full knowledge of God. Our intuition needs wisdom and revelation.", "norm_zh": "以弗所一章十七至十八节说求我们主耶稣基督的神荣耀的父将哪智慧和启示的灵编者按原文无赐人二字赏给你们使你们真知道祂并且照明你们心中的眼睛使你们知道祂的这告诉我们使徒为着哪些已经得着重生的在以弗所的信徒祈求愿意他们得着哪智慧和启示的灵好叫他们在直觉里真知道神无论这智慧和启示的灵是信徒灵中所已有潜藏的功能因着祷告得着神的启发也好或者是因着祈求而圣灵在信徒的灵中叫他重新得着智慧和启示也好这智慧和启示的灵总是叫信徒能真知道祂我们的直觉需要智慧和启示", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ephesians 11718 says That the God of our Lord Jesus Christ the Father of glory may give to you a spirit of wisdom and revelation in the full knowledge of Him the eyes of your heart having been enlightened that you may know These verses tell us that the Apostle prayed for the believers at Ephesus who had been regenerated that they might receive the spirit of wisdom and revelation and that they might have the full knowledge of God in their intuition Whether this spirit of wisdom and revelation is a function which has been hidden in the spirit of the believer and which will be uncovered by God through prayer or whether it is through prayer that the Holy Spirit causes the believer to receive anew the wisdom and revelation in his spirit is difficult to say in any case this spirit of wisdom and revelation enables the believer to have the full knowledge of God Our intuition needs wisdom and revelation"}
{"zh": "里面认识神有多深，外面彰显神也有多深", "en": "The depth to which we know God inwardly is the depth to which we express God outwardly.", "norm_zh": "里面认识神有多深外面彰显神也有多深", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The depth to which we know God inwardly is the depth to which we express God outwardly"}
{"zh": "使徒保罗说，“……那把我从母腹里分别出来，又施恩召我的神，既然乐意将祂儿子启示在我里面，叫我把祂传在外邦人中，我就没有与属血气的人商量，也没有上耶路撒冷去，见那些比我先作使徒的……”。这给我们看见，保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人，就是因他对于神的儿子的认识，是从启示来的。这一种的认识，不是凭肉体所能认识的。人认识在自己里面的基督，也就认识在别人里面的基督，这就是保罗所说的“我们从今以后，不凭着肉体认人了”的意思。凭着肉体认人的人，不容易从人得着生命的供应，很容易受人外貌弱点的影响。人外面的一点瑕疵，都是他批评论断的资料，都是滋长他骄傲的因素。所以，一个人认识不认识别人里面的基督，是要看他认识不认识在他里面的基督。保罗说，“……我们……虽然凭着肉体认过基督，如今却不再这样认祂了。”", "en": "The Apostle Paul said, \"But when it pleased God, Who set me apart from my mother's womb and called me through His grace, to reveal His Son in me, that I might preach Him among the nations, immediately I did not confer with flesh and blood, neither did I go up to Jerusalem to those who were apostles before me.\" This shows that the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation. This kind of knowledge cannot be obtained through the flesh. When a person knows Christ in himself, he will also know Christ in others. This is what Paul had in mind when he said, \"We henceforth know no man after the flesh.\" Those who know men according to the flesh find it rather difficult to receive the life supply from men. They are easily affected by the shortcomings in men's appearance. If there is any flaw in others, it becomes material for them to criticize and judge, and it also becomes the element for them to nourish their own pride. Therefore, whether a person can know Christ in others depends upon whether he knows Christ in himself. Paul continued, \"Even though we have known Christ after the flesh, yet now we know him so no more.\"", "norm_zh": "使徒保罗说哪把我从母腹里分别出来又施恩召我的神既然乐意将祂儿子启示在我里面叫我把祂传在外邦人中我就没有与属血气的人商量也没有上耶路撒冷去见哪些比我先作使徒的这给我们看见保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人就是因他对于神的儿子的认识是从启示来的这一种的认识不是凭肉体所能认识的人认识在自己里面的基督也就认识在别人里面的基督这就是保罗所说的我们从今以后不凭着肉体认人了的意思凭着肉体认人的人不容易从人得着生命的供应很容易受人外貌弱点的影响人外面的一点瑕疵都是他批评论断的资料都是滋长他骄傲的因素所以一个人认识不认识别人里面的基督是要看他认识不认识在他里面的基督保罗说我们虽然凭着肉体认过基督如今却不再这样认祂了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Apostle Paul said But when it pleased God Who set me apart from my mothers womb and called me through His grace to reveal His Son in me that I might preach Him among the nations immediately I did not confer with flesh and blood neither did I go up to Jerusalem to those who were apostles before me This shows that the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation This kind of knowledge cannot be obtained through the flesh When a person knows Christ in himself he will also know Christ in others This is what Paul had in mind when he said We henceforth know no man after the flesh Those who know men according to the flesh find it rather difficult to receive the life supply from men They are easily affected by the shortcomings in mens appearance If there is any flaw in others it becomes material for them to criticize and judge and it also becomes the element for them to nourish their own pride Therefore whether a person can know Christ in others depends upon whether he knows Christ in himself Paul continued Even though we have known Christ after the flesh yet now we know him so no more"}
{"zh": "使徒约翰说，“凡灵不认耶稣，就不是出于神；这是那敌基督者的灵；……小子们哪，你们是属神的，并且胜了他们；因为那在你们里面的，比那在世界上的更大。”真认识神的人，对于那些假使徒，假先知（太二四），假弟兄（林后十一，加二），假装的光明的天使，也能鉴别。什么时候，我们如果受欺骗，那必定因为我们不凭着里面的基督来认识人。真认识神的人，就有胆量宣告：住在我们里面的，比那敌基督者的灵更大！", "en": "The Apostle John said, \"And every spirit that confesseth not Jesus is not of God: and this is the spirit of the antichrist, ... Ye are of God, my little children, and have overcome them: because greater is he that is in you than he that is in the world.\" Those who truly know God can discern the false apostles, the false prophets (Matt. 24), the false brethren (2 Cor. 11; Gal. 2), and the false angels of light. Whenever we are deceived it must be because we do not know men by Christ, who is in us. Those who truly know God have the boldness to declare, \"Greater is He who dwells in us than the spirit of antichrist!\"", "norm_zh": "使徒约翰说凡灵不认耶稣就不是出于神这是哪敌基督者的灵小子们哪你们是属神的并且胜了他们因为哪在你们里面的比哪在世界上的更大真认识神的人对于哪些假使徒假先知太二四假弟兄林后十一加二假装的光明的天使也能鉴别什么时候我们如果受欺骗哪必定因为我们不凭着里面的基督来认识人真认识神的人就有胆量宣告住在我们里面的比哪敌基督者的灵更大", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Apostle John said And every spirit that confesseth not Jesus is not of God and this is the spirit of the antichrist Ye are of God my little children and have overcome them because greater is he that is in you than he that is in the world Those who truly know God can discern the false apostles the false prophets Matt 24 the false brethren 2 Cor 11 Gal 2 and the false angels of light Whenever we are deceived it must be because we do not know men by Christ who is in us Those who truly know God have the boldness to declare Greater is He who dwells in us than the spirit of antichrist"}
{"zh": "真认识神的人，不只有胆量作见证，不只不怕那敌基督者的灵，并且特别敬畏神。象保罗工作的脚步，一再受神的禁止，他敬畏神。象他那一次责骂了大祭司，人一显出，他就软下来，他敬畏神。真认识神的人，是束上“心中的腰”的人，在他的言语、态度、动作上，是一点都不敢放松的。他这样的约束自己，并非用自己的力气在那里约束自己，乃是受他里面生命的勒住或者说禁止。他不只在人面前如此，就当他一人独处的时候也是如此。他的言语行动，一与里面的生命不合，就受里面的禁止；他一摸到神，就立刻软下来。凡是外面松懈的人，必定是里面先松懈了。凡是放松，没有约束；凡是本来如此，得救后还是如此；凡是随便说话，随便行事的基督徒，都是不敬畏神的人。凡是在人前是一套，在人后又是一套；凡是在讲台上是一套，在讲台下又是一套的人，都是不敬畏神的人。敬畏神，是随时、随地、随事，都不敢随便，都有敬畏神的存心。所以，如果有人自称是属乎神的人，而他的言语行动，一点不敬畏神，我们就替这样的人担心害怕。因为今天在他的感觉里不认识神，但总有一天，他要见神的面。这样的弟兄姊妹们哪，请听主的话：“小子们哪，你们要住在主里面；这样，祂若显现，我们就可以坦然无惧；当祂来的时候，在祂面前也不至于惭愧。”（约壹二）哦，弟兄姊妹们，我们一想到总有一天要见主的面，我们里面坦然不坦然呢？将来在主面前敞开的时候，有没有什么叫我们惭愧的呢？", "en": "One who truly knows God, not only has the boldness to testify, and is not afraid of the spirit of antichrist, but he especially fears God. For example, the steps Paul took in his work were, many times, forbidden by God. He feared God. Another example of his fear of God is when, being reminded that he rebuked the high priest, he became softened. This means that he feared God. Those who truly know God gird up the loins of their mind. There is nothing loose in their words, attitude, and actions. The reason they are so girded up is not because they have some strength of their own, but because the life in them is restraining them and forbidding them. They are such not only before others, but even when they are by themselves they are girded up. Whenever their words and actions do not match the life in them, those words and actions are forbidden. Also, whenever they touch God they become softened. Those who are loose outwardly must first be loose inwardly. Those who are loose and without restraint, who remain the same after being saved, who are careless in what they say and in what they do, are Christians who do not fear God. Those who act one way in front of people and another way behind their backs, who are one way in the pulpit and another way in daily living, are those who do not fear God. To fear God means that anywhere, at any time, in any activity, we dare not be loose. Within there is the attitude of fearing God. Therefore, if someone claims to belong to God, and yet his words and his actions do not indicate that he fears God in the least, we will have a genuine concern for such a person. We fear for him because the day will come when he will see God's face, though today he does not know God in his consciousness. Brothers and sisters, if this is your case, then you need to hear God's word: \"And now, my little children, abide in him; that, if he shall be manifested, we may have boldness, and not be ashamed before him at his coming\" (1 John 2). Whenever we think of the fact that one day we shall see the Lord's face, do we feel confident within? In the future, when everything shall be opened before the Lord, will there be anything which will cause us to be ashamed?", "norm_zh": "真认识神的人不只有胆量作见证不只不怕哪敌基督者的灵并且特别敬畏神象保罗工作的脚步一再受神的禁止他敬畏神象他哪一次责骂了大祭司人一显出他就软下来他敬畏神真认识神的人是束上心中的腰的人在他的言语态度动作上是一点都不敢放松的他这样的约束自己并非用自己的力气在哪里约束自己乃是受他里面生命的勒住或者说禁止他不只在人面前如此就当他一人独处的时候也是如此他的言语行动一与里面的生命不合就受里面的禁止他一摸到神就立刻软下来凡是外面松懈的人必定是里面先松懈了凡是放松没有约束凡是本来如此得救后还是如此凡是随便说话随便行事的基督徒都是不敬畏神的人凡是在人前是一套在人后又是一套凡是在讲台上是一套在讲台下又是一套的人都是不敬畏神的人敬畏神是随时随地随事都不敢随便都有敬畏神的存心所以如果有人自称是属乎神的人而他的言语行动一点不敬畏神我们就替这样的人担心害怕因为今天在他的感觉里不认识神但总有一天他要见神的面这样的弟兄姊妹们哪请听主的话小子们哪你们要住在主里面这样祂若显现我们就可以坦然无惧当祂来的时候在祂面前也不至于惭愧约壹二哦弟兄姊妹们我们一想到总有一天要见主的面我们里面坦然不坦然呢将来在主面前敞开的时候有没有什么叫我们惭愧的呢", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "One who truly knows God not only has the boldness to testify and is not afraid of the spirit of antichrist but he especially fears God For example the steps Paul took in his work were many times forbidden by God He feared God Another example of his fear of God is when being reminded that he rebuked the high priest he became softened This means that he feared God Those who truly know God gird up the loins of their mind There is nothing loose in their words attitude and actions The reason they are so girded up is not because they have some strength of their own but because the life in them is restraining them and forbidding them They are such not only before others but even when they are by themselves they are girded up Whenever their words and actions do not match the life in them those words and actions are forbidden Also whenever they touch God they become softened Those who are loose outwardly must first be loose inwardly Those who are loose and without restraint who remain the same after being saved who are careless in what they say and in what they do are Christians who do not fear God Those who act one way in front of people and another way behind their backs who are one way in the pulpit and another way in daily living are those who do not fear God To fear God means that anywhere at any time in any activity we dare not be loose Within there is the attitude of fearing God Therefore if someone claims to belong to God and yet his words and his actions do not indicate that he fears God in the least we will have a genuine concern for such a person We fear for him because the day will come when he will see Gods face though today he does not know God in his consciousness Brothers and sisters if this is your case then you need to hear Gods word And now my little children abide in him that if he shall be manifested we may have boldness and not be ashamed before him at his coming 1 John 2 Whenever we think of the fact that one day we shall see the Lords face do we feel confident within In the future when everything shall be opened before the Lord will there be anything which will cause us to be ashamed"}
{"zh": "真认识神的人，没有不敬拜神的。劳伦斯说，“以真诚拜神，就是承认神是神，也承认我们是谁。以真诚拜神，就是以至诚的心承认神实际是谁，这就是说，祂是无限的完全，配得着无限的敬重，绝对远离罪恶的一位神。而人是极微小的，并且没有将神该得的敬拜献上给神。”这给我们看见，真认识神的人，对神才有真诚的敬拜。就如雅各吧，他在伯特利对于神的认识，固然也叫他惧怕，但还不过是外面的认识，所以他的许愿，都是讲条件，都是讲个人的利益，等到“毗努伊勒”，雅各所认识的就大不同了。", "en": "There is no one who truly knows God, yet does not worship God. Brother Lawrence said, \"To worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is, and ourselves as what in very fact we are. To worship Him in truth is to acknowledge with heartfelt sincerity what God in truth is — that is to say, infinitely perfect, worthy of infinite adoration, infinitely removed from sin, and so of all the Divine attributes. That man is little guided by reason, who does not employ all his powers to render to this great God the worship that is His due.\" This indicates that only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truth. For example, though Jacob's knowledge of God at Bethel caused him to fear God, it was only an outward kind of knowledge. For this reason his vow was conditional and was concerned with his own interests. But when he came to Peniel, Jacob's knowledge of God was much different.", "norm_zh": "真认识神的人没有不敬拜神的劳伦斯说以真诚拜神就是承认神是神也承认我们是谁以真诚拜神就是以至诚的心承认神实际是谁这就是说祂是无限的完全配得着无限的敬重绝对远离罪恶的一位神而人是极微小的并且没有将神该得的敬拜献上给神这给我们看见真认识神的人对神才有真诚的敬拜就如雅各吧他在伯特利对于神的认识固然也叫他惧怕但还不过是外面的认识所以他的许愿都是讲条件都是讲个人的利益等到毗努伊勒雅各所认识的就大不同了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "There is no one who truly knows God yet does not worship God Brother Lawrence said To worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is and ourselves as what in very fact we are To worship Him in truth is to acknowledge with heartfelt sincerity what God in truth is that is to say infinitely perfect worthy of infinite adoration infinitely removed from sin and so of all the Divine attributes That man is little guided by reason who does not employ all his powers to render to this great God the worship that is His due This indicates that only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truth For example though Jacobs knowledge of God at Bethel caused him to fear God it was only an outward kind of knowledge For this reason his vow was conditional and was concerned with his own interests But when he came to Peniel Jacobs knowledge of God was much different"}
{"zh": "我们要知道，敬虔并不是一种苦修，敬虔乃是一种生命的知觉，乃是神生命的一种本性。所以使徒保罗说到属乎主的人要追求公义、敬虔、信心、爱心、忍耐、温柔（提前六）的时候，是把敬虔列在这一类。当我们得重生的那一天，神的神能已将一切关乎生命和敬虔的事赐给我们了（彼后一），而且这敬虔有今生和来生生命的应许（提前四）。我们知道，“主所应许我们的就是永生”。这永生在我们信神儿子的时候就已经有了（约壹五）。但是，今天把这永生活出来，把这永生彰显在我们的思想上，彰显在我们的言语上，彰显在我们的态度上，彰显在我们的行动上，还是在乎这生命在我们里面运行的大能。所以使徒保罗说，“……我们的指望在乎永生的神；祂是万人的救主，更是信徒的救主。”", "en": "We must know that godliness is not a kind of asceticism; godliness is a consciousness of life, a nature of God's life. Therefore, when the Apostle Paul spoke of those who belong to the Lord pursuing righteousness, godliness, faith, love, endurance, and meekness (1 Tim. 6), he put godliness in this category. When we were regenerated, God, according to His divine power, gave to us all things that pertain to life and godliness (2 Pet. 1). Also, this godliness has the promise of the present life and of the life which is coming (1 Tim. 4). We know that \"the promise which He Himself promised us is the eternal life.\" This eternal life we already have when we believe in the Son of God (1 John 5). However, to live out this eternal life today, to express this eternal life in our thoughts, words, attitude, and actions, depends upon the power of the moving of this life within us. Therefore, the Apostle Paul said: \"...We have set our hope on the living God, Who is the Savior of all men, especially of those who believe.\"", "norm_zh": "我们要知道敬虔并不是一种苦修敬虔乃是一种生命的知觉乃是神生命的一种本性所以使徒保罗说到属乎主的人要追求公义敬虔信心爱心忍耐温柔提前六的时候是把敬虔列在这一类当我们得重生的哪一天神的神能已将一切关乎生命和敬虔的事赐给我们了彼后一而且这敬虔有今生和来生生命的应许提前四我们知道主所应许我们的就是永生这永生在我们信神儿子的时候就已经有了约壹五但是今天把这永生活出来把这永生彰显在我们的思想上彰显在我们的言语上彰显在我们的态度上彰显在我们的行动上还是在乎这生命在我们里面运行的大能所以使徒保罗说我们的指望在乎永生的神祂是万人的救主更是信徒的救主", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must know that godliness is not a kind of asceticism godliness is a consciousness of life a nature of Gods life Therefore when the Apostle Paul spoke of those who belong to the Lord pursuing righteousness godliness faith love endurance and meekness 1 Tim 6 he put godliness in this category When we were regenerated God according to His divine power gave to us all things that pertain to life and godliness 2 Pet 1 Also this godliness has the promise of the present life and of the life which is coming 1 Tim 4 We know that the promise which He Himself promised us is the eternal life This eternal life we already have when we believe in the Son of God 1 John 5 However to live out this eternal life today to express this eternal life in our thoughts words attitude and actions depends upon the power of the moving of this life within us Therefore the Apostle Paul said We have set our hope on the living God Who is the Savior of all men especially of those who believe"}
{"zh": "我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命，而要把这生命的本性表达出来，就需要在敬虔上操练自己。我们要知道，敬畏是一种存心，就是在任何的事情上怕有自己在里头，在任何的事情上怕得罪神；敬虔乃是在任何的事情上都要让神出来。在敬虔上操练自己，就是在消极方面要“除去不敬虔”，就是除去不象神的地方。在积极方面，要让神在凡事上出来。这一种的操练，并非苦修，并非关起门来百事不管，乃是按着恩膏的教训住在主里面，乃是学习让生命的律把神生命的特性在我们日常的生活上表达出来（提前二）。这一种的操练敬虔，是比操练身体更有益处的。因为我们今天虽然不能完全经历这永生，但是天天在经历着，到有一天，就要完全象祂。到有一天，身体得赎时，就要完全象祂，就要完全享受这永生。这是神永远的目的，这是新约的荣耀，我们要存着指望的心赞美主！", "en": "Within us we already have the godly life of God, but to manifest the nature of this life, we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness. We know that fear of God is a matter of attitude. This means that we are afraid of having our self in anything we do. We are afraid to sin against God. On the other hand, godliness means that we let God come forth in everything we do. To exercise ourselves unto godliness, on the negative side, means to \"deny ungodliness,\" which is to remove the things which do not conform to God. On the positive side, we need to let God come forth in everything. This kind of godliness is not some kind of mortification. It is not a matter of closing the doors and ignoring everything, but it is a matter of abiding in the Lord according to the teaching of the anointing, and learning to let the law of life manifest the nature of God's life in our daily life (1 Tim. 2). This kind of exercising unto godliness is more profitable than bodily exercise. Although today we cannot experience this eternal life completely, if we experience it day by day, one day we will be completely like Him when our body has been redeemed, and we will fully enjoy this eternal life. This is God's eternal purpose. This is the glory of the new covenant. We need to praise the Lord with a heart full of expectation.", "norm_zh": "我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命而要把这生命的本性表达出来就需要在敬虔上操练自己我们要知道敬畏是一种存心就是在任何的事情上怕有自己在里头在任何的事情上怕得罪神敬虔乃是在任何的事情上都要让神出来在敬虔上操练自己就是在消极方面要除去不敬虔就是除去不象神的地方在积极方面要让神在凡事上出来这一种的操练并非苦修并非关起门来百事不管乃是按着恩膏的教训住在主里面乃是学习让生命的律把神生命的特性在我们日常的生活上表达出来提前二这一种的操练敬虔是比操练身体更有益处的因为我们今天虽然不能完全经历这永生但是天天在经历着到有一天就要完全象祂到有一天身体得赎时就要完全象祂就要完全享受这永生这是神永远的目的这是新约的荣耀我们要存着指望的心赞美主", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Within us we already have the godly life of God but to manifest the nature of this life we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness We know that fear of God is a matter of attitude This means that we are afraid of having our self in anything we do We are afraid to sin against God On the other hand godliness means that we let God come forth in everything we do To exercise ourselves unto godliness on the negative side means to deny ungodliness which is to remove the things which do not conform to God On the positive side we need to let God come forth in everything This kind of godliness is not some kind of mortification It is not a matter of closing the doors and ignoring everything but it is a matter of abiding in the Lord according to the teaching of the anointing and learning to let the law of life manifest the nature of Gods life in our daily life 1 Tim 2 This kind of exercising unto godliness is more profitable than bodily exercise Although today we cannot experience this eternal life completely if we experience it day by day one day we will be completely like Him when our body has been redeemed and we will fully enjoy this eternal life This is Gods eternal purpose This is the glory of the new covenant We need to praise the Lord with a heart full of expectation"}
{"zh": "有的形态，可以说是病态，是有缺欠的", "en": "Some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects.", "norm_zh": "有的形态可以说是病态是有缺欠的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects"}
{"zh": "弟兄姊妹们，我们的主是“道成了肉身，住在我们中间，充充满满地有恩典，有真理”，这是敬虔的大启示。对提摩太说“惟独敬虔，凡事都有益处”的保罗，他是“有谁软弱，我不软弱呢？有谁跌倒，我不焦急呢？”他也是“亲手作工”（林前四），“比众使徒格外劳苦”的人。哦，弟兄姊妹们，这是我们的榜样，这是我们应该尊重，应该学习的。", "en": "Brothers and sisters, our Lord is the Word who became flesh and tabernacled among us, full of grace and reality; this is a great revelation of godliness. Paul, who told Timothy that \"only godliness is profitable for all things,\" is the one who said, \"Who is weak, and I am not weak? who is caused to stumble, and I burn not?\" He was also one who \"worked with his own hands\" (1 Cor. 4), and \"labored more abundantly than all the apostles.\" Oh, brothers and sisters, this is our example. We should respect Paul and learn of him.", "norm_zh": "弟兄姊妹们我们的主是道成了肉身住在我们中间充充满满地有恩典有真理这是敬虔的大启示对提摩太说惟独敬虔凡事都有益处的保罗他是有谁软弱我不软弱呢有谁跌倒我不焦急呢他也是亲手作工林前四比众使徒格外劳苦的人哦弟兄姊妹们这是我们的榜样这是我们应该尊重应该学习的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:29:41.536516+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Brothers and sisters our Lord is the Word who became flesh and tabernacled among us full of grace and reality this is a great revelation of godliness Paul who told Timothy that only godliness is profitable for all things is the one who said Who is weak and I am not weak who is caused to stumble and I burn not He was also one who worked with his own hands 1 Cor 4 and labored more abundantly than all the apostles Oh brothers and sisters this is our example We should respect Paul and learn of him"}
{"zh": "壹\t神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点，就是认识神的自己；新约的特点，就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己—来八11，约十七3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "I. Through the Spirit, God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point, that is, to know Himself; the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of life—Heb. 8:11; John 17:3:", "norm_zh": "壹神借着圣灵把祂所救赎的人带到最高点就是认识神的自己新约的特点就是使人在生命的律里来认识神的自己来八11约十七3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Through the Spirit God is bringing His redeemed ones to the highest point that is to know Himself the characteristic of the new covenant is that man may know God Himself in the law of lifeHeb 811 John 173"}
{"zh": "一\t何西阿四章六节说，“我的民因无知识而灭亡”；这里所说的无知识，就是无认识神的知识；以色列人所以那样背道以至于灭亡，最大的原因，就是因为他们不认识神。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. Hosea 4:6 says, \"My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge\"; the lack of knowledge in this verse is the lack of knowing God Himself; the children of Israel were disobedient to the extent that they were destroyed; this was mainly due to the fact that they did not know God.", "norm_zh": "一何西阿四章六节说我的民因无知识而灭亡这里所说的无知识就是无认识神的知识以色列人所以哪样背道以至于灭亡最大的原因就是因为他们不认识神李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hosea 46 says My people are destroyed for lack of knowledge the lack of knowledge in this verse is the lack of knowing God Himself the children of Israel were disobedient to the extent that they were destroyed this was mainly due to the fact that they did not know God"}
{"zh": "二\t新约的特点，就是神在生命的律里启示我们，引导我们，叫我们能敬拜神，事奉神，与神有交通，而一步一步地长进，而越过越认识神—约四24，西一6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. The characteristic of the new covenant is that God gives us revelation and guidance in the law of life. He enables us to worship Him, to serve Him, and to have fellowship with Him, so that we may go on step by step and get to know Him more and more.—John 4:24; Col. 1:6.", "norm_zh": "二新约的特点就是神在生命的律里启示我们引导我们叫我们能敬拜神事奉神与神有交通而一步一步地长进而越过越认识神约四24西一6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The characteristic of the new covenant is that God gives us revelation and guidance in the law of life He enables us to worship Him to serve Him and to have fellowship with Him so that we may go on step by step and get to know Him more and moreJohn 424 Col 16"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩膏的教训—来八11，约壹二20、27：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "II. The Teaching of the Anointing—Heb. 8:11; 1 John 2:20, 27:", "norm_zh": "贰恩膏的教训来八11约壹二2027李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The Teaching of the AnointingHeb 811 1 John 220 27"}
{"zh": "一\t希伯来八章十一节：“他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻，和自己的弟兄，说，你该认识主；因为他们从最小的到至大的，都必认识我”；这里所说的，与约壹二章二十七节所说“你们从主所受的恩膏，住在你们里面，并不用人教训你们；自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们”的话正相合。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. Hebrews 8:11 says, \"They shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother, saying, Know the Lord, for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them\"; what is spoken here corresponds to the word in 1 John 2:27, \"The anointing which you have received from Him abides in you, and you have no need that anyone teach you; but as His anointing teaches you concerning all things.\"", "norm_zh": "一希伯来八章十一节他们决不用各人教导自己的乡邻和自己的弟兄说你该认识主因为他们从最小的到至大的都必认识我这里所说的与约壹二章二十七节所说你们从主所受的恩膏住在你们里面并不用人教训你们自有主的恩膏在凡事上教训你们的话正相合李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Hebrews 811 says They shall by no means teach each one his fellow citizen and each one his brother saying Know the Lord for all shall know Me from the little one to the great among them what is spoken here corresponds to the word in 1 John 227 The anointing which you have received from Him abides in you and you have no need that anyone teach you but as His anointing teaches you concerning all things"}
{"zh": "二\t灵有交通的功用；圣灵就是在人的灵里引导人敬拜神，引导人与神交通—约四24。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. The spirit has the function of fellowship; the Holy Spirit guides man in his spirit to worship God and to have fellowship with God.—John 4:24.", "norm_zh": "二灵有交通的功用圣灵就是在人的灵里引导人敬拜神引导人与神交通约四24李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The spirit has the function of fellowship the Holy Spirit guides man in his spirit to worship God and to have fellowship with GodJohn 424"}
{"zh": "三\t灵有良心的功用；圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何；如果我们错了，圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们—徒二四16，林后一12。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "C. The spirit has the function of conscience; the Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk; if we are wrong, the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscience.—Acts 24:16; 2 Cor. 1:12.", "norm_zh": "三灵有良心的功用圣灵是在我们的良心里见证我们的行事为人到底如何如果我们错了圣灵就在我们的良心里责备我们徒二四16林后一12李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The spirit has the function of conscience the Holy Spirit testifies in our conscience concerning our behavior and walk if we are wrong the Holy Spirit will condemn us in our conscienceActs 2416 2 Cor 112"}
{"zh": "四\t灵有直觉的功用；人的身体有它的知觉，人的灵也有它的知觉；这灵的知觉，我们所以称它为“直觉”，是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的—来四12，创二7注5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "D. The spirit has the function of intuition; man's body has its sense, and man's spirit also has its sense; we call the sense of the spirit \"intuition\" because it comes directly from the spirit.—Heb. 4:12; Gen. 2:7, note 5.", "norm_zh": "四灵有直觉的功用人的身体有它的知觉人的灵也有它的知觉这灵的知觉我们所以称它为直觉是因为这种知觉是从灵直接发出来的来四12创二7注5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The spirit has the function of intuition mans body has its sense and mans spirit also has its sense we call the sense of the spirit intuition because it comes directly from the spiritHeb 412 Gen 27 note 5"}
{"zh": "五\t恩膏是在灵的直觉里—约壹二20、27：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "E. The Anointing is in the Intuition of the Spirit—1 John 2:20, 27:", "norm_zh": "五恩膏是在灵的直觉里约壹二2027李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Anointing is in the Intuition of the Spirit1 John 220 27"}
{"zh": "1\t主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们，意思就是圣灵在灵的直觉里教训我们，叫我们在灵里有所觉得，象膏油涂在人的身体上叫人有所觉得一样—20节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. The Lord's anointing teaches us all things. This means that the Holy Spirit teaches us in the intuition of the spirit, causing us to have some feeling in our spirit, just as when ointment is applied to man's body, causing him to have some sensation.—v. 20.", "norm_zh": "1主的恩膏在凡事上教训我们意思就是圣灵在灵的直觉里教训我们叫我们在灵里有所觉得象膏油涂在人的身体上叫人有所觉得一样20节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lords anointing teaches us all things This means that the Holy Spirit teaches us in the intuition of the spirit causing us to have some feeling in our spirit just as when ointment is applied to mans body causing him to have some sensationv 20"}
{"zh": "2\t知道是灵知道，明白是心思明白；我们是借着灵的直觉来“知道”一件事，然后心思里得着亮光，“明白”直觉所知道的事；这一种的知道，是比心思中的明白更深的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. We know in our spirit, but we understand with our mind; we know a certain thing through the intuition of the spirit; then the mind is enlightened to understand what the intuition knows; this kind of knowing is deeper than the understanding in the mind.", "norm_zh": "2知道是灵知道明白是心思明白我们是借着灵的直觉来知道一件事然后心思里得着亮光明白直觉所知道的事这一种的知道是比心思中的明白更深的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We know in our spirit but we understand with our mind we know a certain thing through the intuition of the spirit then the mind is enlightened to understand what the intuition knows this kind of knowing is deeper than the understanding in the mind"}
{"zh": "六\t外面再复述—罗六3，林前三16，五6，六2~3、9、15、19，雅四4：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "F. Outward Repetition—Rom. 6:3; 1 Cor. 3:16; 5:6; 6:2-3, 9, 15, 19; James 4:4:", "norm_zh": "六外面再复述罗六3林前三16五6六2391519雅四4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Outward RepetitionRom 63 1 Cor 316 56 623 9 15 19 James 44"}
{"zh": "1\t我们如果读新约的书信，就要看见，有许多的教导是复述的，是因教会有了难处才说的。新约的书信常说到“岂不知”—罗六3，林前三16，五6，六2~3，雅四4。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. When we read the Epistles in the New Testament, we realize that many teachings are repetitions. They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church. In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase, \"Know ye not?\"—Rom. 6:3; 1 Cor. 3:16; 5:6; 6:2-3; James 4:4.", "norm_zh": "1我们如果读新约的书信就要看见有许多的教导是复述的是因教会有了难处才说的新约的书信常说到岂不知罗六3林前三16五6六23雅四4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we read the Epistles in the New Testament we realize that many teachings are repetitions They were repeated because of some difficulties in the church In the Epistles of the New Testament we often find the phrase Know ye notRom 63 1 Cor 316 56 623 James 44"}
{"zh": "2\t圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说，乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的—林前三16。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within, but simply repeat what the anointing has already said.—1 Cor. 3:16.", "norm_zh": "2圣经不是代替在你里面的恩膏来说乃是复述恩膏在你里面所已经说的林前三16李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Scriptures do not speak in place of the anointing within but simply repeat what the anointing has already said1 Cor 316"}
{"zh": "3\t里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的，但是外面的不能代替里面的；里面的说话，是活的，是生命的；这是新约的特点—林后三6。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "3. The inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful, but the outward teaching must not replace that which is inward; the inward speaking is living and of life; this is the characteristic of the new covenant.—2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "3里面的教导和外面的教导是互相为用的但是外面的不能代替里面的里面的说话是活的是生命的这是新约的特点林后三6李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The inward teaching and the outward teaching are mutually helpful but the outward teaching must not replace that which is inward the inward speaking is living and of life this is the characteristic of the new covenant2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "七\t悟性必须更新—罗十二2，西一9：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "G. The Mind Must be Renewed—Rom. 12:2; Col. 1:9:", "norm_zh": "七悟性必须更新罗十二2西一9李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G The Mind Must be RenewedRom 122 Col 19"}
{"zh": "1\t我们的悟性必须更新，然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的—二2。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. Our mind must be renewed, and then we can understand what the anointing is teaching us.—Col. 2:2.", "norm_zh": "1我们的悟性必须更新然后我们才能懂得恩膏在里面所教训的二2李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Our mind must be renewed and then we can understand what the anointing is teaching usCol 22"}
{"zh": "2\t更新的工作是圣灵作的；罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见，是先“将身体献上当作活祭”，然后才是“悟性更新而变化”。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. The work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit; Romans 12:1-2 makes it clear that first we must present our bodies as a living sacrifice; then we may be transformed by the renewing of the mind.", "norm_zh": "2更新的工作是圣灵作的罗马十二章一至二节给我们看见是先将身体献上当作活祭然后才是悟性更新而变化李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The work of renewing is done by the Holy Spirit Romans 1212 makes it clear that first we must present our bodies as a living sacrifice then we may be transformed by the renewing of the mind"}
{"zh": "3\t以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见，更新悟性的灵，是要在经历上先“脱去……从前行为上的旧人”；所以，悟性的更新是要借着十字架的。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "3. Ephesians 4:22-23 shows us that for the renewing of the spirit of the mind we must, in our experience, first put off the old man regarding our former manner of life; therefore, the renewing of the mind is something which is done through the cross.", "norm_zh": "3以弗所四章二十二至二十三节给我们看见更新悟性的灵是要在经历上先脱去从前行为上的旧人所以悟性的更新是要借着十字架的李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Ephesians 42223 shows us that for the renewing of the spirit of the mind we must in our experience first put off the old man regarding our former manner of life therefore the renewing of the mind is something which is done through the cross"}
{"zh": "八\t用圣经校对里面的感觉—约壹四6，约十六13：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "H. Checking Our Inner Feeling by the Scriptures—1 John 4:6; John 16:13:", "norm_zh": "八用圣经校对里面的感觉约壹四6约十六13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H Checking Our Inner Feeling by the Scriptures1 John 46 John 1613"}
{"zh": "1\t里面的感觉是活的；但是，外面的圣经是准的；光有圣经的话，只是准，只是稳，不活；光有里面的感觉，可能有时活而不准，活而不稳—诗一一九105。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. The inner sense is living, but the Scriptures without are accurate; if we merely have the words of the Scripture, there is accuracy and security, but no life; having merely the inner sense may be living, but not accurate; or it may be living, but not secure.—Psa. 119:105.", "norm_zh": "1里面的感觉是活的但是外面的圣经是准的光有圣经的话只是准只是稳不活光有里面的感觉可能有时活而不准活而不稳诗一一九105李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The inner sense is living but the Scriptures without are accurate if we merely have the words of the Scripture there is accuracy and security but no life having merely the inner sense may be living but not accurate or it may be living but not securePsa 119105"}
{"zh": "2\t以色列人出埃及的时候，在他们前面，有云柱，是白日的引导者；有火柱，是黑夜的引导者；如果没有黑夜，就用不着灯和光—出十三21~22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. When the Israelites came out of Egypt, they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night; without the night there is no need for the lamp and the light.—Exo. 13:21-22.", "norm_zh": "2以色列人出埃及的时候在他们前面有云柱是白日的引导者有火柱是黑夜的引导者如果没有黑夜就用不着灯和光出十三2122李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When the Israelites came out of Egypt they had before them the pillar of cloud as their guide in the day and the pillar of fire as their guide in the night without the night there is no need for the lamp and the lightExo 132122"}
{"zh": "3\t生命加上真理，才是真的能力，才是稳的力量；我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "3. Life plus truth equals real power; life and truth result in secure strength; we need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth.", "norm_zh": "3生命加上真理才是真的能力才是稳的力量我们要走在生命和真理的平稳的路上李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Life plus truth equals real power life and truth result in secure strength we need to walk upon the secure path of life and truth"}
{"zh": "叁\t两种的认识神—来八11，何六6，彼后一2、8：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "III. Two Ways of Knowing God—Heb. 8:11; Hos. 6:6; 2 Pet. 1:2, 8:", "norm_zh": "叁两种的认识神来八11何六6彼后一28李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Two Ways of Knowing GodHeb 811 Hos 66 2 Pet 12 8"}
{"zh": "一\t第一个认识的意思是指普通的认识，第二个认识的意思是指在直觉里的认识—2、8节：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. The first knowing signifies the ordinary knowledge; the second knowing refers to knowledge in the intuition.—vv. 2, 8:", "norm_zh": "一第一个认识的意思是指普通的认识第二个认识的意思是指在直觉里的认识28节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first knowing signifies the ordinary knowledge the second knowing refers to knowledge in the intuitionvv 2 8"}
{"zh": "1\t普通的认识，是客观的认识，是外面的认识；在直觉里的认识，是主观的认识，是里面的认识—8节。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. The ordinary knowledge is the objective, outward knowledge, while the intuitive knowledge is the subjective, inward knowledge.—v. 8.", "norm_zh": "1普通的认识是客观的认识是外面的认识在直觉里的认识是主观的认识是里面的认识8节李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The ordinary knowledge is the objective outward knowledge while the intuitive knowledge is the subjective inward knowledgev 8"}
{"zh": "2\t属灵的东西是要尝的；感谢神，新约的特点，不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西，并且叫我们能尝到神—诗三四8，来六4~5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. Spiritual things need to be tasted; thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things; it even enables us to taste God Himself.—Psa. 34:8; Heb. 6:4-5.", "norm_zh": "2属灵的东西是要尝的感谢神新约的特点不只叫我们能尝到属灵的东西并且叫我们能尝到神诗三四8来六45李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Spiritual things need to be tasted thank God that the characteristic of the new covenant not only enables us to taste spiritual things it even enables us to taste God HimselfPsa 348 Heb 645"}
{"zh": "二\t三步地认识神；凭圣经看来，人对于神的认识是分作三步的—诗一〇三7，来八11：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. Knowing God in Three Steps; according to the Scriptures, man's knowing God can be divided into three steps—Psa. 103:7; Heb. 8:11:", "norm_zh": "二三步地认识神凭圣经看来人对于神的认识是分作三步的诗一〇三7来八11李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Knowing God in Three Steps according to the Scriptures mans knowing God can be divided into three stepsPsa 1037 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "1\t第一步是认识神的作为，第二步是认识神的法则，第三步是认识神的自己；认识神的作为和法则，还不过是外面的认识；在里面认识神的性情，认识神的自己，才是更深的认识，这是最宝贵的—诗一〇三7，来八11。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. The first step is to know God's doings; the second step is to know God's ways; and the third step is to know God Himself; to know God's doings and ways are only outward knowing, but the inward knowing of God's nature and knowing God Himself is the deeper knowing. This is the most precious—Psa. 103:7; Heb. 8:11.", "norm_zh": "1第一步是认识神的作为第二步是认识神的法则第三步是认识神的自己认识神的作为和法则还不过是外面的认识在里面认识神的性情认识神的自己才是更深的认识这是最宝贵的诗一〇三7来八11李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The first step is to know Gods doings the second step is to know Gods ways and the third step is to know God Himself to know Gods doings and ways are only outward knowing but the inward knowing of Gods nature and knowing God Himself is the deeper knowing This is the most preciousPsa 1037 Heb 811"}
{"zh": "2\t认识神的作为；神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事—出七~十一、十四、十七。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. Knowing God's doings; God's doings are the miracles and wonders which He performs—Exo. 7-11, 14, 17.", "norm_zh": "2认识神的作为神的作为就是神所行的神迹奇事出七十一十四十七李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Knowing Gods doings Gods doings are the miracles and wonders which He performsExo 711 14 17"}
{"zh": "3\t认识神的法则，也可以说就是认识神作事的原则；象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求，他就是站在神的公义一边来求神—创十八23~33，民十六46~48，撒上十五22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "3. To know God's ways means to know the principle by which God does things; for example, when Abraham prayed for Sodom, he prayed by standing on the side of God's righteousness.—Gen. 18:23-33; Num. 16:46-48; 1 Sam. 15:22.", "norm_zh": "3认识神的法则也可以说就是认识神作事的原则象亚伯拉罕为所多玛祈求他就是站在神的公义一边来求神创十八2333民十六4648撒上十五22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 To know Gods ways means to know the principle by which God does things for example when Abraham prayed for Sodom he prayed by standing on the side of Gods righteousnessGen 182333 Num 164648 1 Sam 1522"}
{"zh": "4\t认识神的性情，就是认识神的自己—诗二五8，八六5，太十17，徒三14，林后一3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "4. To know God's nature means to know God Himself.—Psa. 25:8; 86:5; Matt. 10:17; Acts 3:14; 2 Cor. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "4认识神的性情就是认识神的自己诗二五8八六5太十17徒三14林后一3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 To know Gods nature means to know God HimselfPsa 258 865 Matt 1017 Acts 314 2 Cor 13"}
{"zh": "a\t祂的性情是良善正直的，是圣洁的；这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己—诗二五8。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "a. His nature is goodness, uprightness, and holiness; this nature will express God Himself through light.—Psa. 25:8.", "norm_zh": "a祂的性情是良善正直的是圣洁的这性情要借着光来彰显祂的自己诗二五8李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a His nature is goodness uprightness and holiness this nature will express God Himself through lightPsa 258"}
{"zh": "b\t多少时候，我们的一言一行，良心虽然不定罪，但是，里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服，好像不阿们似的，那就是神生命性情的感觉，那是超过良心的感觉的；我们如果有学习，如果肯顺服，我们就在这里摸着神的自己，就在这里认识神的自己。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "b. Many times, both in our words and in our actions, although our conscience may not condemn us, there is still within a sense of discomfort, a sense which does not say \"amen.\" This is the sense of the nature of God's life, and it exceeds the feeling of the conscience; if we have learned and are willing to obey, it is at such times that we touch God Himself. On these occasions we will know God Himself.", "norm_zh": "b多少时候我们的一言一行良心虽然不定罪但是里面总隐隐约约觉得不舒服好像不阿们似的哪就是神生命性情的感觉哪是超过良心的感觉的我们如果有学习如果肯顺服我们就在这里摸着神的自己就在这里认识神的自己李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b Many times both in our words and in our actions although our conscience may not condemn us there is still within a sense of discomfort a sense which does not say amen This is the sense of the nature of Gods life and it exceeds the feeling of the conscience if we have learned and are willing to obey it is at such times that we touch God Himself On these occasions we will know God Himself"}
{"zh": "5\t在直觉里认识神—约十七3，林前二11~12：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "5. Knowing God in Our Intuition—John 17:3; 1 Cor. 2:11-12:", "norm_zh": "5在直觉里认识神约十七3林前二1112李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Knowing God in Our IntuitionJohn 173 1 Cor 21112"}
{"zh": "a\t人有了永生，人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神，这永生有一种功能叫人认识神—约十七3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "a. When a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before. This eternal life has a function which enables man to know God.—John 17:3.", "norm_zh": "a人有了永生人就得着了他本来所没有的一种直觉上的认识神这永生有一种功能叫人认识神约十七3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a When a man receives eternal life he receives a knowing of God in the intuition which he did not possess before This eternal life has a function which enables man to know GodJohn 173"}
{"zh": "b\t我们所领受的，并不是世上的灵，乃是从神来的灵，叫我们能知道神开恩赐给我们的事；这智慧和启示的灵，总是叫信徒能“真知道祂”；我们的直觉需要智慧和启示。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "b. We have received not the spirit of the world but the Spirit which is from God, that we may know the things which have been graciously given to us by God; this spirit of wisdom and revelation always enables believers to \"truly know Him\"; our intuition needs wisdom and revelation.", "norm_zh": "b我们所领受的并不是世上的灵乃是从神来的灵叫我们能知道神开恩赐给我们的事这智慧和启示的灵总是叫信徒能真知道祂我们的直觉需要智慧和启示李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b We have received not the spirit of the world but the Spirit which is from God that we may know the things which have been graciously given to us by God this spirit of wisdom and revelation always enables believers to truly know Him our intuition needs wisdom and revelation"}
{"zh": "c\t启示是在灵的直觉里，光照是照在魂的心思里；在直觉里是觉得的知道，在心思里是看见而明白；神就是这样赐给我们智慧和启示的灵，叫我们真知道祂，也真明白祂—弗一17~18。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "c. Revelation is in the intuition of the spirit, while enlightenment is in the mind of the soul; in the intuition we know by sensing, while in the mind we understand by seeing; thus, God gives us the spirit of wisdom and revelation, that we may truly know Him and truly understand Him.—Eph. 1:17-18.", "norm_zh": "c启示是在灵的直觉里光照是照在魂的心思里在直觉里是觉得的知道在心思里是看见而明白神就是这样赐给我们智慧和启示的灵叫我们真知道祂也真明白祂弗一1718李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c Revelation is in the intuition of the spirit while enlightenment is in the mind of the soul in the intuition we know by sensing while in the mind we understand by seeing thus God gives us the spirit of wisdom and revelation that we may truly know Him and truly understand HimEph 11718"}
{"zh": "d\t我们如果每件事都在灵里寻求神的旨意，结果就要叫我们“在真知道神里长大”，意思就是我们在认识神的知识上逐渐长大—西一9~10。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "d. If in everything we seek God's will in our spirit, the result will be that we are \"growing by the full knowledge of God,\" which means that we grow gradually in our knowledge of God.—Col. 1:9-10.", "norm_zh": "d我们如果每件事都在灵里寻求神的旨意结果就要叫我们在真知道神里长大意思就是我们在认识神的知识上逐渐长大西一910李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "d If in everything we seek Gods will in our spirit the result will be that we are growing by the full knowledge of God which means that we grow gradually in our knowledge of GodCol 1910"}
{"zh": "6\t劳伦斯说，“如果你的心要认识神，爱是惟一的道路。人心的喜好与情绪是不同的，情绪合宜的出路就是爱，爱的目的物就是神。”（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "6. Brother Lawrence said, \"If your heart is to know God, love is the only way. The pleasures of man's heart are different from his sentiments; the proper outlet of sentiments is love, and the object of love is God.\"", "norm_zh": "6劳伦斯说如果你的心要认识神爱是惟一的道路人心的喜好与情绪是不同的情绪合宜的出路就是爱爱的目的物就是神李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 Brother Lawrence said If your heart is to know God love is the only way The pleasures of mans heart are different from his sentiments the proper outlet of sentiments is love and the object of love is God"}
{"zh": "肆\t我们在里面认识神有多深，我们就在外面彰显神也有多深—加一16，徒二三3：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "IV. The degree of our inward knowledge of God determines the extent of our outward expression of Him.—Gal. 1:16; Acts 23:3:", "norm_zh": "肆我们在里面认识神有多深我们就在外面彰显神也有多深加一16徒二三3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The degree of our inward knowledge of God determines the extent of our outward expression of HimGal 116 Acts 233"}
{"zh": "一\t彰显于胆量和鉴别；保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人，就是因他对于神的儿子的认识，是从启示来的；真认识神的人，就有胆量宣告：住在我们里面的，比那敌基督者的灵更大！—加一6，但十一32，林后五16，约壹四4。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. Manifested in boldness and discernment; the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation; one who truly knows God has the boldness to declare: He who is in us is greater than the spirit of the antichrist!—Gal. 1:6; Dan. 11:32; 2 Cor. 5:16; 1 John 4:4.", "norm_zh": "一彰显于胆量和鉴别保罗所以有胆量传福音给外邦人就是因他对于神的儿子的认识是从启示来的真认识神的人就有胆量宣告住在我们里面的比哪敌基督者的灵更大加一6但十一32林后五16约壹四4李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Manifested in boldness and discernment the reason Paul had the boldness to preach the gospel to the nations was because his knowledge of the Son of God was by revelation one who truly knows God has the boldness to declare He who is in us is greater than the spirit of the antichristGal 16 Dan 1132 2 Cor 516 1 John 44"}
{"zh": "二\t彰显于敬畏；敬畏神，是随时、随地、随事，都不敢随便，都有敬畏神的存心—徒十六：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. Manifested in fearing God; to fear God means that anywhere, at any time, in any activity, we dare not be loose. Within there is the attitude of fearing God—Acts 16:", "norm_zh": "二彰显于敬畏敬畏神是随时随地随事都不敢随便都有敬畏神的存心徒十六李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Manifested in fearing God to fear God means that anywhere at any time in any activity we dare not be loose Within there is the attitude of fearing GodActs 16"}
{"zh": "1\t象保罗工作的脚步，一再受神的禁止，他敬畏神—徒二三3~5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "1. For example, the steps Paul took in his work were, many times, forbidden by God. He feared God.—Acts 23:3-5.", "norm_zh": "1象保罗工作的脚步一再受神的禁止他敬畏神徒二三35李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 For example the steps Paul took in his work were many times forbidden by God He feared GodActs 2335"}
{"zh": "2\t真认识神的人，是束上“心中的腰”的人，在他的言语、态度、动作上，是一点都不敢放松的—彼前一13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "2. Those who truly know God are those who gird up the loins of their mind; there is nothing loose in their words, attitude, and actions.—1 Pet. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "2真认识神的人是束上心中的腰的人在他的言语态度动作上是一点都不敢放松的彼前一13李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Those who truly know God are those who gird up the loins of their mind there is nothing loose in their words attitude and actions1 Pet 113"}
{"zh": "三\t彰显于敬拜；以真诚拜神，就是承认神是神，也承认我们是谁；祂是无限的完全，配得着无限的敬重；真认识神的人，对神才有真诚的敬拜—创三二30，提前二5。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "C. Manifested in worship; to worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is, and ourselves as what in very fact we are; He is infinitely perfect, worthy of infinite adoration; only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truth—Gen. 32:30; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "三彰显于敬拜以真诚拜神就是承认神是神也承认我们是谁祂是无限的完全配得着无限的敬重真认识神的人对神才有真诚的敬拜创三二30提前二5李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Manifested in worship to worship God in truth is to acknowledge Him to be what He is and ourselves as what in very fact we are He is infinitely perfect worthy of infinite adoration only the person who truly knows God can worship God in truthGen 3230 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "四\t彰显于敬虔；真认识神的人，就要把神彰显出来，这就是敬虔的生活；我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命，而要把这生命的本性表达出来，就需要在敬虔上操练自己—提前四7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "D. Manifested in godliness; those who truly know God will manifest God, and this is a godly life; within us we already have the godly life of God, but to manifest the nature of this life, we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness—1 Tim. 4:7.", "norm_zh": "四彰显于敬虔真认识神的人就要把神彰显出来这就是敬虔的生活我们里面已经有了神敬虔的生命而要把这生命的本性表达出来就需要在敬虔上操练自己提前四7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Manifested in godliness those who truly know God will manifest God and this is a godly life within us we already have the godly life of God but to manifest the nature of this life we need to exercise ourselves unto godliness1 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "伍\t操练敬虔，在基督耶稣里敬虔度日，是一种属灵的追求；但是，有的形态，可以说是病态，是有缺欠的，我们要分开来说一下—提后三12，提前四7：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "V. Exercising unto godliness, or living godly in Christ Jesus, is a spiritual pursuit; however, some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects, which we will discuss separately.—2 Tim. 3:12; 1 Tim. 4:7:", "norm_zh": "伍操练敬虔在基督耶稣里敬虔度日是一种属灵的追求但是有的形态可以说是病态是有缺欠的我们要分开来说一下提后三12提前四7李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Exercising unto godliness or living godly in Christ Jesus is a spiritual pursuit however some manifestations may be considered sick conditions and are defects which we will discuss separately2 Tim 312 1 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "一\t懒惰；有的基督徒生性懒惰，就是不肯劳动，不肯操作，就拿祷告，拿属灵的话作他懒惰的护符；我们要说，这是病态，这不是敬虔—罗十二11，徒二十19，林前十五58。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. Laziness; some Christians, it seems, were born lazy; they neither like to labor nor to work, and they use prayer and spiritual words as a shelter for their laziness; we must say that this is a sick condition and is not godliness.—Rom. 12:11; Acts 20:19; 1 Cor. 15:58.", "norm_zh": "一懒惰有的基督徒生性懒惰就是不肯劳动不肯操作就拿祷告拿属灵的话作他懒惰的护符我们要说这是病态这不是敬虔罗十二11徒二十19林前十五58李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Laziness some Christians it seems were born lazy they neither like to labor nor to work and they use prayer and spiritual words as a shelter for their laziness we must say that this is a sick condition and is not godlinessRom 1211 Acts 2019 1 Cor 1558"}
{"zh": "二\t拘谨；有的基督徒把拘谨当作敬虔，弄得他这个人象个假人；所以，我们操练敬虔的时候，应该是活泼新鲜的，是神从我们这个人的言语态度里出来—罗十二15，启三1。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. Rigidness; some Christians think that godliness means to be rigid, making them appear artificial; therefore, whenever we exercise ourselves unto godliness, we should be living and fresh; it must be God who comes forth in our words and in our attitude.—Rom. 12:15; Rev. 3:1.", "norm_zh": "二拘谨有的基督徒把拘谨当作敬虔弄得他这个人象个假人所以我们操练敬虔的时候应该是活泼新鲜的是神从我们这个人的言语态度里出来罗十二15启三1李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Rigidness some Christians think that godliness means to be rigid making them appear artificial therefore whenever we exercise ourselves unto godliness we should be living and fresh it must be God who comes forth in our words and in our attitudeRom 1215 Rev 31"}
{"zh": "三\t冷硬；但这并非说我们可以对人没有爱，没有礼貌；我们想想看，这一种的自以为敬虔，这一种的冷硬，能吸引人羡慕神么？—来十二14，罗十二10，彼前一22。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "C. Cold and hardheartedness; this is not to say, however, that we may be negligent in love and in courtesy toward others; let us not think that such a self-assumed godliness and such a cold, hardhearted attitude will ever attract others to long after God.—Heb. 12:14; Rom. 12:10; 1 Pet. 1:22.", "norm_zh": "三冷硬但这并非说我们可以对人没有爱没有礼貌我们想想看这一种的自以为敬虔这一种的冷硬能吸引人羡慕神么来十二14罗十二10彼前一22李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Cold and hardheartedness this is not to say however that we may be negligent in love and in courtesy toward others let us not think that such a selfassumed godliness and such a cold hardhearted attitude will ever attract others to long after GodHeb 1214 Rom 1210 1 Pet 122"}
{"zh": "四\t被动；有的基督徒，操练敬虔，特别是学盖恩夫人，学劳伦斯的“与神同在”，这是可敬可慕的；可是，有的基督徒学习他们而流于被动，却是可惜的—罗十二10、13。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "D. Passivity; some Christians who admire Madame Guyon and Brother Lawrence (who practiced the presence of God) seek to practice godliness as they did; this is something to be respected; it is even desirable; however, unfortunately, there are others who imitate them and become passive.—Rom. 12:10, 13.", "norm_zh": "四被动有的基督徒操练敬虔特别是学盖恩夫人学劳伦斯的与神同在这是可敬可慕的可是有的基督徒学习他们而流于被动却是可惜的罗十二1013李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Passivity some Christians who admire Madame Guyon and Brother Lawrence who practiced the presence of God seek to practice godliness as they did this is something to be respected it is even desirable however unfortunately there are others who imitate them and become passiveRom 1210 13"}
{"zh": "陆\t需要神继续的赦免与洗净—弗一5~7，约壹一5~7：（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "VI. The Need for God's Continual Forgiveness and Cleansing—Eph. 1:5-7; 1 John 1:5-7:", "norm_zh": "陆需要神继续的赦免与洗净弗一57约壹一57李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The Need for Gods Continual Forgiveness and CleansingEph 157 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "一\t像以弗所第一章，先说神“预定我们，借着耶稣基督得儿子的名分”，因为这是目的；后说“我们借这爱子的血，得蒙救赎，过犯得以赦免”，因为这是手续；神要把生命给我们之前，神必须先赦免我们的罪，先洁净我们。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "A. As in Ephesians 1, first we are told that God \"predestinated us unto sonship through Jesus Christ to Himself,\" because this is the purpose; later it is mentioned that \"we have redemption through His blood, the forgiveness of offenses,\" because this is the procedure; before God gives us life, He must first forgive our sins and cleanse us.", "norm_zh": "一像以弗所第一章先说神预定我们借着耶稣基督得儿子的名分因为这是目的后说我们借这爱子的血得蒙救赎过犯得以赦免因为这是手续神要把生命给我们之前神必须先赦免我们的罪先洁净我们李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As in Ephesians 1 first we are told that God predestinated us unto sonship through Jesus Christ to Himself because this is the purpose later it is mentioned that we have redemption through His blood the forgiveness of offenses because this is the procedure before God gives us life He must first forgive our sins and cleanse us"}
{"zh": "二\t生命要求交通，也带进交通；交通就带进光；光要求血；这四件东西也是循环不已的；这个循环叫我们在生命里前进；一直这样一周一周的往前转，我们就要在神的生命里一直前进不已—诗三六9，约壹一5~7。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "B. Life requires fellowship and also brings in fellowship; fellowship brings in light; and light requires the blood; these four items are also in a cycle; this cycle will cause us to move ahead in life; as we pass through one cycle after another, we will continue to move on in God's life.—Psa. 36:9; 1 John 1:5-7.", "norm_zh": "二生命要求交通也带进交通交通就带进光光要求血这四件东西也是循环不已的这个循环叫我们在生命里前进一直这样一周一周的往前转我们就要在神的生命里一直前进不已诗三六9约壹一57李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Life requires fellowship and also brings in fellowship fellowship brings in light and light requires the blood these four items are also in a cycle this cycle will cause us to move ahead in life as we pass through one cycle after another we will continue to move on in Gods lifePsa 369 1 John 157"}
{"zh": "三\t我们认识神是在生命的律里认识神，是在直觉里认识神，这是非常实际的；这是新约的高峰，这是新约的荣耀！—来八11，约十七3。（李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册，什么是新约，第八章）", "en": "C. It is in the law of life and in the intuition that we know God; this is very practical; this is the climax of the new covenant; this is the glory of the new covenant!—Heb. 8:11; John 17:3.", "norm_zh": "三我们认识神是在生命的律里认识神是在直觉里认识神这是非常实际的这是新约的高峰这是新约的荣耀来八11约十七3李常受文集一九三二年至一九四九年第三册什么是新约第八章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:32:53.909285+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It is in the law of life and in the intuition that we know God this is very practical this is the climax of the new covenant this is the glory of the new covenantHeb 811 John 173"}
{"zh": "读经：来一1~2，徒二42，约十四10，五24，太二八19~20，约十六12~15，启二1、7，林前四17下，彼后三15~16，启一1~2", "en": "Scripture Reading: Heb. 1:1-2; Acts 2:42; John 14:10; 5:24; Matt. 28:19-20; John 16:12-15; Rev. 2:1, 7; 1 Cor. 4:17b; 2 Pet. 3:15-16; Rev. 1:1-2", "norm_zh": "读经来一12徒二42约十四10五24太二八1920约十六1215启二17林前四17下彼后三1516启一12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Heb 112 Acts 242 John 1410 524 Matt 281920 John 161215 Rev 21 7 1 Cor 417b 2 Pet 31516 Rev 112"}
{"zh": "一\t教训和交通成为一组，是使徒的教训和交通，与神的经纶有直接的关系，乃是为着保守召会，就是基督身体的一；二者都是惟一的—41~42节：", "en": "A.\tThe teaching and the fellowship form one group, which is of the apostles and related directly to God's economy for the keeping of the oneness of the Body of Christ; both are unique:—vv. 41-42:", "norm_zh": "一教训和交通成为一组是使徒的教训和交通与神的经纶有直接的关系乃是为着保守召会就是基督身体的一二者都是惟一的4142节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The teaching and the fellowship form one group which is of the apostles and related directly to Gods economy for the keeping of the oneness of the Body of Christ both are uniquevv 4142"}
{"zh": "1\t使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素—42节上，46节上。", "en": "1\tThe teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord.—vv. 42a, 46a.", "norm_zh": "1使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素42节上46节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accordvv 42a 46a"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若将自己限制于使徒的教训之内，就是限制在关于神新约经纶的教训之内，我们就会被保守在一里，也会有一条道路，为着一个目标—41~47节。", "en": "2\tIf we limit ourselves to the apostles' teaching, the teaching concerning God's New Testament economy, we will be kept in oneness and will have one way for one goal.—vv. 41-47.", "norm_zh": "2我们若将自己限制于使徒的教训之内就是限制在关于神新约经纶的教训之内我们就会被保守在一里也会有一条道路为着一个目标4147节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we limit ourselves to the apostles teaching the teaching concerning Gods New Testament economy we will be kept in oneness and will have one way for one goalvv 4147"}
{"zh": "3\t在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训—使徒的教训；不仅如此，也应当只有一个惟一的交通，而这交通是由使徒的教训所产生的—一14~15，二42。", "en": "3\tIn the church there should be only one unique teaching—the teaching of the apostles; furthermore, there should be one unique fellowship, which is produced by the apostles' teaching.—1:14-15; 2:42.", "norm_zh": "3在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训使徒的教训不仅如此也应当只有一个惟一的交通而这交通是由使徒的教训所产生的一1415二42", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In the church there should be only one unique teachingthe teaching of the apostles furthermore there should be one unique fellowship which is produced by the apostles teaching11415 242"}
{"zh": "4\t任何在使徒的交通之外的交通，都是分裂的；我们的交通必须在使徒的交通之内—罗六17。", "en": "4\tAny fellowship outside the fellowship of the apostles is divisive; our fellowship must be inside the fellowship of the apostles.—Rom. 6:17.", "norm_zh": "4任何在使徒的交通之外的交通都是分裂的我们的交通必须在使徒的交通之内罗六17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Any fellowship outside the fellowship of the apostles is divisive our fellowship must be inside the fellowship of the apostlesRom 617"}
{"zh": "二\t擘饼和祷告成为第二组，是信徒之基督徒生活的实行—徒二41~42。", "en": "B.\tThe breaking of bread and the prayers form a second group and are practices of the believers' Christian life.—Acts 2:41-42.", "norm_zh": "二擘饼和祷告成为第二组是信徒之基督徒生活的实行徒二4142", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The breaking of bread and the prayers form a second group and are practices of the believers Christian lifeActs 24142"}
{"zh": "一\t宇宙中有一件美妙的事，就是神的说话—2节，徒三21，约十30：", "en": "A.\tIn the universe there is a marvelous matter—God's speaking:—v. 2; Acts 3:21; John 10:30:", "norm_zh": "一宇宙中有一件美妙的事就是神的说话2节徒三21约十30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the universe there is a marvelous matterGods speakingv 2 Acts 321 John 1030"}
{"zh": "1\t在新约时代，神不是多分多方，或借着申言者，向祂的子民说话—来一2。", "en": "1\tIn the New Testament God does not speak to His people in many portions and in many ways or through the prophets.—Heb. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "1在新约时代神不是多分多方或借着申言者向祂的子民说话来一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In the New Testament God does not speak to His people in many portions and in many ways or through the prophetsHeb 12"}
{"zh": "2\t在新约时代，神只在子这一个人位里说话—约十四10。", "en": "2\tIn the New Testament God speaks in one person, the Son.—John 14:10.", "norm_zh": "2在新约时代神只在子这一个人位里说话约十四10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the New Testament God speaks in one person the SonJohn 1410"}
{"zh": "二\t神首先在为人的子里，在四福音里说话—10节，五24，十六12，十30。", "en": "B.\tGod first spoke in the Son as a man in the four Gospels;—John 1:10; 5:24; 16:12; 10:30.", "norm_zh": "二神首先在为人的子里在四福音里说话10节五24十六12十30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God first spoke in the Son as a man in the four GospelsJohn 110 524 1612 1030"}
{"zh": "三\t其次，神借着使徒们，在那成为灵的子里，在使徒行传和二十一卷书信（罗马书到犹大书）里说话—十六12~15，太二八19~20，来二3~4，彼后三15~16，西一25~27。", "en": "C.\tGod secondly spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles in Acts and the twenty-one Epistles (Romans through Jude)—John 16:12-15; Matt. 28:19-20; Heb. 2:3-4; 2 Pet. 3:15-16; Col. 1:25-27.", "norm_zh": "三其次神借着使徒们在哪成为灵的子里在使徒行传和二十一卷书信罗马书到犹大书里说话十六1215太二八1920来二34彼后三1516西一2527", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God secondly spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles in Acts and the twentyone Epistles Romans through JudeJohn 161215 Matt 281920 Heb 234 2 Pet 31516 Col 12527"}
{"zh": "四\t第三，神借着使徒约翰，在那成为七灵的子里，在启示录里说话—启一2、4、11，二1、7。", "en": "D.\tGod thirdly spoke in the Son as the seven Spirits through the apostle John in Revelation—Rev. 1:2, 4, 11; 2:1, 7.", "norm_zh": "四第三神借着使徒约翰在哪成为七灵的子里在启示录里说话启一2411二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God thirdly spoke in the Son as the seven Spirits through the apostle John in RevelationRev 12 4 11 21 7"}
{"zh": "五\t神在新约教训里的说话，是借着保罗和约翰完成的—西一25~27，启二二18~19：", "en": "E.\tGod's speaking in the teaching of the New Testament was completed through Paul and John:—Col. 1:25-27; Rev. 22:18-19:", "norm_zh": "五神在新约教训里的说话是借着保罗和约翰完成的西一2527启二二1819", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Gods speaking in the teaching of the New Testament was completed through Paul and JohnCol 12527 Rev 221819"}
{"zh": "2\t全部新约是借着约翰的著作完成的—启二二18~19。", "en": "2.\tThe entire New Testament was completed by John's writings—Rev. 22:18-19.", "norm_zh": "2全部新约是借着约翰的着作完成的启二二1819", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The entire New Testament was completed by Johns writingsRev 221819"}
{"zh": "六\t在子里的这个说话，就是使徒的教训，并不强调诸如洗脚、受浸、蒙头等类的事；这些都不包含在关于神永远经纶之新约启示中，那些基本、内在、中心和基础的事里面—提前一4，多三9。", "en": "F.\tThis speaking in the Son, the apostles' teaching, does not stress matters such as foot-washing, baptism, head covering, etc.; these are not the basic, intrinsic, central, and elementary things contained in the New Testament revelation concerning God's eternal economy.—1 Tim. 1:4; Titus 3:9.", "norm_zh": "六在子里的这个说话就是使徒的教训并不强调诸如洗脚受浸蒙头等类的事这些都不包含在关于神永远经纶之新约启示中哪些基本内在中心和基础的事里面提前一4多三9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F This speaking in the Son the apostles teaching does not stress matters such as footwashing baptism head covering etc these are not the basic intrinsic central and elementary things contained in the New Testament revelation concerning Gods eternal economy1 Tim 14 Titus 39"}
{"zh": "叁\t使徒的教训是神新约经纶的惟一神圣启示，从神的成为肉体到新耶路撒冷的终极完成，由基督在三个神圣奥秘的时期里丰满的职事所完成，为着成就神永远的经纶—弗一10，赛九6，林前十五45，启五6：", "en": "III.\tThe teaching of the apostles is the unique divine revelation of God's New Testament economy from the incarnation of God to the consummation of the New Jerusalem, carried out by the full ministry of Christ in three divine and mystical stages for the fulfillment of God's eternal economy:—Eph. 1:10; Isa. 9:6; 1 Cor. 15:45; Rev. 5:6:", "norm_zh": "叁使徒的教训是神新约经纶的惟一神圣启示从神的成为肉体到新耶路撒冷的终极完成由基督在三个神圣奥秘的时期里丰满的职事所完成为着成就神永远的经纶弗一10赛九6林前十五45启五6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The teaching of the apostles is the unique divine revelation of Gods New Testament economy from the incarnation of God to the consummation of the New Jerusalem carried out by the full ministry of Christ in three divine and mystical stages for the fulfillment of Gods eternal economyEph 110 Isa 96 1 Cor 1545 Rev 56"}
{"zh": "一\t第一个时期，成肉体的时期，乃是为使基督将神带到人里，在人性里彰显神，并完成祂法理的的救赎—赛九6，约八28。", "en": "A.\tThe first stage, the stage of incarnation, is for Christ to bring God into man, to express God in humanity, and to accomplish His judicial redemption.—Isa. 9:6; John 8:28.", "norm_zh": "一第一个时期成肉体的时期乃是为使基督将神带到人里在人性里彰显神并完成祂法理的的救赎赛九6约八28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first stage the stage of incarnation is for Christ to bring God into man to express God in humanity and to accomplish His judicial redemptionIsa 96 John 828"}
{"zh": "二\t第二个时期，总括的时期，乃是为使基督生为神的长子，成为赐生命的灵，并为着祂的身体重生信徒—林前十五45，约十六13。", "en": "B.\tThe second stage, the stage of inclusion, is for Christ to be begotten as God's firstborn Son, to become the life-giving Spirit, and to regenerate the believers for His Body.—1 Cor. 15:45; John 16:13.", "norm_zh": "二第二个时期总括的时期乃是为使基督生为神的长子成为赐生命的灵并为着祂的身体重生信徒林前十五45约十六13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The second stage the stage of inclusion is for Christ to be begotten as Gods firstborn Son to become the lifegiving Spirit and to regenerate the believers for His Body1 Cor 1545 John 1613"}
{"zh": "三\t第三个时期，加强的时期，乃是为使基督加强祂生机的救恩，产生得胜者，并终极完成新耶路撒冷—启四5，五6。", "en": "C.\tThe third stage, the stage of intensification, is for Christ to intensify His organic salvation, to produce the overcomers, and to consummate the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 4:5; 5:6.", "norm_zh": "三第三个时期加强的时期乃是为使基督加强祂生机的救恩产生得胜者并终极完成新耶路撒冷启四5五6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The third stage the stage of intensification is for Christ to intensify His organic salvation to produce the overcomers and to consummate the New JerusalemRev 45 56"}
{"zh": "伍\t使徒的教训是召会的宪法：召会必须持守，并完全在其管制之下—犹3，提前一19，六12，提后四7：", "en": "V.\tThe apostles' teaching is the church's constitution; the church must hold it and be under it absolutely:—Jude 3; 1 Tim. 1:19; 6:12; 2 Tim. 4:7:", "norm_zh": "伍使徒的教训是召会的宪法召会必须持守并完全在其管制之下犹3提前一19六12提后四7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The apostles teaching is the churchs constitution the church must hold it and be under it absolutelyJude 3 1 Tim 119 612 2 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "二\t使徒的教训是召会的宪法，应当普遍的在各处各召会中，同样的教导—林前四17，七17，多一9：", "en": "B.\tThe apostles' teaching, as the church's constitution, should be universally taught everywhere in every church in the same way.—1 Cor. 4:17; 7:17; Titus 1:9:", "norm_zh": "二使徒的教训是召会的宪法应当普遍的在各处各召会中同样的教导林前四17七17多一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The apostles teaching as the churchs constitution should be universally taught everywhere in every church in the same way1 Cor 417 717 Titus 19"}
{"zh": "1\t使徒的教训是为着神的经纶，而这教训是主耶稣健康的话—提前—3~4，六3。", "en": "1. The apostles' teaching is for God's economy, and this teaching is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus—1 Tim. 1:3-4; 6:3.", "norm_zh": "1使徒的教训是为着神的经纶而这教训是主耶稣健康的话提前34六3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The apostles teaching is for Gods economy and this teaching is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus1 Tim 134 63"}
{"zh": "2\t一切教训都必须受使徒教训之界限和范围的限制—一3~4。", "en": "2.\tAll teachings must be restricted by the limit and sphere of the apostles' teaching.—1:3-4.", "norm_zh": "2一切教训都必须受使徒教训之界限和范围的限制一34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All teachings must be restricted by the limit and sphere of the apostles teaching134"}
{"zh": "3\t基督教因为使徒教训界限之外的许多教训，而有许多的路—帖后二9~11。", "en": "3.\tChristianity has many ways because of the many teachings outside the limit of the apostles' teaching.—2 Thes. 2:9-11.", "norm_zh": "3基督教因为使徒教训界限之外的许多教训而有许多的路帖后二911", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Christianity has many ways because of the many teachings outside the limit of the apostles teaching2 Thes 2911"}
{"zh": "4\t今天基督徒中间一切的难处、分裂和混乱，都是由于一件事—不是只注重使徒教训的惟一启示—10~11节。", "en": "4.\tAll the problems, divisions, and confusion among Christians today are due to one thing—not caring only for the unique revelation of the apostles' teaching.—vv. 10-11.", "norm_zh": "4今天基督徒中间一切的难处分裂和混乱都是由于一件事不是只注重使徒教训的惟一启示1011节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 All the problems divisions and confusion among Christians today are due to one thingnot caring only for the unique revelation of the apostles teachingvv 1011"}
{"zh": "三\t在召会中，应当只有一个惟一的教训，就是使徒的教训，而没有不同的教训—15节，加一7~9。", "en": "C.\tIn the church there should be one unique teaching, the apostles' teaching, not different teachings.—v. 15; Gal. 1:7-9.", "norm_zh": "三在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训就是使徒的教训而没有不同的教训15节加一79", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the church there should be one unique teaching the apostles teaching not different teachingsv 15 Gal 179"}
{"zh": "四\t这个宪法，就像每个宪法一样，必须正确的加以解释—彼后三16，提后二15。", "en": "D.\tThis constitution, like every constitution, must be properly interpreted.—2 Pet. 3:16; 2 Tim. 2:15.", "norm_zh": "四这个宪法就像每个宪法一样必须正确的加以解释彼后三16提后二15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D This constitution like every constitution must be properly interpreted2 Pet 316 2 Tim 215"}
{"zh": "陆\t使徒不许可任何与使徒教训不同的教训—加一7~9，约贰9~11：", "en": "VI.\tAny teaching that was different from the apostles' teaching was not allowed by the apostles:—Gal. 1:7-9; 2 John 9-11:", "norm_zh": "陆使徒不许可任何与使徒教训不同的教训加一79约贰911", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Any teaching that was different from the apostles teaching was not allowed by the apostlesGal 179 2 John 911"}
{"zh": "三\t使徒不许可不同的教训，包括旧约时代中那些与神经纶不同的教训—提前一3~4，林后三7、11、13~14。", "en": "C.\tThe different teachings, including those from the Old Testament dispensation that were different from God's economy, were not allowed by the apostles.—1 Tim. 1:3-4; 2 Cor. 3:7, 11, 13-14.", "norm_zh": "三使徒不许可不同的教训包括旧约时代中哪些与神经纶不同的教训提前一34林后三7111314", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The different teachings including those from the Old Testament dispensation that were different from Gods economy were not allowed by the apostles1 Tim 134 2 Cor 37 11 1314"}
{"zh": "四\t使徒把一切与神新约经纶的惟一启示不同的教训，看作是教训之风—弗四14，提前一3~4。", "en": "D.\tAll teachings that were different from the unique revelation of God's New Testament economy were considered by the apostles to be winds of teaching.—Eph. 4:14; 1 Tim. 1:3-4.", "norm_zh": "四使徒把一切与神新约经纶的惟一启示不同的教训看作是教训之风弗四14提前一34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D All teachings that were different from the unique revelation of Gods New Testament economy were considered by the apostles to be winds of teachingEph 414 1 Tim 134"}
{"zh": "柒\t使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素，使我们有一个心、一条路和一个目标—徒一14，二42上，46上，耶三二39：", "en": "VII.\tThe teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord, causing us to have one heart, one way, and one goal.—Acts 1:14; 2:42a, 46a; Jer. 32:39:", "norm_zh": "柒使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素使我们有一个心一条路和一个目标徒一14二42上46上耶三二39", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord causing us to have one heart one way and one goalActs 114 242a 46a Jer 3239"}
{"zh": "一\t与使徒的教训不同的教训，乃是召会败落、堕落、并变质的主要根源—提前一3~7，六3~5、20~21上：", "en": "A.\tDifferent teachings, other than the teaching of the apostles, are the major source of the church's decline, degradation, and deterioration.—1 Tim. 1:3-7; 6:3-5, 20-21a:", "norm_zh": "一与使徒的教训不同的教训乃是召会败落堕落并变质的主要根源提前一37六352021上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Different teachings other than the teaching of the apostles are the major source of the churchs decline degradation and deterioration1 Tim 137 635 2021a"}
{"zh": "二\t我们必须是那些“坚守那按照使徒教训可信靠的话”的人—多一9，帖后二15，启三8：", "en": "B.\tWe must be those who are \"holding to the faithful word, which is according to the teaching of the apostles.\"—Titus 1:9; 2 Thes. 2:15; Rev. 3:8:", "norm_zh": "二我们必须是哪些坚守哪按照使徒教训可信靠的话的人多一9帖后二15启三8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We must be those who are holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching of the apostlesTitus 19 2 Thes 215 Rev 38"}
{"zh": "1\t众召会是按照使徒的教训建立的，并且遵守使徒的教训；召会的秩序，是凭着那按照使徒教训所教导可信靠的话，得以维持的—西一17。", "en": "1\tThe churches were established according to the apostles' teaching and followed their teaching, and the order of the churches was maintained by the faithful word, which was given according to the apostles' teaching.—Col. 1:17.", "norm_zh": "1众召会是按照使徒的教训建立的并且遵守使徒的教训召会的秩序是凭着哪按照使徒教训所教导可信靠的话得以维持的西一17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The churches were established according to the apostles teaching and followed their teaching and the order of the churches was maintained by the faithful word which was given according to the apostles teachingCol 117"}
{"zh": "2\t我们必须讲使徒那合乎健康教训的话，就是神经纶的教训—多二1、7~8，提前六3，一4。", "en": "2\tWe must speak the things that are fitting to the healthy teaching of the apostles, the teaching of God's economy.—Titus 2:1, 7-8; 1 Tim. 6:3; 1:4.", "norm_zh": "2我们必须讲使徒哪合乎健康教训的话就是神经纶的教训多二178提前六3一4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We must speak the things that are fitting to the healthy teaching of the apostles the teaching of Gods economyTitus 21 78 1 Tim 63 14"}
{"zh": "捌\t召会的蒙恩，在于召会坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里—徒一14，二42、46，六7，十六5。", "en": "VIII.\tThe blessing of the church is dependent upon the church's continuing steadfastly in the teaching and fellowship of the apostles.—Acts 1:14; 2:42, 46; 6:7; 16:5.", "norm_zh": "捌召会的蒙恩在于召会坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里徒一14二4246六7十六5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The blessing of the church is dependent upon the churchs continuing steadfastly in the teaching and fellowship of the apostlesActs 114 242 46 67 165"}
{"zh": "教训和交通", "en": "The teaching and the fellowship", "norm_zh": "教训和交通", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The teaching and the fellowship"}
{"zh": "这节里有两件事属于使徒：教训和交通。按我所知，使徒们过去以后，只有一班基督徒曾充分留意这节。从一八二〇年代起，弟兄们非常强调使徒的教训。达秘（J. N. Darby）和其他弟兄会教师强调说，我们必须持续在使徒的教训和使徒的交通里。能必须我们必须持续在两件事里–使徒的教训和使徒的交通。我们若想要持续在使徒的交通里，就必须先持续在使徒的教训里。教训必须在先，然后才有交通。很少基督徒能告诉我们，使徒的教训和使徒的交通是什么。因为这两件事完全被人忽略了，所以整个基督教是混乱和分裂的。今天基督教的特征乃是混乱和分裂。", "en": "In this verse there are two things pertaining to the apostles: the teaching and the fellowship. According to my knowledge, after the apostles, only one group of Christians has paid adequate attention to this verse. Beginning from the 1820s, the Brethren stressed the apostles' teaching very much. John Nelson Darby and other Brethren teachers stressed that we must continue in the apostles' teaching and in the apostles' fellowship. We must continue in two things—the apostles' teaching and the apostles' fellowship. If we want to continue in the apostles' fellowship, we must first continue in the apostles' teaching. Teaching must be first, and then fellowship. Very few Christians can tell us what the apostles' teaching and the apostles' fellowship are. Because these two things have been completely neglected, the entire Christianity is in confusion and division. Today the characteristic of Christianity is confusion and division.", "norm_zh": "这节里有两件事属于使徒教训和交通按我所知使徒们过去以后只有一班基督徒曾充分留意这节从一八二〇年代起弟兄们非常强调使徒的教训达秘JNDarby和其他弟兄会教师强调说我们必须持续在使徒的教训和使徒的交通里能必须我们必须持续在两件事里使徒的教训和使徒的交通我们若想要持续在使徒的交通里就必须先持续在使徒的教训里教训必须在先然后才有交通很少基督徒能告诉我们使徒的教训和使徒的交通是什么因为这两件事完全被人忽略了所以整个基督教是混乱和分裂的今天基督教的特征乃是混乱和分裂", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In this verse there are two things pertaining to the apostles the teaching and the fellowship According to my knowledge after the apostles only one group of Christians has paid adequate attention to this verse Beginning from the 1820s the Brethren stressed the apostles teaching very much John Nelson Darby and other Brethren teachers stressed that we must continue in the apostles teaching and in the apostles fellowship We must continue in two thingsthe apostles teaching and the apostles fellowship If we want to continue in the apostles fellowship we must first continue in the apostles teaching Teaching must be first and then fellowship Very few Christians can tell us what the apostles teaching and the apostles fellowship are Because these two things have been completely neglected the entire Christianity is in confusion and division Today the characteristic of Christianity is confusion and division"}
{"zh": "我们的宪法乃是使徒的教训。我一九六二年十二月来到这个国家，并开始尽职。我在这里尽职事奉，已经超过二十七年了。我从头一年就说，我们所作的每一件事，都必须照着使徒的教训。使徒的教训是我们的宪法。令人悲伤的是：几乎整个基督教都不认识使徒的教训，或者甚至不知道有这件事。我们在这方面从弟兄会得了很多帮助，他们传给我们一些基本、正确的教训，乃是照着使徒教训的。在“使徒的教训”这辞中，“使徒”是复数的，但“教训”是单数的。使徒的教训乃是众使徒的教训，不仅是彼得、约翰或保罗的教训，也是其他一些人的教训。", "en": "Our constitution is the apostles' teaching. I came to this country in December of 1962 and began to minister. I have been ministering here for over twenty-seven years. From the very first year, I said that everything we do must be according to the apostles' teaching. The apostles' teaching is our constitution. Sadly, almost the entire Christianity does not know the apostles' teaching or even that there is such a thing. We received much help in this matter from the Brethren, who passed on to us some basic, correct teachings according to the apostles' teaching. In the term \"the apostles' teaching,\" \"apostles\" is plural, but \"teaching\" is singular. The apostles' teaching is the teaching of the apostles, not only of Peter, John, or Paul, but also of some others.", "norm_zh": "我们的宪法乃是使徒的教训我一九六二年十二月来到这个国家并开始尽职我在这里尽职事奉已经超过二十七年了我从头一年就说我们所作的每一件事都必须照着使徒的教训使徒的教训是我们的宪法令人悲伤的是几乎整个基督教都不认识使徒的教训或者甚至不知道有这件事我们在这方面从弟兄会得了很多帮助他们传给我们一些基本正确的教训乃是照着使徒教训的在使徒的教训这辞中使徒是复数的但教训是单数的使徒的教训乃是众使徒的教训不仅是彼得约翰或保罗的教训也是其他一些人的教训", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Our constitution is the apostles teaching I came to this country in December of 1962 and began to minister I have been ministering here for over twentyseven years From the very first year I said that everything we do must be according to the apostles teaching The apostles teaching is our constitution Sadly almost the entire Christianity does not know the apostles teaching or even that there is such a thing We received much help in this matter from the Brethren who passed on to us some basic correct teachings according to the apostles teaching In the term the apostles teaching apostles is plural but teaching is singular The apostles teaching is the teaching of the apostles not only of Peter John or Paul but also of some others"}
{"zh": "神借着使徒，在是那灵的子里，从行传到启里的说话", "en": "God's speaking in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles from Acts to Revelation", "norm_zh": "神借着使徒在是哪灵的子里从行传到启里的说话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods speaking in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles from Acts to Revelation"}
{"zh": "在使徒行传、使徒保罗的十四封书信、雅各书、彼得的两封书信、约翰的三封书信、犹大书、和启里，神进一步说话。这些全是神在子里的说话。首先，神的说话是在子的人位里。其次，神的说话是在那灵的人位里。神首先在为人的子里，在四福音里说话。在徒、书信和启里，神借着使徒，在是那灵的子里进一步说话。在四福音里，神并不是“借着”一些人说话。但在徒、书信和启里，神借着使徒，在是那灵的子里说话。神在是那灵的子里说话，是借着几位使徒，就是彼得、约翰、保罗、雅各和犹大。整本新约几乎是由这五个人说出来的。", "en": "God spoke further in the Acts, in the fourteen Epistles of the Apostle Paul, in James, in Peter's two Epistles, in John's three Epistles, in Jude, and in Revelation. All these are God's speaking in the Son. First, God's speaking is in the person of the Son. Second, God's speaking is in the person of the Spirit. God spoke first in the Son as the man in the four Gospels. In the Acts, in the Epistles, and in Revelation, God spoke further, in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles. In the four Gospels God did not speak \"through\" someone. But in the Acts, in the Epistles, and in Revelation, God spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles. The apostles through whom God spoke in the Son as the Spirit were only a few. They were Peter, John, Paul, James, and Jude. Nearly the entire New Testament was uttered by these five persons.", "norm_zh": "在使徒行传使徒保罗的十四封书信雅各书彼得的两封书信约翰的三封书信犹大书和启里神进一步说话这些全是神在子里的说话首先神的说话是在子的人位里其次神的说话是在哪灵的人位里神首先在为人的子里在四福音里说话在徒书信和启里神借着使徒在是哪灵的子里进一步说话在四福音里神并不是借着一些人说话但在徒书信和启里神借着使徒在是哪灵的子里说话神在是哪灵的子里说话是借着几位使徒就是彼得约翰保罗雅各和犹大整本新约几乎是由这五个人说出来的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "God spoke further in the Acts in the fourteen Epistles of the Apostle Paul in James in Peters two Epistles in Johns three Epistles in Jude and in Revelation All these are Gods speaking in the Son First Gods speaking is in the person of the Son Second Gods speaking is in the person of the Spirit God spoke first in the Son as the man in the four Gospels In the Acts in the Epistles and in Revelation God spoke further in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles In the four Gospels God did not speak through someone But in the Acts in the Epistles and in Revelation God spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles The apostles through whom God spoke in the Son as the Spirit were only a few They were Peter John Paul James and Jude Nearly the entire New Testament was uttered by these five persons"}
{"zh": "四福音是主耶稣说的话。然后在马太二十八章二十节，祂吩咐门徒，凡祂所吩咐他们的，他们都要教训那些被他们浸入三一神里面的人。马太五、六、七章记载了所谓的山上宝训。马太十三章记载了关于国度之奥秘的七个比喻。马太二十四、二十五章记载了主在橄榄山上所说的预言。太这三段话很美妙。没有一位哲学家或伟大的教师，能说出像这几段里所记载那样有深度、有智慧的话。毫无疑问，使徒们必定将这六章圣经教训在他们以后信主的人。约翰十四、十五、十六和十七章很深奥，远超我们所能领会，这些话却是那人耶稣所说的。耶稣嘱咐祂的信徒，将这几段话教训那些在他们以后跟随的人。四福音的所有内容，必定出使徒们一再的复述。", "en": "The four Gospels were spoken by the Lord Jesus. Then in Matthew 28:20 He told His disciples that whatever He had commanded them, they were to teach to those whom they would baptize into the Triune God. Matthew 5, 6, and 7 record the so-called Sermon on the Mount. Matthew 13 records the seven parables concerning the mystery of the kingdom. Matthew 24 and 25 record the prophecies given by the Lord on the Mount of Olives. These three portions of the Gospel of Matthew are marvelous. No philosopher or great teacher can speak words of depth and wisdom like those recorded in these portions. No doubt these six chapters were taught by the apostles to the believers who came to the Lord after them. John 14, 15, 16, and 17 are profound and far beyond our understanding, yet they were spoken by the man Jesus. Jesus charged His believers to teach these portions to the ones who would follow after them. All the contents of the four Gospels must have been repeated again and again by the apostles.", "norm_zh": "四福音是主耶稣说的话然后在马太二十八章二十节祂吩咐门徒凡祂所吩咐他们的他们都要教训哪些被他们浸入三一神里面的人马太五六七章记载了所谓的山上宝训马太十三章记载了关于国度之奥秘的七个比喻马太二十四二十五章记载了主在橄榄山上所说的预言太这三段话很美妙没有一位哲学家或伟大的教师能说出像这几段里所记载哪样有深度有智慧的话毫无疑问使徒们必定将这六章圣经教训在他们以后信主的人约翰十四十五十六和十七章很深奥远超我们所能领会这些话却是哪人耶稣所说的耶稣嘱咐祂的信徒将这几段话教训哪些在他们以后跟随的人四福音的所有内容必定出使徒们一再的复述", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The four Gospels were spoken by the Lord Jesus Then in Matthew 2820 He told His disciples that whatever He had commanded them they were to teach to those whom they would baptize into the Triune God Matthew 5 6 and 7 record the socalled Sermon on the Mount Matthew 13 records the seven parables concerning the mystery of the kingdom Matthew 24 and 25 record the prophecies given by the Lord on the Mount of Olives These three portions of the Gospel of Matthew are marvelous No philosopher or great teacher can speak words of depth and wisdom like those recorded in these portions No doubt these six chapters were taught by the apostles to the believers who came to the Lord after them John 14 15 16 and 17 are profound and far beyond our understanding yet they were spoken by the man Jesus Jesus charged His believers to teach these portions to the ones who would follow after them All the contents of the four Gospels must have been repeated again and again by the apostles"}
{"zh": "福音书之后有徒，其中有彼得和保罗的说话。然后是保罗所说的十四封书信、雅各所说的一封书信、彼得所说的两封书信、约翰所说的三封书信、以及犹大所说的一封书信。最后是借着约翰所写的启，这是主耶稣成为那灵所说的话。我们仔细读启，就能看见，这是主成了那灵，借着约翰所说的话，因为是约翰写了那卷书。这真是美妙！启二、三章里有七封书信。每封信的开头都是主耶稣在“说”，但每封信到末了却告诉我们：“那灵向众召会所说的话…应当听”。这指明主的说话就是那灵的说话，因为祂就是那灵。（林后三17）这说话借着约翰写出来。写给个别召会的各封书信，也是为着众召会的。（林前四17下，七17下，西四16）这是神的说话。", "en": "After the Gospels we have the Acts, where Peter and Paul spoke. Then we have the fourteen Epistles spoken by Paul, the one Epistle spoken by James, the two Epistles spoken by Peter, the three Epistles spoken by John, and the one Epistle spoken by Jude. Finally, we have Revelation, which the Lord Jesus spoke as the Spirit and which was given through John. In reading Revelation carefully we can realize that this was the word spoken by the Lord as the Spirit through John, because John wrote that book. This is marvelous! In chapters two and three of Revelation there are seven epistles. At the beginning of each epistle it is the Lord Jesus who \"says.\" But at the end of each epistle we are told to \"hear what the Spirit says to the churches.\" This indicates that the Lord's speaking was the Spirit's speaking, because He is the Spirit (2 Cor. 3:17). This speaking was written through John. All the epistles written to individual churches were also for all the churches (1 Cor. 4:17b; 7:17b; Col. 4:16). This is God's speaking.", "norm_zh": "福音书之后有徒其中有彼得和保罗的说话然后是保罗所说的十四封书信雅各所说的一封书信彼得所说的两封书信约翰所说的三封书信以及犹大所说的一封书信最后是借着约翰所写的启这是主耶稣成为哪灵所说的话我们仔细读启就能看见这是主成了哪灵借着约翰所说的话因为是约翰写了哪卷书这真是美妙启二三章里有七封书信每封信的开头都是主耶稣在说但每封信到末了却告诉我们哪灵向众召会所说的话应当听这指明主的说话就是哪灵的说话因为祂就是哪灵林后三17这说话借着约翰写出来写给个别召会的各封书信也是为着众召会的林前四17下七17下西四16这是神的说话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "After the Gospels we have the Acts where Peter and Paul spoke Then we have the fourteen Epistles spoken by Paul the one Epistle spoken by James the two Epistles spoken by Peter the three Epistles spoken by John and the one Epistle spoken by Jude Finally we have Revelation which the Lord Jesus spoke as the Spirit and which was given through John In reading Revelation carefully we can realize that this was the word spoken by the Lord as the Spirit through John because John wrote that book This is marvelous In chapters two and three of Revelation there are seven epistles At the beginning of each epistle it is the Lord Jesus who says But at the end of each epistle we are told to hear what the Spirit says to the churches This indicates that the Lords speaking was the Spirits speaking because He is the Spirit 2 Cor 317 This speaking was written through John All the epistles written to individual churches were also for all the churches 1 Cor 417b 717b Col 416 This is Gods speaking"}
{"zh": "神新约的计划是要使自己成为肉体。（路一30~31、34~35）这是何等美妙！几千年来神仍然是神圣的神，但祂有一个新约的计划。祂这计划的头一步是成为肉体，使祂自己与人调和，好进入人里面。这是神被带进人里面，使祂能将自己与人调和的步骤。神生在一个童女里面，（太一18、20）在马利亚的腹中过了九个月。这样祂就有分于人的血肉之体。（来一2上）祂出生后经过了为人的生活。（徒十38，一21）为人生活是成为肉体的一部分。神成了一个人，为要活在这地上。祂不是成了一个人，然后只留在地上几个小时就回到诸天之上。不，祂留在这里三十三年半之久。祂花了约三十年在一个木匠家里。然后祂开始周游布道。那是祂的生活。祂受了很多苦，祂也历经寒暑，祂知道人常有的一切困扰。", "en": "God's New Testament plan is to incarnate Himself (Luke 1:30-31, 34-35). How wonderful! For thousands of years God remained only the divine God, but He had a New Testament plan. The first step of His plan was the incarnation, to mingle Himself with man so that He could enter into man. This was the step for God to be brought into man so that He could mingle Himself with man. God was born in a virgin (Matt. 1:18, 20) and spent nine months in Mary's womb. In this way He partook of man's blood and flesh (Heb. 2:14a). After His birth He passed through human living (Acts 10:38; 1:21). Human living is a part of the incarnation. God became a man in order to live on this earth. He did not become a man to stay on the earth for only a few hours and then go back to the heavens. No, He stayed here for thirty-three and a half years. He spent approximately thirty years in a carpenter's home. Then He began to travel as a traveling preacher. That was His living. He suffered very much, and He knew the feeling of summer and of winter. He knew all the turmoils common to man.", "norm_zh": "神新约的计划是要使自己成为肉体路一30313435这是何等美妙几千年来神仍然是神圣的神但祂有一个新约的计划祂这计划的头一步是成为肉体使祂自己与人调和好进入人里面这是神被带进人里面使祂能将自己与人调和的步骤神生在一个童女里面太一1820在马利亚的腹中过了九个月这样祂就有分于人的血肉之体来一2上祂出生后经过了为人的生活徒十38一21为人生活是成为肉体的一部分神成了一个人为要活在这地上祂不是成了一个人然后只留在地上几个小时就回到诸天之上不祂留在这里三十三年半之久祂花了约三十年在一个木匠家里然后祂开始周游布道哪是祂的生活祂受了很多苦祂也历经寒暑祂知道人常有的一切困扰", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods New Testament plan is to incarnate Himself Luke 13031 3435 How wonderful For thousands of years God remained only the divine God but He had a New Testament plan The first step of His plan was the incarnation to mingle Himself with man so that He could enter into man This was the step for God to be brought into man so that He could mingle Himself with man God was born in a virgin Matt 118 20 and spent nine months in Marys womb In this way He partook of mans blood and flesh Heb 214a After His birth He passed through human living Acts 1038 121 Human living is a part of the incarnation God became a man in order to live on this earth He did not become a man to stay on the earth for only a few hours and then go back to the heavens No He stayed here for thirtythree and a half years He spent approximately thirty years in a carpenters home Then He began to travel as a traveling preacher That was His living He suffered very much and He knew the feeling of summer and of winter He knew all the turmoils common to man"}
{"zh": "我每天带看期望等看看报纸。最近苏俄在政治上的变动，指明苏联渐渐要成为民主国家。我在等待到底共产中国不久是否会成为民主国家。在但以理二那个预言中的大像，有金头、银胸、银臂、铜腹、铜腰、以及两条铁腿。那像的脚是半铁半泥的，（但二32~33）就是铁与泥混在一起的。当共产党是苏俄惟一统治的党，所有的“泥”都被抹煞。现在泥起来说话了。这帮助我们看见，但以理二那个预言的应验。按照那个预言，主耶稣要回来，如同一块非人手所凿，乃是神所凿出来的石头。这块石头会打在半铁半泥的十隻脚趾头上，把大像的脚砸碎。（但二34）若没有过去这年所发生的事件，但以理二的预言就不能应验。阿利路亚，基督是调度万有的元首！（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一篇）", "en": "Each day I wait with anticipation for the newspaper. Recent political changes in Russia indicate that the Soviet Union is becoming a democratic country. I am waiting to see whether Red China might also become democratic before long. The great image in the prophecy in Daniel chapter two has a head of gold, breasts and arms of silver, an abdomen of brass, and two legs of iron. The feet of that image are partly of iron and partly of clay (Dan. 2:32-33), that is, of iron mixed with clay. When the Communist Party was the only party governing Russia, all the \"clay\" was annulled. Now the clay has risen up to say something. This helps us to see the fulfillment of the prophecy in Daniel 2. According to that prophecy, the Lord Jesus will come back as a stone hewn not by man's hands but by God. This stone will smash the feet of the great image, on the ten toes of clay mixed with iron (Dan. 2:34). Without the events of this previous year, the prophecy in Daniel 2 could not be fulfilled. Hallelujah, Christ is the Leader who manages all things!", "norm_zh": "我每天带看期望等看看报纸最近苏俄在政治上的变动指明苏联渐渐要成为民主国家我在等待到底共产中国不久是否会成为民主国家在但以理二哪个预言中的大像有金头银胸银臂铜腹铜腰以及两条铁腿哪像的脚是半铁半泥的但二3233就是铁与泥混在一起的当共产党是苏俄惟一统治的党所有的泥都被抹煞现在泥起来说话了这帮助我们看见但以理二哪个预言的应验按照哪个预言主耶稣要回来如同一块非人手所凿乃是神所凿出来的石头这块石头会打在半铁半泥的十只脚趾头上把大像的脚砸碎但二34若没有过去这年所发生的事件但以理二的预言就不能应验阿利路亚基督是调度万有的元首李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Each day I wait with anticipation for the newspaper Recent political changes in Russia indicate that the Soviet Union is becoming a democratic country I am waiting to see whether Red China might also become democratic before long The great image in the prophecy in Daniel chapter two has a head of gold breasts and arms of silver an abdomen of brass and two legs of iron The feet of that image are partly of iron and partly of clay Dan 23233 that is of iron mixed with clay When the Communist Party was the only party governing Russia all the clay was annulled Now the clay has risen up to say something This helps us to see the fulfillment of the prophecy in Daniel 2 According to that prophecy the Lord Jesus will come back as a stone hewn not by mans hands but by God This stone will smash the feet of the great image on the ten toes of clay mixed with iron Dan 234 Without the events of this previous year the prophecy in Daniel 2 could not be fulfilled Hallelujah Christ is the Leader who manages all things"}
{"zh": "我们已经看过，在旧约里律法可视为神百姓的成文宪法。在新约里，为着神在祂子民中间的行政，是什么顶替了律法？我们知道是基督顶替了律法，但我们在这里是说到在神的行政这一方面和意义上，是什么顶替了律法。在新约里，乃是使徒的教训顶替了律法。行传二章四十二节说，“他们都坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里”在五旬节那天，三千人得救以后，就立即开始坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里。在旧约神的国里，宪法就是律法；在新约神的国里，宪法乃是使徒的教训。（长老训练（九）长老职分与神命定之路（一），第四章）", "en": "We have seen that in the Old Testament, the law could be considered as the written constitution of God's people. In the New Testament what replaced the law for God's administration among His people? We know that Christ replaced the law, but we are referring to the aspect and sense of replacing the law in God's administration. In the New Testament, the teaching of the apostles replaced the law. Acts 2:42 says, \"And they were continuing steadfastly in the teaching and the fellowship of the apostles.\" Immediately after the three thousand were saved on the day of Pentecost, they began to continue steadfastly in the teaching and the fellowship of the apostles. In the Old Testament kingdom of God, the constitution was the law, and in the New Testament kingdom of God, the constitution is the teaching of the apostles. (Elders' Training, Book 9: Eldership and the God-ordained Way (1), Chapter 4)", "norm_zh": "我们已经看过在旧约里律法可视为神百姓的成文宪法在新约里为着神在祂子民中间的行政是什么顶替了律法我们知道是基督顶替了律法但我们在这里是说到在神的行政这一方面和意义上是什么顶替了律法在新约里乃是使徒的教训顶替了律法行传二章四十二节说他们都坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里在五旬节哪天三千人得救以后就立即开始坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里在旧约神的国里宪法就是律法在新约神的国里宪法乃是使徒的教训长老训练九长老职分与神命定之路一第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have seen that in the Old Testament the law could be considered as the written constitution of Gods people In the New Testament what replaced the law for Gods administration among His people We know that Christ replaced the law but we are referring to the aspect and sense of replacing the law in Gods administration In the New Testament the teaching of the apostles replaced the law Acts 242 says And they were continuing steadfastly in the teaching and the fellowship of the apostles Immediately after the three thousand were saved on the day of Pentecost they began to continue steadfastly in the teaching and the fellowship of the apostles In the Old Testament kingdom of God the constitution was the law and in the New Testament kingdom of God the constitution is the teaching of the apostles Elders Training Book 9 Eldership and the Godordained Way 1 Chapter 4"}
{"zh": "与使徒教训不同的教训，是使徒所不许可的。使徒不许可在惟一信仰之外的其它信仰，（加一7~9）那些越过基督之教训的教训，也是使徒所不许可的。（约贰9~11）不仅如此，各种不同的教训，包括旧约时代中那些与神经纶不同的教训，都是使徒所不许可的。（提前一3~4）（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，新约的职事以及使徒的教训和交通，第二章）", "en": "Teachings different from the teaching of the apostles are not allowed by the apostles. The apostles do not allow any other belief besides the unique faith (Gal. 1:7-9); teachings that go beyond the teaching of Christ are also not allowed by the apostles (2 John 9-11). Furthermore, different teachings of any kind, including those in the Old Testament dispensation that are different from God's economy, are not allowed by the apostles (1 Tim. 1:3-4).", "norm_zh": "与使徒教训不同的教训是使徒所不许可的使徒不许可在惟一信仰之外的其它信仰加一79哪些越过基督之教训的教训也是使徒所不许可的约贰911不仅如此各种不同的教训包括旧约时代中哪些与神经纶不同的教训都是使徒所不许可的提前一34李常受文集一九九三年第一册新约的职事以及使徒的教训和交通第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Teachings different from the teaching of the apostles are not allowed by the apostles The apostles do not allow any other belief besides the unique faith Gal 179 teachings that go beyond the teaching of Christ are also not allowed by the apostles 2 John 911 Furthermore different teachings of any kind including those in the Old Testament dispensation that are different from Gods economy are not allowed by the apostles 1 Tim 134"}
{"zh": "（在主的恢复里，我们必须）为着这一个目标走这一条路，…没有不同的教训。（提前一3~4）我们只接受使徒的教训，（徒二42）就是主耶稣健康的话。（提前六3）…这一条为着一个目标的路是完全在使徒教训的界限和范围里。今天基督徒中间一切的问题、分裂与混乱，都是由于一件事—不顾使徒的教训。许多基督徒教导与使徒的教训不同的事。他们并没有严格地受限制、受约束并被保守在使徒教训的范围里。这一条为着一个目标之路的决定因素，乃是使徒的教训。（李常受文集一九八七年第二册，神命定实行新约经纶的路，第十七章）", "en": "(In the Lord's recovery, we must) take this one way for this one goal... with no different teachings (1 Tim. 1:3-4). We receive only the teaching of the apostles (Acts 2:42), which is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus (1 Tim. 6:3)... This way for the one goal is entirely in the limit and realm of the teaching of the apostles. All the problems, divisions, and confusion among Christians today are due to one thing—the disregard of the teaching of the apostles. Many Christians teach things different from the teaching of the apostles. They are not strictly limited, restricted, and kept in the realm of the teaching of the apostles. The deciding factor of this way for the one goal is the teaching of the apostles.", "norm_zh": "在主的恢复里我们必须为着这一个目标走这一条路没有不同的教训提前一34我们只接受使徒的教训徒二42就是主耶稣健康的话提前六3这一条为着一个目标的路是完全在使徒教训的界限和范围里今天基督徒中间一切的问提分裂与混乱都是由于一件事不顾使徒的教训许多基督徒教导与使徒的教训不同的事他们并没有严格地受限制受约束并被保守在使徒教训的范围里这一条为着一个目标之路的决定因素乃是使徒的教训李常受文集一九八七年第二册神命定实行新约经纶的路第十七章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the Lords recovery we must take this one way for this one goal with no different teachings 1 Tim 134 We receive only the teaching of the apostles Acts 242 which is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus 1 Tim 63 This way for the one goal is entirely in the limit and realm of the teaching of the apostles All the problems divisions and confusion among Christians today are due to one thingthe disregard of the teaching of the apostles Many Christians teach things different from the teaching of the apostles They are not strictly limited restricted and kept in the realm of the teaching of the apostles The deciding factor of this way for the one goal is the teaching of the apostles"}
{"zh": "使徒不许可任何在这独一信仰之外的其它信仰。（加一7~9）加拉太一章八节说，“但即使是我们，或是从天上来的使者，若在我们所传给你们的福音之外，另传一个福音给你们，他就该受咒诅”…使徒在他们的教训上，就是在新约的教训，神完全福音的内容…上，非常严格。", "en": "Any other belief besides this unique faith is not allowed by the apostles (Gal. 1:7-9). Galatians 1:8 says, \"But if even we or an angel out of heaven should preach to you a gospel besides that which we have preached to you, let him be accursed\"... The apostles were very strict in their teaching, that is, in the New Testament teaching, the contents of the full gospel of God...", "norm_zh": "使徒不许可任何在这独一信仰之外的其它信仰加一79加拉太一章八节说但即使是我们或是从天上来的使者若在我们所传给你们的福音之外另传一个福音给你们他就该受咒诅使徒在他们的教训上就是在新约的教训神完全福音的内容上非常严格", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Any other belief besides this unique faith is not allowed by the apostles Gal 179 Galatians 18 says But if even we or an angel out of heaven should preach to you a gospel besides that which we have preached to you let him be accursed The apostles were very strict in their teaching that is in the New Testament teaching the contents of the full gospel of God"}
{"zh": "使徒把一切与神新约经纶的独一启示不同的教训看作是教训之风。（弗四14）…（这些教训之风）的目的是要将人引入撒但错谬的系统。…撒但有一个系统，若是可能，他要将所有的基督徒都引入其中。他这系统的目标，目的，是要将圣徒从神圣启示的中心线上带走，用意是要拦阻，甚至拆毁基督身体的建造。有些教训之风似乎不是邪恶的。然而，邪恶的因素在那里。", "en": "The apostles considered all teachings different from the unique revelation of God's New Testament economy as winds of teaching (Eph. 4:14)... The purpose of (these winds of teaching) is to bring people into Satan's system of error... Satan has a system, and if possible, he wants to bring all Christians into it. The goal, the purpose, of his system is to carry the saints away from the central line of the divine revelation, with the intention of frustrating, even tearing down, the building up of the Body of Christ. Some winds of teaching do not seem to be evil; however, the evil element is there.", "norm_zh": "使徒把一切与神新约经纶的独一启示不同的教训看作是教训之风弗四14这些教训之风的目的是要将人引入撒但错谬的系统撒但有一个系统若是可能他要将所有的基督徒都引入其中他这系统的目标目的是要将圣徒从神圣启示的中心线上带走用意是要拦阻甚至拆毁基督身体的建造有些教训之风似乎不是邪恶的然而邪恶的因素在哪里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The apostles considered all teachings different from the unique revelation of Gods New Testament economy as winds of teaching Eph 414 The purpose of these winds of teaching is to bring people into Satans system of error Satan has a system and if possible he wants to bring all Christians into it The goal the purpose of his system is to carry the saints away from the central line of the divine revelation with the intention of frustrating even tearing down the building up of the Body of Christ Some winds of teaching do not seem to be evil however the evil element is there"}
{"zh": "所有同心合意的人都持续在使徒的教训里", "en": "All those who were one in one accord were continuing in the teaching of the apostles", "norm_zh": "所有同心合意的人都持续在使徒的教训里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "All those who were one in one accord were continuing in the teaching of the apostles"}
{"zh": "在行传一章，地上若没有同心合意，大能大力的灵绝不能浇灌下来。因为那里没有器皿来接受祂，得着祂，盛装祂，并彰显祂。因此，同心合意是极其重要的。那是对神作为的回应，是为着神的行动给神的配搭与合作。主的行动在神的一面倚赖完成的灵，在我们的一面倚赖同心合意。在那灵浇灌下来以前，有一班人在一起同心合意的祷告。（徒一14）那种同心合意乃是预备他们来接受那灵的浇灌。在这浇灌以后，他们仍继续与五旬节那天得救的三千人同心合意。（徒二46）在使徒行传整卷书里，这种同心合意乃是主行动的基本因素。", "en": "If there had been no one accord on the earth in Acts 1, the powerful and dynamic Spirit could have never been poured out. There would have been no vessels to take Him, receive Him, contain Him, and express Him. Thus, the one accord is critical. It is a response to God's doing, a coordination or cooperation offered to God for His move. The Lord's move on God's side depends upon the consummated Spirit and on our side depends upon one accord. Before the pouring out of the Spirit, there was a group of people praying together with one accord (Acts 1:14). That one accord was a preparation for them to receive the pouring out of the Spirit. After this pouring out, they remained and continued in this one accord along with the three thousand saved on the day of Pentecost (Acts 2:46). This one accord was the basic factor of the Lord's move through the entire book of Acts.", "norm_zh": "在行传一章地上若没有同心合意大能大力的灵绝不能浇灌下来因为哪里没有器皿来接受祂得着祂盛装祂并彰显祂因此同心合意是极其重要的哪是对神作为的回应是为着神的行动给神的配搭与合作主的行动在神的一面倚赖完成的灵在我们的一面倚赖同心合意在哪灵浇灌下来以前有一班人在一起同心合意的祷告徒一14哪种同心合意乃是预备他们来接受哪灵的浇灌在这浇灌以后他们仍继续与五旬节哪天得救的三千人同心合意徒二46在使徒行传整卷书里这种同心合意乃是主行动的基本因素", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If there had been no one accord on the earth in Acts 1 the powerful and dynamic Spirit could have never been poured out There would have been no vessels to take Him receive Him contain Him and express Him Thus the one accord is critical It is a response to Gods doing a coordination or cooperation offered to God for His move The Lords move on Gods side depends upon the consummated Spirit and on our side depends upon one accord Before the pouring out of the Spirit there was a group of people praying together with one accord Acts 114 That one accord was a preparation for them to receive the pouring out of the Spirit After this pouring out they remained and continued in this one accord along with the three thousand saved on the day of Pentecost Acts 246 This one accord was the basic factor of the Lords move through the entire book of Acts"}
{"zh": "同心合意这件事在一面控制关于主行动的整个启示。倘若主的一面没有灵，主就完全不可能在地上行动。同样的原则，倘若没有我们这面的同心合意，神也就无法行动。我们必须与神配合。祂如今是完成的灵，我们必须说，“主，我们在这里预备好了，我们同心合意。我们不但要把这同心合意给你，也预备好把这同心合意献上。”在这里立刻有了一种结合，一对夫妻产生了。这时任何事情都能作成。", "en": "On the one hand, this matter of the one accord controls the entire revelation concerning the Lord's move. If there were no Spirit on the Lord's side, it would be absolutely impossible for the Lord to move on the earth. In the same principle, if there were no one accord on our side, God would also be unable to move. We must cooperate with God. He is now the consummated Spirit, and we must say, \"Lord, we are ready here; we are in one accord. We not only want to give this one accord to You, but we are also ready to offer this one accord.\" Immediately there is a union here; a husband and wife are produced. At this time, anything can be done.", "norm_zh": "同心合意这件事在一面控制关于主行动的整个启示倘若主的一面没有灵主就完全不可能在地上行动同样的原则倘若没有我们这面的同心合意神也就无法行动我们必须与神配合祂如今是完成的灵我们必须说主我们在这里预备好了我们同心合意我们不但要把这同心合意给你也预备好把这同心合意献上在这里立刻有了一种结合一对夫妻产生了这时任何事情都能作成", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:35:31.011905+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "On the one hand this matter of the one accord controls the entire revelation concerning the Lords move If there were no Spirit on the Lords side it would be absolutely impossible for the Lord to move on the earth In the same principle if there were no one accord on our side God would also be unable to move We must cooperate with God He is now the consummated Spirit and we must say Lord we are ready here we are in one accord We not only want to give this one accord to You but we are also ready to offer this one accord Immediately there is a union here a husband and wife are produced At this time anything can be done"}
{"zh": "一\t教训和交通成为一组，是使徒的教训和交通，与神的经纶有直接的关系，乃是为着保守召会，就是基督身体的一；二者都是惟一的—41~42节：（1997年夏训，第一篇***）", "en": "A.\tThe teaching and the fellowship form one group, which is of the apostles and related directly to God's economy for the keeping of the oneness of the church, the Body of Christ; both are unique:—vv. 41-42:", "norm_zh": "一教训和交通成为一组是使徒的教训和交通与神的经纶有直接的关系乃是为着保守召会就是基督身体的一二者都是惟一的4142节1997年夏训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The teaching and the fellowship form one group which is of the apostles and related directly to Gods economy for the keeping of the oneness of the church the Body of Christ both are uniquevv 4142"}
{"zh": "1\t使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素—42上、46上节。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八六年第一册，长老训练七—同心合意为着主的行动，第八章，第十四段*）", "en": "1\tThe teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord.—vv. 42a, 46a.", "norm_zh": "1使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素42上46上节1997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八六年第一册长老训练七同心合意为着主的行动第八章第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accordvv 42a 46a"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若将自己限制于使徒的教训之内，就是限制在关于神新约经纶的教训之内，我们就会被保守在一里，也会有一条道路，为着一个目标—41~47节。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九五七年第三册，活神与复活的神，第十七章，第十段*）", "en": "2\tIf we limit ourselves to the apostles' teaching, the teaching concerning God's New Testament economy, we will be kept in oneness and will have one way for one goal.—vv. 41-47.", "norm_zh": "2我们若将自己限制于使徒的教训之内就是限制在关于神新约经纶的教训之内我们就会被保守在一里也会有一条道路为着一个目标4147节1997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九五七年第三册活神与复活的神第十七章第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we limit ourselves to the apostles teaching the teaching concerning Gods New Testament economy we will be kept in oneness and will have one way for one goalvv 4147"}
{"zh": "3\t在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训—使徒的教训；不仅如此，也应当只有一个惟一的交通，而这交通是由使徒的教训所产生的—一14~15，二42。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九五七年第三册，活神与复活的神，第十七章，第十三段*）", "en": "3\tIn the church there should be only one unique teaching—the teaching of the apostles; furthermore, there should be one unique fellowship, which is produced by the apostles' teaching.—1:14-15; 2:42.", "norm_zh": "3在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训使徒的教训不仅如此也应当只有一个惟一的交通而这交通是由使徒的教训所产生的一1415二421997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九五七年第三册活神与复活的神第十七章第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In the church there should be only one unique teachingthe teaching of the apostles furthermore there should be one unique fellowship which is produced by the apostles teaching11415 242"}
{"zh": "4\t任何在使徒的交通之外的交通，都是分裂的；我们的交通必须在使徒的交通之内—罗六17。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八七年第二册，神命定实行新约经纶的路，第十七章，第二段*）", "en": "4\tAny fellowship outside the fellowship of the apostles is divisive; our fellowship must be inside the fellowship of the apostles.—Rom. 6:17.", "norm_zh": "4任何在使徒的交通之外的交通都是分裂的我们的交通必须在使徒的交通之内罗六171997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八七年第二册神命定实行新约经纶的路第十七章第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Any fellowship outside the fellowship of the apostles is divisive our fellowship must be inside the fellowship of the apostlesRom 617"}
{"zh": "二\t擘饼和祷告成为第二组，是信徒之基督徒生活的实行—徒二41~42。（1997年夏训，第一篇；圣经恢复本，徒二42注1*）", "en": "B.\tThe breaking of bread and the prayers form a second group and are practices of the believers' Christian life.—Acts 2:41-42.", "norm_zh": "二擘饼和祷告成为第二组是信徒之基督徒生活的实行徒二41421997年夏训第一篇圣经恢复本徒二42注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The breaking of bread and the prayers form a second group and are practices of the believers Christian lifeActs 24142"}
{"zh": "一\t宇宙中有一件美妙的事，就是神的说话—2节，徒三21，约十30：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第十四段*）", "en": "A.\tIn the universe there is a marvelous matter—God's speaking.—v. 2; Acts 3:21; John 10:30:", "norm_zh": "一宇宙中有一件美妙的事就是神的说话2节徒三21约十301997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the universe there is a marvelous matterGods speakingv 2 Acts 321 John 1030"}
{"zh": "1\t在新约时代，神不是多分多方，或借着申言者，向祂的子民说话—来一2。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九七八年第三册，正当召会生活极重要的原则，第四章，第十七段**）", "en": "1\tIn the New Testament age God does not speak to His people in many portions and in many ways or through the prophets.—Heb. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "1在新约时代神不是多分多方或借着申言者向祂的子民说话来一21997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九七八年第三册正当召会生活极重要的原则第四章第十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In the New Testament age God does not speak to His people in many portions and in many ways or through the prophetsHeb 12"}
{"zh": "2\t在新约时代，神只在子这一个人位里说话—约十四10。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九七八年第一册，与服事者的交通，第一章，第十段*）", "en": "2\tIn the New Testament age God only speaks in one person, the Son.—John 14:10.", "norm_zh": "2在新约时代神只在子这一个人位里说话约十四101997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九七八年第一册与服事者的交通第一章第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the New Testament age God only speaks in one person the SonJohn 1410"}
{"zh": "二\t神首先在为人的子里，在四福音里说话—10节，五24，十六12，十30。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第二十段）", "en": "B.\tGod first spoke in the Son as a man in the four Gospels.—v. 10; 5:24; 16:12; 10:30.", "norm_zh": "二神首先在为人的子里在四福音里说话10节五24十六12十301997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God first spoke in the Son as a man in the four Gospelsv 10 524 1612 1030"}
{"zh": "三\t其次，神借着使徒们，在那成为灵的子里，在使徒行传和二十一卷书信（罗马书到犹大书）里说话—十六12~15，太二八19~20，来二3~4，彼后三15~16，西一25~27。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第二十段**）", "en": "C.\tGod secondly spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles in Acts and the twenty-one Epistles (Romans through Jude)—John 16:12-15; Matt. 28:19-20; Heb. 2:3-4; 2 Pet. 3:15-16; Col. 1:25-27.", "norm_zh": "三其次神借着使徒们在哪成为灵的子里在使徒行传和二十一卷书信罗马书到犹大书里说话十六1215太二八1920来二34彼后三1516西一25271997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God secondly spoke in the Son as the Spirit through the apostles in Acts and the twentyone Epistles Romans through JudeJohn 161215 Matt 281920 Heb 234 2 Pet 31516 Col 12527"}
{"zh": "四\t第三，神借着使徒约翰，在那成为七灵的子里，在启示录里说话—启一2、4、11，二1、7。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第二十段**）", "en": "D.\tGod thirdly spoke in the Son as the seven Spirits through the apostle John in Revelation—Rev. 1:2, 4, 11; 2:1, 7.", "norm_zh": "四第三神借着使徒约翰在哪成为七灵的子里在启示录里说话启一2411二171997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God thirdly spoke in the Son as the seven Spirits through the apostle John in RevelationRev 12 4 11 21 7"}
{"zh": "五\t神在新约教训里的说话，是借着保罗和约翰完成的—西一25~27，启二二18~19：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八九年第四册，使徒的教训与新约中的领导，第一章，第四十三段*）", "en": "E.\tGod's speaking in the teaching of the New Testament was completed through Paul and John:—Col. 1:25-27; Rev. 22:18-19:", "norm_zh": "五神在新约教训里的说话是借着保罗和约翰完成的西一2527启二二18191997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八九年第四册使徒的教训与新约中的领导第一章第四十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Gods speaking in the teaching of the New Testament was completed through Paul and JohnCol 12527 Rev 221819"}
{"zh": "2\t全部新约是借着约翰的著作完成的—启二二18~19。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八九年第四册，使徒的教训与新约中的领导，第一章，第四十三段*）", "en": "2.\tThe entire New Testament was completed by John's writings—Rev. 22:18-19.", "norm_zh": "2全部新约是借着约翰的着作完成的启二二18191997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八九年第四册使徒的教训与新约中的领导第一章第四十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The entire New Testament was completed by Johns writingsRev 221819"}
{"zh": "六\t在子里的这个说话，就是使徒的教训，并不强调诸如洗脚、受浸、蒙头等类的事；这些都不包含在关于神永远经纶之新约启示中，那些基本、内在、中心和基础的事里面—提前一4，多三9。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第十三段**）", "en": "F.\tThis speaking in the Son, the apostles' teaching, does not stress matters such as foot-washing, baptism, head covering, etc.; these are not the basic, intrinsic, central, and elementary things contained in the New Testament revelation concerning God's eternal economy.—1 Tim. 1:4; Titus 3:9.", "norm_zh": "六在子里的这个说话就是使徒的教训并不强调诸如洗脚受浸蒙头等类的事这些都不包含在关于神永远经纶之新约启示中哪些基本内在中心和基础的事里面提前一4多三91997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F This speaking in the Son the apostles teaching does not stress matters such as footwashing baptism head covering etc these are not the basic intrinsic central and elementary things contained in the New Testament revelation concerning Gods eternal economy1 Tim 14 Titus 39"}
{"zh": "叁\t使徒的教训是神新约经纶的惟一神圣启示，从神的成为肉体到新耶路撒冷的终极完成，由基督在三个神圣奥秘的时期里丰满的职事所完成，为着成就神永远的经纶—弗一10，赛九6，林前十五45，启五6：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八九年第四册，使徒的教训与新约中的领导，第一章，第四十七段*；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第一章，第二十六段**）", "en": "III.\tThe teaching of the apostles is the unique divine revelation of God's New Testament economy from the incarnation of God to the consummation of the New Jerusalem, carried out by the full ministry of Christ in three divine and mystical stages for the fulfillment of God's eternal economy:—Eph. 1:10; Isa. 9:6; 1 Cor. 15:45; Rev. 5:6:", "norm_zh": "叁使徒的教训是神新约经纶的惟一神圣启示从神的成为肉体到新耶路撒冷的终极完成由基督在三个神圣奥秘的时期里丰满的职事所完成为着成就神永远的经纶弗一10赛九6林前十五45启五61997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八九年第四册使徒的教训与新约中的领导第一章第四十七段李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第一章第二十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The teaching of the apostles is the unique divine revelation of Gods New Testament economy from the incarnation of God to the consummation of the New Jerusalem carried out by the full ministry of Christ in three divine and mystical stages for the fulfillment of Gods eternal economyEph 110 Isa 96 1 Cor 1545 Rev 56"}
{"zh": "一\t第一个时期，成肉体的时期，乃是为使基督将神带到人里，在人性里彰显神，并完成祂法理的的救赎—赛九6，约八28。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，如何作同工与长老，并如何履行同工与长老的义务，第一章，第二十七段*）", "en": "A.\tThe first stage, the stage of incarnation, is for Christ to bring God into man, to express God in humanity, and to accomplish His judicial redemption.—Isa. 9:6; John 8:28.", "norm_zh": "一第一个时期成肉体的时期乃是为使基督将神带到人里在人性里彰显神并完成祂法理的的救赎赛九6约八281997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册如何作同工与长老并如何履行同工与长老的义务第一章第二十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The first stage the stage of incarnation is for Christ to bring God into man to express God in humanity and to accomplish His judicial redemptionIsa 96 John 828"}
{"zh": "二\t第二个时期，总括的时期，乃是为使基督生为神的长子，成为赐生命的灵，并为着祂的身体重生信徒—林前十五45，约十六13。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，如何作同工与长老，并如何履行同工与长老的义务，第一章，第二十八段*）", "en": "B.\tThe second stage, the stage of inclusion, is for Christ to be begotten as God's firstborn Son, to become the life-giving Spirit, and to regenerate the believers for His Body.—1 Cor. 15:45; John 16:13.", "norm_zh": "二第二个时期总括的时期乃是为使基督生为神的长子成为赐生命的灵并为着祂的身体重生信徒林前十五45约十六131997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册如何作同工与长老并如何履行同工与长老的义务第一章第二十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The second stage the stage of inclusion is for Christ to be begotten as Gods firstborn Son to become the lifegiving Spirit and to regenerate the believers for His Body1 Cor 1545 John 1613"}
{"zh": "三\t第三个时期，加强的时期，乃是为使基督加强祂生机的救恩，产生得胜者，并终极完成新耶路撒冷—启四5，五6。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，如何作同工与长老，并如何履行同工与长老的义务，第一章，第二十九段*）", "en": "C.\tThe third stage, the stage of intensification, is for Christ to intensify His organic salvation, to produce the overcomers, and to consummate the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 4:5; 5:6.", "norm_zh": "三第三个时期加强的时期乃是为使基督加强祂生机的救恩产生得胜者并终极完成新耶路撒冷启四5五61997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册如何作同工与长老并如何履行同工与长老的义务第一章第二十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The third stage the stage of intensification is for Christ to intensify His organic salvation to produce the overcomers and to consummate the New JerusalemRev 45 56"}
{"zh": "伍\t使徒的教训是召会的宪法：召会必须持守，并完全在其管制之下—犹3，提前一19，六12，提后四7：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八八年第一册，为着基督身体的长大与建造，实行合乎圣经彼此互相的聚会之路，并持守使徒的教训作为新约中的领导，第三章，第三段*）", "en": "V.\tThe apostles' teaching is the church's constitution; the church must hold it and be under it absolutely:—Jude 3; 1 Tim. 1:19; 6:12; 2 Tim. 4:7:", "norm_zh": "伍使徒的教训是召会的宪法召会必须持守并完全在其管制之下犹3提前一19六12提后四71997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八八年第一册为着基督身体的长大与建造实行合乎圣经彼此互相的聚会之路并持守使徒的教训作为新约中的领导第三章第三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The apostles teaching is the churchs constitution the church must hold it and be under it absolutelyJude 3 1 Tim 119 612 2 Tim 47"}
{"zh": "二\t使徒的教训是召会的宪法，应当普遍的在各处各召会中，同样的教导—林前四17，七17，多一9：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八八年第三册，受成全以建造基督的身体，第五章，第十一段**）", "en": "B.\tThe apostles' teaching, as the church's constitution, should be universally taught everywhere in every church in the same way.—1 Cor. 4:17; 7:17; Tit. 1:9:", "norm_zh": "二使徒的教训是召会的宪法应当普遍的在各处各召会中同样的教导林前四17七17多一91997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八八年第三册受成全以建造基督的身体第五章第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The apostles teaching as the churchs constitution should be universally taught everywhere in every church in the same way1 Cor 417 717 Tit 19"}
{"zh": "1\t使徒的教训是为着神的经纶，而这教训是主耶稣健康的话—提前—3~4，六3。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九五七年第三册，活神与复活的神，第十六章，第二十七段*）", "en": "1.\tThe apostles' teaching is for God's economy, and this teaching is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus—1 Tim. 1:3-4; 6:3.", "norm_zh": "1使徒的教训是为着神的经纶而这教训是主耶稣健康的话提前34六31997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九五七年第三册活神与复活的神第十六章第二十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The apostles teaching is for Gods economy and this teaching is the healthy words of the Lord Jesus1 Tim 134 63"}
{"zh": "2\t一切教训都必须受使徒教训之界限和范围的限制—一3~4。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八七年第二册，神命定实行新约经纶的路，第十七章，第二段*）", "en": "2.\tAll teachings must be restricted by the limit and sphere of the apostles' teaching.—1:3-4.", "norm_zh": "2一切教训都必须受使徒教训之界限和范围的限制一341997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八七年第二册神命定实行新约经纶的路第十七章第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All teachings must be restricted by the limit and sphere of the apostles teaching134"}
{"zh": "3\t基督教因为使徒教训界限之外的许多教训，而有许多的路—帖后二9~11。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八七年第二册，神命定实行新约经纶的路，第十七章，第八段**）", "en": "3.\tChristianity has many ways because of the many teachings outside the limit of the apostles' teaching.—2 Thess. 2:9-11.", "norm_zh": "3基督教因为使徒教训界限之外的许多教训而有许多的路帖后二9111997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八七年第二册神命定实行新约经纶的路第十七章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Christianity has many ways because of the many teachings outside the limit of the apostles teaching2 Thess 2911"}
{"zh": "4\t今天基督徒中间一切的难处、分裂和混乱，都是由于一件事—不是只注重使徒教训的惟一启示—10~11节。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九五七年第三册，活神与复活的神，第十七章，第四段**）", "en": "4.\tAll the problems, divisions, and confusion among Christians today are due to one thing—not caring only for the unique revelation of the apostles' teaching.—vv. 10-11.", "norm_zh": "4今天基督徒中间一切的难处分裂和混乱都是由于一件事不是只注重使徒教训的惟一启示1011节1997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九五七年第三册活神与复活的神第十七章第四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 All the problems divisions and confusion among Christians today are due to one thingnot caring only for the unique revelation of the apostles teachingvv 1011"}
{"zh": "三\t在召会中，应当只有一个惟一的教训，就是使徒的教训，而没有不同的教训—15节，加一7~9。（1997年夏训，第一篇；使徒行传生命读经，第十二篇，第二十二段**）", "en": "C.\tIn the church there should be one unique teaching, the apostles' teaching, not different teachings.—v. 15; Gal. 1:7-9.", "norm_zh": "三在召会中应当只有一个惟一的教训就是使徒的教训而没有不同的教训15节加一791997年夏训第一篇使徒行传生命读经第十二篇第二十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the church there should be one unique teaching the apostles teaching not different teachingsv 15 Gal 179"}
{"zh": "四\t这个宪法，就像每个宪法一样，必须正确的加以解释—彼后三16，提后二15。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八八年第三册，在一里建造基督的身体，第五章，第三十四段**）", "en": "D.\tThis constitution, like every constitution, must be properly interpreted.—2 Pet. 3:16; 2 Tim. 2:15.", "norm_zh": "四这个宪法就像每个宪法一样必须正确的加以解释彼后三16提后二151997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八八年第三册在一里建造基督的身体第五章第三十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D This constitution like every constitution must be properly interpreted2 Pet 316 2 Tim 215"}
{"zh": "陆\t使徒不许可任何与使徒教训不同的教训—加一7~9，约贰9~11：（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八九年第四册，使徒的教训与新约中的领导，第一章，第二十四段*）", "en": "VI.\tAny teaching that was different from the apostles' teaching was not allowed by the apostles:—Gal. 1:7-9; 2 John 9-11:", "norm_zh": "陆使徒不许可任何与使徒教训不同的教训加一79约贰9111997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八九年第四册使徒的教训与新约中的领导第一章第二十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Any teaching that was different from the apostles teaching was not allowed by the apostlesGal 179 2 John 911"}
{"zh": "三\t使徒不许可不同的教训，包括旧约时代中那些与神经纶不同的教训—提前一3~4，林后三7、11、13~14。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八八年第二册，主恢复中划时代的带领，第二册—带领圣徒实行主所命定的新路，第十二章，第五十四段**）", "en": "C.\tThe different teachings, including those from the Old Testament dispensation that were different from God's economy, were not allowed by the apostles.—1 Tim. 1:3-4; 2 Cor. 3:7, 11, 13-14.", "norm_zh": "三使徒不许可不同的教训包括旧约时代中哪些与神经纶不同的教训提前一34林后三71113141997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八八年第二册主恢复中划时代的带领第二册带领圣徒实行主所命定的新路第十二章第五十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The different teachings including those from the Old Testament dispensation that were different from Gods economy were not allowed by the apostles1 Tim 134 2 Cor 37 11 1314"}
{"zh": "四\t使徒把一切与神新约经纶的惟一启示不同的教训，看作是教训之风—弗四14，提前一3~4。（1997年夏训，第一篇；李常受文集一九八九年第四册，使徒的教训与新约中的领导，第一章，第五十四段*）", "en": "D.\tAll teachings that were different from the unique revelation of God's New Testament economy were considered by the apostles to be winds of teaching.—Eph. 4:14; 1 Tim. 1:3-4.", "norm_zh": "四使徒把一切与神新约经纶的惟一启示不同的教训看作是教训之风弗四14提前一341997年夏训第一篇李常受文集一九八九年第四册使徒的教训与新约中的领导第一章第五十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D All teachings that were different from the unique revelation of Gods New Testament economy were considered by the apostles to be winds of teachingEph 414 1 Tim 134"}
{"zh": "柒\t使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素，使我们有一个心、一条路和一个目标—徒一14，二42上，46上，耶三二39：（2008年冬训，第四篇；李常受文集一九八六年第一册，长老训练，第七册—同心合意为着主的行动，第八章，第十四段*；李常受文集一九八七年第二册，神命定实行新约经纶的路，第十七章，第四段*）", "en": "VII.\tThe teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord, causing us to have one heart, one way, and one goal.—Acts 1:14; 2:42a, 46a; Jer. 32:39:", "norm_zh": "柒使徒的教训是维持同心合意的因素使我们有一个心一条路和一个目标徒一14二42上46上耶三二392008年冬训第四篇李常受文集一九八六年第一册长老训练第七册同心合意为着主的行动第八章第十四段李常受文集一九八七年第二册神命定实行新约经纶的路第十七章第四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The teaching of the apostles is the holding factor of the one accord causing us to have one heart one way and one goalActs 114 242a 46a Jer 3239"}
{"zh": "一\t与使徒的教训不同的教训，乃是召会败落、堕落、并变质的主要根源—提前一3~7，六3~5、20~21上：（2008年冬训，第四篇；提摩太前书生命读经，第二篇，第十三段*）", "en": "A.\tDifferent teachings, other than the teaching of the apostles, are the major source of the church's decline, degradation, and deterioration.—1 Tim. 1:3-7; 6:3-5, 20-21a:", "norm_zh": "一与使徒的教训不同的教训乃是召会败落堕落并变质的主要根源提前一37六352021上2008年冬训第四篇提摩太前书生命读经第二篇第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Different teachings other than the teaching of the apostles are the major source of the churchs decline degradation and deterioration1 Tim 137 635 2021a"}
{"zh": "二\t我们必须是那些“坚守那按照使徒教训可信靠的话”的人—多一9，帖后二15，启三8：（2008年冬训，第四篇；提多书生命读经，第一篇，第二十五段*）", "en": "B.\tWe must be those who are \"holding to the faithful word, which is according to the teaching of the apostles.\"—Titus 1:9; 2 Thes. 2:15; Rev. 3:8:", "norm_zh": "二我们必须是哪些坚守哪按照使徒教训可信靠的话的人多一9帖后二15启三82008年冬训第四篇提多书生命读经第一篇第二十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We must be those who are holding to the faithful word which is according to the teaching of the apostlesTitus 19 2 Thes 215 Rev 38"}
{"zh": "1\t众召会是按照使徒的教训建立的，并且遵守使徒的教训；召会的秩序，是凭着那按照使徒教训所教导可信靠的话，得以维持的—西一17。（2008年冬训，第四篇；提多书生命读经，第一篇，第二十七段*）", "en": "1\tThe churches were established according to the apostles' teaching and followed their teaching, and the order of the churches was maintained by the faithful word, which was given according to the apostles' teaching.—Col. 1:17.", "norm_zh": "1众召会是按照使徒的教训建立的并且遵守使徒的教训召会的秩序是凭着哪按照使徒教训所教导可信靠的话得以维持的西一172008年冬训第四篇提多书生命读经第一篇第二十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The churches were established according to the apostles teaching and followed their teaching and the order of the churches was maintained by the faithful word which was given according to the apostles teachingCol 117"}
{"zh": "2\t我们必须讲使徒那合乎健康教训的话，就是神经纶的教训—多二1、7~8，提前六3，一4。（2008年冬训，第四篇；新约总论，第二百二十二篇，第十段**）", "en": "2\tWe must speak the things that are fitting to the healthy teaching of the apostles, the teaching of God's economy.—Titus 2:1, 7-8; 1 Tim. 6:3; 1:4.", "norm_zh": "2我们必须讲使徒哪合乎健康教训的话就是神经纶的教训多二178提前六3一42008年冬训第四篇新约总论第二百二十二篇第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We must speak the things that are fitting to the healthy teaching of the apostles the teaching of Gods economyTitus 21 78 1 Tim 63 14"}
{"zh": "捌\t召会的蒙恩，在于召会坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里—徒一14，二42、46，六7，十六5。（1997年夏训，第一篇***）", "en": "VIII.\tThe blessing of the church is dependent upon the church's continuing steadfastly in the teaching and fellowship of the apostles.—Acts 1:14; 2:42, 46; 6:7; 16:5.", "norm_zh": "捌召会的蒙恩在于召会坚定持续在使徒的教训和交通里徒一14二4246六7十六51997年夏训第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:36:49.900098+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The blessing of the church is dependent upon the churchs continuing steadfastly in the teaching and fellowship of the apostlesActs 114 242 46 67 165"}
{"zh": "读经：路一78~79，二8~14、32，七41~42、50，十25~37，十五3~32，十七20~24，二四27、44~53，徒二33~36，五31，十36，十七26~27，来一9", "en": "Scripture Reading: Luke 1:78-79; 2:8-14, 32; 7:41-42, 50; 10:25-37; 15:3-32; 17:20-24; 24:27, 44-53; Acts 2:33-36; 5:31; 10:36; 17:26-27; Heb. 1:9", "norm_zh": "读经路一7879二81432七414250十2537十五332十七2024二四274453徒二3336五31十36十七2627来一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Luke 17879 2814 32 74142 50 102537 15332 172024 2427 4453 Acts 23336 531 1036 172627 Heb 19"}
{"zh": "贰\t基督的升天乃是神将祂高举—徒二33~36，五31，来二9，腓二9，弗一22，太二八18：", "en": "II.\tChrist's ascension was God's exaltation of Him—Acts 2:33-36; 5:31; Heb. 2:9; Phil. 2:9; Eph. 1:22; Matt. 28:18:", "norm_zh": "贰基督的升天乃是神将祂高举徒二3336五31来二9腓二9弗一22太二八18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Christs ascension was Gods exaltation of HimActs 23336 531 Heb 29 Phil 29 Eph 122 Matt 2818"}
{"zh": "一\t主被立为主，作万有的主，是要得着万有；祂被立为基督，作神的受膏者，是要完成神的使命—徒二36，十36，来一9。", "en": "A.\tThe Lord was made Lord, the Lord of all, to possess all, and He was made Christ, God's Anointed, to carry out God's commission—Acts 2:36; 10:36; Heb. 1:9.", "norm_zh": "一主被立为主作万有的主是要得着万有祂被立为基督作神的受膏者是要完成神的使命徒二36十36来一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Lord was made Lord the Lord of all to possess all and He was made Christ Gods Anointed to carry out Gods commissionActs 236 1036 Heb 19"}
{"zh": "二\t神将基督高举“在自己的右边，作元首，作救主”—徒五31，太二八18。", "en": "B.\tGod exalted Christ \"to His right hand as Leader and Savior\"—Acts 5:31; Matt. 28:18.", "norm_zh": "二神将基督高举在自己的右边作元首作救主徒五31太二八18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God exalted Christ to His right hand as Leader and SaviorActs 531 Matt 2818"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督在祂的升天里超越阴间（拘留死人的地方）、地（堕落之人行动反对神的地方）、空中（撒但和他黑暗权势行事抵挡神的地方）和诸天（撒但能去的地方）—弗一20~21，四8~10，来四14，七26。", "en": "III.\tChrist in His ascension transcended Hades (where the dead are held), the earth (where fallen men move against God), the air (where Satan and his power of darkness act against God), and all the heavens (where Satan can go)—Eph. 1:20-21; 4:8-10; Heb. 4:14; 7:26.", "norm_zh": "叁基督在祂的升天里超越阴间拘留死人的地方地堕落之人行动反对神的地方空中撒但和他黑暗权势行事抵挡神的地方和诸天撒但能去的地方弗一2021四810来四14七26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Christ in His ascension transcended Hades where the dead are held the earth where fallen men move against God the air where Satan and his power of darkness act against God and all the heavens where Satan can goEph 12021 4810 Heb 414 726"}
{"zh": "肆\t从升天和超越的基督向着召会有一种输供；祂超越的输供包括了三一神一切丰富的分赐—弗一19~23、3~14，三20：", "en": "IV. There is a transmission from the ascended and transcending Christ to the church; His transcending transmission includes all the rich dispensing of the Triune God—Eph. 1:19-23, 3-14; 3:20:", "norm_zh": "肆从升天和超越的基督向着召会有一种输供祂超越的输供包括了三一神一切丰富的分赐弗一1923314三20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV There is a transmission from the ascended and transcending Christ to the church His transcending transmission includes all the rich dispensing of the Triune GodEph 11923 314 320"}
{"zh": "一\t这样包罗一切的输供，不仅将我们带到与成为肉体并钉十字架之基督的联结里，也将我们带到与复活并超越之基督的联结里；在与这位超越之基督的联结里，我们超过了一切消极的事物，并且远远超越它们—一3~14、21~23，二6。", "en": "A.\tSuch an all-inclusive transmission brings us into union not only with the incarnate, crucified Christ but also with the resurrected, ascended Christ; in union with this ascended Christ, we have surpassed all the negative things and transcended above them all—Eph. 1:3-14, 21-23; 2:6.", "norm_zh": "一这样包罗一切的输供不仅将我们带到与成为肉体并钉十字架之基督的联结里也将我们带到与复活并超越之基督的联结里在与这位超越之基督的联结里我们超过了一切消极的事物并且远远超越它们一3142123二6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Such an allinclusive transmission brings us into union not only with the incarnate crucified Christ but also with the resurrected ascended Christ in union with this ascended Christ we have surpassed all the negative things and transcended above them allEph 1314 2123 26"}
{"zh": "二\t超越之基督的输供，是将三一神在基督里所成就、所达到并所得着的，灌注到召会，就是基督的身体里，使万有在基督里归一于一个元首之下—一10、19、22~23，三10、21。", "en": "B.\tThe transmission of the ascended Christ is to transfuse into the church, the Body of Christ, what the Triune God has accomplished, attained, and obtained for the heading up of all things in Christ—Eph. 1:10, 19, 22-23; 3:10, 21.", "norm_zh": "二超越之基督的输供是将三一神在基督里所成就所达到并所得着的灌注到召会就是基督的身体里使万有在基督里归一于一个元首之下一10192223三1021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The transmission of the ascended Christ is to transfuse into the church the Body of Christ what the Triune God has accomplished attained and obtained for the heading up of all things in ChristEph 110 19 2223 310 21"}
{"zh": "三\t超越之基督的输供，也将我们带到基督在祂十二种身分的属天职事里，这些身分是祂在祂的升天里所达到的并得着的，作为耶稣基督之灵全备的供应—腓一19，来八1~2：", "en": "C.\tThe ascended Christ's transmission also brings us into Christ's heavenly ministry in His twelve statuses, which He has attained and obtained in His ascension, for the bountiful supply of the Spirit of Jesus Christ—Phil. 1:19; Heb. 8:1-2:", "norm_zh": "三超越之基督的输供也将我们带到基督在祂十二种身分的属天职事里这些身分是祂在祂的升天里所达到的并得着的作为耶稣基督之灵全备的供应腓一19来八12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The ascended Christs transmission also brings us into Christs heavenly ministry in His twelve statuses which He has attained and obtained in His ascension for the bountiful supply of the Spirit of Jesus ChristPhil 119 Heb 812"}
{"zh": "1\t万有的主—徒二36，十36，罗十四9，腓二11，林后四5，太二一3。", "en": "1.\tThe Lord of all—Acts 2:36; 10:36; Rom. 14:9; Phil. 2:11; 2 Cor. 4:5; Matt. 21:3.", "norm_zh": "1万有的主徒二36十36罗十四9腓二11林后四5太二一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:40:08.838924+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lord of allActs 236 1036 Rom 149 Phil 211 2 Cor 45 Matt 213"}
