{"zh": "最后，二十七节说到末了一个七的七年。这七年乃是为给敌基督与以色列人坚定盟约。但在六十九个七和末七之间有一空档，已经持续将近二千年。（真理课程—第四级（卷二），第三十一课）", "en": "Finally, verse 27 speaks of the last week of seven years. This week will be for Antichrist to make a firm covenant with the people of Israel. Between the sixty-ninth week and the last week, there is a gap, which has already lasted for nearly two thousand years.", "norm_zh": "最后二十七节说到末了一个七的七年这七年乃是为给敌基督与以色列人坚定盟约但在六十九个七和末七之间有一空档已经持续将近二千年真理课程第四级卷二第三十一课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:55:27.090921+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Finally verse 27 speaks of the last week of seven years This week will be for Antichrist to make a firm covenant with the people of Israel Between the sixtyninth week and the last week there is a gap which has already lasted for nearly two thousand years"}
{"zh": "奥秘的时代，恩典时代，召会时代", "en": "The age of mystery, the age of grace, the age of the church", "norm_zh": "奥秘的时代恩典时代召会时代", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:55:27.090921+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The age of mystery the age of grace the age of the church"}
{"zh": "六十二个七之后与七十个七的末一个七之前，中间有一段插入的时间，这时间有多久，并没有启示出来；在其间耶路撒冷和圣所被一王的民（提多的罗马军兵），在主后七十年毁灭；结局必有洪水，并一直到底的争战；荒凉的事已经定了（但九26下）。六十二个七之后与七十个七的末一个七之前，这段插入的时间，是恩典时代，就是召会时代。这也是奥秘的时代。在这段时间里，凡神所已经作的，正在作的，将要作的都是一个奥秘。在这段时间里，基督是神的奥秘（西二2），召会是基督的奥秘（弗三4）。基督和召会是极大的奥秘（弗五32）。启示录十章七节说，这些奥秘在吹第七号的时候就要完全了，完成了，过去了。（李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，圣经中四个七的预言，第一篇）", "en": "After the sixty-two weeks and before the last week of the seventy weeks, there was an interval, the length of which is not revealed and in which was the destruction of the city of Jerusalem and the sanctuary by the people of the prince (the Roman army of Titus) in A.D. 70; and the end of it would be with a flood, and there would be war even to the end; the desolations were determined (Dan. 9:26b). The interval after the sixty-two weeks and before the last week of the seventy weeks is the age of grace and the age of the church. This is also the age of mysteries. In this interval, everything that God did, is doing, and will do is a mystery. In this interval Christ is the mystery of God (Col. 2:2) and the church is the mystery of Christ (Eph. 3:4). Christ and the church are the great mystery (Eph. 5:32). Revelation 10:7 says that these mysteries will be completed, finished, and over at the trumpeting of the seventh trumpet.", "norm_zh": "六十二个七之后与七十个七的末一个七之前中间有一段插入的时间这时间有多久并没有启示出来在其间耶路撒冷和圣所被一王的民提多的罗马军兵在主后七十年毁灭结局必有洪水并一直到底的争战荒凉的事已经定了但九26下六十二个七之后与七十个七的末一个七之前这段插入的时间是恩典时代就是召会时代这也是奥秘的时代在这段时间里凡神所已经作的正在作的将要作的都是一个奥秘在这段时间里基督是神的奥秘西二2召会是基督的奥秘弗三4基督和召会是极大的奥秘弗五32启示录十章七节说这些奥秘在吹第七号的时候就要完全了完成了过去了李常受文集一九九〇年第三册圣经中四个七的预言第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:55:27.090921+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "After the sixtytwo weeks and before the last week of the seventy weeks there was an interval the length of which is not revealed and in which was the destruction of the city of Jerusalem and the sanctuary by the people of the prince the Roman army of Titus in AD 70 and the end of it would be with a flood and there would be war even to the end the desolations were determined Dan 926b The interval after the sixtytwo weeks and before the last week of the seventy weeks is the age of grace and the age of the church This is also the age of mysteries In this interval everything that God did is doing and will do is a mystery In this interval Christ is the mystery of God Col 22 and the church is the mystery of Christ Eph 34 Christ and the church are the great mystery Eph 532 Revelation 107 says that these mysteries will be completed finished and over at the trumpeting of the seventh trumpet"}
{"zh": "根据我的观察，我有一个很深的感觉，有史以来，没有一个差会、传道会、基督教团体、或大布道家，不盼望他们传道的门大开，但至终没有一个差会、传道会、基督教团体、或是大布道家，实现这个心愿。凯瑞威廉（William Carey）到印度，李文斯敦（David Livingstone）到非洲，戴德生（Hudson Taylor）到中国内地，都没有借着他们将福音传遍全地。然而今天向着主的恢复，全世界都开了。这一点不是夸大，若是我们有一千位弟兄姊妹，个个立刻都能被打发出去；因为欧洲开了，纽西兰开了，澳洲开了，甚至东欧、非洲、南美、中美都开了。来自全球各大洲的信，一封封都是和我们交通需要人去。然而人在哪里？即使仅仅为应付台湾，甚至台北的需要，我们都已经人手不足了，何况全地。人在哪里？（李常受文集一九八六年第二册，福乐的人生，第四篇）", "en": "Based on my observation, I have a deep feeling. Since the dawn of history there has never been a mission, an evangelical group, a Christian organization, or a great evangelist that did not want the door of the gospel to be opened to them; yet none of them has had their desire fulfilled. William Carey went to India, David Livingstone went to Africa, and Hudson Taylor went to inland China, but the gospel was not spread to the whole earth through them. However, today the whole world is opened to the Lord's recovery. This is not an exaggeration. If we have one thousand brothers and sisters, each one can immediately be sent out, because Western Europe is opened, New Zealand is opened, Australia is opened, and even Eastern Europe, Africa, South America, and Central America are all opened up. Every letter sent to us from the major continents all over the globe has fellowshipped with us regarding the need for people to go. But where are the people? We do not have enough people even to meet the need of Taiwan, or even just Taipei, not to mention the whole earth. Where are the people?", "norm_zh": "根据我的观察我有一个很深的感觉有史以来没有一个差会传道会基督教团体或大布道家不盼望他们传道的门大开但至终没有一个差会传道会基督教团体或是大布道家实现这个心愿凯瑞威廉WilliamCarey到印度李文斯敦DavidLivingstone到非洲戴德生HudsonTaylor到中国内地都没有借着他们将福音传遍全地然而今天向着主的恢复全世界都开了这一点不是夸大若是我们有一千位弟兄姊妹个个立刻都能被打发出去因为欧洲开了纽西兰开了澳洲开了甚至东欧非洲南美中美都开了来自全球各大洲的信一封封都是和我们交通需要人去然而人在哪里即使仅仅为应付台湾甚至台北的需要我们都已经人手不足了何况全地人在哪里李常受文集一九八六年第二册福乐的人生第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:55:27.090921+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Based on my observation I have a deep feeling Since the dawn of history there has never been a mission an evangelical group a Christian organization or a great evangelist that did not want the door of the gospel to be opened to them yet none of them has had their desire fulfilled William Carey went to India David Livingstone went to Africa and Hudson Taylor went to inland China but the gospel was not spread to the whole earth through them However today the whole world is opened to the Lords recovery This is not an exaggeration If we have one thousand brothers and sisters each one can immediately be sent out because Western Europe is opened New Zealand is opened Australia is opened and even Eastern Europe Africa South America and Central America are all opened up Every letter sent to us from the major continents all over the globe has fellowshipped with us regarding the need for people to go But where are the people We do not have enough people even to meet the need of Taiwan or even just Taipei not to mention the whole earth Where are the people"}
{"zh": "保罗在提后四章一节对提摩太说：“我在神并那将要审判活人死人的基督耶稣面前，凭着祂的显现和祂的国度，郑重地嘱咐你。”那是保罗将要殉道之时的劝勉。他说他美好的仗已经打过了。当跑的赛程已经跑尽了，当守的信仰也已经守住；在审判台前他必要得公义冠冕的赏赐；这冠冕也是赐给凡爱慕祂显现的人（提后四6~8）。他以审判和国度提醒提摩太，也提醒我仰，要过一个爱慕主显现的生活，这会叫我们不灰心、不退后、不软弱，忠心到底。", "en": "In 2 Timothy 4:1 Paul said to Timothy, \"I solemnly charge you before God and Christ Jesus, who is about to judge the living and the dead, and by His appearing and His kingdom.\" This is an exhortation from Paul immediately before his martyrdom. He said that he had fought the good fight, he had finished the course, and he had kept the faith, and that at the judgment seat he would be awarded the crown of righteousness, which would be awarded to all those who have loved His appearing (2 Tim. 4:6-8). He reminded Timothy, and also us, by the Lord's judgment and kingdom that we should have a living that loves the Lord's appearing. This will cause us not to be discouraged, not to backslide, not to become weak, but to remain faithful to the end.", "norm_zh": "保罗在提后四章一节对提摩太说我在神并哪将要审判活人死人的基督耶稣面前凭着祂的显现和祂的国度郑重地嘱咐你哪是保罗将要殉道之时的劝勉他说他美好的仗已经打过了当跑的赛程已经跑尽了当守的信仰也已经守住在审判台前他必要得公义冠冕的赏赐这冠冕也是赐给凡爱慕祂显现的人提后四68他以审判和国度提醒提摩太也提醒我仰要过一个爱慕主显现的生活这会叫我们不灰心不退后不软弱忠心到底", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:55:27.090921+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In 2 Timothy 41 Paul said to Timothy I solemnly charge you before God and Christ Jesus who is about to judge the living and the dead and by His appearing and His kingdom This is an exhortation from Paul immediately before his martyrdom He said that he had fought the good fight he had finished the course and he had kept the faith and that at the judgment seat he would be awarded the crown of righteousness which would be awarded to all those who have loved His appearing 2 Tim 468 He reminded Timothy and also us by the Lords judgment and kingdom that we should have a living that loves the Lords appearing This will cause us not to be discouraged not to backslide not to become weak but to remain faithful to the end"}
{"zh": "壹\t给帖撒罗尼迦人的两封书信是在主来临的光中写成的；主的来临（希腊文，parousia，巴路西亚）就是主的同在—帖前四15，太二四3，帖后二19：（2005年夏训，第十篇；新约总论，第三百五十九篇，第三段*；圣经恢复本，帖前二19注1*）", "en": "I.\tThe two Epistles to the Thessalonians were written in the light of the Lord's coming; the Lord's coming (Gk. *parousia*) is His presence:—1 Thes. 4:15; Matt. 24:3; 2 Thes. 2:1, 9:", "norm_zh": "壹给帖撒罗尼迦人的两封书信是在主来临的光中写成的主的来临希腊文parousia巴路西亚就是主的同在帖前四15太二四3帖后二192005年夏训第十篇新约总论第三百五十九篇第三段圣经恢复本帖前二19注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The two Epistles to the Thessalonians were written in the light of the Lords coming the Lords coming Gk parousia is His presence1 Thes 415 Matt 243 2 Thes 21 9"}
{"zh": "一\t帖撒罗尼迦前书每章都结束于主的来临；这说明著者保罗是生活工作在主的来临前，以此为吸引、鼓励、目标并警惕—一10，二19，三13，四15~18，五23。（2005年夏训，第十篇；新约总论，第三百五十九篇，第三段*）", "en": "A. Every chapter of 1 Thessalonians ends with the coming of the Lord; this shows that the writer, Paul, lived and worked with the Lord’s coming before him, taking it as an attraction, an incentive, a goal, and a warning—1 Thes. 1:10; 2:19; 3:13; 4:15-18; 5:23.", "norm_zh": "一帖撒罗尼迦前书每章都结束于主的来临这说明着者保罗是生活工作在主的来临前以此为吸引鼓励目标并警惕一10二19三13四1518五232005年夏训第十篇新约总论第三百五十九篇第三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Every chapter of 1 Thessalonians ends with the coming of the Lord this shows that the writer Paul lived and worked with the Lords coming before him taking it as an attraction an incentive a goal and a warning1 Thes 110 219 313 41518 523"}
{"zh": "二\t在三年半（就是但以理九章二十七节里末七的后半）之大灾难的末了，大体的信徒，包括死了又复活以及活着的，都要被提到基督在空中的同在（巴路西亚）里；帖前四章十六至十七节说到这种被提，这与启示录十四章十四至十六节的收割庄稼相符。（2005年夏训，第十篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，圣经中四个“七”的预言，第一章，第七十五段*；帖撒罗尼迦后书生命读经，第二篇，第十三段*；李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，圣经中四个“七”的预言，第六章，第二十五段**）", "en": "B.\tAt the end of the three and a half years of the great tribulation, the second half of the last week in Daniel 9:27, the majority of the believers, both the dead (who will be resurrected) and the living, will be raptured into Christ's presence (*parousia*) in the air; 1 Thessalonians 4:16-17 speaks of this rapture, which corresponds to the reaping of the harvest in Revelation 14:14-16.", "norm_zh": "二在三年半就是但以理九章二十七节里末七的后半之大灾难的末了大体的信徒包括死了又复活以及活着的都要被提到基督在空中的同在巴路西亚里帖前四章十六至十七节说到这种被提这与启示录十四章十四至十六节的收割庄稼相符2005年夏训第十篇李常受文集一九九〇年第三册圣经中四个七的预言第一章第七十五段帖撒罗尼迦后书生命读经第二篇第十三段李常受文集一九九〇年第三册圣经中四个七的预言第六章第二十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B At the end of the three and a half years of the great tribulation the second half of the last week in Daniel 927 the majority of the believers both the dead who will be resurrected and the living will be raptured into Christs presence parousia in the air 1 Thessalonians 41617 speaks of this rapture which corresponds to the reaping of the harvest in Revelation 141416"}
{"zh": "一\t首先，七个七（四十九年）的截定，是从出令重新修建耶路撒冷，到重建完成—尼二1~8，但九25。（2012年冬训，第四篇；圣经恢复本，但九25注2）", "en": "A.\tFirst, seven weeks (forty-nine years) were apportioned from the issuing of the decree to restore and rebuild Jerusalem to the completion of the rebuilding;—Neh. 2:1-8; Dan. 9:25.", "norm_zh": "一首先七个七四十九年的截定是从出令重新修建耶路撒冷到重建完成尼二18但九252012年冬训第四篇圣经恢复本但九25注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A First seven weeks fortynine years were apportioned from the issuing of the decree to restore and rebuild Jerusalem to the completion of the rebuildingNeh 218 Dan 925"}
{"zh": "二\t第二，六十二个七（四百三十四年）的截定，是从耶路撒冷重建完成，到弥赛亚被剪除（钉十字架）—25~26节。（2012年冬训，第四篇；圣经恢复本，但九25注2）", "en": "B.\tSecond, sixty-two weeks (434 years) were apportioned from the completion of the rebuilding of Jerusalem to the cutting off (crucifixion) of the Messiah;—vv. 25-26.", "norm_zh": "二第二六十二个七四百三十四年的截定是从耶路撒冷重建完成到弥赛亚被剪除钉十字架2526节2012年冬训第四篇圣经恢复本但九25注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Second sixtytwo weeks 434 years were apportioned from the completion of the rebuilding of Jerusalem to the cutting off crucifixion of the Messiahvv 2526"}
{"zh": "三\t第三，末七的七年，将是敌基督与以色列人坚定盟约之时；这七年之半他要毁约，使以色列对神的祭祀和供献止息，并逼迫敬畏神的人；这将是持续三年半之大灾难的开始—27节，启十三：（2005年夏训，第十篇；圣经恢复本，但九25注2；李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，神命定之路最新的陈明与基督来临的兆头，第六章，第十六段**；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，结常存的果子讨主喜悦，第十二章，第六段*）", "en": "C. Third, the last week of seven years will be for Antichrist to make a firm covenant with the people of Israel; in the middle of that week, he will break the covenant, terminate Israel's sacrifices and oblations to God, and persecute those who fear God; this will be the beginning of the great tribulation, which will last for three and a half years.—v. 27; Rev. 13:", "norm_zh": "三第三末七的七年将是敌基督与以色列人坚定盟约之时这七年之半他要毁约使以色列对神的祭祀和供献止息并逼迫敬畏神的人这将是持续三年半之大灾难的开始27节启十三2005年夏训第十篇圣经恢复本但九25注2李常受文集一九九〇年第三册神命定之路最新的陈明与基督来临的兆头第六章第十六段李常受文集一九九〇年第一册结常存的果子讨主喜悦第十二章第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Third the last week of seven years will be for Antichrist to make a firm covenant with the people of Israel in the middle of that week he will break the covenant terminate Israels sacrifices and oblations to God and persecute those who fear God this will be the beginning of the great tribulation which will last for three and a half yearsv 27 Rev 13"}
{"zh": "2\t在大灾难开始时，敌基督的像要被当作偶像立在殿中，并且他要坐在神的殿中，高举自己超过一切受人敬拜的对象；这意思是圣殿必须在大灾难开始之前重建—15、21节，启十三14~15，帖后二3~4，但十一36~37。（2005年夏训，第十篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，圣经中四个“七”的预言，第二章，第四段**）", "en": "2. At the beginning of the great tribulation, Antichrist's image will be set up in the temple as an idol and he will sit in the temple of God, exalting himself above every object of worship; this means that the temple must be rebuilt before the great tribulation begins—vv. 15, 21; Rev. 13:14-15; 2 Thes. 2:3-4; Dan. 11:36-37.", "norm_zh": "2在大灾难开始时敌基督的像要被当作偶像立在殿中并且他要坐在神的殿中高举自己超过一切受人敬拜的对象这意思是圣殿必须在大灾难开始之前重建1521节启十三1415帖后二34但十一36372005年夏训第十篇李常受文集一九九〇年第三册圣经中四个七的预言第二章第四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 At the beginning of the great tribulation Antichrists image will be set up in the temple as an idol and he will sit in the temple of God exalting himself above every object of worship this means that the temple must be rebuilt before the great tribulation beginsvv 15 21 Rev 131415 2 Thes 234 Dan 113637"}
{"zh": "1\t在这时代中，基督秘密的、奥秘的在新造里建造召会，作祂的身体和新妇—太十六18，弗五25~32。（2005年夏训，第十篇；圣经恢复本，但九25注2）", "en": "1.\tDuring this age Christ is secretly and mysteriously building up the church in the new creation to be His Body and His bride.—Matt. 16:18; Eph. 5:25-32.", "norm_zh": "1在这时代中基督秘密的奥秘的在新造里建造召会作祂的身体和新妇太十六18弗五25322005年夏训第十篇圣经恢复本但九25注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 During this age Christ is secretly and mysteriously building up the church in the new creation to be His Body and His brideMatt 1618 Eph 52532"}
{"zh": "一\t每一次神要有时代的行动，就是转移时代的行动，祂都必须得着祂时代的器皿；我们必须是在末后日子对神有时代价值的人，以转移时代─启十二5~11，一20，但十二3，九23，十11、19。（2005年感恩节特会，第六篇；译自“圣洁没有瑕疵”英文版附**）", "en": "A.\tEvery time God wants to make a dispensational move, an age-turning move, He must obtain His dispensational instrument; we must be those who have dispensational value to God in the last days to turn the age.—Rev. 12:5-11; 1:20; Dan. 12:3; 9:23; 10:11, 19.", "norm_zh": "一每一次神要有时代的行动就是转移时代的行动祂都必须得着祂时代的器皿我们必须是在末后日子对神有时代价值的人以转移时代启十二511一20但十二3九23十11192005年感恩节特会第六篇译自圣洁没有瑕疵英文版附", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Every time God wants to make a dispensational move an ageturning move He must obtain His dispensational instrument we must be those who have dispensational value to God in the last days to turn the ageRev 12511 120 Dan 123 923 1011 19"}
{"zh": "二\t神永远经纶的目标，就是神圣历史在人类历史中的目标，乃是要得着团体的基督，就是基督与祂的得胜者如同砸人的石头，作祂时代的器皿，以结束这时代，并且成为一座大山，就是神的国─二28、31~45，珥三11，启十二1~2、5，十四1~5，十九7~21。（2005年感恩节特会，第六篇；但以理书生命读经，第十二篇，第十五段**）", "en": "B.\tThe goal of God's eternal economy, the goal of the divine history within human history, is to have the corporate Christ, Christ with His overcomers, as the crushing stone to be His dispensational instrument to end this age and become a great mountain, the kingdom of God.—Dan. 2:28, 31-45; Joel 3:11; Rev. 12:1-2, 5; 14:1-5; 19:7-21.", "norm_zh": "二神永远经纶的目标就是神圣历史在人类历史中的目标乃是要得着团体的基督就是基督与祂的得胜者如同砸人的石头作祂时代的器皿以结束这时代并且成为一座大山就是神的国二283145珥三11启十二125十四15十九7212005年感恩节特会第六篇但以理书生命读经第十二篇第十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The goal of Gods eternal economy the goal of the divine history within human history is to have the corporate Christ Christ with His overcomers as the crushing stone to be His dispensational instrument to end this age and become a great mountain the kingdom of GodDan 228 3145 Joel 311 Rev 1212 5 1415 19721"}
{"zh": "三\t简单的说，恢复就是得胜；在主的恢复里，就是在主的得胜里，预备作祂得胜的新妇，使祂得以回来─二7，三21，十九7~9。（2005年感恩节特会，第六篇；李常受文集一九八六年第二册，福乐的人生，第四章，第十一段**）", "en": "C.\tSimply speaking, recovery is to overcome; to be in the Lord's recovery is to be in the Lord's overcoming, being prepared to be His overcoming bride for His return.—Rev. 2:7; 3:21; 19:7-9.", "norm_zh": "三简单的说恢复就是得胜在主的恢复里就是在主的得胜里预备作祂得胜的新妇使祂得以回来二7三21十九792005年感恩节特会第六篇李常受文集一九八六年第二册福乐的人生第四章第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Simply speaking recovery is to overcome to be in the Lords recovery is to be in the Lords overcoming being prepared to be His overcoming bride for His returnRev 27 321 1979"}
{"zh": "伍\t主要像贼一样，隐密的临到那些爱祂的人，把他们当作宝贝偷去，带到祂诸天之上的同在里；因此，我们必须儆醒并预备自己成为祂的新妇—但十19，太二四42~44，二五13，启十九7，二二20：（2005年夏训，第十篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第三册，神命定之路最新的陈明与基督来临的兆头，第七章，第三十四段**）", "en": "V. The Lord will come secretly as a thief to those who love Him and will steal them away as His treasures to bring them into His presence in the heavens; hence, we must watch and make ourselves ready to be His bride—Dan. 10:19; Matt. 24:42-44; 25:13; Rev. 19:7; 22:20:", "norm_zh": "伍主要像贼一样隐密的临到哪些爱祂的人把他们当作宝贝偷去带到祂诸天之上的同在里因此我们必须儆醒并预备自己成为祂的新妇但十19太二四4244二五13启十九7二二202005年夏训第十篇李常受文集一九九〇年第三册神命定之路最新的陈明与基督来临的兆头第七章第三十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The Lord will come secretly as a thief to those who love Him and will steal them away as His treasures to bring them into His presence in the heavens hence we must watch and make ourselves ready to be His brideDan 1019 Matt 244244 2513 Rev 197 2220"}
{"zh": "五\t我们必须为着我们的祷告生活儆醒、警觉，与内住、圣别的灵合作，过喜乐、祷告并谢恩的生活；这样的生活对神是荣耀，对神的仇敌是羞辱—太二五13，帖前五16~18。（2005年夏训，第十篇；圣经恢复本，弗六18注3**；帖撒罗尼迦前书生命读经，第十八篇，第二十九段*）", "en": "E.\tWe must be watchful, on the alert, for our prayer life, cooperating with the indwelling, sanctifying Spirit to live a rejoicing, praying, and thanking life as a glory to God and a shame to His enemy.—Matt. 25:13; 1 Thes. 5:16-18.", "norm_zh": "五我们必须为着我们的祷告生活儆醒警觉与内住圣别的灵合作过喜乐祷告并谢恩的生活这样的生活对神是荣耀对神的仇敌是羞辱太二五13帖前五16182005年夏训第十篇圣经恢复本弗六18注3帖撒罗尼迦前书生命读经第十八篇第二十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T04:57:27.393559+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E We must be watchful on the alert for our prayer life cooperating with the indwelling sanctifying Spirit to live a rejoicing praying and thanking life as a glory to God and a shame to His enemyMatt 2513 1 Thes 51618"}
{"zh": "读经：启十九11、14，二十4~6，但二31~35，创十一4、9，摩九11，徒十五16，太十九28，腓三11~14，路十四14", "en": "Scripture Reading: Rev. 19:11, 14; 20:4-6; Dan. 2:31-35; Gen. 11:4, 9; Amos 9:11; Acts 15:16; Matt. 19:28; Phil. 3:11-14; Luke 14:14", "norm_zh": "读经启十九1114二十46但二3135创十一49摩九11徒十五16太十九28腓三1114路十四14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Rev 1911 14 2046 Dan 23135 Gen 114 9 Amos 911 Acts 1516 Matt 1928 Phil 31114 Luke 1414"}
{"zh": "二\t在生命上，基督要扩增为召会；在行政上，基督要扩增为国度—约三29~30，可四26，但二35。", "en": "B.\tIn life Christ increases to become the church; in administration Christ increases to become the kingdom—John 3:29-30; Mark 4:26; Dan. 2:35.", "norm_zh": "二在生命上基督要扩增为召会在行政上基督要扩增为国度约三2930可四26但二35", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In life Christ increases to become the church in administration Christ increases to become the kingdomJohn 32930 Mark 426 Dan 235"}
{"zh": "贰\t“到那日，我必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕，堵住其中的破口，把那毁坏的建立起来，重新修造，像古时一样”—摩九11，徒十五16：", "en": "II.\t\"In that day I will raise up / The fallen tabernacle of David, / And I will wall up its breaches / And raise up its ruins / And build it up as it was in the days of old\"—Amos 9:11; Acts 15:16:", "norm_zh": "贰到哪日我必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕堵住其中的破口把哪毁坏的建立起来重新修造像古时一样摩九11徒十五16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II In that day I will raise up The fallen tabernacle of David And I will wall up its breaches And raise up its ruins And build it up as it was in the days of oldAmos 911 Acts 1516"}
{"zh": "一\t大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室—摩九11，徒十五16~18：", "en": "A.\tThe tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of David—Amos 9:11; Acts 15:16-18:", "norm_zh": "一大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室摩九11徒十五1618", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of DavidAmos 911 Acts 151618"}
{"zh": "1\t古时王室与国乃是一；大卫的国就是大卫的王室—摩九11。", "en": "1\tIn ancient times the royal family and the kingdom were one; David's kingdom was David's royal family.—Amos 9:11.", "norm_zh": "1古时王室与国乃是一大卫的国就是大卫的王室摩九11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In ancient times the royal family and the kingdom were one Davids kingdom was Davids royal familyAmos 911"}
{"zh": "3\t在阿摩司九章十一节，神进来应许，有一日祂必建立“大卫倒塌的帐幕”，也就是恢复倒塌的大卫之国；在那日，大卫的国和大卫的王室要得着复兴，万国必称为耶和华名下的国─11、12节。", "en": "3\tIn Amos 9:11 God came in to promise that one day He would raise up \"the fallen tabernacle of David,\" that is, restore the fallen kingdom of David; in that day the kingdom of David and the family of David will be restored, and all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovah—vv. 11, 12.", "norm_zh": "3在阿摩司九章十一节神进来应许有一日祂必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕也就是恢复倒塌的大卫之国在哪日大卫的国和大卫的王室要得着复兴万国必称为耶和华名下的国1112节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In Amos 911 God came in to promise that one day He would raise up the fallen tabernacle of David that is restore the fallen kingdom of David in that day the kingdom of David and the family of David will be restored and all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovahvv 11 12"}
{"zh": "b\t千年国的属地部分，乃是人子的国，弥赛亚国，就是大卫的帐幕—太十三41，启十一15，撒下七13，摩九11。", "en": "b. The earthly part of the millennium is the kingdom of the Son of Man, the kingdom of the Messiah, even the tabernacle of David—Matt. 13:41; Rev. 11:15; 2 Sam. 7:13; Amos 9:11.", "norm_zh": "b千年国的属地部分乃是人子的国弥赛亚国就是大卫的帐幕太十三41启十一15撒下七13摩九11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The earthly part of the millennium is the kingdom of the Son of Man the kingdom of the Messiah even the tabernacle of DavidMatt 1341 Rev 1115 2 Sam 713 Amos 911"}
{"zh": "（一）这是复兴的以色列国，大卫的国，为着得救的犹太人—徒一6，可十一10，路一32~33，撒下七12~13。", "en": "1) This is the restored nation of Israel, the kingdom of David, for the saved Jews—Acts 1:6; Mark 11:10; Luke 1:32-33; 2 Sam. 7:12-13.", "norm_zh": "一这是复兴的以色列国大卫的国为着得救的犹太人徒一6可十一10路一3233撒下七1213", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This is the restored nation of Israel the kingdom of David for the saved JewsActs 16 Mark 1110 Luke 13233 2 Sam 71213"}
{"zh": "（二）在大卫复兴的国里，基督作为人子，大卫王室的后裔，要作以色列人的王—摩九11，太一1，十九28，二五31。", "en": "2) In the restored kingdom of David, Christ as the Son of Man, David's royal descendant, will be the King over the children of Israel—Amos 9:11; Matt. 1:1; 19:28; 25:31.", "norm_zh": "二在大卫复兴的国里基督作为人子大卫王室的后裔要作以色列人的王摩九11太一1十九28二五31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the restored kingdom of David Christ as the Son of Man Davids royal descendant will be the King over the children of IsraelAmos 911 Matt 11 1928 2531"}
{"zh": "叁\t在召会时代被成全的信徒，要得着赏赐，在来世国度时代，就是诸天之国的实现里，与基督一同作王一千年—启二十4~6，太十九28，提后二12上，参启三21：", "en": "III.\tThe believers who are perfected in the church age will be rewarded to reign with Christ for a thousand years in the next age, the kingdom age, the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens—Rev. 20:4-6; Matt. 19:28; 2 Tim. 2:12a; cf. Rev. 3:21:", "norm_zh": "叁在召会时代被成全的信徒要得着赏赐在来世国度时代就是诸天之国的实现里与基督一同作王一千年启二十46太十九28提后二12上参启三21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The believers who are perfected in the church age will be rewarded to reign with Christ for a thousand years in the next age the kingdom age the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavensRev 2046 Matt 1928 2 Tim 212a cf Rev 321"}
{"zh": "一\t在千年国里的得胜者坐在宝座上，有审判的权柄赐给他们—二26，五10，二十4，来二5：", "en": "A.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are sitting upon thrones, and judgment is given to them—Rev. 2:26; 5:10; 20:4; Heb. 2:5:", "norm_zh": "一在千年国里的得胜者坐在宝座上有审判的权柄赐给他们二26五10二十4来二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are sitting upon thrones and judgment is given to themRev 226 510 204 Heb 25"}
{"zh": "1\t与主一同坐宝座，是给得胜者的奖赏，使他们有分于主的权柄，与祂一同作王，管理全地—启二26，三21，路十九13~19。", "en": "1\tTo sit with the Lord on His throne will be a prize to the overcomers, that they may participate in the Lord's authority and be co-kings with Him in ruling over the whole earth—Rev. 2:26; 3:21; Luke 19:13-19.", "norm_zh": "1与主一同坐宝座是给得胜者的奖赏使他们有分于主的权柄与祂一同作王管理全地启二26三21路十九1319", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To sit with the Lord on His throne will be a prize to the overcomers that they may participate in the Lords authority and be cokings with Him in ruling over the whole earthRev 226 321 Luke 191319"}
{"zh": "二\t在千年国里的得胜者乃是殉道者—启二10，二十4：", "en": "B.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyrs—Rev. 2:10; 20:4:", "norm_zh": "二在千年国里的得胜者乃是殉道者启二10二十4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyrsRev 210 204"}
{"zh": "1\t所有的信徒都该是基督的见证人，也就是祂的殉道者—徒一8、22，二13、32，五32，二六16。", "en": "1\tAll of the believers should be Christ's witnesses, His martyrs—Acts 1:8, 22; 2:13, 32; 5:32; 26:16.", "norm_zh": "1所有的信徒都该是基督的见证人也就是祂的殉道者徒一822二1332五32二六16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 All of the believers should be Christs witnesses His martyrsActs 18 22 213 32 532 2616"}
{"zh": "2\t基督情深的爱困迫我们，使我们向祂活并向祂死—林后五14~15，罗十四7~9，加二19。", "en": "2\tChrist's love of affection constrains us to live and to die to Him—2 Cor. 5:14-15; Rom. 14:7-9; Gal. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "2基督情深的爱困迫我们使我们向祂活并向祂死林后五1415罗十四79加二19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christs love of affection constrains us to live and to die to Him2 Cor 51415 Rom 1479 Gal 219"}
{"zh": "4\t在千年国里的得胜者乃是因神的话，就是启示出来的基督，并因耶稣的见证，就是作见证的召会，而殉道的—启一2、9，六9，十九13，二十4。", "en": "4\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyred because of the Word of God, the revealed Christ, and the testimony of Jesus, the testifying church—Rev. 1:2, 9; 6:9; 19:13; 20:4.", "norm_zh": "4在千年国里的得胜者乃是因神的话就是启示出来的基督并因耶稣的见证就是作见证的召会而殉道的启一29六9十九13二十4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyred because of the Word of God the revealed Christ and the testimony of Jesus the testifying churchRev 12 9 69 1913 204"}
{"zh": "三\t在千年国里的得胜者惟独敬拜事奉神—二10，二十4。", "en": "C.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom worship and serve God only—Rev. 2:10; 20:4.", "norm_zh": "三在千年国里的得胜者惟独敬拜事奉神二10二十4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The overcomers in the millennial kingdom worship and serve God onlyRev 210 204"}
{"zh": "四\t在千年国里的得胜者，额上都写着羔羊的名和父的名—十四1，三12，二二4，参二17。", "en": "D.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom have the name of the Lamb and the name of the Father written on their foreheads—Rev. 14:1; 3:12; 22:4; cf. 2:17.", "norm_zh": "四在千年国里的得胜者额上都写着羔羊的名和父的名十四1三12二二4参二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The overcomers in the millennial kingdom have the name of the Lamb and the name of the Father written on their foreheadsRev 141 312 224 cf 217"}
{"zh": "重建大卫倒塌的帐幕", "en": "Rebuilding the fallen tabernacle of David", "norm_zh": "重建大卫倒塌的帐幕", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Rebuilding the fallen tabernacle of David"}
{"zh": "大卫的国和大卫的王室", "en": "The kingdom of David and the royal family of David", "norm_zh": "大卫的国和大卫的王室", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The kingdom of David and the royal family of David"}
{"zh": "成为基督的国和神的国", "en": "Becoming the Kingdom of Christ and the Kingdom of God", "norm_zh": "成为基督的国和神的国", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Becoming the Kingdom of Christ and the Kingdom of God"}
{"zh": "大卫是基督作王的预表。大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室。当尼布甲尼撒来掳掠以色列国、蹂躏那地、焚烧城邑、毁坏圣殿、掳走君王的时候，大卫的国，他的王室就倒塌了（王下二五1~21）在阿摩司的预言里，神应许有一日，大卫的国和大卫的家要得着复兴，万国必称为耶和华名下的国。这预言指明，基督要回来作真大卫（赛九7，十六5，耶三十9，结三四23~24，三七24~25，何三5）并要重建（即恢复）祂先祖大卫的国，好复兴整个宇宙。那时大卫的国要成为基督和神的国，直到永远（启十一15）在复兴的国里，万国必称为耶和华名下的国，即万国必属于神。雅各在徒十五16~18引用阿摩司在11~12节的预言，印证彼得和保罗到外邦人那里去，因为在复兴的时候，所有的外邦人都要成为神的子民，就像犹太人一样。（圣经恢复本，摩九11注1）", "en": "David is a type of Christ as the King. The tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of David. That kingdom, that royal family, fell when Nebuchadnezzar came to capture the nation of Israel, devastate the land, burn the city, destroy the temple, and carry off the king (2 Kings 25:1-21). In Amos's prophecy God promised that in a certain day the kingdom of David and the family of David would be restored, and all the nations would be called by the name of Jehovah. This prophecy indicates that Christ will come back to be the real David (Isa. 9:7; 16:5; Jer. 30:9; Ezek. 34:23-24; 37:24-25; Hosea 3:5) and will rebuild, i.e., restore, the kingdom of His forefather David for the restoration of the entire universe. At that time the kingdom of David will become the kingdom of Christ and of God for eternity (Rev. 11:15). In the restored kingdom all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovah; i.e., all the nations will belong to God. Amos's prophecy in vv. 11-12 was quoted by James in Acts 15:16-18 to confirm Peter's and Paul's going to the Gentiles, because in the restoration all the Gentiles will become God's people, just as the Jews are.", "norm_zh": "大卫是基督作王的预表大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室当尼布甲尼撒来掳掠以色列国蹂躏哪地焚烧城邑毁坏圣殿掳走君王的时候大卫的国他的王室就倒塌了王下二五121在阿摩司的预言里神应许有一日大卫的国和大卫的家要得着复兴万国必称为耶和华名下的国这预言指明基督要回来作真大卫赛九7十六5耶三十9结三四2324三七2425何三5并要重建即恢复祂先祖大卫的国好复兴整个宇宙哪时大卫的国要成为基督和神的国直到永远启十一15在复兴的国里万国必称为耶和华名下的国即万国必属于神雅各在徒十五1618引用阿摩司在1112节的预言印证彼得和保罗到外邦人哪里去因为在复兴的时候所有的外邦人都要成为神的子民就像犹太人一样圣经恢复本摩九11注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "David is a type of Christ as the King The tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of David That kingdom that royal family fell when Nebuchadnezzar came to capture the nation of Israel devastate the land burn the city destroy the temple and carry off the king 2 Kings 25121 In Amoss prophecy God promised that in a certain day the kingdom of David and the family of David would be restored and all the nations would be called by the name of Jehovah This prophecy indicates that Christ will come back to be the real David Isa 97 165 Jer 309 Ezek 342324 372425 Hosea 35 and will rebuild ie restore the kingdom of His forefather David for the restoration of the entire universe At that time the kingdom of David will become the kingdom of Christ and of God for eternity Rev 1115 In the restored kingdom all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovah ie all the nations will belong to God Amoss prophecy in vv 1112 was quoted by James in Acts 151618 to confirm Peters and Pauls going to the Gentiles because in the restoration all the Gentiles will become Gods people just as the Jews are"}
{"zh": "千年国的两部分", "en": "The Two Parts of the Millennium", "norm_zh": "千年国的两部分", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Two Parts of the Millennium"}
{"zh": "在千年国里将有三班人。第一班是得胜的圣徒，包括新旧约中得胜的圣徒。这些得胜的圣徒要与基督一同作王，基督是至高的王，我们将是祂的小王。所以上部是千年国的君王部分。在下端部分的第二班人，乃是蒙保全正确的犹太人，他们要在主回来时得救。照着撒迦利亚十二章十至十四节，这些犹太人必仰望他们所扎的那位，然后他们要悔改。这些就是三分之一要经过火受熬炼的犹太人（亚十三9。）这些得救的犹太人要进入千年国作祭司，教导万民寻求神，认识神。那时以赛亚二章二至三节就应验了。三节说，“必有许多国的民前往，说，来吧，我们登耶和华的山，奔雅各神的殿；主必将祂的道教训我们，我们也要行祂的路；因为训诲必出于锡安，耶和华的言语，必出于耶路撒冷”。借着作祭司之犹太人的教导，万民都必认识神。以赛亚六十一章六节清楚的说，“你们倒要称为耶和华的祭司，人必称你们为我们神的仆役”。当千年国的时候，万民都必认犹太人为神的祭司，这话也就得应验了。", "en": "In the millennial kingdom there will be three peoples. The first are the overcoming saints, including those of both the Old Testament and the New Testament. These overcoming saints will be co-kings of Christ. Christ is the highest King, and we will be His sub-kings. Therefore, the upper section is the royal portion of the millennium. The second group, found in the lower section, is the preserved and proper Jews, who will be saved at the time of the Lord's coming back. According to Zechariah 12:10-14, these Jews will look on Him whom they have pierced, and then they will repent. These are the Jews who will be the third part who will pass through fire and be refined (Zech. 13:9). These saved Jews will enter into the millennium as priests and will teach the nations to seek God and to know Him. Isaiah 2:2-3 will be fulfilled at that time. Verse 3 says, \"And many people shall go and say, Come ye, and let us go up to the mountain of the Lord, to the house of the God of Jacob; and he will teach us of his ways, and we will walk in his paths: for out of Zion shall go forth the law, and the word of the Lord from Jerusalem.\" The nations will learn of God through the instruction of the Jews, who will be priests. Isaiah 61:6 clearly says, \"But ye shall be named the Priests of the Lord: men shall call you the Ministers of our God.\" This word will also be fulfilled during the millennium, when the nations will recognize the Jews as God's priests.", "norm_zh": "在千年国里将有三班人第一班是得胜的圣徒包括新旧约中得胜的圣徒这些得胜的圣徒要与基督一同作王基督是至高的王我们将是祂的小王所以上部是千年国的君王部分在下端部分的第二班人乃是蒙保全正确的犹太人他们要在主回来时得救照着撒迦利亚十二章十至十四节这些犹太人必仰望他们所扎的哪位然后他们要悔改这些就是三分之一要经过火受熬炼的犹太人亚十三9这些得救的犹太人要进入千年国作祭司教导万民寻求神认识神哪时以赛亚二章二至三节就应验了三节说必有许多国的民前往说来吧我们登耶和华的山奔雅各神的殿主必将祂的道教训我们我们也要行祂的路因为训诲必出于锡安耶和华的言语必出于耶路撒冷借着作祭司之犹太人的教导万民都必认识神以赛亚六十一章六节清楚的说你们倒要称为耶和华的祭司人必称你们为我们神的仆役当千年国的时候万民都必认犹太人为神的祭司这话也就得应验了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the millennial kingdom there will be three peoples The first are the overcoming saints including those of both the Old Testament and the New Testament These overcoming saints will be cokings of Christ Christ is the highest King and we will be His subkings Therefore the upper section is the royal portion of the millennium The second group found in the lower section is the preserved and proper Jews who will be saved at the time of the Lords coming back According to Zechariah 121014 these Jews will look on Him whom they have pierced and then they will repent These are the Jews who will be the third part who will pass through fire and be refined Zech 139 These saved Jews will enter into the millennium as priests and will teach the nations to seek God and to know Him Isaiah 223 will be fulfilled at that time Verse 3 says And many people shall go and say Come ye and let us go up to the mountain of the Lord to the house of the God of Jacob and he will teach us of his ways and we will walk in his paths for out of Zion shall go forth the law and the word of the Lord from Jerusalem The nations will learn of God through the instruction of the Jews who will be priests Isaiah 616 clearly says But ye shall be named the Priests of the Lord men shall call you the Ministers of our God This word will also be fulfilled during the millennium when the nations will recognize the Jews as Gods priests"}
{"zh": "和基督一同作王一千年", "en": "reign with Christ for a thousand years", "norm_zh": "和基督一同作王一千年", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "reign with Christ for a thousand years"}
{"zh": "弥赛亚国是将来千年国的属地部分；天国（指天国的实现而言）是将来千年国的属天部分。弥赛亚国是属地的，天国是属天的。弥赛亚国尚未来到，天国（指天国的实际而言）已经在得胜的信徒身上了。弥赛亚国是为着将来得着复兴的犹太人，和那些作绵羊的外邦人的；天国是为教会中的得胜者的。将来的弥赛亚国，是犹太人所盼望的；将来的天国（指天国的实现而言）是信徒（得胜的）所该盼望的。将来在弥赛亚国里的，是作祭司的犹太人，和作百姓的外邦人；将来在天国里的，是作君王的得胜的信徒。在弥赛亚国里，有祭司，有百姓；但在将来的天国里，都是君王，没有百姓。将来天国里这些君王所管的百姓，就是弥赛亚国里的人。所以弥赛亚国，是将来天国的属治；将来的天国，是弥赛亚国的主管。教会中的得胜者，将来就是在天国里，和基督一同作王一千年，管治弥赛亚国里的犹太人和外邦人。（启二十4、6，太十九28，启二26。）（圣经要道（卷五），第四十八题）", "en": "The kingdom of Messiah is the earthly portion of the millennium; the kingdom of the heavens, that is, the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens, is the heavenly portion in the millennium. The kingdom of Messiah is earthly; the kingdom of the heavens is heavenly. Before the kingdom of Messiah comes, the kingdom of the heavens, that is, the reality of the kingdom of the heavens, is already with the overcoming believers. The kingdom of Messiah is for the Jewish people to be restored in the future and for the Gentiles as \"sheep\"; the kingdom of the heavens is for the overcomers in the church. The future kingdom of Messiah is the expectation of the Jews; the future kingdom of the heavens, that is, the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens, should be the expectation of the believers (the overcoming ones). In the kingdom of Messiah there will be the Jewish people as the priests and the Gentiles as the people; in the future kingdom of the heavens, there are only the kings and not the people. The people to be ruled over by the kings in the future kingdom of the heavens are the ones who will be in the kingdom of Messiah. Therefore, the kingdom of Messiah is the subordinate of the future kingdom of the heavens; the future kingdom of the heavens is the ruling authority of the kingdom of Messiah. The overcomers in the church will reign with Christ for one thousand years in the kingdom of the heavens, ruling over the Jews and Gentiles in the kingdom of Messiah (Rev. 20:4, 6; Matt. 19:28; Rev. 2:26). (The Crucial Truths in the Holy Scriptures, vol. 5, subject 48)", "norm_zh": "弥赛亚国是将来千年国的属地部分天国指天国的实现而言是将来千年国的属天部分弥赛亚国是属地的天国是属天的弥赛亚国尚未来到天国指天国的实际而言已经在得胜的信徒身上了弥赛亚国是为着将来得着复兴的犹太人和哪些作绵羊的外邦人的天国是为教会中的得胜者的将来的弥赛亚国是犹太人所盼望的将来的天国指天国的实现而言是信徒得胜的所该盼望的将来在弥赛亚国里的是作祭司的犹太人和作百姓的外邦人将来在天国里的是作君王的得胜的信徒在弥赛亚国里有祭司有百姓但在将来的天国里都是君王没有百姓将来天国里这些君王所管的百姓就是弥赛亚国里的人所以弥赛亚国是将来天国的属治将来的天国是弥赛亚国的主管教会中的得胜者将来就是在天国里和基督一同作王一千年管治弥赛亚国里的犹太人和外邦人启二十46太十九28启二26圣经要道卷五第四十八提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The kingdom of Messiah is the earthly portion of the millennium the kingdom of the heavens that is the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens is the heavenly portion in the millennium The kingdom of Messiah is earthly the kingdom of the heavens is heavenly Before the kingdom of Messiah comes the kingdom of the heavens that is the reality of the kingdom of the heavens is already with the overcoming believers The kingdom of Messiah is for the Jewish people to be restored in the future and for the Gentiles as sheep the kingdom of the heavens is for the overcomers in the church The future kingdom of Messiah is the expectation of the Jews the future kingdom of the heavens that is the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens should be the expectation of the believers the overcoming ones In the kingdom of Messiah there will be the Jewish people as the priests and the Gentiles as the people in the future kingdom of the heavens there are only the kings and not the people The people to be ruled over by the kings in the future kingdom of the heavens are the ones who will be in the kingdom of Messiah Therefore the kingdom of Messiah is the subordinate of the future kingdom of the heavens the future kingdom of the heavens is the ruling authority of the kingdom of Messiah The overcomers in the church will reign with Christ for one thousand years in the kingdom of the heavens ruling over the Jews and Gentiles in the kingdom of Messiah Rev 204 6 Matt 1928 Rev 226 The Crucial Truths in the Holy Scriptures vol 5 subject 48"}
{"zh": "有审判的权柄赐给他们", "en": "judgment is given to them", "norm_zh": "有审判的权柄赐给他们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "judgment is given to them"}
{"zh": "“我又看见几个宝座，也有坐在上面的，并有审判的权柄赐给他们；我又看见那些因为给耶稣作见证，并为神之道被斩者的灵魂，和那没有拜过兽与兽像，也没有在额上和手上受过它印记之人的灵魂；他们都复活了，与基督一同作王一千年。这是头一次的复活。其余的死人还没有复活，直等那一千年完了。在头一次复活有分的，有福了，圣洁了；第二次的死在他们身上没有权柄；他们必作神和基督的祭司，并要与基督一同作王一千年”。这里告诉我们，掌权的是什么人，与基督一同作王一千年的是什么人。国度并不是为着所有的人，国度只是为着殉道者，为着弃绝撒但和敌基督的人。这样的人，才能作王一千年。所以只有殉道者才能作王，只有不接受撒但和敌基督的人才能作王。这就是证明给我们看见，人得着千年国，不是因着白白的恩赐，乃是因着在神面前有好行为。虽然在别的地方，我们看见还有别种的人作王，但是启示录给我们看见，必须有专一的义才能赴羔羊的筵席，必须为主殉道才能作王。如果没有专一的义，没有殉道，就与作王没有分。这是千年国。（倪柝声文集第二辑第九册，神的福音（卷二），第二十二篇）", "en": "\"And I saw thrones, and they sat upon them, and judgment was given to them. And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded because of the testimony of Jesus and because of the word of God, and of those who had not worshipped the beast nor his image, and had not received the mark on their forehead and on their hand; and they lived and reigned with Christ for a thousand years. The rest of the dead did not live again until the thousand years were completed. This is the first resurrection. Blessed and holy is he who has part in the first resurrection; over these the second death has no authority, but they will be priests of God and of Christ and will reign with Him for a thousand years.\" These verses tell us who will be the kings who reign with Christ a thousand years. The kingdom is not for everybody. The kingdom is only for the martyrs. It is only for those who reject Satan and Antichrist. Only these ones can reign for a thousand years. Hence, only the martyrs can reign; only those who reject Satan and Antichrist will be kings. This proves to us that the millennial kingdom is not given as a free gift, but is obtained through good works before God. Although in other passages we see other kinds of people reigning, in Revelation we see that there must be specific righteousness before there can be participation in the marriage feast of the Lamb. Only those who are the martyrs can be the kings. Without having the particular righteousness and without being martyred, no one can have a part in the kingship. This is the millennium.", "norm_zh": "我又看见几个宝座也有坐在上面的并有审判的权柄赐给他们我又看见哪些因为给耶稣作见证并为神之道被斩者的灵魂和哪没有拜过兽与兽像也没有在额上和手上受过它印记之人的灵魂他们都复活了与基督一同作王一千年这是头一次的复活其余的死人还没有复活直等哪一千年完了在头一次复活有分的有福了圣洁了第二次的死在他们身上没有权柄他们必作神和基督的祭司并要与基督一同作王一千年这里告诉我们掌权的是什么人与基督一同作王一千年的是什么人国度并不是为着所有的人国度只是为着殉道者为着弃绝撒但和敌基督的人这样的人才能作王一千年所以只有殉道者才能作王只有不接受撒但和敌基督的人才能作王这就是证明给我们看见人得着千年国不是因着白白的恩赐乃是因着在神面前有好行为虽然在别的地方我们看见还有别种的人作王但是启示录给我们看见必须有专一的义才能赴羔羊的筵席必须为主殉道才能作王如果没有专一的义没有殉道就与作王没有分这是千年国倪柝声文集第二辑第九册神的福音卷二第二十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "And I saw thrones and they sat upon them and judgment was given to them And I saw the souls of those who had been beheaded because of the testimony of Jesus and because of the word of God and of those who had not worshipped the beast nor his image and had not received the mark on their forehead and on their hand and they lived and reigned with Christ for a thousand years The rest of the dead did not live again until the thousand years were completed This is the first resurrection Blessed and holy is he who has part in the first resurrection over these the second death has no authority but they will be priests of God and of Christ and will reign with Him for a thousand years These verses tell us who will be the kings who reign with Christ a thousand years The kingdom is not for everybody The kingdom is only for the martyrs It is only for those who reject Satan and Antichrist Only these ones can reign for a thousand years Hence only the martyrs can reign only those who reject Satan and Antichrist will be kings This proves to us that the millennial kingdom is not given as a free gift but is obtained through good works before God Although in other passages we see other kinds of people reigning in Revelation we see that there must be specific righteousness before there can be participation in the marriage feast of the Lamb Only those who are the martyrs can be the kings Without having the particular righteousness and without being martyred no one can have a part in the kingship This is the millennium"}
{"zh": "清明的天里，有宝座", "en": "A clear sky with a throne", "norm_zh": "清明的天里有宝座", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A clear sky with a throne"}
