{"zh": "十四万四千活着的得胜者", "en": "The one hundred forty-four thousand living overcomers", "norm_zh": "十四万四千活着的得胜者", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The one hundred fortyfour thousand living overcomers"}
{"zh": "启示录十五章说到在大灾难中受敌基督逼迫的殉道者，要在大灾难快结束时复活被提，站在玻璃海上（十五2~4，十三7上）掺杂着火的玻璃海是火湖的表号，所以这些殉道者是站在火湖之上。这些人是晚期的得胜者，他们经过大灾难，且胜了敌基督，没有敬拜他。他们要受敌基督的逼迫而殉道，然后复活，在千年国里与基督一同作王（二十4）当男孩子和初熟果子被提到三层天时，有许多信徒因为没有成熟而被留在地上。这指明他们所过的生活很少在基督里有长大，所以他们被留在地上经过大灾难。那将是他们的试炼，他们的试验，那会帮助他们放弃世界。倘若一位弟兄爱主，但仍然爱世界；当大灾难来临，得胜者被提时，这样一位弟兄还会爱世界么？他可能会喊说，“主耶稣啊，你为什么把我留在这里？与我一起事奉多年的某某弟兄已经被提了，但我仍然在这里”。这位弟兄必然会向主悔改，迫切的转向主。他不会想要留在地上直到大灾难的最后一日。这会使他成熟。大体圣徒的复活和被提，乃是在非常靠近大灾难结束的时候。甚至他们当中，也有些人要得着赏赐，因为他们经过大灾难而成熟了。在这次被提之后，主要在空中设立审判台，审判所有的信徒（林后五10）信徒或是要得着国度为赏赐一千年，或是要进入外面的黑暗里受惩治。（太二五21、23、30）（李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第四册，得胜者，第六篇）", "en": "Revelation 15 speaks of the martyrs in the great tribulation under the persecution of Antichrist resurrected and raptured to stand on the glassy sea close to the end of the great tribulation (15:2-4; 13:7a). The glassy sea mingled with fire is a sign of the lake of fire, so these martyrs stand above the lake of fire. These are the late overcomers who will pass through the great tribulation and overcome Antichrist and the worshipping of Antichrist. They will be martyred under the persecution of Antichrist and then resurrected to reign with Christ in the millennium (20:4). When the man-child and the firstfruits are raptured to the third heaven, many believers will be left on the earth because they are not mature. This indicates that they lived a life with very little growth in Christ; hence, they are left on the earth to pass through the great tribulation. That will be their trial, their testing, which will help them to give up the world. If a brother loves the Lord but still loves the world, when the great tribulation comes and the overcomers are raptured, will such a brother still love the world? He may cry out, \"Lord Jesus, why have You left me here? Brother So-and-so, who has served with me for many years, has been raptured, but I am still here.\" This brother will surely repent to the Lord and turn to Him urgently. He will not want to remain on the earth until the last day of the great tribulation. This will cause him to mature. The resurrection and rapture of the majority of the saints will be at a time very close to the end of the great tribulation. Even among them, some will receive a reward because they have matured through the great tribulation. After this rapture, the Lord will set up the judgment seat in the air to judge all the believers (2 Cor. 5:10). The believers will either receive the kingdom as a reward for a thousand years or enter into the outer darkness to be disciplined (Matt. 25:21, 23, 30).", "norm_zh": "启示录十五章说到在大灾难中受敌基督逼迫的殉道者要在大灾难快结束时复活被提站在玻璃海上十五24十三7上掺杂着火的玻璃海是火湖的表号所以这些殉道者是站在火湖之上这些人是晚期的得胜者他们经过大灾难且胜了敌基督没有敬拜他他们要受敌基督的逼迫而殉道然后复活在千年国里与基督一同作王二十4当男孩子和初熟果子被提到三层天时有许多信徒因为没有成熟而被留在地上这指明他们所过的生活很少在基督里有长大所以他们被留在地上经过大灾难哪将是他们的试炼他们的试验哪会帮助他们放弃世界倘若一位弟兄爱主但仍然爱世界当大灾难来临得胜者被提时这样一位弟兄还会爱世界么他可能会喊说主耶稣啊你为什么把我留在这里与我一起事奉多年的某某弟兄已经被提了但我仍然在这里这位弟兄必然会向主悔改迫切的转向主他不会想要留在地上直到大灾难的最后一日这会使他成熟大体圣徒的复活和被提乃是在非常靠近大灾难结束的时候甚至他们当中也有些人要得着赏赐因为他们经过大灾难而成熟了在这次被提之后主要在空中设立审判台审判所有的信徒林后五10信徒或是要得着国度为赏赐一千年或是要进入外面的黑暗里受惩治太二五212330李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第四册得胜者第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Revelation 15 speaks of the martyrs in the great tribulation under the persecution of Antichrist resurrected and raptured to stand on the glassy sea close to the end of the great tribulation 1524 137a The glassy sea mingled with fire is a sign of the lake of fire so these martyrs stand above the lake of fire These are the late overcomers who will pass through the great tribulation and overcome Antichrist and the worshipping of Antichrist They will be martyred under the persecution of Antichrist and then resurrected to reign with Christ in the millennium 204 When the manchild and the firstfruits are raptured to the third heaven many believers will be left on the earth because they are not mature This indicates that they lived a life with very little growth in Christ hence they are left on the earth to pass through the great tribulation That will be their trial their testing which will help them to give up the world If a brother loves the Lord but still loves the world when the great tribulation comes and the overcomers are raptured will such a brother still love the world He may cry out Lord Jesus why have You left me here Brother Soandso who has served with me for many years has been raptured but I am still here This brother will surely repent to the Lord and turn to Him urgently He will not want to remain on the earth until the last day of the great tribulation This will cause him to mature The resurrection and rapture of the majority of the saints will be at a time very close to the end of the great tribulation Even among them some will receive a reward because they have matured through the great tribulation After this rapture the Lord will set up the judgment seat in the air to judge all the believers 2 Cor 510 The believers will either receive the kingdom as a reward for a thousand years or enter into the outer darkness to be disciplined Matt 2521 23 30"}
{"zh": "生命的复活", "en": "The resurrection of life", "norm_zh": "生命的复活", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:00:55.490123+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The resurrection of life"}
{"zh": "二\t在生命上，基督要扩增为召会；在行政上，基督要扩增为国度—约三29~30，可四26，但二35。（1999年冬训，第二十篇；但以理书生命读经，第三篇，第三十九段*）", "en": "B.\tIn life Christ increases to become the church; in administration Christ increases to become the kingdom—John 3:29-30; Mark 4:26; Dan. 2:35.", "norm_zh": "二在生命上基督要扩增为召会在行政上基督要扩增为国度约三2930可四26但二351999年冬训第二十篇但以理书生命读经第三篇第三十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In life Christ increases to become the church in administration Christ increases to become the kingdomJohn 32930 Mark 426 Dan 235"}
{"zh": "贰\t“到那日，我必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕，堵住其中的破口，把那毁坏的建立起来，重新修造，像古时一样”—摩九11，徒十五16：（2012年夏训，第七篇）", "en": "II.\t\"In that day I will raise up / The fallen tabernacle of David, / And I will wall up its breaches / And raise up its ruins / And build it up as it was in the days of old\"—Amos 9:11; Acts 15:16:", "norm_zh": "贰到哪日我必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕堵住其中的破口把哪毁坏的建立起来重新修造像古时一样摩九11徒十五162012年夏训第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II In that day I will raise up The fallen tabernacle of David And I will wall up its breaches And raise up its ruins And build it up as it was in the days of oldAmos 911 Acts 1516"}
{"zh": "一\t大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室—摩九11，徒十五16~18：（2012年夏训，第七篇；阿摩司书生命读经，第三篇，第五十七段*）", "en": "A.\tThe tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of David—Amos 9:11; Acts 15:16-18:", "norm_zh": "一大卫的帐幕就是大卫的国和大卫的王室摩九11徒十五16182012年夏训第七篇阿摩司书生命读经第三篇第五十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The tabernacle of David is the kingdom of David and the royal family of DavidAmos 911 Acts 151618"}
{"zh": "1\t古时王室与国乃是一；大卫的国就是大卫的王室—摩九11。（2012年夏训，第七篇；阿摩司书生命读经，第三篇，第五十七段*）", "en": "1.\tIn ancient times the royal family and the kingdom were one; David's kingdom was David's royal family.—Amos 9:11.", "norm_zh": "1古时王室与国乃是一大卫的国就是大卫的王室摩九112012年夏训第七篇阿摩司书生命读经第三篇第五十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In ancient times the royal family and the kingdom were one Davids kingdom was Davids royal familyAmos 911"}
{"zh": "3\t在阿摩司九章十一节，神进来应许，有一日祂必建立“大卫倒塌的帐幕”，也就是恢复倒塌的大卫之国；在那日，大卫的国和大卫的王室要得着复兴，万国必称为耶和华名下的国─11、12节。（2012年夏训，第七篇；阿摩司书生命读经，第三篇，第五十七段**）", "en": "3.\tIn Amos 9:11 God came in to promise that one day He would raise up \"the fallen tabernacle of David,\" that is, restore the fallen kingdom of David; in that day the kingdom of David and the family of David will be restored, and all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovah.—vv. 11-12.", "norm_zh": "3在阿摩司九章十一节神进来应许有一日祂必建立大卫倒塌的帐幕也就是恢复倒塌的大卫之国在哪日大卫的国和大卫的王室要得着复兴万国必称为耶和华名下的国1112节2012年夏训第七篇阿摩司书生命读经第三篇第五十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In Amos 911 God came in to promise that one day He would raise up the fallen tabernacle of David that is restore the fallen kingdom of David in that day the kingdom of David and the family of David will be restored and all the nations will be called by the name of Jehovahvv 1112"}
{"zh": "b\t千年国的属地部分，乃是人子的国，弥赛亚国，就是大卫的帐幕—太十三41，启十一15，撒下七13，摩九11：（2012年夏训，第七篇；圣经恢复本，太五3注4*）", "en": "b. The earthly part of the millennium is the kingdom of the Son of Man, the kingdom of the Messiah, even the tabernacle of David.—Matt. 13:41; Rev. 11:15; 2 Sam. 7:13; Amos 9:11:", "norm_zh": "b千年国的属地部分乃是人子的国弥赛亚国就是大卫的帐幕太十三41启十一15撒下七13摩九112012年夏训第七篇圣经恢复本太五3注4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The earthly part of the millennium is the kingdom of the Son of Man the kingdom of the Messiah even the tabernacle of DavidMatt 1341 Rev 1115 2 Sam 713 Amos 911"}
{"zh": "（一）　这是复兴的以色列国，大卫的国，为着得救的犹太人—徒一6，可十一10，路一32~33，撒下七12~13。（2012年夏训，第七篇；新约总论，第二百四十四篇，第四十段*）", "en": "1) This is the restored nation of Israel, the kingdom of David, for the saved Jews.—Acts 1:6; Mark 11:10; Luke 1:32-33; 2 Sam. 7:12-13.", "norm_zh": "一这是复兴的以色列国大卫的国为着得救的犹太人徒一6可十一10路一3233撒下七12132012年夏训第七篇新约总论第二百四十四篇第四十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This is the restored nation of Israel the kingdom of David for the saved JewsActs 16 Mark 1110 Luke 13233 2 Sam 71213"}
{"zh": "（二）　在大卫复兴的国里，基督作为人子，大卫王室的后裔，要作以色列人的王—摩九11，太一1，十九28，二五31。（2012年夏训，第七篇；李常受文集一九八三年第三册，圣经中的基本启示，第七章，第四十五段*）", "en": "2) In the restored kingdom of David, Christ as the Son of Man, David's royal descendant, will be the King over the children of Israel.—Amos 9:11; Matt. 1:1; 19:28; 25:31.", "norm_zh": "二在大卫复兴的国里基督作为人子大卫王室的后裔要作以色列人的王摩九11太一1十九28二五312012年夏训第七篇李常受文集一九八三年第三册圣经中的基本启示第七章第四十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In the restored kingdom of David Christ as the Son of Man Davids royal descendant will be the King over the children of IsraelAmos 911 Matt 11 1928 2531"}
{"zh": "叁\t在召会时代被成全的信徒，要得着赏赐，在来世国度时代，就是诸天之国的实现里，与基督一同作王一千年—启二十4~6，太十九28，提后二12上，参启三21：（1999年冬训，第二十篇；李常受文集一九八三年第三册，圣经中的基本启示，第七章，第四十三段**）", "en": "III.\tThe believers who are perfected in the church age will be rewarded to reign with Christ for a thousand years in the next age, the kingdom age, the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens—Rev. 20:4-6; Matt. 19:28; 2 Tim. 2:12a; cf. Rev. 3:21:", "norm_zh": "叁在召会时代被成全的信徒要得着赏赐在来世国度时代就是诸天之国的实现里与基督一同作王一千年启二十46太十九28提后二12上参启三211999年冬训第二十篇李常受文集一九八三年第三册圣经中的基本启示第七章第四十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The believers who are perfected in the church age will be rewarded to reign with Christ for a thousand years in the next age the kingdom age the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavensRev 2046 Matt 1928 2 Tim 212a cf Rev 321"}
{"zh": "一\t在千年国里的得胜者坐在宝座上，有审判的权柄赐给他们—二26，五10，二十4，来二5：（1999年冬训，第二十篇；李常受文集一九六九年第二册，圣经中关于生命的重要启示，第二章，第十四段*）", "en": "A.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are sitting upon thrones, and judgment is given to them—Rev. 2:26; 5:10; 20:4; Heb. 2:5:", "norm_zh": "一在千年国里的得胜者坐在宝座上有审判的权柄赐给他们二26五10二十4来二51999年冬训第二十篇李常受文集一九六九年第二册圣经中关于生命的重要启示第二章第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are sitting upon thrones and judgment is given to themRev 226 510 204 Heb 25"}
{"zh": "1\t与主一同坐宝座，是给得胜者的奖赏，使他们有分于主的权柄，与祂一同作王，管理全地—启二26，三21，路十九13~19。（1999年冬训，第二十篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第三册，在旧造里撒但的混乱以及为着新造的神圣经纶，第三章，第一百段*）", "en": "1.\tTo sit with the Lord on His throne will be a prize to the overcomers, that they may participate in the Lord's authority and be co-kings with Him in ruling over the whole earth.—Rev. 2:26; 3:21; Luke 19:13-19.", "norm_zh": "1与主一同坐宝座是给得胜者的奖赏使他们有分于主的权柄与祂一同作王管理全地启二26三21路十九13191999年冬训第二十篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第三册在旧造里撒但的混乱以及为着新造的神圣经纶第三章第一百段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To sit with the Lord on His throne will be a prize to the overcomers that they may participate in the Lords authority and be cokings with Him in ruling over the whole earthRev 226 321 Luke 191319"}
{"zh": "a\t有清明的天，意思就是与主之间没有阴翳和黑暗；有宝座，意思就是在诸天的管治之下，在主管理的同在之下—约壹一5、7节，但四26。（1999年冬训，第二十篇；以西结书生命读经，第十二篇，第二段**）", "en": "a.\tTo have a clear sky means that we have no clouds or darkness between us and the Lord, and to have the throne means that we are under the ruling of the heavens, His ruling presence.—1 John 1:5, 7; Dan. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "a有清明的天意思就是与主之间没有阴翳和黑暗有宝座意思就是在诸天的管治之下在主管理的同在之下约壹一57节但四261999年冬训第二十篇以西结书生命读经第十二篇第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a To have a clear sky means that we have no clouds or darkness between us and the Lord and to have the throne means that we are under the ruling of the heavens His ruling presence1 John 15 7 Dan 426"}
{"zh": "二\t在千年国里的得胜者乃是殉道者—启二10，二十4：（1999年冬训，第二十篇***）", "en": "B.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyrs—Rev. 2:10; 20:4:", "norm_zh": "二在千年国里的得胜者乃是殉道者启二10二十41999年冬训第二十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyrsRev 210 204"}
{"zh": "1\t所有的信徒都该是基督的见证人，也就是祂的殉道者—徒一8、22，二13、32，五32，二六16。（1999年冬训，第二十篇；李常受文集一九七八年第三册，关于长老职分的基本原则，第九章，第五段**）", "en": "1\tAll the believers should be Christ's witnesses, His martyrs—Acts 1:8, 22; 2:13, 32; 5:32; 26:16.", "norm_zh": "1所有的信徒都该是基督的见证人也就是祂的殉道者徒一822二1332五32二六161999年冬训第二十篇李常受文集一九七八年第三册关于长老职分的基本原则第九章第五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 All the believers should be Christs witnesses His martyrsActs 18 22 213 32 532 2616"}
{"zh": "2\t基督情深的爱困迫我们，使我们向祂活并向祂死—林后五14~15，罗十四7~9，加二19。（2011年冬训，第一篇；新约总论，第三百一十八篇，第四段**）", "en": "2\tChrist's affectionate love constrains us to live and to die to Him—2 Cor. 5:14-15; Rom. 14:7-9; Gal. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "2基督情深的爱困迫我们使我们向祂活并向祂死林后五1415罗十四79加二192011年冬训第一篇新约总论第三百一十八篇第四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christs affectionate love constrains us to live and to die to Him2 Cor 51415 Rom 1479 Gal 219"}
{"zh": "4\t在千年国里的得胜者乃是因神的话，就是启示出来的基督，并因耶稣的见证，就是作见证的召会，而殉道的—启一2、9，六9，十九13，二十4。（1999年冬训，第二十篇***）", "en": "4\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyred because of the word of God, the revealed Christ, and the testimony of Jesus, the testifying church—Rev. 1:2, 9; 6:9; 19:13; 20:4.", "norm_zh": "4在千年国里的得胜者乃是因神的话就是启示出来的基督并因耶稣的见证就是作见证的召会而殉道的启一29六9十九13二十41999年冬训第二十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The overcomers in the millennial kingdom are martyred because of the word of God the revealed Christ and the testimony of Jesus the testifying churchRev 12 9 69 1913 204"}
{"zh": "三\t在千年国里的得胜者惟独敬拜事奉神—二10，二十4。（1999年冬训，第二十篇***）", "en": "C.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom worship and serve God only—Rev. 2:10; 20:4.", "norm_zh": "三在千年国里的得胜者惟独敬拜事奉神二10二十41999年冬训第二十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The overcomers in the millennial kingdom worship and serve God onlyRev 210 204"}
{"zh": "四\t在千年国里的得胜者，额上都写着羔羊的名和父的名—十四1，三12，二二4，参二17。（1999年冬训，第二十篇；新约总论，第四百零二十二篇，第十五段*）", "en": "D.\tThe overcomers in the millennial kingdom have the name of the Lamb and the name of His Father written on their foreheads—Rev. 14:1; 3:12; 22:4; cf. 2:17.", "norm_zh": "四在千年国里的得胜者额上都写着羔羊的名和父的名十四1三12二二4参二171999年冬训第二十篇新约总论第四百零二十二篇第十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:03:25.483839+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The overcomers in the millennial kingdom have the name of the Lamb and the name of His Father written on their foreheadsRev 141 312 224 cf 217"}
{"zh": "读经：启二17，三12，二一1~二二5、14~15，林后五17，加六15，弗二15、20，三4~5", "en": "Scripture Reading: Rev. 2:17; 3:12; 21:1—22:5, 14-15; 2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Eph. 2:15, 20; 3:4-5", "norm_zh": "读经启二17三12二一1二二51415林后五17加六15弗二1520三45", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Rev 217 312 211225 1415 2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Eph 215 20 345"}
{"zh": "壹\t新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结，以及整个神圣启示中心并终极完成的意义─启二一2、9~10，三12：", "en": "I.\tThe New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation and the central and ultimate significance of the entire divine revelation:—Rev. 21:2, 9-10; 3:12:", "norm_zh": "壹新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结以及整个神圣启示中心并终极完成的意义启二一2910三12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation and the central and ultimate significance of the entire divine revelationRev 212 910 312"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是圣经整个神圣启示的总结及总和的组成—二一2~3、9~10，来十一10。", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is the conclusion and the total composition of the entire revelation of the Bible.—21:2-3, 9-10; Heb. 11:10.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是圣经整个神圣启示的总结及总和的组成二一23910来十一10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is the conclusion and the total composition of the entire revelation of the Bible2123 910 Heb 1110"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经的一切启示与异象都终极完成于新耶路撒冷—启二一9~10，三12。", "en": "B.\tAll the revelations and visions of the Scriptures consummate in the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 21:9-10; 3:12.", "norm_zh": "二圣经的一切启示与异象都终极完成于新耶路撒冷启二一910三12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B All the revelations and visions of the Scriptures consummate in the New JerusalemRev 21910 312"}
{"zh": "贰\t新耶路撒冷不是一座物质的城，乃是一个生机的构成，由救赎之经过过程并终极完成的三一神与蒙救赎、变化、并荣化之三部分人所构成，作终极完成之三一神的生机体，使祂借着得荣之三部分人，得着永远的扩大和彰显—三12，二一12~14、18~21：", "en": "II.\tThe New Jerusalem is not a physical city but an organic constitution constituted with the redeeming, processed, and consummated Triune God and the redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified tripartite man as an organism of the consummated Triune God for His eternal enlargement and expression through the glorified tripartite man:—3:12; 21:12-14, 18-21:", "norm_zh": "贰新耶路撒冷不是一座物质的城乃是一个生机的构成由救赎之经过过程并终极完成的三一神与蒙救赎变化并荣化之三部分人所构成作终极完成之三一神的生机体使祂借着得荣之三部分人得着永远的扩大和彰显三12二一12141821", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The New Jerusalem is not a physical city but an organic constitution constituted with the redeeming processed and consummated Triune God and the redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified tripartite man as an organism of the consummated Triune God for His eternal enlargement and expression through the glorified tripartite man312 211214 1821"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是由旧约和新约所有的圣徒组成，他们建造在一起，作神永远的建筑—五9，二一12~24，弗二15。", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is the composition of all the Old Testament and New Testament saints built together as God's eternal building.—5:9; 21:12-24; Eph. 2:15.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是由旧约和新约所有的圣徒组成他们建造在一起作神永远的建筑五9二一1224弗二15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is the composition of all the Old Testament and New Testament saints built together as Gods eternal building59 211224 Eph 215"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是所有蒙救赎、重生、变化、荣化之三部分人，与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和—林后五17，启二一18~21。", "en": "B.\tThe New Jerusalem is the mingling of all the redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified tripartite men with the processed and consummated Triune God.—2 Cor. 5:17; Rev. 21:18-21.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是所有蒙救赎重生变化荣化之三部分人与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和林后五17启二一1821", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the mingling of all the redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified tripartite men with the processed and consummated Triune God2 Cor 517 Rev 211821"}
{"zh": "三\t新耶路撒冷是经过过程并终极完成之三一神终极的显出，使祂得着彰显，直到永远—12~14、18~21节。", "en": "C.\tThe New Jerusalem is the ultimate manifestation of the processed and consummated Triune God for His expression for eternity.—vv. 12-14, 18-21.", "norm_zh": "三新耶路撒冷是经过过程并终极完成之三一神终极的显出使祂得着彰显直到永远12141821节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The New Jerusalem is the ultimate manifestation of the processed and consummated Triune God for His expression for eternityvv 1214 1821"}
{"zh": "叁\t新耶路撒冷是一个表号─是圣经中最大并终极的表号─表征神在旧造里、在各时代中，新造工作之结果的集大成—一1，二一1~2，林后五17：", "en": "III. The New Jerusalem is a sign—the greatest and ultimate sign in the Scriptures—of the aggregate of God's work of the new creation in all the dispensations within the old creation—1:1; 21:1-2; 2 Cor. 5:17:", "norm_zh": "叁新耶路撒冷是一个表号是圣经中最大并终极的表号表征神在旧造里在各时代中新造工作之结果的集大成一1二一12林后五17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The New Jerusalem is a signthe greatest and ultimate sign in the Scripturesof the aggregate of Gods work of the new creation in all the dispensations within the old creation11 2112 2 Cor 517"}
{"zh": "一\t神在列祖时代在列祖身上的工作—启十二1，创十二3下，二二18。", "en": "A.\tGod's work in the dispensation of the patriarchs on the patriarchs.—Rev. 12:1; Gen. 12:3b; 22:18.", "norm_zh": "一神在列祖时代在列祖身上的工作启十二1创十二3下二二18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods work in the dispensation of the patriarchs on the patriarchsRev 121 Gen 123b 2218"}
{"zh": "二\t神在律法时代在以色列人身上的工作—启十二1，加三24。", "en": "B.\tGod's work in the dispensation of the law on the children of Israel.—Rev. 12:1; Gal. 3:24.", "norm_zh": "二神在律法时代在以色列人身上的工作启十二1加三24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Gods work in the dispensation of the law on the children of IsraelRev 121 Gal 324"}
{"zh": "三\t神在恩典时代在新约信徒身上的工作—启十二1，约一14，林前十五10。", "en": "C.\tGod's work in the dispensation of grace on the New Testament believers.—Rev. 12:1; John 1:14; 1 Cor. 15:10.", "norm_zh": "三神在恩典时代在新约信徒身上的工作启十二1约一14林前十五10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Gods work in the dispensation of grace on the New Testament believersRev 121 John 114 1 Cor 1510"}
{"zh": "四\t神在公义时代在得救的以色列人，和其余尚未得成全的新约信徒身上的工作—十五52，帖前四15~17，启十四14~16。", "en": "D.\tGod's work in the dispensation of righteousness on the saved Israelites and on the rest of the New Testament believers not yet perfected.—1 Cor. 15:52; 1 Thes. 4:15-17; Rev. 14:14-16.", "norm_zh": "四神在公义时代在得救的以色列人和其余尚未得成全的新约信徒身上的工作十五52帖前四1517启十四1416", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods work in the dispensation of righteousness on the saved Israelites and on the rest of the New Testament believers not yet perfected1 Cor 1552 1 Thes 41517 Rev 141416"}
{"zh": "肆\t新耶路撒冷是神经纶终极的目标—三21，二一1~2、10：", "en": "IV.\tThe New Jerusalem is the ultimate goal of God's economy:—Rev. 3:21; 21:1-2, 10:", "norm_zh": "肆新耶路撒冷是神经纶终极的目标三21二一1210", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The New Jerusalem is the ultimate goal of Gods economyRev 321 2112 10"}
{"zh": "一\t神只有一个终极的目标─新耶路撒冷，作神的扩大、扩展和彰显—2、9、22节。", "en": "A.\tGod has only one ultimate goal—the New Jerusalem, God's enlargement, expansion, and expression.—vv. 2, 9, 22.", "norm_zh": "一神只有一个终极的目标新耶路撒冷作神的扩大扩展和彰显2922节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God has only one ultimate goalthe New Jerusalem Gods enlargement expansion and expressionvv 2 9 22"}
{"zh": "二\t根据新约的整个启示，基督徒工作的惟一目标该是新耶路撒冷—二一2、10，二7，三12：", "en": "B.\tAccording to the entire revelation of the New Testament, the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 21:2, 10; 2:7; 3:12:", "norm_zh": "二根据新约的整个启示基督徒工作的惟一目标该是新耶路撒冷二一210二7三12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to the entire revelation of the New Testament the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New JerusalemRev 212 10 27 312"}
{"zh": "1\t新耶路撒冷是使徒们生活与工作的最高点—2、10节。", "en": "1.\tThe New Jerusalem was the highest point of the apostles' living and work.—vv. 2, 10.", "norm_zh": "1新耶路撒冷是使徒们生活与工作的最高点210节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The New Jerusalem was the highest point of the apostles living and workvv 2 10"}
{"zh": "2\t我们必须以神永远经纶的目标─新耶路撒冷─为我们惟一并终极的目标—2、10节。", "en": "2.\tWe must take the goal of God's eternal economy—the New Jerusalem—as our unique and ultimate goal:—vv. 2, 10:", "norm_zh": "2我们必须以神永远经纶的目标新耶路撒冷为我们惟一并终极的目标210节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We must take the goal of Gods eternal economythe New Jerusalemas our unique and ultimate goalvv 2 10"}
{"zh": "伍\t新耶路撒冷是照着使徒的教训建造的—二一14，徒二42，太十六18：", "en": "V.\tThe New Jerusalem is built according to the apostles' teaching:—Rev. 21:14; Acts 2:42; Matt. 16:18:", "norm_zh": "伍新耶路撒冷是照着使徒的教训建造的二一14徒二42太十六18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The New Jerusalem is built according to the apostles teachingRev 2114 Acts 242 Matt 1618"}
{"zh": "二\t使徒的教训是神在新约中的整个说话，论到神新约的经纶，就是要得着一个神人二性联结调和的宇宙合并—启五9，二一3、22，约十四10~11。", "en": "B.\tThe teaching of the apostles is the entire speaking of God in the New Testament concerning God's New Testament economy, which is to gain a universal incorporation of the union and mingling of divinity with humanity.—Rev. 5:9; 21:3, 22; John 14:10-11.", "norm_zh": "二使徒的教训是神在新约中的整个说话论到神新约的经纶就是要得着一个神人二性联结调和的宇宙合并启五9二一322约十四1011", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The teaching of the apostles is the entire speaking of God in the New Testament concerning Gods New Testament economy which is to gain a universal incorporation of the union and mingling of divinity with humanityRev 59 213 22 John 141011"}
{"zh": "陆\t新耶路撒冷是神完整救恩的具体表现—罗五18，八10，启二一19~20：", "en": "VI.\tThe New Jerusalem is the embodiment of God's complete salvation:—Rom. 5:18; 8:10; Rev. 21:19-20:", "norm_zh": "陆新耶路撒冷是神完整救恩的具体表现罗五18八10启二一1920", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The New Jerusalem is the embodiment of Gods complete salvationRom 518 810 Rev 211920"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷的根基是神的义和神的信实，其完成是神的生命和神的性情—启二一19~20，创九8~17。", "en": "B.\tThe foundation of the New Jerusalem is the righteousness of God with God's faithfulness, and the consummation is God's life with God's nature.—Rev. 21:19-20; Gen. 9:8-17.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷的根基是神的义和神的信实其完成是神的生命和神的性情启二一1920创九817", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The foundation of the New Jerusalem is the righteousness of God with Gods faithfulness and the consummation is Gods life with Gods natureRev 211920 Gen 9817"}
{"zh": "三\t整个新耶路撒冷乃是生命建造在神义之根基上的事—启二一14、19~20，诗八九14。", "en": "C.\tThe entire New Jerusalem is a matter of life built on the foundation of God's righteousness.—Rev. 21:14, 19-20; Psa. 89:14.", "norm_zh": "三整个新耶路撒冷乃是生命建造在神义之根基上的事启二一141920诗八九14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The entire New Jerusalem is a matter of life built on the foundation of Gods righteousnessRev 2114 1920 Psa 8914"}
{"zh": "一\t在上的耶路撒冷作信徒之母，乃是恩典的新约，由撒拉所象征—创十七15，来十二22。", "en": "A.\tThe Jerusalem above as the mother of the believers is the new covenant of grace symbolized by Sarah.—Gen. 17:15; Heb. 12:22.", "norm_zh": "一在上的耶路撒冷作信徒之母乃是恩典的新约由撒拉所象征创十七15来十二22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Jerusalem above as the mother of the believers is the new covenant of grace symbolized by SarahGen 1715 Heb 1222"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是由经过过程之三一神分赐到信徒里面作恩典所产生的，好将他们生为许多儿子，组成新耶路撒冷，就是他们的母─启二一7，加四26。", "en": "B. The New Jerusalem is produced by the dispensing of the processed Triune God into the believers as grace to beget them as many sons to compose the New Jerusalem, which is their mother—Rev. 21:7; Gal. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是由经过过程之三一神分赐到信徒里面作恩典所产生的好将他们生为许多儿子组成新耶路撒冷就是他们的母启二一7加四26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is produced by the dispensing of the processed Triune God into the believers as grace to beget them as many sons to compose the New Jerusalem which is their motherRev 217 Gal 426"}
{"zh": "三\t父（恩典的源头）、恩典、母、众子、城和新约，要成为一个实体─新耶路撒冷—来十二22，启二一2~3，三12，加四26。", "en": "C.\tThe Father (the source of grace), the grace, the mother, the sons, the city, and the new covenant will become one entity—the New Jerusalem.—Heb. 12:22; Rev. 21:2-3; 3:12; Gal. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "三父恩典的源头恩典母众子城和新约要成为一个实体新耶路撒冷来十二22启二一23三12加四26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Father the source of grace the grace the mother the sons the city and the new covenant will become one entitythe New JerusalemHeb 1222 Rev 2123 312 Gal 426"}
{"zh": "捌\t新耶路撒冷是神圣儿子名分的总和─启三12，十四1，二一7：", "en": "VIII.\tThe New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonship.—Rev. 3:12; 14:1; 21:7:", "norm_zh": "捌新耶路撒冷是神圣儿子名分的总和启三12十四1二一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonshipRev 312 141 217"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是神众子的组合，他们有神的生命和性情，承受了经过过程之三一神的一切所是—7、10、18~21节，来二10~12。", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is a composition of all the sons of God, who have God's life and nature and who inherit all that the processed Triune God is.—vv. 7, 10, 18-21; Heb. 2:10-12.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是神众子的组合他们有神的生命和性情承受了经过过程之三一神的一切所是7101821节来二1012", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is a composition of all the sons of God who have Gods life and nature and who inherit all that the processed Triune God isvv 7 10 1821 Heb 21012"}
{"zh": "1\t神预定我们得儿子的名分─弗一5，加四5。", "en": "1\tGod predestinated us unto sonship.—Eph. 1:5; Gal. 4:5.", "norm_zh": "1神预定我们得儿子的名分弗一5加四5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God predestinated us unto sonshipEph 15 Gal 45"}
{"zh": "4\t因此，新约启示，神的心意是要产生众子，并启示新耶路撒冷乃是神圣儿子名分的总和—约十二24，启二一7。", "en": "4\tHence, the New Testament reveals that God's intention is to produce sons and that the New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonship.—John 12:24; Rev. 21:7.", "norm_zh": "4因此新约启示神的心意是要产生众子并启示新耶路撒冷乃是神圣儿子名分的总和约十二24启二一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Hence the New Testament reveals that Gods intention is to produce sons and that the New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonshipJohn 1224 Rev 217"}
{"zh": "玖\t新耶路撒冷是涌流之三一神的目的─约四14下，启二二1~2：", "en": "IX.\tThe New Jerusalem is the destination of the flowing Triune God.—John 4:14b; Rev. 22:1-2:", "norm_zh": "玖新耶路撒冷是涌流之三一神的目的约四14下启二二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The New Jerusalem is the destination of the flowing Triune GodJohn 414b Rev 2212"}
{"zh": "1\t“涌入”（即罗马五章二十一节的“得”，直译，以至于）说到目的，指明永远的生命是涌流之三一神的目的—罗五21。", "en": "1\t“Into” speaks of destination, indicating that eternal life is the destination of the flowing Triune God.—Rom. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1涌入即罗马五章二十一节的得直译以至于说到目的指明永远的生命是涌流之三一神的目的罗五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Into speaks of destination indicating that eternal life is the destination of the flowing Triune GodRom 521"}
{"zh": "2\t永远的生命至终要成为新耶路撒冷，就是神圣生命的总和；因此，“涌入永远的生命”意思是“归入新耶路撒冷”—约四14下。", "en": "2\tThe eternal life eventually will become the New Jerusalem, the totality of the divine life; hence, “into eternal life” means “into the New Jerusalem.”—John 4:14b.", "norm_zh": "2永远的生命至终要成为新耶路撒冷就是神圣生命的总和因此涌入永远的生命意思是归入新耶路撒冷约四14下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The eternal life eventually will become the New Jerusalem the totality of the divine life hence into eternal life means into the New JerusalemJohn 414b"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是神在三个阶段涌流的结果：父的阶段、子的阶段、灵的阶段—十五26，启二二1~2：", "en": "B. The New Jerusalem is the issue of God's flowing in three stages: in the Father's stage, in the Son's stage, and in the Spirit's stage:—John 15:26; Rev. 22:1-2:", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是神在三个阶段涌流的结果父的阶段子的阶段灵的阶段十五26启二二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the issue of Gods flowing in three stages in the Fathers stage in the Sons stage and in the Spirits stageJohn 1526 Rev 2212"}
{"zh": "1\t父是源，就是源头；子是泉，灵是涌流的河，这个涌流的结果是永远的生命，就是新耶路撒冷—约十五26。", "en": "1. The Father is the fountain as the source, the Son is the spring, the Spirit is the flowing river, and this flowing issues in the eternal life, which is the New Jerusalem.—John 15:26.", "norm_zh": "1父是源就是源头子是泉灵是涌流的河这个涌流的结果是永远的生命就是新耶路撒冷约十五26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Father is the fountain as the source the Son is the spring the Spirit is the flowing river and this flowing issues in the eternal life which is the New JerusalemJohn 1526"}
{"zh": "2\t“源”涌现，“泉”涌出，这涌出乃是流，也就是河，涌成新耶路撒冷—启二二1~2。", "en": "2. The fountain emerges, the spring gushes, and the gushing is the flowing as a river into the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 22:1-2.", "norm_zh": "2源涌现泉涌出这涌出乃是流也就是河涌成新耶路撒冷启二二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The fountain emerges the spring gushes and the gushing is the flowing as a river into the New JerusalemRev 2212"}
{"zh": "拾\t新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿，乃是救赎之神和蒙祂救赎之人相互的居所─二一2~3、22，弗二21~22：", "en": "X. The New Jerusalem, which is both the tabernacle and the temple, is a mutual dwelling place for the redeeming God and His redeemed.—Rev. 21:2-3, 22; Eph. 2:21-22:", "norm_zh": "拾新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿乃是救赎之神和蒙祂救赎之人相互的居所二一2322弗二2122", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X The New Jerusalem which is both the tabernacle and the temple is a mutual dwelling place for the redeeming God and His redeemedRev 2123 22 Eph 22122"}
{"zh": "一\t帐幕是神所救赎的人，殿是救赎的神—启七15，二一22：", "en": "A. The tabernacle is God's redeemed, and the temple is the redeeming God:—Rev. 7:15; 21:22:", "norm_zh": "一帐幕是神所救赎的人殿是救赎的神启七15二一22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The tabernacle is Gods redeemed and the temple is the redeeming GodRev 715 2122"}
{"zh": "1\t帐幕主要是用神所救赎之人的人性建造的，作神的居所—七15。", "en": "1. The tabernacle is built mostly with the humanity of God's redeemed to be God's dwelling place.—Rev. 7:15.", "norm_zh": "1帐幕主要是用神所救赎之人的人性建造的作神的居所七15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The tabernacle is built mostly with the humanity of Gods redeemed to be Gods dwelling placeRev 715"}
{"zh": "2\t殿主要用神性建造的，作神所救赎之人的居所—二一22。", "en": "2. The temple is built mostly with divinity to be the dwelling place of God's redeemed.—Rev. 21:22.", "norm_zh": "2殿主要用神性建造的作神所救赎之人的居所二一22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The temple is built mostly with divinity to be the dwelling place of Gods redeemedRev 2122"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是神与蒙祂救赎之人的调和，而这调和乃是相互的居所—创五1注1。", "en": "B. The New Jerusalem is the mingling of God with His redeemed, and this mingling is a mutual dwelling place.—Gen. 5:1 note 1.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是神与蒙祂救赎之人的调和而这调和乃是相互的居所创五1注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the mingling of God with His redeemed and this mingling is a mutual dwelling placeGen 51 note 1"}
{"zh": "三\t经过过程之三一神与蒙祂救赎的人，乃是一个调和的实体，直到永远—启二一7、22，弗四4~6。", "en": "C. The processed Triune God and His redeemed will be one mingled entity for eternity.—Rev. 21:7, 22; Eph. 4:4-6.", "norm_zh": "三经过过程之三一神与蒙祂救赎的人乃是一个调和的实体直到永远启二一722弗四46", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The processed Triune God and His redeemed will be one mingled entity for eternityRev 217 22 Eph 446"}
{"zh": "拾壹\t新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦—“永世对耦”─神圣罗曼史的完成─启二一2，二二17：", "en": "XI. The New Jerusalem is a universal couple—\"a loving pair eternally\"—the consummation of the divine romance—Rev. 21:2; 22:17:", "norm_zh": "拾壹新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦永世对耦神圣罗曼史的完成启二一2二二17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XI The New Jerusalem is a universal couplea loving pair eternallythe consummation of the divine romanceRev 212 2217"}
{"zh": "一\t按其人性说，新耶路撒冷是羔羊那人性的妻子（有神圣的生命和性情）─二一2、9。", "en": "A. According to its humanity, the New Jerusalem is the human wife (with the divine life and nature) of the Lamb.—Rev. 21:2, 9.", "norm_zh": "一按其人性说新耶路撒冷是羔羊哪人性的妻子有神圣的生命和性情二一29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A According to its humanity the New Jerusalem is the human wife with the divine life and nature of the LambRev 212 9"}
{"zh": "二\t按其神性说，新耶路撒冷是蒙神救赎之选民那神性的丈夫（救赎的神，在祂终极完成之具体化身基督里，有祂的人性生命和性情）—2节、赛五四5，启十二1~6、13~17。", "en": "B.\tAccording to its divinity, the New Jerusalem is the divine Husband (the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment, Christ, with His human life and nature) of God's redeemed elect.—v. 2; Isa. 54:5; Rev. 12:1-6, 13-17.", "norm_zh": "二按其神性说新耶路撒冷是蒙神救赎之选民哪神性的丈夫救赎的神在祂终极完成之具体化身基督里有祂的人性生命和性情2节赛五四5启十二161317", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to its divinity the New Jerusalem is the divine Husband the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment Christ with His human life and nature of Gods redeemed electv 2 Isa 545 Rev 1216 1317"}
{"zh": "三\t启示录二十二章十七节指明，基督与作祂妻子的新耶路撒冷乃是宇宙的对耦，直到永远：", "en": "C. Revelation 22:17 indicates that Christ and the New Jerusalem as His wife will be a universal couple for eternity:", "norm_zh": "三启示录二十二章十七节指明基督与作祂妻子的新耶路撒冷乃是宇宙的对耦直到永远", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Revelation 2217 indicates that Christ and the New Jerusalem as His wife will be a universal couple for eternity"}
{"zh": "1\t那是经过过程之三一神总和的那灵，与那些如今已完全成熟、作祂新妇的信徒成为一—17节，二一9。", "en": "1.\tThe Spirit, who is the totality of the processed Triune God, becomes one with the believers, who are now fully matured to be the bride.—v. 17; Rev. 21:9.", "norm_zh": "1哪是经过过程之三一神总和的哪灵与哪些如今已完全成熟作祂新妇的信徒成为一17节二一9", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Spirit who is the totality of the processed Triune God becomes one with the believers who are now fully matured to be the bridev 17 Rev 219"}
{"zh": "2\t经过过程之三一神的终极完成，与蒙祂拣选、救赎、重生、变化之人的终极完成，成为宇宙的对耦，彰显三一神直到永远—2节。", "en": "2. The consummation of the processed Triune God and the consummation of His chosen, redeemed, regenerated, and transformed people will be a universal couple expressing the Triune God for eternity—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2经过过程之三一神的终极完成与蒙祂拣选救赎重生变化之人的终极完成成为宇宙的对耦彰显三一神直到永远2节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The consummation of the processed Triune God and the consummation of His chosen redeemed regenerated and transformed people will be a universal couple expressing the Triune God for eternityv 2"}
{"zh": "拾贰\t新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并─经过过程并终极完成之三一神，与蒙祂救赎、重生、变化、并荣化之选民，合并成为一个合并—12~14节，帖前五23：", "en": "XII.\tThe New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and man—the processed and consummated Triune God incorporated into an incorporation with His redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified elect:—vv. 12-14; 1 Thes. 5:23:", "norm_zh": "拾贰新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并经过过程并终极完成之三一神与蒙祂救赎重生变化并荣化之选民合并成为一个合并1214节帖前五23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XII The New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and manthe processed and consummated Triune God incorporated into an incorporation with His redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified electvv 1214 1 Thes 523"}
{"zh": "一\t神的心意是要所有在基督里的信徒都合并到神自己的合并里，成为一个扩大、神人二性的合并—启二一2、12~14，二二17上。", "en": "A.\tGod's intention is that all the believers in Christ would be incorporated into Himself as an incorporation to be an enlarged, divine and human incorporation.—Rev. 21:2, 12-14; 22:17a.", "norm_zh": "一神的心意是要所有在基督里的信徒都合并到神自己的合并里成为一个扩大神人二性的合并启二一21214二二17上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods intention is that all the believers in Christ would be incorporated into Himself as an incorporation to be an enlarged divine and human incorporationRev 212 1214 2217a"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经向我们揭示，神的经纶是要将神与人合并成为一个合并，这个合并先是基督的身体，然后是新耶路撒冷—弗一23，启二一3。", "en": "B.\tThe Bible unveils to us that God's economy is to have God and man incorporated into an incorporation, which is first the Body of Christ and then the New Jerusalem.—Eph. 1:23; Rev. 21:3.", "norm_zh": "二圣经向我们揭示神的经纶是要将神与人合并成为一个合并这个合并先是基督的身体然后是新耶路撒冷弗一23启二一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Bible unveils to us that Gods economy is to have God and man incorporated into an incorporation which is first the Body of Christ and then the New JerusalemEph 123 Rev 213"}
{"zh": "三\t经过过程并终极完成之三一神与重生信徒之联结、调和与合并，终极完成为新耶路撒冷—三12，二一2。", "en": "C.\tThe union, mingling, and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God with the regenerated believers consummates as the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 3:12; 21:2.", "norm_zh": "三经过过程并终极完成之三一神与重生信徒之联结调和与合并终极完成为新耶路撒冷三12二一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The union mingling and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God with the regenerated believers consummates as the New JerusalemRev 312 212"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结", "en": "The New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation"}
{"zh": "神在已过的永远里是单独的。但在启示录末了，祂有了一位新妇。启示录十九章给我们看见羔羊的婚娶和祂的婚筵。（启十九7~9）神有一位团体的妻子，这团体的妻子包括来自各支派、各方言、各民族、各邦国的人。（启五9）召会作基督的妻子这面，乃是终极完成于新耶路撒冷。神在她里面将得着完满爱的满足并极致彰显的安息，直到永永远远。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第十二篇）", "en": "In eternity past, God was single. But at the end of Revelation, He has a bride. Revelation 19 shows us the Lamb's marriage and His marriage dinner (Rev. 19:7-9). God has a corporate wife, and this corporate wife includes men from every tribe and tongue and people and nation (Rev. 5:9). The aspect of the church as the wife of Christ is ultimately consummated in the New Jerusalem. In her, God will have the fullest satisfaction in love and the utmost rest in expression forever and ever.", "norm_zh": "神在已过的永远里是单独的但在启示录末了祂有了一位新妇启示录十九章给我们看见羔羊的婚娶和祂的婚筵启十九79神有一位团体的妻子这团体的妻子包括来自各支派各方言各民族各邦国的人启五9召会作基督的妻子这面乃是终极完成于新耶路撒冷神在她里面将得着完满爱的满足并极致彰显的安息直到永永远远李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In eternity past God was single But at the end of Revelation He has a bride Revelation 19 shows us the Lambs marriage and His marriage dinner Rev 1979 God has a corporate wife and this corporate wife includes men from every tribe and tongue and people and nation Rev 59 The aspect of the church as the wife of Christ is ultimately consummated in the New Jerusalem In her God will have the fullest satisfaction in love and the utmost rest in expression forever and ever"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷乃是一个生机的构成", "en": "The New Jerusalem is an organic constitution", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷乃是一个生机的构成", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is an organic constitution"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷是所有旧约及新约时代得重生之圣徒的一个组合，他们凭着神建造在一起，作神永远的建筑；新耶路撒冷也是所有蒙救赎、重生、变化并得荣之三部分人，与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和。在成为肉体、钉死和复活里，三一神已经经过过程并终极完成，与人，就是祂所拣选的人成为一。历经神各时代里许多的世代，三部分的人已经蒙救赎、重生、变化并得荣，要与在已过的永远里拣选他们作祂配偶、住处并彰显的三一神，在将来的永远里成为一。", "en": "The New Jerusalem is a composition of all the Old and New Testament regenerated saints built together by God as His eternal building; it is also the mingling of the tripartite man, who has been redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified, with the Triune God, who has been processed and consummated. In incarnation, crucifixion, and resurrection, the Triune God was processed and consummated to be one with man, His chosen people. Throughout many generations in God's dispensations, the tripartite man has been redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified to be one in the coming eternity with the Triune God, who chose them in eternity past to be His spouse, His dwelling place, and His expression.", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷是所有旧约及新约时代得重生之圣徒的一个组合他们凭着神建造在一起作神永远的建筑新耶路撒冷也是所有蒙救赎重生变化并得荣之三部分人与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和在成为肉体钉死和复活里三一神已经经过过程并终极完成与人就是祂所拣选的人成为一历经神各时代里许多的世代三部分的人已经蒙救赎重生变化并得荣要与在已过的永远里拣选他们作祂配偶住处并彰显的三一神在将来的永远里成为一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is a composition of all the Old and New Testament regenerated saints built together by God as His eternal building it is also the mingling of the tripartite man who has been redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified with the Triune God who has been processed and consummated In incarnation crucifixion and resurrection the Triune God was processed and consummated to be one with man His chosen people Throughout many generations in Gods dispensations the tripartite man has been redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified to be one in the coming eternity with the Triune God who chose them in eternity past to be His spouse His dwelling place and His expression"}
{"zh": "在启示录一章一节，我们看见，神圣的启示乃是给了耶稣基督，并且祂是用表号指示给人。……启示录这卷书的启示主要的是由表号组成，表号就是有属灵意义的象征……。新耶路撒冷也是一个表号，表征神经纶终极的完成。", "en": "In Revelation 1:1 we see that the divine revelation was given to Jesus Christ, and He made it known by signs. ... The revelation in the book of Revelation is composed mainly of signs, and a sign is a symbol with spiritual significance. ... The New Jerusalem is also a sign, signifying the ultimate consummation of God's economy.", "norm_zh": "在启示录一章一节我们看见神圣的启示乃是给了耶稣基督并且祂是用表号指示给人启示录这卷书的启示主要的是由表号组成表号就是有属灵意义的象征新耶路撒冷也是一个表号表征神经纶终极的完成", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In Revelation 11 we see that the divine revelation was given to Jesus Christ and He made it known by signs The revelation in the book of Revelation is composed mainly of signs and a sign is a symbol with spiritual significance The New Jerusalem is also a sign signifying the ultimate consummation of Gods economy"}
{"zh": "在列祖时代，神得着了蒙拣选的列祖，作为祂新造里新族类的头一部分，由启示录十二章宇宙妇人头上所戴十二星的冠冕来表征，为着建造新耶路撒冷，作神在将来永远里的彰显。", "en": "In the dispensation of the patriarchs, God gained the chosen patriarchs as the first part of the new race in His new creation, signified by the crown of twelve stars on the head of the universal woman in Revelation 12, for the building of the New Jerusalem to be God's expression in the coming eternity.", "norm_zh": "在列祖时代神得着了蒙拣选的列祖作为祂新造里新族类的头一部分由启示录十二章宇宙妇人头上所戴十二星的冠冕来表征为着建造新耶路撒冷作神在将来永远里的彰显", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the dispensation of the patriarchs God gained the chosen patriarchs as the first part of the new race in His new creation signified by the crown of twelve stars on the head of the universal woman in Revelation 12 for the building of the New Jerusalem to be Gods expression in the coming eternity"}
{"zh": "在律法时代，神得着了一班人，就是启示录十二章宇宙妇人脚踏的月亮所表征的，作为新造族类的第二部分，好构成新耶路撒冷，作神在新天新地里永远的彰显。", "en": "In the age of law, God gained a group of people, signified by the moon under the feet of the universal woman in Revelation 12, as the second part of the new race of the new creation, to constitute the New Jerusalem to be God's eternal expression in the new heaven and new earth.", "norm_zh": "在律法时代神得着了一班人就是启示录十二章宇宙妇人脚踏的月亮所表征的作为新造族类的第二部分好构成新耶路撒冷作神在新天新地里永远的彰显", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the age of law God gained a group of people signified by the moon under the feet of the universal woman in Revelation 12 as the second part of the new race of the new creation to constitute the New Jerusalem to be Gods eternal expression in the new heaven and new earth"}
{"zh": "在恩典时代，神就得着所有在新约里相信基督的人，作为神新造里新族类的第三部分，也是主要部分，由启示录十二章宇宙妇人身披的日头所表征，为着完成新耶路撒冷的构成，好作神在永世里终极并完满的彰显。", "en": "In the age of grace, God gained all those who believe in Christ in the New Testament as the third part, which is also the main part, of the new race of the new creation, signified by the sun with which the universal woman in Revelation 12 is clothed, for the completion of the constitution of the New Jerusalem to be God's ultimate and consummate expression in eternity.", "norm_zh": "在恩典时代神就得着所有在新约里相信基督的人作为神新造里新族类的第三部分也是主要部分由启示录十二章宇宙妇人身披的日头所表征为着完成新耶路撒冷的构成好作神在永世里终极并完满的彰显", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the age of grace God gained all those who believe in Christ in the New Testament as the third part which is also the main part of the new race of the new creation signified by the sun with which the universal woman in Revelation 12 is clothed for the completion of the constitution of the New Jerusalem to be Gods ultimate and consummate expression in eternity"}
{"zh": "在国度时代，就是公义时代里，神要使在恩典时代里不成熟的信徒，达到在生命上的成熟；祂也要使悔改的以色列人，……成为在神新造里新族类的构成成分。……这新族类的人，将是永世里新天新地之新耶路撒冷的构成成分。（新约总论，二百五十七篇）", "en": "In the age of the kingdom, which is the age of righteousness, God will cause the believers who are immature in the age of grace to reach maturity in life; He will also cause the repenting Israelites... to become the constituents of the new race in God's new creation. ...The people of this new race will be the constituents of the New Jerusalem in the new heaven and new earth in eternity.", "norm_zh": "在国度时代就是公义时代里神要使在恩典时代里不成熟的信徒达到在生命上的成熟祂也要使悔改的以色列人成为在神新造里新族类的构成成分这新族类的人将是永世里新天新地之新耶路撒冷的构成成分新约总论二百五十七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the age of the kingdom which is the age of righteousness God will cause the believers who are immature in the age of grace to reach maturity in life He will also cause the repenting Israelites to become the constituents of the new race in Gods new creation The people of this new race will be the constituents of the New Jerusalem in the new heaven and new earth in eternity"}
{"zh": "根据新约的整个启示，基督徒工作的独一目标该是新耶路撒冷，就是神永远经纶终极的目标。……召会的堕落，主要的是由于这个事实：几乎所有的基督工人都被岔开，以新耶路撒冷之外的许多事物为他们的目标。因此，在召会的堕落下，我们要作一个得胜者答应主的呼召，就不仅需要胜过消极的事物，更需要胜过那些顶替新耶路撒冷为目标的积极的事物。那一种仅以救灵魂为目标的传福音，我们不要。我们传福音的目标，必须是新耶路撒冷。要成为得胜者，我们应当以神永远经纶的目标，就是新耶路撒冷，为独一无二且终极无比的目标。", "en": "According to the entire revelation of the New Testament, the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New Jerusalem, which is the ultimate goal of God's eternal economy. ...The degradation of the church is mainly due to this fact: almost all Christian workers have been distracted to take many things other than the New Jerusalem as their goal. Therefore, under the degradation of the church, to be an overcomer answering the Lord's call, we need to overcome not only the negative things but even more the positive things that replace the New Jerusalem as the goal. We do not want that kind of gospel preaching that has only the saving of souls as its goal. The goal of our gospel preaching must be the New Jerusalem. To be overcomers, we should take the goal of God's eternal economy, the New Jerusalem, as our unique and ultimate goal.", "norm_zh": "根据新约的整个启示基督徒工作的独一目标该是新耶路撒冷就是神永远经纶终极的目标召会的堕落主要的是由于这个事实几乎所有的基督工人都被岔开以新耶路撒冷之外的许多事物为他们的目标因此在召会的堕落下我们要作一个得胜者答应主的呼召就不仅需要胜过消极的事物更需要胜过哪些顶替新耶路撒冷为目标的积极的事物哪一种仅以救灵魂为目标的传福音我们不要我们传福音的目标必须是新耶路撒冷要成为得胜者我们应当以神永远经纶的目标就是新耶路撒冷为独一无二且终极无比的目标", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "According to the entire revelation of the New Testament the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New Jerusalem which is the ultimate goal of Gods eternal economy The degradation of the church is mainly due to this fact almost all Christian workers have been distracted to take many things other than the New Jerusalem as their goal Therefore under the degradation of the church to be an overcomer answering the Lords call we need to overcome not only the negative things but even more the positive things that replace the New Jerusalem as the goal We do not want that kind of gospel preaching that has only the saving of souls as its goal The goal of our gospel preaching must be the New Jerusalem To be overcomers we should take the goal of Gods eternal economy the New Jerusalem as our unique and ultimate goal"}
{"zh": "十二使徒代表新约使徒的教训", "en": "The twelve apostles represent the apostles' teaching of the New Testament", "norm_zh": "十二使徒代表新约使徒的教训", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The twelve apostles represent the apostles teaching of the New Testament"}
{"zh": "神圣儿子名分的总和", "en": "The totality of the divine sonship", "norm_zh": "神圣儿子名分的总和", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The totality of the divine sonship"}
{"zh": "作涌流之三一神的目的地", "en": "As the destination of the flowing Triune God", "norm_zh": "作涌流之三一神的目的地", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "As the destination of the flowing Triune God"}
{"zh": "主在四章十四节下半说，“我所赐的水，要在他里面成为泉源，直涌入永远的生命”。父神是源，显在子神这泉里，涌流成为一道河，表征灵神。三一神涌流成为永远的生命，而这永远的生命有其总和。我们属人的生命也有其总和；一个活的人，就是属人生命的总和。神圣生命的总和乃是新耶路撒冷，就是这位涌流之三一神的目的地。约翰的着作所涵盖的，是从神直到新耶路撒冷。至终，这位三一、永远的神成了与我们众人合并的新耶路撒冷。我们不是进入新耶路撒冷，我们乃是成为新耶路撒冷。我们的成为，就是我们的进入。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十五篇）", "en": "In John 4:14b the Lord said, \"The water that I will give him will become in him a fountain of water springing up into eternal life.\" God the Father is the fountain emerging in God the Son as a spring gushing up to be a river, signifying God the Spirit. The Triune God flows into eternal life, and the eternal life has its totality. Our human life also has its totality. A living person is the totality of the human life. The totality of the divine life is the New Jerusalem, which is the destination of the flowing Triune God. John's writings cover from God to the New Jerusalem. Eventually, this triune, eternal God becomes the New Jerusalem incorporated with us all. We do not enter into the New Jerusalem; we become the New Jerusalem. Our becoming is our entering.", "norm_zh": "主在四章十四节下半说我所赐的水要在他里面成为泉源直涌入永远的生命父神是源显在子神这泉里涌流成为一道河表征灵神三一神涌流成为永远的生命而这永远的生命有其总和我们属人的生命也有其总和一个活的人就是属人生命的总和神圣生命的总和乃是新耶路撒冷就是这位涌流之三一神的目的地约翰的着作所涵盖的是从神直到新耶路撒冷至终这位三一永远的神成了与我们众人合并的新耶路撒冷我们不是进入新耶路撒冷我们乃是成为新耶路撒冷我们的成为就是我们的进入李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In John 414b the Lord said The water that I will give him will become in him a fountain of water springing up into eternal life God the Father is the fountain emerging in God the Son as a spring gushing up to be a river signifying God the Spirit The Triune God flows into eternal life and the eternal life has its totality Our human life also has its totality A living person is the totality of the human life The totality of the divine life is the New Jerusalem which is the destination of the flowing Triune God Johns writings cover from God to the New Jerusalem Eventually this triune eternal God becomes the New Jerusalem incorporated with us all We do not enter into the New Jerusalem we become the New Jerusalem Our becoming is our entering"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿", "en": "The New Jerusalem is both the tabernacle and the temple", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is both the tabernacle and the temple"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷有两种性情：人性与神性。按其人性说，新耶路撒冷是神在人间的帐幕─神在祂人性里在地上人间的居所。（启二一3）……新耶路撒冷是属人的居所，因为牠是由人性构成的。……按其神性说，新耶路撒冷是神的殿，作蒙祂救赎之选民的居所。（22）圣城是神的殿，因为祂是神圣的。……按其人性说，是人的帐幕；按其神性说，是神的殿。这是属人的居所，居住者却是神。神怎么能住在人的地方？因为祂成了一个人。同样的，我们人怎么能住在神的殿里？因为我们（在生命和性情上）成了神（但无分于神的神格）。这是神与人彼此互住。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒，第一篇）", "en": "The New Jerusalem has two natures: humanity and divinity. According to its humanity, the New Jerusalem is the tabernacle of God among men—the dwelling place of God in His humanity among men on earth (Rev. 21:3). ...The New Jerusalem is a human dwelling place because it is constituted of humanity. ...According to its divinity, the New Jerusalem is the temple of God as the dwelling place of His redeemed elect (v. 22). The holy city is the temple of God because it is divine. ...According to its humanity, it is a human tabernacle; according to its divinity, it is a divine temple. It is a human dwelling place, but the Dweller is God. How can God dwell in a human place? Because He became a man. In the same way, how can we humans dwell in God's temple? Because we (in life and in nature) have been made God (but not in the Godhead). This is the mutual abiding of God and man.", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷有两种性情人性与神性按其人性说新耶路撒冷是神在人间的帐幕神在祂人性里在地上人间的居所启二一3新耶路撒冷是属人的居所因为它是由人性构成的按其神性说新耶路撒冷是神的殿作蒙祂救赎之选民的居所22圣城是神的殿因为祂是神圣的按其人性说是人的帐幕按其神性说是神的殿这是属人的居所居住者却是神神怎么能住在人的地方因为祂成了一个人同样的我们人怎么能住在神的殿里因为我们在生命和性情上成了神但无分于神的神格这是神与人彼此互住李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem has two natures humanity and divinity According to its humanity the New Jerusalem is the tabernacle of God among menthe dwelling place of God in His humanity among men on earth Rev 213 The New Jerusalem is a human dwelling place because it is constituted of humanity According to its divinity the New Jerusalem is the temple of God as the dwelling place of His redeemed elect v 22 The holy city is the temple of God because it is divine According to its humanity it is a human tabernacle according to its divinity it is a divine temple It is a human dwelling place but the Dweller is God How can God dwell in a human place Because He became a man In the same way how can we humans dwell in Gods temple Because we in life and in nature have been made God but not in the Godhead This is the mutual abiding of God and man"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦神圣罗曼史的完成", "en": "The New Jerusalem is the consummation of the divine romance of a universal couple.", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦神圣罗曼史的完成", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is the consummation of the divine romance of a universal couple"}
{"zh": "按其人性说，新耶路撒冷是羔羊─救赎之神─的人性妻子，有神的生命和性情。（启二一2、9）这属人的妻子能与神圣的人位成为婚配，因为她有神圣的生命和性情。这使她有资格与救赎的神相配。一面，她是属人的；但另一面，她是神圣的。因为她是属人的，她就能成为救赎之神的人性妻子。因为她是神圣的，她就能与祂这神圣的人位成为婚配。按其神性说，这城是蒙神救赎之选民的神性丈夫（救赎之神在祂终极完成的具体化身基督里，有人的生命和性情）。妻子是属人的，丈夫是神圣的。属人的妻子怎么能与神圣的人位成为婚配？因为她有神圣人位的神圣性情和生命。同一个实体怎么能又是丈夫？因为新耶路撒冷是神圣的，神圣的神乃是其构成的一部分。所以，新耶路撒冷一面是妻子，另一面又是丈夫。新耶路撒冷按其人性说是妻子，按其神性说乃是丈夫。但作为神圣的丈夫，新耶路撒冷有属人的生命的性情。在其人性和神性里，新耶路撒冷乃是一个相互的住处，也是一对配偶，一对夫妇。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒，第一篇）", "en": "According to its humanity the New Jerusalem is the human wife (with the divine life and nature) of the Lamb—the redeeming God—(Rev. 21:2, 9). This human wife can marry a divine Person because she has the divine life and nature. This qualifies her to match the redeeming God. On the one hand, she is human; but on the other hand, she is divine. Because she is human, she can be the human wife of the redeeming God. Because she is divine, she can marry Him, this divine Person. According to its divinity, it is the divine Husband (the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment, Christ, with the human life and nature) of God's redeemed elect. The wife is human, and the Husband is divine. How can a human wife marry a divine Person? Because she has the divine Person's divine nature and life. How can the same entity also be a husband? Because the New Jerusalem is divine. The divine God is a part of its constituent. Therefore, on the one hand, it is a wife. On the other hand, it is a husband. The New Jerusalem is the wife according to its humanity and the husband according to its divinity. But as the divine Husband, the New Jerusalem has the human life and nature. In its humanity and in its divinity it is both a mutual abode and a couple, a wife and a husband.", "norm_zh": "按其人性说新耶路撒冷是羔羊救赎之神的人性妻子有神的生命和性情启二一29这属人的妻子能与神圣的人位成为婚配因为她有神圣的生命和性情这使她有资格与救赎的神相配一面她是属人的但另一面她是神圣的因为她是属人的她就能成为救赎之神的人性妻子因为她是神圣的她就能与祂这神圣的人位成为婚配按其神性说这城是蒙神救赎之选民的神性丈夫救赎之神在祂终极完成的具体化身基督里有人的生命和性情妻子是属人的丈夫是神圣的属人的妻子怎么能与神圣的人位成为婚配因为她有神圣人位的神圣性情和生命同一个实体怎么能又是丈夫因为新耶路撒冷是神圣的神圣的神乃是其构成的一部分所以新耶路撒冷一面是妻子另一面又是丈夫新耶路撒冷按其人性说是妻子按其神性说乃是丈夫但作为神圣的丈夫新耶路撒冷有属人的生命的性情在其人性和神性里新耶路撒冷乃是一个相互的住处也是一对配偶一对夫妇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "According to its humanity the New Jerusalem is the human wife with the divine life and nature of the Lambthe redeeming GodRev 212 9 This human wife can marry a divine Person because she has the divine life and nature This qualifies her to match the redeeming God On the one hand she is human but on the other hand she is divine Because she is human she can be the human wife of the redeeming God Because she is divine she can marry Him this divine Person According to its divinity it is the divine Husband the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment Christ with the human life and nature of Gods redeemed elect The wife is human and the Husband is divine How can a human wife marry a divine Person Because she has the divine Persons divine nature and life How can the same entity also be a husband Because the New Jerusalem is divine The divine God is a part of its constituent Therefore on the one hand it is a wife On the other hand it is a husband The New Jerusalem is the wife according to its humanity and the husband according to its divinity But as the divine Husband the New Jerusalem has the human life and nature In its humanity and in its divinity it is both a mutual abode and a couple a wife and a husband"}
{"zh": "新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并", "en": "The New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and man", "norm_zh": "新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and man"}
{"zh": "在我们的职事里，我们用了三个辞来描述信徒与三一神的关系：联结（union）、调和（mingling）、合并（incorporation）。……“联结”关系到我们与主在生命上的一。“调和”与神圣的性情和属人的性情有关。主又进一步给我们看见，我们与祂的关系不只是联结与调和，更是合并。", "en": "In our ministry we have used three words to describe the relationship of the believers with the Triune God: union, mingling, and incorporation. ... \"Union\" concerns our oneness with the Lord in life. \"Mingling\" has to do with the divine nature and the human nature. The Lord has further shown us that our relationship with Him is not only a union and a mingling but also an incorporation.", "norm_zh": "在我们的职事里我们用了三个辞来描述信徒与三一神的关系联结union调和mingling合并incorporation联结关系到我们与主在生命上的一调和与神圣的性情和属人的性情有关主又进一步给我们看见我们与祂的关系不只是联结与调和更是合并", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In our ministry we have used three words to describe the relationship of the believers with the Triune God union mingling and incorporation Union concerns our oneness with the Lord in life Mingling has to do with the divine nature and the human nature The Lord has further shown us that our relationship with Him is not only a union and a mingling but also an incorporation"}
{"zh": "联结与调和是指我们与主在生命和性情上（但不是在人位上）的关系。按着人而言，没有一个人能在另一个人里面。但在神圣奥秘的范围里，终极完成的神与得重生的信徒，这些人位乃是彼此内住的。这就是合并。在这宇宙、神圣且属人的合并里，有一些人位住在彼此里面，也就是互相内住。", "en": "Union and mingling refer to our relationship with the Lord in our life and nature (but not in our person). Humanly speaking, no person can be in another person. But in the divine and mystical realm, the consummated God and the regenerated believers, the persons, indwell one another. This is an incorporation. In this universal, divine-human incorporation, persons indwell one another, that is, they coinhere.", "norm_zh": "联结与调和是指我们与主在生命和性情上但不是在人位上的关系按着人而言没有一个人能在另一个人里面但在神圣奥秘的范围里终极完成的神与得重生的信徒这些人位乃是彼此内住的这就是合并在这宇宙神圣且属人的合并里有一些人位住在彼此里面也就是互相内住", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Union and mingling refer to our relationship with the Lord in our life and nature but not in our person Humanly speaking no person can be in another person But in the divine and mystical realm the consummated God and the regenerated believers the persons indwell one another This is an incorporation In this universal divinehuman incorporation persons indwell one another that is they coinhere"}
{"zh": "“合并”一辞也指明这些人位合并一起以完成其目的，就是完成神的经纶。……神经纶的目标乃是终极完成的神与重生信徒扩大的、宇宙的、神人二性的合并。……所有信徒至终都要合并到这一个伟大的合并里。这宇宙合并最终的完成乃是新耶路撒冷。（李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果，第五篇）", "en": "The word \"incorporation\" also indicates that these persons are incorporated together to carry out their purpose, that is, to carry out God's economy. ... The goal of God's economy is the enlarged, universal, divine-human incorporation of the consummated God with the regenerated believers. ... Eventually, all the believers will be incorporated into this great incorporation. The ultimate consummation of this universal incorporation is the New Jerusalem.", "norm_zh": "合并一辞也指明这些人位合并一起以完成其目的就是完成神的经纶神经纶的目标乃是终极完成的神与重生信徒扩大的宇宙的神人二性的合并所有信徒至终都要合并到这一个伟大的合并里这宇宙合并最终的完成乃是新耶路撒冷李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:06:05.410500+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The word incorporation also indicates that these persons are incorporated together to carry out their purpose that is to carry out Gods economy The goal of Gods economy is the enlarged universal divinehuman incorporation of the consummated God with the regenerated believers Eventually all the believers will be incorporated into this great incorporation The ultimate consummation of this universal incorporation is the New Jerusalem"}
{"zh": "壹\t新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结，以及整个神圣启示中心并终极完成的意义─启二一2、9~10，三12：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百六十四篇，第一段*）", "en": "I.\tThe New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation and the central and ultimate consummate significance of the entire divine revelation—Rev. 21:2, 9-10; 3:12:", "norm_zh": "壹新耶路撒冷是整个神圣启示的总结以及整个神圣启示中心并终极完成的意义启二一2910三121997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百六十四篇第一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The New Jerusalem is the conclusion of the entire divine revelation and the central and ultimate consummate significance of the entire divine revelationRev 212 910 312"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是圣经整个神圣启示的总结及总和的组成—二一2~3、9~10，来十一10。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第四十七篇，第十六段*）", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is the conclusion and the total composition of the entire revelation of the Bible.—Rev. 21:2-3, 9-10; Heb. 11:10.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是圣经整个神圣启示的总结及总和的组成二一23910来十一101997年夏训第十二篇以赛亚书生命读经第四十七篇第十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is the conclusion and the total composition of the entire revelation of the BibleRev 2123 910 Heb 1110"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经的一切启示与异象都终极完成于新耶路撒冷—启二一9~10，三12。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，在安那翰的各种聚会，第十三章，第十一段*）", "en": "B.\tAll the revelations and visions of the Scriptures consummate in the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 21:9-10; 3:12.", "norm_zh": "二圣经的一切启示与异象都终极完成于新耶路撒冷启二一910三121997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册在安哪翰的各种聚会第十三章第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B All the revelations and visions of the Scriptures consummate in the New JerusalemRev 21910 312"}
{"zh": "贰\t新耶路撒冷不是一座物质的城，乃是一个生机的构成，由救赎之经过过程并终极完成的三一神与蒙救赎、变化、并荣化之三部分人所构成，作终极完成之三一神的生机体，使祂借着得荣之三部分人，得着永远的扩大和彰显—三12，二一12~14、18~21：（1997年春季长老训练，第四篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，神人，第四章，第七十一段**）", "en": "II.\tThe New Jerusalem is not a physical city but an organic constitution constituted with the redeeming, processed, and consummated Triune God and the redeemed, transformed, and glorified tripartite men as an organism of the consummated Triune God for His eternal enlargement and expression through the glorified tripartite men.—Rev. 3:12; 21:12-14, 18-21:", "norm_zh": "贰新耶路撒冷不是一座物质的城乃是一个生机的构成由救赎之经过过程并终极完成的三一神与蒙救赎变化并荣化之三部分人所构成作终极完成之三一神的生机体使祂借着得荣之三部分人得着永远的扩大和彰显三12二一121418211997年春季长老训练第四篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册神人第四章第七十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The New Jerusalem is not a physical city but an organic constitution constituted with the redeeming processed and consummated Triune God and the redeemed transformed and glorified tripartite men as an organism of the consummated Triune God for His eternal enlargement and expression through the glorified tripartite menRev 312 211214 1821"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是由旧约和新约所有的圣徒组成，他们建造在一起，作神永远的建筑—五9，二一12~24，弗二15。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第二十八段*）", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is the composition of all the Old Testament and New Testament saints built together as God's eternal building.—Rev. 5:9; 21:12-24; Eph. 2:15.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是由旧约和新约所有的圣徒组成他们建造在一起作神永远的建筑五9二一1224弗二151997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第二十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is the composition of all the Old Testament and New Testament saints built together as Gods eternal buildingRev 59 211224 Eph 215"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是所有蒙救赎、重生、变化、荣化之三部分人，与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和—林后五17，启二一18~21。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒，第一章，第十八段*）", "en": "B.\tThe New Jerusalem is the mingling of all the redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified tripartite men with the processed and consummated Triune God.—2 Cor. 5:17; Rev. 21:18-21.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是所有蒙救赎重生变化荣化之三部分人与经过过程并终极完成之三一神的调和林后五17启二一18211997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒第一章第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the mingling of all the redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified tripartite men with the processed and consummated Triune God2 Cor 517 Rev 211821"}
{"zh": "三\t新耶路撒冷是经过过程并终极完成之三一神终极的显出，使祂得着彰显，直到永远—12~14、18~21节，二二5。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，过照着圣经中神圣启示高峰之生活实行的路，第一章，第一百二十九段**）", "en": "C.\tThe New Jerusalem is the ultimate manifestation of the processed and consummated Triune God for His expression for eternity.—vv. 12-14, 18-21; 22:5.", "norm_zh": "三新耶路撒冷是经过过程并终极完成之三一神终极的显出使祂得着彰显直到永远12141821节二二51997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册过照着圣经中神圣启示高峰之生活实行的路第一章第一百二十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The New Jerusalem is the ultimate manifestation of the processed and consummated Triune God for His expression for eternityvv 1214 1821 225"}
{"zh": "叁\t新耶路撒冷是一个表号─是圣经中最大并终极的表号─表征神在旧造里、在各时代中，新造工作之结果的集大成—一1，二一1~2，林后五17：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第十二段**）", "en": "III. The New Jerusalem is a sign—the greatest and ultimate sign in the Scriptures—of the aggregate of God's work of the new creation in all the dispensations within the old creation—Rev. 1:1; 21:1-2; 2 Cor. 5:17:", "norm_zh": "叁新耶路撒冷是一个表号是圣经中最大并终极的表号表征神在旧造里在各时代中新造工作之结果的集大成一1二一12林后五171997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The New Jerusalem is a signthe greatest and ultimate sign in the Scripturesof the aggregate of Gods work of the new creation in all the dispensations within the old creationRev 11 2112 2 Cor 517"}
{"zh": "一\t神在列祖时代在列祖身上的工作—启十二1，创十二3下，二二18。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第十三段*）", "en": "A.\tGod's work in the dispensation of the patriarchs on the patriarchs.—Rev. 12:1; Gen. 12:3b; 22:18.", "norm_zh": "一神在列祖时代在列祖身上的工作启十二1创十二3下二二181997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods work in the dispensation of the patriarchs on the patriarchsRev 121 Gen 123b 2218"}
{"zh": "二\t神在律法时代在以色列人身上的工作—启十二1，加三24。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第十五段*）", "en": "B.\tGod's work in the dispensation of the law on the children of Israel.—Rev. 12:1; Gal. 3:24.", "norm_zh": "二神在律法时代在以色列人身上的工作启十二1加三241997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Gods work in the dispensation of the law on the children of IsraelRev 121 Gal 324"}
{"zh": "三\t神在恩典时代在新约信徒身上的工作—启十二1，约一14，林前十五10。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第十八段*）", "en": "C.\tGod's work in the dispensation of grace on the New Testament believers.—Rev. 12:1; John 1:14; 1 Cor. 15:10.", "norm_zh": "三神在恩典时代在新约信徒身上的工作启十二1约一14林前十五101997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Gods work in the dispensation of grace on the New Testament believersRev 121 John 114 1 Cor 1510"}
{"zh": "四\t神在公义时代在得救的以色列人，和其余尚未得成全的新约信徒身上的工作—十五52，帖前四15~17，启十四14~16。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第二十一段*）", "en": "D. God's work in the dispensation of righteousness on the saved Israelites and on the rest of the New Testament believers not yet perfected.—1 Cor. 15:52; 1 Thess. 4:15-17; Rev. 14:14-16.", "norm_zh": "四神在公义时代在得救的以色列人和其余尚未得成全的新约信徒身上的工作十五52帖前四1517启十四14161997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第二十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods work in the dispensation of righteousness on the saved Israelites and on the rest of the New Testament believers not yet perfected1 Cor 1552 1 Thess 41517 Rev 141416"}
{"zh": "肆\t新耶路撒冷是神经纶终极的目标—三21，二一1~2、10：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第七章，第七段*）", "en": "IV. The New Jerusalem is the ultimate goal of God's economy:—Rev. 3:21; 21:1-2, 10:", "norm_zh": "肆新耶路撒冷是神经纶终极的目标三21二一12101997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第七章第七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The New Jerusalem is the ultimate goal of Gods economyRev 321 2112 10"}
{"zh": "一\t神只有一个终极的目标─新耶路撒冷，作神的扩大、扩展和彰显—2、9、22节。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果，第四章，第二十一段* *）", "en": "A. God has only one ultimate goal—the New Jerusalem, God's enlargement, expansion, and expression.—vv. 2, 9, 22.", "norm_zh": "一神只有一个终极的目标新耶路撒冷作神的扩大扩展和彰显2922节1997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果第四章第二十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God has only one ultimate goalthe New Jerusalem Gods enlargement expansion and expressionvv 2 9 22"}
{"zh": "二\t根据新约的整个启示，基督徒工作的惟一目标该是新耶路撒冷—二一2、10，二7，三12：（1997年春季长老训练，第四篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，活力排，第十四章，第三十五段*）", "en": "B. According to the entire revelation of the New Testament, the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 21:2, 10; 2:7; 3:12:", "norm_zh": "二根据新约的整个启示基督徒工作的惟一目标该是新耶路撒冷二一210二7三121997年春季长老训练第四篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册活力排第十四章第三十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to the entire revelation of the New Testament the unique goal of the Christian work should be the New JerusalemRev 212 10 27 312"}
{"zh": "1\t新耶路撒冷是使徒们生活与工作的最高点—二一2、10。（1997年夏训，第十二篇***）", "en": "1 The New Jerusalem was the highest point of the apostles' living and work.—Rev. 21:2, 10.", "norm_zh": "1新耶路撒冷是使徒们生活与工作的最高点二一2101997年夏训第十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The New Jerusalem was the highest point of the apostles living and workRev 212 10"}
{"zh": "2\t我们必须以神永远经纶的目标─新耶路撒冷─为我们惟一并终极的目标—2、10节。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，如何作同工与长老，并如何履行同工与长老的义务，第三章，第五十四段**）", "en": "2 We must take the goal of God's eternal economy—the New Jerusalem—as our unique and ultimate goal:—vv. 2, 10.", "norm_zh": "2我们必须以神永远经纶的目标新耶路撒冷为我们惟一并终极的目标210节1997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册如何作同工与长老并如何履行同工与长老的义务第三章第五十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We must take the goal of Gods eternal economythe New Jerusalemas our unique and ultimate goalvv 2 10"}
{"zh": "伍\t新耶路撒冷是照着使徒的教训建造的—二一14，徒二42，太十六18：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第四百零二十九篇，第十一段*）", "en": "V. The New Jerusalem is built according to the apostles' teaching:—Rev. 21:14; Acts 2:42; Matt. 16:18:", "norm_zh": "伍新耶路撒冷是照着使徒的教训建造的二一14徒二42太十六181997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第四百零二十九篇第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The New Jerusalem is built according to the apostles teachingRev 2114 Acts 242 Matt 1618"}
{"zh": "二\t使徒的教训是神在新约中的整个说话，论到神新约的经纶，就是要得着一个神人二性联结调和的宇宙合并—启五9，二一3、22，约十四10~11。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二章，第九段**）", "en": "B. The teaching of the apostles is the entire speaking of God in the New Testament concerning God's New Testament economy, which is to gain a universal incorporation of the union and mingling of divinity with humanity.—Rev. 5:9; 21:3, 22; John 14:10-11.", "norm_zh": "二使徒的教训是神在新约中的整个说话论到神新约的经纶就是要得着一个神人二性联结调和的宇宙合并启五9二一322约十四10111997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二章第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The teaching of the apostles is the entire speaking of God in the New Testament concerning Gods New Testament economy which is to gain a universal incorporation of the union and mingling of divinity with humanityRev 59 213 22 John 141011"}
{"zh": "陆\t新耶路撒冷是神完整救恩的具体表现—罗五18，八10，启二一19~20：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第四十七篇，第十九段**）", "en": "VI. The New Jerusalem is the embodiment of God's complete salvation:—Rom. 5:18; 8:10; Rev. 21:19-20:", "norm_zh": "陆新耶路撒冷是神完整救恩的具体表现罗五18八10启二一19201997年夏训第十二篇以赛亚书生命读经第四十七篇第十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI The New Jerusalem is the embodiment of Gods complete salvationRom 518 810 Rev 211920"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷的根基是神的义和神的信实，其完成是神的生命和神的性情—启二一19~20，创九8~17。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；*）", "en": "B. The foundation of the New Jerusalem is the righteousness of God with God's faithfulness, and the consummation is God's life with God's nature.—Rev. 21:19-20; Gen. 9:8-17.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷的根基是神的义和神的信实其完成是神的生命和神的性情启二一1920创九8171997年夏训第十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The foundation of the New Jerusalem is the righteousness of God with Gods faithfulness and the consummation is Gods life with Gods natureRev 211920 Gen 9817"}
{"zh": "三\t整个新耶路撒冷乃是生命建造在神义之根基上的事—启二一14、19~20，诗八九14。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第四十七篇，第十八段*）", "en": "C.\tThe entire New Jerusalem is a matter of life built on the foundation of God's righteousness.—Rev. 21:14, 19-20; Psa. 89:14.", "norm_zh": "三整个新耶路撒冷乃是生命建造在神义之根基上的事启二一141920诗八九141997年夏训第十二篇以赛亚书生命读经第四十七篇第十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The entire New Jerusalem is a matter of life built on the foundation of Gods righteousnessRev 2114 1920 Psa 8914"}
{"zh": "一\t在上的耶路撒冷作信徒之母，乃是恩典的新约，由撒拉所象征—创十七15，来十二22。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第二十八章，第三十一段*）", "en": "A.\tThe Jerusalem above as the mother of the believers is the new covenant of grace symbolized by Sarah.—Gen. 17:15; Heb. 12:22.", "norm_zh": "一在上的耶路撒冷作信徒之母乃是恩典的新约由撒拉所象征创十七15来十二221997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第二十八章第三十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Jerusalem above as the mother of the believers is the new covenant of grace symbolized by SarahGen 1715 Heb 1222"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是由经过过程之三一神分赐到信徒里面作恩典所产生的，好将他们生为许多儿子，组成新耶路撒冷，就是他们的母─启二一7，加四26。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十五篇，第十四段**）", "en": "B. The New Jerusalem is produced by the dispensing of the processed Triune God into the believers as grace to beget them as many sons to compose the New Jerusalem, which is their mother—Rev. 21:7; Gal. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是由经过过程之三一神分赐到信徒里面作恩典所产生的好将他们生为许多儿子组成新耶路撒冷就是他们的母启二一7加四261997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十五篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is produced by the dispensing of the processed Triune God into the believers as grace to beget them as many sons to compose the New Jerusalem which is their motherRev 217 Gal 426"}
{"zh": "三\t父（恩典的源头）、恩典、母、众子、城和新约，要成为一个实体─新耶路撒冷—来十二22，启二一2~3，三12，加四26。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十五篇，第十四段*）", "en": "C.\tThe Father (the source of grace), the grace, the mother, the sons, the city, and the new covenant will become one entity—the New Jerusalem.—Heb. 12:22; Rev. 21:2-3; 3:12; Gal. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "三父恩典的源头恩典母众子城和新约要成为一个实体新耶路撒冷来十二22启二一23三12加四261997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十五篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Father the source of grace the grace the mother the sons the city and the new covenant will become one entitythe New JerusalemHeb 1222 Rev 2123 312 Gal 426"}
{"zh": "捌\t新耶路撒冷是神圣儿子名分的总和─启三12，十四1，二一7：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；以弗所书生命读经，第十七篇，第六段）", "en": "VIII.\tThe New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonship—Rev. 3:12; 14:1; 21:7:", "norm_zh": "捌新耶路撒冷是神圣儿子名分的总和启三12十四1二一71997年夏训第十二篇以弗所书生命读经第十七篇第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonshipRev 312 141 217"}
{"zh": "一\t新耶路撒冷是神众子的组合，他们有神的生命和性情，承受了经过过程之三一神的一切所是—7、10、18~21节，来二10~12。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十七篇，第二十六段**）", "en": "A.\tThe New Jerusalem is a composition of all the sons of God, who have God's life and nature and who inherit all that the processed Triune God is.—vv. 7, 10, 18-21; Heb. 2:10-12.", "norm_zh": "一新耶路撒冷是神众子的组合他们有神的生命和性情承受了经过过程之三一神的一切所是7101821节来二10121997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十七篇第二十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Jerusalem is a composition of all the sons of God who have Gods life and nature and who inherit all that the processed Triune God isvv 7 10 1821 Heb 21012"}
{"zh": "1\t神预定我们得儿子的名分─弗一5，加四5。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九八三年第三册，圣经中的基本启示，第十一章，第三十一段）", "en": "1.\tGod predestinated us unto sonship.—Eph. 1:5; Gal. 4:5.", "norm_zh": "1神预定我们得儿子的名分弗一5加四51997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九八三年第三册圣经中的基本启示第十一章第三十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God predestinated us unto sonshipEph 15 Gal 45"}
{"zh": "4\t因此，新约启示，神的心意是要产生众子，并启示新耶路撒冷乃是神圣儿子名分的总和—约十二24，启二一7。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百六十四篇，第三十一段*）", "en": "4.\tHence, the New Testament reveals that God's intention is to produce sons and that the New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonship.—John 12:24; Rev. 21:7.", "norm_zh": "4因此新约启示神的心意是要产生众子并启示新耶路撒冷乃是神圣儿子名分的总和约十二24启二一71997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百六十四篇第三十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Hence the New Testament reveals that Gods intention is to produce sons and that the New Jerusalem is the totality of the divine sonshipJohn 1224 Rev 217"}
{"zh": "玖\t新耶路撒冷是涌流之三一神的目的─约四14下，启二二1~2：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百七十八篇，第十三段*）", "en": "IX.\tThe New Jerusalem is the destination of the flowing Triune God—John 4:14b; Rev. 22:1-2:", "norm_zh": "玖新耶路撒冷是涌流之三一神的目的约四14下启二二121997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百七十八篇第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IX The New Jerusalem is the destination of the flowing Triune GodJohn 414b Rev 2212"}
{"zh": "1\t“涌入”（即罗马五章二十一节的“得”，直译，以至于）说到目的，指明永远的生命是涌流之三一神的目的—罗五21。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十四章，第二段**）", "en": "1.\t“Into” speaks of destination, indicating that eternal life is the destination of the flowing Triune God.—Rom. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1涌入即罗马五章二十一节的得直译以至于说到目的指明永远的生命是涌流之三一神的目的罗五211997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十四章第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Into speaks of destination indicating that eternal life is the destination of the flowing Triune GodRom 521"}
{"zh": "2\t永远的生命至终要成为新耶路撒冷，就是神圣生命的总和；因此，“涌入永远的生命”意思是“归入新耶路撒冷”—约四14下。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十四章，第二段*；新约总论，第二百七十八篇，第十二段**）", "en": "2.\tThe eternal life eventually will become the New Jerusalem, the totality of the divine life; hence, “into eternal life” means “into the New Jerusalem.”—John 4:14b.", "norm_zh": "2永远的生命至终要成为新耶路撒冷就是神圣生命的总和因此涌入永远的生命意思是归入新耶路撒冷约四14下1997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十四章第二段新约总论第二百七十八篇第十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The eternal life eventually will become the New Jerusalem the totality of the divine life hence into eternal life means into the New JerusalemJohn 414b"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是神在三个阶段涌流的结果：父的阶段、子的阶段、灵的阶段—十五26，启二二1~2：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十四章，第十段*）", "en": "B.\tThe New Jerusalem is the issue of God's flowing in three stages: in the Father's stage, in the Son's stage, and in the Spirit's stage:—John 15:26; Rev. 22:1-2:", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是神在三个阶段涌流的结果父的阶段子的阶段灵的阶段十五26启二二121997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十四章第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the issue of Gods flowing in three stages in the Fathers stage in the Sons stage and in the Spirits stageJohn 1526 Rev 2212"}
{"zh": "1\t父是源，就是源头；子是泉，灵是涌流的河，这个涌流的结果是永远的生命，就是新耶路撒冷—约十五26。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九三年第二册，主今日恢复之主要项目的重点，主今日恢复之主要项目的重点，第十二段；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十四章，第二段*）", "en": "1.\tThe Father is the fountain as the source, the Son is the spring, the Spirit is the flowing river, and this flowing issues in the eternal life, which is the New Jerusalem.—John 15:26.", "norm_zh": "1父是源就是源头子是泉灵是涌流的河这个涌流的结果是永远的生命就是新耶路撒冷约十五261997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九三年第二册主今日恢复之主要项目的重点主今日恢复之主要项目的重点第十二段李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十四章第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Father is the fountain as the source the Son is the spring the Spirit is the flowing river and this flowing issues in the eternal life which is the New JerusalemJohn 1526"}
{"zh": "2\t“源”涌现，“泉”涌出，这涌出乃是流，也就是河，涌成新耶路撒冷—启二二1~2。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十四章，第十段*）", "en": "2.\tThe fountain emerges, the spring gushes, and the gushing is the flowing as a river into the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 22:1-2.", "norm_zh": "2源涌现泉涌出这涌出乃是流也就是河涌成新耶路撒冷启二二121997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十四章第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The fountain emerges the spring gushes and the gushing is the flowing as a river into the New JerusalemRev 2212"}
{"zh": "拾\t新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿，乃是救赎之神和蒙祂救赎之人相互的居所─二一2~3、22，弗二21~22：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册，神圣启示的中心路线，第二十八章，第二十段*）", "en": "X.\tThe New Jerusalem, which is both the tabernacle and the temple, is a mutual dwelling place for the redeeming God and His redeemed:—Rev. 21:2-3, 22; Eph. 2:21-22:", "norm_zh": "拾新耶路撒冷是帐幕也是殿乃是救赎之神和蒙祂救赎之人相互的居所二一2322弗二21221997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第一册神圣启示的中心路线第二十八章第二十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "X The New Jerusalem which is both the tabernacle and the temple is a mutual dwelling place for the redeeming God and His redeemedRev 2123 22 Eph 22122"}
{"zh": "一\t帐幕是神所救赎的人，殿是救赎的神—启七15，二一22：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百六十二篇，第九段*）", "en": "A.\tThe tabernacle is God's redeemed, and the temple is the redeeming God:—Rev. 7:15; 21:22:", "norm_zh": "一帐幕是神所救赎的人殿是救赎的神启七15二一221997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百六十二篇第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The tabernacle is Gods redeemed and the temple is the redeeming GodRev 715 2122"}
{"zh": "1\t帐幕主要是用神所救赎之人的人性建造的，作神的居所—七15。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，神人，第五章，第七十六段*）", "en": "1.\tThe tabernacle is built mostly with the humanity of God's redeemed to be God's dwelling place.—Rev. 7:15.", "norm_zh": "1帐幕主要是用神所救赎之人的人性建造的作神的居所七151997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册神人第五章第七十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The tabernacle is built mostly with the humanity of Gods redeemed to be Gods dwelling placeRev 715"}
{"zh": "2\t殿主要用神性建造的，作神所救赎之人的居所—二一22。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，神人，第五章，第七十六段*）", "en": "2.\tThe temple is built mostly with divinity to be the dwelling place of God's redeemed.—Rev. 21:22.", "norm_zh": "2殿主要用神性建造的作神所救赎之人的居所二一221997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册神人第五章第七十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The temple is built mostly with divinity to be the dwelling place of Gods redeemedRev 2122"}
{"zh": "二\t新耶路撒冷是神与蒙祂救赎之人的调和，而这调和乃是相互的居所—创五一注1。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，神人，第四章，第六十七段**）", "en": "B. The New Jerusalem is the mingling of God with His redeemed ones, and this mingling is a mutual dwelling—Gen. 5:1, note 1.", "norm_zh": "二新耶路撒冷是神与蒙祂救赎之人的调和而这调和乃是相互的居所创五一注11997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册神人第四章第六十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The New Jerusalem is the mingling of God with His redeemed ones and this mingling is a mutual dwellingGen 51 note 1"}
{"zh": "三\t经过过程之三一神与蒙祂救赎的人，乃是一个调和的实体，直到永远—启二一7、22，弗四4~6。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十八篇，第十六段**）", "en": "D.\tThe processed Triune God and His redeemed will be one mingled entity for eternity.—Rev. 21:7, 22; Eph. 4:4-6.", "norm_zh": "三经过过程之三一神与蒙祂救赎的人乃是一个调和的实体直到永远启二一722弗四461997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十八篇第十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The processed Triune God and His redeemed will be one mingled entity for eternityRev 217 22 Eph 446"}
{"zh": "拾壹\t新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦—“永世对耦”─神圣罗曼史的完成─启二一2，二二17：（1997年夏训，第十二篇***）", "en": "XI. The New Jerusalem is a universal couple—\"a loving pair eternally\"—the consummation of the divine romance—Rev. 21:2; 22:17:", "norm_zh": "拾壹新耶路撒冷是宇宙的对耦永世对耦神圣罗曼史的完成启二一2二二171997年夏训第十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XI The New Jerusalem is a universal couplea loving pair eternallythe consummation of the divine romanceRev 212 2217"}
{"zh": "一\t按其人性说，新耶路撒冷是羔羊那人性的妻子（有神圣的生命和性情）─二一2、9。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒，第一章，第八段*）", "en": "B.\tAccording to its humanity, the New Jerusalem is the human wife (with the divine life and nature) of the Lamb.—Rev. 21:2, 9.", "norm_zh": "一按其人性说新耶路撒冷是羔羊哪人性的妻子有神圣的生命和性情二一291997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒第一章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B According to its humanity the New Jerusalem is the human wife with the divine life and nature of the LambRev 212 9"}
{"zh": "二\t按其神性说，新耶路撒冷是蒙神救赎之选民那神性的丈夫（救赎的神，在祂终极完成之具体化身基督里，有祂的人性生命和性情）—2节、赛五四5，启十二1~6、13~17。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册，新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒，第一章，第九段*）", "en": "C.\tAccording to its divinity, the New Jerusalem is the divine Husband (the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment, Christ, with His human life and nature) of God's redeemed elect.—v. 2; Isa. 54:5; Rev. 12:1-6, 13-17.", "norm_zh": "二按其神性说新耶路撒冷是蒙神救赎之选民哪神性的丈夫救赎的神在祂终极完成之具体化身基督里有祂的人性生命和性情2节赛五四5启十二1613171997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第三册新耶路撒冷的解释应用于寻求的信徒第一章第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C According to its divinity the New Jerusalem is the divine Husband the redeeming God in His consummated embodiment Christ with His human life and nature of Gods redeemed electv 2 Isa 545 Rev 1216 1317"}
{"zh": "三\t启示录二十二章十七节指明，基督与作祂妻子的新耶路撒冷乃是宇宙的对耦，直到永远：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第四百零二十八篇，第十三段*）", "en": "C. Revelation 22:17 indicates that Christ and the New Jerusalem as His wife will be a universal couple for eternity:", "norm_zh": "三启示录二十二章十七节指明基督与作祂妻子的新耶路撒冷乃是宇宙的对耦直到永远1997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第四百零二十八篇第十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Revelation 2217 indicates that Christ and the New Jerusalem as His wife will be a universal couple for eternity"}
{"zh": "1\t那是经过过程之三一神总和的那灵，与那些如今已完全成熟、作祂新妇的信徒成为一—17节，二一9。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十八篇，第三十三段*）", "en": "1\tThe Spirit, who is the totality of the processed Triune God, becomes one with the believers, who are now fully matured to be the bride.—v. 17; Rev. 21:9.", "norm_zh": "1哪是经过过程之三一神总和的哪灵与哪些如今已完全成熟作祂新妇的信徒成为一17节二一91997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十八篇第三十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Spirit who is the totality of the processed Triune God becomes one with the believers who are now fully matured to be the bridev 17 Rev 219"}
{"zh": "2\t经过过程之三一神的终极完成，与蒙祂拣选、救赎、重生、变化之人的终极完成，成为宇宙的对耦，彰显三一神直到永远—2节。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；新约总论，第二百五十八篇，第三十三段*）", "en": "2. The consummation of the processed Triune God and the consummation of His chosen, redeemed, regenerated, and transformed people becoming a universal couple expressing the Triune God for eternity—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2经过过程之三一神的终极完成与蒙祂拣选救赎重生变化之人的终极完成成为宇宙的对耦彰显三一神直到永远2节1997年夏训第十二篇新约总论第二百五十八篇第三十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The consummation of the processed Triune God and the consummation of His chosen redeemed regenerated and transformed people becoming a universal couple expressing the Triune God for eternityv 2"}
{"zh": "拾贰\t新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并─经过过程并终极完成之三一神，与蒙祂救赎、重生、变化、并荣化之选民，合并成为一个合并—12~14节，帖前五23：（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册，约翰福音结晶读经，第十一章，第一百零九段*）", "en": "XII\tThe New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and man—the processed and consummated Triune God incorporated into an incorporation with His redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified elect:—vv. 12-14; 1 Thes. 5:23:", "norm_zh": "拾贰新耶路撒冷是神与人终极的合并经过过程并终极完成之三一神与蒙祂救赎重生变化并荣化之选民合并成为一个合并1214节帖前五231997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第四册约翰福音结晶读经第十一章第一百零九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "XII The New Jerusalem is the consummate incorporation of God and manthe processed and consummated Triune God incorporated into an incorporation with His redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified electvv 1214 1 Thes 523"}
{"zh": "一\t神的心意是要所有在基督里的信徒都合并到神自己的合并里，成为一个扩大、神人二性的合并—启二一2、12~14，二二17上。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果，第三章，第四十四段*）", "en": "A.\tGod's intention is that all the believers in Christ would be incorporated into Himself as an incorporation to be an enlarged, divine and human incorporation.—Rev. 21:2, 12-14; 22:17a.", "norm_zh": "一神的心意是要所有在基督里的信徒都合并到神自己的合并里成为一个扩大神人二性的合并启二一21214二二17上1997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册基督为父用神圣的荣耀所荣耀的结果第三章第四十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods intention is that all the believers in Christ would be incorporated into Himself as an incorporation to be an enlarged divine and human incorporationRev 212 1214 2217a"}
{"zh": "二\t圣经向我们揭示，神的经纶是要将神与人合并成为一个合并，这个合并先是基督的身体，然后是新耶路撒冷—弗一23，启二一3。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册，基督的人性结晶读经，第二章，第三十一段*）", "en": "B.\tThe Bible unveils to us that God's economy is to have God and man incorporated into an incorporation, which is first the Body of Christ and then the New Jerusalem.—Eph. 1:23; Rev. 21:3.", "norm_zh": "二圣经向我们揭示神的经纶是要将神与人合并成为一个合并这个合并先是基督的身体然后是新耶路撒冷弗一23启二一31997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第五册基督的人性结晶读经第二章第三十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Bible unveils to us that Gods economy is to have God and man incorporated into an incorporation which is first the Body of Christ and then the New JerusalemEph 123 Rev 213"}
{"zh": "三\t经过过程并终极完成之三一神与重生信徒之联结、调和与合并，终极完成为新耶路撒冷—三12，二一2。（1997年夏训，第十二篇；李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册，神人，第四章，第六十四段**）", "en": "C.\tThe union, mingling, and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God with the regenerated believers consummates as the New Jerusalem.—Rev. 3:12; 21:2.", "norm_zh": "三经过过程并终极完成之三一神与重生信徒之联结调和与合并终极完成为新耶路撒冷三12二一21997年夏训第十二篇李常受文集一九九四至一九九七年第二册神人第四章第六十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:09:37.106292+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The union mingling and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God with the regenerated believers consummates as the New JerusalemRev 312 212"}
{"zh": "读经：赛五三1下~3，创三15，二二18，加三16，弗一5、9，约一1、14上、16~17，林前六17，罗三23，约十四6，十五4", "en": "Scripture Reading: Isa. 53:1b-3; Gen. 3:15; 22:18; Gal. 3:16; Eph. 1:5, 9; John 1:1, 14a, 16-17; 1 Cor. 6:17; Rom. 3:23; John 14:6; 15:4", "norm_zh": "读经赛五三1下3创三15二二18加三16弗一59约一114上1617林前六17罗三23约十四6十五4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Isa 531b3 Gen 315 2218 Gal 316 Eph 15 9 John 11 14a 1617 1 Cor 617 Rom 323 John 146 154"}
{"zh": "壹\t以赛亚五十三章一节下半至三节说到基督的成为肉体；基督的头一个阶段，就是成为肉体的阶段：", "en": "I. Isaiah 53:1b-3 refers to Christ's incarnation; the first stage of Christ, the stage of incarnation:", "norm_zh": "壹以赛亚五十三章一节下半至三节说到基督的成为肉体基督的头一个阶段就是成为肉体的阶段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Isaiah 531b3 refers to Christs incarnation the first stage of Christ the stage of incarnation"}
{"zh": "一\t基督是完整的神，由耶和华的膀臂，神的大能，所表征，祂成了完全的人，由多受痛苦的人所表征—1节下，林前一24，赛五三3上，约一1、14，提前二5下。", "en": "A.\tAs the complete God, signified by the arm of Jehovah, the power of God, Christ became a perfect man, signified by a man of sorrows.—v. 1b; 1 Cor. 1:24; Isa. 53:3a; John 1:1, 14; 1 Tim. 2:5b.", "norm_zh": "一基督是完整的神由耶和华的膀臂神的大能所表征祂成了完全的人由多受痛苦的人所表征1节下林前一24赛五三3上约一114提前二5下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As the complete God signified by the arm of Jehovah the power of God Christ became a perfect man signified by a man of sorrowsv 1b 1 Cor 124 Isa 533a John 11 14 1 Tim 25b"}
{"zh": "二\t基督作为完全的人，过着卑微痛苦的为人生活—赛五三3上，约一1、14，提前二5下：", "en": "B. As a perfect man, Christ lived a lowly and sorrowful human life—Isa. 53:3a; John 1:1, 14; 1 Tim. 2:5b:", "norm_zh": "二基督作为完全的人过着卑微痛苦的为人生活赛五三3上约一114提前二5下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B As a perfect man Christ lived a lowly and sorrowful human lifeIsa 533a John 11 14 1 Tim 25b"}
{"zh": "1\t祂在耶和华面前生长如嫩芽（生长如微小柔弱的人）；祂也像根出于干地，出生于贫寒之家—赛五三2上。", "en": "1. He grew up like a tender plant (like a small, delicate person) before Jehovah; He was also like a root out of dry ground, born of a poor family—Isa. 53:2a.", "norm_zh": "1祂在耶和华面前生长如嫩芽生长如微小柔弱的人祂也像根出于干地出生于贫寒之家赛五三2上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 He grew up like a tender plant like a small delicate person before Jehovah He was also like a root out of dry ground born of a poor familyIsa 532a"}
{"zh": "2\t祂无佳形美容，人看见祂的时候，也无美貌使人羡慕祂—2节下。", "en": "2. He had no attracting form nor majesty that men should look upon Him, nor beautiful appearance that men should desire Him—v. 2b.", "norm_zh": "2祂无佳形美容人看见祂的时候也无美貌使人羡慕祂2节下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He had no attracting form nor majesty that men should look upon Him nor beautiful appearance that men should desire Himv 2b"}
{"zh": "3\t基督被藐视，被人厌弃，好像被人掩面不看的一样，人也不尊重祂—3节。", "en": "3. Christ was despised and forsaken of men, like one from whom men hide their faces and whom men do not esteem—v. 3.", "norm_zh": "3基督被藐视被人厌弃好像被人掩面不看的一样人也不尊重祂3节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Christ was despised and forsaken of men like one from whom men hide their faces and whom men do not esteemv 3"}
{"zh": "4\t基督过着多受痛苦，常经忧患的人的生活—3节上。", "en": "4. Christ lived as a man of sorrows and acquainted with grief—v. 3a.", "norm_zh": "4基督过着多受痛苦常经忧患的人的生活3节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Christ lived as a man of sorrows and acquainted with griefv 3a"}
{"zh": "三\t基督是这样的一个人，过着这样卑微并痛苦的人性生活，使祂完全够资格作救主，拯救堕落的人脱离四件事：撒但、罪、死和己—来二14~18，太一21。", "en": "C. Christ's being such a man and living such a lowly and sorrowful human life fully qualified Him to be the Savior to save fallen men from four things: Satan, sin, death, and self—Heb. 2:14-18; Matt. 1:21.", "norm_zh": "三基督是这样的一个人过着这样卑微并痛苦的人性生活使祂完全够资格作救主拯救堕落的人脱离四件事撒但罪死和己来二1418太一21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Christs being such a man and living such a lowly and sorrowful human life fully qualified Him to be the Savior to save fallen men from four things Satan sin death and selfHeb 21418 Matt 121"}
{"zh": "贰神创造人之后，等了四千年才来成为人；头一个论到祂要来的应许，是对亚当说的，二千年后，又有第二个应许，是对亚伯拉罕说的—创三15，二二18：", "en": "II. After God created man, He waited four thousand years before becoming a man; the first promise concerning His coming was spoken to Adam, and two thousand years later, a second promise was spoken to Abraham—Gen. 3:15; 22:18:", "norm_zh": "贰神创造人之后等了四千年才来成为人头一个论到祂要来的应许是对亚当说的二千年后又有第二个应许是对亚伯拉罕说的创三15二二18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II After God created man He waited four thousand years before becoming a man the first promise concerning His coming was spoken to Adam and two thousand years later a second promise was spoken to AbrahamGen 315 2218"}
{"zh": "一\t在神造人这第一步之后，人堕落了；然后神进来，要给人一个应许：女人的后裔要来，祂要伤那伤害人之蛇的头；那个应许指明神自己要来作女人的后裔—三15，赛七14，加四4，太一20、16。", "en": "A. After the first step of God's creation of man, man became fallen; then God came in to give man a promise: the seed of the woman would come to bruise the head of the damaging serpent; that promise indicated that God Himself would come to be the seed of woman—Gen. 3:15; Isa. 7:14; Gal. 4:4; Matt. 1:20, 16.", "norm_zh": "一在神造人这第一步之后人堕落了然后神进来要给人一个应许女人的后裔要来祂要伤哪伤害人之蛇的头哪个应许指明神自己要来作女人的后裔三15赛七14加四4太一2016", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A After the first step of Gods creation of man man became fallen then God came in to give man a promise the seed of the woman would come to bruise the head of the damaging serpent that promise indicated that God Himself would come to be the seed of womanGen 315 Isa 714 Gal 44 Matt 120 16"}
{"zh": "二\t神给亚当那个应许之后，等了二千年；直到亚伯拉罕的时候，祂再进一步给亚伯拉罕一个应许，就是神自己要来作亚伯拉罕的后裔—创二二18，加三16，太一1。", "en": "B. After the promise given to Adam, God waited two thousand years; until the time of Abraham, He made a further promise to Abraham, which was that God Himself would come to be the seed of Abraham—Gen. 22:18; Gal. 3:16; Matt. 1:1.", "norm_zh": "二神给亚当哪个应许之后等了二千年直到亚伯拉罕的时候祂再进一步给亚伯拉罕一个应许就是神自己要来作亚伯拉罕的后裔创二二18加三16太一1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B After the promise given to Adam God waited two thousand years until the time of Abraham He made a further promise to Abraham which was that God Himself would come to be the seed of AbrahamGen 2218 Gal 316 Matt 11"}
{"zh": "叁\t神照着祂的喜悦创造了人有一个身体，又有一个灵，并将他摆在生命树前，但人仍然没有神；因此，神必须再往前一步，成为一个人；神人耶稣乃是神的喜悦和应许的应验—弗一5、9，创一31：", "en": "III. God created man according to His good pleasure with a body and with a spirit and placed him before the tree of life, but man still did not have God; thus, God had to take a further step, the step of becoming a man; the God-man Jesus being the fulfillment of God's good pleasure and promise—Eph. 1:5, 9; Gen. 1:31:", "norm_zh": "叁神照着祂的喜悦创造了人有一个身体又有一个灵并将他摆在生命树前但人仍然没有神因此神必须再往前一步成为一个人神人耶稣乃是神的喜悦和应许的应验弗一59创一31", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III God created man according to His good pleasure with a body and with a spirit and placed him before the tree of life but man still did not have God thus God had to take a further step the step of becoming a man the Godman Jesus being the fulfillment of Gods good pleasure and promiseEph 15 9 Gen 131"}
{"zh": "一\t借着祂的成为肉体，祂这话，就是那解释并说明出来的神，成了肉体—约一1、14上，罗八3中。", "en": "A. Through His incarnation, He, the Word as the defined and explained God, became flesh—John 1:1, 14a; Rom. 8:3b.", "norm_zh": "一借着祂的成为肉体祂这话就是哪解释并说明出来的神成了肉体约一114上罗八3中", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through His incarnation He the Word as the defined and explained God became fleshJohn 11 14a Rom 83b"}
{"zh": "二\t神成为人，与人成为一，好叫人与祂成为一约一1、14，十二24，提前一4。", "en": "B. God becoming a man, to be one with man that man may be one with Him—John 1:1, 14; 12:24; 1 Tim. 1:4.", "norm_zh": "二神成为人与人成为一好叫人与祂成为一约一114十二24提前一4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God becoming a man to be one with man that man may be one with HimJohn 11 14 1224 1 Tim 14"}
{"zh": "三\t神借着一个童女，亲自成了人；祂是神成了人，所以有神性，又有人性；祂这神人支搭帐幕在人中间，满有神的恩典和实际—约一14、16~17。", "en": "C. God Himself became a man through a virgin; as God who became a man, He has divinity, and He also has humanity; as the God-man He tabernacled among men, full of God's grace and reality—John 1:14, 16-17.", "norm_zh": "三神借着一个童女亲自成了人祂是神成了人所以有神性又有人性祂这神人支搭帐幕在人中间满有神的恩典和实际约一141617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God Himself became a man through a virgin as God who became a man He has divinity and He also has humanity as the Godman He tabernacled among men full of Gods grace and realityJohn 114 1617"}
{"zh": "肆\t神的愿望是要进到我们里面作生命；成为肉体乃是要将神这生命带给人—10节下，约壹五11~12：", "en": "IV. God's desire is to come into us to be our life; the incarnation was to bring God as life to man—v. 10b; 1 John 5:11-12:", "norm_zh": "肆神的愿望是要进到我们里面作生命成为肉体乃是要将神这生命带给人10节下约壹五1112", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Gods desire is to come into us to be our life the incarnation was to bring God as life to manv 10b 1 John 51112"}
{"zh": "一\t神的生命乃是在成为肉体的话里—约一1~4上，十四6上。", "en": "A. The life of God being in the incarnated Word—John 1:1-4a; 14:6a.", "norm_zh": "一神的生命乃是在成为肉体的话里约一14上十四6上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The life of God being in the incarnated WordJohn 114a 146a"}
{"zh": "二\t这成为肉体的话来了，将神的生命丰盛的带给人—十10下。", "en": "B. This incarnated Word came to bring God's life to man abundantly—10:10b.", "norm_zh": "二这成为肉体的话来了将神的生命丰盛的带给人十10下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B This incarnated Word came to bring Gods life to man abundantly1010b"}
{"zh": "三\t祂作为一粒麦子死了，将神圣的生命释放出来—十二24。", "en": "C. He died as a grain of wheat to release the divine life—12:24.", "norm_zh": "三祂作为一粒麦子死了将神圣的生命释放出来十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C He died as a grain of wheat to release the divine life1224"}
{"zh": "四\t在祂的复活里成为赐生命的灵—林前十五45下，林后三17~18。", "en": "D. In His resurrection becoming the life-giving Spirit—1 Cor. 15:45b; 2 Cor. 3:17-18.", "norm_zh": "四在祂的复活里成为赐生命的灵林前十五45下林后三1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D In His resurrection becoming the lifegiving Spirit1 Cor 1545b 2 Cor 31718"}
{"zh": "五\t祂成了这样赐生命的灵，就进入信祂的人里面，作他们的生命—约二十22，西三4上。", "en": "E. As such a life-giving Spirit He enters into His believers to be their life—John 20:22; Col. 3:4a.", "norm_zh": "五祂成了这样赐生命的灵就进入信祂的人里面作他们的生命约二十22西三4上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E As such a lifegiving Spirit He enters into His believers to be their lifeJohn 2022 Col 34a"}
{"zh": "六\t神进入信祂的人里面之后，就在神圣生命的生机联结里，使祂与信祂的人成为一林前十五45下，六17：", "en": "F. After entering into His believing people, God, in the organic union of the divine life, makes Him one with His believing people—1 Cor. 15:45b, 6:17:", "norm_zh": "六神进入信祂的人里面之后就在神圣生命的生机联结里使祂与信祂的人成为一林前十五45下六17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F After entering into His believing people God in the organic union of the divine life makes Him one with His believing people1 Cor 1545b 617"}
{"zh": "1\t在神圣生命的生机联结里，与他们成为一灵—17节。", "en": "1. In the organic union of the divine life, becoming one spirit with them—v. 17.", "norm_zh": "1在神圣生命的生机联结里与他们成为一灵17节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In the organic union of the divine life becoming one spirit with themv 17"}
{"zh": "2\t在这生机的联结里，神与人成为一个人位，就是约翰十五章一节里的真葡萄树所表征的：", "en": "2. In this organic union God and man are one person, signified by the true vine in John 15:1:", "norm_zh": "2在这生机的联结里神与人成为一个人位就是约翰十五章一节里的真葡萄树所表征的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In this organic union God and man are one person signified by the true vine in John 151"}
{"zh": "a\t葡萄树与枝子互相内住─5节。", "en": "a. The vine and the branches coinhere—v. 5.", "norm_zh": "a葡萄树与枝子互相内住5节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a The vine and the branches coinherev 5"}
{"zh": "b\t第一者，葡萄树—活在第二者—枝子—里面─加二20上。", "en": "b. The first, the vine—living in the second, the branches—Gal. 2:20a.", "norm_zh": "b第一者葡萄树活在第二者枝子里面加二20上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "b The first the vineliving in the second the branchesGal 220a"}
{"zh": "c\t第二者活在第一者里面以彰显祂─腓一20~21上。", "en": "c. The second living in the first to manifest Him—Phil. 1:20-21a.", "norm_zh": "c第二者活在第一者里面以彰显祂腓一2021上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "c The second living in the first to manifest HimPhil 12021a"}
{"zh": "伍\t神是要人归于祂，作祂的彰显，然而祂所造的人犯罪、堕落了，亏缺了神的荣耀；神要为人成功救赎，就必须成为肉体；原因最少有六个—创一26，罗三23：", "en": "V. God intended man to belong to Him to be His expression, but the man He created sinned and fell, falling short of the glory of God; in order to accomplish redemption for man, God had to become flesh; there are at least six reasons:—Gen. 1:26; Rom. 3:23:", "norm_zh": "伍神是要人归于祂作祂的彰显然而祂所造的人犯罪堕落了亏缺了神的荣耀神要为人成功救赎就必须成为肉体原因最少有六个创一26罗三23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V God intended man to belong to Him to be His expression but the man He created sinned and fell falling short of the glory of God in order to accomplish redemption for man God had to become flesh there are at least six reasonsGen 126 Rom 323"}
{"zh": "一\t神必须照着祂荣耀、圣别和公义的要求，解决人在祂面前的罪；神要为人解决罪，就需要祂自己站在人的地位上，以人的身分，替人担当罪的咒诅，受祂公义的审判；所以，神必须成为肉体来作人—来十19~20与20注2，林后五21。", "en": "A. God had to deal with man's sins in accordance with the requirements of His righteousness, holiness, and glory; in order to deal with man's sins, He had to stand in the position of a man, according to the status of a man, to bear the curse of sin and receive His righteous judgment on behalf of man; therefore, God had to become a man through incarnation—Heb. 10:19-20 and note 2; 2 Cor. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "一神必须照着祂荣耀圣别和公义的要求解决人在祂面前的罪神要为人解决罪就需要祂自己站在人的地位上以人的身分替人担当罪的咒诅受祂公义的审判所以神必须成为肉体来作人来十1920与20注2林后五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God had to deal with mans sins in accordance with the requirements of His righteousness holiness and glory in order to deal with mans sins He had to stand in the position of a man according to the status of a man to bear the curse of sin and receive His righteous judgment on behalf of man therefore God had to become a man through incarnationHeb 101920 and note 2 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "二\t神必须为人解决人因着堕落而有的败坏性情；神一面需要救回祂所创造的人，一面又需要结束那败坏的人；为着达到这两面的目的，神必须成为肉体—罗八20~21。", "en": "B. God had to deal with corruption in man's nature, which was an issue of the fall; on the one hand, God needed to rescue the man whom He had created, but on the other hand, He needed to terminate the man who was corrupted; to achieve this twofold purpose, God had to become flesh—Rom. 8:20-21.", "norm_zh": "二神必须为人解决人因着堕落而有的败坏性情神一面需要救回祂所创造的人一面又需要结束哪败坏的人为着达到这两面的目的神必须成为肉体罗八2021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God had to deal with corruption in mans nature which was an issue of the fall on the one hand God needed to rescue the man whom He had created but on the other hand He needed to terminate the man who was corrupted to achieve this twofold purpose God had to become fleshRom 82021"}
{"zh": "三\t神必须为人解决那败坏人的撒但；神若一面要从撒但手中救回撒但所骗去的人，一面仍要借着受造的人毁灭那受造而背叛神的天使长，神就必须成为肉体，作一个受造者—西一15，太四11，约壹三8。", "en": "C. God had to deal with Satan, who corrupted man; in order to rescue the Satan-deceived man from Satan's hand and also to destroy this rebellious archangel through man, God had to become a creature through incarnation—Col. 1:15; Matt. 4:11; 1 John 3:8.", "norm_zh": "三神必须为人解决哪败坏人的撒但神若一面要从撒但手中救回撒但所骗去的人一面仍要借着受造的人毁灭哪受造而背叛神的天使长神就必须成为肉体作一个受造者西一15太四11约壹三8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C God had to deal with Satan who corrupted man in order to rescue the Satandeceived man from Satans hand and also to destroy this rebellious archangel through man God had to become a creature through incarnationCol 115 Matt 411 1 John 38"}
{"zh": "四\t神必须作一些事，使堕落的人能接近祂；人因着堕落已经远离神，若要人去就近神，根本是一件作不到的事；并且堕落的罪人无法接近这位荣耀的神，所以神必须成为肉体—提前六16，创三24。", "en": "D. God had to enable fallen men to come near to Him; as a result of the fall, human beings were far from God, and it was impossible for them to come near to God; furthermore, fallen sinners have no way to approach this God of glory, so God had to become flesh—1 Tim. 6:16; Gen. 3:24.", "norm_zh": "四神必须作一些事使堕落的人能接近祂人因着堕落已经远离神若要人去就近神根本是一件作不到的事并且堕落的罪人无法接近这位荣耀的神所以神必须成为肉体提前六16创三24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God had to enable fallen men to come near to Him as a result of the fall human beings were far from God and it was impossible for them to come near to God furthermore fallen sinners have no way to approach this God of glory so God had to become flesh1 Tim 616 Gen 324"}
{"zh": "五\t神必须将祂自己给人看见，使人能认识祂；神若不从天上的圣所里出来，以人的形像来到人中间，人就没法看见祂，更不能认识祂；所以，神必须成为肉体—太十六14注1，罗一20。", "en": "E. God had to reveal Himself so that men could know Him; unless He came out of His sanctuary in the heavens to be among men as a person in the likeness of a man, man would have no way to see Him, much less to know Him; therefore, God had to become flesh—Matt. 16:14 and note 1; Rom. 1:20.", "norm_zh": "五神必须将祂自己给人看见使人能认识祂神若不从天上的圣所里出来以人的形像来到人中间人就没法看见祂更不能认识祂所以神必须成为肉体太十六14注1罗一20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E God had to reveal Himself so that men could know Him unless He came out of His sanctuary in the heavens to be among men as a person in the likeness of a man man would have no way to see Him much less to know Him therefore God had to become fleshMatt 1614 and note 1 Rom 120"}
{"zh": "六\t神必须与人联合为一；祂若不与人联合为一，祂所作所成全的，就不能是人所作所成全的；并且神原初造人的目的，是要人与祂联合为一；神要与人联合为一，就必须成为肉体—约十四6，十五4。", "en": "F. God had to be joined with man as one; if He were not joined with man as one, what He did and accomplished could not be what man did and accomplished; furthermore, God's original purpose in creating man was for man to be joined with Him as one; in order for God to be joined with man as one, He had to become flesh—John 14:6; 15:4.", "norm_zh": "六神必须与人联合为一祂若不与人联合为一祂所作所成全的就不能是人所作所成全的并且神原初造人的目的是要人与祂联合为一神要与人联合为一就必须成为肉体约十四6十五4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F God had to be joined with man as one if He were not joined with man as one what He did and accomplished could not be what man did and accomplished furthermore Gods original purpose in creating man was for man to be joined with Him as one in order for God to be joined with man as one He had to become fleshJohn 146 154"}
{"zh": "多受痛苦的人", "en": "A man of sorrows", "norm_zh": "多受痛苦的人", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A man of sorrows"}
{"zh": "这是神的创造，这是神的成为肉体，这也是我们的悔改得救。六千年前祂创造我们，二千年前祂来成为我们，今天祂进到我们里面。因此，我们是祂的一部分。我们是祂的配偶。神的配偶就是神的一部分。祂所是的，我们就是。祂是头，我们是身体。我们不能说，头是神而身体不是神。身体与头乃是一，且是相同的。基督徒不仅是有最高道德标准的人。作基督徒就是成为神，成为神的一部分，成为神的配偶。我们既是基督徒，就该借着在灵里、照着灵行事并作每一件事，来活神、彰显神、并显大神。我们成了这位神的配偶，祂乃是赐生命、复合、包罗万有的灵，这灵就是经过过程之三一神的终极完成、总和、集大成。在耶稣基督里，这样一位灵乃是赐给地上万国的大福。（李常受文集一九九三年第二册，在神与人关系里生机的联结，第二篇）", "en": "This is God's creation, this is God's incarnation, and this is also our repentance and salvation. Six thousand years ago He created us, two thousand years ago He came to become us, and today He enters into us. Therefore, we are a part of Him. We are His counterpart. God's counterpart is a part of God. What He is, we are. He is the Head, and we are the body. We cannot say that the Head is God and the body is not God. The body and the Head are one and are the same. A Christian is not only a person with the highest standard of morality. To be a Christian is to become God, to become a part of God, and to become God's counterpart. Since we are Christians, we should live God, express God, and magnify God by walking and doing everything in the spirit and according to the spirit. We have become the counterpart of this God, who is the life-giving, compound, all-inclusive Spirit; this Spirit is the consummation, the sum, and the totality of the processed Triune God. In Jesus Christ, such a Spirit is the great blessing given to the nations of the earth.", "norm_zh": "这是神的创造这是神的成为肉体这也是我们的悔改得救六千年前祂创造我们二千年前祂来成为我们今天祂进到我们里面因此我们是祂的一部分我们是祂的配偶神的配偶就是神的一部分祂所是的我们就是祂是头我们是身体我们不能说头是神而身体不是神身体与头乃是一且是相同的基督徒不仅是有最高道德标准的人作基督徒就是成为神成为神的一部分成为神的配偶我们既是基督徒就该借着在灵里照着灵行事并作每一件事来活神彰显神并显大神我们成了这位神的配偶祂乃是赐生命复合包罗万有的灵这灵就是经过过程之三一神的终极完成总和集大成在耶稣基督里这样一位灵乃是赐给地上万国的大福李常受文集一九九三年第二册在神与人关系里生机的联结第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:12:29.121754+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "This is Gods creation this is Gods incarnation and this is also our repentance and salvation Six thousand years ago He created us two thousand years ago He came to become us and today He enters into us Therefore we are a part of Him We are His counterpart Gods counterpart is a part of God What He is we are He is the Head and we are the body We cannot say that the Head is God and the body is not God The body and the Head are one and are the same A Christian is not only a person with the highest standard of morality To be a Christian is to become God to become a part of God and to become Gods counterpart Since we are Christians we should live God express God and magnify God by walking and doing everything in the spirit and according to the spirit We have become the counterpart of this God who is the lifegiving compound allinclusive Spirit this Spirit is the consummation the sum and the totality of the processed Triune God In Jesus Christ such a Spirit is the great blessing given to the nations of the earth"}
