{"zh": "贰\t神在人性生活的各阶段里，显现于肉体—赛五三2，路二7、40、42：（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "II. God was manifested in the flesh in the stages of human life.—Isa. 53:2; Luke 2:7, 40, 42:", "norm_zh": "贰神在人性生活的各阶段里显现于肉体赛五三2路二74042李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II God was manifested in the flesh in the stages of human lifeIsa 532 Luke 27 40 42"}
{"zh": "一\t当祂成为人时，祂在耶和华面前生长如嫩芽，像根出于干地—赛五三2~3。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "A. When He became a man, He was growing before Jehovah as a tender plant and as a root out of dry ground.—Isa. 53:2-3.", "norm_zh": "一当祂成为人时祂在耶和华面前生长如嫩芽像根出于干地赛五三23李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A When He became a man He was growing before Jehovah as a tender plant and as a root out of dry groundIsa 5323"}
{"zh": "二\t神显现于肉体，先是在婴孩时期；天使告诉牧羊人说，“你们要看见一个婴孩，包着布，卧在马槽里，那就是给你们的记号了”—路二7、12。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "B. God was manifested in the flesh in babyhood; the angel told the shepherds, \"This will be the sign to you: you will find a baby wrapped in swaddling clothes and lying in a manger\"—Luke 2:7, 12.", "norm_zh": "二神显现于肉体先是在婴孩时期天使告诉牧羊人说你们要看见一个婴孩包着布卧在马槽里哪就是给你们的记号了路二712李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God was manifested in the flesh in babyhood the angel told the shepherds This will be the sign to you you will find a baby wrapped in swaddling clothes and lying in a mangerLuke 27 12"}
{"zh": "三\t祂在孩童时期，在智慧和身量，在神的恩，并神与人对祂的喜爱上，都不断增长；祂也在十二岁的时候，关心神的事—40、52、42、46~47、49节。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "C. In His boyhood He grew in wisdom and stature, in the grace of God, and in favor with God and men; He was also concerned about the things of God at twelve years of age.—vv. 40, 52, 42, 46-47, 49.", "norm_zh": "三祂在孩童时期在智慧和身量在神的恩并神与人对祂的喜爱上都不断增长祂也在十二岁的时候关心神的事405242464749节李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In His boyhood He grew in wisdom and stature in the grace of God and in favor with God and men He was also concerned about the things of God at twelve years of agevv 40 52 42 4647 49"}
{"zh": "四\t祂在三十岁长大成人时，开始尽职事奉神—三23与注1：（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "D. In His maturity as a man at the age of thirty, He began His ministry for God.—Luke 3:23 and note 1:", "norm_zh": "四祂在三十岁长大成人时开始尽职事奉神三23与注1李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D In His maturity as a man at the age of thirty He began His ministry for GodLuke 323 and note 1"}
{"zh": "1\t从祂成为神的执事起，祂也是忧患之子，遭人藐视、厌弃并逼迫—赛五三3，太十三55~57，路四28~30，太二六4、16。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "1. From the time that He became a minister of God, He also became a man of sorrows, suffering the despising, rejection, and persecution of man.—Isa. 53:3; Matt. 13:55-57; Luke 4:28-30; Matt. 26:4, 16.", "norm_zh": "1从祂成为神的执事起祂也是忧患之子遭人藐视厌弃并逼迫赛五三3太十三5557路四2830太二六416李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 From the time that He became a minister of God He also became a man of sorrows suffering the despising rejection and persecution of manIsa 533 Matt 135557 Luke 42830 Matt 264 16"}
{"zh": "2\t祂到了三十岁后，受魔鬼试诱；这试诱乃是在神的灵引导之下；在那试诱里，祂击败魔鬼，并且有天使服事—四1、11。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第三篇）", "en": "2. After He became thirty years old, He was tempted by the devil, and this temptation was under the leading of the Spirit of God; in that temptation He defeated the devil, and was ministered to by the angels.—Matt. 4:1, 11.", "norm_zh": "2祂到了三十岁后受魔鬼试诱这试诱乃是在神的灵引导之下在哪试诱里祂击败魔鬼并且有天使服事四111李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 After He became thirty years old He was tempted by the devil and this temptation was under the leading of the Spirit of God in that temptation He defeated the devil and was ministered to by the angelsMatt 41 11"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督借着成为肉体，成了在地上生活的人；就着在人性生活里的基督，祂的生活和祂的工作并没有什么区别；祂的生活就是祂的工作，祂的工作就是祂的生活—约六57上，可一14~45：（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "III. Through incarnation Christ became a man living on the earth; with Christ in His human living, there was no difference between life and work; His life was His work, and His work was His life—John 6:57a; Mark 1:14-45:", "norm_zh": "叁基督借着成为肉体成了在地上生活的人就着在人性生活里的基督祂的生活和祂的工作并没有什么区别祂的生活就是祂的工作祂的工作就是祂的生活约六57上可一1445新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Through incarnation Christ became a man living on the earth with Christ in His human living there was no difference between life and work His life was His work and His work was His lifeJohn 657a Mark 11445"}
{"zh": "一\t基督在祂的人性生活里显为人的样子，甚至奴仆的形状—腓二7~8：（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "A.\tIn His human living Christ was found in fashion as a man, even in the form of a slave.—Phil. 2:7-8:", "norm_zh": "一基督在祂的人性生活里显为人的样子甚至奴仆的形状腓二78新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In His human living Christ was found in fashion as a man even in the form of a slavePhil 278"}
{"zh": "1\t基督在人性生活里建立人的样子，并取了奴仆的形状，祂这工作乃是祂职事的根基和背景—路四14~19。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "1. Christ's work in His human living to build up the fashion of a man and to take on the form of a slave was the foundation and background of His ministry—Luke 4:14-19.", "norm_zh": "1基督在人性生活里建立人的样子并取了奴仆的形状祂这工作乃是祂职事的根基和背景路四1419新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Christs work in His human living to build up the fashion of a man and to take on the form of a slave was the foundation and background of His ministryLuke 41419"}
{"zh": "2\t我们这些渴望事奉主的人需要有一种工作，不是凭着作为，乃是凭着生活以建立一种工作，作他们将来事奉主的扎实立场和坚固背景—徒十六1~3上，提后四5、11下，西四17。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "2. We who aspire to serve the Lord need to have a work not by doing but by living to build up a work that will be the solid ground and strong background for our coming service to the Lord—Acts 16:1-3a; 2 Tim. 4:5, 11b; Col. 4:17.", "norm_zh": "2我们这些渴望事奉主的人需要有一种工作不是凭着作为乃是凭着生活以建立一种工作作他们将来事奉主的扎实立场和坚固背景徒十六13上提后四511下西四17新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We who aspire to serve the Lord need to have a work not by doing but by living to build up a work that will be the solid ground and strong background for our coming service to the LordActs 1613a 2 Tim 45 11b Col 417"}
{"zh": "二\t马可六章三节告诉我们，基督是一个卑微家庭的木匠；在这样的工作里，基督显为人的样子，不是崇高的，乃是卑微、细致、忍耐的。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "B. Mark 6:3 tells us that Christ was a carpenter in a lowly home; in such a work Christ was found in fashion as a man, not in loftiness but in lowliness, fineness, and patience", "norm_zh": "二马可六章三节告诉我们基督是一个卑微家庭的木匠在这样的工作里基督显为人的样子不是崇高的乃是卑微细致忍耐的新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Mark 63 tells us that Christ was a carpenter in a lowly home in such a work Christ was found in fashion as a man not in loftiness but in lowliness fineness and patience"}
{"zh": "三\t基督在为人生活里之工作的另一面是表明神；按约翰一章一至十八节，基督是借着话、生命、光、恩典和实际，将神表明出来—1、14、4~5、16、17节：（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "C. Another aspect of Christ's work in His human living was to declare God; according to John 1:1-18, Christ declared God by the Word, life, light, grace, and reality—vv. 1, 14, 4-5, 16, 17:", "norm_zh": "三基督在为人生活里之工作的另一面是表明神按约翰一章一至十八节基督是借着话生命光恩典和实际将神表明出来114451617节新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Another aspect of Christs work in His human living was to declare God according to John 1118 Christ declared God by the Word life light grace and realityvv 1 14 45 16 17"}
{"zh": "四\t基督在人性生活里的工作也包括祂彰显父—约十四9，七17~18，十七4上：（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "D. Christ's work in His human living also includes His expressing the Father—John 14:9; 7:17-18; 17:4a:", "norm_zh": "四基督在人性生活里的工作也包括祂彰显父约十四9七1718十七4上新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Christs work in His human living also includes His expressing the FatherJohn 149 71718 174a"}
{"zh": "1\t按约翰福音，子基督在父的名里来，在父的名里行事，行父的旨意，说父的话，并寻求父的荣耀；祂与父是一—五43，十25，六38，三34上，十四24，七16~17，十二47~50，七18，十30。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "1. According to the Gospel of John, Christ the Son came in the Father's name, worked in the Father's name, did the Father's will, spoke the Father's word, and sought the Father's glory; He was one with the Father—5:43; 10:25; 6:38; 3:34a; 14:24; 7:16-17; 12:47-50; 7:18; 10:30.", "norm_zh": "1按约翰福音子基督在父的名里来在父的名里行事行父的旨意说父的话并寻求父的荣耀祂与父是一五43十25六38三34上十四24七1617十二4750七18十30新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to the Gospel of John Christ the Son came in the Fathers name worked in the Fathers name did the Fathers will spoke the Fathers word and sought the Fathers glory He was one with the Father543 1025 638 334a 1424 71617 124750 718 1030"}
{"zh": "2\t祂为着自己没有工作，没有旨意，没有话语，没有荣耀，也没有野心；基督是这样的一个人，单单彰显父；祂没有彰显自己；祂是子，然而祂彰显父—五43，十25，三34上，十四24，七16~18，十二47~50。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "2. He had no work, no will, no word, no glory, and no ambition for Himself; as such a one, Christ expressed only the Father; He did not express Himself; He was the Son, yet He expressed the Father—5:43; 10:25; 3:34a; 14:24; 7:16-18; 12:47-50.", "norm_zh": "2祂为着自己没有工作没有旨意没有话语没有荣耀也没有野心基督是这样的一个人单单彰显父祂没有彰显自己祂是子然而祂彰显父五43十25三34上十四24七1618十二4750新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He had no work no will no word no glory and no ambition for Himself as such a one Christ expressed only the Father He did not express Himself He was the Son yet He expressed the Father543 1025 334a 1424 71618 124750"}
{"zh": "3\t因为子不是彰显自己，乃是彰显父，我们若看见子，就看见了父，父具体化身在子里，借着祂在人性生活里得着彰显—七18。（新约总论，第六十四篇）", "en": "3. Because the Son expresses not Himself but the Father, if we have seen the Son, we have seen the Father; the Father is embodied in the Son to be expressed through Him in His human living—7:18.", "norm_zh": "3因为子不是彰显自己乃是彰显父我们若看见子就看见了父父具体化身在子里借着祂在人性生活里得着彰显七18新约总论第六十四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:19:58.936716+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Because the Son expresses not Himself but the Father if we have seen the Son we have seen the Father the Father is embodied in the Son to be expressed through Him in His human living718"}
{"zh": "读经：赛五三4~5、8、11下、12下，太二七45~46，罗五16中，可十五25，赛五三6下", "en": "Scripture Reading: Isa. 53:4-5, 8, 11b, 12b; Matt. 27:45-46; Rom. 5:16m; Mark 15:25; Isa. 53:6b", "norm_zh": "读经赛五三45811下12下太二七4546罗五16中可十五25赛五三6下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Isa 5345 8 11b 12b Matt 274546 Rom 516m Mark 1525 Isa 536b"}
{"zh": "壹\t神救赎的第一步乃是成为肉体，第二步乃是十字架；基督在祂钉十字架的阶段里，作为神人救主，代替罪人而死—赛五三4~5、8、11下、12下：", "en": "I. The first step of God's redemption is incarnation, and the second step is the cross; Christ in the stage of His crucifixion, as a God-man Savior, died a vicarious death for sinners.—Isa. 53:4-5, 8, 11b, 12b:", "norm_zh": "壹神救赎的第一步乃是成为肉体第二步乃是十字架基督在祂钉十字架的阶段里作为神人救主代替罪人而死赛五三45811下12下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The first step of Gods redemption is incarnation and the second step is the cross Christ in the stage of His crucifixion as a Godman Savior died a vicarious death for sinnersIsa 5345 8 11b 12b"}
{"zh": "一\t作为神人救主，基督代替罪人而死—4~5、8、11下、12节下，彼前二24：", "en": "A. As a God-man Savior, Christ died a vicarious death for sinners.—vv. 4-5, 8, 11b, 12b; 1 Pet. 2:24:", "norm_zh": "一作为神人救主基督代替罪人而死45811下12节下彼前二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As a Godman Savior Christ died a vicarious death for sinnersvv 45 8 11b 12b 1 Pet 224"}
{"zh": "1\t在基督为我们这些罪人的代死里，祂担当了我们的疾病，背负了我们的痛苦—赛五三4。", "en": "1. In His vicarious death for us, the sinners, Christ bore our sicknesses and carried our sorrows.—Isa. 53:4.", "norm_zh": "1在基督为我们这些罪人的代死里祂担当了我们的疾病背负了我们的痛苦赛五三4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In His vicarious death for us the sinners Christ bore our sicknesses and carried our sorrowsIsa 534"}
{"zh": "2\t在基督为我们的代死里，祂为我们的过犯被刺透，为我们的罪孽被压伤；因我们的罪过，祂从活人之地被剪除，并且担当我们的罪，使我们得平安，得医治—5、8节下。", "en": "2. In His vicarious death for us, Christ was wounded for our transgressions, crushed for our iniquities, and cut off out of the land of the living for our transgression, and He bore our sin, that we may have peace and be healed.—vv. 5, 8b.", "norm_zh": "2在基督为我们的代死里祂为我们的过犯被刺透为我们的罪孽被压伤因我们的罪过祂从活人之地被剪除并且担当我们的罪使我们得平安得医治58节下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In His vicarious death for us Christ was wounded for our transgressions crushed for our iniquities and cut off out of the land of the living for our transgression and He bore our sin that we may have peace and be healedvv 5 8b"}
{"zh": "3\t在基督为罪人的代死里，祂被欺压，受苦害，像羊羔被牵到宰杀之地，又像羊在剪毛的人面前被剪而无反应—7节。", "en": "3. In His vicarious death for sinners, Christ was oppressed, afflicted, and led to the slaughter like a lamb and sheared before the shearers like a sheep, with no reaction.—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "3在基督为罪人的代死里祂被欺压受苦害像羊羔被牵到宰杀之地又像羊在剪毛的人面前被剪而无反应7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In His vicarious death for sinners Christ was oppressed afflicted and led to the slaughter like a lamb and sheared before the shearers like a sheep with no reactionv 7"}
{"zh": "4\t以赛亚五十三章八节说，基督因受欺压（被假冒为善之犹太首领）和审判（被不公正之罗马官长）而被夺去—太二六57，路二三1~12。", "en": "4. Isaiah 53:8 says that Christ was taken away by oppression (of the hypocritical Jewish leaders) and by judgment (of the unjust Roman officials).—Matt. 26:57; Luke 23:1-12.", "norm_zh": "4以赛亚五十三章八节说基督因受欺压被假冒为善之犹太首领和审判被不公正之罗马官长而被夺去太二六57路二三112", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Isaiah 538 says that Christ was taken away by oppression of the hypocritical Jewish leaders and by judgment of the unjust Roman officialsMatt 2657 Luke 23112"}
{"zh": "5\t按照以赛亚五十三章十二节下半，当基督被钉在十字架上时，祂被列在罪犯之中，又为罪犯代求—32~33、34节上。", "en": "5. According to Isaiah 53:12c, when Christ was crucified on the cross, He was numbered with the transgressors and He interceded for the transgressors.—vv. 32-33, 34a.", "norm_zh": "5按照以赛亚五十三章十二节下半当基督被钉在十字架上时祂被列在罪犯之中又为罪犯代求323334节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 According to Isaiah 5312c when Christ was crucified on the cross He was numbered with the transgressors and He interceded for the transgressorsvv 3233 34a"}
{"zh": "6\t按照以赛亚五十三章九节，虽然基督未行强暴，口中也没有诡诈，但祂被分配与罪人同埋，死的时候却与财主同葬。", "en": "6. According to Isaiah 53:9, Christ was assigned a grave with the wicked, but with a rich man in His death, although He had done no violence, nor was there any deceit in His mouth.", "norm_zh": "6按照以赛亚五十三章九节虽然基督未行强暴口中也没有诡诈但祂被分配与罪人同埋死的时候却与财主同葬", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 According to Isaiah 539 Christ was assigned a grave with the wicked but with a rich man in His death although He had done no violence nor was there any deceit in His mouth"}
{"zh": "二\t以上所说的一切都是人所作的；人作了这一切事后，耶和华就使我们这些如羊走迷，偏行己路之人的罪孽，都归在祂身上—赛五三6，太二七45~46：", "en": "B. All the aforementioned things were done by man; after man had done all these things, Jehovah caused the iniquity of us all, who have gone astray like sheep and have turned to our own way, to fall on Him.—Isa. 53:6; Matt. 27:45-46:", "norm_zh": "二以上所说的一切都是人所作的人作了这一切事后耶和华就使我们这些如羊走迷偏行己路之人的罪孽都归在祂身上赛五三6太二七4546", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B All the aforementioned things were done by man after man had done all these things Jehovah caused the iniquity of us all who have gone astray like sheep and have turned to our own way to fall on HimIsa 536 Matt 274546"}
{"zh": "1\t当基督在十字架上末了的三个小时，耶和华将祂看作是罪人的代替，并在那时刻弃绝了祂这惟一的罪人—彼前三18，太二七45~46。", "en": "1. During the last three hours that Christ was on the cross, Jehovah considered Him as the Substitute for sinners and forsook Him as the unique sinner at that moment.—1 Pet. 3:18; Matt. 27:45-46.", "norm_zh": "1当基督在十字架上末了的三个小时耶和华将祂看作是罪人的代替并在哪时刻弃绝了祂这惟一的罪人彼前三18太二七4546", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 During the last three hours that Christ was on the cross Jehovah considered Him as the Substitute for sinners and forsook Him as the unique sinner at that moment1 Pet 318 Matt 274546"}
{"zh": "2\t按照以赛亚五十三章十节上半，基督作罪人的代替经过这代死时，耶和华喜悦将祂压伤，使祂受痛苦。", "en": "2. According to Isaiah 53:10a, in Christ's vicarious death as the Substitute for sinners, Jehovah was pleased to crush Him, to afflict Him with grief.", "norm_zh": "2按照以赛亚五十三章十节上半基督作罪人的代替经过这代死时耶和华喜悦将祂压伤使祂受痛苦", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 According to Isaiah 5310a in Christs vicarious death as the Substitute for sinners Jehovah was pleased to crush Him to afflict Him with grief"}
{"zh": "三\t以赛亚五十三章十节下半说到基督使自己成为赎罪祭：", "en": "C. Isaiah 53:10b says that Christ made Himself an offering for sin:", "norm_zh": "三以赛亚五十三章十节下半说到基督使自己成为赎罪祭", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Isaiah 5310b says that Christ made Himself an offering for sin"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来九章十四节说，基督借着永远的灵，将自己献给神。", "en": "1. Hebrews 9:14 says that Christ offered Himself through the eternal Spirit to God.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来九章十四节说基督借着永远的灵将自己献给神", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Hebrews 914 says that Christ offered Himself through the eternal Spirit to God"}
{"zh": "2\t以赛亚五十三章十二节下半说，基督将命倾倒，以至于死。", "en": "2. Isaiah 53:12b says that Christ poured out His life unto death.", "norm_zh": "2以赛亚五十三章十二节下半说基督将命倾倒以至于死", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Isaiah 5312b says that Christ poured out His life unto death"}
{"zh": "四\t基督的钉十字架乃是为着完成神永远的救赎，使在基督里的信徒得蒙救赎（得蒙赦罪—徒十43，得著称义—徒十三39，并与神和好—罗五10），达到在祂复活里生命的联结，其实际乃是祂的赐生命之灵—来九12，林前十五45下，罗八9下，腓一19下。", "en": "D. Christ's crucifixion is for the accomplishing of God's eternal redemption, that the believers in Christ may be redeemed (forgiven of sins—Acts 10:43, justified—Acts 13:39, and reconciled to God—Rom. 5:10), attaining to the life union in His resurrection, the reality of which is His life-giving Spirit.—Heb. 9:12; 1 Cor. 15:45b; Rom. 8:9b; Phil. 1:19b.", "norm_zh": "四基督的钉十字架乃是为着完成神永远的救赎使在基督里的信徒得蒙救赎得蒙赦罪徒十43得着称义徒十三39并与神和好罗五10达到在祂复活里生命的联结其实际乃是祂的赐生命之灵来九12林前十五45下罗八9下腓一19下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Christs crucifixion is for the accomplishing of Gods eternal redemption that the believers in Christ may be redeemed forgiven of sinsActs 1043 justifiedActs 1339 and reconciled to GodRom 510 attaining to the life union in His resurrection the reality of which is His lifegiving SpiritHeb 912 1 Cor 1545b Rom 89b Phil 119b"}
{"zh": "贰\t神的计划有一个目的，但人的堕落带来三个难处；基督要成功神的计划，必须到十字架上受死；十字架是说到基督的死，所以我们来看十字架，就是来看基督的死—罗五16中，可十五25，赛五三6下：", "en": "II. God has a purpose in His plan, but man's fall brought in three problems; in order for Christ to fulfill God's plan, He must go to the cross to die; the cross speaks of Christ's death, so to look at the cross is to look at Christ's death.—Rom. 5:16b; Mark 15:25; Isa. 53:6b:", "norm_zh": "贰神的计划有一个目的但人的堕落带来三个难处基督要成功神的计划必须到十字架上受死十字架是说到基督的死所以我们来看十字架就是来看基督的死罗五16中可十五25赛五三6下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II God has a purpose in His plan but mans fall brought in three problems in order for Christ to fulfill Gods plan He must go to the cross to die the cross speaks of Christs death so to look at the cross is to look at Christs deathRom 516b Mark 1525 Isa 536b"}
{"zh": "一\t人在神面前因着堕落而有的第一个难处，就是罪；基督的十字架解决人的罪—罗五16中，林后五21上：", "en": "A. As a result of the fall, man's first problem before God is sin; Christ's cross solves man's sin.—Rom. 5:16b; 2 Cor. 5:21a:", "norm_zh": "一人在神面前因着堕落而有的第一个难处就是罪基督的十字架解决人的罪罗五16中林后五21上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As a result of the fall mans first problem before God is sin Christs cross solves mans sinRom 516b 2 Cor 521a"}
{"zh": "1\t人虽然是神为着祂自己的计划所创造的，是神所器重、所爱的，但人的堕落却使神的公义不能不定人的罪—罗五16中，诗八九14。", "en": "1. God loves the man whom He created, but His righteousness requires Him to condemn man because of the fall.—Rom. 5:16b; Psa. 89:14.", "norm_zh": "1人虽然是神为着祂自己的计划所创造的是神所器重所爱的但人的堕落却使神的公义不能不定人的罪罗五16中诗八九14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 God loves the man whom He created but His righteousness requires Him to condemn man because of the fallRom 516b Psa 8914"}
{"zh": "2\t神按着祂的公义定人的罪，人就得死，就得灭亡；神的计划就发生问题，神的爱也不能容忍；在这里，神的公义对神的爱有了难处—结十八4，来九27。", "en": "2. According to His righteousness, God condemned man; hence, man cannot escape death; there is a problem with God's plan, and God's love cannot tolerate this; here, satisfying the requirement of His righteousness is complicated by His love.—Ezek. 18:4; Heb. 9:27.", "norm_zh": "2神按着祂的公义定人的罪人就得死就得灭亡神的计划就发生问提神的爱也不能容忍在这里神的公义对神的爱有了难处结十八4来九27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 According to His righteousness God condemned man hence man cannot escape death there is a problem with Gods plan and Gods love cannot tolerate this here satisfying the requirement of His righteousness is complicated by His loveEzek 184 Heb 927"}
{"zh": "3\t神要应付这个难处，解决这个问题，祂自己来到人里面作人的代替，站在人的地位为人担罪，替人受死—赛五三6下，彼前二24上。", "en": "3. To meet this difficulty and solve this problem, God Himself came into man to be man's Substitute, standing in the position of man to bear man's sins and die in man's place.—Isa. 53:6b; 1 Pet. 2:24a.", "norm_zh": "3神要应付这个难处解决这个问提祂自己来到人里面作人的代替站在人的地位为人担罪替人受死赛五三6下彼前二24上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 To meet this difficulty and solve this problem God Himself came into man to be mans Substitute standing in the position of man to bear mans sins and die in mans placeIsa 536b 1 Pet 224a"}
{"zh": "4\t主耶稣在十字架上受死，就是神在人里面替人担罪受罚；祂替我们担当罪，使我们在神面前得赦罪，蒙称义；祂替我们成为罪，使我们在祂里面成为神的义，蒙神悦纳—林后五21上。", "en": "4. The death of the Lord Jesus on the cross is God bearing sin and suffering punishment on man's behalf in man; He bore our sins so that we might receive the forgiveness of sins and be justified by God, and He was made sin on our behalf so that we might become God's righteousness and be acceptable to God in Him—2 Cor. 5:21a.", "norm_zh": "4主耶稣在十字架上受死就是神在人里面替人担罪受罚祂替我们担当罪使我们在神面前得赦罪蒙称义祂替我们成为罪使我们在祂里面成为神的义蒙神悦纳林后五21上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The death of the Lord Jesus on the cross is God bearing sin and suffering punishment on mans behalf in man He bore our sins so that we might receive the forgiveness of sins and be justified by God and He was made sin on our behalf so that we might become Gods righteousness and be acceptable to God in Him2 Cor 521a"}
{"zh": "二\t主耶稣在十字架上，不只担当人的罪而死，也包括担当了人自己；基督的十字架解决人自己—罗五18，六6，加二20，五24：", "en": "B. When the Lord Jesus died on the cross, He not only bore man's sins; He also bore our humanity; the cross of Christ deals with man himself—Rom. 5:18; 6:6; Gal. 2:20; 5:24:", "norm_zh": "二主耶稣在十字架上不只担当人的罪而死也包括担当了人自己基督的十字架解决人自己罗五18六6加二20五24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B When the Lord Jesus died on the cross He not only bore mans sins He also bore our humanity the cross of Christ deals with man himselfRom 518 66 Gal 220 524"}
{"zh": "1\t祂到十字架上受死，是穿着人，将人带到那里和祂同死；所以，当祂钉十字架时，我们众人也都在那里，和祂一同钉死—罗五18。", "en": "1. He went to the cross to die, putting on man and bringing man there to die with Him; therefore, when He was crucified, we all were also there, crucified together with Him—Rom. 5:18.", "norm_zh": "1祂到十字架上受死是穿着人将人带到哪里和祂同死所以当祂钉十字架时我们众人也都在哪里和祂一同钉死罗五18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 He went to the cross to die putting on man and bringing man there to die with Him therefore when He was crucified we all were also there crucified together with HimRom 518"}
{"zh": "2\t基督是“一切受造之物的首生者”，是包罗万有的，所以祂的死是包罗万有的，也是超乎时间的；基督死了，一切在时间里的受造者，也都在祂里面与祂同死了—西一15。", "en": "2. Christ is the \"Firstborn of all creation,\" being all-inclusive, so His death is all-inclusive and also transcends time; when Christ died, all creation in time also died with Him in Him—Col. 1:15.", "norm_zh": "2基督是一切受造之物的首生者是包罗万有的所以祂的死是包罗万有的也是超乎时间的基督死了一切在时间里的受造者也都在祂里面与祂同死了西一15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christ is the Firstborn of all creation being allinclusive so His death is allinclusive and also transcends time when Christ died all creation in time also died with Him in HimCol 115"}
{"zh": "3\t神看我们在基督里已经死了，我们也信我们在基督里已经死了；正因此，我们一信主，与祂联合，就要受浸归入祂的死，与祂一同埋葬，结束我们的旧人，和属于我们旧人的一切—罗六4~6。", "en": "3. God considers that we died in Christ, and we also believe that we have died in Christ; because of this, everyone who believes in the Lord is joined to the Lord and needs to be baptized into His death in order to be buried with Him and to terminate the old man and everything related to the old man—Rom. 6:4-6.", "norm_zh": "3神看我们在基督里已经死了我们也信我们在基督里已经死了正因此我们一信主与祂联合就要受浸归入祂的死与祂一同埋葬结束我们的旧人和属于我们旧人的一切罗六46", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 God considers that we died in Christ and we also believe that we have died in Christ because of this everyone who believes in the Lord is joined to the Lord and needs to be baptized into His death in order to be buried with Him and to terminate the old man and everything related to the old manRom 646"}
{"zh": "三\t如果主的十字架只解决人的罪和人自己，神在宇宙中的仇敌仍然存在，神的计划仍有拦阻；基督的十字架解决撒但—约十二31，来二14：", "en": "C. If the Lord had dealt only with sins and our fallen humanity on the cross, God's enemy would be able to continue to frustrate God's plan unhindered; the cross of Christ deals with Satan—John 12:31; Heb. 2:14:", "norm_zh": "三如果主的十字架只解决人的罪和人自己神在宇宙中的仇敌仍然存在神的计划仍有拦阻基督的十字架解决撒但约十二31来二14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C If the Lord had dealt only with sins and our fallen humanity on the cross Gods enemy would be able to continue to frustrate Gods plan unhindered the cross of Christ deals with SatanJohn 1231 Heb 214"}
{"zh": "1\t撒但引诱人堕落时，他自己也进到了人里面，和人调在一起；所以，当主耶稣在十字架上，用祂的死解决人自己时，也就解决了在人里面的撒但—创三1~6。", "en": "1. When Satan enticed man to fall, he himself also entered into man and was mingled with man; thus, when the Lord Jesus dealt with man in His death on the cross, He dealt with the Satan who was in man—Gen. 3:1-6.", "norm_zh": "1撒但引诱人堕落时他自己也进到了人里面和人调在一起所以当主耶稣在十字架上用祂的死解决人自己时也就解决了在人里面的撒但创三16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When Satan enticed man to fall he himself also entered into man and was mingled with man thus when the Lord Jesus dealt with man in His death on the cross He dealt with the Satan who was in manGen 316"}
{"zh": "2\t不只如此，主的十字架也毁坏了他黑暗的国度，并其中一切执政的、掌权的—弗六12。", "en": "2. Not only so, the Lord's cross also destroyed his kingdom of darkness, including all its rulers and authorities—Eph. 6:12.", "norm_zh": "2不只如此主的十字架也毁坏了他黑暗的国度并其中一切执政的掌权的弗六12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Not only so the Lords cross also destroyed his kingdom of darkness including all its rulers and authoritiesEph 612"}
{"zh": "3\t主的十字架也审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界—约十六11。", "en": "3. The Lord's cross also judged and destroyed the world ruled by Satan—John 16:11.", "norm_zh": "3主的十字架也审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界约十六11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Lords cross also judged and destroyed the world ruled by SatanJohn 1611"}
{"zh": "四\t神计划的目的是要将祂的生命作到人里面；基督的十字架释放出神的生命—创二9，约十九34：", "en": "D. God's purpose in His plan is to work His life into man; the cross of Christ released the divine life—Gen. 2:9; John 19:34:", "norm_zh": "四神计划的目的是要将祂的生命作到人里面基督的十字架释放出神的生命创二9约十九34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods purpose in His plan is to work His life into man the cross of Christ released the divine lifeGen 29 John 1934"}
{"zh": "1\t解决罪和人的自己，并除灭撒但，乃是基督的十字架在消极方面所作的；在积极方面，基督的十字架把神在基督里的生命释放出来，以成功神永远的目的—十二24。", "en": "1. To deal with sin and the self of man, and to annihilate Satan, is what the cross of Christ did on the negative side; on the positive side, the cross of Christ released the life of God in Christ to accomplish God's eternal purpose.—12:24.", "norm_zh": "1解决罪和人的自己并除灭撒但乃是基督的十字架在消极方面所作的在积极方面基督的十字架把神在基督里的生命释放出来以成功神永远的目的十二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To deal with sin and the self of man and to annihilate Satan is what the cross of Christ did on the negative side on the positive side the cross of Christ released the life of God in Christ to accomplish Gods eternal purpose1224"}
{"zh": "2\t主是神的化身，里面藏着神的生命；祂若不死，祂里面所藏神的生命，就不能释放出来，进到人里面—24节。", "en": "2. The Lord is the embodiment of God, and the life of God is hidden in Him; if He did not die, the life of God hidden within Him could not be released to enter into man.—v. 24.", "norm_zh": "2主是神的化身里面藏着神的生命祂若不死祂里面所藏神的生命就不能释放出来进到人里面24节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Lord is the embodiment of God and the life of God is hidden in Him if He did not die the life of God hidden within Him could not be released to enter into manv 24"}
{"zh": "3\t祂在十字架上的死毁坏了祂外面人的壳子，使祂里面神的生命释放出来，进到许多人里面，叫他们成为神的儿子，成功神永远的目的—创二21~22，彼前一3。", "en": "3. His death on the cross destroyed His human shell so that God's life could be released and then imparted into many through His resurrection to make them sons of God and thus accomplish God's eternal purpose.—Gen. 2:21-22; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "3祂在十字架上的死毁坏了祂外面人的壳子使祂里面神的生命释放出来进到许多人里面叫他们成为神的儿子成功神永远的目的创二2122彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 His death on the cross destroyed His human shell so that Gods life could be released and then imparted into many through His resurrection to make them sons of God and thus accomplish Gods eternal purposeGen 22122 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "基督的死—在祂钉十字架的阶段里", "en": "Christ's death—in the stage of His crucifixion", "norm_zh": "基督的死在祂钉十字架的阶段里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Christs deathin the stage of His crucifixion"}
{"zh": "担当我们的罪，使我们得平安，得医治", "en": "Bearing our sins, that we may have peace and be healed", "norm_zh": "担当我们的罪使我们得平安得医治", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Bearing our sins that we may have peace and be healed"}
{"zh": "被欺压，受苦害，被牵到宰杀之地", "en": "Being oppressed, afflicted, and led to the slaughter", "norm_zh": "被欺压受苦害被牵到宰杀之地", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Being oppressed afflicted and led to the slaughter"}
{"zh": "神救赎的第二步乃是十字架；十字架是说到基督的死，所以我们来看十字架，就是来看基督的死。", "en": "The second step of God's redemption is the cross; the cross speaks of Christ's death; hence, to consider the cross is to consider Christ's death.", "norm_zh": "神救赎的第二步乃是十字架十字架是说到基督的死所以我们来看十字架就是来看基督的死", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The second step of Gods redemption is the cross the cross speaks of Christs death hence to consider the cross is to consider Christs death"}
{"zh": "祂虽是无罪的，但当祂在十字架上时，神竟然离弃了祂。因为在这时，祂身上担当着我们众人所有的罪，在神看来，祂就是个罪人，是极大的罪人，是完全的罪人，所以神离弃了祂。虽然祂自己是无罪的，是不知罪的，但神把我们众人的罪都归在祂身上（赛五三6下），以祂为我们的赎罪祭和赎愆祭（10上），要祂替我们担当罪。所以在这时，神不只离弃了祂，并且击打祂，责罚祂，将祂压伤（5），使祂受死的痛苦，为我们尝尽死味（来二9），好使神的公义在我们身上的要求得到满足。神是叫祂那义的代替我们这不义的（彼前三18），为要使我们在神面前得蒙救赎，而成为义的（赛五三11）。", "en": "Although He was sinless, when He was on the cross, God actually forsook Him. Because at this time, He bore all the sins of us all on Him; in the eyes of God, He was a sinner, a great sinner, a complete sinner; therefore, God forsook Him. Although He Himself was sinless and did not know sin, God caused the iniquity of us all to fall on Him (Isa. 53:6b), making Him our sin offering and trespass offering (v. 10a) so that He could bear our sins on our behalf. Hence, at this time, God not only forsook Him but also smote Him, afflicted Him, and crushed Him (v. 5) so that He might suffer the pain of death and taste death on our behalf (Heb. 2:9) in order that the requirements of God's righteousness might be fulfilled in us. God caused the Righteous to suffer on behalf of the unrighteous (1 Pet. 3:18) to make us redeemed before God and become righteous (Isa. 53:11).", "norm_zh": "祂虽是无罪的但当祂在十字架上时神竟然离弃了祂因为在这时祂身上担当着我们众人所有的罪在神看来祂就是个罪人是极大的罪人是完全的罪人所以神离弃了祂虽然祂自己是无罪的是不知罪的但神把我们众人的罪都归在祂身上赛五三6下以祂为我们的赎罪祭和赎愆祭10上要祂替我们担当罪所以在这时神不只离弃了祂并且击打祂责罚祂将祂压伤5使祂受死的痛苦为我们尝尽死味来二9好使神的公义在我们身上的要求得到满足神是叫祂哪义的代替我们这不义的彼前三18为要使我们在神面前得蒙救赎而成为义的赛五三11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Although He was sinless when He was on the cross God actually forsook Him Because at this time He bore all the sins of us all on Him in the eyes of God He was a sinner a great sinner a complete sinner therefore God forsook Him Although He Himself was sinless and did not know sin God caused the iniquity of us all to fall on Him Isa 536b making Him our sin offering and trespass offering v 10a so that He could bear our sins on our behalf Hence at this time God not only forsook Him but also smote Him afflicted Him and crushed Him v 5 so that He might suffer the pain of death and taste death on our behalf Heb 29 in order that the requirements of Gods righteousness might be fulfilled in us God caused the Righteous to suffer on behalf of the unrighteous 1 Pet 318 to make us redeemed before God and become righteous Isa 5311"}
{"zh": "我们与基督联合，神是把我们算在基督里面。神不单独地看我们，神是在基督里看我们。在基督里，神看我们已经和基督同死了。所以，神在祂的话里清楚启示，我们在基督里属基督的人，肉体、旧人和自己都已经与基督同钉十字架（罗六6，加二20，五24）。在神看来，我们已经和基督同钉十字架了，已经在基督里和祂同死。不只是我们的罪在基督的十字架上解决了，连我们这个人也在基督的十字架上解决了。", "en": "We are joined to Christ; hence, God considers us as being in Christ. God does not see us apart from Christ; He sees us in Christ. In Christ, God sees us as already dead with Christ. Therefore, the Word of God clearly reveals that the flesh, the old man, and the self of those who are in Christ have been crucified with Christ (Rom. 6:6; Gal. 2:20; 5:24). In God's eyes we have been crucified with Christ and have already died with Him in Christ. In addition to our sins, the cross of Christ dealt with our person as well.", "norm_zh": "我们与基督联合神是把我们算在基督里面神不单独地看我们神是在基督里看我们在基督里神看我们已经和基督同死了所以神在祂的话里清楚启示我们在基督里属基督的人肉体旧人和自己都已经与基督同钉十字架罗六6加二20五24在神看来我们已经和基督同钉十字架了已经在基督里和祂同死不只是我们的罪在基督的十字架上解决了连我们这个人也在基督的十字架上解决了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We are joined to Christ hence God considers us as being in Christ God does not see us apart from Christ He sees us in Christ In Christ God sees us as already dead with Christ Therefore the Word of God clearly reveals that the flesh the old man and the self of those who are in Christ have been crucified with Christ Rom 66 Gal 220 524 In Gods eyes we have been crucified with Christ and have already died with Him in Christ In addition to our sins the cross of Christ dealt with our person as well"}
{"zh": "我们已经看过，撒但引诱人堕落时，他自己也进到了人里面。从那时起，他就在堕落的人里面，和人调在一起。所以，当主耶稣在十字架上，用祂的死解决人自己时，也就解决了在人里面的撒但。因此，当主耶稣要到十字架上受死前，祂曾说，“这世界的王要被赶出去。”（约十二31）这世界的王就是撒但，他调在人里面，霸占人，辖制人。主到十字架上，用祂的死解决了撒但所调在里面而霸占的人，自然也解决了这调在人里面而霸占人的撒但。所以圣经才说，主是借着死，就是十字架上的死，毁坏了撒但（来二14）。当初撒但借着引诱人堕落而进到人里头，以为他的诡计得逞，其实是弄巧成拙，反而给神得着机会对付他，解决他。撒但以为他将人骗去，可以霸占人作他的居所，其实他所骗去的人是他的陷阱，使他落到神的审判和毁坏里。神就是在撒但所骗去而霸占的人里面，审判了撒但，毁坏了撒但。", "en": "We have already seen that when Satan enticed man to fall, he himself also entered into man. From that time on, he has been in fallen man, mixed with man. Therefore, when the Lord Jesus dealt with man's self by His death on the cross, He also dealt with the Satan who was in man. Hence, before the Lord Jesus was about to die on the cross, He said, \"Now shall the ruler of this world be cast out\" (John 12:31). The ruler of this world is Satan, who is mixed with man, usurping and ruling over man. When the Lord went to the cross and dealt by His death with man, who was mixed with and usurped by Satan, He naturally also dealt with Satan, who was mixed with and usurped man. Hence, the Bible says that the Lord destroyed Satan through His death, that is, His death on the cross (Heb. 2:14). In the beginning, when Satan entered into man by enticing him to fall, he thought his scheme had succeeded, but actually his trick backfired, giving God the opportunity to deal with him and resolve him. Satan thought that by deceiving man he could usurp man to be his dwelling place; actually, the man he deceived was a trap for him, causing him to fall into God's judgment and destruction. It was in the very man whom Satan deceived and usurped that God judged and destroyed Satan.", "norm_zh": "我们已经看过撒但引诱人堕落时他自己也进到了人里面从哪时起他就在堕落的人里面和人调在一起所以当主耶稣在十字架上用祂的死解决人自己时也就解决了在人里面的撒但因此当主耶稣要到十字架上受死前祂曾说这世界的王要被赶出去约十二31这世界的王就是撒但他调在人里面霸占人辖制人主到十字架上用祂的死解决了撒但所调在里面而霸占的人自然也解决了这调在人里面而霸占人的撒但所以圣经才说主是借着死就是十字架上的死毁坏了撒但来二14当初撒但借着引诱人堕落而进到人里头以为他的诡计得逞其实是弄巧成拙反而给神得着机会对付他解决他撒但以为他将人骗去可以霸占人作他的居所其实他所骗去的人是他的陷阱使他落到神的审判和毁坏里神就是在撒但所骗去而霸占的人里面审判了撒但毁坏了撒但", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have already seen that when Satan enticed man to fall he himself also entered into man From that time on he has been in fallen man mixed with man Therefore when the Lord Jesus dealt with mans self by His death on the cross He also dealt with the Satan who was in man Hence before the Lord Jesus was about to die on the cross He said Now shall the ruler of this world be cast out John 1231 The ruler of this world is Satan who is mixed with man usurping and ruling over man When the Lord went to the cross and dealt by His death with man who was mixed with and usurped by Satan He naturally also dealt with Satan who was mixed with and usurped man Hence the Bible says that the Lord destroyed Satan through His death that is His death on the cross Heb 214 In the beginning when Satan entered into man by enticing him to fall he thought his scheme had succeeded but actually his trick backfired giving God the opportunity to deal with him and resolve him Satan thought that by deceiving man he could usurp man to be his dwelling place actually the man he deceived was a trap for him causing him to fall into Gods judgment and destruction It was in the very man whom Satan deceived and usurped that God judged and destroyed Satan"}
{"zh": "当我们这被撒但骗去，跟从他犯罪、顶撞神的人，在主的十字架上，借着主的死，受神审判并治死时，撒但也在我们里面受了神的审判和毁坏。不只如此，还有撒但手下的使者，就是诸天界里那些执政的、掌权的、管辖这黑暗世界的以及诸天界里那邪恶的属灵势力（弗六12），也和撒但一同受了神的审判和毁坏。撒但既是他们的首领（二2），他们既是跟随他的，撒但受了神的审判和毁坏，当然他们也与撒但一同受了神的审判和毁坏。所以撒但和他的使者，也是主的十字架所解决的。主的十字架毁坏了那黑暗的君王撒但，也毁坏了他黑暗的国度，并其中一切执政的、掌权的。这是许多信徒不太知道的，但是撒但和他的使者，就是他黑暗国度里的鬼，却十分清楚。当我们赶鬼的时候，我们就能知道，主的十字架在鬼身上是何等有权能。我们在属灵的争战里，能经历主的十字架与祂所流的血叫我们胜过撒但（启十二11），使撒但和他的使者蒙羞，不能站立。", "en": "When we, who were deceived by Satan to follow him in sinning and opposing God, were judged and put to death by God through the Lord's death on the cross, Satan was also judged and destroyed by God within us. Furthermore, the angels under Satan—the rulers, the authorities, the world-rulers of this darkness, and the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenlies (Eph. 6:12)—were also judged and destroyed with Satan by God. Since Satan is their ruler (2:2) and they follow him, when Satan was judged and destroyed by God, they naturally were judged and destroyed with Satan. Therefore, Satan and his angels were also dealt with by the cross of Christ. The cross of the Lord destroyed Satan, the ruler of darkness, as well as his kingdom of darkness and all the rulers and authorities in it. Not many believers know this fact, but Satan, his angels, and the demons in his kingdom of darkness are well aware of this matter. When we cast out demons, we can know how powerful the Lord's cross is over the demons. In spiritual warfare we can experience the Lord's cross and His shed blood enabling us to overcome Satan (Rev. 12:11), causing Satan and his angels to be put to shame and be unable to stand.", "norm_zh": "当我们这被撒但骗去跟从他犯罪顶撞神的人在主的十字架上借着主的死受神审判并治死时撒但也在我们里面受了神的审判和毁坏不只如此还有撒但手下的使者就是诸天界里哪些执政的掌权的管辖这黑暗世界的以及诸天界里哪邪恶的属灵势力弗六12也和撒但一同受了神的审判和毁坏撒但既是他们的首领二2他们既是跟随他的撒但受了神的审判和毁坏当然他们也与撒但一同受了神的审判和毁坏所以撒但和他的使者也是主的十字架所解决的主的十字架毁坏了哪黑暗的君王撒但也毁坏了他黑暗的国度并其中一切执政的掌权的这是许多信徒不太知道的但是撒但和他的使者就是他黑暗国度里的鬼却十分清楚当我们赶鬼的时候我们就能知道主的十字架在鬼身上是何等有权能我们在属灵的争战里能经历主的十字架与祂所流的血叫我们胜过撒但启十二11使撒但和他的使者蒙羞不能站立", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "When we who were deceived by Satan to follow him in sinning and opposing God were judged and put to death by God through the Lords death on the cross Satan was also judged and destroyed by God within us Furthermore the angels under Satanthe rulers the authorities the worldrulers of this darkness and the spiritual forces of evil in the heavenlies Eph 612were also judged and destroyed with Satan by God Since Satan is their ruler 22 and they follow him when Satan was judged and destroyed by God they naturally were judged and destroyed with Satan Therefore Satan and his angels were also dealt with by the cross of Christ The cross of the Lord destroyed Satan the ruler of darkness as well as his kingdom of darkness and all the rulers and authorities in it Not many believers know this fact but Satan his angels and the demons in his kingdom of darkness are well aware of this matter When we cast out demons we can know how powerful the Lords cross is over the demons In spiritual warfare we can experience the Lords cross and His shed blood enabling us to overcome Satan Rev 1211 causing Satan and his angels to be put to shame and be unable to stand"}
{"zh": "主的十字架怎样审判并毁坏了撒但，也照样审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界。这个顶撞神的世界是属于撒但的，是挂在撒但身上的。撒但既在主的十字架上受了审判并毁坏，自然挂在他身上的世界也就和他一同受了审判并毁坏。在神面前，世界是已经在十字架上受了审判并毁坏（约十六11）。在有神眼光的人跟前，世界也是已经钉在十字架上，被解决了（加六14）。", "en": "Just as the Lord's cross judged and destroyed Satan, so also it judged and destroyed the world ruled by Satan. This God-opposing world belongs to Satan; it hangs upon him. Since Satan has been judged and destroyed on the Lord's cross, naturally the world that hangs upon him has also been judged and destroyed with him. Before God, the world has already been judged and destroyed on the cross (John 16:11). In the eyes of those who have God's view, the world has also been crucified and dealt with (Gal. 6:14).", "norm_zh": "主的十字架怎样审判并毁坏了撒但也照样审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界这个顶撞神的世界是属于撒但的是挂在撒但身上的撒但既在主的十字架上受了审判并毁坏自然挂在他身上的世界也就和他一同受了审判并毁坏在神面前世界是已经在十字架上受了审判并毁坏约十六11在有神眼光的人跟前世界也是已经钉在十字架上被解决了加六14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Just as the Lords cross judged and destroyed Satan so also it judged and destroyed the world ruled by Satan This Godopposing world belongs to Satan it hangs upon him Since Satan has been judged and destroyed on the Lords cross naturally the world that hangs upon him has also been judged and destroyed with him Before God the world has already been judged and destroyed on the cross John 1611 In the eyes of those who have Gods view the world has also been crucified and dealt with Gal 614"}
{"zh": "主释放生命，分赐生命这面的死，是当日亚当沉睡所预表的。当日神使亚当睡一觉，肋旁裂开，产生了夏娃（创二21~22）。照样，神也使主在十字架上睡了一觉，在十字架上受死，肋旁裂开，流出血和水（约十九34），使人得着祂的生命，就是神的生命，而产生召会。", "en": "The life-releasing aspect, the life-imparting aspect, of the Lord's death is typified by Adam's deep sleep. God caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam, and He took out one of Adam's ribs. Then God built Eve out of the rib that He had taken from Adam's side (Gen. 2:21-22). Similarly, God caused a deep sleep to fall upon the Lord Jesus when He died on the cross so that blood and water could flow out of His pierced side (John 19:34). Now the life of God is available to man in order to produce the church.", "norm_zh": "主释放生命分赐生命这面的死是当日亚当沉睡所预表的当日神使亚当睡一觉肋旁裂开产生了夏娃创二2122照样神也使主在十字架上睡了一觉在十字架上受死肋旁裂开流出血和水约十九34使人得着祂的生命就是神的生命而产生召会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The lifereleasing aspect the lifeimparting aspect of the Lords death is typified by Adams deep sleep God caused a deep sleep to fall upon Adam and He took out one of Adams ribs Then God built Eve out of the rib that He had taken from Adams side Gen 22122 Similarly God caused a deep sleep to fall upon the Lord Jesus when He died on the cross so that blood and water could flow out of His pierced side John 1934 Now the life of God is available to man in order to produce the church"}
{"zh": "就近基督的十字架，借着祂的死，得蒙神的救赎", "en": "Drawing near to the cross of Christ to be redeemed by God through His death", "norm_zh": "就近基督的十字架借着祂的死得蒙神的救赎", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:23:29.195647+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Drawing near to the cross of Christ to be redeemed by God through His death"}
{"zh": "壹\t神救赎的第一步乃是成为肉体，第二步乃是十字架；基督在祂钉十字架的阶段里，作为神人救主，代替罪人而死—赛五三4~5、8、11下、12下：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇；以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "I. The first step of God's redemption is incarnation, and the second step is the cross; Christ, in the stage of His crucifixion, as a God-man Savior, died a vicarious death for sinners—Isa. 53:4-5, 8, 11b, 12b:", "norm_zh": "壹神救赎的第一步乃是成为肉体第二步乃是十字架基督在祂钉十字架的阶段里作为神人救主代替罪人而死赛五三45811下12下李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The first step of Gods redemption is incarnation and the second step is the cross Christ in the stage of His crucifixion as a Godman Savior died a vicarious death for sinnersIsa 5345 8 11b 12b"}
{"zh": "一\t作为神人救主，基督代替罪人而死—4~5、8、11下、12节下，彼前二24：（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "A. As a God-man Savior, Christ died a vicarious death for sinners—vv. 4-5, 8, 11b, 12b; 1 Pet. 2:24:", "norm_zh": "一作为神人救主基督代替罪人而死45811下12节下彼前二24以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As a Godman Savior Christ died a vicarious death for sinnersvv 45 8 11b 12b 1 Pet 224"}
{"zh": "1\t在基督为我们这些罪人的代死里，祂担当了我们的疾病，背负了我们的痛苦—赛五三4。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "1. In His vicarious death for us, the sinners, Christ bore our sicknesses and carried our sorrows—Isa. 53:4.", "norm_zh": "1在基督为我们这些罪人的代死里祂担当了我们的疾病背负了我们的痛苦赛五三4以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 In His vicarious death for us the sinners Christ bore our sicknesses and carried our sorrowsIsa 534"}
{"zh": "2\t在基督为我们的代死里，祂为我们的过犯被刺透，为我们的罪孽被压伤；因我们的罪过，祂从活人之地被剪除，并且担当我们的罪，使我们得平安，得医治—5、8节下。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "2. In His vicarious death for us, Christ was wounded for our transgressions, crushed for our iniquities, and cut off out of the land of the living for our transgression, and He bore our sin, that we may have peace and be healed—vv. 5, 8b.", "norm_zh": "2在基督为我们的代死里祂为我们的过犯被刺透为我们的罪孽被压伤因我们的罪过祂从活人之地被剪除并且担当我们的罪使我们得平安得医治58节下以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 In His vicarious death for us Christ was wounded for our transgressions crushed for our iniquities and cut off out of the land of the living for our transgression and He bore our sin that we may have peace and be healedvv 5 8b"}
{"zh": "3\t在基督为罪人的代死里，祂被欺压，受苦害，像羊羔被牵到宰杀之地，又像羊在剪毛的人面前被剪而无反应—7节。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "3. In His vicarious death for sinners, Christ was oppressed, afflicted, and led to the slaughter like a lamb and sheared before the shearers like a sheep, with no reaction—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "3在基督为罪人的代死里祂被欺压受苦害像羊羔被牵到宰杀之地又像羊在剪毛的人面前被剪而无反应7节以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 In His vicarious death for sinners Christ was oppressed afflicted and led to the slaughter like a lamb and sheared before the shearers like a sheep with no reactionv 7"}
{"zh": "4\t以赛亚五十三章八节说，基督因受欺压（被假冒为善之犹太首领）和审判（被不公正之罗马官长）而被夺去—太二六57，路二三1~12。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "4. Isaiah 53:8 says that Christ was taken away by oppression (of the hypocritical Jewish leaders) and by judgment (of the unjust Roman officials)—Matt. 26:57; Luke 23:1-12.", "norm_zh": "4以赛亚五十三章八节说基督因受欺压被假冒为善之犹太首领和审判被不公正之罗马官长而被夺去太二六57路二三112以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Isaiah 538 says that Christ was taken away by oppression of the hypocritical Jewish leaders and by judgment of the unjust Roman officialsMatt 2657 Luke 23112"}
{"zh": "5\t按照以赛亚五十三章十二节下半，当基督被钉在十字架上时，祂被列在罪犯之中，又为罪犯代求—32~33、34节上。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "5. According to Isaiah 53:12c, when Christ was crucified on the cross, He was numbered with the transgressors and He interceded for the transgressors—vv. 32-33, 34a.", "norm_zh": "5按照以赛亚五十三章十二节下半当基督被钉在十字架上时祂被列在罪犯之中又为罪犯代求323334节上以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 According to Isaiah 5312c when Christ was crucified on the cross He was numbered with the transgressors and He interceded for the transgressorsvv 3233 34a"}
{"zh": "6\t按照以赛亚五十三章九节，虽然基督未行强暴，口中也没有诡诈，但祂被分配与罪人同埋，死的时候却与财主同葬。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "6. According to Isaiah 53:9, Christ was assigned a grave with the wicked, but with a rich man in His death, although He had done no violence, nor was there any deceit in His mouth.", "norm_zh": "6按照以赛亚五十三章九节虽然基督未行强暴口中也没有诡诈但祂被分配与罪人同埋死的时候却与财主同葬以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 According to Isaiah 539 Christ was assigned a grave with the wicked but with a rich man in His death although He had done no violence nor was there any deceit in His mouth"}
{"zh": "二\t以上所说的一切都是人所作的；人作了这一切事后，耶和华就使我们这些如羊走迷，偏行己路之人的罪孽，都归在祂身上—赛五三6，太二七45~46：（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "B. All the aforementioned things were done by man; after man had done all these things, Jehovah caused the iniquity of us all, who have gone astray like sheep and have turned to our own way, to fall on Him—Isa. 53:6; Matt. 27:45-46:", "norm_zh": "二以上所说的一切都是人所作的人作了这一切事后耶和华就使我们这些如羊走迷偏行己路之人的罪孽都归在祂身上赛五三6太二七4546以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B All the aforementioned things were done by man after man had done all these things Jehovah caused the iniquity of us all who have gone astray like sheep and have turned to our own way to fall on HimIsa 536 Matt 274546"}
{"zh": "1\t当基督在十字架上末了的三个小时，耶和华将祂看作是罪人的代替，并在那时刻弃绝了祂这惟一的罪人—彼前三18，太二七45~46。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "1. During the last three hours that Christ was on the cross, Jehovah considered Him as the Substitute for sinners and forsook Him as the unique sinner at that moment—1 Pet. 3:18; Matt. 27:45-46.", "norm_zh": "1当基督在十字架上末了的三个小时耶和华将祂看作是罪人的代替并在哪时刻弃绝了祂这惟一的罪人彼前三18太二七4546以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 During the last three hours that Christ was on the cross Jehovah considered Him as the Substitute for sinners and forsook Him as the unique sinner at that moment1 Pet 318 Matt 274546"}
{"zh": "2\t按照以赛亚五十三章十节上半，基督作罪人的代替经过这代死时，耶和华喜悦将祂压伤，使祂受痛苦。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "2. According to Isaiah 53:10a, in Christ's vicarious death as the Substitute for sinners, Jehovah was pleased to crush Him, to afflict Him with grief.", "norm_zh": "2按照以赛亚五十三章十节上半基督作罪人的代替经过这代死时耶和华喜悦将祂压伤使祂受痛苦以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 According to Isaiah 5310a in Christs vicarious death as the Substitute for sinners Jehovah was pleased to crush Him to afflict Him with grief"}
{"zh": "三\t以赛亚五十三章十节下半说到基督使自己成为赎罪祭：（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "C. Isaiah 53:10b says that Christ made Himself an offering for sin:", "norm_zh": "三以赛亚五十三章十节下半说到基督使自己成为赎罪祭以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Isaiah 5310b says that Christ made Himself an offering for sin"}
{"zh": "1\t希伯来九章十四节说，基督借着永远的灵，将自己献给神。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "1. Hebrews 9:14 says that Christ offered Himself through the eternal Spirit to God.", "norm_zh": "1希伯来九章十四节说基督借着永远的灵将自己献给神以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Hebrews 914 says that Christ offered Himself through the eternal Spirit to God"}
{"zh": "2\t以赛亚五十三章十二节下半说，基督将命倾倒，以至于死。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "2. Isaiah 53:12b says that Christ poured out His life unto death.", "norm_zh": "2以赛亚五十三章十二节下半说基督将命倾倒以至于死以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Isaiah 5312b says that Christ poured out His life unto death"}
{"zh": "四\t基督的钉十字架乃是为着完成神永远的救赎，使在基督里的信徒得蒙救赎（得蒙赦罪—徒十43，得著称义—徒十三39，并与神和好—罗五10），达到在祂复活里生命的联结，其实际乃是祂的赐生命之灵—来九12，林前十五45下，罗八9下，腓一19下。（以赛亚书生命读经，第五十篇）", "en": "D. Christ's crucifixion was for the accomplishing of God's eternal redemption, that the believers in Christ may be redeemed (forgiven of sins—Acts 10:43, justified—Acts 13:39, and reconciled to God—Rom. 5:10), attaining to the life union in His resurrection, the reality of which is His life-giving Spirit—Heb. 9:12; 1 Cor. 15:45b; Rom. 8:9b; Phil. 1:19b.", "norm_zh": "四基督的钉十字架乃是为着完成神永远的救赎使在基督里的信徒得蒙救赎得蒙赦罪徒十43得着称义徒十三39并与神和好罗五10达到在祂复活里生命的联结其实际乃是祂的赐生命之灵来九12林前十五45下罗八9下腓一19下以赛亚书生命读经第五十篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Christs crucifixion was for the accomplishing of Gods eternal redemption that the believers in Christ may be redeemed forgiven of sinsActs 1043 justifiedActs 1339 and reconciled to GodRom 510 attaining to the life union in His resurrection the reality of which is His lifegiving SpiritHeb 912 1 Cor 1545b Rom 89b Phil 119b"}
{"zh": "贰\t神的计划有一个目的，但人的堕落带来三个难处；基督要成功神的计划，必须到十字架上受死；十字架是说到基督的死，所以我们来看十字架，就是来看基督的死—罗五16中，可十五25，赛五三6下：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "II. God has a purpose in His plan, but man's fall brought in three problems; in order for Christ to fulfill God's plan, He had to die on the cross; the cross speaks of Christ's death; therefore, for us to look at the cross is to look at Christ's death—Rom. 5:16b; Mark 15:25; Isa. 53:6b:", "norm_zh": "贰神的计划有一个目的但人的堕落带来三个难处基督要成功神的计划必须到十字架上受死十字架是说到基督的死所以我们来看十字架就是来看基督的死罗五16中可十五25赛五三6下李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II God has a purpose in His plan but mans fall brought in three problems in order for Christ to fulfill Gods plan He had to die on the cross the cross speaks of Christs death therefore for us to look at the cross is to look at Christs deathRom 516b Mark 1525 Isa 536b"}
{"zh": "一\t人在神面前因着堕落而有的第一个难处，就是罪；基督的十字架解决人的罪—罗五16中，林后五21上：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "A. As a result of the fall, man's first problem before God is sin; the cross of Christ solves man's sin—Rom. 5:16b; 2 Cor. 5:21a:", "norm_zh": "一人在神面前因着堕落而有的第一个难处就是罪基督的十字架解决人的罪罗五16中林后五21上李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A As a result of the fall mans first problem before God is sin the cross of Christ solves mans sinRom 516b 2 Cor 521a"}
{"zh": "1\t人虽然是神为着祂自己的计划所创造的，是神所器重、所爱的，但人的堕落却使神的公义不能不定人的罪—罗五16中，诗八九14。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "1. Although man was created by God for His own plan and is highly regarded and loved by God, yet man's fall makes it impossible for God's righteousness not to condemn man—Rom. 5:16b; Psa. 89:14.", "norm_zh": "1人虽然是神为着祂自己的计划所创造的是神所器重所爱的但人的堕落却使神的公义不能不定人的罪罗五16中诗八九14李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Although man was created by God for His own plan and is highly regarded and loved by God yet mans fall makes it impossible for Gods righteousness not to condemn manRom 516b Psa 8914"}
{"zh": "2\t神按着祂的公义定人的罪，人就得死，就得灭亡；神的计划就发生问题，神的爱也不能容忍；在这里，神的公义对神的爱有了难处—结十八4，来九27。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "2. According to His righteousness, God condemns man, and man must die and perish; God's plan has a problem, and God's love cannot tolerate it; here, God's righteousness has a problem with God's love—Ezek. 18:4; Heb. 9:27.", "norm_zh": "2神按着祂的公义定人的罪人就得死就得灭亡神的计划就发生问提神的爱也不能容忍在这里神的公义对神的爱有了难处结十八4来九27李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 According to His righteousness God condemns man and man must die and perish Gods plan has a problem and Gods love cannot tolerate it here Gods righteousness has a problem with Gods loveEzek 184 Heb 927"}
{"zh": "3\t神要应付这个难处，解决这个问题，祂自己来到人里面作人的代替，站在人的地位为人担罪，替人受死—赛五三6下，彼前二24上。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "3. To meet this difficulty and solve this problem, He Himself came into man to be man's Substitute, standing in man's position to bear man's sins and die for man—Isa. 53:6b; 1 Pet. 2:24a.", "norm_zh": "3神要应付这个难处解决这个问提祂自己来到人里面作人的代替站在人的地位为人担罪替人受死赛五三6下彼前二24上李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 To meet this difficulty and solve this problem He Himself came into man to be mans Substitute standing in mans position to bear mans sins and die for manIsa 536b 1 Pet 224a"}
{"zh": "4\t主耶稣在十字架上受死，就是神在人里面替人担罪受罚；祂替我们担当罪，使我们在神面前得赦罪，蒙称义；祂替我们成为罪，使我们在祂里面成为神的义，蒙神悦纳—林后五21上。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "4. The death of the Lord Jesus on the cross is God's bearing man's sin and suffering punishment on man's behalf in man; He bore our sins so that we might receive the forgiveness of sins and be justified by God, and He was made sin on our behalf so that we might become God's righteousness and be acceptable to God in Him—2 Cor. 5:21a.", "norm_zh": "4主耶稣在十字架上受死就是神在人里面替人担罪受罚祂替我们担当罪使我们在神面前得赦罪蒙称义祂替我们成为罪使我们在祂里面成为神的义蒙神悦纳林后五21上李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The death of the Lord Jesus on the cross is Gods bearing mans sin and suffering punishment on mans behalf in man He bore our sins so that we might receive the forgiveness of sins and be justified by God and He was made sin on our behalf so that we might become Gods righteousness and be acceptable to God in Him2 Cor 521a"}
{"zh": "二\t主耶稣在十字架上，不只担当人的罪而死，也包括担当了人自己；基督的十字架解决人自己—罗五18，六6，加二20，五24：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "B. On the cross, the Lord Jesus not only died bearing man's sins but also included the bearing of man himself; the cross of Christ deals with man himself—Rom. 5:18; 6:6; Gal. 2:20; 5:24:", "norm_zh": "二主耶稣在十字架上不只担当人的罪而死也包括担当了人自己基督的十字架解决人自己罗五18六6加二20五24李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B On the cross the Lord Jesus not only died bearing mans sins but also included the bearing of man himself the cross of Christ deals with man himselfRom 518 66 Gal 220 524"}
{"zh": "1\t祂到十字架上受死，是穿着人，将人带到那里和祂同死；所以，当祂钉十字架时，我们众人也都在那里，和祂一同钉死—罗五18。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "1. He went to the cross to die, putting on man and bringing man there to die with Him; therefore, when He was crucified, we all were also there, crucified with Him—Rom. 5:18.", "norm_zh": "1祂到十字架上受死是穿着人将人带到哪里和祂同死所以当祂钉十字架时我们众人也都在哪里和祂一同钉死罗五18李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 He went to the cross to die putting on man and bringing man there to die with Him therefore when He was crucified we all were also there crucified with HimRom 518"}
{"zh": "2\t基督是“一切受造之物的首生者”，是包罗万有的，所以祂的死是包罗万有的，也是超乎时间的；基督死了，一切在时间里的受造者，也都在祂里面与祂同死了—西一15。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "2. Christ is the \"Firstborn of all creation\" and is all-inclusive, so His death is all-inclusive and transcends time; when Christ died, all creation in time also died with Him and in Him—Col. 1:15.", "norm_zh": "2基督是一切受造之物的首生者是包罗万有的所以祂的死是包罗万有的也是超乎时间的基督死了一切在时间里的受造者也都在祂里面与祂同死了西一15李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Christ is the Firstborn of all creation and is allinclusive so His death is allinclusive and transcends time when Christ died all creation in time also died with Him and in HimCol 115"}
{"zh": "3\t神看我们在基督里已经死了，我们也信我们在基督里已经死了；正因此，我们一信主，与祂联合，就要受浸归入祂的死，与祂一同埋葬，结束我们的旧人，和属于我们旧人的一切—罗六4~6。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "3. God considers that we died in Christ, and we also believe that we have died in Christ; because of this, once we believe in the Lord and are joined to Him, we need to be baptized into His death and buried with Him to terminate our old man and everything belonging to our old man—Rom. 6:4-6.", "norm_zh": "3神看我们在基督里已经死了我们也信我们在基督里已经死了正因此我们一信主与祂联合就要受浸归入祂的死与祂一同埋葬结束我们的旧人和属于我们旧人的一切罗六46李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 God considers that we died in Christ and we also believe that we have died in Christ because of this once we believe in the Lord and are joined to Him we need to be baptized into His death and buried with Him to terminate our old man and everything belonging to our old manRom 646"}
{"zh": "1\t撒但引诱人堕落时，他自己也进到了人里面，和人调在一起；所以，当主耶稣在十字架上，用祂的死解决人自己时，也就解决了在人里面的撒但—创三1~6。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "1. When Satan enticed man to fall, he himself also entered into man and was mingled with man; therefore, when the Lord Jesus dealt with man himself by His death on the cross, He also dealt with the Satan who was in man—Gen. 3:1-6.", "norm_zh": "1撒但引诱人堕落时他自己也进到了人里面和人调在一起所以当主耶稣在十字架上用祂的死解决人自己时也就解决了在人里面的撒但创三16李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When Satan enticed man to fall he himself also entered into man and was mingled with man therefore when the Lord Jesus dealt with man himself by His death on the cross He also dealt with the Satan who was in manGen 316"}
{"zh": "2\t不只如此，主的十字架也毁坏了他黑暗的国度，并其中一切执政的、掌权的—弗六12。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "2. Not only so, the Lord's cross also destroyed his kingdom of darkness, including all its rulers and authorities—Eph. 6:12.", "norm_zh": "2不只如此主的十字架也毁坏了他黑暗的国度并其中一切执政的掌权的弗六12李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Not only so the Lords cross also destroyed his kingdom of darkness including all its rulers and authoritiesEph 612"}
{"zh": "3\t主的十字架也审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界—约十六11。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "3. The Lord's cross also judged and destroyed the world ruled by Satan—John 16:11.", "norm_zh": "3主的十字架也审判并毁坏了撒但所管辖的世界约十六11李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The Lords cross also judged and destroyed the world ruled by SatanJohn 1611"}
{"zh": "四\t神计划的目的是要将祂的生命作到人里面；基督的十字架释放出神的生命—创二9，约十九34：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "D. God's purpose in His plan is to work His life into man; the cross of Christ releases the life of God—Gen. 2:9; John 19:34:", "norm_zh": "四神计划的目的是要将祂的生命作到人里面基督的十字架释放出神的生命创二9约十九34李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Gods purpose in His plan is to work His life into man the cross of Christ releases the life of GodGen 29 John 1934"}
{"zh": "1\t解决罪和人的自己，并除灭撒但，乃是基督的十字架在消极方面所作的；在积极方面，基督的十字架把神在基督里的生命释放出来，以成功神永远的目的—十二24。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "1. To deal with sin and man himself and destroy Satan is what the cross of Christ did on the negative side; on the positive side, the cross of Christ released the life of God in Christ to accomplish God's eternal purpose—12:24.", "norm_zh": "1解决罪和人的自己并除灭撒但乃是基督的十字架在消极方面所作的在积极方面基督的十字架把神在基督里的生命释放出来以成功神永远的目的十二24李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To deal with sin and man himself and destroy Satan is what the cross of Christ did on the negative side on the positive side the cross of Christ released the life of God in Christ to accomplish Gods eternal purpose1224"}
{"zh": "2\t主是神的化身，里面藏着神的生命；祂若不死，祂里面所藏神的生命，就不能释放出来，进到人里面—24节。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "2. The Lord is the embodiment of God, and the life of God is hidden in Him; if He did not die, the life of God hidden within Him could not be released to enter into man—v. 24.", "norm_zh": "2主是神的化身里面藏着神的生命祂若不死祂里面所藏神的生命就不能释放出来进到人里面24节李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Lord is the embodiment of God and the life of God is hidden in Him if He did not die the life of God hidden within Him could not be released to enter into manv 24"}
{"zh": "3\t祂在十字架上的死毁坏了祂外面人的壳子，使祂里面神的生命释放出来，进到许多人里面，叫他们成为神的儿子，成功神永远的目的—创二21~22，彼前一3。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第六篇）", "en": "3. His death on the cross destroyed His human shell so that God's life could be released and then imparted into many through His resurrection to make them sons of God and thus accomplish God's eternal purpose.—Gen. 2:21-22; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "3祂在十字架上的死毁坏了祂外面人的壳子使祂里面神的生命释放出来进到许多人里面叫他们成为神的儿子成功神永远的目的创二2122彼前一3李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:27:42.337471+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 His death on the cross destroyed His human shell so that Gods life could be released and then imparted into many through His resurrection to make them sons of God and thus accomplish Gods eternal purposeGen 22122 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "读经：林前十五14、17，罗四25，林后五21，罗一4，约十17~18，十一25，徒二24，十三33，彼前一3", "en": "Scripture Reading: 1 Cor. 15:14, 17; Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21; Rom. 1:4; John 10:17-18; 11:25; Acts 2:24; 13:33; 1 Pet. 1:3", "norm_zh": "读经林前十五1417罗四25林后五21罗一4约十1718十一25徒二24十三33彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 1 Cor 1514 17 Rom 425 2 Cor 521 Rom 14 John 101718 1125 Acts 224 1333 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "壹\t基督复活的必须—林前十五14、17，罗四25，林后五21：", "en": "I. THE NECESSITY OF CHRIST'S RESURRECTION—1 Cor. 15:14, 17; Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21:", "norm_zh": "壹基督复活的必须林前十五1417罗四25林后五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I THE NECESSITY OF CHRISTS RESURRECTION1 Cor 1514 17 Rom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "一\t基督的死成功了完全的救赎，为我们也为神解决了一切的难处；一切关乎神要救赎我们的事，和我们蒙救赎的事，基督的死都已经为我们作成了；没有人能在基督的死所成功的救赎上，再加上一点工作—西一20、22，来二9，罗八21，约一29，来九26、28。", "en": "A. The death of Christ accomplished a full redemption and dealt with all our problems; it fulfilled all God's requirements related to our redemption; nothing needs to be added to Christ's redemption.—Col. 1:20, 22; Heb. 2:9; Rom. 8:21; John 1:29; Heb. 9:26, 28.", "norm_zh": "一基督的死成功了完全的救赎为我们也为神解决了一切的难处一切关乎神要救赎我们的事和我们蒙救赎的事基督的死都已经为我们作成了没有人能在基督的死所成功的救赎上再加上一点工作西一2022来二9罗八21约一29来九2628", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The death of Christ accomplished a full redemption and dealt with all our problems it fulfilled all Gods requirements related to our redemption nothing needs to be added to Christs redemptionCol 120 22 Heb 29 Rom 821 John 129 Heb 926 28"}
{"zh": "二\t祂的复活，是这些事的明证和确据；为着使我们确实知道，并向我们证实这些事，基督必须复活—罗四25，林前十五17。", "en": "B. His resurrection is the proof and assurance of these matters; Christ's resurrection enables us to know these matters.—Rom. 4:25; 1 Cor. 15:17.", "norm_zh": "二祂的复活是这些事的明证和确据为着使我们确实知道并向我们证实这些事基督必须复活罗四25林前十五17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B His resurrection is the proof and assurance of these matters Christs resurrection enables us to know these mattersRom 425 1 Cor 1517"}
{"zh": "三\t虽然如此，若是基督没有复活，祂的死为我们所作的仍无功效，仍不能与我们发生关系—林后五21，林前十五14：", "en": "C. However, the resurrection of Christ is still necessary for the effective accomplishments of His death to be applied to us.—2 Cor. 5:21; 1 Cor. 15:14:", "norm_zh": "三虽然如此若是基督没有复活祂的死为我们所作的仍无功效仍不能与我们发生关系林后五21林前十五14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C However the resurrection of Christ is still necessary for the effective accomplishments of His death to be applied to us2 Cor 521 1 Cor 1514"}
{"zh": "1\t祂的死虽然为我们赎清了罪恶，满足了神公义的要求，但祂若没有复活，叫我们得着祂的生命，与祂联合，我们就无法在祂里面，也不能有分于祂赎罪的代替，不能在祂里面成为神的义，而蒙神悦纳—罗四25，林前十五17，林后五21。", "en": "1. His death redeemed us from our sins and satisfied God's righteous requirement. His resurrection, however, enables us to receive His life and to be joined with Him, that is, to enter into Him and receive the benefits of His substitutionary death. Through His resurrection we also become the righteousness of God in Him and are acceptable to God.—Rom. 4:25; 1 Cor. 15:17; 2 Cor. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1祂的死虽然为我们赎清了罪恶满足了神公义的要求但祂若没有复活叫我们得着祂的生命与祂联合我们就无法在祂里面也不能有分于祂赎罪的代替不能在祂里面成为神的义而蒙神悦纳罗四25林前十五17林后五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 His death redeemed us from our sins and satisfied Gods righteous requirement His resurrection however enables us to receive His life and to be joined with Him that is to enter into Him and receive the benefits of His substitutionary death Through His resurrection we also become the righteousness of God in Him and are acceptable to GodRom 425 1 Cor 1517 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "2\t基督虽然带着我们，包括着我们和祂同死了，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能成为赐生命的灵进到我们里面，将祂奥秘之死的成分带到我们里面，种到我们里面，使我们在祂里面，也就是在祂的生命里，经历祂的死—林前十五45，提后四22，罗八16。", "en": "2. Although we were included in Christ's death on the cross, He can sow the element of His mysterious death into our being only because He became the life-giving Spirit in resurrection.—1 Cor. 15:45; 2 Tim. 4:22; Rom. 8:16.", "norm_zh": "2基督虽然带着我们包括着我们和祂同死了但祂若没有复活祂就不能成为赐生命的灵进到我们里面将祂奥秘之死的成分带到我们里面种到我们里面使我们在祂里面也就是在祂的生命里经历祂的死林前十五45提后四22罗八16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Although we were included in Christs death on the cross He can sow the element of His mysterious death into our being only because He became the lifegiving Spirit in resurrection1 Cor 1545 2 Tim 422 Rom 816"}
{"zh": "3\t祂的死虽然为我们废除了撒但，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能进到我们里面，叫我们得着祂作我们胜过撒但的生命，而使我们有胜过撒但的经历—来二14。", "en": "3. Although His death destroyed Satan, we can experience His overcoming of Satan only because His Satan-overcoming life has entered into us through His resurrection.—Heb. 2:14.", "norm_zh": "3祂的死虽然为我们废除了撒但但祂若没有复活祂就不能进到我们里面叫我们得着祂作我们胜过撒但的生命而使我们有胜过撒但的经历来二14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Although His death destroyed Satan we can experience His overcoming of Satan only because His Satanovercoming life has entered into us through His resurrectionHeb 214"}
{"zh": "4\t祂虽然借着死，为我们尝尽了死味，为我们废掉了死，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能将祂的生命彰显出来—9节，提后一10。", "en": "4. Although He tasted death for us and nullified death, His life has been made available to us only because of His resurrection.—v. 9; 2 Tim. 1:10.", "norm_zh": "4祂虽然借着死为我们尝尽了死味为我们废掉了死但祂若没有复活祂就不能将祂的生命彰显出来9节提后一10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Although He tasted death for us and nullified death His life has been made available to us only because of His resurrectionv 9 2 Tim 110"}
{"zh": "5\t祂的死虽然是要释放出祂的生命，好叫我们得着，但祂若没有复活，祂的生命仍然不能进到我们里面给我们得着—彼前一3。", "en": "5. Without resurrection His life would not be able to enter into us.—1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "5祂的死虽然是要释放出祂的生命好叫我们得着但祂若没有复活祂的生命仍然不能进到我们里面给我们得着彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Without resurrection His life would not be able to enter into us1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "6\t这些都是在于祂的复活；祂若没有复活，这些就都成为泡影；所以，祂必须复活！—林前十五14。", "en": "6. The fulfillment of all these matters depends on His resurrection; without His resurrection, the fulfillment of these matters would be impossible; therefore, His resurrection is essential.—1 Cor. 15:14.", "norm_zh": "6这些都是在于祂的复活祂若没有复活这些就都成为泡影所以祂必须复活林前十五14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 The fulfillment of all these matters depends on His resurrection without His resurrection the fulfillment of these matters would be impossible therefore His resurrection is essential1 Cor 1514"}
{"zh": "贰\t基督复活的实际—罗一4，约十17~18，十一25，徒二24，罗六9，启一18：", "en": "II. The reality of Christ's resurrection—Rom. 1:4; John 10:17-18; 11:25; Acts 2:24; Rom. 6:9; Rev. 1:18:", "norm_zh": "贰基督复活的实际罗一4约十1718十一25徒二24罗六9启一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The reality of Christs resurrectionRom 14 John 101718 1125 Acts 224 Rom 69 Rev 118"}
{"zh": "一\t因着基督的复活是必须的，也是必定的，所以主耶稣实在复活了；祂的死如何是实在的，祂的复活也如何是实际的—罗六10，约十18。", "en": "A. Because Christ's resurrection is necessary and assured, the Lord Jesus resurrected in reality; just as His death is real, His resurrection also is a reality—Rom. 6:10; John 10:18.", "norm_zh": "一因着基督的复活是必须的也是必定的所以主耶稣实在复活了祂的死如何是实在的祂的复活也如何是实际的罗六10约十18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Because Christs resurrection is necessary and assured the Lord Jesus resurrected in reality just as His death is real His resurrection also is a realityRom 610 John 1018"}
{"zh": "二\t祂的死和人的死不同；人是因犯罪而死，祂是为赎罪而死；我们既是因犯罪而死，所以我们死了，就伏在死的审判之下，不能脱离；祂既是为赎罪而死，所以祂死了，就解除了死的审判，而得着自由—罗六23，徒二24。", "en": "B. His death is different from that of every other person; man dies because he has committed sins, whereas He died to redeem man from sin; since we die because we have committed sins, we are subject to the judgment of death and unable to escape; since He died for the redemption from sin, He removed the judgment of death and obtained freedom—Rom. 6:23; Acts 2:24.", "norm_zh": "二祂的死和人的死不同人是因犯罪而死祂是为赎罪而死我们既是因犯罪而死所以我们死了就伏在死的审判之下不能脱离祂既是为赎罪而死所以祂死了就解除了死的审判而得着自由罗六23徒二24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B His death is different from that of every other person man dies because he has committed sins whereas He died to redeem man from sin since we die because we have committed sins we are subject to the judgment of death and unable to escape since He died for the redemption from sin He removed the judgment of death and obtained freedomRom 623 Acts 224"}
{"zh": "三\t撒但虽是掌死权的，但主是生命的创始者；并且主就是复活，就是生命—来二14，徒三15，约十一25：", "en": "C. Although Satan has the might of death, the Lord is the Author of life; and the Lord is the resurrection and the life—Heb. 2:14; Acts 3:15; John 11:25:", "norm_zh": "三撒但虽是掌死权的但主是生命的创始者并且主就是复活就是生命来二14徒三15约十一25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Although Satan has the might of death the Lord is the Author of life and the Lord is the resurrection and the lifeHeb 214 Acts 315 John 1125"}
{"zh": "1\t当主进入死里的时候，那掌死权的撒但，必是用尽所有阴府和死的权势，包围祂，拘禁祂；虽然撒但能用死扣留那些为死所胜，被死所俘的人，却不能用死拘禁这位自己走进死里，要借着死而废掉死的主，因为祂里面有复活的生命—林前十五55~56，约十17~18。", "en": "1. When the Lord entered into death, Satan, who has the might of death, must have exhausted all the power of Hades and death to surround Him and confine Him; although Satan can use death to hold those who are overcome by death and taken captive by death, he cannot use death to confine this One who walked into death of Himself to nullify death through death, because He has the resurrection life within Him—1 Cor. 15:55-56; John 10:17-18.", "norm_zh": "1当主进入死里的时候哪掌死权的撒但必是用尽所有阴府和死的权势包围祂拘禁祂虽然撒但能用死扣留哪些为死所胜被死所俘的人却不能用死拘禁这位自己走进死里要借着死而废掉死的主因为祂里面有复活的生命林前十五5556约十1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When the Lord entered into death Satan who has the might of death must have exhausted all the power of Hades and death to surround Him and confine Him although Satan can use death to hold those who are overcome by death and taken captive by death he cannot use death to confine this One who walked into death of Himself to nullify death through death because He has the resurrection life within Him1 Cor 155556 John 101718"}
{"zh": "2\t反而生命能吞灭死，复活能胜过死；祂冲破死，冲出阴府，复活了；祂大能的生命，复活的大能，叫祂胜过死，脱离死的拘禁，而从死里复活了—林前十五3~4，罗六9，启一18。", "en": "2. On the contrary, life swallows up death, and resurrection overcomes death; He broke through death, broke out of Hades, and resurrected; His powerful life and the power of resurrection caused Him to overcome death, escape the confinement of death, and resurrect from the dead—1 Cor. 15:3-4; Rom. 6:9; Rev. 1:18.", "norm_zh": "2反而生命能吞灭死复活能胜过死祂冲破死冲出阴府复活了祂大能的生命复活的大能叫祂胜过死脱离死的拘禁而从死里复活了林前十五34罗六9启一18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 On the contrary life swallows up death and resurrection overcomes death He broke through death broke out of Hades and resurrected His powerful life and the power of resurrection caused Him to overcome death escape the confinement of death and resurrect from the dead1 Cor 1534 Rom 69 Rev 118"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督复活的果效；祂救赎的一切果效，是在祂的复活里，给我们取用并享受的—罗四25，徒十三33，彼前一3，约二十17，林前十五45：", "en": "III. The results of Christ's resurrection; all the results of His redemption are in His resurrection for us to appropriate and enjoy—Rom. 4:25; Acts 13:33; 1 Pet. 1:3; John 20:17; 1 Cor. 15:45:", "norm_zh": "叁基督复活的果效祂救赎的一切果效是在祂的复活里给我们取用并享受的罗四25徒十三33彼前一3约二十17林前十五45", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The results of Christs resurrection all the results of His redemption are in His resurrection for us to appropriate and enjoyRom 425 Acts 1333 1 Pet 13 John 2017 1 Cor 1545"}
{"zh": "一\t证明基督为我们的死已经满足了神的要求—罗四25，林后五21：", "en": "A. Proving That God's Requirements Were Satisfied by the Death of Christ for Us—Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21:", "norm_zh": "一证明基督为我们的死已经满足了神的要求罗四25林后五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Proving That Gods Requirements Were Satisfied by the Death of Christ for UsRom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "1\t我们因基督的死已经蒙神称义，并且我们在基督这位复活者里面，已经在神面前蒙悦纳—罗四25，林后五21。", "en": "1. We are justified by God because of Christ's death, and in Christ, the resurrected One, we are accepted before God—Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1我们因基督的死已经蒙神称义并且我们在基督这位复活者里面已经在神面前蒙悦纳罗四25林后五21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We are justified by God because of Christs death and in Christ the resurrected One we are accepted before GodRom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "2\t祂又使这位复活的基督在我们里面，活出一种能得神称义，且一直蒙神悦纳的生活—罗四25下。", "en": "2. He also makes the resurrected Christ live within us a life that can be justified by Him and that is always acceptable to Him.—Rom. 4:25b.", "norm_zh": "2祂又使这位复活的基督在我们里面活出一种能得神称义且一直蒙神悦纳的生活罗四25下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He also makes the resurrected Christ live within us a life that can be justified by Him and that is always acceptable to HimRom 425b"}
{"zh": "二\t使我们得重生；神的生命原是藏在主耶稣里面，等到主耶稣借着祂的死，将神的生命释放出来，祂就借着祂的复活，叫神的生命进入我们里面，使我们得着重生—彼前一3、23。", "en": "B. Regenerating Us; God's life was originally hidden in the Lord Jesus, until through His death the Lord Jesus released God's life, and through His resurrection He caused God's life to enter into us, thereby regenerating us—1 Pet. 1:3, 23.", "norm_zh": "二使我们得重生神的生命原是藏在主耶稣里面等到主耶稣借着祂的死将神的生命释放出来祂就借着祂的复活叫神的生命进入我们里面使我们得着重生彼前一323", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Regenerating Us Gods life was originally hidden in the Lord Jesus until through His death the Lord Jesus released Gods life and through His resurrection He caused Gods life to enter into us thereby regenerating us1 Pet 13 23"}
{"zh": "三\t使我们成为祂的弟兄—约二十17，来二11~12，徒十三33，罗八29：", "en": "C. Making Us His Brothers—John 20:17; Heb. 2:11-12; Acts 13:33; Rom. 8:29:", "norm_zh": "三使我们成为祂的弟兄约二十17来二1112徒十三33罗八29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Making Us His BrothersJohn 2017 Heb 21112 Acts 1333 Rom 829"}
{"zh": "1\t神在祂永远里的计划，是要叫许多人有祂儿子的生命，得着祂儿子的名分，成为祂的儿子，像主耶稣一样有神的生命，作神的表现—来二10。", "en": "1. According to His eternal plan, however, God desires that many would have the life of His Son, become His sons, and receive the sonship.—Heb. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1神在祂永远里的计划是要叫许多人有祂儿子的生命得着祂儿子的名分成为祂的儿子像主耶稣一样有神的生命作神的表现来二10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to His eternal plan however God desires that many would have the life of His Son become His sons and receive the sonshipHeb 210"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣的复活，就叫神这个计划的目的得以达到；神既借着基督的复活重生了我们，叫我们得着神的生命，就叫我们成为神的儿子，是祂许多的儿子—约二十17。", "en": "2. The resurrection of the Lord Jesus fulfilled this purpose in God's plan; through Christ's resurrection God regenerated us so that we would have His life and become His many sons.—John 20:17.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣的复活就叫神这个计划的目的得以达到神既借着基督的复活重生了我们叫我们得着神的生命就叫我们成为神的儿子是祂许多的儿子约二十17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The resurrection of the Lord Jesus fulfilled this purpose in Gods plan through Christs resurrection God regenerated us so that we would have His life and become His many sonsJohn 2017"}
{"zh": "3\t神原来只有一个儿子，只有一个独生子，现在借着基督的复活，生出了许多儿子，使基督“在许多弟兄中作长子”—罗八29。", "en": "3. Originally God had only one Son, the only begotten Son, but through His resurrection Christ became the \"Firstborn among many brothers,\" the many sons who were regenerated through His resurrection.—Rom. 8:29.", "norm_zh": "3神原来只有一个儿子只有一个独生子现在借着基督的复活生出了许多儿子使基督在许多弟兄中作长子罗八29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Originally God had only one Son the only begotten Son but through His resurrection Christ became the Firstborn among many brothers the many sons who were regenerated through His resurrectionRom 829"}
{"zh": "4\t主的复活将我们带到一个地步，叫我们和祂一样，有神的生命，作神的表现，和祂同作神的儿子，是祂的弟兄，是祂的伴侣；在主的复活里，我们所得到神儿子的名分，乃是神救恩里最高的福分—太二八10。", "en": "4. The resurrection of the Lord brings us to a point where we are exactly the same as He is, having the life of God in order to express God. We are sons of God with Him; we are His brothers and partners; the sonship that we received in the Lord's resurrection is the top blessing in God's salvation.—Matt. 28:10.", "norm_zh": "4主的复活将我们带到一个地步叫我们和祂一样有神的生命作神的表现和祂同作神的儿子是祂的弟兄是祂的伴侣在主的复活里我们所得到神儿子的名分乃是神救恩里最高的福分太二八10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The resurrection of the Lord brings us to a point where we are exactly the same as He is having the life of God in order to express God We are sons of God with Him we are His brothers and partners the sonship that we received in the Lords resurrection is the top blessing in Gods salvationMatt 2810"}
{"zh": "四\t使那在肉体里是末后亚当的基督，成为赐生命的灵—林前十五45，提后四22，罗八16。", "en": "D. Making Christ, Who Was the Last Adam in the Flesh, the Life-giving Spirit—1 Cor. 15:45; 2 Tim. 4:22; Rom. 8:16.", "norm_zh": "四使哪在肉体里是末后亚当的基督成为赐生命的灵林前十五45提后四22罗八16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Making Christ Who Was the Last Adam in the Flesh the Lifegiving Spirit1 Cor 1545 2 Tim 422 Rom 816"}
{"zh": "五\t使我们得着祂活在我们里面—加二20，西三3~4，约十四19：", "en": "E. Christ Entering into Us to Be Our Life—Gal. 2:20; Col. 3:3-4; John 14:19:", "norm_zh": "五使我们得着祂活在我们里面加二20西三34约十四19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Christ Entering into Us to Be Our LifeGal 220 Col 334 John 1419"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣复活，不只叫我们得着祂的生命进到我们里面，使我们得着重生，并且叫我们得着祂自己进到我们里面，作我们的生命；实在说，祂的生命进到我们里面，就是祂自己进到我们里面，因为祂自己就是那个生命—西三3~4。", "en": "1. Through Christ's resurrection we not only received His life for our regeneration, but we also received Him into us to be our life; actually, His life entering into us is just Himself entering into us, because He is life.—Col. 3:3-4.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣复活不只叫我们得着祂的生命进到我们里面使我们得着重生并且叫我们得着祂自己进到我们里面作我们的生命实在说祂的生命进到我们里面就是祂自己进到我们里面因为祂自己就是哪个生命西三34", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Through Christs resurrection we not only received His life for our regeneration but we also received Him into us to be our life actually His life entering into us is just Himself entering into us because He is lifeCol 334"}
{"zh": "2\t祂原是在神里面，与神为一的；祂的复活既叫我们在祂里面，与祂联合，也就叫我们在神里面，与神联合；既叫祂活在我们里面，也就叫神活在我们里面—罗六5，约十四20。", "en": "2. Since He is in God and one with God, His resurrection has brought us into God and joined us with God; through His resurrection God can live in us, and we can be joined with God.—Rom. 6:5; John 14:20.", "norm_zh": "2祂原是在神里面与神为一的祂的复活既叫我们在祂里面与祂联合也就叫我们在神里面与神联合既叫祂活在我们里面也就叫神活在我们里面罗六5约十四20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Since He is in God and one with God His resurrection has brought us into God and joined us with God through His resurrection God can live in us and we can be joined with GodRom 65 John 1420"}
{"zh": "六\t叫信徒与基督一同从死人中复活—弗二6上，罗六8：", "en": "F. Raising the Believers Up with Christ from the Dead—Eph. 2:6a; Rom. 6:8:", "norm_zh": "六叫信徒与基督一同从死人中复活弗二6上罗六8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Raising the Believers Up with Christ from the DeadEph 26a Rom 68"}
{"zh": "1\t当日的方舟怎样包括着其中的人和一切活物，经过洪水的淹没，又从洪水里出来，基督也照样包括着我们进入死，又从死里复活出来；在神看，我们是在祂的死里与祂一同死了，也是在祂的复活里与祂一同复活了—创七1~12，八13~19，罗六8，加二20，弗二6。", "en": "1. Just as the people and the living creatures in the ark passed through the waters of the flood, we also passed through death together with Christ and were raised together with Christ; in God's eyes we died together with Christ in His death, and we were raised together with Him in His resurrection—Gen. 7:1-12; 8:13-19; Rom. 6:8; Gal. 2:20; Eph. 2:6.", "norm_zh": "1当日的方舟怎样包括着其中的人和一切活物经过洪水的淹没又从洪水里出来基督也照样包括着我们进入死又从死里复活出来在神看我们是在祂的死里与祂一同死了也是在祂的复活里与祂一同复活了创七112八1319罗六8加二20弗二6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Just as the people and the living creatures in the ark passed through the waters of the flood we also passed through death together with Christ and were raised together with Christ in Gods eyes we died together with Christ in His death and we were raised together with Him in His resurrectionGen 7112 81319 Rom 68 Gal 220 Eph 26"}
{"zh": "2\t借着祂的复活，我们得以进入神里面，享受属乎神的一切；一切属乎神的，在祂的复活里，都是我们的分，都成为我们的—6节。", "en": "2. Through Christ's resurrection we entered into God to enjoy everything of God; everything of God is our portion in His resurrection and has become ours—v. 6.", "norm_zh": "2借着祂的复活我们得以进入神里面享受属乎神的一切一切属乎神的在祂的复活里都是我们的分都成为我们的6节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through Christs resurrection we entered into God to enjoy everything of God everything of God is our portion in His resurrection and has become oursv 6"}
{"zh": "七\t使那借着基督十字架上之死而裂开的一粒麦子，释放出神圣的生命，产生许多子粒，以构成基督的身体—约十二24，林前十17。", "en": "G. Releasing the Divine Life from the One Grain Broken through the Death of the Cross of Christ to Produce Many Grains for the Constitution of the Body of Christ—John 12:24; 1 Cor. 10:17.", "norm_zh": "七使哪借着基督十字架上之死而裂开的一粒麦子释放出神圣的生命产生许多子粒以构成基督的身体约十二24林前十17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G Releasing the Divine Life from the One Grain Broken through the Death of the Cross of Christ to Produce Many Grains for the Constitution of the Body of ChristJohn 1224 1 Cor 1017"}
{"zh": "八\t使我们成为新造—彼前一3，林后五17，弗四24，彼后三13：", "en": "H. Making us a new creation—1 Pet. 1:3; 2 Cor. 5:17; Eph. 4:24; 2 Pet. 3:13:", "norm_zh": "八使我们成为新造彼前一3林后五17弗四24彼后三13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H Making us a new creation1 Pet 13 2 Cor 517 Eph 424 2 Pet 313"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣的复活使我们有分于祂，得着祂的生命，而得着重生，就使我们变成新造，旧事已过，都变成新的了—彼前一3，林后五17。", "en": "1. The resurrection of the Lord Jesus caused us to partake of Him and receive His life for regeneration; in this way we were made the new creation: the old things have passed away; behold, they have become new—1 Pet. 1:3; 2 Cor. 5:17.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣的复活使我们有分于祂得着祂的生命而得着重生就使我们变成新造旧事已过都变成新的了彼前一3林后五17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The resurrection of the Lord Jesus caused us to partake of Him and receive His life for regeneration in this way we were made the new creation the old things have passed away behold they have become new1 Pet 13 2 Cor 517"}
{"zh": "2\t这个新造，不像旧造是神用祂的能力，在祂之外所造的一个单纯的人；这个新造乃是神用祂的生命，在祂自己里面所造的一个与神联合的人—弗四24。", "en": "2. Unlike the old creation, the new creation is not another man who has been created by God with His power but is apart from Him; the new creation is man in union with God, created by God with His life in Himself—Eph. 4:24.", "norm_zh": "2这个新造不像旧造是神用祂的能力在祂之外所造的一个单纯的人这个新造乃是神用祂的生命在祂自己里面所造的一个与神联合的人弗四24", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Unlike the old creation the new creation is not another man who has been created by God with His power but is apart from Him the new creation is man in union with God created by God with His life in HimselfEph 424"}
{"zh": "九\t施行那灵的流；那灵的一道流变成许多道江河；活水的江河作那灵的流，在复活里从我们里面流出来—约七38~39。", "en": "I. Carrying out the flow of the Spirit; the one flow of the Spirit becomes many rivers; the rivers of living water as the flow of the Spirit flow out of us in resurrection—John 7:38-39.", "norm_zh": "九施行哪灵的流哪灵的一道流变成许多道江河活水的江河作哪灵的流在复活里从我们里面流出来约七3839", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Carrying out the flow of the Spirit the one flow of the Spirit becomes many rivers the rivers of living water as the flow of the Spirit flow out of us in resurrectionJohn 73839"}
{"zh": "十\t成为神在基督升天里行动的基础，为着形成召会，就是基督的身体—徒五30~31，弗一20~23：", "en": "J. Forming the Base of His Move in the Ascension of Christ for the Formation of the Church, the Body of Christ—Acts 5:30-31; Eph. 1:20-23:", "norm_zh": "十成为神在基督升天里行动的基础为着形成召会就是基督的身体徒五3031弗一2023", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "J Forming the Base of His Move in the Ascension of Christ for the Formation of the Church the Body of ChristActs 53031 Eph 12023"}
{"zh": "1\t若没有复活，基督绝不能升到诸天之上，所以复活为祂的升天立下基础—徒五30~31。", "en": "1. Without resurrection Christ could never ascend to the heavens, so the resurrection laid the base for His ascension—Acts 5:30-31.", "norm_zh": "1若没有复活基督绝不能升到诸天之上所以复活为祂的升天立下基础徒五3031", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Without resurrection Christ could never ascend to the heavens so the resurrection laid the base for His ascensionActs 53031"}
{"zh": "2\t基督乃是在升天里，将祂在复活里所产生的一切重生的肢体，形成祂那一个生机的身体—弗一20~23。", "en": "2. It was in His ascension that He formed all the regenerated members, produced in His resurrection, into His one organic Body—Eph. 1:20-23.", "norm_zh": "2基督乃是在升天里将祂在复活里所产生的一切重生的肢体形成祂哪一个生机的身体弗一2023", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 It was in His ascension that He formed all the regenerated members produced in His resurrection into His one organic BodyEph 12023"}
{"zh": "十一\t以基督复活的大能加力给信徒，使信徒在基督徒的行事为人中模成祂的死—腓三10，罗六5。", "en": "K. Empowering the Believers with the Power of Christ's Resurrection for the Conformation to His Death in the Believers' Christian Walk—Phil. 3:10; Rom. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "十一以基督复活的大能加力给信徒使信徒在基督徒的行事为人中模成祂的死腓三10罗六5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "K Empowering the Believers with the Power of Christs Resurrection for the Conformation to His Death in the Believers Christian WalkPhil 310 Rom 65"}
{"zh": "十二\t施行基督之死的功效和杀死，好在复活里释放出神的生命—林后四10，罗六8。", "en": "L. Carrying Out the Effectiveness and Killing of the Death of Christ for the Release of the Divine Life in Resurrection—2 Cor. 4:10; Rom. 6:8.", "norm_zh": "十二施行基督之死的功效和杀死好在复活里释放出神的生命林后四10罗六8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "L Carrying Out the Effectiveness and Killing of the Death of Christ for the Release of the Divine Life in Resurrection2 Cor 410 Rom 68"}
{"zh": "肆\t“虽然祂的死成功了神的救赎，但祂的死所成功的，是重在消极方面解决我们在神面前的难处，和神在我们身上的拦阻；然而基督的复活，是在积极方面使神成全了祂的计划，达到了祂的目的。虽然基督的死是祂救赎的根基，是祂复活的根据，但祂的死所成功的一切，都是在祂的复活里才得有功效，才成为实际。”（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "IV. \"Although Christ's death accomplished God's redemption, His death mainly dealt with the negative aspects of our problems before God. The resurrection of Christ, however, allowed God to fulfill His plan and attain His positive goal. The death of Christ is the foundation of His redemption and the basis for His resurrection, but the accomplishments of His death were made effective and real to us through His resurrection.\"", "norm_zh": "肆虽然祂的死成功了神的救赎但祂的死所成功的是重在消极方面解决我们在神面前的难处和神在我们身上的拦阻然而基督的复活是在积极方面使神成全了祂的计划达到了祂的目的虽然基督的死是祂救赎的根基是祂复活的根据但祂的死所成功的一切都是在祂的复活里才得有功效才成为实际李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:31:06.258257+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Although Christs death accomplished Gods redemption His death mainly dealt with the negative aspects of our problems before God The resurrection of Christ however allowed God to fulfill His plan and attain His positive goal The death of Christ is the foundation of His redemption and the basis for His resurrection but the accomplishments of His death were made effective and real to us through His resurrection"}
{"zh": "一\t基督的死成功了完全的救赎，为我们也为神解决了一切的难处；一切关乎神要救赎我们的事，和我们蒙救赎的事，基督的死都已经为我们作成了；没有人能在基督的死所成功的救赎上，再加上一点工作—西一20、22，来二9，罗八21，约一29，来九26、28。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "A.\tThe death of Christ accomplished a full redemption and dealt with all our problems, and it fulfilled all God's requirements related to our redemption; nothing needs to be added to Christ's redemption—Col. 1:20, 22; Heb. 2:9; Rom. 8:21; John 1:29; Heb. 9:26, 28.", "norm_zh": "一基督的死成功了完全的救赎为我们也为神解决了一切的难处一切关乎神要救赎我们的事和我们蒙救赎的事基督的死都已经为我们作成了没有人能在基督的死所成功的救赎上再加上一点工作西一2022来二9罗八21约一29来九2628李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The death of Christ accomplished a full redemption and dealt with all our problems and it fulfilled all Gods requirements related to our redemption nothing needs to be added to Christs redemptionCol 120 22 Heb 29 Rom 821 John 129 Heb 926 28"}
{"zh": "二\t祂的复活，是这些事的明证和确据；为着使我们确实知道，并向我们证实这些事，基督必须复活—罗四25，林前十五17。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "B.\tHis resurrection is the proof and assurance of these matters; Christ's resurrection enables us to know these matters—Rom. 4:25; 1 Cor. 15:17.", "norm_zh": "二祂的复活是这些事的明证和确据为着使我们确实知道并向我们证实这些事基督必须复活罗四25林前十五17李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B His resurrection is the proof and assurance of these matters Christs resurrection enables us to know these mattersRom 425 1 Cor 1517"}
{"zh": "三\t虽然如此，若是基督没有复活，祂的死为我们所作的仍无功效，仍不能与我们发生关系—林后五21，林前十五14：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "C.\tHowever, the resurrection of Christ is still necessary for the effective accomplishments of His death to be applied to us—2 Cor. 5:21; 1 Cor. 15:14:", "norm_zh": "三虽然如此若是基督没有复活祂的死为我们所作的仍无功效仍不能与我们发生关系林后五21林前十五14李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C However the resurrection of Christ is still necessary for the effective accomplishments of His death to be applied to us2 Cor 521 1 Cor 1514"}
{"zh": "1\t祂的死虽然为我们赎清了罪恶，满足了神公义的要求，但祂若没有复活，叫我们得着祂的生命，与祂联合，我们就无法在祂里面，也不能有分于祂赎罪的代替，不能在祂里面成为神的义，而蒙神悦纳—罗四25，林前十五17，林后五21。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1.\tHis death redeemed us from our sins and satisfied God's righteous requirement. His resurrection, however, enables us to receive His life and to be joined with Him, that is, to enter into Him and receive the benefits of His substitutionary death. Through His resurrection we also become the righteousness of God in Him and are acceptable to God—Rom. 4:25; 1 Cor. 15:17; 2 Cor. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1祂的死虽然为我们赎清了罪恶满足了神公义的要求但祂若没有复活叫我们得着祂的生命与祂联合我们就无法在祂里面也不能有分于祂赎罪的代替不能在祂里面成为神的义而蒙神悦纳罗四25林前十五17林后五21李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 His death redeemed us from our sins and satisfied Gods righteous requirement His resurrection however enables us to receive His life and to be joined with Him that is to enter into Him and receive the benefits of His substitutionary death Through His resurrection we also become the righteousness of God in Him and are acceptable to GodRom 425 1 Cor 1517 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "2\t基督虽然带着我们，包括着我们和祂同死了，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能成为赐生命的灵进到我们里面，将祂奥秘之死的成分带到我们里面，种到我们里面，使我们在祂里面，也就是在祂的生命里，经历祂的死—林前十五45，提后四22，罗八16。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2.\tAlthough we were included in Christ's death on the cross, He can sow the element of His mysterious death into our being only because He became the life-giving Spirit in resurrection.—1 Cor. 15:45; 2 Tim. 4:22; Rom. 8:16.", "norm_zh": "2基督虽然带着我们包括着我们和祂同死了但祂若没有复活祂就不能成为赐生命的灵进到我们里面将祂奥秘之死的成分带到我们里面种到我们里面使我们在祂里面也就是在祂的生命里经历祂的死林前十五45提后四22罗八16李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Although we were included in Christs death on the cross He can sow the element of His mysterious death into our being only because He became the lifegiving Spirit in resurrection1 Cor 1545 2 Tim 422 Rom 816"}
{"zh": "3\t祂的死虽然为我们废除了撒但，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能进到我们里面，叫我们得着祂作我们胜过撒但的生命，而使我们有胜过撒但的经历—来二14。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "3.\tAlthough His death destroyed Satan, we can experience His overcoming of Satan only because His Satan-overcoming life has entered into us through His resurrection.—Heb. 2:14.", "norm_zh": "3祂的死虽然为我们废除了撒但但祂若没有复活祂就不能进到我们里面叫我们得着祂作我们胜过撒但的生命而使我们有胜过撒但的经历来二14李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Although His death destroyed Satan we can experience His overcoming of Satan only because His Satanovercoming life has entered into us through His resurrectionHeb 214"}
{"zh": "4\t祂虽然借着死，为我们尝尽了死味，为我们废掉了死，但祂若没有复活，祂就不能将祂的生命彰显出来—9节，提后一10。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "4.\tAlthough He tasted death for us and nullified death, His life has been made available to us only because of His resurrection.—v. 9; 2 Tim. 1:10.", "norm_zh": "4祂虽然借着死为我们尝尽了死味为我们废掉了死但祂若没有复活祂就不能将祂的生命彰显出来9节提后一10李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 Although He tasted death for us and nullified death His life has been made available to us only because of His resurrectionv 9 2 Tim 110"}
{"zh": "5\t祂的死虽然是要释放出祂的生命，好叫我们得着，但祂若没有复活，祂的生命仍然不能进到我们里面给我们得着—彼前一3。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "5.\tWithout resurrection His life would not be able to enter into us.—1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "5祂的死虽然是要释放出祂的生命好叫我们得着但祂若没有复活祂的生命仍然不能进到我们里面给我们得着彼前一3李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "5 Without resurrection His life would not be able to enter into us1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "6\t这些都是在于祂的复活；祂若没有复活，这些就都成为泡影；所以，祂必须复活！—林前十五14。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "6.\tThe fulfillment of all these matters depends on His resurrection; without His resurrection, the fulfillment of these matters would be impossible; His resurrection is essential!—1 Cor. 15:14.", "norm_zh": "6这些都是在于祂的复活祂若没有复活这些就都成为泡影所以祂必须复活林前十五14李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "6 The fulfillment of all these matters depends on His resurrection without His resurrection the fulfillment of these matters would be impossible His resurrection is essential1 Cor 1514"}
{"zh": "贰\t基督复活的实际—罗一4，约十17~18，十一25，徒二24，罗六9，启一18：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "II.\tThe reality of Christ's resurrection—Rom. 1:4; John 10:17-18; 11:25; Acts 2:24; Rom. 6:9; Rev. 1:18:", "norm_zh": "贰基督复活的实际罗一4约十1718十一25徒二24罗六9启一18李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The reality of Christs resurrectionRom 14 John 101718 1125 Acts 224 Rom 69 Rev 118"}
{"zh": "一\t因着基督的复活是必须的，也是必定的，所以主耶稣实在复活了；祂的死如何是实在的，祂的复活也如何是实际的—罗六10，约十18。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "A. Because Christ's resurrection is necessary and destined, the Lord Jesus actually resurrected; even as His death is real, His resurrection is also real.—Rom. 6:10; John 10:18.", "norm_zh": "一因着基督的复活是必须的也是必定的所以主耶稣实在复活了祂的死如何是实在的祂的复活也如何是实际的罗六10约十18李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Because Christs resurrection is necessary and destined the Lord Jesus actually resurrected even as His death is real His resurrection is also realRom 610 John 1018"}
{"zh": "二\t祂的死和人的死不同；人是因犯罪而死，祂是为赎罪而死；我们既是因犯罪而死，所以我们死了，就伏在死的审判之下，不能脱离；祂既是为赎罪而死，所以祂死了，就解除了死的审判，而得着自由—罗六23，徒二24。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "B. His death is different from that of every other person; man dies because he has committed sins, whereas He died to redeem man from sin; since we die because we have committed sins, when we die, we are subject to the judgment of death and unable to escape; since He died for the redemption from sin, when He died, He removed the judgment of death and obtained freedom.—Rom. 6:23; Acts 2:24.", "norm_zh": "二祂的死和人的死不同人是因犯罪而死祂是为赎罪而死我们既是因犯罪而死所以我们死了就伏在死的审判之下不能脱离祂既是为赎罪而死所以祂死了就解除了死的审判而得着自由罗六23徒二24李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B His death is different from that of every other person man dies because he has committed sins whereas He died to redeem man from sin since we die because we have committed sins when we die we are subject to the judgment of death and unable to escape since He died for the redemption from sin when He died He removed the judgment of death and obtained freedomRom 623 Acts 224"}
{"zh": "三\t撒但虽是掌死权的，但主是生命的创始者；并且主就是复活，就是生命—来二14，徒三15，约十一25：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "C. Satan has the might of death, but the Lord is the Author of life; and the Lord is the resurrection and the life.—Heb. 2:14; Acts 3:15; John 11:25:", "norm_zh": "三撒但虽是掌死权的但主是生命的创始者并且主就是复活就是生命来二14徒三15约十一25李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Satan has the might of death but the Lord is the Author of life and the Lord is the resurrection and the lifeHeb 214 Acts 315 John 1125"}
{"zh": "1\t当主进入死里的时候，那掌死权的撒但，必是用尽所有阴府和死的权势，包围祂，拘禁祂；虽然撒但能用死扣留那些为死所胜，被死所俘的人，却不能用死拘禁这位自己走进死里，要借着死而废掉死的主，因为祂里面有复活的生命—林前十五55~56，约十17~18。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1. When the Lord entered into death, Satan, who has the might of death, must have exhausted all the power of Hades and death to hold Him; although Satan uses death to hold those who have been taken captive by sin and death, he cannot use death to hold the Lord, who walked into death voluntarily to nullify death through death by the resurrection life in Him.—1 Cor. 15:55-56; John 10:17-18.", "norm_zh": "1当主进入死里的时候哪掌死权的撒但必是用尽所有阴府和死的权势包围祂拘禁祂虽然撒但能用死扣留哪些为死所胜被死所俘的人却不能用死拘禁这位自己走进死里要借着死而废掉死的主因为祂里面有复活的生命林前十五5556约十1718李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When the Lord entered into death Satan who has the might of death must have exhausted all the power of Hades and death to hold Him although Satan uses death to hold those who have been taken captive by sin and death he cannot use death to hold the Lord who walked into death voluntarily to nullify death through death by the resurrection life in Him1 Cor 155556 John 101718"}
{"zh": "2\t反而生命能吞灭死，复活能胜过死；祂冲破死，冲出阴府，复活了；祂大能的生命，复活的大能，叫祂胜过死，脱离死的拘禁，而从死里复活了—林前十五3~4，罗六9，启一18。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2. Rather, life swallows up death, and resurrection overcomes death; in His resurrection the Lord broke through death and Hades; His powerful resurrection life caused Him to overcome death, break the hold of death, and resurrect from the dead.—1 Cor. 15:3-4; Rom. 6:9; Rev. 1:18.", "norm_zh": "2反而生命能吞灭死复活能胜过死祂冲破死冲出阴府复活了祂大能的生命复活的大能叫祂胜过死脱离死的拘禁而从死里复活了林前十五34罗六9启一18李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Rather life swallows up death and resurrection overcomes death in His resurrection the Lord broke through death and Hades His powerful resurrection life caused Him to overcome death break the hold of death and resurrect from the dead1 Cor 1534 Rom 69 Rev 118"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督复活的果效；祂救赎的一切果效，是在祂的复活里，给我们取用并享受的—罗四25，徒十三33，彼前一3，约二十17，林前十五45：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "III. The Results of Christ's Resurrection; All the Results of His Redemption Are for Us to Appropriate and Enjoy in His Resurrection—Rom. 4:25; Acts 13:33; 1 Pet. 1:3; John 20:17; 1 Cor. 15:45:", "norm_zh": "叁基督复活的果效祂救赎的一切果效是在祂的复活里给我们取用并享受的罗四25徒十三33彼前一3约二十17林前十五45李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The Results of Christs Resurrection All the Results of His Redemption Are for Us to Appropriate and Enjoy in His ResurrectionRom 425 Acts 1333 1 Pet 13 John 2017 1 Cor 1545"}
{"zh": "一\t证明基督为我们的死已经满足了神的要求—罗四25，林后五21：（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "A. Proving That God's Requirements Were Satisfied by the Death of Christ for Us—Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21:", "norm_zh": "一证明基督为我们的死已经满足了神的要求罗四25林后五21李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Proving That Gods Requirements Were Satisfied by the Death of Christ for UsRom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "1\t我们因基督的死已经蒙神称义，并且我们在基督这位復活者里面，已经在神面前蒙悦纳—罗四25，林后五21。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "1. We are justified by God because of Christ's death, and in Christ, the resurrected One, we are accepted before God.—Rom. 4:25; 2 Cor. 5:21.", "norm_zh": "1我们因基督的死已经蒙神称义并且我们在基督这位复活者里面已经在神面前蒙悦纳罗四25林后五21李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We are justified by God because of Christs death and in Christ the resurrected One we are accepted before GodRom 425 2 Cor 521"}
{"zh": "2\t祂又使这位復活的基督在我们里面，活出一种能得神称义，且一直蒙神悦纳的生活—罗四25下。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "2. He also makes the resurrected Christ live within us a life that can be justified by Him and that is always acceptable to Him.—Rom. 4:25b.", "norm_zh": "2祂又使这位复活的基督在我们里面活出一种能得神称义且一直蒙神悦纳的生活罗四25下李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 He also makes the resurrected Christ live within us a life that can be justified by Him and that is always acceptable to HimRom 425b"}
{"zh": "二\t使我们得重生；神的生命原是藏在主耶稣里面，等到主耶稣借着祂的死，将神的生命释放出来，祂就借着祂的复活，叫神的生命进入我们里面，使我们得着重生—彼前一3、23。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "B. Regenerating us; God's life was originally hidden in the Lord Jesus, until the Lord Jesus released God's life through His death, and through His resurrection He caused God's life to enter into us, thereby regenerating us.—1 Pet. 1:3, 23.", "norm_zh": "二使我们得重生神的生命原是藏在主耶稣里面等到主耶稣借着祂的死将神的生命释放出来祂就借着祂的复活叫神的生命进入我们里面使我们得着重生彼前一323李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Regenerating us Gods life was originally hidden in the Lord Jesus until the Lord Jesus released Gods life through His death and through His resurrection He caused Gods life to enter into us thereby regenerating us1 Pet 13 23"}
{"zh": "三\t使我们成为祂的弟兄—约二十17，来二11~12，徒十三33，罗八29：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "C. Making Us His Brothers—John 20:17; Heb. 2:11-12; Acts 13:33; Rom. 8:29:", "norm_zh": "三使我们成为祂的弟兄约二十17来二1112徒十三33罗八29李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Making Us His BrothersJohn 2017 Heb 21112 Acts 1333 Rom 829"}
{"zh": "1\t神在祂永远里的计划，是要叫许多人有祂儿子的生命，得着祂儿子的名分，成为祂的儿子，像主耶稣一样有神的生命，作神的表现—来二10。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1. According to His eternal plan, God desires that many would have the life of His Son, receive the sonship, and become His sons, having God's life to be God's expression just like the Lord Jesus.—Heb. 2:10.", "norm_zh": "1神在祂永远里的计划是要叫许多人有祂儿子的生命得着祂儿子的名分成为祂的儿子像主耶稣一样有神的生命作神的表现来二10李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to His eternal plan God desires that many would have the life of His Son receive the sonship and become His sons having Gods life to be Gods expression just like the Lord JesusHeb 210"}
{"zh": "2\t主耶稣的复活，就叫神这个计划的目的得以达到；神既借着基督的复活重生了我们，叫我们得着神的生命，就叫我们成为神的儿子，是祂许多的儿子—约二十17。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2. The resurrection of the Lord Jesus fulfilled this purpose in God's plan; through Christ's resurrection God regenerated us so that we would have His life and become His many sons.—John 20:17.", "norm_zh": "2主耶稣的复活就叫神这个计划的目的得以达到神既借着基督的复活重生了我们叫我们得着神的生命就叫我们成为神的儿子是祂许多的儿子约二十17李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The resurrection of the Lord Jesus fulfilled this purpose in Gods plan through Christs resurrection God regenerated us so that we would have His life and become His many sonsJohn 2017"}
{"zh": "3\t神原来只有一个儿子，只有一个独生子，现在借着基督的复活，生出了许多儿子，使基督“在许多弟兄中作长子”—罗八29。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "3. Originally God had only one Son, the only begotten Son, but now through Christ's resurrection, He has brought forth many sons, making Christ \"the Firstborn among many brothers\"—Rom. 8:29.", "norm_zh": "3神原来只有一个儿子只有一个独生子现在借着基督的复活生出了许多儿子使基督在许多弟兄中作长子罗八29李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Originally God had only one Son the only begotten Son but now through Christs resurrection He has brought forth many sons making Christ the Firstborn among many brothersRom 829"}
{"zh": "4\t主的复活将我们带到一个地步，叫我们和祂一样，有神的生命，作神的表现，和祂同作神的儿子，是祂的弟兄，是祂的伴侣；在主的复活里，我们所得到神儿子的名分，乃是神救恩里最高的福分—太二八10。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "4. The resurrection of the Lord brings us to a point where we are exactly the same as He is, having the life of God in order to express God. We are sons of God with Him; we are His brothers and partners; the sonship that we received in the Lord's resurrection is the top blessing in God's salvation.—Matt. 28:10.", "norm_zh": "4主的复活将我们带到一个地步叫我们和祂一样有神的生命作神的表现和祂同作神的儿子是祂的弟兄是祂的伴侣在主的复活里我们所得到神儿子的名分乃是神救恩里最高的福分太二八10李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 The resurrection of the Lord brings us to a point where we are exactly the same as He is having the life of God in order to express God We are sons of God with Him we are His brothers and partners the sonship that we received in the Lords resurrection is the top blessing in Gods salvationMatt 2810"}
{"zh": "五\t使我们得着祂活在我们里面—加二20，西三3~4，约十四19：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "E. Christ Entering into Us to Be Our Life—Gal. 2:20; Col. 3:3-4; John 14:19:", "norm_zh": "五使我们得着祂活在我们里面加二20西三34约十四19李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Christ Entering into Us to Be Our LifeGal 220 Col 334 John 1419"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣复活，不只叫我们得着祂的生命进到我们里面，使我们得着重生，并且叫我们得着祂自己进到我们里面，作我们的生命；实在说，祂的生命进到我们里面，就是祂自己进到我们里面，因为祂自己就是那个生命—西三3~4。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1. Through Christ's resurrection we not only received His life for our regeneration, but we also received Him into us to be our life; actually, His life entering into us is just Himself entering into us, because He is life.—Col. 3:3-4.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣复活不只叫我们得着祂的生命进到我们里面使我们得着重生并且叫我们得着祂自己进到我们里面作我们的生命实在说祂的生命进到我们里面就是祂自己进到我们里面因为祂自己就是哪个生命西三34李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Through Christs resurrection we not only received His life for our regeneration but we also received Him into us to be our life actually His life entering into us is just Himself entering into us because He is lifeCol 334"}
{"zh": "2\t祂原是在神里面，与神为一的；祂的复活既叫我们在祂里面，与祂联合，也就叫我们在神里面，与神联合；既叫祂活在我们里面，也就叫神活在我们里面—罗六5，约十四20。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2. Since He is in God and one with God; His resurrection has brought us into God and joined us with God. Through His resurrection God can live in us, and we can be joined with God.—Rom. 6:5; John 14:20.", "norm_zh": "2祂原是在神里面与神为一的祂的复活既叫我们在祂里面与祂联合也就叫我们在神里面与神联合既叫祂活在我们里面也就叫神活在我们里面罗六5约十四20李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Since He is in God and one with God His resurrection has brought us into God and joined us with God Through His resurrection God can live in us and we can be joined with GodRom 65 John 1420"}
{"zh": "六\t叫信徒与基督一同从死人中复活—弗二6上，罗六8：（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "F. Raising the Believers Up with Christ from the Dead—Eph. 2:6a; Rom. 6:8:", "norm_zh": "六叫信徒与基督一同从死人中复活弗二6上罗六8李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Raising the Believers Up with Christ from the DeadEph 26a Rom 68"}
{"zh": "1\t当日的方舟怎样包括着其中的人和一切活物，经过洪水的淹没，又从洪水里出来，基督也照样包括着我们进入死，又从死里复活出来；在神看，我们是在祂的死里与祂一同死了，也是在祂的复活里与祂一同复活了—创七1~12，八13~19，罗六8，加二20，弗二6。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1. Just as the ark of that day included the people and all the living creatures in it, passing through the submersion of the flood and coming out of the flood, so also Christ included us in entering into death and rising up from the dead; in God's eyes, we died with Him in His death and also rose with Him in His resurrection.—Gen. 7:1-12; 8:13-19; Rom. 6:8; Gal. 2:20; Eph. 2:6.", "norm_zh": "1当日的方舟怎样包括着其中的人和一切活物经过洪水的淹没又从洪水里出来基督也照样包括着我们进入死又从死里复活出来在神看我们是在祂的死里与祂一同死了也是在祂的复活里与祂一同复活了创七112八1319罗六8加二20弗二6李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Just as the ark of that day included the people and all the living creatures in it passing through the submersion of the flood and coming out of the flood so also Christ included us in entering into death and rising up from the dead in Gods eyes we died with Him in His death and also rose with Him in His resurrectionGen 7112 81319 Rom 68 Gal 220 Eph 26"}
{"zh": "2\t借着祂的复活，我们得以进入神里面，享受属乎神的一切；一切属乎神的，在祂的复活里，都是我们的分，都成为我们的—6节。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2. Through Christ's resurrection we entered into God to enjoy everything of God; everything of God is our portion in His resurrection.—v. 6.", "norm_zh": "2借着祂的复活我们得以进入神里面享受属乎神的一切一切属乎神的在祂的复活里都是我们的分都成为我们的6节李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through Christs resurrection we entered into God to enjoy everything of God everything of God is our portion in His resurrectionv 6"}
{"zh": "七\t使那借着基督十字架上之死而裂开的一粒麦子，释放出神圣的生命，产生许多子粒，以构成基督的身体—约十二24，林前十17。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "G. Releasing the Divine Life from the One Grain Broken through the Death of the Cross of Christ to Produce Many Grains for the Constitution of the Body of Christ—John 12:24; 1 Cor. 10:17.", "norm_zh": "七使哪借着基督十字架上之死而裂开的一粒麦子释放出神圣的生命产生许多子粒以构成基督的身体约十二24林前十17李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G Releasing the Divine Life from the One Grain Broken through the Death of the Cross of Christ to Produce Many Grains for the Constitution of the Body of ChristJohn 1224 1 Cor 1017"}
{"zh": "八\t使我们成为新造—彼前一3，林后五17，弗四24，彼后三13：（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "H. Making us a new creation—1 Pet. 1:3; 2 Cor. 5:17; Eph. 4:24; 2 Pet. 3:13:", "norm_zh": "八使我们成为新造彼前一3林后五17弗四24彼后三13李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H Making us a new creation1 Pet 13 2 Cor 517 Eph 424 2 Pet 313"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣的复活使我们有分于祂，得着祂的生命，而得着重生，就使我们变成新造，旧事已过，都变成新的了—彼前一3，林后五17。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "1. The resurrection of the Lord Jesus caused us to partake of Him and receive His life for regeneration. In this way we were made the new creation: \"The old things have passed away; behold, they have become new\" (2 Cor. 5:17).—1 Pet. 1:3; 2 Cor. 5:17.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣的复活使我们有分于祂得着祂的生命而得着重生就使我们变成新造旧事已过都变成新的了彼前一3林后五17李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The resurrection of the Lord Jesus caused us to partake of Him and receive His life for regeneration In this way we were made the new creation The old things have passed away behold they have become new 2 Cor 5171 Pet 13 2 Cor 517"}
{"zh": "2\t这个新造，不像旧造是神用祂的能力，在祂之外所造的一个单纯的人；这个新造乃是神用祂的生命，在祂自己里面所造的一个与神联合的人—弗四24。（李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册，神计划里的救赎，第七篇）", "en": "2. Unlike the old creation, the new creation is not another man who has been created by God with His power but is apart from Him; the new creation is man in union with God, created by God with His life in Himself (Eph. 4:24).—Eph. 4:24.", "norm_zh": "2这个新造不像旧造是神用祂的能力在祂之外所造的一个单纯的人这个新造乃是神用祂的生命在祂自己里面所造的一个与神联合的人弗四24李常受文集一九五〇至一九五一年第二册神计划里的救赎第七篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Unlike the old creation the new creation is not another man who has been created by God with His power but is apart from Him the new creation is man in union with God created by God with His life in Himself Eph 424Eph 424"}
{"zh": "九\t施行那灵的流；那灵的一道流变成许多道江河；活水的江河作那灵的流，在復活里从我们里面流出来—约七38~39。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "I. Carrying out the flow of the Spirit; the one flow of the Spirit becomes many rivers; the rivers of living water as the flow of the Spirit flow out of us in resurrection.—John 7:38-39.", "norm_zh": "九施行哪灵的流哪灵的一道流变成许多道江河活水的江河作哪灵的流在复活里从我们里面流出来约七3839李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Carrying out the flow of the Spirit the one flow of the Spirit becomes many rivers the rivers of living water as the flow of the Spirit flow out of us in resurrectionJohn 73839"}
{"zh": "十\t成为神在基督升天里行动的基础，为着形成召会，就是基督的身体—徒五30~31，弗一20~23：（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "J. Forming the Base of His Move in the Ascension of Christ for the Formation of the Church, the Body of Christ—Acts 5:30-31; Eph. 1:20-23:", "norm_zh": "十成为神在基督升天里行动的基础为着形成召会就是基督的身体徒五3031弗一2023李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "J Forming the Base of His Move in the Ascension of Christ for the Formation of the Church the Body of ChristActs 53031 Eph 12023"}
{"zh": "1\t若没有復活，基督绝不能升到诸天之上，所以復活为祂的升天立下基础—徒五30~31。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "1. Without resurrection Christ could never ascend to the heavens, so the resurrection laid the base for His ascension.—Acts 5:30-31.", "norm_zh": "1若没有复活基督绝不能升到诸天之上所以复活为祂的升天立下基础徒五3031李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Without resurrection Christ could never ascend to the heavens so the resurrection laid the base for His ascensionActs 53031"}
{"zh": "2\t基督乃是在升天里，将祂在復活里所产生的一切重生的肢体，形成祂那一个生机的身体—弗一20~23。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "2. It was in His ascension that He formed all the regenerated members, produced in His resurrection, into His one organic Body.—Eph. 1:20-23.", "norm_zh": "2基督乃是在升天里将祂在复活里所产生的一切重生的肢体形成祂哪一个生机的身体弗一2023李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 It was in His ascension that He formed all the regenerated members produced in His resurrection into His one organic BodyEph 12023"}
{"zh": "十一\t以基督復活的大能加力给信徒，使信徒在基督徒的行事为人中模成祂的死—腓三10，罗六5。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "K. Empowering the Believers with the Power of Christ's Resurrection for the Conformation to His Death in the Believers' Christian Walk—Phil. 3:10; Rom. 6:5.", "norm_zh": "十一以基督复活的大能加力给信徒使信徒在基督徒的行事为人中模成祂的死腓三10罗六5李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "K Empowering the Believers with the Power of Christs Resurrection for the Conformation to His Death in the Believers Christian WalkPhil 310 Rom 65"}
{"zh": "十二\t施行基督之死的功效和杀死，好在復活里释放出神的生命—林后四10，罗六8。（李常受文集一九九三年第一册，神在人里的行动，第六篇）", "en": "L. Carrying Out the Effectiveness and Killing of the Death of Christ for the Release of the Divine Life in Resurrection—2 Cor. 4:10; Rom. 6:8.", "norm_zh": "十二施行基督之死的功效和杀死好在复活里释放出神的生命林后四10罗六8李常受文集一九九三年第一册神在人里的行动第六篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:34:40.595657+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "L Carrying Out the Effectiveness and Killing of the Death of Christ for the Release of the Divine Life in Resurrection2 Cor 410 Rom 68"}
{"zh": "读经：林前一2，十17，十二12~13，路二四49，约十四17，二十22，徒一5、8，二4、33，四8，六3，十三52，弗一22~23，四4", "en": "Scripture Reading: 1 Cor. 1:2; 10:17; 12:12-13; Luke 24:49; John 14:17; 20:22; Acts 1:5, 8; 2:4, 33; 4:8; 6:3; 13:52; Eph. 1:22-23; 4:4", "norm_zh": "读经林前一2十17十二1213路二四49约十四17二十22徒一58二433四8六3十三52弗一2223四4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 1 Cor 12 1017 121213 Luke 2449 John 1417 2022 Acts 15 8 24 33 48 63 1352 Eph 12223 44"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经启示圣灵的工作有两面：里面为着生命的一面，是素质的灵；外面为着能力和权柄的一面，是经纶的灵─约十四17，二十22，路二四49，徒一5、8，路二四49：", "en": "I.\tThe Scriptures reveal that there are two aspects of the work of the Holy Spirit: the inward aspect for life—the essential Spirit—and the outward aspect for power and authority—the economical Spirit.—John 14:17; 20:22; Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; Luke 24:49:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经启示圣灵的工作有两面里面为着生命的一面是素质的灵外面为着能力和权柄的一面是经纶的灵约十四17二十22路二四49徒一58路二四49", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Scriptures reveal that there are two aspects of the work of the Holy Spirit the inward aspect for lifethe essential Spiritand the outward aspect for power and authoritythe economical SpiritJohn 1417 2022 Luke 2449 Acts 15 8 Luke 2449"}
{"zh": "一\t“素质”指存在、所是、以及为着生存的生命；“经纶”指工作、功用和能力—弗一10，提一4。", "en": "A.\tEssential refers to the existence, to the being, and to the life for existence; economical refers to work, function, and power.—Eph. 1:10; 1 Tim. 1:4.", "norm_zh": "一素质指存在所是以及为着生存的生命经纶指工作功用和能力弗一10提一4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Essential refers to the existence to the being and to the life for existence economical refers to work function and powerEph 110 1 Tim 14"}
{"zh": "二\t原则上，圣灵的这两面在我们身上，如同在主耶稣身上一样；每一位在基督里的信徒，都应当经历圣灵的这两面─路二四49，约十四17，二十22：", "en": "B.\tIn principle, both aspects of the Spirit are the same with us as they were with the Lord Jesus; every believer in Christ should experience both aspects of the Spirit.—Luke 24:49; John 14:17; 20:22:", "norm_zh": "二原则上圣灵的这两面在我们身上如同在主耶稣身上一样每一位在基督里的信徒都应当经历圣灵的这两面路二四49约十四17二十22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In principle both aspects of the Spirit are the same with us as they were with the Lord Jesus every believer in Christ should experience both aspects of the SpiritLuke 2449 John 1417 2022"}
{"zh": "3\t经历那灵作我们的生命，为着我们属灵的所是和存在，乃是素质的；经历那灵作能力，为着我们属灵的工作和功用，乃是经纶的─罗八11，路二四49，徒一5、8，约二十22：", "en": "1.\tTo experience the Spirit as our life for our spiritual being and existence is essential; to experience the Spirit as power for our spiritual work and function is economical.—Rom. 8:11; Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; John 20:22:", "norm_zh": "3经历哪灵作我们的生命为着我们属灵的所是和存在乃是素质的经历哪灵作能力为着我们属灵的工作和功用乃是经纶的罗八11路二四49徒一58约二十22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 To experience the Spirit as our life for our spiritual being and existence is essential to experience the Spirit as power for our spiritual work and function is economicalRom 811 Luke 2449 Acts 15 8 John 2022"}
{"zh": "a\t在复活那天，主将生命的灵吹到门徒里面；这是素质的─22节。", "en": "a.\tOn the day of resurrection, the Lord breathed the Spirit of life into the disciples; this is essential.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "a在复活哪天主将生命的灵吹到门徒里面这是素质的22节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a On the day of resurrection the Lord breathed the Spirit of life into the disciples this is essentialv 22"}
{"zh": "贰\t在圣灵里的浸就是元首将总结为包罗万有复合之灵的三一神，浇灌在祂的身体上─路二四49，徒一5、8，二1~4，十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二13，太三11：", "en": "II.\tThe baptism in the Holy Spirit is the outpouring of the consummated Triune God as the all-inclusive compound Spirit by the Head upon His Body.—Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; 2:1-4; 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:13; Matt. 3:11:", "norm_zh": "贰在圣灵里的浸就是元首将总结为包罗万有复合之灵的三一神浇灌在祂的身体上路二四49徒一58二14十4447十一1517林前十二13太三11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The baptism in the Holy Spirit is the outpouring of the consummated Triune God as the allinclusive compound Spirit by the Head upon His BodyLuke 2449 Acts 15 8 214 104447 111517 1 Cor 1213 Matt 311"}
{"zh": "一\t借着圣灵里的浸，信徒被摆在一起，形成基督的身体，联于祂这头─林前十二13，徒一5。", "en": "A.\tThrough the baptism in the Holy Spirit, the believers were put together to form the Body of Christ, joined to Him as the Head.—1 Cor. 12:13; Acts 1:5.", "norm_zh": "一借着圣灵里的浸信徒被摆在一起形成基督的身体联于祂这头林前十二13徒一5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through the baptism in the Holy Spirit the believers were put together to form the Body of Christ joined to Him as the Head1 Cor 1213 Acts 15"}
{"zh": "二\t在圣灵里的浸真正的意义，乃是我们浸入三一神，并穿上三一神作我们的制服─路二四49，加三27。", "en": "B.\tThe real meaning of the baptism in the Holy Spirit is that we are immersed in the Triune God and that we put on the Triune God as our uniform.—Luke 24:49; Gal. 3:27.", "norm_zh": "二在圣灵里的浸真正的意义乃是我们浸入三一神并穿上三一神作我们的制服路二四49加三27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The real meaning of the baptism in the Holy Spirit is that we are immersed in the Triune God and that we put on the Triune God as our uniformLuke 2449 Gal 327"}
{"zh": "三\t在圣灵里的浸是分两段完成的—徒二1~4，十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二13，约十四17：", "en": "C.\tThe baptism in the Holy Spirit was accomplished in two sections:—Acts 2:1-4; 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:17:", "norm_zh": "三在圣灵里的浸是分两段完成的徒二14十4447十一1517林前十二13约十四17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The baptism in the Holy Spirit was accomplished in two sectionsActs 214 104447 111517 1 Cor 1213 John 1417"}
{"zh": "1\t所有的犹太信徒，都在五旬节那天，在圣灵里受浸─徒二1~4，约十四17，林前十二11。", "en": "1.\tAll the Jewish believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit on the day of Pentecost.—Acts 2:1-4; John 14:17; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "1所有的犹太信徒都在五旬节哪天在圣灵里受浸徒二14约十四17林前十二11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 All the Jewish believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit on the day of PentecostActs 214 John 1417 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "2\t所有的外邦信徒，都在哥尼流家里，在圣灵里受浸─徒十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二11。", "en": "2\tAll the Gentile believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit in the house of Cornelius—Acts 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "2所有的外邦信徒都在哥尼流家里在圣灵里受浸徒十4447十一1517林前十二11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All the Gentile believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit in the house of CorneliusActs 104447 111517 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "四\t在其他三个事例中，元首在基督身体上所已经完成之圣灵里的浸，乃是借着与基督身体的联合为一，传输到祂身体的新肢体上；这三个事例乃是基督身体所已经接受，圣灵里一个浸的三个经历─徒八15~17，九17，十九1~7：", "en": "D.\tIn the other cases the baptism in the Holy Spirit that had already been accomplished upon the Body by the Head was transmitted to the new members of the Body through identification with the Body; these three cases were experiences of the one baptism in the Holy Spirit, which the Body of Christ had already received—Acts 8:15-17; 9:17; 19:1-7:", "norm_zh": "四在其他三个事例中元首在基督身体上所已经完成之圣灵里的浸乃是借着与基督身体的联合为一传输到祂身体的新肢体上这三个事例乃是基督身体所已经接受圣灵里一个浸的三个经历徒八1517九17十九17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D In the other cases the baptism in the Holy Spirit that had already been accomplished upon the Body by the Head was transmitted to the new members of the Body through identification with the Body these three cases were experiences of the one baptism in the Holy Spirit which the Body of Christ had already receivedActs 81517 917 1917"}
{"zh": "1\t在撒玛利亚有好些人相信主耶稣，浸入祂的名里，并接受了圣灵；然而，这些信徒没有得着圣灵在他们身上；当彼得和约翰两位使徒按手在撒玛利亚人身上，圣灵就降在他们身上—12、16下，15、17。", "en": "1. There were a number of people in Samaria who had believed in the Lord Jesus, had been baptized into His name, and had received the Holy Spirit; however, these believers did not have the Holy Spirit upon them; when Peter and John, two of the apostles, laid their hands on the Samaritans, the Holy Spirit came upon them—vv. 12, 16b, 15, 17.", "norm_zh": "1在撒玛利亚有好些人相信主耶稣浸入祂的名里并接受了圣灵然而这些信徒没有得着圣灵在他们身上当彼得和约翰两位使徒按手在撒玛利亚人身上圣灵就降在他们身上1216下1517", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 There were a number of people in Samaria who had believed in the Lord Jesus had been baptized into His name and had received the Holy Spirit however these believers did not have the Holy Spirit upon them when Peter and John two of the apostles laid their hands on the Samaritans the Holy Spirit came upon themvv 12 16b 15 17"}
{"zh": "2\t扫罗在往大马色的路上得救；那时他接受主作他的救主，那灵进到他里面，他就重生了；然而，直到一个名叫亚拿尼亚的门徒来到保罗那里，为他祷告，并按手在他身上，他才在外面被圣灵充溢—九11、17~18。", "en": "2. Saul was saved on the way to Damascus; at that time he received the Lord as his Savior, the Spirit entered into him, and he was regenerated; however, it was not until a disciple by the name of Ananias came to him, prayed for him, and laid hands on him that Paul was outwardly filled with the Holy Spirit—9:11, 17-18.", "norm_zh": "2扫罗在往大马色的路上得救哪时他接受主作他的救主哪灵进到他里面他就重生了然而直到一个名叫亚拿尼亚的门徒来到保罗哪里为他祷告并按手在他身上他才在外面被圣灵充溢九111718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Saul was saved on the way to Damascus at that time he received the Lord as his Savior the Spirit entered into him and he was regenerated however it was not until a disciple by the name of Ananias came to him prayed for him and laid hands on him that Paul was outwardly filled with the Holy Spirit911 1718"}
{"zh": "3\t在以弗所的信徒是真信徒，但只受了约翰的浸；有圣灵在他们里面，但他们没有圣灵在他们身上；因此，当使徒保罗按手在他们身上，圣灵就降在他们身上，他们就在圣灵里受浸，并穿上圣灵—十九2~6。", "en": "3. The believers in Ephesus were genuine believers, but they had only been baptized into John's baptism; they had the Holy Spirit within them, but they did not have the Holy Spirit upon them; therefore, when the apostle Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they were baptized in the Holy Spirit and put on the Holy Spirit—19:2-6.", "norm_zh": "3在以弗所的信徒是真信徒但只受了约翰的浸有圣灵在他们里面但他们没有圣灵在他们身上因此当使徒保罗按手在他们身上圣灵就降在他们身上他们就在圣灵里受浸并穿上圣灵十九26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The believers in Ephesus were genuine believers but they had only been baptized into Johns baptism they had the Holy Spirit within them but they did not have the Holy Spirit upon them therefore when the apostle Paul laid his hands on them the Holy Spirit came upon them and they were baptized in the Holy Spirit and put on the Holy Spirit1926"}
{"zh": "叁\t“因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人，是为奴的或自主的，都已经在一位灵里受浸，成了一个身体，且都得以喝一位灵”─林前十二13，约十四16~17，十五26：", "en": "III. \"For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one Body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether slaves or free, and were all given to drink one Spirit\"—1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:16-17; 15:26:", "norm_zh": "叁因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人是为奴的或自主的都已经在一位灵里受浸成了一个身体且都得以喝一位灵林前十二13约十四1617十五26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one Body whether Jews or Greeks whether slaves or free and were all given to drink one Spirit1 Cor 1213 John 141617 1526"}
{"zh": "一\t在一位灵里，我们众人浸成一个生机的实体，就是基督的身体—林前十二13，约十四16~17，十五26。", "en": "A.\tIn one Spirit we were all baptized into one organic entity, the Body of Christ—1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:16-17; 15:26.", "norm_zh": "一在一位灵里我们众人浸成一个生机的实体就是基督的身体林前十二13约十四1617十五26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In one Spirit we were all baptized into one organic entity the Body of Christ1 Cor 1213 John 141617 1526"}
{"zh": "二\t基督是这身体的生命和构成成分，那灵是基督的实际─十四16~17，十五26，林前十二11。", "en": "B. Christ is the life and constituent of this Body, and the Spirit is the reality of Christ—14:16-17; 15:26; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "二基督是这身体的生命和构成成分哪灵是基督的实际十四1617十五26林前十二11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ is the life and constituent of this Body and the Spirit is the reality of Christ141617 1526 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "三\t在那灵里受浸，乃是进入那灵，消失在祂里面；喝那灵，乃是把那灵接受进来，使我们全人被祂浸透；借这两种手续，我们就与那灵调和，而被构成为基督的一个身体─13、20、27节。", "en": "C. To be baptized in the Spirit is to get into the Spirit and be lost in Him; to drink the Spirit is to take the Spirit in and have our being saturated with Him; by these two procedures we are mingled with the Spirit and are constituted the one Body of Christ—vv. 13, 20, 27.", "norm_zh": "三在哪灵里受浸乃是进入哪灵消失在祂里面喝哪灵乃是把哪灵接受进来使我们全人被祂浸透借这两种手续我们就与哪灵调和而被构成为基督的一个身体132027节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C To be baptized in the Spirit is to get into the Spirit and be lost in Him to drink the Spirit is to take the Spirit in and have our being saturated with Him by these two procedures we are mingled with the Spirit and are constituted the one Body of Christvv 13 20 27"}
{"zh": "肆\t在哥林多神的召会，是基督独一无二之宇宙身体在地方上的彰显─弗一22~23，四4，林前一2，十二27：", "en": "IV. The church of God in Corinth is the local expression of the unique, universal Body of Christ—Eph. 1:22-23; 4:4; 1 Cor. 1:2; 12:27:", "norm_zh": "肆在哥林多神的召会是基督独一无二之宇宙身体在地方上的彰显弗一2223四4林前一2十二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The church of God in Corinth is the local expression of the unique universal Body of ChristEph 12223 44 1 Cor 12 1227"}
{"zh": "一\t众地方召会是基督的一个身体在许多地方的许多彰显─弗二21~22，四16，启一11，林后八1：", "en": "A. The local churches are the many expressions in many localities of the one Body of Christ—Eph. 2:21-22; 4:16; Rev. 1:11; 2 Cor. 8:1:", "norm_zh": "一众地方召会是基督的一个身体在许多地方的许多彰显弗二2122四16启一11林后八1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The local churches are the many expressions in many localities of the one Body of ChristEph 22122 416 Rev 111 2 Cor 81"}
{"zh": "1\t地方召会是基督身体的存在，好尽其功用，乃是基督身体的许多彰显─弗四4，启二1。", "en": "1. The local churches, being the existence of the Body of Christ for its function, are the many expressions of the Body of Christ—Eph. 4:4; Rev. 2:1.", "norm_zh": "1地方召会是基督身体的存在好尽其功用乃是基督身体的许多彰显弗四4启二1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The local churches being the existence of the Body of Christ for its function are the many expressions of the Body of ChristEph 44 Rev 21"}
{"zh": "2\t基督的身体要得着彰显，就必须成为地方召会—西一18、24。", "en": "2. For the Body of Christ to be expressed, it must become the local churches—Col. 1:18, 24.", "norm_zh": "2基督的身体要得着彰显就必须成为地方召会西一1824", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 For the Body of Christ to be expressed it must become the local churchesCol 118 24"}
{"zh": "二\t我们需要过正确的召会生活，作为基督身体地方的彰显，照着神的经纶成为基督地方的见证─一11、20节。", "en": "B. We need to have the proper church life as the local expression of the Body of Christ to be a local testimony of Christ according to God's economy—vv. 11, 20.", "norm_zh": "二我们需要过正确的召会生活作为基督身体地方的彰显照着神的经纶成为基督地方的见证一1120节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We need to have the proper church life as the local expression of the Body of Christ to be a local testimony of Christ according to Gods economyvv 11 20"}
{"zh": "三\t地方召会的建造，不仅是为其本身在地方一面的建造，也是为整个身体在宇宙一面的建造─林前十四3~4，弗四12。", "en": "C. The building up of a local church is not only for its own building up locally but also for the building up of the entire Body universally—1 Cor. 14:3-4; Eph. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "三地方召会的建造不仅是为其本身在地方一面的建造也是为整个身体在宇宙一面的建造林前十四34弗四12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The building up of a local church is not only for its own building up locally but also for the building up of the entire Body universally1 Cor 1434 Eph 412"}
{"zh": "伍\t“因着只有一个饼，我们虽多，还是一个身体，因我们都分受这一个饼”─林前十17，太二六26：", "en": "V.\t\"Seeing that there is one bread, we who are many are one Body, for we all partake of the one bread\"—1 Cor. 10:17; Matt. 26:26:", "norm_zh": "伍因着只有一个饼我们虽多还是一个身体因我们都分受这一个饼林前十17太二六26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Seeing that there is one bread we who are many are one Body for we all partake of the one bread1 Cor 1017 Matt 2626"}
{"zh": "一\t这一个饼，乃是表征基督的一个身体；我们众人是这一个身体，因为我们都分受这一个饼─林前五7~8，十3，约六35、51、56~57，参十五1、5：", "en": "A. This one bread signifies the one Body of Christ; we all are this one Body because we all partake of this one bread—1 Cor. 5:7-8; 10:3; John 6:35, 51, 56-57; cf. 15:1, 5:", "norm_zh": "一这一个饼乃是表征基督的一个身体我们众人是这一个身体因为我们都分受这一个饼林前五78十3约六35515657参十五15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A This one bread signifies the one Body of Christ we all are this one Body because we all partake of this one bread1 Cor 578 103 John 635 51 5657 cf 151 5"}
{"zh": "1\t我们众人所分受的这位基督，把我们构成祂的一个身体—林前十17。", "en": "1\tThe Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body.—1 Cor. 10:17.", "norm_zh": "1我们众人所分受的这位基督把我们构成祂的一个身体林前十17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body1 Cor 1017"}
{"zh": "2\t当我们共同有分于（吃）这象征基督个人身体的饼时，这饼就进到我们里面，使我们成为那表征基督团体身体的一个饼─17节，十二12。", "en": "2. When we jointly partake of (eat) the bread, which symbolizes the individual body of Christ, it comes into us to make us one bread, which signifies the corporate Body of Christ—v. 17; 12:12.", "norm_zh": "2当我们共同有分于吃这象征基督个人身体的饼时这饼就进到我们里面使我们成为哪表征基督团体身体的一个饼17节十二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we jointly partake of eat the bread which symbolizes the individual body of Christ it comes into us to make us one bread which signifies the corporate Body of Christv 17 1212"}
{"zh": "二\t基督是那一粒麦子落在地里死了，又在复活里长出来，产生许多信徒作许多子粒，被破碎、碾磨、调成一个饼，就是基督的身体─约十二24，林前十二12。", "en": "B. Christ is the one grain of wheat who fell into the ground and died and grew up in resurrection to produce many believers as many grains to be broken, ground, and blended together into one bread, which is the Body of Christ—John 12:24; 1 Cor. 12:12.", "norm_zh": "二基督是哪一粒麦子落在地里死了又在复活里长出来产生许多信徒作许多子粒被破碎碾磨调成一个饼就是基督的身体约十二24林前十二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ is the one grain of wheat who fell into the ground and died and grew up in resurrection to produce many believers as many grains to be broken ground and blended together into one bread which is the Body of ChristJohn 1224 1 Cor 1212"}
{"zh": "三\t这一个饼，不仅表征我们有分于基督的生命，也表征基督身体的交通─林前十16~17。", "en": "C.\tThe one bread signifies not only our participation in the life of Christ but also the fellowship of the Body of Christ—1 Cor. 10:16-17.", "norm_zh": "三这一个饼不仅表征我们有分于基督的生命也表征基督身体的交通林前十1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The one bread signifies not only our participation in the life of Christ but also the fellowship of the Body of Christ1 Cor 101617"}
{"zh": "陆\t“就如身体是一个，却有许多肢体，而且身体上一切的肢体虽多，仍是一个身体，基督也是这样”─十二12：", "en": "VI.\t\"Even as the body is one and has many members, yet all the members of the body, being many, are one body, so also is the Christ\"—1 Cor. 12:12:—v. 12:", "norm_zh": "陆就如身体是一个却有许多肢体而且身体上一切的肢体虽多仍是一个身体基督也是这样十二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Even as the body is one and has many members yet all the members of the body being many are one body so also is the Christ1 Cor 1212v 12"}
{"zh": "一\t这启示基督与召会乃是团体的基督，就是身体基督—12节，弗一23。", "en": "A. This reveals that Christ and the church are the corporate Christ, the Body-Christ—v. 12; Eph. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "一这启示基督与召会乃是团体的基督就是身体基督12节弗一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A This reveals that Christ and the church are the corporate Christ the BodyChristv 12 Eph 123"}
{"zh": "二\t基督在祂自己里面是头，基督在我们众人里面是身体─林前十二12，弗一22~23：", "en": "B.\tChrist in Himself is the Head, and Christ in all of us is the Body—1 Cor. 12:12; Eph. 1:22-23:", "norm_zh": "二基督在祂自己里面是头基督在我们众人里面是身体林前十二12弗一2223", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ in Himself is the Head and Christ in all of us is the Body1 Cor 1212 Eph 12223"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣在祂自己里面是头，但是当祂构成到我们众人里面时，祂乃是身体─西一18，二19，三4、10~11、15。", "en": "1\tThe Lord Jesus in Himself is the Head, but when He is constituted into us, He is the Body—Col. 1:18; 2:19; 3:4, 10-11, 15.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣在祂自己里面是头但是当祂构成到我们众人里面时祂乃是身体西一18二19三4101115", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lord Jesus in Himself is the Head but when He is constituted into us He is the BodyCol 118 219 34 1011 15"}
{"zh": "2\t头是个人的，身体是团体的─林前十二12。", "en": "2. The Head is individual, while the Body is corporate—1 Cor. 12:12.", "norm_zh": "2头是个人的身体是团体的林前十二12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Head is individual while the Body is corporate1 Cor 1212"}
{"zh": "3\t基督是头，也是身体，但我们只能是身体，不能是头，因为头是关乎神格的事─西二9~10。", "en": "3. Christ is the Head and also the Body, but we can be only the Body and cannot be the Head, because the Head is a matter of the Godhead—Col. 2:9-10.", "norm_zh": "3基督是头也是身体但我们只能是身体不能是头因为头是关乎神格的事西二910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Christ is the Head and also the Body but we can be only the Body and cannot be the Head because the Head is a matter of the GodheadCol 2910"}
{"zh": "三\t所有基督的信徒，都与祂有生机的联结，并都是用祂的生命和元素所构成的，成为祂的身体这个生机体，以彰显祂─林前六17，约十五1、4~5，西三4、10~11、15。", "en": "C.\tAll the believers in Christ are organically united with Him and constituted with His life and element and have thus become His Body, an organism to express Him—1 Cor. 6:17; John 15:1, 4-5; Col. 3:4, 10-11, 15.", "norm_zh": "三所有基督的信徒都与祂有生机的联结并都是用祂的生命和元素所构成的成为祂的身体这个生机体以彰显祂林前六17约十五145西三4101115", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C All the believers in Christ are organically united with Him and constituted with His life and element and have thus become His Body an organism to express Him1 Cor 617 John 151 45 Col 34 1011 15"}
{"zh": "在五旬节以前，门徒已经得着实际的圣灵并生命的圣灵。他们里面有生命的圣灵，但外面还没有接受能力的圣灵。乃是在五旬节那天，当他们在楼房上一起祷告的时候，能力的圣灵从天上降在他们身上，主耶稣这身体的头将他们浸成了一个身体。在那一天，主是施浸者，那一百二十位是身体的代表。身体的头把身体浸在圣灵里。", "en": "Before Pentecost the disciples had already received the Holy Spirit of reality and the Holy Spirit of life. They had the Holy Spirit of life within, but they had not received the Holy Spirit of power without. It was on the day of Pentecost, as they were praying together in the upper room, that the Holy Spirit of power came down from heaven upon them, and the Lord Jesus as the Head of the Body baptized them as the Body. On that day the Lord was the Baptizer, and the one hundred twenty were the representatives of the Body. The Head baptized the Body in the Holy Spirit.", "norm_zh": "在五旬节以前门徒已经得着实际的圣灵并生命的圣灵他们里面有生命的圣灵但外面还没有接受能力的圣灵乃是在五旬节哪天当他们在楼房上一起祷告的时候能力的圣灵从天上降在他们身上主耶稣这身体的头将他们浸成了一个身体在哪一天主是施浸者哪一百二十位是身体的代表身体的头把身体浸在圣灵里", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Before Pentecost the disciples had already received the Holy Spirit of reality and the Holy Spirit of life They had the Holy Spirit of life within but they had not received the Holy Spirit of power without It was on the day of Pentecost as they were praying together in the upper room that the Holy Spirit of power came down from heaven upon them and the Lord Jesus as the Head of the Body baptized them as the Body On that day the Lord was the Baptizer and the one hundred twenty were the representatives of the Body The Head baptized the Body in the Holy Spirit"}
{"zh": "在十七节保罗有力的说到一个饼和一个身体：“因着只有一个饼，我们虽多，还是一个身体，因我们都分受这一个饼”。这一个饼，乃是象征基督那是一的身体。我们众人是这一个身体，因为我们都分受这一个饼。我们一同分受这一个饼，使我们众人成为一。这指明我们有分于基督，就使我们众人成为祂的一个身体。我们众人所分受的这位基督，把我们构成祂的一个身体。分受（即吃─28~30）这一个饼，使我们与这饼联合为一。这指明我们有分于基督、享受基督，使我们与祂联合为一，与祂成为一。（哥林多前书生命读经，第四十九篇）", "en": "In verse 17 Paul speaks strongly of one bread and one Body: “Seeing that there is one bread, we who are many are one Body; for we all partake of the one bread.” The one bread signifies the one Body of Christ. We all are one Body because we all partake of the one bread. Our joint partaking of the one bread makes us all one. This indicates that our partaking of Christ makes us all His one Body. The very Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body. Partaking of (that is, eating—vv. 28-30) the one bread makes us one with the bread. This indicates that our partaking of Christ, our enjoying of Christ, makes us one with Him.", "norm_zh": "在十七节保罗有力的说到一个饼和一个身体因着只有一个饼我们虽多还是一个身体因我们都分受这一个饼这一个饼乃是象征基督哪是一的身体我们众人是这一个身体因为我们都分受这一个饼我们一同分受这一个饼使我们众人成为一这指明我们有分于基督就使我们众人成为祂的一个身体我们众人所分受的这位基督把我们构成祂的一个身体分受即吃2830这一个饼使我们与这饼联合为一这指明我们有分于基督享受基督使我们与祂联合为一与祂成为一哥林多前书生命读经第四十九篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In verse 17 Paul speaks strongly of one bread and one Body Seeing that there is one bread we who are many are one Body for we all partake of the one bread The one bread signifies the one Body of Christ We all are one Body because we all partake of the one bread Our joint partaking of the one bread makes us all one This indicates that our partaking of Christ makes us all His one Body The very Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body Partaking of that is eatingvv 2830 the one bread makes us one with the bread This indicates that our partaking of Christ our enjoying of Christ makes us one with Him"}
{"zh": "召会是身体", "en": "The church is the Body", "norm_zh": "召会是身体", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:37:29.899291+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The church is the Body"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣经启示圣灵的工作有两面：里面为着生命的一面，是素质的灵；外面为着能力和权柄的一面，是经纶的灵─约十四17，二十22，路二四49，徒一5、8，路二四49：（2008年冬训，第三篇；路加福音生命读经，第八篇，第二十八段**）", "en": "I.\tThe Scriptures reveal that there are two aspects of the work of the Holy Spirit: the inward aspect for life—the essential Spirit—and the outward aspect for power and authority—the economical Spirit.—John 14:17; 20:22; Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; Luke 24:49:", "norm_zh": "壹圣经启示圣灵的工作有两面里面为着生命的一面是素质的灵外面为着能力和权柄的一面是经纶的灵约十四17二十22路二四49徒一58路二四492008年冬训第三篇路加福音生命读经第八篇第二十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The Scriptures reveal that there are two aspects of the work of the Holy Spirit the inward aspect for lifethe essential Spiritand the outward aspect for power and authoritythe economical SpiritJohn 1417 2022 Luke 2449 Acts 15 8 Luke 2449"}
{"zh": "一\t“素质”指存在、所是、以及为着生存的生命；“经纶”指工作、功用和能力—弗一10，提一4。（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第七章，第四十段*）", "en": "A.\tEssential refers to the existence, to the being, and to the life for existence; economical refers to work, function, and power.—Eph. 1:10; 1 Tim. 1:4.", "norm_zh": "一素质指存在所是以及为着生存的生命经纶指工作功用和能力弗一10提一42008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第七章第四十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Essential refers to the existence to the being and to the life for existence economical refers to work function and powerEph 110 1 Tim 14"}
{"zh": "二\t原则上，圣灵的这两面在我们身上，如同在主耶稣身上一样；每一位在基督里的信徒，都应当经历圣灵的这两面─路二四49，约十四17，二十22：（2008年冬训，第三篇；路加福音生命读经，第八篇，第三十段*；使徒行传生命读经，第七篇，第二十七段*）", "en": "B.\tIn principle, both aspects of the Spirit are the same with us as they were with the Lord Jesus; every believer in Christ should experience both aspects of the Spirit.—Luke 24:49; John 14:17; 20:22:", "norm_zh": "二原则上圣灵的这两面在我们身上如同在主耶稣身上一样每一位在基督里的信徒都应当经历圣灵的这两面路二四49约十四17二十222008年冬训第三篇路加福音生命读经第八篇第三十段使徒行传生命读经第七篇第二十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In principle both aspects of the Spirit are the same with us as they were with the Lord Jesus every believer in Christ should experience both aspects of the SpiritLuke 2449 John 1417 2022"}
{"zh": "3\t经历那灵作我们的生命，为着我们属灵的所是和存在，乃是素质的；经历那灵作能力，为着我们属灵的工作和功用，乃是经纶的─罗八11，路二四49，徒一5、8，约二十22：（2012年秋季长老训练，第三篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第七章，第四十段*）", "en": "3.\tTo experience the Spirit as our life for our spiritual being and existence is essential; to experience the Spirit as power for our spiritual work and function is economical.—Rom. 8:11; Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; John 20:22:", "norm_zh": "3经历哪灵作我们的生命为着我们属灵的所是和存在乃是素质的经历哪灵作能力为着我们属灵的工作和功用乃是经纶的罗八11路二四49徒一58约二十222012年秋季长老训练第三篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第七章第四十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 To experience the Spirit as our life for our spiritual being and existence is essential to experience the Spirit as power for our spiritual work and function is economicalRom 811 Luke 2449 Acts 15 8 John 2022"}
{"zh": "a\t在复活那天，主将生命的灵吹到门徒里面；这是素质的─22节。（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第二册，基督徒的生活，第五章，第二十五段*）", "en": "a.\tOn the day of resurrection, the Lord breathed the Spirit of life into the disciples; this is essential.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "a在复活哪天主将生命的灵吹到门徒里面这是素质的22节2008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九九一至一九九二年第二册基督徒的生活第五章第二十五段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "a On the day of resurrection the Lord breathed the Spirit of life into the disciples this is essentialv 22"}
{"zh": "贰\t在圣灵里的浸就是元首将总结为包罗万有复合之灵的三一神，浇灌在祂的身体上─路二四49，徒一5、8，二1~4，十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二13，太三11：（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第八章，第六段**）", "en": "II.\tThe baptism in the Holy Spirit is the outpouring of the consummated Triune God as the all-inclusive compound Spirit by the Head upon His Body.—Luke 24:49; Acts 1:5, 8; 2:1-4; 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:13; Matt. 3:11:", "norm_zh": "贰在圣灵里的浸就是元首将总结为包罗万有复合之灵的三一神浇灌在祂的身体上路二四49徒一58二14十4447十一1517林前十二13太三112008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第八章第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The baptism in the Holy Spirit is the outpouring of the consummated Triune God as the allinclusive compound Spirit by the Head upon His BodyLuke 2449 Acts 15 8 214 104447 111517 1 Cor 1213 Matt 311"}
{"zh": "一\t借着圣灵里的浸，信徒被摆在一起，形成基督的身体，联于祂这头─林前十二13，徒一5。（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第八章，第十七段*）", "en": "A.\tThrough the baptism in the Holy Spirit, the believers were put together to form the Body of Christ, joined to Him as the Head.—1 Cor. 12:13; Acts 1:5.", "norm_zh": "一借着圣灵里的浸信徒被摆在一起形成基督的身体联于祂这头林前十二13徒一52008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第八章第十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through the baptism in the Holy Spirit the believers were put together to form the Body of Christ joined to Him as the Head1 Cor 1213 Acts 15"}
{"zh": "二\t在圣灵里的浸真正的意义，乃是我们浸入三一神，并穿上三一神作我们的制服─路二四49，加三27。（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九六四年第二册，由基督与召会的观点看新约概要，第一部分，第六章，第三十一段*）", "en": "B.\tThe real meaning of the baptism in the Holy Spirit is that we are immersed in the Triune God and that we put on the Triune God as our uniform.—Luke 24:49; Gal. 3:27.", "norm_zh": "二在圣灵里的浸真正的意义乃是我们浸入三一神并穿上三一神作我们的制服路二四49加三272008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九六四年第二册由基督与召会的观点看新约概要第一部分第六章第三十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The real meaning of the baptism in the Holy Spirit is that we are immersed in the Triune God and that we put on the Triune God as our uniformLuke 2449 Gal 327"}
{"zh": "三\t在圣灵里的浸是分两段完成的—徒二1~4，十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二13，约十四17：（2008年冬训，第三篇；圣经恢复本，徒一5注2*）", "en": "C.\tThe baptism in the Holy Spirit was accomplished in two sections:—Acts 2:1-4; 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:17:", "norm_zh": "三在圣灵里的浸是分两段完成的徒二14十4447十一1517林前十二13约十四172008年冬训第三篇圣经恢复本徒一5注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The baptism in the Holy Spirit was accomplished in two sectionsActs 214 104447 111517 1 Cor 1213 John 1417"}
{"zh": "1\t所有的犹太信徒，都在五旬节那天，在圣灵里受浸─徒二1~4，约十四17，林前十二11。（2008年冬训，第三篇；圣经恢复本，徒一5注2*）", "en": "1.\tAll the Jewish believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit on the day of Pentecost.—Acts 2:1-4; John 14:17; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "1所有的犹太信徒都在五旬节哪天在圣灵里受浸徒二14约十四17林前十二112008年冬训第三篇圣经恢复本徒一5注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 All the Jewish believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit on the day of PentecostActs 214 John 1417 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "2\t所有的外邦信徒，都在哥尼流家里，在圣灵里受浸─徒十44~47，十一15~17，林前十二11。（2008年冬训，第三篇；圣经恢复本，徒一5注2*）", "en": "2.\tAll the Gentile believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit in the house of Cornelius—Acts 10:44-47; 11:15-17; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "2所有的外邦信徒都在哥尼流家里在圣灵里受浸徒十4447十一1517林前十二112008年冬训第三篇圣经恢复本徒一5注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All the Gentile believers were baptized in the Holy Spirit in the house of CorneliusActs 104447 111517 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "四\t在其他三个事例中，元首在基督身体上所已经完成之圣灵里的浸，乃是借着与基督身体的联合为一，传输到祂身体的新肢体上；这三个事例乃是基督身体所已经接受，圣灵里一个浸的三个经历─徒八15~17，九17，十九1~7：（2008年冬训，第三篇；李常受文集一九六五年第一册，在圣灵里的浸，在圣灵里的浸，第九段*）", "en": "D.\tIn the other cases the baptism in the Holy Spirit that had already been accomplished upon the Body by the Head was transmitted to the new members of the Body through identification with the Body; these three cases were experiences of the one baptism in the Holy Spirit, which the Body of Christ had already received—Acts 8:15-17; 9:17; 19:1-7:", "norm_zh": "四在其他三个事例中元首在基督身体上所已经完成之圣灵里的浸乃是借着与基督身体的联合为一传输到祂身体的新肢体上这三个事例乃是基督身体所已经接受圣灵里一个浸的三个经历徒八1517九17十九172008年冬训第三篇李常受文集一九六五年第一册在圣灵里的浸在圣灵里的浸第九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D In the other cases the baptism in the Holy Spirit that had already been accomplished upon the Body by the Head was transmitted to the new members of the Body through identification with the Body these three cases were experiences of the one baptism in the Holy Spirit which the Body of Christ had already receivedActs 81517 917 1917"}
{"zh": "1\t在撒玛利亚有好些人相信主耶稣，浸入祂的名里，并接受了圣灵；然而，这些信徒没有得着圣灵在他们身上；当彼得和约翰两位使徒按手在撒玛利亚人身上，圣灵就降在他们身上—12、16下，15、17。（李常受文集一九六三年第一册，为着基督身体的一经历神人调和，第十二章）", "en": "1. There were a number of people in Samaria who had believed in the Lord Jesus, had been baptized into His name, and had received the Holy Spirit; however, these believers did not have the Holy Spirit upon them; when Peter and John, two of the apostles, laid their hands on the Samaritans, the Holy Spirit came upon them—vv. 12, 16b, 15, 17.", "norm_zh": "1在撒玛利亚有好些人相信主耶稣浸入祂的名里并接受了圣灵然而这些信徒没有得着圣灵在他们身上当彼得和约翰两位使徒按手在撒玛利亚人身上圣灵就降在他们身上1216下1517李常受文集一九六三年第一册为着基督身体的一经历神人调和第十二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 There were a number of people in Samaria who had believed in the Lord Jesus had been baptized into His name and had received the Holy Spirit however these believers did not have the Holy Spirit upon them when Peter and John two of the apostles laid their hands on the Samaritans the Holy Spirit came upon themvv 12 16b 15 17"}
{"zh": "2\t扫罗在往大马色的路上得救；那时他接受主作他的救主，那灵进到他里面，他就重生了；然而，直到一个名叫亚拿尼亚的门徒来到保罗那里，为他祷告，并按手在他身上，他才在外面被圣灵充溢—九11、17~18。（李常受文集一九六三年第一册，为着基督身体的一经历神人调和，第十二章）", "en": "2. Saul was saved on the way to Damascus; at that time he received the Lord as his Savior, the Spirit entered into him, and he was regenerated; however, it was not until a disciple by the name of Ananias came to him, prayed for him, and laid hands on him that Paul was outwardly filled with the Holy Spirit—9:11, 17-18.", "norm_zh": "2扫罗在往大马色的路上得救哪时他接受主作他的救主哪灵进到他里面他就重生了然而直到一个名叫亚拿尼亚的门徒来到保罗哪里为他祷告并按手在他身上他才在外面被圣灵充溢九111718李常受文集一九六三年第一册为着基督身体的一经历神人调和第十二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Saul was saved on the way to Damascus at that time he received the Lord as his Savior the Spirit entered into him and he was regenerated however it was not until a disciple by the name of Ananias came to him prayed for him and laid hands on him that Paul was outwardly filled with the Holy Spirit911 1718"}
{"zh": "3\t在以弗所的信徒是真信徒，但只受了约翰的浸；有圣灵在他们里面，但他们没有圣灵在他们身上；因此，当使徒保罗按手在他们身上，圣灵就降在他们身上，他们就在圣灵里受浸，并穿上圣灵—十九2~6。（李常受文集一九六三年第一册，为着基督身体的一经历神人调和，第十二章）", "en": "3. The believers in Ephesus were genuine believers, but had only been baptized into John's baptism; they had the Holy Spirit within them, but they did not have the Holy Spirit upon them; therefore, when the apostle Paul laid his hands on them, the Holy Spirit came upon them, and they were baptized in the Holy Spirit and clothed with the Holy Spirit—19:2-6.", "norm_zh": "3在以弗所的信徒是真信徒但只受了约翰的浸有圣灵在他们里面但他们没有圣灵在他们身上因此当使徒保罗按手在他们身上圣灵就降在他们身上他们就在圣灵里受浸并穿上圣灵十九26李常受文集一九六三年第一册为着基督身体的一经历神人调和第十二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The believers in Ephesus were genuine believers but had only been baptized into Johns baptism they had the Holy Spirit within them but they did not have the Holy Spirit upon them therefore when the apostle Paul laid his hands on them the Holy Spirit came upon them and they were baptized in the Holy Spirit and clothed with the Holy Spirit1926"}
{"zh": "叁\t“因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人，是为奴的或自主的，都已经在一位灵里受浸，成了一个身体，且都得以喝一位灵”─林前十二13，约十四16~17，十五26：（2006年夏训，第五篇）", "en": "III. \"For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one Body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether slaves or free, and were all given to drink one Spirit\"—1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:16-17; 15:26:", "norm_zh": "叁因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人是为奴的或自主的都已经在一位灵里受浸成了一个身体且都得以喝一位灵林前十二13约十四1617十五262006年夏训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one Body whether Jews or Greeks whether slaves or free and were all given to drink one Spirit1 Cor 1213 John 141617 1526"}
{"zh": "一\t在一位灵里，我们众人浸成一个生机的实体，就是基督的身体—林前十二13，约十四16~17，十五26。（1997年冬训，哥林多前后书结晶读经，第四篇；哥林多前书生命读经，第五十八篇，第十一段*）", "en": "A.\tIn one Spirit we were all baptized into one organic entity, the Body of Christ—1 Cor. 12:13; John 14:16-17; 15:26.", "norm_zh": "一在一位灵里我们众人浸成一个生机的实体就是基督的身体林前十二13约十四1617十五261997年冬训哥林多前后书结晶读经第四篇哥林多前书生命读经第五十八篇第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In one Spirit we were all baptized into one organic entity the Body of Christ1 Cor 1213 John 141617 1526"}
{"zh": "二\t基督是这身体的生命和构成成分，那灵是基督的实际─十四16~17，十五26，林前十二11。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九八四年第三册，神新约的经纶，第十二章，第二十八段*）", "en": "B. Christ is the life and constituent of this Body, and the Spirit is the reality of Christ—14:16-17; 15:26; 1 Cor. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "二基督是这身体的生命和构成成分哪灵是基督的实际十四1617十五26林前十二112006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九八四年第三册神新约的经纶第十二章第二十八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ is the life and constituent of this Body and the Spirit is the reality of Christ141617 1526 1 Cor 1211"}
{"zh": "三\t在那灵里受浸，乃是进入那灵，消失在祂里面；喝那灵，乃是把那灵接受进来，使我们全人被祂浸透；借这两种手续，我们就与那灵调和，而被构成为基督的一个身体─13、20、27节。（2006年夏训，第五篇；哥林多前书生命读经，第五十八篇，第十四段**）", "en": "C. To be baptized in the Spirit is to get into the Spirit and be lost in Him; to drink the Spirit is to take the Spirit in and have our being saturated with Him; by these two procedures we are mingled with the Spirit and are constituted the one Body of Christ—vv. 13, 20, 27.", "norm_zh": "三在哪灵里受浸乃是进入哪灵消失在祂里面喝哪灵乃是把哪灵接受进来使我们全人被祂浸透借这两种手续我们就与哪灵调和而被构成为基督的一个身体132027节2006年夏训第五篇哥林多前书生命读经第五十八篇第十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C To be baptized in the Spirit is to get into the Spirit and be lost in Him to drink the Spirit is to take the Spirit in and have our being saturated with Him by these two procedures we are mingled with the Spirit and are constituted the one Body of Christvv 13 20 27"}
{"zh": "肆\t在哥林多神的召会，是基督独一无二之宇宙身体在地方上的彰显─弗一22~23，四4，林前一2，十二27：（2006年夏训，第五篇***）", "en": "IV. The church of God in Corinth is the local expression of the unique, universal Body of Christ—Eph. 1:22-23; 4:4; 1 Cor. 1:2; 12:27:", "norm_zh": "肆在哥林多神的召会是基督独一无二之宇宙身体在地方上的彰显弗一2223四4林前一2十二272006年夏训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The church of God in Corinth is the local expression of the unique universal Body of ChristEph 12223 44 1 Cor 12 1227"}
{"zh": "一\t众地方召会是基督的一个身体在许多地方的许多彰显─弗二21~22，四16，启一11，林后八1：（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第二册，主恢复的简说，主恢复的简说，第一百六十七段）", "en": "A. The local churches are the many expressions in many localities of the one Body of Christ—Eph. 2:21-22; 4:16; Rev. 1:11; 2 Cor. 8:1:", "norm_zh": "一众地方召会是基督的一个身体在许多地方的许多彰显弗二2122四16启一11林后八12006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九九〇年第二册主恢复的简说主恢复的简说第一百六十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The local churches are the many expressions in many localities of the one Body of ChristEph 22122 416 Rev 111 2 Cor 81"}
{"zh": "1\t地方召会是基督身体的存在，好尽其功用，乃是基督身体的许多彰显─弗四4，启二1。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第二册，主恢复的简说，主恢复的简说，第一百六十七段）", "en": "1. The local churches, being the existence of the Body of Christ for its function, are the many expressions of the Body of Christ—Eph. 4:4; Rev. 2:1.", "norm_zh": "1地方召会是基督身体的存在好尽其功用乃是基督身体的许多彰显弗四4启二12006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九九〇年第二册主恢复的简说主恢复的简说第一百六十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The local churches being the existence of the Body of Christ for its function are the many expressions of the Body of ChristEph 44 Rev 21"}
{"zh": "2\t基督的身体要得着彰显，就必须成为地方召会—西一18、24。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第二册，主恢复的简说，主恢复的简说，第一百六十七段*）", "en": "2. For the Body of Christ to be expressed, it must become the local churches—Col. 1:18, 24.", "norm_zh": "2基督的身体要得着彰显就必须成为地方召会西一18242006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九九〇年第二册主恢复的简说主恢复的简说第一百六十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 For the Body of Christ to be expressed it must become the local churchesCol 118 24"}
{"zh": "二\t我们需要过正确的召会生活，作为基督身体地方的彰显，照着神的经纶成为基督地方的见证─一11、20节。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第二册，罗马书中所启示在基督的生命里得救，第四章，第二段*）", "en": "B. We need to have the proper church life as the local expression of the Body of Christ, to be a local testimony of Christ according to God's economy—vv. 11, 20.", "norm_zh": "二我们需要过正确的召会生活作为基督身体地方的彰显照着神的经纶成为基督地方的见证一1120节2006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九九〇年第二册罗马书中所启示在基督的生命里得救第四章第二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We need to have the proper church life as the local expression of the Body of Christ to be a local testimony of Christ according to Gods economyvv 11 20"}
{"zh": "三\t地方召会的建造，不仅是为其本身在地方一面的建造，也是为整个身体在宇宙一面的建造─林前十四3~4，弗四12。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九九〇年第二册，主恢复的简说，主恢复的简说，第一百八十七段*）", "en": "C. The building up of a local church is not only for its own building up locally but also for the building up of the entire Body universally—1 Cor. 14:3-4; Eph. 4:12.", "norm_zh": "三地方召会的建造不仅是为其本身在地方一面的建造也是为整个身体在宇宙一面的建造林前十四34弗四122006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九九〇年第二册主恢复的简说主恢复的简说第一百八十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The building up of a local church is not only for its own building up locally but also for the building up of the entire Body universally1 Cor 1434 Eph 412"}
{"zh": "伍\t“因着只有一个饼，我们虽多，还是一个身体，因我们都分受这一个饼”─林前十17，太二六26：（2001年安那翰春季全时间训练，第十二篇）", "en": "V.\t\"Seeing that there is one bread, we who are many are one Body, for we all partake of the one bread\"—1 Cor. 10:17; Matt. 26:26:", "norm_zh": "伍因着只有一个饼我们虽多还是一个身体因我们都分受这一个饼林前十17太二六262001年安哪翰春季全时间训练第十二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Seeing that there is one bread we who are many are one Body for we all partake of the one bread1 Cor 1017 Matt 2626"}
{"zh": "一\t这一个饼，乃是表征基督的一个身体；我们众人是这一个身体，因为我们都分受这一个饼─林前五7~8，十3，约六35、51、56~57，参十五1、5：（2006年夏训，第五篇；哥林多前书生命读经，第四十九篇，第十一段*）", "en": "A. The one bread signifies the one Body of Christ; we all are one Body because we all partake of the one bread—1 Cor. 5:7-8; 10:3; John 6:35, 51, 56-57; cf. 15:1, 5:", "norm_zh": "一这一个饼乃是表征基督的一个身体我们众人是这一个身体因为我们都分受这一个饼林前五78十3约六35515657参十五152006年夏训第五篇哥林多前书生命读经第四十九篇第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The one bread signifies the one Body of Christ we all are one Body because we all partake of the one bread1 Cor 578 103 John 635 51 5657 cf 151 5"}
{"zh": "1\t我们众人所分受的这位基督，把我们构成祂的一个身体—林前十17。（2006年夏训，第五篇；路加福音生命读经，第五十篇，第六段）", "en": "1.\tThe Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body.—1 Cor. 10:17.", "norm_zh": "1我们众人所分受的这位基督把我们构成祂的一个身体林前十172006年夏训第五篇路加福音生命读经第五十篇第六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Christ of whom we all partake constitutes us His one Body1 Cor 1017"}
{"zh": "2\t当我们共同有分于（吃）这象征基督个人身体的饼时，这饼就进到我们里面，使我们成为那表征基督团体身体的一个饼─17节，十二12。（2006年夏训，第五篇；新约总论，第三百一十一篇，第二十二段*）", "en": "2. When we jointly partake of (eat) the bread, which symbolizes the individual body of Christ, it comes into us to make us one bread, which signifies the corporate Body of Christ—v. 17; 12:12.", "norm_zh": "2当我们共同有分于吃这象征基督个人身体的饼时这饼就进到我们里面使我们成为哪表征基督团体身体的一个饼17节十二122006年夏训第五篇新约总论第三百一十一篇第二十二段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 When we jointly partake of eat the bread which symbolizes the individual body of Christ it comes into us to make us one bread which signifies the corporate Body of Christv 17 1212"}
{"zh": "二\t基督是那一粒麦子落在地里死了，又在复活里长出来，产生许多信徒作许多子粒，被破碎、碾磨、调成一个饼，就是基督的身体─约十二24，林前十二12。（2006年夏训，第五篇；新约总论，第三百一十一篇，第二十三段**）", "en": "B. Christ is the one grain of wheat who fell into the ground and died and grew up in resurrection to produce many believers as the many grains, to be broken, ground, and blended into one bread, which is the Body of Christ—John 12:24; 1 Cor. 12:12.", "norm_zh": "二基督是哪一粒麦子落在地里死了又在复活里长出来产生许多信徒作许多子粒被破碎碾磨调成一个饼就是基督的身体约十二24林前十二122006年夏训第五篇新约总论第三百一十一篇第二十三段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ is the one grain of wheat who fell into the ground and died and grew up in resurrection to produce many believers as the many grains to be broken ground and blended into one bread which is the Body of ChristJohn 1224 1 Cor 1212"}
{"zh": "三\t这一个饼，不仅表征我们有分于基督的生命，也表征基督身体的交通─林前十16~17。（2006年夏训，第五篇；新约总论，第三百一十一篇，第二十四段**）", "en": "C.\tThe one bread signifies not only our participation in the life of Christ but also the fellowship of the Body of Christ—1 Cor. 10:16-17.", "norm_zh": "三这一个饼不仅表征我们有分于基督的生命也表征基督身体的交通林前十16172006年夏训第五篇新约总论第三百一十一篇第二十四段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The one bread signifies not only our participation in the life of Christ but also the fellowship of the Body of Christ1 Cor 101617"}
{"zh": "陆\t“就如身体是一个，却有许多肢体，而且身体上一切的肢体虽多，仍是一个身体，基督也是这样”─十二12：（2006年夏训，第五篇）", "en": "VI.\t\"Even as the body is one and has many members, yet all the members of the body, being many, are one body, so also is the Christ\"—1 Cor. 12:12:—v. 12:", "norm_zh": "陆就如身体是一个却有许多肢体而且身体上一切的肢体虽多仍是一个身体基督也是这样十二122006年夏训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Even as the body is one and has many members yet all the members of the body being many are one body so also is the Christ1 Cor 1212v 12"}
{"zh": "一\t这启示基督与召会乃是团体的基督，就是身体基督—12节，弗一23。（2006年夏训，第五篇***）", "en": "A. This reveals that Christ and the church are the corporate Christ, the Body-Christ—v. 12; Eph. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "一这启示基督与召会乃是团体的基督就是身体基督12节弗一232006年夏训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A This reveals that Christ and the church are the corporate Christ the BodyChristv 12 Eph 123"}
{"zh": "二\t基督在祂自己里面是头，基督在我们众人里面是身体─林前十二12，弗一22~23：（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九七七年第三册，一个身体，一位灵，一个新人，第四章，第八段**）", "en": "B.\tChrist in Himself is the Head, and Christ in all of us is the Body—1 Cor. 12:12; Eph. 1:22-23:", "norm_zh": "二基督在祂自己里面是头基督在我们众人里面是身体林前十二12弗一22232006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九七七年第三册一个身体一位灵一个新人第四章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Christ in Himself is the Head and Christ in all of us is the Body1 Cor 1212 Eph 12223"}
{"zh": "1\t主耶稣在祂自己里面是头，但是当祂构成到我们众人里面时，祂乃是身体─西一18，二19，三4、10~11、15。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九七七年第三册，一个身体，一位灵，一个新人，第四章，第八段*）", "en": "1.\tThe Lord Jesus in Himself is the Head, but when He is constituted into us, He is the Body—Col. 1:18; 2:19; 3:4, 10-11, 15.", "norm_zh": "1主耶稣在祂自己里面是头但是当祂构成到我们众人里面时祂乃是身体西一18二19三41011152006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九七七年第三册一个身体一位灵一个新人第四章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The Lord Jesus in Himself is the Head but when He is constituted into us He is the BodyCol 118 219 34 1011 15"}
{"zh": "2\t头是个人的，身体是团体的─林前十二12。（2006年夏训，第五篇***）", "en": "2. The Head is individual, while the Body is corporate—1 Cor. 12:12.", "norm_zh": "2头是个人的身体是团体的林前十二122006年夏训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The Head is individual while the Body is corporate1 Cor 1212"}
{"zh": "3\t基督是头，也是身体，但我们只能是身体，不能是头，因为头是关乎神格的事─西二9~10。（2006年夏训，第五篇；李常受文集一九七七年第三册，一个身体，一位灵，一个新人，第四章，第八段**）", "en": "3. Christ is the Head and also the Body, but we can be only the Body and cannot be the Head, because the Head is a matter of the Godhead—Col. 2:9-10.", "norm_zh": "3基督是头也是身体但我们只能是身体不能是头因为头是关乎神格的事西二9102006年夏训第五篇李常受文集一九七七年第三册一个身体一位灵一个新人第四章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Christ is the Head and also the Body but we can be only the Body and cannot be the Head because the Head is a matter of the GodheadCol 2910"}
{"zh": "三\t所有基督的信徒，都与祂有生机的联结，并都是用祂的生命和元素所构成的，成为祂的身体这个生机体，以彰显祂─林前六17，约十五1、4~5，西三4、10~11、15。（2006年安那翰秋季全时间训练，第四篇；哥林多前书生命读经，第五十八篇，第十段）", "en": "C.\tAll the believers in Christ are organically united with Him and constituted with His life and element and have thus become His Body, an organism to express Him—1 Cor. 6:17; John 15:1, 4-5; Col. 3:4, 10-11, 15.", "norm_zh": "三所有基督的信徒都与祂有生机的联结并都是用祂的生命和元素所构成的成为祂的身体这个生机体以彰显祂林前六17约十五145西三41011152006年安哪翰秋季全时间训练第四篇哥林多前书生命读经第五十八篇第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:40:24.936711+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C All the believers in Christ are organically united with Him and constituted with His life and element and have thus become His Body an organism to express Him1 Cor 617 John 151 45 Col 34 1011 15"}
{"zh": "读经：徒二1~4，十四22下，弗一23，二19，四24，五23下，启十九7、9，西三10，约三29~30，四24，林前一2", "en": "Scripture Reading: Acts 2:1-4; 14:22b; Eph. 1:23; 2:19; 4:24; 5:23b; Rev. 19:7, 9; Col. 3:10; John 3:29-30; 4:24; 1 Cor. 1:2", "norm_zh": "读经徒二14十四22下弗一23二19四24五23下启十九79西三10约三2930四24林前一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Acts 214 1422b Eph 123 219 424 523b Rev 197 9 Col 310 John 32930 424 1 Cor 12"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣灵（就是终极完成的三一神）的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体；所有的信徒，无论在时间或空间上，都普遍的在那灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体；这一个身体包含许多项目：基督的身体、基督的新妇、宇宙的新人、神的家人、神的殿、召会和国度—徒二1~4，十四22下，弗一23，二19，四24，五23下，启十九7、9，西三10，约四24，林前一2。", "en": "I. The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body; all the believers universally, in space and in time, were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body; this one Body comprises a number of items: the Body of Christ, the bride of Christ, the universal new man, the household of God, the temple of God, the church, and the kingdom—Acts 2:1-4; 14:22b; Eph. 1:23; 2:19; 4:24; 5:23b; Rev. 19:7, 9; Col. 3:10; John 4:24; 1 Cor. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "壹圣灵就是终极完成的三一神的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体所有的信徒无论在时间或空间上都普遍的在哪灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体这一个身体包含许多项目基督的身体基督的新妇宇宙的新人神的家人神的殿召会和国度徒二14十四22下弗一23二19四24五23下启十九79西三10约四24林前一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body all the believers universally in space and in time were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body this one Body comprises a number of items the Body of Christ the bride of Christ the universal new man the household of God the temple of God the church and the kingdomActs 214 1422b Eph 123 219 424 523b Rev 197 9 Col 310 John 424 1 Cor 12"}
{"zh": "贰\t所有信徒都浸成了一个身体，使他们能成为基督的身体，有基督作头—弗一23，五23下：", "en": "II. All the believers were baptized into one Body in order that they might be the Body of Christ having Christ as the Head—Eph. 1:23; 5:23b:", "norm_zh": "贰所有信徒都浸成了一个身体使他们能成为基督的身体有基督作头弗一23五23下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II All the believers were baptized into one Body in order that they might be the Body of Christ having Christ as the HeadEph 123 523b"}
{"zh": "一\t行传二章、十章和十一章里的这些经节，给我们看见一个完整的浸，历世历代所有的犹太信徒和外邦信徒都浸成了一个身体。", "en": "A. These passages in Acts 2 and in Acts 10 and 11 show a complete baptism, with all the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers through all the generations being baptized together into one Body.", "norm_zh": "一行传二章十章和十一章里的这些经节给我们看见一个完整的浸历世历代所有的犹太信徒和外邦信徒都浸成了一个身体", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A These passages in Acts 2 and in Acts 10 and 11 show a complete baptism with all the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers through all the generations being baptized together into one Body"}
{"zh": "二\t在林前十二章十三节，保罗也印证这点：“因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人，是为奴的或自主的，都已经在一位灵里受浸，成了一个身体，且都得以喝一位灵”；这就是圣灵的浇灌，所有的信徒都浸入一个身体里，以形成一个身体。", "en": "B. Paul confirmed this in 1 Corinthians 12:13: \"For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether slaves or free, and were all given to drink one Spirit\"; this is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit, the baptism of all the believers into one Body for the formation of the one Body.", "norm_zh": "二在林前十二章十三节保罗也印证这点因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人是为奴的或自主的都已经在一位灵里受浸成了一个身体且都得以喝一位灵这就是圣灵的浇灌所有的信徒都浸入一个身体里以形成一个身体", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Paul confirmed this in 1 Corinthians 1213 For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body whether Jews or Greeks whether slaves or free and were all given to drink one Spirit this is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit the baptism of all the believers into one Body for the formation of the one Body"}
{"zh": "三\t这身体是基督—那在万有中充满万有者的丰满—弗一23，四13：", "en": "C. The Body is the fullness of Christ, the One who fills all in all—Eph. 1:23; 4:13:", "norm_zh": "三这身体是基督哪在万有中充满万有者的丰满弗一23四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Body is the fullness of Christ the One who fills all in allEph 123 413"}
{"zh": "1\t“那在万有中充满万有者的丰满”一辞，指明基督是宇宙般的大；祂的大没有极限，因为祂在万有中充满了万有—一23。", "en": "1. The phrase \"the fullness of the One who fills all in all\" indicates that Christ is universally great; His greatness has no limit, because He fills all in all—1:23.", "norm_zh": "1哪在万有中充满万有者的丰满一辞指明基督是宇宙般的大祂的大没有极限因为祂在万有中充满了万有一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The phrase the fullness of the One who fills all in all indicates that Christ is universally great His greatness has no limit because He fills all in all123"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若只顾到头而不顾到身体，就不会有丰满—23节。", "en": "2. If we care only for the Head and not for the Body, there will be no fullness—v. 23.", "norm_zh": "2我们若只顾到头而不顾到身体就不会有丰满23节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we care only for the Head and not for the Body there will be no fullnessv 23"}
{"zh": "四\t基督的身体也是基督的长成，基督的富余—二21，西二19：", "en": "D. The Body of Christ is also the full growth, the rich surplus, of Christ—Eph. 2:21; Col. 2:19:", "norm_zh": "四基督的身体也是基督的长成基督的富余二21西二19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Body of Christ is also the full growth the rich surplus of ChristEph 221 Col 219"}
{"zh": "1\t人可能有正常大小的头却有小小的身体，像侏儒一样；这样的身体没有长成—二19。", "en": "1. A person may have a normal-sized head and a small body, like that of a dwarf; such a body does not have the full growth—Col. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "1人可能有正常大小的头却有小小的身体像侏儒一样这样的身体没有长成二19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A person may have a normalsized head and a small body like that of a dwarf such a body does not have the full growthCol 219"}
{"zh": "2\t所以，基督的身体召会，是基督的长成，并基督的富余—19节。", "en": "2. Therefore, the church as the Body of Christ is Christ's full growth and Christ's rich surplus—v. 19.", "norm_zh": "2所以基督的身体召会是基督的长成并基督的富余19节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Therefore the church as the Body of Christ is Christs full growth and Christs rich surplusv 19"}
{"zh": "五\t基督的身体也是基督的延伸、扩展—约十五1上，5节上，弗一22~23：", "en": "E. The Body of Christ is also the extension, the spread, of Christ.—John 15:1a, 5a; Eph. 1:22-23:", "norm_zh": "五基督的身体也是基督的延伸扩展约十五1上5节上弗一2223", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Body of Christ is also the extension the spread of ChristJohn 151a 5a Eph 12223"}
{"zh": "1\t一面，基督就像松树，向天空生长—1节上，5节上。", "en": "1. On one hand, Christ is like a pine tree, shooting toward the sky.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "1一面基督就像松树向天空生长1节上5节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 On one hand Christ is like a pine tree shooting toward the skyvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "2\t另一面，祂还是葡萄树，蔓延布满全地—1节上，5节上。", "en": "2. On the other hand, He is also the vine, spreading to cover the entire earth.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "2另一面祂还是葡萄树蔓延布满全地1节上5节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 On the other hand He is also the vine spreading to cover the entire earthvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "3\t今天基督正在全地上延伸祂自己，作这棵葡萄树，就是基督的身体，召会—1节上，5节上。", "en": "3. Today Christ is extending Himself as the vine, the Body of Christ, the church, all over the earth.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "3今天基督正在全地上延伸祂自己作这棵葡萄树就是基督的身体召会1节上5节上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Today Christ is extending Himself as the vine the Body of Christ the church all over the earthvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "六\t这身体也是基督的延续；基督并没有被了结，反而祂今天是在延续；基督的身体是基督的繁殖、复制和繁增—十二23~24，诗歌第一百五十四首。", "en": "F. The Body is also the continuation of Christ; Christ has not been terminated; rather, He is continuing today; the Body of Christ is the reproduction, duplication, and multiplication of Christ.—John 12:23-24; Hymns, No. 154.", "norm_zh": "六这身体也是基督的延续基督并没有被了结反而祂今天是在延续基督的身体是基督的繁殖复制和繁增十二2324诗歌第一百五十四首", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The Body is also the continuation of Christ Christ has not been terminated rather He is continuing today the Body of Christ is the reproduction duplication and multiplication of ChristJohn 122324 Hymns No 154"}
{"zh": "七\t基督的身体也是基督—三一神具体化身的彰显；基督的身体彰显了那是三一神具体化身的一位—西二19，弗四13。", "en": "G. The Body of Christ is also the expression of Christ, who is the embodiment of the Triune God; the Body of Christ expresses the One who is the embodiment of the Triune God.—Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "七基督的身体也是基督三一神具体化身的彰显基督的身体彰显了哪是三一神具体化身的一位西二19弗四13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G The Body of Christ is also the expression of Christ who is the embodiment of the Triune God the Body of Christ expresses the One who is the embodiment of the Triune GodCol 219 Eph 413"}
{"zh": "叁\t召会也是基督的新妇；新妇是基督的扩增、扩大—启十九7、9，约三29~30：", "en": "III. The church is also the bride of Christ; the bride is the increase, the enlargement, of Christ.—Rev. 19:7, 9; John 3:29-30:", "norm_zh": "叁召会也是基督的新妇新妇是基督的扩增扩大启十九79约三2930", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The church is also the bride of Christ the bride is the increase the enlargement of ChristRev 197 9 John 32930"}
{"zh": "一\t基督的新妇是基督的配偶，由夏娃作亚当的配偶所预表男人是丈夫，女人是那丈夫的配偶；夏娃被建造以后，她与亚当成为一；召会之于基督，也是这样—创二20下，23，弗五31~32：", "en": "A. The bride of Christ is the counterpart of Christ, typified by Eve as the counterpart of Adam—the man is the husband, and the woman is the counterpart of that husband; after Eve was built, she and Adam became one; the same is true of the church in relation to Christ.—Gen. 2:20b, 23; Eph. 5:31-32:", "norm_zh": "一基督的新妇是基督的配偶由夏娃作亚当的配偶所预表男人是丈夫女人是哪丈夫的配偶夏娃被建造以后她与亚当成为一召会之于基督也是这样创二20下23弗五3132", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The bride of Christ is the counterpart of Christ typified by Eve as the counterpart of Adamthe man is the husband and the woman is the counterpart of that husband after Eve was built she and Adam became one the same is true of the church in relation to ChristGen 220b 23 Eph 53132"}
{"zh": "1\t单身的男人是不完整的，因为他只是一对夫妇中的一半；结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇—创二18。", "en": "1. A man who is single is not complete, because he is only half of a couple; marriage makes a man and a woman a couple.—Gen. 2:18.", "norm_zh": "1单身的男人是不完整的因为他只是一对夫妇中的一半结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇创二18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A man who is single is not complete because he is only half of a couple marriage makes a man and a woman a coupleGen 218"}
{"zh": "2\t结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇；在神眼中，人独居不好；因此，神为男人建造一个妻子，使这对夫妇得以完整；头一部分，男人，乃是源头；第二部分，女人，乃是第一部分的扩大—18节。", "en": "2. Marriage makes a man and a woman a couple; in the eyes of God, it is not good for man to live alone; thus, God built a wife for man so that the couple could be complete; the first part, the man, is the source, and the second part, the woman, is the enlargement of the first part.—v. 18.", "norm_zh": "2结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇在神眼中人独居不好因此神为男人建造一个妻子使这对夫妇得以完整头一部分男人乃是源头第二部分女人乃是第一部分的扩大18节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Marriage makes a man and a woman a couple in the eyes of God it is not good for man to live alone thus God built a wife for man so that the couple could be complete the first part the man is the source and the second part the woman is the enlargement of the first partv 18"}
{"zh": "二\t新妇是基督的妻子，这妻子要终极完成于新耶路撒冷；在新耶路撒冷，所有的圣徒，包括旧约和新约的圣徒，成了基督终极完成的妻子—弗五24~25，启二一2、9~10。", "en": "B. The bride is the wife of Christ, and this wife will be consummated in the New Jerusalem; in the New Jerusalem, all the saints, including the Old Testament and the New Testament saints, become the consummated wife of Christ.—Eph. 5:24-25; Rev. 21:2, 9-10.", "norm_zh": "二新妇是基督的妻子这妻子要终极完成于新耶路撒冷在新耶路撒冷所有的圣徒包括旧约和新约的圣徒成了基督终极完成的妻子弗五2425启二一2910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The bride is the wife of Christ and this wife will be consummated in the New Jerusalem in the New Jerusalem all the saints including the Old Testament and the New Testament saints become the consummated wife of ChristEph 52425 Rev 212 910"}
{"zh": "肆\t召会也是宇宙的新人；这新人的头是基督，这新人的身体是召会—西三10，弗四24，五23：", "en": "IV. The church is also the universal new man; the Head of this new man is Christ, and the Body of this new man is the church.—Col. 3:10; Eph. 4:24; 5:23:", "norm_zh": "肆召会也是宇宙的新人这新人的头是基督这新人的身体是召会西三10弗四24五23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The church is also the universal new man the Head of this new man is Christ and the Body of this new man is the churchCol 310 Eph 424 523"}
{"zh": "一\t这新人是借着基督的死，将犹太人和外邦人创造成一个身体而成的；在祂的死与复活里，祂将旧造里的两下了结，使他们在新造里有新生的起头，使他们不仅成为一个身体，更成为一个新人—二14~16，加三28，林前十二13。", "en": "A. The new man is created of the Jews and the Gentiles as one Body through Christ's death; in His death and resurrection, He terminated these two parties in the old creation and germinated them in the new creation, making them not just a body but a new man.—Eph. 2:14-16; Gal. 3:28; 1 Cor. 12:13.", "norm_zh": "一这新人是借着基督的死将犹太人和外邦人创造成一个身体而成的在祂的死与复活里祂将旧造里的两下了结使他们在新造里有新生的起头使他们不仅成为一个身体更成为一个新人二1416加三28林前十二13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new man is created of the Jews and the Gentiles as one Body through Christs death in His death and resurrection He terminated these two parties in the old creation and germinated them in the new creation making them not just a body but a new manEph 21416 Gal 328 1 Cor 1213"}
{"zh": "二\t在基督的身体里有很多肢体，基督乃是所有肢体；祂在你里面，祂在我里面，祂在祂身体的每个肢体里面；整个新人就是基督—20节，西三11。", "en": "B. In the Body of Christ there are many members, and Christ is all the members; He is in you, He is in me, and He is in every member of His Body; the entire new man is Christ.—v. 20; Col. 3:11.", "norm_zh": "二在基督的身体里有很多肢体基督乃是所有肢体祂在你里面祂在我里面祂在祂身体的每个肢体里面整个新人就是基督20节西三11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In the Body of Christ there are many members and Christ is all the members He is in you He is in me and He is in every member of His Body the entire new man is Christv 20 Col 311"}
{"zh": "三\t宇宙的新人乃是借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新，而终极完成的；我们必须借着脱去旧人并穿上新人，日日得更新—弗四22~24，西三9~10，林后四16。", "en": "C. The universal new man is being consummated by being renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man; we must be renewed day by day by putting off the old man and by putting on the new man.—Eph. 4:22-24; Col. 3:9-10; 2 Cor. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "三宇宙的新人乃是借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新而终极完成的我们必须借着脱去旧人并穿上新人日日得更新弗四2224西三910林后四16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The universal new man is being consummated by being renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man we must be renewed day by day by putting off the old man and by putting on the new manEph 42224 Col 3910 2 Cor 416"}
{"zh": "伍\t这身体是神的家人，神的家；神的家人就是神的家；我们是神的家人，神的家—弗二19，提前三15，来三6，彼前四17：", "en": "V. This Body is the household of God, the family of God; the household of God is the family of God; we are the household of God, God's family.—Eph. 2:19; 1 Tim. 3:15; Heb. 3:6; 1 Pet. 4:17:", "norm_zh": "伍这身体是神的家人神的家神的家人就是神的家我们是神的家人神的家弗二19提前三15来三6彼前四17", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V This Body is the household of God the family of God the household of God is the family of God we are the household of God Gods familyEph 219 1 Tim 315 Heb 36 1 Pet 417"}
{"zh": "一\t我们得救以前，我们是人的家庭，由亚当所生；但如今我们是神圣家庭的一分子—弗二19，提前三15。", "en": "A. Before we were saved, we were a human family, born of Adam, but now we are members of the divine family.—Eph. 2:19; 1 Tim. 3:15.", "norm_zh": "一我们得救以前我们是人的家庭由亚当所生但如今我们是神圣家庭的一分子弗二19提前三15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we were saved we were a human family born of Adam but now we are members of the divine familyEph 219 1 Tim 315"}
{"zh": "二\t我们有一位伟大的父，我们都是祂的儿女；祂把祂所有的儿女都看作是祂的家人，祂的亲人；我们这些神的儿女，构成了祂的家—约二十17，弗二19。", "en": "B. We have a great Father, and we are His children; He considers all His children His household, His folks; we, as God's children, constitute His family.—John 20:17; Eph. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "二我们有一位伟大的父我们都是祂的儿女祂把祂所有的儿女都看作是祂的家人祂的亲人我们这些神的儿女构成了祂的家约二十17弗二19", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We have a great Father and we are His children He considers all His children His household His folks we as Gods children constitute His familyJohn 2017 Eph 219"}
{"zh": "陆\t这身体成为神的殿，神这灵在此居住，我们这些祂的子民在此敬拜祂—约四24，林前三17，弗二21~22：", "en": "VI. This Body becomes the temple of God, where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him.—John 4:24; 1 Cor. 3:17; Eph. 2:21-22:", "norm_zh": "陆这身体成为神的殿神这灵在此居住我们这些祂的子民在此敬拜祂约四24林前三17弗二2122", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI This Body becomes the temple of God where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship HimJohn 424 1 Cor 317 Eph 22122"}
{"zh": "一\t在原文，“殿”这字是指内殿，不是指外殿；神的殿乃是神这灵居住的所在，也是我们这些神子民敬拜祂的地方—林前三17，弗二21。", "en": "A. The Greek word for temple refers to the inner temple, not the outer temple; the temple of God is where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him.—1 Cor. 3:17; Eph. 2:21.", "norm_zh": "一在原文殿这字是指内殿不是指外殿神的殿乃是神这灵居住的所在也是我们这些神子民敬拜祂的地方林前三17弗二21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Greek word for temple refers to the inner temple not the outer temple the temple of God is where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him1 Cor 317 Eph 221"}
{"zh": "二\t这殿也就是一个身体，就是召会；地方召会每一个都是神惟一的殿的一个彰显；在这每一个彰显里，我们都联结一起，长成在主里的圣殿—21节，林前三16。", "en": "B. The temple is also the one Body, the church; each one of the local churches is an expression of God's one temple; in each of these expressions, we are being fitted together and are growing into a holy temple in the Lord—v. 21; 1 Cor. 3:16.", "norm_zh": "二这殿也就是一个身体就是召会地方召会每一个都是神惟一的殿的一个彰显在这每一个彰显里我们都联结一起长成在主里的圣殿21节林前三16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The temple is also the one Body the church each one of the local churches is an expression of Gods one temple in each of these expressions we are being fitted together and are growing into a holy temple in the Lordv 21 1 Cor 316"}
{"zh": "三\t无论是宇宙的，或是地方的人这些殿都是神的居所，神居住的地方；居所既是居住的地方，神就能住在祂的殿中，得享安息—弗二22，林前三16~17。", "en": "C. Whether universal or local, all of these temples are God's habitation, God's dwelling place; since a habitation is a dwelling place, God can dwell in His temple and rest there—Eph. 2:22; 1 Cor. 3:16-17.", "norm_zh": "三无论是宇宙的或是地方的人这些殿都是神的居所神居住的地方居所既是居住的地方神就能住在祂的殿中得享安息弗二22林前三1617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Whether universal or local all of these temples are Gods habitation Gods dwelling place since a habitation is a dwelling place God can dwell in His temple and rest thereEph 222 1 Cor 31617"}
{"zh": "柒\t这身体成为召会—蒙召出来的聚集—一2，十32：", "en": "VII. This Body becoming the church—the called-out assembly—1 Cor. 1:2; 10:32:", "norm_zh": "柒这身体成为召会蒙召出来的聚集一2十32", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII This Body becoming the churchthe calledout assembly1 Cor 12 1032"}
{"zh": "一\t新约用ekklesia，艾克利西亚这个希腊字，意即召出来的聚集，表征召会的所是—一2，十32。", "en": "A. The New Testament uses the Greek word ekklesia, meaning a called-out assembly, to signify what the church is—1 Cor. 1:2; 10:32.", "norm_zh": "一新约用ekklesia艾克利西亚这个希腊字意即召出来的聚集表征召会的所是一2十32", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Testament uses the Greek word ekklesia meaning a calledout assembly to signify what the church is1 Cor 12 1032"}
{"zh": "二\t由于召会在全宇宙中是独一的一个，所以召会是宇宙的，包括一切时间之内，在一切地方，在基督里所有的信徒—一22~23，林前一2，十二27。", "en": "B. Since the church is uniquely one in the whole universe, the church is universal, comprising all the believers in Christ in all times and in all places—Eph. 1:22-23; 1 Cor. 1:2; 12:27.", "norm_zh": "二由于召会在全宇宙中是独一的一个所以召会是宇宙的包括一切时间之内在一切地方在基督里所有的信徒一2223林前一2十二27", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since the church is uniquely one in the whole universe the church is universal comprising all the believers in Christ in all times and in all placesEph 12223 1 Cor 12 1227"}
{"zh": "三\t在地上每一地方，都应当只有一个地方召会；地方召会仅由住在当地在基督里的信徒所构成—徒八1，十三1，罗十六1，林前一2，启一4上，11。", "en": "C. In each locality on the earth, there should be only one local church; the local church comprises only those believers in Christ who live in a particular locality—Acts 8:1; 13:1; Rom. 16:1; 1 Cor. 1:2; Rev. 1:4a, 11.", "norm_zh": "三在地上每一地方都应当只有一个地方召会地方召会仅由住在当地在基督里的信徒所构成徒八1十三1罗十六1林前一2启一4上11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In each locality on the earth there should be only one local church the local church comprises only those believers in Christ who live in a particular localityActs 81 131 Rom 161 1 Cor 12 Rev 14a 11"}
{"zh": "捌\t这身体成为神的国和诸天的国—徒十四22下，林前四20，六9~10，十五50，罗十四17，西四11下，太三2，五3、10：", "en": "VIII. This Body becoming the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens—Acts 14:22b; 1 Cor. 4:20; 6:9-10; 15:50; Rom. 14:17; Col. 4:11b; Matt. 3:2; 5:3, 10:", "norm_zh": "捌这身体成为神的国和诸天的国徒十四22下林前四20六910十五50罗十四17西四11下太三2五310", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII This Body becoming the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavensActs 1422b 1 Cor 420 6910 1550 Rom 1417 Col 411b Matt 32 53 10"}
{"zh": "一\t在圣经里，国度有许多方面的讲究；国度的头一面是神的国，第二面是诸天的国；马可福音、路加福音、和约翰福音说到神的国，而马太福音说到诸天的国—可一15，四26，太三2，五3、10。", "en": "A. In the Bible the kingdom has many aspects; the first aspect of the kingdom is the kingdom of God, and the second is the kingdom of the heavens; Mark, Luke, and John refer to the kingdom of God, whereas Matthew refers to the kingdom of the heavens—Mark 1:15; 4:26; Matt. 3:2; 5:3, 10.", "norm_zh": "一在圣经里国度有许多方面的讲究国度的头一面是神的国第二面是诸天的国马可福音路加福音和约翰福音说到神的国而马太福音说到诸天的国可一15四26太三2五310", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the Bible the kingdom has many aspects the first aspect of the kingdom is the kingdom of God and the second is the kingdom of the heavens Mark Luke and John refer to the kingdom of God whereas Matthew refers to the kingdom of the heavensMark 115 426 Matt 32 53 10"}
{"zh": "二\t神的国是神行政管理的范围，这范围正如祂的存在一样，是从永远到永远的——诗九十2，但二44，太二一43：", "en": "B. The kingdom of God is the realm of God's governmental administration, which, like His existence, is from eternity to eternity—Psa. 90:2; Dan. 2:44; Matt. 21:43:", "norm_zh": "二神的国是神行政管理的范围这范围正如祂的存在一样是从永远到永远的诗九十2但二44太二一43", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The kingdom of God is the realm of Gods governmental administration which like His existence is from eternity to eternityPsa 902 Dan 244 Matt 2143"}
{"zh": "1\t神的存在几乎等于祂的国度；神的存在是从永远到永远的；因此，祂的国也是从永远到永远的—诗九十2，但二44。", "en": "1. God's existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom; God's existence is from eternity to eternity; hence, His kingdom also is from eternity to eternity—Psa. 90:2; Dan. 2:44.", "norm_zh": "1神的存在几乎等于祂的国度神的存在是从永远到永远的因此祂的国也是从永远到永远的诗九十2但二44", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom Gods existence is from eternity to eternity hence His kingdom also is from eternity to eternityPsa 902 Dan 244"}
{"zh": "2\t神的国在神新约的经纶里有神圣生命的部分—可一15。", "en": "2. The kingdom of God has a section of the divine life in God's New Testament economy—Mark 1:15.", "norm_zh": "2神的国在神新约的经纶里有神圣生命的部分可一15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The kingdom of God has a section of the divine life in Gods New Testament economyMark 115"}
{"zh": "三\t诸天的国是在神新约的经纶里，包括召会时代和国度时代；是在新约信基督之人里神属天管治的范围—15节，四26，太三2，十三24，参但四26：", "en": "C. The kingdom of the heavens is in the New Testament economy of God and includes the church age and the kingdom age; it is the realm of God's heavenly rule in the New Testament believers in Christ—v. 15; 4:26; Matt. 3:2; 13:24; cf. Dan. 4:26:", "norm_zh": "三诸天的国是在神新约的经纶里包括召会时代和国度时代是在新约信基督之人里神属天管治的范围15节四26太三2十三24参但四26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The kingdom of the heavens is in the New Testament economy of God and includes the church age and the kingdom age it is the realm of Gods heavenly rule in the New Testament believers in Christv 15 426 Matt 32 1324 cf Dan 426"}
{"zh": "1\t诸天的国开始于新约时代里的五旬节那日，并要终结于千年国结束时—太三2。", "en": "1. The kingdom of the heavens began on the day of Pentecost in the New Testament age and will conclude at the close of the millennium.—Matt. 3:2.", "norm_zh": "1诸天的国开始于新约时代里的五旬节哪日并要终结于千年国结束时太三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The kingdom of the heavens began on the day of Pentecost in the New Testament age and will conclude at the close of the millenniumMatt 32"}
{"zh": "2\t我们今天就在诸天的国里，我们甚至就是诸天之国的一部分—2节。", "en": "2. We are in the kingdom of the heavens today, and we are even part of the kingdom of the heavens.—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2我们今天就在诸天的国里我们甚至就是诸天之国的一部分2节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We are in the kingdom of the heavens today and we are even part of the kingdom of the heavensv 2"}
{"zh": "一个身体包含许多项目", "en": "This one Body comprises a number of items", "norm_zh": "一个身体包含许多项目", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "This one Body comprises a number of items"}
{"zh": "圣灵（就是终极完成的三一神）的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体。所有的信徒，无论在时间或空间上，都普遍的在那灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体。这一个身体包含许多项目：基督的身体、基督的新妇、宇宙的新人、神的家人、神的殿、召会和国度。头三个项目—基督的身体、基督的新妇、和宇宙的新人—与基督有关。末四个项目—神的家人、神的殿、召会、和国度—与神有关。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第五篇）", "en": "The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body. All the believers universally, in space and in time, were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body. This one Body comprises a number of items: the Body of Christ, the bride of Christ, the universal new man, the household of God, the temple of God, the church, and the kingdom. The first three items—the Body of Christ, the bride of Christ, and the universal new man—are related to Christ. The last four items—the household of God, the temple of God, the church, and the kingdom—are related to God.", "norm_zh": "圣灵就是终极完成的三一神的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体所有的信徒无论在时间或空间上都普遍的在哪灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体这一个身体包含许多项目基督的身体基督的新妇宇宙的新人神的家人神的殿召会和国度头三个项目基督的身体基督的新妇和宇宙的新人与基督有关末四个项目神的家人神的殿召会和国度与神有关李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body All the believers universally in space and in time were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body This one Body comprises a number of items the Body of Christ the bride of Christ the universal new man the household of God the temple of God the church and the kingdom The first three itemsthe Body of Christ the bride of Christ and the universal new manare related to Christ The last four itemsthe household of God the temple of God the church and the kingdomare related to God"}
{"zh": "祂这三一神把自己浇灌在所有信祂的人身上，这些人包括犹太人、外邦人、古时的信徒、和现今的信徒。我们都在这终极完成的灵里，就是在三一神终极的完成里受浸，并且都浸成一个身体。所有信徒浸成一个宇宙的身体，是浸的团体一面。除了这一面，还有个人的一面，就是团体之浸的应用、实化和有分。（徒十47~48，二38、41，十六33，十九5，太二八19，加三27~28。）", "en": "He, the Triune God, poured Himself out upon all those who believe in Him, who include the Jews, the Gentiles, the believers of old, and the present believers. We were all baptized in this consummated Spirit, that is, in the ultimate consummation of the Triune God, and were all baptized into one Body. The baptizing of all the believers into one Body universally is the corporate aspect of baptism. In addition to this aspect, there is an individual aspect, which is the application and realization of, and participation in, the corporate baptism (Acts 10:47-48; 2:38, 41; 16:33; 19:5; Matt. 28:19; Gal. 3:27-28).", "norm_zh": "祂这三一神把自己浇灌在所有信祂的人身上这些人包括犹太人外邦人古时的信徒和现今的信徒我们都在这终极完成的灵里就是在三一神终极的完成里受浸并且都浸成一个身体所有信徒浸成一个宇宙的身体是浸的团体一面除了这一面还有个人的一面就是团体之浸的应用实化和有分徒十4748二3841十六33十九5太二八19加三2728", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "He the Triune God poured Himself out upon all those who believe in Him who include the Jews the Gentiles the believers of old and the present believers We were all baptized in this consummated Spirit that is in the ultimate consummation of the Triune God and were all baptized into one Body The baptizing of all the believers into one Body universally is the corporate aspect of baptism In addition to this aspect there is an individual aspect which is the application and realization of and participation in the corporate baptism Acts 104748 238 41 1633 195 Matt 2819 Gal 32728"}
{"zh": "借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新", "en": "renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man", "norm_zh": "借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man"}
{"zh": "身体这许多的讲究，其源头乃是圣灵—经过过程之三一神的终极完成—的浇灌。在已过的永远，我们的神是三一的，但还没有经过过程。祂借着成为肉体，开始经过过程。祂借着钉死在十字架上，继续经过过程。祂借着从死亡和阴间里复活，更进一步的经过过程。祂在升天里完成了祂所经过的过程。现今祂是经过过程的三一神。祂这位经过过程的三一神，将自己浇灌下来，作为圣灵，把所有祂拣选的人，就是在基督里的信徒，浸成一个身体。这个身体第一乃是基督的身体，其次是基督的新妇，其次是宇宙的新人，其次是神的家人，或神的家庭，再其次是神的殿，就是神的居所。", "en": "The source of these aspects of the Body is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit, who is the consummation of the processed Triune God. In eternity past, our God was triune, but He was not yet processed. He began to be processed by being incarnated. He continued His process by being crucified on the cross. He was processed further by being resurrected from death and Hades. He completed His process in His ascension. Now He is the processed Triune God. As the processed Triune God, He poured Himself out as the Holy Spirit to baptize all His chosen ones, the believers in Christ, into one Body. This one Body is first the Body of Christ, then the bride of Christ, then the universal new man, then God's household or God's family, and then God's temple, which is God's habitation.", "norm_zh": "身体这许多的讲究其源头乃是圣灵经过过程之三一神的终极完成的浇灌在已过的永远我们的神是三一的但还没有经过过程祂借着成为肉体开始经过过程祂借着钉死在十字架上继续经过过程祂借着从死亡和阴间里复活更进一步的经过过程祂在升天里完成了祂所经过的过程现今祂是经过过程的三一神祂这位经过过程的三一神将自己浇灌下来作为圣灵把所有祂拣选的人就是在基督里的信徒浸成一个身体这个身体第一乃是基督的身体其次是基督的新妇其次是宇宙的新人其次是神的家人或神的家庭再其次是神的殿就是神的居所", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The source of these aspects of the Body is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit who is the consummation of the processed Triune God In eternity past our God was triune but He was not yet processed He began to be processed by being incarnated He continued His process by being crucified on the cross He was processed further by being resurrected from death and Hades He completed His process in His ascension Now He is the processed Triune God As the processed Triune God He poured Himself out as the Holy Spirit to baptize all His chosen ones the believers in Christ into one Body This one Body is first the Body of Christ then the bride of Christ then the universal new man then Gods household or Gods family and then Gods temple which is Gods habitation"}
{"zh": "神的存在几乎等于祂的国度", "en": "God's existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom.", "norm_zh": "神的存在几乎等于祂的国度", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Gods existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom"}
{"zh": "诸天的国", "en": "The kingdom of the heavens", "norm_zh": "诸天的国", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The kingdom of the heavens"}
{"zh": "诸天的国是有关基督身体的最后一项，这身体是五旬节那日由圣灵的浇灌所构成的。圣灵（就是终极完成的三一神）的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体。在新约里，国度含示神的国和诸天的国。这些不是一个，乃是两个东西。它们是国度的两方面。", "en": "The kingdom of the heavens is the last item related to the Body that was constituted by the outpouring of the Spirit on the day of Pentecost. The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body. In the New Testament, the kingdom implies the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens. These are not one but two things. They are two aspects of the kingdom.", "norm_zh": "诸天的国是有关基督身体的最后一项这身体是五旬节哪日由圣灵的浇灌所构成的圣灵就是终极完成的三一神的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体在新约里国度含示神的国和诸天的国这些不是一个乃是两个东西它们是国度的两方面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:44:13.318848+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The kingdom of the heavens is the last item related to the Body that was constituted by the outpouring of the Spirit on the day of Pentecost The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body In the New Testament the kingdom implies the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens These are not one but two things They are two aspects of the kingdom"}
{"zh": "壹\t圣灵（就是终极完成的三一神）的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体；所有的信徒，无论在时间或空间上，都普遍的在那灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体；这一个身体包含许多项目：基督的身体、基督的新妇、宇宙的新人、神的家人、神的殿、召会和国度—徒二1~4，十四22下，弗一23，二19，四24，五23下，启十九7、9，西三10，约四24，林前一2。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第五篇）", "en": "I. The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body; all the believers universally, in space and in time, were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body; this one Body comprises a number of items: the Body of Christ, the bride of Christ, the universal new man, the household of God, the temple of God, the church, and the kingdom—Acts 2:1-4; 14:22b; Eph. 1:23; 2:19; 4:24; 5:23b; Rev. 19:7, 9; Col. 3:10; John 4:24; 1 Cor. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "壹圣灵就是终极完成的三一神的浇灌是为着将所有信徒浸成一个身体所有的信徒无论在时间或空间上都普遍的在哪灵的这个浇灌里浸成了一个身体这一个身体包含许多项目基督的身体基督的新妇宇宙的新人神的家人神的殿召会和国度徒二14十四22下弗一23二19四24五23下启十九79西三10约四24林前一2李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The outpouring of the Holy Spirit as the consummated Triune God was for the baptizing of all the believers into one Body all the believers universally in space and in time were baptized in this outpouring of the Spirit into one Body this one Body comprises a number of items the Body of Christ the bride of Christ the universal new man the household of God the temple of God the church and the kingdomActs 214 1422b Eph 123 219 424 523b Rev 197 9 Col 310 John 424 1 Cor 12"}
{"zh": "贰\t所有信徒都浸成了一个身体，使他们能成为基督的身体，有基督作头—弗一23，五23下：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "II. All the believers were baptized into one Body in order that they might be the Body of Christ having Christ as the Head—Eph. 1:23; 5:23b:", "norm_zh": "贰所有信徒都浸成了一个身体使他们能成为基督的身体有基督作头弗一23五23下李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II All the believers were baptized into one Body in order that they might be the Body of Christ having Christ as the HeadEph 123 523b"}
{"zh": "一\t行传二章、十章和十一章里的这些经节，给我们看见一个完整的浸，历世历代所有的犹太信徒和外邦信徒都浸成了一个身体。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "A. These passages in Acts 2 and in Acts 10 and 11 show a complete baptism, with all the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers through all the generations being baptized together into one Body.", "norm_zh": "一行传二章十章和十一章里的这些经节给我们看见一个完整的浸历世历代所有的犹太信徒和外邦信徒都浸成了一个身体李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A These passages in Acts 2 and in Acts 10 and 11 show a complete baptism with all the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers through all the generations being baptized together into one Body"}
{"zh": "二\t在林前十二章十三节，保罗也印证这点：“因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人，是为奴的或自主的，都已经在一位灵里受浸，成了一个身体，且都得以喝一位灵”；这就是圣灵的浇灌，所有的信徒都浸入一个身体里，以形成一个身体。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "B. Paul confirmed this in 1 Corinthians 12:13: \"For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body, whether Jews or Greeks, whether slaves or free, and were all given to drink one Spirit\"; this is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit, the baptism of all the believers into one Body for the formation of the one Body.", "norm_zh": "二在林前十二章十三节保罗也印证这点因为我们不拘是犹太人或希利尼人是为奴的或自主的都已经在一位灵里受浸成了一个身体且都得以喝一位灵这就是圣灵的浇灌所有的信徒都浸入一个身体里以形成一个身体李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Paul confirmed this in 1 Corinthians 1213 For also in one Spirit we were all baptized into one body whether Jews or Greeks whether slaves or free and were all given to drink one Spirit this is the outpouring of the Holy Spirit the baptism of all the believers into one Body for the formation of the one Body"}
{"zh": "三\t这身体是基督—那在万有中充满万有者的丰满—弗一23，四13：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "C. The Body is the fullness of Christ, the One who fills all in all—Eph. 1:23; 4:13:", "norm_zh": "三这身体是基督哪在万有中充满万有者的丰满弗一23四13李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Body is the fullness of Christ the One who fills all in allEph 123 413"}
{"zh": "1\t“那在万有中充满万有者的丰满”一辞，指明基督是宇宙般的大；祂的大没有极限，因为祂在万有中充满了万有—一23。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "1. The phrase the fullness of the One who fills all in all indicates that Christ is universally great; His greatness has no limit, because He fills all in all—1:23.", "norm_zh": "1哪在万有中充满万有者的丰满一辞指明基督是宇宙般的大祂的大没有极限因为祂在万有中充满了万有一23李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The phrase the fullness of the One who fills all in all indicates that Christ is universally great His greatness has no limit because He fills all in all123"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若只顾到头而不顾到身体，就不会有丰满—23节。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "2. If we care only for the Head and not for the Body, there will be no fullness—v. 23.", "norm_zh": "2我们若只顾到头而不顾到身体就不会有丰满23节李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we care only for the Head and not for the Body there will be no fullnessv 23"}
{"zh": "四\t基督的身体也是基督的长成，基督的富余—弗二21，西二19：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "D. The Body of Christ is also the full growth, the rich surplus, of Christ—Eph. 2:21; Col. 2:19:", "norm_zh": "四基督的身体也是基督的长成基督的富余弗二21西二19李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The Body of Christ is also the full growth the rich surplus of ChristEph 221 Col 219"}
{"zh": "1\t人可能有正常大小的头却有小小的身体，像侏儒一样；这样的身体没有长成—二19。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "1. A person may have a normal-sized head and a small body, like that of a dwarf; such a body does not have the full growth—2:19.", "norm_zh": "1人可能有正常大小的头却有小小的身体像侏儒一样这样的身体没有长成二19李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A person may have a normalsized head and a small body like that of a dwarf such a body does not have the full growth219"}
{"zh": "2\t所以，基督的身体召会，是基督的长成，并基督的富余—19节。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "2. Therefore, the church as the Body of Christ is Christ's full growth and Christ's rich surplus—v. 19.", "norm_zh": "2所以基督的身体召会是基督的长成并基督的富余19节李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Therefore the church as the Body of Christ is Christs full growth and Christs rich surplusv 19"}
{"zh": "五\t基督的身体也是基督的延伸、扩展—约十五1上，5节上，弗一22~23：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "E. The Body of Christ is also the extension, the spread, of Christ.—John 15:1a, 5a; Eph. 1:22-23:", "norm_zh": "五基督的身体也是基督的延伸扩展约十五1上5节上弗一2223李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The Body of Christ is also the extension the spread of ChristJohn 151a 5a Eph 12223"}
{"zh": "1\t一面，基督就像松树，向天空生长—1节上，5节上。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "1. On one hand, Christ is like a pine tree, shooting toward the sky.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "1一面基督就像松树向天空生长1节上5节上李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 On one hand Christ is like a pine tree shooting toward the skyvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "2\t另一面，祂还是葡萄树，蔓延布满全地—1节上，5节上。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "2. On the other hand, He is also the vine, spreading to cover the entire earth.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "2另一面祂还是葡萄树蔓延布满全地1节上5节上李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 On the other hand He is also the vine spreading to cover the entire earthvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "3\t今天基督正在全地上延伸祂自己，作这棵葡萄树，就是基督的身体，召会—1节上，5节上。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "3. Today Christ is extending Himself as the vine, the Body of Christ, the church, all over the earth.—vv. 1a, 5a.", "norm_zh": "3今天基督正在全地上延伸祂自己作这棵葡萄树就是基督的身体召会1节上5节上李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Today Christ is extending Himself as the vine the Body of Christ the church all over the earthvv 1a 5a"}
{"zh": "六\t这身体也是基督的延续；基督并没有被了结，反而祂今天是在延续；基督的身体是基督的繁殖、复制和繁增—约十二23~24。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "F. The Body is also the continuation of Christ; Christ has not been terminated; rather, He is continuing today; the Body of Christ is the reproduction, duplication, and multiplication of Christ.—John 12:23-24.", "norm_zh": "六这身体也是基督的延续基督并没有被了结反而祂今天是在延续基督的身体是基督的繁殖复制和繁增约十二2324李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The Body is also the continuation of Christ Christ has not been terminated rather He is continuing today the Body of Christ is the reproduction duplication and multiplication of ChristJohn 122324"}
{"zh": "七\t基督的身体也是基督—三一神具体化身的彰显；基督的身体彰显了那是三一神具体化身的一位—西二19，弗四13。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "G. The Body of Christ is also the expression of Christ, who is the embodiment of the Triune God; the Body of Christ expresses the One who is the embodiment of the Triune God.—Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:13.", "norm_zh": "七基督的身体也是基督三一神具体化身的彰显基督的身体彰显了哪是三一神具体化身的一位西二19弗四13李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G The Body of Christ is also the expression of Christ who is the embodiment of the Triune God the Body of Christ expresses the One who is the embodiment of the Triune GodCol 219 Eph 413"}
{"zh": "叁\t召会也是基督的新妇；新妇是基督的扩增、扩大—启十九7、9，约三29~30：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "III. The church is also the bride of Christ; the bride is the increase, the enlargement, of Christ.—Rev. 19:7, 9; John 3:29-30:", "norm_zh": "叁召会也是基督的新妇新妇是基督的扩增扩大启十九79约三2930李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The church is also the bride of Christ the bride is the increase the enlargement of ChristRev 197 9 John 32930"}
{"zh": "一\t基督的新妇是基督的配偶，由夏娃作亚当的配偶所预表男人是丈夫，女人是那丈夫的配偶；夏娃被建造以后，她与亚当成为一；召会之于基督，也是这样—创二20下，23，弗五31~32：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "A. The bride of Christ is the counterpart of Christ, typified by Eve as the counterpart of Adam; the man is the husband, and the woman is the counterpart of that husband; after Eve was built, she and Adam became one; the same is true of the church in relation to Christ.—Gen. 2:20b, 23; Eph. 5:31-32:", "norm_zh": "一基督的新妇是基督的配偶由夏娃作亚当的配偶所预表男人是丈夫女人是哪丈夫的配偶夏娃被建造以后她与亚当成为一召会之于基督也是这样创二20下23弗五3132李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The bride of Christ is the counterpart of Christ typified by Eve as the counterpart of Adam the man is the husband and the woman is the counterpart of that husband after Eve was built she and Adam became one the same is true of the church in relation to ChristGen 220b 23 Eph 53132"}
{"zh": "1\t单身的男人是不完整的，因为他只是一对夫妇中的一半；结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇—创二18。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "1. A man who is single is not complete, because he is only half of a couple; marriage makes a man and a woman a couple.—Gen. 2:18.", "norm_zh": "1单身的男人是不完整的因为他只是一对夫妇中的一半结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇创二18李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 A man who is single is not complete because he is only half of a couple marriage makes a man and a woman a coupleGen 218"}
{"zh": "2\t结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇；在神眼中，人独居不好；因此，神为男人建造一个妻子，使这对夫妇得以完整；头一部分，男人，乃是源头；第二部分，女人，乃是第一部分的扩大—18节。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "2. Marriage makes a man and a woman a couple; in the eyes of God, it is not good for man to live alone; thus, God built a wife for man so that the couple could be complete; the first part, the man, is the source, and the second part, the woman, is the enlargement of the first part.—v. 18.", "norm_zh": "2结婚使男人和女人成为一对夫妇在神眼中人独居不好因此神为男人建造一个妻子使这对夫妇得以完整头一部分男人乃是源头第二部分女人乃是第一部分的扩大18节李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Marriage makes a man and a woman a couple in the eyes of God it is not good for man to live alone thus God built a wife for man so that the couple could be complete the first part the man is the source and the second part the woman is the enlargement of the first partv 18"}
{"zh": "二\t新妇是基督的妻子，这妻子要终极完成于新耶路撒冷；在新耶路撒冷，所有的圣徒，包括旧约和新约的圣徒，成了基督终极完成的妻子—弗五24~25，启二一2、9~10。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "II. The bride is the wife of Christ, and this wife will be consummated in the New Jerusalem; in the New Jerusalem, all the saints, including the Old Testament and the New Testament saints, become the consummated wife of Christ.—Eph. 5:24-25; Rev. 21:2, 9-10.", "norm_zh": "二新妇是基督的妻子这妻子要终极完成于新耶路撒冷在新耶路撒冷所有的圣徒包括旧约和新约的圣徒成了基督终极完成的妻子弗五2425启二一2910李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The bride is the wife of Christ and this wife will be consummated in the New Jerusalem in the New Jerusalem all the saints including the Old Testament and the New Testament saints become the consummated wife of ChristEph 52425 Rev 212 910"}
{"zh": "肆\t召会也是宇宙的新人；这新人的头是基督，这新人的身体是召会—西三10，弗四24，五23：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "IV. The church is also the universal new man; the Head of this new man is Christ, and the Body of this new man is the church.—Col. 3:10; Eph. 4:24; 5:23:", "norm_zh": "肆召会也是宇宙的新人这新人的头是基督这新人的身体是召会西三10弗四24五23李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The church is also the universal new man the Head of this new man is Christ and the Body of this new man is the churchCol 310 Eph 424 523"}
{"zh": "一\t这新人是借着基督的死，将犹太人和外邦人创造成一个身体而成的；在祂的死与复活里，祂将旧造里的两下了结，使他们在新造里有新生的起头，使他们不仅成为一个身体，更成为一个新人—二14~16，加三28，林前十二13。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "A. The new man is created of the Jews and the Gentiles as one Body through Christ's death; in His death and resurrection, He terminated these two parties in the old creation and germinated them in the new creation, making them not just a body but a new man.—Eph. 2:14-16; Gal. 3:28; 1 Cor. 12:13.", "norm_zh": "一这新人是借着基督的死将犹太人和外邦人创造成一个身体而成的在祂的死与复活里祂将旧造里的两下了结使他们在新造里有新生的起头使他们不仅成为一个身体更成为一个新人二1416加三28林前十二13李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The new man is created of the Jews and the Gentiles as one Body through Christs death in His death and resurrection He terminated these two parties in the old creation and germinated them in the new creation making them not just a body but a new manEph 21416 Gal 328 1 Cor 1213"}
{"zh": "二\t在基督的身体里有很多肢体，基督乃是所有肢体；祂在你里面，祂在我里面，祂在祂身体的每个肢体里面；整个新人就是基督—20节，西三11。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "B. In the Body of Christ there are many members, and Christ is all the members; He is in you, He is in me, and He is in every member of His Body; the entire new man is Christ.—v. 20; Col. 3:11.", "norm_zh": "二在基督的身体里有很多肢体基督乃是所有肢体祂在你里面祂在我里面祂在祂身体的每个肢体里面整个新人就是基督20节西三11李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In the Body of Christ there are many members and Christ is all the members He is in you He is in me and He is in every member of His Body the entire new man is Christv 20 Col 311"}
{"zh": "三\t宇宙的新人乃是借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新，而终极完成的；我们必须借着脱去旧人并穿上新人，日日得更新—弗四22~24，西三9~10，林后四16。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第二篇）", "en": "C. The universal new man is being consummated by being renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man; we must be renewed day by day by putting off the old man and by putting on the new man.—Eph. 4:22-24; Col. 3:9-10; 2 Cor. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "三宇宙的新人乃是借着脱去旧人并穿上新人得了更新而终极完成的我们必须借着脱去旧人并穿上新人日日得更新弗四2224西三910林后四16李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第二篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The universal new man is being consummated by being renewed through the putting off of the old man and the putting on of the new man we must be renewed day by day by putting off the old man and by putting on the new manEph 42224 Col 3910 2 Cor 416"}
{"zh": "伍\t这身体是神的家人，神的家；神的家人就是神的家；我们是神的家人，神的家—弗二19，提前三15，来三6，彼前四17：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "V. This Body is the household of God, the family of God; the household of God is the family of God; we are the household of God, God's family.—Eph. 2:19; 1 Tim. 3:15; Heb. 3:6; 1 Pet. 4:17:", "norm_zh": "伍这身体是神的家人神的家神的家人就是神的家我们是神的家人神的家弗二19提前三15来三6彼前四17李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V This Body is the household of God the family of God the household of God is the family of God we are the household of God Gods familyEph 219 1 Tim 315 Heb 36 1 Pet 417"}
{"zh": "一\t我们得救以前，我们是人的家庭，由亚当所生；但如今我们是神圣家庭的一分子—弗二19，提前三15。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "A. Before we were saved, we were a human family, born of Adam, but now we are members of the divine family.—Eph. 2:19; 1 Tim. 3:15.", "norm_zh": "一我们得救以前我们是人的家庭由亚当所生但如今我们是神圣家庭的一分子弗二19提前三15李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Before we were saved we were a human family born of Adam but now we are members of the divine familyEph 219 1 Tim 315"}
{"zh": "二\t我们有一位伟大的父，我们都是祂的儿女；祂把祂所有的儿女都看作是祂的家人，祂的亲人；我们这些神的儿女，构成了祂的家—约二十17，弗二19。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "B. We have a great Father, and we are His children; He considers all His children His household, His folks; we, as God's children, constitute His family.—John 20:17; Eph. 2:19.", "norm_zh": "二我们有一位伟大的父我们都是祂的儿女祂把祂所有的儿女都看作是祂的家人祂的亲人我们这些神的儿女构成了祂的家约二十17弗二19李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We have a great Father and we are His children He considers all His children His household His folks we as Gods children constitute His familyJohn 2017 Eph 219"}
{"zh": "陆\t这身体成为神的殿，神这灵在此居住，我们这些祂的子民在此敬拜祂—约四24，林前三17，弗二21~22：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "VI. This Body becomes the temple of God, where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him.—John 4:24; 1 Cor. 3:17; Eph. 2:21-22:", "norm_zh": "陆这身体成为神的殿神这灵在此居住我们这些祂的子民在此敬拜祂约四24林前三17弗二2122李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI This Body becomes the temple of God where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship HimJohn 424 1 Cor 317 Eph 22122"}
{"zh": "一\t在原文，“殿”这字是指内殿，不是指外殿；神的殿乃是神这灵居住的所在，也是我们这些神子民敬拜祂的地方—林前三17，弗二21。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "A. The Greek word for temple refers to the inner temple, not the outer temple; the temple of God is where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him.—1 Cor. 3:17; Eph. 2:21.", "norm_zh": "一在原文殿这字是指内殿不是指外殿神的殿乃是神这灵居住的所在也是我们这些神子民敬拜祂的地方林前三17弗二21李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Greek word for temple refers to the inner temple not the outer temple the temple of God is where God as the Spirit dwells and where we as His people worship Him1 Cor 317 Eph 221"}
{"zh": "二\t这殿也就是一个身体，就是召会；地方召会每一个都是神惟一的殿的一个彰显；在这每一个彰显里，我们都联结一起，长成在主里的圣殿—21节，林前三16。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "B. The temple is also the one Body, the church; each of the local churches is an expression of God's one temple; in each of these expressions, we are being fitted together and are growing into a holy temple in the Lord—v. 21; 1 Cor. 3:16.", "norm_zh": "二这殿也就是一个身体就是召会地方召会每一个都是神惟一的殿的一个彰显在这每一个彰显里我们都联结一起长成在主里的圣殿21节林前三16李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The temple is also the one Body the church each of the local churches is an expression of Gods one temple in each of these expressions we are being fitted together and are growing into a holy temple in the Lordv 21 1 Cor 316"}
{"zh": "二\t无论是宇宙的，或是地方的人这些殿都是神的居所，神居住的地方；居所既是居住的地方，神就能住在祂的殿中，得享安息—弗二22，林前三16~17。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "B. Whether universal or local, all of these temples are God's habitation, God's dwelling place; since a habitation is a dwelling place, God can dwell in His temple and rest there—Eph. 2:22; 1 Cor. 3:16-17.", "norm_zh": "二无论是宇宙的或是地方的人这些殿都是神的居所神居住的地方居所既是居住的地方神就能住在祂的殿中得享安息弗二22林前三1617李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Whether universal or local all of these temples are Gods habitation Gods dwelling place since a habitation is a dwelling place God can dwell in His temple and rest thereEph 222 1 Cor 31617"}
{"zh": "柒\t这身体成为召会—蒙召出来的聚集—一2，十32：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "VII. This Body becomes the church—the called-out assembly—1:2; 10:32:", "norm_zh": "柒这身体成为召会蒙召出来的聚集一2十32李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII This Body becomes the churchthe calledout assembly12 1032"}
{"zh": "一\t新约用ekklesia，艾克利西亚这个希腊字，意即召出来的聚集，表征召会的所是—一2，十32。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "A. The New Testament uses the Greek word ekklesia, meaning a called-out assembly, to signify what the church is—1:2; 10:32.", "norm_zh": "一新约用ekklesia艾克利西亚这个希腊字意即召出来的聚集表征召会的所是一2十32李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The New Testament uses the Greek word ekklesia meaning a calledout assembly to signify what the church is12 1032"}
{"zh": "二\t由于召会在全宇宙中是独一的一个，所以召会是宇宙的，包括一切时间之内，在一切地方，在基督里所有的信徒—一22~23，林前一2，十二27。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "B. Since the church is uniquely one in the whole universe, the church is universal, comprising all the believers in Christ in all times and in all places—Eph. 1:22-23; 1 Cor. 1:2; 12:27.", "norm_zh": "二由于召会在全宇宙中是独一的一个所以召会是宇宙的包括一切时间之内在一切地方在基督里所有的信徒一2223林前一2十二27李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Since the church is uniquely one in the whole universe the church is universal comprising all the believers in Christ in all times and in all placesEph 12223 1 Cor 12 1227"}
{"zh": "三\t在地上每一地方，都应当只有一个地方召会；地方召会仅由住在当地在基督里的信徒所构成—徒八1，十三1，罗十六1，林前一2，启一4上，11。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第三篇）", "en": "C. In each locality on the earth, there should be only one local church; the local church comprises only those believers in Christ who live in a particular locality—Acts 8:1; 13:1; Rom. 16:1; 1 Cor. 1:2; Rev. 1:4a, 11.", "norm_zh": "三在地上每一地方都应当只有一个地方召会地方召会仅由住在当地在基督里的信徒所构成徒八1十三1罗十六1林前一2启一4上11李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第三篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In each locality on the earth there should be only one local church the local church comprises only those believers in Christ who live in a particular localityActs 81 131 Rom 161 1 Cor 12 Rev 14a 11"}
{"zh": "捌\t这身体成为神的国和诸天的国—徒十四22下，林前四20，六9~10，十五50，罗十四17，西四11下，太三2，五3、10：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "VIII. This Body becomes the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens—Acts 14:22b; 1 Cor. 4:20; 6:9-10; 15:50; Rom. 14:17; Col. 4:11b; Matt. 3:2; 5:3, 10:", "norm_zh": "捌这身体成为神的国和诸天的国徒十四22下林前四20六910十五50罗十四17西四11下太三2五310李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII This Body becomes the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavensActs 1422b 1 Cor 420 6910 1550 Rom 1417 Col 411b Matt 32 53 10"}
{"zh": "一\t在圣经里，国度有许多方面的讲究；国度的头一面是神的国，第二面是诸天的国；马可福音、路加福音、和约翰福音说到神的国，而马太福音说到诸天的国—可一15，四26，太三2，五3、10。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "A. In the Bible the kingdom has many aspects; the first aspect of the kingdom is the kingdom of God, and the second is the kingdom of the heavens; Mark, Luke, and John refer to the kingdom of God, whereas Matthew refers to the kingdom of the heavens—Mark 1:15; 4:26; Matt. 3:2; 5:3, 10.", "norm_zh": "一在圣经里国度有许多方面的讲究国度的头一面是神的国第二面是诸天的国马可福音路加福音和约翰福音说到神的国而马太福音说到诸天的国可一15四26太三2五310李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A In the Bible the kingdom has many aspects the first aspect of the kingdom is the kingdom of God and the second is the kingdom of the heavens Mark Luke and John refer to the kingdom of God whereas Matthew refers to the kingdom of the heavensMark 115 426 Matt 32 53 10"}
{"zh": "二\t神的国是神行政管理的范围，这范围正如祂的存在一样，是从永远到永远的——诗九十2，但二44，太二一43：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "B. The kingdom of God is the realm of God's governmental administration, which like His existence, is from eternity to eternity—Psa. 90:2; Dan. 2:44; Matt. 21:43:", "norm_zh": "二神的国是神行政管理的范围这范围正如祂的存在一样是从永远到永远的诗九十2但二44太二一43李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The kingdom of God is the realm of Gods governmental administration which like His existence is from eternity to eternityPsa 902 Dan 244 Matt 2143"}
{"zh": "1\t神的存在几乎等于祂的国度；神的存在是从永远到永远的；因此，祂的国也是从永远到永远的—诗九十2，但二44。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "1. God's existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom; God's existence is from eternity to eternity; hence, His kingdom also is from eternity to eternity—Psa. 90:2; Dan. 2:44.", "norm_zh": "1神的存在几乎等于祂的国度神的存在是从永远到永远的因此祂的国也是从永远到永远的诗九十2但二44李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Gods existence is nearly equivalent to His kingdom Gods existence is from eternity to eternity hence His kingdom also is from eternity to eternityPsa 902 Dan 244"}
{"zh": "2\t神的国在神新约的经纶里有神圣生命的部分—可一15。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "2. The kingdom of God has a section of the divine life in God's New Testament economy—Mark 1:15.", "norm_zh": "2神的国在神新约的经纶里有神圣生命的部分可一15李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The kingdom of God has a section of the divine life in Gods New Testament economyMark 115"}
{"zh": "三\t诸天的国是在神新约的经纶里，包括召会时代和国度时代；是在新约信基督之人里神属天管治的范围—15节，四26，太三2，十三24，参但四26：（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第五篇）", "en": "C. The kingdom of the heavens is in the New Testament economy of God and includes the church age and the kingdom age; it is the realm of God's heavenly rule in the New Testament believers in Christ—v. 15; 4:26; Matt. 3:2; 13:24; cf. Dan. 4:26:", "norm_zh": "三诸天的国是在神新约的经纶里包括召会时代和国度时代是在新约信基督之人里神属天管治的范围15节四26太三2十三24参但四26李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The kingdom of the heavens is in the New Testament economy of God and includes the church age and the kingdom age it is the realm of Gods heavenly rule in the New Testament believers in Christv 15 426 Matt 32 1324 cf Dan 426"}
{"zh": "1\t诸天的国开始于新约时代里的五旬节那日，并要终结于千年国结束时—太三2。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第五篇）", "en": "1. The kingdom of the heavens began on the day of Pentecost in the New Testament age and will conclude at the close of the millennium—Matt. 3:2.", "norm_zh": "1诸天的国开始于新约时代里的五旬节哪日并要终结于千年国结束时太三2李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The kingdom of the heavens began on the day of Pentecost in the New Testament age and will conclude at the close of the millenniumMatt 32"}
{"zh": "2\t我们今天就在诸天的国里，我们甚至就是诸天之国的一部分—2节。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第五篇）", "en": "2. We are in the kingdom of the heavens today, and we are even part of the kingdom of the heavens—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2我们今天就在诸天的国里我们甚至就是诸天之国的一部分2节李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第五篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:47:07.792709+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 We are in the kingdom of the heavens today and we are even part of the kingdom of the heavensv 2"}
{"zh": "读经：可一15，四3、26~29，六20，太五3，六33，路九2、60，十七20~21，约三3、5、15~16，林前六10", "en": "Scripture Reading: Mark 1:15; 4:3, 26-29; 6:20; Matt. 5:3; 6:33; Luke 9:2, 60; 17:20-21; John 3:3, 5, 15-16; 1 Cor. 6:10", "norm_zh": "读经可一15四32629六20太五3六33路九260十七2021约三351516林前六10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Mark 115 43 2629 620 Matt 53 633 Luke 92 60 172021 John 33 5 1516 1 Cor 610"}
{"zh": "壹\t神的国就是神自己─可一15，四26、30，太六33，约三3，林前四20，路九2、60：", "en": "I.\tThe kingdom of God is God Himself—Mark 1:15; 4:26, 30; Matt. 6:33; John 3:3; 1 Cor. 4:20; Luke 9:2, 60:", "norm_zh": "壹神的国就是神自己可一15四2630太六33约三3林前四20路九260", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The kingdom of God is God HimselfMark 115 426 30 Matt 633 John 33 1 Cor 420 Luke 92 60"}
{"zh": "一\t神的国是以神为内容；神自己就是一切，作祂的国的内容─林前四20，十五28，路九2、60。", "en": "A.\tGod's kingdom has God as its content; God Himself is everything as the content of His kingdom—1 Cor. 4:20; 15:28; Luke 9:2, 60.", "norm_zh": "一神的国是以神为内容神自己就是一切作祂的国的内容林前四20十五28路九260", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods kingdom has God as its content God Himself is everything as the content of His kingdom1 Cor 420 1528 Luke 92 60"}
{"zh": "三\t实际上，神在我们身上的掌权不是外在的，乃是神圣生命本能的事─罗八2、4下，5~6节。", "en": "C.\tIn actuality, God's reigning over us is not an outward matter but a matter of the innate ability of the divine life—Rom. 8:2, 4b, 5-6.", "norm_zh": "三实际上神在我们身上的掌权不是外在的乃是神圣生命本能的事罗八24下56节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In actuality Gods reigning over us is not an outward matter but a matter of the innate ability of the divine lifeRom 82 4b 56"}
{"zh": "五\t神的国的性质是神圣的，因为是“神”的国—罗十四17，太五3、20，约三3、5，来十二28。", "en": "E.\tThe nature of the kingdom of God is divine because it is the kingdom of God.—Rom. 14:17; Matt. 5:3, 20; John 3:3, 5; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "五神的国的性质是神圣的因为是神的国罗十四17太五320约三35来十二28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The nature of the kingdom of God is divine because it is the kingdom of GodRom 1417 Matt 53 20 John 33 5 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "六\t主耶稣说，“神的国已经临近了”─可一15，太十二28，路十一20，十七21，二一31，约三3、5：", "en": "F.\tThe Lord Jesus said, \"The kingdom of God has drawn near\"—Mark 1:15; Matt. 12:28; Luke 11:20; 17:21; 21:31; John 3:3, 5:", "norm_zh": "六主耶稣说神的国已经临近了可一15太十二28路十一20十七21二一31约三35", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The Lord Jesus said The kingdom of God has drawn nearMark 115 Matt 1228 Luke 1120 1721 2131 John 33 5"}
{"zh": "一\t神的国乃是神圣生命的范围，让这生命行动、工作、治理、管治，使生命能完成其目的─3、5节。", "en": "A.\tThe kingdom of God is the realm of the divine life for this life to move, to work, to rule, and to govern so that life may accomplish its purpose—vv. 3, 5.", "norm_zh": "一神的国乃是神圣生命的范围让这生命行动工作治理管治使生命能完成其目的35节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The kingdom of God is the realm of the divine life for this life to move to work to rule and to govern so that life may accomplish its purposevv 3 5"}
{"zh": "二\t神的国是由神的生命所构成的生机体，作为生命的范围，让祂得以治理，在其中祂以祂的生命掌权，并在神圣生命里彰显祂自己这神圣的三一—─3、5、15~16节，十五1~8、16、26。", "en": "B.\tThe kingdom of God is an organism constituted with God's life as the realm of life for His ruling, in which He reigns by His life and expresses Himself as the Divine Trinity in the divine life—vv. 3, 5, 15-16; 15:1-8, 16, 26.", "norm_zh": "二神的国是由神的生命所构成的生机体作为生命的范围让祂得以治理在其中祂以祂的生命掌权并在神圣生命里彰显祂自己这神圣的三一351516节十五181626", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The kingdom of God is an organism constituted with Gods life as the realm of life for His ruling in which He reigns by His life and expresses Himself as the Divine Trinity in the divine lifevv 3 5 1516 1518 16 26"}
{"zh": "三\t神的国乃是神在基督里作生命连同其一切活动的总和─十一25，十10下，十四6、10~11。", "en": "C.\tThe kingdom of God is God in Christ being the totality of life with all its activities—11:25; 10:10b; 14:6, 10-11.", "norm_zh": "三神的国乃是神在基督里作生命连同其一切活动的总和十一25十10下十四61011", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The kingdom of God is God in Christ being the totality of life with all its activities1125 1010b 146 1011"}
{"zh": "4\t我们已经生入神的国，现今那在我们灵里神圣的生命认识神的国─3、5~6节，太五3，路十七21。", "en": "D.\tWe have been born into the kingdom of God, and now the divine life in our spirit knows the kingdom of God—vv. 3, 5-6; Matt. 5:3; Luke 17:21.", "norm_zh": "4我们已经生入神的国现今哪在我们灵里神圣的生命认识神的国356节太五3路十七21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D We have been born into the kingdom of God and now the divine life in our spirit knows the kingdom of Godvv 3 56 Matt 53 Luke 1721"}
{"zh": "五\t国度有其实际，这实际就是神圣生命的生活─太五3、8、20，六33，七21，罗十四17，路十七21。", "en": "E.\tThe kingdom has its reality, and this reality is the living of the divine life—Matt. 5:3, 8, 20; 6:33; 7:21; Rom. 14:17; Luke 17:21.", "norm_zh": "五国度有其实际这实际就是神圣生命的生活太五3820六33七21罗十四17路十七21", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E The kingdom has its reality and this reality is the living of the divine lifeMatt 53 8 20 633 721 Rom 1417 Luke 1721"}
{"zh": "叁\t神的国在生命一面乃是主耶稣作生命的种子，撒到祂的信徒里面，并发展成为一个范围，就是神的国，使神在祂神圣的生命里，能在其中掌权─十七20~21，可四3、26：", "en": "III. The kingdom of God in the sense of life is the Lord Jesus as the seed of life sown into His believers and developing into a realm over which God can rule as His kingdom in His divine life—Luke 17:20-21; Mark 4:3, 26:", "norm_zh": "叁神的国在生命一面乃是主耶稣作生命的种子撒到祂的信徒里面并发展成为一个范围就是神的国使神在祂神圣的生命里能在其中掌权十七2021可四326", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The kingdom of God in the sense of life is the Lord Jesus as the seed of life sown into His believers and developing into a realm over which God can rule as His kingdom in His divine lifeLuke 172021 Mark 43 26"}
{"zh": "三\t基督作为神国第一粒的生命种子，将祂自己撒在相信祂的人里面，使祂能在他们里面长大并生活，且从他们里面发展出来，产生许多子粒─太十三3~8、18~23，约十二24，彼前一23。", "en": "C. Christ, as the seed of the kingdom of God, sowed Himself into His believers that He might grow and live in them and be developed from within them to bring forth many grains—Matt. 13:3-8, 18-23; John 12:24; 1 Pet. 1:23.", "norm_zh": "三基督作为神国第一粒的生命种子将祂自己撒在相信祂的人里面使祂能在他们里面长大并生活且从他们里面发展出来产生许多子粒太十三381823约十二24彼前一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Christ as the seed of the kingdom of God sowed Himself into His believers that He might grow and live in them and be developed from within them to bring forth many grainsMatt 1338 1823 John 1224 1 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "六\t国度乃是基督自己作生命的种子，撒在我们里面，在我们里面生长，在我们里面扩展，并在我们里面成熟，直到有了完满的收割─国度的实现─太十三43上，3~8、18~23节，启十四15。", "en": "F. The kingdom is Christ Himself as the seed of life sown into us, growing in us, spreading in us, and maturing in us until there is a full harvest—the manifestation of the kingdom—Matt. 13:43a, 3-8, 18-23; Rev. 14:15.", "norm_zh": "六国度乃是基督自己作生命的种子撒在我们里面在我们里面生长在我们里面扩展并在我们里面成熟直到有了完满的收割国度的实现太十三43上381823节启十四15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The kingdom is Christ Himself as the seed of life sown into us growing in us spreading in us and maturing in us until there is a full harvestthe manifestation of the kingdomMatt 1343a 38 1823 Rev 1415"}
{"zh": "一\t承受神的国不仅仅是进入国度，乃是得着国度为赏赐，作我们的享受─太二五14、21，十九29，约壹一2。", "en": "A. To inherit the kingdom of God is not simply to enter the kingdom; it is to receive the kingdom as a reward for our enjoyment—Matt. 25:14, 21; 19:29; 1 John 1:2.", "norm_zh": "一承受神的国不仅仅是进入国度乃是得着国度为赏赐作我们的享受太二五1421十九29约壹一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A To inherit the kingdom of God is not simply to enter the kingdom it is to receive the kingdom as a reward for our enjoymentMatt 2514 21 1929 1 John 12"}
{"zh": "二\t承受神的国就是承受永远的生命，作我们的享受─可四26~27，约壹一2，二25，五11~13。", "en": "B. To inherit the kingdom of God is to inherit eternal life as our enjoyment—Mark 4:26-27; 1 John 1:2; 2:25; 5:11-13.", "norm_zh": "二承受神的国就是承受永远的生命作我们的享受可四2627约壹一2二25五1113", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B To inherit the kingdom of God is to inherit eternal life as our enjoymentMark 42627 1 John 12 225 51113"}
{"zh": "四\t承受神的国与借着重生进入神的国不同─林前六10下，约三5，一12~13，三5、15，加五21下，弗五5下：", "en": "D. Inheriting the kingdom of God is different from entering the kingdom of God through regeneration—1 Cor. 6:10b; John 3:5; 1:12-13; 3:5, 15; Gal. 5:21b; Eph. 5:5b:", "norm_zh": "四承受神的国与借着重生进入神的国不同林前六10下约三5一1213三515加五21下弗五5下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Inheriting the kingdom of God is different from entering the kingdom of God through regeneration1 Cor 610b John 35 11213 35 15 Gal 521b Eph 55b"}
{"zh": "1\t当我们相信主耶稣，我们就蒙重生，得着永远的生命，并且进入国度—约一12~13，三5、15。", "en": "1. When we believed in the Lord Jesus, we were regenerated, received eternal life, and entered the kingdom—John 1:12-13; 3:5, 15.", "norm_zh": "1当我们相信主耶稣我们就蒙重生得着永远的生命并且进入国度约一1213三515", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we believed in the Lord Jesus we were regenerated received eternal life and entered the kingdomJohn 11213 35 15"}
{"zh": "伍\t我们需要凭永远的生命活在神的国里，在今世经历并享受永远的生命，使我们在来世可以承受神的国，也就是承受对神永远生命完满的享受，作我们的赏赐─约三5，罗八2、6、10~11，十四17，林前六10下：", "en": "V. We need to live in the kingdom of God by the eternal life, experiencing and enjoying the eternal life in this age, so that we may inherit the kingdom of God in the coming age, that is, inherit the full enjoyment of God's eternal life as our reward—John 3:5; Rom. 8:2, 6, 10-11; 14:17; 1 Cor. 6:10b:", "norm_zh": "伍我们需要凭永远的生命活在神的国里在今世经历并享受永远的生命使我们在来世可以承受神的国也就是承受对神永远生命完满的享受作我们的赏赐约三5罗八261011十四17林前六10下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V We need to live in the kingdom of God by the eternal life experiencing and enjoying the eternal life in this age so that we may inherit the kingdom of God in the coming age that is inherit the full enjoyment of Gods eternal life as our rewardJohn 35 Rom 82 6 1011 1417 1 Cor 610b"}
{"zh": "一\t接受永远的生命而进入神的国，以及照着永远的生命活着而承受神的国，两者都是生命的事─约三3、15，太十九29。", "en": "A. To receive eternal life and enter the kingdom of God and to live according to eternal life and inherit the kingdom of God are both a matter of life—John 3:3, 15; Matt. 19:29.", "norm_zh": "一接受永远的生命而进入神的国以及照着永远的生命活着而承受神的国两者都是生命的事约三315太十九29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A To receive eternal life and enter the kingdom of God and to live according to eternal life and inherit the kingdom of God are both a matter of lifeJohn 33 15 Matt 1929"}
{"zh": "二\t我们应当殷勤追求让我们里面的神圣生命长大并发展，直到我们得着丰富充足的供应，以进入“我们主和救主耶稣基督永远的国”—彼后一5~11，罗八2、6、10，林前六10，太十九29。", "en": "B. We should be diligent to pursue the growth and development of the divine life within us until we are richly and bountifully supplied the entrance into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ—2 Pet. 1:5-11; Rom. 8:2, 6, 10; 1 Cor. 6:10; Matt. 19:29.", "norm_zh": "二我们应当殷勤追求让我们里面的神圣生命长大并发展直到我们得着丰富充足的供应以进入我们主和救主耶稣基督永远的国彼后一511罗八2610林前六10太十九29", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We should be diligent to pursue the growth and development of the divine life within us until we are richly and bountifully supplied the entrance into the eternal kingdom of our Lord and Savior Jesus Christ2 Pet 1511 Rom 82 6 10 1 Cor 610 Matt 1929"}
{"zh": "在新约里，国度是一件复杂的事。譬如，新约有些部分指明，即使在使徒时代，神的国还是将来要来临的，（徒十四22下，林前六9~10，十五50）而新约别的部分却指明神的国现今已经存在。（罗十四17，林前四20，西四11下）因此，我们不容易认识圣经中有关国度的真理。按照新约的教训，我们必须将神的国和诸天的国分类为两件不同的事。在本篇信息里，我们要说到神的国。（李常受文集一九九〇年第一册，使徒的教训，第四篇）", "en": "In the New Testament the kingdom is a complicated matter. For example, certain portions of the New Testament indicate that even at the time of the apostles the kingdom of God was something that would come in the future (Acts 14:22b; 1 Cor. 6:9-10; 15:50); whereas other portions of the New Testament indicate that it is present now (Rom. 14:17; 1 Cor. 4:20; Col. 4:11b). Thus, it is not easy to know the truth concerning the kingdom in the Bible. According to the New Testament teaching, we must classify the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens as two different, particular matters. In this message we shall cover the kingdom of God.", "norm_zh": "在新约里国度是一件复杂的事譬如新约有些部分指明即使在使徒时代神的国还是将来要来临的徒十四22下林前六910十五50而新约别的部分却指明神的国现今已经存在罗十四17林前四20西四11下因此我们不容易认识圣经中有关国度的真理按照新约的教训我们必须将神的国和诸天的国分类为两件不同的事在本篇信息里我们要说到神的国李常受文集一九九〇年第一册使徒的教训第四篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the New Testament the kingdom is a complicated matter For example certain portions of the New Testament indicate that even at the time of the apostles the kingdom of God was something that would come in the future Acts 1422b 1 Cor 6910 1550 whereas other portions of the New Testament indicate that it is present now Rom 1417 1 Cor 420 Col 411b Thus it is not easy to know the truth concerning the kingdom in the Bible According to the New Testament teaching we must classify the kingdom of God and the kingdom of the heavens as two different particular matters In this message we shall cover the kingdom of God"}
{"zh": "神的国就是神自己", "en": "The Kingdom of God Being God Himself", "norm_zh": "神的国就是神自己", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Kingdom of God Being God Himself"}
{"zh": "人需要重生，也是为着进神的国。因为人若不重生，就不能见神的国，就不能进神的国。神的国是属灵的，看见神这属灵的国，就等于进神的国。重生乃是人这样进神的国惟一的入门。神的国乃是神之所是的范围，犹如植物国度是植物之所是的范围，动物国度是动物之所是的范围。没有植物，就没有植物国度；没有动物，就没有动物国度。人之所是和神之所是，根本是不同的，是在两个不同的范围，两个不同的国里。要进入人的国，就必须从人生，有人的生命；照样，要进入神的国，就必须从神生，有神的生命。所以人必须从神生，就是重生，好得着神的生命，能进入神的国。（生命课程，第四十二课）", "en": "Man also needs to be regenerated in order to enter into the kingdom of God. Unless a man is regenerated, he cannot see the kingdom of God, nor can he enter into it. The kingdom of God is spiritual, and to see this spiritual kingdom of God is to enter into it. Regeneration is the unique entrance through which man enters into God's kingdom. The kingdom of God is the realm of what God is, just as the plant kingdom is the realm of what plants are, and the animal kingdom is the realm of what animals are. Without plants there is no plant kingdom, and without animals there is no animal kingdom. What man is and what God is are basically different, being in two different realms and in two different kingdoms. In order to enter into the human kingdom, one must be born of man to have the human life; likewise, in order to enter into God's kingdom, one must be born of God to have God's life. Therefore, man must be born of God, that is, he must be regenerated that he may have God's life and may enter into the kingdom of God. (Life Lessons, Lesson Forty-two)", "norm_zh": "人需要重生也是为着进神的国因为人若不重生就不能见神的国就不能进神的国神的国是属灵的看见神这属灵的国就等于进神的国重生乃是人这样进神的国惟一的入门神的国乃是神之所是的范围犹如植物国度是植物之所是的范围动物国度是动物之所是的范围没有植物就没有植物国度没有动物就没有动物国度人之所是和神之所是根本是不同的是在两个不同的范围两个不同的国里要进入人的国就必须从人生有人的生命照样要进入神的国就必须从神生有神的生命所以人必须从神生就是重生好得着神的生命能进入神的国生命课程第四十二课", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Man also needs to be regenerated in order to enter into the kingdom of God Unless a man is regenerated he cannot see the kingdom of God nor can he enter into it The kingdom of God is spiritual and to see this spiritual kingdom of God is to enter into it Regeneration is the unique entrance through which man enters into Gods kingdom The kingdom of God is the realm of what God is just as the plant kingdom is the realm of what plants are and the animal kingdom is the realm of what animals are Without plants there is no plant kingdom and without animals there is no animal kingdom What man is and what God is are basically different being in two different realms and in two different kingdoms In order to enter into the human kingdom one must be born of man to have the human life likewise in order to enter into Gods kingdom one must be born of God to have Gods life Therefore man must be born of God that is he must be regenerated that he may have Gods life and may enter into the kingdom of God Life Lessons Lesson Fortytwo"}
{"zh": "神圣的领域或范围", "en": "The divine realm or sphere", "norm_zh": "神圣的领域或范围", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:48:44.168570+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The divine realm or sphere"}
