{"zh": "壹\t诸天的国是诸天的掌权；是神国里特殊的部分，是神在生命上特别的掌权；根据马太福音，诸天的国有实际、外表和实现三面—但四26，太三2，十六18~19。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "I. The kingdom of the heavens is the ruling of the heavens; it is a special section of the kingdom of God, God's reigning in a particular way, in the sense of life; according to the Gospel of Matthew, there are three aspects of the kingdom of the heavens: the reality, the outward appearance, and the manifestation.—Dan. 4:26; Matt. 3:2; 16:18-19.", "norm_zh": "壹诸天的国是诸天的掌权是神国里特殊的部分是神在生命上特别的掌权根据马太福音诸天的国有实际外表和实现三面但四26太三2十六1819李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The kingdom of the heavens is the ruling of the heavens it is a special section of the kingdom of God Gods reigning in a particular way in the sense of life according to the Gospel of Matthew there are three aspects of the kingdom of the heavens the reality the outward appearance and the manifestationDan 426 Matt 32 161819"}
{"zh": "贰\t诸天之国的实际，乃是诸天之国属天和属灵性质上的内容，如在五至七章所启示的：（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "II. The reality of the kingdom of the heavens is the inward content of the kingdom of the heavens in its heavenly and spiritual nature, as revealed in chapters 5 through 7:", "norm_zh": "贰诸天之国的实际乃是诸天之国属天和属灵性质上的内容如在五至七章所启示的李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II The reality of the kingdom of the heavens is the inward content of the kingdom of the heavens in its heavenly and spiritual nature as revealed in chapters 5 through 7"}
{"zh": "一\t马太五至七章的记载，给我们看见一种实际，就是神圣生命高标准的实际，这乃是得胜的召会生活。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "A. The record of Matthew 5—7 gives us a view of a certain kind of reality, the reality of the high standard of the divine life; this is the overcoming church life.", "norm_zh": "一马太五至七章的记载给我们看见一种实际就是神圣生命高标准的实际这乃是得胜的召会生活李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The record of Matthew 57 gives us a view of a certain kind of reality the reality of the high standard of the divine life this is the overcoming church life"}
{"zh": "二\t今天的基督教里，没有多少诸天之国的实际；诸天之国的实际，今天在召会时代存于召会里面—太十三24~43。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "B. There is not much of the reality of the kingdom of the heavens in today's Christianity; the reality of the kingdom of the heavens exists today within the church in the church age.—Matt. 13:24-43.", "norm_zh": "二今天的基督教里没有多少诸天之国的实际诸天之国的实际今天在召会时代存于召会里面太十三2443李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There is not much of the reality of the kingdom of the heavens in todays Christianity the reality of the kingdom of the heavens exists today within the church in the church ageMatt 132443"}
{"zh": "三\t诸天之国的实际对寻求的信徒是操练—五4~10：（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "C.\tThe reality of the kingdom of the heavens is an exercise to the seeking believers—5:4-10:", "norm_zh": "三诸天之国的实际对寻求的信徒是操练五410李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The reality of the kingdom of the heavens is an exercise to the seeking believers5410"}
{"zh": "1\t我们人的这部分，必须是贫穷的、倒空的、卸去旧有的，这样我们才能领悟并得着诸天的国—3节。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "1. We need to be poor, emptied, unloaded, in this part of our being so that we may realize and possess the kingdom of the heavens.—v. 3.", "norm_zh": "1我们人的这部分必须是贫穷的倒空的卸去旧有的这样我们才能领悟并得着诸天的国3节李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We need to be poor emptied unloaded in this part of our being so that we may realize and possess the kingdom of the heavensv 3"}
{"zh": "2\t世界的每一面都是不义的；我们若是义的，就会遭受定罪、反对并逼迫；我们若出代价寻求义，诸天的国就成为我们的—约壹五19，太五6、10。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "2. Every aspect of the world is unrighteous; if we are righteous, we shall be condemned, opposed, and persecuted; if we pay a price to seek righteousness, the kingdom of the heavens becomes ours.—1 John 5:19; Matt. 5:6, 10.", "norm_zh": "2世界的每一面都是不义的我们若是义的就会遭受定罪反对并逼迫我们若出代价寻求义诸天的国就成为我们的约壹五19太五610李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Every aspect of the world is unrighteous if we are righteous we shall be condemned opposed and persecuted if we pay a price to seek righteousness the kingdom of the heavens becomes ours1 John 519 Matt 56 10"}
{"zh": "3\t“你们的义，若不超过经学家和法利赛人的义，绝不能进诸天的国”；进诸天的国，要求我们重生之后，在生活中有超凡的义，意即今天活在诸天之国的实际里，将来有分于诸天之国的实现—20节，林前一30，罗三26。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "3. \"Unless your righteousness surpasses that of the scribes and Pharisees, you shall by no means enter into the kingdom of the heavens\"; to enter into the kingdom of the heavens demands surpassing righteousness in our living after regeneration, which means to live in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens today and to participate in its manifestation in the future.—v. 20; 1 Cor. 1:30; Rom. 3:26.", "norm_zh": "3你们的义若不超过经学家和法利赛人的义绝不能进诸天的国进诸天的国要求我们重生之后在生活中有超凡的义意即今天活在诸天之国的实际里将来有分于诸天之国的实现20节林前一30罗三26李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 Unless your righteousness surpasses that of the scribes and Pharisees you shall by no means enter into the kingdom of the heavens to enter into the kingdom of the heavens demands surpassing righteousness in our living after regeneration which means to live in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens today and to participate in its manifestation in the futurev 20 1 Cor 130 Rom 326"}
{"zh": "4\t我们要进诸天的国，需要呼求主，并实行天父的旨意；进神的国是借着神圣生命的出生，进诸天的国是借着神圣生命的生活—约三3、5，太七21，罗十13。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "4. To enter into the kingdom of the heavens, we need to call on the Lord and do the will of the heavenly Father; entrance into the kingdom of God is through the birth of the divine life, and entrance into the kingdom of the heavens is through the living of the divine life.—John 3:3, 5; Matt. 7:21; Rom. 10:13.", "norm_zh": "4我们要进诸天的国需要呼求主并实行天父的旨意进神的国是借着神圣生命的出生进诸天的国是借着神圣生命的生活约三35太七21罗十13李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "4 To enter into the kingdom of the heavens we need to call on the Lord and do the will of the heavenly Father entrance into the kingdom of God is through the birth of the divine life and entrance into the kingdom of the heavens is through the living of the divine lifeJohn 33 5 Matt 721 Rom 1013"}
{"zh": "叁\t诸天之国的外表，乃是诸天之国名义上的外状，如在马太十三章二十四至四十三节，借着稗子、芥菜种和面酵的比喻所启示的：（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "III. The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens is the outward condition of the kingdom of the heavens in name, as revealed in Matthew 13:24-43 through the parables of the tares, the mustard seed, and the leaven:", "norm_zh": "叁诸天之国的外表乃是诸天之国名义上的外状如在马太十三章二十四至四十三节借着稗子芥菜种和面酵的比喻所启示的李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens is the outward condition of the kingdom of the heavens in name as revealed in Matthew 132443 through the parables of the tares the mustard seed and the leaven"}
{"zh": "一\t诸天之国的外表，就是今日的基督教国，包括罗马天主教和一切假基督徒—十三24~43：（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "A. The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens is today's Christendom, which includes the Roman Catholic Church and all the false Christians.—13:24-43:", "norm_zh": "一诸天之国的外表就是今日的基督教国包括罗马天主教和一切假基督徒十三2443李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens is todays Christendom which includes the Roman Catholic Church and all the false Christians132443"}
{"zh": "1\t稗子的比喻启示国度的建立及其假冒的成分；国度之子构成了国度；恶者之子形成了国度的外表，就是今天所谓的基督教国—24~30、36~43节。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "1. The parable of the tares reveals the establishment of the kingdom and its false constituents; whereas the sons of the kingdom constitute the kingdom, the sons of the evil one have formed the outward appearance of the kingdom, which today is called Christendom.—vv. 24-30, 36-43.", "norm_zh": "1稗子的比喻启示国度的建立及其假冒的成分国度之子构成了国度恶者之子形成了国度的外表就是今天所谓的基督教国24303643节李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The parable of the tares reveals the establishment of the kingdom and its false constituents whereas the sons of the kingdom constitute the kingdom the sons of the evil one have formed the outward appearance of the kingdom which today is called Christendomvv 2430 3643"}
{"zh": "2\t芥菜种的比喻说到国度外表的畸形发展；召会是国度的具体表现，该像菜蔬一样生产食物，却成了树，作飞鸟的宿处，其性质和功用都变了；这形成了诸天之国外表的外在组织—十三31~32。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "2. The parable of the mustard seed speaks of the abnormal growth of the outward appearance of the kingdom; the church, which is the embodiment of the kingdom, should be like an herb to produce food, but it became a tree, a lodge for birds, having its nature and function changed; this has formed the outward organization of the outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens.—13:31-32.", "norm_zh": "2芥菜种的比喻说到国度外表的畸形发展召会是国度的具体表现该像菜蔬一样生产食物却成了树作飞鸟的宿处其性质和功用都变了这形成了诸天之国外表的外在组织十三3132李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The parable of the mustard seed speaks of the abnormal growth of the outward appearance of the kingdom the church which is the embodiment of the kingdom should be like an herb to produce food but it became a tree a lodge for birds having its nature and function changed this has formed the outward organization of the outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens133132"}
{"zh": "3\t面酵藏在细面里的比喻说到国度外表的内在腐败；酵藏在三斗面里，象征天主教暗中使一切关于基督的教训都发了酵；这就成为诸天之国外表的腐败内容—33节，十六6、11~12，，林前五6、8，利二1，创十八6，林前五7~8。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "3. The parable of the leaven hidden in the fine flour speaks of the inward corruption of the outward appearance of the kingdom; the leaven hidden in three measures of meal signifies that the Catholic Church has leavened in a hidden way all the teachings concerning Christ; this became the corrupted content of the outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens.—v. 33; 16:6, 11-12; 1 Cor. 5:6, 8; Lev. 2:1; Gen. 18:6; 1 Cor. 5:7-8.", "norm_zh": "3面酵藏在细面里的比喻说到国度外表的内在腐败酵藏在三斗面里象征天主教暗中使一切关于基督的教训都发了酵这就成为诸天之国外表的腐败内容33节十六61112林前五68利二1创十八6林前五78李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The parable of the leaven hidden in the fine flour speaks of the inward corruption of the outward appearance of the kingdom the leaven hidden in three measures of meal signifies that the Catholic Church has leavened in a hidden way all the teachings concerning Christ this became the corrupted content of the outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavensv 33 166 1112 1 Cor 56 8 Lev 21 Gen 186 1 Cor 578"}
{"zh": "二\t诸天之国的外表，在召会时代与召会一同存在；原则上，我们不允许稗子在召会生活里，我们也不允许大树及其畸形发展，或面酵及其腐败在召会里—太十三24~30、36~43。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "B. The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens exists along with the church in the church age; as a principle, we do not allow tares in the church life, and we do not allow the big tree with its abnormal growth or the leaven with its corruption to be in the church.—Matt. 13:24-30, 36-43.", "norm_zh": "二诸天之国的外表在召会时代与召会一同存在原则上我们不允许稗子在召会生活里我们也不允许大树及其畸形发展或面酵及其腐败在召会里太十三24303643李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The outward appearance of the kingdom of the heavens exists along with the church in the church age as a principle we do not allow tares in the church life and we do not allow the big tree with its abnormal growth or the leaven with its corruption to be in the churchMatt 132430 3643"}
{"zh": "肆\t诸天的国乃是主耶稣的属天管治，属天行政—二五31、34：（2000年冬训，第一篇；李常受文集一九七二年第二册，国度，第四十八章，第三十六段）", "en": "IV.\tThe kingdom of the heavens is the heavenly ruling, the heavenly government, of the Lord Jesus—25:31, 34:", "norm_zh": "肆诸天的国乃是主耶稣的属天管治属天行政二五31342000年冬训第一篇李常受文集一九七二年第二册国度第四十八章第三十六段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV The kingdom of the heavens is the heavenly ruling the heavenly government of the Lord Jesus2531 34"}
{"zh": "一\t马太福音里的基督乃是君王救主，在我们里面建立诸天的国管治我们—五3，四17。（2000年冬训，第一篇；马太福音生命读经，第五篇，第四十七段*）", "en": "A.\tThe Christ in Matthew is the King-Savior who sets up the kingdom of the heavens over us and within us—5:3; 4:17.", "norm_zh": "一马太福音里的基督乃是君王救主在我们里面建立诸天的国管治我们五3四172000年冬训第一篇马太福音生命读经第五篇第四十七段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The Christ in Matthew is the KingSavior who sets up the kingdom of the heavens over us and within us53 417"}
{"zh": "1\t祂进入我们的灵，国度就与祂一同进来—22节。（2000年冬训，第一篇；马太福音生命读经，第十四篇，第十段*）", "en": "1\tWhen He came into our spirit, the kingdom arrived with Him.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "1祂进入我们的灵国度就与祂一同进来22节2000年冬训第一篇马太福音生命读经第十四篇第十段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When He came into our spirit the kingdom arrived with Himv 22"}
{"zh": "2\t如今在我们灵里，我们有王带着国度；因此，说主与我们的灵同在，意思就是国度与我们的灵同在—22节。（2000年冬训，第一篇；马太福音生命读经，第十四篇，第十段*；第十一段*）", "en": "2\tNow in our spirit we have the King with the kingdom; thus, to say that the Lord is with our spirit means that the kingdom is with our spirit.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "2如今在我们灵里我们有王带着国度因此说主与我们的灵同在意思就是国度与我们的灵同在22节2000年冬训第一篇马太福音生命读经第十四篇第十段第十一段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Now in our spirit we have the King with the kingdom thus to say that the Lord is with our spirit means that the kingdom is with our spiritv 22"}
{"zh": "三\t神重生我们的目的，是要把我们带到祂属天的管治之下—约三3、5：（2000年冬训，第一篇；李常受文集一九七二年第二册，国度，第四十八章，第八段*）", "en": "C.\tGod's intention in regenerating us is to bring us under His heavenly rule—John 3:3, 5:", "norm_zh": "三神重生我们的目的是要把我们带到祂属天的管治之下约三352000年冬训第一篇李常受文集一九七二年第二册国度第四十八章第八段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Gods intention in regenerating us is to bring us under His heavenly ruleJohn 33 5"}
{"zh": "1\t我们已经生在君尊、属天的家庭里，我们必须有属天的操练，并受属天管治的支配—太五48。（2000年冬训，第一篇；李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第四章，第十九段*）", "en": "1\tWe have been born into a royal, heavenly family, and we must be exercised in a heavenly way and be governed by a heavenly rule.—Matt. 5:48.", "norm_zh": "1我们已经生在君尊属天的家庭里我们必须有属天的操练并受属天管治的支配太五482000年冬训第一篇李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第四章第十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We have been born into a royal heavenly family and we must be exercised in a heavenly way and be governed by a heavenly ruleMatt 548"}
{"zh": "2\t我们若在这管治之下，我们就是得胜的，我们就在诸天之国的实际里，我们也进入诸天之国的实现里，与主一同管治并掌权—二五21、23，启二十4、6。（2000年冬训，第一篇；李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第三章，第二十九段*）", "en": "2\tIf we are under this ruling, we will be victorious and overcoming, we will be in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens, and we will enter into the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens to rule and reign with the Lord.—25:21, 23; Rev. 20:4, 6.", "norm_zh": "2我们若在这管治之下我们就是得胜的我们就在诸天之国的实际里我们也进入诸天之国的实现里与主一同管治并掌权二五2123启二十462000年冬训第一篇李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第三章第二十九段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 If we are under this ruling we will be victorious and overcoming we will be in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens and we will enter into the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens to rule and reign with the Lord2521 23 Rev 204 6"}
{"zh": "伍\t诸天之国的实现，乃是诸天之国在大能里实际地来临，如在马太二十四章四十四节至二十五章三十节所启示的：（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "V. The manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens is the practical coming of the kingdom of the heavens in power, as revealed in Matthew 24:44—25:30:", "norm_zh": "伍诸天之国的实现乃是诸天之国在大能里实际地来临如在马太二十四章四十四节至二十五章三十节所启示的李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V The manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens is the practical coming of the kingdom of the heavens in power as revealed in Matthew 24442530"}
{"zh": "一\t在现今的时代，国度的实际与国度的外表同时进展；然而，主耶稣回来时，国度的实际要转为国度的实现，国度的外表要被烧尽—十三40~42。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "A. During the present age, the reality of the kingdom and the appearance of the kingdom progress simultaneously; however, when the Lord Jesus comes back, the reality of the kingdom will be transferred into the manifestation of the kingdom, and the appearance of the kingdom will be burned away.—13:40-42.", "norm_zh": "一在现今的时代国度的实际与国度的外表同时进展然而主耶稣回来时国度的实际要转为国度的实现国度的外表要被烧尽十三4042李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A During the present age the reality of the kingdom and the appearance of the kingdom progress simultaneously however when the Lord Jesus comes back the reality of the kingdom will be transferred into the manifestation of the kingdom and the appearance of the kingdom will be burned away134042"}
{"zh": "二\t千年国的属天部分将是父的国；这将是诸天之国的实现，作得胜者的赏赐；千年国时，在国度属天部分的得胜者，要与基督一同掌权管理属地部分，就是大卫复兴的国，在那里基督为人子，大卫王室的后裔，要作以色列人的王—41、43节，撒下七13，徒十五16，启十一15。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "B. The heavenly section of the millennial kingdom will be the kingdom of the Father; this will be the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens as a reward to the overcomers; in the millennium the overcomers in the heavenly part of the kingdom will reign with Christ over the earthly part, which will be the restored kingdom of David, where Christ as the Son of Man, David’s royal descendant, will be the King over the children of Israel.—vv. 41, 43; 2 Sam. 7:13; Acts 15:16; Rev. 11:15.", "norm_zh": "二千年国的属天部分将是父的国这将是诸天之国的实现作得胜者的赏赐千年国时在国度属天部分的得胜者要与基督一同掌权管理属地部分就是大卫复兴的国在哪里基督为人子大卫王室的后裔要作以色列人的王4143节撒下七13徒十五16启十一15李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The heavenly section of the millennial kingdom will be the kingdom of the Father this will be the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens as a reward to the overcomers in the millennium the overcomers in the heavenly part of the kingdom will reign with Christ over the earthly part which will be the restored kingdom of David where Christ as the Son of Man Davids royal descendant will be the King over the children of Israelvv 41 43 2 Sam 713 Acts 1516 Rev 1115"}
{"zh": "三\t惟有今天在诸天之国实际里的得胜者，将来才会有分于诸天之国的实现；诸天之国的实现将是给得胜者的赏赐，奖赏—提后四18，太十三43，二六29，弗五5，彼后一11。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "C. Only the overcomers who are in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens today will have a share in the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens in the future; the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will be a reward, a prize, given to the overcomers.—2 Tim. 4:18; Matt. 13:43; 26:29; Eph. 5:5; 2 Pet. 1:11.", "norm_zh": "三惟有今天在诸天之国实际里的得胜者将来才会有分于诸天之国的实现诸天之国的实现将是给得胜者的赏赐奖赏提后四18太十三43二六29弗五5彼后一11李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Only the overcomers who are in the reality of the kingdom of the heavens today will have a share in the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens in the future the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will be a reward a prize given to the overcomers2 Tim 418 Matt 1343 2629 Eph 55 2 Pet 111"}
{"zh": "四\t诸天之国的实现将在千年国时代，存于千年国；诸天之国的实际是随着今世的召会，而诸天之国的实现将是在来世—11节，罗十四17。（李常受文集一九六三年第三册，诸天之国的要义，第二章）", "en": "D. The manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will exist in the millennium during the age of the millennium; whereas the reality of the kingdom of the heavens is with the church in this age, the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will be in the coming age.—v. 11; Rom. 14:17.", "norm_zh": "四诸天之国的实现将在千年国时代存于千年国诸天之国的实际是随着今世的召会而诸天之国的实现将是在来世11节罗十四17李常受文集一九六三年第三册诸天之国的要义第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:55:37.670462+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will exist in the millennium during the age of the millennium whereas the reality of the kingdom of the heavens is with the church in this age the manifestation of the kingdom of the heavens will be in the coming agev 11 Rom 1417"}
{"zh": "读经：约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12，腓二5~8，罗八9~11，弗三16~19", "en": "Scripture Reading: 1 John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12; Phil. 2:5-8; Rom. 8:9-11; Eph. 3:16-19", "norm_zh": "读经约一141617赛五五1林后一8912腓二58罗八911弗三1619", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 1 John 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12 Phil 258 Rom 8911 Eph 31619"}
{"zh": "壹\t神所赐给我们的恩典，不是任何物质的东西，也不仅仅是救恩、救赎或天堂；神所赐给我们的恩典，乃是一个神圣的人位；基督是神真实的恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12：", "en": "I. The grace God has given us is not any material thing, nor is it merely salvation, redemption, or heaven; the grace God has given us is a divine person; Christ is the true grace of God—1 John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12:", "norm_zh": "壹神所赐给我们的恩典不是任何物质的东西也不仅仅是救恩救赎或天堂神所赐给我们的恩典乃是一个神圣的人位基督是神真实的恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The grace God has given us is not any material thing nor is it merely salvation redemption or heaven the grace God has given us is a divine person Christ is the true grace of God1 John 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12"}
{"zh": "一\t唯有基督是真实的恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12：", "en": "A. Only Christ is the true grace—1 John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12:", "norm_zh": "一惟有基督是真实的恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Only Christ is the true grace1 John 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12"}
{"zh": "1\t有些人以为，神爱世人，甚至将救恩、救赎、或天堂赐给相信祂儿子的人；他们信这就是恩典；其他人以为，好房子、好车子、好妻子、好丈夫、或顺从的儿女就是恩典；他们说神爱我们，甚至将许多美好的东西当作恩典赐给我们—约一14、16~17，赛五五1。", "en": "1. Some think that God so loved the world that He gave salvation, redemption, or heaven to those who believe in His Son; they believe that this is grace; others think that a good house, a fine car, a nice wife, a good husband, or obedient children are grace; they say that God so loved us that He gave us many good things as grace—1 John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1.", "norm_zh": "1有些人以为神爱世人甚至将救恩救赎或天堂赐给相信祂儿子的人他们信这就是恩典其他人以为好房子好车子好妻子好丈夫或顺从的儿女就是恩典他们说神爱我们甚至将许多美好的东西当作恩典赐给我们约一141617赛五五1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Some think that God so loved the world that He gave salvation redemption or heaven to those who believe in His Son they believe that this is grace others think that a good house a fine car a nice wife a good husband or obedient children are grace they say that God so loved us that He gave us many good things as grace1 John 114 1617 Isa 551"}
{"zh": "2\t但这些东西不是恩典，因为不是神在实际里所赐给我们的—约一14、16~17。", "en": "2. But these things are not grace, for they are not what God has given us in reality—1 John 1:14, 16-17.", "norm_zh": "2但这些东西不是恩典因为不是神在实际里所赐给我们的约一141617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 But these things are not grace for they are not what God has given us in reality1 John 114 1617"}
{"zh": "二\t在腓立比三章八节保罗告诉我们，基督以外的一切都是垃圾、粪土；我们可能认为是恩典的一切东西，实际上是垃圾；基督不是垃圾，祂是全然超绝。", "en": "B. In Phil. 3:8 Paul tells us that everything other than Christ is rubbish, dung; everything we may consider as grace is actually rubbish; Christ is not rubbish; He is utterly superb", "norm_zh": "二在腓立比三章八节保罗告诉我们基督以外的一切都是垃圾粪土我们可能认为是恩典的一切东西实际上是垃圾基督不是垃圾祂是全然超绝", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In Phil 38 Paul tells us that everything other than Christ is rubbish dung everything we may consider as grace is actually rubbish Christ is not rubbish He is utterly superb"}
{"zh": "三\t约翰一章一节、十四节和十六节说，“太初有话，话与神同在，话就是神。……话成了肉体，支搭帐幕在我们中间，丰丰满满地有恩典，有实际。……从祂的丰满里我们都领受了，而且恩上加恩”； 所以，恩典乃是三一神成为肉体，来作我们的分，给我们享受。", "en": "C. John 1:1, 14, and 16 say, \"In the beginning was the Word, and the Word was with God, and the Word was God... And the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us..., full of grace and reality... For of His fullness we have all received, and grace upon grace\"; therefore, grace is the Triune God incarnated to be our portion for our enjoyment", "norm_zh": "三约翰一章一节十四节和十六节说太初有话话与神同在话就是神话成了肉体支搭帐幕在我们中间丰丰满满地有恩典有实际从祂的丰满里我们都领受了而且恩上加恩所以恩典乃是三一神成为肉体来作我们的分给我们享受", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C John 11 14 and 16 say In the beginning was the Word and the Word was with God and the Word was God And the Word became flesh and tabernacled among us full of grace and reality For of His fullness we have all received and grace upon grace therefore grace is the Triune God incarnated to be our portion for our enjoyment"}
{"zh": "四\t约翰的福音书启示，这奇妙的人位对我们何其便利；我们能喝祂，能吃祂，还能吸入祂；这就是神真实的恩典；我们绝不该将物质的东西看作恩典；真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神作我们的享受—四10、14，七37~39。", "en": "D. John's Gospel reveals how available this wonderful person is to us; we can drink Him, we can eat Him, and we can breathe Him; this is the true grace of God; we should never count material things as grace; the true grace is nothing less than the Triune God as our enjoyment—John 4:10, 14; 7:37-39.", "norm_zh": "四约翰的福音书启示这奇妙的人位对我们何其便利我们能喝祂能吃祂还能吸入祂这就是神真实的恩典我们绝不该将物质的东西看作恩典真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神作我们的享受四1014七3739", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Johns Gospel reveals how available this wonderful person is to us we can drink Him we can eat Him and we can breathe Him this is the true grace of God we should never count material things as grace the true grace is nothing less than the Triune God as our enjoymentJohn 410 14 73739"}
{"zh": "贰\t现在我们要来到彼得在书信中所提起恩典的九方面—彼前一2、7、10：", "en": "II. Now we must come to the nine aspects of grace that are mentioned by Peter in his Epistles—1 Pet. 1:2, 7, 10:", "norm_zh": "贰现在我们要来到彼得在书信中所提起恩典的九方面彼前一2710", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Now we must come to the nine aspects of grace that are mentioned by Peter in his Epistles1 Pet 12 7 10"}
{"zh": "一\t繁增的恩典—彼前一2、3：", "en": "A. Multiplied grace—1 Pet. 1:2-3:", "norm_zh": "一繁增的恩典彼前一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Multiplied grace1 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "1\t彼得祷告，愿恩典繁增的归与我们；我们许多人尝过恩典，但我们必须学习以繁增的方式来尝恩典—2、3节。", "en": "1. Peter prays that grace will be multiplied to us; many of us have tasted grace, but we must learn to taste grace in the way of multiplication—vv. 2-3.", "norm_zh": "1彼得祷告愿恩典繁增的归与我们我们许多人尝过恩典但我们必须学习以繁增的方式来尝恩典23节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Peter prays that grace will be multiplied to us many of us have tasted grace but we must learn to taste grace in the way of multiplicationvv 23"}
{"zh": "2\t恩典的繁增伴随这四件事：神的拣选、基督借血的救赎、那灵的圣别、和父的重生；拣选是借着父神，救赎是借着子神，圣别是借着灵神；这就是三一神将祂自己分赐到我们里面—2、3节。", "en": "2. The multiplication of grace goes with these four things: God's selection, Christ's redemption by His blood, the Spirit's sanctification, and the Father's regeneration; selection is by God the Father, redemption is by God the Son, and sanctification is by God the Spirit; this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into us.2. The multiplication of grace goes with these four things: God's selection, Christ's redemption by His blood, the Spirit's sanctification, and the Father's regeneration; selection is by God the Father, redemption is by God the Son, and sanctification is by God the Spirit; this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into us—vv. 2-3.", "norm_zh": "2恩典的繁增伴随这四件事神的拣选基督借血的救赎哪灵的圣别和父的重生拣选是借着父神救赎是借着子神圣别是借着灵神这就是三一神将祂自己分赐到我们里面23节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The multiplication of grace goes with these four things Gods selection Christs redemption by His blood the Spirits sanctification and the Fathers regeneration selection is by God the Father redemption is by God the Son and sanctification is by God the Spirit this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into us2 The multiplication of grace goes with these four things Gods selection Christs redemption by His blood the Spirits sanctification and the Fathers regeneration selection is by God the Father redemption is by God the Son and sanctification is by God the Spirit this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into usvv 23"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典的来临；恩典是众申言者所预言那要临到我们的奇妙人位；祂临到彼得，临到约翰，临到我，也临到你—彼前一10：", "en": "B. The coming of grace; grace is a wonderful person whom the prophets prophesied would come unto us; He came unto Peter, He came unto John, He came unto me, and He came also unto you—1 Pet. 1:10:", "norm_zh": "二恩典的来临恩典是众申言者所预言哪要临到我们的奇妙人位祂临到彼得临到约翰临到我也临到你彼前一10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The coming of grace grace is a wonderful person whom the prophets prophesied would come unto us He came unto Peter He came unto John He came unto me and He came also unto you1 Pet 110"}
{"zh": "1\t我们有这神圣的人位，就有救赎、救恩、赦罪、本于信得称义、圣别、重生、并生命里的成熟—10节。", "en": "1. With this divine person we have redemption, salvation, forgiveness of sins, justification by faith, sanctification, regeneration, and the maturity in life.—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "1我们有这神圣的人位就有救赎救恩赦罪本于信得称义圣别重生并生命里的成熟10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 With this divine person we have redemption salvation forgiveness of sins justification by faith sanctification regeneration and the maturity in lifev 10"}
{"zh": "2\t这人位临到我们，一切神圣、圣别、属天、属灵的事物都包含在内；我们有这一个人位，就领受了一切—10节。", "en": "2. All the divine, holy, heavenly, and spiritual things were included when this person came unto us; with this one person we received everything.—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "2这人位临到我们一切神圣圣别属天属灵的事物都包含在内我们有这一个人位就领受了一切10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All the divine holy heavenly and spiritual things were included when this person came unto us with this one person we received everythingv 10"}
{"zh": "三\t生命之恩；恩典属于生命，而我们乃是这恩典的承受者；生命之恩就是那是生命的三一神，进入我们里面作我们的生命—约十一25，十四6，彼前三7：", "en": "C. The grace of life; grace is something of life, and we are heirs of this grace; the grace of life is the Triune God, who is life, coming into us to be our life—John 11:25; 14:6; 1 Pet. 3:7:", "norm_zh": "三生命之恩恩典属于生命而我们乃是这恩典的承受者生命之恩就是哪是生命的三一神进入我们里面作我们的生命约十一25十四6彼前三7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The grace of life grace is something of life and we are heirs of this grace the grace of life is the Triune God who is life coming into us to be our lifeJohn 1125 146 1 Pet 37"}
{"zh": "1\t我们是承受者以承受，是器皿以盛装；我们是承受者以承受生命之恩，同时我们也是器皿以盛装生命之恩—7节。", "en": "1. We are heirs to inherit and vessels to contain; we are heirs to inherit the grace of life, and at the same time we are vessels to contain the grace of life.—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "1我们是承受者以承受是器皿以盛装我们是承受者以承受生命之恩同时我们也是器皿以盛装生命之恩7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We are heirs to inherit and vessels to contain we are heirs to inherit the grace of life and at the same time we are vessels to contain the grace of lifev 7"}
{"zh": "2\t我们许多人从父母或祖父母承受了一些东西可能我们承受了银行里的一笔钱或一块地产；但今天我们都有所承受，并且我们是一同承受，作一同承受者；我们是一同承受生命之恩的—7节。", "en": "2. Many of us have inherited something from our parents or grandparents; perhaps we inherited a sum of money in the bank or a piece of property; but today we have all inherited something, and we have inherited it together as fellow heirs; we are fellow heirs of the grace of life—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "2我们许多人从父母或祖父母承受了一些东西可能我们承受了银行里的一笔钱或一块地产但今天我们都有所承受并且我们是一同承受作一同承受者我们是一同承受生命之恩的7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Many of us have inherited something from our parents or grandparents perhaps we inherited a sum of money in the bank or a piece of property but today we have all inherited something and we have inherited it together as fellow heirs we are fellow heirs of the grace of lifev 7"}
{"zh": "四\t恩典的管家；“各人要照所得的恩赐，将这恩赐彼此供应，作神诸般恩典的好管家”；我们不但是恩典的承受者，也是管家将恩典服事给人—7节：", "en": "D. Stewards of grace; \"Each one, as he has received a gift, ministering it among yourselves as good stewards of the varied grace of God\"; we are not only heirs of grace but also stewards to serve others with grace—v. 7:", "norm_zh": "四恩典的管家各人要照所得的恩赐将这恩赐彼此供应作神诸般恩典的好管家我们不但是恩典的承受者也是管家将恩典服事给人7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Stewards of grace Each one as he has received a gift ministering it among yourselves as good stewards of the varied grace of God we are not only heirs of grace but also stewards to serve others with gracev 7"}
{"zh": "1\t恩典的管家职分不是只为着少数人；身体上所有的肢体都必须学习作神诸般恩典的好管家；我若将生命供应你，你也必须将生命供应我；我若以恩典服事你，你也必须以恩典服事我—7节。", "en": "1. The stewardship of grace is not just for a few; all the members of the Body must learn to be good stewards of the varied grace of God; if I minister life to you, you must minister life to me; if I serve you with grace, you must serve me with grace—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "1恩典的管家职分不是只为着少数人身体上所有的肢体都必须学习作神诸般恩典的好管家我若将生命供应你你也必须将生命供应我我若以恩典服事你你也必须以恩典服事我7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The stewardship of grace is not just for a few all the members of the Body must learn to be good stewards of the varied grace of God if I minister life to you you must minister life to me if I serve you with grace you must serve me with gracev 7"}
{"zh": "2\t我们借着呼求主名和祷读主话这两种实行，将主多而又多的接受到我们里面，恩典就在我们里面得以繁增；然后我们就预备好向别人作这恩典的管家—7节。", "en": "2. By the two practices of calling on the name of the Lord and pray-reading the Word, we take the Lord into us more and more, and grace in us is multiplied; then we are ready to be stewards of this grace to others.—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "2我们借着呼求主名和祷读主话这两种实行将主多而又多的接受到我们里面恩典就在我们里面得以繁增然后我们就预备好向别人作这恩典的管家7节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 By the two practices of calling on the name of the Lord and prayreading the Word we take the Lord into us more and more and grace in us is multiplied then we are ready to be stewards of this grace to othersv 7"}
{"zh": "五\t“神敌挡狂傲的人，赐恩给谦卑的人”（彼前五5）；我们若是狂傲的，就绝不会从神领受恩典；所以，我们必须学习谦卑自己，并彼此服从。", "en": "E. \"God resists the proud but gives grace to the humble\" (1 Pet. 5:5); if we are proud, we will never receive grace from God; therefore, we must learn to humble ourselves and submit to one another", "norm_zh": "五神敌挡狂傲的人赐恩给谦卑的人彼前五5我们若是狂傲的就绝不会从神领受恩典所以我们必须学习谦卑自己并彼此服从", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E God resists the proud but gives grace to the humble 1 Pet 55 if we are proud we will never receive grace from God therefore we must learn to humble ourselves and submit to one another"}
{"zh": "六\t全般恩典的神—10节：", "en": "F. The God of all grace—v. 10:", "norm_zh": "六全般恩典的神10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The God of all gracev 10"}
{"zh": "1\t今天这位全般恩典的神就是三一神，祂已分赐到我们里面，作我们的生命，给我们享受—10节。", "en": "1. Today this God of all grace is the Triune God, who has been dispensed into us as our life for our enjoyment—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "1今天这位全般恩典的神就是三一神祂已分赐到我们里面作我们的生命给我们享受10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Today this God of all grace is the Triune God who has been dispensed into us as our life for our enjoymentv 10"}
{"zh": "2\t这神圣的人位，作为在我们里面作工的恩典，要成全我们，坚固我们，加强我们，给我们立定根基—10节。", "en": "2. This divine person, as the grace that is working in us, will perfect us, strengthen us, establish us, and ground us—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "2这神圣的人位作为在我们里面作工的恩典要成全我们坚固我们加强我们给我们立定根基10节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 This divine person as the grace that is working in us will perfect us strengthen us establish us and ground usv 10"}
{"zh": "七\t真实的恩典；神真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神在我们里面，作我们的生命；这就是我们在其中站住的恩典—12节。", "en": "G. True grace; the true grace of God is nothing less than the Triune God in us as our life; this is the grace in which we stand—v. 12.", "norm_zh": "七真实的恩典神真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神在我们里面作我们的生命这就是我们在其中站住的恩典12节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G True grace the true grace of God is nothing less than the Triune God in us as our life this is the grace in which we standv 12"}
{"zh": "八\t彼后一章二至四节，恩典繁增的归与我们，是根据神圣的能力已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们；基于神圣的能力已将这些事赐给我们的事实，恩典就繁增的归与我们。", "en": "H. 2 Pet. 1:2-4, grace being multiplied to us is based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us all things that relate to life and godliness; based on the fact that the divine power has granted these things to us, grace is multiplied to us", "norm_zh": "八彼后一章二至四节恩典繁增的归与我们是根据神圣的能力已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们基于神圣的能力已将这些事赐给我们的事实恩典就繁增的归与我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H 2 Pet 124 grace being multiplied to us is based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us all things that relate to life and godliness based on the fact that the divine power has granted these things to us grace is multiplied to us"}
{"zh": "九\t彼得告诉我们，要在恩典上长大；这证明恩典不是物质的东西；恩典是活的，我们能在其上长大—三18。", "en": "I. Peter tells us to grow in grace; this proves that grace is not material things; grace is something living, something in which we can grow—3:18.", "norm_zh": "九彼得告诉我们要在恩典上长大这证明恩典不是物质的东西恩典是活的我们能在其上长大三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Peter tells us to grow in grace this proves that grace is not material things grace is something living something in which we can grow318"}
{"zh": "叁\t这恩典就是神圣的人位—那已分赐到我们里面，作我们的生命，给我们享受的三一神这就是我们在其上长大的恩典；愿主使我们众人都在那是恩典的神圣人位上长大—18节，彼前一2。", "en": "III. This grace is the divine person—the very Triune God who has been imparted into us as our life for our enjoyment; this is the grace in which we grow; may the Lord grant us all to grow in the divine person who is grace—v. 18; 1 Pet. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "叁这恩典就是神圣的人位哪已分赐到我们里面作我们的生命给我们享受的三一神这就是我们在其上长大的恩典愿主使我们众人都在哪是恩典的神圣人位上长大18节彼前一2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III This grace is the divine personthe very Triune God who has been imparted into us as our life for our enjoyment this is the grace in which we grow may the Lord grant us all to grow in the divine person who is gracev 18 1 Pet 12"}
{"zh": "神所赐给我们的恩典，乃是一个神圣的人位", "en": "The grace God has given us is a divine person", "norm_zh": "神所赐给我们的恩典乃是一个神圣的人位", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The grace God has given us is a divine person"}
{"zh": "唯有基督是真实的恩典", "en": "Only Christ is the true grace", "norm_zh": "惟有基督是真实的恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T05:58:43.919265+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Only Christ is the true grace"}
{"zh": "四\t约翰的福音书启示，这奇妙的人位对我们何其便利；我们能喝祂，能吃祂，还能吸入祂；这就是神真实的恩典；我们绝不该将物质的东西看作恩典；真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神作我们的享受—四10、14，七37~39。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "D. John's Gospel reveals how available this wonderful person is to us; we can drink Him, we can eat Him, and we can breathe Him; this is the true grace of God; we should never count material things as grace; the true grace is nothing less than the Triune God as our enjoyment.—John 4:10, 14; 7:37-39.", "norm_zh": "四约翰的福音书启示这奇妙的人位对我们何其便利我们能喝祂能吃祂还能吸入祂这就是神真实的恩典我们绝不该将物质的东西看作恩典真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神作我们的享受四1014七3739李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Johns Gospel reveals how available this wonderful person is to us we can drink Him we can eat Him and we can breathe Him this is the true grace of God we should never count material things as grace the true grace is nothing less than the Triune God as our enjoymentJohn 410 14 73739"}
{"zh": "贰\t现在我们要来到彼得在书信中所提起恩典的九方面—彼前一2、7、10：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "II. Now we must come to the nine aspects of grace that are mentioned by Peter in his Epistles.—1 Pet. 1:2, 7, 10:", "norm_zh": "贰现在我们要来到彼得在书信中所提起恩典的九方面彼前一2710李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Now we must come to the nine aspects of grace that are mentioned by Peter in his Epistles1 Pet 12 7 10"}
{"zh": "一\t繁增的恩典—彼前一2、3：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "A. Multiplied Grace—1 Pet. 1:2-3:", "norm_zh": "一繁增的恩典彼前一23李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Multiplied Grace1 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "1\t彼得祷告，愿恩典繁增的归与我们；我们许多人尝过恩典，但我们必须学习以繁增的方式来尝恩典—2、3节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. Peter prays that grace will be multiplied to us; many of us have tasted grace, but we must learn to taste grace in the way of multiplication.—vv. 2-3.", "norm_zh": "1彼得祷告愿恩典繁增的归与我们我们许多人尝过恩典但我们必须学习以繁增的方式来尝恩典23节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Peter prays that grace will be multiplied to us many of us have tasted grace but we must learn to taste grace in the way of multiplicationvv 23"}
{"zh": "2\t恩典的繁增伴随这四件事：神的拣选、基督借血的救赎、那灵的圣别、和父的重生；拣选是借着父神，救赎是借着子神，圣别是借着灵神；这就是三一神将祂自己分赐到我们里面—2、3节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. The multiplication of grace goes with these four things: God's selection, Christ's redemption by His blood, the Spirit's sanctification, and the Father's regeneration; selection is by God the Father, redemption is by God the Son, and sanctification is by God the Spirit; this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into us.—vv. 2-3.", "norm_zh": "2恩典的繁增伴随这四件事神的拣选基督借血的救赎哪灵的圣别和父的重生拣选是借着父神救赎是借着子神圣别是借着灵神这就是三一神将祂自己分赐到我们里面23节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The multiplication of grace goes with these four things Gods selection Christs redemption by His blood the Spirits sanctification and the Fathers regeneration selection is by God the Father redemption is by God the Son and sanctification is by God the Spirit this is the Triune God dispensing Himself into usvv 23"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典的来临；恩典是众申言者所预言那要临到我们的奇妙人位；祂临到彼得，临到约翰，临到我，也临到你—彼前一10：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "B. The Coming of Grace; grace is a wonderful person whom the prophets prophesied would come unto us; He came unto Peter, He came unto John, He came unto me, and He came also unto you.—1 Pet. 1:10:", "norm_zh": "二恩典的来临恩典是众申言者所预言哪要临到我们的奇妙人位祂临到彼得临到约翰临到我也临到你彼前一10李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The Coming of Grace grace is a wonderful person whom the prophets prophesied would come unto us He came unto Peter He came unto John He came unto me and He came also unto you1 Pet 110"}
{"zh": "1\t我们有这神圣的人位，就有救赎、救恩、赦罪、本于信得称义、圣别、重生、并生命里的成熟—10节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. With this divine person we have redemption, salvation, forgiveness of sins, justification by faith, sanctification, regeneration, and the maturity in life.—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "1我们有这神圣的人位就有救赎救恩赦罪本于信得称义圣别重生并生命里的成熟10节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 With this divine person we have redemption salvation forgiveness of sins justification by faith sanctification regeneration and the maturity in lifev 10"}
{"zh": "2\t这人位临到我们，一切神圣、圣别、属天、属灵的事物都包含在内；我们有这一个人位，就领受了一切—10节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. All the divine, holy, heavenly, and spiritual things were included when this person came unto us; with this one person we received everything.—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "2这人位临到我们一切神圣圣别属天属灵的事物都包含在内我们有这一个人位就领受了一切10节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 All the divine holy heavenly and spiritual things were included when this person came unto us with this one person we received everythingv 10"}
{"zh": "三\t生命之恩；恩典属于生命，而我们乃是这恩典的承受者；生命之恩就是那是生命的三一神，进入我们里面作我们的生命—约十一25，十四6，彼前三7：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "C. The Grace of Life; grace is something of life, and we are heirs of this grace; the grace of life is the Triune God, who is life, coming into us to be our life.—John 11:25; 14:6; 1 Pet. 3:7:", "norm_zh": "三生命之恩恩典属于生命而我们乃是这恩典的承受者生命之恩就是哪是生命的三一神进入我们里面作我们的生命约十一25十四6彼前三7李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C The Grace of Life grace is something of life and we are heirs of this grace the grace of life is the Triune God who is life coming into us to be our lifeJohn 1125 146 1 Pet 37"}
{"zh": "1\t我们是承受者以承受，是器皿以盛装；我们是承受者以承受生命之恩，同时我们也是器皿以盛装生命之恩—7节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. We are heirs to inherit and vessels to contain; we are heirs to inherit the grace of life, and at the same time we are vessels to contain the grace of life.—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "1我们是承受者以承受是器皿以盛装我们是承受者以承受生命之恩同时我们也是器皿以盛装生命之恩7节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 We are heirs to inherit and vessels to contain we are heirs to inherit the grace of life and at the same time we are vessels to contain the grace of lifev 7"}
{"zh": "2\t我们许多人从父母或祖父母承受了一些东西可能我们承受了银行里的一笔钱或一块地产；但今天我们都有所承受，并且我们是一同承受，作一同承受者；我们是一同承受生命之恩的—7节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. Many of us have inherited something from our parents or grandparents; perhaps we inherited a sum of money in the bank or a piece of property; but today we have all inherited something, and we have inherited it together as fellow heirs; we are fellow heirs of the grace of life—v. 7.", "norm_zh": "2我们许多人从父母或祖父母承受了一些东西可能我们承受了银行里的一笔钱或一块地产但今天我们都有所承受并且我们是一同承受作一同承受者我们是一同承受生命之恩的7节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Many of us have inherited something from our parents or grandparents perhaps we inherited a sum of money in the bank or a piece of property but today we have all inherited something and we have inherited it together as fellow heirs we are fellow heirs of the grace of lifev 7"}
{"zh": "四\t恩典的管家；“各人要照所得的恩赐，将这恩赐彼此供应，作神诸般恩典的好管家”；我们不但是恩典的承受者，也是管家将恩典服事给人—7节：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "D. Stewards of grace; \"Each one, as he has received a gift, ministering it among yourselves as good stewards of the varied grace of God\"; we are not only heirs of grace but also stewards to serve others with grace—v. 10:", "norm_zh": "四恩典的管家各人要照所得的恩赐将这恩赐彼此供应作神诸般恩典的好管家我们不但是恩典的承受者也是管家将恩典服事给人7节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Stewards of grace Each one as he has received a gift ministering it among yourselves as good stewards of the varied grace of God we are not only heirs of grace but also stewards to serve others with gracev 10"}
{"zh": "1\t恩典的管家职分不是只为着少数人；身体上所有的肢体都必须学习作神诸般恩典的好管家；我若将生命供应你，你也必须将生命供应我；我若以恩典服事你，你也必须以恩典服事我—7节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. The stewardship of grace is not just for a few; all the members of the Body must learn to be good stewards of the varied grace of God; if I minister life to you, you must minister life to me; if I serve you with grace, you must serve me with grace—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "1恩典的管家职分不是只为着少数人身体上所有的肢体都必须学习作神诸般恩典的好管家我若将生命供应你你也必须将生命供应我我若以恩典服事你你也必须以恩典服事我7节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The stewardship of grace is not just for a few all the members of the Body must learn to be good stewards of the varied grace of God if I minister life to you you must minister life to me if I serve you with grace you must serve me with gracev 10"}
{"zh": "2\t我们借着呼求主名和祷读主话这两种实行，将主多而又多的接受到我们里面，恩典就在我们里面得以繁增；然后我们就预备好向别人作这恩典的管家—7节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. By the two practices of calling on the name of the Lord and pray-reading the Word, we take the Lord into us more and more, and grace in us is multiplied; then we are ready to be stewards of this grace to others—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "2我们借着呼求主名和祷读主话这两种实行将主多而又多的接受到我们里面恩典就在我们里面得以繁增然后我们就预备好向别人作这恩典的管家7节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 By the two practices of calling on the name of the Lord and prayreading the Word we take the Lord into us more and more and grace in us is multiplied then we are ready to be stewards of this grace to othersv 10"}
{"zh": "五\t“神敌挡狂傲的人，赐恩给谦卑的人”（彼前五5）；我们若是狂傲的，就绝不会从神领受恩典；所以，我们必须学习谦卑自己，并彼此服从。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "E. \"God resists the proud but gives grace to the humble\" (1 Pet. 5:5); if we are proud, we will never receive grace from God; therefore, we must learn to humble ourselves and submit to one another.", "norm_zh": "五神敌挡狂傲的人赐恩给谦卑的人彼前五5我们若是狂傲的就绝不会从神领受恩典所以我们必须学习谦卑自己并彼此服从李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E God resists the proud but gives grace to the humble 1 Pet 55 if we are proud we will never receive grace from God therefore we must learn to humble ourselves and submit to one another"}
{"zh": "六\t全般恩典的神—10节：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "F. The God of All Grace—v. 10:", "norm_zh": "六全般恩典的神10节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F The God of All Gracev 10"}
{"zh": "1\t今天这位全般恩典的神就是三一神，祂已分赐到我们里面，作我们的生命，给我们享受—10节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "1. Today this God of all grace is the Triune God, who has been dispensed into us as our life for our enjoyment—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "1今天这位全般恩典的神就是三一神祂已分赐到我们里面作我们的生命给我们享受10节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Today this God of all grace is the Triune God who has been dispensed into us as our life for our enjoymentv 10"}
{"zh": "2\t这神圣的人位，作为在我们里面作工的恩典，要成全我们，坚固我们，加强我们，给我们立定根基—10节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "2. This divine person, as the grace that is working in us, will perfect us, strengthen us, establish us, and ground us—v. 10.", "norm_zh": "2这神圣的人位作为在我们里面作工的恩典要成全我们坚固我们加强我们给我们立定根基10节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 This divine person as the grace that is working in us will perfect us strengthen us establish us and ground usv 10"}
{"zh": "七\t真实的恩典；神真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神在我们里面，作我们的生命；这就是我们在其中站住的恩典—12节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "G. True grace; the true grace of God is nothing less than the Triune God in us as our life; this is the grace in which we stand—v. 12.", "norm_zh": "七真实的恩典神真实的恩典一点不差就是三一神在我们里面作我们的生命这就是我们在其中站住的恩典12节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "G True grace the true grace of God is nothing less than the Triune God in us as our life this is the grace in which we standv 12"}
{"zh": "八\t彼后一章二至四节，恩典繁增的归与我们，是根据神圣的能力已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们；基于神圣的能力已将这些事赐给我们的事实，恩典就繁增的归与我们。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "H. In 2 Peter 1:2-4, grace being multiplied to us is based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us all things that relate to life and godliness; based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us these things, grace is multiplied to us.", "norm_zh": "八彼后一章二至四节恩典繁增的归与我们是根据神圣的能力已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们基于神圣的能力已将这些事赐给我们的事实恩典就繁增的归与我们李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "H In 2 Peter 124 grace being multiplied to us is based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us all things that relate to life and godliness based on the fact that the divine power has granted to us these things grace is multiplied to us"}
{"zh": "九\t彼得告诉我们，要在恩典上长大；这证明恩典不是物质的东西；恩典是活的，我们能在其上长大—三18。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "I. Peter tells us to grow in grace; this proves that grace is not material things; grace is something living, something in which we can grow—2 Pet. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "九彼得告诉我们要在恩典上长大这证明恩典不是物质的东西恩典是活的我们能在其上长大三18李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Peter tells us to grow in grace this proves that grace is not material things grace is something living something in which we can grow2 Pet 318"}
{"zh": "叁\t这恩典就是神圣的人位—那已分赐到我们里面，作我们的生命，给我们享受的三一神这就是我们在其上长大的恩典；愿主使我们众人都在那是恩典的神圣人位上长大—18节，彼前一2。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第一章）", "en": "III. This grace is the divine person—the very Triune God who has been imparted into us as our life for our enjoyment; this is the grace in which we grow; may the Lord grant us all to grow in the divine person who is grace—v. 18; 1 Pet. 1:2.", "norm_zh": "叁这恩典就是神圣的人位哪已分赐到我们里面作我们的生命给我们享受的三一神这就是我们在其上长大的恩典愿主使我们众人都在哪是恩典的神圣人位上长大18节彼前一2李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第一章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:01:02.823555+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III This grace is the divine personthe very Triune God who has been imparted into us as our life for our enjoyment this is the grace in which we grow may the Lord grant us all to grow in the divine person who is gracev 18 1 Pet 12"}
{"zh": "读经：徒四33，十一23，林前十四25，十五9~10，罗五20~21，十二6，林后十三14", "en": "Scripture Reading: Acts 4:33; 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25; 15:9-10; Rom. 5:20-21; 12:6; 2 Cor. 13:14", "norm_zh": "读经徒四33十一23林前十四25十五910罗五2021十二6林后十三14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Acts 433 1123 1 Cor 1425 15910 Rom 52021 126 2 Cor 1314"}
{"zh": "壹\t行传四章三十三节，“使徒大有能力，见证主耶稣的复活，众人也都蒙大恩”；说这恩是基督，太简单了；这不仅仅是基督，乃是行动的基督、作工的基督、掌权的基督、使人信服的基督、征服一切的基督、施行拯救的基督、和将人拔高的基督：", "en": "I. Acts 4:33, \"With great power the apostles gave testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus, and great grace was upon them all\"; to say that this grace was Christ is too simple; it was not merely Christ but Christ moving, Christ working, Christ reigning, Christ convincing, Christ subduing, Christ saving, and Christ uplifting:", "norm_zh": "壹行传四章三十三节使徒大有能力见证主耶稣的复活众人也都蒙大恩说这恩是基督太简单了这不仅仅是基督乃是行动的基督作工的基督掌权的基督使人信服的基督征服一切的基督施行拯救的基督和将人拔高的基督", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Acts 433 With great power the apostles gave testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus and great grace was upon them all to say that this grace was Christ is too simple it was not merely Christ but Christ moving Christ working Christ reigning Christ convincing Christ subduing Christ saving and Christ uplifting"}
{"zh": "一\t首先，我们必然看见恩典是一个人位，神圣而属人的人位，这一个人位既神圣又属人；这人位原在永远里，而后进入时间里；祂成了人，活在地上，死于十字架，从死人中复活，升上诸天，并且登宝座、得荣耀、且受托以宇宙中所有的权柄（太二八18）；这样的人位作为恩典降临，眷临祂所有的信徒。", "en": "A. First, of course, we see that grace is a person, a divine-human person, a person who is divine as well as human; this person was in eternity, and He came into time; He became a man who lived on the earth, died on the cross, rose from the dead, ascended into the heavens, and was enthroned, glorified, and entrusted with all the authority in the universe (Matt. 28:18); such a person came down as grace to visit all His believers.", "norm_zh": "一首先我们必然看见恩典是一个人位神圣而属人的人位这一个人位既神圣又属人这人位原在永远里而后进入时间里祂成了人活在地上死于十字架从死人中复活升上诸天并且登宝座得荣耀且受托以宇宙中所有的权柄太二八18这样的人位作为恩典降临眷临祂所有的信徒", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A First of course we see that grace is a person a divinehuman person a person who is divine as well as human this person was in eternity and He came into time He became a man who lived on the earth died on the cross rose from the dead ascended into the heavens and was enthroned glorified and entrusted with all the authority in the universe Matt 2818 such a person came down as grace to visit all His believers"}
{"zh": "二\t我们能看见，恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的，以及这奇妙人位所成就的—林后十二9，林前十五10。", "en": "B. We can see that grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person—2 Cor. 12:9; 1 Cor. 15:10.", "norm_zh": "二我们能看见恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的以及这奇妙人位所成就的林后十二9林前十五10", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We can see that grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person2 Cor 129 1 Cor 1510"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩典能产生一种情况，在其中恩典能被人看见—徒十一23，林前十四25：", "en": "II. Grace is able to produce a situation in which grace can be seen by people—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25:", "norm_zh": "贰恩典能产生一种情况在其中恩典能被人看见徒十一23林前十四25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Grace is able to produce a situation in which grace can be seen by peopleActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "一\t巴拿巴来到安提阿，在那里看见神的恩典；有犹太信徒和外邦信徒来在一起赞美神，并且在基督里是一—徒十一23，林前十四25。", "en": "A. Barnabas came to Antioch, and there he saw the grace of God; the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers had come together to praise God and to be one in Christ—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "一巴拿巴来到安提阿在哪里看见神的恩典有犹太信徒和外邦信徒来在一起赞美神并且在基督里是一徒十一23林前十四25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Barnabas came to Antioch and there he saw the grace of God the Jewish believers and the Gentile believers had come together to praise God and to be one in ChristActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "二\t倘若我们是外人，来到在安提阿的召会，就和巴拿巴一样，看见许多脸发光，许多口赞美神，我们只能说，“恩典，恩典！”看见恩典是美妙的；恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会—徒十一23，林前十四25。", "en": "B. If we came to the church in Antioch as a stranger, as Barnabas did, and saw many faces glowing with many mouths praising God, we could only say, \"Grace, Grace!\" it is wonderful to see grace; grace should be seen in all our church meetings—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "二倘若我们是外人来到在安提阿的召会就和巴拿巴一样看见许多脸发光许多口赞美神我们只能说恩典恩典看见恩典是美妙的恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会徒十一23林前十四25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B If we came to the church in Antioch as a stranger as Barnabas did and saw many faces glowing with many mouths praising God we could only say Grace Grace it is wonderful to see grace grace should be seen in all our church meetingsActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "三\t或许你很受压，感觉非常低落；你可能来到召会的聚会中，就发觉满了恩典；然后你也许开始深深感觉，有东西流进你里面；若是这样，你就会得着安慰、鼓励和盼望—徒十一23，林前十四25。", "en": "C. Perhaps you are depressed and feel very low; you may come to a meeting of the church and find that it is full of grace; then you may begin to have the deep sensation that something is flowing into you; if this is the case, you will receive comfort, encouragement, and hope—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "三或许你很受压感觉非常低落你可能来到召会的聚会中就发觉满了恩典然后你也许开始深深感觉有东西流进你里面若是这样你就会得着安慰鼓励和盼望徒十一23林前十四25", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Perhaps you are depressed and feel very low you may come to a meeting of the church and find that it is full of grace then you may begin to have the deep sensation that something is flowing into you if this is the case you will receive comfort encouragement and hopeActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "四\t真实的恩典就是耶稣自己；祂不计任何代价的为我们行事，祂也不计代价的把东西赐给我们；恩典就是耶稣连同祂恩典的作为和祂恩典的赐给—约一14、16~17。", "en": "D. The real grace is Jesus Himself; He does things for us without any cost, and He gives things to us without any cost; grace is Jesus with His gracious doing and His gracious giving—John 1:14, 16-17.", "norm_zh": "四真实的恩典就是耶稣自己祂不计任何代价的为我们行事祂也不计代价的把东西赐给我们恩典就是耶稣连同祂恩典的作为和祂恩典的赐给约一141617", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The real grace is Jesus Himself He does things for us without any cost and He gives things to us without any cost grace is Jesus with His gracious doing and His gracious givingJohn 114 1617"}
{"zh": "叁\t行传十五章四十节说，“保罗却拣选了西拉，也出去，蒙弟兄们把他交与主的恩典”：", "en": "III. Acts 15:40 says, \"But Paul chose Silas and went out, having been commended to the grace of the Lord by the brothers\":", "norm_zh": "叁行传十五章四十节说保罗却拣选了西拉也出去蒙弟兄们把他交与主的恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Acts 1540 says But Paul chose Silas and went out having been commended to the grace of the Lord by the brothers"}
{"zh": "一\t无论保罗往那里去，主耶稣都与他同在，一直给与、扶持、分授、供应，并借着保罗作许多事；那就是恩典—40节，弗三8。", "en": "A. Wherever Paul went, the Lord Jesus was with him, giving, supporting, imparting, supplying, and doing many things through Paul; that was grace—v. 40; Eph. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "一无论保罗往哪里去主耶稣都与他同在一直给与扶持分授供应并借着保罗作许多事哪就是恩典40节弗三8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Wherever Paul went the Lord Jesus was with him giving supporting imparting supplying and doing many things through Paul that was gracev 40 Eph 38"}
{"zh": "二\t保罗作工，不是凭着他的教育、才能或智慧，乃是凭着神的恩典；这意思就是，保罗凭着一个奇妙的人位耶稣，作了一切奇妙的工作；耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面，并借着保罗成就许多事—8节。", "en": "B. Paul worked not by his education, his ability, or his wisdom but by the grace of God. This simply means that Paul did all his wonderful work by a wonderful person, Jesus, who imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paul.—v. 8.", "norm_zh": "二保罗作工不是凭着他的教育才能或智慧乃是凭着神的恩典这意思就是保罗凭着一个奇妙的人位耶稣作了一切奇妙的工作耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面并借着保罗成就许多事8节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Paul worked not by his education his ability or his wisdom but by the grace of God This simply means that Paul did all his wonderful work by a wonderful person Jesus who imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paulv 8"}
{"zh": "三\t我们没有借口；我们都必须尽功用，因为基督的恩典是够用的；我们不但该学习说，“不再是我，乃是基督，”也该说，“不是我，乃是恩典”；我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己，乃信靠神的恩—林前十五10，加二20。", "en": "C. We have no excuse; we all must function because the grace of Christ is sufficient; we should learn to say not only \"No longer I but Christ\" but also \"Not I but grace.\" We all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God.—1 Cor. 15:10; Gal. 2:20.", "norm_zh": "三我们没有借口我们都必须尽功用因为基督的恩典是够用的我们不但该学习说不再是我乃是基督也该说不是我乃是恩典我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己乃信靠神的恩林前十五10加二20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We have no excuse we all must function because the grace of Christ is sufficient we should learn to say not only No longer I but Christ but also Not I but grace We all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God1 Cor 1510 Gal 220"}
{"zh": "肆\t保罗说恩典洋溢，恩典也作王掌权；恩典若不是一个人位，怎能作王掌权？赞美主，恩典是王—罗五20~21：", "en": "IV. Paul says that grace has abounded and that grace reigns as a king. If grace were not a person, how could grace reign as a king? Praise the Lord that grace is a king.—Rom. 5:20-21:", "norm_zh": "肆保罗说恩典洋溢恩典也作王掌权恩典若不是一个人位怎能作王掌权赞美主恩典是王罗五2021", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Paul says that grace has abounded and that grace reigns as a king If grace were not a person how could grace reign as a king Praise the Lord that grace is a kingRom 52021"}
{"zh": "一\t恩典作王管理撒但，管理罪，管理肉体，管理死，并管理宇宙中一切消极的事物；所以，恩典无疑就是主耶稣，也是耶稣这活的人位，赐给我们所需要的一切，并作成神所要求的一切—20~21节。", "en": "A. Grace reigns over Satan, over sin, over the flesh, over death, and over all the negative things in the universe. Therefore, grace is no doubt the Lord Jesus, and it is also Jesus, the living person, giving us whatever we need and doing whatever God requires.—vv. 20-21.", "norm_zh": "一恩典作王管理撒但管理罪管理肉体管理死并管理宇宙中一切消极的事物所以恩典无疑就是主耶稣也是耶稣这活的人位赐给我们所需要的一切并作成神所要求的一切2021节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Grace reigns over Satan over sin over the flesh over death and over all the negative things in the universe Therefore grace is no doubt the Lord Jesus and it is also Jesus the living person giving us whatever we need and doing whatever God requiresvv 2021"}
{"zh": "二\t神说，人若犯罪就必死（一32，六23上）；但基督来为我们死（五8）；这是耶稣恩典的作为；我们因恩典，因耶稣恩典的作为得称义。", "en": "B. God says that if man sins, he must die (1:32; 6:23a). But Christ came and died for us (5:8). This is the gracious doing of Jesus. We have been justified by grace, by the gracious doing of Jesus.", "norm_zh": "二神说人若犯罪就必死一32六23上但基督来为我们死五8这是耶稣恩典的作为我们因恩典因耶稣恩典的作为得称义", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God says that if man sins he must die 132 623a But Christ came and died for us 58 This is the gracious doing of Jesus We have been justified by grace by the gracious doing of Jesus"}
{"zh": "三\t我们呼求主，就经历甜美的享受，并且我们呼求祂，祂就成为我们里面的恩典无论我们需要什么，祂都供应；无论神要求我们什么，祂都应付；我们只需要作一件事：享受恩典—哀三55。", "en": "C. When we call on the Lord, we experience a sweet enjoyment, and as we call on Him, He becomes grace within us. Whatever we need, He supplies. Whatever God requires of us, He meets that requirement. All we need to do is enjoy grace.—Lam. 3:55.", "norm_zh": "三我们呼求主就经历甜美的享受并且我们呼求祂祂就成为我们里面的恩典无论我们需要什么祂都供应无论神要求我们什么祂都应付我们只需要作一件事享受恩典哀三55", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C When we call on the Lord we experience a sweet enjoyment and as we call on Him He becomes grace within us Whatever we need He supplies Whatever God requires of us He meets that requirement All we need to do is enjoy graceLam 355"}
{"zh": "伍\t最后，罗马书告诉我们，属灵的恩赐是照着恩典赐给我们的—十二6，林前十五9~10：", "en": "V. Finally, the book of Romans tells us that the spiritual gifts are given to us according to grace.—12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10:", "norm_zh": "伍最后罗马书告诉我们属灵的恩赐是照着恩典赐给我们的十二6林前十五910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Finally the book of Romans tells us that the spiritual gifts are given to us according to grace126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "一\t我们享受越多恩典，就得着越多恩赐；我们若在恩典上贫穷，在恩赐上也必然贫穷—罗十二6，林前十五9~10。", "en": "A. The more grace we enjoy, the more gifts we will have. If we are poor in grace, surely we will be poor in gifts.—Rom. 12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10.", "norm_zh": "一我们享受越多恩典就得着越多恩赐我们若在恩典上贫穷在恩赐上也必然贫穷罗十二6林前十五910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The more grace we enjoy the more gifts we will have If we are poor in grace surely we will be poor in giftsRom 126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "二\t这些恩赐不是来自我们的教育，也不是来自我们在圣经学校或神学院里的学习；这些恩赐来自恩典；我们越享受恩典，就越有出于这恩典的属灵恩赐；我们越享受基督的恩典，就越能为基督说话，并为祂行事—罗十二6，林前十五9~10。", "en": "B. These gifts do not come from our education or from our learning in a Bible school or a seminary. These gifts come from grace. The more we enjoy grace, the more we will have spiritual gifts out of this grace. The more we enjoy the grace of Christ, the more we will be able to speak for Christ and do something for Him.—Rom. 12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10.", "norm_zh": "二这些恩赐不是来自我们的教育也不是来自我们在圣经学校或神学院里的学习这些恩赐来自恩典我们越享受恩典就越有出于这恩典的属灵恩赐我们越享受基督的恩典就越能为基督说话并为祂行事罗十二6林前十五910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B These gifts do not come from our education or from our learning in a Bible school or a seminary These gifts come from grace The more we enjoy grace the more we will have spiritual gifts out of this grace The more we enjoy the grace of Christ the more we will be able to speak for Christ and do something for HimRom 126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "陆\t保罗三次祷告主除去他肉体上的刺，但主告诉他，祂不会除去；反之，保罗必须学习享受祂够用的恩典—林后十二7~9：", "en": "VI. Paul prayed three times that the Lord would take away the thorn in his flesh, but the Lord told him that He would not take it away; instead, Paul had to learn to enjoy His sufficient grace.—2 Cor. 12:7-9:", "norm_zh": "陆保罗三次祷告主除去他肉体上的刺但主告诉他祂不会除去反之保罗必须学习享受祂够用的恩典林后十二79", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Paul prayed three times that the Lord would take away the thorn in his flesh but the Lord told him that He would not take it away instead Paul had to learn to enjoy His sufficient grace2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "一\t也许你的妻子对你是一根刺，但她是宝贵的刺，因为她帮助你享受基督；你不需要祷告求主把刺除去；祂绝不会那样作—7~9节。", "en": "A. It may be that your wife is a thorn to you, but she is a precious thorn because she helps you to enjoy Christ; there is no need for you to pray that the Lord will take away the thorn; He will never do that—vv. 7-9.", "norm_zh": "一也许你的妻子对你是一根刺但她是宝贵的刺因为她帮助你享受基督你不需要祷告求主把刺除去祂绝不会哪样作79节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A It may be that your wife is a thorn to you but she is a precious thorn because she helps you to enjoy Christ there is no need for you to pray that the Lord will take away the thorn He will never do thatvv 79"}
{"zh": "二\t反之，祂会说，“我的恩典是够用的。刺帮助你享受我的恩典，因为我的能力，是在你的软弱上显得完全”；这是主耶稣够用的恩典—7~9节。", "en": "B. Instead, He will say, \"My grace is sufficient. The thorn helps you to enjoy My grace, for My power is perfected in your weakness\"; this is the sufficient grace of the Lord Jesus—vv. 7-9.", "norm_zh": "二反之祂会说我的恩典是够用的刺帮助你享受我的恩典因为我的能力是在你的软弱上显得完全这是主耶稣够用的恩典79节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Instead He will say My grace is sufficient The thorn helps you to enjoy My grace for My power is perfected in your weakness this is the sufficient grace of the Lord Jesusvv 79"}
{"zh": "柒\t“愿主耶稣基督的恩，神的爱，圣灵的交通，与你们众人同在”（林后十三14）；这是三一神将祂一切的所是施作、涌流、流通、输送、传输、并分赐到我们里面：", "en": "VII. \"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ and the love of God and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all\" (2 Cor. 13:14); this is the Triune God working, flowing, communicating, transporting, transmitting, and dispensing all that He is into us:", "norm_zh": "柒愿主耶稣基督的恩神的爱圣灵的交通与你们众人同在林后十三14这是三一神将祂一切的所是施作涌流流通输送传输并分赐到我们里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ and the love of God and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all 2 Cor 1314 this is the Triune God working flowing communicating transporting transmitting and dispensing all that He is into us"}
{"zh": "一\t我们有子神的恩典、父神的爱和灵神的交通；这是借着父的爱、子的恩、那灵的交通，分赐到我们里面的三一神—14节，提前二5。", "en": "A. We have the grace of God the Son, the love of God the Father, and the fellowship of God the Spirit; this is the Triune God dispensed into us by the Father's love, the Son's grace, and the Spirit's fellowship—v. 14; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "一我们有子神的恩典父神的爱和灵神的交通这是借着父的爱子的恩哪灵的交通分赐到我们里面的三一神14节提前二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We have the grace of God the Son the love of God the Father and the fellowship of God the Spirit this is the Triune God dispensed into us by the Fathers love the Sons grace and the Spirits fellowshipv 14 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典就是三一神把东西赐给我们，并在我们里面行事；我们绝不该信靠自己，因为我们不能给什么，也不能作什么；但耶稣有许多可给的，祂在我们里面也能作许多事；这就是恩典—林后十三14，提前二5。", "en": "B. Grace is simply the Triune God giving things to us and doing things within us; we should never trust in ourselves, for we can give nothing and can do nothing; but Jesus has much to give, and He can do much in us; this is grace—2 Cor. 13:14; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "二恩典就是三一神把东西赐给我们并在我们里面行事我们绝不该信靠自己因为我们不能给什么也不能作什么但耶稣有许多可给的祂在我们里面也能作许多事这就是恩典林后十三14提前二5", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace is simply the Triune God giving things to us and doing things within us we should never trust in ourselves for we can give nothing and can do nothing but Jesus has much to give and He can do much in us this is grace2 Cor 1314 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "捌\t主耶稣的恩不是与我们的心思同在，也不是与我们的心同在，乃是与我们的灵同在；所以，让我们转向我们的灵，并呼求，“哦，主耶稣，哦，主耶稣，”借此接受恩典；祂的恩典够我们用的—加六18，来十二28。", "en": "VIII. The grace of the Lord Jesus is not with our mind, nor is it with our heart; it is with our spirit; therefore, let us have grace by turning to our spirit and calling, \"O Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus\"; His grace is sufficient for us—Gal. 6:18; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "捌主耶稣的恩不是与我们的心思同在也不是与我们的心同在乃是与我们的灵同在所以让我们转向我们的灵并呼求哦主耶稣哦主耶稣借此接受恩典祂的恩典够我们用的加六18来十二28", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The grace of the Lord Jesus is not with our mind nor is it with our heart it is with our spirit therefore let us have grace by turning to our spirit and calling O Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus His grace is sufficient for usGal 618 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "恩典是一个人位", "en": "Grace is a person", "norm_zh": "恩典是一个人位", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Grace is a person"}
{"zh": "恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的，以及这奇妙人位所成就的", "en": "Grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person", "norm_zh": "恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的以及这奇妙人位所成就的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person"}
{"zh": "恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会", "en": "Grace should be seen in all our church meetings", "norm_zh": "恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Grace should be seen in all our church meetings"}
{"zh": "耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面，并借着保罗成就许多事", "en": "Jesus imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paul", "norm_zh": "耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面并借着保罗成就许多事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jesus imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paul"}
{"zh": "我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己，乃信靠神的恩", "en": "We all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God", "norm_zh": "我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己乃信靠神的恩", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:03:46.531063+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God"}
{"zh": "壹\t行传四章三十三节，“使徒大有能力，见证主耶稣的复活，众人也都蒙大恩”；说这恩是基督，太简单了；这不仅仅是基督，乃是行动的基督、作工的基督、掌权的基督、使人信服的基督、征服一切的基督、施行拯救的基督、和将人拔高的基督：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "I. Acts 4:33, \"With great power the apostles gave testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus, and great grace was upon them all\"; to say that this grace was Christ is too simple; it was not merely Christ but Christ moving, Christ working, Christ reigning, Christ convincing, Christ subduing, Christ saving, and Christ uplifting:", "norm_zh": "壹行传四章三十三节使徒大有能力见证主耶稣的复活众人也都蒙大恩说这恩是基督太简单了这不仅仅是基督乃是行动的基督作工的基督掌权的基督使人信服的基督征服一切的基督施行拯救的基督和将人拔高的基督李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Acts 433 With great power the apostles gave testimony of the resurrection of the Lord Jesus and great grace was upon them all to say that this grace was Christ is too simple it was not merely Christ but Christ moving Christ working Christ reigning Christ convincing Christ subduing Christ saving and Christ uplifting"}
{"zh": "一\t首先，我们必然看见恩典是一个人位，神圣而属人的人位，这一个人位既神圣又属人；这人位原在永远里，而后进入时间里；祂成了人，活在地上，死于十字架，从死人中复活，升上诸天，并且登宝座、得荣耀、且受托以宇宙中所有的权柄（太二八18）；这样的人位作为恩典降临，眷临祂所有的信徒。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. First, of course, we see that grace is a person, a divine-human person, a person who is divine as well as human; this person was in eternity, and He came into time; He became a man who lived on the earth, died on the cross, rose from the dead, ascended into the heavens, and was enthroned, glorified, and entrusted with all the authority in the universe (Matt. 28:18); such a person came down as grace to visit all His believers.", "norm_zh": "一首先我们必然看见恩典是一个人位神圣而属人的人位这一个人位既神圣又属人这人位原在永远里而后进入时间里祂成了人活在地上死于十字架从死人中复活升上诸天并且登宝座得荣耀且受托以宇宙中所有的权柄太二八18这样的人位作为恩典降临眷临祂所有的信徒李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A First of course we see that grace is a person a divinehuman person a person who is divine as well as human this person was in eternity and He came into time He became a man who lived on the earth died on the cross rose from the dead ascended into the heavens and was enthroned glorified and entrusted with all the authority in the universe Matt 2818 such a person came down as grace to visit all His believers"}
{"zh": "二\t我们能看见，恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的，以及这奇妙人位所成就的—林后十二9，林前十五10。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. We can see that grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person—2 Cor. 12:9; 1 Cor. 15:10.", "norm_zh": "二我们能看见恩典也是这奇妙人位所赐给的以及这奇妙人位所成就的林后十二9林前十五10李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We can see that grace is also something given by this wonderful person and something done by this wonderful person2 Cor 129 1 Cor 1510"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩典能产生一种情况，在其中恩典能被人看见—徒十一23，林前十四25：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "II. Grace is able to produce a situation in which grace can be seen by people—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25:", "norm_zh": "贰恩典能产生一种情况在其中恩典能被人看见徒十一23林前十四25李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Grace is able to produce a situation in which grace can be seen by peopleActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "一\t巴拿巴来到安提阿，在那里看见神的恩典；有犹太信徒和外邦信徒来在一起赞美神，并且在基督里是一—徒十一23，林前十四25。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. Barnabas came to Antioch, and there he saw the grace of God; the Jewish believers and the Gentiles believers had come together to praise God and to be one in Christ—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "一巴拿巴来到安提阿在哪里看见神的恩典有犹太信徒和外邦信徒来在一起赞美神并且在基督里是一徒十一23林前十四25李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Barnabas came to Antioch and there he saw the grace of God the Jewish believers and the Gentiles believers had come together to praise God and to be one in ChristActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "二\t倘若我们是外人，来到在安提阿的召会，就和巴拿巴一样，看见许多脸发光，许多口赞美神，我们只能说，“恩典，恩典！”看见恩典是美妙的；恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会—徒十一23，林前十四25。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. If we came to the church in Antioch as a stranger, as Barnabas did, and saw many faces glowing with many mouths praising God, we could only say, \"Grace, Grace!\"; it is wonderful to see grace; grace should be seen in all our church meetings—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "二倘若我们是外人来到在安提阿的召会就和巴拿巴一样看见许多脸发光许多口赞美神我们只能说恩典恩典看见恩典是美妙的恩典应当见于我们所有的召会聚会徒十一23林前十四25李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B If we came to the church in Antioch as a stranger as Barnabas did and saw many faces glowing with many mouths praising God we could only say Grace Grace it is wonderful to see grace grace should be seen in all our church meetingsActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "三\t或许你很受压，感觉非常低落；你可能来到召会的聚会中，就发觉满了恩典；然后你也许开始深深感觉，有东西流进你里面；若是这样，你就会得着安慰、鼓励和盼望—徒十一23，林前十四25。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "C. Perhaps you are depressed and feel very low; you may come to a meeting of the church and find that it is full of grace; then you may begin to have the deep sensation that something is flowing into you; if this is the case, you will receive comfort, encouragement, and hope—Acts 11:23; 1 Cor. 14:25.", "norm_zh": "三或许你很受压感觉非常低落你可能来到召会的聚会中就发觉满了恩典然后你也许开始深深感觉有东西流进你里面若是这样你就会得着安慰鼓励和盼望徒十一23林前十四25李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Perhaps you are depressed and feel very low you may come to a meeting of the church and find that it is full of grace then you may begin to have the deep sensation that something is flowing into you if this is the case you will receive comfort encouragement and hopeActs 1123 1 Cor 1425"}
{"zh": "四\t真实的恩典就是耶稣自己；祂不计任何代价的为我们行事，祂也不计代价的把东西赐给我们；恩典就是耶稣连同祂恩典的作为和祂恩典的赐给—约一14、16~17。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "D. The real grace is Jesus Himself; He does things for us without any cost, and He gives things to us without any cost; grace is Jesus with His gracious doing and His gracious giving—John 1:14, 16-17.", "norm_zh": "四真实的恩典就是耶稣自己祂不计任何代价的为我们行事祂也不计代价的把东西赐给我们恩典就是耶稣连同祂恩典的作为和祂恩典的赐给约一141617李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D The real grace is Jesus Himself He does things for us without any cost and He gives things to us without any cost grace is Jesus with His gracious doing and His gracious givingJohn 114 1617"}
{"zh": "叁\t行传十五章四十节说，“保罗却拣选了西拉，也出去，蒙弟兄们把他交与主的恩典”：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "III. Acts 15:40 says, \"But Paul chose Silas and went out, having been commended to the grace of the Lord by the brothers\":", "norm_zh": "叁行传十五章四十节说保罗却拣选了西拉也出去蒙弟兄们把他交与主的恩典李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Acts 1540 says But Paul chose Silas and went out having been commended to the grace of the Lord by the brothers"}
{"zh": "一\t无论保罗往那里去，主耶稣都与他同在，一直给与、扶持、分授、供应，并借着保罗作许多事；那就是恩典—40节，弗三8。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. Wherever Paul went, the Lord Jesus was with him, giving, supporting, imparting, supplying, and doing many things through Paul; that was grace—v. 40; Eph. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "一无论保罗往哪里去主耶稣都与他同在一直给与扶持分授供应并借着保罗作许多事哪就是恩典40节弗三8李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Wherever Paul went the Lord Jesus was with him giving supporting imparting supplying and doing many things through Paul that was gracev 40 Eph 38"}
{"zh": "二\t保罗作工，不是凭着他的教育、才能或智慧，乃是凭着神的恩典；这意思就是，保罗凭着一个奇妙的人位耶稣，作了一切奇妙的工作；耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面，并借着保罗成就许多事—8节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. Paul worked not by his education, his ability, or his wisdom but by the grace of God; this simply means that Paul did all his wonderful work by a wonderful person, Jesus, who imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paul.—v. 8.", "norm_zh": "二保罗作工不是凭着他的教育才能或智慧乃是凭着神的恩典这意思就是保罗凭着一个奇妙的人位耶稣作了一切奇妙的工作耶稣将祂一切的丰富分授到保罗里面并借着保罗成就许多事8节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Paul worked not by his education his ability or his wisdom but by the grace of God this simply means that Paul did all his wonderful work by a wonderful person Jesus who imparted all His riches into Paul and accomplished much through Paulv 8"}
{"zh": "三\t我们没有借口；我们都必须尽功用，因为基督的恩典是够用的；我们不但该学习说，“不再是我，乃是基督，”也该说，“不是我，乃是恩典”；我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己，乃信靠神的恩—林前十五10，加二20。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "C. We have no excuse; we all must function because the grace of Christ is sufficient; we should learn to say not only \"No longer I but Christ\" but also \"Not I but grace\"; we all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God.—1 Cor. 15:10; Gal. 2:20.", "norm_zh": "三我们没有借口我们都必须尽功用因为基督的恩典是够用的我们不但该学习说不再是我乃是基督也该说不是我乃是恩典我们都必须学习不信靠我们自己乃信靠神的恩林前十五10加二20李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We have no excuse we all must function because the grace of Christ is sufficient we should learn to say not only No longer I but Christ but also Not I but grace we all must learn not to trust in ourselves but in the grace of God1 Cor 1510 Gal 220"}
{"zh": "肆\t保罗说恩典洋溢，恩典也作王掌权；恩典若不是一个人位，怎能作王掌权？赞美主，恩典是王—罗五20~21：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "IV. Paul says that grace has abounded and that grace reigns as a king; if grace were not a person, how could grace reign as a king? Praise the Lord that grace is a king.—Rom. 5:20-21:", "norm_zh": "肆保罗说恩典洋溢恩典也作王掌权恩典若不是一个人位怎能作王掌权赞美主恩典是王罗五2021李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Paul says that grace has abounded and that grace reigns as a king if grace were not a person how could grace reign as a king Praise the Lord that grace is a kingRom 52021"}
{"zh": "一\t恩典作王管理撒但，管理罪，管理肉体，管理死，并管理宇宙中一切消极的事物；所以，恩典无疑就是主耶稣，也是耶稣这活的人位，赐给我们所需要的一切，并作成神所要求的一切—20~21节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. Grace reigns over Satan, over sin, over the flesh, over death, and over all the negative things in the universe; therefore, grace is no doubt the Lord Jesus, and it is also Jesus, the living person, giving us whatever we need and doing whatever God requires.—vv. 20-21.", "norm_zh": "一恩典作王管理撒但管理罪管理肉体管理死并管理宇宙中一切消极的事物所以恩典无疑就是主耶稣也是耶稣这活的人位赐给我们所需要的一切并作成神所要求的一切2021节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Grace reigns over Satan over sin over the flesh over death and over all the negative things in the universe therefore grace is no doubt the Lord Jesus and it is also Jesus the living person giving us whatever we need and doing whatever God requiresvv 2021"}
{"zh": "二\t神说，人若犯罪就必死（一32，六23上）；但基督来为我们死（五8）；这是耶稣恩典的作为；我们因恩典，因耶稣恩典的作为得称义。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. God says that if man sins, he must die (1:32; 6:23a); but Christ came and died for us (5:8); this is the gracious doing of Jesus; we have been justified by grace, by the gracious doing of Jesus.", "norm_zh": "二神说人若犯罪就必死一32六23上但基督来为我们死五8这是耶稣恩典的作为我们因恩典因耶稣恩典的作为得称义李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God says that if man sins he must die 132 623a but Christ came and died for us 58 this is the gracious doing of Jesus we have been justified by grace by the gracious doing of Jesus"}
{"zh": "三\t我们呼求主，就经历甜美的享受，并且我们呼求祂，祂就成为我们里面的恩典无论我们需要什么，祂都供应；无论神要求我们什么，祂都应付；我们只需要作一件事：享受恩典—哀三55。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "C. When we call on the Lord, we experience a sweet enjoyment, and as we call on Him, He becomes grace within us; whatever we need, He supplies; whatever God requires of us, He meets that requirement; all we need to do is enjoy grace.—Lam. 3:55.", "norm_zh": "三我们呼求主就经历甜美的享受并且我们呼求祂祂就成为我们里面的恩典无论我们需要什么祂都供应无论神要求我们什么祂都应付我们只需要作一件事享受恩典哀三55李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C When we call on the Lord we experience a sweet enjoyment and as we call on Him He becomes grace within us whatever we need He supplies whatever God requires of us He meets that requirement all we need to do is enjoy graceLam 355"}
{"zh": "伍\t最后，罗马书告诉我们，属灵的恩赐是照着恩典赐给我们的—十二6，林前十五9~10：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "V. Finally, the book of Romans tells us that the spiritual gifts are given to us according to grace.—Rom. 12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10:", "norm_zh": "伍最后罗马书告诉我们属灵的恩赐是照着恩典赐给我们的十二6林前十五910李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V Finally the book of Romans tells us that the spiritual gifts are given to us according to graceRom 126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "一\t我们享受越多恩典，就得着越多恩赐；我们若在恩典上贫穷，在恩赐上也必然贫穷—罗十二6，林前十五9~10。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. The more grace we enjoy, the more gifts we will have; if we are poor in grace, surely we will be poor in gifts.—Rom. 12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10.", "norm_zh": "一我们享受越多恩典就得着越多恩赐我们若在恩典上贫穷在恩赐上也必然贫穷罗十二6林前十五910李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A The more grace we enjoy the more gifts we will have if we are poor in grace surely we will be poor in giftsRom 126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "二\t这些恩赐不是来自我们的教育，也不是来自我们在圣经学校或神学院里的学习；这些恩赐来自恩典；我们越享受恩典，就越有出于这恩典的属灵恩赐；我们越享受基督的恩典，就越能为基督说话，并为祂行事—罗十二6，林前十五9~10。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. These gifts do not come from our education or from our learning in a Bible school or a seminary; these gifts come from grace; the more we enjoy grace, the more we will have spiritual gifts out of this grace; the more we enjoy the grace of Christ, the more we will be able to speak for Christ and do something for Him.—Rom. 12:6; 1 Cor. 15:9-10.", "norm_zh": "二这些恩赐不是来自我们的教育也不是来自我们在圣经学校或神学院里的学习这些恩赐来自恩典我们越享受恩典就越有出于这恩典的属灵恩赐我们越享受基督的恩典就越能为基督说话并为祂行事罗十二6林前十五910李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B These gifts do not come from our education or from our learning in a Bible school or a seminary these gifts come from grace the more we enjoy grace the more we will have spiritual gifts out of this grace the more we enjoy the grace of Christ the more we will be able to speak for Christ and do something for HimRom 126 1 Cor 15910"}
{"zh": "陆\t保罗三次祷告主除去他肉体上的刺，但主告诉他，祂不会除去；反之，保罗必须学习享受祂够用的恩典—林后十二7~9：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "VI. Paul prayed three times that the Lord would take away the thorn in his flesh, but the Lord told him that He would not take it away; instead, Paul had to learn to enjoy His sufficient grace.—2 Cor. 12:7-9:", "norm_zh": "陆保罗三次祷告主除去他肉体上的刺但主告诉他祂不会除去反之保罗必须学习享受祂够用的恩典林后十二79李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Paul prayed three times that the Lord would take away the thorn in his flesh but the Lord told him that He would not take it away instead Paul had to learn to enjoy His sufficient grace2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "一\t也许你的妻子对你是一根刺，但她是宝贵的刺，因为她帮助你享受基督；你不需要祷告求主把刺除去；祂绝不会那样作—7~9节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. It may be that your wife is a thorn to you, but she is a precious thorn because she helps you to enjoy Christ; there is no need for you to pray that the Lord will take away the thorn; He will never do that—vv. 7-9.", "norm_zh": "一也许你的妻子对你是一根刺但她是宝贵的刺因为她帮助你享受基督你不需要祷告求主把刺除去祂绝不会哪样作79节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A It may be that your wife is a thorn to you but she is a precious thorn because she helps you to enjoy Christ there is no need for you to pray that the Lord will take away the thorn He will never do thatvv 79"}
{"zh": "二\t反之，祂会说，“我的恩典是够用的。刺帮助你享受我的恩典，因为我的能力，是在你的软弱上显得完全”；这是主耶稣够用的恩典—7~9节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. Instead, He will say, \"My grace is sufficient. The thorn helps you to enjoy My grace, for My power is perfected in your weakness\"; this is the sufficient grace of the Lord Jesus—vv. 7-9.", "norm_zh": "二反之祂会说我的恩典是够用的刺帮助你享受我的恩典因为我的能力是在你的软弱上显得完全这是主耶稣够用的恩典79节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Instead He will say My grace is sufficient The thorn helps you to enjoy My grace for My power is perfected in your weakness this is the sufficient grace of the Lord Jesusvv 79"}
{"zh": "柒\t“愿主耶稣基督的恩，神的爱，圣灵的交通，与你们众人同在”（林后十三14）；这是三一神将祂一切的所是施作、涌流、流通、输送、传输、并分赐到我们里面：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "VII. \"The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ and the love of God and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all\" (2 Cor. 13:14); this is the Triune God working, flowing, communicating, transporting, transmitting, and dispensing all that He is into us:", "norm_zh": "柒愿主耶稣基督的恩神的爱圣灵的交通与你们众人同在林后十三14这是三一神将祂一切的所是施作涌流流通输送传输并分赐到我们里面李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VII The grace of the Lord Jesus Christ and the love of God and the fellowship of the Holy Spirit be with you all 2 Cor 1314 this is the Triune God working flowing communicating transporting transmitting and dispensing all that He is into us"}
{"zh": "一\t我们有子神的恩典、父神的爱和灵神的交通；这是借着父的爱、子的恩、那灵的交通，分赐到我们里面的三一神—14节，提前二5。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "A. We have the grace of God the Son, the love of God the Father, and the fellowship of God the Spirit; this is the Triune God dispensed into us by the Father's love, the Son's grace, and the Spirit's fellowship—v. 14; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "一我们有子神的恩典父神的爱和灵神的交通这是借着父的爱子的恩哪灵的交通分赐到我们里面的三一神14节提前二5李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We have the grace of God the Son the love of God the Father and the fellowship of God the Spirit this is the Triune God dispensed into us by the Fathers love the Sons grace and the Spirits fellowshipv 14 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典就是三一神把东西赐给我们，并在我们里面行事；我们绝不该信靠自己，因为我们不能给什么，也不能作什么；但耶稣有许多可给的，祂在我们里面也能作许多事；这就是恩典—林后十三14，提前二5。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "B. Grace is simply the Triune God giving things to us and doing things within us; we should never trust in ourselves, for we can give nothing and can do nothing; but Jesus has much to give, and He can do much in us; this is grace—2 Cor. 13:14; 1 Tim. 2:5.", "norm_zh": "二恩典就是三一神把东西赐给我们并在我们里面行事我们绝不该信靠自己因为我们不能给什么也不能作什么但耶稣有许多可给的祂在我们里面也能作许多事这就是恩典林后十三14提前二5李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace is simply the Triune God giving things to us and doing things within us we should never trust in ourselves for we can give nothing and can do nothing but Jesus has much to give and He can do much in us this is grace2 Cor 1314 1 Tim 25"}
{"zh": "捌\t主耶稣的恩不是与我们的心思同在，也不是与我们的心同在，乃是与我们的灵同在；所以，让我们转向我们的灵，并呼求，“哦，主耶稣，哦，主耶稣，”借此接受恩典；祂的恩典够我们用的—加六18，来十二28。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第二章）", "en": "VIII. The grace of the Lord Jesus is not with our mind, nor is it with our heart. It is with our spirit; therefore, let us have grace by turning to our spirit and calling, \"O Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus\"; His grace is sufficient for us—Gal. 6:18; Heb. 12:28.", "norm_zh": "捌主耶稣的恩不是与我们的心思同在也不是与我们的心同在乃是与我们的灵同在所以让我们转向我们的灵并呼求哦主耶稣哦主耶稣借此接受恩典祂的恩典够我们用的加六18来十二28李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第二章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:07:00.340399+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VIII The grace of the Lord Jesus is not with our mind nor is it with our heart It is with our spirit therefore let us have grace by turning to our spirit and calling O Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus His grace is sufficient for usGal 618 Heb 1228"}
{"zh": "读经：约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后十二7~9，林前一30，西三11，彼后一2、3", "en": "Scripture Reading: John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 12:7-9; 1 Cor. 1:30; Col. 3:11; 2 Pet. 1:2-3", "norm_zh": "读经约一141617赛五五1林后十二79林前一30西三11彼后一23", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading John 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 1279 1 Cor 130 Col 311 2 Pet 123"}
{"zh": "壹\t基督是那赐给我们作恩典的奇妙人位；但恩典不仅仅是这奇妙的人位自己；恩典是这奇妙人位，也是祂的作为—约一14、16~17，赛五五1：", "en": "I. Christ is the wonderful person given to us as grace; but grace is not simply this wonderful person Himself; grace is this wonderful person as well as His doing—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1:", "norm_zh": "壹基督是哪赐给我们作恩典的奇妙人位但恩典不仅仅是这奇妙的人位自己恩典是这奇妙人位也是祂的作为约一141617赛五五1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Christ is the wonderful person given to us as grace but grace is not simply this wonderful person Himself grace is this wonderful person as well as His doingJohn 114 1617 Isa 551"}
{"zh": "一\t祂将自己赐给了我们，现今祂在为我们作许多事；在许多事上我们无法背负担子，但基督为我们背负担子；这样背负我们的担子，就是恩典—林后十二7~9。", "en": "A. He has given Himself to us, and now He is doing many things for us; in many things we cannot bear the burden, but Christ bears the burden for us; this bearing of our burden is grace—2 Cor. 12:7-9.", "norm_zh": "一祂将自己赐给了我们现今祂在为我们作许多事在许多事上我们无法背负担子但基督为我们背负担子这样背负我们的担子就是恩典林后十二79", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A He has given Himself to us and now He is doing many things for us in many things we cannot bear the burden but Christ bears the burden for us this bearing of our burden is grace2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "二\t我们常常有无法解决的难处，但我们里面的基督解决那难处；这就是恩典—7~9节，参一12、15。", "en": "B. Many times we have a problem that we cannot solve, but Christ within us solves the problem; this is grace—vv. 7-9; cf. 1:12, 15.", "norm_zh": "二我们常常有无法解决的难处但我们里面的基督解决哪难处这就是恩典79节参一1215", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Many times we have a problem that we cannot solve but Christ within us solves the problem this is gracevv 79 cf 112 15"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩典也是这神圣人位的赐给；祂一直把属于祂自己的东西赐给我们；日复一日，我们该享受主的赐给；若不然，我们就错失了主的恩典—林后十二7~9，林前一30：", "en": "IV. Grace is also the giving of this divine person; He is constantly giving us something of Himself; day by day we should be enjoying the Lord's giving; if we are not, we are missing the grace of the Lord—2 Cor. 12:7-9; 1 Cor. 1:30:", "norm_zh": "贰恩典也是这神圣人位的赐给祂一直把属于祂自己的东西赐给我们日复一日我们该享受主的赐给若不然我们就错失了主的恩典林后十二79林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV Grace is also the giving of this divine person He is constantly giving us something of Himself day by day we should be enjoying the Lords giving if we are not we are missing the grace of the Lord2 Cor 1279 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "一\t我们需要为着我们的短缺赞美主，并告诉主，我们没有什么可说；然后祂就会进来赐给，并填满缺口—林后十二7~9。", "en": "A. We need to praise the Lord for our shortage and tell the Lord that we have nothing to say; then He will come in to give us something and fill the gap—2 Cor. 12:7-9.", "norm_zh": "一我们需要为着我们的短缺赞美主并告诉主我们没有什么可说然后祂就会进来赐给并填满缺口林后十二79", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We need to praise the Lord for our shortage and tell the Lord that we have nothing to say then He will come in to give us something and fill the gap2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "二\t唯一使我们能享受祂赐给的路，见于罗马十章十二节，这节说，“众人同有一位主，祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的”；我们越呼求主的名，就越享受祂的恩典。", "en": "B. The only way we can enjoy His giving is found in Rom. 10:12, which says, \"The same Lord is... rich to all who call upon Him.\"; the more we call on the Lord's name, the more we enjoy His grace.", "norm_zh": "二惟一使我们能享受祂赐给的路见于罗马十章十二节这节说众人同有一位主祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们越呼求主的名就越享受祂的恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The only way we can enjoy His giving is found in Rom 1012 which says The same Lord is rich to all who call upon Him the more we call on the Lords name the more we enjoy His grace"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事—西三11，林前一30：", "en": "III. The Christian life is altogether a matter of grace—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30:", "norm_zh": "叁基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事西三11林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The Christian life is altogether a matter of graceCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "一\t我们没有忍耐，但当我们说“主耶稣，我没有忍耐”的时候，祂就成为我们里面的忍耐；这样，我们就享受祂作忍耐—西三11，林前一30。", "en": "A. We have no patience, but when we say, \"Lord Jesus, I have no patience,\" He becomes the patience within us; in this way we enjoy Him as patience—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "一我们没有忍耐但当我们说主耶稣我没有忍耐的时候祂就成为我们里面的忍耐这样我们就享受祂作忍耐西三11林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We have no patience but when we say Lord Jesus I have no patience He becomes the patience within us in this way we enjoy Him as patienceCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "二\t凡我们所能作的，都不是恩典；凡我们所有，可以运用并应用在我们情况里的，都不是恩典；唯在我们什么也不能作的时候，主才供应恩典—西三11，林前一30。", "en": "B. Whatever we can do is not grace; whatever we have to use and apply in our situation is not grace; grace is supplied only when we cannot do anything—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "二凡我们所能作的都不是恩典凡我们所有可以运用并应用在我们情况里的都不是恩典惟在我们什么也不能作的时候主才供应恩典西三11林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Whatever we can do is not grace whatever we have to use and apply in our situation is not grace grace is supplied only when we cannot do anythingCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "三\t唯在我们没有什么可应用，没有什么可运用，一切都短缺的时候，恩典才给我们取用；那时我们才会祷告：“主耶稣，我一无所有，一无所能”；我们这样祷告，主耶稣就会为我们行事，并且无论我们需要什么，祂都会赐给我们；这就是基督徒生活—西三11，林前一30。", "en": "C. It is only when we have nothing to apply, nothing to use, and are short of everything that grace is available; it is then that we will pray, \"Lord Jesus, I have nothing, and I can do nothing\"; when we pray in this way, the Lord Jesus will do things for us, and He will give us whatever we need; this is the Christian life—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "三惟在我们没有什么可应用没有什么可运用一切都短缺的时候恩典才给我们取用哪时我们才会祷告主耶稣我一无所有一无所能我们这样祷告主耶稣就会为我们行事并且无论我们需要什么祂都会赐给我们这就是基督徒生活西三11林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It is only when we have nothing to apply nothing to use and are short of everything that grace is available it is then that we will pray Lord Jesus I have nothing and I can do nothing when we pray in this way the Lord Jesus will do things for us and He will give us whatever we need this is the Christian lifeCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "四\t恩典就是奇妙的基督作我们的一切，赐给我们一切，并为我们作一切；我们不需要别的；除了基督同祂一切的赐给和作为，我们一无所需—西三11，林前一30。", "en": "D. Grace is the wonderful Christ being everything to us, giving everything to us, and doing everything for us; we have no other need; we need nothing but Christ with all His giving and doing.—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "四恩典就是奇妙的基督作我们的一切赐给我们一切并为我们作一切我们不需要别的除了基督同祂一切的赐给和作为我们一无所需西三11林前一30", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Grace is the wonderful Christ being everything to us giving everything to us and doing everything for us we have no other need we need nothing but Christ with all His giving and doingCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "肆\t彼得在他的书信中告诉我们，恩典应当繁增；他说，“愿恩典与平安，因你们充分认识神和我们的主耶稣，繁增的归与你们”（彼后一2）；在三章十八节，他也告诉我们：“要在……恩典……上长大”：", "en": "IV. In his Epistles Peter tells us that grace should be multiplied; he says, \"Grace to you and peace be multiplied in the full knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord\" (2 Pet. 1:2); in 3:18 he also tells us to \"grow in... grace\":", "norm_zh": "肆彼得在他的书信中告诉我们恩典应当繁增他说愿恩典与平安因你们充分认识神和我们的主耶稣繁增的归与你们彼后一2在三章十八节他也告诉我们要在恩典上长大", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In his Epistles Peter tells us that grace should be multiplied he says Grace to you and peace be multiplied in the full knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord 2 Pet 12 in 318 he also tells us to grow in grace"}
{"zh": "一\t我们必须领悟，我们里面有个会长大并繁增的东西；作为神重生的儿女，我们里面有许多奇妙的东西；最要紧的，乃是神自己已分授到我们这人里面；我们已由神而生；这当然就是恩典—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3：", "en": "A. We must realize that we have something within us that can grow and be multiplied; as a born-again child of God, we have many wonderful things in us; the most important is that God Himself has been imparted into our being; we have been begotten of God; surely this is grace.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "一我们必须领悟我们里面有个会长大并繁增的东西作为神重生的儿女我们里面有许多奇妙的东西最要紧的乃是神自己已分授到我们这人里面我们已由神而生这当然就是恩典彼后一2三18彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We must realize that we have something within us that can grow and be multiplied as a bornagain child of God we have many wonderful things in us the most important is that God Himself has been imparted into our being we have been begotten of God surely this is grace2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "1\t我们将自己向主耶稣敞开，就有个东西进入我们里面；一旦这种子进入我们里面，我们就永远摆脱不掉；我们也许想要把它丢弃，但它会留了再留，等候机会；这种子会在我们里面，直到永远—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3。", "en": "1. When we opened ourselves to the Lord Jesus, something got into us; once this seed has come into us, we can never get rid of it; we may try to give it up, but it will stay and stay, waiting for an opportunity; for eternity this seed will be within us.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "1我们将自己向主耶稣敞开就有个东西进入我们里面一旦这种子进入我们里面我们就永远摆脱不掉我们也许想要把它丢弃但它会留了再留等候机会这种子会在我们里面直到永远彼后一2三18彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we opened ourselves to the Lord Jesus something got into us once this seed has come into us we can never get rid of it we may try to give it up but it will stay and stay waiting for an opportunity for eternity this seed will be within us2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "2\t彼得说，我们蒙了重生，是由于不能坏的种子，这种子就是神活而常存的话；这活而常存的话就是神自己，神自己就是我们里面不能坏的种子—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3。", "en": "2. Peter says that we have been regenerated of incorruptible seed, which is the living and abiding word of God; this living and abiding word is God Himself; God Himself is the incorruptible seed within us.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "2彼得说我们蒙了重生是由于不能坏的种子这种子就是神活而常存的话这活而常存的话就是神自己神自己就是我们里面不能坏的种子彼后一2三18彼前一3", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Peter says that we have been regenerated of incorruptible seed which is the living and abiding word of God this living and abiding word is God Himself God Himself is the incorruptible seed within us2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "二\t“愿恩典……繁增的归与你们。神的神能，……已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们”（彼后一2~3）；生命是在里面，而敬虔是外面的彰显；神的能力已将一切关于里面生命和外面敬虔的事，都赐给我们；现今恩典必须基于这神圣能力的赐给而繁增。", "en": "B. \"Grace to you... be multiplied... seeing that His divine power has granted to us all things which relate to life and godliness\" (2 Pet. 1:2-3); life is something within, and godliness is something as an expression without; all things that relate to life within and godliness without have already been given to us by the divine power; now grace must be multiplied based upon the giving of this divine power.", "norm_zh": "二愿恩典繁增的归与你们神的神能已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们彼后一23生命是在里面而敬虔是外面的彰显神的能力已将一切关于里面生命和外面敬虔的事都赐给我们现今恩典必须基于这神圣能力的赐给而繁增", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace to you be multiplied seeing that His divine power has granted to us all things which relate to life and godliness 2 Pet 123 life is something within and godliness is something as an expression without all things that relate to life within and godliness without have already been given to us by the divine power now grace must be multiplied based upon the giving of this divine power"}
{"zh": "三\t此外，神也赐给我们又宝贵又极大的应许—林后十二9，太二八20：", "en": "C. In addition, we have been given precious and exceedingly great promises.—2 Cor. 12:9; Matt. 28:20:", "norm_zh": "三此外神也赐给我们又宝贵又极大的应许林后十二9太二八20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In addition we have been given precious and exceedingly great promises2 Cor 129 Matt 2820"}
{"zh": "1\t彼得后书一章四节说，“借这荣耀和美德，祂已将又宝贵又极大的应许赐给我们，叫你们既逃离世上从情欲来的败坏，就借着这些应许，得有分于神的性情。”", "en": "1. Second Peter 1:4 says, \"Through which He has granted to us precious and exceedingly great promises, that through these you might become partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption which is in the world by lust.\"", "norm_zh": "1彼得后书一章四节说借这荣耀和美德祂已将又宝贵又极大的应许赐给我们叫你们既逃离世上从情欲来的败坏就借着这些应许得有分于神的性情", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Second Peter 14 says Through which He has granted to us precious and exceedingly great promises that through these you might become partakers of the divine nature having escaped the corruption which is in the world by lust"}
{"zh": "2\t旧约和新约里都有许多应许，如“我的恩典够你用的”（林后十二9），以及“看哪，我天天与你们同在，直到这世代的终结”（太二八20）；这些是何等的应许！", "en": "2. There are many promises in both the Old Testament and the New Testament, such as \"My grace is sufficient for you\" (2 Cor. 12:9) and \"Behold, I am with you all the days until the consummation of the age\" (Matt. 28:20); what promises these are!", "norm_zh": "2旧约和新约里都有许多应许如我的恩典够你用的林后十二9以及看哪我天天与你们同在直到这世代的终结太二八20这些是何等的应许", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 There are many promises in both the Old Testament and the New Testament such as My grace is sufficient for you 2 Cor 129 and Behold I am with you all the days until the consummation of the age Matt 2820 what promises these are"}
{"zh": "3\t“约”字的意思是“遗命”；圣经乃是遗命；不仅仅是合同或契约，乃比这个多得多；立神圣遗命者就是耶稣；祂死了，遗命就生效（太二六28，路二二20）；现今在复活里，祂这赐生命的灵乃是遗命的执行者（林前十五45，来八6，九15）。", "en": "3. The word testament means \"a will\"; the Bible is a will; it is not merely an agreement or a contract; it is much more than this; the maker of the divine will is Jesus; He died so that the will could become effective (Matt. 26:28; Luke 22:20); now in resurrection He as the life-giving Spirit is the Executor of the will (1 Cor. 15:45; Heb. 8:6; 9:15).", "norm_zh": "3约字的意思是遗命圣经乃是遗命不仅仅是合同或契约乃比这个多得多立神圣遗命者就是耶稣祂死了遗命就生效太二六28路二二20现今在复活里祂这赐生命的灵乃是遗命的执行者林前十五45来八6九15", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The word testament means a will the Bible is a will it is not merely an agreement or a contract it is much more than this the maker of the divine will is Jesus He died so that the will could become effective Matt 2628 Luke 2220 now in resurrection He as the lifegiving Spirit is the Executor of the will 1 Cor 1545 Heb 86 915"}
{"zh": "伍\t除了呼求主名和祷读主话，没有别的路；我们若忠信的这样作，里面就会有属灵的繁增；这就是在恩典上长大—创四26，罗十6~8，弗六17~18：", "en": "V. There is no other way except to call on the name of the Lord and pray-read the Word; if we are faithful to do this, there will be the spiritual multiplication within; this is the growth in grace—Gen. 4:26; Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "伍除了呼求主名和祷读主话没有别的路我们若忠信的这样作里面就会有属灵的繁增这就是在恩典上长大创四26罗十68弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V There is no other way except to call on the name of the Lord and prayread the Word if we are faithful to do this there will be the spiritual multiplication within this is the growth in graceGen 426 Rom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "一\t借着写在遗命里的应许，我们就能有分于神的性情；我们可以翻开遗命的任何一页，简单的把话接受进来—创四26。", "en": "A. Through the promises written in the will, we can be partakers of the divine nature; we can open the will to any page and simply take the word in—Gen. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "一借着写在遗命里的应许我们就能有分于神的性情我们可以翻开遗命的任何一页简单的把话接受进来创四26", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through the promises written in the will we can be partakers of the divine nature we can open the will to any page and simply take the word inGen 426"}
{"zh": "二\t要接受话奶，只有一条路，就是喝；借着我们的喝，话奶就被消化并吸收到我们这人里面，然后成为我们的一部分，恩典也会繁增的归与我们。", "en": "B. There is only one way to take the milk of the word, and that is to drink it; by our drinking the milk of the word, it will be digested and assimilated into our being. Then it will become part of us, and grace will be multiplied to us.", "norm_zh": "二要接受话奶只有一条路就是喝借着我们的喝话奶就被消化并吸收到我们这人里面然后成为我们的一部分恩典也会繁增的归与我们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There is only one way to take the milk of the word and that is to drink it by our drinking the milk of the word it will be digested and assimilated into our being Then it will become part of us and grace will be multiplied to us"}
{"zh": "三\t我们绝不该走宗教的路，学习道理和教训我们必须回到主纯净的路上；祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的；我们要有分于基督的丰富，就必须呼求祂的名，并将祂的话祷告到我们里面；恩典每天都会繁增的归与我们—罗十6~8，弗六17~18。", "en": "C. We should never take the religious way of learning doctrines and teachings; we must come back to the Lord's pure way; He is rich to all who call upon Him; in order to partake of the riches of Christ, we must call on His name and pray His Word into us; every day grace will be multiplied to us—Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "三我们绝不该走宗教的路学习道理和教训我们必须回到主纯净的路上祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们要有分于基督的丰富就必须呼求祂的名并将祂的话祷告到我们里面恩典每天都会繁增的归与我们罗十68弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We should never take the religious way of learning doctrines and teachings we must come back to the Lords pure way He is rich to all who call upon Him in order to partake of the riches of Christ we must call on His name and pray His Word into us every day grace will be multiplied to usRom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "四\t我的妻子也许没有看见我读圣经，但我里面时时在祷读宝贵的应许，并有分于神的性情；这就是为什么我因耶稣奇妙的人位而“疯狂”；我的确经历祂的洋溢之恩；我时时经历祂的赐给、祂的作为、祂的扶持、祂的滋养、祂的顾惜、祂的圣别、祂的炼净、和祂的满足；这就是为什么耶稣这恩典正在我里面繁增—林后五13。", "en": "D. My wife may not see me reading the Bible, but all the time within me I am pray-reading the precious promises and partaking of the divine nature; this is why I am \"crazy\" with the wonderful person of Jesus; I do experience His abounding grace; all the time I experience His giving, His doing, His supporting, His nourishing, His cherishing, His sanctifying, His purifying, and His satisfying; this is why Jesus as grace is being multiplied within me—2 Cor. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "四我的妻子也许没有看见我读圣经但我里面时时在祷读宝贵的应许并有分于神的性情这就是为什么我因耶稣奇妙的人位而疯狂我的确经历祂的洋溢之恩我时时经历祂的赐给祂的作为祂的扶持祂的滋养祂的顾惜祂的圣别祂的炼净和祂的满足这就是为什么耶稣这恩典正在我里面繁增林后五13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D My wife may not see me reading the Bible but all the time within me I am prayreading the precious promises and partaking of the divine nature this is why I am crazy with the wonderful person of Jesus I do experience His abounding grace all the time I experience His giving His doing His supporting His nourishing His cherishing His sanctifying His purifying and His satisfying this is why Jesus as grace is being multiplied within me2 Cor 513"}
{"zh": "陆\t神圣的能力已将每件关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们；宝贵的应许就在遗命里；我们若简单的呼求主名，祷读主话，就会真正经历恩典的繁增；这就是产生真正召会生活的正确基督徒生活—罗十6~8，弗六17~18。", "en": "VI. Everything that relates to life and godliness has been given to us by the divine power; the precious promises are in the will; if we simply call on the name of the Lord and pray-read His Word, we will truly experience the multiplication of grace; this is the proper Christian life that produces the genuine church life—Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "陆神圣的能力已将每件关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们宝贵的应许就在遗命里我们若简单的呼求主名祷读主话就会真正经历恩典的繁增这就是产生真正召会生活的正确基督徒生活罗十68弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Everything that relates to life and godliness has been given to us by the divine power the precious promises are in the will if we simply call on the name of the Lord and prayread His Word we will truly experience the multiplication of grace this is the proper Christian life that produces the genuine church lifeRom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "越有担子，就越有机会经历基督的恩典", "en": "The more burdens we have, the more opportunity there is for us to experience the grace of Christ", "norm_zh": "越有担子就越有机会经历基督的恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The more burdens we have the more opportunity there is for us to experience the grace of Christ"}
{"zh": "我们若缺少什么，这项短缺就是让主供应我们的上好机会", "en": "If we are short of something, this shortage is the best opportunity for the Lord to supply us", "norm_zh": "我们若缺少什么这项短缺就是让主供应我们的上好机会", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "If we are short of something this shortage is the best opportunity for the Lord to supply us"}
{"zh": "我们越呼求主的名，就越享受祂的恩典", "en": "The more we call on the Lord's name, the more we enjoy His grace", "norm_zh": "我们越呼求主的名就越享受祂的恩典", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The more we call on the Lords name the more we enjoy His grace"}
{"zh": "基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事", "en": "The Christian life is altogether a matter of grace", "norm_zh": "基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Christian life is altogether a matter of grace"}
{"zh": "恩典应当繁增", "en": "Grace should be multiplied", "norm_zh": "恩典应当繁增", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Grace should be multiplied"}
{"zh": "呼求祂的名，并将祂的话祷告到我们里面", "en": "Calling on His name and praying His Word into us", "norm_zh": "呼求祂的名并将祂的话祷告到我们里面", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:09:15.615264+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Calling on His name and praying His Word into us"}
{"zh": "壹\t基督是那赐给我们作恩典的奇妙人位；但恩典不仅仅是这奇妙的人位自己；恩典是这奇妙人位，也是祂的作为—约一14、16~17，赛五五1：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "I.\tChrist is the wonderful person given to us as grace; but grace is not simply this wonderful person Himself; grace is this wonderful person as well as His doing—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1:", "norm_zh": "壹基督是哪赐给我们作恩典的奇妙人位但恩典不仅仅是这奇妙的人位自己恩典是这奇妙人位也是祂的作为约一141617赛五五1李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I Christ is the wonderful person given to us as grace but grace is not simply this wonderful person Himself grace is this wonderful person as well as His doingJohn 114 1617 Isa 551"}
{"zh": "一\t祂将自己赐给了我们，现今祂在为我们作许多事；在许多事上我们无法背负担子，但基督为我们背负担子；这样背负我们的担子，就是恩典—林后十二7~9。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "A.\tHe has given Himself to us, and now He is doing many things for us; in many things we cannot bear the burden, but Christ bears the burden for us; this bearing of our burden is grace—2 Cor. 12:7-9.", "norm_zh": "一祂将自己赐给了我们现今祂在为我们作许多事在许多事上我们无法背负担子但基督为我们背负担子这样背负我们的担子就是恩典林后十二79李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A He has given Himself to us and now He is doing many things for us in many things we cannot bear the burden but Christ bears the burden for us this bearing of our burden is grace2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "二\t我们常常有无法解决的难处，但我们里面的基督解决那难处；这就是恩典—7~9节，参一12、15。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "B.\tMany times we have a problem that we cannot solve, but Christ within us solves the problem; this is grace—vv. 7-9; cf. 1:12, 15.", "norm_zh": "二我们常常有无法解决的难处但我们里面的基督解决哪难处这就是恩典79节参一1215李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Many times we have a problem that we cannot solve but Christ within us solves the problem this is gracevv 79 cf 112 15"}
{"zh": "贰\t恩典也是这神圣人位的赐给；祂一直把属于祂自己的东西赐给我们；日复一日，我们该享受主的赐给；若不然，我们就错失了主的恩典—林后十二7~9，林前一30：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "II.\tGrace is also the giving of this divine person; He is constantly giving us something of Himself; day by day we should be enjoying the Lord's giving; if we are not, we are missing the grace of the Lord—2 Cor. 12:7-9; 1 Cor. 1:30:", "norm_zh": "贰恩典也是这神圣人位的赐给祂一直把属于祂自己的东西赐给我们日复一日我们该享受主的赐给若不然我们就错失了主的恩典林后十二79林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II Grace is also the giving of this divine person He is constantly giving us something of Himself day by day we should be enjoying the Lords giving if we are not we are missing the grace of the Lord2 Cor 1279 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "一\t我们需要为着我们的短缺赞美主，并告诉主，我们没有什么可说；然后祂就会进来赐给，并填满缺口—林后十二7~9。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "A.\tWe need to praise the Lord for our shortage and tell the Lord that we have nothing to say; then He will come in to give us something and fill the gap—2 Cor. 12:7-9.", "norm_zh": "一我们需要为着我们的短缺赞美主并告诉主我们没有什么可说然后祂就会进来赐给并填满缺口林后十二79李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We need to praise the Lord for our shortage and tell the Lord that we have nothing to say then He will come in to give us something and fill the gap2 Cor 1279"}
{"zh": "二\t唯一使我们能享受祂赐给的路，见于罗马十章十二节，这节说，“众人同有一位主，祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的”；我们越呼求主的名，就越享受祂的恩典。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "B.\tThe only way we can enjoy His giving is found in Romans 10:12, which says, \"The same Lord is... rich to all who call upon Him\"; the more we call on the Lord's name, the more we enjoy His grace.", "norm_zh": "二惟一使我们能享受祂赐给的路见于罗马十章十二节这节说众人同有一位主祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们越呼求主的名就越享受祂的恩典李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The only way we can enjoy His giving is found in Romans 1012 which says The same Lord is rich to all who call upon Him the more we call on the Lords name the more we enjoy His grace"}
{"zh": "叁\t基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事—西三11，林前一30：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "III.\tThe Christian life is altogether a matter of grace—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30:", "norm_zh": "叁基督徒的生活全然是恩典的事西三11林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The Christian life is altogether a matter of graceCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "一\t我们没有忍耐，但当我们说“主耶稣，我没有忍耐”的时候，祂就成为我们里面的忍耐；这样，我们就享受祂作忍耐—西三11，林前一30。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "A.\tWe have no patience, but when we say, \"Lord Jesus, I have no patience,\" He becomes the patience within us; in this way we enjoy Him as patience—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "一我们没有忍耐但当我们说主耶稣我没有忍耐的时候祂就成为我们里面的忍耐这样我们就享受祂作忍耐西三11林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We have no patience but when we say Lord Jesus I have no patience He becomes the patience within us in this way we enjoy Him as patienceCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "二\t凡我们所能作的，都不是恩典；凡我们所有，可以运用并应用在我们情况里的，都不是恩典；唯在我们什么也不能作的时候，主才供应恩典—西三11，林前一30。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "B.\tWhatever we can do is not grace; whatever we have to use and apply in our situation is not grace; grace is supplied only when we cannot do anything—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "二凡我们所能作的都不是恩典凡我们所有可以运用并应用在我们情况里的都不是恩典惟在我们什么也不能作的时候主才供应恩典西三11林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Whatever we can do is not grace whatever we have to use and apply in our situation is not grace grace is supplied only when we cannot do anythingCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "三\t唯在我们没有什么可应用，没有什么可运用，一切都短缺的时候，恩典才给我们取用；那时我们才会祷告：“主耶稣，我一无所有，一无所能”；我们这样祷告，主耶稣就会为我们行事，并且无论我们需要什么，祂都会赐给我们；这就是基督徒生活—西三11，林前一30。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "C.\tIt is only when we have nothing to apply, nothing to use, and are short of everything that grace is available; it is then that we will pray, \"Lord Jesus, I have nothing, and I can do nothing\"; when we pray in this way, the Lord Jesus will do things for us, and He will give us whatever we need; this is the Christian life—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "三惟在我们没有什么可应用没有什么可运用一切都短缺的时候恩典才给我们取用哪时我们才会祷告主耶稣我一无所有一无所能我们这样祷告主耶稣就会为我们行事并且无论我们需要什么祂都会赐给我们这就是基督徒生活西三11林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C It is only when we have nothing to apply nothing to use and are short of everything that grace is available it is then that we will pray Lord Jesus I have nothing and I can do nothing when we pray in this way the Lord Jesus will do things for us and He will give us whatever we need this is the Christian lifeCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "四\t恩典就是奇妙的基督作我们的一切，赐给我们一切，并为我们作一切；我们不需要别的；除了基督同祂一切的赐给和作为，我们一无所需—西三11，林前一30。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "D. Grace is the wonderful Christ being everything to us, giving everything to us, and doing everything for us; we have no other need; we need nothing but Christ with all His giving and doing.—Col. 3:11; 1 Cor. 1:30.", "norm_zh": "四恩典就是奇妙的基督作我们的一切赐给我们一切并为我们作一切我们不需要别的除了基督同祂一切的赐给和作为我们一无所需西三11林前一30李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Grace is the wonderful Christ being everything to us giving everything to us and doing everything for us we have no other need we need nothing but Christ with all His giving and doingCol 311 1 Cor 130"}
{"zh": "肆\t彼得在他的书信中告诉我们，恩典应当繁增；他说，“愿恩典与平安，因你们充分认识神和我们的主耶稣，繁增的归与你们”（彼后一2）；在三章十八节，他也告诉我们：“要在……恩典……上长大”：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "IV. In his Epistles Peter tells us that grace should be multiplied; he says, \"Grace to you and peace be multiplied in the full knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord\" (2 Pet. 1:2); in 3:18 he also tells us to \"grow in... grace\":", "norm_zh": "肆彼得在他的书信中告诉我们恩典应当繁增他说愿恩典与平安因你们充分认识神和我们的主耶稣繁增的归与你们彼后一2在三章十八节他也告诉我们要在恩典上长大李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV In his Epistles Peter tells us that grace should be multiplied he says Grace to you and peace be multiplied in the full knowledge of God and of Jesus our Lord 2 Pet 12 in 318 he also tells us to grow in grace"}
{"zh": "一\t我们必须领悟，我们里面有个会长大并繁增的东西；作为神重生的儿女，我们里面有许多奇妙的东西；最要紧的，乃是神自己已分授到我们这人里面；我们已由神而生；这当然就是恩典—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "A. We must realize that we have something within us that can grow and be multiplied; as a born-again child of God, we have many wonderful things in us; the most important is that God Himself has been imparted into our being; we have been begotten of God; surely this is grace.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3:", "norm_zh": "一我们必须领悟我们里面有个会长大并繁增的东西作为神重生的儿女我们里面有许多奇妙的东西最要紧的乃是神自己已分授到我们这人里面我们已由神而生这当然就是恩典彼后一2三18彼前一3李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We must realize that we have something within us that can grow and be multiplied as a bornagain child of God we have many wonderful things in us the most important is that God Himself has been imparted into our being we have been begotten of God surely this is grace2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "1\t我们将自己向主耶稣敞开，就有个东西进入我们里面；一旦这种子进入我们里面，我们就永远摆脱不掉；我们也许想要把它丢弃，但它会留了再留，等候机会；这种子会在我们里面，直到永远—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "1. When we opened ourselves to the Lord Jesus, something got into us; once this seed has come into us, we can never get rid of it; we may try to give it up, but it will stay and stay, waiting for an opportunity; for eternity this seed will be within us.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "1我们将自己向主耶稣敞开就有个东西进入我们里面一旦这种子进入我们里面我们就永远摆脱不掉我们也许想要把它丢弃但它会留了再留等候机会这种子会在我们里面直到永远彼后一2三18彼前一3李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we opened ourselves to the Lord Jesus something got into us once this seed has come into us we can never get rid of it we may try to give it up but it will stay and stay waiting for an opportunity for eternity this seed will be within us2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "2\t彼得说，我们蒙了重生，是由于不能坏的种子，这种子就是神活而常存的话；这活而常存的话就是神自己，神自己就是我们里面不能坏的种子—彼后一2，三18，彼前一3。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "2. Peter says that we have been regenerated of incorruptible seed, which is the living and abiding word of God; this living and abiding word is God Himself; God Himself is the incorruptible seed within us.—2 Pet. 1:2; 3:18; 1 Pet. 1:3.", "norm_zh": "2彼得说我们蒙了重生是由于不能坏的种子这种子就是神活而常存的话这活而常存的话就是神自己神自己就是我们里面不能坏的种子彼后一2三18彼前一3李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Peter says that we have been regenerated of incorruptible seed which is the living and abiding word of God this living and abiding word is God Himself God Himself is the incorruptible seed within us2 Pet 12 318 1 Pet 13"}
{"zh": "二\t“愿恩典……繁增的归与你们。神的神能，……已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们”（彼后一2~3）；生命是在里面，而敬虔是外面的彰显；神的能力已将一切关于里面生命和外面敬虔的事，都赐给我们；现今恩典必须基于这神圣能力的赐给而繁增。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "B. \"Grace to you... be multiplied... seeing that His divine power has granted to us all things which relate to life and godliness\" (2 Pet. 1:2-3); life is something within, and godliness is something as an expression without; all things that relate to life within and godliness without have already been given to us by the divine power; now grace must be multiplied based upon the giving of this divine power.", "norm_zh": "二愿恩典繁增的归与你们神的神能已将一切关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们彼后一23生命是在里面而敬虔是外面的彰显神的能力已将一切关于里面生命和外面敬虔的事都赐给我们现今恩典必须基于这神圣能力的赐给而繁增李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace to you be multiplied seeing that His divine power has granted to us all things which relate to life and godliness 2 Pet 123 life is something within and godliness is something as an expression without all things that relate to life within and godliness without have already been given to us by the divine power now grace must be multiplied based upon the giving of this divine power"}
{"zh": "三\t此外，神也赐给我们又宝贵又极大的应许—林后十二9，太二八20：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "C. In addition, we have been given precious and exceedingly great promises.—2 Cor. 12:9; Matt. 28:20:", "norm_zh": "三此外神也赐给我们又宝贵又极大的应许林后十二9太二八20李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In addition we have been given precious and exceedingly great promises2 Cor 129 Matt 2820"}
{"zh": "1\t彼得后书一章四节说，“借这荣耀和美德，祂已将又宝贵又极大的应许赐给我们，叫你们既逃离世上从情欲来的败坏，就借着这些应许，得有分于神的性情。”（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "1. Second Peter 1:4 says, \"Through which He has granted to us precious and exceedingly great promises, that through these you might become partakers of the divine nature, having escaped the corruption which is in the world by lust.\"", "norm_zh": "1彼得后书一章四节说借这荣耀和美德祂已将又宝贵又极大的应许赐给我们叫你们既逃离世上从情欲来的败坏就借着这些应许得有分于神的性情李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 Second Peter 14 says Through which He has granted to us precious and exceedingly great promises that through these you might become partakers of the divine nature having escaped the corruption which is in the world by lust"}
{"zh": "2\t旧约和新约里都有许多应许，如“我的恩典够你用的”（林后十二9），以及“看哪，我天天与你们同在，直到这世代的终结”（太二八20）；这些是何等的应许！（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "2. There are many promises in both the Old Testament and the New Testament, such as \"My grace is sufficient for you\" (2 Cor. 12:9) and \"Behold, I am with you all the days until the consummation of the age\" (Matt. 28:20); what promises these are!", "norm_zh": "2旧约和新约里都有许多应许如我的恩典够你用的林后十二9以及看哪我天天与你们同在直到这世代的终结太二八20这些是何等的应许李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 There are many promises in both the Old Testament and the New Testament such as My grace is sufficient for you 2 Cor 129 and Behold I am with you all the days until the consummation of the age Matt 2820 what promises these are"}
{"zh": "3\t“约”字的意思是“遗命”；圣经乃是遗命；不仅仅是合同或契约，乃比这个多得多；立神圣遗命者就是耶稣；祂死了，遗命就生效（太二六28，路二二20）；现今在复活里，祂这赐生命的灵乃是遗命的执行者（林前十五45，来八6，九15）。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "3. The word testament means \"a will\"; the Bible is a will; it is not merely an agreement or a contract; it is much more than this; the maker of the divine will is Jesus; He died so that the will could become effective (Matt. 26:28; Luke 22:20); now in resurrection He as the life-giving Spirit is the Executor of the will (1 Cor. 15:45; Heb. 8:6; 9:15).", "norm_zh": "3约字的意思是遗命圣经乃是遗命不仅仅是合同或契约乃比这个多得多立神圣遗命者就是耶稣祂死了遗命就生效太二六28路二二20现今在复活里祂这赐生命的灵乃是遗命的执行者林前十五45来八6九15李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The word testament means a will the Bible is a will it is not merely an agreement or a contract it is much more than this the maker of the divine will is Jesus He died so that the will could become effective Matt 2628 Luke 2220 now in resurrection He as the lifegiving Spirit is the Executor of the will 1 Cor 1545 Heb 86 915"}
{"zh": "伍\t除了呼求主名和祷读主话，没有别的路；我们若忠信的这样作，里面就会有属灵的繁增；这就是在恩典上长大—创四26，罗十6~8，弗六17~18：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "V. There is no other way except to call on the name of the Lord and pray-read the Word; if we are faithful to do this, there will be the spiritual multiplication within; this is the growth in grace—Gen. 4:26; Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "伍除了呼求主名和祷读主话没有别的路我们若忠信的这样作里面就会有属灵的繁增这就是在恩典上长大创四26罗十68弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V There is no other way except to call on the name of the Lord and prayread the Word if we are faithful to do this there will be the spiritual multiplication within this is the growth in graceGen 426 Rom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "一\t借着写在遗命里的应许，我们就能有分于神的性情；我们可以翻开遗命的任何一页，简单的把话接受进来—创四26。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "A. Through the promises written in the will, we can be partakers of the divine nature; we can open the will to any page and simply take the word in—Gen. 4:26.", "norm_zh": "一借着写在遗命里的应许我们就能有分于神的性情我们可以翻开遗命的任何一页简单的把话接受进来创四26李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Through the promises written in the will we can be partakers of the divine nature we can open the will to any page and simply take the word inGen 426"}
{"zh": "二\t要接受话奶，只有一条路，就是喝；借着我们的喝，话奶就被消化并吸收到我们这人里面，然后成为我们的一部分，恩典也会繁增的归与我们。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "B. There is only one way to take the milk of the word, and that is to drink it; by our drinking the milk of the word, it will be digested and assimilated into our being. Then it will become part of us, and grace will be multiplied to us.", "norm_zh": "二要接受话奶只有一条路就是喝借着我们的喝话奶就被消化并吸收到我们这人里面然后成为我们的一部分恩典也会繁增的归与我们李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B There is only one way to take the milk of the word and that is to drink it by our drinking the milk of the word it will be digested and assimilated into our being Then it will become part of us and grace will be multiplied to us"}
{"zh": "三\t我们绝不该走宗教的路，学习道理和教训我们必须回到主纯净的路上；祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的；我们要有分于基督的丰富，就必须呼求祂的名，并将祂的话祷告到我们里面；恩典每天都会繁增的归与我们—罗十6~8，弗六17~18。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "C. We should never take the religious way of learning doctrines and teachings; we must come back to the Lord's pure way; He is rich to all who call upon Him; in order to partake of the riches of Christ, we must call on His name and pray His Word into us; every day grace will be multiplied to us—Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "三我们绝不该走宗教的路学习道理和教训我们必须回到主纯净的路上祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们要有分于基督的丰富就必须呼求祂的名并将祂的话祷告到我们里面恩典每天都会繁增的归与我们罗十68弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We should never take the religious way of learning doctrines and teachings we must come back to the Lords pure way He is rich to all who call upon Him in order to partake of the riches of Christ we must call on His name and pray His Word into us every day grace will be multiplied to usRom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "四\t我的妻子也许没有看见我读圣经，但我里面时时在祷读宝贵的应许，并有分于神的性情；这就是为什么我因耶稣奇妙的人位而“疯狂”；我的确经历祂的洋溢之恩；我时时经历祂的赐给、祂的作为、祂的扶持、祂的滋养、祂的顾惜、祂的圣别、祂的炼净、和祂的满足；这就是为什么耶稣这恩典正在我里面繁增—林后五13。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "D. My wife may not see me reading the Bible, but all the time within me I am pray-reading the precious promises and partaking of the divine nature; this is why I am \"crazy\" with the wonderful person of Jesus; I do experience His abounding grace; all the time I experience His giving, His doing, His supporting, His nourishing, His cherishing, His sanctifying, His purifying, and His satisfying; this is why Jesus as grace is being multiplied within me—2 Cor. 5:13.", "norm_zh": "四我的妻子也许没有看见我读圣经但我里面时时在祷读宝贵的应许并有分于神的性情这就是为什么我因耶稣奇妙的人位而疯狂我的确经历祂的洋溢之恩我时时经历祂的赐给祂的作为祂的扶持祂的滋养祂的顾惜祂的圣别祂的炼净和祂的满足这就是为什么耶稣这恩典正在我里面繁增林后五13李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D My wife may not see me reading the Bible but all the time within me I am prayreading the precious promises and partaking of the divine nature this is why I am crazy with the wonderful person of Jesus I do experience His abounding grace all the time I experience His giving His doing His supporting His nourishing His cherishing His sanctifying His purifying and His satisfying this is why Jesus as grace is being multiplied within me2 Cor 513"}
{"zh": "陆\t神圣的能力已将每件关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们；宝贵的应许就在遗命里；我们若简单的呼求主名，祷读主话，就会真正经历恩典的繁增；这就是产生真正召会生活的正确基督徒生活—罗十6~8，弗六17~18。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第三章）", "en": "VI. Everything that relates to life and godliness has been given to us by the divine power; the precious promises are in the will; if we simply call on the name of the Lord and pray-read His Word, we will truly experience the multiplication of grace; this is the proper Christian life that produces the genuine church life—Rom. 10:6-8; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "陆神圣的能力已将每件关于生命和敬虔的事赐给我们宝贵的应许就在遗命里我们若简单的呼求主名祷读主话就会真正经历恩典的繁增这就是产生真正召会生活的正确基督徒生活罗十68弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第三章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:11:31.580143+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI Everything that relates to life and godliness has been given to us by the divine power the precious promises are in the will if we simply call on the name of the Lord and prayread His Word we will truly experience the multiplication of grace this is the proper Christian life that produces the genuine church lifeRom 1068 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "读经：提后一9~10，二1，四22，太十三24~30，罗十二11，提前一10，六3，提后二22", "en": "Scripture Reading: 2 Tim. 1:9-10; 2:1; 4:22; Matt. 13:24-30; Rom. 12:11; 1 Tim. 1:10; 6:3; 2 Tim. 2:22", "norm_zh": "读经提后一910二1四22太十三2430罗十二11提前一10六3提后二22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading 2 Tim 1910 21 422 Matt 132430 Rom 1211 1 Tim 110 63 2 Tim 222"}
{"zh": "壹\t在永远里所赐给我们的恩典，借着基督的来临而显明出来；基督来了，就带着恩典同来—提后一9~10：", "en": "I. The grace that was given to us in eternity was manifested by the coming of Christ; when Christ came, He brought grace with Him.—2 Tim. 1:9-10:", "norm_zh": "壹在永远里所赐给我们的恩典借着基督的来临而显明出来基督来了就带着恩典同来提后一910", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The grace that was given to us in eternity was manifested by the coming of Christ when Christ came He brought grace with Him2 Tim 1910"}
{"zh": "一\t神按祂永远的定旨和恩典，救了我们并召了我们；这恩典借着我们救主基督耶稣的显现，才显明出来；主耶稣来了，恩典也来了—9~10节。", "en": "A. God saved us and called us according to His eternal purpose and grace; this grace was manifested through the appearing of our Savior Christ Jesus; when the Lord Jesus came, grace also came.—vv. 9-10.", "norm_zh": "一神按祂永远的定旨和恩典救了我们并召了我们这恩典借着我们救主基督耶稣的显现才显明出来主耶稣来了恩典也来了910节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God saved us and called us according to His eternal purpose and grace this grace was manifested through the appearing of our Savior Christ Jesus when the Lord Jesus came grace also camevv 910"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典就是祂的所是、祂的赐给、和祂的作为；无论祂是什么，都是为着我们；无论祂赐给什么，也是为着我们；无论祂作什么，都是替我们作的；这就是恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12，加二20。", "en": "B. Grace is His being, His giving, and His doing; whatever He is, is for us, whatever He gives also is for us, and whatever He does is on our behalf; this is grace.—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12; Gal. 2:20.", "norm_zh": "二恩典就是祂的所是祂的赐给和祂的作为无论祂是什么都是为着我们无论祂赐给什么也是为着我们无论祂作什么都是替我们作的这就是恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912加二20", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace is His being His giving and His doing whatever He is is for us whatever He gives also is for us and whatever He does is on our behalf this is graceJohn 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12 Gal 220"}
{"zh": "三\t无论基督对我们是什么，无论祂赐给我们什么，无论祂为我们作什么，都是恩典，无价且免费；我们不需要买什么，只需要接受—罗五17，彼前一13。", "en": "C. Whatever Christ is to us, whatever He gives to us, and whatever He does for us is grace, with no cost and no charge; we do not need to buy anything; we only need to receive.—Rom. 5:17; 1 Pet. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "三无论基督对我们是什么无论祂赐给我们什么无论祂为我们作什么都是恩典无价且免费我们不需要买什么只需要接受罗五17彼前一13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Whatever Christ is to us whatever He gives to us and whatever He does for us is grace with no cost and no charge we do not need to buy anything we only need to receiveRom 517 1 Pet 113"}
{"zh": "四\t神已将美好的托付交托我们；这就是神圣的种子，包含神圣的能力所赐一切关于生命和敬虔的事；魔鬼和他一切的邪灵，一直想要夺去我们对基督丰富恩典的享受；所以，我们必须借着那住在我们里面的圣灵，保守这托付—提后一14。", "en": "D. God has committed the good deposit to us; this is the divine seed, containing all things which relate to life and godliness given by the divine power; the devil and all his evil spirits are always trying to rob us of our enjoyment of the rich grace of Christ; therefore, we must guard this deposit through the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.—2 Tim. 1:14.", "norm_zh": "四神已将美好的托付交托我们这就是神圣的种子包含神圣的能力所赐一切关于生命和敬虔的事魔鬼和他一切的邪灵一直想要夺去我们对基督丰富恩典的享受所以我们必须借着哪住在我们里面的圣灵保守这托付提后一14", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God has committed the good deposit to us this is the divine seed containing all things which relate to life and godliness given by the divine power the devil and all his evil spirits are always trying to rob us of our enjoyment of the rich grace of Christ therefore we must guard this deposit through the Holy Spirit who dwells in us2 Tim 114"}
{"zh": "贰\t在二章一节保罗接着告诉我们，我们需要在恩典上得着加力：", "en": "II. In 2:1 Paul goes on to tell us that we need to be empowered in grace:", "norm_zh": "贰在二章一节保罗接着告诉我们我们需要在恩典上得着加力", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II In 21 Paul goes on to tell us that we need to be empowered in grace"}
{"zh": "一\t我们将电器插入，电器就借着电流得着加力我们有属天电力极大的存量；我们借着运用我们的灵“插入插座”，就经历恩典的加力—1节。", "en": "A. When we plug it in, the appliance is empowered by the current of electricity; we have a great deposit of the heavenly electricity; when we \"plug in\" by exercising our spirit, we experience the empowering of grace.—v. 1.", "norm_zh": "一我们将电器插入电器就借着电流得着加力我们有属天电力极大的存量我们借着运用我们的灵插入插座就经历恩典的加力1节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A When we plug it in the appliance is empowered by the current of electricity we have a great deposit of the heavenly electricity when we plug in by exercising our spirit we experience the empowering of gracev 1"}
{"zh": "二\t每天早晨我起床时，就需要再次得着加力；我的秘诀就是简单的运用我的灵呼求：“哦，主耶稣。哦，主耶稣。哦，主耶稣”；立刻我就得着加力—罗十12，弗三8。", "en": "B. Every morning when I get up, I need to be empowered again; my secret is simply to exercise my spirit to call, \"o Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus.\"; immediately, I am empowered.—Rom. 10:12; Eph. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "二每天早晨我起床时就需要再次得着加力我的秘诀就是简单的运用我的灵呼求哦主耶稣哦主耶稣哦主耶稣立刻我就得着加力罗十12弗三8", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Every morning when I get up I need to be empowered again my secret is simply to exercise my spirit to call o Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus immediately I am empoweredRom 1012 Eph 38"}
{"zh": "叁\t提摩太后书第三次、也是最后一次提起恩典，乃在末了一节，这节说，“愿主与你的灵同在；愿恩典与你同在”—四22：", "en": "III. The third and last time that grace is mentioned in 2 Timothy is in the last verse, which says, \"The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you\"—4:22:", "norm_zh": "叁提摩太后书第三次也是最后一次提起恩典乃在末了一节这节说愿主与你的灵同在愿恩典与你同在四22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The third and last time that grace is mentioned in 2 Timothy is in the last verse which says The Lord be with your spirit Grace be with you422"}
{"zh": "一\t提摩太后书开始于拯救的恩典，继续于加力的恩典，结束于常在的恩典—22节。", "en": "A. Second Timothy begins with saving grace, continues with empowering grace, and ends with ever-present grace.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "一提摩太后书开始于拯救的恩典继续于加力的恩典结束于常在的恩典22节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Second Timothy begins with saving grace continues with empowering grace and ends with everpresent gracev 22"}
{"zh": "二\t神按恩典拯救了我们，我们必须在恩典上得着加力，这恩典一直与我们同在—22节。", "en": "B. God has saved us according to grace, we must be empowered in grace, and this grace is with us all the time.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "二神按恩典拯救了我们我们必须在恩典上得着加力这恩典一直与我们同在22节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God has saved us according to grace we must be empowered in grace and this grace is with us all the timev 22"}
{"zh": "肆\t提摩太后书是保罗所写的末了一封书信，内容很短，却给人一幅末后日子之光景的完满图画—三4：", "en": "IV. As the last Epistle written by Paul, 2 Timothy is short, yet it gives a full picture of the situation of the last days.—3:4:", "norm_zh": "肆提摩太后书是保罗所写的末了一封书信内容很短却给人一幅末后日子之光景的完满图画三4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV As the last Epistle written by Paul 2 Timothy is short yet it gives a full picture of the situation of the last days34"}
{"zh": "一\t这光景可分为三类：世俗世界（非宗教世界）的光景、宗教世界（基督教）的光景、和真正寻求并爱基督之人的光景—太十三24~30：", "en": "A. This situation can be classified into three categories: the situation of the secular world (the unreligious world), the situation of the religious world (the religion of Christianity), and the situation of the genuine seekers and lovers of Christ.—Matt. 13:24-30:", "norm_zh": "一这光景可分为三类世俗世界非宗教世界的光景宗教世界基督教的光景和真正寻求并爱基督之人的光景太十三2430", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A This situation can be classified into three categories the situation of the secular world the unreligious world the situation of the religious world the religion of Christianity and the situation of the genuine seekers and lovers of ChristMatt 132430"}
{"zh": "1\t世俗的人不在意宗教；他们全然并绝对为着世界；他们不在意神，不在意基督，也不在意基督教；他们不在意任何宗教的事。", "en": "1. The secular people care nothing for religion; they are wholly and absolutely for the world; they do not care for God, they do not care for Christ, and they do not care for Christianity; they do not care for anything religious.", "norm_zh": "1世俗的人不在意宗教他们全然并绝对为着世界他们不在意神不在意基督也不在意基督教他们不在意任何宗教的事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The secular people care nothing for religion they are wholly and absolutely for the world they do not care for God they do not care for Christ and they do not care for Christianity they do not care for anything religious"}
{"zh": "2\t最大和最好的宗教就是有基督的名在其中的宗教；这宗教称为基督教；基督教给基督加上了一些东西；我们绝不该给基督加上任何东西—太十三24~30。", "en": "2. The largest and best religion is the religion with the name of Christ in it; this religion is called Christianity; in Christianity something has been added to Christ; we should never add anything to Christ.—Matt. 13:24-30.", "norm_zh": "2最大和最好的宗教就是有基督的名在其中的宗教这宗教称为基督教基督教给基督加上了一些东西我们绝不该给基督加上任何东西太十三2430", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The largest and best religion is the religion with the name of Christ in it this religion is called Christianity in Christianity something has been added to Christ we should never add anything to ChristMatt 132430"}
{"zh": "3\t第三类是真正寻求基督并爱基督的人；我们都必须属于这类；我们只该是爱基督并寻求祂的人；人生最美好的事就是爱耶稣并寻求耶稣。", "en": "3. The third category is the real seekers and lovers of Christ; we all must belong to this category; we should simply be those who love Christ and seek Him; the best thing in human life is to love Jesus and seek Jesus.", "norm_zh": "3第三类是真正寻求基督并爱基督的人我们都必须属于这类我们只该是爱基督并寻求祂的人人生最美好的事就是爱耶稣并寻求耶稣", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The third category is the real seekers and lovers of Christ we all must belong to this category we should simply be those who love Christ and seek Him the best thing in human life is to love Jesus and seek Jesus"}
{"zh": "二\t在这幅图画里有三类爱者—爱自己者、爱钱财者、爱宴乐者；也有两类不爱者—不爱良善者和不爱神者—提后三4。", "en": "B. In this picture there are three kinds of lovers—lovers of self, lovers of money, and lovers of pleasure—and two kinds of nonlovers—nonlovers of good and nonlovers of God.—2 Tim. 3:4.", "norm_zh": "二在这幅图画里有三类爱者爱自己者爱钱财者爱宴乐者也有两类不爱者不爱良善者和不爱神者提后三4", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In this picture there are three kinds of loverslovers of self lovers of money and lovers of pleasureand two kinds of nonloversnonlovers of good and nonlovers of God2 Tim 34"}
{"zh": "三\t这封书信在第五节也说到基督教这宗教，说有些人“有敬虔的外形，却否认了敬虔的能力”；这节表明在末后的日子，宗教将会只有敬虔的外形，却没有能力或实际。", "en": "C. In verse 5 this Epistle also speaks of the religion of Christianity, saying that some have \"an outward form of godliness, though denying its power\"; this verse shows that in the last days religion will have only a form of godliness, but there will be no power or reality.", "norm_zh": "三这封书信在第五节也说到基督教这宗教说有些人有敬虔的外形却否认了敬虔的能力这节表明在末后的日子宗教将会只有敬虔的外形却没有能力或实际", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In verse 5 this Epistle also speaks of the religion of Christianity saying that some have an outward form of godliness though denying its power this verse shows that in the last days religion will have only a form of godliness but there will be no power or reality"}
{"zh": "四\t今天基督教里的另一个现象在四章三至四节提起，那里说，“时候要到，那时人必容不下健康的教训，反而耳朵发痒，随着自己的情欲，给自己堆积起教师来；并且转耳离弃真理，偏向虚构无稽之事。”", "en": "D. Another phenomenon in today's Christianity is mentioned in 2 Timothy 4:3-4, which says, \"The time will come when they will not tolerate the healthy teaching; but according to their own lusts they will heap up to themselves teachers, having itching ears, and they will turn away their ear from the truth and will be turned aside to myths.\"", "norm_zh": "四今天基督教里的另一个现象在四章三至四节提起哪里说时候要到哪时人必容不下健康的教训反而耳朵发痒随着自己的情欲给自己堆积起教师来并且转耳离弃真理偏向虚构无稽之事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Another phenomenon in todays Christianity is mentioned in 2 Timothy 434 which says The time will come when they will not tolerate the healthy teaching but according to their own lusts they will heap up to themselves teachers having itching ears and they will turn away their ear from the truth and will be turned aside to myths"}
{"zh": "伍\t提摩太后书清楚的说到第三类人—爱基督并寻求基督者—罗十二11，提前一10，六3，提后二22：", "en": "V. 2 Timothy speaks clearly concerning the third category of persons—the lovers and seekers of Christ.—Rom. 12:11; 1 Tim. 1:10; 6:3; 2 Tim. 2:22:", "norm_zh": "伍提摩太后书清楚的说到第三类人爱基督并寻求基督者罗十二11提前一10六3提后二22", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V 2 Timothy speaks clearly concerning the third category of personsthe lovers and seekers of ChristRom 1211 1 Tim 110 63 2 Tim 222"}
{"zh": "一\t我们必须有火热的灵（罗十二11），不可有发痒的耳朵；我们不该在意任何一种形式；我们只该在意活的基督在我们灵里的实际。", "en": "A. We must have a burning spirit (Rom. 12:11), not an itching ear; we should not care for any kind of form; we should care only for the reality of the living Christ in our spirit.", "norm_zh": "一我们必须有火热的灵罗十二11不可有发痒的耳朵我们不该在意任何一种形式我们只该在意活的基督在我们灵里的实际", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We must have a burning spirit Rom 1211 not an itching ear we should not care for any kind of form we should care only for the reality of the living Christ in our spirit"}
{"zh": "二\t不但如此，我们不在意美好愉悦的说话，乃在意主健康的话语和健康的教训；健康指生命的东西；我们需要话中的生命，不是死字句的杀死（约六63，林后三6下）。", "en": "B. Furthermore, we do not care for good and pleasant speaking but for the healthy words and healthy teaching of the Lord; being healthy refers to something of life; we need the life in the word, not the killing of the dead letter (John 6:63; 2 Cor. 3:6b).", "norm_zh": "二不但如此我们不在意美好愉悦的说话乃在意主健康的话语和健康的教训健康指生命的东西我们需要话中的生命不是死字句的杀死约六63林后三6下", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Furthermore we do not care for good and pleasant speaking but for the healthy words and healthy teaching of the Lord being healthy refers to something of life we need the life in the word not the killing of the dead letter John 663 2 Cor 36b"}
{"zh": "三\t我们这些有恩典托付的人，里面有个器官，可以用来领取我们的“存款”，这器官就是我们人的灵；因着我们的灵，我们该有刚强的意志、爱的情感、以及清明且健全的心思—提后一7。", "en": "C. We who have the deposit of grace have an organ within us with which we can draw out our \"deposit\"; this is our human spirit; because of our spirit, we should have a strong will, a loving emotion, and a sober and sound mind.—2 Tim. 1:7.", "norm_zh": "三我们这些有恩典托付的人里面有个器官可以用来领取我们的存款这器官就是我们人的灵因着我们的灵我们该有刚强的意志爱的情感以及清明且健全的心思提后一7", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We who have the deposit of grace have an organ within us with which we can draw out our deposit this is our human spirit because of our spirit we should have a strong will a loving emotion and a sober and sound mind2 Tim 17"}
{"zh": "四\t我们不但里面有托付，外面也有话全本圣经都是神所呼出的；这话滋养、洁净、纯净、圣化、甚至荣化我们；神已呼出这神圣的话，我们所需要作的就是吸入—三16，弗六17~18上，徒六10，林后三6。", "en": "D. We have not only the deposit within but also the Word without; the entire Scripture has been breathed out by God; this word nourishes, cleanses, purifies, sanctifies, and even glorifies us; God has breathed out this divine word, and what we need to do is to breathe it in.—3:16; Eph. 6:17-18a; Acts 6:10; 2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "四我们不但里面有托付外面也有话全本圣经都是神所呼出的这话滋养洁净纯净圣化甚至荣化我们神已呼出这神圣的话我们所需要作的就是吸入三16弗六1718上徒六10林后三6", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D We have not only the deposit within but also the Word without the entire Scripture has been breathed out by God this word nourishes cleanses purifies sanctifies and even glorifies us God has breathed out this divine word and what we need to do is to breathe it in316 Eph 61718a Acts 610 2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "五\t消极一面，我们必须逃离败坏，并逃避青年人的私欲；积极一面，我们必须追求公义、对神的信、对人的爱、以及给我们自己内里享受的和平；追求的路就是同那清心呼求主的人在一起—提后二22，三1~5，传四9~12。", "en": "E. Negatively, we must escape corruption and flee youthful lusts; positively, we must pursue righteousness, faith in God, love toward others, and peace for our own inward enjoyment; the way to do this is to be with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.—2 Tim. 2:22; 3:1-5; Eccl. 4:9-12.", "norm_zh": "五消极一面我们必须逃离败坏并逃避青年人的私欲积极一面我们必须追求公义对神的信对人的爱以及给我们自己内里享受的和平追求的路就是同哪清心呼求主的人在一起提后二22三15传四912", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "E Negatively we must escape corruption and flee youthful lusts positively we must pursue righteousness faith in God love toward others and peace for our own inward enjoyment the way to do this is to be with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart2 Tim 222 315 Eccl 4912"}
{"zh": "六\t最终，第三类的人必须领悟，主耶稣在他们的灵里；在四章二十二节保罗说，“愿主与你的灵同在。愿恩典与你同在”；这是我们能向全宇宙宣告并宣扬的事。", "en": "F. Finally, those in the third category must realize that the Lord Jesus is in their spirit; in 4:22 Paul says, \"The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you\"; this is something that we can declare and proclaim to the whole universe.", "norm_zh": "六最终第三类的人必须领悟主耶稣在他们的灵里在四章二十二节保罗说愿主与你的灵同在愿恩典与你同在这是我们能向全宇宙宣告并宣扬的事", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "F Finally those in the third category must realize that the Lord Jesus is in their spirit in 422 Paul says The Lord be with your spirit Grace be with you this is something that we can declare and proclaim to the whole universe"}
{"zh": "陆\t乃是借着这样操练并实行，我们得有分于基督所是的一切、祂所赐的一切、和祂所替我们作的一切；自然而然，我们就会被基督充满，也会逃离世上的败坏，并逃避各种情欲；这就是对恩典有真正经历的正确召会生活—提后二22，三1~5，传四9~12，罗十二11。", "en": "VI. It is by exercising and practicing in this way that we participate in all that Christ is, all that He gives, and all that He does on our behalf; spontaneously, we will be filled with Christ and will escape the corruption in the world and flee every kind of lust; this is the proper church life in the genuine experience of grace.—2 Tim. 2:22; 3:1-5; Eccl. 4:9-12; Rom. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "陆乃是借着这样操练并实行我们得有分于基督所是的一切祂所赐的一切和祂所替我们作的一切自然而然我们就会被基督充满也会逃离世上的败坏并逃避各种情欲这就是对恩典有真正经历的正确召会生活提后二22三15传四912罗十二11", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI It is by exercising and practicing in this way that we participate in all that Christ is all that He gives and all that He does on our behalf spontaneously we will be filled with Christ and will escape the corruption in the world and flee every kind of lust this is the proper church life in the genuine experience of grace2 Tim 222 315 Eccl 4912 Rom 1211"}
{"zh": "基督来了，恩典就显明出来了", "en": "When Christ came, grace was manifested.", "norm_zh": "基督来了恩典就显明出来了", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:13:15.997744+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "When Christ came grace was manifested"}
