{"zh": "壹\t在永远里所赐给我们的恩典，借着基督的来临而显明出来；基督来了，就带着恩典同来—提后一9~10：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "I. The grace that was given to us in eternity was manifested by the coming of Christ; when Christ came, He brought grace with Him.—2 Tim. 1:9-10:", "norm_zh": "壹在永远里所赐给我们的恩典借着基督的来临而显明出来基督来了就带着恩典同来提后一910李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I The grace that was given to us in eternity was manifested by the coming of Christ when Christ came He brought grace with Him2 Tim 1910"}
{"zh": "一\t神按祂永远的定旨和恩典，救了我们并召了我们；这恩典借着我们救主基督耶稣的显现，才显明出来；主耶稣来了，恩典也来了—9~10节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "A. God saved us and called us according to His eternal purpose and grace; this grace was manifested through the appearing of our Savior Christ Jesus; when the Lord Jesus came, grace also came.—vv. 9-10.", "norm_zh": "一神按祂永远的定旨和恩典救了我们并召了我们这恩典借着我们救主基督耶稣的显现才显明出来主耶稣来了恩典也来了910节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A God saved us and called us according to His eternal purpose and grace this grace was manifested through the appearing of our Savior Christ Jesus when the Lord Jesus came grace also camevv 910"}
{"zh": "二\t恩典就是祂的所是、祂的赐给、和祂的作为；无论祂是什么，都是为着我们；无论祂赐给什么，也是为着我们；无论祂作什么，都是替我们作的；这就是恩典—约一14、16~17，赛五五1，林后一8~9、12，加二20。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "B. Grace is His being, His giving, and His doing; whatever He is, is for us, whatever He gives also is for us, and whatever He does is on our behalf; this is grace.—John 1:14, 16-17; Isa. 55:1; 2 Cor. 1:8-9, 12; Gal. 2:20.", "norm_zh": "二恩典就是祂的所是祂的赐给和祂的作为无论祂是什么都是为着我们无论祂赐给什么也是为着我们无论祂作什么都是替我们作的这就是恩典约一141617赛五五1林后一8912加二20李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Grace is His being His giving and His doing whatever He is is for us whatever He gives also is for us and whatever He does is on our behalf this is graceJohn 114 1617 Isa 551 2 Cor 189 12 Gal 220"}
{"zh": "三\t无论基督对我们是什么，无论祂赐给我们什么，无论祂为我们作什么，都是恩典，无价且免费；我们不需要买什么，只需要接受—罗五17，彼前一13。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "C. Whatever Christ is to us, whatever He gives to us, and whatever He does for us is grace, there is no cost and no charge; we do not need to buy anything; we only need to receive.—Rom. 5:17; 1 Pet. 1:13.", "norm_zh": "三无论基督对我们是什么无论祂赐给我们什么无论祂为我们作什么都是恩典无价且免费我们不需要买什么只需要接受罗五17彼前一13李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C Whatever Christ is to us whatever He gives to us and whatever He does for us is grace there is no cost and no charge we do not need to buy anything we only need to receiveRom 517 1 Pet 113"}
{"zh": "四\t神已将美好的托付交托我们；这就是神圣的种子，包含神圣的能力所赐一切关于生命和敬虔的事；魔鬼和他一切的邪灵，一直想要夺去我们对基督丰富恩典的享受；所以，我们必须借着那住在我们里面的圣灵，保守这托付—提后一14。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "D. God has committed the good deposit to us; this is the divine seed, containing all things which relate to life and godliness given by the divine power; the devil and all his evil spirits are always trying to rob us of our enjoyment of the rich grace of Christ; therefore, we must guard this deposit through the Holy Spirit who dwells in us.—2 Tim. 1:14.", "norm_zh": "四神已将美好的托付交托我们这就是神圣的种子包含神圣的能力所赐一切关于生命和敬虔的事魔鬼和他一切的邪灵一直想要夺去我们对基督丰富恩典的享受所以我们必须借着哪住在我们里面的圣灵保守这托付提后一14李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D God has committed the good deposit to us this is the divine seed containing all things which relate to life and godliness given by the divine power the devil and all his evil spirits are always trying to rob us of our enjoyment of the rich grace of Christ therefore we must guard this deposit through the Holy Spirit who dwells in us2 Tim 114"}
{"zh": "贰\t在二章一节保罗接着告诉我们，我们需要在恩典上得着加力：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "II. In 2:1 Paul goes on to tell us that we need to be empowered in grace:", "norm_zh": "贰在二章一节保罗接着告诉我们我们需要在恩典上得着加力李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II In 21 Paul goes on to tell us that we need to be empowered in grace"}
{"zh": "一\t我们将电器插入，电器就借着电流得着加力我们有属天电力极大的存量；我们借着运用我们的灵“插入插座”，就经历恩典的加力—1节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "A. When we plug it in, the appliance is empowered by the current of electricity; we have a great deposit of the heavenly electricity; when we \"plug in\" by exercising our spirit, we experience the empowering of grace.—v. 1.", "norm_zh": "一我们将电器插入电器就借着电流得着加力我们有属天电力极大的存量我们借着运用我们的灵插入插座就经历恩典的加力1节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A When we plug it in the appliance is empowered by the current of electricity we have a great deposit of the heavenly electricity when we plug in by exercising our spirit we experience the empowering of gracev 1"}
{"zh": "二\t每天早晨我起床时，就需要再次得着加力；我的秘诀就是简单的运用我的灵呼求：“哦，主耶稣。哦，主耶稣。哦，主耶稣”；立刻我就得着加力—罗十12，弗三8。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "B. Every morning when I get up, I need to be empowered again; my secret is simply to exercise my spirit to call, \"o Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus. O Lord Jesus\"; immediately, I am empowered.—Rom. 10:12; Eph. 3:8.", "norm_zh": "二每天早晨我起床时就需要再次得着加力我的秘诀就是简单的运用我的灵呼求哦主耶稣哦主耶稣哦主耶稣立刻我就得着加力罗十12弗三8李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Every morning when I get up I need to be empowered again my secret is simply to exercise my spirit to call o Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus O Lord Jesus immediately I am empoweredRom 1012 Eph 38"}
{"zh": "叁\t提摩太后书第三次、也是最后一次提起恩典，乃在末了一节，这节说，“愿主与你的灵同在；愿恩典与你同在”—四22：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "III. The third and last time that grace is mentioned in 2 Timothy is in the last verse, which says, \"The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you\"—4:22:", "norm_zh": "叁提摩太后书第三次也是最后一次提起恩典乃在末了一节这节说愿主与你的灵同在愿恩典与你同在四22李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III The third and last time that grace is mentioned in 2 Timothy is in the last verse which says The Lord be with your spirit Grace be with you422"}
{"zh": "一\t提摩太后书开始于拯救的恩典，继续于加力的恩典，结束于常在的恩典—22节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "A. Second Timothy begins with saving grace, continues with empowering grace, and ends with ever-present grace.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "一提摩太后书开始于拯救的恩典继续于加力的恩典结束于常在的恩典22节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Second Timothy begins with saving grace continues with empowering grace and ends with everpresent gracev 22"}
{"zh": "二\t神按恩典拯救了我们，我们必须在恩典上得着加力，这恩典一直与我们同在—22节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "B. God has saved us according to grace, we must be empowered in grace, and this grace is with us all the time.—v. 22.", "norm_zh": "二神按恩典拯救了我们我们必须在恩典上得着加力这恩典一直与我们同在22节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B God has saved us according to grace we must be empowered in grace and this grace is with us all the timev 22"}
{"zh": "肆\t提摩太后书是保罗所写的末了一封书信，内容很短，却给人一幅末后日子之光景的完满图画—三4：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "IV. As the last Epistle written by Paul, 2 Timothy is short, yet it gives a full picture of the situation of the last days.—2 Tim. 3:4:", "norm_zh": "肆提摩太后书是保罗所写的末了一封书信内容很短却给人一幅末后日子之光景的完满图画三4李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV As the last Epistle written by Paul 2 Timothy is short yet it gives a full picture of the situation of the last days2 Tim 34"}
{"zh": "一\t这光景可分为三类：世俗世界（非宗教世界）的光景、宗教世界（基督教）的光景、和真正寻求并爱基督之人的光景—太十三24~30：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "A. This situation can be classified into three categories: the situation of the secular world (the unreligious world), the situation of the religious world (the religion of Christianity), and the situation of the genuine seekers and lovers of Christ.—Matt. 13:24-30:", "norm_zh": "一这光景可分为三类世俗世界非宗教世界的光景宗教世界基督教的光景和真正寻求并爱基督之人的光景太十三2430李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A This situation can be classified into three categories the situation of the secular world the unreligious world the situation of the religious world the religion of Christianity and the situation of the genuine seekers and lovers of ChristMatt 132430"}
{"zh": "1\t世俗的人不在意宗教；他们全然并绝对为着世界；他们不在意神，不在意基督，也不在意基督教；他们不在意任何宗教的事。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "1. The secular people care nothing for religion; they are wholly and absolutely for the world; they do not care for God, they do not care for Christ, and they do not care for Christianity; they do not care for anything religious.", "norm_zh": "1世俗的人不在意宗教他们全然并绝对为着世界他们不在意神不在意基督也不在意基督教他们不在意任何宗教的事李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 The secular people care nothing for religion they are wholly and absolutely for the world they do not care for God they do not care for Christ and they do not care for Christianity they do not care for anything religious"}
{"zh": "2\t最大和最好的宗教就是有基督的名在其中的宗教；这宗教称为基督教；基督教给基督加上了一些东西；我们绝不该给基督加上任何东西—太十三24~30。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "2. The largest and best religion is the religion with the name of Christ in it; this religion is called Christianity; in Christianity something has been added to Christ; we should never add anything to Christ.—Matt. 13:24-30.", "norm_zh": "2最大和最好的宗教就是有基督的名在其中的宗教这宗教称为基督教基督教给基督加上了一些东西我们绝不该给基督加上任何东西太十三2430李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 The largest and best religion is the religion with the name of Christ in it this religion is called Christianity in Christianity something has been added to Christ we should never add anything to ChristMatt 132430"}
{"zh": "3\t第三类是真正寻求基督并爱基督的人；我们都必须属于这类；我们只该是爱基督并寻求祂的人；人生最美好的事就是爱耶稣并寻求耶稣。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "3. The third category is the real seekers and lovers of Christ; we all must belong to this category; we should simply be those who love Christ and seek Him; the best thing in human life is to love Jesus and seek Jesus.", "norm_zh": "3第三类是真正寻求基督并爱基督的人我们都必须属于这类我们只该是爱基督并寻求祂的人人生最美好的事就是爱耶稣并寻求耶稣李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "3 The third category is the real seekers and lovers of Christ we all must belong to this category we should simply be those who love Christ and seek Him the best thing in human life is to love Jesus and seek Jesus"}
{"zh": "二\t在这幅图画里有三类爱者—爱自己者、爱钱财者、爱宴乐者；也有两类不爱者—不爱良善者和不爱神者—提后三4。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "B. In this picture there are three kinds of lovers—lovers of self, lovers of money, and lovers of pleasure—and two kinds of nonlovers—nonlovers of good and nonlovers of God.—2 Tim. 3:4.", "norm_zh": "二在这幅图画里有三类爱者爱自己者爱钱财者爱宴乐者也有两类不爱者不爱良善者和不爱神者提后三4李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B In this picture there are three kinds of loverslovers of self lovers of money and lovers of pleasureand two kinds of nonloversnonlovers of good and nonlovers of God2 Tim 34"}
{"zh": "三\t这封书信在第五节也说到基督教这宗教，说有些人“有敬虔的外形，却否认了敬虔的能力”；这节表明在末后的日子，宗教将会只有敬虔的外形，却没有能力或实际。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "C. In verse 5 this Epistle also speaks of the religion of Christianity, saying that some have \"an outward form of godliness, though denying its power\"; this verse shows that in the last days religion will have only a form of godliness, but there will be no power or reality.", "norm_zh": "三这封书信在第五节也说到基督教这宗教说有些人有敬虔的外形却否认了敬虔的能力这节表明在末后的日子宗教将会只有敬虔的外形却没有能力或实际李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In verse 5 this Epistle also speaks of the religion of Christianity saying that some have an outward form of godliness though denying its power this verse shows that in the last days religion will have only a form of godliness but there will be no power or reality"}
{"zh": "四\t今天基督教里的另一个现象在四章三至四节提起，那里说，“时候要到，那时人必容不下健康的教训，反而耳朵发痒，随着自己的情欲，给自己堆积起教师来；并且转耳离弃真理，偏向虚构无稽之事。”（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "D. Another phenomenon in today's Christianity is mentioned in 2 Timothy 4:3-4, which says, \"The time will come when they will not tolerate the healthy teaching; but according to their own lusts they will heap up to themselves teachers, having itching ears, and they will turn away their ear from the truth and will be turned aside to myths.\"", "norm_zh": "四今天基督教里的另一个现象在四章三至四节提起哪里说时候要到哪时人必容不下健康的教训反而耳朵发痒随着自己的情欲给自己堆积起教师来并且转耳离弃真理偏向虚构无稽之事李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D Another phenomenon in todays Christianity is mentioned in 2 Timothy 434 which says The time will come when they will not tolerate the healthy teaching but according to their own lusts they will heap up to themselves teachers having itching ears and they will turn away their ear from the truth and will be turned aside to myths"}
{"zh": "伍\t提摩太后书清楚的说到第三类人—爱基督并寻求基督者—罗十二11，提前一10，六3，提后二22：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "V. 2 Timothy speaks clearly concerning the third category of persons—the lovers and seekers of Christ.—Rom. 12:11; 1 Tim. 1:10; 6:3; 2 Tim. 2:22:", "norm_zh": "伍提摩太后书清楚的说到第三类人爱基督并寻求基督者罗十二11提前一10六3提后二22李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "V 2 Timothy speaks clearly concerning the third category of personsthe lovers and seekers of ChristRom 1211 1 Tim 110 63 2 Tim 222"}
{"zh": "一\t我们必须有火热的灵（罗十二11），不可有发痒的耳朵；我们不该在意任何一种形式；我们只该在意活的基督在我们灵里的实际。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "We must have a burning spirit (Rom. 12:11), not an itching ear; we should not care for any kind of form; we should care only for the reality of the living Christ in our spirit.", "norm_zh": "一我们必须有火热的灵罗十二11不可有发痒的耳朵我们不该在意任何一种形式我们只该在意活的基督在我们灵里的实际李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We must have a burning spirit Rom 1211 not an itching ear we should not care for any kind of form we should care only for the reality of the living Christ in our spirit"}
{"zh": "二\t不但如此，我们不在意美好愉悦的说话，乃在意主健康的话语和健康的教训；健康指生命的东西；我们需要话中的生命，不是死字句的杀死（约六63，林后三6下）。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "Furthermore, we do not care for good and pleasant speaking but for the healthy words and healthy teaching of the Lord; being healthy refers to something of life; we need the life in the word, not the killing of the dead letter (John 6:63; 2 Cor. 3:6b).", "norm_zh": "二不但如此我们不在意美好愉悦的说话乃在意主健康的话语和健康的教训健康指生命的东西我们需要话中的生命不是死字句的杀死约六63林后三6下李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Furthermore we do not care for good and pleasant speaking but for the healthy words and healthy teaching of the Lord being healthy refers to something of life we need the life in the word not the killing of the dead letter John 663 2 Cor 36b"}
{"zh": "三\t我们这些有恩典托付的人，里面有个器官，可以用来领取我们的“存款”，这器官就是我们人的灵；因着我们的灵，我们该有刚强的意志、爱的情感、以及清明且健全的心思—提后一7。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "We who have the deposit of grace have an organ within us with which we can draw out our \"deposit\"—this is our human spirit; because of our spirit, we should have a strong will, a loving emotion, and a sober and sound mind.—2 Tim. 1:7.", "norm_zh": "三我们这些有恩典托付的人里面有个器官可以用来领取我们的存款这器官就是我们人的灵因着我们的灵我们该有刚强的意志爱的情感以及清明且健全的心思提后一7李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We who have the deposit of grace have an organ within us with which we can draw out our depositthis is our human spirit because of our spirit we should have a strong will a loving emotion and a sober and sound mind2 Tim 17"}
{"zh": "四\t我们不但里面有托付，外面也有话全本圣经都是神所呼出的；这话滋养、洁净、纯净、圣化、甚至荣化我们；神已呼出这神圣的话，我们所需要作的就是吸入—三16，弗六17~18上，徒六10，林后三6。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "We have not only the deposit within but also the Word without; the entire Scripture has been breathed out by God; this word nourishes, cleanses, purifies, sanctifies, and even glorifies us; God has breathed out this divine word, and what we need to do is to breathe it in.—2 Tim. 3:16; Eph. 6:17-18a; Acts 6:10; 2 Cor. 3:6.", "norm_zh": "四我们不但里面有托付外面也有话全本圣经都是神所呼出的这话滋养洁净纯净圣化甚至荣化我们神已呼出这神圣的话我们所需要作的就是吸入三16弗六1718上徒六10林后三6李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "We have not only the deposit within but also the Word without the entire Scripture has been breathed out by God this word nourishes cleanses purifies sanctifies and even glorifies us God has breathed out this divine word and what we need to do is to breathe it in2 Tim 316 Eph 61718a Acts 610 2 Cor 36"}
{"zh": "五\t消极一面，我们必须逃离败坏，并逃避青年人的私欲；积极一面，我们必须追求公义、对神的信、对人的爱、以及给我们自己内里享受的和平；追求的路就是同那清心呼求主的人在一起—提后二22，三1~5，传四9~12。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "Negatively, we must escape corruption and flee youthful lusts; positively, we must pursue righteousness, faith in God, love toward others, and peace for our own inward enjoyment; the way to do this is to be with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart.—2 Tim. 2:22; 3:1-5; Eccl. 4:9-12.", "norm_zh": "五消极一面我们必须逃离败坏并逃避青年人的私欲积极一面我们必须追求公义对神的信对人的爱以及给我们自己内里享受的和平追求的路就是同哪清心呼求主的人在一起提后二22三15传四912李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Negatively we must escape corruption and flee youthful lusts positively we must pursue righteousness faith in God love toward others and peace for our own inward enjoyment the way to do this is to be with those who call on the Lord out of a pure heart2 Tim 222 315 Eccl 4912"}
{"zh": "六\t最终，第三类的人必须领悟，主耶稣在他们的灵里；在四章二十二节保罗说，“愿主与你的灵同在。愿恩典与你同在”；这是我们能向全宇宙宣告并宣扬的事。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "Finally, those in the third category must realize that the Lord Jesus is in their spirit; in 4:22 Paul says, \"The Lord be with your spirit. Grace be with you\"; this is something that we can declare and proclaim to the whole universe.", "norm_zh": "六最终第三类的人必须领悟主耶稣在他们的灵里在四章二十二节保罗说愿主与你的灵同在愿恩典与你同在这是我们能向全宇宙宣告并宣扬的事李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Finally those in the third category must realize that the Lord Jesus is in their spirit in 422 Paul says The Lord be with your spirit Grace be with you this is something that we can declare and proclaim to the whole universe"}
{"zh": "陆\t乃是借着这样操练并实行，我们得有分于基督所是的一切、祂所赐的一切、和祂所替我们作的一切；自然而然，我们就会被基督充满，也会逃离世上的败坏，并逃避各种情欲；这就是对恩典有真正经历的正确召会生活—提后二22，三1~5，传四9~12，罗十二11。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第四章）", "en": "VI. It is by exercising and practicing in this way that we participate in all that Christ is, all that He gives, and all that He does on our behalf; spontaneously, we will be filled with Christ and will escape the corruption in the world and flee every kind of lust; this is the proper church life in the genuine experience of grace.—2 Tim. 2:22; 3:1-5; Eccl. 4:9-12; Rom. 12:11.", "norm_zh": "陆乃是借着这样操练并实行我们得有分于基督所是的一切祂所赐的一切和祂所替我们作的一切自然而然我们就会被基督充满也会逃离世上的败坏并逃避各种情欲这就是对恩典有真正经历的正确召会生活提后二22三15传四912罗十二11李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第四章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:15:45.446401+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "VI It is by exercising and practicing in this way that we participate in all that Christ is all that He gives and all that He does on our behalf spontaneously we will be filled with Christ and will escape the corruption in the world and flee every kind of lust this is the proper church life in the genuine experience of grace2 Tim 222 315 Eccl 4912 Rom 1211"}
{"zh": "读经：弗一22~23，二21~22，三14~21，四13、15~16，罗八2、29，十二2，约壹三2", "en": "Scripture Reading: Eph. 1:22-23; 2:21-22; 3:14-21; 4:13, 15-16; Rom. 8:2, 29; 12:2; 1 John 3:2", "norm_zh": "读经弗一2223二2122三1421四131516罗八229十二2约壹三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Scripture Reading Eph 12223 22122 31421 413 1516 Rom 82 29 122 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要来看享受恩典的结果、终极完成；这终极完成乃是神在永远里定意要得着的；照着新约的启示，神永远的定旨是要得着一个团体的身体，作伟大、宇宙的器皿，以盛装并彰显祂自己—弗一22~23，二21~22，三14~21：", "en": "I. We will consider the issue, the consummation, of the enjoyment of grace; this consummation is what God purposed to have in eternity; according to the revelation of the New Testament, God's eternal purpose is to gain a corporate Body as a great, universal vessel to contain and express Himself.—Eph. 1:22-23; 2:21-22; 3:14-21:", "norm_zh": "壹我们要来看享受恩典的结果终极完成这终极完成乃是神在永远里定意要得着的照着新约的启示神永远的定旨是要得着一个团体的身体作伟大宇宙的器皿以盛装并彰显祂自己弗一2223二2122三1421", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I We will consider the issue the consummation of the enjoyment of grace this consummation is what God purposed to have in eternity according to the revelation of the New Testament Gods eternal purpose is to gain a corporate Body as a great universal vessel to contain and express HimselfEph 12223 22122 31421"}
{"zh": "一\t神的定旨乃是要得着一个活的团体器皿，由祂所创造、救赎、并重生之人所组成；神的心意是要所有的婴孩都借着享受神圣的恩典，从作婴孩的阶段，长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段—彼前一2~3、23：", "en": "A. God's purpose is to have a corporate, living vessel composed of His created, redeemed, and regenerated people; God's intention is that through their enjoying of the divine grace, all the babes will grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for God's building.—1 Pet. 1:2-3, 23:", "norm_zh": "一神的定旨乃是要得着一个活的团体器皿由祂所创造救赎并重生之人所组成神的心意是要所有的婴孩都借着享受神圣的恩典从作婴孩的阶段长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段彼前一2323", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods purpose is to have a corporate living vessel composed of His created redeemed and regenerated people Gods intention is that through their enjoying of the divine grace all the babes will grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for Gods building1 Pet 123 23"}
{"zh": "1\t彼前二章二节说，所有重生的人都该像才生的婴孩一样，切慕那纯净的话奶，叫他们靠此长大，以致得救；才生的婴孩借着他们所吃、所喝的长大。", "en": "1. First Peter 2:2 says that all the reborn ones as newborn babes should long for the guileless milk of the word in order that by it they may grow unto salvation; newborn babes grow by what they eat and what they drink.", "norm_zh": "1彼前二章二节说所有重生的人都该像才生的婴孩一样切慕哪纯净的话奶叫他们靠此长大以致得救才生的婴孩借着他们所吃所喝的长大", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 First Peter 22 says that all the reborn ones as newborn babes should long for the guileless milk of the word in order that by it they may grow unto salvation newborn babes grow by what they eat and what they drink"}
{"zh": "2\t才生的婴孩借着长大，被变化成为活石，并且被建造成为属灵的殿，成为圣别的祭司体系—2节。", "en": "2. Through their growth the newborn babes are transformed into living stones and are built up as a spiritual house into a holy priesthood.—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2才生的婴孩借着长大被变化成为活石并且被建造成为属灵的殿成为圣别的祭司体系2节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through their growth the newborn babes are transformed into living stones and are built up as a spiritual house into a holy priesthoodv 2"}
{"zh": "二\t我们重生为才生的婴孩，但我们能被变化成为活石；神永远定旨的终极完成，是要得着建造起来的殿—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16：", "en": "B. We were regenerated as newborn babes, but we can be transformed into living stones; the ultimate consummation of His eternal purpose is to have a built-up house.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16:", "norm_zh": "二我们重生为才生的婴孩但我们能被变化成为活石神永远定旨的终极完成是要得着建造起来的殿创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We were regenerated as newborn babes but we can be transformed into living stones the ultimate consummation of His eternal purpose is to have a builtup houseGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "1\t照着圣经，石头是为着建造；我们需要问问自己是否已被建造到神属灵的殿里；我们若停留在作婴孩的阶段，就无法同被建造—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。", "en": "1. According to the Bible, a stone is for building; we need to ask ourselves whether we have been built into God's spiritual house; if we remain in the stage of being babes, we cannot be built together.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "1照着圣经石头是为着建造我们需要问问自己是否已被建造到神属灵的殿里我们若停留在作婴孩的阶段就无法同被建造创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to the Bible a stone is for building we need to ask ourselves whether we have been built into Gods spiritual house if we remain in the stage of being babes we cannot be built togetherGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "2\t彼得说，我们作为活石，正被建造成为属灵的殿；这意思是建造现今正在进行—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。", "en": "2. Peter says that as living stones, we are being built up as a spiritual house; this means that the building is progressing right now.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "2彼得说我们作为活石正被建造成为属灵的殿这意思是建造现今正在进行创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Peter says that as living stones we are being built up as a spiritual house this means that the building is progressing right nowGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "三\t今天在主的恢复里，主所作唯一的事，就是恢复地方召会生活真实的建造；这地方召会生活的建造，只能借着我们享受基督作恩典而进行—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。", "en": "C. In the Lord's recovery today the unique thing that the Lord is doing is to recover the genuine building up of the local church life; this building up of the local church life can take place only by our enjoying Christ as grace.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "三今天在主的恢复里主所作惟一的事就是恢复地方召会生活真实的建造这地方召会生活的建造只能借着我们享受基督作恩典而进行创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the Lords recovery today the unique thing that the Lord is doing is to recover the genuine building up of the local church life this building up of the local church life can take place only by our enjoying Christ as graceGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "贰\t我们若天天享受耶稣作我们的恩典，就会经历在生命里实际且逐渐的长大—弗四13、15~16：", "en": "II. If we enjoy Jesus as our grace day by day, we will experience the practical and gradual growth in life.—Eph. 4:13, 15-16:", "norm_zh": "贰我们若天天享受耶稣作我们的恩典就会经历在生命里实际且逐渐的长大弗四131516", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II If we enjoy Jesus as our grace day by day we will experience the practical and gradual growth in lifeEph 413 1516"}
{"zh": "一\t青年人若日复一日运用他们的灵呼求主名并祷读活的话，就会享受基督这活的人位，连同祂所是的一切、祂所赐的一切、和祂所作的一切，作他们的恩典；自然而然，他们享受恩典的结果，就是在神圣的生命里长大—林前三6，十四20，十六13。", "en": "A. If the young people exercise their spirit to call on the name of the Lord and pray-read the living word day after day, they will enjoy Christ, the living person, with all that He is, all that He gives, and all that He does as their grace; spontaneously, as the issue of their enjoyment of grace, they will grow in the divine life.—1 Cor. 3:6; 14:20; 16:13.", "norm_zh": "一青年人若日复一日运用他们的灵呼求主名并祷读活的话就会享受基督这活的人位连同祂所是的一切祂所赐的一切和祂所作的一切作他们的恩典自然而然他们享受恩典的结果就是在神圣的生命里长大林前三6十四20十六13", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A If the young people exercise their spirit to call on the name of the Lord and prayread the living word day after day they will enjoy Christ the living person with all that He is all that He gives and all that He does as their grace spontaneously as the issue of their enjoyment of grace they will grow in the divine life1 Cor 36 1420 1613"}
{"zh": "二\t变化是在我们内里素质上新陈代谢的改变，显明于我们外面的形状或彰显；我们将更多基督的生命元素接受到全人里面，就发生这样的改变—林后五17，加六15，西三10~11，林后三18：", "en": "B. Transformation is a metabolic change in our inward essence that is manifested in our outward form, or expression; such a change takes place when we receive more of the life element of Christ into our being.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 3:18:", "norm_zh": "二变化是在我们内里素质上新陈代谢的改变显明于我们外面的形状或彰显我们将更多基督的生命元素接受到全人里面就发生这样的改变林后五17加六15西三1011林后三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Transformation is a metabolic change in our inward essence that is manifested in our outward form or expression such a change takes place when we receive more of the life element of Christ into our being2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "1\t这新元素排除我们天然所是的旧元素，并以基督的新元素顶替旧元素，就导致形状或外面彰显上的改变—五17，加六15，西三10~11。", "en": "1. This new element discharges the old element of our natural being and replaces it with the new element of Christ, issuing in a change in form, or outward expression.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11.", "norm_zh": "1这新元素排除我们天然所是的旧元素并以基督的新元素顶替旧元素就导致形状或外面彰显上的改变五17加六15西三1011", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This new element discharges the old element of our natural being and replaces it with the new element of Christ issuing in a change in form or outward expression2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011"}
{"zh": "2\t因此，林后三章十八节说，我们“渐渐变化成为与祂同样的形像”，那就是成为复活并得荣之基督的形像。", "en": "2. Thus, 2 Cor. 3:18 says that we are \"being transformed into the same image,\" that is, into the image of the resurrected and glorified Christ.", "norm_zh": "2因此林后三章十八节说我们渐渐变化成为与祂同样的形像哪就是成为复活并得荣之基督的形像", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Thus 2 Cor 318 says that we are being transformed into the same image that is into the image of the resurrected and glorified Christ"}
{"zh": "三\t借着呼求：“哦，主耶稣，”并祷读主话，我们就接受耶稣作赐生命之神圣的气，和滋养的神圣食物；这位丰富的耶稣进入我们里面，祂一切滋养的元素就借着属灵新陈代谢的过程，开始在我们里面作工—约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18：", "en": "C. By calling, \"O Lord Jesus,\" and pray-reading the Word, we receive Jesus as the life-giving divine breath and the nourishing divine food; when this rich Jesus enters into us, all His nourishing elements begin to work in us through a process of spiritual metabolism.—John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "三借着呼求哦主耶稣并祷读主话我们就接受耶稣作赐生命之神圣的气和滋养的神圣食物这位丰富的耶稣进入我们里面祂一切滋养的元素就借着属灵新陈代谢的过程开始在我们里面作工约六355763耶十五16弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C By calling O Lord Jesus and prayreading the Word we receive Jesus as the lifegiving divine breath and the nourishing divine food when this rich Jesus enters into us all His nourishing elements begin to work in us through a process of spiritual metabolismJohn 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "1\t我们呼求：“哦，主耶稣，”就将这位耶稣连同祂一切丰富的元素，接受到我们里面；罗马十章十二节说，“众人同有一位主，祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的”；我们能借着呼求祂而吸入祂，我们能借着祷读祂的话而吃祂（约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18）。", "en": "1. When we call, \"O Lord Jesus,\" we receive this Jesus with all His rich elements into us; Rom. 10:12 says, \"The same Lord is Lord of all and rich to all who call upon Him\"; we can breathe Him by calling on Him, and we can eat Him by pray-reading His Word (John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18).", "norm_zh": "1我们呼求哦主耶稣就将这位耶稣连同祂一切丰富的元素接受到我们里面罗马十章十二节说众人同有一位主祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们能借着呼求祂而吸入祂我们能借着祷读祂的话而吃祂约六355763耶十五16弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we call O Lord Jesus we receive this Jesus with all His rich elements into us Rom 1012 says The same Lord is Lord of all and rich to all who call upon Him we can breathe Him by calling on Him and we can eat Him by prayreading His Word John 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "2\t我们无法凭自己排除里面的老旧；排除一切老旧最好的路，就是把耶稣接受进来；借着我们呼吸、吃、喝耶稣，属天和神圣的元素就进入我们里面；这元素会使我们得着新陈代谢的变化—林后五17，加六15，西三10~11，林后三18。", "en": "2. By ourselves there is no way for us to discharge the oldness that is in us; the best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in; through our breathing, eating, and drinking of Jesus, the heavenly and divine element enters into us; this element will cause us to be metabolically transformed.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "2我们无法凭自己排除里面的老旧排除一切老旧最好的路就是把耶稣接受进来借着我们呼吸吃喝耶稣属天和神圣的元素就进入我们里面这元素会使我们得着新陈代谢的变化林后五17加六15西三1011林后三18", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 By ourselves there is no way for us to discharge the oldness that is in us the best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in through our breathing eating and drinking of Jesus the heavenly and divine element enters into us this element will cause us to be metabolically transformed2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "叁\t借着变化胜过我们的乖僻—罗八2、29，约壹三2：", "en": "III. OVERCOMING OUR PECULIARITY THROUGH TRANSFORMATION—Rom. 8:2, 29; 1 John 3:2:", "norm_zh": "叁借着变化胜过我们的乖僻罗八229约壹三2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III OVERCOMING OUR PECULIARITY THROUGH TRANSFORMATIONRom 82 29 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "一\t我们都有自己天然的构成；照着这构成，我们永远无法与别人是一；我们因着乖僻而有的难处越多，享受基督的机会就越多—林前二14~16。", "en": "A. We all have our own natural constitution; according to this constitution, we could never be one with others; the more trouble we have because of our peculiarities, the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ.—1 Cor. 2:14-16.", "norm_zh": "一我们都有自己天然的构成照着这构成我们永远无法与别人是一我们因着乖僻而有的难处越多享受基督的机会就越多林前二1416", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We all have our own natural constitution according to this constitution we could never be one with others the more trouble we have because of our peculiarities the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ1 Cor 21416"}
{"zh": "二\t被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话，好将祂接受进来；姊妹们若行这些事，主耶稣就会在她们里面作变化的工作；祂不会仅仅改正她们，乃会变化她们；祂会以祂自己顶替她们—约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18。", "en": "B. The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and pray-read His Word in order to take Him in; if the sisters will do these things, the Lord Jesus will do a transforming work within them; He will not merely correct them but will transform them; He will replace them with Himself.—John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "二被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话好将祂接受进来姊妹们若行这些事主耶稣就会在她们里面作变化的工作祂不会仅仅改正她们乃会变化她们祂会以祂自己顶替她们约六355763耶十五16弗六1718", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and prayread His Word in order to take Him in if the sisters will do these things the Lord Jesus will do a transforming work within them He will not merely correct them but will transform them He will replace them with HimselfJohn 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "三\t经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造；她无论在哪里，不管在家庭里，在姊妹之家里，或在召会的圣徒当中，都不会与任何人有难处—罗八16，十二1~2、4~5。", "en": "C. A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others; wherever she is, whether in a family, in a sisters' house, or among the saints in the church, she will have no problem with anyone.—Rom. 8:16; 12:1-2, 4-5.", "norm_zh": "三经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造她无论在哪里不管在家庭里在姊妹之家里或在召会的圣徒当中都不会与任何人有难处罗八16十二1245", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others wherever she is whether in a family in a sisters house or among the saints in the church she will have no problem with anyoneRom 816 1212 45"}
{"zh": "四\t信徒经过变化以后，就变得非常有弹性，能适合任何一种情况，并且能与任何一种信徒一同被建造；这样的人适合建造—八16，十二1~2、4~5。", "en": "D. After being transformed, a believer becomes very flexible; he is_ able to fit into any kind of situation and be built with any kind of believer. Such a person is fit for the building.—Rom. 8:16; 12:1-2, 4-5.", "norm_zh": "四信徒经过变化以后就变得非常有弹性能适合任何一种情况并且能与任何一种信徒一同被建造这样的人适合建造八16十二1245", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D After being transformed a believer becomes very flexible he is_ able to fit into any kind of situation and be built with any kind of believer Such a person is fit for the buildingRom 816 1212 45"}
{"zh": "肆\t被变化并建造，为着召会的扩增与扩展—创三二28，三五10、15：", "en": "IV. TRANSFORMED AND BUILT UP FOR THE INCREASE AND SPREAD OF THE CHURCH—Gen. 32:28; 35:10, 15:", "norm_zh": "肆被变化并建造为着召会的扩增与扩展创三二28三五1015", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV TRANSFORMED AND BUILT UP FOR THE INCREASE AND SPREAD OF THE CHURCHGen 3228 3510 15"}
{"zh": "一\t弟兄们若对主认真，并且是真实寻求主和纯诚爱主的人，就会到主面前去迫切祷告，不但为着自己的变化祷告，也为着召会的扩增祷告—罗八28~29，十二2。", "en": "A. If the brothers mean business with the Lord and are genuine seekers and sincere lovers of the Lord, they will go to the Lord and pray desperately not only for their transformation but also for the increase of the church.—Rom. 8:28-29; 12:2.", "norm_zh": "一弟兄们若对主认真并且是真实寻求主和纯诚爱主的人就会到主面前去迫切祷告不但为着自己的变化祷告也为着召会的扩增祷告罗八2829十二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A If the brothers mean business with the Lord and are genuine seekers and sincere lovers of the Lord they will go to the Lord and pray desperately not only for their transformation but also for the increase of the churchRom 82829 122"}
{"zh": "二\t我鼓励姊妹们更多的接受基督进来，作她们的享受，我也告诫弟兄们要有迫切的态度，与主彻底的办交涉；弟兄们需要告诉主：“主，我不要不冷不热或冷淡！我要火热！我要焚烧！”我们当中需要建造，而建造来自变化—八28~29，十二2。", "en": "B. I encourage the sisters to take in more of Christ for their enjoyment, and I admonish the brothers to have a thorough dealing with the Lord with an attitude of desperation; the brothers need to tell the Lord, \"Lord, I don't want to be lukewarm or cold! I want to be hot! I want to be burning!\" Among us we need the building, and the building comes from transformation.—Rom. 8:28-29; 12:2.", "norm_zh": "二我鼓励姊妹们更多的接受基督进来作她们的享受我也告诫弟兄们要有迫切的态度与主彻底的办交涉弟兄们需要告诉主主我不要不冷不热或冷淡我要火热我要焚烧我们当中需要建造而建造来自变化八2829十二2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B I encourage the sisters to take in more of Christ for their enjoyment and I admonish the brothers to have a thorough dealing with the Lord with an attitude of desperation the brothers need to tell the Lord Lord I dont want to be lukewarm or cold I want to be hot I want to be burning Among us we need the building and the building comes from transformationRom 82829 122"}
{"zh": "三\t我们不该忘记，享受恩典是为着在生命里长大，在生命里长大是为着变化，变化终极完成于建造，而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展—罗十二2，启二一18上。", "en": "C. We should not forget that the enjoyment of grace is for the growth in life, the growth in life is for transformation, transformation consummates in the building, and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lord's testimony.—Rom. 12:2; Rev. 21:18a.", "norm_zh": "三我们不该忘记享受恩典是为着在生命里长大在生命里长大是为着变化变化终极完成于建造而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展罗十二2启二一18上", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We should not forget that the enjoyment of grace is for the growth in life the growth in life is for transformation transformation consummates in the building and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lords testimonyRom 122 Rev 2118a"}
{"zh": "像才生的婴孩一样，切慕那纯净的话奶", "en": "As newborn babes, long for the guileless milk of the word", "norm_zh": "像才生的婴孩一样切慕哪纯净的话奶", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "As newborn babes long for the guileless milk of the word"}
{"zh": "从作婴孩的阶段，长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段", "en": "To grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for God's building", "norm_zh": "从作婴孩的阶段长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "To grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for Gods building"}
{"zh": "排除一切老旧最好的路，就是把耶稣接受进来", "en": "The best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in.", "norm_zh": "排除一切老旧最好的路就是把耶稣接受进来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in"}
{"zh": "因着乖僻而有的难处越多，享受基督的机会就越多", "en": "The more trouble we have because of our peculiarities, the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ.", "norm_zh": "因着乖僻而有的难处越多享受基督的机会就越多", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The more trouble we have because of our peculiarities the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ"}
{"zh": "在任何召会中，姊妹们若都是一，召会就会享受一", "en": "In any church, if all the sisters are one, the church will enjoy oneness", "norm_zh": "在任何召会中姊妹们若都是一召会就会享受一", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In any church if all the sisters are one the church will enjoy oneness"}
{"zh": "被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话，好将祂接受进来", "en": "The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and pray-read His Word in order to take Him in.", "norm_zh": "被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话好将祂接受进来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and prayread His Word in order to take Him in"}
{"zh": "经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造", "en": "A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others.", "norm_zh": "经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others"}
{"zh": "弟兄们需要更迫切的到主面前去", "en": "The brothers need to go to the Lord more desperately.", "norm_zh": "弟兄们需要更迫切的到主面前去", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The brothers need to go to the Lord more desperately"}
{"zh": "建造在于变化，变化来自生命里的长大", "en": "Building depends on transformation, and transformation comes from the growth in life.", "norm_zh": "建造在于变化变化来自生命里的长大", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Building depends on transformation and transformation comes from the growth in life"}
{"zh": "弟兄们都需要到主面前去，迫切的与主办交涉", "en": "The brothers all need to go to the Lord to have a desperate dealing with Him.", "norm_zh": "弟兄们都需要到主面前去迫切的与主办交涉", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The brothers all need to go to the Lord to have a desperate dealing with Him"}
{"zh": "我们当中需要建造，而建造来自变化", "en": "Among us we need the building, and the building comes from transformation.", "norm_zh": "我们当中需要建造而建造来自变化", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Among us we need the building and the building comes from transformation"}
{"zh": "变化终极完成于建造，而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展", "en": "Transformation consummates in the building, and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lord's testimony.", "norm_zh": "变化终极完成于建造而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:17:39.721530+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Transformation consummates in the building and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lords testimony"}
{"zh": "壹\t我们要来看享受恩典的结果、终极完成；这终极完成乃是神在永远里定意要得着的；照着新约的启示，神永远的定旨是要得着一个团体的身体，作伟大、宇宙的器皿，以盛装并彰显祂自己—弗一22~23，二21~22，三14~21：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "I. We will consider the issue, the consummation, of the enjoyment of grace; this consummation is what God purposed to have in eternity; according to the revelation of the New Testament, God's eternal purpose is to gain a corporate Body as a great, universal vessel to contain and express Himself.—Eph. 1:22-23; 2:21-22; 3:14-21:", "norm_zh": "壹我们要来看享受恩典的结果终极完成这终极完成乃是神在永远里定意要得着的照着新约的启示神永远的定旨是要得着一个团体的身体作伟大宇宙的器皿以盛装并彰显祂自己弗一2223二2122三1421李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "I We will consider the issue the consummation of the enjoyment of grace this consummation is what God purposed to have in eternity according to the revelation of the New Testament Gods eternal purpose is to gain a corporate Body as a great universal vessel to contain and express HimselfEph 12223 22122 31421"}
{"zh": "一\t神的定旨乃是要得着一个活的团体器皿，由祂所创造、救赎、并重生之人所组成；神的心意是要所有的婴孩都借着享受神圣的恩典，从作婴孩的阶段，长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段—彼前一2~3、23：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "A. God's purpose is to have a corporate, living vessel composed of His created, redeemed, and regenerated people; God's intention is that through their enjoying of the divine grace, all the babes will grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for God's building.—1 Pet. 1:2-3, 23:", "norm_zh": "一神的定旨乃是要得着一个活的团体器皿由祂所创造救赎并重生之人所组成神的心意是要所有的婴孩都借着享受神圣的恩典从作婴孩的阶段长大到被变化成为活石为着神建造的阶段彼前一2323李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A Gods purpose is to have a corporate living vessel composed of His created redeemed and regenerated people Gods intention is that through their enjoying of the divine grace all the babes will grow from the stage of being babes into the stage of being transformed into living stones for Gods building1 Pet 123 23"}
{"zh": "1\t彼前二章二节说，所有重生的人都该像才生的婴孩一样，切慕那纯净的话奶，叫他们靠此长大，以致得救；才生的婴孩借着他们所吃、所喝的长大。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "1. 1 Peter 2:2 says that all the reborn ones as newborn babes should long for the guileless milk of the word in order that by it they may grow unto salvation; newborn babes grow by what they eat and what they drink.", "norm_zh": "1彼前二章二节说所有重生的人都该像才生的婴孩一样切慕哪纯净的话奶叫他们靠此长大以致得救才生的婴孩借着他们所吃所喝的长大李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 1 Peter 22 says that all the reborn ones as newborn babes should long for the guileless milk of the word in order that by it they may grow unto salvation newborn babes grow by what they eat and what they drink"}
{"zh": "2\t才生的婴孩借着长大，被变化成为活石，并且被建造成为属灵的殿，成为圣别的祭司体系—2节。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "2. Through their growth the newborn babes are transformed into living stones and are built up as a spiritual house into a holy priesthood.—v. 2.", "norm_zh": "2才生的婴孩借着长大被变化成为活石并且被建造成为属灵的殿成为圣别的祭司体系2节李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Through their growth the newborn babes are transformed into living stones and are built up as a spiritual house into a holy priesthoodv 2"}
{"zh": "二\t我们重生为才生的婴孩，但我们能被变化成为活石；神永远定旨的终极完成，是要得着建造起来的殿—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "B. We were regenerated as newborn babes, but we can be transformed into living stones; in the ultimate consummation of His eternal purpose, God will have a built-up house.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16:", "norm_zh": "二我们重生为才生的婴孩但我们能被变化成为活石神永远定旨的终极完成是要得着建造起来的殿创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B We were regenerated as newborn babes but we can be transformed into living stones in the ultimate consummation of His eternal purpose God will have a builtup houseGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "1\t照着圣经，石头是为着建造；我们需要问问自己是否已被建造到神属灵的殿里；我们若停留在作婴孩的阶段，就无法同被建造—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "1. According to the Bible, a stone is for building; we need to ask ourselves whether we have been built into God's spiritual house; if we remain in the stage of being babes, we cannot be built together.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "1照着圣经石头是为着建造我们需要问问自己是否已被建造到神属灵的殿里我们若停留在作婴孩的阶段就无法同被建造创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 According to the Bible a stone is for building we need to ask ourselves whether we have been built into Gods spiritual house if we remain in the stage of being babes we cannot be built togetherGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "2\t彼得说，我们作为活石，正被建造成为属灵的殿；这意思是建造现今正在进行—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "2. Peter says that as living stones, we are being built up as a spiritual house; this means that the building is progressing right now.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "2彼得说我们作为活石正被建造成为属灵的殿这意思是建造现今正在进行创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Peter says that as living stones we are being built up as a spiritual house this means that the building is progressing right nowGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "三\t今天在主的恢复里，主所作唯一的事，就是恢复地方召会生活真实的建造；这地方召会生活的建造，只能借着我们享受基督作恩典而进行—创二8~9、22，太十六18，西二19，弗四16。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "C. In the Lord's recovery today the unique thing that the Lord is doing is to recover the genuine building up of the local church life; this building up of the local church life can take place only by our enjoying Christ as grace.—Gen. 2:8-9, 22; Matt. 16:18; Col. 2:19; Eph. 4:16.", "norm_zh": "三今天在主的恢复里主所作惟一的事就是恢复地方召会生活真实的建造这地方召会生活的建造只能借着我们享受基督作恩典而进行创二8922太十六18西二19弗四16李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C In the Lords recovery today the unique thing that the Lord is doing is to recover the genuine building up of the local church life this building up of the local church life can take place only by our enjoying Christ as graceGen 289 22 Matt 1618 Col 219 Eph 416"}
{"zh": "贰\t我们若天天享受耶稣作我们的恩典，就会经历在生命里实际且逐渐的长大—弗四13、15~16：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "II. If we enjoy Jesus as our grace day by day, we will experience the practical and gradual growth in life.—Eph. 4:13, 15-16:", "norm_zh": "贰我们若天天享受耶稣作我们的恩典就会经历在生命里实际且逐渐的长大弗四131516李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "II If we enjoy Jesus as our grace day by day we will experience the practical and gradual growth in lifeEph 413 1516"}
{"zh": "一\t青年人若日复一日运用他们的灵呼求主名并祷读活的话，就会享受基督这活的人位，连同祂所是的一切、祂所赐的一切、和祂所作的一切，作他们的恩典；自然而然，他们享受恩典的结果，就是在神圣的生命里长大—林前三6，十四20，十六13。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "A. If the young people exercise their spirit to call on the name of the Lord and pray-read the living word day after day, they will enjoy Christ, the living person, with all that He is, all that He gives, and all that He does as their grace; spontaneously, as the issue of their enjoyment of grace, they will grow in the divine life.—1 Cor. 3:6; 14:20; 16:13.", "norm_zh": "一青年人若日复一日运用他们的灵呼求主名并祷读活的话就会享受基督这活的人位连同祂所是的一切祂所赐的一切和祂所作的一切作他们的恩典自然而然他们享受恩典的结果就是在神圣的生命里长大林前三6十四20十六13李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A If the young people exercise their spirit to call on the name of the Lord and prayread the living word day after day they will enjoy Christ the living person with all that He is all that He gives and all that He does as their grace spontaneously as the issue of their enjoyment of grace they will grow in the divine life1 Cor 36 1420 1613"}
{"zh": "二\t变化是在我们内里素质上新陈代谢的改变，显明于我们外面的形状或彰显；我们将更多基督的生命元素接受到全人里面，就发生这样的改变—林后五17，加六15，西三10~11，林后三18：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "B. Transformation is a metabolic change in our inward essence that is manifested in our outward form, or expression; such a change takes place when we receive more of the life element of Christ into our being.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 3:18:", "norm_zh": "二变化是在我们内里素质上新陈代谢的改变显明于我们外面的形状或彰显我们将更多基督的生命元素接受到全人里面就发生这样的改变林后五17加六15西三1011林后三18李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B Transformation is a metabolic change in our inward essence that is manifested in our outward form or expression such a change takes place when we receive more of the life element of Christ into our being2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "1\t这新元素排除我们天然所是的旧元素，并以基督的新元素顶替旧元素，就导致形状或外面彰显上的改变—五17，加六15，西三10~11。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "1. This new element discharges the old element of our natural being and replaces it with the new element of Christ, issuing in a change in form, or outward expression.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11.", "norm_zh": "1这新元素排除我们天然所是的旧元素并以基督的新元素顶替旧元素就导致形状或外面彰显上的改变五17加六15西三1011李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 This new element discharges the old element of our natural being and replaces it with the new element of Christ issuing in a change in form or outward expression2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011"}
{"zh": "2\t因此，林后三章十八节说，我们“渐渐变化成为与祂同样的形像”，那就是成为复活并得荣之基督的形像。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "2. Thus, 2 Cor. 3:18 says that we are \"being transformed into the same image,\" that is, into the image of the resurrected and glorified Christ.", "norm_zh": "2因此林后三章十八节说我们渐渐变化成为与祂同样的形像哪就是成为复活并得荣之基督的形像李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 Thus 2 Cor 318 says that we are being transformed into the same image that is into the image of the resurrected and glorified Christ"}
{"zh": "三\t借着呼求：“哦，主耶稣，”并祷读主话，我们就接受耶稣作赐生命之神圣的气，和滋养的神圣食物；这位丰富的耶稣进入我们里面，祂一切滋养的元素就借着属灵新陈代谢的过程，开始在我们里面作工—约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "C. By calling, \"O Lord Jesus,\" and pray-reading the Word, we receive Jesus as the life-giving divine breath and the nourishing divine food; when this rich Jesus enters into us, all His nourishing elements begin to work in us through a process of spiritual metabolism.—John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18:", "norm_zh": "三借着呼求哦主耶稣并祷读主话我们就接受耶稣作赐生命之神圣的气和滋养的神圣食物这位丰富的耶稣进入我们里面祂一切滋养的元素就借着属灵新陈代谢的过程开始在我们里面作工约六355763耶十五16弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C By calling O Lord Jesus and prayreading the Word we receive Jesus as the lifegiving divine breath and the nourishing divine food when this rich Jesus enters into us all His nourishing elements begin to work in us through a process of spiritual metabolismJohn 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "1\t我们呼求：“哦，主耶稣，”就将这位耶稣连同祂一切丰富的元素，接受到我们里面；罗马十章十二节说，“众人同有一位主，祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的”；我们能借着呼求祂而吸入祂，我们能借着祷读祂的话而吃祂（约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18）。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "1. When we call, \"O Lord Jesus,\" we receive this Jesus with all His rich elements into us; Rom. 10:12 says, \"The same Lord is Lord of all and rich to all who call upon Him\"; we can breathe Him by calling on Him, and we can eat Him by pray-reading His Word (John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18).", "norm_zh": "1我们呼求哦主耶稣就将这位耶稣连同祂一切丰富的元素接受到我们里面罗马十章十二节说众人同有一位主祂对一切呼求祂的人是丰富的我们能借着呼求祂而吸入祂我们能借着祷读祂的话而吃祂约六355763耶十五16弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 When we call O Lord Jesus we receive this Jesus with all His rich elements into us Rom 1012 says The same Lord is Lord of all and rich to all who call upon Him we can breathe Him by calling on Him and we can eat Him by prayreading His Word John 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "2\t我们无法凭自己排除里面的老旧；排除一切老旧最好的路，就是把耶稣接受进来；借着我们呼吸、吃、喝耶稣，属天和神圣的元素就进入我们里面；这元素会使我们得着新陈代谢的变化—林后五17，加六15，西三10~11，林后三18。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "2. By ourselves there is no way for us to discharge the oldness that is in us; the best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in; through our breathing, eating, and drinking of Jesus, the heavenly and divine element enters into us; this element will cause us to be metabolically transformed.—2 Cor. 5:17; Gal. 6:15; Col. 3:10-11; 2 Cor. 3:18.", "norm_zh": "2我们无法凭自己排除里面的老旧排除一切老旧最好的路就是把耶稣接受进来借着我们呼吸吃喝耶稣属天和神圣的元素就进入我们里面这元素会使我们得着新陈代谢的变化林后五17加六15西三1011林后三18李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "2 By ourselves there is no way for us to discharge the oldness that is in us the best way to discharge all the oldness is to take Jesus in through our breathing eating and drinking of Jesus the heavenly and divine element enters into us this element will cause us to be metabolically transformed2 Cor 517 Gal 615 Col 31011 2 Cor 318"}
{"zh": "叁\t借着变化胜过我们的乖僻—罗八2、29，约壹三2：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "III. Overcoming Our Peculiarity through TransformationIV. Overcoming Our Peculiarity through Transformation—Rom. 8:2, 29; 1 John 3:2:", "norm_zh": "叁借着变化胜过我们的乖僻罗八229约壹三2李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "III Overcoming Our Peculiarity through TransformationIV Overcoming Our Peculiarity through TransformationRom 82 29 1 John 32"}
{"zh": "一\t我们都有自己天然的构成；照着这构成，我们永远无法与别人是一；我们因着乖僻而有的难处越多，享受基督的机会就越多—林前二14~16。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "A. We all have our own natural constitution; according to this constitution, we could never be one with others; the more trouble we have because of our peculiarities, the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ.—1 Cor. 2:14-16.", "norm_zh": "一我们都有自己天然的构成照着这构成我们永远无法与别人是一我们因着乖僻而有的难处越多享受基督的机会就越多林前二1416李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A We all have our own natural constitution according to this constitution we could never be one with others the more trouble we have because of our peculiarities the more opportunities we have to enjoy Christ1 Cor 21416"}
{"zh": "二\t被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话，好将祂接受进来；姊妹们若行这些事，主耶稣就会在她们里面作变化的工作；祂不会仅仅改正她们，乃会变化她们；祂会以祂自己顶替她们—约六35、57、63，耶十五16，弗六17~18。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "B. The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and pray-read His Word in order to take Him in; if the sisters will do these things, the Lord Jesus will do a transforming work within them; He will not merely correct them but will transform them; He will replace them with Himself.—John 6:35, 57, 63; Jer. 15:16; Eph. 6:17-18.", "norm_zh": "二被变化的路就是呼求耶稣的名并祷读祂的话好将祂接受进来姊妹们若行这些事主耶稣就会在她们里面作变化的工作祂不会仅仅改正她们乃会变化她们祂会以祂自己顶替她们约六355763耶十五16弗六1718李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B The way to be transformed is to call on the name of Jesus and prayread His Word in order to take Him in if the sisters will do these things the Lord Jesus will do a transforming work within them He will not merely correct them but will transform them He will replace them with HimselfJohn 635 57 63 Jer 1516 Eph 61718"}
{"zh": "三\t经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造；她无论在哪里，不管在家庭里，在姊妹之家里，或在召会的圣徒当中，都不会与任何人有难处—罗八16，十二1~2、4~5。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "C. A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others; wherever she is, whether in a family, in a sisters' house, or among the saints in the church, she will have no problem with anyone.—Rom. 8:16; 12:1-2, 4-5.", "norm_zh": "三经过变化的姊妹适合与别人一同被建造她无论在哪里不管在家庭里在姊妹之家里或在召会的圣徒当中都不会与任何人有难处罗八16十二1245李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C A transformed sister is fit to be built up with others wherever she is whether in a family in a sisters house or among the saints in the church she will have no problem with anyoneRom 816 1212 45"}
{"zh": "四\t信徒经过变化以后，就变得非常有弹性，能适合任何一种情况，并且能与任何一种信徒一同被建造；这样的人适合建造—八16，十二1~2、4~5。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "D. After being transformed, a believer becomes very flexible; he is_ able to fit into any kind of situation and be built with any kind of believer; such a person is fit for the building.—Rom. 8:16; 12:1-2, 4-5.", "norm_zh": "四信徒经过变化以后就变得非常有弹性能适合任何一种情况并且能与任何一种信徒一同被建造这样的人适合建造八16十二1245李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "D After being transformed a believer becomes very flexible he is_ able to fit into any kind of situation and be built with any kind of believer such a person is fit for the buildingRom 816 1212 45"}
{"zh": "肆\t被变化并建造，为着召会的扩增与扩展—创三二28，三五10、15：（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "IV. TRANSFORMED AND BUILT UP FOR THE INCREASE AND SPREAD OF THE CHURCH—Gen. 32:28; 35:10, 15:", "norm_zh": "肆被变化并建造为着召会的扩增与扩展创三二28三五1015李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IV TRANSFORMED AND BUILT UP FOR THE INCREASE AND SPREAD OF THE CHURCHGen 3228 3510 15"}
{"zh": "一\t弟兄们若对主认真，并且是真实寻求主和纯诚爱主的人，就会到主面前去迫切祷告，不但为着自己的变化祷告，也为着召会的扩增祷告—罗八28~29，十二2。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "A. If the brothers mean business with the Lord and are genuine seekers and sincere lovers of the Lord, they will go to the Lord and pray desperately not only for their transformation but also for the increase of the church.—Rom. 8:28-29; 12:2.", "norm_zh": "一弟兄们若对主认真并且是真实寻求主和纯诚爱主的人就会到主面前去迫切祷告不但为着自己的变化祷告也为着召会的扩增祷告罗八2829十二2李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "A If the brothers mean business with the Lord and are genuine seekers and sincere lovers of the Lord they will go to the Lord and pray desperately not only for their transformation but also for the increase of the churchRom 82829 122"}
{"zh": "二\t我鼓励姊妹们更多的接受基督进来，作她们的享受，我也告诫弟兄们要有迫切的态度，与主彻底的办交涉；弟兄们需要告诉主：“主，我不要不冷不热或冷淡！我要火热！我要焚烧！”我们当中需要建造，而建造来自变化—八28~29，十二2。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "B. I encourage the sisters to take in more of Christ for their enjoyment, and I admonish the brothers to have a thorough dealing with the Lord with an attitude of desperation; the brothers need to tell the Lord, \"Lord, I don't want to be lukewarm or cold! I want to be hot! I want to be burning!\" Among us we need the building, and the building comes from transformation.—Rom. 8:28-29; 12:2.", "norm_zh": "二我鼓励姊妹们更多的接受基督进来作她们的享受我也告诫弟兄们要有迫切的态度与主彻底的办交涉弟兄们需要告诉主主我不要不冷不热或冷淡我要火热我要焚烧我们当中需要建造而建造来自变化八2829十二2李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "B I encourage the sisters to take in more of Christ for their enjoyment and I admonish the brothers to have a thorough dealing with the Lord with an attitude of desperation the brothers need to tell the Lord Lord I dont want to be lukewarm or cold I want to be hot I want to be burning Among us we need the building and the building comes from transformationRom 82829 122"}
{"zh": "三\t我们不该忘记，享受恩典是为着在生命里长大，在生命里长大是为着变化，变化终极完成于建造，而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展—罗十二2，启二一18上。（李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册，新约中的恩典，第五章）", "en": "C. We should not forget that the enjoyment of grace is for the growth in life, the growth in life is for transformation, transformation consummates in the building, and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lord's testimony.—Rom. 12:2; Rev. 21:18a.", "norm_zh": "三我们不该忘记享受恩典是为着在生命里长大在生命里长大是为着变化变化终极完成于建造而建造是为着主见证的扩增与扩展罗十二2启二一18上李常受文集一九七三至一九七四年第一册新约中的恩典第五章", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:19:36.238302+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "C We should not forget that the enjoyment of grace is for the growth in life the growth in life is for transformation transformation consummates in the building and the building is for the increase and spread of the Lords testimonyRom 122 Rev 2118a"}
{"zh": "引言—旧约卷书的主题", "en": "Introduction—The Subject of the Books of the Old Testament", "norm_zh": "引言旧约卷书的主提", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "IntroductionThe Subject of the Books of the Old Testament"}
{"zh": "出埃及记         基督是神子民的救赎、拯救和供应，也是他们敬拜并事奉的凭借，使他们在祂里面与神建造在一起，而得与神相见，彼此交通，互为居所。", "en": "Exodus—Christ is the redemption, salvation, and supply of God's people and the means for them to worship and serve God, so that they may be built up with God in Him for them to meet with God, fellowship with each other, and be a mutual dwelling place.", "norm_zh": "出埃及记基督是神子民的救赎拯救和供应也是他们敬拜并事奉的凭借使他们在祂里面与神建造在一起而得与神相见彼此交通互为居所", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "ExodusChrist is the redemption salvation and supply of Gods people and the means for them to worship and serve God so that they may be built up with God in Him for them to meet with God fellowship with each other and be a mutual dwelling place"}
{"zh": "利未记            基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通、事奉和生活上的一切。", "en": "Leviticus—Christ is everything to the redeemed people of God in their fellowship, service, and living.", "norm_zh": "利未记基督是蒙神救赎的人在交通事奉和生活上的一切", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "LeviticusChrist is everything to the redeemed people of God in their fellowship service and living"}
{"zh": "约书亚记         以色列人占有并得着美地为业，以完成神的经纶。", "en": "Joshua—The children of Israel possessing and inheriting the good land for the fulfillment of God's economy.", "norm_zh": "约书亚记以色列人占有并得着美地为业以完成神的经纶", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "JoshuaThe children of Israel possessing and inheriting the good land for the fulfillment of Gods economy"}
{"zh": "士师记            以色列离弃神，遭仇敌击败，渐渐腐败。", "en": "Judges—Israel forsaking God, being defeated by their enemies, and becoming corrupted.", "norm_zh": "士师记以色列离弃神遭仇敌击败渐渐腐败", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "JudgesIsrael forsaking God being defeated by their enemies and becoming corrupted"}
{"zh": "路得记            一幅完整的表号，说到外邦的罪人，借着基督的救赎，而与基督联结，与神的选民以色列同被带进神的产业。", "en": "Ruth—A complete type of the Gentile sinners being brought, through Christ's redemption, into the association with Christ and into the organic union with Christ's elect, Israel, for the inheritance of God's partition.", "norm_zh": "路得记一幅完整的表号说到外邦的罪人借着基督的救赎而与基督联结与神的选民以色列同被带进神的产业", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "RuthA complete type of the Gentile sinners being brought through Christs redemption into the association with Christ and into the organic union with Christs elect Israel for the inheritance of Gods partition"}
{"zh": "撒母耳记上下  享受神所赐美地之路的例证。", "en": "1 & 2 Samuel—Illustrations of the way to enjoy the God-given good land.", "norm_zh": "撒母耳记上下享受神所赐美地之路的例证", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 2 SamuelIllustrations of the way to enjoy the Godgiven good land"}
{"zh": "列王纪上下     在神经纶中神行政的对付，连同神的君王职分在地上因着列王而遭破坏与毁灭，以及神公正对付的悲惨结果。", "en": "1 & 2 Kings—God's governmental dealing, in God's economy, with the devastation and ruin of the divine kingship on the earth by the kings and the tragic issue of the just dealing of God.", "norm_zh": "列王纪上下在神经纶中神行政的对付连同神的君王职分在地上因着列王而遭破坏与毁灭以及神公正对付的悲惨结果", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 2 KingsGods governmental dealing in Gods economy with the devastation and ruin of the divine kingship on the earth by the kings and the tragic issue of the just dealing of God"}
{"zh": "历代志上下     神在人历史中行动的全部纪事，就是从亚当经过撒母耳到以色列被掳归回，向我们陈明神对付犹大诸王的一些重要细节。", "en": "1 & 2 Chronicles—A full chronology of God's move in man's history from Adam through Samuel to the return of Israel from their captivity, presenting to us some of the important details of God's dealing with the kings of Judah.", "norm_zh": "历代志上下神在人历史中行动的全部纪事就是从亚当经过撒母耳到以色列被掳归回向我们陈明神对付犹大诸王的一些重要细节", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 2 ChroniclesA full chronology of Gods move in mans history from Adam through Samuel to the return of Israel from their captivity presenting to us some of the important details of Gods dealing with the kings of Judah"}
{"zh": "以斯拉记         以色列人从被掳中归回，重建神的殿，开始了神选民中间照着神的经纶，为着神在地上见证的恢复。", "en": "Ezra—The return of the children of Israel from their captivity and the rebuilding of the temple of God, initiating the recovery of God's testimony among His elect on the earth according to His economy.", "norm_zh": "以斯拉记以色列人从被掳中归回重建神的殿开始了神选民中间照着神的经纶为着神在地上见证的恢复", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "EzraThe return of the children of Israel from their captivity and the rebuilding of the temple of God initiating the recovery of Gods testimony among His elect on the earth according to His economy"}
{"zh": "尼希米记         重建耶路撒冷的城墙，继续神选民中间祂见证的恢复，以完成祂的经纶。", "en": "Nehemiah         The rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem and the continuation of the recovery of His testimony among His elect for the accomplishment of His economy.", "norm_zh": "尼希米记重建耶路撒冷的城墙继续神选民中间祂见证的恢复以完成祂的经纶", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Nehemiah The rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem and the continuation of the recovery of His testimony among His elect for the accomplishment of His economy"}
{"zh": "以斯帖记         拣选以色列人作选民的这位神，在他们被掳到外邦列国中的期间，对他们成了隐藏的神，秘密的照顾他们，并在隐密中公开的拯救他们。", "en": "Esther         The very God who chose Israel as His elect becoming a hidden God to them to take care of them secretly and save them openly in secrecy during their captivity among the Gentile nations.", "norm_zh": "以斯帖记拣选以色列人作选民的这位神在他们被掳到外邦列国中的期间对他们成了隐藏的神秘密的照顾他们并在隐密中公开的拯救他们", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Esther The very God who chose Israel as His elect becoming a hidden God to them to take care of them secretly and save them openly in secrecy during their captivity among the Gentile nations"}
{"zh": "约伯记            神对付祂选民的目的。", "en": "Job         The purpose of God's dealing with His elect.", "norm_zh": "约伯记神对付祂选民的目的", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Job The purpose of Gods dealing with His elect"}
{"zh": "诗篇               寻求并接触神的敬虔之人，借着他们的赞美、祷告、并欢腾的歌唱，表达他们的情绪、感觉、感想和经历。", "en": "Psalms—The expressions of the sentiments, feelings, impressions, and experiences of godly men seeking and contacting God, through their praises, prayers, and jubilant singings.", "norm_zh": "诗篇寻求并接触神的敬虔之人借着他们的赞美祷告并欢腾的歌唱表达他们的情绪感觉感想和经历", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "PsalmsThe expressions of the sentiments feelings impressions and experiences of godly men seeking and contacting God through their praises prayers and jubilant singings"}
{"zh": "箴言               智慧的话，教导人如何在人生中行事为人，并建立他们的性格。", "en": "Proverbs         Words of wisdom teaching people how to behave and how to build up their character in the human life.", "norm_zh": "箴言智慧的话教导人如何在人生中行事为人并建立他们的性格", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Proverbs Words of wisdom teaching people how to behave and how to build up their character in the human life"}
{"zh": "传道书            所罗门的教训，给人看见在败坏世界里的人生，都是虚空，都是捕风。", "en": "Ecclesiastes         The teachings of Solomon showing that the human life in the corrupted world is vanity, a chasing after wind.", "norm_zh": "传道书所罗门的教训给人看见在败坏世界里的人生都是虚空都是捕风", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ecclesiastes The teachings of Solomon showing that the human life in the corrupted world is vanity a chasing after wind"}
{"zh": "雅歌               一个超绝婚姻里爱的历史，启示出个别信徒与基督爱的交通中进展的经历。", "en": "Song of Songs         A history of love in an excellent marriage, revealing the progressive experience of an individual believer's loving fellowship with Christ.", "norm_zh": "雅歌一个超绝婚姻里爱的历史启示出个别信徒与基督爱的交通中进展的经历", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Song of Songs A history of love in an excellent marriage revealing the progressive experience of an individual believers loving fellowship with Christ"}
{"zh": "以赛亚书         耶和华借着成为肉体、钉死十架、复活、升天、并再来的基督所施的救恩。", "en": "Isaiah         The salvation of Jehovah through Christ, incarnated, crucified, resurrected, ascended, and coming again.", "norm_zh": "以赛亚书耶和华借着成为肉体钉死十架复活升天并再来的基督所施的救恩", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Isaiah The salvation of Jehovah through Christ incarnated crucified resurrected ascended and coming again"}
{"zh": "耶利米书         基督在神对付以色列和列国时，成为耶和华对神选民的义，作他们的中心和圆周。", "en": "Jeremiah         Christ as the righteousness of Jehovah to God's elect as their center and circumference in God's dealing with Israel and the nations.", "norm_zh": "耶利米书基督在神对付以色列和列国时成为耶和华对神选民的义作他们的中心和圆周", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jeremiah Christ as the righteousness of Jehovah to Gods elect as their center and circumference in Gods dealing with Israel and the nations"}
{"zh": "耶利米哀歌     耶利米对神的圣城和圣民之忧伤与爱的发表。", "en": "Lamentations         The expression of Jeremiah's sorrow and love over the holy city and the holy people of God.", "norm_zh": "耶利米哀歌耶利米对神的圣城和圣民之忧伤与爱的发表", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Lamentations The expression of Jeremiahs sorrow and love over the holy city and the holy people of God"}
{"zh": "以西结书         神在荣耀里向人显现；祂对自己百姓和列国的审判，以及祂选民的恢复，为着建造一个居所，为祂并作祂相互的住处和完全的彰显。", "en": "Ezekiel         The manifestation of God in glory to man; His judgment upon His own people and the nations, and the recovery of His elect for the building of a dwelling place for Him and to be His and their mutual abode and complete expression.", "norm_zh": "以西结书神在荣耀里向人显现祂对自己百姓和列国的审判以及祂选民的恢复为着建造一个居所为祂并作祂相互的住处和完全的彰显", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ezekiel The manifestation of God in glory to man His judgment upon His own people and the nations and the recovery of His elect for the building of a dwelling place for Him and to be His and their mutual abode and complete expression"}
{"zh": "但以理书         神截定给以色列的定命，就是七十个七的内容。", "en": "Daniel—The destiny of Israel apportioned out by God, the contents of the seventy weeks.", "norm_zh": "但以理书神截定给以色列的定命就是七十个七的内容", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "DanielThe destiny of Israel apportioned out by God the contents of the seventy weeks"}
{"zh": "何西阿书         耶和华是邪淫背道之以色列的救恩，接受并接纳她回来。", "en": "Hosea—Jehovah as salvation to adulterous and apostate Israel in receiving and welcoming her back.", "norm_zh": "何西阿书耶和华是邪淫背道之以色列的救恩接受并接纳她回来", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "HoseaJehovah as salvation to adulterous and apostate Israel in receiving and welcoming her back"}
{"zh": "约珥书            人类政权对以色列四个阶段的残害，以及基督对残害者的毁坏，并祂在复兴时在以色列中间的掌权。", "en": "Joel—The devastation of human government in four stages upon Israel and the destruction of the devastators by Christ with His reigning among Israel in the restoration.", "norm_zh": "约珥书人类政权对以色列四个阶段的残害以及基督对残害者的毁坏并祂在复兴时在以色列中间的掌权", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "JoelThe devastation of human government in four stages upon Israel and the destruction of the devastators by Christ with His reigning among Israel in the restoration"}
{"zh": "俄巴底亚书     耶和华对以扫的对付，以及雅各为着耶和华之国的胜利。", "en": "Obadiah—Jehovah's dealing with Esau and Jacob's victory for the kingdom of Jehovah.", "norm_zh": "俄巴底亚书耶和华对以扫的对付以及雅各为着耶和华之国的胜利", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "ObadiahJehovahs dealing with Esau and Jacobs victory for the kingdom of Jehovah"}
{"zh": "约拿书            耶和华的救恩，甚至临到外邦人的城尼尼微。", "en": "Jonah—Jehovah's salvation extending even to the Gentile city Nineveh.", "norm_zh": "约拿书耶和华的救恩甚至临到外邦人的城尼尼微", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "JonahJehovahs salvation extending even to the Gentile city Nineveh"}
{"zh": "弥迦书            耶和华对以色列的责备，以及祂对以色列的复兴。", "en": "Micah—Jehovah's reproof on Israel and His restoration of Israel.", "norm_zh": "弥迦书耶和华对以色列的责备以及祂对以色列的复兴", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "MicahJehovahs reproof on Israel and His restoration of Israel"}
{"zh": "那鸿书            耶和华对邪恶亚述之京城尼尼微的审判。", "en": "Nahum—Jehovah's judgment on Nineveh, the capital of evil Assyria.", "norm_zh": "哪鸿书耶和华对邪恶亚述之京城尼尼微的审判", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "NahumJehovahs judgment on Nineveh the capital of evil Assyria"}
{"zh": "哈巴谷书         神先借着迦勒底人对以色列施行公义的审判，然后又借着列国对迦勒底人施行公义的审判。", "en": "Habakkuk—The righteous judgment of God, first upon Israel through the Chaldeans, and then upon the Chaldeans through the nations.", "norm_zh": "哈巴谷书神先借着迦勒底人对以色列施行公义的审判然后又借着列国对迦勒底人施行公义的审判", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "HabakkukThe righteous judgment of God first upon Israel through the Chaldeans and then upon the Chaldeans through the nations"}
{"zh": "西番雅书         耶和华对以色列和列国的审判，以及祂对外邦和以色列的拯救。", "en": "Zephaniah—Jehovah's judgment on Israel and on the nations, and His salvation to the nations and to Israel.", "norm_zh": "西番雅书耶和华对以色列和列国的审判以及祂对外邦和以色列的拯救", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "ZephaniahJehovahs judgment on Israel and on the nations and His salvation to the nations and to Israel"}
{"zh": "哈该书            耶和华对付被掳归回的人，为着建造祂的殿。", "en": "Haggai—Jehovah's dealing with the returned captives for the building of His temple.", "norm_zh": "哈该书耶和华对付被掳归回的人为着建造祂的殿", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "HaggaiJehovahs dealing with the returned captives for the building of His temple"}
{"zh": "圣经是神的说话，分为两部分：第一部分，旧约，是神借着众申言者说话；第二部分，新约，是神在子里，就是在子的人位里说话。（来一1~2）", "en": "The Bible is the speaking of God, divided into two parts: the first part, the Old Testament, is God's speaking in the prophets; the second part, the New Testament, is God's speaking in the Son, that is, in the Person of the Son (Heb. 1:1-2).", "norm_zh": "圣经是神的说话分为两部分第一部分旧约是神借着众申言者说话第二部分新约是神在子里就是在子的人位里说话来一12", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Bible is the speaking of God divided into two parts the first part the Old Testament is Gods speaking in the prophets the second part the New Testament is Gods speaking in the Son that is in the Person of the Son Heb 112"}
{"zh": "摩西的五卷书（摩西五经）—创世记、出埃及记、利未记、民数记与申命记", "en": "The five books of Moses (the Pentateuch)—Genesis, Exodus, Leviticus, Numbers, and Deuteronomy", "norm_zh": "摩西的五卷书摩西五经创世记出埃及记利未记民数记与申命记", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The five books of Moses the PentateuchGenesis Exodus Leviticus Numbers and Deuteronomy"}
{"zh": "摩西的五卷书（摩西五经）：在神圣启示的进展里，有神圣启示的进步。在创世记，有神与祂的创造。在出埃及记，有神的救恩与祂居所的建造。在利未记，有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活。在民数记，我们看见神所救赎的人编组成为神的军队，以及他们为神争战的行程。申命记重申神圣的律法，不仅是摩西五经的结语，也是律法的结语。（民数记生命读经，第一篇；申命记生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "The five books of Moses (the Pentateuch): In the progress of the divine revelation, there is an advancement of the divine revelation. In Genesis, there is God and His creation. In Exodus, there is God's salvation and the building of His dwelling place. In Leviticus, there is the worship and living of the redeemed ones. In Numbers, we see God's redeemed people formed into His army and their journeying to fight for God. Deuteronomy rehearses the divine law, which is not only the conclusion of the Pentateuch but also the conclusion of the law.", "norm_zh": "摩西的五卷书摩西五经在神圣启示的进展里有神圣启示的进步在创世记有神与祂的创造在出埃及记有神的救恩与祂居所的建造在利未记有蒙救赎者的敬拜与生活在民数记我们看见神所救赎的人编组成为神的军队以及他们为神争战的行程申命记重申神圣的律法不仅是摩西五经的结语也是律法的结语民数记生命读经第一篇申命记生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The five books of Moses the Pentateuch In the progress of the divine revelation there is an advancement of the divine revelation In Genesis there is God and His creation In Exodus there is Gods salvation and the building of His dwelling place In Leviticus there is the worship and living of the redeemed ones In Numbers we see Gods redeemed people formed into His army and their journeying to fight for God Deuteronomy rehearses the divine law which is not only the conclusion of the Pentateuch but also the conclusion of the law"}
{"zh": "历史书—约书亚记、士师记、路得记、撒母耳记上和下、列王纪上和下、历代志上和下、以斯拉记、尼希米记与以斯帖记", "en": "The books of history—Joshua, Judges, Ruth, 1 and 2 Samuel, 1 and 2 Kings, 1 and 2 Chronicles, Ezra, Nehemiah, and Esther", "norm_zh": "历史书约书亚记士师记路得记撒母耳记上和下列王纪上和下历代志上和下以斯拉记尼希米记与以斯帖记", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The books of historyJoshua Judges Ruth 1 and 2 Samuel 1 and 2 Kings 1 and 2 Chronicles Ezra Nehemiah and Esther"}
{"zh": "照着从约书亚记到以斯帖记所记载的历史，其内在的启示乃是向我们揭示，神永远的经纶如何在地上由祂的选民所施行。首先，约书亚记给我们看见，如何取得、占有、并守住美地。然后，士师记、路得记、撒母耳记上、下这几卷书，描绘出一些人的图画，给我们看见他们在得了美地为业之后，如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地。在士师记里所记载的几位士师，路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯，撒母耳记上、下所记载的以利、撒母耳、扫罗、约拿单、大卫，呈现一幅幅生动的图画，给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地。虽然那些图画刻画得很详细，但仍然需要列王纪上、下提供更多人物的图画，给我们看见他们如何留在美地上，并如何享受美地。以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关；尼希米记与修复、重建圣城有关；以斯帖记给我们看见，无所不在、无所不能的神，如何成了隐藏的神，保护在被掳中祂分散的选民。", "en": "According to the history recorded from Joshua to Esther, the intrinsic revelation is to unveil to us how God's eternal economy is carried out on earth by His elect. First, the book of Joshua shows us how to gain, possess, and keep the good land. Then, the books of Judges, Ruth, and 1 and 2 Samuel present pictures of certain persons, showing us how they, after inheriting the good land, remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land. The judges recorded in Judges, Ruth and Boaz in Ruth, and Eli, Samuel, Saul, Jonathan, and David in 1 and 2 Samuel present vivid pictures showing us how these people remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land. Although those pictures are portrayed in detail, there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to provide pictures of more persons to show us how they remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land. Ezra is related to the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple; Nehemiah is related to the recovery and rebuilding of the holy city; Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became a hidden God to protect His scattered elect in captivity.", "norm_zh": "照着从约书亚记到以斯帖记所记载的历史其内在的启示乃是向我们揭示神永远的经纶如何在地上由祂的选民所施行首先约书亚记给我们看见如何取得占有并守住美地然后士师记路得记撒母耳记上下这几卷书描绘出一些人的图画给我们看见他们在得了美地为业之后如何留在美地上并如何享受美地在士师记里所记载的几位士师路得记里所记载的路得和波阿斯撒母耳记上下所记载的以利撒母耳扫罗约拿单大卫呈现一幅幅生动的图画给我们看见这些人如何留在美地上并如何享受美地虽然哪些图画刻画得很详细但仍然需要列王纪上下提供更多人物的图画给我们看见他们如何留在美地上并如何享受美地以斯拉记与归回耶路撒冷重建圣殿有关尼希米记与修复重建圣城有关以斯帖记给我们看见无所不在无所不能的神如何成了隐藏的神保护在被掳中祂分散的选民", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "According to the history recorded from Joshua to Esther the intrinsic revelation is to unveil to us how Gods eternal economy is carried out on earth by His elect First the book of Joshua shows us how to gain possess and keep the good land Then the books of Judges Ruth and 1 and 2 Samuel present pictures of certain persons showing us how they after inheriting the good land remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land The judges recorded in Judges Ruth and Boaz in Ruth and Eli Samuel Saul Jonathan and David in 1 and 2 Samuel present vivid pictures showing us how these people remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land Although those pictures are portrayed in detail there is still the need of 1 and 2 Kings to provide pictures of more persons to show us how they remained in the good land and enjoyed the good land Ezra is related to the return to Jerusalem to rebuild the temple Nehemiah is related to the recovery and rebuilding of the holy city Esther shows us how the omnipresent and omnipotent God became a hidden God to protect His scattered elect in captivity"}
{"zh": "五卷诗歌书的顺序", "en": "The sequence of the five books of poetry", "norm_zh": "五卷诗歌书的顺序", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The sequence of the five books of poetry"}
{"zh": "小申言者书—何西阿书、俄巴底亚书、阿摩司书、约珥书、约拿书、弥迦书、那鸿书、哈巴谷书、西番雅书、哈该书、撒迦利亚书与玛拉基书", "en": "The Minor Prophets—Hosea, Obadiah, Amos, Joel, Jonah, Micah, Nahum, Habakkuk, Zephaniah, Haggai, Zechariah, and Malachi", "norm_zh": "小申言者书何西阿书俄巴底亚书阿摩司书约珥书约拿书弥迦书哪鸿书哈巴谷书西番雅书哈该书撒迦利亚书与玛拉基书", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Minor ProphetsHosea Obadiah Amos Joel Jonah Micah Nahum Habakkuk Zephaniah Haggai Zechariah and Malachi"}
{"zh": "小申言者书着重四个主要的点：神以色列爱的惩治和行政的对付、祂对列国的审判、基督的显现以及万物的复兴。虽然小申言者书是较小的，但这些书所带进的启示是大的。小申言者书之神圣启示的中心点与大申言者书中的相同。（何西阿书生命读经，一四三至一四五页）", "en": "The Minor Prophets focus on four main points: God's loving chastisement and governmental dealing with Israel, His judgment upon the nations, the manifestation of Christ, and the restoration of all things. Although the Minor Prophets are minor, the revelation brought in by these books is great. The central point of the divine revelation in the Minor Prophets is the same as that in the Major Prophets.", "norm_zh": "小申言者书着重四个主要的点神以色列爱的惩治和行政的对付祂对列国的审判基督的显现以及万物的复兴虽然小申言者书是较小的但这些书所带进的启示是大的小申言者书之神圣启示的中心点与大申言者书中的相同何西阿书生命读经一四三至一四五页", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Minor Prophets focus on four main points Gods loving chastisement and governmental dealing with Israel His judgment upon the nations the manifestation of Christ and the restoration of all things Although the Minor Prophets are minor the revelation brought in by these books is great The central point of the divine revelation in the Minor Prophets is the same as that in the Major Prophets"}
{"zh": "圣经由旧约和新约二约组成，是神写给人完整的神圣启示。整本圣经主要的启示，乃是独一的三一神惟一的神圣经纶。（弗一10，三9，提前一4下）这神圣经纶的中心与普及，乃是包罗万有且追测不尽之丰富的基督，作三一神的具体化身和彰显。（西二9，一15~19，约一18）神圣经纶的目标，乃是召会作基督的身体，基督的丰满和彰显，（弗一22下~23，三8~11）终极完成于新耶路撒冷，作经过过程并终极完成之三一神，与祂所救赎、重生、变化、并荣化之三部分人的联结、调和与合并。神圣经纶的完成有许多步骤，在圣经中渐进的启示出来，开始于创一~二神的创造，完成于启二一~二二的新耶路撒冷。在旧约里，神经纶的内容主要是以预表、表号、和影儿启示出来；在新约里，一切的预表、表号、和影儿都应验并实现了。因此，旧约是神永远经纶的象征描绘，新约是它实际的应验。", "en": "The Bible, composed of two testaments, the Old Testament and the New Testament, is the complete written divine revelation of God to man. The major revelation in the entire Bible is the unique divine economy of the unique Triune God (Eph. 1:10; 3:9; 1 Tim. 1:4). The centrality and universality of this divine economy is the all-inclusive and unsearchably rich Christ as the embodiment and expression of the Triune God (Col. 2:9; 1:15-19; John 1:18). The goal of the divine economy is the church as the Body, the fullness, the expression, of Christ (Eph. 1:22-23; 3:8-11), which will consummate in the New Jerusalem as the union, mingling, and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God and His redeemed, regenerated, transformed, and glorified tripartite people. The accomplishing of the divine economy is revealed in the Bible progressively in many steps, beginning with God's creation in Gen. 1, Gen. 2 and consummating with the New Jerusalem in Rev. 21, Rev. 22. In the Old Testament the contents of God's economy are revealed mainly in types, figures, and shadows, whereas in the New Testament all the types, figures, and shadows are fulfilled and realized. Thus, the Old Testament is a figurative portrait of God's eternal economy, and the New Testament is the practical fulfillment.", "norm_zh": "圣经由旧约和新约二约组成是神写给人完整的神圣启示整本圣经主要的启示乃是独一的三一神惟一的神圣经纶弗一10三9提前一4下这神圣经纶的中心与普及乃是包罗万有且追测不尽之丰富的基督作三一神的具体化身和彰显西二9一1519约一18神圣经纶的目标乃是召会作基督的身体基督的丰满和彰显弗一22下23三811终极完成于新耶路撒冷作经过过程并终极完成之三一神与祂所救赎重生变化并荣化之三部分人的联结调和与合并神圣经纶的完成有许多步骤在圣经中渐进的启示出来开始于创一二神的创造完成于启二一二二的新耶路撒冷在旧约里神经纶的内容主要是以预表表号和影儿启示出来在新约里一切的预表表号和影儿都应验并实现了因此旧约是神永远经纶的象征描绘新约是它实际的应验", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Bible composed of two testaments the Old Testament and the New Testament is the complete written divine revelation of God to man The major revelation in the entire Bible is the unique divine economy of the unique Triune God Eph 110 39 1 Tim 14 The centrality and universality of this divine economy is the allinclusive and unsearchably rich Christ as the embodiment and expression of the Triune God Col 29 11519 John 118 The goal of the divine economy is the church as the Body the fullness the expression of Christ Eph 12223 3811 which will consummate in the New Jerusalem as the union mingling and incorporation of the processed and consummated Triune God and His redeemed regenerated transformed and glorified tripartite people The accomplishing of the divine economy is revealed in the Bible progressively in many steps beginning with Gods creation in Gen 1 Gen 2 and consummating with the New Jerusalem in Rev 21 Rev 22 In the Old Testament the contents of Gods economy are revealed mainly in types figures and shadows whereas in the New Testament all the types figures and shadows are fulfilled and realized Thus the Old Testament is a figurative portrait of Gods eternal economy and the New Testament is the practical fulfillment"}
{"zh": "“创世记”是七十士希腊文译本所采用本卷的书名，其拉丁文意为，生产，起源。创世记为圣经第一卷书，生出圣言中神圣的真理，也是圣言中神圣真理的起源。因此，神圣真理的种子乃是撒在这卷书里。这些种子在以后各卷书中，特别在新约里，长大并发展，至终收成于末一卷书启示录。", "en": "Genesis, adopted by the Septuagint as the title of this book, is a Latin word meaning giving of birth, origin. As the first book in the Bible, Genesis gives birth to and is the origin of the divine truths in the holy Word. Thus, the seeds of the divine truths are sown in this book. These seeds grow and develop in the succeeding books, especially in the New Testament, and are finally harvested in the last book, the book of Revelation.", "norm_zh": "创世记是七十士希腊文译本所采用本卷的书名其拉丁文意为生产起源创世记为圣经第一卷书生出圣言中神圣的真理也是圣言中神圣真理的起源因此神圣真理的种子乃是撒在这卷书里这些种子在以后各卷书中特别在新约里长大并发展至终收成于末一卷书启示录", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Genesis adopted by the Septuagint as the title of this book is a Latin word meaning giving of birth origin As the first book in the Bible Genesis gives birth to and is the origin of the divine truths in the holy Word Thus the seeds of the divine truths are sown in this book These seeds grow and develop in the succeeding books especially in the New Testament and are finally harvested in the last book the book of Revelation"}
{"zh": "表面上，创一~二仅仅是创造的记载；事实上，这两章的记载中，几乎每一项都启示基督作神子民的生命，（约一1、4，十一25，十四6）为着产生并建造召会。三~五十章陈明八大人物的传记。这八大人物分为两组，各有四人，代表人类的两个族类：亚当、亚伯、以诺和挪亚，代表受造的族类；亚伯拉罕、以撒、雅各和约瑟，代表蒙召的族类。其中所记载的，主要不是这些人的工作，乃是他们的生命、生活、并他们在神面前的道路。在创世记里，神用创造的记载和八个人物的传记，启示出完成祂定旨的生命。（圣经恢复本，创一1注1）", "en": "Apparently, chs. 1—2 of Genesis are merely a record of creation; actually, nearly every item in the record of these two chapters is a revelation of Christ, who is life to God's people (John 1:1, 4; 11:25; 14:6) for the producing and building up of the church. Chapters 3—50 present biographies of eight great persons in two groups of four, representing two races of men: Adam, Abel, Enoch, and Noah, representing the created race, and Abraham, Isaac, Jacob, and Joseph, representing the called race. What is recorded is not primarily the works of these men but mainly their life, their living, and their way with God. In Genesis God uses both the record of creation and the biographies of eight persons to reveal the life that fulfills His purpose.", "norm_zh": "表面上创一二仅仅是创造的记载事实上这两章的记载中几乎每一项都启示基督作神子民的生命约一14十一25十四6为着产生并建造召会三五十章陈明八大人物的传记这八大人物分为两组各有四人代表人类的两个族类亚当亚伯以诺和挪亚代表受造的族类亚伯拉罕以撒雅各和约瑟代表蒙召的族类其中所记载的主要不是这些人的工作乃是他们的生命生活并他们在神面前的道路在创世记里神用创造的记载和八个人物的传记启示出完成祂定旨的生命圣经恢复本创一1注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:21:17.705685+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Apparently chs 12 of Genesis are merely a record of creation actually nearly every item in the record of these two chapters is a revelation of Christ who is life to Gods people John 11 4 1125 146 for the producing and building up of the church Chapters 350 present biographies of eight great persons in two groups of four representing two races of men Adam Abel Enoch and Noah representing the created race and Abraham Isaac Jacob and Joseph representing the called race What is recorded is not primarily the works of these men but mainly their life their living and their way with God In Genesis God uses both the record of creation and the biographies of eight persons to reveal the life that fulfills His purpose"}
{"zh": "以斯拉记 以色列人从被掳中归回，重建神的殿，开始了神选民中间照着神的经纶，为着神在地上见证的恢复。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Ezra—The return of the children of Israel from their captivity and the rebuilding of the temple of God, initiating the recovery of God's testimony among His elect on the earth according to His economy.", "norm_zh": "以斯拉记以色列人从被掳中归回重建神的殿开始了神选民中间照着神的经纶为着神在地上见证的恢复圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "EzraThe return of the children of Israel from their captivity and the rebuilding of the temple of God initiating the recovery of Gods testimony among His elect on the earth according to His economy"}
{"zh": "尼希米记 重建耶路撒冷的城墙，继续神选民中间祂见证的恢复，以完成祂的经纶。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Nehemiah—The rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem and the continuing of the recovery of God's testimony among His elect for the carrying out of His economy.", "norm_zh": "尼希米记重建耶路撒冷的城墙继续神选民中间祂见证的恢复以完成祂的经纶圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "NehemiahThe rebuilding of the wall of Jerusalem and the continuing of the recovery of Gods testimony among His elect for the carrying out of His economy"}
{"zh": "以斯帖记 拣选以色列人作选民的这位神，在他们被掳到外邦列国中的期间，对他们成了隐藏的神，秘密的照顾他们，并在隐密中公开的拯救他们。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Esther — The God who chose Israel as His elect, becoming a hidden God to them during the period of their captivity to the Gentile nations, secretly taking care of them and openly saving them in secrecy.", "norm_zh": "以斯帖记拣选以色列人作选民的这位神在他们被掳到外邦列国中的期间对他们成了隐藏的神秘密的照顾他们并在隐密中公开的拯救他们圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Esther The God who chose Israel as His elect becoming a hidden God to them during the period of their captivity to the Gentile nations secretly taking care of them and openly saving them in secrecy"}
{"zh": "约伯记 神对付祂选民的目的。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Job — The purpose of God's dealing with His elect.", "norm_zh": "约伯记神对付祂选民的目的圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Job The purpose of Gods dealing with His elect"}
{"zh": "诗篇 寻求并接触神的敬虔之人，借着他们的赞美、祷告、并欢腾的歌唱，表达他们的情绪、感觉、感想和经历。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Psalms—the expressions of the sentiments, feelings, impressions, and experiences of godly men seeking and contacting God through their praises, prayers, and jubilant singings.", "norm_zh": "诗篇寻求并接触神的敬虔之人借着他们的赞美祷告并欢腾的歌唱表达他们的情绪感觉感想和经历圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Psalmsthe expressions of the sentiments feelings impressions and experiences of godly men seeking and contacting God through their praises prayers and jubilant singings"}
{"zh": "传道书 所罗门的教训，给人看见在败坏世界里的人生，都是虚空，都是捕风。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Ecclesiastes — The teachings of Solomon, showing that the human life in the corrupted world is vanity, a chasing after wind.", "norm_zh": "传道书所罗门的教训给人看见在败坏世界里的人生都是虚空都是捕风圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ecclesiastes The teachings of Solomon showing that the human life in the corrupted world is vanity a chasing after wind"}
{"zh": "雅歌 一个超绝婚姻里爱的历史，启示出个别信徒与基督爱的交通中进展的经历。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Song of Songs — A history of love in an excellent marriage, revealing the progressive experience of an individual believer's loving fellowship with Christ.", "norm_zh": "雅歌一个超绝婚姻里爱的历史启示出个别信徒与基督爱的交通中进展的经历圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Song of Songs A history of love in an excellent marriage revealing the progressive experience of an individual believers loving fellowship with Christ"}
{"zh": "以赛亚书 耶和华借着成为肉体、钉死十架、复活、升天、并再来的基督所施的救恩。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Isaiah — The salvation of Jehovah through Christ, incarnated, crucified, resurrected, ascended, and coming again.", "norm_zh": "以赛亚书耶和华借着成为肉体钉死十架复活升天并再来的基督所施的救恩圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Isaiah The salvation of Jehovah through Christ incarnated crucified resurrected ascended and coming again"}
{"zh": "耶利米书 基督在神对付以色列和列国时，成为耶和华对神选民的义，作他们的中心和圆周。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Jeremiah — Christ being made the righteousness of Jehovah to God's elect as their center and circumference in God's dealing with Israel and the nations.", "norm_zh": "耶利米书基督在神对付以色列和列国时成为耶和华对神选民的义作他们的中心和圆周圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jeremiah Christ being made the righteousness of Jehovah to Gods elect as their center and circumference in Gods dealing with Israel and the nations"}
{"zh": "耶利米哀歌 耶利米对神的圣城和圣民之忧伤与爱的发表。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Lamentations — The expression of Jeremiah's sorrow and love over the holy city and the holy people of God.", "norm_zh": "耶利米哀歌耶利米对神的圣城和圣民之忧伤与爱的发表圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Lamentations The expression of Jeremiahs sorrow and love over the holy city and the holy people of God"}
{"zh": "以西结书 神在荣耀里向人显现；祂对自己百姓和列国的审判，以及祂选民的恢复，为着建造一个居所，为祂并作祂相互的住处和完全的彰显。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Ezekiel — God's appearing to man in glory, His judgment upon His own people and the nations, and the recovery of His elect for the building of a dwelling place to be His and their mutual abode and complete expression.", "norm_zh": "以西结书神在荣耀里向人显现祂对自己百姓和列国的审判以及祂选民的恢复为着建造一个居所为祂并作祂相互的住处和完全的彰显圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Ezekiel Gods appearing to man in glory His judgment upon His own people and the nations and the recovery of His elect for the building of a dwelling place to be His and their mutual abode and complete expression"}
{"zh": "但以理书 神截定给以色列的定命，就是七十个七的内容。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Daniel — The destiny of Israel apportioned out by God, the contents of the seventy weeks.", "norm_zh": "但以理书神截定给以色列的定命就是七十个七的内容圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Daniel The destiny of Israel apportioned out by God the contents of the seventy weeks"}
{"zh": "何西阿书 耶和华是邪淫背道之以色列的救恩，接受并接纳她回来。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Hosea — Jehovah as the salvation to the adulterous and apostate Israel, receiving her and receiving her back.", "norm_zh": "何西阿书耶和华是邪淫背道之以色列的救恩接受并接纳她回来圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Hosea Jehovah as the salvation to the adulterous and apostate Israel receiving her and receiving her back"}
{"zh": "约珥书 人类政权对以色列四个阶段的残害，以及基督对残害者的毁坏，并祂在复兴时在以色列中间的掌权。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Joel — The devastation of the human government in four stages on Israel and the destruction of the devastators by Christ, as well as His reigning in the midst of Israel in the restoration.", "norm_zh": "约珥书人类政权对以色列四个阶段的残害以及基督对残害者的毁坏并祂在复兴时在以色列中间的掌权圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Joel The devastation of the human government in four stages on Israel and the destruction of the devastators by Christ as well as His reigning in the midst of Israel in the restoration"}
{"zh": "约拿书 耶和华的救恩，甚至临到外邦人的城尼尼微。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Jonah — Jehovah's salvation extending even to the Gentile city Nineveh.", "norm_zh": "约拿书耶和华的救恩甚至临到外邦人的城尼尼微圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Jonah Jehovahs salvation extending even to the Gentile city Nineveh"}
{"zh": "弥迦书 耶和华对以色列的责备，以及祂对以色列的复兴。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Micah — Jehovah's reproof on Israel and His restoration of Israel.", "norm_zh": "弥迦书耶和华对以色列的责备以及祂对以色列的复兴圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Micah Jehovahs reproof on Israel and His restoration of Israel"}
{"zh": "那鸿书 耶和华对邪恶亚述之京城尼尼微的审判。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Nahum — Jehovah's judgment on the evil capital of Assyria, Nineveh.", "norm_zh": "哪鸿书耶和华对邪恶亚述之京城尼尼微的审判圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Nahum Jehovahs judgment on the evil capital of Assyria Nineveh"}
{"zh": "哈巴谷书 神先借着迦勒底人对以色列施行公义的审判，然后又借着列国对迦勒底人施行公义的审判。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Habakkuk — God's righteous judgment, first on Israel by the Chaldeans and then on the Chaldeans by the nations.", "norm_zh": "哈巴谷书神先借着迦勒底人对以色列施行公义的审判然后又借着列国对迦勒底人施行公义的审判圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Habakkuk Gods righteous judgment first on Israel by the Chaldeans and then on the Chaldeans by the nations"}
{"zh": "西番雅书 耶和华对以色列和列国的审判，以及祂对外邦和以色列的拯救。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Zephaniah — Jehovah's judgment on Israel and on the nations, and His salvation to the Gentiles and to Israel.", "norm_zh": "西番雅书耶和华对以色列和列国的审判以及祂对外邦和以色列的拯救圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Zephaniah Jehovahs judgment on Israel and on the nations and His salvation to the Gentiles and to Israel"}
{"zh": "哈该书 耶和华对付被掳归回的人，为着建造祂的殿。（圣经恢复本）", "en": "Haggai — Jehovah's dealing with the returned captives for the building of His temple.", "norm_zh": "哈该书耶和华对付被掳归回的人为着建造祂的殿圣经恢复本", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:22:54.012004+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Haggai Jehovahs dealing with the returned captives for the building of His temple"}
