{"zh": "圣经乃是神的说话", "en": "The Bible is God's speaking", "norm_zh": "圣经乃是神的说话", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The Bible is Gods speaking"}
{"zh": "在旧约，神是借着众申言者，就是借着被神的灵推动的人说话。（彼后一21）在新约，神是在子里，就是在子的人位里说话。子就是神自己，（8）是彰显出来的神。父神是隐藏的，子神是显出的。从来没有人见过神；惟有子，就是神的话，（约一1，启十九13）和神的说话，借着完全的彰显、说明并解释，将神表明出来。（约一18）（圣经恢复本，来一2注2）", "en": "In the Old Testament, God spoke in the prophets, in men borne by His Spirit (2 Pet. 1:21). In the New Testament, He speaks in the Son, in the person of the Son. The Son is God Himself (v. 8), God expressed. God the Father is hidden; God the Son is expressed. No one has ever seen God; the Son, as the Word of God (John 1:1; Rev. 19:13) and the speaking of God, has declared Him with a full expression, explanation, and definition of Him (John 1:18).", "norm_zh": "在旧约神是借着众申言者就是借着被神的灵推动的人说话彼后一21在新约神是在子里就是在子的人位里说话子就是神自己8是彰显出来的神父神是隐藏的子神是显出的从来没有人见过神惟有子就是神的话约一1启十九13和神的说话借着完全的彰显说明并解释将神表明出来约一18圣经恢复本来一2注2", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In the Old Testament God spoke in the prophets in men borne by His Spirit 2 Pet 121 In the New Testament He speaks in the Son in the person of the Son The Son is God Himself v 8 God expressed God the Father is hidden God the Son is expressed No one has ever seen God the Son as the Word of God John 11 Rev 1913 and the speaking of God has declared Him with a full expression explanation and definition of Him John 118"}
{"zh": "论到新约", "en": "Concerning the New Covenant", "norm_zh": "论到新约", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Concerning the New Covenant"}
{"zh": "四卷福音书", "en": "The four Gospels", "norm_zh": "四卷福音书", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "The four Gospels"}
{"zh": "在罗马书里我们看见，基督的生命是义的生命，使我们得称义；是圣的生命，使我们蒙圣别；也是得胜的生命，使我们成为得胜者。罗马书也告诉我们，我们能在基督这神圣的生命中作王。这生命能使我们成为王，使我们成为君尊的。在哥林多书，基督在实行的召会生活中是一切。（雅歌生命读经，第八篇；希伯来书生命读经，第一篇）", "en": "In Romans we see that Christ's life is a life of righteousness for our justification, a holy life for our sanctification, and a victorious life to make us overcomers. Romans also tells us that we can reign in this divine life of Christ. This life can make us kings; it can make us royal. In Corinthians, Christ is everything in the practical church life.", "norm_zh": "在罗马书里我们看见基督的生命是义的生命使我们得称义是圣的生命使我们蒙圣别也是得胜的生命使我们成为得胜者罗马书也告诉我们我们能在基督这神圣的生命中作王这生命能使我们成为王使我们成为君尊的在哥林多书基督在实行的召会生活中是一切雅歌生命读经第八篇希伯来书生命读经第一篇", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "In Romans we see that Christs life is a life of righteousness for our justification a holy life for our sanctification and a victorious life to make us overcomers Romans also tells us that we can reign in this divine life of Christ This life can make us kings it can make us royal In Corinthians Christ is everything in the practical church life"}
{"zh": "加拉太、以弗所、腓立比和歌罗西", "en": "Galatians, Ephesians, Philippians, and Colossians", "norm_zh": "加拉太以弗所腓立比和歌罗西", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "Galatians Ephesians Philippians and Colossians"}
{"zh": "帖撒罗尼迦前后书启示为着召会生活之圣别生活的三方面—事奉活神、圣别为人，并等候主来；前书是为着鼓励和安慰，后书是为着改正和平衡。（圣经恢复本，帖撒罗尼迦前书主题；帖前一3注1）", "en": "1 and 2 Thessalonians reveal three aspects of a holy life for the church life—serving a living God, conducting a holy life, and waiting for the Lord's coming; the first book is for encouragement and comfort, and the second is for correction and balance.", "norm_zh": "帖撒罗尼迦前后书启示为着召会生活之圣别生活的三方面事奉活神圣别为人并等候主来前书是为着鼓励和安慰后书是为着改正和平衡圣经恢复本帖撒罗尼迦前书主提帖前一3注1", "saved_at": "2026-07-08T06:23:42.375739+00:00", "prompt_version": "", "source": "enhanced_translate", "norm_en": "1 and 2 Thessalonians reveal three aspects of a holy life for the church lifeserving a living God conducting a holy life and waiting for the Lords coming the first book is for encouragement and comfort and the second is for correction and balance"}
